{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DAczZ9opHKE7CFpRRkonWL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t--- requirements.json ---\n2\t{\n3\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n4\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n5\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n6\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n7\t\n8\t  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n9\t    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: User (email, passwordHash, role, status, lockout fields), AuthToken (invite/reset tokens, SHA-256 hash, expiry) and AuditLog (actor, action, entity, metadata, IP) via the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n10\t    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"/login page built from MUI patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email/password fields, submitting via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 1\" },\n11\t    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"authorize() lower-cases/trims the email, rejects a non-existent user, a user whose status is not ACTIVE, an archived user, or a locked user, and otherwise compares the password with bcrypt (cost 12).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 2\" },\n12\t    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in failure messaging: the same 'Email or password is incorrect.' message for unknown-user/wrong-password, a distinct locked-account message with the remaining minutes, and a distinct disabled-account message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 3\" },\n13\t    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"Lockout counter: increment failedLoginCount on a wrong password; at 5 failures set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the counter; on success reset the counter to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 4\" },\n14\t    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in rate limit of 10 attempts per IP per 5-minute sliding window (in-memory, src/server/rate-limit.ts, exported for reuse); exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and a 'Too many attempts' message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 5\" },\n15\t    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl when it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 6\" },\n16\t    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout for the relevant sign-in outcomes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 7\" },\n17\t    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"JWT session strategy, 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the token and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 1\" },\n18\t    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"If passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time the session is treated as invalid, forcing re-login on every device after a password change; checked at most once every 5 minutes per token in the jwt callback.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 2\" },\n19\t    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated requests for any (app)-group path to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 JSON for /api/* paths except /api/health, /api/auth/* and paths listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 3\" },\n20\t    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] looks the token up by SHA-256 hash; it must be type INVITE, unused and not expired (7-day expiry), otherwise show the invalid/expired-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 1\" },\n21\t    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation form shows the invited user's name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },\n22\t    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },\n23\t    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },\n24\t    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },\n25\t    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },\n26\t    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },\n27\t    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },\n28\t    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },\n29\t    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },\n30\t    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },\n31\t    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },\n32\t    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },\n33\t    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },\n34\t    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },\n35\t    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },\n36\t    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n37\t  ],\n38\t\n39\t  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n40\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },\n41\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },\n42\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },\n43\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },\n44\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n45\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n46\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n47\t    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n48\t  ],\n49\t\n50\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n51\t  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n52\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n53\t}\n54\t--- handoff-to-architect.json ---\n55\t{\n56\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n57\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n58\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n59\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n60\t\n61\t  \"status\": \"complete\",\n62\t  \"requirementsCount\": 36,\n63\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n64\t  \"blockers\": [],\n65\t  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n66\t}\n67\t--- tech-stack.json ---\n68\t{\n69\t  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n70\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n71\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n72\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n73\t\n74\t  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n75\t  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n76\t  \"detectionNotes\": \"PRD run mode explicitly states '--brownfield --tech-stack react'. This is PRD-01 on top of the PRD-00 foundation already in the workspace (ticket abcd-1): Next.js 14 App Router / React 18 / TypeScript strict, Material UI v9 via @emotion styling, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod, React Hook Form, Vitest + Testing Library + Playwright — all reused unchanged, not re-scaffolded. This PRD adds Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider with JWT session strategy and bcrypt password hashing on top of that base. No enum value exists for 'nextjs' specifically, so 'react' is used as the closest match, consistent with abcd-1's detection.\",\n77\t  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n78\t}\n79\t--- tech-stack-decisions.md ---\n80\t# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n81\t\n82\tTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n83\t\n84\tThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\n85\tRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\n86\tReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\n87\tNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\n88\tADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\n89\tconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n90\t\n91\t---\n92\t\n93\t## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n94\t\n95\t**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n96\t\n97\t**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\n98\tcalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\n99\tactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\n100\tcredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\n101\ta single-provider app.\n102\t\n103\t**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n104\t(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n105\t`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\n106\troute through, not a new auth layer.\n107\t\n108\t---\n109\t\n110\t## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n111\t\n112\t**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n113\t\n114\t**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\n115\tverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\n116\truns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\n117\tso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\n118\tCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\n119\tif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\n120\tto revisit.\n121\t\n122\t**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\n123\tother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n128\t\n129\t**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n130\t\n131\t**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\n132\tencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\n133\tLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\n134\tlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\n135\tconstant-time comparison outright.\n136\t\n137\t**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n138\t(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\n139\telsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n140\t\n141\t---\n142\t\n143\t## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n144\t\n145\t**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n146\t\n147\t**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\n148\tand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\n149\tMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\n150\tRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n151\t\n152\t**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\n153\tacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n154\t`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n155\t\n156\t---\n157\t\n158\t## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n159\t\n160\t**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n161\t\n162\t**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n163\t`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n164\t`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n165\t`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n166\t\n167\t**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n168\t(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n169\t(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n170\t\n171\t---\n172\t\n173\t## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n174\t\n175\t**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n176\t\n177\t**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n178\t`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\n179\tbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\n180\tpattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\n181\tZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\n182\tstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\n183\tschema, not two.\n184\t\n185\t**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\n186\tUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n187\t\n188\t---\n189\t\n190\t## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n191\t\n192\t**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n193\t\n194\t**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\n195\thashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\n196\tintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\n197\tchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\n198\texisting Playwright setup.\n199\t\n200\t**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n201\t(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\n202\tinfra to stand up.\n203\t\n204\t---\n205\t\n206\t## Status\n207\t\n208\tSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\n209\tspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\n210\tof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n211\t`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n212\t--- requirements-analysis-notes.md ---\n213\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-2\n214\t\n215\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\n216\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 requirements — 28 FR + 8 NFR,\n217\t98% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`).\n218\t\n219\tArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Credentials\n220\tAuth Core**, **Rate Limiting**, **Session / Route Guard**, **Invite Flow**,\n221\t**Password Policy**, **Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Service\n222\tLayer**, **Permission Helpers**, **Audit Logging**, **App Shell Integration**,\n223\t**Notifications Stub**, **Seed Data**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Design System\n224\t(MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**.\n225\t\n226\t## Functional Requirements\n227\t\n228\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n229\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n230\t| FR-1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these three tables. Foundation entity; must land before any service/route work. |\n231\t| FR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | `/login` page, MUI-only form (Card/TextField/Button/InputAdornment+IconButton/Alert). Pure UI surface over FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should keep this a thin client wrapper around `signIn('credentials')`. |\n232\t| FR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` — the single chokepoint every sign-in attempt routes through (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare). Depends on FR-1's `User` fields; feeds FR-4 (messaging), FR-5 (lockout), FR-8 (audit), NFR-2 (timing). This is the one function `arch-design-system` should design as a named module, not inline route code. |\n233\t| FR-4 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in failure messaging matrix (unknown/wrong-password vs locked vs disabled) — a branch inside/alongside `authorize()`'s result, consumed by FR-2's Alert. Must stay consistent with NFR-2 (same-message branches can't differ in timing either). |\n234\t| FR-5 | Credentials Auth Core | Lockout counter (`failedLoginCount`/`lockedUntil`) — state mutation on `User` (FR-1) triggered from within `authorize()` (FR-3). Threshold/window (5 failures / 15 min) is a named constant the design doc should surface once, not re-literal. |\n235\t| FR-6 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, `src/server/rate-limit.ts`, explicitly exported for reuse — `arch-design-system` should treat this as a shared utility other PRDs' rate limits (e.g. FR-17's forgot-password limits) can reuse rather than re-implement. |\n236\t| FR-7 | Credentials Auth Core | Post-sign-in redirect with same-origin `callbackUrl` validation — a small pure function (open-redirect guard); shared by FR-11's middleware-generated `callbackUrl` and FR-12/14's invite-accept redirect-to-dashboard pattern. |\n237\t| FR-8 | Audit Logging | `auth.login.success`/`auth.login.failure`/`auth.lockout` entries — first concrete caller of FR-24's `audit()` helper; fires from inside `authorize()` (FR-3), so the design doc should clarify whether `authorize()` calls `audit()` directly or returns a result the route layer audits. |\n238\t| FR-9 | Session / Route Guard | JWT session strategy, 8h lifetime, `jwt`/`session` callbacks carry id/role/firstName/lastName/email — this is Auth.js config, not a new module; shapes what FR-23's `getCurrentUser()` can read without a DB round-trip. |\n239\t| FR-10 | Session / Route Guard | `passwordChangedAt`-vs-token-issue-time invalidation, throttled to once per 5 minutes in the `jwt` callback — lives in the same Auth.js config object as FR-9; ties directly to FR-20 (change-password must bump `passwordChangedAt` to actually invalidate other sessions). |\n240\t| FR-11 | Session / Route Guard | `middleware.ts` — redirect-to-login for `(app)` pages, 401 JSON for `/api/*` except an explicit allowlist (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `src/config/public-routes.ts`). This is the perimeter every protected route sits behind; MEDIUM confidence (allowlist file doesn't exist yet) — design doc should treat `public-routes.ts` as a new config file, not assume it. |\n241\t| FR-12 | Invite Flow | `/invite/[token]` lookup by SHA-256 hash, type/used/expiry checks (7-day) — reads `AuthToken` (FR-1); the expired/invalid branch needs its own UI state distinct from FR-4's sign-in-failure messaging. |\n242\t| FR-13 | Invite Flow | Accept-invitation form (read-only name/email + new/confirm password) — UI surface over FR-14's submit handler, same MUI-component constraint as FR-2. |\n243\t| FR-14 | Invite Flow | Accept-invite submit: FR-15 password-policy validation → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → mark token used → sign in → redirect `/dashboard` → audit `auth.invite.accepted`. Multi-step transaction; design doc should specify this as one service-layer function (likely alongside FR-22's `users.ts`) so the steps stay atomic rather than split across the route handler. |\n244\t| FR-15 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — length/letter+digit/not-email/not-in-common-list rules. Pure validation module with no DB/session dependency; shared by FR-14 (invite accept), FR-19 (reset), FR-20 (change-password) — three call sites, one rule set. |\n245\t| FR-16 | Password Policy | Live password-strength checklist UI — client-side mirror of FR-15's rules; design doc should flag the risk of the client-side rule list drifting from the server-side one and specify a single shared source (e.g. export rule predicates from `auth.ts` for both server validation and client display). |\n246\t| FR-17 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` — constant response message regardless of account existence (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2), plus its own rate limits (3/email/hour, 10/IP/hour) — second consumer of FR-6's rate-limit module, different window/key shape (per-email in addition to per-IP). |\n247\t| FR-18 | Password Reset Flow | Reset-token issuance: 32 random bytes base64url, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens for the user, `sendAuthEmail(..., 'password-reset', ...)`. Second `AuthToken` producer after FR-12's invite tokens — same table, different `AuthTokenType`; \"invalidate older unused tokens\" is a stateful rule the design doc should name explicitly (e.g. a `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper shared with FR-14's token-used marking). |\n248\t| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow | `/reset-password/[token]` — set new hash + `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout fields, mark token used, audit `auth.password.reset`, redirect to `/login`. Reuses FR-15 (policy), and clearing lockout fields here is a detail that must stay in sync with FR-5's lockout field set. |\n249\t| FR-20 | Change Password | `/account/security` change-password form — current-password check (field error on mismatch) + FR-15 policy on new password; success bumps `passwordChangedAt` (which is what makes FR-10's other-session invalidation actually fire) and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out too. |\n250\t| FR-21 | App Shell Integration | \"Account security\" user-menu entry → `/account/security`. Small nav-config addition, same user-menu surface as FR-25. |\n251\t| FR-22 | Service Layer | `src/server/services/users.ts`: `createUser`/`createInviteToken`/`sendInvite`/`setUserStatus`/`unlockUser`. Explicitly \"for later PRDs\" — this phase defines the module's public surface/signatures even though only `createInviteToken`-adjacent logic (FR-14/28 seeding) is exercised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |\n252\t| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |\n253\t| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |\n254\t| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |\n255\t| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |\n256\t| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |\n257\t| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |\n258\t\n259\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n260\t\n261\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n262\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n263\t| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |\n264\t| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |\n265\t| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |\n266\t| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |\n267\t| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |\n268\t| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |\n269\t| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |\n270\t| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |\n271\t\n272\t## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n273\t\n274\t- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.\n275\t- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.\n276\t- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.\n277\t- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"\n278\t- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.\n279\t- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8.\n280\t--- ls architect dir ---\n281\ttotal 96\n282\tdrwxr-xr-x  8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Oct 16 21:36 .\n283\tdrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n284\t-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   1571 Oct 16 20:13 api-contracts.json\n285\t-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff    206 Oct 16 20:13 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n286\t-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  13957 Oct 16 21:36 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n287\t-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   8590 Oct 16 20:12 system-design.md\n288\t-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   5339 Oct 16 21:32 tech-stack-decisions.md\n289\t-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff    398 Oct 16 20:14 threat-model-notes.json\n290\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22baf961-7824-4991-a527-ffc6e7677d2f","uuid":"68a13184-5389-4ded-93a4-741dd6d9537d","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:37:04.857Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub-prds/22baf961-7824-4991-a527-ffc6e7677d2f/tool-results/bz33os5ap.txt","content":"--- requirements.json ---\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"FR-1\",  \"description\": \"Data model: User (email, passwordHash, role, status, lockout fields), AuthToken (invite/reset tokens, SHA-256 hash, expiry) and AuditLog (actor, action, entity, metadata, IP) via the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-1 Data model\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-2\",  \"description\": \"/login page built from MUI patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors) with email/password fields, submitting via Auth.js signIn('credentials').\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-3\",  \"description\": \"authorize() lower-cases/trims the email, rejects a non-existent user, a user whose status is not ACTIVE, an archived user, or a locked user, and otherwise compares the password with bcrypt (cost 12).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-4\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in failure messaging: the same 'Email or password is incorrect.' message for unknown-user/wrong-password, a distinct locked-account message with the remaining minutes, and a distinct disabled-account message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-5\",  \"description\": \"Lockout counter: increment failedLoginCount on a wrong password; at 5 failures set lockedUntil = now + 15 minutes and reset the counter; on success reset the counter to 0 and set lastLoginAt.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 4\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-6\",  \"description\": \"Sign-in rate limit of 10 attempts per IP per 5-minute sliding window (in-memory, src/server/rate-limit.ts, exported for reuse); exceeding it returns RATE_LIMITED and a 'Too many attempts' message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 5\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-7\",  \"description\": \"After sign-in, redirect to callbackUrl when it is a same-origin relative path, otherwise redirect to /dashboard.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-8\",  \"description\": \"Write audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email, reason) and auth.lockout for the relevant sign-in outcomes.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-2 Sign-in (/login), item 7\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-9\",  \"description\": \"JWT session strategy, 8-hour lifetime refreshed on activity; the token and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-10\", \"description\": \"If passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time the session is treated as invalid, forcing re-login on every device after a password change; checked at most once every 5 minutes per token in the jwt callback.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-11\", \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated requests for any (app)-group path to /login?callbackUrl=<path>, and returns 401 JSON for /api/* paths except /api/health, /api/auth/* and paths listed in src/config/public-routes.ts.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-3 Session, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-12\", \"description\": \"/invite/[token] looks the token up by SHA-256 hash; it must be type INVITE, unused and not expired (7-day expiry), otherwise show the invalid/expired-link message.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-13\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation form shows the invited user's name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n--- handoff-to-architect.json ---\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 36,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}\n--- tech-stack.json ---\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-2\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-16T16:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"PRD run mode explicitly states '--brownfield --tech-stack react'. This is PRD-01 on top of the PRD-00 foundation already in the workspace (ticket abcd-1): Next.js 14 App Router / React 18 / TypeScript strict, Material UI v9 via @emotion styling, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod, React Hook Form, Vitest + Testing Library + Playwright — all reused unchanged, not re-scaffolded. This PRD adds Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider with JWT session strategy and bcrypt password hashing on top of that base. No enum value exists for 'nextjs' specifically, so 'react' is used as the closest match, consistent with abcd-1's detection.\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}\n--- tech-stack-decisions.md ---\n# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\nRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\nNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\nADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\nconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n\n**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\ncalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\nactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\ncredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\na single-provider app.\n\n**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\nroute through, not a new auth layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n\n**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\nverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\nruns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\nso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\nCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\nif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\nto revisit.\n\n**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\nother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n\n**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\nencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\nLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\nlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\nconstant-time comparison outright.\n\n**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\nelsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n\n**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n\n**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\nand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\nMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\nRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n\n**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\nacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n\n**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\nbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\npattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\nZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\nstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\nschema, not two.\n\n**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\nUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n\n**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n\n**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\nhashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\nintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\nchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\nexisting Playwright setup.\n\n**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\ninfra to stand up.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\nspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\nof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n--- requirements-analysis-notes.md ---\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-2\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 requirements — 28 FR + 8 NFR,\n98% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`).\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Credentials\nAuth Core**, **Rate Limiting**, **Session / Route Guard**, **Invite Flow**,\n**Password Policy**, **Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Service\nLayer**, **Permission Helpers**, **Audit Logging**, **App Shell Integration**,\n**Notifications Stub**, **Seed Data**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Design System\n(MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these three tables. Foundation entity; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | `/login` page, MUI-only form (Card/TextField/Button/InputAdornment+IconButton/Alert). Pure UI surface over FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should keep this a thin client wrapper around `signIn('credentials')`. |\n| FR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` — the single chokepoint every sign-in attempt routes through (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare). Depends on FR-1's `User` fields; feeds FR-4 (messaging), FR-5 (lockout), FR-8 (audit), NFR-2 (timing). This is the one function `arch-design-system` should design as a named module, not inline route code. |\n| FR-4 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in failure messaging matrix (unknown/wrong-password vs locked vs disabled) — a branch inside/alongside `authorize()`'s result, consumed by FR-2's Alert. Must stay consistent with NFR-2 (same-message branches can't differ in timing either). |\n| FR-5 | Credentials Auth Core | Lockout counter (`failedLoginCount`/`lockedUntil`) — state mutation on `User` (FR-1) triggered from within `authorize()` (FR-3). Threshold/window (5 failures / 15 min) is a named constant the design doc should surface once, not re-literal. |\n| FR-6 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, `src/server/rate-limit.ts`, explicitly exported for reuse — `arch-design-system` should treat this as a shared utility other PRDs' rate limits (e.g. FR-17's forgot-password limits) can reuse rather than re-implement. |\n| FR-7 | Credentials Auth Core | Post-sign-in redirect with same-origin `callbackUrl` validation — a small pure function (open-redirect guard); shared by FR-11's middleware-generated `callbackUrl` and FR-12/14's invite-accept redirect-to-dashboard pattern. |\n| FR-8 | Audit Logging | `auth.login.success`/`auth.login.failure`/`auth.lockout` entries — first concrete caller of FR-24's `audit()` helper; fires from inside `authorize()` (FR-3), so the design doc should clarify whether `authorize()` calls `audit()` directly or returns a result the route layer audits. |\n| FR-9 | Session / Route Guard | JWT session strategy, 8h lifetime, `jwt`/`session` callbacks carry id/role/firstName/lastName/email — this is Auth.js config, not a new module; shapes what FR-23's `getCurrentUser()` can read without a DB round-trip. |\n| FR-10 | Session / Route Guard | `passwordChangedAt`-vs-token-issue-time invalidation, throttled to once per 5 minutes in the `jwt` callback — lives in the same Auth.js config object as FR-9; ties directly to FR-20 (change-password must bump `passwordChangedAt` to actually invalidate other sessions). |\n| FR-11 | Session / Route Guard | `middleware.ts` — redirect-to-login for `(app)` pages, 401 JSON for `/api/*` except an explicit allowlist (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `src/config/public-routes.ts`). This is the perimeter every protected route sits behind; MEDIUM confidence (allowlist file doesn't exist yet) — design doc should treat `public-routes.ts` as a new config file, not assume it. |\n| FR-12 | Invite Flow | `/invite/[token]` lookup by SHA-256 hash, type/used/expiry checks (7-day) — reads `AuthToken` (FR-1); the expired/invalid branch needs its own UI state distinct from FR-4's sign-in-failure messaging. |\n| FR-13 | Invite Flow | Accept-invitation form (read-only name/email + new/confirm password) — UI surface over FR-14's submit handler, same MUI-component constraint as FR-2. |\n| FR-14 | Invite Flow | Accept-invite submit: FR-15 password-policy validation → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → mark token used → sign in → redirect `/dashboard` → audit `auth.invite.accepted`. Multi-step transaction; design doc should specify this as one service-layer function (likely alongside FR-22's `users.ts`) so the steps stay atomic rather than split across the route handler. |\n| FR-15 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — length/letter+digit/not-email/not-in-common-list rules. Pure validation module with no DB/session dependency; shared by FR-14 (invite accept), FR-19 (reset), FR-20 (change-password) — three call sites, one rule set. |\n| FR-16 | Password Policy | Live password-strength checklist UI — client-side mirror of FR-15's rules; design doc should flag the risk of the client-side rule list drifting from the server-side one and specify a single shared source (e.g. export rule predicates from `auth.ts` for both server validation and client display). |\n| FR-17 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` — constant response message regardless of account existence (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2), plus its own rate limits (3/email/hour, 10/IP/hour) — second consumer of FR-6's rate-limit module, different window/key shape (per-email in addition to per-IP). |\n| FR-18 | Password Reset Flow | Reset-token issuance: 32 random bytes base64url, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens for the user, `sendAuthEmail(..., 'password-reset', ...)`. Second `AuthToken` producer after FR-12's invite tokens — same table, different `AuthTokenType`; \"invalidate older unused tokens\" is a stateful rule the design doc should name explicitly (e.g. a `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper shared with FR-14's token-used marking). |\n| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow | `/reset-password/[token]` — set new hash + `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout fields, mark token used, audit `auth.password.reset`, redirect to `/login`. Reuses FR-15 (policy), and clearing lockout fields here is a detail that must stay in sync with FR-5's lockout field set. |\n| FR-20 | Change Password | `/account/security` change-password form — current-password check (field error on mismatch) + FR-15 policy on new password; success bumps `passwordChangedAt` (which is what makes FR-10's other-session invalidation actually fire) and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out too. |\n| FR-21 | App Shell Integration | \"Account security\" user-menu entry → `/account/security`. Small nav-config addition, same user-menu surface as FR-25. |\n| FR-22 | Service Layer | `src/server/services/users.ts`: `createUser`/`createInviteToken`/`sendInvite`/`setUserStatus`/`unlockUser`. Explicitly \"for later PRDs\" — this phase defines the module's public surface/signatures even though only `createInviteToken`-adjacent logic (FR-14/28 seeding) is exercised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |\n| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |\n| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |\n| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |\n| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |\n| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |\n| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |\n| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |\n| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |\n| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |\n| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |\n| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |\n| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |\n\n## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.\n- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.\n- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.\n- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"\n- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.\n- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8.\n--- ls architect dir ---\ntotal 96\ndrwxr-xr-x  8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Oct 16 21:36 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   1571 Oct 16 20:13 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff    206 Oct 16 20:13 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  13957 Oct 16 21:36 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   8590 Oct 16 20:12 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   5339 Oct 16 21:32 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff    398 Oct 16 20:14 threat-model-notes.json\n","numLines":290,"startLine":1,"totalLines":290}}}
