→ mark-used → sign-in → redirect → audit) | `src/app/(public)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (accept-invite step) | FR-12, FR-13, FR-14 |\n| 6 | Password Policy | Single Zod rule set (length, letter+digit, not-email, not-common-password) exported for both server validation and the client-side live checklist — one schema, not two | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |\n| 7 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` constant-response + rate limit, reset-token issuance (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens via a shared `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper), `/reset-password/[token]` (set hash, clear lockout fields, mark used, audit, redirect) | `src/app/(public)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-17, FR-18, FR-19 |\n| 8 | Change Password | `/account/security` form (current-password check, FR-15 policy on new password, bumps `passwordChangedAt`, re-issues current session token) | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` | FR-20, FR-21 |\n| 9 | Service Layer | Stable exported surface for this and later PRDs: `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-22, NFR-7 |\n| 10 | Permission Helpers | `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to `/login`), `requireRole(...roles)` (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to `/forbidden`) — no generic `can()` by design | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` | FR-23, NFR-8 |\n| 11 | Audit Logging | `audit()` insert-only helper: captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets — single call site signature for FR-8/14/19 | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-8, FR-14 (audit step), FR-19 (audit step), FR-24, NFR-1 |\n| 12 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu wired to real session (name/role badge/avatar initials, sign-out), \"Account security\" menu entry, `navigation.ts` switched from placeholder to real session role | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (user menu), `src/config/navigation.ts` | FR-21 (menu entry), FR-25, FR-26 |\n| 13 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info`; stable signature so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites | `src/server/email/send-auth-email.ts` | FR-27 |\n| 14 | Seed Data | Seeds six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user via the Service Layer (component 9), logs the invite link via component 13 | `prisma/seed.ts` | FR-28 |\n| 15 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) built from existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod resolver patterns; shared form-error pattern (`aria-live=\"polite\"`, focus-to-first-invalid-field) | reuses abcd-1's `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-4, NFR-5 |\n| 16 | Lint/CI Gate | No new lint rule; existing `no-restricted-imports` ESLint rule from abcd-1 continues to apply; `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` stay green, scope capped to this PRD's test list | `.eslintrc*` (unchanged) | NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| 17 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard), Vitest integration against test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password), Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2, 5, 7, 8 all depend\non 1 + 6 (Password Policy) + 11 (Audit) + 3 (Rate Limiting where noted). 4\n(Session/Route Guard) depends on 1 + 2 (consumes `authorize()`'s result) and\ngates 12 (App Shell) and every `(app)` page. 9 (Service Layer) is called by\n5, 7's reset-issuance, and 14 (Seed). 10 (Permission Helpers) backs up 4's\nperimeter at the page/handler level. 13 is called by 5 (seed-time invite\nlink) and 7 (reset email). 15–17 wrap all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Sign-in, `POST` via `signIn('credentials')` → `authorize()` (FR-2/3/4/5/7/8, NFR-2/3):**\n1. Rate limiter (component 3) checks 10 attempts/IP/5-min before any DB\n   work; over the limit short-circuits with `RATE_LIMITED` (FR-6).\n2. `authorize()` lower-cases/trims the email and looks up the `User`.\n3. Non-existent user → run the dummy bcrypt compare against a fixed hash\n   (NFR-2) anyway, then fail with the generic message (FR-4).\n4. Existing user: status ≠ ACTIVE, archived, or `lockedUntil` in the future\n   → fail with the disabled/locked message (locked message includes\n   remaining minutes) — no bcrypt compare needed here since the account\n   doesn't reach the password check per FR-4/FR-3's branch order.\n5. Otherwise bcrypt-compare (cost 12) the password.\n   - Wrong password: increment `failedLoginCount`; at 5 increments set\n     `lockedUntil = now + 15min` and reset the counter (FR-5); write\n     `auth.login.failure` (and `auth.lockout` if the threshold was just hit)\n     via `audit()` (component 11, FR-8).\n   - Correct password: reset `failedLoginCount` to 0, set `lastLoginAt`,\n     write `auth.login.success` (FR-8).\n6. On success, the `jwt` callback (component 4) stamps id/role/firstName/\n   lastName/email into the token (FR-9); the route layer validates\n   `callbackUrl` is a same-origin relative path before redirecting, else\n   falls back to `/dashboard` (FR-7).\n\n**Session validation, every request through `middleware.ts` + the `jwt`\ncallback (FR-9/10/11, NFR-1):**\n1. `middleware.ts` redirects unauthenticated `(app)` requests to\n   `/login?callbackUrl=<path>`; for `/api/*` it returns 401 JSON unless the\n   path is `/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, or listed in\n   `src/config/public-routes.ts`.\n2. The `jwt` callback checks — at most once per 5 minutes per token, to\n   bound cost — whether `passwordChangedAt` is later than the token's issue\n   time; if so the session is invalid and re-login is forced on that\n   device.\n\n**Invite acceptance, `/invite/[token]` (FR-12/13/14):**\n1. Look up the token by its SHA-256 hash (never store/compare the raw\n   token, NFR-1); it must be type INVITE, unused, and within 7 days of\n   issuance, else show the invalid/expired state (distinct from sign-in's\n   failure messaging).\n2. Valid token renders the invited user's name/email read-only plus\n   new/confirm-password fields.\n3. Submit runs as one service-layer step in `src/server/services/users.ts`:\n   validate against the Password Policy module (component 6) → hash →\n   `status = ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt = now` → mark token used → sign the\n   user in → redirect to `/dashboard` → `audit('auth.invite.accepted')`.\n   These steps stay together so a failure partway doesn't leave a used\n   token with no activated account.\n\n**Forgot/reset password (FR-17/18/19, pairs with NFR-2's anti-enumeration\nintent):**\n1. `/forgot-password` always returns the same message regardless of account\n   existence; rate-limited both per-email (3/hr) and per-IP (10/hr) through\n   component 3's configurable-key limiter.\n2. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issue a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random\n   bytes, base64url, 60-min expiry) and call `revokeUnusedTokens(userId,\n   'PASSWORD_RESET')` to invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user\n   — this invalidate-on-reissue rule is reset-specific and must not leak\n   into the invite path's token producer. Then `sendAuthEmail(user,\n   'password-reset', link)` (component 13).\n3. `/reset-password/[token]` sets the new hash and `passwordChangedAt`,\n   clears the lockout fields (`failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil` — kept in\n   sync with FR-5's lockout field set), marks the token used, audits\n   `auth.password.reset`, redirects to `/login`.\n\n**`passwordChangedAt` — one field, three writers, one reader:** FR-19\n(reset), FR-20 (change-password), and FR-14 (invite acceptance) each write\nthis timestamp; the `jwt` callback (FR-10) is the single reader that forces\nre-login elsewhere. Change-password (FR-20) additionally re-issues the\n*current* session's token immediately after writing it, so the acting user\nisn't logged out by their own action while every other session is.\n\n**App shell integration (FR-21/25/26):** once component 4 produces a real\nsession, component 12 replaces abcd-1's placeholder user-menu slot and\n`navigation.ts`'s placeholder role with the session's real name/role/\navatar-initials and `Role` value — a wiring change against abcd-1's existing\nfilter signature, not new UI.\n\n**Seed flow (FR-28):** `prisma/seed.ts` calls `createUser`/\n`createInviteToken` (component 9, not duplicated logic) to create six\nACTIVE users and one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), and\nlogs the invited user's invite link through `sendAuthEmail`'s `logger.info`\npath (component 13).\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + enums |\n| FR-2 | Component 2 — `/login` page (MUI form) |\n| FR-3 | Component 2 — `authorize()` |\n| FR-4 | Component 2 — failure-messaging matrix |\n| FR-5 | Component 2 — lockout counter mutation |\n| FR-6 | Component 3 — sign-in rate limit (10/IP/5min) |\n| FR-7 | Component 2 — `callbackUrl` same-origin guard |\n| FR-8 | Component 11 — `audit()` calls from `authorize()` |\n| FR-9 | Component 4 — `jwt`/`session` callbacks |\n| FR-10 | Component 4 — `passwordChangedAt` invalidation check |\n| FR-11 | Component 4 — `middleware.ts` + `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-12 | Component 5 — invite-token lookup |\n| FR-13 | Component 5 — accept-invitation form |\n| FR-14 | Component 5 — accept-invite submit (service-layer transaction) |\n| FR-15 | Component 6 — password-policy Zod schema |\n| FR-16 | Component 6 — live strength checklist (client mirror) |\n| FR-17 | Component 7 — `/forgot-password` + rate limit |\n| FR-18 | Component 7 — reset-token issuance + `revokeUnusedTokens` |\n| FR-19 | Component 7 — `/reset-password/[token]` |\n| FR-20 | Component 8 — `/account/security` change-password form |\n| FR-21 | Component 8 + Component 12 — \"Account security\" menu entry |\n| FR-22 | Component 9 — `src/server/services/users.ts` exports |\n| FR-23 | Component 10 — `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` |\n| FR-24 | Component 11 — `audit()` helper signature |\n| FR-25 | Component 12 — top-bar user menu (real session) |\n| FR-26 | Component 12 — `navigation.ts` real role wiring |\n| FR-27 | Component 13 — `sendAuthEmail()` stub |\n| FR-28 | Component 14 — `prisma/seed.ts` |\n| NFR-1 | Component 1 + 4 + 11 — hash-only tokens, constant-time compare, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite cookies, Auth.js CSRF |\n| NFR-2 | Component 2 — dummy bcrypt-compare branch |\n| NFR-3 | Component 2 — p95 < 1s budget at cost 12 |\n| NFR-4 | Component 15 — shared form-error pattern (all 5 auth forms) |\n| NFR-5 | Component 15 + 16 — MUI-only enforcement, existing ESLint rule |\n| NFR-6 | Component 17 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |\n| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 9 + 10 + 11 — brownfield reuse of abcd-1 conventions |\n| NFR-8 | Component 16 — lint/typecheck/test gate, scope cap |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 28 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\ndropped. FR-11 and FR-26 carry forward intake's MEDIUM-confidence notes\n(new `public-routes.ts` file; assumed-compatible `navigation.ts` signature)\nfor `arch-api-contracts` and dev-planning to verify against the real\nabcd-1 code rather than treat as settled. No blockers to carry forward —\n`arch-api-contracts` can proceed to deriving the API surface (the `/login`,\n`/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, and\n`/account/security` form-submission endpoints, plus Auth.js's own\n`/api/auth/*` routes).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":141,"newStart":1,"newLines":201,"lines":["-# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (SchoolHub scaffold PRD)","+# System Design — ticket abcd-2 (SchoolHub auth PRD)"," "," Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete"," "," ## Overview"," ","-This PRD is a greenfield scaffold: Next.js 14 App Router monolith, Postgres","-16 via Prisma, MUI v9 as the sole UI library, centralized API helpers, and a","-role-aware (but auth-unwired) app shell. Intake reported **100% confidence","-and zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is nothing to flag","-here beyond that figure. All 48 requirements are HIGH confidence with no","-clarification log entries.","+This PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 scaffold: it adds credentials","+authentication, session/route guarding, invite acceptance, password","+reset/change, permission helpers, and audit logging to the existing Next.js","+14 App Router / Prisma / MUI v9 app. Intake reported **98% confidence and","+zero blockers** (`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is","+nothing to flag here beyond that figure; all 28 FRs and 8 NFRs are HIGH","+confidence except FR-11 (MEDIUM — `src/config/public-routes.ts` doesn't","+exist yet and is treated below as a new file) and FR-26 (MEDIUM — assumed","+wiring change, not a rewrite, of `navigation.ts`'s existing filter","+signature)."," ","-Architecturally this is one deployable Next.js app with two route-group","-trees — `(app)` for the authenticated shell and `(public)` for the marketing","-page — sharing one design-system layer, one API-helper chokepoint","-(`src/server/http.ts`), and one data model (`SchoolSettings`, a singleton","-row later PRDs will extend). Auth does not exist yet: every place a later","-PRD will wire sign-in (user menu, `/forbidden`, nav role-filtering) is built","-as a placeholder/slot only, per the explicit \"for later PRDs\" language in","-FR-33/FR-39 and the cross-cutting note in `requirements-analysis-notes.md`.","-No new architecture decisions are made here beyond what `tech-stack-decisions.md`","-(ADR-1 through ADR-9) already fixed — this document arranges those choices","-into components and data flow.","+No new architecture decisions are made here beyond what","+`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 through ADR-7) already fixed: Auth.js","+(NextAuth v5) Credentials provider with JWT sessions, bcrypt (cost 12) with","+a dummy-compare for timing safety, Node's built-in `crypto` for tokens, an","+in-memory sliding-window rate limiter, Prisma-schema extension (no new","+DB/ORM), reuse of MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for every screen, and reuse","+of the existing Vitest/Playwright stack. This document arranges those","+choices into components and data flow, per NFR-7's brownfield discipline","+(reuse abcd-1's models/services/helpers; never re-scaffold or duplicate)."," ","+Three shared chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are","+designed below as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline","+route code: `authorize()` (sign-in), `audit()` (every audited action), and","+the password-policy module (every password-setting path). A fourth","+cross-cutting mechanism, the `passwordChangedAt` timestamp, ties together","+session invalidation, change-password, and reset-password and is called out","+in its own Data Flow subsection so its three writers don't drift.","+"," ## Component Breakdown"," ","-| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files |","-|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|","-| 1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline, npm script surface, path alias | `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.eslintrc*` |","-| 2 | Server Infra | Env validation, Prisma client singleton, structured logger, local Postgres | `src/lib/env.ts`, `src/server/db.ts`, `src/lib/logger.ts`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example` |","-| 3 | Data Model | Singleton `SchoolSettings` schema + idempotent seed | `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts` |","-| 4 | API Layer | Response envelopes, error mapping, pagination/body parsing, the one concrete endpoint | `src/server/http.ts`, `src/app/api/health/route.ts` |","-| 5 | Design System | Theme + provider tree + 10 shared MUI-composed components | `src/theme/theme.ts`, `src/components/*` |","-| 6 | App Shell (authenticated) | Sidebar/top-bar layout, role-filtered nav config, student-tab extension point, dashboard page | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/config/navigation.ts`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` |","-| 7 | Public Layout & Pages | Public header/footer, landing page, error/forbidden pages | `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/page.tsx`, `src/app/not-found.tsx`, `src/app/error.tsx`, `src/app/global-error.tsx`, `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` |","-| 8 | Lint/CI Gate | Banned-import ESLint rule, security headers | `.eslintrc*` (`no-restricted-imports`), `next.config.js` |","-| 9 | Test Harness | Unit/component + e2e/axe coverage of the above | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` |","+| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |","+|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|","+| 1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` models + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums, extending the existing Prisma schema | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-1, NFR-7 |","+| 2 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` chokepoint (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare → dummy-compare branch), `/login` page, failure-messaging matrix, lockout counter mutation, same-origin `callbackUrl` guard | `src/server/auth/authorize.ts`, `src/app/(public)/login/page.tsx`, `src/lib/callback-url.ts` | FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-7, NFR-2, NFR-3 |","+| 3 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, configurable key (per-IP, or per-email+per-IP), exported for reuse | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | FR-6, FR-17 |","+| 4 | Session / Route Guard | Auth.js config (`jwt`/`session` callbacks carrying id/role/firstName/lastName/email, 8h lifetime, `passwordChangedAt` invalidation throttled to 5-min checks), `middleware.ts` perimeter, new allowlist file | `src/server/auth/config.ts` (or `auth.ts`), `middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 |","+| 5 | Invite Flow | Token lookup by SHA-256 hash (type=INVITE, unused, 7-day expiry), accept-invite form + atomic submit (validate → hash → activate → mark-used → sign-in → redirect → audit) | `src/app/(public)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (accept-invite step) | FR-12, FR-13, FR-14 |","+| 6 | Password Policy | Single Zod rule set (length, letter+digit, not-email, not-common-password) exported for both server validation and the client-side live checklist — one schema, not two | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |","+| 7 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` constant-response + rate limit, reset-token issuance (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens via a shared `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper), `/reset-password/[token]` (set hash, clear lockout fields, mark used, audit, redirect) | `src/app/(public)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-17, FR-18, FR-19 |","+| 8 | Change Password | `/account/security` form (current-password check, FR-15 policy on new password, bumps `passwordChangedAt`, re-issues current session token) | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` | FR-20, FR-21 |","+| 9 | Service Layer | Stable exported surface for this and later PRDs: `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-22, NFR-7 |","+| 10 | Permission Helpers | `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to `/login`), `requireRole(...roles)` (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to `/forbidden`) — no generic `can()` by design | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` | FR-23, NFR-8 |","+| 11 | Audit Logging | `audit()` insert-only helper: captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets — single call site signature for FR-8/14/19 | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-8, FR-14 (audit step), FR-19 (audit step), FR-24, NFR-1 |","+| 12 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu wired to real session (name/role badge/avatar initials, sign-out), \"Account security\" menu entry, `navigation.ts` switched from placeholder to real session role | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (user menu), `src/config/navigation.ts` | FR-21 (menu entry), FR-25, FR-26 |","+| 13 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info`; stable signature so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites | `src/server/email/send-auth-email.ts` | FR-27 |","+| 14 | Seed Data | Seeds six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user via the Service Layer (component 9), logs the invite link via component 13 | `prisma/seed.ts` | FR-28 |","+| 15 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) built from existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod resolver patterns; shared form-error pattern (`aria-live=\"polite\"`, focus-to-first-invalid-field) | reuses abcd-1's `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-4, NFR-5 |","+| 16 | Lint/CI Gate | No new lint rule; existing `no-restricted-imports` ESLint rule from abcd-1 continues to apply; `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` stay green, scope capped to this PRD's test list | `.eslintrc*` (unchanged) | NFR-5, NFR-8 |","+| 17 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard), Vitest integration against test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password), Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |"," ","-Dependency order between components: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, and 1+2 → 5 → 6/7 (the","-shell and public layout both consume the design system and, for branding,","-`SchoolSettings` from component 3). Component 8 wraps all of 5–7. Component","-9 observes all of 2–7.","+Dependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2, 5, 7, 8 all depend","+on 1 + 6 (Password Policy) + 11 (Audit) + 3 (Rate Limiting where noted). 4","+(Session/Route Guard) depends on 1 + 2 (consumes `authorize()`'s result) and","+gates 12 (App Shell) and every `(app)` page. 9 (Service Layer) is called by","+5, 7's reset-issuance, and 14 (Seed). 10 (Permission Helpers) backs up 4's","+perimeter at the page/handler level. 13 is called by 5 (seed-time invite","+link) and 7 (reset email). 15–17 wrap all of the above."," "," ## Data Flow"," ","-**Page render (authenticated), e.g. `GET /dashboard`:**","-1. `(app)/layout.tsx` (server component) fetches the `SchoolSettings`","-   singleton once (FR-7) for top-bar branding (FR-33) — not re-queried by","-   child components.","-2. Root layout's provider tree (`AppRouterCacheProvider` → `ThemeProvider`","-   (`cssVariables`, light/dark) → `CssBaseline` → `LocalizationProvider`,","-   plus `InitColorSchemeScript`) wraps the shell so every page below inherits","-   theme/mode without a client-side flash (NFR-2's LCP budget depends on","-   this being server-rendered, not client-hydrated).","-3. Sidebar renders from `src/config/navigation.ts`, filtered by current","-   user role (role source is a stub today — no auth yet — filtering logic","-   exists so later PRDs plug a real role in without touching the shell).","-4. `/dashboard` page renders `PageHeader` + `EmptyState` (FR-34) — no data","-   fetch beyond step 1.","+**Sign-in, `POST` via `signIn('credentials')` → `authorize()` (FR-2/3/4/5/7/8, NFR-2/3):**","+1. Rate limiter (component 3) checks 10 attempts/IP/5-min before any DB","+   work; over the limit short-circuits with `RATE_LIMITED` (FR-6).","+2. `authorize()` lower-cases/trims the email and looks up the `User`.","+3. Non-existent user → run the dummy bcrypt compare against a fixed hash","+   (NFR-2) anyway, then fail with the generic message (FR-4).","+4. Existing user: status ≠ ACTIVE, archived, or `lockedUntil` in the future","+   → fail with the disabled/locked message (locked message includes","+   remaining minutes) — no bcrypt compare needed here since the account","+   doesn't reach the password check per FR-4/FR-3's branch order.","+5. Otherwise bcrypt-compare (cost 12) the password.","+   - Wrong password: increment `failedLoginCount`; at 5 increments set","+     `lockedUntil = now + 15min` and reset the counter (FR-5); write","+     `auth.login.failure` (and `auth.lockout` if the threshold was just hit)","+     via `audit()` (component 11, FR-8).","+   - Correct password: reset `failedLoginCount` to 0, set `lastLoginAt`,","+     write `auth.login.success` (FR-8).","+6. On success, the `jwt` callback (component 4) stamps id/role/firstName/","+   lastName/email into the token (FR-9); the route layer validates","+   `callbackUrl` is a same-origin relative path before redirecting, else","+   falls back to `/dashboard` (FR-7)."," ","-**API call, e.g. a future list endpoint or `GET /api/health`:**","-1. Route handler is wrapped in `withHandler(fn)` (ADR-4) — the single","-   chokepoint every route (including `/api/health`) must go through.","-2. Input parsing: `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (Zod) for request shape,","-   `parsePagination` for list endpoints (clamps `pageSize` ≤ 100, `page` ≥ 1).","-3. Handler body runs (for `/api/health`: `SELECT 1` against Prisma with a","-   2000ms budget).","-4. Success → `ok(data)` or `paginated(data, meta)`; failure inside","-   `withHandler` maps `ZodError` → `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `AppError` → its","-   status, Prisma `P2002`/`P2025` → `CONFLICT`/`NOT_FOUND`, anything else →","-   `INTERNAL` (stack logged via `src/lib/logger.ts`, never returned to the","-   client).","-5. Client-side, `DataTable` (for list endpoints) reads `rowCount`/`total`","-   straight from the `paginated()` envelope and syncs page/sort state to URL","-   query params — no separate client-side pagination state machine.","+**Session validation, every request through `middleware.ts` + the `jwt`","+callback (FR-9/10/11, NFR-1):**","+1. `middleware.ts` redirects unauthenticated `(app)` requests to","+   `/login?callbackUrl=<path>`; for `/api/*` it returns 401 JSON unless the","+   path is `/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, or listed in","+   `src/config/public-routes.ts`.","+2. The `jwt` callback checks — at most once per 5 minutes per token, to","+   bound cost — whether `passwordChangedAt` is later than the token's issue","+   time; if so the session is invalid and re-login is forced on that","+   device."," ","-**Env/startup flow:** `src/lib/env.ts` validates `process.env` via Zod","-before `src/server/db.ts` or any server entrypoint runs, throwing a","-readable per-variable error on failure — this is a fail-fast boundary, not","-a runtime-checked one.","+**Invite acceptance, `/invite/[token]` (FR-12/13/14):**","+1. Look up the token by its SHA-256 hash (never store/compare the raw","+   token, NFR-1); it must be type INVITE, unused, and within 7 days of","+   issuance, else show the invalid/expired state (distinct from sign-in's","+   failure messaging).","+2. Valid token renders the invited user's name/email read-only plus","+   new/confirm-password fields.","+3. Submit runs as one service-layer step in `src/server/services/users.ts`:","+   validate against the Password Policy module (component 6) → hash →","+   `status = ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt = now` → mark token used → sign the","+   user in → redirect to `/dashboard` → `audit('auth.invite.accepted')`.","+   These steps stay together so a failure partway doesn't leave a used","+   token with no activated account."," ","+**Forgot/reset password (FR-17/18/19, pairs with NFR-2's anti-enumeration","+intent):**","+1. `/forgot-password` always returns the same message regardless of account","+   existence; rate-limited both per-email (3/hr) and per-IP (10/hr) through","+   component 3's configurable-key limiter.","+2. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issue a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random","+   bytes, base64url, 60-min expiry) and call `revokeUnusedTokens(userId,","+   'PASSWORD_RESET')` to invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user","+   — this invalidate-on-reissue rule is reset-specific and must not leak","+   into the invite path's token producer. Then `sendAuthEmail(user,","+   'password-reset', link)` (component 13).","+3. `/reset-password/[token]` sets the new hash and `passwordChangedAt`,","+   clears the lockout fields (`failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil` — kept in","+   sync with FR-5's lockout field set), marks the token used, audits","+   `auth.password.reset`, redirects to `/login`.","+","+**`passwordChangedAt` — one field, three writers, one reader:** FR-19","+(reset), FR-20 (change-password), and FR-14 (invite acceptance) each write","+this timestamp; the `jwt` callback (FR-10) is the single reader that forces","+re-login elsewhere. Change-password (FR-20) additionally re-issues the","+*current* session's token immediately after writing it, so the acting user","+isn't logged out by their own action while every other session is.","+","+**App shell integration (FR-21/25/26):** once component 4 produces a real","+session, component 12 replaces abcd-1's placeholder user-menu slot and","+`navigation.ts`'s placeholder role with the session's real name/role/","+avatar-initials and `Role` value — a wiring change against abcd-1's existing","+filter signature, not new UI.","+","+**Seed flow (FR-28):** `prisma/seed.ts` calls `createUser`/","+`createInviteToken` (component 9, not duplicated logic) to create six","+ACTIVE users and one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), and","+logs the invited user's invite link through `sendAuthEmail`'s `logger.info`","+path (component 13).","+"," ## Requirements Traceability"," "," | Requirement | Design Element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | Component 1 — Scaffold/Tooling |","-| FR-2 | Component 1 — npm script surface |","-| FR-3 | Component 1 — `tsconfig.json` path alias |","-| FR-4 | Component 2 — `docker-compose.yml` |","-| FR-5 | Component 2 — `.env.example` |","-| FR-6 | Component 2 — `src/lib/env.ts` (startup flow) |","-| FR-7 | Component 3 — `prisma/schema.prisma` (`SchoolSettings`) |","-| FR-8 | Component 2 — `src/server/db.ts` singleton |","-| FR-9 | Component 3 — `prisma/seed.ts` |","-| FR-10 | Component 4 — `ok()` |","-| FR-11 | Component 4 — `paginated()` |","-| FR-12 | Component 4 — `apiError()` |","-| FR-13 | Component 4 — `withHandler()` (API call flow step 1/4) |","-| FR-14 | Component 4 — `parsePagination()` |","-| FR-15 | Component 4 — `parseBody`/`parseQuery` |","-| FR-16 | Component 4 — `GET /api/health` |","-| FR-17 | Component 5 — MUI package set (dependency, see ADR-5) |","-| FR-18 | Component 5 — `theme.ts` + provider tree (page render flow step 2) |","-| FR-19 | Component 8 — ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |","-| FR-20 | Component 5 — `PageHeader` |","-| FR-21 | Component 5 — `DataTable` (API call flow step 5) |","-| FR-22 | Component 5 — `EmptyState` |","-| FR-23 | Component 5 — `ConfirmDialog` |","-| FR-24 | Component 5 — `useToast`/`ToastProvider` |","-| FR-25 | Component 5 — `FormField` helpers |","-| FR-26 | Component 5 — `StatCard` |","-| FR-27 | Component 5 — `UserAvatar` |","-| FR-28 | Component 5 — `DateDisplay` + `formatInSchoolTz` (reads `SchoolSettings` tz) |","-| FR-29 | Component 5 — `LoadingSkeleton` |","-| FR-30 | Component 6 — `(app)/layout.tsx` sidebar/top bar |","-| FR-31 | Component 6 — responsive Drawer fork (<1024px) |","-| FR-32 | Component 6 — `src/config/navigation.ts` (page render flow step 3) |","-| FR-33 | Component 6 — top bar branding + user-menu/bell placeholders (auth slot, not wired) |","-| FR-34 | Component 6 — `/dashboard` page (page render flow step 4) |","-| FR-35 | Component 6 — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` extension point |","-| FR-36 | Component 7 — `(public)/layout.tsx` |","-| FR-37 | Component 7 — `/` landing page |","-| FR-38 | Component 7 — `not-found.tsx`/`error.tsx`/`global-error.tsx` |","-| FR-39 | Component 7 — `/forbidden` (auth slot, not wired) |","-| FR-40 | Component 2 — `src/lib/logger.ts` (API call flow step 4) |","-| NFR-1 | Component 8 — MUI-only enforcement (ESLint + MCP-docs process constraint) |","-| NFR-2 | Component 5 + 6 — server-rendered provider tree, no client-side theme flash |","-| NFR-3 | Component 5 + 9 — WCAG AA on shared components, axe-core e2e gate |","-| NFR-4 | Component 6 — responsive shell (360–1920px), generalizes FR-31 |","-| NFR-5 | Component 8 — `next.config.js` security headers |","-| NFR-6 | Component 9 — Vitest/Testing Library + Playwright coverage |","-| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 2 + 3 — fresh-clone bring-up script chain |","-| NFR-8 | Component 8 + 9 — lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e CI gate |","+| FR-1 | Component 1 — `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + enums |","+| FR-2 | Component 2 — `/login` page (MUI form) |","+| FR-3 | Component 2 — `authorize()` |","+| FR-4 | Component 2 — failure-messaging matrix |","+| FR-5 | Component 2 — lockout counter mutation |","+| FR-6 | Component 3 — sign-in rate limit (10/IP/5min) |","+| FR-7 | Component 2 — `callbackUrl` same-origin guard |","+| FR-8 | Component 11 — `audit()` calls from `authorize()` |","+| FR-9 | Component 4 — `jwt`/`session` callbacks |","+| FR-10 | Component 4 — `passwordChangedAt` invalidation check |","+| FR-11 | Component 4 — `middleware.ts` + `public-routes.ts` |","+| FR-12 | Component 5 — invite-token lookup |","+| FR-13 | Component 5 — accept-invitation form |","+| FR-14 | Component 5 — accept-invite submit (service-layer transaction) |","+| FR-15 | Component 6 — password-policy Zod schema |","+| FR-16 | Component 6 — live strength checklist (client mirror) |","+| FR-17 | Component 7 — `/forgot-password` + rate limit |","+| FR-18 | Component 7 — reset-token issuance + `revokeUnusedTokens` |","+| FR-19 | Component 7 — `/reset-password/[token]` |","+| FR-20 | Component 8 — `/account/security` change-password form |","+| FR-21 | Component 8 + Component 12 — \"Account security\" menu entry |","+| FR-22 | Component 9 — `src/server/services/users.ts` exports |","+| FR-23 | Component 10 — `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` |","+| FR-24 | Component 11 — `audit()` helper signature |","+| FR-25 | Component 12 — top-bar user menu (real session) |","+| FR-26 | Component 12 — `navigation.ts` real role wiring |","+| FR-27 | Component 13 — `sendAuthEmail()` stub |","+| FR-28 | Component 14 — `prisma/seed.ts` |","+| NFR-1 | Component 1 + 4 + 11 — hash-only tokens, constant-time compare, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite cookies, Auth.js CSRF |","+| NFR-2 | Component 2 — dummy bcrypt-compare branch |","+| NFR-3 | Component 2 — p95 < 1s budget at cost 12 |","+| NFR-4 | Component 15 — shared form-error pattern (all 5 auth forms) |","+| NFR-5 | Component 15 + 16 — MUI-only enforcement, existing ESLint rule |","+| NFR-6 | Component 17 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |","+| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 9 + 10 + 11 — brownfield reuse of abcd-1 conventions |","+| NFR-8 | Component 16 — lint/typecheck/test gate, scope cap |"," "," ## Status"," ","-Complete. All 48 requirement ids are accounted for above; none were dropped.","-No blockers to carry forward — `arch-api-contracts` can proceed directly to","-deriving the API surface (in practice, just `/api/health` plus the envelope","-contract every future endpoint must follow).","+Complete. All 28 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were","+dropped. FR-11 and FR-26 carry forward intake's MEDIUM-confidence notes","+(new `public-routes.ts` file; assumed-compatible `navigation.ts` signature)","+for `arch-api-contracts` and dev-planning to verify against the real","+abcd-1 code rather than treat as settled. No blockers to carry forward —","+`arch-api-contracts` can proceed to deriving the API surface (the `/login`,","+`/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, and","+`/account/security` form-submission endpoints, plus Auth.js's own","+`/api/auth/*` routes)."]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (SchoolHub scaffold PRD)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nThis PRD is a greenfield scaffold: Next.js 14 App Router monolith, Postgres\n16 via Prisma, MUI v9 as the sole UI library, centralized API helpers, and a\nrole-aware (but auth-unwired) app shell. Intake reported **100% confidence\nand zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is nothing to flag\nhere beyond that figure. All 48 requirements are HIGH confidence with no\nclarification log entries.\n\nArchitecturally this is one deployable Next.js app with two route-group\ntrees — `(app)` for the authenticated shell and `(public)` for the marketing\npage — sharing one design-system layer, one API-helper chokepoint\n(`src/server/http.ts`), and one data model (`SchoolSettings`, a singleton\nrow later PRDs will extend). Auth does not exist yet: every place a later\nPRD will wire sign-in (user menu, `/forbidden`, nav role-filtering) is built\nas a placeholder/slot only, per the explicit \"for later PRDs\" language in\nFR-33/FR-39 and the cross-cutting note in `requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\nNo new architecture decisions are made here beyond what `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9) already fixed — this document arranges those choices\ninto components and data flow.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|\n| 1 | Scaffold/Tooling | Next.js 14 + React 18 + TS strict + ESLint/Prettier baseline, npm script surface, path alias | `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.eslintrc*` |\n| 2 | Server Infra | Env validation, Prisma client singleton, structured logger, local Postgres | `src/lib/env.ts`, `src/server/db.ts`, `src/lib/logger.ts`, `docker-compose.yml`, `.env.example` |\n| 3 | Data Model | Singleton `SchoolSettings` schema + idempotent seed | `prisma/schema.prisma`, `prisma/seed.ts` |\n| 4 | API Layer | Response envelopes, error mapping, pagination/body parsing, the one concrete endpoint | `src/server/http.ts`, `src/app/api/health/route.ts` |\n| 5 | Design System | Theme + provider tree + 10 shared MUI-composed components | `src/theme/theme.ts`, `src/components/*` |\n| 6 | App Shell (authenticated) | Sidebar/top-bar layout, role-filtered nav config, student-tab extension point, dashboard page | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/config/navigation.ts`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` |\n| 7 | Public Layout & Pages | Public header/footer, landing page, error/forbidden pages | `src/app/(public)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/page.tsx`, `src/app/not-found.tsx`, `src/app/error.tsx`, `src/app/global-error.tsx`, `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` |\n| 8 | Lint/CI Gate | Banned-import ESLint rule, security headers | `.eslintrc*` (`no-restricted-imports`), `next.config.js` |\n| 9 | Test Harness | Unit/component + e2e/axe coverage of the above | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` |\n\nDependency order between components: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4, and 1+2 → 5 → 6/7 (the\nshell and public layout both consume the design system and, for branding,\n`SchoolSettings` from component 3). Component 8 wraps all of 5–7. Component\n9 observes all of 2–7.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Page render (authenticated), e.g. `GET /dashboard`:**\n1. `(app)/layout.tsx` (server component) fetches the `SchoolSettings`\n   singleton once (FR-7) for top-bar branding (FR-33) — not re-queried by\n   child components.\n2. Root layout's provider tree (`AppRouterCacheProvider` → `ThemeProvider`\n   (`cssVariables`, light/dark) → `CssBaseline` → `LocalizationProvider`,\n   plus `InitColorSchemeScript`) wraps the shell so every page below inherits\n   theme/mode without a client-side flash (NFR-2's LCP budget depends on\n   this being server-rendered, not client-hydrated).\n3. Sidebar renders from `src/config/navigation.ts`, filtered by current\n   user role (role source is a stub today — no auth yet — filtering logic\n   exists so later PRDs plug a real role in without touching the shell).\n4. `/dashboard` page renders `PageHeader` + `EmptyState` (FR-34) — no data\n   fetch beyond step 1.\n\n**API call, e.g. a future list endpoint or `GET /api/health`:**\n1. Route handler is wrapped in `withHandler(fn)` (ADR-4) — the single\n   chokepoint every route (including `/api/health`) must go through.\n2. Input parsing: `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (Zod) for request shape,\n   `parsePagination` for list endpoints (clamps `pageSize` ≤ 100, `page` ≥ 1).\n3. Handler body runs (for `/api/health`: `SELECT 1` against Prisma with a\n   2000ms budget).\n4. Success → `ok(data)` or `paginated(data, meta)`; failure inside\n   `withHandler` maps `ZodError` → `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `AppError` → its\n   status, Prisma `P2002`/`P2025` → `CONFLICT`/`NOT_FOUND`, anything else →\n   `INTERNAL` (stack logged via `src/lib/logger.ts`, never returned to the\n   client).\n5. Client-side, `DataTable` (for list endpoints) reads `rowCount`/`total`\n   straight from the `paginated()` envelope and syncs page/sort state to URL\n   query params — no separate client-side pagination state machine.\n\n**Env/startup flow:** `src/lib/env.ts` validates `process.env` via Zod\nbefore `src/server/db.ts` or any server entrypoint runs, throwing a\nreadable per-variable error on failure — this is a fail-fast boundary, not\na runtime-checked one.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — Scaffold/Tooling |\n| FR-2 | Component 1 — npm script surface |\n| FR-3 | Component 1 — `tsconfig.json` path alias |\n| FR-4 | Component 2 — `docker-compose.yml` |\n| FR-5 | Component 2 — `.env.example` |\n| FR-6 | Component 2 — `src/lib/env.ts` (startup flow) |\n| FR-7 | Component 3 — `prisma/schema.prisma` (`SchoolSettings`) |\n| FR-8 | Component 2 — `src/server/db.ts` singleton |\n| FR-9 | Component 3 — `prisma/seed.ts` |\n| FR-10 | Component 4 — `ok()` |\n| FR-11 | Component 4 — `paginated()` |\n| FR-12 | Component 4 — `apiError()` |\n| FR-13 | Component 4 — `withHandler()` (API call flow step 1/4) |\n| FR-14 | Component 4 — `parsePagination()` |\n| FR-15 | Component 4 — `parseBody`/`parseQuery` |\n| FR-16 | Component 4 — `GET /api/health` |\n| FR-17 | Component 5 — MUI package set (dependency, see ADR-5) |\n| FR-18 | Component 5 — `theme.ts` + provider tree (page render flow step 2) |\n| FR-19 | Component 8 — ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |\n| FR-20 | Component 5 — `PageHeader` |\n| FR-21 | Component 5 — `DataTable` (API call flow step 5) |\n| FR-22 | Component 5 — `EmptyState` |\n| FR-23 | Component 5 — `ConfirmDialog` |\n| FR-24 | Component 5 — `useToast`/`ToastProvider` |\n| FR-25 | Component 5 — `FormField` helpers |\n| FR-26 | Component 5 — `StatCard` |\n| FR-27 | Component 5 — `UserAvatar` |\n| FR-28 | Component 5 — `DateDisplay` + `formatInSchoolTz` (reads `SchoolSettings` tz) |\n| FR-29 | Component 5 — `LoadingSkeleton` |\n| FR-30 | Component 6 — `(app)/layout.tsx` sidebar/top bar |\n| FR-31 | Component 6 — responsive Drawer fork (<1024px) |\n| FR-32 | Component 6 — `src/config/navigation.ts` (page render flow step 3) |\n| FR-33 | Component 6 — top bar branding + user-menu/bell placeholders (auth slot, not wired) |\n| FR-34 | Component 6 — `/dashboard` page (page render flow step 4) |\n| FR-35 | Component 6 — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` extension point |\n| FR-36 | Component 7 — `(public)/layout.tsx` |\n| FR-37 | Component 7 — `/` landing page |\n| FR-38 | Component 7 — `not-found.tsx`/`error.tsx`/`global-error.tsx` |\n| FR-39 | Component 7 — `/forbidden` (auth slot, not wired) |\n| FR-40 | Component 2 — `src/lib/logger.ts` (API call flow step 4) |\n| NFR-1 | Component 8 — MUI-only enforcement (ESLint + MCP-docs process constraint) |\n| NFR-2 | Component 5 + 6 — server-rendered provider tree, no client-side theme flash |\n| NFR-3 | Component 5 + 9 — WCAG AA on shared components, axe-core e2e gate |\n| NFR-4 | Component 6 — responsive shell (360–1920px), generalizes FR-31 |\n| NFR-5 | Component 8 — `next.config.js` security headers |\n| NFR-6 | Component 9 — Vitest/Testing Library + Playwright coverage |\n| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 2 + 3 — fresh-clone bring-up script chain |\n| NFR-8 | Component 8 + 9 — lint/typecheck/test/test:e2e CI gate |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 48 requirement ids are accounted for above; none were dropped.\nNo blockers to carry forward — `arch-api-contracts` can proceed directly to\nderiving the API surface (in practice, just `/api/health` plus the envelope\ncontract every future endpoint must follow).\n","userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg6FAR4bu5voZdyMD1trm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"system-design.md is rewritten for ticket abcd-2 (the auth PRD) — the file on disk was stale, carrying over abcd-1's scaffold design from a prior run.\n\nKey findings while doing this:\n- `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` were already correctly updated for abcd-2 (timestamps 21:32/21:36), so I read those as the upstream inputs per the architect.md spec.\n- `system-design.md`, `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, and `threat-model-notes.json` were all still `ticketId: \"abcd-1\"` leftovers. I only own `system-design.md` for this sub-task, so I left the other three untouched — they belong to `arch-api-contracts` (or aren't part of my schema at all, in the case of `threat-model-notes.json`) and will need regenerating when that sub-task runs for abcd-2.\n\nNew `system-design.md` covers:\n- **Overview** — brownfield auth PRD on abcd-1, 98% confidence/no blockers, flags the two MEDIUM-confidence FRs (FR-11's new `public-routes.ts`, FR-26's assumed `navigation.ts` signature), and names the three cross-cutting chokepoints (`authorize()`, `audit()`, password-policy module) plus the `passwordChangedAt` three-writer/one-reader mechanism.\n- **Component Breakdown** — 17 components (Data Model, Credentials Auth Core, Rate Limiting, Session/Route Guard, Invite Flow, Password Policy, Password Reset Flow, Change Password, Service Layer, Permission Helpers, Audit Logging, App Shell Integration, Notifications Stub, Seed Data, Design System, Lint/CI Gate, Test Harness), each with files and FR/NFR citations.\n- **Data Flow** — sign-in, session validation, invite acceptance, forgot/reset, the `passwordChangedAt` cross-cutting note, app-shell wiring, seed flow.\n- **Requirements Traceability** — all 28 FRs + 8 NFRs mapped to components, none dropped.\n\nNext sub-task (`arch-api-contracts`) can proceed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7873,"cache_read_input_tokens":47896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7873},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"22baf961-7824-4991-a527-ffc6e7677d2f","uuid":"b3e99762-c649-48ad-a358-ed7ba30ab48a","timestamp":"2026-10-16T16:38:42.088Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6FAQTdyT6kk7gHNS9bs"}
