s name and email read-only plus new-password and confirm-password fields.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-14\", \"description\": \"Accept-invitation submit validates the password policy, hashes it, sets status = ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt = now, marks the token used, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-4 Accept invitation, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-15\", \"description\": \"Password policy (src/lib/validators/auth.ts): 10-128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, must not equal the user's email, must not appear in the bundled 1,000 most-common-passwords list.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-16\", \"description\": \"A live password-strength checklist under the password field shows each policy rule as met or unmet as the user types.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-5 Password policy, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-17\", \"description\": \"/forgot-password always returns the same 'If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.' message regardless of whether the account exists; rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-18\", \"description\": \"For an existing ACTIVE user, create a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random bytes, base64url, 60-minute expiry), invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user, and call sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link).\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-19\", \"description\": \"/reset-password/[token] sets the new password hash and passwordChangedAt, clears lockout fields, marks the token used, audits auth.password.reset, and redirects to /login with a success toast.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-6 Forgot / reset password, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-20\", \"description\": \"/account/security change-password form: current/new/confirm-password fields; a wrong current password shows a field error; success shows a toast, invalidates other sessions via passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-21\", \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' entry to the user menu, linking to /account/security.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-7 Change password (signed in), item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-22\", \"description\": \"Service functions in src/server/services/users.ts for later PRDs: createUser (throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken, sendInvite, setUserStatus, unlockUser.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-8 Service functions for later PRDs\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-23\", \"description\": \"Permission helpers in src/server/auth/permissions.ts: getCurrentUser(), requireUser() (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to /login in server pages), requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to /forbidden); no generic can() helper is built — explicit role checks plus later per-entity helpers are the sanctioned pattern.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-9 Permissions\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-24\", \"description\": \"Audit helper audit() in src/server/audit.ts inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, never throws (logs on error), and never writes password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords into metadata.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-10 Audit helper\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-25\", \"description\": \"App shell top-bar user menu shows the real signed-in user's name, role badge and avatar initials; 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-26\", \"description\": \"navigation.ts filtering now uses the real session role in place of the PRD-00 placeholder role.\", \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\", \"source\": \"FR-11 App shell integration, item 2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-27\", \"description\": \"Until PRD-04 lands, sendAuthEmail() logs the recipient, subject and link via logger.info instead of sending a real email.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Out of Scope, item 3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"FR-28\", \"description\": \"Seed six ACTIVE users (admin, two teachers, two students, one parent; password SchoolHub123! for all) plus one INVITED user, logging the invited user's invite link during seeding.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Seed Data\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-1\", \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored (only SHA-256 hashes), token comparison is constant-time, cookies are HttpOnly/Secure(prod)/SameSite=Lax, and all auth forms carry CSRF protection supplied by Auth.js.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 1 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-2\", \"description\": \"Sign-in response time for 'no such user' and 'wrong password' must be similar (a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist) to prevent user-enumeration via timing.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 2 (Security)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-3\", \"description\": \"Sign-in must complete in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 3 (Performance)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-4\", \"description\": \"Form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\" and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements, item 4 (Accessibility)\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-5\", \"description\": \"Every visible element in this PRD is built from Material UI (@mui/material, @mui/icons-material) only, looked up through the MUI MCP server before use; the platform's banned UI/styling library list is enforced by ESLint.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"UI component rule (mandatory), items 1-6\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-6\", \"description\": \"Test coverage: Vitest unit tests for the password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl same-origin check; Vitest integration tests against a test database for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password; Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, failed-login messaging and forgot-to-reset flow.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Test Requirements\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-7\", \"description\": \"Brownfield discipline: reuse existing PRD-00 models/services/components/helpers; never re-scaffold the project, duplicate an existing helper, or rename an existing route or model.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Platform Context, paragraph 1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"NFR-8\", \"description\": \"Delivery discipline: keep npm run lint/typecheck/test passing, add only the tests listed in this PRD, do not expand scope beyond this PRD's sections, and do not modify behaviour owned by later PRDs.\", \"confidence\": \"HIGH\", \"source\": \"Assumptions and constraints, Constraints\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 98,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBG255UzHg8qwzuVPX4e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XRzhDWGWaVpLrWEFvRydSM","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":944,"cache_read_input_tokens":28099,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":944},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"202fbf25-aa76-4ef2-9363-ea2ba123e140","uuid":"19caedf0-761d-44bb-93de-950ac630db6a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T08:12:52.667Z","request_id":"req_011CgBG24rb2fWThrS1Vqu5E"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XRzhDWGWaVpLrWEFvRydSM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\n6\tRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\n7\tReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\n8\tNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\n9\tADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\n10\tconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n15\t\n16\t**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n17\t\n18\t**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\n19\tcalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\n20\tactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\n21\tcredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\n22\ta single-provider app.\n23\t\n24\t**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n25\t(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n26\t`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\n27\troute through, not a new auth layer.\n28\t\n29\t---\n30\t\n31\t## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n32\t\n33\t**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n34\t\n35\t**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\n36\tverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\n37\truns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\n38\tso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\n39\tCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\n40\tif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\n41\tto revisit.\n42\t\n43\t**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\n44\tother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n49\t\n50\t**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n51\t\n52\t**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\n53\tencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\n54\tLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\n55\tlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\n56\tconstant-time comparison outright.\n57\t\n58\t**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n59\t(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\n60\telsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n61\t\n62\t---\n63\t\n64\t## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n65\t\n66\t**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n67\t\n68\t**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\n69\tand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\n70\tMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\n71\tRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n72\t\n73\t**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\n74\tacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n75\t`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n76\t\n77\t---\n78\t\n79\t## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n80\t\n81\t**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n82\t\n83\t**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n84\t`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n85\t`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n86\t`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n87\t\n88\t**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n89\t(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n90\t(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n91\t\n92\t---\n93\t\n94\t## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n95\t\n96\t**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n97\t\n98\t**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n99\t`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\n100\tbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\n101\tpattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\n102\tZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\n103\tstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\n104\tschema, not two.\n105\t\n106\t**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\n107\tUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n108\t\n109\t---\n110\t\n111\t## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n112\t\n113\t**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n114\t\n115\t**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\n116\thashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\n117\tintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\n118\tchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\n119\texisting Playwright setup.\n120\t\n121\t**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n122\t(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\n123\tinfra to stand up.\n124\t\n125\t---\n126\t\n127\t## Status\n128\t\n129\tSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\n130\tspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\n131\tof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n132\t`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n133\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"202fbf25-aa76-4ef2-9363-ea2ba123e140","uuid":"0e107651-2295-4b9e-a6f4-7d88af29faa1","timestamp":"2026-10-19T08:12:52.678Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-2 | Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) | Status: complete\n\nThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 foundation (Next.js 14 App\nRouter, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9, PostgreSQL 16 via Prisma, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright — see `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json`).\nNFR-7 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating what already exists, so these\nADRs only cover the *new* tech decisions this PRD (auth) introduces, plus\nconfirming that everything else is reused unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Auth.js (NextAuth v5) Credentials provider, JWT session strategy\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-3, FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 (CSRF).\n\n**Decision:** Use Auth.js (NextAuth v5) with a single Credentials provider\ncalling `authorize()`, JWT session strategy (8-hour lifetime, refreshed on\nactivity). No OAuth providers, no database session adapter — the PRD is\ncredentials-only and a DB session store would be an unused abstraction for\na single-provider app.\n\n**Consequences:** CSRF protection on all auth forms comes free from Auth.js\n(NFR-1) instead of being hand-rolled. `middleware.ts` (FR-11) and the `jwt`/\n`session` callbacks (FR-9, FR-10) are the integration points later PRDs must\nroute through, not a new auth layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: bcrypt (cost 12) with a dummy-compare for timing safety\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-3.\n\n**Decision:** `bcrypt` npm package, cost factor 12, for password hashing and\nverification. When the looked-up user doesn't exist, `authorize()` still\nruns a bcrypt compare against a fixed dummy hash before returning failure,\nso unknown-user and wrong-password paths take comparable time (NFR-2).\nCost 12 is kept as-is per NFR-3's p95 < 1s budget rather than tuned down —\nif real hardware ever misses that budget, the cost factor is the one knob\nto revisit.\n\n**Consequences:** `bcrypt` is a new dependency (not present in abcd-1); no\nother hashing library is introduced alongside it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Node's built-in `crypto` for token generation and hashing\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-12, FR-18, NFR-1.\n\n**Decision:** Invite/reset tokens are `crypto.randomBytes(32)` base64url-\nencoded; stored as `crypto.createHash('sha256')` hashes only, never raw.\nLookup compares hashes with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. No token/crypto\nlibrary is added — Node stdlib covers random generation, hashing, and\nconstant-time comparison outright.\n\n**Consequences:** The raw token exists only in the generated link\n(logged via `sendAuthEmail`, FR-27) and is never persisted or logged\nelsewhere, satisfying NFR-1's \"raw tokens never stored\" rule.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: In-memory sliding-window rate limiter, no new store\n\n**Context:** FR-6, FR-17.\n\n**Decision:** `src/server/rate-limit.ts` implements the sign-in (10/IP/5min)\nand forgot-password (3/email/hr, 10/IP/hr) limits with an in-memory\nMap-based sliding window, exported for reuse across both call sites. No\nRedis or other external store is introduced for this PRD.\n\n**Consequences:** Limits reset on process restart and don't share state\nacross horizontally-scaled instances.\n`ponytail: in-memory single-instance rate limiter; move to Redis/shared store if the app scales past one instance.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Extend the existing Prisma schema; no new ORM/DB\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-22, NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:** Add `User`, `AuthToken`, `AuditLog` models and the\n`Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums to the existing\n`prisma/schema.prisma` from abcd-1, migrated through the existing\n`db:migrate` script. No second database or query layer.\n\n**Consequences:** Service functions (FR-22) and permission/audit helpers\n(FR-23, FR-24) are built directly on the existing Prisma client singleton\n(`src/server/db.ts`), not a new data-access layer.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Reuse existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for all auth UI\n\n**Context:** FR-2, FR-13, FR-15, FR-16, FR-20, FR-21, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:** All auth screens (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`,\n`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) are\nbuilt from the same MUI v9 components, React Hook Form + Zod resolver\npattern already established in abcd-1. The password policy (FR-15) is one\nZod schema in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, reused by both the live\nstrength checklist (FR-16, client-side) and server-side validation — one\nschema, not two.\n\n**Consequences:** No new UI, form, or validation library. The ESLint-enforced\nUI ban from abcd-1 (NFR-5) applies unchanged to every new screen.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Reuse existing Vitest + Playwright test stack\n\n**Context:** NFR-6, NFR-8.\n\n**Decision:** No new test tooling. Unit tests (password policy, token\nhashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl check) and\nintegration tests (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password,\nchange-password) run under the existing Vitest setup; e2e flows under the\nexisting Playwright setup.\n\n**Consequences:** Integration tests need a real test database connection\n(already provisioned by abcd-1's Docker Compose Postgres) — no new test\ninfra to stand up.\n\n---\n\n## Status\n\nSeven decisions above; six (ADR-1 through ADR-4, ADR-6, ADR-7) trace to\nspecific new FR/NFR ids this PRD introduces, ADR-5 and ADR-7 confirm reuse\nof abcd-1 infrastructure per NFR-7. No open questions block\n`arch-research-reqs` or `arch-design-system` — proceed.\n","numLines":133,"startLine":1,"totalLines":133}}}
