{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mn6wHfPDNv5bciZG6r2R23","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-2\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 requirements — 28 FR + 8 NFR,\n5\t98% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`).\n6\t\n7\tArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Credentials\n8\tAuth Core**, **Rate Limiting**, **Session / Route Guard**, **Invite Flow**,\n9\t**Password Policy**, **Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Service\n10\tLayer**, **Permission Helpers**, **Audit Logging**, **App Shell Integration**,\n11\t**Notifications Stub**, **Seed Data**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Design System\n12\t(MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**.\n13\t\n14\t## Functional Requirements\n15\t\n16\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n17\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n18\t| FR-1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these three tables. Foundation entity; must land before any service/route work. |\n19\t| FR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | `/login` page, MUI-only form (Card/TextField/Button/InputAdornment+IconButton/Alert). Pure UI surface over FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should keep this a thin client wrapper around `signIn('credentials')`. |\n20\t| FR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` — the single chokepoint every sign-in attempt routes through (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare). Depends on FR-1's `User` fields; feeds FR-4 (messaging), FR-5 (lockout), FR-8 (audit), NFR-2 (timing). This is the one function `arch-design-system` should design as a named module, not inline route code. |\n21\t| FR-4 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in failure messaging matrix (unknown/wrong-password vs locked vs disabled) — a branch inside/alongside `authorize()`'s result, consumed by FR-2's Alert. Must stay consistent with NFR-2 (same-message branches can't differ in timing either). |\n22\t| FR-5 | Credentials Auth Core | Lockout counter (`failedLoginCount`/`lockedUntil`) — state mutation on `User` (FR-1) triggered from within `authorize()` (FR-3). Threshold/window (5 failures / 15 min) is a named constant the design doc should surface once, not re-literal. |\n23\t| FR-6 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, `src/server/rate-limit.ts`, explicitly exported for reuse — `arch-design-system` should treat this as a shared utility other PRDs' rate limits (e.g. FR-17's forgot-password limits) can reuse rather than re-implement. |\n24\t| FR-7 | Credentials Auth Core | Post-sign-in redirect with same-origin `callbackUrl` validation — a small pure function (open-redirect guard); shared by FR-11's middleware-generated `callbackUrl` and FR-12/14's invite-accept redirect-to-dashboard pattern. |\n25\t| FR-8 | Audit Logging | `auth.login.success`/`auth.login.failure`/`auth.lockout` entries — first concrete caller of FR-24's `audit()` helper; fires from inside `authorize()` (FR-3), so the design doc should clarify whether `authorize()` calls `audit()` directly or returns a result the route layer audits. |\n26\t| FR-9 | Session / Route Guard | JWT session strategy, 8h lifetime, `jwt`/`session` callbacks carry id/role/firstName/lastName/email — this is Auth.js config, not a new module; shapes what FR-23's `getCurrentUser()` can read without a DB round-trip. |\n27\t| FR-10 | Session / Route Guard | `passwordChangedAt`-vs-token-issue-time invalidation, throttled to once per 5 minutes in the `jwt` callback — lives in the same Auth.js config object as FR-9; ties directly to FR-20 (change-password must bump `passwordChangedAt` to actually invalidate other sessions). |\n28\t| FR-11 | Session / Route Guard | `middleware.ts` — redirect-to-login for `(app)` pages, 401 JSON for `/api/*` except an explicit allowlist (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `src/config/public-routes.ts`). This is the perimeter every protected route sits behind; MEDIUM confidence (allowlist file doesn't exist yet) — design doc should treat `public-routes.ts` as a new config file, not assume it. |\n29\t| FR-12 | Invite Flow | `/invite/[token]` lookup by SHA-256 hash, type/used/expiry checks (7-day) — reads `AuthToken` (FR-1); the expired/invalid branch needs its own UI state distinct from FR-4's sign-in-failure messaging. |\n30\t| FR-13 | Invite Flow | Accept-invitation form (read-only name/email + new/confirm password) — UI surface over FR-14's submit handler, same MUI-component constraint as FR-2. |\n31\t| FR-14 | Invite Flow | Accept-invite submit: FR-15 password-policy validation → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → mark token used → sign in → redirect `/dashboard` → audit `auth.invite.accepted`. Multi-step transaction; design doc should specify this as one service-layer function (likely alongside FR-22's `users.ts`) so the steps stay atomic rather than split across the route handler. |\n32\t| FR-15 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — length/letter+digit/not-email/not-in-common-list rules. Pure validation module with no DB/session dependency; shared by FR-14 (invite accept), FR-19 (reset), FR-20 (change-password) — three call sites, one rule set. |\n33\t| FR-16 | Password Policy | Live password-strength checklist UI — client-side mirror of FR-15's rules; design doc should flag the risk of the client-side rule list drifting from the server-side one and specify a single shared source (e.g. export rule predicates from `auth.ts` for both server validation and client display). |\n34\t| FR-17 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` — constant response message regardless of account existence (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2), plus its own rate limits (3/email/hour, 10/IP/hour) — second consumer of FR-6's rate-limit module, different window/key shape (per-email in addition to per-IP). |\n35\t| FR-18 | Password Reset Flow | Reset-token issuance: 32 random bytes base64url, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens for the user, `sendAuthEmail(..., 'password-reset', ...)`. Second `AuthToken` producer after FR-12's invite tokens — same table, different `AuthTokenType`; \"invalidate older unused tokens\" is a stateful rule the design doc should name explicitly (e.g. a `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper shared with FR-14's token-used marking). |\n36\t| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow | `/reset-password/[token]` — set new hash + `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout fields, mark token used, audit `auth.password.reset`, redirect to `/login`. Reuses FR-15 (policy), and clearing lockout fields here is a detail that must stay in sync with FR-5's lockout field set. |\n37\t| FR-20 | Change Password | `/account/security` change-password form — current-password check (field error on mismatch) + FR-15 policy on new password; success bumps `passwordChangedAt` (which is what makes FR-10's other-session invalidation actually fire) and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out too. |\n38\t| FR-21 | App Shell Integration | \"Account security\" user-menu entry → `/account/security`. Small nav-config addition, same user-menu surface as FR-25. |\n39\t| FR-22 | Service Layer | `src/server/services/users.ts`: `createUser`/`createInviteToken`/`sendInvite`/`setUserStatus`/`unlockUser`. Explicitly \"for later PRDs\" — this phase defines the module's public surface/signatures even though only `createInviteToken`-adjacent logic (FR-14/28 seeding) is exercised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |\n40\t| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |\n41\t| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |\n42\t| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |\n43\t| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |\n44\t| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |\n45\t| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |\n46\t\n47\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n48\t\n49\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n50\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n51\t| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |\n52\t| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |\n53\t| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |\n54\t| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |\n55\t| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |\n56\t| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |\n57\t| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |\n58\t| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |\n59\t\n60\t## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n61\t\n62\t- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.\n63\t- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.\n64\t- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.\n65\t- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"\n66\t- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.\n67\t- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"202fbf25-aa76-4ef2-9363-ea2ba123e140","uuid":"88e577b3-0908-481c-94b1-3d9ea2cb431f","timestamp":"2026-10-19T08:12:53.114Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-2\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (36 requirements — 28 FR + 8 NFR,\n98% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`).\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Credentials\nAuth Core**, **Rate Limiting**, **Session / Route Guard**, **Invite Flow**,\n**Password Policy**, **Password Reset Flow**, **Change Password**, **Service\nLayer**, **Permission Helpers**, **Audit Logging**, **App Shell Integration**,\n**Notifications Stub**, **Seed Data**, **Lint/CI Gate**, **Design System\n(MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these three tables. Foundation entity; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | `/login` page, MUI-only form (Card/TextField/Button/InputAdornment+IconButton/Alert). Pure UI surface over FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should keep this a thin client wrapper around `signIn('credentials')`. |\n| FR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` — the single chokepoint every sign-in attempt routes through (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare). Depends on FR-1's `User` fields; feeds FR-4 (messaging), FR-5 (lockout), FR-8 (audit), NFR-2 (timing). This is the one function `arch-design-system` should design as a named module, not inline route code. |\n| FR-4 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in failure messaging matrix (unknown/wrong-password vs locked vs disabled) — a branch inside/alongside `authorize()`'s result, consumed by FR-2's Alert. Must stay consistent with NFR-2 (same-message branches can't differ in timing either). |\n| FR-5 | Credentials Auth Core | Lockout counter (`failedLoginCount`/`lockedUntil`) — state mutation on `User` (FR-1) triggered from within `authorize()` (FR-3). Threshold/window (5 failures / 15 min) is a named constant the design doc should surface once, not re-literal. |\n| FR-6 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, `src/server/rate-limit.ts`, explicitly exported for reuse — `arch-design-system` should treat this as a shared utility other PRDs' rate limits (e.g. FR-17's forgot-password limits) can reuse rather than re-implement. |\n| FR-7 | Credentials Auth Core | Post-sign-in redirect with same-origin `callbackUrl` validation — a small pure function (open-redirect guard); shared by FR-11's middleware-generated `callbackUrl` and FR-12/14's invite-accept redirect-to-dashboard pattern. |\n| FR-8 | Audit Logging | `auth.login.success`/`auth.login.failure`/`auth.lockout` entries — first concrete caller of FR-24's `audit()` helper; fires from inside `authorize()` (FR-3), so the design doc should clarify whether `authorize()` calls `audit()` directly or returns a result the route layer audits. |\n| FR-9 | Session / Route Guard | JWT session strategy, 8h lifetime, `jwt`/`session` callbacks carry id/role/firstName/lastName/email — this is Auth.js config, not a new module; shapes what FR-23's `getCurrentUser()` can read without a DB round-trip. |\n| FR-10 | Session / Route Guard | `passwordChangedAt`-vs-token-issue-time invalidation, throttled to once per 5 minutes in the `jwt` callback — lives in the same Auth.js config object as FR-9; ties directly to FR-20 (change-password must bump `passwordChangedAt` to actually invalidate other sessions). |\n| FR-11 | Session / Route Guard | `middleware.ts` — redirect-to-login for `(app)` pages, 401 JSON for `/api/*` except an explicit allowlist (`/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, `src/config/public-routes.ts`). This is the perimeter every protected route sits behind; MEDIUM confidence (allowlist file doesn't exist yet) — design doc should treat `public-routes.ts` as a new config file, not assume it. |\n| FR-12 | Invite Flow | `/invite/[token]` lookup by SHA-256 hash, type/used/expiry checks (7-day) — reads `AuthToken` (FR-1); the expired/invalid branch needs its own UI state distinct from FR-4's sign-in-failure messaging. |\n| FR-13 | Invite Flow | Accept-invitation form (read-only name/email + new/confirm password) — UI surface over FR-14's submit handler, same MUI-component constraint as FR-2. |\n| FR-14 | Invite Flow | Accept-invite submit: FR-15 password-policy validation → hash → `status=ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt=now` → mark token used → sign in → redirect `/dashboard` → audit `auth.invite.accepted`. Multi-step transaction; design doc should specify this as one service-layer function (likely alongside FR-22's `users.ts`) so the steps stay atomic rather than split across the route handler. |\n| FR-15 | Password Policy | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` — length/letter+digit/not-email/not-in-common-list rules. Pure validation module with no DB/session dependency; shared by FR-14 (invite accept), FR-19 (reset), FR-20 (change-password) — three call sites, one rule set. |\n| FR-16 | Password Policy | Live password-strength checklist UI — client-side mirror of FR-15's rules; design doc should flag the risk of the client-side rule list drifting from the server-side one and specify a single shared source (e.g. export rule predicates from `auth.ts` for both server validation and client display). |\n| FR-17 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` — constant response message regardless of account existence (anti-enumeration, pairs with NFR-2), plus its own rate limits (3/email/hour, 10/IP/hour) — second consumer of FR-6's rate-limit module, different window/key shape (per-email in addition to per-IP). |\n| FR-18 | Password Reset Flow | Reset-token issuance: 32 random bytes base64url, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens for the user, `sendAuthEmail(..., 'password-reset', ...)`. Second `AuthToken` producer after FR-12's invite tokens — same table, different `AuthTokenType`; \"invalidate older unused tokens\" is a stateful rule the design doc should name explicitly (e.g. a `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper shared with FR-14's token-used marking). |\n| FR-19 | Password Reset Flow | `/reset-password/[token]` — set new hash + `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout fields, mark token used, audit `auth.password.reset`, redirect to `/login`. Reuses FR-15 (policy), and clearing lockout fields here is a detail that must stay in sync with FR-5's lockout field set. |\n| FR-20 | Change Password | `/account/security` change-password form — current-password check (field error on mismatch) + FR-15 policy on new password; success bumps `passwordChangedAt` (which is what makes FR-10's other-session invalidation actually fire) and re-issues the current session's token so the acting user isn't logged out too. |\n| FR-21 | App Shell Integration | \"Account security\" user-menu entry → `/account/security`. Small nav-config addition, same user-menu surface as FR-25. |\n| FR-22 | Service Layer | `src/server/services/users.ts`: `createUser`/`createInviteToken`/`sendInvite`/`setUserStatus`/`unlockUser`. Explicitly \"for later PRDs\" — this phase defines the module's public surface/signatures even though only `createInviteToken`-adjacent logic (FR-14/28 seeding) is exercised yet. Design doc should list these as stable exports later PRDs will import, not inline route logic. |\n| FR-23 | Permission Helpers | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`: `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()`, `requireRole(...roles)`. No generic `can()` — explicit role checks is the sanctioned pattern, which the design doc should state plainly so later PRDs don't reintroduce a generic ACL layer. `requireUser`/`requireRole` are what FR-11's middleware perimeter is backed up by at the page/handler level. |\n| FR-24 | Audit Logging | `audit()` in `src/server/audit.ts` — single insert-only helper, captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets. Every audit call site in this PRD (FR-8, FR-14, FR-19) goes through this one function; design doc should pin its signature once since it's the shared chokepoint. |\n| FR-25 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu: real name/role badge/avatar initials, \"Sign out\" → `signOut()` → `/login`. Replaces PRD-00's placeholder menu slot (per `requirements-analysis-notes.md` history, FR-33 of abcd-1) — first real consumer of FR-9's session shape. |\n| FR-26 | App Shell Integration | `navigation.ts` role filtering switches from PRD-00's placeholder role to the real session role (FR-9). One-line dependency change, but the design doc should confirm `navigation.ts`'s existing filter signature already accepts a `Role` value so this is a wiring change, not a rewrite. |\n| FR-27 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info` instead of sending mail, pending PRD-04. Both FR-14 (invite... actually invite link is logged at seed time per FR-28) and FR-18 (reset email) call through this one stub — design doc should give it a stable signature now so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites. |\n| FR-28 | Seed Data | Seed six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), log the invited user's invite link. Depends on FR-1 (schema), FR-22 (`createUser`/`createInviteToken` — seed script should call the service functions, not duplicate their logic), and FR-27 (invite link logging path). |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Credentials Auth Core / Data Model | Hash-only token storage (no raw tokens persisted), constant-time comparison, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Lax cookies, Auth.js-supplied CSRF. Cross-cutting constraint on FR-1 (`AuthToken` schema), FR-12/18 (token lookup must hash-then-compare, not store-then-compare), and the Auth.js config backing FR-9/10. |\n| NFR-2 | Credentials Auth Core | Dummy bcrypt compare on nonexistent-user path so timing doesn't leak user existence — a specific branch inside FR-3's `authorize()`; design doc should call this out as a required no-op compare, not an optimization to skip. |\n| NFR-3 | Credentials Auth Core | Sign-in p95 < 1s at bcrypt cost 12 — bounds how much extra work `authorize()` (FR-3) can do per attempt (e.g. rate-limit check, lockout read, dummy-compare branch all have to fit inside that budget). |\n| NFR-4 | Design System (MUI-only) | `aria-live=\"polite\"` error announcements + focus-to-first-invalid-field on submit — applies to every form in this PRD (FR-2 login, FR-13 invite-accept, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`, FR-20 change-password). One shared form-error pattern, five call sites. |\n| NFR-5 | Lint/CI Gate | MUI-only constraint, enforced by the existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` rule from PRD-00 (abcd-1 FR-19) — no new lint rule needed here, just compliance; design doc should note this phase adds zero new UI libraries. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (password policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard) + Vitest integration against a test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password) + Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset). Defines the testability bar for every pure function named above (FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-15, FR-18) — they should be exported as standalone functions, not buried in route handlers, specifically so these tests can call them directly. |\n| NFR-7 | Service Layer / Permission Helpers | Brownfield discipline: reuse PRD-00's models/services/components/helpers, never re-scaffold, duplicate, or rename. Directly constrains FR-22/FR-23/FR-24's naming and location choices — they must slot into PRD-00's existing `src/server/` conventions rather than introduce a parallel structure. |\n| NFR-8 | Lint/CI Gate | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green, add only the tests this PRD lists, no scope creep into later-PRD behavior (e.g. don't build the generic `can()` helper FR-23 explicitly excludes, don't implement real email sending that FR-27 explicitly defers). |\n\n## Cross-cutting observations for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three shared chokepoints recur across almost every FR**: `authorize()` (FR-3) for sign-in, `audit()` (FR-24) for every audited action (FR-8/14/19), and the password-policy module (FR-15) for every password-setting path (FR-14/19/20). Design these three as named, independently-testable modules first — nearly everything else in this PRD calls into one of them.\n- **`AuthToken` has two producers with different rules**: invite tokens (FR-12, 7-day expiry) and reset tokens (FR-18, 60-min expiry, and uniquely \"invalidate older unused tokens for that user\" on each new issuance). Model both through the same table/enum (FR-1) but don't let the invalidate-on-reissue rule leak into the invite path — it's reset-specific per the PRD text.\n- **`passwordChangedAt` is the single mechanism tying together session invalidation (FR-10), change-password (FR-20), and reset-password (FR-19)** — one timestamp field, three write sites, one read site (the `jwt` callback). Worth a dedicated subsection in system-design.md's data-flow so the three writers don't drift.\n- **Rate limiting has two distinct key shapes on the same underlying module (FR-6)**: per-IP only (sign-in, FR-6) vs per-email-and-per-IP (forgot-password, FR-17). The module's exported API should accept a configurable key, not hardcode \"IP.\"\n- **No blockers were raised by intake** (`handoff-to-architect.json` blockers: none, 98% confidence) — nothing additional to surface in system-design.md's Overview beyond that confidence figure.\n- **This phase explicitly does not build**: a generic `can()`/ACL helper (FR-23 rules it out), real outbound email (FR-27 defers to PRD-04). Treat any such code found while implementing as scope creep per NFR-8.\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}}}
