{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015vm8fvbYowHvbNWtkH6DhT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket abcd-2 (SchoolHub auth PRD)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t## Overview\n6\t\n7\tThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 scaffold: it adds credentials\n8\tauthentication, session/route guarding, invite acceptance, password\n9\treset/change, permission helpers, and audit logging to the existing Next.js\n10\t14 App Router / Prisma / MUI v9 app. Intake reported **98% confidence and\n11\tzero blockers** (`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is\n12\tnothing to flag here beyond that figure; all 28 FRs and 8 NFRs are HIGH\n13\tconfidence except FR-11 (MEDIUM — `src/config/public-routes.ts` doesn't\n14\texist yet and is treated below as a new file) and FR-26 (MEDIUM — assumed\n15\twiring change, not a rewrite, of `navigation.ts`'s existing filter\n16\tsignature).\n17\t\n18\tNo new architecture decisions are made here beyond what\n19\t`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 through ADR-7) already fixed: Auth.js\n20\t(NextAuth v5) Credentials provider with JWT sessions, bcrypt (cost 12) with\n21\ta dummy-compare for timing safety, Node's built-in `crypto` for tokens, an\n22\tin-memory sliding-window rate limiter, Prisma-schema extension (no new\n23\tDB/ORM), reuse of MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for every screen, and reuse\n24\tof the existing Vitest/Playwright stack. This document arranges those\n25\tchoices into components and data flow, per NFR-7's brownfield discipline\n26\t(reuse abcd-1's models/services/helpers; never re-scaffold or duplicate).\n27\t\n28\tThree shared chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are\n29\tdesigned below as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline\n30\troute code: `authorize()` (sign-in), `audit()` (every audited action), and\n31\tthe password-policy module (every password-setting path). A fourth\n32\tcross-cutting mechanism, the `passwordChangedAt` timestamp, ties together\n33\tsession invalidation, change-password, and reset-password and is called out\n34\tin its own Data Flow subsection so its three writers don't drift.\n35\t\n36\t## Component Breakdown\n37\t\n38\t| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n39\t|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n40\t| 1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` models + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums, extending the existing Prisma schema | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-1, NFR-7 |\n41\t| 2 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` chokepoint (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare → dummy-compare branch), `/login` page, failure-messaging matrix, lockout counter mutation, same-origin `callbackUrl` guard | `src/server/auth/authorize.ts`, `src/app/(public)/login/page.tsx`, `src/lib/callback-url.ts` | FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-7, NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n42\t| 3 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, configurable key (per-IP, or per-email+per-IP), exported for reuse | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n43\t| 4 | Session / Route Guard | Auth.js config (`jwt`/`session` callbacks carrying id/role/firstName/lastName/email, 8h lifetime, `passwordChangedAt` invalidation throttled to 5-min checks), `middleware.ts` perimeter, new allowlist file | `src/server/auth/config.ts` (or `auth.ts`), `middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 |\n44\t| 5 | Invite Flow | Token lookup by SHA-256 hash (type=INVITE, unused, 7-day expiry), accept-invite form + atomic submit (validate → hash → activate → mark-used → sign-in → redirect → audit) | `src/app/(public)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (accept-invite step) | FR-12, FR-13, FR-14 |\n45\t| 6 | Password Policy | Single Zod rule set (length, letter+digit, not-email, not-common-password) exported for both server validation and the client-side live checklist — one schema, not two | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |\n46\t| 7 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` constant-response + rate limit, reset-token issuance (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens via a shared `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper), `/reset-password/[token]` (set hash, clear lockout fields, mark used, audit, redirect) | `src/app/(public)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-17, FR-18, FR-19 |\n47\t| 8 | Change Password | `/account/security` form (current-password check, FR-15 policy on new password, bumps `passwordChangedAt`, re-issues current session token) | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` | FR-20, FR-21 |\n48\t| 9 | Service Layer | Stable exported surface for this and later PRDs: `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-22, NFR-7 |\n49\t| 10 | Permission Helpers | `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to `/login`), `requireRole(...roles)` (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to `/forbidden`) — no generic `can()` by design | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` | FR-23, NFR-8 |\n50\t| 11 | Audit Logging | `audit()` insert-only helper: captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets — single call site signature for FR-8/14/19 | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-8, FR-14 (audit step), FR-19 (audit step), FR-24, NFR-1 |\n51\t| 12 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu wired to real session (name/role badge/avatar initials, sign-out), \"Account security\" menu entry, `navigation.ts` switched from placeholder to real session role | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (user menu), `src/config/navigation.ts` | FR-21 (menu entry), FR-25, FR-26 |\n52\t| 13 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info`; stable signature so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites | `src/server/email/send-auth-email.ts` | FR-27 |\n53\t| 14 | Seed Data | Seeds six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user via the Service Layer (component 9), logs the invite link via component 13 | `prisma/seed.ts` | FR-28 |\n54\t| 15 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) built from existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod resolver patterns; shared form-error pattern (`aria-live=\"polite\"`, focus-to-first-invalid-field) | reuses abcd-1's `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-4, NFR-5 |\n55\t| 16 | Lint/CI Gate | No new lint rule; existing `no-restricted-imports` ESLint rule from abcd-1 continues to apply; `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` stay green, scope capped to this PRD's test list | `.eslintrc*` (unchanged) | NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n56\t| 17 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard), Vitest integration against test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password), Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |\n57\t\n58\tDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2, 5, 7, 8 all depend\n59\ton 1 + 6 (Password Policy) + 11 (Audit) + 3 (Rate Limiting where noted). 4\n60\t(Session/Route Guard) depends on 1 + 2 (consumes `authorize()`'s result) and\n61\tgates 12 (App Shell) and every `(app)` page. 9 (Service Layer) is called by\n62\t5, 7's reset-issuance, and 14 (Seed). 10 (Permission Helpers) backs up 4's\n63\tperimeter at the page/handler level. 13 is called by 5 (seed-time invite\n64\tlink) and 7 (reset email). 15–17 wrap all of the above.\n65\t\n66\t## Data Flow\n67\t\n68\t**Sign-in, `POST` via `signIn('credentials')` → `authorize()` (FR-2/3/4/5/7/8, NFR-2/3):**\n69\t1. Rate limiter (component 3) checks 10 attempts/IP/5-min before any DB\n70\t   work; over the limit short-circuits with `RATE_LIMITED` (FR-6).\n71\t2. `authorize()` lower-cases/trims the email and looks up the `User`.\n72\t3. Non-existent user → run the dummy bcrypt compare against a fixed hash\n73\t   (NFR-2) anyway, then fail with the generic message (FR-4).\n74\t4. Existing user: status ≠ ACTIVE, archived, or `lockedUntil` in the future\n75\t   → fail with the disabled/locked message (locked message includes\n76\t   remaining minutes) — no bcrypt compare needed here since the account\n77\t   doesn't reach the password check per FR-4/FR-3's branch order.\n78\t5. Otherwise bcrypt-compare (cost 12) the password.\n79\t   - Wrong password: increment `failedLoginCount`; at 5 increments set\n80\t     `lockedUntil = now + 15min` and reset the counter (FR-5); write\n81\t     `auth.login.failure` (and `auth.lockout` if the threshold was just hit)\n82\t     via `audit()` (component 11, FR-8).\n83\t   - Correct password: reset `failedLoginCount` to 0, set `lastLoginAt`,\n84\t     write `auth.login.success` (FR-8).\n85\t6. On success, the `jwt` callback (component 4) stamps id/role/firstName/\n86\t   lastName/email into the token (FR-9); the route layer validates\n87\t   `callbackUrl` is a same-origin relative path before redirecting, else\n88\t   falls back to `/dashboard` (FR-7).\n89\t\n90\t**Session validation, every request through `middleware.ts` + the `jwt`\n91\tcallback (FR-9/10/11, NFR-1):**\n92\t1. `middleware.ts` redirects unauthenticated `(app)` requests to\n93\t   `/login?callbackUrl=<path>`; for `/api/*` it returns 401 JSON unless the\n94\t   path is `/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, or listed in\n95\t   `src/config/public-routes.ts`.\n96\t2. The `jwt` callback checks — at most once per 5 minutes per token, to\n97\t   bound cost — whether `passwordChangedAt` is later than the token's issue\n98\t   time; if so the session is invalid and re-login is forced on that\n99\t   device.\n100\t\n101\t**Invite acceptance, `/invite/[token]` (FR-12/13/14):**\n102\t1. Look up the token by its SHA-256 hash (never store/compare the raw\n103\t   token, NFR-1); it must be type INVITE, unused, and within 7 days of\n104\t   issuance, else show the invalid/expired state (distinct from sign-in's\n105\t   failure messaging).\n106\t2. Valid token renders the invited user's name/email read-only plus\n107\t   new/confirm-password fields.\n108\t3. Submit runs as one service-layer step in `src/server/services/users.ts`:\n109\t   validate against the Password Policy module (component 6) → hash →\n110\t   `status = ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt = now` → mark token used → sign the\n111\t   user in → redirect to `/dashboard` → `audit('auth.invite.accepted')`.\n112\t   These steps stay together so a failure partway doesn't leave a used\n113\t   token with no activated account.\n114\t\n115\t**Forgot/reset password (FR-17/18/19, pairs with NFR-2's anti-enumeration\n116\tintent):**\n117\t1. `/forgot-password` always returns the same message regardless of account\n118\t   existence; rate-limited both per-email (3/hr) and per-IP (10/hr) through\n119\t   component 3's configurable-key limiter.\n120\t2. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issue a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random\n121\t   bytes, base64url, 60-min expiry) and call `revokeUnusedTokens(userId,\n122\t   'PASSWORD_RESET')` to invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user\n123\t   — this invalidate-on-reissue rule is reset-specific and must not leak\n124\t   into the invite path's token producer. Then `sendAuthEmail(user,\n125\t   'password-reset', link)` (component 13).\n126\t3. `/reset-password/[token]` sets the new hash and `passwordChangedAt`,\n127\t   clears the lockout fields (`failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil` — kept in\n128\t   sync with FR-5's lockout field set), marks the token used, audits\n129\t   `auth.password.reset`, redirects to `/login`.\n130\t\n131\t**`passwordChangedAt` — one field, three writers, one reader:** FR-19\n132\t(reset), FR-20 (change-password), and FR-14 (invite acceptance) each write\n133\tthis timestamp; the `jwt` callback (FR-10) is the single reader that forces\n134\tre-login elsewhere. Change-password (FR-20) additionally re-issues the\n135\t*current* session's token immediately after writing it, so the acting user\n136\tisn't logged out by their own action while every other session is.\n137\t\n138\t**App shell integration (FR-21/25/26):** once component 4 produces a real\n139\tsession, component 12 replaces abcd-1's placeholder user-menu slot and\n140\t`navigation.ts`'s placeholder role with the session's real name/role/\n141\tavatar-initials and `Role` value — a wiring change against abcd-1's existing\n142\tfilter signature, not new UI.\n143\t\n144\t**Seed flow (FR-28):** `prisma/seed.ts` calls `createUser`/\n145\t`createInviteToken` (component 9, not duplicated logic) to create six\n146\tACTIVE users and one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), and\n147\tlogs the invited user's invite link through `sendAuthEmail`'s `logger.info`\n148\tpath (component 13).\n149\t\n150\t## Requirements Traceability\n151\t\n152\t| Requirement | Design Element |\n153\t|---|---|\n154\t| FR-1 | Component 1 — `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + enums |\n155\t| FR-2 | Component 2 — `/login` page (MUI form) |\n156\t| FR-3 | Component 2 — `authorize()` |\n157\t| FR-4 | Component 2 — failure-messaging matrix |\n158\t| FR-5 | Component 2 — lockout counter mutation |\n159\t| FR-6 | Component 3 — sign-in rate limit (10/IP/5min) |\n160\t| FR-7 | Component 2 — `callbackUrl` same-origin guard |\n161\t| FR-8 | Component 11 — `audit()` calls from `authorize()` |\n162\t| FR-9 | Component 4 — `jwt`/`session` callbacks |\n163\t| FR-10 | Component 4 — `passwordChangedAt` invalidation check |\n164\t| FR-11 | Component 4 — `middleware.ts` + `public-routes.ts` |\n165\t| FR-12 | Component 5 — invite-token lookup |\n166\t| FR-13 | Component 5 — accept-invitation form |\n167\t| FR-14 | Component 5 — accept-invite submit (service-layer transaction) |\n168\t| FR-15 | Component 6 — password-policy Zod schema |\n169\t| FR-16 | Component 6 — live strength checklist (client mirror) |\n170\t| FR-17 | Component 7 — `/forgot-password` + rate limit |\n171\t| FR-18 | Component 7 — reset-token issuance + `revokeUnusedTokens` |\n172\t| FR-19 | Component 7 — `/reset-password/[token]` |\n173\t| FR-20 | Component 8 — `/account/security` change-password form |\n174\t| FR-21 | Component 8 + Component 12 — \"Account security\" menu entry |\n175\t| FR-22 | Component 9 — `src/server/services/users.ts` exports |\n176\t| FR-23 | Component 10 — `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` |\n177\t| FR-24 | Component 11 — `audit()` helper signature |\n178\t| FR-25 | Component 12 — top-bar user menu (real session) |\n179\t| FR-26 | Component 12 — `navigation.ts` real role wiring |\n180\t| FR-27 | Component 13 — `sendAuthEmail()` stub |\n181\t| FR-28 | Component 14 — `prisma/seed.ts` |\n182\t| NFR-1 | Component 1 + 4 + 11 — hash-only tokens, constant-time compare, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite cookies, Auth.js CSRF |\n183\t| NFR-2 | Component 2 — dummy bcrypt-compare branch |\n184\t| NFR-3 | Component 2 — p95 < 1s budget at cost 12 |\n185\t| NFR-4 | Component 15 — shared form-error pattern (all 5 auth forms) |\n186\t| NFR-5 | Component 15 + 16 — MUI-only enforcement, existing ESLint rule |\n187\t| NFR-6 | Component 17 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |\n188\t| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 9 + 10 + 11 — brownfield reuse of abcd-1 conventions |\n189\t| NFR-8 | Component 16 — lint/typecheck/test gate, scope cap |\n190\t\n191\t## Status\n192\t\n193\tComplete. All 28 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\n194\tdropped. FR-11 and FR-26 carry forward intake's MEDIUM-confidence notes\n195\t(new `public-routes.ts` file; assumed-compatible `navigation.ts` signature)\n196\tfor `arch-api-contracts` and dev-planning to verify against the real\n197\tabcd-1 code rather than treat as settled. No blockers to carry forward —\n198\t`arch-api-contracts` can proceed to deriving the API surface (the `/login`,\n199\t`/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, and\n200\t`/account/security` form-submission endpoints, plus Auth.js's own\n201\t`/api/auth/*` routes).\n202\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"202fbf25-aa76-4ef2-9363-ea2ba123e140","uuid":"7d78ce96-e825-41bc-9358-8ce56c9f4c10","timestamp":"2026-10-19T08:13:08.386Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-2 (SchoolHub auth PRD)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nThis PRD is brownfield on top of the abcd-1 scaffold: it adds credentials\nauthentication, session/route guarding, invite acceptance, password\nreset/change, permission helpers, and audit logging to the existing Next.js\n14 App Router / Prisma / MUI v9 app. Intake reported **98% confidence and\nzero blockers** (`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`) — there is\nnothing to flag here beyond that figure; all 28 FRs and 8 NFRs are HIGH\nconfidence except FR-11 (MEDIUM — `src/config/public-routes.ts` doesn't\nexist yet and is treated below as a new file) and FR-26 (MEDIUM — assumed\nwiring change, not a rewrite, of `navigation.ts`'s existing filter\nsignature).\n\nNo new architecture decisions are made here beyond what\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 through ADR-7) already fixed: Auth.js\n(NextAuth v5) Credentials provider with JWT sessions, bcrypt (cost 12) with\na dummy-compare for timing safety, Node's built-in `crypto` for tokens, an\nin-memory sliding-window rate limiter, Prisma-schema extension (no new\nDB/ORM), reuse of MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod for every screen, and reuse\nof the existing Vitest/Playwright stack. This document arranges those\nchoices into components and data flow, per NFR-7's brownfield discipline\n(reuse abcd-1's models/services/helpers; never re-scaffold or duplicate).\n\nThree shared chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are\ndesigned below as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline\nroute code: `authorize()` (sign-in), `audit()` (every audited action), and\nthe password-policy module (every password-setting path). A fourth\ncross-cutting mechanism, the `passwordChangedAt` timestamp, ties together\nsession invalidation, change-password, and reset-password and is called out\nin its own Data Flow subsection so its three writers don't drift.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | Data Model | `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` models + `Role`/`UserStatus`/`AuthTokenType` enums, extending the existing Prisma schema | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-1, NFR-7 |\n| 2 | Credentials Auth Core | `authorize()` chokepoint (normalize email → status/lockout checks → bcrypt compare → dummy-compare branch), `/login` page, failure-messaging matrix, lockout counter mutation, same-origin `callbackUrl` guard | `src/server/auth/authorize.ts`, `src/app/(public)/login/page.tsx`, `src/lib/callback-url.ts` | FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-7, NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| 3 | Rate Limiting | In-memory sliding-window limiter, configurable key (per-IP, or per-email+per-IP), exported for reuse | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n| 4 | Session / Route Guard | Auth.js config (`jwt`/`session` callbacks carrying id/role/firstName/lastName/email, 8h lifetime, `passwordChangedAt` invalidation throttled to 5-min checks), `middleware.ts` perimeter, new allowlist file | `src/server/auth/config.ts` (or `auth.ts`), `middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | FR-9, FR-10, FR-11, NFR-1 |\n| 5 | Invite Flow | Token lookup by SHA-256 hash (type=INVITE, unused, 7-day expiry), accept-invite form + atomic submit (validate → hash → activate → mark-used → sign-in → redirect → audit) | `src/app/(public)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (accept-invite step) | FR-12, FR-13, FR-14 |\n| 6 | Password Policy | Single Zod rule set (length, letter+digit, not-email, not-common-password) exported for both server validation and the client-side live checklist — one schema, not two | `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |\n| 7 | Password Reset Flow | `/forgot-password` constant-response + rate limit, reset-token issuance (32 random bytes, 60-min expiry, invalidate prior unused reset tokens via a shared `revokeUnusedTokens(userId, type)` helper), `/reset-password/[token]` (set hash, clear lockout fields, mark used, audit, redirect) | `src/app/(public)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(public)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-17, FR-18, FR-19 |\n| 8 | Change Password | `/account/security` form (current-password check, FR-15 policy on new password, bumps `passwordChangedAt`, re-issues current session token) | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` | FR-20, FR-21 |\n| 9 | Service Layer | Stable exported surface for this and later PRDs: `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-22, NFR-7 |\n| 10 | Permission Helpers | `getCurrentUser()`, `requireUser()` (throws UNAUTHENTICATED / redirects to `/login`), `requireRole(...roles)` (throws FORBIDDEN / redirects to `/forbidden`) — no generic `can()` by design | `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` | FR-23, NFR-8 |\n| 11 | Audit Logging | `audit()` insert-only helper: captures IP from `x-forwarded-for`, never throws, never logs secrets — single call site signature for FR-8/14/19 | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-8, FR-14 (audit step), FR-19 (audit step), FR-24, NFR-1 |\n| 12 | App Shell Integration | Top-bar user menu wired to real session (name/role badge/avatar initials, sign-out), \"Account security\" menu entry, `navigation.ts` switched from placeholder to real session role | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (user menu), `src/config/navigation.ts` | FR-21 (menu entry), FR-25, FR-26 |\n| 13 | Notifications Stub | `sendAuthEmail()` logs recipient/subject/link via `logger.info`; stable signature so PRD-04 can swap the implementation without touching call sites | `src/server/email/send-auth-email.ts` | FR-27 |\n| 14 | Seed Data | Seeds six ACTIVE users + one INVITED user via the Service Layer (component 9), logs the invite link via component 13 | `prisma/seed.ts` | FR-28 |\n| 15 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen (`/login`, `/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/account/security`) built from existing MUI v9 + React Hook Form + Zod resolver patterns; shared form-error pattern (`aria-live=\"polite\"`, focus-to-first-invalid-field) | reuses abcd-1's `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-4, NFR-5 |\n| 16 | Lint/CI Gate | No new lint rule; existing `no-restricted-imports` ESLint rule from abcd-1 continues to apply; `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` stay green, scope capped to this PRD's test list | `.eslintrc*` (unchanged) | NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| 17 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (policy, token hash/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter, callbackUrl guard), Vitest integration against test DB (authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password, change-password), Playwright e2e (sign-in/out, failed-login messaging, forgot-to-reset) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2, 5, 7, 8 all depend\non 1 + 6 (Password Policy) + 11 (Audit) + 3 (Rate Limiting where noted). 4\n(Session/Route Guard) depends on 1 + 2 (consumes `authorize()`'s result) and\ngates 12 (App Shell) and every `(app)` page. 9 (Service Layer) is called by\n5, 7's reset-issuance, and 14 (Seed). 10 (Permission Helpers) backs up 4's\nperimeter at the page/handler level. 13 is called by 5 (seed-time invite\nlink) and 7 (reset email). 15–17 wrap all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Sign-in, `POST` via `signIn('credentials')` → `authorize()` (FR-2/3/4/5/7/8, NFR-2/3):**\n1. Rate limiter (component 3) checks 10 attempts/IP/5-min before any DB\n   work; over the limit short-circuits with `RATE_LIMITED` (FR-6).\n2. `authorize()` lower-cases/trims the email and looks up the `User`.\n3. Non-existent user → run the dummy bcrypt compare against a fixed hash\n   (NFR-2) anyway, then fail with the generic message (FR-4).\n4. Existing user: status ≠ ACTIVE, archived, or `lockedUntil` in the future\n   → fail with the disabled/locked message (locked message includes\n   remaining minutes) — no bcrypt compare needed here since the account\n   doesn't reach the password check per FR-4/FR-3's branch order.\n5. Otherwise bcrypt-compare (cost 12) the password.\n   - Wrong password: increment `failedLoginCount`; at 5 increments set\n     `lockedUntil = now + 15min` and reset the counter (FR-5); write\n     `auth.login.failure` (and `auth.lockout` if the threshold was just hit)\n     via `audit()` (component 11, FR-8).\n   - Correct password: reset `failedLoginCount` to 0, set `lastLoginAt`,\n     write `auth.login.success` (FR-8).\n6. On success, the `jwt` callback (component 4) stamps id/role/firstName/\n   lastName/email into the token (FR-9); the route layer validates\n   `callbackUrl` is a same-origin relative path before redirecting, else\n   falls back to `/dashboard` (FR-7).\n\n**Session validation, every request through `middleware.ts` + the `jwt`\ncallback (FR-9/10/11, NFR-1):**\n1. `middleware.ts` redirects unauthenticated `(app)` requests to\n   `/login?callbackUrl=<path>`; for `/api/*` it returns 401 JSON unless the\n   path is `/api/health`, `/api/auth/*`, or listed in\n   `src/config/public-routes.ts`.\n2. The `jwt` callback checks — at most once per 5 minutes per token, to\n   bound cost — whether `passwordChangedAt` is later than the token's issue\n   time; if so the session is invalid and re-login is forced on that\n   device.\n\n**Invite acceptance, `/invite/[token]` (FR-12/13/14):**\n1. Look up the token by its SHA-256 hash (never store/compare the raw\n   token, NFR-1); it must be type INVITE, unused, and within 7 days of\n   issuance, else show the invalid/expired state (distinct from sign-in's\n   failure messaging).\n2. Valid token renders the invited user's name/email read-only plus\n   new/confirm-password fields.\n3. Submit runs as one service-layer step in `src/server/services/users.ts`:\n   validate against the Password Policy module (component 6) → hash →\n   `status = ACTIVE`, `passwordChangedAt = now` → mark token used → sign the\n   user in → redirect to `/dashboard` → `audit('auth.invite.accepted')`.\n   These steps stay together so a failure partway doesn't leave a used\n   token with no activated account.\n\n**Forgot/reset password (FR-17/18/19, pairs with NFR-2's anti-enumeration\nintent):**\n1. `/forgot-password` always returns the same message regardless of account\n   existence; rate-limited both per-email (3/hr) and per-IP (10/hr) through\n   component 3's configurable-key limiter.\n2. For an existing ACTIVE user only: issue a PASSWORD_RESET token (32 random\n   bytes, base64url, 60-min expiry) and call `revokeUnusedTokens(userId,\n   'PASSWORD_RESET')` to invalidate older unused reset tokens for that user\n   — this invalidate-on-reissue rule is reset-specific and must not leak\n   into the invite path's token producer. Then `sendAuthEmail(user,\n   'password-reset', link)` (component 13).\n3. `/reset-password/[token]` sets the new hash and `passwordChangedAt`,\n   clears the lockout fields (`failedLoginCount`, `lockedUntil` — kept in\n   sync with FR-5's lockout field set), marks the token used, audits\n   `auth.password.reset`, redirects to `/login`.\n\n**`passwordChangedAt` — one field, three writers, one reader:** FR-19\n(reset), FR-20 (change-password), and FR-14 (invite acceptance) each write\nthis timestamp; the `jwt` callback (FR-10) is the single reader that forces\nre-login elsewhere. Change-password (FR-20) additionally re-issues the\n*current* session's token immediately after writing it, so the acting user\nisn't logged out by their own action while every other session is.\n\n**App shell integration (FR-21/25/26):** once component 4 produces a real\nsession, component 12 replaces abcd-1's placeholder user-menu slot and\n`navigation.ts`'s placeholder role with the session's real name/role/\navatar-initials and `Role` value — a wiring change against abcd-1's existing\nfilter signature, not new UI.\n\n**Seed flow (FR-28):** `prisma/seed.ts` calls `createUser`/\n`createInviteToken` (component 9, not duplicated logic) to create six\nACTIVE users and one INVITED user (shared password `SchoolHub123!`), and\nlogs the invited user's invite link through `sendAuthEmail`'s `logger.info`\npath (component 13).\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — `User`/`AuthToken`/`AuditLog` + enums |\n| FR-2 | Component 2 — `/login` page (MUI form) |\n| FR-3 | Component 2 — `authorize()` |\n| FR-4 | Component 2 — failure-messaging matrix |\n| FR-5 | Component 2 — lockout counter mutation |\n| FR-6 | Component 3 — sign-in rate limit (10/IP/5min) |\n| FR-7 | Component 2 — `callbackUrl` same-origin guard |\n| FR-8 | Component 11 — `audit()` calls from `authorize()` |\n| FR-9 | Component 4 — `jwt`/`session` callbacks |\n| FR-10 | Component 4 — `passwordChangedAt` invalidation check |\n| FR-11 | Component 4 — `middleware.ts` + `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-12 | Component 5 — invite-token lookup |\n| FR-13 | Component 5 — accept-invitation form |\n| FR-14 | Component 5 — accept-invite submit (service-layer transaction) |\n| FR-15 | Component 6 — password-policy Zod schema |\n| FR-16 | Component 6 — live strength checklist (client mirror) |\n| FR-17 | Component 7 — `/forgot-password` + rate limit |\n| FR-18 | Component 7 — reset-token issuance + `revokeUnusedTokens` |\n| FR-19 | Component 7 — `/reset-password/[token]` |\n| FR-20 | Component 8 — `/account/security` change-password form |\n| FR-21 | Component 8 + Component 12 — \"Account security\" menu entry |\n| FR-22 | Component 9 — `src/server/services/users.ts` exports |\n| FR-23 | Component 10 — `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` |\n| FR-24 | Component 11 — `audit()` helper signature |\n| FR-25 | Component 12 — top-bar user menu (real session) |\n| FR-26 | Component 12 — `navigation.ts` real role wiring |\n| FR-27 | Component 13 — `sendAuthEmail()` stub |\n| FR-28 | Component 14 — `prisma/seed.ts` |\n| NFR-1 | Component 1 + 4 + 11 — hash-only tokens, constant-time compare, HttpOnly/Secure/SameSite cookies, Auth.js CSRF |\n| NFR-2 | Component 2 — dummy bcrypt-compare branch |\n| NFR-3 | Component 2 — p95 < 1s budget at cost 12 |\n| NFR-4 | Component 15 — shared form-error pattern (all 5 auth forms) |\n| NFR-5 | Component 15 + 16 — MUI-only enforcement, existing ESLint rule |\n| NFR-6 | Component 17 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |\n| NFR-7 | Component 1 + 9 + 10 + 11 — brownfield reuse of abcd-1 conventions |\n| NFR-8 | Component 16 — lint/typecheck/test gate, scope cap |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 28 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\ndropped. FR-11 and FR-26 carry forward intake's MEDIUM-confidence notes\n(new `public-routes.ts` file; assumed-compatible `navigation.ts` signature)\nfor `arch-api-contracts` and dev-planning to verify against the real\nabcd-1 code rather than treat as settled. No blockers to carry forward —\n`arch-api-contracts` can proceed to deriving the API surface (the `/login`,\n`/invite/[token]`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, and\n`/account/security` form-submission endpoints, plus Auth.js's own\n`/api/auth/*` routes).\n","numLines":202,"startLine":1,"totalLines":202}}}
