{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XBvX7LuVUwgfRaUWnDJBdi","type":"tool_result","content":"=== requirements-analysis-notes.md head ===\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,\n97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nPRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,\nstudent/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter\nService**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/\nLifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV\nImport Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service\nProfile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,\n**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery\nDiscipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n=== tech-stack-decisions.md head ===\n# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n\nBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\nfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\nand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\nevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\nreal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\nreports no blockers.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n\n- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n  passing with no scope creep.\n- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n=== api-contracts ticketId ===\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-02\",\n=== handoff-to-dev-planning ===\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-02\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T13:31:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"endpointCount\": 21,\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"arch-design-system's output (artifacts/architect/system-design.md for ticketId abcd-02) was not found anywhere on disk at task start — only stale system-design.md/tech-stack-decisions.md/requirements-analysis-notes.md from a prior ticket (abcd-2) existed in artifacts/architect/. api-contracts.json was derived directly from artifacts/intake/requirements.json (ticketId abcd-02) and the source PRD's explicit API table (02-academic-structure.md) instead, since both fully specify method/path/role/body per endpoint. Contracts are sound, but dev-planning will not have a system-design.md component/data-flow document to work from for this ticket — consider re-running arch-design-system before dev-planning if that document is needed.\",\n    \"artifacts/intake/* for ticketId abcd-02 was also found misplaced at /Users/ikramaansari/artifacts/intake/ (outside this project directory) rather than under this project's artifacts/intake/, which still holds a stale prior ticket (abcd-2). Not fixed here as it is outside arch-api-contracts' scope, but dev-planning should be aware the canonical intake record for abcd-02 lives at /Users/ikramaansari/artifacts/intake/, not artifacts/intake/ in this repo.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"dev-planning\"\n}\n=== intake requirements ticketId ===\n  \"ticketId\": \"abcd-03\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a933411-2428-4c0f-ab5f-3414109df7d8","uuid":"8a63