{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015coCUaEaNjmusPgPbhicd4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,\n5\t97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\n6\tPRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,\n7\tstudent/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer.\n8\t\n9\tArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter\n10\tService**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/\n11\tLifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV\n12\tImport Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service\n13\tProfile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,\n14\t**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery\n15\tDiscipline**.\n16\t\n17\t## Functional Requirements\n18\t\n19\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n20\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n21\t| FR-1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`. Foundation entity set — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these tables; must land before any service/route work. |\n22\t| FR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | `/admin/users` DataTable (MUI X data-grid) columns incl. role/status chips. Read surface over the list service designed for FR-3/NFR-2. |\n23\t| FR-3 | Admin List/Filter Service | Filters (role, status, grade level, search) + archived-hidden-by-default rule. Drives the query shape the list service and its index (NFR-2) must support. |\n24\t| FR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | Row actions (View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore) — thin UI dispatch onto FR-7/FR-12/FR-13/FR-31 service calls. |\n25\t| FR-5 | Admin List/Filter Service | Bulk actions (resend/disable/export CSV) — same service calls as FR-4 applied to a selection; export path also triggers NFR-4 (formula-injection escaping). |\n26\t| FR-6 | User CRUD Form Flow | MUI Stepper create/edit form with role-specific fields incl. inline family linking. Single form component the service layer (create/update user) must support for all four roles. |\n27\t| FR-7 | User CRUD Form Flow | \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox → `sendInvite` on creation. Reuses the PRD-01 invite mechanism (NFR-7 brownfield reuse). |\n28\t| FR-8 | User CRUD Form Flow | Email-change confirmation dialog + pending invite token invalidation — a guarded mutation path, not a plain field update. |\n29\t| FR-9 | User CRUD Form Flow | Role immutable post-creation; edit form renders it read-only — a form/service-layer invariant, not just UI. |\n30\t| FR-10 | User CRUD Form Flow | Field validation (DOB 3–21yo, phone regex) — shared validator used by both the form and FR-20's server-side re-validation. |\n31\t| FR-11 | Admin List/Filter Service | User detail page: profile + status + last sign-in + linked family + 20 most recent audit entries. Composes the data model (FR-1), family links (FR-15), and audit log (FR-29) into one read view. |\n32\t| FR-12 | Session Invalidation | Disable → `status=DISABLED` + PRD-01 session check extended so sessions die within 5 minutes. Touches the existing session-validation chokepoint from PRD-01 — must extend, not duplicate (NFR-7). |\n33\t| FR-13 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Archive → `archivedAt` + `DISABLED`, excluded from pickers app-wide, history retained. Affects every picker/query that lists users (incl. FR-28's directory picker). |\n34\t| FR-14 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Self-disable/self-archive block + \"last active admin\" invariant. A service-layer guard checked on every disable/archive mutation, not just the UI. |\n35\t| FR-15 | Family Linking | Parent-student links manageable from student form, parent form, or student detail \"Family\" card — one link-management service, three entry points. |\n36\t| FR-16 | Family Linking | Max 4 parents/student; exactly one `isPrimary` link (set-one-clears-others) — a data-integrity invariant enforced in the link service/transaction, not the UI. |\n37\t| FR-17 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` + `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` in `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`. Shared authorization chokepoint every student-scoped read (FR-11, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26) must route through; returns `[]` for TEACHER pending PRD-05. |\n38\t| FR-18 | CSV Import Pipeline | Downloadable CSV templates (students/teachers) — static asset/route, defines the column contract FR-19/FR-20 parse against. |\n39\t| FR-19 | CSV Import Pipeline | Client-side parse (papaparse) into a preview DataGrid with per-row/per-cell validation status — browser-only, no server round-trip yet. |\n40\t| FR-20 | CSV Import Pipeline | `POST /api/users/import`, batches of 200, server re-validates, one transaction per batch, per-row results. The real import boundary — ties to NFR-3 (all-or-nothing batches) and reuses FR-10's validators server-side. |\n41\t| FR-21 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import options (invite toggle, case-insensitive grade-level match, strict date format) — parsing/matching rules inside the FR-20 service. |\n42\t| FR-22 | CSV Import Pipeline | Post-import summary + \"Download error report\" CSV — a response-shaping concern on top of FR-20's per-row results. |\n43\t| FR-23 | CSV Import Pipeline | Idempotent re-import: existing emails reported \"Skipped — already exists\", no duplicates — an upsert/lookup rule inside the FR-20 transaction. |\n44\t| FR-24 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header + \"Overview\" tab registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (medical notes gated to ADMIN/TEACHER — ties to NFR-1). Extends an existing tab-registry pattern (NFR-7), not a new page framework. |\n45\t| FR-25 | Student Surface | Page access gated through `assertCanViewStudent` (FR-17) — no separate auth logic here by design. |\n46\t| FR-26 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): card list of linked children with empty state — a thin read view over FR-15's links, scoped via FR-17. |\n47\t| FR-27 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: self name/email/role read-only, phone (+occupation/address for parents) editable; adds a user-menu entry. Separate, narrower mutation path from the admin CRUD flow (FR-6) — must not reuse the admin-only form. |\n48\t| FR-28 | Directory Picker API | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived) + reusable `UserPicker` (MUI Autocomplete). A shared lookup endpoint/component other PRDs will likely reuse — keep it generic, not page-specific. |\n49\t| FR-29 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table + filters + detail Drawer with pretty-printed JSON metadata. Pure read surface over the existing PRD-01 `AuditLog` table (NFR-7 reuse, no new write path). |\n50\t| FR-30 | Navigation | New nav entries (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) — a config/registration change in the existing nav structure, not a new shell. |\n51\t| FR-31 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | `POST /api/users/:id/unlock` clears `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` from PRD-01's lockout mechanism. Lower confidence (MEDIUM, inferred) — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm the exact field names against the PRD-01 schema before finalizing the endpoint contract. |\n52\t\n53\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n54\t\n55\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n56\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n57\t| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |\n58\t| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |\n59\t| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |\n60\t| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |\n61\t| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |\n62\t| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |\n63\t| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |\n64\t| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |\n65\t\n66\t## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n67\t\n68\t- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the\n69\t  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction\n70\t  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).\n71\t  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of\n72\t  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).\n73\t- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check\n74\t  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table\n75\t  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should\n76\t  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes\n77\t  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.\n78\t- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an\n79\t  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s\n80\t  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01\n81\t  field names before implementation.\n82\t- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**\n83\t  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student\n84\t  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,\n85\t  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule.\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a933411-2428-4c0f-ab5f-3414109df7d8","uuid":"2bb6a2ad-8802-4155-8b0d-c644eb233410","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:10:16.166Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-03\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 requirements — 31 FR + 8 NFR,\n97% confidence, no blockers per `handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is\nPRD-03 (User Management): profiles, admin user CRUD/list, CSV import,\nstudent/parent detail surfaces, directory pickers, audit log viewer.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin List/Filter\nService**, **User CRUD Form Flow**, **Session Invalidation**, **Status/\nLifecycle Guard**, **Family Linking**, **Access Control Helper**, **CSV\nImport Pipeline**, **Student Surface**, **Parent Surface**, **Self-Service\nProfile**, **Directory Picker API**, **Audit Log Viewer**, **Navigation**,\n**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Test Harness**, **Brownfield/Delivery\nDiscipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`. Foundation entity set — every other FR in this PRD reads or writes one of these tables; must land before any service/route work. |\n| FR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | `/admin/users` DataTable (MUI X data-grid) columns incl. role/status chips. Read surface over the list service designed for FR-3/NFR-2. |\n| FR-3 | Admin List/Filter Service | Filters (role, status, grade level, search) + archived-hidden-by-default rule. Drives the query shape the list service and its index (NFR-2) must support. |\n| FR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | Row actions (View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore) — thin UI dispatch onto FR-7/FR-12/FR-13/FR-31 service calls. |\n| FR-5 | Admin List/Filter Service | Bulk actions (resend/disable/export CSV) — same service calls as FR-4 applied to a selection; export path also triggers NFR-4 (formula-injection escaping). |\n| FR-6 | User CRUD Form Flow | MUI Stepper create/edit form with role-specific fields incl. inline family linking. Single form component the service layer (create/update user) must support for all four roles. |\n| FR-7 | User CRUD Form Flow | \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox → `sendInvite` on creation. Reuses the PRD-01 invite mechanism (NFR-7 brownfield reuse). |\n| FR-8 | User CRUD Form Flow | Email-change confirmation dialog + pending invite token invalidation — a guarded mutation path, not a plain field update. |\n| FR-9 | User CRUD Form Flow | Role immutable post-creation; edit form renders it read-only — a form/service-layer invariant, not just UI. |\n| FR-10 | User CRUD Form Flow | Field validation (DOB 3–21yo, phone regex) — shared validator used by both the form and FR-20's server-side re-validation. |\n| FR-11 | Admin List/Filter Service | User detail page: profile + status + last sign-in + linked family + 20 most recent audit entries. Composes the data model (FR-1), family links (FR-15), and audit log (FR-29) into one read view. |\n| FR-12 | Session Invalidation | Disable → `status=DISABLED` + PRD-01 session check extended so sessions die within 5 minutes. Touches the existing session-validation chokepoint from PRD-01 — must extend, not duplicate (NFR-7). |\n| FR-13 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Archive → `archivedAt` + `DISABLED`, excluded from pickers app-wide, history retained. Affects every picker/query that lists users (incl. FR-28's directory picker). |\n| FR-14 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | Self-disable/self-archive block + \"last active admin\" invariant. A service-layer guard checked on every disable/archive mutation, not just the UI. |\n| FR-15 | Family Linking | Parent-student links manageable from student form, parent form, or student detail \"Family\" card — one link-management service, three entry points. |\n| FR-16 | Family Linking | Max 4 parents/student; exactly one `isPrimary` link (set-one-clears-others) — a data-integrity invariant enforced in the link service/transaction, not the UI. |\n| FR-17 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` + `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` in `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`. Shared authorization chokepoint every student-scoped read (FR-11, FR-24, FR-25, FR-26) must route through; returns `[]` for TEACHER pending PRD-05. |\n| FR-18 | CSV Import Pipeline | Downloadable CSV templates (students/teachers) — static asset/route, defines the column contract FR-19/FR-20 parse against. |\n| FR-19 | CSV Import Pipeline | Client-side parse (papaparse) into a preview DataGrid with per-row/per-cell validation status — browser-only, no server round-trip yet. |\n| FR-20 | CSV Import Pipeline | `POST /api/users/import`, batches of 200, server re-validates, one transaction per batch, per-row results. The real import boundary — ties to NFR-3 (all-or-nothing batches) and reuses FR-10's validators server-side. |\n| FR-21 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import options (invite toggle, case-insensitive grade-level match, strict date format) — parsing/matching rules inside the FR-20 service. |\n| FR-22 | CSV Import Pipeline | Post-import summary + \"Download error report\" CSV — a response-shaping concern on top of FR-20's per-row results. |\n| FR-23 | CSV Import Pipeline | Idempotent re-import: existing emails reported \"Skipped — already exists\", no duplicates — an upsert/lookup rule inside the FR-20 transaction. |\n| FR-24 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header + \"Overview\" tab registered in `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (medical notes gated to ADMIN/TEACHER — ties to NFR-1). Extends an existing tab-registry pattern (NFR-7), not a new page framework. |\n| FR-25 | Student Surface | Page access gated through `assertCanViewStudent` (FR-17) — no separate auth logic here by design. |\n| FR-26 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): card list of linked children with empty state — a thin read view over FR-15's links, scoped via FR-17. |\n| FR-27 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: self name/email/role read-only, phone (+occupation/address for parents) editable; adds a user-menu entry. Separate, narrower mutation path from the admin CRUD flow (FR-6) — must not reuse the admin-only form. |\n| FR-28 | Directory Picker API | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived) + reusable `UserPicker` (MUI Autocomplete). A shared lookup endpoint/component other PRDs will likely reuse — keep it generic, not page-specific. |\n| FR-29 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table + filters + detail Drawer with pretty-printed JSON metadata. Pure read surface over the existing PRD-01 `AuditLog` table (NFR-7 reuse, no new write path). |\n| FR-30 | Navigation | New nav entries (Users, Import users, Audit log, My children, Profile) — a config/registration change in the existing nav structure, not a new shell. |\n| FR-31 | Status/Lifecycle Guard | `POST /api/users/:id/unlock` clears `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` from PRD-01's lockout mechanism. Lower confidence (MEDIUM, inferred) — flag for `arch-design-system` to confirm the exact field names against the PRD-01 schema before finalizing the endpoint contract. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Access Control Helper | `medicalNotes` must never reach STUDENT/PARENT — stripped in the service layer (not just the client) from `GET /api/students/:id`, and excluded from CSV exports (FR-5/FR-22 export paths). A field-level redaction rule the service layer and every export path must both honor. |\n| NFR-2 | Admin List/Filter Service | Sub-300ms user-list page at 5,000 users, backed by a `(lastName, firstName, email)` index. Directly constrains FR-2/FR-3's query design — pushes toward server-side pagination/filtering, not client-side. |\n| NFR-3 | CSV Import Pipeline | Import batch is all-or-rollback — reinforces FR-20's \"one transaction per batch\" requirement; no partial-success state is ever persisted. |\n| NFR-4 | Admin List/Filter Service | CSV export must neutralise formula injection (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) — applies to FR-5's bulk export and FR-22's error-report CSV alike; best implemented as one shared CSV-serialization helper. |\n| NFR-5 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every surface in this PRD (list, stepper form, pickers, drawer, cards) must be MUI-only (`@mui/material`, `@mui/icons-material`, MUI X), checked via the MUI MCP server, enforced by ESLint `no-restricted-imports`. No non-MUI component library may be introduced. |\n| NFR-6 | Test Harness | Vitest unit tests (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, formula-injection escaping, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children → student page). Scopes exactly what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for — no more, no less. |\n| NFR-7 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Reuse PRD-00/01/02 models, services, components, helpers — never re-scaffold, duplicate a helper, or rename an existing route/model. Directly constrains FR-7 (reuse `sendInvite`), FR-12 (extend, don't duplicate, the PRD-01 session check), FR-24 (extend the existing tab registry), FR-29 (reuse the existing `AuditLog` table/write path), FR-31 (reuse PRD-01 lockout fields). |\n| NFR-8 | Brownfield/Delivery Discipline | Keep lint/typecheck/test green, add only the tests NFR-6 lists, don't expand scope, don't touch behaviour owned by later PRDs (e.g. class/section membership is PRD-05's) — bounds `arch-design-system`'s scope the same way it bounds dev's. |\n\n## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **Three chokepoints to design as named modules, not inline code**: the\n  user list/filter service (FR-2/FR-3/NFR-2), the CSV import transaction\n  (FR-19–FR-23/NFR-3), and `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` (FR-17/NFR-1).\n  Every other FR in this PRD is a thin UI or read-view wrapper around one of\n  these three, or around the family-link service (FR-15/FR-16).\n- **Reuse, don't re-derive, from PRD-00/01/02** (NFR-7): session check\n  (FR-12), invite mechanism (FR-7), lockout fields (FR-31), `AuditLog` table\n  (FR-11/FR-29), student-tabs registry (FR-24). `arch-design-system` should\n  cite the existing modules by name/path if intake's tech-stack notes\n  identify them, rather than re-specifying their behaviour.\n- **FR-31 confidence is MEDIUM** (inferred from the API table, not an\n  explicit spec sentence) — worth a one-line flag in `system-design.md`'s\n  traceability table so `dev-planning` knows to verify the exact PRD-01\n  field names before implementation.\n- **Formula-injection escaping (NFR-4) and medicalNotes redaction (NFR-1)**\n  both cut across multiple export/read paths (FR-5, FR-11, FR-22, student\n  detail reads) — design each as one shared helper applied everywhere,\n  not per-endpoint logic, to avoid an endpoint missing the rule.\n","numLines":86,"startLine":1,"totalLines":86}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBLQRHjmwxzEDztfrux7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the tech-stack-decisions.md:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4778,"cache_read_input_tokens":42098,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4778},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a933411-2428-4c0f-ab5f-3414109df7d8","uuid":"3d82cd37-8d3b-4254-9ae7-3bb4bf0a6878","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:10:18.273Z","request_id":"req_011CgBLQR4bNfHSew7bjZLAi"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBLQRHjmwxzEDztfrux7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X6yU44g7rPw658Gb5emDfW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4778,"cache_read_input_tokens":42098,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4778},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a933411-2428-4c0f-ab5f-3414109df7d8","uuid":"3d886035-b1a3-439d-8190-56f30b71c83f","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:10:18.807Z","request_id":"req_011CgBLQR4bNfHSew7bjZLAi"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X6yU44g7rPw658Gb5emDfW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n2\t\n3\tTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\tBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n6\t`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\n7\tfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\n8\tand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\n9\tReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\n10\tevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\n11\treal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\n12\treports no blockers.\n13\t\n14\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n15\t\n16\t- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n17\t  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n18\t  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n19\t  passing with no scope creep.\n20\t- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n21\t  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n22\t- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n23\t  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n24\t  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n25\t\n26\t## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n27\t\n28\t- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n29\t  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n30\t  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n31\t- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n32\t  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n33\t  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n34\t- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n35\t  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n36\t  browser before anything hits the network.\n37\t\n38\t## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n39\t\n40\t- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n41\t  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n42\t- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n43\t  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n44\t  table.\n45\t- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n46\t  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n47\t  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n48\t  request lifetime).\n49\t\n50\t## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n51\t\n52\t- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n53\t  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n54\t  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n55\t  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n56\t- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n57\t  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n58\t  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n59\t- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n60\t  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n61\t\n62\t## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n63\t\n64\t- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n65\t  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n66\t  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n67\t  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n68\t- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n69\t  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n70\t  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n71\t  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n72\t  wrapper design-system package.\n73\t- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n74\t\n75\t## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n76\t\n77\t- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n78\t  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n79\t  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n80\t- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n81\t  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n82\t  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n83\t- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n84\t  queries unaffected.\n85\t\n86\t## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n87\t\n88\t- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n89\t  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n90\t  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n91\t- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n92\t  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n93\t  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n94\t  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n95\t- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n96\t  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n97\t\n98\t## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n99\t\n100\t- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n101\t  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n102\t  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n103\t  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n104\t- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n105\t  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n106\t  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n107\t  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n108\t  user service.\n109\t- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n110\t  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n111\t  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n112\t  re-implements.\n113\t\n114\t## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n115\t\n116\t- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n117\t  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n118\t- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n119\t  not generated at request time.\n120\t- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n121\t  edit, not a code change.\n122\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a933411-2428-4c0f-ab5f-3414109df7d8","uuid":"835d6789-bf4d-4208-9f46-926cf8911fef","timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:10:18.819Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — ADR Log\n\nTicket: abcd-03 | Phase: architect (`arch-research-stack`) | Status: complete\n\nBrownfield PRD-03 (User Management) on top of PRD-00/01/02. Per\n`artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` (confidence 100%) the stack is already\nfixed: Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 (+emotion)\nand MUI X (data-grid, date-pickers), Auth.js v5, Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Zod,\nReact Hook Form, Vitest/Testing Library/Playwright. No new framework\nevaluation is needed or wanted (NFR-7). The ADRs below cover the handful of\nreal choices this PRD introduces inside that stack. `handoff-to-architect.json`\nreports no blockers.\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack, no new framework\n\n- **Context:** FR-1..FR-31 are all additive feature work inside an existing\n  brownfield app. NFR-7 explicitly forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating\n  existing helpers/models/routes. NFR-8 requires lint/typecheck/test to keep\n  passing with no scope creep.\n- **Decision:** Build entirely on the detected stack (Next.js API routes,\n  Prisma, MUI, Zod, RHF, Auth.js). No new runtime, ORM, or UI framework.\n- **Consequences:** Zero migration/learning cost; every new file must match\n  existing conventions in `src/`. If a pattern doesn't exist yet (e.g. a\n  Stepper form), it still uses MUI/RHF, not a new library.\n\n## ADR-2: Client-side CSV parsing stays on papaparse, server stays plain JSON\n\n- **Context:** FR-19 mandates papaparse for in-browser parsing into a preview\n  grid; FR-20 then POSTs validated rows (not the raw file) to\n  `/api/users/import` in batches of 200.\n- **Decision:** No server-side multipart/CSV-parsing library. The API route\n  only ever receives already-parsed JSON row arrays. papaparse is the one and\n  only CSV parser in the system, used client-side only.\n- **Consequences:** Smaller server surface, no file-upload middleware to\n  maintain; row size caps (2 MB / 2,000 rows, FR-19) are enforced in the\n  browser before anything hits the network.\n\n## ADR-3: Import batches run synchronously in the API route — no job queue\n\n- **Context:** FR-20/NFR-3 require each 200-row batch to fully succeed or\n  fully roll back; max file size is 2,000 rows (10 batches).\n- **Decision:** Each batch is one `prisma.$transaction(...)` call inside the\n  `/api/users/import` route handler. No background worker, queue, or job\n  table.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible implementation for the stated volume;\n  revisit only if row/file limits grow materially beyond 2,000 rows\n  (ponytail: sync-per-batch, add a queue if import volume outgrows a single\n  request lifetime).\n\n## ADR-4: One shared CSV-escaping utility, not a library\n\n- **Context:** NFR-4 requires neutralising formula injection (`=`, `+`, `-`,\n  `@` prefix → leading apostrophe) on every CSV export path: bulk \"Export\n  CSV\" (FR-5) and the import \"Download error report\" (FR-22); NFR-1 also\n  requires `medicalNotes` to be excluded from exports.\n- **Decision:** A single pure function (e.g. `escapeCsvCell`) in a shared\n  server util module, called by every CSV-generation path. No CSV-writer\n  dependency — rows are small, flat objects.\n- **Consequences:** One tested choke point (NFR-6 unit test) instead of\n  per-export escaping logic that could drift.\n\n## ADR-5: MUI-only UI surface, enforced by existing ESLint rule\n\n- **Context:** NFR-5 requires every visible element to come from\n  `@mui/material` / `@mui/icons-material` / MUI X, looked up via the MUI MCP\n  server, with banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Chakra, Ant Design,\n  react-select, react-datepicker, etc.) blocked by `no-restricted-imports`.\n- **Decision:** Reuse the PRD-00 ESLint config as-is; extend its glob only if\n  new source directories fall outside current coverage. New composite UI\n  (Stepper wizard, DataTable + filters, Autocomplete picker, DataGrid import\n  preview, right Drawer) is built from existing MUI/MUI X primitives — no\n  wrapper design-system package.\n- **Consequences:** Consistent look/feel with PRD-00..02; zero new UI deps.\n\n## ADR-6: Data model grows additively; one new composite index\n\n- **Context:** FR-1 adds `StudentProfile`, `TeacherProfile`, `ParentProfile`,\n  `ParentStudentLink`, `Gender`, `GuardianRelationship`, with relations from\n  `User`. NFR-2 requires the user list to return in <300ms at 5,000 users.\n- **Decision:** Additive Prisma migration only — no renaming of existing\n  models/fields (NFR-7). Add a composite index on `User(lastName, firstName,\n  email)` to back the list/search query (FR-3, NFR-2).\n- **Consequences:** One migration, backward compatible; existing PRD-00/01/02\n  queries unaffected.\n\n## ADR-7: Zod schemas shared across form, CSV-row, and API re-validation\n\n- **Context:** FR-10 (DOB/phone validation), FR-19 (per-cell CSV validation\n  before import), FR-20 (server must re-validate every row before the\n  transaction), NFR-3 (no partial batches).\n- **Decision:** One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row),\n  reused as the React Hook Form resolver for the Stepper form and as the\n  row-validator for both the browser preview grid and the server-side\n  re-validation in `/api/users/import`.\n- **Consequences:** Single source of truth for validation rules; satisfies\n  NFR-6's \"CSV row validator\" unit-test target directly.\n\n## ADR-8: Disable/unlock reuse PRD-01's session + lockout plumbing\n\n- **Context:** FR-12 requires a disabled user's sessions to stop working\n  within 5 minutes, riding on the PRD-01 session check; FR-31 (`POST\n  /api/users/:id/unlock`) just clears the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`\n  fields PRD-01 already defined.\n- **Decision:** No new session/lockout infrastructure. Disable only flips\n  `status=DISABLED`; the existing PRD-01 session-validity check (re-reading\n  user status, short-lived token/refresh) is the thing that makes the\n  5-minute bound hold. Unlock is a plain field update through the existing\n  user service.\n- **Consequences:** Keeps auth boundary in one place (`src/server/auth/`);\n  if PRD-01's session check does not already re-verify status on an\n  interval ≤5 min, that's a PRD-01 defect to flag, not something this PRD\n  re-implements.\n\n## ADR-9: CSV import templates are static files, not generated\n\n- **Context:** FR-18 needs downloadable `students-template.csv` /\n  `teachers-template.csv` with fixed column headers.\n- **Decision:** Ship them as static assets (e.g. under `public/templates/`),\n  not generated at request time.\n- **Consequences:** Simplest possible option; editing the template is a file\n  edit, not a code change.\n","numLines":122,"startLine":1,"totalLines":122}}}
