{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014dFnZeieMoQnGQNbSuLaF6","type":"tool_result","content":"88:- As an admin, I want to search and filter users by role, status and grade level so that I can find people fast.\n104:  admissionNumber   String     @unique        // \"S2026-0001\"\n107:  gradeLevelId      String\n108:  gradeLevel        GradeLevel @relation(fields: [gradeLevelId], references: [id])\n110:  addressLine1      String?\n112:  medicalNotes      String?                   // visible to ADMIN and the student's teachers only\n129:  occupation  String?\n130:  address     String?\n148:1. `DataTable` columns: avatar + full name, email, role `Chip`, status `Chip` (Invited = warning, Active = success, Disabled = default, Archived = outlined), grade level (students), last sign-in, actions menu.\n149:2. Filters: role (multi-select), status, grade level (shown when role filter includes Student), search by name, email, admission number or employee number. Archived users are hidden unless \"Show archived\" is checked.\n155:   - Student: admission number (auto-suggested as `S<year>-<4-digit sequence>`), date of birth, gender, grade level, enrollment date (defaults to today), address, emergency contact and phone, medical notes, and a \"Parents/guardians\" section to link existing parents or create new parent users inline.\n156:   - Teacher: employee number (auto-suggested `T-<4-digit sequence>`), title, qualifications, hire date.\n157:   - Parent: occupation, address, and a \"Children\" section to link existing students.\n179:1. Download template button provides `students-template.csv` with columns: `first_name,last_name,email,admission_number,date_of_birth,gender,grade_level,enrollment_date,parent1_first_name,parent1_last_name,parent1_email,parent1_phone,parent1_relationship,parent2_first_name,parent2_last_name,parent2_email,parent2_phone,parent2_relationship`. A second template `teachers-template.csv` has `first_name,last_name,email,em