{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PuGNS4H6XzgfEsu4vVEbp9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket abcd-03 (PRD-03 User Management)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t## Overview\n6\t\n7\tPRD-03 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation) and PRD-02 (academic\n8\tstructure), both of which are actually built in `src/`. Intake reports\n9\t**97% confidence and zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`), and\n10\tonly one requirement (FR-31, unlock) carries MEDIUM confidence — both\n11\tcarried forward unchanged below.\n12\t\n13\t**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\n14\tthe design:** `requirements.json` and the source PRD (`03-user-management.md`)\n15\tboth write FR-7, FR-12, FR-31 and NFR-7 as if PRD-01 (auth/RBAC) already\n16\texists to be \"reused\" or \"extended\". Reading the actual codebase shows it\n17\tdoes not — `src/server/auth/` contains only `requireRole.ts`, whose own\n18\tdoc comment states plainly: *\"PRD-01 (real auth/session) has not landed in\n19\tthis workspace yet... returns the same ADMIN placeholder identity\n20\tAppShell renders.\"* There is no `authorize()`, no `middleware.ts`, no\n21\t`src/server/services/users.ts`, no `sendInvite`/`sendAuthEmail`, no login\n22\tpage, and the seed script creates no users. The `User`/`AuthToken`/\n23\t`AuditLog` Prisma models and the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/\n24\t`passwordChangedAt` columns *do* exist in `prisma/schema.prisma` (PRD-01's\n25\tmigration landed), and `src/server/audit.ts`'s `audit()` helper is real\n26\tand working — only the service/route/session layer is missing.\n27\t\n28\tThis does **not** block `arch-design-system` from producing a design — it\n29\tchanges what the design must say: PRD-03's auth-adjacent requirements are\n30\tdesigned against the *interfaces PRD-01's own design doc already commits\n31\tto* (`src/server/services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)`, `src/server/\n32\tauth/permissions.ts`'s `requireRole`), on the assumption PRD-01 lands\n33\tfirst. `requireRole.ts`'s placeholder is itself built to absorb that swap\n34\twith zero call-site changes, so PRD-03 calls it exactly as it will call\n35\tthe real thing later. Flagged explicitly in the Requirements Traceability\n36\ttable below (FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7) and restated for `dev-planning` in\n37\tthe Status section — this is a sequencing dependency, not a design defect.\n38\t\n39\tNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n40\t(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, papaparse client-side only,\n41\tsynchronous per-batch transactions, one shared CSV-escaping util, MUI-only\n42\tUI, additive schema with one new index, shared Zod schemas, reuse of\n43\tPRD-01's session/lockout plumbing (per the finding above), static CSV\n44\ttemplates. This document arranges those choices into components, data\n45\tflow, and per-FR/NFR traceability, per NFR-7/NFR-8's brownfield-and-scope\n46\tdiscipline.\n47\t\n48\tThree chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\n49\tbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\n50\tcode: the **user list/filter query** (FR-2/3/11, NFR-2), the **CSV import\n51\ttransaction** (FR-18–23, NFR-3), and **`student-access.ts`** (FR-17, NFR-1).\n52\tA fourth cross-cutting rule, **CSV-escaping + medicalNotes redaction**\n53\t(NFR-1/NFR-4), is designed as one shared helper applied at every\n54\texport/read boundary rather than per-endpoint logic.\n55\t\n56\t## Component Breakdown\n57\t\n58\t| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n59\t|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n60\t| 1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`; one composite index `User(lastName, firstName, email)` | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-2 |\n61\t| 2 | User Service Layer | `createUser`, `updateUser`, `setUserStatus`, `archiveUser`/`restoreUser`, `unlockUser`, admission-number/employee-number generators (`S<year>-####` / `T-####`), last-active-admin guard, self-disable/self-archive guard | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-3..FR-5, FR-9, FR-10, FR-14, FR-31 |\n62\t| 3 | List/Filter Query | `GET /api/users` query builder: role/status/gradeLevelId/q/includeArchived filters, search across name/email/admissionNumber/employeeNumber, server-side pagination via `src/server/http.ts`'s `parsePagination`, ordered to use the new index | `src/app/api/users/route.ts`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (`listUsers`) | FR-2, FR-3, NFR-2 |\n63\t| 4 | User Detail Composition | `GET /api/users/:id` assembling profile + status + lastLoginAt + family links (component 6) + 20 most recent `AuditLog` rows where `actorId = id OR entityId = id` | `src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts` | FR-11 |\n64\t| 5 | Create/Edit Form Flow | MUI `Stepper` (role select → common + role-specific fields), inline parent/student linking, \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox, email-change confirm dialog (reuses `ConfirmDialog`), read-only role on edit, shared Zod schemas from component 11 as the RHF resolver | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/new/page.tsx`, `.../[id]/edit/page.tsx` | FR-6, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10 |\n65\t| 6 | Family Linking Service | `linkParentToStudent`/`unlinkParentFromStudent` — max-4-parents check, single-`isPrimary` invariant (set-one-clears-others) inside one transaction; called from student form, parent form, and the student-detail Family card | `src/server/services/userLinks.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |\n66\t| 7 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` (ADMIN→`\"ALL\"`, STUDENT→`[user.id]`, PARENT→linked ids via component 6's link table, TEACHER→`[]` until PRD-05), `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` (FORBIDDEN/NOT_FOUND) | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-17, FR-25, NFR-1 |\n67\t| 8 | CSV Import — Client | Template download links (component 9), 2 MB/2,000-row cap enforced before upload, papaparse parse into a preview `DataGrid` with per-row Valid/Warning/Error + per-cell reason | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/import/page.tsx` | FR-18, FR-19 |\n68\t| 9 | CSV Import — Server Transaction | `POST /api/users/import`: re-validates every row against component 11's Zod schemas (never trusts the client), batches of 200, one `prisma.$transaction` per batch (all-or-rollback, NFR-3), case-insensitive grade-level match by `name`/`shortName`, strict `YYYY-MM-DD` dates, existing-email rows → \"Skipped — already exists\", summary + error-report CSV via component 10 | `src/app/api/users/import/route.ts`, `src/server/services/userImport.ts`, `public/templates/students-template.csv`, `public/templates/teachers-template.csv` | FR-18, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-3 |\n69\t| 10 | CSV Export/Escaping Util | `escapeCsvCell()` (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) and `toCsv()` used by bulk \"Export CSV\" (`GET /api/users/export`), the import error report, and nowhere else is CSV built ad hoc; also strips `medicalNotes` from every export row | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-5 (export), FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-4 |\n70\t| 11 | Shared Validators | One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row): DOB 3–21yo, phone `^\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$`, used as the RHF resolver (component 5) and the CSV row validator (components 8 & 9) — single source of truth | `src/lib/validators/users.ts` | FR-10, FR-19, FR-20 |\n71\t| 12 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header (avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status) + \"Overview\" tab registered in the existing tab registry (profile, family via component 6, emergency contact; `medicalNotes` gated to ADMIN/TEACHER, enforced server-side by component 7/13, not just hidden in the UI) | `src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/page.tsx`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (extend existing empty array) | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-1 |\n72\t| 13 | Student Detail API | `GET /api/students/:id`: gated by `assertCanViewStudent` (component 7), strips `medicalNotes` for STUDENT/PARENT in the service layer (not the client) | `src/app/api/students/[id]/route.ts` | FR-24, NFR-1 |\n73\t| 14 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): cards (name, grade level, admission number) from `GET /api/me/children`, linking to component 12; empty state via existing `EmptyState` component | `src/app/(app)/my-children/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/children/route.ts` | FR-26 |\n74\t| 15 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: read-only name/email/role, editable phone (+occupation/address for PARENT) via `PATCH /api/me/profile` — a narrower mutation path, deliberately not routed through component 2's admin service | `src/app/(app)/account/profile/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/profile/route.ts` | FR-27 |\n75\t| 16 | Directory Picker API + Component | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived, ≤20 results, `{id,name,email,role}`); reusable `UserPicker` on MUI `Autocomplete` (async, `multiple`, avatar+name+role `renderOption`) | `src/app/api/users/search/route.ts`, `src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx` | FR-28 |\n76\t| 17 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table (time, actor, action, entityType, entityId linked when a user, IP) + filters (actor, action prefix, date range) + right-anchored `Drawer` with pretty-printed metadata JSON on row click; reads the existing `AuditLog` table, no new write path | `src/app/(app)/admin/audit-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/audit-logs/route.ts` | FR-29 |\n77\t| 18 | Navigation | New entries: Administration→Users/Import users/Audit log, Parent→\"My children\", user menu→\"Profile\" | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-30 |\n78\t| 19 | Admin Row/Bulk Actions UI | View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore row actions + Resend/Disable/Export-CSV bulk actions on `DataTable`'s selection — thin dispatch onto components 2/9/10's service calls, confirmed via `ConfirmDialog` for destructive ones | reuses `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `src/components/ConfirmDialog/ConfirmDialog.tsx` | FR-4, FR-5 |\n79\t| 20 | Auth/Session Touchpoints (sequencing dependency) | FR-7's `sendInvite(userId)`, FR-12's session-status re-check, FR-31's lockout-field clear — all called through the stable interfaces PRD-01's own design doc defines (`src/server/services/users.ts`, `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`) rather than re-implemented here (NFR-7); see Overview finding | *(PRD-01, not yet landed)* | FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7 |\n80\t| 21 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only; reuses `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `UserAvatar`, `EmptyState`, `FormField`, `PageHeader`, `Toast` | reuses `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-5 |\n81\t| 22 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, `escapeCsvCell`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import-batch rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children→student page) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |\n82\t\n83\tDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (User Service)\n84\tdepends on 1 and is called by 3, 4, 5, 9, 19. 6 (Family Linking) depends on\n85\t1 and feeds 4, 5, 12, 14. 7 (Access Control Helper) depends on 6 and gates\n86\t12, 13, 14. 8→9 is one pipeline; 9 depends on 2, 6, 11 and feeds 10's\n87\terror-report path. 16 depends on 2. 17 depends only on the existing\n88\t`AuditLog` table. 20 is the one component this PRD does not build —\n89\teverything that calls into it (5, 2, 19) must tolerate it landing late or\n90\tbeing stubbed, per the Overview finding. 21–22 wrap all of the above.\n91\t\n92\t## Data Flow\n93\t\n94\t**User list, `GET /api/users` (FR-2/3, NFR-2):**\n95\t1. `parseQuery` (existing `src/server/http.ts` helper) validates\n96\t   `role`/`status`/`gradeLevelId`/`q`/`includeArchived`/pagination params.\n97\t2. Component 3 builds one Prisma query: `status != ARCHIVED` unless\n98\t   `includeArchived`, `q` matched against name/email/admissionNumber/\n99\t   employeeNumber, ordered/filtered to use the `(lastName, firstName,\n100\t   email)` index (component 1) so the 5,000-row/<300ms budget (NFR-2) holds\n101\t   without client-side filtering.\n102\t3. `paginated()` (existing `http.ts` helper) returns rows + meta; the\n103\t   `DataTable` (component 19/21) reads page/pageSize/sort from the URL, not\n104\t   local state, matching its existing contract.\n105\t\n106\t**Create user, `POST /api/users` (FR-6/7/8/9/10):**\n107\t1. Component 11's Zod schema (role-specific) validates the Stepper's step-2\n108\t   payload server-side (never trust the client-validated form alone).\n109\t2. Component 2's `createUser` generates `admissionNumber`/`employeeNumber`\n110\t   where applicable, creates the `User` + profile row + any inline\n111\t   parent/student links (component 6) in one transaction.\n112\t3. If \"Send invitation email now\" is checked, calls component 20's\n113\t   `sendInvite(userId)` — see Overview finding: this call is wired to the\n114\t   interface PRD-01 commits to, and is a no-op/stub until that interface is\n115\t   real.\n116\t4. `audit('user.created', ...)` via the existing `src/server/audit.ts`.\n117\t\n118\t**Edit user / email change (FR-8/9):**\n119\t1. Role is rejected server-side if present and different from the existing\n120\t   row (not just hidden in the UI) — a service-layer invariant, not a form\n121\t   convenience.\n122\t2. An email diff triggers `ConfirmDialog` client-side; on confirm, the PATCH\n123\t   handler updates the email and invalidates (marks used/expired) any\n124\t   pending `AuthToken` rows of type INVITE for that user, so a stale invite\n125\t   link can't activate the old address.\n126\t\n127\t**Status changes (FR-12/13/14):**\n128\t1. `setUserStatus`/`archiveUser` (component 2) check: not self, and —if\n129\t   disabling an ADMIN— that at least one other ACTIVE ADMIN remains, else\n130\t   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'At least one active admin is required.')`.\n131\t2. Disable sets `status=DISABLED`; archive additionally sets\n132\t   `archivedAt=now`. Both are pure data writes today; the \"stops working\n133\t   within 5 minutes\" session-level effect (FR-12) is PRD-01's session check\n134\t   re-reading `status` on its token-refresh interval — this PRD does not\n135\t   and should not build that check (NFR-7), it only guarantees `status` is\n136\t   correct the instant the mutation commits.\n137\t3. Every list/picker query (components 3, 16) and `getAccessibleStudentIds`\n138\t   (component 7) excludes `ARCHIVED` users by default, so archival's\n139\t   app-wide picker exclusion (FR-13) is enforced once, at the query layer,\n140\t   not per-caller.\n141\t\n142\t**Family linking (FR-15/16):**\n143\t1. `linkParentToStudent` runs inside one transaction: count existing links\n144\t   for the student (reject the 5th with `VALIDATION_ERROR`), and if the new\n145\t   link is `isPrimary`, clear `isPrimary` on every other link for that\n146\t   student first, then insert.\n147\t2. Reachable from three entry points (student form, parent form, student\n148\t   detail \"Family\" card) that all call this one function — no duplicated\n149\t   invariant logic.\n150\t\n151\t**CSV import (FR-18–23, NFR-3):**\n152\t1. Browser: papaparse parses the uploaded file (component 8), rejecting\n153\t   >2 MB/>2,000 rows before parsing; each row runs through component 11's\n154\t   Zod schema plus a grade-level-name lookup for Valid/Warning/Error\n155\t   classification with a per-cell reason, rendered in a preview `DataGrid`.\n156\t2. \"Import N valid rows\" POSTs rows (not the file) in chunks of 200 to\n157\t   component 9.\n158\t3. Server re-validates every row independently of the client (NFR-3's\n159\t   trust boundary), matches grade levels case-insensitively by `name` or\n160\t   `shortName`, parses dates strictly as `YYYY-MM-DD`, and skips rows whose\n161\t   email already exists (\"Skipped — already exists\", FR-23) rather than\n162\t   erroring.\n163\t4. Each 200-row batch runs in one `prisma.$transaction` (ADR-3): any row\n164\t   failure that isn't a plain \"skip\" rolls back only that batch, never the\n165\t   whole import; results aggregate into the post-import summary (component\n166\t   10) and, for failed rows, an escaped error-report CSV.\n167\t\n168\t**Student/parent surfaces (FR-24/25/26):**\n169\t1. `/students/[studentId]` and `/my-children` both resolve access through\n170\t   component 7 (`assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds`) — no\n171\t   page implements its own authorization check.\n172\t2. `GET /api/students/:id` (component 13) strips `medicalNotes` for\n173\t   STUDENT/PARENT roles in the service layer before the response is built,\n174\t   so no client-side hiding can leak it (NFR-1); the same strip applies\n175\t   inside component 10's CSV export path.\n176\t\n177\t**Directory picker (FR-28):** `GET /api/users/search` reuses component 3's\n178\tunderlying query (role/q filters, archived excluded) capped to 20 rows and\n179\tprojected down to `{id,name,email,role}` — no separate search index.\n180\t\n181\t**Audit log viewer (FR-29):** pure read over the existing `AuditLog` table\n182\t(`src/server/audit.ts`'s schema) with actor/action-prefix/date-range\n183\tfilters and pagination; no new write path, matching NFR-7.\n184\t\n185\t## Requirements Traceability\n186\t\n187\t| Requirement | Design Element |\n188\t|---|---|\n189\t| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enums + relations |\n190\t| FR-2 | Component 3 — `GET /api/users` list query |\n191\t| FR-3 | Component 3 — filters (role/status/gradeLevel/search/archived) |\n192\t| FR-4 | Component 19 — row actions dispatch |\n193\t| FR-5 | Component 19 (UI) + Component 10 (export) — bulk actions |\n194\t| FR-6 | Component 5 — Stepper create/edit form |\n195\t| FR-7 | Component 5 (checkbox) + **Component 20** — `sendInvite` call (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |\n196\t| FR-8 | Component 5 — email-change confirm + invite-token invalidation |\n197\t| FR-9 | Component 2 + 5 — role immutability, service + form |\n198\t| FR-10 | Component 11 — shared DOB/phone Zod schema |\n199\t| FR-11 | Component 4 — user detail composition |\n200\t| FR-12 | Component 2 (status write) + **Component 20** — session-level effect (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |\n201\t| FR-13 | Component 2 — archive write; Components 3/7/16 — app-wide picker exclusion |\n202\t| FR-14 | Component 2 — self/last-admin guard |\n203\t| FR-15 | Component 6 — link service, 3 entry points |\n204\t| FR-16 | Component 6 — max-4 / single-primary invariant |\n205\t| FR-17 | Component 7 — `student-access.ts` |\n206\t| FR-18 | Component 9 — static templates; Component 8 — download UI |\n207\t| FR-19 | Component 8 — client parse + preview grid |\n208\t| FR-20 | Component 9 — server re-validation + batched transactions |\n209\t| FR-21 | Component 9 — invite toggle, grade-level matching, strict dates |\n210\t| FR-22 | Component 9 + 10 — summary + error-report CSV |\n211\t| FR-23 | Component 9 — existing-email skip rule |\n212\t| FR-24 | Component 12 — student detail page + Overview tab |\n213\t| FR-25 | Component 7 + 12 — `assertCanViewStudent` gate |\n214\t| FR-26 | Component 14 — `/my-children` |\n215\t| FR-27 | Component 15 — `/account/profile` |\n216\t| FR-28 | Component 16 — search API + `UserPicker` |\n217\t| FR-29 | Component 17 — audit log viewer |\n218\t| FR-30 | Component 18 — navigation entries |\n219\t| FR-31 | **Component 20** — unlock clears PRD-01's lockout fields (MEDIUM confidence, carried from intake — verify exact field names against `prisma/schema.prisma`, which already has `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`) |\n220\t| NFR-1 | Component 7 + 13 + 10 — `medicalNotes` redaction (service layer + export) |\n221\t| NFR-2 | Component 1 + 3 — composite index + server-side pagination |\n222\t| NFR-3 | Component 9 — one transaction per 200-row batch |\n223\t| NFR-4 | Component 10 — `escapeCsvCell` shared util |\n224\t| NFR-5 | Component 21 — MUI-only, existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |\n225\t| NFR-6 | Component 22 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |\n226\t| NFR-7 | Component 2/6/7 (new, additive) + **Component 20** (reuse, not rebuild, PRD-01's interfaces — see Overview) |\n227\t| NFR-8 | All components — additive only, no PRD-05 (class/section) behavior touched |\n228\t\n229\t## Status\n230\t\n231\tComplete. All 31 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\n232\tdropped. Two things carry forward for `arch-api-contracts` and\n233\t`dev-planning`:\n234\t\n235\t1. **FR-31 (MEDIUM confidence):** confirm `POST /api/users/:id/unlock`\n236\t   clears exactly `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` (both already in\n237\t   `prisma/schema.prisma`) before finalizing the contract.\n238\t2. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 20):** `src/server/\n239\t   services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite`, and the session-status re-check\n240\t   behind FR-12, do not exist in `src/` yet — only their schema\n241\t   (`User.status`/`lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/`passwordChangedAt`,\n242\t   `AuthToken`) and the `requireRole()` placeholder exist. This is not a\n243\t   reason to re-implement them inside PRD-03 (NFR-7 forbids it) — it is a\n244\t   reason `dev-planning` should either sequence PRD-01's dev work ahead of\n245\t   PRD-03's component 20 items, or stub `sendInvite`/the status re-check\n246\t   behind the same placeholder convention `requireRole.ts` already\n247\t   establishes, so call sites don't change when PRD-01 lands. The source\n248\t   API table in `03-user-management.md` is otherwise fully specified and\n249\t   ready for `arch-api-contracts` to derive `api-contracts.json` directly\n250\t   from (18 endpoints: `GET/POST /api/users`, `GET/PATCH /api/users/:id`,\n251\t   `POST /api/users/:id/{invite,unlock,status,archive,restore}`, `POST\n252\t   /api/users/import`, `GET /api/users/export`, `GET /api/users/search`,\n253\t   `POST /api/students/:id/parents`, `DELETE /api/students/:id/parents/\n254\t   :parentId`, `GET /api/students/:id`, `GET /api/me/children`, `PATCH\n255\t   /api/me/profile`, `GET /api/audit-logs`).\n256\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecdd0a7a-9233-4799-bc04-313a457b4439","uuid":"b9aacfcc-fabb-4744-ba7c-877cbfd4990a","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:08:03.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-03 (PRD-03 User Management)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-03 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation) and PRD-02 (academic\nstructure), both of which are actually built in `src/`. Intake reports\n**97% confidence and zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`), and\nonly one requirement (FR-31, unlock) carries MEDIUM confidence — both\ncarried forward unchanged below.\n\n**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\nthe design:** `requirements.json` and the source PRD (`03-user-management.md`)\nboth write FR-7, FR-12, FR-31 and NFR-7 as if PRD-01 (auth/RBAC) already\nexists to be \"reused\" or \"extended\". Reading the actual codebase shows it\ndoes not — `src/server/auth/` contains only `requireRole.ts`, whose own\ndoc comment states plainly: *\"PRD-01 (real auth/session) has not landed in\nthis workspace yet... returns the same ADMIN placeholder identity\nAppShell renders.\"* There is no `authorize()`, no `middleware.ts`, no\n`src/server/services/users.ts`, no `sendInvite`/`sendAuthEmail`, no login\npage, and the seed script creates no users. The `User`/`AuthToken`/\n`AuditLog` Prisma models and the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/\n`passwordChangedAt` columns *do* exist in `prisma/schema.prisma` (PRD-01's\nmigration landed), and `src/server/audit.ts`'s `audit()` helper is real\nand working — only the service/route/session layer is missing.\n\nThis does **not** block `arch-design-system` from producing a design — it\nchanges what the design must say: PRD-03's auth-adjacent requirements are\ndesigned against the *interfaces PRD-01's own design doc already commits\nto* (`src/server/services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)`, `src/server/\nauth/permissions.ts`'s `requireRole`), on the assumption PRD-01 lands\nfirst. `requireRole.ts`'s placeholder is itself built to absorb that swap\nwith zero call-site changes, so PRD-03 calls it exactly as it will call\nthe real thing later. Flagged explicitly in the Requirements Traceability\ntable below (FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7) and restated for `dev-planning` in\nthe Status section — this is a sequencing dependency, not a design defect.\n\nNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, papaparse client-side only,\nsynchronous per-batch transactions, one shared CSV-escaping util, MUI-only\nUI, additive schema with one new index, shared Zod schemas, reuse of\nPRD-01's session/lockout plumbing (per the finding above), static CSV\ntemplates. This document arranges those choices into components, data\nflow, and per-FR/NFR traceability, per NFR-7/NFR-8's brownfield-and-scope\ndiscipline.\n\nThree chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\nbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\ncode: the **user list/filter query** (FR-2/3/11, NFR-2), the **CSV import\ntransaction** (FR-18–23, NFR-3), and **`student-access.ts`** (FR-17, NFR-1).\nA fourth cross-cutting rule, **CSV-escaping + medicalNotes redaction**\n(NFR-1/NFR-4), is designed as one shared helper applied at every\nexport/read boundary rather than per-endpoint logic.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`; one composite index `User(lastName, firstName, email)` | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-2 |\n| 2 | User Service Layer | `createUser`, `updateUser`, `setUserStatus`, `archiveUser`/`restoreUser`, `unlockUser`, admission-number/employee-number generators (`S<year>-####` / `T-####`), last-active-admin guard, self-disable/self-archive guard | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-3..FR-5, FR-9, FR-10, FR-14, FR-31 |\n| 3 | List/Filter Query | `GET /api/users` query builder: role/status/gradeLevelId/q/includeArchived filters, search across name/email/admissionNumber/employeeNumber, server-side pagination via `src/server/http.ts`'s `parsePagination`, ordered to use the new index | `src/app/api/users/route.ts`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (`listUsers`) | FR-2, FR-3, NFR-2 |\n| 4 | User Detail Composition | `GET /api/users/:id` assembling profile + status + lastLoginAt + family links (component 6) + 20 most recent `AuditLog` rows where `actorId = id OR entityId = id` | `src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts` | FR-11 |\n| 5 | Create/Edit Form Flow | MUI `Stepper` (role select → common + role-specific fields), inline parent/student linking, \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox, email-change confirm dialog (reuses `ConfirmDialog`), read-only role on edit, shared Zod schemas from component 11 as the RHF resolver | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/new/page.tsx`, `.../[id]/edit/page.tsx` | FR-6, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10 |\n| 6 | Family Linking Service | `linkParentToStudent`/`unlinkParentFromStudent` — max-4-parents check, single-`isPrimary` invariant (set-one-clears-others) inside one transaction; called from student form, parent form, and the student-detail Family card | `src/server/services/userLinks.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |\n| 7 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` (ADMIN→`\"ALL\"`, STUDENT→`[user.id]`, PARENT→linked ids via component 6's link table, TEACHER→`[]` until PRD-05), `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` (FORBIDDEN/NOT_FOUND) | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-17, FR-25, NFR-1 |\n| 8 | CSV Import — Client | Template download links (component 9), 2 MB/2,000-row cap enforced before upload, papaparse parse into a preview `DataGrid` with per-row Valid/Warning/Error + per-cell reason | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/import/page.tsx` | FR-18, FR-19 |\n| 9 | CSV Import — Server Transaction | `POST /api/users/import`: re-validates every row against component 11's Zod schemas (never trusts the client), batches of 200, one `prisma.$transaction` per batch (all-or-rollback, NFR-3), case-insensitive grade-level match by `name`/`shortName`, strict `YYYY-MM-DD` dates, existing-email rows → \"Skipped — already exists\", summary + error-report CSV via component 10 | `src/app/api/users/import/route.ts`, `src/server/services/userImport.ts`, `public/templates/students-template.csv`, `public/templates/teachers-template.csv` | FR-18, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-3 |\n| 10 | CSV Export/Escaping Util | `escapeCsvCell()` (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) and `toCsv()` used by bulk \"Export CSV\" (`GET /api/users/export`), the import error report, and nowhere else is CSV built ad hoc; also strips `medicalNotes` from every export row | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-5 (export), FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-4 |\n| 11 | Shared Validators | One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row): DOB 3–21yo, phone `^\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$`, used as the RHF resolver (component 5) and the CSV row validator (components 8 & 9) — single source of truth | `src/lib/validators/users.ts` | FR-10, FR-19, FR-20 |\n| 12 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header (avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status) + \"Overview\" tab registered in the existing tab registry (profile, family via component 6, emergency contact; `medicalNotes` gated to ADMIN/TEACHER, enforced server-side by component 7/13, not just hidden in the UI) | `src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/page.tsx`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (extend existing empty array) | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-1 |\n| 13 | Student Detail API | `GET /api/students/:id`: gated by `assertCanViewStudent` (component 7), strips `medicalNotes` for STUDENT/PARENT in the service layer (not the client) | `src/app/api/students/[id]/route.ts` | FR-24, NFR-1 |\n| 14 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): cards (name, grade level, admission number) from `GET /api/me/children`, linking to component 12; empty state via existing `EmptyState` component | `src/app/(app)/my-children/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/children/route.ts` | FR-26 |\n| 15 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: read-only name/email/role, editable phone (+occupation/address for PARENT) via `PATCH /api/me/profile` — a narrower mutation path, deliberately not routed through component 2's admin service | `src/app/(app)/account/profile/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/profile/route.ts` | FR-27 |\n| 16 | Directory Picker API + Component | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived, ≤20 results, `{id,name,email,role}`); reusable `UserPicker` on MUI `Autocomplete` (async, `multiple`, avatar+name+role `renderOption`) | `src/app/api/users/search/route.ts`, `src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx` | FR-28 |\n| 17 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table (time, actor, action, entityType, entityId linked when a user, IP) + filters (actor, action prefix, date range) + right-anchored `Drawer` with pretty-printed metadata JSON on row click; reads the existing `AuditLog` table, no new write path | `src/app/(app)/admin/audit-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/audit-logs/route.ts` | FR-29 |\n| 18 | Navigation | New entries: Administration→Users/Import users/Audit log, Parent→\"My children\", user menu→\"Profile\" | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-30 |\n| 19 | Admin Row/Bulk Actions UI | View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore row actions + Resend/Disable/Export-CSV bulk actions on `DataTable`'s selection — thin dispatch onto components 2/9/10's service calls, confirmed via `ConfirmDialog` for destructive ones | reuses `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `src/components/ConfirmDialog/ConfirmDialog.tsx` | FR-4, FR-5 |\n| 20 | Auth/Session Touchpoints (sequencing dependency) | FR-7's `sendInvite(userId)`, FR-12's session-status re-check, FR-31's lockout-field clear — all called through the stable interfaces PRD-01's own design doc defines (`src/server/services/users.ts`, `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`) rather than re-implemented here (NFR-7); see Overview finding | *(PRD-01, not yet landed)* | FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7 |\n| 21 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only; reuses `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `UserAvatar`, `EmptyState`, `FormField`, `PageHeader`, `Toast` | reuses `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-5 |\n| 22 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, `escapeCsvCell`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import-batch rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children→student page) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (User Service)\ndepends on 1 and is called by 3, 4, 5, 9, 19. 6 (Family Linking) depends on\n1 and feeds 4, 5, 12, 14. 7 (Access Control Helper) depends on 6 and gates\n12, 13, 14. 8→9 is one pipeline; 9 depends on 2, 6, 11 and feeds 10's\nerror-report path. 16 depends on 2. 17 depends only on the existing\n`AuditLog` table. 20 is the one component this PRD does not build —\neverything that calls into it (5, 2, 19) must tolerate it landing late or\nbeing stubbed, per the Overview finding. 21–22 wrap all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**User list, `GET /api/users` (FR-2/3, NFR-2):**\n1. `parseQuery` (existing `src/server/http.ts` helper) validates\n   `role`/`status`/`gradeLevelId`/`q`/`includeArchived`/pagination params.\n2. Component 3 builds one Prisma query: `status != ARCHIVED` unless\n   `includeArchived`, `q` matched against name/email/admissionNumber/\n   employeeNumber, ordered/filtered to use the `(lastName, firstName,\n   email)` index (component 1) so the 5,000-row/<300ms budget (NFR-2) holds\n   without client-side filtering.\n3. `paginated()` (existing `http.ts` helper) returns rows + meta; the\n   `DataTable` (component 19/21) reads page/pageSize/sort from the URL, not\n   local state, matching its existing contract.\n\n**Create user, `POST /api/users` (FR-6/7/8/9/10):**\n1. Component 11's Zod schema (role-specific) validates the Stepper's step-2\n   payload server-side (never trust the client-validated form alone).\n2. Component 2's `createUser` generates `admissionNumber`/`employeeNumber`\n   where applicable, creates the `User` + profile row + any inline\n   parent/student links (component 6) in one transaction.\n3. If \"Send invitation email now\" is checked, calls component 20's\n   `sendInvite(userId)` — see Overview finding: this call is wired to the\n   interface PRD-01 commits to, and is a no-op/stub until that interface is\n   real.\n4. `audit('user.created', ...)` via the existing `src/server/audit.ts`.\n\n**Edit user / email change (FR-8/9):**\n1. Role is rejected server-side if present and different from the existing\n   row (not just hidden in the UI) — a service-layer invariant, not a form\n   convenience.\n2. An email diff triggers `ConfirmDialog` client-side; on confirm, the PATCH\n   handler updates the email and invalidates (marks used/expired) any\n   pending `AuthToken` rows of type INVITE for that user, so a stale invite\n   link can't activate the old address.\n\n**Status changes (FR-12/13/14):**\n1. `setUserStatus`/`archiveUser` (component 2) check: not self, and —if\n   disabling an ADMIN— that at least one other ACTIVE ADMIN remains, else\n   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'At least one active admin is required.')`.\n2. Disable sets `status=DISABLED`; archive additionally sets\n   `archivedAt=now`. Both are pure data writes today; the \"stops working\n   within 5 minutes\" session-level effect (FR-12) is PRD-01's session check\n   re-reading `status` on its token-refresh interval — this PRD does not\n   and should not build that check (NFR-7), it only guarantees `status` is\n   correct the instant the mutation commits.\n3. Every list/picker query (components 3, 16) and `getAccessibleStudentIds`\n   (component 7) excludes `ARCHIVED` users by default, so archival's\n   app-wide picker exclusion (FR-13) is enforced once, at the query layer,\n   not per-caller.\n\n**Family linking (FR-15/16):**\n1. `linkParentToStudent` runs inside one transaction: count existing links\n   for the student (reject the 5th with `VALIDATION_ERROR`), and if the new\n   link is `isPrimary`, clear `isPrimary` on every other link for that\n   student first, then insert.\n2. Reachable from three entry points (student form, parent form, student\n   detail \"Family\" card) that all call this one function — no duplicated\n   invariant logic.\n\n**CSV import (FR-18–23, NFR-3):**\n1. Browser: papaparse parses the uploaded file (component 8), rejecting\n   >2 MB/>2,000 rows before parsing; each row runs through component 11's\n   Zod schema plus a grade-level-name lookup for Valid/Warning/Error\n   classification with a per-cell reason, rendered in a preview `DataGrid`.\n2. \"Import N valid rows\" POSTs rows (not the file) in chunks of 200 to\n   component 9.\n3. Server re-validates every row independently of the client (NFR-3's\n   trust boundary), matches grade levels case-insensitively by `name` or\n   `shortName`, parses dates strictly as `YYYY-MM-DD`, and skips rows whose\n   email already exists (\"Skipped — already exists\", FR-23) rather than\n   erroring.\n4. Each 200-row batch runs in one `prisma.$transaction` (ADR-3): any row\n   failure that isn't a plain \"skip\" rolls back only that batch, never the\n   whole import; results aggregate into the post-import summary (component\n   10) and, for failed rows, an escaped error-report CSV.\n\n**Student/parent surfaces (FR-24/25/26):**\n1. `/students/[studentId]` and `/my-children` both resolve access through\n   component 7 (`assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds`) — no\n   page implements its own authorization check.\n2. `GET /api/students/:id` (component 13) strips `medicalNotes` for\n   STUDENT/PARENT roles in the service layer before the response is built,\n   so no client-side hiding can leak it (NFR-1); the same strip applies\n   inside component 10's CSV export path.\n\n**Directory picker (FR-28):** `GET /api/users/search` reuses component 3's\nunderlying query (role/q filters, archived excluded) capped to 20 rows and\nprojected down to `{id,name,email,role}` — no separate search index.\n\n**Audit log viewer (FR-29):** pure read over the existing `AuditLog` table\n(`src/server/audit.ts`'s schema) with actor/action-prefix/date-range\nfilters and pagination; no new write path, matching NFR-7.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enums + relations |\n| FR-2 | Component 3 — `GET /api/users` list query |\n| FR-3 | Component 3 — filters (role/status/gradeLevel/search/archived) |\n| FR-4 | Component 19 — row actions dispatch |\n| FR-5 | Component 19 (UI) + Component 10 (export) — bulk actions |\n| FR-6 | Component 5 — Stepper create/edit form |\n| FR-7 | Component 5 (checkbox) + **Component 20** — `sendInvite` call (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |\n| FR-8 | Component 5 — email-change confirm + invite-token invalidation |\n| FR-9 | Component 2 + 5 — role immutability, service + form |\n| FR-10 | Component 11 — shared DOB/phone Zod schema |\n| FR-11 | Component 4 — user detail composition |\n| FR-12 | Component 2 (status write) + **Component 20** — session-level effect (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |\n| FR-13 | Component 2 — archive write; Components 3/7/16 — app-wide picker exclusion |\n| FR-14 | Component 2 — self/last-admin guard |\n| FR-15 | Component 6 — link service, 3 entry points |\n| FR-16 | Component 6 — max-4 / single-primary invariant |\n| FR-17 | Component 7 — `student-access.ts` |\n| FR-18 | Component 9 — static templates; Component 8 — download UI |\n| FR-19 | Component 8 — client parse + preview grid |\n| FR-20 | Component 9 — server re-validation + batched transactions |\n| FR-21 | Component 9 — invite toggle, grade-level matching, strict dates |\n| FR-22 | Component 9 + 10 — summary + error-report CSV |\n| FR-23 | Component 9 — existing-email skip rule |\n| FR-24 | Component 12 — student detail page + Overview tab |\n| FR-25 | Component 7 + 12 — `assertCanViewStudent` gate |\n| FR-26 | Component 14 — `/my-children` |\n| FR-27 | Component 15 — `/account/profile` |\n| FR-28 | Component 16 — search API + `UserPicker` |\n| FR-29 | Component 17 — audit log viewer |\n| FR-30 | Component 18 — navigation entries |\n| FR-31 | **Component 20** — unlock clears PRD-01's lockout fields (MEDIUM confidence, carried from intake — verify exact field names against `prisma/schema.prisma`, which already has `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`) |\n| NFR-1 | Component 7 + 13 + 10 — `medicalNotes` redaction (service layer + export) |\n| NFR-2 | Component 1 + 3 — composite index + server-side pagination |\n| NFR-3 | Component 9 — one transaction per 200-row batch |\n| NFR-4 | Component 10 — `escapeCsvCell` shared util |\n| NFR-5 | Component 21 — MUI-only, existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |\n| NFR-6 | Component 22 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |\n| NFR-7 | Component 2/6/7 (new, additive) + **Component 20** (reuse, not rebuild, PRD-01's interfaces — see Overview) |\n| NFR-8 | All components — additive only, no PRD-05 (class/section) behavior touched |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 31 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\ndropped. Two things carry forward for `arch-api-contracts` and\n`dev-planning`:\n\n1. **FR-31 (MEDIUM confidence):** confirm `POST /api/users/:id/unlock`\n   clears exactly `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` (both already in\n   `prisma/schema.prisma`) before finalizing the contract.\n2. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 20):** `src/server/\n   services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite`, and the session-status re-check\n   behind FR-12, do not exist in `src/` yet — only their schema\n   (`User.status`/`lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/`passwordChangedAt`,\n   `AuthToken`) and the `requireRole()` placeholder exist. This is not a\n   reason to re-implement them inside PRD-03 (NFR-7 forbids it) — it is a\n   reason `dev-planning` should either sequence PRD-01's dev work ahead of\n   PRD-03's component 20 items, or stub `sendInvite`/the status re-check\n   behind the same placeholder convention `requireRole.ts` already\n   establishes, so call sites don't change when PRD-01 lands. The source\n   API table in `03-user-management.md` is otherwise fully specified and\n   ready for `arch-api-contracts` to derive `api-contracts.json` directly\n   from (18 endpoints: `GET/POST /api/users`, `GET/PATCH /api/users/:id`,\n   `POST /api/users/:id/{invite,unlock,status,archive,restore}`, `POST\n   /api/users/import`, `GET /api/users/export`, `GET /api/users/search`,\n   `POST /api/students/:id/parents`, `DELETE /api/students/:id/parents/\n   :parentId`, `GET /api/students/:id`, `GET /api/me/children`, `PATCH\n   /api/me/profile`, `GET /api/audit-logs`).\n","numLines":256,"startLine":1,"totalLines":256}}}
