{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NRjm8fLziX3zsaLZTLM3Rn","type":"tool_result","content":"## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1 Data model\n\n```prisma\nenum EmailStatus { PENDING SENDING SENT FAILED }\n\nmodel Notification {\n  id         String    @id @default(cuid())\n  userId     String\n  user       User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  type       String                       // key from notification type registry\n  title      String                       // max 140 chars\n  body       String?                      // max 500 chars, plain text\n  link       String?                      // relative app path, e.g. \"/courses/abc/assignments/xyz\"\n  readAt     DateTime?\n  createdAt  DateTime  @default(now())\n  @@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])\n}\n\nmodel NotificationPreference {\n  userId     String\n  type       String\n  inApp      Boolean  @default(true)\n  email      Boolean  @default(true)\n  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt\n  @@id([userId, type])\n}\n\nmodel EmailOutbox {\n  id            String      @id @default(cuid())\n  toEmail       String\n  toName        String?\n  subject       String\n  html          String\n  text          String\n  status        EmailStatus @default(PENDING)\n  attempts      Int         @default(0)\n  lastError     String?\n  nextAttemptAt DateTime    @default(now())\n  sentAt        DateTime?\n  createdAt     DateTime    @default(now())\n  @@index([status, nextAttemptAt])\n}\n```\n\n### FR-2 Notification type registry (`src/server/notifications/types.ts`)\n1. Export `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` as a typed record: key → `{ label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }`. Categories: `ACCOUNT`, `ACADEMIC`, `ATTENDANCE`, `COMMUNICATION`, `FINANCE`, `SYSTEM`.\n2. Register in this PRD: `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` (email only, not shown in preferences), `system.test` (admin test message).\n3. Later PRDs add their own keys (for example `assignment.published`, `attendance.absent`). TypeScript must reject unknown keys in `notify()`.\n\n### FR-3 `notify()` service (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`)\n1. Signature: `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })`.\n2. For each recipient: skip archived or disabled users; read preference rows (falling back to registry defaults); create a `Notification` row when in-app is enabled or `mandatoryInApp` is true; enqueue an `EmailOutbox` row when email is enabled and the user has an email.\n3. Uses `createMany` so notifying 1,000 users performs at most 3 database round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\n4. Must never throw to the caller: failures are logged and the calling feature's transaction is unaffected. Callers invoke `notify()` after their own transaction commits.\n5. Helper `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (deduplicated) — used by attendance, grades and assignments later.\n\n### FR-4 Email templates (`src/server/email/templates/`)\n1. Built with `@react-email/components`, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\n2. A base layout: school logo and name header, content area, footer with school address, \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` and the sentence \"You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.\"\n3. Templates in this PRD: `invite` (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), `password-reset` (link, 60-minute expiry notice), `generic-notification` (title, body, call-to-action button to `APP_URL + link`).\n4. `sendAuthEmail()` from PRD-01 now enqueues `invite` / `password-reset` templates via the outbox.\n\n### FR-5 Dispatcher\n1. `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` selects `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now` using `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, marks them `SENDING`, sends via Nodemailer, and marks `SENT` or schedules a retry.\n2. Retry schedule: attempts 1–5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; after the 5th failure set `FAILED`.\n3. Trigger options: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` protected by header `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}` (for an external scheduler, every minute), and `npm run worker:email` — a Node script that loops `dispatchEmails` every 15 seconds for local development and simple deployments.\n4. New env vars: `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, `SMTP_SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM` (for example `\"SchoolHub <no-reply@schoolhub.test>\"`), `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp` | `console`, default `console` in development). The console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\n\n### FR-6 Notification bell (top bar)\n1. Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell. Shows unread count badge (displays \"9+\" above 9). Polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 seconds while the tab is visible (pause on `visibilitychange` hidden).\n2. The bell is an MUI `IconButton` + `Badge`. Clicking opens an MUI `Popover` containing a `List` with the 10 most recent notifications (unread ones bold with a dot), each showing title, body (2-line clamp) and relative time (\"5 min ago\"). Clicking an item marks it read and navigates to `link`. Footer: \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\".\n\n### FR-7 Notifications page (`/notifications`)\n1. Paginated list (20 per page), filter tabs All / Unread, category filter. Bulk \"Mark all as read\". Each row has a mark read / unread toggle.\n2. Notifications older than 180 days are deleted by `purgeOldNotifications()`, called by the dispatcher endpoint once per day (track last run in memory; acceptable to run more than once per day after restarts).\n\n### FR-8 Preferences (`/account/notifications`)\n1. MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader`-style group rows): each type visible to the user's role shows label, description, an \"In app\" switch and an \"Email\" switch. Mandatory in-app types show a disabled MUI `Switch` with tooltip \"Required by the school\".\n2. Changes save immediately (optimistic UI with rollback on error) via `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`.\n\n### FR-9 Admin email log (`/admin/email-log`)\n1. Table: created, recipient, subject, status, attempts, last error. Filter by status. Row action \"Retry now\" for `FAILED` rows resets `attempts = 0`, `status = PENDING`, `nextAttemptAt = now`.\n2. Button \"Send test notification to me\" calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', … })` for the current admin.\n\n## API\n\n| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/notifications` | any | `?unread=true&category=&page=` — own notifications only |\n| `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` | any | `{ data: { count } }` |\n| `POST /api/notifications/:id/read` · `/unread` | owner | |\n| `POST /api/notifications/read-all` | any | |\n| `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | Merged with registry defaults |\n| `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | `{ type, inApp, email }`; `inApp=false` refused for mandatory types |\n| `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` | `CRON_SECRET` | Returns `{ sent, failed, retried }` |\n| `GET /api/admin/email-log` | ADMIN | |\n| `POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry` | ADMIN | |\n| `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` | ADMIN | |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n1. **Performance:** `notify()` for 1,000 recipients must finish in under 2 seconds. Unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50 ms (indexed).\n2. **Reliability:** an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row locking). A crash mid-send leaves rows in `SENDING`; rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 minutes return to `PENDING`.\n3. **Security:** notification `link` values must be relative paths starting with `/` (validated) to prevent open redirects. Email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\n4. **Deliverability:** every email has both HTML and plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Given a user with default preferences, when `notify()` is called for type `system.test`, then one `Notification` row and one `EmailOutbox` row are created and the bell count increases by 1 within 30 seconds.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecdd0a7a-9233-4799-bc04-313a457b4439","uuid":"13ffbc6c-09e6-4851-82e8-cc50ba08e19d","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:08:47.424Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1 Data model\n\n```prisma\nenum EmailStatus { PENDING SENDING SENT FAILED }\n\nmodel Notification {\n  id         String    @id @default(cuid())\n  userId     String\n  user       User      @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  type       String                       // key from notification type registry\n  title      String                       // max 140 chars\n  body       String?                      // max 500 chars, plain text\n  link       String?                      // relative app path, e.g. \"/courses/abc/assignments/xyz\"\n  readAt     DateTime?\n  createdAt  DateTime  @default(now())\n  @@index([userId, readAt, createdAt])\n}\n\nmodel NotificationPreference {\n  userId     String\n  type       String\n  inApp      Boolean  @default(true)\n  email      Boolean  @default(true)\n  updatedAt  DateTime @updatedAt\n  @@id([userId, type])\n}\n\nmodel EmailOutbox {\n  id            String      @id @default(cuid())\n  toEmail       String\n  toName        String?\n  subject       String\n  html          String\n  text          String\n  status        EmailStatus @default(PENDING)\n  attempts      Int         @default(0)\n  lastError     String?\n  nextAttemptAt DateTime    @default(now())\n  sentAt        DateTime?\n  createdAt     DateTime    @default(now())\n  @@index([status, nextAttemptAt])\n}\n```\n\n### FR-2 Notification type registry (`src/server/notifications/types.ts`)\n1. Export `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` as a typed record: key → `{ label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles }`. Categories: `ACCOUNT`, `ACADEMIC`, `ATTENDANCE`, `COMMUNICATION`, `FINANCE`, `SYSTEM`.\n2. Register in this PRD: `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` (email only, not shown in preferences), `system.test` (admin test message).\n3. Later PRDs add their own keys (for example `assignment.published`, `attendance.absent`). TypeScript must reject unknown keys in `notify()`.\n\n### FR-3 `notify()` service (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`)\n1. Signature: `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })`.\n2. For each recipient: skip archived or disabled users; read preference rows (falling back to registry defaults); create a `Notification` row when in-app is enabled or `mandatoryInApp` is true; enqueue an `EmailOutbox` row when email is enabled and the user has an email.\n3. Uses `createMany` so notifying 1,000 users performs at most 3 database round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails.\n4. Must never throw to the caller: failures are logged and the calling feature's transaction is unaffected. Callers invoke `notify()` after their own transaction commits.\n5. Helper `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` expands each student to the student plus all linked parents (deduplicated) — used by attendance, grades and assignments later.\n\n### FR-4 Email templates (`src/server/email/templates/`)\n1. Built with `@react-email/components`, rendered to both HTML and plain text.\n2. A base layout: school logo and name header, content area, footer with school address, \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` and the sentence \"You are receiving this because you have a SchoolHub account.\"\n3. Templates in this PRD: `invite` (name, school name, accept link, expiry date), `password-reset` (link, 60-minute expiry notice), `generic-notification` (title, body, call-to-action button to `APP_URL + link`).\n4. `sendAuthEmail()` from PRD-01 now enqueues `invite` / `password-reset` templates via the outbox.\n\n### FR-5 Dispatcher\n1. `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })` selects `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now` using `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, marks them `SENDING`, sends via Nodemailer, and marks `SENT` or schedules a retry.\n2. Retry schedule: attempts 1–5 back off at 1, 5, 15, 60 and 240 minutes; after the 5th failure set `FAILED`.\n3. Trigger options: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` protected by header `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}` (for an external scheduler, every minute), and `npm run worker:email` — a Node script that loops `dispatchEmails` every 15 seconds for local development and simple deployments.\n4. New env vars: `SMTP_HOST`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USER`, `SMTP_PASS`, `SMTP_SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM` (for example `\"SchoolHub <no-reply@schoolhub.test>\"`), `CRON_SECRET`, `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (`smtp` | `console`, default `console` in development). The console transport logs subject, recipient and text body.\n\n### FR-6 Notification bell (top bar)\n1. Replace the PRD-00 placeholder bell. Shows unread count badge (displays \"9+\" above 9). Polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30 seconds while the tab is visible (pause on `visibilitychange` hidden).\n2. The bell is an MUI `IconButton` + `Badge`. Clicking opens an MUI `Popover` containing a `List` with the 10 most recent notifications (unread ones bold with a dot), each showing title, body (2-line clamp) and relative time (\"5 min ago\"). Clicking an item marks it read and navigates to `link`. Footer: \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\".\n\n### FR-7 Notifications page (`/notifications`)\n1. Paginated list (20 per page), filter tabs All / Unread, category filter. Bulk \"Mark all as read\". Each row has a mark read / unread toggle.\n2. Notifications older than 180 days are deleted by `purgeOldNotifications()`, called by the dispatcher endpoint once per day (track last run in memory; acceptable to run more than once per day after restarts).\n\n### FR-8 Preferences (`/account/notifications`)\n1. MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader`-style group rows): each type visible to the user's role shows label, description, an \"In app\" switch and an \"Email\" switch. Mandatory in-app types show a disabled MUI `Switch` with tooltip \"Required by the school\".\n2. Changes save immediately (optimistic UI with rollback on error) via `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`.\n\n### FR-9 Admin email log (`/admin/email-log`)\n1. Table: created, recipient, subject, status, attempts, last error. Filter by status. Row action \"Retry now\" for `FAILED` rows resets `attempts = 0`, `status = PENDING`, `nextAttemptAt = now`.\n2. Button \"Send test notification to me\" calls `notify({ type: 'system.test', … })` for the current admin.\n\n## API\n\n| Method & path | Role | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/notifications` | any | `?unread=true&category=&page=` — own notifications only |\n| `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` | any | `{ data: { count } }` |\n| `POST /api/notifications/:id/read` · `/unread` | owner | |\n| `POST /api/notifications/read-all` | any | |\n| `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | Merged with registry defaults |\n| `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` | any | `{ type, inApp, email }`; `inApp=false` refused for mandatory types |\n| `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` | `CRON_SECRET` | Returns `{ sent, failed, retried }` |\n| `GET /api/admin/email-log` | ADMIN | |\n| `POST /api/admin/email-log/:id/retry` | ADMIN | |\n| `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` | ADMIN | |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n1. **Performance:** `notify()` for 1,000 recipients must finish in under 2 seconds. Unread-count endpoint must respond in under 50 ms (indexed).\n2. **Reliability:** an email is never sent twice by concurrent dispatchers (row locking). A crash mid-send leaves rows in `SENDING`; rows stuck in `SENDING` for more than 10 minutes return to `PENDING`.\n3. **Security:** notification `link` values must be relative paths starting with `/` (validated) to prevent open redirects. Email HTML escapes all user-provided text.\n4. **Deliverability:** every email has both HTML and plain-text parts and a `List-Unsubscribe` header pointing at the preferences page.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. Given a user with default preferences, when `notify()` is called for type `system.test`, then one `Notification` row and one `EmailOutbox` row are created and the bell count increases by 1 within 30 seconds.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBQsFg1H9pC2nr49DeRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have everything I need. Now writing `system-design.md` for ticket abcd-04 (overwriting the stale PRD-03 content currently on disk)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3282,"cache_read_input_tokens":69968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3282},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecdd0a7a-9233-4799-bc04-313a457b4439","uuid":"2187c940-5615-4824-a6f4-80b121847cc9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:08:49.580Z","request_id":"req_011CgBQsFQt8vZ7HzMdV9BuG"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgBQsFg1H9pC2nr49DeRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A4G2fgPshtsNmbNjX9TnZH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-04 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-01 (auth/RBAC,\ndesign-only — not landed), PRD-02 (academic structure) and PRD-03 (user\nmanagement). Intake reports **97% confidence and zero blockers**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`); the one MEDIUM-confidence item (FR-23, exact\nnav entries) is resolved below rather than carried forward as a gap.\n\n**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\nthe design — the same PRD-01 sequencing gap PRD-03's system-design.md\nalready flagged:** every source PRD, including this one, documents\n`src/server/auth/permissions.ts` exporting `requireUser()` and\n`requireRole()`. That file does not exist. `src/server/auth/` contains only\n`requireRole.ts` — a placeholder that returns a hardcoded ADMIN identity and\nchecks role — and `student-access.ts`. There is no `requireUser()`\nanywhere in `src/`. NFR-7 requires \"own-notifications-only\" checks on every\nuser-facing route (`GET /api/notifications`, read/unread, preferences),\nwhich needs a resolved *user identity*, not just a role gate. Since PRD-01\nhas not landed, this design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — the same\nplaceholder `requireRole.ts` already exports, called with every role —\neverywhere a real `requireUser()` would go, documented inline as a\nsequencing dependency (Component 12 below) exactly as PRD-03's Component 20\ndid for `sendInvite`. No new auth module is built here (that is PRD-01's\njob); call sites are written so swapping the placeholder for the real\n`requireUser()` later is a one-file change, not a per-route rewrite.\n\nSecond brownfield fact confirmed directly in source: `src/server/services/\nusers.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)` (lines ~385-390) is a logging-only stub\nreturning `{ id, inviteSentAt }`. FR-9 replaces its *body* with a real\n`sendAuthEmail()` call while preserving that exact signature, so PRD-03's\ncall sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, the create-user \"send invitation\"\ncheckbox) do not change.\n\nNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, Nodemailer + console transport,\n`@react-email/components` for templates (the one explicit exemption from\nthe MUI-only rule — scoped to `src/server/email/templates/**`), raw\n`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for dispatch (no queue library), one dispatch\nfunction behind two thin drivers (HTTP route + loop script), a compile-time\ntype registry (no DB table), in-memory scheduling for both the stuck-row\nrecovery and the daily purge. This document arranges those choices into\ncomponents, data flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability.\n\nTwo chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\nbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\ncode: **`notify()`** (FR-3/4/5/6) and **`dispatchEmails()`** (FR-10/11).\nOne list/read service backs both the bell popover (FR-15) and the\n`/notifications` page (FR-16) — not two query paths. FR-23's nav entries\nare resolved here (Component 11) rather than left open.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum, exactly per the schema block in `04-notifications.md` FR-1 (composite index `Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt)`, `EmailOutbox(status, nextAttemptAt)`) | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| 2 | Notification Type Registry | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const object (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles) across ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM; seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`; `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is `notify()`'s type parameter so unknown keys are a compile error (FR-3) | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-2, FR-3 |\n| 3 | Notification Service (`notify()`) | `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`: filters out archived/disabled users, resolves per-user `NotificationPreference` (falling back to registry defaults), `createMany` for `Notification` rows where in-app applies (including when `mandatoryInApp` overrides an off preference), `createMany` for `EmailOutbox` rows where email applies and the user has an email; never throws — failures logged via `logger`, caller's own transaction already committed by the time this runs; `link` values validated as `/`-prefixed relative paths before write (NFR-5) | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-5 |\n| 4 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })`: expands each student id to itself + linked parent ids via the existing `ParentStudentLink` table (PRD-03's model, read-only here), dedupes, calls Component 3 once with the combined id list — no new link model | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` (co-located, thin wrapper) | FR-6 |\n| 5 | Email Templates | `BaseLayout` (logo/name header, content slot, footer with school address + \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` + required disclosure sentence) plus `invite`, `password-reset`, `generic-notification` templates, each rendered via `@react-email/render`'s `render()` for HTML and `render(..., { plainText: true })` for text — one render call backs both `EmailOutbox.html`/`.text` columns so the two parts can't drift; all interpolated user text passes through React Email's escaping (NFR-5's HTML-escape rule) | `src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx`, `invite.tsx`, `password-reset.tsx`, `generic-notification.tsx` | FR-7, FR-8, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| 6 | Auth Email Integration | `sendAuthEmail()` replaces the body of the existing `sendInvite()` stub in `src/server/services/users.ts` (same exported signature `(userId) => Promise<{ id, inviteSentAt }>`, so PRD-03's call sites are untouched): looks up the user, renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset` template, inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (bypasses Component 3 — auth emails are not user-preference-gated), returns the existing shape | `src/server/services/users.ts` (edit, not new file) | FR-9 |\n| 7 | Email Transport | One module building either a real SMTP `nodemailer.createTransport` or a `console` transport (logs subject/recipient/text) from `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (default `console` in dev), reading `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`; sets the `List-Unsubscribe` header on every send pointing at `/account/notifications` (NFR-6) | `src/server/email/transport.ts`, env vars in `.env.example` | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| 8 | Email Dispatcher (`dispatchEmails()`) | One function: (a) recovers rows stuck in `SENDING` >10 min back to `PENDING` (NFR-4), (b) `prisma.$transaction` containing `$queryRaw SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim up to `batchSize` (default 50) `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now`, flips them to `SENDING`; (c) outside the lock, sends each via Component 7's transport, marks `SENT`/`sentAt` on success or applies the FR-11 backoff (1/5/15/60/240 min across attempts 1-5, `FAILED` after the 5th) on failure; also runs Component 9's purge once per calendar day via an in-memory last-run timestamp checked at the top of each call | `src/server/email/dispatcher.ts` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-4 |\n| 9 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()`: deletes `Notification` rows with `createdAt` older than 180 days; a plain function called from Component 8's daily check, not a separate cron/queue | `src/server/notifications/purge.ts` | FR-17 |\n| 10 | Dispatch Drivers | Two thin callers of Component 8: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET` check, 401 via standard error envelope on mismatch — NFR-8) returning `{ sent, failed, retried }`; and `npm run worker:email`, a `tsx`-run Node script looping Component 8 every 15s (matches the existing `db:seed` script pattern) | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `scripts/worker-email.ts` | FR-12, NFR-8 |\n| 11 | Notification List/Read Service | One query module: `listNotifications({ userId, unread?, category?, page, pageSize })` (own-rows-only, joins registry metadata for category/label), `getUnreadCount(userId)` (indexed by Component 1's composite index, NFR-3's <50ms budget), `markRead(userId, id)` / `markUnread` / `markAllRead(userId)` — the single implementation backing both the popover (FR-15) and the `/notifications` page (FR-16) | `src/server/notifications/list.ts` | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-3 |\n| 12 | Auth Touchpoint (sequencing dependency) | Every user-facing notification/preferences route calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` where a real `requireUser()` is specified — see Overview finding. `ADMIN`-only routes (email-log, test-send) call `requireRole('ADMIN')` directly, already real today. The internal dispatch route uses its own `CRON_SECRET` bearer check (Component 10), not this helper. One-file swap when PRD-01's real `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` lands | *(calls into existing `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`; no new file)* | NFR-7 |\n| 13 | Bell/Popover UI | Replaces the static `Badge badgeContent={0}` in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (~line 141) with a live MUI `IconButton` + `Badge` driven by a shared `useUnreadCount()` hook (`fetch` + `setInterval(30_000)`, paused on `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'` via a `visibilitychange` listener, \"9+\" cap above 9); clicking opens an MUI `Popover` with a `List` of the 10 most recent notifications from Component 11 (unread bold + dot, 2-line-clamped body, relative time), click marks read + navigates to `link`; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\" | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (edit), `src/hooks/useUnreadCount.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` | FR-14, FR-15 |\n| 14 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page) `DataTable`-less simple MUI `List`/`Table` over Component 11, All/Unread `Tabs`, category filter, bulk \"Mark all as read\", per-row read/unread toggle | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` | FR-16 |\n| 15 | Preferences UI + API | `/account/notifications`: MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader` rows) over Component 2's registry filtered to the current user's role, each row an In-app `Switch` + Email `Switch` (mandatory-in-app types render a disabled `Switch` + `Tooltip` \"Required by the school\"); `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves one `{type, inApp, email}` row immediately, client does optimistic update with rollback on a non-2xx response; server rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types with `VALIDATION_ERROR` (defense in depth alongside the disabled switch) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` | FR-18, FR-19, FR-22, NFR-7 |\n| 16 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table over `EmailOutbox` (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), status filter, \"Retry now\" row action (`attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now` — same reset shape Component 8 expects on its next pass), \"Send test notification to me\" button calling Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'` for the current admin | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts`, `.../email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` | FR-20 |\n| 17 | REST API Surface | All 12 endpoints from the PRD's API table, built on `src/server/http.ts`'s existing `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError`/`AppError` conventions — finalized verbatim in `api-contracts.json` by `arch-api-contracts` | `src/app/api/notifications/**`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/**`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/**`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/**`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/**` | FR-21 |\n| 18 | Navigation | Resolves FR-23 (MEDIUM confidence in intake): add \"Notifications\" (`/notifications`, all roles) under the existing top-level entries, and \"Email log\" (`/admin/email-log`, ADMIN only) grouped with other admin-only entries — following the existing flat `NavItem[]` + `roles` convention (no \"Administration\" group exists yet in `navigation.ts`; PRD-02/03's group ideas are a later PRD's concern, not introduced here) | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-23 |\n| 19 | Design System (MUI-only, directory-scoped) | Every app-UI surface (bell, popover, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only, looked up via the MUI MCP server; `src/server/email/templates/**` is the one ESLint `no-restricted-imports` exemption glob so `@react-email/components` imports there aren't flagged, while every other path stays MUI-only | ESLint config (exemption glob addition), reuses existing `theme.ts` | NFR-1 |\n| 20 | Seed Data | 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`, linking to `/dashboard` — depends on Component 1's schema and Component 2's registry key existing first | `prisma/seed.ts` (extend existing script) | FR-24 |\n| 21 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (registry compile-time key rejection via a type-level test, retry-backoff schedule math, link-path validator, CSV-free here — N/A); Vitest integration (`notify()` batching round-trip count, `dispatchEmails()` claim-and-send with concurrent-dispatcher race, stuck-row recovery, mandatory-preference server rejection); Playwright e2e (bell unread count updates after `notify()`, mark-all-read, preferences toggle persists, admin retry-now, admin test-send) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-9 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (Registry) depends\non 1's `type: String` column and feeds 3, 4, 11, 15, 16. 3 (`notify()`)\ndepends on 1, 2 and is called by 4, 6 (indirectly — 6 bypasses it, see its\nrow), 16's test-send, and every later PRD per FR-6's stated intent. 5\n(Templates) feeds 6 and 8. 6 edits an existing file and depends on 5. 7\nfeeds 8. 8 (`dispatchEmails`) depends on 1, 5 (indirectly via rows already\nrendered), 7, 9, and is called only by 10. 11 depends on 1, 2 and feeds 13,\n14. 12 is a calling convention, not a buildable unit — it gates 11, 13, 14,\n15, 16's non-ADMIN-already-real routes. 17 wraps 3/8/11/15/16 behind routes.\n18–20 are independent leaf tasks. 21 wraps all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**`notify()` call (FR-3/4/5/6, NFR-2, NFR-5):**\n1. Caller (any service, after its own transaction commits) invokes\n   `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`. Component 3\n   validates `link` is `/`-prefixed if present (NFR-5) — throws\n   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', ...)` only for this programmer-error case;\n   every other failure mode (missing user, send failure) is logged, not\n   thrown.\n2. Filters `userIds` to non-archived, non-disabled users in one query, then\n   reads each remaining user's `NotificationPreference` row for `type`\n   (one query, `findMany` with `in`), falling back to Component 2's\n   registry defaults (`defaultEmail`, `mandatoryInApp`) where no row exists.\n3. One `createMany` writes all qualifying `Notification` rows (in-app\n   enabled OR `mandatoryInApp`); one `createMany` writes all qualifying\n   `EmailOutbox` rows (email enabled AND user has an email) — ≤3 round\n   trips total per FR-5, holding NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/<2s budget.\n4. `notifyStudentAndParents` (Component 4) is a pre-step: resolve\n   `studentIds` → student + linked-parent ids via `ParentStudentLink`\n   (existing table), dedupe, then run steps 1-3 once over the combined list.\n\n**Email dispatch (FR-10/11/12, NFR-4):**\n1. Either driver (Component 10) calls `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })`.\n2. Top of the call: `UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='PENDING' WHERE\n   status='SENDING' AND updatedAt-equivalent < now()-10min` (recovers\n   crashed-mid-send rows, NFR-4) — tracked via `nextAttemptAt`/a dedicated\n   timestamp set when flipped to `SENDING`.\n3. One `prisma.$transaction` runs `SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE\n   status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now() ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\"\n   LIMIT $batchSize FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then `UPDATE ... SET\n   status='SENDING'` on exactly those ids — this is the only raw SQL in the\n   codebase, isolated to this function (no double-send across concurrent\n   dispatchers, NFR-4).\n4. Outside the lock: each claimed row renders through Component 7's\n   transport. Success → `status='SENT', sentAt=now()`. Failure → bump\n   `attempts`; if `attempts < 5`, `status='PENDING'` with `nextAttemptAt`\n   set per the 1/5/15/60/240-minute schedule (FR-11); at `attempts === 5`,\n   `status='FAILED'`.\n5. Once per calendar day (in-memory last-run check): call Component 9's\n   `purgeOldNotifications()`.\n\n**Auth email (FR-9):**\n1. PRD-03 call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, \"send invitation now\"\n   checkbox) call `sendInvite(userId)` exactly as before — signature\n   unchanged.\n2. Internally it now renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset`\n   template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (no preference gate\n   — auth emails are mandatory), then returns the same `{ id,\n   inviteSentAt }` shape the stub always returned.\n\n**Bell + popover (FR-14/15):**\n1. `useUnreadCount()` polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s\n   while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`; a `visibilitychange`\n   listener clears/restarts the interval.\n2. Popover open → one call to Component 11's `listNotifications` capped at\n   10 rows, newest first. Item click → `POST /api/notifications/:id/read`\n   then client-side navigate to `link`.\n\n**Preferences (FR-18/19/22):**\n1. Page load merges Component 2's registry (filtered to the signed-in\n   user's role) with the user's existing `NotificationPreference` rows\n   (defaults where absent).\n2. Switch toggle → optimistic local state update + `PUT\n   /api/me/notification-preferences` with `{type, inApp, email}`; server\n   rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types before any write\n   (`VALIDATION_ERROR`); a non-2xx response rolls the toggle back\n   client-side.\n\n**Admin email log (FR-20):** pure read/action surface over `EmailOutbox`\n(Component 1) — \"Retry now\" is a plain update (`attempts=0,\nstatus=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`), picked up by the next\n`dispatchEmails()` pass (step 3 above), not a separate send path. \"Send\ntest\" is a direct call into Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'`.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enum |\n| FR-2 | Component 2 — type registry |\n| FR-3 | Component 2 (compile-time union) + Component 3 (`notify()` signature) |\n| FR-4 | Component 3 — core `notify()` logic |\n| FR-5 | Component 3 — `createMany` batching + never-throw contract |\n| FR-6 | Component 4 — `notifyStudentAndParents` |\n| FR-7 | Component 5 — base layout + HTML/text render |\n| FR-8 | Component 5 — invite/password-reset/generic templates |\n| FR-9 | Component 6 — `sendAuthEmail()` swap, signature preserved |\n| FR-10 | Component 8 — `dispatchEmails()` claim/send/update |\n| FR-11 | Component 8 — retry backoff schedule |\n| FR-12 | Component 10 — HTTP route + worker script, one shared function |\n| FR-13 | Component 7 — transport + env vars |\n| FR-14 | Component 13 — bell poll/pause |\n| FR-15 | Component 13 — popover list (via Component 11) |\n| FR-16 | Component 14 — `/notifications` page (via Component 11) |\n| FR-17 | Component 9 — purge, triggered from Component 8 |\n| FR-18 | Component 15 — preferences table UI |\n| FR-19 | Component 15 — optimistic PUT |\n| FR-20 | Component 16 — admin email log |\n| FR-21 | Component 17 — full REST surface |\n| FR-22 | Component 15 — server-side mandatory-type rejection |\n| FR-23 | Component 18 — nav entries (MEDIUM confidence resolved: flat entries, not a new group) |\n| FR-24 | Component 20 — seed rows |\n| NFR-1 | Component 19 — MUI-only, directory-scoped ESLint exemption |\n| NFR-2 | Component 3 — ≤3-round-trip batching |\n| NFR-3 | Component 1 (index) + Component 11 (`getUnreadCount` query shape) |\n| NFR-4 | Component 8 — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` + stuck-row recovery |\n| NFR-5 | Component 3 (`link` validation) + Component 5 (template escaping) |\n| NFR-6 | Component 5 (HTML+text render) + Component 7 (`List-Unsubscribe` header) |\n| NFR-7 | Component 12 — `requireRole` placeholder standing in for `requireUser` (sequencing dependency, see Overview) + Component 15/16's ADMIN/own-row checks |\n| NFR-8 | Component 10 — `CRON_SECRET` bearer check, 401 on mismatch |\n| NFR-9 | Component 21 — test harness |\n| NFR-10 | All components — no SMS/push/websockets/digests introduced |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 24 FR ids and 10 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\ndropped. FR-23's MEDIUM-confidence nav question is resolved (flat entries\nunder existing roles-based filtering, no new nav group introduced since\n`navigation.ts` has none today). Two things carry forward for\n`arch-api-contracts` and `dev-planning`:\n\n1. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 12):** `src/server/auth/\n   permissions.ts`'s `requireUser()` does not exist in `src/` yet — only\n   `requireRole.ts`'s ADMIN-placeholder and `student-access.ts` do. This\n   design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` everywhere a real `requireUser()`\n   would go on user-facing notification/preferences routes, so the later\n   swap to PRD-01's real session-aware helper is confined to that one file\n   plus each route's import line — not a redesign. ADMIN-only and\n   `CRON_SECRET`-gated routes need no placeholder; they already have a real\n   check today.\n2. **Ready for `arch-api-contracts`:** the 12-endpoint API table in\n   `04-notifications.md` is fully specified (methods, paths, roles, notes)\n   and maps 1:1 onto Components 3/8/11/15/16 above — no net-new business\n   logic to invent at the route layer, only envelope/pagination/error-code\n   wiring per `src/server/http.ts`'s existing conventions.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3282,"cache_read_input_tokens":69968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3282},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecdd0a7a-9233-4799-bc04-313a457b4439","uuid":"0789387c-b714-4b43-9d89-a433558e348c","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:10:15.670Z","request_id":"req_011CgBQsFQt8vZ7HzMdV9BuG"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A4G2fgPshtsNmbNjX9TnZH","type":"tool_result","content":"The file artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecdd0a7a-9233-4799-bc04-313a457b4439","uuid":"d9cd05aa-3a24-4471-a3d8-7f80df674580","timestamp":"2026-10-19T10:10:15.762Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-04 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-01 (auth/RBAC,\ndesign-only — not landed), PRD-02 (academic structure) and PRD-03 (user\nmanagement). Intake reports **97% confidence and zero blockers**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`); the one MEDIUM-confidence item (FR-23, exact\nnav entries) is resolved below rather than carried forward as a gap.\n\n**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\nthe design — the same PRD-01 sequencing gap PRD-03's system-design.md\nalready flagged:** every source PRD, including this one, documents\n`src/server/auth/permissions.ts` exporting `requireUser()` and\n`requireRole()`. That file does not exist. `src/server/auth/` contains only\n`requireRole.ts` — a placeholder that returns a hardcoded ADMIN identity and\nchecks role — and `student-access.ts`. There is no `requireUser()`\nanywhere in `src/`. NFR-7 requires \"own-notifications-only\" checks on every\nuser-facing route (`GET /api/notifications`, read/unread, preferences),\nwhich needs a resolved *user identity*, not just a role gate. Since PRD-01\nhas not landed, this design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — the same\nplaceholder `requireRole.ts` already exports, called with every role —\neverywhere a real `requireUser()` would go, documented inline as a\nsequencing dependency (Component 12 below) exactly as PRD-03's Component 20\ndid for `sendInvite`. No new auth module is built here (that is PRD-01's\njob); call sites are written so swapping the placeholder for the real\n`requireUser()` later is a one-file change, not a per-route rewrite.\n\nSecond brownfield fact confirmed directly in source: `src/server/services/\nusers.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)` (lines ~385-390) is a logging-only stub\nreturning `{ id, inviteSentAt }`. FR-9 replaces its *body* with a real\n`sendAuthEmail()` call while preserving that exact signature, so PRD-03's\ncall sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, the create-user \"send invitation\"\ncheckbox) do not change.\n\nNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, Nodemailer + console transport,\n`@react-email/components` for templates (the one explicit exemption from\nthe MUI-only rule — scoped to `src/server/email/templates/**`), raw\n`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for dispatch (no queue library), one dispatch\nfunction behind two thin drivers (HTTP route + loop script), a compile-time\ntype registry (no DB table), in-memory scheduling for both the stuck-row\nrecovery and the daily purge. This document arranges those choices into\ncomponents, data flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability.\n\nTwo chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\nbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\ncode: **`notify()`** (FR-3/4/5/6) and **`dispatchEmails()`** (FR-10/11).\nOne list/read service backs both the bell popover (FR-15) and the\n`/notifications` page (FR-16) — not two query paths. FR-23's nav entries\nare resolved here (Component 11) rather than left open.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum, exactly per the schema block in `04-notifications.md` FR-1 (composite index `Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt)`, `EmailOutbox(status, nextAttemptAt)`) | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| 2 | Notification Type Registry | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const object (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles) across ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM; seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`; `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is `notify()`'s type parameter so unknown keys are a compile error (FR-3) | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-2, FR-3 |\n| 3 | Notification Service (`notify()`) | `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`: filters out archived/disabled users, resolves per-user `NotificationPreference` (falling back to registry defaults), `createMany` for `Notification` rows where in-app applies (including when `mandatoryInApp` overrides an off preference), `createMany` for `EmailOutbox` rows where email applies and the user has an email; never throws — failures logged via `logger`, caller's own transaction already committed by the time this runs; `link` values validated as `/`-prefixed relative paths before write (NFR-5) | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-5 |\n| 4 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })`: expands each student id to itself + linked parent ids via the existing `ParentStudentLink` table (PRD-03's model, read-only here), dedupes, calls Component 3 once with the combined id list — no new link model | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` (co-located, thin wrapper) | FR-6 |\n| 5 | Email Templates | `BaseLayout` (logo/name header, content slot, footer with school address + \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` + required disclosure sentence) plus `invite`, `password-reset`, `generic-notification` templates, each rendered via `@react-email/render`'s `render()` for HTML and `render(..., { plainText: true })` for text — one render call backs both `EmailOutbox.html`/`.text` columns so the two parts can't drift; all interpolated user text passes through React Email's escaping (NFR-5's HTML-escape rule) | `src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx`, `invite.tsx`, `password-reset.tsx`, `generic-notification.tsx` | FR-7, FR-8, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| 6 | Auth Email Integration | `sendAuthEmail()` replaces the body of the existing `sendInvite()` stub in `src/server/services/users.ts` (same exported signature `(userId) => Promise<{ id, inviteSentAt }>`, so PRD-03's call sites are untouched): looks up the user, renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset` template, inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (bypasses Component 3 — auth emails are not user-preference-gated), returns the existing shape | `src/server/services/users.ts` (edit, not new file) | FR-9 |\n| 7 | Email Transport | One module building either a real SMTP `nodemailer.createTransport` or a `console` transport (logs subject/recipient/text) from `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (default `console` in dev), reading `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`; sets the `List-Unsubscribe` header on every send pointing at `/account/notifications` (NFR-6) | `src/server/email/transport.ts`, env vars in `.env.example` | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| 8 | Email Dispatcher (`dispatchEmails()`) | One function: (a) recovers rows stuck in `SENDING` >10 min back to `PENDING` (NFR-4), (b) `prisma.$transaction` containing `$queryRaw SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim up to `batchSize` (default 50) `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now`, flips them to `SENDING`; (c) outside the lock, sends each via Component 7's transport, marks `SENT`/`sentAt` on success or applies the FR-11 backoff (1/5/15/60/240 min across attempts 1-5, `FAILED` after the 5th) on failure; also runs Component 9's purge once per calendar day via an in-memory last-run timestamp checked at the top of each call | `src/server/email/dispatcher.ts` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-4 |\n| 9 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()`: deletes `Notification` rows with `createdAt` older than 180 days; a plain function called from Component 8's daily check, not a separate cron/queue | `src/server/notifications/purge.ts` | FR-17 |\n| 10 | Dispatch Drivers | Two thin callers of Component 8: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET` check, 401 via standard error envelope on mismatch — NFR-8) returning `{ sent, failed, retried }`; and `npm run worker:email`, a `tsx`-run Node script looping Component 8 every 15s (matches the existing `db:seed` script pattern) | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `scripts/worker-email.ts` | FR-12, NFR-8 |\n| 11 | Notification List/Read Service | One query module: `listNotifications({ userId, unread?, category?, page, pageSize })` (own-rows-only, joins registry metadata for category/label), `getUnreadCount(userId)` (indexed by Component 1's composite index, NFR-3's <50ms budget), `markRead(userId, id)` / `markUnread` / `markAllRead(userId)` — the single implementation backing both the popover (FR-15) and the `/notifications` page (FR-16) | `src/server/notifications/list.ts` | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-3 |\n| 12 | Auth Touchpoint (sequencing dependency) | Every user-facing notification/preferences route calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` where a real `requireUser()` is specified — see Overview finding. `ADMIN`-only routes (email-log, test-send) call `requireRole('ADMIN')` directly, already real today. The internal dispatch route uses its own `CRON_SECRET` bearer check (Component 10), not this helper. One-file swap when PRD-01's real `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` lands | *(calls into existing `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`; no new file)* | NFR-7 |\n| 13 | Bell/Popover UI | Replaces the static `Badge badgeContent={0}` in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (~line 141) with a live MUI `IconButton` + `Badge` driven by a shared `useUnreadCount()` hook (`fetch` + `setInterval(30_000)`, paused on `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'` via a `visibilitychange` listener, \"9+\" cap above 9); clicking opens an MUI `Popover` with a `List` of the 10 most recent notifications from Component 11 (unread bold + dot, 2-line-clamped body, relative time), click marks read + navigates to `link`; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\" | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (edit), `src/hooks/useUnreadCount.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` | FR-14, FR-15 |\n| 14 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page) `DataTable`-less simple MUI `List`/`Table` over Component 11, All/Unread `Tabs`, category filter, bulk \"Mark all as read\", per-row read/unread toggle | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` | FR-16 |\n| 15 | Preferences UI + API | `/account/notifications`: MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader` rows) over Component 2's registry filtered to the current user's role, each row an In-app `Switch` + Email `Switch` (mandatory-in-app types render a disabled `Switch` + `Tooltip` \"Required by the school\"); `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves one `{type, inApp, email}` row immediately, client does optimistic update with rollback on a non-2xx response; server rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types with `VALIDATION_ERROR` (defense in depth alongside the disabled switch) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` | FR-18, FR-19, FR-22, NFR-7 |\n| 16 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table over `EmailOutbox` (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), status filter, \"Retry now\" row action (`attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now` — same reset shape Component 8 expects on its next pass), \"Send test notification to me\" button calling Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'` for the current admin | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts`, `.../email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` | FR-20 |\n| 17 | REST API Surface | All 12 endpoints from the PRD's API table, built on `src/server/http.ts`'s existing `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError`/`AppError` conventions — finalized verbatim in `api-contracts.json` by `arch-api-contracts` | `src/app/api/notifications/**`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/**`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/**`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/**`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/**` | FR-21 |\n| 18 | Navigation | Resolves FR-23 (MEDIUM confidence in intake): add \"Notifications\" (`/notifications`, all roles) under the existing top-level entries, and \"Email log\" (`/admin/email-log`, ADMIN only) grouped with other admin-only entries — following the existing flat `NavItem[]` + `roles` convention (no \"Administration\" group exists yet in `navigation.ts`; PRD-02/03's group ideas are a later PRD's concern, not introduced here) | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-23 |\n| 19 | Design System (MUI-only, directory-scoped) | Every app-UI surface (bell, popover, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only, looked up via the MUI MCP server; `src/server/email/templates/**` is the one ESLint `no-restricted-imports` exemption glob so `@react-email/components` imports there aren't flagged, while every other path stays MUI-only | ESLint config (exemption glob addition), reuses existing `theme.ts` | NFR-1 |\n| 20 | Seed Data | 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`, linking to `/dashboard` — depends on Component 1's schema and Component 2's registry key existing first | `prisma/seed.ts` (extend existing script) | FR-24 |\n| 21 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (registry compile-time key rejection via a type-level test, retry-backoff schedule math, link-path validator, CSV-free here — N/A); Vitest integration (`notify()` batching round-trip count, `dispatchEmails()` claim-and-send with concurrent-dispatcher race, stuck-row recovery, mandatory-preference server rejection); Playwright e2e (bell unread count updates after `notify()`, mark-all-read, preferences toggle persists, admin retry-now, admin test-send) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-9 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (Registry) depends\non 1's `type: String` column and feeds 3, 4, 11, 15, 16. 3 (`notify()`)\ndepends on 1, 2 and is called by 4, 6 (indirectly — 6 bypasses it, see its\nrow), 16's test-send, and every later PRD per FR-6's stated intent. 5\n(Templates) feeds 6 and 8. 6 edits an existing file and depends on 5. 7\nfeeds 8. 8 (`dispatchEmails`) depends on 1, 5 (indirectly via rows already\nrendered), 7, 9, and is called only by 10. 11 depends on 1, 2 and feeds 13,\n14. 12 is a calling convention, not a buildable unit — it gates 11, 13, 14,\n15, 16's non-ADMIN-already-real routes. 17 wraps 3/8/11/15/16 behind routes.\n18–20 are independent leaf tasks. 21 wraps all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**`notify()` call (FR-3/4/5/6, NFR-2, NFR-5):**\n1. Caller (any service, after its own transaction commits) invokes\n   `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`. Component 3\n   validates `link` is `/`-prefixed if present (NFR-5) — throws\n   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', ...)` only for this programmer-error case;\n   every other failure mode (missing user, send failure) is logged, not\n   thrown.\n2. Filters `userIds` to non-archived, non-disabled users in one query, then\n   reads each remaining user's `NotificationPreference` row for `type`\n   (one query, `findMany` with `in`), falling back to Component 2's\n   registry defaults (`defaultEmail`, `mandatoryInApp`) where no row exists.\n3. One `createMany` writes all qualifying `Notification` rows (in-app\n   enabled OR `mandatoryInApp`); one `createMany` writes all qualifying\n   `EmailOutbox` rows (email enabled AND user has an email) — ≤3 round\n   trips total per FR-5, holding NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/<2s budget.\n4. `notifyStudentAndParents` (Component 4) is a pre-step: resolve\n   `studentIds` → student + linked-parent ids via `ParentStudentLink`\n   (existing table), dedupe, then run steps 1-3 once over the combined list.\n\n**Email dispatch (FR-10/11/12, NFR-4):**\n1. Either driver (Component 10) calls `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })`.\n2. Top of the call: `UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='PENDING' WHERE\n   status='SENDING' AND updatedAt-equivalent < now()-10min` (recovers\n   crashed-mid-send rows, NFR-4) — tracked via `nextAttemptAt`/a dedicated\n   timestamp set when flipped to `SENDING`.\n3. One `prisma.$transaction` runs `SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE\n   status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now() ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\"\n   LIMIT $batchSize FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then `UPDATE ... SET\n   status='SENDING'` on exactly those ids — this is the only raw SQL in the\n   codebase, isolated to this function (no double-send across concurrent\n   dispatchers, NFR-4).\n4. Outside the lock: each claimed row renders through Component 7's\n   transport. Success → `status='SENT', sentAt=now()`. Failure → bump\n   `attempts`; if `attempts < 5`, `status='PENDING'` with `nextAttemptAt`\n   set per the 1/5/15/60/240-minute schedule (FR-11); at `attempts === 5`,\n   `status='FAILED'`.\n5. Once per calendar day (in-memory last-run check): call Component 9's\n   `purgeOldNotifications()`.\n\n**Auth email (FR-9):**\n1. PRD-03 call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, \"send invitation now\"\n   checkbox) call `sendInvite(userId)` exactly as before — signature\n   unchanged.\n2. Internally it now renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset`\n   template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (no preference gate\n   — auth emails are mandatory), then returns the same `{ id,\n   inviteSentAt }` shape the stub always returned.\n\n**Bell + popover (FR-14/15):**\n1. `useUnreadCount()` polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s\n   while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`; a `visibilitychange`\n   listener clears/restarts the interval.\n2. Popover open → one call to Component 11's `listNotifications` capped at\n   10 rows, newest first. Item click → `POST /api/notifications/:id/read`\n   then client-side navigate to `link`.\n\n**Preferences (FR-18/19/22):**\n1. Page load merges Component 2's registry (filtered to the signed-in\n   user's role) with the user's existing `NotificationPreference` rows\n   (defaults where absent).\n2. Switch toggle → optimistic local state update + `PUT\n   /api/me/notification-preferences` with `{type, inApp, email}`; server\n   rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types before any write\n   (`VALIDATION_ERROR`); a non-2xx response rolls the toggle back\n   client-side.\n\n**Admin email log (FR-20):** pure read/action surface over `EmailOutbox`\n(Component 1) — \"Retry now\" is a plain update (`attempts=0,\nstatus=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`), picked up by the next\n`dispatchEmails()` pass (step 3 above), not a separate send path. \"Send\ntest\" is a direct call into Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'`.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enum |\n| FR-2 | Component 2 — type registry |\n| FR-3 | Component 2 (compile-time union) + Component 3 (`notify()` signature) |\n| FR-4 | Component 3 — core `notify()` logic |\n| FR-5 | Component 3 — `createMany` batching + never-throw contract |\n| FR-6 | Component 4 — `notifyStudentAndParents` |\n| FR-7 | Component 5 — base layout + HTML/text render |\n| FR-8 | Component 5 — invite/password-reset/generic templates |\n| FR-9 | Component 6 — `sendAuthEmail()` swap, signature preserved |\n| FR-10 | Component 8 — `dispatchEmails()` claim/send/update |\n| FR-11 | Component 8 — retry backoff schedule |\n| FR-12 | Component 10 — HTTP route + worker script, one shared function |\n| FR-13 | Component 7 — transport + env vars |\n| FR-14 | Component 13 — bell poll/pause |\n| FR-15 | Component 13 — popover list (via Component 11) |\n| FR-16 | Component 14 — `/notifications` page (via Component 11) |\n| FR-17 | Component 9 — purge, triggered from Component 8 |\n| FR-18 | Component 15 — preferences table UI |\n| FR-19 | Component 15 — optimistic PUT |\n| FR-20 | Component 16 — admin email log |\n| FR-21 | Component 17 — full REST surface |\n| FR-22 | Component 15 — server-side mandatory-type rejection |\n| FR-23 | Component 18 — nav entries (MEDIUM confidence resolved: flat entries, not a new group) |\n| FR-24 | Component 20 — seed rows |\n| NFR-1 | Component 19 — MUI-only, directory-scoped ESLint exemption |\n| NFR-2 | Component 3 — ≤3-round-trip batching |\n| NFR-3 | Component 1 (index) + Component 11 (`getUnreadCount` query shape) |\n| NFR-4 | Component 8 — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` + stuck-row recovery |\n| NFR-5 | Component 3 (`link` validation) + Component 5 (template escaping) |\n| NFR-6 | Component 5 (HTML+text render) + Component 7 (`List-Unsubscribe` header) |\n| NFR-7 | Component 12 — `requireRole` placeholder standing in for `requireUser` (sequencing dependency, see Overview) + Component 15/16's ADMIN/own-row checks |\n| NFR-8 | Component 10 — `CRON_SECRET` bearer check, 401 on mismatch |\n| NFR-9 | Component 21 — test harness |\n| NFR-10 | All components — no SMS/push/websockets/digests introduced |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 24 FR ids and 10 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\ndropped. FR-23's MEDIUM-confidence nav question is resolved (flat entries\nunder existing roles-based filtering, no new nav group introduced since\n`navigation.ts` has none today). Two things carry forward for\n`arch-api-contracts` and `dev-planning`:\n\n1. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 12):** `src/server/auth/\n   permissions.ts`'s `requireUser()` does not exist in `src/` yet — only\n   `requireRole.ts`'s ADMIN-placeholder and `student-access.ts` do. This\n   design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` everywhere a real `requireUser()`\n   would go on user-facing notification/preferences routes, so the later\n   swap to PRD-01's real session-aware helper is confined to that one file\n   plus each route's import line — not a redesign. ADMIN-only and\n   `CRON_SECRET`-gated routes need no placeholder; they already have a real\n   check today.\n2. **Ready for `arch-api-contracts`:** the 12-endpoint API table in\n   `04-notifications.md` is fully specified (methods, paths, roles, notes)\n   and maps 1:1 onto Components 3/8/11/15/16 above — no net-new business\n   logic to invent at the route layer, only envelope/pagination/error-code\n   wiring per `src/server/http.ts`'s existing conventions.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":255,"newStart":1,"newLines":226,"lines":["-# System Design — ticket abcd-03 (PRD-03 User Management)","+# System Design — ticket abcd-04 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email)"," "," Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete"," "," ## Overview"," ","-PRD-03 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation) and PRD-02 (academic","-structure), both of which are actually built in `src/`. Intake reports","-**97% confidence and zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`), and","-only one requirement (FR-31, unlock) carries MEDIUM confidence — both","-carried forward unchanged below.","+PRD-04 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-01 (auth/RBAC,","+design-only — not landed), PRD-02 (academic structure) and PRD-03 (user","+management). Intake reports **97% confidence and zero blockers**","+(`handoff-to-architect.json`); the one MEDIUM-confidence item (FR-23, exact","+nav entries) is resolved below rather than carried forward as a gap."," "," **Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes","-the design:** `requirements.json` and the source PRD (`03-user-management.md`)","-both write FR-7, FR-12, FR-31 and NFR-7 as if PRD-01 (auth/RBAC) already","-exists to be \"reused\" or \"extended\". Reading the actual codebase shows it","-does not — `src/server/auth/` contains only `requireRole.ts`, whose own","-doc comment states plainly: *\"PRD-01 (real auth/session) has not landed in","-this workspace yet... returns the same ADMIN placeholder identity","-AppShell renders.\"* There is no `authorize()`, no `middleware.ts`, no","-`src/server/services/users.ts`, no `sendInvite`/`sendAuthEmail`, no login","-page, and the seed script creates no users. The `User`/`AuthToken`/","-`AuditLog` Prisma models and the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/","-`passwordChangedAt` columns *do* exist in `prisma/schema.prisma` (PRD-01's","-migration landed), and `src/server/audit.ts`'s `audit()` helper is real","-and working — only the service/route/session layer is missing.","+the design — the same PRD-01 sequencing gap PRD-03's system-design.md","+already flagged:** every source PRD, including this one, documents","+`src/server/auth/permissions.ts` exporting `requireUser()` and","+`requireRole()`. That file does not exist. `src/server/auth/` contains only","+`requireRole.ts` — a placeholder that returns a hardcoded ADMIN identity and","+checks role — and `student-access.ts`. There is no `requireUser()`","+anywhere in `src/`. NFR-7 requires \"own-notifications-only\" checks on every","+user-facing route (`GET /api/notifications`, read/unread, preferences),","+which needs a resolved *user identity*, not just a role gate. Since PRD-01","+has not landed, this design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — the same","+placeholder `requireRole.ts` already exports, called with every role —","+everywhere a real `requireUser()` would go, documented inline as a","+sequencing dependency (Component 12 below) exactly as PRD-03's Component 20","+did for `sendInvite`. No new auth module is built here (that is PRD-01's","+job); call sites are written so swapping the placeholder for the real","+`requireUser()` later is a one-file change, not a per-route rewrite."," ","-This does **not** block `arch-design-system` from producing a design — it","-changes what the design must say: PRD-03's auth-adjacent requirements are","-designed against the *interfaces PRD-01's own design doc already commits","-to* (`src/server/services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)`, `src/server/","-auth/permissions.ts`'s `requireRole`), on the assumption PRD-01 lands","-first. `requireRole.ts`'s placeholder is itself built to absorb that swap","-with zero call-site changes, so PRD-03 calls it exactly as it will call","-the real thing later. Flagged explicitly in the Requirements Traceability","-table below (FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7) and restated for `dev-planning` in","-the Status section — this is a sequencing dependency, not a design defect.","+Second brownfield fact confirmed directly in source: `src/server/services/","+users.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)` (lines ~385-390) is a logging-only stub","+returning `{ id, inviteSentAt }`. FR-9 replaces its *body* with a real","+`sendAuthEmail()` call while preserving that exact signature, so PRD-03's","+call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, the create-user \"send invitation\"","+checkbox) do not change."," "," No new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`","-(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, papaparse client-side only,","-synchronous per-batch transactions, one shared CSV-escaping util, MUI-only","-UI, additive schema with one new index, shared Zod schemas, reuse of","-PRD-01's session/lockout plumbing (per the finding above), static CSV","-templates. This document arranges those choices into components, data","-flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability, per NFR-7/NFR-8's brownfield-and-scope","-discipline.","+(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, Nodemailer + console transport,","+`@react-email/components` for templates (the one explicit exemption from","+the MUI-only rule — scoped to `src/server/email/templates/**`), raw","+`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for dispatch (no queue library), one dispatch","+function behind two thin drivers (HTTP route + loop script), a compile-time","+type registry (no DB table), in-memory scheduling for both the stuck-row","+recovery and the daily purge. This document arranges those choices into","+components, data flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability."," ","-Three chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed","+Two chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed"," below as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route","-code: the **user list/filter query** (FR-2/3/11, NFR-2), the **CSV import","-transaction** (FR-18–23, NFR-3), and **`student-access.ts`** (FR-17, NFR-1).","-A fourth cross-cutting rule, **CSV-escaping + medicalNotes redaction**","-(NFR-1/NFR-4), is designed as one shared helper applied at every","-export/read boundary rather than per-endpoint logic.","+code: **`notify()`** (FR-3/4/5/6) and **`dispatchEmails()`** (FR-10/11).","+One list/read service backs both the bell popover (FR-15) and the","+`/notifications` page (FR-16) — not two query paths. FR-23's nav entries","+are resolved here (Component 11) rather than left open."," "," ## Component Breakdown"," "," | # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |"," |---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|","-| 1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`; one composite index `User(lastName, firstName, email)` | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-2 |","-| 2 | User Service Layer | `createUser`, `updateUser`, `setUserStatus`, `archiveUser`/`restoreUser`, `unlockUser`, admission-number/employee-number generators (`S<year>-####` / `T-####`), last-active-admin guard, self-disable/self-archive guard | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-3..FR-5, FR-9, FR-10, FR-14, FR-31 |","-| 3 | List/Filter Query | `GET /api/users` query builder: role/status/gradeLevelId/q/includeArchived filters, search across name/email/admissionNumber/employeeNumber, server-side pagination via `src/server/http.ts`'s `parsePagination`, ordered to use the new index | `src/app/api/users/route.ts`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (`listUsers`) | FR-2, FR-3, NFR-2 |","-| 4 | User Detail Composition | `GET /api/users/:id` assembling profile + status + lastLoginAt + family links (component 6) + 20 most recent `AuditLog` rows where `actorId = id OR entityId = id` | `src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts` | FR-11 |","-| 5 | Create/Edit Form Flow | MUI `Stepper` (role select → common + role-specific fields), inline parent/student linking, \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox, email-change confirm dialog (reuses `ConfirmDialog`), read-only role on edit, shared Zod schemas from component 11 as the RHF resolver | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/new/page.tsx`, `.../[id]/edit/page.tsx` | FR-6, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10 |","-| 6 | Family Linking Service | `linkParentToStudent`/`unlinkParentFromStudent` — max-4-parents check, single-`isPrimary` invariant (set-one-clears-others) inside one transaction; called from student form, parent form, and the student-detail Family card | `src/server/services/userLinks.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |","-| 7 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` (ADMIN→`\"ALL\"`, STUDENT→`[user.id]`, PARENT→linked ids via component 6's link table, TEACHER→`[]` until PRD-05), `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` (FORBIDDEN/NOT_FOUND) | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-17, FR-25, NFR-1 |","-| 8 | CSV Import — Client | Template download links (component 9), 2 MB/2,000-row cap enforced before upload, papaparse parse into a preview `DataGrid` with per-row Valid/Warning/Error + per-cell reason | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/import/page.tsx` | FR-18, FR-19 |","-| 9 | CSV Import — Server Transaction | `POST /api/users/import`: re-validates every row against component 11's Zod schemas (never trusts the client), batches of 200, one `prisma.$transaction` per batch (all-or-rollback, NFR-3), case-insensitive grade-level match by `name`/`shortName`, strict `YYYY-MM-DD` dates, existing-email rows → \"Skipped — already exists\", summary + error-report CSV via component 10 | `src/app/api/users/import/route.ts`, `src/server/services/userImport.ts`, `public/templates/students-template.csv`, `public/templates/teachers-template.csv` | FR-18, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-3 |","-| 10 | CSV Export/Escaping Util | `escapeCsvCell()` (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) and `toCsv()` used by bulk \"Export CSV\" (`GET /api/users/export`), the import error report, and nowhere else is CSV built ad hoc; also strips `medicalNotes` from every export row | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-5 (export), FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-4 |","-| 11 | Shared Validators | One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row): DOB 3–21yo, phone `^\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$`, used as the RHF resolver (component 5) and the CSV row validator (components 8 & 9) — single source of truth | `src/lib/validators/users.ts` | FR-10, FR-19, FR-20 |","-| 12 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header (avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status) + \"Overview\" tab registered in the existing tab registry (profile, family via component 6, emergency contact; `medicalNotes` gated to ADMIN/TEACHER, enforced server-side by component 7/13, not just hidden in the UI) | `src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/page.tsx`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (extend existing empty array) | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-1 |","-| 13 | Student Detail API | `GET /api/students/:id`: gated by `assertCanViewStudent` (component 7), strips `medicalNotes` for STUDENT/PARENT in the service layer (not the client) | `src/app/api/students/[id]/route.ts` | FR-24, NFR-1 |","-| 14 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): cards (name, grade level, admission number) from `GET /api/me/children`, linking to component 12; empty state via existing `EmptyState` component | `src/app/(app)/my-children/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/children/route.ts` | FR-26 |","-| 15 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: read-only name/email/role, editable phone (+occupation/address for PARENT) via `PATCH /api/me/profile` — a narrower mutation path, deliberately not routed through component 2's admin service | `src/app/(app)/account/profile/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/profile/route.ts` | FR-27 |","-| 16 | Directory Picker API + Component | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived, ≤20 results, `{id,name,email,role}`); reusable `UserPicker` on MUI `Autocomplete` (async, `multiple`, avatar+name+role `renderOption`) | `src/app/api/users/search/route.ts`, `src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx` | FR-28 |","-| 17 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table (time, actor, action, entityType, entityId linked when a user, IP) + filters (actor, action prefix, date range) + right-anchored `Drawer` with pretty-printed metadata JSON on row click; reads the existing `AuditLog` table, no new write path | `src/app/(app)/admin/audit-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/audit-logs/route.ts` | FR-29 |","-| 18 | Navigation | New entries: Administration→Users/Import users/Audit log, Parent→\"My children\", user menu→\"Profile\" | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-30 |","-| 19 | Admin Row/Bulk Actions UI | View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore row actions + Resend/Disable/Export-CSV bulk actions on `DataTable`'s selection — thin dispatch onto components 2/9/10's service calls, confirmed via `ConfirmDialog` for destructive ones | reuses `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `src/components/ConfirmDialog/ConfirmDialog.tsx` | FR-4, FR-5 |","-| 20 | Auth/Session Touchpoints (sequencing dependency) | FR-7's `sendInvite(userId)`, FR-12's session-status re-check, FR-31's lockout-field clear — all called through the stable interfaces PRD-01's own design doc defines (`src/server/services/users.ts`, `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`) rather than re-implemented here (NFR-7); see Overview finding | *(PRD-01, not yet landed)* | FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7 |","-| 21 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only; reuses `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `UserAvatar`, `EmptyState`, `FormField`, `PageHeader`, `Toast` | reuses `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-5 |","-| 22 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, `escapeCsvCell`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import-batch rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children→student page) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |","+| 1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum, exactly per the schema block in `04-notifications.md` FR-1 (composite index `Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt)`, `EmailOutbox(status, nextAttemptAt)`) | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-3, NFR-4 |","+| 2 | Notification Type Registry | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const object (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles) across ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM; seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`; `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is `notify()`'s type parameter so unknown keys are a compile error (FR-3) | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-2, FR-3 |","+| 3 | Notification Service (`notify()`) | `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`: filters out archived/disabled users, resolves per-user `NotificationPreference` (falling back to registry defaults), `createMany` for `Notification` rows where in-app applies (including when `mandatoryInApp` overrides an off preference), `createMany` for `EmailOutbox` rows where email applies and the user has an email; never throws — failures logged via `logger`, caller's own transaction already committed by the time this runs; `link` values validated as `/`-prefixed relative paths before write (NFR-5) | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-5 |","+| 4 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })`: expands each student id to itself + linked parent ids via the existing `ParentStudentLink` table (PRD-03's model, read-only here), dedupes, calls Component 3 once with the combined id list — no new link model | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` (co-located, thin wrapper) | FR-6 |","+| 5 | Email Templates | `BaseLayout` (logo/name header, content slot, footer with school address + \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` + required disclosure sentence) plus `invite`, `password-reset`, `generic-notification` templates, each rendered via `@react-email/render`'s `render()` for HTML and `render(..., { plainText: true })` for text — one render call backs both `EmailOutbox.html`/`.text` columns so the two parts can't drift; all interpolated user text passes through React Email's escaping (NFR-5's HTML-escape rule) | `src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx`, `invite.tsx`, `password-reset.tsx`, `generic-notification.tsx` | FR-7, FR-8, NFR-5, NFR-6 |","+| 6 | Auth Email Integration | `sendAuthEmail()` replaces the body of the existing `sendInvite()` stub in `src/server/services/users.ts` (same exported signature `(userId) => Promise<{ id, inviteSentAt }>`, so PRD-03's call sites are untouched): looks up the user, renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset` template, inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (bypasses Component 3 — auth emails are not user-preference-gated), returns the existing shape | `src/server/services/users.ts` (edit, not new file) | FR-9 |","+| 7 | Email Transport | One module building either a real SMTP `nodemailer.createTransport` or a `console` transport (logs subject/recipient/text) from `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (default `console` in dev), reading `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`; sets the `List-Unsubscribe` header on every send pointing at `/account/notifications` (NFR-6) | `src/server/email/transport.ts`, env vars in `.env.example` | FR-13, NFR-6 |","+| 8 | Email Dispatcher (`dispatchEmails()`) | One function: (a) recovers rows stuck in `SENDING` >10 min back to `PENDING` (NFR-4), (b) `prisma.$transaction` containing `$queryRaw SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim up to `batchSize` (default 50) `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now`, flips them to `SENDING`; (c) outside the lock, sends each via Component 7's transport, marks `SENT`/`sentAt` on success or applies the FR-11 backoff (1/5/15/60/240 min across attempts 1-5, `FAILED` after the 5th) on failure; also runs Component 9's purge once per calendar day via an in-memory last-run timestamp checked at the top of each call | `src/server/email/dispatcher.ts` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-4 |","+| 9 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()`: deletes `Notification` rows with `createdAt` older than 180 days; a plain function called from Component 8's daily check, not a separate cron/queue | `src/server/notifications/purge.ts` | FR-17 |","+| 10 | Dispatch Drivers | Two thin callers of Component 8: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET` check, 401 via standard error envelope on mismatch — NFR-8) returning `{ sent, failed, retried }`; and `npm run worker:email`, a `tsx`-run Node script looping Component 8 every 15s (matches the existing `db:seed` script pattern) | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `scripts/worker-email.ts` | FR-12, NFR-8 |","+| 11 | Notification List/Read Service | One query module: `listNotifications({ userId, unread?, category?, page, pageSize })` (own-rows-only, joins registry metadata for category/label), `getUnreadCount(userId)` (indexed by Component 1's composite index, NFR-3's <50ms budget), `markRead(userId, id)` / `markUnread` / `markAllRead(userId)` — the single implementation backing both the popover (FR-15) and the `/notifications` page (FR-16) | `src/server/notifications/list.ts` | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-3 |","+| 12 | Auth Touchpoint (sequencing dependency) | Every user-facing notification/preferences route calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` where a real `requireUser()` is specified — see Overview finding. `ADMIN`-only routes (email-log, test-send) call `requireRole('ADMIN')` directly, already real today. The internal dispatch route uses its own `CRON_SECRET` bearer check (Component 10), not this helper. One-file swap when PRD-01's real `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` lands | *(calls into existing `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`; no new file)* | NFR-7 |","+| 13 | Bell/Popover UI | Replaces the static `Badge badgeContent={0}` in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (~line 141) with a live MUI `IconButton` + `Badge` driven by a shared `useUnreadCount()` hook (`fetch` + `setInterval(30_000)`, paused on `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'` via a `visibilitychange` listener, \"9+\" cap above 9); clicking opens an MUI `Popover` with a `List` of the 10 most recent notifications from Component 11 (unread bold + dot, 2-line-clamped body, relative time), click marks read + navigates to `link`; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\" | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (edit), `src/hooks/useUnreadCount.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` | FR-14, FR-15 |","+| 14 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page) `DataTable`-less simple MUI `List`/`Table` over Component 11, All/Unread `Tabs`, category filter, bulk \"Mark all as read\", per-row read/unread toggle | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` | FR-16 |","+| 15 | Preferences UI + API | `/account/notifications`: MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader` rows) over Component 2's registry filtered to the current user's role, each row an In-app `Switch` + Email `Switch` (mandatory-in-app types render a disabled `Switch` + `Tooltip` \"Required by the school\"); `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves one `{type, inApp, email}` row immediately, client does optimistic update with rollback on a non-2xx response; server rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types with `VALIDATION_ERROR` (defense in depth alongside the disabled switch) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` | FR-18, FR-19, FR-22, NFR-7 |","+| 16 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table over `EmailOutbox` (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), status filter, \"Retry now\" row action (`attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now` — same reset shape Component 8 expects on its next pass), \"Send test notification to me\" button calling Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'` for the current admin | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts`, `.../email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` | FR-20 |","+| 17 | REST API Surface | All 12 endpoints from the PRD's API table, built on `src/server/http.ts`'s existing `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError`/`AppError` conventions — finalized verbatim in `api-contracts.json` by `arch-api-contracts` | `src/app/api/notifications/**`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/**`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/**`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/**`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/**` | FR-21 |","+| 18 | Navigation | Resolves FR-23 (MEDIUM confidence in intake): add \"Notifications\" (`/notifications`, all roles) under the existing top-level entries, and \"Email log\" (`/admin/email-log`, ADMIN only) grouped with other admin-only entries — following the existing flat `NavItem[]` + `roles` convention (no \"Administration\" group exists yet in `navigation.ts`; PRD-02/03's group ideas are a later PRD's concern, not introduced here) | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-23 |","+| 19 | Design System (MUI-only, directory-scoped) | Every app-UI surface (bell, popover, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only, looked up via the MUI MCP server; `src/server/email/templates/**` is the one ESLint `no-restricted-imports` exemption glob so `@react-email/components` imports there aren't flagged, while every other path stays MUI-only | ESLint config (exemption glob addition), reuses existing `theme.ts` | NFR-1 |","+| 20 | Seed Data | 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`, linking to `/dashboard` — depends on Component 1's schema and Component 2's registry key existing first | `prisma/seed.ts` (extend existing script) | FR-24 |","+| 21 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (registry compile-time key rejection via a type-level test, retry-backoff schedule math, link-path validator, CSV-free here — N/A); Vitest integration (`notify()` batching round-trip count, `dispatchEmails()` claim-and-send with concurrent-dispatcher race, stuck-row recovery, mandatory-preference server rejection); Playwright e2e (bell unread count updates after `notify()`, mark-all-read, preferences toggle persists, admin retry-now, admin test-send) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-9 |"," ","-Dependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (User Service)","-depends on 1 and is called by 3, 4, 5, 9, 19. 6 (Family Linking) depends on","-1 and feeds 4, 5, 12, 14. 7 (Access Control Helper) depends on 6 and gates","-12, 13, 14. 8→9 is one pipeline; 9 depends on 2, 6, 11 and feeds 10's","-error-report path. 16 depends on 2. 17 depends only on the existing","-`AuditLog` table. 20 is the one component this PRD does not build —","-everything that calls into it (5, 2, 19) must tolerate it landing late or","-being stubbed, per the Overview finding. 21–22 wrap all of the above.","+Dependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (Registry) depends","+on 1's `type: String` column and feeds 3, 4, 11, 15, 16. 3 (`notify()`)","+depends on 1, 2 and is called by 4, 6 (indirectly — 6 bypasses it, see its","+row), 16's test-send, and every later PRD per FR-6's stated intent. 5","+(Templates) feeds 6 and 8. 6 edits an existing file and depends on 5. 7","+feeds 8. 8 (`dispatchEmails`) depends on 1, 5 (indirectly via rows already","+rendered), 7, 9, and is called only by 10. 11 depends on 1, 2 and feeds 13,","+14. 12 is a calling convention, not a buildable unit — it gates 11, 13, 14,","+15, 16's non-ADMIN-already-real routes. 17 wraps 3/8/11/15/16 behind routes.","+18–20 are independent leaf tasks. 21 wraps all of the above."," "," ## Data Flow"," ","-**User list, `GET /api/users` (FR-2/3, NFR-2):**","-1. `parseQuery` (existing `src/server/http.ts` helper) validates","-   `role`/`status`/`gradeLevelId`/`q`/`includeArchived`/pagination params.","-2. Component 3 builds one Prisma query: `status != ARCHIVED` unless","-   `includeArchived`, `q` matched against name/email/admissionNumber/","-   employeeNumber, ordered/filtered to use the `(lastName, firstName,","-   email)` index (component 1) so the 5,000-row/<300ms budget (NFR-2) holds","-   without client-side filtering.","-3. `paginated()` (existing `http.ts` helper) returns rows + meta; the","-   `DataTable` (component 19/21) reads page/pageSize/sort from the URL, not","-   local state, matching its existing contract.","+**`notify()` call (FR-3/4/5/6, NFR-2, NFR-5):**","+1. Caller (any service, after its own transaction commits) invokes","+   `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`. Component 3","+   validates `link` is `/`-prefixed if present (NFR-5) — throws","+   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', ...)` only for this programmer-error case;","+   every other failure mode (missing user, send failure) is logged, not","+   thrown.","+2. Filters `userIds` to non-archived, non-disabled users in one query, then","+   reads each remaining user's `NotificationPreference` row for `type`","+   (one query, `findMany` with `in`), falling back to Component 2's","+   registry defaults (`defaultEmail`, `mandatoryInApp`) where no row exists.","+3. One `createMany` writes all qualifying `Notification` rows (in-app","+   enabled OR `mandatoryInApp`); one `createMany` writes all qualifying","+   `EmailOutbox` rows (email enabled AND user has an email) — ≤3 round","+   trips total per FR-5, holding NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/<2s budget.","+4. `notifyStudentAndParents` (Component 4) is a pre-step: resolve","+   `studentIds` → student + linked-parent ids via `ParentStudentLink`","+   (existing table), dedupe, then run steps 1-3 once over the combined list."," ","-**Create user, `POST /api/users` (FR-6/7/8/9/10):**","-1. Component 11's Zod schema (role-specific) validates the Stepper's step-2","-   payload server-side (never trust the client-validated form alone).","-2. Component 2's `createUser` generates `admissionNumber`/`employeeNumber`","-   where applicable, creates the `User` + profile row + any inline","-   parent/student links (component 6) in one transaction.","-3. If \"Send invitation email now\" is checked, calls component 20's","-   `sendInvite(userId)` — see Overview finding: this call is wired to the","-   interface PRD-01 commits to, and is a no-op/stub until that interface is","-   real.","-4. `audit('user.created', ...)` via the existing `src/server/audit.ts`.","+**Email dispatch (FR-10/11/12, NFR-4):**","+1. Either driver (Component 10) calls `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })`.","+2. Top of the call: `UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='PENDING' WHERE","+   status='SENDING' AND updatedAt-equivalent < now()-10min` (recovers","+   crashed-mid-send rows, NFR-4) — tracked via `nextAttemptAt`/a dedicated","+   timestamp set when flipped to `SENDING`.","+3. One `prisma.$transaction` runs `SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE","+   status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now() ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\"","+   LIMIT $batchSize FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then `UPDATE ... SET","+   status='SENDING'` on exactly those ids — this is the only raw SQL in the","+   codebase, isolated to this function (no double-send across concurrent","+   dispatchers, NFR-4).","+4. Outside the lock: each claimed row renders through Component 7's","+   transport. Success → `status='SENT', sentAt=now()`. Failure → bump","+   `attempts`; if `attempts < 5`, `status='PENDING'` with `nextAttemptAt`","+   set per the 1/5/15/60/240-minute schedule (FR-11); at `attempts === 5`,","+   `status='FAILED'`.","+5. Once per calendar day (in-memory last-run check): call Component 9's","+   `purgeOldNotifications()`."," ","-**Edit user / email change (FR-8/9):**","-1. Role is rejected server-side if present and different from the existing","-   row (not just hidden in the UI) — a service-layer invariant, not a form","-   convenience.","-2. An email diff triggers `ConfirmDialog` client-side; on confirm, the PATCH","-   handler updates the email and invalidates (marks used/expired) any","-   pending `AuthToken` rows of type INVITE for that user, so a stale invite","-   link can't activate the old address.","+**Auth email (FR-9):**","+1. PRD-03 call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, \"send invitation now\"","+   checkbox) call `sendInvite(userId)` exactly as before — signature","+   unchanged.","+2. Internally it now renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset`","+   template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (no preference gate","+   — auth emails are mandatory), then returns the same `{ id,","+   inviteSentAt }` shape the stub always returned."," ","-**Status changes (FR-12/13/14):**","-1. `setUserStatus`/`archiveUser` (component 2) check: not self, and —if","-   disabling an ADMIN— that at least one other ACTIVE ADMIN remains, else","-   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'At least one active admin is required.')`.","-2. Disable sets `status=DISABLED`; archive additionally sets","-   `archivedAt=now`. Both are pure data writes today; the \"stops working","-   within 5 minutes\" session-level effect (FR-12) is PRD-01's session check","-   re-reading `status` on its token-refresh interval — this PRD does not","-   and should not build that check (NFR-7), it only guarantees `status` is","-   correct the instant the mutation commits.","-3. Every list/picker query (components 3, 16) and `getAccessibleStudentIds`","-   (component 7) excludes `ARCHIVED` users by default, so archival's","-   app-wide picker exclusion (FR-13) is enforced once, at the query layer,","-   not per-caller.","+**Bell + popover (FR-14/15):**","+1. `useUnreadCount()` polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s","+   while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`; a `visibilitychange`","+   listener clears/restarts the interval.","+2. Popover open → one call to Component 11's `listNotifications` capped at","+   10 rows, newest first. Item click → `POST /api/notifications/:id/read`","+   then client-side navigate to `link`."," ","-**Family linking (FR-15/16):**","-1. `linkParentToStudent` runs inside one transaction: count existing links","-   for the student (reject the 5th with `VALIDATION_ERROR`), and if the new","-   link is `isPrimary`, clear `isPrimary` on every other link for that","-   student first, then insert.","-2. Reachable from three entry points (student form, parent form, student","-   detail \"Family\" card) that all call this one function — no duplicated","-   invariant logic.","+**Preferences (FR-18/19/22):**","+1. Page load merges Component 2's registry (filtered to the signed-in","+   user's role) with the user's existing `NotificationPreference` rows","+   (defaults where absent).","+2. Switch toggle → optimistic local state update + `PUT","+   /api/me/notification-preferences` with `{type, inApp, email}`; server","+   rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types before any write","+   (`VALIDATION_ERROR`); a non-2xx response rolls the toggle back","+   client-side."," ","-**CSV import (FR-18–23, NFR-3):**","-1. Browser: papaparse parses the uploaded file (component 8), rejecting","-   >2 MB/>2,000 rows before parsing; each row runs through component 11's","-   Zod schema plus a grade-level-name lookup for Valid/Warning/Error","-   classification with a per-cell reason, rendered in a preview `DataGrid`.","-2. \"Import N valid rows\" POSTs rows (not the file) in chunks of 200 to","-   component 9.","-3. Server re-validates every row independently of the client (NFR-3's","-   trust boundary), matches grade levels case-insensitively by `name` or","-   `shortName`, parses dates strictly as `YYYY-MM-DD`, and skips rows whose","-   email already exists (\"Skipped — already exists\", FR-23) rather than","-   erroring.","-4. Each 200-row batch runs in one `prisma.$transaction` (ADR-3): any row","-   failure that isn't a plain \"skip\" rolls back only that batch, never the","-   whole import; results aggregate into the post-import summary (component","-   10) and, for failed rows, an escaped error-report CSV.","+**Admin email log (FR-20):** pure read/action surface over `EmailOutbox`","+(Component 1) — \"Retry now\" is a plain update (`attempts=0,","+status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`), picked up by the next","+`dispatchEmails()` pass (step 3 above), not a separate send path. \"Send","+test\" is a direct call into Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'`."," ","-**Student/parent surfaces (FR-24/25/26):**","-1. `/students/[studentId]` and `/my-children` both resolve access through","-   component 7 (`assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds`) — no","-   page implements its own authorization check.","-2. `GET /api/students/:id` (component 13) strips `medicalNotes` for","-   STUDENT/PARENT roles in the service layer before the response is built,","-   so no client-side hiding can leak it (NFR-1); the same strip applies","-   inside component 10's CSV export path.","-","-**Directory picker (FR-28):** `GET /api/users/search` reuses component 3's","-underlying query (role/q filters, archived excluded) capped to 20 rows and","-projected down to `{id,name,email,role}` — no separate search index.","-","-**Audit log viewer (FR-29):** pure read over the existing `AuditLog` table","-(`src/server/audit.ts`'s schema) with actor/action-prefix/date-range","-filters and pagination; no new write path, matching NFR-7.","-"," ## Requirements Traceability"," "," | Requirement | Design Element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enums + relations |","-| FR-2 | Component 3 — `GET /api/users` list query |","-| FR-3 | Component 3 — filters (role/status/gradeLevel/search/archived) |","-| FR-4 | Component 19 — row actions dispatch |","-| FR-5 | Component 19 (UI) + Component 10 (export) — bulk actions |","-| FR-6 | Component 5 — Stepper create/edit form |","-| FR-7 | Component 5 (checkbox) + **Component 20** — `sendInvite` call (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |","-| FR-8 | Component 5 — email-change confirm + invite-token invalidation |","-| FR-9 | Component 2 + 5 — role immutability, service + form |","-| FR-10 | Component 11 — shared DOB/phone Zod schema |","-| FR-11 | Component 4 — user detail composition |","-| FR-12 | Component 2 (status write) + **Component 20** — session-level effect (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |","-| FR-13 | Component 2 — archive write; Components 3/7/16 — app-wide picker exclusion |","-| FR-14 | Component 2 — self/last-admin guard |","-| FR-15 | Component 6 — link service, 3 entry points |","-| FR-16 | Component 6 — max-4 / single-primary invariant |","-| FR-17 | Component 7 — `student-access.ts` |","-| FR-18 | Component 9 — static templates; Component 8 — download UI |","-| FR-19 | Component 8 — client parse + preview grid |","-| FR-20 | Component 9 — server re-validation + batched transactions |","-| FR-21 | Component 9 — invite toggle, grade-level matching, strict dates |","-| FR-22 | Component 9 + 10 — summary + error-report CSV |","-| FR-23 | Component 9 — existing-email skip rule |","-| FR-24 | Component 12 — student detail page + Overview tab |","-| FR-25 | Component 7 + 12 — `assertCanViewStudent` gate |","-| FR-26 | Component 14 — `/my-children` |","-| FR-27 | Component 15 — `/account/profile` |","-| FR-28 | Component 16 — search API + `UserPicker` |","-| FR-29 | Component 17 — audit log viewer |","-| FR-30 | Component 18 — navigation entries |","-| FR-31 | **Component 20** — unlock clears PRD-01's lockout fields (MEDIUM confidence, carried from intake — verify exact field names against `prisma/schema.prisma`, which already has `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`) |","-| NFR-1 | Component 7 + 13 + 10 — `medicalNotes` redaction (service layer + export) |","-| NFR-2 | Component 1 + 3 — composite index + server-side pagination |","-| NFR-3 | Component 9 — one transaction per 200-row batch |","-| NFR-4 | Component 10 — `escapeCsvCell` shared util |","-| NFR-5 | Component 21 — MUI-only, existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |","-| NFR-6 | Component 22 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |","-| NFR-7 | Component 2/6/7 (new, additive) + **Component 20** (reuse, not rebuild, PRD-01's interfaces — see Overview) |","-| NFR-8 | All components — additive only, no PRD-05 (class/section) behavior touched |","+| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enum |","+| FR-2 | Component 2 — type registry |","+| FR-3 | Component 2 (compile-time union) + Component 3 (`notify()` signature) |","+| FR-4 | Component 3 — core `notify()` logic |","+| FR-5 | Component 3 — `createMany` batching + never-throw contract |","+| FR-6 | Component 4 — `notifyStudentAndParents` |","+| FR-7 | Component 5 — base layout + HTML/text render |","+| FR-8 | Component 5 — invite/password-reset/generic templates |","+| FR-9 | Component 6 — `sendAuthEmail()` swap, signature preserved |","+| FR-10 | Component 8 — `dispatchEmails()` claim/send/update |","+| FR-11 | Component 8 — retry backoff schedule |","+| FR-12 | Component 10 — HTTP route + worker script, one shared function |","+| FR-13 | Component 7 — transport + env vars |","+| FR-14 | Component 13 — bell poll/pause |","+| FR-15 | Component 13 — popover list (via Component 11) |","+| FR-16 | Component 14 — `/notifications` page (via Component 11) |","+| FR-17 | Component 9 — purge, triggered from Component 8 |","+| FR-18 | Component 15 — preferences table UI |","+| FR-19 | Component 15 — optimistic PUT |","+| FR-20 | Component 16 — admin email log |","+| FR-21 | Component 17 — full REST surface |","+| FR-22 | Component 15 — server-side mandatory-type rejection |","+| FR-23 | Component 18 — nav entries (MEDIUM confidence resolved: flat entries, not a new group) |","+| FR-24 | Component 20 — seed rows |","+| NFR-1 | Component 19 — MUI-only, directory-scoped ESLint exemption |","+| NFR-2 | Component 3 — ≤3-round-trip batching |","+| NFR-3 | Component 1 (index) + Component 11 (`getUnreadCount` query shape) |","+| NFR-4 | Component 8 — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` + stuck-row recovery |","+| NFR-5 | Component 3 (`link` validation) + Component 5 (template escaping) |","+| NFR-6 | Component 5 (HTML+text render) + Component 7 (`List-Unsubscribe` header) |","+| NFR-7 | Component 12 — `requireRole` placeholder standing in for `requireUser` (sequencing dependency, see Overview) + Component 15/16's ADMIN/own-row checks |","+| NFR-8 | Component 10 — `CRON_SECRET` bearer check, 401 on mismatch |","+| NFR-9 | Component 21 — test harness |","+| NFR-10 | All components — no SMS/push/websockets/digests introduced |"," "," ## Status"," ","-Complete. All 31 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were","-dropped. Two things carry forward for `arch-api-contracts` and","-`dev-planning`:","+Complete. All 24 FR ids and 10 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were","+dropped. FR-23's MEDIUM-confidence nav question is resolved (flat entries","+under existing roles-based filtering, no new nav group introduced since","+`navigation.ts` has none today). Two things carry forward for","+`arch-api-contracts` and `dev-planning`:"," ","-1. **FR-31 (MEDIUM confidence):** confirm `POST /api/users/:id/unlock`","-   clears exactly `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` (both already in","-   `prisma/schema.prisma`) before finalizing the contract.","-2. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 20):** `src/server/","-   services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite`, and the session-status re-check","-   behind FR-12, do not exist in `src/` yet — only their schema","-   (`User.status`/`lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/`passwordChangedAt`,","-   `AuthToken`) and the `requireRole()` placeholder exist. This is not a","-   reason to re-implement them inside PRD-03 (NFR-7 forbids it) — it is a","-   reason `dev-planning` should either sequence PRD-01's dev work ahead of","-   PRD-03's component 20 items, or stub `sendInvite`/the status re-check","-   behind the same placeholder convention `requireRole.ts` already","-   establishes, so call sites don't change when PRD-01 lands. The source","-   API table in `03-user-management.md` is otherwise fully specified and","-   ready for `arch-api-contracts` to derive `api-contracts.json` directly","-   from (18 endpoints: `GET/POST /api/users`, `GET/PATCH /api/users/:id`,","-   `POST /api/users/:id/{invite,unlock,status,archive,restore}`, `POST","-   /api/users/import`, `GET /api/users/export`, `GET /api/users/search`,","-   `POST /api/students/:id/parents`, `DELETE /api/students/:id/parents/","-   :parentId`, `GET /api/students/:id`, `GET /api/me/children`, `PATCH","-   /api/me/profile`, `GET /api/audit-logs`).","+1. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 12):** `src/server/auth/","+   permissions.ts`'s `requireUser()` does not exist in `src/` yet — only","+   `requireRole.ts`'s ADMIN-placeholder and `student-access.ts` do. This","+   design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` everywhere a real `requireUser()`","+   would go on user-facing notification/preferences routes, so the later","+   swap to PRD-01's real session-aware helper is confined to that one file","+   plus each route's import line — not a redesign. ADMIN-only and","+   `CRON_SECRET`-gated routes need no placeholder; they already have a real","+   check today.","+2. **Ready for `arch-api-contracts`:** the 12-endpoint API table in","+   `04-notifications.md` is fully specified (methods, paths, roles, notes)","+   and maps 1:1 onto Components 3/8/11/15/16 above — no net-new business","+   logic to invent at the route layer, only envelope/pagination/error-code","+   wiring per `src/server/http.ts`'s existing conventions."]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — ticket abcd-03 (PRD-03 User Management)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-03 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation) and PRD-02 (academic\nstructure), both of which are actually built in `src/`. Intake reports\n**97% confidence and zero blockers** (`handoff-to-architect.json`), and\nonly one requirement (FR-31, unlock) carries MEDIUM confidence — both\ncarried forward unchanged below.\n\n**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\nthe design:** `requirements.json` and the source PRD (`03-user-management.md`)\nboth write FR-7, FR-12, FR-31 and NFR-7 as if PRD-01 (auth/RBAC) already\nexists to be \"reused\" or \"extended\". Reading the actual codebase shows it\ndoes not — `src/server/auth/` contains only `requireRole.ts`, whose own\ndoc comment states plainly: *\"PRD-01 (real auth/session) has not landed in\nthis workspace yet... returns the same ADMIN placeholder identity\nAppShell renders.\"* There is no `authorize()`, no `middleware.ts`, no\n`src/server/services/users.ts`, no `sendInvite`/`sendAuthEmail`, no login\npage, and the seed script creates no users. The `User`/`AuthToken`/\n`AuditLog` Prisma models and the `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/\n`passwordChangedAt` columns *do* exist in `prisma/schema.prisma` (PRD-01's\nmigration landed), and `src/server/audit.ts`'s `audit()` helper is real\nand working — only the service/route/session layer is missing.\n\nThis does **not** block `arch-design-system` from producing a design — it\nchanges what the design must say: PRD-03's auth-adjacent requirements are\ndesigned against the *interfaces PRD-01's own design doc already commits\nto* (`src/server/services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)`, `src/server/\nauth/permissions.ts`'s `requireRole`), on the assumption PRD-01 lands\nfirst. `requireRole.ts`'s placeholder is itself built to absorb that swap\nwith zero call-site changes, so PRD-03 calls it exactly as it will call\nthe real thing later. Flagged explicitly in the Requirements Traceability\ntable below (FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7) and restated for `dev-planning` in\nthe Status section — this is a sequencing dependency, not a design defect.\n\nNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, papaparse client-side only,\nsynchronous per-batch transactions, one shared CSV-escaping util, MUI-only\nUI, additive schema with one new index, shared Zod schemas, reuse of\nPRD-01's session/lockout plumbing (per the finding above), static CSV\ntemplates. This document arranges those choices into components, data\nflow, and per-FR/NFR traceability, per NFR-7/NFR-8's brownfield-and-scope\ndiscipline.\n\nThree chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\nbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\ncode: the **user list/filter query** (FR-2/3/11, NFR-2), the **CSV import\ntransaction** (FR-18–23, NFR-3), and **`student-access.ts`** (FR-17, NFR-1).\nA fourth cross-cutting rule, **CSV-escaping + medicalNotes redaction**\n(NFR-1/NFR-4), is designed as one shared helper applied at every\nexport/read boundary rather than per-endpoint logic.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | Data Model | `StudentProfile`/`TeacherProfile`/`ParentProfile`/`ParentStudentLink` + `Gender`/`GuardianRelationship` enums, relations from `User`; one composite index `User(lastName, firstName, email)` | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-2 |\n| 2 | User Service Layer | `createUser`, `updateUser`, `setUserStatus`, `archiveUser`/`restoreUser`, `unlockUser`, admission-number/employee-number generators (`S<year>-####` / `T-####`), last-active-admin guard, self-disable/self-archive guard | `src/server/services/users.ts` | FR-3..FR-5, FR-9, FR-10, FR-14, FR-31 |\n| 3 | List/Filter Query | `GET /api/users` query builder: role/status/gradeLevelId/q/includeArchived filters, search across name/email/admissionNumber/employeeNumber, server-side pagination via `src/server/http.ts`'s `parsePagination`, ordered to use the new index | `src/app/api/users/route.ts`, `src/server/services/users.ts` (`listUsers`) | FR-2, FR-3, NFR-2 |\n| 4 | User Detail Composition | `GET /api/users/:id` assembling profile + status + lastLoginAt + family links (component 6) + 20 most recent `AuditLog` rows where `actorId = id OR entityId = id` | `src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts` | FR-11 |\n| 5 | Create/Edit Form Flow | MUI `Stepper` (role select → common + role-specific fields), inline parent/student linking, \"Send invitation email now\" checkbox, email-change confirm dialog (reuses `ConfirmDialog`), read-only role on edit, shared Zod schemas from component 11 as the RHF resolver | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/new/page.tsx`, `.../[id]/edit/page.tsx` | FR-6, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10 |\n| 6 | Family Linking Service | `linkParentToStudent`/`unlinkParentFromStudent` — max-4-parents check, single-`isPrimary` invariant (set-one-clears-others) inside one transaction; called from student form, parent form, and the student-detail Family card | `src/server/services/userLinks.ts` | FR-15, FR-16 |\n| 7 | Access Control Helper | `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` (ADMIN→`\"ALL\"`, STUDENT→`[user.id]`, PARENT→linked ids via component 6's link table, TEACHER→`[]` until PRD-05), `assertCanViewStudent(user, studentId)` (FORBIDDEN/NOT_FOUND) | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-17, FR-25, NFR-1 |\n| 8 | CSV Import — Client | Template download links (component 9), 2 MB/2,000-row cap enforced before upload, papaparse parse into a preview `DataGrid` with per-row Valid/Warning/Error + per-cell reason | `src/app/(app)/admin/users/import/page.tsx` | FR-18, FR-19 |\n| 9 | CSV Import — Server Transaction | `POST /api/users/import`: re-validates every row against component 11's Zod schemas (never trusts the client), batches of 200, one `prisma.$transaction` per batch (all-or-rollback, NFR-3), case-insensitive grade-level match by `name`/`shortName`, strict `YYYY-MM-DD` dates, existing-email rows → \"Skipped — already exists\", summary + error-report CSV via component 10 | `src/app/api/users/import/route.ts`, `src/server/services/userImport.ts`, `public/templates/students-template.csv`, `public/templates/teachers-template.csv` | FR-18, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-3 |\n| 10 | CSV Export/Escaping Util | `escapeCsvCell()` (leading `=`,`+`,`-`,`@` → apostrophe-prefixed) and `toCsv()` used by bulk \"Export CSV\" (`GET /api/users/export`), the import error report, and nowhere else is CSV built ad hoc; also strips `medicalNotes` from every export row | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-5 (export), FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-4 |\n| 11 | Shared Validators | One Zod schema per entity (student/teacher/parent row): DOB 3–21yo, phone `^\\+?[0-9 ()-]{7,20}$`, used as the RHF resolver (component 5) and the CSV row validator (components 8 & 9) — single source of truth | `src/lib/validators/users.ts` | FR-10, FR-19, FR-20 |\n| 12 | Student Surface | `/students/[studentId]` header (avatar, name, admission number, grade level, status) + \"Overview\" tab registered in the existing tab registry (profile, family via component 6, emergency contact; `medicalNotes` gated to ADMIN/TEACHER, enforced server-side by component 7/13, not just hidden in the UI) | `src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/page.tsx`, `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (extend existing empty array) | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-1 |\n| 13 | Student Detail API | `GET /api/students/:id`: gated by `assertCanViewStudent` (component 7), strips `medicalNotes` for STUDENT/PARENT in the service layer (not the client) | `src/app/api/students/[id]/route.ts` | FR-24, NFR-1 |\n| 14 | Parent Surface | `/my-children` (PARENT only): cards (name, grade level, admission number) from `GET /api/me/children`, linking to component 12; empty state via existing `EmptyState` component | `src/app/(app)/my-children/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/children/route.ts` | FR-26 |\n| 15 | Self-Service Profile | `/account/profile`: read-only name/email/role, editable phone (+occupation/address for PARENT) via `PATCH /api/me/profile` — a narrower mutation path, deliberately not routed through component 2's admin service | `src/app/(app)/account/profile/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/profile/route.ts` | FR-27 |\n| 16 | Directory Picker API + Component | `GET /api/users/search?role=&q=` (ADMIN/TEACHER only, excludes archived, ≤20 results, `{id,name,email,role}`); reusable `UserPicker` on MUI `Autocomplete` (async, `multiple`, avatar+name+role `renderOption`) | `src/app/api/users/search/route.ts`, `src/components/UserPicker/UserPicker.tsx` | FR-28 |\n| 17 | Audit Log Viewer | `/admin/audit-log`: read-only table (time, actor, action, entityType, entityId linked when a user, IP) + filters (actor, action prefix, date range) + right-anchored `Drawer` with pretty-printed metadata JSON on row click; reads the existing `AuditLog` table, no new write path | `src/app/(app)/admin/audit-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/audit-logs/route.ts` | FR-29 |\n| 18 | Navigation | New entries: Administration→Users/Import users/Audit log, Parent→\"My children\", user menu→\"Profile\" | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-30 |\n| 19 | Admin Row/Bulk Actions UI | View/Edit/Resend/Unlock/Disable-Enable/Archive-Restore row actions + Resend/Disable/Export-CSV bulk actions on `DataTable`'s selection — thin dispatch onto components 2/9/10's service calls, confirmed via `ConfirmDialog` for destructive ones | reuses `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `src/components/ConfirmDialog/ConfirmDialog.tsx` | FR-4, FR-5 |\n| 20 | Auth/Session Touchpoints (sequencing dependency) | FR-7's `sendInvite(userId)`, FR-12's session-status re-check, FR-31's lockout-field clear — all called through the stable interfaces PRD-01's own design doc defines (`src/server/services/users.ts`, `src/server/auth/permissions.ts`) rather than re-implemented here (NFR-7); see Overview finding | *(PRD-01, not yet landed)* | FR-7, FR-12, FR-31, NFR-7 |\n| 21 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every new screen built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only; reuses `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `UserAvatar`, `EmptyState`, `FormField`, `PageHeader`, `Toast` | reuses `src/components/*`, `src/theme/theme.ts` | NFR-5 |\n| 22 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (CSV row validator, admission-number generator, `escapeCsvCell`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` per role); Vitest integration (import-batch rollback, last-admin guard, primary-link uniqueness); Playwright e2e (create-student-with-parent, CSV import w/ error row, parent My-children→student page) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-6 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (User Service)\ndepends on 1 and is called by 3, 4, 5, 9, 19. 6 (Family Linking) depends on\n1 and feeds 4, 5, 12, 14. 7 (Access Control Helper) depends on 6 and gates\n12, 13, 14. 8→9 is one pipeline; 9 depends on 2, 6, 11 and feeds 10's\nerror-report path. 16 depends on 2. 17 depends only on the existing\n`AuditLog` table. 20 is the one component this PRD does not build —\neverything that calls into it (5, 2, 19) must tolerate it landing late or\nbeing stubbed, per the Overview finding. 21–22 wrap all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**User list, `GET /api/users` (FR-2/3, NFR-2):**\n1. `parseQuery` (existing `src/server/http.ts` helper) validates\n   `role`/`status`/`gradeLevelId`/`q`/`includeArchived`/pagination params.\n2. Component 3 builds one Prisma query: `status != ARCHIVED` unless\n   `includeArchived`, `q` matched against name/email/admissionNumber/\n   employeeNumber, ordered/filtered to use the `(lastName, firstName,\n   email)` index (component 1) so the 5,000-row/<300ms budget (NFR-2) holds\n   without client-side filtering.\n3. `paginated()` (existing `http.ts` helper) returns rows + meta; the\n   `DataTable` (component 19/21) reads page/pageSize/sort from the URL, not\n   local state, matching its existing contract.\n\n**Create user, `POST /api/users` (FR-6/7/8/9/10):**\n1. Component 11's Zod schema (role-specific) validates the Stepper's step-2\n   payload server-side (never trust the client-validated form alone).\n2. Component 2's `createUser` generates `admissionNumber`/`employeeNumber`\n   where applicable, creates the `User` + profile row + any inline\n   parent/student links (component 6) in one transaction.\n3. If \"Send invitation email now\" is checked, calls component 20's\n   `sendInvite(userId)` — see Overview finding: this call is wired to the\n   interface PRD-01 commits to, and is a no-op/stub until that interface is\n   real.\n4. `audit('user.created', ...)` via the existing `src/server/audit.ts`.\n\n**Edit user / email change (FR-8/9):**\n1. Role is rejected server-side if present and different from the existing\n   row (not just hidden in the UI) — a service-layer invariant, not a form\n   convenience.\n2. An email diff triggers `ConfirmDialog` client-side; on confirm, the PATCH\n   handler updates the email and invalidates (marks used/expired) any\n   pending `AuthToken` rows of type INVITE for that user, so a stale invite\n   link can't activate the old address.\n\n**Status changes (FR-12/13/14):**\n1. `setUserStatus`/`archiveUser` (component 2) check: not self, and —if\n   disabling an ADMIN— that at least one other ACTIVE ADMIN remains, else\n   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', 'At least one active admin is required.')`.\n2. Disable sets `status=DISABLED`; archive additionally sets\n   `archivedAt=now`. Both are pure data writes today; the \"stops working\n   within 5 minutes\" session-level effect (FR-12) is PRD-01's session check\n   re-reading `status` on its token-refresh interval — this PRD does not\n   and should not build that check (NFR-7), it only guarantees `status` is\n   correct the instant the mutation commits.\n3. Every list/picker query (components 3, 16) and `getAccessibleStudentIds`\n   (component 7) excludes `ARCHIVED` users by default, so archival's\n   app-wide picker exclusion (FR-13) is enforced once, at the query layer,\n   not per-caller.\n\n**Family linking (FR-15/16):**\n1. `linkParentToStudent` runs inside one transaction: count existing links\n   for the student (reject the 5th with `VALIDATION_ERROR`), and if the new\n   link is `isPrimary`, clear `isPrimary` on every other link for that\n   student first, then insert.\n2. Reachable from three entry points (student form, parent form, student\n   detail \"Family\" card) that all call this one function — no duplicated\n   invariant logic.\n\n**CSV import (FR-18–23, NFR-3):**\n1. Browser: papaparse parses the uploaded file (component 8), rejecting\n   >2 MB/>2,000 rows before parsing; each row runs through component 11's\n   Zod schema plus a grade-level-name lookup for Valid/Warning/Error\n   classification with a per-cell reason, rendered in a preview `DataGrid`.\n2. \"Import N valid rows\" POSTs rows (not the file) in chunks of 200 to\n   component 9.\n3. Server re-validates every row independently of the client (NFR-3's\n   trust boundary), matches grade levels case-insensitively by `name` or\n   `shortName`, parses dates strictly as `YYYY-MM-DD`, and skips rows whose\n   email already exists (\"Skipped — already exists\", FR-23) rather than\n   erroring.\n4. Each 200-row batch runs in one `prisma.$transaction` (ADR-3): any row\n   failure that isn't a plain \"skip\" rolls back only that batch, never the\n   whole import; results aggregate into the post-import summary (component\n   10) and, for failed rows, an escaped error-report CSV.\n\n**Student/parent surfaces (FR-24/25/26):**\n1. `/students/[studentId]` and `/my-children` both resolve access through\n   component 7 (`assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds`) — no\n   page implements its own authorization check.\n2. `GET /api/students/:id` (component 13) strips `medicalNotes` for\n   STUDENT/PARENT roles in the service layer before the response is built,\n   so no client-side hiding can leak it (NFR-1); the same strip applies\n   inside component 10's CSV export path.\n\n**Directory picker (FR-28):** `GET /api/users/search` reuses component 3's\nunderlying query (role/q filters, archived excluded) capped to 20 rows and\nprojected down to `{id,name,email,role}` — no separate search index.\n\n**Audit log viewer (FR-29):** pure read over the existing `AuditLog` table\n(`src/server/audit.ts`'s schema) with actor/action-prefix/date-range\nfilters and pagination; no new write path, matching NFR-7.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enums + relations |\n| FR-2 | Component 3 — `GET /api/users` list query |\n| FR-3 | Component 3 — filters (role/status/gradeLevel/search/archived) |\n| FR-4 | Component 19 — row actions dispatch |\n| FR-5 | Component 19 (UI) + Component 10 (export) — bulk actions |\n| FR-6 | Component 5 — Stepper create/edit form |\n| FR-7 | Component 5 (checkbox) + **Component 20** — `sendInvite` call (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |\n| FR-8 | Component 5 — email-change confirm + invite-token invalidation |\n| FR-9 | Component 2 + 5 — role immutability, service + form |\n| FR-10 | Component 11 — shared DOB/phone Zod schema |\n| FR-11 | Component 4 — user detail composition |\n| FR-12 | Component 2 (status write) + **Component 20** — session-level effect (sequencing dependency, see Overview) |\n| FR-13 | Component 2 — archive write; Components 3/7/16 — app-wide picker exclusion |\n| FR-14 | Component 2 — self/last-admin guard |\n| FR-15 | Component 6 — link service, 3 entry points |\n| FR-16 | Component 6 — max-4 / single-primary invariant |\n| FR-17 | Component 7 — `student-access.ts` |\n| FR-18 | Component 9 — static templates; Component 8 — download UI |\n| FR-19 | Component 8 — client parse + preview grid |\n| FR-20 | Component 9 — server re-validation + batched transactions |\n| FR-21 | Component 9 — invite toggle, grade-level matching, strict dates |\n| FR-22 | Component 9 + 10 — summary + error-report CSV |\n| FR-23 | Component 9 — existing-email skip rule |\n| FR-24 | Component 12 — student detail page + Overview tab |\n| FR-25 | Component 7 + 12 — `assertCanViewStudent` gate |\n| FR-26 | Component 14 — `/my-children` |\n| FR-27 | Component 15 — `/account/profile` |\n| FR-28 | Component 16 — search API + `UserPicker` |\n| FR-29 | Component 17 — audit log viewer |\n| FR-30 | Component 18 — navigation entries |\n| FR-31 | **Component 20** — unlock clears PRD-01's lockout fields (MEDIUM confidence, carried from intake — verify exact field names against `prisma/schema.prisma`, which already has `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`) |\n| NFR-1 | Component 7 + 13 + 10 — `medicalNotes` redaction (service layer + export) |\n| NFR-2 | Component 1 + 3 — composite index + server-side pagination |\n| NFR-3 | Component 9 — one transaction per 200-row batch |\n| NFR-4 | Component 10 — `escapeCsvCell` shared util |\n| NFR-5 | Component 21 — MUI-only, existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` |\n| NFR-6 | Component 22 — Vitest unit/integration + Playwright e2e |\n| NFR-7 | Component 2/6/7 (new, additive) + **Component 20** (reuse, not rebuild, PRD-01's interfaces — see Overview) |\n| NFR-8 | All components — additive only, no PRD-05 (class/section) behavior touched |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 31 FR ids and 8 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\ndropped. Two things carry forward for `arch-api-contracts` and\n`dev-planning`:\n\n1. **FR-31 (MEDIUM confidence):** confirm `POST /api/users/:id/unlock`\n   clears exactly `lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount` (both already in\n   `prisma/schema.prisma`) before finalizing the contract.\n2. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 20):** `src/server/\n   services/users.ts`'s `sendInvite`, and the session-status re-check\n   behind FR-12, do not exist in `src/` yet — only their schema\n   (`User.status`/`lockedUntil`/`failedLoginCount`/`passwordChangedAt`,\n   `AuthToken`) and the `requireRole()` placeholder exist. This is not a\n   reason to re-implement them inside PRD-03 (NFR-7 forbids it) — it is a\n   reason `dev-planning` should either sequence PRD-01's dev work ahead of\n   PRD-03's component 20 items, or stub `sendInvite`/the status re-check\n   behind the same placeholder convention `requireRole.ts` already\n   establishes, so call sites don't change when PRD-01 lands. The source\n   API table in `03-user-management.md` is otherwise fully specified and\n   ready for `arch-api-contracts` to derive `api-contracts.json` directly\n   from (18 endpoints: `GET/POST /api/users`, `GET/PATCH /api/users/:id`,\n   `POST /api/users/:id/{invite,unlock,status,archive,restore}`, `POST\n   /api/users/import`, `GET /api/users/export`, `GET /api/users/search`,\n   `POST /api/students/:id/parents`, `DELETE /api/students/:id/parents/\n   :parentId`, `GET /api/students/:id`, `GET /api/me/children`, `PATCH\n   /api/me/profile`, `GET /api/audit-logs`).\n","userModified":false}}
