{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hi4i97pSFwn3fknHY8xQgo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# System Design — ticket abcd-04 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email)\n2\t\n3\tPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t## Overview\n6\t\n7\tPRD-04 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-01 (auth/RBAC,\n8\tdesign-only — not landed), PRD-02 (academic structure) and PRD-03 (user\n9\tmanagement). Intake reports **97% confidence and zero blockers**\n10\t(`handoff-to-architect.json`); the one MEDIUM-confidence item (FR-23, exact\n11\tnav entries) is resolved below rather than carried forward as a gap.\n12\t\n13\t**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\n14\tthe design — the same PRD-01 sequencing gap PRD-03's system-design.md\n15\talready flagged:** every source PRD, including this one, documents\n16\t`src/server/auth/permissions.ts` exporting `requireUser()` and\n17\t`requireRole()`. That file does not exist. `src/server/auth/` contains only\n18\t`requireRole.ts` — a placeholder that returns a hardcoded ADMIN identity and\n19\tchecks role — and `student-access.ts`. There is no `requireUser()`\n20\tanywhere in `src/`. NFR-7 requires \"own-notifications-only\" checks on every\n21\tuser-facing route (`GET /api/notifications`, read/unread, preferences),\n22\twhich needs a resolved *user identity*, not just a role gate. Since PRD-01\n23\thas not landed, this design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — the same\n24\tplaceholder `requireRole.ts` already exports, called with every role —\n25\teverywhere a real `requireUser()` would go, documented inline as a\n26\tsequencing dependency (Component 12 below) exactly as PRD-03's Component 20\n27\tdid for `sendInvite`. No new auth module is built here (that is PRD-01's\n28\tjob); call sites are written so swapping the placeholder for the real\n29\t`requireUser()` later is a one-file change, not a per-route rewrite.\n30\t\n31\tSecond brownfield fact confirmed directly in source: `src/server/services/\n32\tusers.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)` (lines ~385-390) is a logging-only stub\n33\treturning `{ id, inviteSentAt }`. FR-9 replaces its *body* with a real\n34\t`sendAuthEmail()` call while preserving that exact signature, so PRD-03's\n35\tcall sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, the create-user \"send invitation\"\n36\tcheckbox) do not change.\n37\t\n38\tNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n39\t(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, Nodemailer + console transport,\n40\t`@react-email/components` for templates (the one explicit exemption from\n41\tthe MUI-only rule — scoped to `src/server/email/templates/**`), raw\n42\t`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for dispatch (no queue library), one dispatch\n43\tfunction behind two thin drivers (HTTP route + loop script), a compile-time\n44\ttype registry (no DB table), in-memory scheduling for both the stuck-row\n45\trecovery and the daily purge. This document arranges those choices into\n46\tcomponents, data flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability.\n47\t\n48\tTwo chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\n49\tbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\n50\tcode: **`notify()`** (FR-3/4/5/6) and **`dispatchEmails()`** (FR-10/11).\n51\tOne list/read service backs both the bell popover (FR-15) and the\n52\t`/notifications` page (FR-16) — not two query paths. FR-23's nav entries\n53\tare resolved here (Component 11) rather than left open.\n54\t\n55\t## Component Breakdown\n56\t\n57\t| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n58\t|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n59\t| 1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum, exactly per the schema block in `04-notifications.md` FR-1 (composite index `Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt)`, `EmailOutbox(status, nextAttemptAt)`) | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n60\t| 2 | Notification Type Registry | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const object (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles) across ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM; seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`; `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is `notify()`'s type parameter so unknown keys are a compile error (FR-3) | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-2, FR-3 |\n61\t| 3 | Notification Service (`notify()`) | `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`: filters out archived/disabled users, resolves per-user `NotificationPreference` (falling back to registry defaults), `createMany` for `Notification` rows where in-app applies (including when `mandatoryInApp` overrides an off preference), `createMany` for `EmailOutbox` rows where email applies and the user has an email; never throws — failures logged via `logger`, caller's own transaction already committed by the time this runs; `link` values validated as `/`-prefixed relative paths before write (NFR-5) | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-5 |\n62\t| 4 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })`: expands each student id to itself + linked parent ids via the existing `ParentStudentLink` table (PRD-03's model, read-only here), dedupes, calls Component 3 once with the combined id list — no new link model | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` (co-located, thin wrapper) | FR-6 |\n63\t| 5 | Email Templates | `BaseLayout` (logo/name header, content slot, footer with school address + \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` + required disclosure sentence) plus `invite`, `password-reset`, `generic-notification` templates, each rendered via `@react-email/render`'s `render()` for HTML and `render(..., { plainText: true })` for text — one render call backs both `EmailOutbox.html`/`.text` columns so the two parts can't drift; all interpolated user text passes through React Email's escaping (NFR-5's HTML-escape rule) | `src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx`, `invite.tsx`, `password-reset.tsx`, `generic-notification.tsx` | FR-7, FR-8, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n64\t| 6 | Auth Email Integration | `sendAuthEmail()` replaces the body of the existing `sendInvite()` stub in `src/server/services/users.ts` (same exported signature `(userId) => Promise<{ id, inviteSentAt }>`, so PRD-03's call sites are untouched): looks up the user, renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset` template, inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (bypasses Component 3 — auth emails are not user-preference-gated), returns the existing shape | `src/server/services/users.ts` (edit, not new file) | FR-9 |\n65\t| 7 | Email Transport | One module building either a real SMTP `nodemailer.createTransport` or a `console` transport (logs subject/recipient/text) from `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (default `console` in dev), reading `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`; sets the `List-Unsubscribe` header on every send pointing at `/account/notifications` (NFR-6) | `src/server/email/transport.ts`, env vars in `.env.example` | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n66\t| 8 | Email Dispatcher (`dispatchEmails()`) | One function: (a) recovers rows stuck in `SENDING` >10 min back to `PENDING` (NFR-4), (b) `prisma.$transaction` containing `$queryRaw SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim up to `batchSize` (default 50) `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now`, flips them to `SENDING`; (c) outside the lock, sends each via Component 7's transport, marks `SENT`/`sentAt` on success or applies the FR-11 backoff (1/5/15/60/240 min across attempts 1-5, `FAILED` after the 5th) on failure; also runs Component 9's purge once per calendar day via an in-memory last-run timestamp checked at the top of each call | `src/server/email/dispatcher.ts` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-4 |\n67\t| 9 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()`: deletes `Notification` rows with `createdAt` older than 180 days; a plain function called from Component 8's daily check, not a separate cron/queue | `src/server/notifications/purge.ts` | FR-17 |\n68\t| 10 | Dispatch Drivers | Two thin callers of Component 8: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET` check, 401 via standard error envelope on mismatch — NFR-8) returning `{ sent, failed, retried }`; and `npm run worker:email`, a `tsx`-run Node script looping Component 8 every 15s (matches the existing `db:seed` script pattern) | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `scripts/worker-email.ts` | FR-12, NFR-8 |\n69\t| 11 | Notification List/Read Service | One query module: `listNotifications({ userId, unread?, category?, page, pageSize })` (own-rows-only, joins registry metadata for category/label), `getUnreadCount(userId)` (indexed by Component 1's composite index, NFR-3's <50ms budget), `markRead(userId, id)` / `markUnread` / `markAllRead(userId)` — the single implementation backing both the popover (FR-15) and the `/notifications` page (FR-16) | `src/server/notifications/list.ts` | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-3 |\n70\t| 12 | Auth Touchpoint (sequencing dependency) | Every user-facing notification/preferences route calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` where a real `requireUser()` is specified — see Overview finding. `ADMIN`-only routes (email-log, test-send) call `requireRole('ADMIN')` directly, already real today. The internal dispatch route uses its own `CRON_SECRET` bearer check (Component 10), not this helper. One-file swap when PRD-01's real `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` lands | *(calls into existing `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`; no new file)* | NFR-7 |\n71\t| 13 | Bell/Popover UI | Replaces the static `Badge badgeContent={0}` in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (~line 141) with a live MUI `IconButton` + `Badge` driven by a shared `useUnreadCount()` hook (`fetch` + `setInterval(30_000)`, paused on `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'` via a `visibilitychange` listener, \"9+\" cap above 9); clicking opens an MUI `Popover` with a `List` of the 10 most recent notifications from Component 11 (unread bold + dot, 2-line-clamped body, relative time), click marks read + navigates to `link`; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\" | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (edit), `src/hooks/useUnreadCount.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` | FR-14, FR-15 |\n72\t| 14 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page) `DataTable`-less simple MUI `List`/`Table` over Component 11, All/Unread `Tabs`, category filter, bulk \"Mark all as read\", per-row read/unread toggle | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` | FR-16 |\n73\t| 15 | Preferences UI + API | `/account/notifications`: MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader` rows) over Component 2's registry filtered to the current user's role, each row an In-app `Switch` + Email `Switch` (mandatory-in-app types render a disabled `Switch` + `Tooltip` \"Required by the school\"); `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves one `{type, inApp, email}` row immediately, client does optimistic update with rollback on a non-2xx response; server rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types with `VALIDATION_ERROR` (defense in depth alongside the disabled switch) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` | FR-18, FR-19, FR-22, NFR-7 |\n74\t| 16 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table over `EmailOutbox` (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), status filter, \"Retry now\" row action (`attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now` — same reset shape Component 8 expects on its next pass), \"Send test notification to me\" button calling Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'` for the current admin | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts`, `.../email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` | FR-20 |\n75\t| 17 | REST API Surface | All 12 endpoints from the PRD's API table, built on `src/server/http.ts`'s existing `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError`/`AppError` conventions — finalized verbatim in `api-contracts.json` by `arch-api-contracts` | `src/app/api/notifications/**`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/**`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/**`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/**`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/**` | FR-21 |\n76\t| 18 | Navigation | Resolves FR-23 (MEDIUM confidence in intake): add \"Notifications\" (`/notifications`, all roles) under the existing top-level entries, and \"Email log\" (`/admin/email-log`, ADMIN only) grouped with other admin-only entries — following the existing flat `NavItem[]` + `roles` convention (no \"Administration\" group exists yet in `navigation.ts`; PRD-02/03's group ideas are a later PRD's concern, not introduced here) | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-23 |\n77\t| 19 | Design System (MUI-only, directory-scoped) | Every app-UI surface (bell, popover, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only, looked up via the MUI MCP server; `src/server/email/templates/**` is the one ESLint `no-restricted-imports` exemption glob so `@react-email/components` imports there aren't flagged, while every other path stays MUI-only | ESLint config (exemption glob addition), reuses existing `theme.ts` | NFR-1 |\n78\t| 20 | Seed Data | 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`, linking to `/dashboard` — depends on Component 1's schema and Component 2's registry key existing first | `prisma/seed.ts` (extend existing script) | FR-24 |\n79\t| 21 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (registry compile-time key rejection via a type-level test, retry-backoff schedule math, link-path validator, CSV-free here — N/A); Vitest integration (`notify()` batching round-trip count, `dispatchEmails()` claim-and-send with concurrent-dispatcher race, stuck-row recovery, mandatory-preference server rejection); Playwright e2e (bell unread count updates after `notify()`, mark-all-read, preferences toggle persists, admin retry-now, admin test-send) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-9 |\n80\t\n81\tDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (Registry) depends\n82\ton 1's `type: String` column and feeds 3, 4, 11, 15, 16. 3 (`notify()`)\n83\tdepends on 1, 2 and is called by 4, 6 (indirectly — 6 bypasses it, see its\n84\trow), 16's test-send, and every later PRD per FR-6's stated intent. 5\n85\t(Templates) feeds 6 and 8. 6 edits an existing file and depends on 5. 7\n86\tfeeds 8. 8 (`dispatchEmails`) depends on 1, 5 (indirectly via rows already\n87\trendered), 7, 9, and is called only by 10. 11 depends on 1, 2 and feeds 13,\n88\t14. 12 is a calling convention, not a buildable unit — it gates 11, 13, 14,\n89\t15, 16's non-ADMIN-already-real routes. 17 wraps 3/8/11/15/16 behind routes.\n90\t18–20 are independent leaf tasks. 21 wraps all of the above.\n91\t\n92\t## Data Flow\n93\t\n94\t**`notify()` call (FR-3/4/5/6, NFR-2, NFR-5):**\n95\t1. Caller (any service, after its own transaction commits) invokes\n96\t   `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`. Component 3\n97\t   validates `link` is `/`-prefixed if present (NFR-5) — throws\n98\t   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', ...)` only for this programmer-error case;\n99\t   every other failure mode (missing user, send failure) is logged, not\n100\t   thrown.\n101\t2. Filters `userIds` to non-archived, non-disabled users in one query, then\n102\t   reads each remaining user's `NotificationPreference` row for `type`\n103\t   (one query, `findMany` with `in`), falling back to Component 2's\n104\t   registry defaults (`defaultEmail`, `mandatoryInApp`) where no row exists.\n105\t3. One `createMany` writes all qualifying `Notification` rows (in-app\n106\t   enabled OR `mandatoryInApp`); one `createMany` writes all qualifying\n107\t   `EmailOutbox` rows (email enabled AND user has an email) — ≤3 round\n108\t   trips total per FR-5, holding NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/<2s budget.\n109\t4. `notifyStudentAndParents` (Component 4) is a pre-step: resolve\n110\t   `studentIds` → student + linked-parent ids via `ParentStudentLink`\n111\t   (existing table), dedupe, then run steps 1-3 once over the combined list.\n112\t\n113\t**Email dispatch (FR-10/11/12, NFR-4):**\n114\t1. Either driver (Component 10) calls `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })`.\n115\t2. Top of the call: `UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='PENDING' WHERE\n116\t   status='SENDING' AND updatedAt-equivalent < now()-10min` (recovers\n117\t   crashed-mid-send rows, NFR-4) — tracked via `nextAttemptAt`/a dedicated\n118\t   timestamp set when flipped to `SENDING`.\n119\t3. One `prisma.$transaction` runs `SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE\n120\t   status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now() ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\"\n121\t   LIMIT $batchSize FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then `UPDATE ... SET\n122\t   status='SENDING'` on exactly those ids — this is the only raw SQL in the\n123\t   codebase, isolated to this function (no double-send across concurrent\n124\t   dispatchers, NFR-4).\n125\t4. Outside the lock: each claimed row renders through Component 7's\n126\t   transport. Success → `status='SENT', sentAt=now()`. Failure → bump\n127\t   `attempts`; if `attempts < 5`, `status='PENDING'` with `nextAttemptAt`\n128\t   set per the 1/5/15/60/240-minute schedule (FR-11); at `attempts === 5`,\n129\t   `status='FAILED'`.\n130\t5. Once per calendar day (in-memory last-run check): call Component 9's\n131\t   `purgeOldNotifications()`.\n132\t\n133\t**Auth email (FR-9):**\n134\t1. PRD-03 call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, \"send invitation now\"\n135\t   checkbox) call `sendInvite(userId)` exactly as before — signature\n136\t   unchanged.\n137\t2. Internally it now renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset`\n138\t   template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (no preference gate\n139\t   — auth emails are mandatory), then returns the same `{ id,\n140\t   inviteSentAt }` shape the stub always returned.\n141\t\n142\t**Bell + popover (FR-14/15):**\n143\t1. `useUnreadCount()` polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s\n144\t   while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`; a `visibilitychange`\n145\t   listener clears/restarts the interval.\n146\t2. Popover open → one call to Component 11's `listNotifications` capped at\n147\t   10 rows, newest first. Item click → `POST /api/notifications/:id/read`\n148\t   then client-side navigate to `link`.\n149\t\n150\t**Preferences (FR-18/19/22):**\n151\t1. Page load merges Component 2's registry (filtered to the signed-in\n152\t   user's role) with the user's existing `NotificationPreference` rows\n153\t   (defaults where absent).\n154\t2. Switch toggle → optimistic local state update + `PUT\n155\t   /api/me/notification-preferences` with `{type, inApp, email}`; server\n156\t   rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types before any write\n157\t   (`VALIDATION_ERROR`); a non-2xx response rolls the toggle back\n158\t   client-side.\n159\t\n160\t**Admin email log (FR-20):** pure read/action surface over `EmailOutbox`\n161\t(Component 1) — \"Retry now\" is a plain update (`attempts=0,\n162\tstatus=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`), picked up by the next\n163\t`dispatchEmails()` pass (step 3 above), not a separate send path. \"Send\n164\ttest\" is a direct call into Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'`.\n165\t\n166\t## Requirements Traceability\n167\t\n168\t| Requirement | Design Element |\n169\t|---|---|\n170\t| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enum |\n171\t| FR-2 | Component 2 — type registry |\n172\t| FR-3 | Component 2 (compile-time union) + Component 3 (`notify()` signature) |\n173\t| FR-4 | Component 3 — core `notify()` logic |\n174\t| FR-5 | Component 3 — `createMany` batching + never-throw contract |\n175\t| FR-6 | Component 4 — `notifyStudentAndParents` |\n176\t| FR-7 | Component 5 — base layout + HTML/text render |\n177\t| FR-8 | Component 5 — invite/password-reset/generic templates |\n178\t| FR-9 | Component 6 — `sendAuthEmail()` swap, signature preserved |\n179\t| FR-10 | Component 8 — `dispatchEmails()` claim/send/update |\n180\t| FR-11 | Component 8 — retry backoff schedule |\n181\t| FR-12 | Component 10 — HTTP route + worker script, one shared function |\n182\t| FR-13 | Component 7 — transport + env vars |\n183\t| FR-14 | Component 13 — bell poll/pause |\n184\t| FR-15 | Component 13 — popover list (via Component 11) |\n185\t| FR-16 | Component 14 — `/notifications` page (via Component 11) |\n186\t| FR-17 | Component 9 — purge, triggered from Component 8 |\n187\t| FR-18 | Component 15 — preferences table UI |\n188\t| FR-19 | Component 15 — optimistic PUT |\n189\t| FR-20 | Component 16 — admin email log |\n190\t| FR-21 | Component 17 — full REST surface |\n191\t| FR-22 | Component 15 — server-side mandatory-type rejection |\n192\t| FR-23 | Component 18 — nav entries (MEDIUM confidence resolved: flat entries, not a new group) |\n193\t| FR-24 | Component 20 — seed rows |\n194\t| NFR-1 | Component 19 — MUI-only, directory-scoped ESLint exemption |\n195\t| NFR-2 | Component 3 — ≤3-round-trip batching |\n196\t| NFR-3 | Component 1 (index) + Component 11 (`getUnreadCount` query shape) |\n197\t| NFR-4 | Component 8 — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` + stuck-row recovery |\n198\t| NFR-5 | Component 3 (`link` validation) + Component 5 (template escaping) |\n199\t| NFR-6 | Component 5 (HTML+text render) + Component 7 (`List-Unsubscribe` header) |\n200\t| NFR-7 | Component 12 — `requireRole` placeholder standing in for `requireUser` (sequencing dependency, see Overview) + Component 15/16's ADMIN/own-row checks |\n201\t| NFR-8 | Component 10 — `CRON_SECRET` bearer check, 401 on mismatch |\n202\t| NFR-9 | Component 21 — test harness |\n203\t| NFR-10 | All components — no SMS/push/websockets/digests introduced |\n204\t\n205\t## Status\n206\t\n207\tComplete. All 24 FR ids and 10 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\n208\tdropped. FR-23's MEDIUM-confidence nav question is resolved (flat entries\n209\tunder existing roles-based filtering, no new nav group introduced since\n210\t`navigation.ts` has none today). Two things carry forward for\n211\t`arch-api-contracts` and `dev-planning`:\n212\t\n213\t1. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 12):** `src/server/auth/\n214\t   permissions.ts`'s `requireUser()` does not exist in `src/` yet — only\n215\t   `requireRole.ts`'s ADMIN-placeholder and `student-access.ts` do. This\n216\t   design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` everywhere a real `requireUser()`\n217\t   would go on user-facing notification/preferences routes, so the later\n218\t   swap to PRD-01's real session-aware helper is confined to that one file\n219\t   plus each route's import line — not a redesign. ADMIN-only and\n220\t   `CRON_SECRET`-gated routes need no placeholder; they already have a real\n221\t   check today.\n222\t2. **Ready for `arch-api-contracts`:** the 12-endpoint API table in\n223\t   `04-notifications.md` is fully specified (methods, paths, roles, notes)\n224\t   and maps 1:1 onto Components 3/8/11/15/16 above — no net-new business\n225\t   logic to invent at the route layer, only envelope/pagination/error-code\n226\t   wiring per `src/server/http.ts`'s existing conventions.\n227\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6d9c31f-51c5-47dc-956a-0a68c82dec5a","uuid":"ade8fbc8-36f8-410e-89d4-fc555f018b2c","timestamp":"2026-10-20T05:58:53.074Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-04 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-01 (auth/RBAC,\ndesign-only — not landed), PRD-02 (academic structure) and PRD-03 (user\nmanagement). Intake reports **97% confidence and zero blockers**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`); the one MEDIUM-confidence item (FR-23, exact\nnav entries) is resolved below rather than carried forward as a gap.\n\n**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\nthe design — the same PRD-01 sequencing gap PRD-03's system-design.md\nalready flagged:** every source PRD, including this one, documents\n`src/server/auth/permissions.ts` exporting `requireUser()` and\n`requireRole()`. That file does not exist. `src/server/auth/` contains only\n`requireRole.ts` — a placeholder that returns a hardcoded ADMIN identity and\nchecks role — and `student-access.ts`. There is no `requireUser()`\nanywhere in `src/`. NFR-7 requires \"own-notifications-only\" checks on every\nuser-facing route (`GET /api/notifications`, read/unread, preferences),\nwhich needs a resolved *user identity*, not just a role gate. Since PRD-01\nhas not landed, this design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — the same\nplaceholder `requireRole.ts` already exports, called with every role —\neverywhere a real `requireUser()` would go, documented inline as a\nsequencing dependency (Component 12 below) exactly as PRD-03's Component 20\ndid for `sendInvite`. No new auth module is built here (that is PRD-01's\njob); call sites are written so swapping the placeholder for the real\n`requireUser()` later is a one-file change, not a per-route rewrite.\n\nSecond brownfield fact confirmed directly in source: `src/server/services/\nusers.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)` (lines ~385-390) is a logging-only stub\nreturning `{ id, inviteSentAt }`. FR-9 replaces its *body* with a real\n`sendAuthEmail()` call while preserving that exact signature, so PRD-03's\ncall sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, the create-user \"send invitation\"\ncheckbox) do not change.\n\nNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-9): existing stack only, Nodemailer + console transport,\n`@react-email/components` for templates (the one explicit exemption from\nthe MUI-only rule — scoped to `src/server/email/templates/**`), raw\n`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for dispatch (no queue library), one dispatch\nfunction behind two thin drivers (HTTP route + loop script), a compile-time\ntype registry (no DB table), in-memory scheduling for both the stuck-row\nrecovery and the daily purge. This document arranges those choices into\ncomponents, data flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability.\n\nTwo chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\nbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\ncode: **`notify()`** (FR-3/4/5/6) and **`dispatchEmails()`** (FR-10/11).\nOne list/read service backs both the bell popover (FR-15) and the\n`/notifications` page (FR-16) — not two query paths. FR-23's nav entries\nare resolved here (Component 11) rather than left open.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum, exactly per the schema block in `04-notifications.md` FR-1 (composite index `Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt)`, `EmailOutbox(status, nextAttemptAt)`) | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| 2 | Notification Type Registry | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const object (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles) across ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM; seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`; `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is `notify()`'s type parameter so unknown keys are a compile error (FR-3) | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-2, FR-3 |\n| 3 | Notification Service (`notify()`) | `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`: filters out archived/disabled users, resolves per-user `NotificationPreference` (falling back to registry defaults), `createMany` for `Notification` rows where in-app applies (including when `mandatoryInApp` overrides an off preference), `createMany` for `EmailOutbox` rows where email applies and the user has an email; never throws — failures logged via `logger`, caller's own transaction already committed by the time this runs; `link` values validated as `/`-prefixed relative paths before write (NFR-5) | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-5 |\n| 4 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })`: expands each student id to itself + linked parent ids via the existing `ParentStudentLink` table (PRD-03's model, read-only here), dedupes, calls Component 3 once with the combined id list — no new link model | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` (co-located, thin wrapper) | FR-6 |\n| 5 | Email Templates | `BaseLayout` (logo/name header, content slot, footer with school address + \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` + required disclosure sentence) plus `invite`, `password-reset`, `generic-notification` templates, each rendered via `@react-email/render`'s `render()` for HTML and `render(..., { plainText: true })` for text — one render call backs both `EmailOutbox.html`/`.text` columns so the two parts can't drift; all interpolated user text passes through React Email's escaping (NFR-5's HTML-escape rule) | `src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx`, `invite.tsx`, `password-reset.tsx`, `generic-notification.tsx` | FR-7, FR-8, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| 6 | Auth Email Integration | `sendAuthEmail()` replaces the body of the existing `sendInvite()` stub in `src/server/services/users.ts` (same exported signature `(userId) => Promise<{ id, inviteSentAt }>`, so PRD-03's call sites are untouched): looks up the user, renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset` template, inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (bypasses Component 3 — auth emails are not user-preference-gated), returns the existing shape | `src/server/services/users.ts` (edit, not new file) | FR-9 |\n| 7 | Email Transport | One module building either a real SMTP `nodemailer.createTransport` or a `console` transport (logs subject/recipient/text) from `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (default `console` in dev), reading `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`; sets the `List-Unsubscribe` header on every send pointing at `/account/notifications` (NFR-6) | `src/server/email/transport.ts`, env vars in `.env.example` | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| 8 | Email Dispatcher (`dispatchEmails()`) | One function: (a) recovers rows stuck in `SENDING` >10 min back to `PENDING` (NFR-4), (b) `prisma.$transaction` containing `$queryRaw SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim up to `batchSize` (default 50) `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now`, flips them to `SENDING`; (c) outside the lock, sends each via Component 7's transport, marks `SENT`/`sentAt` on success or applies the FR-11 backoff (1/5/15/60/240 min across attempts 1-5, `FAILED` after the 5th) on failure; also runs Component 9's purge once per calendar day via an in-memory last-run timestamp checked at the top of each call | `src/server/email/dispatcher.ts` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-4 |\n| 9 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()`: deletes `Notification` rows with `createdAt` older than 180 days; a plain function called from Component 8's daily check, not a separate cron/queue | `src/server/notifications/purge.ts` | FR-17 |\n| 10 | Dispatch Drivers | Two thin callers of Component 8: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET` check, 401 via standard error envelope on mismatch — NFR-8) returning `{ sent, failed, retried }`; and `npm run worker:email`, a `tsx`-run Node script looping Component 8 every 15s (matches the existing `db:seed` script pattern) | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `scripts/worker-email.ts` | FR-12, NFR-8 |\n| 11 | Notification List/Read Service | One query module: `listNotifications({ userId, unread?, category?, page, pageSize })` (own-rows-only, joins registry metadata for category/label), `getUnreadCount(userId)` (indexed by Component 1's composite index, NFR-3's <50ms budget), `markRead(userId, id)` / `markUnread` / `markAllRead(userId)` — the single implementation backing both the popover (FR-15) and the `/notifications` page (FR-16) | `src/server/notifications/list.ts` | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-3 |\n| 12 | Auth Touchpoint (sequencing dependency) | Every user-facing notification/preferences route calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` where a real `requireUser()` is specified — see Overview finding. `ADMIN`-only routes (email-log, test-send) call `requireRole('ADMIN')` directly, already real today. The internal dispatch route uses its own `CRON_SECRET` bearer check (Component 10), not this helper. One-file swap when PRD-01's real `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` lands | *(calls into existing `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`; no new file)* | NFR-7 |\n| 13 | Bell/Popover UI | Replaces the static `Badge badgeContent={0}` in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (~line 141) with a live MUI `IconButton` + `Badge` driven by a shared `useUnreadCount()` hook (`fetch` + `setInterval(30_000)`, paused on `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'` via a `visibilitychange` listener, \"9+\" cap above 9); clicking opens an MUI `Popover` with a `List` of the 10 most recent notifications from Component 11 (unread bold + dot, 2-line-clamped body, relative time), click marks read + navigates to `link`; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\" | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (edit), `src/hooks/useUnreadCount.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` | FR-14, FR-15 |\n| 14 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page) `DataTable`-less simple MUI `List`/`Table` over Component 11, All/Unread `Tabs`, category filter, bulk \"Mark all as read\", per-row read/unread toggle | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` | FR-16 |\n| 15 | Preferences UI + API | `/account/notifications`: MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader` rows) over Component 2's registry filtered to the current user's role, each row an In-app `Switch` + Email `Switch` (mandatory-in-app types render a disabled `Switch` + `Tooltip` \"Required by the school\"); `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves one `{type, inApp, email}` row immediately, client does optimistic update with rollback on a non-2xx response; server rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types with `VALIDATION_ERROR` (defense in depth alongside the disabled switch) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` | FR-18, FR-19, FR-22, NFR-7 |\n| 16 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table over `EmailOutbox` (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), status filter, \"Retry now\" row action (`attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now` — same reset shape Component 8 expects on its next pass), \"Send test notification to me\" button calling Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'` for the current admin | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts`, `.../email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` | FR-20 |\n| 17 | REST API Surface | All 12 endpoints from the PRD's API table, built on `src/server/http.ts`'s existing `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError`/`AppError` conventions — finalized verbatim in `api-contracts.json` by `arch-api-contracts` | `src/app/api/notifications/**`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/**`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/**`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/**`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/**` | FR-21 |\n| 18 | Navigation | Resolves FR-23 (MEDIUM confidence in intake): add \"Notifications\" (`/notifications`, all roles) under the existing top-level entries, and \"Email log\" (`/admin/email-log`, ADMIN only) grouped with other admin-only entries — following the existing flat `NavItem[]` + `roles` convention (no \"Administration\" group exists yet in `navigation.ts`; PRD-02/03's group ideas are a later PRD's concern, not introduced here) | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-23 |\n| 19 | Design System (MUI-only, directory-scoped) | Every app-UI surface (bell, popover, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only, looked up via the MUI MCP server; `src/server/email/templates/**` is the one ESLint `no-restricted-imports` exemption glob so `@react-email/components` imports there aren't flagged, while every other path stays MUI-only | ESLint config (exemption glob addition), reuses existing `theme.ts` | NFR-1 |\n| 20 | Seed Data | 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`, linking to `/dashboard` — depends on Component 1's schema and Component 2's registry key existing first | `prisma/seed.ts` (extend existing script) | FR-24 |\n| 21 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (registry compile-time key rejection via a type-level test, retry-backoff schedule math, link-path validator, CSV-free here — N/A); Vitest integration (`notify()` batching round-trip count, `dispatchEmails()` claim-and-send with concurrent-dispatcher race, stuck-row recovery, mandatory-preference server rejection); Playwright e2e (bell unread count updates after `notify()`, mark-all-read, preferences toggle persists, admin retry-now, admin test-send) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-9 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (Registry) depends\non 1's `type: String` column and feeds 3, 4, 11, 15, 16. 3 (`notify()`)\ndepends on 1, 2 and is called by 4, 6 (indirectly — 6 bypasses it, see its\nrow), 16's test-send, and every later PRD per FR-6's stated intent. 5\n(Templates) feeds 6 and 8. 6 edits an existing file and depends on 5. 7\nfeeds 8. 8 (`dispatchEmails`) depends on 1, 5 (indirectly via rows already\nrendered), 7, 9, and is called only by 10. 11 depends on 1, 2 and feeds 13,\n14. 12 is a calling convention, not a buildable unit — it gates 11, 13, 14,\n15, 16's non-ADMIN-already-real routes. 17 wraps 3/8/11/15/16 behind routes.\n18–20 are independent leaf tasks. 21 wraps all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**`notify()` call (FR-3/4/5/6, NFR-2, NFR-5):**\n1. Caller (any service, after its own transaction commits) invokes\n   `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`. Component 3\n   validates `link` is `/`-prefixed if present (NFR-5) — throws\n   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', ...)` only for this programmer-error case;\n   every other failure mode (missing user, send failure) is logged, not\n   thrown.\n2. Filters `userIds` to non-archived, non-disabled users in one query, then\n   reads each remaining user's `NotificationPreference` row for `type`\n   (one query, `findMany` with `in`), falling back to Component 2's\n   registry defaults (`defaultEmail`, `mandatoryInApp`) where no row exists.\n3. One `createMany` writes all qualifying `Notification` rows (in-app\n   enabled OR `mandatoryInApp`); one `createMany` writes all qualifying\n   `EmailOutbox` rows (email enabled AND user has an email) — ≤3 round\n   trips total per FR-5, holding NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/<2s budget.\n4. `notifyStudentAndParents` (Component 4) is a pre-step: resolve\n   `studentIds` → student + linked-parent ids via `ParentStudentLink`\n   (existing table), dedupe, then run steps 1-3 once over the combined list.\n\n**Email dispatch (FR-10/11/12, NFR-4):**\n1. Either driver (Component 10) calls `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })`.\n2. Top of the call: `UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='PENDING' WHERE\n   status='SENDING' AND updatedAt-equivalent < now()-10min` (recovers\n   crashed-mid-send rows, NFR-4) — tracked via `nextAttemptAt`/a dedicated\n   timestamp set when flipped to `SENDING`.\n3. One `prisma.$transaction` runs `SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE\n   status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now() ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\"\n   LIMIT $batchSize FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then `UPDATE ... SET\n   status='SENDING'` on exactly those ids — this is the only raw SQL in the\n   codebase, isolated to this function (no double-send across concurrent\n   dispatchers, NFR-4).\n4. Outside the lock: each claimed row renders through Component 7's\n   transport. Success → `status='SENT', sentAt=now()`. Failure → bump\n   `attempts`; if `attempts < 5`, `status='PENDING'` with `nextAttemptAt`\n   set per the 1/5/15/60/240-minute schedule (FR-11); at `attempts === 5`,\n   `status='FAILED'`.\n5. Once per calendar day (in-memory last-run check): call Component 9's\n   `purgeOldNotifications()`.\n\n**Auth email (FR-9):**\n1. PRD-03 call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, \"send invitation now\"\n   checkbox) call `sendInvite(userId)` exactly as before — signature\n   unchanged.\n2. Internally it now renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset`\n   template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (no preference gate\n   — auth emails are mandatory), then returns the same `{ id,\n   inviteSentAt }` shape the stub always returned.\n\n**Bell + popover (FR-14/15):**\n1. `useUnreadCount()` polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s\n   while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`; a `visibilitychange`\n   listener clears/restarts the interval.\n2. Popover open → one call to Component 11's `listNotifications` capped at\n   10 rows, newest first. Item click → `POST /api/notifications/:id/read`\n   then client-side navigate to `link`.\n\n**Preferences (FR-18/19/22):**\n1. Page load merges Component 2's registry (filtered to the signed-in\n   user's role) with the user's existing `NotificationPreference` rows\n   (defaults where absent).\n2. Switch toggle → optimistic local state update + `PUT\n   /api/me/notification-preferences` with `{type, inApp, email}`; server\n   rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types before any write\n   (`VALIDATION_ERROR`); a non-2xx response rolls the toggle back\n   client-side.\n\n**Admin email log (FR-20):** pure read/action surface over `EmailOutbox`\n(Component 1) — \"Retry now\" is a plain update (`attempts=0,\nstatus=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`), picked up by the next\n`dispatchEmails()` pass (step 3 above), not a separate send path. \"Send\ntest\" is a direct call into Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'`.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enum |\n| FR-2 | Component 2 — type registry |\n| FR-3 | Component 2 (compile-time union) + Component 3 (`notify()` signature) |\n| FR-4 | Component 3 — core `notify()` logic |\n| FR-5 | Component 3 — `createMany` batching + never-throw contract |\n| FR-6 | Component 4 — `notifyStudentAndParents` |\n| FR-7 | Component 5 — base layout + HTML/text render |\n| FR-8 | Component 5 — invite/password-reset/generic templates |\n| FR-9 | Component 6 — `sendAuthEmail()` swap, signature preserved |\n| FR-10 | Component 8 — `dispatchEmails()` claim/send/update |\n| FR-11 | Component 8 — retry backoff schedule |\n| FR-12 | Component 10 — HTTP route + worker script, one shared function |\n| FR-13 | Component 7 — transport + env vars |\n| FR-14 | Component 13 — bell poll/pause |\n| FR-15 | Component 13 — popover list (via Component 11) |\n| FR-16 | Component 14 — `/notifications` page (via Component 11) |\n| FR-17 | Component 9 — purge, triggered from Component 8 |\n| FR-18 | Component 15 — preferences table UI |\n| FR-19 | Component 15 — optimistic PUT |\n| FR-20 | Component 16 — admin email log |\n| FR-21 | Component 17 — full REST surface |\n| FR-22 | Component 15 — server-side mandatory-type rejection |\n| FR-23 | Component 18 — nav entries (MEDIUM confidence resolved: flat entries, not a new group) |\n| FR-24 | Component 20 — seed rows |\n| NFR-1 | Component 19 — MUI-only, directory-scoped ESLint exemption |\n| NFR-2 | Component 3 — ≤3-round-trip batching |\n| NFR-3 | Component 1 (index) + Component 11 (`getUnreadCount` query shape) |\n| NFR-4 | Component 8 — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` + stuck-row recovery |\n| NFR-5 | Component 3 (`link` validation) + Component 5 (template escaping) |\n| NFR-6 | Component 5 (HTML+text render) + Component 7 (`List-Unsubscribe` header) |\n| NFR-7 | Component 12 — `requireRole` placeholder standing in for `requireUser` (sequencing dependency, see Overview) + Component 15/16's ADMIN/own-row checks |\n| NFR-8 | Component 10 — `CRON_SECRET` bearer check, 401 on mismatch |\n| NFR-9 | Component 21 — test harness |\n| NFR-10 | All components — no SMS/push/websockets/digests introduced |\n\n## Status\n\nComplete. All 24 FR ids and 10 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were\ndropped. FR-23's MEDIUM-confidence nav question is resolved (flat entries\nunder existing roles-based filtering, no new nav group introduced since\n`navigation.ts` has none today). Two things carry forward for\n`arch-api-contracts` and `dev-planning`:\n\n1. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 12):** `src/server/auth/\n   permissions.ts`'s `requireUser()` does not exist in `src/` yet — only\n   `requireRole.ts`'s ADMIN-placeholder and `student-access.ts` do. This\n   design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` everywhere a real `requireUser()`\n   would go on user-facing notification/preferences routes, so the later\n   swap to PRD-01's real session-aware helper is confined to that one file\n   plus each route's import line — not a redesign. ADMIN-only and\n   `CRON_SECRET`-gated routes need no placeholder; they already have a real\n   check today.\n2. **Ready for `arch-api-contracts`:** the 12-endpoint API table in\n   `04-notifications.md` is fully specified (methods, paths, roles, notes)\n   and maps 1:1 onto Components 3/8/11/15/16 above — no net-new business\n   logic to invent at the route layer, only envelope/pagination/error-code\n   wiring per `src/server/http.ts`'s existing conventions.\n","numLines":227,"startLine":1,"totalLines":227}}}
