{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lrn89QMaxd9ZZJo51EQvwZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-05\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (31 requirements — 24 FR + 7\n5\tNFR, 97% confidence, 2 MEDIUM-confidence blockers per\n6\t`handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is the Sections/Courses/Enrollment PRD:\n7\tSection/Course/Enrollment data model, admin Sections and Courses CRUD UIs,\n8\tthe roster auto-enroll/auto-drop engine, capacity enforcement, the public\n9\tcourse surface (`/courses/[courseId]`, course tabs, `/my-courses`), course\n10\taccess control, student-side course tab, navigation, and the REST API\n11\tsurface.\n12\t\n13\tArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin Sections\n14\tUI**, **Section Detail & Membership**, **Core Courses Bootstrap**, **Roster\n15\tEnrollment Engine**, **Year Rollover**, **Admin Courses UI**, **Course Public\n16\tSurface**, **Auth/Access Control**, **My Courses Page**, **Navigation**,\n17\t**Student Tab Integration**, **REST API Surface**, **Audit Logging**,\n18\t**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Performance**, **Privacy/Roster Scrubbing**,\n19\t**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n20\t\n21\t## Functional Requirements\n22\t\n23\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n24\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n25\t| FR-1 | Data Model | `Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` + `CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, with the specified unique constraints/index. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. The `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` is also NFR-2's integrity backstop, not just a schema detail. |\n26\t| FR-2 | Admin Sections UI | `/admin/sections` list: filter by academic year (defaults to current, reuses `AcademicYear`), table with capacity warning colour at >=90%. Read-only view over FR-1's tables plus a capacity/course-count aggregate query. |\n27\t| FR-3 | Admin Sections UI | Section create/edit dialog incl. `UserPicker` (role=TEACHER) reuse and the \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" rule. That uniqueness rule is app-level validation (not a DB constraint per FR-1) — `arch-design-system` should decide where it's enforced (service layer) since two concurrent writes could race. |\n28\t| FR-4 | Section Detail & Membership | `/admin/sections/[id]`: members table (add/remove), course list, \"Create core courses\" button. Add/remove here is the trigger point for FR-7/FR-8's enrollment side effects — this page is a thin UI over the Roster Enrollment Engine, not its own business logic. |\n29\t| FR-5 | Core Courses Bootstrap | \"Create core courses\" dialog: one CORE course per checked subject, enrolls all current section members. Must call the same course-creation path as FR-10 (creating a CORE course always enrolls current members) — one code path, two entry points (bulk vs. single). |\n30\t| FR-6 | Year Rollover | \"Copy sections to next year\": grade level advanced by `order`, no members/teacher. Independent of the enrollment engine — a structural copy only, gated on a future non-current academic year existing. |\n31\t| FR-7 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-enroll on section add: ACTIVE-enrolls into every non-archived CORE course of the section; reactivates DROPPED rather than duplicating. Central business rule — same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics FR-9/FR-10 must share. |\n32\t| FR-8 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-drop on section removal: CORE enrollments → DROPPED + `droppedAt`; electives untouched. Mirror of FR-7; both must be designed as one named module (e.g. `enrollInSectionCoreCourses` / `dropSectionCoreCourses`), not inlined per call site. |\n33\t| FR-9 | Roster Enrollment Engine | `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` — FR-7 enroll + FR-8 drop in one DB transaction. The only place FR-7+FR-8 compose; confirms both must be transaction-safe, composable functions rather than route-level logic. |\n34\t| FR-10 | Core Courses Bootstrap | New CORE course on a section enrolls all current members (ACTIVE). Same enroll path as FR-7 — triggered from course-creation instead of membership-add. |\n35\t| FR-11 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Capacity enforcement: CONFLICT error with exact message pattern, \"Override capacity\" escape hatch. A guard that must sit in front of every enroll path (FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, and the course-level \"Add students\" of FR-15) — one shared capacity-check function, not four. |\n36\t| FR-12 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Dropped enrollments keep historical data visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active rosters and add-student pickers. A query-filtering concern (`status = ACTIVE` everywhere user-facing lists are built) layered on top of FR-8's state transition. |\n37\t| FR-13 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses` list: filters (year/grade/subject/teacher/kind/search), reuses `Subject.color`. Read-only view, same shape as FR-2 but for courses. |\n38\t| FR-14 | Admin Courses UI | Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (required iff kind=CORE), teacher + up to 3 co-teachers, auto-filled uppercase code. Validation rule (\"section required iff CORE\") needs to live in one shared validator the dialog and the API route both call. |\n39\t| FR-15 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`: roster table with drop/reactivate + add-students picker; CORE courses show an info note (membership managed via section). This page's \"Add students\" must still run through FR-11's capacity guard even though it bypasses the section-membership trigger. |\n40\t| FR-16 | Course Public Surface | `/courses/[courseId]` header: subject colour band, teachers incl. co-teachers, section, room. Read-only composition of FR-1 data, gated by FR-18's `assertCanViewCourse`. |\n41\t| FR-17 | Course Public Surface | New `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry (mirrors `student-tabs.ts`, adds `roles`), registers Overview + Roster tabs with per-role visibility (student sees classmates' names only; parent tab hidden). Roster tab's student-facing truncation is also NFR-4's privacy rule — same tab, two render paths by role. |\n42\t| FR-18 | Auth/Access Control | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`: `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse`. The authorization chokepoint every course route (FR-15, FR-16, FR-23) and the course-tabs registry (FR-17) must call — do not re-derive role logic per route. Built on top of NFR-7's existing `requireRole` stand-in, not a new auth primitive. |\n43\t| FR-19 | My Courses Page | `/my-courses`: role-specific MUI Card grids (teacher/student/parent-by-child). Read view composing FR-18's access rules per role; parent grouping needs whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, same pattern as the prior PRD's family fan-out). |\n44\t| FR-20 | Navigation | Sidebar entries: \"My courses\" (TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT) + \"Sections\"/\"Courses\" under an \"Administration\" group for ADMIN. **MEDIUM confidence / flagged blocker**: `NavItem` has no `group` field today and no other admin pages exist yet. `arch-design-system` must decide: add a lightweight `group` field now, or ship flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav PRD lands — this is an explicit architect decision point, not a detail to infer silently. |\n45\t| FR-21 | Student Tab Integration | Register `student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab: student's courses, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read view, no new service — reuses FR-1 data + FR-18-equivalent visibility (whoever can view the student). |\n46\t| FR-22 | Auth/Access Control | Extend `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`: TEACHER additionally sees students via taught/co-taught course enrollments and their homeroom section. A brownfield extension to an existing exported function — must preserve its existing signature/contract for current PRD-01/PRD-04 callers, only add to the TEACHER branch. |\n47\t| FR-23 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (sections CRUD+members+move-section+core-courses+copy-to-year; courses CRUD+roster+enrollments+status PATCH; `GET /api/me/courses`) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following the existing envelope/pagination/search conventions. Every endpoint must map 1:1 to a service already named above (FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11 enrollment engine, FR-18 access control) — no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n48\t| FR-24 | Audit Logging | Every `section.*`/`course.*`/`enrollment.*` write records an `AuditLog` row via the existing `audit()` helper. A cross-cutting call that belongs at the service layer (alongside FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11's shared functions), not duplicated per route handler. |\n49\t\n50\t## Non-Functional Requirements\n51\t\n52\t| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n53\t|----|------------------------|-------|\n54\t| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible element across sections/courses/enrollment screens is MUI/MUI-X only (DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, `useToast()`), looked up via the MUI MCP server first; no Tailwind/shadcn/Radix/react-select. Applies uniformly — unlike the prior PRD, there's no template-rendering exemption needed here (no React Email in scope). |\n55\t| NFR-2 | Data Model | One-section-per-student-per-year enforced by the DB unique constraint on `SectionMember`, not just app code — directly backs FR-1's schema and is the safety net under FR-3's app-level homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (which has no DB constraint and must be designed knowing that). |\n56\t| NFR-3 | Performance | 30 students × 8 core courses (240 enrollments) in under 1s — a batching requirement on FR-7's auto-enroll path specifically; `arch-design-system` should spec `createMany`/batched writes the same way the enrollment engine is designed, not per-row inserts. |\n57\t| NFR-4 | Privacy/Roster Scrubbing | Students see classmates' names only on the Roster tab and `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` — no email/admission number/profile link. A response-shape rule on FR-17's Roster tab and FR-23's roster endpoint; must be enforced server-side at the API layer (FR-23), not just hidden in the FR-17 UI. |\n58\t| NFR-5 | Test Harness | Keep `lint`/`typecheck`/`test` green; add unit/integration/Playwright tests per Test Requirements. Scopes what `dev-planning` must schedule test-writing for; the roster engine (FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11) and capacity enforcement (FR-11) are the highest-value test targets given their reuse across routes. |\n59\t| NFR-6 | Scope Discipline | No timetable slots, no course content, no prerequisites/course-request workflows, no automatic year-to-year promotion (only the manual FR-6 copy). Bounds `arch-design-system`'s design the same way it bounds dev's — don't let FR-6's \"copy\" grow into a promotion workflow. |\n60\t| NFR-7 | Auth/Access Control | **Flagged blocker (MEDIUM confidence)**: `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` / `requireUser()` described in Platform Context do not exist yet — only `requireRole.ts` and `student-access.ts` are present (same gap PRD-04 flagged). New routes in this PRD (FR-23) must use the existing `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` stand-in rather than invent a new helper, until PRD-01 lands. This directly constrains FR-18's `course-access.ts` implementation — it should wrap `requireRole`, not assume `permissions.ts` exists. |\n61\t\n62\t## Cross-cutting notes for `arch-design-system`\n63\t\n64\t- **One enrollment engine, four callers**: FR-7 (add to section), FR-8\n65\t  (remove from section), FR-9 (move-section transaction), and FR-10 (new\n66\t  CORE course) all drive the same enroll/drop/reactivate semantics, and\n67\t  FR-11's capacity guard plus FR-24's audit call must sit in front of/behind\n68\t  all four. Design this as named, reusable service functions (e.g.\n69\t  `enrollSectionCoreCourses`, `dropSectionCoreCourses`,\n70\t  `checkCapacityOrThrow`), not duplicated per route — FR-9's single-transaction\n71\t  requirement is the clearest signal these must already be composable,\n72\t  transaction-safe units.\n73\t- **FR-20's nav-grouping question is an explicit decision point**, not a\n74\t  detail to quietly resolve — `handoff-to-architect.json` lists it as a\n75\t  blocker. Record the chosen approach (add `group` to `NavItem` vs. flat\n76\t  entries) in `system-design.md`'s Overview per Compliance Rule 5.\n77\t- **NFR-7's auth-helper gap is also a carried-forward blocker** — FR-18's\n78\t  `course-access.ts` must be designed against today's `requireRole.ts`\n79\t  stand-in, not the not-yet-built `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`. Surface\n80\t  this explicitly in `system-design.md`'s Overview so `dev-planning` doesn't\n81\t  schedule work against auth helpers that don't exist.\n82\t- **Two independent app-level uniqueness rules have no DB backstop and need\n83\t  an explicit concurrency decision**: FR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per\n84\t  section per year\" and FR-14's \"section required iff kind=CORE\" are both\n85\t  service-layer validations only (unlike NFR-2's DB-constrained rule) —\n86\t  `arch-design-system` should say where each is checked and whether a race\n87\t  (two concurrent section edits) is acceptable risk or needs a DB-level\n88\t  constraint too.\n89\t- **NFR-4's roster scrubbing must be enforced at the API layer (FR-23),\n90\t  not just the FR-17 UI tab** — call this out explicitly in the\n91\t  traceability table so the response-shape rule isn't treated as\n92\t  presentation-only.\n93\t- **FR-5 and FR-10 share one course-creation-enrolls-members code path** —\n94\t  bulk (checked subjects) vs. single (one course) are two entry points into\n95\t  the same underlying function, same pattern as the enrollment engine note\n96\t  above.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6adde39-f92b-490f-9ef1-b8393dd3c9ab","uuid":"a3a331b3-a9cb-4a1e-a266-56dda28b3fea","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:30:18.334Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket abcd-05\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system`. Not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (31 requirements — 24 FR + 7\nNFR, 97% confidence, 2 MEDIUM-confidence blockers per\n`handoff-to-architect.json`). Scope is the Sections/Courses/Enrollment PRD:\nSection/Course/Enrollment data model, admin Sections and Courses CRUD UIs,\nthe roster auto-enroll/auto-drop engine, capacity enforcement, the public\ncourse surface (`/courses/[courseId]`, course tabs, `/my-courses`), course\naccess control, student-side course tab, navigation, and the REST API\nsurface.\n\nArchitectural concern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Admin Sections\nUI**, **Section Detail & Membership**, **Core Courses Bootstrap**, **Roster\nEnrollment Engine**, **Year Rollover**, **Admin Courses UI**, **Course Public\nSurface**, **Auth/Access Control**, **My Courses Page**, **Navigation**,\n**Student Tab Integration**, **REST API Surface**, **Audit Logging**,\n**Design System (MUI-only)**, **Performance**, **Privacy/Roster Scrubbing**,\n**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` + `CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, with the specified unique constraints/index. Foundation tables — every other FR reads or writes one of these; must land before any service/route work. The `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` is also NFR-2's integrity backstop, not just a schema detail. |\n| FR-2 | Admin Sections UI | `/admin/sections` list: filter by academic year (defaults to current, reuses `AcademicYear`), table with capacity warning colour at >=90%. Read-only view over FR-1's tables plus a capacity/course-count aggregate query. |\n| FR-3 | Admin Sections UI | Section create/edit dialog incl. `UserPicker` (role=TEACHER) reuse and the \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" rule. That uniqueness rule is app-level validation (not a DB constraint per FR-1) — `arch-design-system` should decide where it's enforced (service layer) since two concurrent writes could race. |\n| FR-4 | Section Detail & Membership | `/admin/sections/[id]`: members table (add/remove), course list, \"Create core courses\" button. Add/remove here is the trigger point for FR-7/FR-8's enrollment side effects — this page is a thin UI over the Roster Enrollment Engine, not its own business logic. |\n| FR-5 | Core Courses Bootstrap | \"Create core courses\" dialog: one CORE course per checked subject, enrolls all current section members. Must call the same course-creation path as FR-10 (creating a CORE course always enrolls current members) — one code path, two entry points (bulk vs. single). |\n| FR-6 | Year Rollover | \"Copy sections to next year\": grade level advanced by `order`, no members/teacher. Independent of the enrollment engine — a structural copy only, gated on a future non-current academic year existing. |\n| FR-7 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-enroll on section add: ACTIVE-enrolls into every non-archived CORE course of the section; reactivates DROPPED rather than duplicating. Central business rule — same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics FR-9/FR-10 must share. |\n| FR-8 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Auto-drop on section removal: CORE enrollments → DROPPED + `droppedAt`; electives untouched. Mirror of FR-7; both must be designed as one named module (e.g. `enrollInSectionCoreCourses` / `dropSectionCoreCourses`), not inlined per call site. |\n| FR-9 | Roster Enrollment Engine | `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` — FR-7 enroll + FR-8 drop in one DB transaction. The only place FR-7+FR-8 compose; confirms both must be transaction-safe, composable functions rather than route-level logic. |\n| FR-10 | Core Courses Bootstrap | New CORE course on a section enrolls all current members (ACTIVE). Same enroll path as FR-7 — triggered from course-creation instead of membership-add. |\n| FR-11 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Capacity enforcement: CONFLICT error with exact message pattern, \"Override capacity\" escape hatch. A guard that must sit in front of every enroll path (FR-7, FR-9, FR-10, and the course-level \"Add students\" of FR-15) — one shared capacity-check function, not four. |\n| FR-12 | Roster Enrollment Engine | Dropped enrollments keep historical data visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active rosters and add-student pickers. A query-filtering concern (`status = ACTIVE` everywhere user-facing lists are built) layered on top of FR-8's state transition. |\n| FR-13 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses` list: filters (year/grade/subject/teacher/kind/search), reuses `Subject.color`. Read-only view, same shape as FR-2 but for courses. |\n| FR-14 | Admin Courses UI | Course create/edit dialog: subject, section (required iff kind=CORE), teacher + up to 3 co-teachers, auto-filled uppercase code. Validation rule (\"section required iff CORE\") needs to live in one shared validator the dialog and the API route both call. |\n| FR-15 | Admin Courses UI | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`: roster table with drop/reactivate + add-students picker; CORE courses show an info note (membership managed via section). This page's \"Add students\" must still run through FR-11's capacity guard even though it bypasses the section-membership trigger. |\n| FR-16 | Course Public Surface | `/courses/[courseId]` header: subject colour band, teachers incl. co-teachers, section, room. Read-only composition of FR-1 data, gated by FR-18's `assertCanViewCourse`. |\n| FR-17 | Course Public Surface | New `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry (mirrors `student-tabs.ts`, adds `roles`), registers Overview + Roster tabs with per-role visibility (student sees classmates' names only; parent tab hidden). Roster tab's student-facing truncation is also NFR-4's privacy rule — same tab, two render paths by role. |\n| FR-18 | Auth/Access Control | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`: `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse`. The authorization chokepoint every course route (FR-15, FR-16, FR-23) and the course-tabs registry (FR-17) must call — do not re-derive role logic per route. Built on top of NFR-7's existing `requireRole` stand-in, not a new auth primitive. |\n| FR-19 | My Courses Page | `/my-courses`: role-specific MUI Card grids (teacher/student/parent-by-child). Read view composing FR-18's access rules per role; parent grouping needs whatever parent-link read path already exists (brownfield reuse, same pattern as the prior PRD's family fan-out). |\n| FR-20 | Navigation | Sidebar entries: \"My courses\" (TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT) + \"Sections\"/\"Courses\" under an \"Administration\" group for ADMIN. **MEDIUM confidence / flagged blocker**: `NavItem` has no `group` field today and no other admin pages exist yet. `arch-design-system` must decide: add a lightweight `group` field now, or ship flat entries until a dedicated admin-nav PRD lands — this is an explicit architect decision point, not a detail to infer silently. |\n| FR-21 | Student Tab Integration | Register `student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab: student's courses, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read view, no new service — reuses FR-1 data + FR-18-equivalent visibility (whoever can view the student). |\n| FR-22 | Auth/Access Control | Extend `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`: TEACHER additionally sees students via taught/co-taught course enrollments and their homeroom section. A brownfield extension to an existing exported function — must preserve its existing signature/contract for current PRD-01/PRD-04 callers, only add to the TEACHER branch. |\n| FR-23 | REST API Surface | Full endpoint list (sections CRUD+members+move-section+core-courses+copy-to-year; courses CRUD+roster+enrollments+status PATCH; `GET /api/me/courses`) — to be finalized verbatim by `arch-api-contracts`, following the existing envelope/pagination/search conventions. Every endpoint must map 1:1 to a service already named above (FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11 enrollment engine, FR-18 access control) — no net-new business logic at the route layer. |\n| FR-24 | Audit Logging | Every `section.*`/`course.*`/`enrollment.*` write records an `AuditLog` row via the existing `audit()` helper. A cross-cutting call that belongs at the service layer (alongside FR-7/FR-8/FR-9/FR-11's shared functions), not duplicated per route handler. |\n\n## Non-Functional Requirements\n\n| ID | Architectural Concern | Notes |\n|----|------------------------|-------|\n| NFR-1 | Design System (MUI-only) | Every visible element across sections/courses/enrollment screens is MUI/MUI-X only (DataTable, Autocomplete, Tabs, Dialog, Drawer, `useToast()`), looked up via the MUI MCP server first; no Tailwind/shadcn/Radix/react-select. Applies uniformly — unlike the prior PRD, there's no template-rendering exemption needed here (no React Email in scope). |\n| NFR-2 | Data Model | One-section-per-student-per-year enforced by the DB unique constraint on `SectionMember`, not just app code — directly backs FR-1's schema and is the safety net under FR-3's app-level homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (which has no DB constraint and must be designed knowing that). |\n| NFR-3 | Performance | 30 students × 8 core courses (240 enrollments) in under 1s — a batching requirement on FR-7's auto-enroll path specifically; `arch-design-system` should spec `createMany`/batched writes the same way the enrollment engine is designed, not per-row inserts. |\n| NFR-4 | Privacy/Roster Scrubbing | Students see classmates' names only on the Roster tab and `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` — no email/admission number/profile link. A response-shape rule on FR-17's Roster tab and FR-23's roster endpoint; must be enforced server-side