{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgT4SJcQ7VGBXXeK15X5d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0189RWjj6RexZPcxBn6uUABD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic\nstructure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03\n(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04\n(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both\nresolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.\n\n**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s\n`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the\nfirst requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"\nunder an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the\ngrouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional\nfield, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small\nMUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;\nitems without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change\nthat satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages\nregistry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add\n`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they\nland, with no further schema change.\n\n**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from\nPRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described\nin the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new\n`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around\n`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object\n`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and\ndoes **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.\nConsolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is\nexplicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not\nschedule that consolidation here.\n\n**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two\nservice-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:\nFR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section\nrequired iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity\nchecks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same\n`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted\nas good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write\nconcurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to\nfix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on\nthese two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,\nhomeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)\n`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus\n`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including\nall four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what\nFR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below\nreads/writes.\n\n### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`\nThe single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,\nFR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions\n(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens\nits own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per\ntech-stack ADR-1):\n\n- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`\n  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below\n  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A\n  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per\n  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per\n  route.\n- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing\n  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs\n  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no\n  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip\n  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row\n  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course\n  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).\n- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:\n  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE\n  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls\n  `audit()`.\n- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then\n  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,\n  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.\n\nFR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both\ncreate `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the\nsection's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry\npoints, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.\n\nFR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active\nrosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter\napplied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,\ncourse roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.\n\n### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,\nFR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)\nand the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level\nadvanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not\nreusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot\nstructural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on\n`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement\nenroll/drop.\n\n### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`\n(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"\nvalidator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side\ncheck and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a\nrefinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on\na non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`\ncreate/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,\nreused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this\npicker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.\n\n### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`\nFR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and\n`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per\nDecision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by\n`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster\nendpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once\nhere, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's\nstated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this\nPRD's scope.\n\n### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\nFR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER\nbranch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section\nmembership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/\nPRD-04 callers unchanged.\n\n### Course public surface\n`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing\n`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers\n`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;\nSTUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`\nfiltering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a\nread-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.\n\n**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'\nnames only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query\n(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when\n`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component\nand `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the\ndata layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.\n\n### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)\nRead view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query\n(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE\nenrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,\ngrouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —\nno new parent-fanout code).\n\n### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)\n`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible\nflat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get\n`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.\n\n### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)\nNew \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +\nteacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses\nFR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the\nstudent page (no new access function).\n\n### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`\nEvery route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`\n→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the\nexisting success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route\nlayer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside\nthe same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it\ninternally so routes don't duplicate the call.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**\n`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST\n/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens\n`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →\n`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the\nuniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course\n`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →\ncommit → envelope response.\n\n**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →\n`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping\n`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old\nCORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for\nthe whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.\n\n**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →\n`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`\n(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course\nagainst current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.\n\n**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET\n/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service\n.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →\nenvelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.\n\n**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST\n/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`\nexisting → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural\n`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no\n`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |\n| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |\n| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |\n| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |\n| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |\n| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |\n| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |\n| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |\n| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |\n| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |\n| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |\n| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |\n| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |\n| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |\n| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |\n| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |\n| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |\n| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |\n| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |\n| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |\n| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |\n| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |\n| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |\n| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |\n| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |\n\n## Status\n\n`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no\nopen gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond\nthe NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":700,"cache_read_input_tokens":42516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":700},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6adde39-f92b-490f-9ef1-b8393dd3c9ab","uuid":"72496eff-68f7-4e54-876c-57f442b037f7","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:31:43.195Z","request_id":"req_011CgT4SJ3RRvueJWHHbpJdB"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0189RWjj6RexZPcxBn6uUABD","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6adde39-f92b-490f-9ef1-b8393dd3c9ab","uuid":"7c7617f8-2319-4559-b61a-d6905d4f914c","timestamp":"2026-10-27T16:31:43.308Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic\nstructure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03\n(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04\n(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both\nresolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.\n\n**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s\n`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the\nfirst requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"\nunder an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the\ngrouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional\nfield, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small\nMUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;\nitems without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change\nthat satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages\nregistry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add\n`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they\nland, with no further schema change.\n\n**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from\nPRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described\nin the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new\n`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around\n`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object\n`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and\ndoes **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.\nConsolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is\nexplicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not\nschedule that consolidation here.\n\n**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two\nservice-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:\nFR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section\nrequired iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity\nchecks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same\n`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted\nas good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write\nconcurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to\nfix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on\nthese two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,\nhomeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)\n`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus\n`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including\nall four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what\nFR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below\nreads/writes.\n\n### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`\nThe single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,\nFR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions\n(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens\nits own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per\ntech-stack ADR-1):\n\n- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`\n  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below\n  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A\n  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per\n  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per\n  route.\n- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing\n  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs\n  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no\n  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip\n  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row\n  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course\n  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).\n- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:\n  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE\n  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls\n  `audit()`.\n- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then\n  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,\n  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.\n\nFR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both\ncreate `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the\nsection's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry\npoints, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.\n\nFR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active\nrosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter\napplied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,\ncourse roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.\n\n### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,\nFR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)\nand the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level\nadvanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not\nreusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot\nstructural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on\n`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement\nenroll/drop.\n\n### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`\n(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"\nvalidator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side\ncheck and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a\nrefinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on\na non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`\ncreate/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,\nreused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this\npicker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.\n\n### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`\nFR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and\n`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per\nDecision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by\n`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster\nendpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once\nhere, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's\nstated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this\nPRD's scope.\n\n### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\nFR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER\nbranch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section\nmembership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/\nPRD-04 callers unchanged.\n\n### Course public surface\n`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing\n`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers\n`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;\nSTUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`\nfiltering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a\nread-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.\n\n**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'\nnames only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query\n(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when\n`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component\nand `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the\ndata layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.\n\n### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)\nRead view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query\n(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE\nenrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,\ngrouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —\nno new parent-fanout code).\n\n### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)\n`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible\nflat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get\n`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.\n\n### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)\nNew \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +\nteacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses\nFR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the\nstudent page (no new access function).\n\n### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`\nEvery route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`\n→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the\nexisting success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route\nlayer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside\nthe same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it\ninternally so routes don't duplicate the call.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**\n`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST\n/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens\n`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →\n`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the\nuniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course\n`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →\ncommit → envelope response.\n\n**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →\n`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping\n`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old\nCORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for\nthe whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.\n\n**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →\n`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`\n(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course\nagainst current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.\n\n**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET\n/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service\n.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →\nenvelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.\n\n**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST\n/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`\nexisting → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural\n`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no\n`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |\n| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |\n| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |\n| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |\n| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |\n| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |\n| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |\n| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |\n| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |\n| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |\n| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |\n| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |\n| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |\n| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |\n| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |\n| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |\n| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |\n| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |\n| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |\n| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |\n| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |\n| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |\n| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |\n| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |\n| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |\n\n## Status\n\n`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no\nopen gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond\nthe NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":226,"newStart":1,"newLines":251,"lines":["-# System Design — ticket abcd-04 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email)","+# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)"," "," Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete"," "," ## Overview"," ","-PRD-04 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-01 (auth/RBAC,","-design-only — not landed), PRD-02 (academic structure) and PRD-03 (user","-management). Intake reports **97% confidence and zero blockers**","-(`handoff-to-architect.json`); the one MEDIUM-confidence item (FR-23, exact","-nav entries) is resolved below rather than carried forward as a gap.","+PRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic","+structure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03","+(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04","+(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**","+(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both","+resolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps."," ","-**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes","-the design — the same PRD-01 sequencing gap PRD-03's system-design.md","-already flagged:** every source PRD, including this one, documents","-`src/server/auth/permissions.ts` exporting `requireUser()` and","-`requireRole()`. That file does not exist. `src/server/auth/` contains only","-`requireRole.ts` — a placeholder that returns a hardcoded ADMIN identity and","-checks role — and `student-access.ts`. There is no `requireUser()`","-anywhere in `src/`. NFR-7 requires \"own-notifications-only\" checks on every","-user-facing route (`GET /api/notifications`, read/unread, preferences),","-which needs a resolved *user identity*, not just a role gate. Since PRD-01","-has not landed, this design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — the same","-placeholder `requireRole.ts` already exports, called with every role —","-everywhere a real `requireUser()` would go, documented inline as a","-sequencing dependency (Component 12 below) exactly as PRD-03's Component 20","-did for `sendInvite`. No new auth module is built here (that is PRD-01's","-job); call sites are written so swapping the placeholder for the real","-`requireUser()` later is a one-file change, not a per-route rewrite.","+**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s","+`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the","+first requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"","+under an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the","+grouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional","+field, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small","+MUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;","+items without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change","+that satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages","+registry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add","+`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they","+land, with no further schema change."," ","-Second brownfield fact confirmed directly in source: `src/server/services/","-users.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)` (lines ~385-390) is a logging-only stub","-returning `{ id, inviteSentAt }`. FR-9 replaces its *body* with a real","-`sendAuthEmail()` call while preserving that exact signature, so PRD-03's","-call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, the create-user \"send invitation\"","-checkbox) do not change.","+**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from","+PRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described","+in the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`","+(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new","+`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around","+`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object","+`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and","+does **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.","+Consolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is","+explicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not","+schedule that consolidation here."," ","-No new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`","-(ADR-1 through ADR-6): existing stack only, Nodemailer + console transport,","-`@react-email/components` for templates (the one explicit exemption from","-the MUI-only rule — scoped to `src/server/email/templates/**`), raw","-`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for dispatch (no queue library), one dispatch","-function behind two thin drivers (HTTP route + loop script), a compile-time","-type registry (no DB table), in-memory scheduling for both the stuck-row","-recovery and the daily purge. This document arranges those choices into","-components, data flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability.","+**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two","+service-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:","+FR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section","+required iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity","+checks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same","+`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted","+as good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write","+concurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to","+fix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on","+these two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,","+homeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign."," ","-Two chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed","-below as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route","-code: **`notify()`** (FR-3/4/5/6) and **`dispatchEmails()`** (FR-10/11).","-One list/read service backs both the bell popover (FR-15) and the","-`/notifications` page (FR-16) — not two query paths. FR-23's nav entries","-are resolved here (Component 11) rather than left open.","-"," ## Component Breakdown"," ","-| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |","-|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|","-| 1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum, exactly per the schema block in `04-notifications.md` FR-1 (composite index `Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt)`, `EmailOutbox(status, nextAttemptAt)`) | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-3, NFR-4 |","-| 2 | Notification Type Registry | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const object (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles) across ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM; seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`; `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is `notify()`'s type parameter so unknown keys are a compile error (FR-3) | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-2, FR-3 |","-| 3 | Notification Service (`notify()`) | `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`: filters out archived/disabled users, resolves per-user `NotificationPreference` (falling back to registry defaults), `createMany` for `Notification` rows where in-app applies (including when `mandatoryInApp` overrides an off preference), `createMany` for `EmailOutbox` rows where email applies and the user has an email; never throws — failures logged via `logger`, caller's own transaction already committed by the time this runs; `link` values validated as `/`-prefixed relative paths before write (NFR-5) | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-5 |","-| 4 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })`: expands each student id to itself + linked parent ids via the existing `ParentStudentLink` table (PRD-03's model, read-only here), dedupes, calls Component 3 once with the combined id list — no new link model | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` (co-located, thin wrapper) | FR-6 |","-| 5 | Email Templates | `BaseLayout` (logo/name header, content slot, footer with school address + \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` + required disclosure sentence) plus `invite`, `password-reset`, `generic-notification` templates, each rendered via `@react-email/render`'s `render()` for HTML and `render(..., { plainText: true })` for text — one render call backs both `EmailOutbox.html`/`.text` columns so the two parts can't drift; all interpolated user text passes through React Email's escaping (NFR-5's HTML-escape rule) | `src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx`, `invite.tsx`, `password-reset.tsx`, `generic-notification.tsx` | FR-7, FR-8, NFR-5, NFR-6 |","-| 6 | Auth Email Integration | `sendAuthEmail()` replaces the body of the existing `sendInvite()` stub in `src/server/services/users.ts` (same exported signature `(userId) => Promise<{ id, inviteSentAt }>`, so PRD-03's call sites are untouched): looks up the user, renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset` template, inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (bypasses Component 3 — auth emails are not user-preference-gated), returns the existing shape | `src/server/services/users.ts` (edit, not new file) | FR-9 |","-| 7 | Email Transport | One module building either a real SMTP `nodemailer.createTransport` or a `console` transport (logs subject/recipient/text) from `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (default `console` in dev), reading `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`; sets the `List-Unsubscribe` header on every send pointing at `/account/notifications` (NFR-6) | `src/server/email/transport.ts`, env vars in `.env.example` | FR-13, NFR-6 |","-| 8 | Email Dispatcher (`dispatchEmails()`) | One function: (a) recovers rows stuck in `SENDING` >10 min back to `PENDING` (NFR-4), (b) `prisma.$transaction` containing `$queryRaw SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim up to `batchSize` (default 50) `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now`, flips them to `SENDING`; (c) outside the lock, sends each via Component 7's transport, marks `SENT`/`sentAt` on success or applies the FR-11 backoff (1/5/15/60/240 min across attempts 1-5, `FAILED` after the 5th) on failure; also runs Component 9's purge once per calendar day via an in-memory last-run timestamp checked at the top of each call | `src/server/email/dispatcher.ts` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-4 |","-| 9 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()`: deletes `Notification` rows with `createdAt` older than 180 days; a plain function called from Component 8's daily check, not a separate cron/queue | `src/server/notifications/purge.ts` | FR-17 |","-| 10 | Dispatch Drivers | Two thin callers of Component 8: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET` check, 401 via standard error envelope on mismatch — NFR-8) returning `{ sent, failed, retried }`; and `npm run worker:email`, a `tsx`-run Node script looping Component 8 every 15s (matches the existing `db:seed` script pattern) | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `scripts/worker-email.ts` | FR-12, NFR-8 |","-| 11 | Notification List/Read Service | One query module: `listNotifications({ userId, unread?, category?, page, pageSize })` (own-rows-only, joins registry metadata for category/label), `getUnreadCount(userId)` (indexed by Component 1's composite index, NFR-3's <50ms budget), `markRead(userId, id)` / `markUnread` / `markAllRead(userId)` — the single implementation backing both the popover (FR-15) and the `/notifications` page (FR-16) | `src/server/notifications/list.ts` | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-3 |","-| 12 | Auth Touchpoint (sequencing dependency) | Every user-facing notification/preferences route calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` where a real `requireUser()` is specified — see Overview finding. `ADMIN`-only routes (email-log, test-send) call `requireRole('ADMIN')` directly, already real today. The internal dispatch route uses its own `CRON_SECRET` bearer check (Component 10), not this helper. One-file swap when PRD-01's real `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` lands | *(calls into existing `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`; no new file)* | NFR-7 |","-| 13 | Bell/Popover UI | Replaces the static `Badge badgeContent={0}` in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (~line 141) with a live MUI `IconButton` + `Badge` driven by a shared `useUnreadCount()` hook (`fetch` + `setInterval(30_000)`, paused on `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'` via a `visibilitychange` listener, \"9+\" cap above 9); clicking opens an MUI `Popover` with a `List` of the 10 most recent notifications from Component 11 (unread bold + dot, 2-line-clamped body, relative time), click marks read + navigates to `link`; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\" | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (edit), `src/hooks/useUnreadCount.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` | FR-14, FR-15 |","-| 14 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page) `DataTable`-less simple MUI `List`/`Table` over Component 11, All/Unread `Tabs`, category filter, bulk \"Mark all as read\", per-row read/unread toggle | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` | FR-16 |","-| 15 | Preferences UI + API | `/account/notifications`: MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader` rows) over Component 2's registry filtered to the current user's role, each row an In-app `Switch` + Email `Switch` (mandatory-in-app types render a disabled `Switch` + `Tooltip` \"Required by the school\"); `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves one `{type, inApp, email}` row immediately, client does optimistic update with rollback on a non-2xx response; server rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types with `VALIDATION_ERROR` (defense in depth alongside the disabled switch) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` | FR-18, FR-19, FR-22, NFR-7 |","-| 16 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table over `EmailOutbox` (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), status filter, \"Retry now\" row action (`attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now` — same reset shape Component 8 expects on its next pass), \"Send test notification to me\" button calling Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'` for the current admin | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts`, `.../email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` | FR-20 |","-| 17 | REST API Surface | All 12 endpoints from the PRD's API table, built on `src/server/http.ts`'s existing `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError`/`AppError` conventions — finalized verbatim in `api-contracts.json` by `arch-api-contracts` | `src/app/api/notifications/**`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/**`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/**`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/**`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/**` | FR-21 |","-| 18 | Navigation | Resolves FR-23 (MEDIUM confidence in intake): add \"Notifications\" (`/notifications`, all roles) under the existing top-level entries, and \"Email log\" (`/admin/email-log`, ADMIN only) grouped with other admin-only entries — following the existing flat `NavItem[]` + `roles` convention (no \"Administration\" group exists yet in `navigation.ts`; PRD-02/03's group ideas are a later PRD's concern, not introduced here) | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-23 |","-| 19 | Design System (MUI-only, directory-scoped) | Every app-UI surface (bell, popover, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only, looked up via the MUI MCP server; `src/server/email/templates/**` is the one ESLint `no-restricted-imports` exemption glob so `@react-email/components` imports there aren't flagged, while every other path stays MUI-only | ESLint config (exemption glob addition), reuses existing `theme.ts` | NFR-1 |","-| 20 | Seed Data | 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`, linking to `/dashboard` — depends on Component 1's schema and Component 2's registry key existing first | `prisma/seed.ts` (extend existing script) | FR-24 |","-| 21 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (registry compile-time key rejection via a type-level test, retry-backoff schedule math, link-path validator, CSV-free here — N/A); Vitest integration (`notify()` batching round-trip count, `dispatchEmails()` claim-and-send with concurrent-dispatcher race, stuck-row recovery, mandatory-preference server rejection); Playwright e2e (bell unread count updates after `notify()`, mark-all-read, preferences toggle persists, admin retry-now, admin test-send) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-9 |","+### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)","+`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus","+`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including","+all four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what","+FR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below","+reads/writes."," ","-Dependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (Registry) depends","-on 1's `type: String` column and feeds 3, 4, 11, 15, 16. 3 (`notify()`)","-depends on 1, 2 and is called by 4, 6 (indirectly — 6 bypasses it, see its","-row), 16's test-send, and every later PRD per FR-6's stated intent. 5","-(Templates) feeds 6 and 8. 6 edits an existing file and depends on 5. 7","-feeds 8. 8 (`dispatchEmails`) depends on 1, 5 (indirectly via rows already","-rendered), 7, 9, and is called only by 10. 11 depends on 1, 2 and feeds 13,","-14. 12 is a calling convention, not a buildable unit — it gates 11, 13, 14,","-15, 16's non-ADMIN-already-real routes. 17 wraps 3/8/11/15/16 behind routes.","-18–20 are independent leaf tasks. 21 wraps all of the above.","+### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`","+The single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,","+FR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions","+(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens","+its own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per","+tech-stack ADR-1):"," ","-## Data Flow","+- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`","+  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below","+  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A","+  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per","+  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per","+  route.","+- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`","+  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing","+  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs","+  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no","+  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip","+  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row","+  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course","+  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).","+- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:","+  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE","+  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls","+  `audit()`.","+- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`","+  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then","+  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,","+  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`."," ","-**`notify()` call (FR-3/4/5/6, NFR-2, NFR-5):**","-1. Caller (any service, after its own transaction commits) invokes","-   `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`. Component 3","-   validates `link` is `/`-prefixed if present (NFR-5) — throws","-   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', ...)` only for this programmer-error case;","-   every other failure mode (missing user, send failure) is logged, not","-   thrown.","-2. Filters `userIds` to non-archived, non-disabled users in one query, then","-   reads each remaining user's `NotificationPreference` row for `type`","-   (one query, `findMany` with `in`), falling back to Component 2's","-   registry defaults (`defaultEmail`, `mandatoryInApp`) where no row exists.","-3. One `createMany` writes all qualifying `Notification` rows (in-app","-   enabled OR `mandatoryInApp`); one `createMany` writes all qualifying","-   `EmailOutbox` rows (email enabled AND user has an email) — ≤3 round","-   trips total per FR-5, holding NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/<2s budget.","-4. `notifyStudentAndParents` (Component 4) is a pre-step: resolve","-   `studentIds` → student + linked-parent ids via `ParentStudentLink`","-   (existing table), dedupe, then run steps 1-3 once over the combined list.","+FR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both","+create `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the","+section's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry","+points, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic."," ","-**Email dispatch (FR-10/11/12, NFR-4):**","-1. Either driver (Component 10) calls `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })`.","-2. Top of the call: `UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='PENDING' WHERE","-   status='SENDING' AND updatedAt-equivalent < now()-10min` (recovers","-   crashed-mid-send rows, NFR-4) — tracked via `nextAttemptAt`/a dedicated","-   timestamp set when flipped to `SENDING`.","-3. One `prisma.$transaction` runs `SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE","-   status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now() ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\"","-   LIMIT $batchSize FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then `UPDATE ... SET","-   status='SENDING'` on exactly those ids — this is the only raw SQL in the","-   codebase, isolated to this function (no double-send across concurrent","-   dispatchers, NFR-4).","-4. Outside the lock: each claimed row renders through Component 7's","-   transport. Success → `status='SENT', sentAt=now()`. Failure → bump","-   `attempts`; if `attempts < 5`, `status='PENDING'` with `nextAttemptAt`","-   set per the 1/5/15/60/240-minute schedule (FR-11); at `attempts === 5`,","-   `status='FAILED'`.","-5. Once per calendar day (in-memory last-run check): call Component 9's","-   `purgeOldNotifications()`.","+FR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active","+rosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter","+applied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,","+course roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes."," ","-**Auth email (FR-9):**","-1. PRD-03 call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, \"send invitation now\"","-   checkbox) call `sendInvite(userId)` exactly as before — signature","-   unchanged.","-2. Internally it now renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset`","-   template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (no preference gate","-   — auth emails are mandatory), then returns the same `{ id,","-   inviteSentAt }` shape the stub always returned.","+### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`","+CRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,","+FR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)","+and the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level","+advanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not","+reusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot","+structural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on","+`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement","+enroll/drop."," ","-**Bell + popover (FR-14/15):**","-1. `useUnreadCount()` polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s","-   while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`; a `visibilitychange`","-   listener clears/restarts the interval.","-2. Popover open → one call to Component 11's `listNotifications` capped at","-   10 rows, newest first. Item click → `POST /api/notifications/:id/read`","-   then client-side navigate to `link`.","+### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`","+CRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`","+(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"","+validator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side","+check and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a","+refinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on","+a non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`","+create/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,","+reused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this","+picker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead."," ","-**Preferences (FR-18/19/22):**","-1. Page load merges Component 2's registry (filtered to the signed-in","-   user's role) with the user's existing `NotificationPreference` rows","-   (defaults where absent).","-2. Switch toggle → optimistic local state update + `PUT","-   /api/me/notification-preferences` with `{type, inApp, email}`; server","-   rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types before any write","-   (`VALIDATION_ERROR`); a non-2xx response rolls the toggle back","-   client-side.","+### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`","+FR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and","+`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per","+Decision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by","+`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster","+endpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once","+here, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's","+stated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this","+PRD's scope."," ","-**Admin email log (FR-20):** pure read/action surface over `EmailOutbox`","-(Component 1) — \"Retry now\" is a plain update (`attempts=0,","-status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now()`), picked up by the next","-`dispatchEmails()` pass (step 3 above), not a separate send path. \"Send","-test\" is a direct call into Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'`.","+### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`","+FR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER","+branch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section","+membership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/","+PRD-04 callers unchanged."," ","+### Course public surface","+`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing","+`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers","+`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;","+STUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`","+filtering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a","+read-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.","+","+**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'","+names only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query","+(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when","+`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component","+and `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the","+data layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.","+","+### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)","+Read view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query","+(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE","+enrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,","+grouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —","+no new parent-fanout code).","+","+### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)","+`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible","+flat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get","+`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.","+","+### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)","+New \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +","+teacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses","+FR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the","+student page (no new access function).","+","+### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`","+Every route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`","+→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the","+existing success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route","+layer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside","+the same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it","+internally so routes don't duplicate the call.","+","+## Data Flow","+","+**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**","+`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST","+/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens","+`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →","+`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the","+uniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course","+`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →","+commit → envelope response.","+","+**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →","+`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping","+`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old","+CORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for","+the whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.","+","+**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →","+`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`","+(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course","+against current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.","+","+**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET","+/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service","+.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →","+envelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.","+","+**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST","+/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`","+existing → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural","+`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no","+`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.","+"," ## Requirements Traceability"," "," | Requirement | Design Element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | Component 1 — Prisma models/enum |","-| FR-2 | Component 2 — type registry |","-| FR-3 | Component 2 (compile-time union) + Component 3 (`notify()` signature) |","-| FR-4 | Component 3 — core `notify()` logic |","-| FR-5 | Component 3 — `createMany` batching + never-throw contract |","-| FR-6 | Component 4 — `notifyStudentAndParents` |","-| FR-7 | Component 5 — base layout + HTML/text render |","-| FR-8 | Component 5 — invite/password-reset/generic templates |","-| FR-9 | Component 6 — `sendAuthEmail()` swap, signature preserved |","-| FR-10 | Component 8 — `dispatchEmails()` claim/send/update |","-| FR-11 | Component 8 — retry backoff schedule |","-| FR-12 | Component 10 — HTTP route + worker script, one shared function |","-| FR-13 | Component 7 — transport + env vars |","-| FR-14 | Component 13 — bell poll/pause |","-| FR-15 | Component 13 — popover list (via Component 11) |","-| FR-16 | Component 14 — `/notifications` page (via Component 11) |","-| FR-17 | Component 9 — purge, triggered from Component 8 |","-| FR-18 | Component 15 — preferences table UI |","-| FR-19 | Component 15 — optimistic PUT |","-| FR-20 | Component 16 — admin email log |","-| FR-21 | Component 17 — full REST surface |","-| FR-22 | Component 15 — server-side mandatory-type rejection |","-| FR-23 | Component 18 — nav entries (MEDIUM confidence resolved: flat entries, not a new group) |","-| FR-24 | Component 20 — seed rows |","-| NFR-1 | Component 19 — MUI-only, directory-scoped ESLint exemption |","-| NFR-2 | Component 3 — ≤3-round-trip batching |","-| NFR-3 | Component 1 (index) + Component 11 (`getUnreadCount` query shape) |","-| NFR-4 | Component 8 — `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` + stuck-row recovery |","-| NFR-5 | Component 3 (`link` validation) + Component 5 (template escaping) |","-| NFR-6 | Component 5 (HTML+text render) + Component 7 (`List-Unsubscribe` header) |","-| NFR-7 | Component 12 — `requireRole` placeholder standing in for `requireUser` (sequencing dependency, see Overview) + Component 15/16's ADMIN/own-row checks |","-| NFR-8 | Component 10 — `CRON_SECRET` bearer check, 401 on mismatch |","-| NFR-9 | Component 21 — test harness |","-| NFR-10 | All components — no SMS/push/websockets/digests introduced |","+| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |","+| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |","+| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |","+| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |","+| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |","+| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |","+| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |","+| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |","+| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |","+| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |","+| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |","+| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |","+| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |","+| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |","+| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |","+| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |","+| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |","+| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |","+| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |","+| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |","+| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |","+| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |","+| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |","+| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |","+| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |","+| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |","+| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |","+| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |","+| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |","+| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |","+| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |"," "," ## Status"," ","-Complete. All 24 FR ids and 10 NFR ids are accounted for above; none were","-dropped. FR-23's MEDIUM-confidence nav question is resolved (flat entries","-under existing roles-based filtering, no new nav group introduced since","-`navigation.ts` has none today). Two things carry forward for","-`arch-api-contracts` and `dev-planning`:","-","-1. **Sequencing dependency on PRD-01 (Component 12):** `src/server/auth/","-   permissions.ts`'s `requireUser()` does not exist in `src/` yet — only","-   `requireRole.ts`'s ADMIN-placeholder and `student-access.ts` do. This","-   design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` everywhere a real `requireUser()`","-   would go on user-facing notification/preferences routes, so the later","-   swap to PRD-01's real session-aware helper is confined to that one file","-   plus each route's import line — not a redesign. ADMIN-only and","-   `CRON_SECRET`-gated routes need no placeholder; they already have a real","-   check today.","-2. **Ready for `arch-api-contracts`:** the 12-endpoint API table in","-   `04-notifications.md` is fully specified (methods, paths, roles, notes)","-   and maps 1:1 onto Components 3/8/11/15/16 above — no net-new business","-   logic to invent at the route layer, only envelope/pagination/error-code","-   wiring per `src/server/http.ts`'s existing conventions.","+`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no","+open gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond","+the NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker)."]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — ticket abcd-04 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-01 (auth/RBAC,\ndesign-only — not landed), PRD-02 (academic structure) and PRD-03 (user\nmanagement). Intake reports **97% confidence and zero blockers**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`); the one MEDIUM-confidence item (FR-23, exact\nnav entries) is resolved below rather than carried forward as a gap.\n\n**Finding beyond intake's blocker list, surfaced here because it changes\nthe design — the same PRD-01 sequencing gap PRD-03's system-design.md\nalready flagged:** every source PRD, including this one, documents\n`src/server/auth/permissions.ts` exporting `requireUser()` and\n`requireRole()`. That file does not exist. `src/server/auth/` contains only\n`requireRole.ts` — a placeholder that returns a hardcoded ADMIN identity and\nchecks role — and `student-access.ts`. There is no `requireUser()`\nanywhere in `src/`. NFR-7 requires \"own-notifications-only\" checks on every\nuser-facing route (`GET /api/notifications`, read/unread, preferences),\nwhich needs a resolved *user identity*, not just a role gate. Since PRD-01\nhas not landed, this design calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — the same\nplaceholder `requireRole.ts` already exports, called with every role —\neverywhere a real `requireUser()` would go, documented inline as a\nsequencing dependency (Component 12 below) exactly as PRD-03's Component 20\ndid for `sendInvite`. No new auth module is built here (that is PRD-01's\njob); call sites are written so swapping the placeholder for the real\n`requireUser()` later is a one-file change, not a per-route rewrite.\n\nSecond brownfield fact confirmed directly in source: `src/server/services/\nusers.ts`'s `sendInvite(userId)` (lines ~385-390) is a logging-only stub\nreturning `{ id, inviteSentAt }`. FR-9 replaces its *body* with a real\n`sendAuthEmail()` call while preserving that exact signature, so PRD-03's\ncall sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, the create-user \"send invitation\"\ncheckbox) do not change.\n\nNo new tech decisions are made here beyond `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n(ADR-1 through ADR-6): existing stack only, Nodemailer + console transport,\n`@react-email/components` for templates (the one explicit exemption from\nthe MUI-only rule — scoped to `src/server/email/templates/**`), raw\n`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` for dispatch (no queue library), one dispatch\nfunction behind two thin drivers (HTTP route + loop script), a compile-time\ntype registry (no DB table), in-memory scheduling for both the stuck-row\nrecovery and the daily purge. This document arranges those choices into\ncomponents, data flow, and per-FR/NFR traceability.\n\nTwo chokepoints recur across nearly every requirement and are designed\nbelow as named, independently-testable modules rather than inline route\ncode: **`notify()`** (FR-3/4/5/6) and **`dispatchEmails()`** (FR-10/11).\nOne list/read service backs both the bell popover (FR-15) and the\n`/notifications` page (FR-16) — not two query paths. FR-23's nav entries\nare resolved here (Component 11) rather than left open.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n| # | Component | Responsibility | Key files | FR/NFR |\n|---|-----------|-----------------|------------|--------|\n| 1 | Data Model | `Notification`, `NotificationPreference`, `EmailOutbox` + `EmailStatus` enum, exactly per the schema block in `04-notifications.md` FR-1 (composite index `Notification(userId, readAt, createdAt)`, `EmailOutbox(status, nextAttemptAt)`) | `prisma/schema.prisma` | FR-1, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| 2 | Notification Type Registry | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const object (label/description/category/defaultEmail/mandatoryInApp/roles) across ACCOUNT/ACADEMIC/ATTENDANCE/COMMUNICATION/FINANCE/SYSTEM; seeded with `account.invite`, `account.password_reset`, `system.test`; `keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is `notify()`'s type parameter so unknown keys are a compile error (FR-3) | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-2, FR-3 |\n| 3 | Notification Service (`notify()`) | `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`: filters out archived/disabled users, resolves per-user `NotificationPreference` (falling back to registry defaults), `createMany` for `Notification` rows where in-app applies (including when `mandatoryInApp` overrides an off preference), `createMany` for `EmailOutbox` rows where email applies and the user has an email; never throws — failures logged via `logger`, caller's own transaction already committed by the time this runs; `link` values validated as `/`-prefixed relative paths before write (NFR-5) | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, NFR-2, NFR-5 |\n| 4 | Family Fan-out Helper | `notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })`: expands each student id to itself + linked parent ids via the existing `ParentStudentLink` table (PRD-03's model, read-only here), dedupes, calls Component 3 once with the combined id list — no new link model | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` (co-located, thin wrapper) | FR-6 |\n| 5 | Email Templates | `BaseLayout` (logo/name header, content slot, footer with school address + \"Manage email preferences\" link to `/account/notifications` + required disclosure sentence) plus `invite`, `password-reset`, `generic-notification` templates, each rendered via `@react-email/render`'s `render()` for HTML and `render(..., { plainText: true })` for text — one render call backs both `EmailOutbox.html`/`.text` columns so the two parts can't drift; all interpolated user text passes through React Email's escaping (NFR-5's HTML-escape rule) | `src/server/email/templates/BaseLayout.tsx`, `invite.tsx`, `password-reset.tsx`, `generic-notification.tsx` | FR-7, FR-8, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| 6 | Auth Email Integration | `sendAuthEmail()` replaces the body of the existing `sendInvite()` stub in `src/server/services/users.ts` (same exported signature `(userId) => Promise<{ id, inviteSentAt }>`, so PRD-03's call sites are untouched): looks up the user, renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset` template, inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (bypasses Component 3 — auth emails are not user-preference-gated), returns the existing shape | `src/server/services/users.ts` (edit, not new file) | FR-9 |\n| 7 | Email Transport | One module building either a real SMTP `nodemailer.createTransport` or a `console` transport (logs subject/recipient/text) from `EMAIL_TRANSPORT` (default `console` in dev), reading `SMTP_HOST/PORT/USER/PASS/SECURE`, `EMAIL_FROM`; sets the `List-Unsubscribe` header on every send pointing at `/account/notifications` (NFR-6) | `src/server/email/transport.ts`, env vars in `.env.example` | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| 8 | Email Dispatcher (`dispatchEmails()`) | One function: (a) recovers rows stuck in `SENDING` >10 min back to `PENDING` (NFR-4), (b) `prisma.$transaction` containing `$queryRaw SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` to claim up to `batchSize` (default 50) `PENDING` rows with `nextAttemptAt <= now`, flips them to `SENDING`; (c) outside the lock, sends each via Component 7's transport, marks `SENT`/`sentAt` on success or applies the FR-11 backoff (1/5/15/60/240 min across attempts 1-5, `FAILED` after the 5th) on failure; also runs Component 9's purge once per calendar day via an in-memory last-run timestamp checked at the top of each call | `src/server/email/dispatcher.ts` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-4 |\n| 9 | Retention Job | `purgeOldNotifications()`: deletes `Notification` rows with `createdAt` older than 180 days; a plain function called from Component 8's daily check, not a separate cron/queue | `src/server/notifications/purge.ts` | FR-17 |\n| 10 | Dispatch Drivers | Two thin callers of Component 8: `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (bearer `CRON_SECRET` check, 401 via standard error envelope on mismatch — NFR-8) returning `{ sent, failed, retried }`; and `npm run worker:email`, a `tsx`-run Node script looping Component 8 every 15s (matches the existing `db:seed` script pattern) | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `scripts/worker-email.ts` | FR-12, NFR-8 |\n| 11 | Notification List/Read Service | One query module: `listNotifications({ userId, unread?, category?, page, pageSize })` (own-rows-only, joins registry metadata for category/label), `getUnreadCount(userId)` (indexed by Component 1's composite index, NFR-3's <50ms budget), `markRead(userId, id)` / `markUnread` / `markAllRead(userId)` — the single implementation backing both the popover (FR-15) and the `/notifications` page (FR-16) | `src/server/notifications/list.ts` | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-3 |\n| 12 | Auth Touchpoint (sequencing dependency) | Every user-facing notification/preferences route calls `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` where a real `requireUser()` is specified — see Overview finding. `ADMIN`-only routes (email-log, test-send) call `requireRole('ADMIN')` directly, already real today. The internal dispatch route uses its own `CRON_SECRET` bearer check (Component 10), not this helper. One-file swap when PRD-01's real `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` lands | *(calls into existing `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`; no new file)* | NFR-7 |\n| 13 | Bell/Popover UI | Replaces the static `Badge badgeContent={0}` in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (~line 141) with a live MUI `IconButton` + `Badge` driven by a shared `useUnreadCount()` hook (`fetch` + `setInterval(30_000)`, paused on `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'` via a `visibilitychange` listener, \"9+\" cap above 9); clicking opens an MUI `Popover` with a `List` of the 10 most recent notifications from Component 11 (unread bold + dot, 2-line-clamped body, relative time), click marks read + navigates to `link`; footer \"Mark all as read\" / \"View all\" | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (edit), `src/hooks/useUnreadCount.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` | FR-14, FR-15 |\n| 14 | Notifications Page | `/notifications`: paginated (20/page) `DataTable`-less simple MUI `List`/`Table` over Component 11, All/Unread `Tabs`, category filter, bulk \"Mark all as read\", per-row read/unread toggle | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` | FR-16 |\n| 15 | Preferences UI + API | `/account/notifications`: MUI `Table` grouped by category (`ListSubheader` rows) over Component 2's registry filtered to the current user's role, each row an In-app `Switch` + Email `Switch` (mandatory-in-app types render a disabled `Switch` + `Tooltip` \"Required by the school\"); `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences` saves one `{type, inApp, email}` row immediately, client does optimistic update with rollback on a non-2xx response; server rejects `inApp=false` for `mandatoryInApp` types with `VALIDATION_ERROR` (defense in depth alongside the disabled switch) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` | FR-18, FR-19, FR-22, NFR-7 |\n| 16 | Admin Email Log | `/admin/email-log`: table over `EmailOutbox` (created/recipient/subject/status/attempts/lastError), status filter, \"Retry now\" row action (`attempts=0, status=PENDING, nextAttemptAt=now` — same reset shape Component 8 expects on its next pass), \"Send test notification to me\" button calling Component 3 with `type: 'system.test'` for the current admin | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts`, `.../email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` | FR-20 |\n| 17 | REST API Surface | All 12 endpoints from the PRD's API table, built on `src/server/http.ts`'s existing `ok`/`paginated`/`apiError`/`AppError` conventions — finalized verbatim in `api-contracts.json` by `arch-api-contracts` | `src/app/api/notifications/**`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/**`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/**`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/**`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/**` | FR-21 |\n| 18 | Navigation | Resolves FR-23 (MEDIUM confidence in intake): add \"Notifications\" (`/notifications`, all roles) under the existing top-level entries, and \"Email log\" (`/admin/email-log`, ADMIN only) grouped with other admin-only entries — following the existing flat `NavItem[]` + `roles` convention (no \"Administration\" group exists yet in `navigation.ts`; PRD-02/03's group ideas are a later PRD's concern, not introduced here) | `src/config/navigation.ts` (extend existing array) | FR-23 |\n| 19 | Design System (MUI-only, directory-scoped) | Every app-UI surface (bell, popover, `/notifications`, `/account/notifications`, `/admin/email-log`) built from `@mui/material`/`@mui/icons-material`/MUI X only, looked up via the MUI MCP server; `src/server/email/templates/**` is the one ESLint `no-restricted-imports` exemption glob so `@react-email/components` imports there aren't flagged, while every other path stays MUI-only | ESLint config (exemption glob addition), reuses existing `theme.ts` | NFR-1 |\n| 20 | Seed Data | 3 `system.test` `Notification` rows (1 read, 2 unread) for `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`, linking to `/dashboard` — depends on Component 1's schema and Component 2's registry key existing first | `prisma/seed.ts` (extend existing script) | FR-24 |\n| 21 | Test Harness | Vitest unit (registry compile-time key rejection via a type-level test, retry-backoff schedule math, link-path validator, CSV-free here — N/A); Vitest integration (`notify()` batching round-trip count, `dispatchEmails()` claim-and-send with concurrent-dispatcher race, stuck-row recovery, mandatory-preference server rejection); Playwright e2e (bell unread count updates after `notify()`, mark-all-read, preferences toggle persists, admin retry-now, admin test-send) | `tests/**`, `tests/e2e/**` | NFR-9 |\n\nDependency order: 1 (Data Model) underlies everything. 2 (Registry) depends\non 1's `type: String` column and feeds 3, 4, 11, 15, 16. 3 (`notify()`)\ndepends on 1, 2 and is called by 4, 6 (indirectly — 6 bypasses it, see its\nrow), 16's test-send, and every later PRD per FR-6's stated intent. 5\n(Templates) feeds 6 and 8. 6 edits an existing file and depends on 5. 7\nfeeds 8. 8 (`dispatchEmails`) depends on 1, 5 (indirectly via rows already\nrendered), 7, 9, and is called only by 10. 11 depends on 1, 2 and feeds 13,\n14. 12 is a calling convention, not a buildable unit — it gates 11, 13, 14,\n15, 16's non-ADMIN-already-real routes. 17 wraps 3/8/11/15/16 behind routes.\n18–20 are independent leaf tasks. 21 wraps all of the above.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**`notify()` call (FR-3/4/5/6, NFR-2, NFR-5):**\n1. Caller (any service, after its own transaction commits) invokes\n   `notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email? })`. Component 3\n   validates `link` is `/`-prefixed if present (NFR-5) — throws\n   `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', ...)` only for this programmer-error case;\n   every other failure mode (missing user, send failure) is logged, not\n   thrown.\n2. Filters `userIds` to non-archived, non-disabled users in one query, then\n   reads each remaining user's `NotificationPreference` row for `type`\n   (one query, `findMany` with `in`), falling back to Component 2's\n   registry defaults (`defaultEmail`, `mandatoryInApp`) where no row exists.\n3. One `createMany` writes all qualifying `Notification` rows (in-app\n   enabled OR `mandatoryInApp`); one `createMany` writes all qualifying\n   `EmailOutbox` rows (email enabled AND user has an email) — ≤3 round\n   trips total per FR-5, holding NFR-2's 1,000-recipient/<2s budget.\n4. `notifyStudentAndParents` (Component 4) is a pre-step: resolve\n   `studentIds` → student + linked-parent ids via `ParentStudentLink`\n   (existing table), dedupe, then run steps 1-3 once over the combined list.\n\n**Email dispatch (FR-10/11/12, NFR-4):**\n1. Either driver (Component 10) calls `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 })`.\n2. Top of the call: `UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='PENDING' WHERE\n   status='SENDING' AND updatedAt-equivalent < now()-10min` (recovers\n   crashed-mid-send rows, NFR-4) — tracked via `nextAttemptAt`/a dedicated\n   timestamp set when flipped to `SENDING`.\n3. One `prisma.$transaction` runs `SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE\n   status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\" <= now() ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\"\n   LIMIT $batchSize FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then `UPDATE ... SET\n   status='SENDING'` on exactly those ids — this is the only raw SQL in the\n   codebase, isolated to this function (no double-send across concurrent\n   dispatchers, NFR-4).\n4. Outside the lock: each claimed row renders through Component 7's\n   transport. Success → `status='SENT', sentAt=now()`. Failure → bump\n   `attempts`; if `attempts < 5`, `status='PENDING'` with `nextAttemptAt`\n   set per the 1/5/15/60/240-minute schedule (FR-11); at `attempts === 5`,\n   `status='FAILED'`.\n5. Once per calendar day (in-memory last-run check): call Component 9's\n   `purgeOldNotifications()`.\n\n**Auth email (FR-9):**\n1. PRD-03 call sites (`POST /api/users/:id/invite`, \"send invitation now\"\n   checkbox) call `sendInvite(userId)` exactly as before — signature\n   unchanged.\n2. Internally it now renders Component 5's `invite`/`password-reset`\n   template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly (no preference gate\n   — auth emails are mandatory), then returns the same `{ id,\n   inviteSentAt }` shape the stub always returned.\n\n**Bell + popover (FR-14/15):**\n1. `useUnreadCount()` polls `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` every 30s\n   while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`; a `visibilitychange`\n   listener clears/restarts the interval.\n2. Popover open → one call to Component 11's `listNotifications` capped at\n   10 rows, newest first. Item click → `POST /api/notifications/:id/read`\n   then client-side navigate to `link`.\n\n**Preferences (FR-18/19/22):**\n1. Page load merges Component 2's registry (filtered to the