{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRePygzYAADX1Tw1sAP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1352,"cache_read_input_tokens":57193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1352},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8ecf6ce-8d48-4a6b-879b-0c956e2c759f","uuid":"81f5507c-5fb5-4deb-aa5c-3536c0b9d704","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:37:08.080Z","request_id":"req_011CghRePjK4HRMtFHoHzTvV","thinking_duration_ms":14436,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghRePygzYAADX1Tw1sAP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JKWN7HGkBB9awmAy712ZTj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:\nAuth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,\npassword reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware\ngate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a\nbrownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new\nruntime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed.\n\nBrownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:\n- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,\n  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).\n  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the\n  two AuditLog indexes.\n- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,\n  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.\n  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.\n  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`\n  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).\n- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.\n  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`\n  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.\n- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at\n  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file.\n\n### Intake blockers and how they're resolved\n\n| Blocker | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |\n| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |\n| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |\n\n---\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)\n- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.\n- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code\n  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip\n  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.\n- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._\n\n### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):\n  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`\n  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`\n  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`\n  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)\n  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,\n  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.\n- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):\n  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`\n    and `checkedAt = now`.\n  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.\n  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run\n    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.\n    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.\n    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.\n  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the\n    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would\n    hide an older password change.\n- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.\n- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.\n  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's\n  route matching, so they can live side by side.\n- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._\n\n### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)\nA plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`\ndelegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).\nOrder of checks:\n1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.\n2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).\n3. Look up the user by email.\n4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**\n   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`\n   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly\n   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).\n5. Branches:\n   - missing user → `invalid`\n   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`\n   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`\n   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`\n   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)\n   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user\n6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns\n   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).\n   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a\n   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent\n   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't\n   matter here.\n7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:\n   - `auth.login.success`\n   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only\n   - `auth.lockout`\n   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.\n8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the\n   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to\n   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"\n   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).\n- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._\n\n### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)\nThis is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.\n- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:\n  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,\n    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.\n  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only\n    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.\n  - Returns the raw token.\n- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:\n  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.\n  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong\n    type, is used or is expired.\n- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.\n  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a\n  double-submit fail cleanly.\n- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.\n- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._\n\n### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)\n- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`\n  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.\n- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.\n- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't\n  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales\n  horizontally.\n- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns\n  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.\n- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._\n\n### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)\n- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.\n- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,\n  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.\n- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the\n  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.\n- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`\n  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.\n- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:\n  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.\n  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus\n    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with\n    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.\n  - Every password-setting service calls it.\n- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules\n  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's\n  error response.\n- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._\n\n### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)\nDelete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:\n```ts\ntype SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser\ngetCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)\nrequireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED\nrequireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN\nrequirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')\nrequirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')\n```\n- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.\n  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.\n- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a\n  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.\n  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,\n  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why\n  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.\n- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,\n  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is\n  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.\n- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`\n  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.\n- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.\n- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._\n\n### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`\n  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and\n  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.\n  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.\n  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).\n- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:\n  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that\n     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present\n     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.\n     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely\n     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.\n  2. If the path is public → `next()`.\n  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.\n     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.\n  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.\n- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files\n  with extensions.\n- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the\n  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper\n  on every page and handler.\n- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._\n\n### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)\nRoute handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below\nrecords an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.\n- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.\n  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.\n  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.\n  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and\n     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.\n  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.\n  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**\n     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the\n     design reuses the one sign-in path.\n- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.\n    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the\n    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email\n    was tried before.\n  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,\n    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.\n  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.\n  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.\n- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.\n  2. Policy check, then hash.\n  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,\n     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.\n  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.\n- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:\n  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`\n     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.\n  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.\n  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.\n  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this\n     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail\n     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.\n- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:\n  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam\n    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\n  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.\n  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in\n    audit metadata.\n- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._\n\n### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)\n- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).\n- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.\n  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.\n- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then\n  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged\n  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.\n- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._\n\n### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)\n- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.\n- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.\n- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:\n  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.\n- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._\n\n### 12. App shell and navigation\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:\n  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.\n  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.\n    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.\n  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:\n  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`\n    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.\n  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.\n  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n    That function doesn't need a provider.\n- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._\n\n### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)\n- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.\n- **`login/page.tsx`**:\n  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton\n    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.\n  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error\n    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to\n    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.\n  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.\n  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).\n- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200\n  and the FR-7-style message on 429.\n- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:\n  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the\n    FR-14 Alert copy.\n  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.\n- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows\n  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.\n- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:\n  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.\n  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the\n    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.\n- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):\n  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,\n    driven by `passwordChecks`.\n  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset\n    pages share it.\n- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**\n  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.\n  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to\n    the first invalid field.\n  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.\n- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._\n\n### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)\n- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:\n  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`\n  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password\n- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and\n  log the link with `logger.info`.\n- `office@` stays as it is.\n- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._\n\n### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)\n- **Unit tests:**\n  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`\n  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches\n  - `computeLockout`\n  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`\n  - `safeCallbackUrl`\n- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):\n  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch\n  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`\n  - Audit metadata never contains secrets\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Sign-in/out with seeded users\n  - The failed-login message\n  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through\n    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable\n    from the DB.\n  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages\n- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.\n- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._\n\n---\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**\n1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →\n   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.\n2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt\n   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.\n3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.\n   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.\n4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.\n   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert.\n\n**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**\n1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.\n   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.\n   - No session on `/api` → 401.\n2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`\n   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).\n3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.\n   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.\n4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page).\n\n**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**\n1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`\n   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).\n2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`\n   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.\n   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.\n4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`.\n\n**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**\n1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →\n   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.\n   The response is always the generic message.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash\n   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it\n   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n\n**Change password (FR-23)**\n1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.\n2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a\n   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.\n3. The toast reads \"Password updated\".\n\n---\n\n## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)\n\n| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |\n| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n\nAll custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the\n`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:\n- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`\n- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401\n- `FORBIDDEN` 403\n- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens\n- `RATE_LIMITED` 429\n\n`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).\n\n## New / changed files\n\n**New:**\n- `src/middleware.ts`\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`\n- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`\n- `src/server/services/auth.ts`\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`\n- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`\n- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`\n- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`\n- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`\n- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`\n\n**Changed:**\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes\n- `prisma/seed.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n- `src/server/audit.ts`\n- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`\n- `src/server/services/users.ts`\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`\n- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants\n- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`\n- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly\n\n**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the\ncomment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).\n\n**Skipped on purpose:**\n- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.\n- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.\n- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.\n- Client-side common-password list.\n- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |\n| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |\n| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |\n| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |\n| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |\n| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |\n| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |\n| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |\n| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |\n| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |\n| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |\n| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |\n| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |\n| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |\n| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |\n| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |\n| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |\n| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |\n| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |\n| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |\n| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |\n| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |\n| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |\n| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |\n| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |\n| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |\n| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |\n| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |\n| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |\n| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |\n| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |\n| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |\n| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |\n| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |\n| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |\n| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |\n| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |\n| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |\n| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |\n| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |\n| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |\n| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |\n| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |\n| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1352,"cache_read_input_tokens":57193,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1352},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8ecf6ce-8d48-4a6b-879b-0c956e2c759f","uuid":"dc0c6069-7567-40ed-970f-bd5c34b94ede","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:39:01.328Z","request_id":"req_011CghRePjK4HRMtFHoHzTvV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JKWN7HGkBB9awmAy712ZTj":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:\nAuth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,\npassword reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware\ngate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a\nbrownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new\nruntime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed.\n\nBrownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:\n- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,\n  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).\n  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the\n  two AuditLog indexes.\n- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,\n  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.\n  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.\n  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`\n  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).\n- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.\n  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`\n  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.\n- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at\n  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file.\n\n### Intake blockers and how they're resolved\n\n| Blocker | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |\n| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |\n| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |\n\n---\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)\n- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.\n- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code\n  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip\n  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.\n- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._\n\n### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):\n  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`\n  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`\n  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`\n  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)\n  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,\n  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.\n- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):\n  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`\n    and `checkedAt = now`.\n  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.\n  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run\n    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.\n    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.\n    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.\n  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the\n    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would\n    hide an older password change.\n- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.\n- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.\n  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's\n  route matching, so they can live side by side.\n- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._\n\n### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)\nA plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`\ndelegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).\nOrder of checks:\n1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.\n2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).\n3. Look up the user by email.\n4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**\n   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`\n   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly\n   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).\n5. Branches:\n   - missing user → `invalid`\n   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`\n   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`\n   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`\n   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)\n   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user\n6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns\n   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).\n   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a\n   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent\n   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't\n   matter here.\n7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:\n   - `auth.login.success`\n   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only\n   - `auth.lockout`\n   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.\n8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the\n   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to\n   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"\n   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).\n- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._\n\n### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)\nThis is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.\n- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:\n  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,\n    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.\n  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only\n    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.\n  - Returns the raw token.\n- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:\n  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.\n  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong\n    type, is used or is expired.\n- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.\n  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a\n  double-submit fail cleanly.\n- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.\n- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._\n\n### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)\n- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`\n  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.\n- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.\n- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't\n  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales\n  horizontally.\n- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns\n  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.\n- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._\n\n### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)\n- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.\n- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,\n  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.\n- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the\n  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.\n- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`\n  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.\n- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:\n  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.\n  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus\n    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with\n    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.\n  - Every password-setting service calls it.\n- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules\n  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's\n  error response.\n- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._\n\n### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)\nDelete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:\n```ts\ntype SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser\ngetCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)\nrequireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED\nrequireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN\nrequirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')\nrequirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')\n```\n- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.\n  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.\n- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a\n  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.\n  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,\n  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why\n  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.\n- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,\n  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is\n  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.\n- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`\n  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.\n- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.\n- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._\n\n### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`\n  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and\n  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.\n  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.\n  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).\n- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:\n  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that\n     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present\n     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.\n     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely\n     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.\n  2. If the path is public → `next()`.\n  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.\n     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.\n  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.\n- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files\n  with extensions.\n- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the\n  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper\n  on every page and handler.\n- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._\n\n### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)\nRoute handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below\nrecords an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.\n- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.\n  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.\n  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.\n  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and\n     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.\n  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.\n  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**\n     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the\n     design reuses the one sign-in path.\n- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.\n    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the\n    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email\n    was tried before.\n  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,\n    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.\n  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.\n  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.\n- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.\n  2. Policy check, then hash.\n  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,\n     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.\n  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.\n- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:\n  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`\n     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.\n  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.\n  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.\n  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this\n     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail\n     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.\n- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:\n  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam\n    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\n  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.\n  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in\n    audit metadata.\n- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._\n\n### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)\n- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).\n- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.\n  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.\n- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then\n  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged\n  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.\n- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._\n\n### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)\n- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.\n- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.\n- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:\n  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.\n- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._\n\n### 12. App shell and navigation\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:\n  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.\n  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.\n    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.\n  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:\n  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`\n    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.\n  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.\n  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n    That function doesn't need a provider.\n- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._\n\n### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)\n- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.\n- **`login/page.tsx`**:\n  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton\n    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.\n  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error\n    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to\n    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.\n  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.\n  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).\n- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200\n  and the FR-7-style message on 429.\n- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:\n  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the\n    FR-14 Alert copy.\n  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.\n- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows\n  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.\n- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:\n  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.\n  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the\n    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.\n- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):\n  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,\n    driven by `passwordChecks`.\n  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset\n    pages share it.\n- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**\n  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.\n  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to\n    the first invalid field.\n  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.\n- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._\n\n### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)\n- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:\n  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`\n  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password\n- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and\n  log the link with `logger.info`.\n- `office@` stays as it is.\n- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._\n\n### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)\n- **Unit tests:**\n  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`\n  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches\n  - `computeLockout`\n  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`\n  - `safeCallbackUrl`\n- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):\n  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch\n  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`\n  - Audit metadata never contains secrets\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Sign-in/out with seeded users\n  - The failed-login message\n  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through\n    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable\n    from the DB.\n  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages\n- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.\n- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._\n\n---\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**\n1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →\n   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.\n2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt\n   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.\n3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.\n   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.\n4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.\n   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert.\n\n**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**\n1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.\n   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.\n   - No session on `/api` → 401.\n2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`\n   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).\n3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.\n   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.\n4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page).\n\n**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**\n1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`\n   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).\n2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`\n   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.\n   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.\n4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`.\n\n**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**\n1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →\n   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.\n   The response is always the generic message.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash\n   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it\n   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n\n**Change password (FR-23)**\n1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.\n2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a\n   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.\n3. The toast reads \"Password updated\".\n\n---\n\n## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)\n\n| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |\n| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n\nAll custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the\n`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:\n- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`\n- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401\n- `FORBIDDEN` 403\n- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens\n- `RATE_LIMITED` 429\n\n`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).\n\n## New / changed files\n\n**New:**\n- `src/middleware.ts`\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`\n- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`\n- `src/server/services/auth.ts`\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`\n- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`\n- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`\n- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`\n- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`\n- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`\n\n**Changed:**\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes\n- `prisma/seed.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n- `src/server/audit.ts`\n- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`\n- `src/server/services/users.ts`\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`\n- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants\n- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`\n- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly\n\n**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the\ncomment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).\n\n**Skipped on purpose:**\n- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.\n- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.\n- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.\n- Client-side common-password list.\n- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |\n| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |\n| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |\n| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |\n| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |\n| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |\n| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |\n| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |\n| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |\n| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |\n| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |\n| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |\n| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |\n| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |\n| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |\n| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |\n| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |\n| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |\n| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |\n| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |\n| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |\n| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |\n| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |\n| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |\n| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |\n| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |\n| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |\n| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |\n| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |\n| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |\n| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |\n| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |\n| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |\n| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |\n| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |\n| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |\n| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |\n| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |\n| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |\n| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |\n| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |\n| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |\n| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |\n| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JKWN7HGkBB9awmAy712ZTj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8ecf6ce-8d48-4a6b-879b-0c956e2c759f","uuid":"05d66e07-407e-4379-890c-b3757310455f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:39:01.432Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:\nAuth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,\npassword reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware\ngate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a\nbrownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new\nruntime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed.\n\nBrownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:\n- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,\n  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).\n  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the\n  two AuditLog indexes.\n- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,\n  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.\n  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.\n  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`\n  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).\n- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.\n  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`\n  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.\n- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at\n  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file.\n\n### Intake blockers and how they're resolved\n\n| Blocker | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |\n| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |\n| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |\n\n---\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)\n- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.\n- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code\n  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip\n  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.\n- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._\n\n### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):\n  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`\n  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`\n  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`\n  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)\n  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,\n  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.\n- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):\n  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`\n    and `checkedAt = now`.\n  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.\n  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run\n    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.\n    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.\n    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.\n  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the\n    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would\n    hide an older password change.\n- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.\n- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.\n  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's\n  route matching, so they can live side by side.\n- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._\n\n### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)\nA plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`\ndelegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).\nOrder of checks:\n1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.\n2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).\n3. Look up the user by email.\n4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**\n   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`\n   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly\n   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).\n5. Branches:\n   - missing user → `invalid`\n   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`\n   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`\n   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`\n   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)\n   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user\n6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns\n   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).\n   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a\n   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent\n   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't\n   matter here.\n7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:\n   - `auth.login.success`\n   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only\n   - `auth.lockout`\n   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.\n8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the\n   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to\n   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"\n   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).\n- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._\n\n### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)\nThis is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.\n- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:\n  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,\n    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.\n  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only\n    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.\n  - Returns the raw token.\n- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:\n  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.\n  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong\n    type, is used or is expired.\n- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.\n  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a\n  double-submit fail cleanly.\n- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.\n- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._\n\n### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)\n- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`\n  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.\n- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.\n- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't\n  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales\n  horizontally.\n- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns\n  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.\n- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._\n\n### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)\n- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.\n- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,\n  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.\n- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the\n  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.\n- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`\n  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.\n- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:\n  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.\n  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus\n    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with\n    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.\n  - Every password-setting service calls it.\n- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules\n  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's\n  error response.\n- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._\n\n### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)\nDelete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:\n```ts\ntype SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser\ngetCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)\nrequireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED\nrequireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN\nrequirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')\nrequirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')\n```\n- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.\n  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.\n- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a\n  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.\n  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,\n  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why\n  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.\n- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,\n  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is\n  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.\n- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`\n  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.\n- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.\n- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._\n\n### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`\n  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and\n  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.\n  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.\n  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).\n- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:\n  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that\n     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present\n     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.\n     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely\n     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.\n  2. If the path is public → `next()`.\n  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.\n     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.\n  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.\n- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files\n  with extensions.\n- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the\n  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper\n  on every page and handler.\n- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._\n\n### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)\nRoute handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below\nrecords an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.\n- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.\n  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.\n  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.\n  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and\n     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.\n  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.\n  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**\n     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the\n     design reuses the one sign-in path.\n- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.\n    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the\n    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email\n    was tried before.\n  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,\n    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.\n  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.\n  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.\n- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.\n  2. Policy check, then hash.\n  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,\n     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.\n  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.\n- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:\n  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`\n     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.\n  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.\n  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.\n  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this\n     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail\n     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.\n- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:\n  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam\n    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\n  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.\n  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in\n    audit metadata.\n- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._\n\n### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)\n- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).\n- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.\n  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.\n- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then\n  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged\n  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.\n- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._\n\n### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)\n- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.\n- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.\n- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:\n  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.\n- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._\n\n### 12. App shell and navigation\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:\n  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.\n  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.\n    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.\n  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:\n  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`\n    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.\n  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.\n  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n    That function doesn't need a provider.\n- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._\n\n### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)\n- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.\n- **`login/page.tsx`**:\n  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton\n    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.\n  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error\n    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to\n    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.\n  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.\n  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).\n- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200\n  and the FR-7-style message on 429.\n- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:\n  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the\n    FR-14 Alert copy.\n  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.\n- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows\n  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.\n- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:\n  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.\n  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the\n    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.\n- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):\n  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,\n    driven by `passwordChecks`.\n  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset\n    pages share it.\n- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**\n  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.\n  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to\n    the first invalid field.\n  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.\n- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._\n\n### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)\n- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:\n  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`\n  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password\n- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and\n  log the link with `logger.info`.\n- `office@` stays as it is.\n- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._\n\n### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)\n- **Unit tests:**\n  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`\n  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches\n  - `computeLockout`\n  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`\n  - `safeCallbackUrl`\n- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):\n  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch\n  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`\n  - Audit metadata never contains secrets\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Sign-in/out with seeded users\n  - The failed-login message\n  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through\n    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable\n    from the DB.\n  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages\n- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.\n- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._\n\n---\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**\n1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →\n   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.\n2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt\n   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.\n3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.\n   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.\n4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.\n   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert.\n\n**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**\n1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.\n   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.\n   - No session on `/api` → 401.\n2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`\n   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).\n3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.\n   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.\n4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page).\n\n**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**\n1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`\n   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).\n2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`\n   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.\n   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.\n4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`.\n\n**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**\n1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →\n   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.\n   The response is always the generic message.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash\n   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it\n   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n\n**Change password (FR-23)**\n1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.\n2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a\n   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.\n3. The toast reads \"Password updated\".\n\n---\n\n## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)\n\n| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |\n| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n\nAll custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the\n`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:\n- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`\n- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401\n- `FORBIDDEN` 403\n- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens\n- `RATE_LIMITED` 429\n\n`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).\n\n## New / changed files\n\n**New:**\n- `src/middleware.ts`\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`\n- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`\n- `src/server/services/auth.ts`\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`\n- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`\n- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`\n- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`\n- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`\n- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`\n\n**Changed:**\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes\n- `prisma/seed.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n- `src/server/audit.ts`\n- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`\n- `src/server/services/users.ts`\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`\n- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants\n- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`\n- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly\n\n**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the\ncomment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).\n\n**Skipped on purpose:**\n- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.\n- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.\n- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.\n- Client-side common-password list.\n- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |\n| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |\n| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |\n| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |\n| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |\n| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |\n| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |\n| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |\n| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |\n| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |\n| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |\n| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |\n| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |\n| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |\n| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |\n| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |\n| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |\n| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |\n| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |\n| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |\n| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |\n| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |\n| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |\n| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |\n| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |\n| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |\n| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |\n| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |\n| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |\n| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |\n| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |\n| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |\n| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |\n| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |\n| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |\n| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |\n| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |\n| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |\n| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |\n| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |\n| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |\n| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |\n| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |\n| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":251,"newStart":1,"newLines":515,"lines":["-# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)","+# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)"," ","-Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete","+Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete"," ","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),","+`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),","+`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),","+`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.","+"," ## Overview"," ","-PRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic","-structure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03","-(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04","-(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**","-(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both","-resolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.","+PRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:","+Auth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,","+password reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware","+gate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a","+brownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new","+runtime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed."," ","-**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s","-`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the","-first requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"","-under an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the","-grouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional","-field, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small","-MUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;","-items without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change","-that satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages","-registry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add","-`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they","-land, with no further schema change.","+Brownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:","+- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,","+  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).","+  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the","+  two AuditLog indexes.","+- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,","+  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.","+  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.","+  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`","+  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).","+- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.","+  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.","+- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`","+  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.","+- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at","+  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file."," ","-**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from","-PRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described","-in the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`","-(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new","-`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around","-`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object","-`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and","-does **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.","-Consolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is","-explicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not","-schedule that consolidation here.","+### Intake blockers and how they're resolved"," ","-**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two","-service-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:","-FR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section","-required iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity","-checks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same","-`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted","-as good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write","-concurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to","-fix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on","-these two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,","-homeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.","+| Blocker | Resolution |","+|---|---|","+| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |","+| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |","+| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |","+| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |"," ","+---","+"," ## Component Breakdown"," ","-### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)","-`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus","-`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including","-all four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what","-FR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below","-reads/writes.","+### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)","+- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.","+- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code","+  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip","+  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.","+- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._"," ","-### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`","-The single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,","-FR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions","-(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens","-its own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per","-tech-stack ADR-1):","+### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)","+- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):","+  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`","+  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`","+  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`","+  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)","+  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.","+- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,","+  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.","+- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):","+  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`","+    and `checkedAt = now`.","+  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.","+  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run","+    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.","+    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.","+    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.","+  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the","+    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would","+    hide an older password change.","+- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.","+- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.","+  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's","+  route matching, so they can live side by side.","+- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._"," ","-- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`","-  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below","-  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A","-  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per","-  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per","-  route.","-- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`","-  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing","-  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs","-  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no","-  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip","-  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row","-  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course","-  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).","-- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:","-  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE","-  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls","-  `audit()`.","-- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`","-  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then","-  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,","-  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.","+### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)","+A plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`","+delegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).","+Order of checks:","+1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.","+2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).","+3. Look up the user by email.","+4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**","+   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`","+   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly","+   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).","+5. Branches:","+   - missing user → `invalid`","+   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`","+   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`","+   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`","+   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)","+   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user","+6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns","+   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).","+   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a","+   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent","+   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't","+   matter here.","+7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:","+   - `auth.login.success`","+   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only","+   - `auth.lockout`","+   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.","+8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the","+   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to","+   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"","+   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).","+- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._"," ","-FR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both","-create `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the","-section's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry","-points, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.","+### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)","+This is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.","+- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:","+  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,","+    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.","+  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only","+    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.","+  - Returns the raw token.","+- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:","+  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.","+  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong","+    type, is used or is expired.","+- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.","+  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a","+  double-submit fail cleanly.","+- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.","+- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._"," ","-FR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active","-rosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter","-applied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,","-course roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.","+### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)","+- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`","+  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.","+- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.","+- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't","+  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales","+  horizontally.","+- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns","+  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.","+- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._"," ","-### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`","-CRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,","-FR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)","-and the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level","-advanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not","-reusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot","-structural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on","-`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement","-enroll/drop.","+### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)","+- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.","+- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,","+  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.","+- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the","+  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.","+- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`","+  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.","+- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:","+  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.","+  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus","+    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with","+    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.","+  - Every password-setting service calls it.","+- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules","+  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's","+  error response.","+- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._"," ","-### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`","-CRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`","-(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"","-validator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side","-check and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a","-refinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on","-a non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`","-create/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,","-reused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this","-picker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.","+### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)","+Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:","+```ts","+type SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser","+getCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)","+requireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED","+requireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN","+requirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')","+requirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')","+```","+- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.","+  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.","+- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a","+  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.","+  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,","+  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why","+  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.","+- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,","+  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is","+  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.","+- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`","+  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.","+- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.","+- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._"," ","-### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`","-FR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and","-`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per","-Decision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by","-`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster","-endpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once","-here, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's","-stated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this","-PRD's scope.","+### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`","+- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`","+  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and","+  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.","+  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.","+  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).","+- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:","+  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that","+     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present","+     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.","+     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely","+     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.","+  2. If the path is public → `next()`.","+  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.","+     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.","+  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.","+- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files","+  with extensions.","+- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the","+  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper","+  on every page and handler.","+- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._"," ","-### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`","-FR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER","-branch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section","-membership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/","-PRD-04 callers unchanged.","+### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)","+Route handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below","+records an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.","+- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:","+  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.","+  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.","+  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.","+  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and","+     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.","+  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.","+  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**","+     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the","+     design reuses the one sign-in path.","+- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:","+  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.","+    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.","+  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the","+    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email","+    was tried before.","+  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,","+    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.","+  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.","+  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.","+- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:","+  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.","+  2. Policy check, then hash.","+  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,","+     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.","+  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.","+- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:","+  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`","+     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.","+  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.","+  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.","+  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this","+     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail","+     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.","+- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:","+  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam","+    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.","+  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.","+  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in","+    audit metadata.","+- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._"," ","-### Course public surface","-`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing","-`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers","-`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;","-STUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`","-filtering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a","-read-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.","+### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)","+- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).","+- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.","+  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.","+- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then","+  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged","+  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.","+- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._"," ","-**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'","-names only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query","-(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when","-`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component","-and `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the","-data layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.","+### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)","+- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.","+- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.","+- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:","+  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.","+- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._"," ","-### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)","-Read view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query","-(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE","-enrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,","-grouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —","-no new parent-fanout code).","+### 12. App shell and navigation","+- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:","+  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.","+  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.","+    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.","+  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).","+- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:","+  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`","+    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.","+  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.","+  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.","+    That function doesn't need a provider.","+- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._"," ","-### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)","-`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible","-flat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get","-`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.","+### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)","+- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.","+- **`login/page.tsx`**:","+  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton","+    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.","+  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error","+    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to","+    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.","+  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.","+  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).","+- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200","+  and the FR-7-style message on 429.","+- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:","+  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the","+    FR-14 Alert copy.","+  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.","+- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows","+  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.","+- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:","+  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.","+  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the","+    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.","+- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):","+  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,","+    driven by `passwordChecks`.","+  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset","+    pages share it.","+- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**","+  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.","+  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to","+    the first invalid field.","+  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.","+- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._"," ","-### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)","-New \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +","-teacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses","-FR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the","-student page (no new access function).","+### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)","+- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:","+  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`","+  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password","+- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and","+  log the link with `logger.info`.","+- `office@` stays as it is.","+- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._"," ","-### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`","-Every route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`","-→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the","-existing success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route","-layer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside","-the same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it","-internally so routes don't duplicate the call.","+### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)","+- **Unit tests:**","+  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`","+  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches","+  - `computeLockout`","+  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`","+  - `safeCallbackUrl`","+- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):","+  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch","+  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`","+  - Audit metadata never contains secrets","+- **Playwright:**","+  - Sign-in/out with seeded users","+  - The failed-login message","+  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through","+    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable","+    from the DB.","+  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages","+- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.","+- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._"," ","+---","+"," ## Data Flow"," ","-**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**","-`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST","-/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens","-`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →","-`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the","-uniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course","-`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →","-commit → envelope response.","+**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**","+1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →","+   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.","+2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt","+   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.","+3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.","+   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.","+4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.","+   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert."," ","-**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →","-`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping","-`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old","-CORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for","-the whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.","+**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**","+1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.","+   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.","+   - No session on `/api` → 401.","+2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`","+   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).","+3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.","+   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.","+4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page)."," ","-**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →","-`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`","-(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course","-against current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.","+**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**","+1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`","+   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).","+2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`","+   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.","+3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.","+   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.","+4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`."," ","-**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET","-/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service","-.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →","-envelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.","+**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**","+1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →","+   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.","+   The response is always the generic message.","+2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash","+   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it","+   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast."," ","-**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST","-/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`","-existing → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural","-`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no","-`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.","+**Change password (FR-23)**","+1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.","+2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a","+   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.","+3. The toast reads \"Password updated\"."," ","-## Requirements Traceability","+---"," ","-| Requirement | Design Element |","-|---|---|","-| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |","-| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |","-| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |","-| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |","-| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |","-| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |","-| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |","-| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |","-| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |","-| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |","-| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |","-| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |","-| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |","-| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |","-| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |","-| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |","-| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |","-| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |","-| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |","-| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |","-| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |","-| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |","-| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |","-| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |","-| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |","-| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |","-| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |","-| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |","-| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |","-| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |","-| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |","+## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)"," ","-## Status","+| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |","+| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |","+| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |","+| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |","+| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |"," ","-`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no","-open gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond","-the NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).","+All custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the","+`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:","+- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`","+- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401","+- `FORBIDDEN` 403","+- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens","+- `RATE_LIMITED` 429","+","+`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).","+","+## New / changed files","+","+**New:**","+- `src/middleware.ts`","+- `src/config/public-routes.ts`","+- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`","+- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`","+- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`","+- `src/server/services/auth.ts`","+- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`","+- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`","+- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`","+- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`","+- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`","+- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`","+- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`","+","+**Changed:**","+- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes","+- `prisma/seed.ts`","+- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`","+- `src/server/audit.ts`","+- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`","+- `src/server/services/users.ts`","+- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`","+- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`","+- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants","+- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`","+- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly","+","+**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the","+comment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).","+","+**Skipped on purpose:**","+- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.","+- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.","+- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.","+- Client-side common-password list.","+- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.","+","+---","+","+## Requirements Traceability","+","+| Req | Design element |","+|---|---|","+| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |","+| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |","+| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |","+| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |","+| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |","+| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |","+| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |","+| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |","+| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |","+| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |","+| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |","+| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |","+| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |","+| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |","+| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |","+| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |","+| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |","+| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |","+| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |","+| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |","+| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |","+| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |","+| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |","+| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |","+| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |","+| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |","+| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |","+| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |","+| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |","+| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |","+| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |","+| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |","+| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |","+| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |","+| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |","+| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |","+| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |","+| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |","+| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |","+| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |","+| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |","+| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |","+| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |","+| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |","+| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |","+| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |","+| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |","+| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |","+| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |"]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — ticket abcd-05 (PRD-05 Classes & Enrollment)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) | Status: complete\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-05 is brownfield on top of PRD-00 (foundation), PRD-02 (academic\nstructure: `AcademicYear`, `Subject.color`, `GradeLevel.order`), PRD-03\n(user management: `UserPicker` with `role` filter), and PRD-04\n(notifications). Intake reports **97% confidence**\n(`handoff-to-architect.json`) with **two MEDIUM-confidence blockers**, both\nresolved as explicit decisions below rather than carried forward as gaps.\n\n**Decision 1 — FR-20 nav grouping (blocker).** `src/config/navigation.ts`'s\n`NavItem` is today a flat array with no grouping concept, and FR-20 is the\nfirst requirement in the codebase that needs one (\"Sections\"/\"Courses\"\nunder an \"Administration\" heading for ADMIN). This PRD does need the\ngrouping now — it is not speculative — so the design adds a single optional\nfield, `group?: string`, to `NavItem`. The sidebar renderer shows a small\nMUI `Typography` subheader above consecutive items sharing a `group` value;\nitems without `group` render exactly as before. This is the minimum change\nthat satisfies FR-20: no new nav data model, no config file, no admin-pages\nregistry for entities PRD-02/PRD-03 haven't exposed yet — those can add\n`group: \"Administration\"` to their own `NavItem` entries whenever they\nland, with no further schema change.\n\n**Decision 2 — NFR-7 auth helper gap (blocker, carried forward from\nPRD-04).** `src/server/auth/permissions.ts` and `requireUser()` described\nin the Platform Context do not exist; only `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n(hardcoded-identity stand-in) and `student-access.ts` exist. FR-18's new\n`src/server/auth/course-access.ts` is designed as a thin wrapper around\n`requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)` — it takes the already-resolved `user` object\n`requireRole` produces and the role-specific checks described in FR-18, and\ndoes **not** assume or forward-declare `permissions.ts`/`requireUser()`.\nConsolidating per-feature `*-access.ts` files into one `permissions.ts` is\nexplicitly PRD-01's job, not this PRD's — `dev-planning` should not\nschedule that consolidation here.\n\n**Decision 3 — un-backstopped uniqueness rules (FR-3, FR-14).** Two\nservice-level uniqueness/validity rules have no DB unique constraint:\nFR-3's \"one homeroom teacher per section per year\" and FR-14's \"section\nrequired iff `kind=CORE`\". Per tech-stack ADR-2's precedent for capacity\nchecks, both are checked with a `findFirst`/validation read inside the same\n`$transaction` as the write, not pre-checked outside it. This is accepted\nas good-enough serialization for an internal admin console with low write\nconcurrency (same risk acceptance as ADR-2's capacity check) — not a gap to\nfix with a new DB constraint in this PRD. If concurrent-admin collisions on\nthese two rules become a real problem, adding `@@unique([academicYearId,\nhomeroomTeacherId])`-style constraints is a small follow-up, not a redesign.\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### Data layer (owned by FR-1, already fully specified there)\n`Section`, `SectionMember`, `Course`, `Enrollment` Prisma models plus\n`CourseKind`/`EnrollmentStatus` enums, exactly as given in FR-1, including\nall four constraints/indexes. No design decisions needed here beyond what\nFR-1 states — this document treats it as the foundation every service below\nreads/writes.\n\n### Roster Enrollment Engine — `src/server/enrollment/roster-engine.ts`\nThe single business-logic module behind FR-5, FR-7, FR-8, FR-9, FR-10,\nFR-11, FR-12, FR-24. Exports four composable, transaction-safe functions\n(each takes a Prisma transaction client `tx` as first argument, never opens\nits own transaction — callers own the `$transaction` boundary per\ntech-stack ADR-1):\n\n- `checkCapacityOrThrow(tx, { sectionId?, courseId?, addingCount, overrideCapacity })`\n  — one shared capacity guard (FR-11) called by every enroll path below\n  before any write; throws the CONFLICT error with the exact `\"Section 7A\n  is full (30/30).\"`-pattern message. One function, four call sites, per\n  the requirements-analysis cross-cutting note — not reimplemented per\n  route.\n- `enrollSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-7/FR-10's shared enroll semantics: `findMany` existing\n  `Enrollment` rows for the (studentIds × section's CORE courses) pairs\n  first, then one `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` for pairs with no\n  row and one `updateMany` keyed on `[courseId, studentId]` to flip\n  DROPPED→ACTIVE (with `droppedAt: null`) for the rest — never per-row\n  create/update loops (NFR-3). Calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` per course\n  first. Calls `audit()` once per course kind of change (FR-24).\n- `dropSectionCoreCourses(tx, sectionId, studentIds)` — FR-8's mirror:\n  `updateMany` ACTIVE→DROPPED + `droppedAt: now()` on that section's CORE\n  courses only; leaves elective `Enrollment` rows untouched. Calls\n  `audit()`.\n- `moveStudentSection(tx, studentId, fromSectionId, toSectionId, { overrideCapacity })`\n  — FR-9's composition: calls `dropSectionCoreCourses` then\n  `enrollSectionCoreCourses` inside one caller-provided `$transaction`,\n  exposed only via `POST /api/students/:id/move-section`.\n\nFR-5 (bulk \"Create core courses\") and FR-10 (single new CORE course) both\ncreate `Course` rows then call `enrollSectionCoreCourses` with the\nsection's current members — one course-creation code path, two entry\npoints, per the requirements note; neither duplicates enroll logic.\n\nFR-12 (dropped rows stay visible to admin/teacher but vanish from active\nrosters/pickers) is not new engine code — it's a `status: 'ACTIVE'` filter\napplied in every user-facing list query (section members-for-picker,\ncourse roster-for-picker) built on top of this engine's writes.\n\n### Sections service — `src/server/sections/sections-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/sections` and `/admin/sections/[id]` (FR-2, FR-3,\nFR-4, FR-6). Owns the FR-3 homeroom-teacher-uniqueness check (Decision 3)\nand the FR-6 \"Copy sections to next year\" structural copy (grade level\nadvanced by `GradeLevel.order`, no members/teacher — intentionally not\nreusing the enrollment engine, since NFR-6 scopes this out as a one-shot\nstructural copy, not a promotion workflow). Member add/remove on\n`/admin/sections/[id]` calls into the roster engine, it does not reimplement\nenroll/drop.\n\n### Courses service — `src/server/courses/courses-service.ts`\nCRUD + list for `/admin/courses` and `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment`\n(FR-13, FR-14, FR-15). Owns the FR-14 \"section required iff `kind=CORE`\"\nvalidator (Decision 3), shared by the create/edit dialog's client-side\ncheck and the API route's server-side check (one `zod` schema with a\nrefinement, not two independent checks). The FR-15 \"Add students\" picker on\na non-CORE course calls `checkCapacityOrThrow` + a direct `Enrollment`\ncreate/reactivate (same reactivate-vs-duplicate semantics as the engine,\nreused as a helper) — CORE courses show the info note and disable this\npicker, routing membership changes back to the section page instead.\n\n### Course access control — `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`\nFR-18's `assertCanViewCourse(user, courseId)` and\n`assertCanManageCourse(user, courseId)`, built on `requireRole` per\nDecision 2. `assertCanViewCourse` is the single chokepoint called by\n`/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16), the course-tabs registry (FR-17), the roster\nendpoint (FR-23), and `/my-courses` (FR-19) — role logic is derived once\nhere, not per route. `assertCanManageCourse` is added now for FR-18's\nstated future write-operation use; no write route calls it yet in this\nPRD's scope.\n\n### Student access extension — `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\nFR-22 adds to the existing `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)`'s TEACHER\nbranch only (students via taught/co-taught enrollments + homeroom section\nmembership), preserving the function's existing signature for PRD-01/\nPRD-04 callers unchanged.\n\n### Course public surface\n`src/config/course-tabs.ts` (FR-17) mirrors the existing\n`src/config/student-tabs.ts` shape plus a `roles` field; registers\n`Overview` (all viewing roles) and `Roster` (TEACHER/ADMIN full view;\nSTUDENT sees the NFR-4-scrubbed view; PARENT tab omitted by `roles`\nfiltering, not a runtime check). `/courses/[courseId]` (FR-16) is a\nread-only composition of FR-1 data behind `assertCanViewCourse`.\n\n**NFR-4 privacy note:** the roster scrubbing (students see classmates'\nnames only) is implemented once in the courses-service roster query\n(`getCourseRoster(courseId, viewerRole)` returns a narrower projection when\n`viewerRole === 'STUDENT'`), and both the `Roster` tab's server component\nand `GET /api/courses/:id/roster` call that same function — enforced at the\ndata layer, not re-derived in the UI tab and independently in the route.\n\n### My Courses — `/my-courses` (FR-19)\nRead view composing `assertCanViewCourse`'s per-role rules: TEACHER query\n(taught/co-taught, non-archived, this year), STUDENT query (ACTIVE\nenrollments), PARENT query (same STUDENT query run per linked child,\ngrouped by child using the existing parent-link read path from prior PRDs —\nno new parent-fanout code).\n\n### Navigation — `src/config/navigation.ts` (FR-20, Decision 1)\n`NavItem.group?: string` added; \"My courses\" entry has no group (visible\nflat to TEACHER/STUDENT/PARENT); \"Sections\" and \"Courses\" entries both get\n`group: \"Administration\"`, visible to ADMIN only.\n\n### Student tab — `src/config/student-tabs.ts` (FR-21)\nNew \"Courses\" tab registered: table of the student's this-year courses +\nteacher + enrollment status, section, homeroom teacher. Pure read, reuses\nFR-1 data and the same visibility rule already governing who can view the\nstudent page (no new access function).\n\n### REST API surface (FR-23, FR-24) — finalized by `arch-api-contracts`\nEvery route in the API table is a thin handler: `requireRole(...ALL_ROLES)`\n→ input validation (`zod`) → call exactly one of the services above → the\nexisting success/list/error envelope. No business logic lives at the route\nlayer. Every write route calls `audit()` once per logical mutation inside\nthe same transaction (FR-24) — the roster engine and services call it\ninternally so routes don't duplicate the call.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Add student to section (FR-7, FR-11, FR-24):**\n`/admin/sections/[id]` add-student dialog → `POST\n/api/sections/:id/members` → `requireRole` → `sections-service` opens\n`$transaction` → `checkCapacityOrThrow` (section capacity) →\n`SectionMember.create` (catches `P2002` → CONFLICT if race loses the\nuniqueness check) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (per-course\n`checkCapacityOrThrow` + batched create/reactivate) → `audit()` ×N →\ncommit → envelope response.\n\n**Move section (FR-9):** `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` →\n`requireRole` → single `$transaction` wrapping\n`sections-service.removeMember(from)` + `moveStudentSection` (drop old\nCORE, enroll new CORE) → `audit()` → commit. One transaction boundary for\nthe whole operation, per tech-stack ADR-1.\n\n**Create core courses, bulk (FR-5):** `/admin/sections/[id]` dialog →\n`POST /api/sections/:id/core-courses` → `$transaction` → `Course.createMany`\n(one per checked subject) → `enrollSectionCoreCourses` for each new course\nagainst current members → `audit()` ×N → commit.\n\n**View course roster as STUDENT (FR-17, NFR-4):** `GET\n/api/courses/:id/roster` → `assertCanViewCourse` → `courses-service\n.getCourseRoster(id, 'STUDENT')` → scrubbed projection (names only) →\nenvelope. Same function backs the server-rendered `Roster` tab.\n\n**Copy sections to next year (FR-6):** `/admin/sections` action → `POST\n/api/sections/copy-to-year` → gated on a future non-current `AcademicYear`\nexisting → `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` → structural\n`Section.createMany` with `gradeLevel` advanced by `order`, no\n`SectionMember`/teacher rows → `audit()` ×N.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Requirement | Design Element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Prisma `Section`/`SectionMember`/`Course`/`Enrollment` models + enums (Data layer) |\n| FR-2 | `/admin/sections` list — Sections service read query |\n| FR-3 | Section create/edit dialog + Decision 3 homeroom-uniqueness check (Sections service) |\n| FR-4 | `/admin/sections/[id]` — Sections service + Roster Enrollment Engine trigger point |\n| FR-5 | \"Create core courses\" dialog — Courses service create + `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (bulk entry point) |\n| FR-6 | \"Copy sections to next year\" — `sections-service.copySectionsToYear` |\n| FR-7 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-8 | `dropSectionCoreCourses` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-9 | `moveStudentSection` (Roster Enrollment Engine) + `POST /api/students/:id/move-section` |\n| FR-10 | `enrollSectionCoreCourses` (single-course entry point, Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-11 | `checkCapacityOrThrow` (Roster Enrollment Engine) |\n| FR-12 | `status: 'ACTIVE'` filtering in list/picker queries (Sections/Courses services) |\n| FR-13 | `/admin/courses` list — Courses service read query |\n| FR-14 | Course create/edit dialog + Decision 3 section-required-iff-CORE validator (Courses service) |\n| FR-15 | `/admin/courses/[id]/enrollment` — Courses service roster + add/drop, `checkCapacityOrThrow` reuse |\n| FR-16 | `/courses/[courseId]` header — read composition behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-17 | `src/config/course-tabs.ts` registry + `getCourseRoster` scrubbed projection |\n| FR-18 | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` (`assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse`, Decision 2) |\n| FR-19 | `/my-courses` — per-role queries behind `assertCanViewCourse` |\n| FR-20 | `src/config/navigation.ts` `NavItem.group` field (Decision 1) |\n| FR-21 | `src/config/student-tabs.ts` \"Courses\" tab |\n| FR-22 | `getAccessibleStudentIds` TEACHER-branch extension (`student-access.ts`) |\n| FR-23 | REST route layer — thin handlers over the services/engine above (finalized by `arch-api-contracts`) |\n| FR-24 | `audit()` calls inside Roster Enrollment Engine + Sections/Courses services |\n| NFR-1 | All UI built from existing MUI v9 + shared `DataTable`/`UserPicker`/`ConfirmDialog`/`useToast` (no new component library) |\n| NFR-2 | `@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` on `SectionMember` (Data layer) |\n| NFR-3 | Batched `createMany`/`updateMany` in `enrollSectionCoreCourses`/`dropSectionCoreCourses`, no per-row loop |\n| NFR-4 | `getCourseRoster(id, viewerRole)` scrubbed projection, shared by UI tab and API route |\n| NFR-5 | Test targets flagged for `dev-planning`: Roster Enrollment Engine + capacity guard (highest reuse) |\n| NFR-6 | FR-6 scoped as structural copy only; no promotion/timetable/content/prerequisite code added anywhere above |\n| NFR-7 | `course-access.ts` wraps `requireRole` stand-in, no new `permissions.ts` (Decision 2) |\n\n## Status\n\n`complete` — both intake blockers resolved as explicit decisions above; no\nopen gaps carried forward to `arch-api-contracts` or `dev-planning` beyond\nthe NFR-5 test-target flag (informational, not a blocker).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JKWN7HGkBB9awmAy712ZTj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
