{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wx4Ve9HF22213Ds8Vicdye","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email\n5\tInfrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in\n6\t`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n7\t\n8\tConcern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,\n9\t**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,\n10\t**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,\n11\t**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,\n12\t**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,\n13\t**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n14\t\n15\t## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)\n16\t\n17\t| # | Finding | Impact |\n18\t|---|---------|--------|\n19\t| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |\n20\t| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |\n21\t| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |\n22\t| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |\n23\t| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |\n24\t| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |\n25\t| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n26\t| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |\n27\t| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |\n28\t| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |\n29\t| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |\n30\t\n31\t## Requirement → architectural concern\n32\t\n33\t| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n34\t|-----|----------------------|-------|\n35\t| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |\n36\t| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |\n37\t| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |\n38\t| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |\n39\t| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |\n40\t| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |\n41\t| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n42\t| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |\n43\t| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |\n44\t| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |\n45\t| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |\n46\t| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n47\t| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |\n48\t| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |\n49\t| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |\n50\t| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |\n51\t| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |\n52\t| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |\n53\t| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |\n54\t| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |\n55\t| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |\n56\t| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |\n57\t| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |\n58\t| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |\n59\t| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n60\t| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |\n61\t| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |\n62\t| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |\n63\t| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |\n64\t| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |\n65\t| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |\n66\t| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |\n67\t| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |\n68\t| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |\n69\t| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |\n70\t| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |\n71\t| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |\n72\t| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |\n73\t| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |\n74\t| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |\n75\t| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |\n76\t| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |\n77\t| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |\n78\t| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |\n79\t| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |\n80\t| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |\n81\t| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n82\t| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |\n83\t| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |\n84\t| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |\n85\t| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |\n86\t| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |\n87\t| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |\n88\t| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |\n89\t| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |\n90\t| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |\n91\t| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |\n92\t| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |\n93\t| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |\n94\t\n95\t## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)\n96\t\n97\t1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.\n98\t2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.\n99\t3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.\n100\t4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.\n101\t5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works.\n102\t\n103\t## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)\n104\t\n105\t- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.\n106\t- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only).\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a6de621-bc72-44a5-9725-5c1b7f039997","uuid":"7b0e8b5e-2139-45d9-a0bb-b67628ac85b4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:01:35.790Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-4\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`. That file covers PRD-04 Notifications & Email\nInfrastructure (41 FR and 18 NFR, so 59 requirements) at 93% confidence, with 4 blockers in\n`handoff-to-architect.json`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\nConcern buckets used below: **Data Model**, **Type Registry**, **Notify Service**,\n**Preference Resolution**, **Email Rendering**, **Auth Email Seam**, **Outbox Dispatcher**,\n**Transport**, **Background Job**, **Internal Endpoint**, **User API**, **Admin API**,\n**UI: Bell**, **UI: Notifications Page**, **UI: Preferences Page**, **UI: Admin Email Log**,\n**Validation**, **Seed**, **Security**, **Performance**, **Reliability**, **Conventions**,\n**Test Harness**, **Scope Discipline**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these add to or correct intake)\n\n| # | Finding | Impact |\n|---|---------|--------|\n| B1 | `src/middleware.ts` returns **401 for any `/api/*` request without a session** unless `isPublicPath()` matches. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is only `['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`. | The cron call to `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` carries no session cookie, so it would be rejected by middleware before the handler runs. **`/api/internal/` must be added to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** (prefix match). The handler then becomes the only gate, so its CRON_SECRET check must be strict (NFR-8). The middleware's cross-origin guard does not block it, because cron calls send no `Origin` header. |\n| B2 | `prisma/seed.ts` (95 lines) seeds only SchoolSettings and academic reference data. **There are no `student@schoolhub.test` or `parent@schoolhub.test` users** anywhere in `prisma/` or `src/`. | FR-40 cannot simply attach notifications to existing users. Options: (a) look up those users by email and skip with a log line when they are missing, or (b) upsert minimal STUDENT/PARENT users. Recommend (a). It keeps the seed idempotent and avoids PRD-04 creating identity data that another PRD owns. Design should confirm. |\n| B3 | `vitest.config.ts` includes only `tests/unit/**` and uses `environment: 'jsdom'`. There is no `tests/integration/` folder and no test-DB setup. | NFR-15 needs a node environment plus a real Postgres to exercise `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. This requires a separate vitest project or config (e.g. `vitest.integration.config.ts`, `environment: 'node'`, `include: tests/integration/**`) that is skipped when `DATABASE_URL_TEST` is absent, so that `npm run test` stays green (NFR-13). |\n| B4 | `EmailOutbox` has **no `userId` and no `type` column**. It stores only `toEmail`, `toName`, `subject`, `html`, `text`, `status`, `attempts`, `lastError`, `nextAttemptAt`, `sentAt`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. | The admin email log (FR-31) can only show recipient email and name, not a user link or type. That is sufficient for FR-31, so the schema should not change (NFR-13). `sendAuthEmail` (FR-16) fits naturally because it has no type. |\n| B5 | `NotificationPreference` uses a composite PK `@@id([userId, type])`. | FR-38's upsert keys on `userId_type`. FR-7's resolution reads with `findMany({ where: { userId: { in }, type } })`, which is a single query. |\n| B6 | `src/server/http.ts` already exports `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parsePagination` (default 20, max 100), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. `ApiErrorCode` already includes `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` and `FORBIDDEN`. | All new route handlers reuse these (NFR-11). No new error codes are needed. |\n| B7 | `src/lib/dates.ts` exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)` (date-fns-tz). `SchoolSettings.timezone` defaults to `'UTC'`. `src/server/services/settings.ts` exists. | NFR-12 reuses these. Relative times (\"5 min ago\") are timezone-independent. Absolute times in the email log and the invite expiry date use `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B8 | `src/server/rate-limit.ts` exports an in-memory `rateLimit()`. | It could optionally guard `POST /api/admin/notifications/test`, but no requirement asks for that. Skip it under compliance rule 1. |\n| B9 | `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx`, `Toast/useToast.ts`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader` and `DateDisplay` exist. | FR-26 and FR-31 reuse DataTable, PageHeader and EmptyState. FR-30 reuses `useToast`. Do not create duplicates. |\n| B10 | Prisma `$transaction` is used in `src/server/sections/`. No `$queryRaw` is used anywhere yet. | FR-17's `SKIP LOCKED` claim is the first raw SQL in the repo. Use tagged `$queryRaw` (parameterised) inside `$transaction`, or a single `UPDATE … WHERE id IN (SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *` statement, which claims rows atomically without holding a transaction across SMTP. |\n| B11 | All other intake brownfield findings were confirmed: there is no migration for the three models, the env vars and `worker:email` script are present, the navigation entries exist, `sendAuthEmail` has exactly 2 callers (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`), and the `requireRole` helpers exist. | — |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|-----|----------------------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | One new migration `2026110400xxxx_notifications_email`. It creates `EmailStatus`, `Notification`, `NotificationPreference` and `EmailOutbox` exactly as `schema.prisma` declares them, including the additive `updatedAt` columns and both indexes. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and do not edit `schema.prisma`. It must sort after `20261104000000_auth_reconcile`. |\n| FR-2 | Type Registry | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` exports `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with `as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>`, which keeps literal keys for FR-5 while type-checking the shape. Add one field, `emailOnly?: true` (or `hidden`), to express FR-4. |\n| FR-3 | Type Registry | `NotificationCategory` is a string-literal union of the 6 values, not a Prisma enum, because the DB stores `type` as a free `String`. The UI groups by category (FR-26, FR-28). |\n| FR-4 | Type Registry, Auth Email Seam | `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are `emailOnly`, hidden from preferences and never passed to `notify()` (blocker default confirmed in \"Decisions for design\" below). `system.test` uses category SYSTEM, `defaultEmail: true` and all roles (AC-1 expects both rows). |\n| FR-5 | Type Registry | `type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. Later PRDs extend the registry by editing this one file, and no plugin mechanism is needed (YAGNI). |\n| FR-6 | Notify Service | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts` is a pure server module. Its `email.template` param is a key into the template map (FR-13), and `data` is typed per template. |\n| FR-7 | Preference Resolution | Load users with `findMany({ id in userIds, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` and prefs with `findMany({ userId in, type })`. Then resolve each user with a pure function `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }`, which is unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-8 | Notify Service | `inApp = row?.inApp ?? true`, with `mandatoryInApp` forcing true. Notifications are written with `createMany`. |\n| FR-9 | Notify Service, Email Rendering | `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` and requires `user.email`. Render once per recipient, because templates contain the name. Rendering cost dominates NFR-1, so `render()` calls should run with bounded `Promise.all` concurrency. Rows are written to `EmailOutbox` with `createMany`. |\n| FR-10 | Performance | 1,000 recipients means 3 round-trips: users, prefs and one `createMany`, per channel. Chunk `createMany` at about 500 rows only if the parameter limit bites (Postgres allows 65,535 params, and Notification has about 7 columns, so 1,000 rows fit in one call). |\n| FR-11 | Notify Service | Wrap the whole body in try/catch, call `logger.error`, and return `void` or a `{ notified, emailed }` summary. Callers invoke it after commit. Document that in JSDoc. |\n| FR-12 | Notify Service | `notifyStudentAndParents` makes one `ParentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call (indexed on `studentId`), merges into a `Set`, then calls `notify`. Expansion and dedupe are a pure function so they can be unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| FR-13 | Email Rendering | `src/server/email/templates/*.tsx` with `@react-email/components`. `src/server/email/render.ts` calls `render(el)` and `render(el, { plainText: true })` from `@react-email/render` 1.0.1, which is async. |\n| FR-14 | Email Rendering | `BaseLayout.tsx` takes `school: Pick<SchoolSettings, name, logoUrl, addressLine1, addressLine2>`. Fetch SchoolSettings once per `notify()` / `sendAuthEmail` call, not once per recipient. The footer link is `APP_URL/account/notifications`. |\n| FR-15 | Email Rendering | There are 3 templates. Invite needs an expiry date, which `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` does not receive. The template can derive it from the known invite TTL constant in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, so the signature stays unchanged. Password reset uses the hardcoded 60-minute notice. The generic CTA href is `APP_URL + link` (the link is already validated by NFR-6). |\n| FR-16 | Auth Email Seam | Only the body of `src/server/auth/email.ts` changes: render the template and call `prisma.emailOutbox.create`. Its 2 callers are untouched. Unlike `notify()`, failures here **should** surface, because the existing callers already handle errors and a silently lost invite is worse. Design should decide whether to keep the current awaited and throwable behaviour (recommended). |\n| FR-17 | Outbox Dispatcher | `src/server/email/dispatch.ts`. First, run stuck-row recovery (NFR-5). Next, claim rows with one atomic `UPDATE … SET status='SENDING', updatedAt=now() WHERE id IN (SELECT id … WHERE status='PENDING' AND nextAttemptAt<=now() ORDER BY nextAttemptAt LIMIT $n FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) RETURNING *`. Then send each row outside any transaction and update it individually. |\n| FR-18 | Outbox Dispatcher | A pure function `backoffMinutes(attempts) → [1,5,15,60,240][attempts-1]`, plus `attempts >= 5 → FAILED`. It is unit-tested (NFR-14). `lastError` is truncated to about 1,000 characters. |\n| FR-19 | Internal Endpoint | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`. Compare the bearer token against `env.CRON_SECRET` with `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. A missing env value always returns 401. The response is `{ data: { sent, failed, retried } }` via `ok()`. **Requires B1** (the middleware allowlist). The route also triggers FR-27. |\n| FR-20 | Background Job | `scripts/worker-email.ts` imports `dispatchEmails` directly (tsx resolves the `@/` alias via tsconfig paths) and runs a `setTimeout` loop every 15 s with SIGINT/SIGTERM handling. It does not go over HTTP and does not call purge, because purge belongs to the endpoint only (FR-27). |\n| FR-21 | Transport | `src/server/email/transport.ts` exports `getTransport()` with 2 branches. `smtp` uses `nodemailer.createTransport` with SMTP_* settings and is memoised. `console` uses `console.log`, which NFR-11 explicitly allows. Each message includes `List-Unsubscribe` (NFR-9). Missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` under `smtp` should fail at transport creation, and the dispatcher must record that as a retryable `lastError`, not crash. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Bell | The `'use client'` component `NotificationBell.tsx` replaces the placeholder in `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`. It uses MUI `Badge` with `max={9}`, which renders \"9+\" natively, so no custom formatting is needed. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Bell | A `setInterval` of 30 s gated on `document.visibilityState`, plus an immediate refetch on `visibilitychange → visible`. There is no SWR or react-query dependency, so plain `fetch` is enough. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Bell | `Popover` + `List` + `ListItemButton`. Unread items use bold `fontWeight` and a `Badge variant=\"dot\"` or small Box. The body is clamped with `sx={{ WebkitLineClamp: 2 }}`. Relative time uses `date-fns` `formatDistanceToNowStrict` (date-fns-tz is already installed, so date-fns is too). The popover fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10` on open. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Bell | On click, call `POST /:id/read`, then `router.push(link)`, then close. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" (`POST /read-all`) and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Notifications Page | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` is a server shell using `requirePageUser()` and a client list. It has `Tabs` (All/Unread), a category `Select`, the pagination from DataTable or MUI `Pagination` with a page size of 20, and a per-row toggle calling `/:id/read` or `/:id/unread`. |\n| FR-27 | Background Job | `purgeOldNotifications()` (`deleteMany createdAt < now-180d`) lives in `src/server/notifications/`. A module-level `let lastPurgeAt` in the dispatch route allows at most one run per 24 h per process. It is best-effort, and its failure is logged and must not fail the dispatch response. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Preferences Page | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`. This is the first page under `/account/`, so the directory is new. It is an MUI `Table` with a full-width category header `TableRow` (the intake default is accepted) and data from `GET /api/me/notification-preferences`. |\n| FR-29 | UI: Preferences Page | `Tooltip` around a **span** wrapping the disabled `Switch`, because MUI Tooltip does not fire on disabled elements. |\n| FR-30 | UI: Preferences Page | Optimistic local state, `PUT`, and on error revert plus `useToast().error(...)`. |\n| FR-31 | UI: Admin Email Log | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` uses `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` with DataTable and a status `Select`. The recipient column shows `toName <toEmail>` (B4). |\n| FR-32 | Admin API, UI: Admin Email Log | The retry action is shown only when `status==='FAILED'`. The server guard uses `updateMany where { id, status: FAILED }`, and a count of 0 returns 409 CONFLICT or 404, so a double click is harmless. |\n| FR-33 | Admin API | `POST /api/admin/notifications/test` uses `requireRole('ADMIN')`, then `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title, body, link: '/dashboard' })`. The button sits on the email-log page because no separate admin page is needed. |\n| FR-34 | User API | `GET /api/notifications` uses `parseQuery` with Zod (`unread`, `category`), `parsePagination` and `paginated()`. **Category filter caveat:** Notification has no category column. Filter by the `type IN (keys of registry with that category)` derived from the registry at request time. This needs no schema change and remains index-compatible with `userId` leading. |\n| FR-35 | User API | `count({ where: { userId, readAt: null } })` is covered by the `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index (NFR-2). |\n| FR-36 | User API | Mark read or unread with `updateMany({ where: { id, userId: me.id } })`. A count of 0 returns 404, which hides existence from non-owners. `read-all` runs `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null })`. Route files: `[id]/read/route.ts`, `[id]/unread/route.ts` and `read-all/route.ts`. **Next.js routing note:** `read-all` and `unread-count` are static siblings of `[id]`, and static segments win, so they do not conflict. |\n| FR-37 | User API, Preference Resolution | `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` (GET and PUT in one file) is the first route under `/api/me/`. It filters the registry by `roles.includes(me.role)` and `!emailOnly`, merges the rows and returns `{ type, label, description, category, inApp, email, mandatoryInApp }[]`. |\n| FR-38 | User API, Validation | The Zod body is `{ type: z.enum(visibleTypeKeys), inApp: boolean, email: boolean }`. The service rejects `inApp=false` for mandatory types and role-invisible or `emailOnly` types with `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR')`, then calls `upsert` on `userId_type`. |\n| FR-39 | Admin API | `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` (GET) and `[id]/retry/route.ts` (POST), both protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The list is ordered by `createdAt desc` and **omits `html` and `text`** to keep the payload small. |\n| FR-40 | Seed | The seed appends to `prisma/seed.ts`. **See B2: the target users do not exist.** For idempotency, skip a user who already has any `system.test` notification (count > 0), giving 3 per user with 1 read and 2 unread, linking to `/dashboard`. |\n| FR-41 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` is a sibling of the existing `auth.ts`, `users.ts` and so on. It holds the list query schema, the preference PUT schema and `safeLink` (NFR-6). It must be client-safe: no server imports, so registry keys are passed in or the type is checked as a string and then against the registry in the service. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | The budget of 2 s for 1,000 recipients is dominated by 1,000 react-email renders. Mitigate with SchoolSettings fetched once, bounded concurrency, and rendering only recipients with email enabled. If renders are too slow, render the generic template once with a name placeholder. Design should note this as the fallback. |\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Covered by the FR-1 index and FR-35 query shape. The bell must not call the list endpoint on every poll. |\n| NFR-3 | Reliability | No SMTP happens in the request path: `notify()` and `sendAuthEmail` only insert rows. The 15 s worker or the cron endpoint keeps delivery under 60 s. |\n| NFR-4 | Reliability | The FR-17 atomic claim with `SKIP LOCKED`. Each claimed row is owned by exactly one dispatcher. |\n| NFR-5 | Reliability | At the start of each dispatch: `updateMany({ status: SENDING, updatedAt < now-10m }, { status: PENDING })`. This relies on the additive `EmailOutbox.updatedAt`, which is why FR-1 keeps it. It does not increment attempts, because a crash mid-send was not proven to be a send failure. |\n| NFR-6 | Security | A shared `isSafeLink(s)` requires `s.startsWith('/')` and rejects `//`, `/\\`, any `\\` and control characters. It is applied in `notify()` (drop or nullify the link and warn instead of throwing, per FR-11) and in the Zod schema. Unit-tested (NFR-14). |\n| NFR-7 | Security | React-email JSX escapes interpolated text by default. **Never** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` in templates. Body text is rendered as text with `white-space: pre-line`, not as HTML. |\n| NFR-8 | Security | Every new handler starts with `requireUser()` or `requireRole('ADMIN')`. The internal route uses a secret check only (B1). Pages use `requirePageUser()` or `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. |\n| NFR-9 | Security, Transport | Each `sendMail` call sets `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<APP_URL/account/notifications>' }` along with both `html` and `text`. Set it at send time rather than storing it in the outbox, because the outbox has no headers column (B4). |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions (UI) | All 4 UI surfaces (bell, notifications page, preferences page, email log) use MUI only. Dev must query mui-mcp before writing UI, and **this is an unresolved blocker carried forward**: if the server is unreachable, there is a hard stop. The existing `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned libs. Email templates are exempt. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | Thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok`/`paginated`. Services live in `src/server/notifications/` and `src/server/email/`, and code uses `logger`, with `console` only in the console transport. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | UTC storage is the Prisma default. Display uses `formatInSchoolTz` (B7). The client components need the timezone, so pass it from the server page as a prop. |\n| NFR-13 | Conventions | Do not touch `schema.prisma`, navigation or env. Keep the `sendAuthEmail` signature. Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. This is the source of B1–B3 handling. |\n| NFR-14 | Test Harness | Pure units are `resolvePrefs`, `backoffMinutes`, `isSafeLink` and `expandStudentRecipients`. They go in `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`, run under the existing vitest config and need no DB. |\n| NFR-15 | Test Harness | **See B3.** A new `tests/integration/` folder with a node-env vitest config against a test DB. One test runs 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails` calls over 10 rows and asserts each row is sent once. A second test backdates a SENDING row's `updatedAt` by 11 minutes and asserts recovery. |\n| NFR-16 | Test Harness | Playwright tests go in `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`. They need a logged-in admin (the existing e2e harness pattern; check `dashboard.spec.ts` for auth setup). The flow is send test → bell count → mark all read → preference toggle persists after reload. |\n| NFR-17 | Scope Discipline | No SMS, push, websockets or digests. Polling only (FR-23), and do not add a `channel` abstraction for future SMS. |\n| NFR-18 | Notify Service | Silently truncate `title` to 140 characters and `body` to 500, with `logger.warn` (intake default accepted, since it is consistent with FR-11). There is no DB constraint, because the schema has plain `String`. |\n\n## Decisions for design (resolving intake blockers)\n\n1. **FR-1 migration**: Accepted. There is one new migration, `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `schema.prisma` is not changed.\n2. **FR-4/FR-16**: Accepted. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues directly and creates no Notification row. The `account.*` types are `emailOnly` and are filtered out of FR-28 and FR-37 and rejected by FR-38.\n3. **FR-40**: Use 3 per user, but the users are missing (B2). The recommendation is to look them up and skip if absent.\n4. **NFR-10**: Carried forward to dev as a precondition, because the architect cannot resolve it.\n5. **New**: Add `/api/internal/` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (B1). Without it, AC-6 still passes (401), but real cron dispatch never works.\n\n## New/changed files implied (for arch-design-system to confirm)\n\n- **New**: `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/`, `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,purge}.ts`, `src/server/email/{transport,render,dispatch}.ts`, `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`, `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`, `src/app/api/notifications/{route,unread-count/route,read-all/route,[id]/read/route,[id]/unread/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/email-log/{route,[id]/retry/route}.ts`, `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts`, `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx`, `scripts/worker-email.ts`, plus tests under `tests/unit`, `tests/integration` and `tests/e2e`.\n- **Modified**: `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (bell), `src/config/public-routes.ts` (one entry), `prisma/seed.ts` (append), and possibly `package.json` (`test:integration` script only).\n","numLines":107,"startLine":1,"totalLines":107}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wx4Ve9HF22213Ds8Vicdye","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
