{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTZAip2dhUGzpkcvrx9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've settled the design conflicts: generic emails render once per notify() call, a single vitest config with runIf, sendAuthEmail stays throwable, and invite expiry comes from a shared 7-day constant. Writing the design now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1823,"cache_read_input_tokens":59250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1823},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a6de621-bc72-44a5-9725-5c1b7f039997","uuid":"f0a0efa7-29ca-4fc4-8e1d-3d1bc363e4dd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:01:59.109Z","request_id":"req_011CghTZARwzFQTk711XDCBG","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":6,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTZAip2dhUGzpkcvrx9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CozE2jE2XHDbfnhvLvo9FF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11).\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:\n\n1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a\n   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.\n2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A\n   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with\n   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport.\n\nProducers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing\n`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,\nno schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the\nalready-declared tables.\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design handles them\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |\n| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |\n| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |\n| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |\n\n### New blocker-level finding (B1)\n\n`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless\n`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\nwould never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check\nthen becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data layer (FR-1)\n\n- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.\n- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`\n  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).\n- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is\n  derived from the registry at query time.\n\n### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)\n\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;\nexport type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];\ntype NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;\n  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },\n} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\nexport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n```\n\n- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or\n  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).\n- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and\n  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.\n- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API.\n\n### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)\n\n- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`\n  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).\n- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination\n  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.\n- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks\n  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).\n- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`.\n\n### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)\n\n| File | Exports | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |\n| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |\n| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |\n\n`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:\n\n1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).\n   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).\n2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).\n3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).\n4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.\n5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the\n   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.\n6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**\n   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).\n   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.\n7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc\n   says: \"call after your transaction commits\".\n\n`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,\npasses the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12).\n\n*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.\nA later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1.\n\n### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |\n| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |\n| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |\n| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |\n| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |\n| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |\n| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |\n| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |\n| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |\n\n**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.\nIt loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.\nThe invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`\nto an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift\nfrom the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.\nThe raw link is no longer logged.\n\n### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)\n\n| Route file | Guard | Service call |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |\n\nThe service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,\nmark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept\nout of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention.\n\n### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)\n\n`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT\nor SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,\nbecause only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script.\n\n### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)\n\n| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |\n| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |\n| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |\n\nThe server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do\nnot depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13).\n\n### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)\n\nFor each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip\nmessage, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.\nOtherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread.\n\n### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)\n\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,\n  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.\n  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls\n  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`\n  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.\n- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a\n  preference, reload and check that it persisted.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)\n\n```\ncaller service (after its tx commits)\n  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()\n       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18\n       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7\n       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7\n       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10\n       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13\n  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11\n\nusers.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset\n  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16\n```\n\n### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)\n\n```\ndispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })\n 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5\n 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()\n              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()\n                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4\n 3. for each claimed row (sequential):\n      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++\n                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →\n                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18\n 4. return { sent, failed, retried }\n```\n\nTriggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path\nmeets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.\n\n### C. Consumer UI\n\n```\nBell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])\n     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10\n     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)\n     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications\nPrefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)\nEmail log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test\n```\n\n### D. Housekeeping\n\nThe dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process\n(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).\n\n## Files\n\n- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;\n  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;\n  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;\n  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.\n- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`\n  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and\n  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).\n- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-17)\n\nNo SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or\nper-recipient email personalisation.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |\n| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |\n| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |\n| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |\n| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |\n| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |\n| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |\n| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |\n| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |\n| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |\n| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |\n| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |\n| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |\n| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |\n| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |\n| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |\n| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |\n| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |\n| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |\n| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |\n| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |\n| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |\n| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |\n| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |\n| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |\n| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |\n| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |\n| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |\n| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |\n| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |\n| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |\n| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |\n| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |\n| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |\n| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |\n| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |\n| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |\n| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |\n| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |\n| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |\n| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |\n| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |\n| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |\n| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |\n| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |\n| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |\n| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |\n| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |\n| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |\n| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |\n| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |\n| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |\n| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |\n| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |\n| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |\n| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |\n| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1823,"cache_read_input_tokens":59250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1823},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a6de621-bc72-44a5-9725-5c1b7f039997","uuid":"439842f8-0731-4033-9ef3-057063be93ee","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:03:27.755Z","request_id":"req_011CghTZARwzFQTk711XDCBG","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CozE2jE2XHDbfnhvLvo9FF":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11).\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:\n\n1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a\n   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.\n2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A\n   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with\n   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport.\n\nProducers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing\n`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,\nno schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the\nalready-declared tables.\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design handles them\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |\n| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |\n| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |\n| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |\n\n### New blocker-level finding (B1)\n\n`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless\n`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\nwould never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check\nthen becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data layer (FR-1)\n\n- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.\n- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`\n  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).\n- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is\n  derived from the registry at query time.\n\n### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)\n\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;\nexport type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];\ntype NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;\n  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },\n} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\nexport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n```\n\n- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or\n  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).\n- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and\n  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.\n- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API.\n\n### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)\n\n- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`\n  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).\n- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination\n  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.\n- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks\n  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).\n- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`.\n\n### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)\n\n| File | Exports | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |\n| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |\n| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |\n\n`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:\n\n1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).\n   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).\n2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).\n3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).\n4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.\n5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the\n   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.\n6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**\n   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).\n   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.\n7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc\n   says: \"call after your transaction commits\".\n\n`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,\npasses the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12).\n\n*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.\nA later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1.\n\n### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |\n| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |\n| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |\n| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |\n| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |\n| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |\n| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |\n| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |\n| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |\n\n**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.\nIt loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.\nThe invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`\nto an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift\nfrom the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.\nThe raw link is no longer logged.\n\n### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)\n\n| Route file | Guard | Service call |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |\n\nThe service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,\nmark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept\nout of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention.\n\n### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)\n\n`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT\nor SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,\nbecause only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script.\n\n### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)\n\n| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |\n| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |\n| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |\n\nThe server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do\nnot depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13).\n\n### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)\n\nFor each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip\nmessage, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.\nOtherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread.\n\n### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)\n\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,\n  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.\n  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls\n  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`\n  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.\n- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a\n  preference, reload and check that it persisted.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)\n\n```\ncaller service (after its tx commits)\n  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()\n       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18\n       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7\n       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7\n       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10\n       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13\n  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11\n\nusers.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset\n  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16\n```\n\n### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)\n\n```\ndispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })\n 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5\n 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()\n              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()\n                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4\n 3. for each claimed row (sequential):\n      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++\n                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →\n                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18\n 4. return { sent, failed, retried }\n```\n\nTriggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path\nmeets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.\n\n### C. Consumer UI\n\n```\nBell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])\n     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10\n     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)\n     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications\nPrefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)\nEmail log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test\n```\n\n### D. Housekeeping\n\nThe dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process\n(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).\n\n## Files\n\n- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;\n  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;\n  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;\n  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.\n- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`\n  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and\n  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).\n- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-17)\n\nNo SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or\nper-recipient email personalisation.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |\n| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |\n| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |\n| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |\n| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |\n| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |\n| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |\n| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |\n| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |\n| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |\n| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |\n| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |\n| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |\n| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |\n| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |\n| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |\n| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |\n| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |\n| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |\n| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |\n| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |\n| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |\n| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |\n| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |\n| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |\n| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |\n| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |\n| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |\n| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |\n| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |\n| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |\n| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |\n| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |\n| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |\n| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |\n| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |\n| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |\n| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |\n| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |\n| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |\n| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |\n| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |\n| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |\n| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |\n| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |\n| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |\n| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |\n| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |\n| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |\n| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |\n| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |\n| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |\n| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |\n| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |\n| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |\n| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |\n| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CozE2jE2XHDbfnhvLvo9FF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a6de621-bc72-44a5-9725-5c1b7f039997","uuid":"aecb9d4d-6af3-4f9f-aaae-298fb311ee12","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:03:27.913Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11).\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:\n\n1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a\n   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.\n2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A\n   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with\n   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport.\n\nProducers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing\n`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,\nno schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the\nalready-declared tables.\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design handles them\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |\n| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |\n| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |\n| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |\n\n### New blocker-level finding (B1)\n\n`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless\n`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\nwould never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check\nthen becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data layer (FR-1)\n\n- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.\n- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`\n  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).\n- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is\n  derived from the registry at query time.\n\n### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)\n\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;\nexport type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];\ntype NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;\n  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },\n} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\nexport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n```\n\n- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or\n  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).\n- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and\n  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.\n- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API.\n\n### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)\n\n- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`\n  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).\n- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination\n  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.\n- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks\n  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).\n- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`.\n\n### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)\n\n| File | Exports | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |\n| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |\n| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |\n\n`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:\n\n1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).\n   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).\n2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).\n3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).\n4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.\n5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the\n   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.\n6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**\n   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).\n   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.\n7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc\n   says: \"call after your transaction commits\".\n\n`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,\npasses the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12).\n\n*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.\nA later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1.\n\n### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |\n| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |\n| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |\n| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |\n| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |\n| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |\n| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |\n| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |\n| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |\n\n**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.\nIt loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.\nThe invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`\nto an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift\nfrom the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.\nThe raw link is no longer logged.\n\n### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)\n\n| Route file | Guard | Service call |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |\n\nThe service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,\nmark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept\nout of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention.\n\n### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)\n\n`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT\nor SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,\nbecause only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script.\n\n### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)\n\n| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |\n| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |\n| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |\n\nThe server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do\nnot depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13).\n\n### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)\n\nFor each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip\nmessage, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.\nOtherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread.\n\n### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)\n\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,\n  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.\n  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls\n  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`\n  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.\n- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a\n  preference, reload and check that it persisted.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)\n\n```\ncaller service (after its tx commits)\n  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()\n       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18\n       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7\n       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7\n       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10\n       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13\n  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11\n\nusers.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset\n  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16\n```\n\n### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)\n\n```\ndispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })\n 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5\n 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()\n              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()\n                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4\n 3. for each claimed row (sequential):\n      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++\n                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →\n                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18\n 4. return { sent, failed, retried }\n```\n\nTriggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path\nmeets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.\n\n### C. Consumer UI\n\n```\nBell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])\n     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10\n     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)\n     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications\nPrefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)\nEmail log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test\n```\n\n### D. Housekeeping\n\nThe dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process\n(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).\n\n## Files\n\n- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;\n  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;\n  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;\n  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.\n- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`\n  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and\n  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).\n- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-17)\n\nNo SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or\nper-recipient email personalisation.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |\n| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |\n| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |\n| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |\n| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |\n| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |\n| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |\n| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |\n| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |\n| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |\n| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |\n| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |\n| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |\n| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |\n| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |\n| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |\n| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |\n| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |\n| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |\n| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |\n| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |\n| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |\n| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |\n| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |\n| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |\n| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |\n| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |\n| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |\n| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |\n| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |\n| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |\n| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |\n| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |\n| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |\n| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |\n| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |\n| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |\n| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |\n| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |\n| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |\n| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |\n| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |\n| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |\n| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |\n| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |\n| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |\n| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |\n| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |\n| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |\n| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |\n| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |\n| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |\n| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |\n| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |\n| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |\n| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |\n| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":515,"newStart":1,"newLines":318,"lines":["-# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)","+# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)"," ","-Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete","+Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),","-`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),","+`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),"," `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),","-`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.","+`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11)."," "," ## Overview"," ","-PRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:","-Auth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,","-password reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware","-gate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a","-brownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new","-runtime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed.","+PRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:"," ","-Brownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:","-- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,","-  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).","-  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the","-  two AuditLog indexes.","-- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,","-  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.","-  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.","-  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`","-  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).","-- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.","-  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.","-- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`","-  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.","-- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at","-  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file.","+1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a","+   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.","+2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A","+   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with","+   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport."," ","-### Intake blockers and how they're resolved","+Producers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing","+`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,","+no schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the","+already-declared tables."," ","-| Blocker | Resolution |","+### Intake blockers and how this design handles them","+","+| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |","-| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |","-| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |","-| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |","+| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |","+| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |","+| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |","+| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |"," ","----","+### New blocker-level finding (B1)"," ","+`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless","+`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`","+would never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in","+`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check","+then becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).","+"," ## Component Breakdown"," ","-### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)","-- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.","-- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code","-  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip","-  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.","-- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._","+### 1. Data layer (FR-1)"," ","-### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)","-- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):","-  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`","-  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`","-  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`","-  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)","-  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.","-- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,","-  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.","-- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):","-  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`","-    and `checkedAt = now`.","-  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.","-  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run","-    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.","-    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.","-    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.","-  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the","-    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would","-    hide an older password change.","-- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.","-- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.","-  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's","-  route matching, so they can live side by side.","-- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._","+- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with","+  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.","+- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`","+  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).","+- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is","+  derived from the registry at query time."," ","-### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)","-A plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`","-delegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).","-Order of checks:","-1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.","-2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).","-3. Look up the user by email.","-4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**","-   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`","-   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly","-   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).","-5. Branches:","-   - missing user → `invalid`","-   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`","-   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`","-   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`","-   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)","-   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user","-6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns","-   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).","-   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a","-   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent","-   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't","-   matter here.","-7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:","-   - `auth.login.success`","-   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only","-   - `auth.lockout`","-   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.","-8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the","-   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to","-   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"","-   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).","-- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._","+### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)"," ","-### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)","-This is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.","-- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:","-  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,","-    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.","-  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only","-    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.","-  - Returns the raw token.","-- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:","-  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.","-  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong","-    type, is used or is expired.","-- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.","-  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a","-  double-submit fail cleanly.","-- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.","-- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._","+```ts","+export const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;","+export type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];","+type NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;","+  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };","+export const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {","+  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },","+  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },","+  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },","+} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;","+export type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;","+```"," ","-### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)","-- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`","-  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.","-- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.","-- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't","-  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales","-  horizontally.","-- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns","-  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.","-- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._","+- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or","+  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).","+- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and","+  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.","+- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API."," ","-### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)","-- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.","-- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,","-  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.","-- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the","-  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.","-- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`","-  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.","-- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:","-  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.","-  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus","-    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with","-    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.","-  - Every password-setting service calls it.","-- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules","-  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's","-  error response.","-- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._","+### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)"," ","-### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)","-Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:","-```ts","-type SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser","-getCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)","-requireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED","-requireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN","-requirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')","-requirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')","-```","-- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.","-  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.","-- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a","-  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.","-  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,","-  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why","-  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.","-- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,","-  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is","-  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.","-- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`","-  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.","-- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.","-- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._","+- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`","+  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).","+- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination","+  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.","+- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks","+  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).","+- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`."," ","-### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`","-- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`","-  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and","-  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.","-  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.","-  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).","-- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:","-  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that","-     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present","-     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.","-     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely","-     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.","-  2. If the path is public → `next()`.","-  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.","-     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.","-  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.","-- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files","-  with extensions.","-- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the","-  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper","-  on every page and handler.","-- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._","+### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)"," ","-### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)","-Route handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below","-records an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.","-- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:","-  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.","-  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.","-  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.","-  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and","-     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.","-  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.","-  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**","-     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the","-     design reuses the one sign-in path.","-- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:","-  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.","-    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.","-  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the","-    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email","-    was tried before.","-  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,","-    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.","-  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.","-  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.","-- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:","-  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.","-  2. Policy check, then hash.","-  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,","-     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.","-  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.","-- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:","-  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`","-     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.","-  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.","-  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.","-  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this","-     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail","-     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.","-- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:","-  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam","-    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.","-  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.","-  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in","-    audit metadata.","-- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._","+| File | Exports | Notes |","+|---|---|---|","+| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |","+| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |","+| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |"," ","-### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)","-- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).","-- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.","-  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.","-- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then","-  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged","-  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.","-- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._","+`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:"," ","-### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)","-- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.","-- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.","-- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:","-  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.","-- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._","+1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).","+   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).","+2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).","+3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).","+4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.","+5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the","+   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.","+6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**","+   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).","+   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.","+7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc","+   says: \"call after your transaction commits\"."," ","-### 12. App shell and navigation","-- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:","-  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.","-  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.","-    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.","-  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).","-- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:","-  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`","-    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.","-  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.","-  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.","-    That function doesn't need a provider.","-- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._","+`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,","+passes the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12)."," ","-### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)","-- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.","-- **`login/page.tsx`**:","-  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton","-    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.","-  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error","-    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to","-    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.","-  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.","-  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).","-- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200","-  and the FR-7-style message on 429.","-- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:","-  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the","-    FR-14 Alert copy.","-  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.","-- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows","-  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.","-- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:","-  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.","-  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the","-    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.","-- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):","-  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,","-    driven by `passwordChecks`.","-  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset","-    pages share it.","-- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**","-  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.","-  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to","-    the first invalid field.","-  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.","-- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._","+*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.","+A later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1."," ","-### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)","-- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:","-  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`","-  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password","-- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and","-  log the link with `logger.info`.","-- `office@` stays as it is.","-- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._","+### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)"," ","-### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)","-- **Unit tests:**","-  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`","-  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches","-  - `computeLockout`","-  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`","-  - `safeCallbackUrl`","-- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):","-  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch","-  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`","-  - Audit metadata never contains secrets","-- **Playwright:**","-  - Sign-in/out with seeded users","-  - The failed-login message","-  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through","-    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable","-    from the DB.","-  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages","-- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.","-- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._","+| File | Responsibility |","+|---|---|","+| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |","+| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |","+| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |","+| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |","+| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |","+| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |","+| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |","+| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |","+| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |"," ","----","+**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.","+It loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.","+The invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`","+to an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift","+from the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.","+The raw link is no longer logged."," ","-## Data Flow","+### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)"," ","-**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**","-1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →","-   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.","-2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt","-   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.","-3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.","-   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.","-4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.","-   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert.","+| Route file | Guard | Service call |","+|---|---|---|","+| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |","+| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |","+| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |","+| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |","+| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |","+| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |","+| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |","+| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |","+| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |"," ","-**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**","-1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.","-   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.","-   - No session on `/api` → 401.","-2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`","-   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).","-3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.","-   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.","-4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page).","+The service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,","+mark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept","+out of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention."," ","-**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**","-1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`","-   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).","-2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`","-   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.","-3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.","-   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.","-4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`.","+### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)"," ","-**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**","-1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →","-   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.","-   The response is always the generic message.","-2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash","-   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it","-   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast.","+`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT","+or SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,","+because only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script."," ","-**Change password (FR-23)**","-1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.","-2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a","-   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.","-3. The toast reads \"Password updated\".","+### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)"," ","----","+| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |","+|---|---|---|","+| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |","+| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |","+| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |","+| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |"," ","-## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)","+The server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do","+not depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13)."," ","-| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |","-| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |","-| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |","-| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |","-| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |","+### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)"," ","-All custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the","-`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:","-- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`","-- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401","-- `FORBIDDEN` 403","-- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens","-- `RATE_LIMITED` 429","+For each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip","+message, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.","+Otherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread."," ","-`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).","+### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)"," ","-## New / changed files","+- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,","+  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.","+- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.","+  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls","+  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`","+  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.","+- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a","+  preference, reload and check that it persisted."," ","-**New:**","-- `src/middleware.ts`","-- `src/config/public-routes.ts`","-- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`","-- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`","-- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`","-- `src/server/services/auth.ts`","-- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`","-- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`","-- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`","-- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`","-- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`","-- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`","-- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`","+## Data Flow"," ","-**Changed:**","-- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes","-- `prisma/seed.ts`","-- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`","-- `src/server/audit.ts`","-- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`","-- `src/server/services/users.ts`","-- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`","-- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`","-- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants","-- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`","-- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly","+### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)"," ","-**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the","-comment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).","+```","+caller service (after its tx commits)","+  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()","+       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18","+       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7","+       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7","+       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10","+       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13","+  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11"," ","-**Skipped on purpose:**","-- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.","-- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.","-- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.","-- Client-side common-password list.","-- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.","+users.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset","+  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16","+```"," ","----","+### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)"," ","+```","+dispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })","+ 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5","+ 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()","+              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()","+                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)","+              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4","+ 3. for each claimed row (sequential):","+      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++","+                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →","+                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18","+ 4. return { sent, failed, retried }","+```","+","+Triggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path","+meets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.","+","+### C. Consumer UI","+","+```","+Bell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])","+     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10","+     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)","+     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications","+Prefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)","+Email log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test","+```","+","+### D. Housekeeping","+","+The dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process","+(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).","+","+## Files","+","+- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;","+  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;","+  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;","+  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.","+- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`","+  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and","+  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).","+- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.","+","+## Out of scope (NFR-17)","+","+No SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or","+per-recipient email personalisation.","+"," ## Requirements Traceability"," "," | Req | Design element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |","-| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |","-| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |","-| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |","-| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |","-| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |","-| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |","-| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |","-| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |","-| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |","-| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |","-| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |","-| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |","-| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |","-| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |","-| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |","-| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |","-| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |","-| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |","-| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |","-| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |","-| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |","-| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |","-| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |","-| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |","-| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |","-| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |","-| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |","-| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |","-| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |","-| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |","-| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |","-| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |","-| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |","-| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |","-| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |","-| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |","-| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |","-| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |","-| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |","-| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |","-| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |","-| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |","-| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |","-| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |","-| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |","-| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |","-| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |","-| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |","+| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |","+| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |","+| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |","+| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |","+| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |","+| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |","+| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |","+| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |","+| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |","+| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |","+| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |","+| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |","+| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |","+| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |","+| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |","+| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |","+| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |","+| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |","+| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |","+| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |","+| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |","+| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |","+| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |","+| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |","+| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |","+| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |","+| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |","+| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |","+| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |","+| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |","+| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |","+| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |","+| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |","+| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |","+| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |","+| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |","+| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |","+| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |","+| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |","+| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |","+| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |","+| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |","+| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |","+| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |","+| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |","+| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |","+| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |","+| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |","+| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |","+| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |","+| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |","+| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |","+| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |","+| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |","+| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |","+| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |","+| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |","+| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |","+| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |"]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC, SCH-001)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T00:02:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (37 FR + 12 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (94% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-01 replaces the `PLACEHOLDER_USER` stand-ins with real authentication:\nAuth.js v5 Credentials sign-in, 8-hour JWT sessions, invite activation,\npassword reset and change, lockout and rate limiting, an edge middleware\ngate, and real session-backed `requireUser()` / `requireRole()`. This is a\nbrownfield change on Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma + MUI v9. **No new\nruntime dependency**: `next-auth` 5 beta and `bcrypt` 6 are already installed.\n\nBrownfield facts re-checked on disk for this design:\n- All User auth columns already exist (`passwordHash`, `failedLoginCount`,\n  `lockedUntil`, `lastLoginAt`, `passwordChangedAt`, `archivedAt`).\n  `AuthToken.tokenHash` is already `@unique`. The only schema gap is the\n  two AuditLog indexes.\n- `requireRole(` has **50 call sites in 43 files: 33 `route.ts`, 8 pages/layouts,\n  1 in `navigation.ts` (a comment), 1 in `course-access.ts` (a comment)**.\n  None use `await` today, and every caller is already in an async function.\n  `course-access.ts` and `student-access.ts` take an `AccessUser {id, role}`\n  argument and don't call `requireRole`, so they stay untouched (NFR-9).\n- `navigationForRole(role)` already exists in `src/config/navigation.ts`.\n  FR-33 is just about feeding it the real role.\n- `src/server/http.ts` already has `AppError`, `withHandler`, `parseBody`\n  and the codes UNAUTHENTICATED/FORBIDDEN/RATE_LIMITED/CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR.\n- The project uses a `src/` dir, so Next only picks up middleware at\n  **`src/middleware.ts`**, not at the repo root. FR-12's \"middleware.ts\" means that file.\n\n### Intake blockers and how they're resolved\n\n| Blocker | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 schema divergences (`ip` vs `ipAddress`, extra `ARCHIVED`, different indexes) | **Resolved, additive only** (ADR-9). Keep `AuditLog.ip`, keep `UserStatus.ARCHIVED`, keep the existing indexes. Add `@@index([entityType, entityId])` and `@@index([actorId, createdAt])` to AuditLog in one migration, `auth_reconcile`. FR-4's `status !== 'ACTIVE'` check already rejects ARCHIVED. |\n| FR-25 `createUser` / `setUserStatus` signatures differ from PRD | **Resolved: keep the existing PRD-03 signatures.** No second `createUser`. A duplicate email already maps P2002 → CONFLICT through `withHandler`. `createUser` must lower-case the email (FR-2). Dev only verifies this and adds a one-line fix if it's missing. |\n| FR-28/29 `requireRole()` is sync, Auth.js `auth()` is async | **Resolved: go async** (ADR-2). Each of the 50 call sites gets a mechanical `await`. The return shape stays a superset of `{id, role}`. The 8 server pages/layouts switch to the redirecting page variants (Component 7). |\n| NFR-6 mui-mcp must be reachable | **Not blocking at architect time.** The `useMuiDocs` / `fetchDocs` tools are registered in this environment. The Dev phase must still confirm it can reach them before writing UI, and must stop and report a blocker if it can't. |\n\n---\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data model (`prisma/schema.prisma`, migration `auth_reconcile`)\n- Add the two AuditLog indexes only. No renames, no drops, no column changes.\n- `User.email` stays `String @unique`. Lower-casing is enforced in app code\n  at every write and lookup through one zod transform (Component 6). Skip\n  `citext`, because switching the column type isn't additive.\n- _FR-1, FR-2, NFR-9, NFR-12 (columns are already UTC `DateTime`)._\n\n### 2. Auth.js core, split config (ADR-1)\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.config.ts`** (edge-safe, no Prisma or bcrypt imports):\n  - `session: { strategy: 'jwt', maxAge: 8 * 3600, updateAge: 15 * 60 }`\n  - `pages: { signIn: '/login' }`, `providers: []`\n  - `callbacks.session`: copies `id, role, firstName, lastName, email` from the token to `session.user`\n  - `callbacks.redirect`: `safeCallbackUrl()` (Component 6)\n  - Cookies use the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and `__Secure-` + Secure in production. Don't override them.\n- **`src/server/auth/auth.ts`** (Node): `NextAuth({ ...authConfig, providers: [Credentials({ authorize })], callbacks: { ...authConfig.callbacks, jwt } })`,\n  exporting `{ handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update }`.\n- **`jwt` callback** (Node only; does session revocation, ADR-4):\n  - On `trigger === 'signIn'`: copy the user fields, then set `authTime = now`\n    and `checkedAt = now`.\n  - On `trigger === 'update'` with `{ reauth: true }` (FR-23): set `authTime = now`.\n  - Otherwise, if `now - checkedAt > 5 min`: run\n    `select { passwordChangedAt, status, role, firstName, lastName }`.\n    Return `null` if `status !== 'ACTIVE'` or `passwordChangedAt > authTime`.\n    Otherwise refresh `role` and the names, and set `checkedAt = now`.\n  - **Use the custom `authTime` claim, not JWT `iat`.** Auth.js re-signs the\n    token on every `updateAge` refresh, so `iat` moves forward and would\n    hide an older password change.\n- **`src/types/next-auth.d.ts`**: module augmentation for the typed `session.user` and JWT fields.\n- **`src/app/api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts`**: `export const { GET, POST } = handlers`.\n  Static siblings like `accept-invite/` win over the catch-all in Next's\n  route matching, so they can live side by side.\n- _FR-3, FR-10, FR-11, FR-34, NFR-2._\n\n### 3. Credential verification (`src/server/auth/credentials.ts`)\nA plain exported `authorizeCredentials(input, request)` that `Credentials.authorize`\ndelegates to, so integration tests can call it without going over HTTP (FR-36).\nOrder of checks:\n1. `rateLimit('login:ip:' + getClientIp(request), 10, 5 min)`. Over the limit → throw `AuthError('rate_limited')`.\n2. Parse `{email, password}` with `signInSchema` (trim + lower-case the email).\n3. Look up the user by email.\n4. **Reject missing or ineligible users only after the bcrypt compare.**\n   Compare against the user's hash, or against a module-level `DUMMY_HASH`\n   (cost 12) if the user is missing or has no hash. Every path runs exactly\n   one bcrypt compare (NFR-3, NFR-4).\n5. Branches:\n   - missing user → `invalid`\n   - `status === 'DISABLED'` → `disabled`\n   - `status !== 'ACTIVE'` (INVITED, ARCHIVED) or `archivedAt` set → `invalid`\n   - `lockedUntil > now` → `locked:<minutes>`, where minutes = `ceil((lockedUntil - now) / 60000)`\n   - wrong password → run `registerFailure`, then `invalid` (or `locked:15` if this attempt triggered the lock)\n   - success → set `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lastLoginAt = now`, return the user\n6. Lockout logic is the pure function `computeLockout(currentCount, now)`, which returns\n   `{ failedLoginCount, lockedUntil | null }` (5 failures → lock for 15 min and reset the count to 0).\n   The DB write is one `update` with `failedLoginCount: { increment: 1 }`, followed by a\n   conditional lock update when the returned count reaches 5. **Ceiling:** concurrent\n   failures can overshoot the count by one before the lock lands, which doesn't\n   matter here.\n7. Audit entries, passing the request so the IP is recorded:\n   - `auth.login.success`\n   - `auth.login.failure` with `{ email, reason }` only\n   - `auth.lockout`\n   - `actorId` is the user id when the user is known, otherwise null.\n8. `class AuthError extends CredentialsSignin { code }`. The login form reads the\n   error `code` from `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` and maps it to\n   the FR-5 / FR-7 messages. For `locked:N`, it renders \"Try again in N minutes.\"\n   N is a duration, so no timezone conversion is needed (NFR-12).\n- _FR-4, FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-9, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-12._\n\n### 4. Token module (`src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, ADR-5)\nThis is the only code that touches the `AuthToken` model.\n- `createToken(userId, type, ttl: { minutes?, days? }, tx?)`:\n  - In one transaction, `updateMany { userId, type, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`,\n    which invalidates older unused tokens (FR-20, FR-26). Then insert the new row.\n  - The raw token is `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`. Only\n    `sha256(raw)` (hex) is stored.\n  - Returns the raw token.\n- `verifyToken(raw, type)`:\n  - Find by `tokenHash`, then confirm with `timingSafeEqual` on the hash buffers.\n  - Returns `{ token, user }`, or `null` if the token is missing, has the wrong\n    type, is used or is expired.\n- `consumeToken(tokenId, tx?)`: `updateMany { id, usedAt: null } → usedAt = now`.\n  Throws `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` if the update count is 0, which makes a\n  double-submit fail cleanly.\n- Pure `hashToken(raw)` is exported so the unit tests can use it.\n- _FR-13, FR-14, FR-20, FR-26, FR-31, NFR-1._\n\n### 5. Rate limiter (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`, ADR-6)\n- `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs, now = Date.now()) → { ok, retryAfterMs }`\n  over a module-level `Map<string, number[]>`. It prunes old timestamps on each call.\n- Exports `__resetRateLimits()` for tests.\n- Add a `ponytail: per-process limiter` comment: it resets on restart and isn't\n  shared across instances. Swap the Map for Redis/Postgres if the app scales\n  horizontally.\n- `getClientIp(request)` goes in the existing **`src/server/http.ts`**. It returns\n  the first `x-forwarded-for` entry, trimmed, or `null`. The limiter and `audit()` share it.\n- _FR-7, FR-19, FR-30, NFR-11._\n\n### 6. Validators and pure helpers (`src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, client-safe)\n- `emailField`: `z.string().trim().toLowerCase().email()`.\n- `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `acceptInviteSchema {token, password, confirm}`,\n  `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordSchema {currentPassword, newPassword, confirm}`.\n- `passwordChecks(pw, email)` returns `{ length, letter, digit, notEmail }`. Both the\n  checklist UI and the schema's `superRefine` use it.\n- `safeCallbackUrl(url)`: returns `url` only if it starts with `/` and not with `//`\n  or `/\\`. Otherwise it returns `/dashboard`.\n- **Server-only `src/server/auth/password-policy.ts`**:\n  - Reads `common-passwords.txt` once into a `Set`.\n  - Exports `assertPasswordAllowed(pw, email)`, which runs `passwordChecks` plus\n    the common-list check and throws `VALIDATION_ERROR` with\n    `details.fieldErrors.password` if any rule fails.\n  - Every password-setting service calls it.\n- The 1,000-word list never ships to the client. The checklist shows four rules\n  live, and the \"not a common password\" rule appears only from the server's\n  error response.\n- _FR-2, FR-8, FR-17, FR-18, NFR-8._\n\n### 7. Authorization helpers (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, ADR-2)\nDelete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Every helper goes through one internal resolver:\n```ts\ntype SessionUser = { id; role; firstName; lastName; email }   // superset of AccessUser\ngetCurrentUser = cache(async (): Promise<SessionUser | null> => (await auth())?.user ?? null)\nrequireUser(): Promise<SessionUser>                // throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED\nrequireRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>        // throws UNAUTHENTICATED / FORBIDDEN\nrequirePageUser(): Promise<SessionUser>            // redirect('/login?callbackUrl=…')\nrequirePageRole(...roles): Promise<SessionUser>    // redirect('/login…') / redirect('/forbidden')\n```\n- **Route handlers** (33 files) change from `requireRole(` to `await requireRole(`.\n  `withHandler` already maps a thrown `AppError` to the 401/403 envelope.\n- **Server pages/layouts** (8 files) change to `await requirePageRole(` because a\n  thrown AppError in a page would render `error.tsx`, not a redirect.\n  `redirect()` throws `NEXT_REDIRECT` and must never run inside `withHandler`,\n  since it would be caught there and turned into an INTERNAL error. That's why\n  the page variants are separate exports instead of a flag.\n- The page variants read the current path from the `x-pathname` request header,\n  which `src/middleware.ts` sets, to build `callbackUrl`. If the header is\n  missing, they fall back to `/dashboard`.\n- **Guardrail for missed awaits:** turn on `@typescript-eslint/no-floating-promises`\n  for `src/**`. Typecheck alone misses a bare `requireRole('ADMIN');` statement.\n- No `permissions.ts`, no `can()`.\n- _FR-28, FR-29, NFR-7, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10._\n\n### 8. Edge middleware (`src/middleware.ts`) and `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `public-routes.ts` exports `PUBLIC_PAGE_PATHS = ['/', '/login', '/forgot-password', '/invite/', '/reset-password/']`\n  (a trailing `/` means prefix match) and\n  `PUBLIC_API_PATHS = ['/api/health', '/api/auth/']`.\n  `/api/auth/` covers the Auth.js catch-all and the three unauthenticated POSTs.\n  The list has **no sign-up path** (FR-37).\n- `export default NextAuth(authConfig).auth(req => …)` runs these steps in order:\n  1. **CSRF origin check (NFR-2):** for any non-GET/HEAD `/api/*` request that\n     isn't under `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`'s own endpoints, if `Origin` is present\n     and doesn't equal the app origin, return 403 FORBIDDEN in the JSON envelope.\n     Auth.js CSRF tokens only protect Auth.js's own endpoints. Custom POSTs rely\n     on this check plus SameSite=Lax.\n  2. If the path is public → `next()`.\n  3. If there's no session: `/api/*` → 401 `{error:{code:'UNAUTHENTICATED',…}}`.\n     Pages → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=<path+search>`.\n  4. Otherwise → `next()` and set the `x-pathname` request header.\n- `matcher` excludes `_next/static`, `_next/image`, `favicon.ico` and files\n  with extensions.\n- Middleware only decodes the JWT. It doesn't check revocation, because the\n  Node `jwt` callback does that. NFR-7's real guard is the server-side helper\n  on every page and handler.\n- _FR-12, FR-37, NFR-2, NFR-7, NFR-8._\n\n### 9. Auth services (`src/server/services/auth.ts`, Node)\nRoute handlers stay thin: zod parse → service → `ok()`. Every service below\nrecords an audit entry with the request so the IP is captured.\n- `acceptInvite({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')`, or throw `INVALID_TOKEN`.\n  2. `assertPasswordAllowed(password, user.email)`.\n  3. `bcrypt.hash(password, 12)`.\n  4. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `status = ACTIVE` and\n     `passwordChangedAt = now`, then `consumeToken`.\n  5. Audit `auth.invite.accepted`.\n  6. Return `{ email }`. **The client then calls `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirectTo: '/dashboard'})`.**\n     Minting an Auth.js session by hand in a custom route is fragile, so the\n     design reuses the one sign-in path.\n- `requestPasswordReset({email}, request)`:\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:ip:'+ip, 10, 1h)`. Over the limit → `RATE_LIMITED` 429.\n    An IP-level response doesn't reveal whether an account exists.\n  - `rateLimit('forgot:email:'+email, 3, 1h)`. Over the limit → **return the\n    generic success message silently**. A 429 here would reveal that the email\n    was tried before.\n  - If the user exists and is ACTIVE: `createToken(id, 'PASSWORD_RESET', {minutes: 60})`,\n    then `sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link)`.\n  - Unknown or inactive email: no DB write.\n  - Always return `{ message: \"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\" }`.\n- `resetPassword({token, password}, request)`:\n  1. `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`.\n  2. Policy check, then hash.\n  3. In one transaction: set `passwordHash`, `passwordChangedAt = now`,\n     `failedLoginCount = 0` and `lockedUntil = null`, then `consumeToken`.\n  4. Audit `auth.password.reset`.\n- `changePassword(user, {currentPassword, newPassword}, request)`:\n  1. bcrypt-compare `currentPassword`. If it's wrong → throw `VALIDATION_ERROR`\n     with `details.fieldErrors.currentPassword = ['Current password is incorrect.']`.\n  2. Policy check, hash, and update `passwordHash` and `passwordChangedAt`.\n  3. Audit `auth.password.changed`.\n  4. The route handler then calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this\n     session's `authTime` moves past `passwordChangedAt`. Other sessions fail\n     the FR-11 check within 5 minutes.\n- **`src/server/auth/email.ts`** `sendAuthEmail(user, kind: 'invite' | 'password-reset', link)`:\n  - Logs `{ to, subject, link }` with `logger.info`. This is the single seam\n    PRD-04 replaces with an EmailOutbox enqueue.\n  - Links are built from `env.AUTH_URL`: `/invite/<raw>` and `/reset-password/<raw>`.\n  - Raw tokens appear only in this log line and in the email itself, never in\n    audit metadata.\n- _FR-16, FR-19, FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, FR-31, NFR-3, NFR-8._\n\n### 10. Users service additions (`src/server/services/users.ts`)\n- Keep `createUser`, `setUserStatus(actorId, userId, status)` and `unlockUser(userId)` as they are (FR-25).\n- Add `createInviteToken(userId)`, which returns `createToken(userId, 'INVITE', { days: 7 })`.\n  `tokens.createToken` already invalidates older unused tokens.\n- Replace the no-op body of `sendInvite(userId)` with: `createInviteToken`, then\n  `sendAuthEmail(user, 'invite', link)`, then return the unchanged\n  `{ id, inviteSentAt }` shape.\n- _FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-2._\n\n### 11. Audit (`src/server/audit.ts`)\n- Add an optional `request?: Request` to the input. Set `ip: request ? getClientIp(request) : null`.\n- The function stays inside its existing try/catch and never throws.\n- Defence in depth: before the insert, strip these metadata keys:\n  `password`, `passwordHash`, `newPassword`, `currentPassword`, `token`, `rawToken`.\n- _FR-9, FR-30, FR-31._\n\n### 12. App shell and navigation\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`:\n  - `const user = await requirePageUser()`.\n  - Pass `user` (id, name, role, email) and `navigationForRole(user.role)` to `<AppShell>`.\n    Props avoid a `SessionProvider` round-trip and the flash of empty UI it causes.\n  - Filtering the nav doesn't protect anything on its own (NFR-7).\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`:\n  - Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and render the user from props: `UserAvatar`\n    (initials), name, and a role `Chip`.\n  - The user menu gains **\"Account security\" → `/account/security`**.\n  - Sign out calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n    That function doesn't need a provider.\n- _FR-24, FR-32, FR-33, NFR-6, NFR-7._\n\n### 13. Auth UI (MUI v9 only, every component looked up through mui-mcp first, NFR-6)\n- **`src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`**: a centred `Container` + `Card` layout without the AppShell.\n- **`login/page.tsx`**:\n  - Uses the MUI Sign-in template patterns: TextField, an InputAdornment + IconButton\n    show-password toggle, and an Alert for form errors.\n  - Client submit calls `signIn('credentials', {redirect: false})`, maps the error\n    code to the FR-5 / FR-7 copy, and on success navigates to\n    `safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl)`.\n  - If the page loads with `?reset=1`, it fires the `useToast` success toast for FR-21.\n  - Links to `/forgot-password`. **No sign-up link** (FR-37).\n- **`forgot-password/page.tsx`**: an email field. It shows the generic message on 200\n  and the FR-7-style message on 429.\n- **`invite/[token]/page.tsx`**:\n  - A server component calls `verifyToken`. If the token is invalid, it shows the\n    FR-14 Alert copy.\n  - Otherwise it renders `<SetPasswordForm>` with the read-only name and email.\n- **`reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`**: verifies the token the same way, then shows\n  `<SetPasswordForm>`. On success it redirects to `/login?reset=1`.\n- **`(app)/account/security/page.tsx`**:\n  - Calls `requirePageUser()`.\n  - The form has current, new and confirm password fields. On success it shows the\n    \"Password updated\" toast. A field error renders on `currentPassword`.\n- **Shared pieces** (in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`):\n  - **`PasswordChecklist`**: an MUI `List` with CheckCircle/RadioButtonUnchecked icons,\n    driven by `passwordChecks`.\n  - **`SetPasswordForm`**: password, confirm and the checklist. The invite and reset\n    pages share it.\n- **Form accessibility, applied to all 5 forms (NFR-5):**\n  - Form-level `Alert` sits inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`.\n  - react-hook-form + `zodResolver` with `shouldFocusError: true`, so focus moves to\n    the first invalid field.\n  - Server `details.fieldErrors` are mapped to `setError`.\n- _FR-3, FR-5, FR-14, FR-15, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-23, FR-37, NFR-5, NFR-6._\n\n### 14. Seed (`prisma/seed.ts`)\n- Upsert by email, so re-running the seed is safe:\n  - `admin@`, `teacher@`, `teacher2@`, `student@`, `student2@` and `parent@schoolhub.test`\n  - All ACTIVE, with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` as the password\n- Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` as INVITED, then call `createInviteToken` and\n  log the link with `logger.info`.\n- `office@` stays as it is.\n- _FR-35, FR-13 (all seeded tokens go through tokens.ts)._\n\n### 15. Tests (Vitest + Playwright, ADR-10)\n- **Unit tests:**\n  - `passwordChecks` / `assertPasswordAllowed`\n  - `hashToken` and the verify expiry/used branches\n  - `computeLockout`\n  - `rateLimit`, with an injected `now`\n  - `safeCallbackUrl`\n- **Integration tests** (against the test DB):\n  - Every `authorizeCredentials` branch\n  - `acceptInvite`, `resetPassword` and `changePassword`\n  - Audit metadata never contains secrets\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Sign-in/out with seeded users\n  - The failed-login message\n  - Forgot → reset. The test reads the token by creating one through\n    `createToken` in a test helper, because the raw token isn't recoverable\n    from the DB.\n  - `@axe-core/playwright` on the auth pages\n- Lint, typecheck and test must stay green. Use `logger` only.\n- _FR-36, NFR-5, NFR-10._\n\n---\n\n## Data Flow\n\n**Sign-in (FR-3–FR-10)**\n1. The browser posts to `/login` → `signIn('credentials')` →\n   `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials`, protected by the Auth.js CSRF token.\n2. `authorize` → `authorizeCredentials`: rate limit, user lookup, one bcrypt\n   compare, then the lockout/branch logic and audit.\n3. The `jwt` callback (`trigger='signIn'`) writes `{id, role, names, email, authTime, checkedAt}`.\n   The session cookie is HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.\n4. The client receives `ok` → `router.push(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))`.\n   On error, the code maps to a message rendered in the aria-live Alert.\n\n**Authenticated request (FR-11, FR-12, FR-28, FR-29)**\n1. `src/middleware.ts` decodes the JWT on the edge.\n   - No session on a page → redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`.\n   - No session on `/api` → 401.\n2. The page or handler calls `await requireRole(...)` → `getCurrentUser()`\n   (React `cache`) → `auth()` (Node).\n3. The `jwt` callback re-checks `passwordChangedAt` / `status` at most every 5 minutes.\n   If the check fails, the session becomes null → UNAUTHENTICATED, or a redirect to `/login`.\n4. The role check fails → FORBIDDEN 403 (API) or `/forbidden` (page).\n\n**Invite (FR-13–FR-16, FR-26, FR-27)**\n1. PRD-03 admin `sendInvite(userId)` → `createInviteToken` → `tokens.createToken`\n   (invalidates older tokens, stores the hash) → `sendAuthEmail` (logs the link).\n2. The user opens `/invite/<raw>`. The server component runs `verifyToken`\n   (hash lookup + timingSafeEqual) and renders the form or the invalid Alert.\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → middleware origin check → `acceptInvite`.\n   In one transaction it sets ACTIVE and the hash, then consumes the token, and audits.\n4. On 200, the client calls `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`.\n\n**Forgot / reset (FR-19–FR-22)**\n1. `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → IP limit (429) → email limit (silent) →\n   ACTIVE user? `createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60 min)` + `sendAuthEmail`.\n   The response is always the generic message.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `POST /api/auth/reset-password`, which sets the hash\n   and `passwordChangedAt`, clears the lockout and consumes the token. Then it\n   audits and the browser goes to `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n\n**Change password (FR-23)**\n1. `/account/security` → `POST /api/account/password` → `await requireUser()` → `changePassword`.\n2. The handler calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`, so this session gets a\n   new `authTime`. Other devices fail the next 5-minute check.\n3. The toast reads \"Password updated\".\n\n---\n\n## API Surface (for `arch-api-contracts`)\n\n| Method | Path | Auth | Handler → service | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| GET/POST | `/api/auth/[...nextauth]` | public (Auth.js protocol) | `handlers` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-34, NFR-2 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/accept-invite` | public + origin check | `acceptInvite` | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-1, NFR-8 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/forgot-password` | public + origin check | `requestPasswordReset` | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-3 |\n| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | public + origin check | `resetPassword` | FR-21, FR-17 |\n| POST | `/api/account/password` | `requireUser()` | `changePassword` | FR-23, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n\nAll custom routes use `withHandler`, `parseBody(schema)` and `ok()`, returning the\n`{data}` / `{error:{code,message,details}}` envelopes. Codes:\n- `VALIDATION_ERROR` 400: policy failures and wrong current password, with `details.fieldErrors`\n- `UNAUTHENTICATED` 401\n- `FORBIDDEN` 403\n- `INVALID_TOKEN` 410: invalid, used or expired invite/reset tokens\n- `RATE_LIMITED` 429\n\n`/api/health` stays public and is unchanged. There's no sign-up endpoint (FR-37).\n\n## New / changed files\n\n**New:**\n- `src/middleware.ts`\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`\n- `src/types/next-auth.d.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/{auth.config.ts, auth.ts, credentials.ts, tokens.ts, email.ts, password-policy.ts, common-passwords.txt}`\n- `src/server/rate-limit.ts`\n- `src/server/services/auth.ts`\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`\n- `src/components/PasswordChecklist/{PasswordChecklist.tsx, SetPasswordForm.tsx, index.ts}`\n- `src/app/(auth)/{layout.tsx, login/page.tsx, forgot-password/page.tsx, invite/[token]/page.tsx, reset-password/[token]/page.tsx}`\n- `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`\n- `src/app/api/auth/{[...nextauth], accept-invite, forgot-password, reset-password}/route.ts`\n- `src/app/api/account/password/route.ts`\n- Prisma migration `auth_reconcile`\n\n**Changed:**\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: 2 indexes\n- `prisma/seed.ts`\n- `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`\n- `src/server/audit.ts`\n- `src/server/http.ts`: `+getClientIp`\n- `src/server/services/users.ts`\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`\n- `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`\n- The 41 `requireRole` call-site files: `await` + page variants\n- ESLint config: `no-floating-promises`\n- `package.json`: pin `next-auth` exactly\n\n**Untouched (NFR-9):** `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts`, `navigation.ts` (the\ncomment on line 21 can be updated, but no logic changes).\n\n**Skipped on purpose:**\n- SessionProvider: the shell gets the user as props.\n- Prisma adapter: not needed for JWT sessions.\n- Redis limiter: one process is enough for now.\n- Client-side common-password list.\n- Signed-in redirect away from `/login`: not required by the PRD.\n\n---\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1: additive migration `auth_reconcile` (2 AuditLog indexes; keep `ip` and ARCHIVED) |\n| FR-2 | C6 `emailField` transform, used by sign-in, forgot and `createUser` (C10) |\n| FR-3 | C13 login page, C2 Credentials provider |\n| FR-4 | C3 `authorizeCredentials` (status/archived/locked checks, bcrypt cost 12) |\n| FR-5 | C3 `AuthError` codes → C13 message mapping |\n| FR-6 | C3 `computeLockout` plus the atomic increment and lock update |\n| FR-7 | C5 `rateLimit('login:ip:…', 10, 5 min)` called from C3 |\n| FR-8 | C6 `safeCallbackUrl`, used in C2's redirect callback and C13 |\n| FR-9 | C3 audit calls (`auth.login.success`, `auth.login.failure`, `auth.lockout`) |\n| FR-10 | C2 JWT session (8 h, `updateAge`) and token/session fields |\n| FR-11 | C2 `jwt` callback: 5-min `passwordChangedAt > authTime` check |\n| FR-12 | C8 `src/middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `tokens.ts` (create/verify/consume, SHA-256) |\n| FR-14 | C13 `invite/[token]` page + C4 `verifyToken` (7-day TTL) |\n| FR-15 | C13 `SetPasswordForm` with the read-only name/email |\n| FR-16 | C9 `acceptInvite` + `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` + client `signIn` |\n| FR-17 | C6 `passwordChecks` + C6 server `assertPasswordAllowed` + `common-passwords.txt` |\n| FR-18 | C13 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-19 | C9 `requestPasswordReset` (generic reply; IP 429, silent email limit) |\n| FR-20 | C9 + C4 (`PASSWORD_RESET` 60 min; invalidate old tokens; no row for unknown emails) |\n| FR-21 | C9 `resetPassword` + `/login?reset=1` toast |\n| FR-22 | C9 `sendAuthEmail` → `logger.info` |\n| FR-23 | C9 `changePassword` + `unstable_update({reauth:true})` + C13 security page |\n| FR-24 | C12 user menu \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-25 | C10: keep the existing `createUser` / `setUserStatus` / `unlockUser` |\n| FR-26 | C10 `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-27 | C10 real `sendInvite` body, same return shape |\n| FR-28 | C7 `getCurrentUser` / `requireUser` / `requirePageUser`; PLACEHOLDER_USER removed |\n| FR-29 | C7 async `requireRole` / `requirePageRole`; 50 call sites awaited |\n| FR-30 | C11 `audit({request})` + C5 `getClientIp` |\n| FR-31 | C11 metadata key stripping; C3/C9 pass explicit metadata only |\n| FR-32 | C12 layout passes the session user; shell shows avatar/name/role; `signOut` |\n| FR-33 | C12 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-34 | C2 `api/auth/[...nextauth]/route.ts` |\n| FR-35 | C14 seed upserts + invited user's link logged |\n| FR-36 | C15 unit/integration/Playwright suites |\n| FR-37 | C8 no sign-up path in `public-routes.ts`; C13 no sign-up link; no sign-up endpoint |\n| NFR-1 | C4 SHA-256 at rest + `timingSafeEqual` |\n| NFR-2 | C2 Auth.js cookie defaults + CSRF; C8 origin check on custom POSTs |\n| NFR-3 | C3 `DUMMY_HASH`, one compare on every path; C9 forgot-password always gives the same reply |\n| NFR-4 | C3 single bcrypt compare, 1 query + ≤2 updates |\n| NFR-5 | C13 aria-live Alert + `shouldFocusError` + server field errors |\n| NFR-6 | C13 / C12 MUI v9 only, looked up through mui-mcp (Dev must confirm it's reachable) |\n| NFR-7 | C7 helpers on every page/handler; C8 is only the first gate; C12 nav filtering is UX only |\n| NFR-8 | C9 thin handlers with `withHandler` / `parseBody` / `ok`; API Surface codes |\n| NFR-9 | Blocker resolutions; C10 reuse; access modules untouched; no renames |\n| NFR-10 | C7 `no-floating-promises`; C15; logger only |\n| NFR-11 | Scope: no admin UI, SSO, MFA or email infrastructure; C5 in-memory limiter |\n| NFR-12 | C1 UTC columns; C3 lockout minutes as a duration; `lastLoginAt` displayed with existing `DateDisplay` in `SchoolSettings.timezone` |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CozE2jE2XHDbfnhvLvo9FF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
