{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTgbJsE4C9vQaFUjzQs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-4. It has the four required sections (Overview, Component Breakdown, Data Flow, Requirements Traceability). I checked that all 59 FR/NFR ids from `requirements.json` appear in it, and that it cites no id that isn't in that file.\n\nThe file I replaced was left over from ticket abcd-1 (PRD-01). Since it's this sub-task's output, I overwrote it.\n\n**Intake blockers:**\n- **FR-1 (migration):** one new migration, built from the existing `schema.prisma` without changing it. The extra `updatedAt` columns stay.\n- **FR-4/FR-16 (auth emails):** confirmed. `sendAuthEmail()` adds a row straight to the email outbox and creates no in-app notification. Unlike `notify()`, it still throws on failure, because a silently lost invite or password reset is worse than an error.\n- **FR-40 (seed):** 3 notifications per user. The seed users `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` don't exist yet, so the seed looks each one up and skips it if missing instead of creating accounts another PRD owns.\n- **NFR-10 (mui-mcp):** passed to dev as a precondition. If the MUI docs server is unreachable during dev, that's a hard stop.\n\n**New finding:** the existing middleware returns 401 for any `/api/*` request without a session. A cron call has no session, so `/api/internal/email/dispatch` would never reach its handler. The fix is to add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. The `CRON_SECRET` check then becomes the only gate, so it must be strict.\n\n**Where the two research notes disagreed, I chose:**\n- **Email rendering:** each generic email is rendered once per `notify()` call, not per recipient. That keeps 1,000 recipients under 2 seconds (NFR-1), but it means generic emails can't include the recipient's name.\n- **Integration tests:** they go in the existing vitest config and are skipped unless `TEST_DATABASE_URL` is set. CI needs that variable, or the locking tests never run.\n- **Invite expiry:** the 7-day invite lifetime moves into one shared `INVITE_TTL` constant, so the date in the email can't drift from the real token.\n\nThe other architect outputs (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, `threat-model-notes.json`) and everything under `artifacts/dev-planning/` are also left over from abcd-1. `arch-api-contracts` should overwrite its own two files. Nobody owns `threat-model-notes.json` in this flow, so either delete it or regenerate it for SH-4."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":360,"cache_read_input_tokens":72739,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":360},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8a6de621-bc72-44a5-9725-5c1b7f039997","uuid":"cbe10e07-c7d3-4800-b163-598dfed1ca6d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:03:43.105Z","request_id":"req_011CghTgb11XPExujNvTGjHJ"}
