{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bk6bg3pwtQ3BFQ2NajLerU","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (36.8KB). Full output saved to: /Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub-prds/197d390e-c577-4a77-aead-08d0e3d6d0a4/tool-results/bk4gc4cev.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\narchitect:\ntotal 184\ndrwxr-xr-x  8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  5 10:15 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  14194 Nov  4 12:04 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   1407 Nov  4 12:05 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  21939 Nov  5 10:15 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  24795 Nov  4 12:03 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  13355 Nov  5 10:15 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff    396 Nov  4 12:05 threat-model-notes.json\n\ndev:\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 ikramaansari  staff   160 Nov  4 19:59 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff   224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  7213 Nov  4 20:09 dev-log.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   127 Nov  4 20:10 dev-rerun-count.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   428 Nov  4 20:09 task-completion-markers.json\n\ndev-planning:\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x  6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  4 12:06 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   5623 Nov  4 12:06 file-ownership-matrix.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   5201 Nov  4 12:06 file-structure.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  16017 Nov  4 12:06 implementation-plan.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   2894 Nov  4 12:06 module-dependencies.json\n# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architec\narchitect/api-contracts.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\narchitect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\narchitect/threat-model-notes.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"197d390e-c577-4a77-aead-08d0e3d6d0a4","uuid":"08baff8a-454c-491d-8bd1-4bf614b3d2e5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:14.893Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"architect:\ntotal 184\ndrwxr-xr-x  8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  5 10:15 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  14194 Nov  4 12:04 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   1407 Nov  4 12:05 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  21939 Nov  5 10:15 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  24795 Nov  4 12:03 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  13355 Nov  5 10:15 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff    396 Nov  4 12:05 threat-model-notes.json\n\ndev:\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 ikramaansari  staff   160 Nov  4 19:59 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff   224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  7213 Nov  4 20:09 dev-log.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   127 Nov  4 20:10 dev-rerun-count.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   428 Nov  4 20:09 task-completion-markers.json\n\ndev-planning:\ntotal 72\ndrwxr-xr-x  6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  4 12:06 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 ikramaansari  staff    224 Oct 16 20:20 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   5623 Nov  4 12:06 file-ownership-matrix.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   5201 Nov  4 12:06 file-structure.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff  16017 Nov  4 12:06 implementation-plan.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 ikramaansari  staff   2894 Nov  4 12:06 module-dependencies.json\n# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architec\narchitect/api-contracts.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\narchitect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\narchitect/threat-model-notes.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\ndev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\ndev-planning/implementation-plan.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\ndev-planning/module-dependencies.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-4\"\n# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable (SCH-006)\n\nTicket: SH-6 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T05:40:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and\n`package.json` confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict,\nPrisma 5.20 on PostgreSQL, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons, x-date-pickers, x-data-grid) with emotion,\nzod 3.23.8, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\nThe stack fits every FR/NFR. **This PRD adds exactly one runtime dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`.**\nThe ADRs below record only the choices the requirements force.\n\n**Workspace facts I checked** (they confirm intake or add detail to it):\n\n- `@dnd-kit/core` is not installed. The current npm release is `6.3.1`, with peer deps `react >=16.8` and `react-dom >=16.8`, so it is compatible with React 18.3.1.\n- No SWR, React Query or TanStack package is installed. Client data fetching in the codebase is plain `fetch` plus local state.\n- `prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => …)` is already used (sections-service, courses-service). No code uses `isolationLevel` or handles `P2034` yet, so this PRD sets the precedent.\n- `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, timezone)`, which wraps `formatInTimeZone`.\n- `.eslintrc` `no-restricted-imports` bans `@fullcalendar/*`, `react-datepicker`, `notistack`, `sonner`, `@radix-ui/*` and others. `@dnd-kit/*` is not banned, so the lint rule needs no change.\n- Vitest runs `tests/unit/**` and `tests/integration/**`. Integration tests are gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL` (precedent: `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`, which also tests a concurrent-race scenario).\n- No `@media print` or `GlobalStyles` print rule exists yet.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack; add `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (exact pin) and nothing else\n\n**Context.** FR-23 requires drag-and-drop to use `@dnd-kit/core` only. NFR-6 allows that one\nnon-visual dependency, plus `@dnd-kit/sortable` only if needed. FR-5 period reorder could\njustify sortable, but intake's default for FR-5 is up/down buttons.\n\n**Decision.** Add `\"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\"` with no caret, matching the repo's exact-pin\nconvention (`\"@mui/material\": \"9.5.0\"`). Do **not** add `@dnd-kit/sortable`,\n`@dnd-kit/utilities` or `@dnd-kit/modifiers`. Period reorder (FR-5, FR-33 `POST /api/periods/reorder`)\nuses MUI `IconButton`s with ArrowUpward and ArrowDownward icons.\n\n**Consequences.** One new lockfile entry. Leaving out sortable keeps the reorder logic\nserver-side and simple. The grid uses only `DndContext`, `useDraggable`, `useDroppable`,\n`DragOverlay` and `PointerSensor`. The ESLint ban list stays as it is.\n\n## ADR-2: Store and compare times as zero-padded `'HH:MM'` strings; derive \"now\" with the existing date-fns-tz helper\n\n**Context.** FR-1 stores `startTime` and `endTime` as `'HH:MM'` strings in the school timezone.\nFR-6 needs overlap and end-after-start checks. FR-31 and FR-45 need the current period and\ntoday's ISO weekday in `SchoolSettings.timezone`. NFR-11 asks for tests that cover multiple timezones.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Zod (FR-39) enforces `/^([01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/`. Zero-padded 24-hour strings sort and compare correctly as plain strings, so `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end` is the overlap test (FR-6). No parsing to `Date` is needed.\n- \"Now\" is `formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz)` and the ISO weekday is `Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz))` (1=Mon…7=Sun, matching FR-2). The `period.startTime <= nowHHMM < period.endTime` comparison is again a string comparison (FR-31, FR-26 Now/Next, FR-24 highlight).\n- `getScheduleForDate` (FR-30) also derives the weekday with `'i'` in the school timezone.\n- MUI X `TimeField` (FR-5) binds a `Date` value. The form converts with date-fns `format(d, 'HH:mm')` and `parse(s, 'HH:mm', ref)`. Both functions are already installed, and the field's `Date` is wall-clock only.\n\n**Consequences.** No new date library and no timezone arithmetic on stored times. Unit tests\npass a fixed `now` and several `tz` values (e.g. `UTC`, `America/Los_Angeles`, `Asia/Kolkata`) into\npure functions. Ceiling: periods cannot cross midnight. That is acceptable for a school day,\nand the endTime-after-startTime check already rejects them.\n\n## ADR-3: Clash check and write in one SERIALIZABLE interactive transaction with bounded retry on `P2034`\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires clash validation and the insert or update to run in one SERIALIZABLE\ntransaction, with retry, so that two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success.\nNFR-12 needs an integration test for this. FR-37 requires that a clash saves nothing and returns 409.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Prisma.TransactionIsolationLevel.Serializable })`, which Prisma 5.20 supports natively on PostgreSQL.\n- Retry the whole transaction up to 3 attempts when the error is `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` with `code === 'P2034'` (write conflict or deadlock). After the last attempt, rethrow so `withHandler` maps it to a 500. The retry loop is a small local function inside `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Do not add a shared util until a second caller exists (NFR-9).\n- Clashes found inside the transaction throw `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` from `src/server/http.ts`. The throw rolls the transaction back, so nothing is saved (FR-37, NFR-8).\n- The FR-3 `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` stays as a last line of defence. Map `P2002` to 409 as well.\n- Teaching-day switch-off (FR-7) and period reorder (FR-5) also use one transaction, at the default isolation level. Reorder needs a two-phase write because `Period.order @unique` would collide mid-update: first set each order to `-(i+1)`, then to `i+1`.\n\n**Consequences.** Clash rules (FR-9–FR-13) must run their reads through `tx`, not the global\n`prisma`, or SERIALIZABLE protects nothing. `validateSlot` therefore takes a client parameter\nthat defaults to `prisma`, so FR-36 availability can reuse the same logic outside a write.\nThe NFR-12 test follows the `email-dispatch.test.ts` pattern: `describe.runIf(TEST_DATABASE_URL)`,\nthen `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting creates, asserting exactly one is fulfilled.\n\n## ADR-4: Clash detection loads candidate slots with set-based Prisma queries and checks them in memory (no raw SQL)\n\n**Context.** FR-9–FR-14 define four clash rules plus the non-class period and non-teaching day\nrule, and `validateSlot` must return all of them. FR-36 availability must cover every\n(day, period) cell for one course in under 300 ms (NFR-3). The section week must load in under\n400 ms (NFR-2). The FR-3 index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` already exists for this.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **validateSlot** (single cell): one `findMany` of the other slots at `(academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId)`, excluding the moving slot's id on PATCH (FR-14). The query includes `course { teacherId, coTeacherIds, sectionId, code, subject, section }`, `room` and `period`. The teacher, room and section rules (FR-9, FR-10, FR-11) are array checks in TypeScript. Student overlap (FR-12) is one `enrollment.groupBy` / `count` over `status: 'ACTIVE'`, with `courseId in [otherCourseIds]` and `studentId in` the new course's active student ids. Both are covered by the existing `@@index([studentId, status])`.\n- **Availability** (FR-36): load all slots in the course's academic year in one query, and the new course's ACTIVE student ids plus the ACTIVE enrollments of those students in one query. Then run the same pure rule functions for each of the up-to-84 cells (7 × 12) in memory. This is a fixed number of queries, not one per cell.\n- The rule functions are pure (`(candidate, others, overlapCounts) => string[]`), so NFR-11 unit tests need no database.\n- **Editor and personal grids** (FR-35, FR-38): one `findMany` per view with `include` (course → subject, teacher; room; period). There are no N+1 queries.\n\n**Consequences.** No `$queryRaw`, so everything stays type-safe under strict TS (NFR-10).\nCeiling: availability does its work in memory over the year's slots, roughly a few thousand rows\nfor a single school (NFR-16), which fits the target comfortably.\n`// ponytail: in-memory clash map over the year's slots; move to SQL aggregation if slot count reaches ~50k.`\n\n## ADR-5: The drag-and-drop grid uses `@dnd-kit/core` with pessimistic updates; keyboard users get an MUI Dialog path\n\n**Context.** FR-16–FR-23 describe the editor grid. FR-20 requires that a rejected drop snaps\nback. FR-19 tints clashing cells while dragging, and NFR-4 says colour must never be the only signal.\nFR-22 and NFR-4 require a keyboard alternative. NFR-5 and NFR-6 allow MUI-only visuals.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `DndContext` with `PointerSensor` only (activation distance about 5px, so a click still opens the FR-21 room Popover). Cells use `useDroppable`. BREAK/LUNCH rows and non-teaching days set `disabled: true` (FR-16). Course cards and placed slots use `useDraggable`. The drag preview is a `DragOverlay` holding an MUI `Paper` (FR-23).\n- **Pessimistic updates.** The grid changes only after the POST or PATCH succeeds. On a 409, nothing moves, so \"snap back\" (FR-20) needs no rollback code. The toast comes from `useToast().showToast({ message, severity: 'error' })` with `details.clashes` joined into the message.\n- The clash map from `GET /api/timetable/availability` is fetched once when a drag starts, cached per courseId while the editor is open, and dropped after any mutation. Cells in the map get a red tint, an ErrorOutline icon and an MUI `Tooltip` listing the messages (FR-19, NFR-4).\n- Keyboard: cells are `tabIndex=0`. Enter on an empty cell opens an MUI `Dialog` listing the section's courses (FR-22). Delete on a focused slot opens the existing `ConfirmDialog` (FR-18). dnd-kit's `KeyboardSensor` is **not** used, because the Dialog path is the required alternative and it avoids the cost of making sensor announcements accessible.\n- Data fetching uses plain `fetch` plus `useState`, as elsewhere in the repo. No SWR or React Query is added.\n\n**Consequences.** Each drop costs one round-trip of latency (no optimistic UI). That is acceptable\nfor an admin tool, and it removes a whole class of state-desync bugs. Every component must still\nbe looked up through mui-mcp before use (NFR-5). The mui-mcp server is connected in this\nenvironment, so the intake blocker is cleared for now, but dev must still call it.\n\n## ADR-6: Print layout uses native `@media print` and `window.print()`, with no PDF or print library\n\n**Context.** FR-29 requires a print-friendly A4 landscape page containing only the grid, the entity\nname and the academic year. NFR-16 requires print to work in the last two versions of Chrome, Edge,\nFirefox and Safari. NFR-6 bans extra UI libraries.\n\n**Decision.** The Print button calls `window.print()`. An MUI `GlobalStyles` block, rendered with\nthe grid, contains `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, an `sx` rule\nhides the app shell (nav drawer, app bar, sidebar, view selectors and buttons), and a print-only\nheading shows the entity name and academic year. Cells use `break-inside: avoid`. Cell background\ncolours need `print-color-adjust: exact`. Course code and teacher text carry the meaning anyway,\nso colour is not required (NFR-4).\n\n**Consequences.** No dependency is added. Firefox and Safari ignore some `@page` size hints,\nwhich is acceptable because the user picks the orientation in the print dialog. The Playwright\ncheck uses `page.emulateMedia({ media: 'print' })` and asserts that the shell is hidden.\n\n## ADR-7: Testing stays on the existing Vitest and Playwright setup\n\n**Context.** NFR-11 (unit tests), NFR-12 (concurrency integration test), NFR-13 (e2e test) and NFR-10 (quality gate).\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts`: the pure rule functions from ADR-4, period overlap validation (FR-6) and `getCurrentSlot`/Now-Next with injected `now` and `tz` (ADR-2).\n- `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node`, gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL` (ADR-3).\n- `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts`: Playwright tests for dragging a course into a cell, a clash toast on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view, all against the FR-41–FR-44 seed. dnd-kit's PointerSensor works with Playwright `mouse.down/move/up` when there are intermediate `move` steps. `locator.dragTo` alone may not cross the activation distance.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed fixtures (FR-44) being idempotent.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes (no stack impact; for `arch-design-system` to decide)\n\n- FR-21 free rooms: no stack choice is needed. Either intake's suggested `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` or the availability payload works with ADR-4's query pattern. One query (rooms not archived, minus `roomId`s used at that day and period) is enough.\n- FR-7 slot count: intake's default (`GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day) is one `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'] })`, which works fine with this stack.\n- FR-40 audit: `audit()` from `src/server/audit.ts` should be called inside the same transaction client where its signature allows. That is for design to confirm.\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-6\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`, which covers PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n(45 FR and 16 NFR, 61 requirements) at 96% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`,\n> `system-design.md`, `tech-stack-decisions.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are **stale SH-4 outputs**.\n> The other sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-6 input, except for\n> `tech-stack-decisions.md` once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-6.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Validation**, **Clash Engine**, **Service**,\n**Admin API**, **Read API**, **Access Control**, **UI: Bell Schedule**, **UI: Editor**,\n**UI: Personal Timetable**, **UI: Tabs/Nav**, **Print**, **Time/TZ**, **Audit**, **Seed**,\n**Concurrency**, **Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `prisma/schema.prisma` has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind. The latest migration is `20261104120000_notifications_email`. | The new migration needs a later timestamp (for example `20261105000000_timetable`). |\n| B2 | `Room` already has a back-relation `sections Section[]`. `Course` has `enrollments` but no slots relation. | Add `Room.timetableSlots`, `Course.timetableSlots` and `Period.slots`. All are additive. |\n| B3 | `Course.coTeacherIds String[]`, nullable `sectionId`, `archivedAt`, `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. `Enrollment @@index([studentId, status])`, `onDelete: Cascade` from Course. | The teacher clash check needs `teacherId IN set OR coTeacherIds hasSome set`. The student-overlap check joins Enrollment on both courses. |\n| B4 | `Section.roomId?` (homeroom room) and `Section.homeroomTeacherId?`. `@@unique([academicYearId, name])`. | FR-17 uses `Section.roomId` as the default room. FR-35 checks TEACHER access through `homeroomTeacherId`. |\n| B5 | `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` with `@@index([studentId])`. `/api/me/children` already exists. | FR-25 and FR-38 can reuse `/api/me/children` for the child selector, so no new endpoint is needed. Parent access goes through `assertCanViewStudent`. |\n| B6 | `SchoolSettings.timezone` (default `'UTC'`) is read by the cached `getSchoolSettings()` in `src/server/services/settings.ts`. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `formatInSchoolTz` (date-fns-tz `formatInTimeZone`). | All \"now\" maths (FR-31, FR-45) uses `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')` and ISO day `'i'`. Plain `HH:MM` string comparison then works. |\n| B7 | SERIALIZABLE precedent: `academicYears.ts` and `terms.ts` use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Serializable })` but **do not retry**. There is no P2034 handling in `src/`. | NFR-1 needs a small retry wrapper for P2034 (serialization failure). It is new code, so keep it local to timetable-service unless the design wants to reuse it. |\n| B8 | `http.ts` has `ApiErrorCode` with CONFLICT=409 and FORBIDDEN=403, plus `AppError`, `withHandler` (maps P2002 → CONFLICT, P2025 → NOT_FOUND), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. | Clashes are thrown as `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })`. The handler shape is already standard. |\n| B9 | `audit({ actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request })` never throws. By convention `action` is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|delete`. | FR-40 actions: `timetableSlot.create\\|update\\|delete`, `period.create\\|update\\|delete\\|reorder`, `schoolDay.update` (metadata includes `deletedSlotCount`). |\n| B10 | Validators live in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` (courses, sections, ...). Feature services live in `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts`. Tabs live in `src/config/course-tabs.ts` and `student-tabs.ts` (`{ key, label, href, roles }`). | FR-39: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`. FR-27 and FR-28 each register one entry. |\n| B11 | API route dirs exist: `rooms`, `sections`, `courses`, `me/*`, `admin/*`. There are no `periods`, `school-days` or `timetable` routes. App admin pages: `admin/courses`, `admin/sections`, `admin/email-log`. | Everything here is new. Nothing gets renamed. |\n| B12 | `package.json` pins `@mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0`, `date-fns 3.6.0`, `date-fns-tz 3.2.0` and `@prisma/client 5.20.0`. `@dnd-kit/*` is absent. | FR-23 and NFR-6 add exactly one pinned dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`. Reorder (FR-5) uses up/down buttons, so `@dnd-kit/sortable` is not needed. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n### Data model and migration\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `enum PeriodKind` and `model Period`. Store `startTime`/`endTime` as `String` `HH:MM`. `order Int @unique` affects reorder (see FR-5). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model | `SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id, isTeaching Boolean }` is a 7-row lookup with no relations. Do not add a FK from TimetableSlot to it (the PRD defines `dayOfWeek Int`). |\n| FR-3 | Data Model | Index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` covers every clash query (all are scoped to year + day + period). `academicYearId` is denormalised from Course. It is set server-side only (FR-37). `periodId` has no cascade, so deletion is guarded by FR-8 in the service. `roomId?` with `onDelete: SetNull` is the safe default, and rooms are archived rather than deleted. |\n| FR-4 | Migration | One additive migration plus the B2 back-relations. `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then review the SQL. It should only contain CREATE TYPE, CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX statements. |\n\n### Validation and the clash engine (core domain)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-6 | Validation + Service | Zod handles the `^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$` format and `end > start`. These are plain string comparisons, so no Date parsing is needed. The overlap check against other periods is in the service, because it needs the DB: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self on update. |\n| FR-9 | Clash Engine | Teacher set T = {teacherId} ∪ coTeacherIds of the new course. Other slots at (year, day, period) whose course has teacherId ∈ T or coTeacherIds overlapping T. The message needs the teacher's display name, so join User. |\n| FR-10 | Clash Engine | Only when roomId ≠ null: same year, day, period and roomId. |\n| FR-11 | Clash Engine | Only when the course's sectionId ≠ null: another slot whose course.sectionId equals it. A cross-section elective (sectionId null) is skipped by this rule but still caught by FR-12. |\n| FR-12 | Clash Engine | One grouped query: count distinct studentIds where Enrollment(ACTIVE) is in the new course and also in course X, for each X in a slot at (year, day, period). Produce one clash per conflicting course with its count N. Use raw SQL or `groupBy`, because this is the costliest rule (NFR-3). |\n| FR-13 | Clash Engine | Precondition rules: Period.kind ≠ CLASS → `Period '<name>' is not a class period.`, and SchoolDay.isTeaching false → non-teaching day. These go into the same clashes[] list. |\n| FR-14 | Clash Engine / Service | `validateSlot({ courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId?, excludeSlotId? })` returns `Clash[]`, collecting **all** clashes. It is a pure-ish function that takes a `tx`, so the transaction (NFR-1) and the availability map (FR-36) can share it. Clash shape: `{ rule: 'TEACHER'\\|'ROOM'\\|'SECTION'\\|'STUDENT'\\|'PERIOD_KIND'\\|'NON_TEACHING_DAY', message }`. |\n| FR-36 | Clash Engine (batch) | Availability for one course covers ≤7 days × ≤12 periods = 84 cells. Do **not** call validateSlot 84 times. Run each rule once as a year-wide query over all slots, then bucket by `day-periodId`. Room rule: the course has no fixed room, so availability uses the default room (the section homeroom) or skips the room rule. **Design decision needed.** Recommendation: skip the room rule in availability, because the room is checked on drop. |\n| NFR-1 | Concurrency | `$transaction(async tx => { clashes = validateSlot(tx,…); if any throw CONFLICT; insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable })`. Retry on P2034 up to 3 times. `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` is a second guard (P2002 → 409 through withHandler). |\n| NFR-11 | Tests | Unit tests for every rule. This argues for keeping message building and the rule predicates pure (input rows → Clash[]), with Prisma calls kept thin so tests can use small fixtures. Testing the timezone current/next calculation needs an injectable `now` and `tz`. |\n| NFR-12 | Tests | Integration test against a real Postgres (docker-compose). Run `Promise.all` with two conflicting POSTs and assert exactly one succeeds. |\n\n### Service functions (exports used by later PRDs)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-30 | Service | `getScheduleForDate(target: { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }, date)`: get the ISO day in the school timezone, return `[]` if the day is not teaching, else that day's slots for the target, ordered by Period.order. Note for PRD-07 (attendance) and PRD-16 (dashboards): holidays are left out (NFR-15). |\n| FR-31 | Service + Time/TZ | `getCurrentSlot(user, now)`: `hhmm = formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')`, then return the slot where `start ≤ hhmm < end`. It reuses the FR-30 query for \"today\". |\n| FR-45 | Time/TZ | Use one helper (`schoolNow(tz, now)` → `{ isoDay, hhmm }`) everywhere: server pages, the service, and the client Today view (pass tz and the server time in props, never the browser timezone). |\n\n### APIs and access control\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-33 | Admin API | Periods CRUD and reorder. GET is open to any authenticated user. |\n| FR-5 (reorder) | Admin API / Data Model | Because `order` is `@unique`, the update must happen in two phases in one transaction: set all to negative temporary values, then to 1..n. The request lists all period ids, so the service validates that the set equals the existing set. |\n| FR-8 | Admin API | DELETE counts slots on the period. If more than 0, return 409 `{ details: { slotCount } }`. |\n| FR-34 + FR-7 | Admin API | GET returns 7 rows plus `slotCount` for each day (for the current academic year), which resolves the intake blocker. PUT `{ days: [{ dayOfWeek, isTeaching }] }`: in one transaction, delete the slots of days being switched off, update the rows, and audit with the deleted count. **Design decision:** should slotCount and the delete be scoped to the current year or to all years? Recommendation: delete across all years, because a non-teaching day makes every slot invalid. Show the count across all years too, so the confirm number matches what gets deleted. |\n| FR-35 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/timetable?view&id&academicYearId`. Run one query with `include` course → subject, teacher, section, and room, then filter by view. The TEACHER rule is: own id for the teacher view; for the section view, homeroom sections (`Section.homeroomTeacherId`) or sections of courses they teach (intake default). Room view is ADMIN only. Anything else is 403. |\n| FR-37 | Admin API | POST/PATCH run NFR-1. PATCH may change day, period and roomId, and validation excludes the slot itself (FR-14). DELETE is a plain delete plus audit. academicYearId comes from Course. Reject archived courses on POST. |\n| FR-21 | Admin API (new) | The intake blocker: no endpoint lists free rooms. Recommendation: **ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId`** returns non-archived rooms that have no slot at that cell. This is one query. The alternative of putting rooms into the availability map adds weight to every drag preload. |\n| FR-38 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId`. TEACHER: courses where teacherId = me or coTeacherIds has me. STUDENT: courses with an ACTIVE enrollment. PARENT: studentId must be a linked child (`assertCanViewStudent`). It is optional when there is exactly one child. Other roles (ADMIN) get an empty result or a 400 (design decision). |\n| FR-27 | Read API reuse | The student tab needs another student's timetable. It reuses the FR-38 service by studentId, with access checked by `assertCanViewStudent` on the server page. No new route is needed. |\n| FR-28 | Read API reuse | The course Schedule tab is a server page. It reads `prisma.timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` with Period and Room after `assertCanViewCourse`. No new route is needed. |\n| NFR-7 | Access Control | `requireRole('ADMIN')` on every mutation, availability and free-rooms. `requireUser` plus a per-entity check on reads. Pages use `requirePageRole` / `requirePageUser`. |\n| NFR-8 | Conventions | Thin handlers: `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (FR-39 schemas) → service → `ok()`. A clash is `{ error: { code: 'CONFLICT', message: <first clash or summary>, details: { clashes } } }`. |\n| FR-39 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`: `periodSchema`, `periodReorderSchema`, `schoolDaysSchema`, `slotCreateSchema`, `slotUpdateSchema`, `timetableQuerySchema`, `availabilityQuerySchema`, `freeRoomsQuerySchema`, `meTimetableQuerySchema`. The `dayOfWeek` type is `int 1..7`. |\n| FR-40 | Audit | Confirming the intake default: audit all slot, period and school-day mutations (see B9). It is cheap, and audit() never throws. |\n\n### UI\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-5 | UI: Bell Schedule | `/admin/timetable/periods`: PageHeader + MUI Table + an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (`@mui/x-date-pickers`, needs a LocalizationProvider with the date-fns adapter; check whether the app already provides one) + up/down reorder IconButtons + ConfirmDialog for delete. Show a 409 slotCount error through useToast. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Bell Schedule | Seven ToggleButtons (multi-select) on the same page. Switching off a day with slotCount > 0 opens a ConfirmDialog with the count before the PUT. |\n| FR-15 | UI: Editor | `/admin/timetable`: view ToggleButtonGroup, entity Autocomplete (sections, teachers via UserPicker or Autocomplete, rooms) and an academic year Select. The selection state goes in URL search params so the view survives a refresh. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Editor | A shared `TimetableGrid` component with editable and read-only modes. It is reused by FR-24, FR-27 and FR-29. Columns are teaching days. BREAK/LUNCH rows are","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub-prds/197d390e-c577-4a77-aead-08d0e3d6d0a4/tool-results/bk4gc4cev.txt","persistedOutputSize":37722},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Bk6bg3pwtQ3BFQ2NajLerU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
