{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BwgC3U8xWKZw2K8o21Xb4K","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-6\n2\t\n3\tSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`, which covers PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n5\t(45 FR and 16 NFR, 61 requirements) at 96% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\n6\tRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n7\t\n8\t> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`,\n9\t> `system-design.md`, `tech-stack-decisions.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are **stale SH-4 outputs**.\n10\t> The other sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-6 input, except for\n11\t> `tech-stack-decisions.md` once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-6.\n12\t\n13\tConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Validation**, **Clash Engine**, **Service**,\n14\t**Admin API**, **Read API**, **Access Control**, **UI: Bell Schedule**, **UI: Editor**,\n15\t**UI: Personal Timetable**, **UI: Tabs/Nav**, **Print**, **Time/TZ**, **Audit**, **Seed**,\n16\t**Concurrency**, **Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n17\t\n18\t## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n19\t\n20\t| # | Fact | Design implication |\n21\t|---|------|--------------------|\n22\t| B1 | `prisma/schema.prisma` has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind. The latest migration is `20261104120000_notifications_email`. | The new migration needs a later timestamp (for example `20261105000000_timetable`). |\n23\t| B2 | `Room` already has a back-relation `sections Section[]`. `Course` has `enrollments` but no slots relation. | Add `Room.timetableSlots`, `Course.timetableSlots` and `Period.slots`. All are additive. |\n24\t| B3 | `Course.coTeacherIds String[]`, nullable `sectionId`, `archivedAt`, `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. `Enrollment @@index([studentId, status])`, `onDelete: Cascade` from Course. | The teacher clash check needs `teacherId IN set OR coTeacherIds hasSome set`. The student-overlap check joins Enrollment on both courses. |\n25\t| B4 | `Section.roomId?` (homeroom room) and `Section.homeroomTeacherId?`. `@@unique([academicYearId, name])`. | FR-17 uses `Section.roomId` as the default room. FR-35 checks TEACHER access through `homeroomTeacherId`. |\n26\t| B5 | `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` with `@@index([studentId])`. `/api/me/children` already exists. | FR-25 and FR-38 can reuse `/api/me/children` for the child selector, so no new endpoint is needed. Parent access goes through `assertCanViewStudent`. |\n27\t| B6 | `SchoolSettings.timezone` (default `'UTC'`) is read by the cached `getSchoolSettings()` in `src/server/services/settings.ts`. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `formatInSchoolTz` (date-fns-tz `formatInTimeZone`). | All \"now\" maths (FR-31, FR-45) uses `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')` and ISO day `'i'`. Plain `HH:MM` string comparison then works. |\n28\t| B7 | SERIALIZABLE precedent: `academicYears.ts` and `terms.ts` use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Serializable })` but **do not retry**. There is no P2034 handling in `src/`. | NFR-1 needs a small retry wrapper for P2034 (serialization failure). It is new code, so keep it local to timetable-service unless the design wants to reuse it. |\n29\t| B8 | `http.ts` has `ApiErrorCode` with CONFLICT=409 and FORBIDDEN=403, plus `AppError`, `withHandler` (maps P2002 → CONFLICT, P2025 → NOT_FOUND), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. | Clashes are thrown as `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })`. The handler shape is already standard. |\n30\t| B9 | `audit({ actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request })` never throws. By convention `action` is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|delete`. | FR-40 actions: `timetableSlot.create\\|update\\|delete`, `period.create\\|update\\|delete\\|reorder`, `schoolDay.update` (metadata includes `deletedSlotCount`). |\n31\t| B10 | Validators live in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` (courses, sections, ...). Feature services live in `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts`. Tabs live in `src/config/course-tabs.ts` and `student-tabs.ts` (`{ key, label, href, roles }`). | FR-39: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`. FR-27 and FR-28 each register one entry. |\n32\t| B11 | API route dirs exist: `rooms`, `sections`, `courses`, `me/*`, `admin/*`. There are no `periods`, `school-days` or `timetable` routes. App admin pages: `admin/courses`, `admin/sections`, `admin/email-log`. | Everything here is new. Nothing gets renamed. |\n33\t| B12 | `package.json` pins `@mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0`, `date-fns 3.6.0`, `date-fns-tz 3.2.0` and `@prisma/client 5.20.0`. `@dnd-kit/*` is absent. | FR-23 and NFR-6 add exactly one pinned dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`. Reorder (FR-5) uses up/down buttons, so `@dnd-kit/sortable` is not needed. |\n34\t\n35\t## Requirement → architectural concern\n36\t\n37\t### Data model and migration\n38\t\n39\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n40\t|-----|---------|-------|\n41\t| FR-1 | Data Model | `enum PeriodKind` and `model Period`. Store `startTime`/`endTime` as `String` `HH:MM`. `order Int @unique` affects reorder (see FR-5). |\n42\t| FR-2 | Data Model | `SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id, isTeaching Boolean }` is a 7-row lookup with no relations. Do not add a FK from TimetableSlot to it (the PRD defines `dayOfWeek Int`). |\n43\t| FR-3 | Data Model | Index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` covers every clash query (all are scoped to year + day + period). `academicYearId` is denormalised from Course. It is set server-side only (FR-37). `periodId` has no cascade, so deletion is guarded by FR-8 in the service. `roomId?` with `onDelete: SetNull` is the safe default, and rooms are archived rather than deleted. |\n44\t| FR-4 | Migration | One additive migration plus the B2 back-relations. `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then review the SQL. It should only contain CREATE TYPE, CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX statements. |\n45\t\n46\t### Validation and the clash engine (core domain)\n47\t\n48\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n49\t|-----|---------|-------|\n50\t| FR-6 | Validation + Service | Zod handles the `^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$` format and `end > start`. These are plain string comparisons, so no Date parsing is needed. The overlap check against other periods is in the service, because it needs the DB: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self on update. |\n51\t| FR-9 | Clash Engine | Teacher set T = {teacherId} ∪ coTeacherIds of the new course. Other slots at (year, day, period) whose course has teacherId ∈ T or coTeacherIds overlapping T. The message needs the teacher's display name, so join User. |\n52\t| FR-10 | Clash Engine | Only when roomId ≠ null: same year, day, period and roomId. |\n53\t| FR-11 | Clash Engine | Only when the course's sectionId ≠ null: another slot whose course.sectionId equals it. A cross-section elective (sectionId null) is skipped by this rule but still caught by FR-12. |\n54\t| FR-12 | Clash Engine | One grouped query: count distinct studentIds where Enrollment(ACTIVE) is in the new course and also in course X, for each X in a slot at (year, day, period). Produce one clash per conflicting course with its count N. Use raw SQL or `groupBy`, because this is the costliest rule (NFR-3). |\n55\t| FR-13 | Clash Engine | Precondition rules: Period.kind ≠ CLASS → `Period '<name>' is not a class period.`, and SchoolDay.isTeaching false → non-teaching day. These go into the same clashes[] list. |\n56\t| FR-14 | Clash Engine / Service | `validateSlot({ courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId?, excludeSlotId? })` returns `Clash[]`, collecting **all** clashes. It is a pure-ish function that takes a `tx`, so the transaction (NFR-1) and the availability map (FR-36) can share it. Clash shape: `{ rule: 'TEACHER'\\|'ROOM'\\|'SECTION'\\|'STUDENT'\\|'PERIOD_KIND'\\|'NON_TEACHING_DAY', message }`. |\n57\t| FR-36 | Clash Engine (batch) | Availability for one course covers ≤7 days × ≤12 periods = 84 cells. Do **not** call validateSlot 84 times. Run each rule once as a year-wide query over all slots, then bucket by `day-periodId`. Room rule: the course has no fixed room, so availability uses the default room (the section homeroom) or skips the room rule. **Design decision needed.** Recommendation: skip the room rule in availability, because the room is checked on drop. |\n58\t| NFR-1 | Concurrency | `$transaction(async tx => { clashes = validateSlot(tx,…); if any throw CONFLICT; insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable })`. Retry on P2034 up to 3 times. `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` is a second guard (P2002 → 409 through withHandler). |\n59\t| NFR-11 | Tests | Unit tests for every rule. This argues for keeping message building and the rule predicates pure (input rows → Clash[]), with Prisma calls kept thin so tests can use small fixtures. Testing the timezone current/next calculation needs an injectable `now` and `tz`. |\n60\t| NFR-12 | Tests | Integration test against a real Postgres (docker-compose). Run `Promise.all` with two conflicting POSTs and assert exactly one succeeds. |\n61\t\n62\t### Service functions (exports used by later PRDs)\n63\t\n64\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n65\t|-----|---------|-------|\n66\t| FR-30 | Service | `getScheduleForDate(target: { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }, date)`: get the ISO day in the school timezone, return `[]` if the day is not teaching, else that day's slots for the target, ordered by Period.order. Note for PRD-07 (attendance) and PRD-16 (dashboards): holidays are left out (NFR-15). |\n67\t| FR-31 | Service + Time/TZ | `getCurrentSlot(user, now)`: `hhmm = formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')`, then return the slot where `start ≤ hhmm < end`. It reuses the FR-30 query for \"today\". |\n68\t| FR-45 | Time/TZ | Use one helper (`schoolNow(tz, now)` → `{ isoDay, hhmm }`) everywhere: server pages, the service, and the client Today view (pass tz and the server time in props, never the browser timezone). |\n69\t\n70\t### APIs and access control\n71\t\n72\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n73\t|-----|---------|-------|\n74\t| FR-33 | Admin API | Periods CRUD and reorder. GET is open to any authenticated user. |\n75\t| FR-5 (reorder) | Admin API / Data Model | Because `order` is `@unique`, the update must happen in two phases in one transaction: set all to negative temporary values, then to 1..n. The request lists all period ids, so the service validates that the set equals the existing set. |\n76\t| FR-8 | Admin API | DELETE counts slots on the period. If more than 0, return 409 `{ details: { slotCount } }`. |\n77\t| FR-34 + FR-7 | Admin API | GET returns 7 rows plus `slotCount` for each day (for the current academic year), which resolves the intake blocker. PUT `{ days: [{ dayOfWeek, isTeaching }] }`: in one transaction, delete the slots of days being switched off, update the rows, and audit with the deleted count. **Design decision:** should slotCount and the delete be scoped to the current year or to all years? Recommendation: delete across all years, because a non-teaching day makes every slot invalid. Show the count across all years too, so the confirm number matches what gets deleted. |\n78\t| FR-35 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/timetable?view&id&academicYearId`. Run one query with `include` course → subject, teacher, section, and room, then filter by view. The TEACHER rule is: own id for the teacher view; for the section view, homeroom sections (`Section.homeroomTeacherId`) or sections of courses they teach (intake default). Room view is ADMIN only. Anything else is 403. |\n79\t| FR-37 | Admin API | POST/PATCH run NFR-1. PATCH may change day, period and roomId, and validation excludes the slot itself (FR-14). DELETE is a plain delete plus audit. academicYearId comes from Course. Reject archived courses on POST. |\n80\t| FR-21 | Admin API (new) | The intake blocker: no endpoint lists free rooms. Recommendation: **ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId`** returns non-archived rooms that have no slot at that cell. This is one query. The alternative of putting rooms into the availability map adds weight to every drag preload. |\n81\t| FR-38 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId`. TEACHER: courses where teacherId = me or coTeacherIds has me. STUDENT: courses with an ACTIVE enrollment. PARENT: studentId must be a linked child (`assertCanViewStudent`). It is optional when there is exactly one child. Other roles (ADMIN) get an empty result or a 400 (design decision). |\n82\t| FR-27 | Read API reuse | The student tab needs another student's timetable. It reuses the FR-38 service by studentId, with access checked by `assertCanViewStudent` on the server page. No new route is needed. |\n83\t| FR-28 | Read API reuse | The course Schedule tab is a server page. It reads `prisma.timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` with Period and Room after `assertCanViewCourse`. No new route is needed. |\n84\t| NFR-7 | Access Control | `requireRole('ADMIN')` on every mutation, availability and free-rooms. `requireUser` plus a per-entity check on reads. Pages use `requirePageRole` / `requirePageUser`. |\n85\t| NFR-8 | Conventions | Thin handlers: `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (FR-39 schemas) → service → `ok()`. A clash is `{ error: { code: 'CONFLICT', message: <first clash or summary>, details: { clashes } } }`. |\n86\t| FR-39 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`: `periodSchema`, `periodReorderSchema`, `schoolDaysSchema`, `slotCreateSchema`, `slotUpdateSchema`, `timetableQuerySchema`, `availabilityQuerySchema`, `freeRoomsQuerySchema`, `meTimetableQuerySchema`. The `dayOfWeek` type is `int 1..7`. |\n87\t| FR-40 | Audit | Confirming the intake default: audit all slot, period and school-day mutations (see B9). It is cheap, and audit() never throws. |\n88\t\n89\t### UI\n90\t\n91\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n92\t|-----|---------|-------|\n93\t| FR-5 | UI: Bell Schedule | `/admin/timetable/periods`: PageHeader + MUI Table + an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (`@mui/x-date-pickers`, needs a LocalizationProvider with the date-fns adapter; check whether the app already provides one) + up/down reorder IconButtons + ConfirmDialog for delete. Show a 409 slotCount error through useToast. |\n94\t| FR-7 | UI: Bell Schedule | Seven ToggleButtons (multi-select) on the same page. Switching off a day with slotCount > 0 opens a ConfirmDialog with the count before the PUT. |\n95\t| FR-15 | UI: Editor | `/admin/timetable`: view ToggleButtonGroup, entity Autocomplete (sections, teachers via UserPicker or Autocomplete, rooms) and an academic year Select. The selection state goes in URL search params so the view survives a refresh. |\n96\t| FR-16 | UI: Editor | A shared `TimetableGrid` component with editable and read-only modes. It is reused by FR-24, FR-27 and FR-29. Columns are teaching days. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and not droppable. The cell is a Paper with the subject colour, which comes from the existing `Subject.color String @default(\"#4F46E5\")`. Choose the text colour for contrast (`theme.palette.getContrastText`). |\n97\t| FR-17 | UI: Editor | Section view only: a sidebar with the section's non-archived courses and a \"placed N\" Chip. On drop, POST with `roomId = section.roomId`. The teacher and room views are read-only grids with no sidebar. |\n98\t| FR-18 | UI: Editor | Drag a slot to a cell to PATCH it. Drop outside the grid or press Delete to open a ConfirmDialog, then DELETE. |\n99\t| FR-19 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | On drag start, fetch or reuse the cached availability map for the course. Clashing cells get a red tint, an ErrorOutline icon and a Tooltip listing the messages (NFR-4). For a slot being moved, ignore its own cell's clashes. |\n100\t| FR-20 | UI: Editor | Optimistic placement is optional. Simplest approach: render from server state only, so there is nothing to snap back. Show a toast with `details.clashes.map(c => c.message)`. |\n101\t| FR-21 | UI: Editor | Clicking a slot opens a Popover with an Autocomplete fed by free-rooms, then PATCH `{ roomId }`. |\n102\t| FR-22 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | Grid cells get `tabIndex=0`. Enter on an empty cell opens a \"Place course\" Dialog (List of section courses) and the same POST as a drop. Delete on a focused slot opens the FR-18 confirm. |\n103\t| FR-23 | UI: Editor | `@dnd-kit/core` only (DndContext, useDraggable, useDroppable). Use MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip for visuals. Do not use a sortable or calendar library. |\n104\t| FR-24 | UI: Personal Timetable | `/timetable` server page, `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')`. Loads the FR-38 data, settings.tz and server \"now\", and renders the read-only grid with the current-period highlight. |\n105\t| FR-25 | UI: Personal Timetable | The child selector (Select from `/api/me/children` or a server query) updates `?studentId=` in the URL. |\n106\t| FR-26 | UI: Personal Timetable | Week/Today ToggleButtonGroup. The Today view is a List with \"Now\" and \"Next\" Chips (text, NFR-4). It is computed with the B6 helper from server-supplied tz. A client tick (every minute) only advances the server-supplied now. |\n107\t| FR-27 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `studentTabs` adds `{ key: 'timetable', href: /students/[id]/timetable }` and a page that reuses the read-only grid. |\n108\t| FR-28 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `courseTabs` adds `{ key: 'schedule', href: /courses/[id]/schedule }` and a page with a simple Table (day, period, times, room). |\n109\t| FR-32 | UI: Tabs/Nav | Add 3 entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: Timetable, plus Timetable editor and Bell schedule with `group: 'Administration'`. |\n110\t| FR-29 | Print | A Print Button calls `window.print()`. `@media print` (via MUI `GlobalStyles` or `sx`, not a CSS library) hides the nav, sidebar and controls, and sets `@page { size: A4 landscape }`. A print-only header shows the entity name and academic year. NFR-16 requires checking Safari print. |\n111\t| NFR-4 | Accessibility | Covered by FR-19, FR-22 and FR-26. Also give each cell an `aria-label` (\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Room 101\"). |\n112\t| NFR-5 | Conventions (UI) | Dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI/MUI X component used (Table, ToggleButton, Autocomplete, Popover, Dialog, Tooltip, Chip, Paper, TimeField, LocalizationProvider, GlobalStyles). If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a hard blocker. This is a dev-phase gate, not a design element. |\n113\t| NFR-6 | Conventions (deps) | Only `@dnd-kit/core` (pinned exact) is added. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` must stay green. |\n114\t\n115\t### Seed\n116\t\n117\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n118\t|-----|---------|-------|\n119\t| FR-41 | Seed | Upsert periods by `order` (1..8). Idempotent. |\n120\t| FR-42 | Seed | Upsert SchoolDay 1..7 (1–5 teaching). |\n121\t| FR-44 | Seed (fixtures) | Intake blocker, using the default. Add minimal idempotent fixtures upserted by email or code: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and a sibling (STUDENT), Pat (PARENT linked to both), sections 7A and 7B (homeroom rooms Room 101 and Room 102), courses `MATH-7A`… (subjects ELA for ENG and SOC for HIST), Robotics Club (ELECTIVE, sectionId null), and enrollments. **Check first:** PRD-03 and PRD-05 seed helpers or users may already exist in another seed file. Reuse them before adding new ones. |\n122\t| FR-43 | Seed | A fixed, hand-written clash-free week (21 class slots per section; 30 = 5 days × 6 class periods). Robotics on Wed P6 with both sections free then. To avoid hidden clashes, the seed should insert through `validateSlot`, or a unit test should assert the seed has zero clashes. Tom teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B, so those courses must never share a cell. |\n123\t\n124\t### Performance, quality and scope\n125\t\n126\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n127\t|-----|---------|-------|\n128\t| NFR-2 | Performance | Section week load (≤84 cells): one indexed query with includes, plus the periods and school days (cached or small). Easily under 400 ms. Avoid N+1 queries for teacher names. |\n129\t| NFR-3 | Performance | Availability under 300 ms means the batch evaluation in FR-36 makes about 4 queries total, not one per cell. The student-overlap rule is a single SQL statement grouped by `(dayOfWeek, periodId, otherCourseId)`. |\n130\t| NFR-9 | Conventions | Reuse http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader and the access helpers. The new service path is `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Do not create a parallel helpers folder. |\n131\t| NFR-10 | Tests | lint, typecheck and test gate. |\n132\t| NFR-13 | Tests | Playwright: drag works through mouse events with dnd-kit's PointerSensor (step-wise `mouse.move`). The keyboard path (FR-22) is a more reliable e2e fallback for placement. |\n133\t| NFR-14 | Conventions | Use `logger` (for example, to log P2034 retries). |\n134\t| NFR-15 | Scope | No solver, no A/B weeks, no substitutes, no holidays. `getScheduleForDate` is the single place PRD-14 will hook holidays later. |\n135\t| NFR-16 | Scope | English only and a single school. Print must be tested across the 4 browsers. |\n136\t\n137\t## Open design decisions handed to `arch-design-system`\n138\t\n139\t1. **Free rooms (FR-21):** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` (recommended), or fold rooms into the availability response.\n140\t2. **Availability room rule (FR-36):** skip it (recommended; it is checked on drop), or evaluate against the section homeroom.\n141\t3. **School-day slotCount and cascade scope (FR-7/FR-34):** all years (recommended) or the current year only.\n142\t4. **Archived entities:** exclude archived courses and rooms from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks (intake default, agreed).\n143\t5. ~~Subject colour (FR-16)~~ Resolved: `Subject.color` already exists in the schema.\n144\t6. **ADMIN on `/api/me/timetable` (FR-38):** return an empty list (recommended) or a 400.\n145\t7. **Serialization retry helper (NFR-1):** a new small `withSerializableRetry` with no existing precedent (B7). Keep it in timetable-service.\n146\t\n147\t## Intake blockers and how this analysis covers them\n148\t\n149\t| Blocker | Covered by |\n150\t|---------|-----------|\n151\t| FR-44 seed fixtures | Seed rows above. Reuse any existing PRD-03/05 fixtures first. |\n152\t| FR-43 ENG/HIST subjects | Reuse ELA/SOC with PRD course codes. |\n153\t| FR-21 free rooms | Decision 1. |\n154\t| FR-7 slot count | GET /api/school-days `slotCount` (FR-34 row), decision 3. |\n155\t| FR-4/NFR-6 migration + dnd-kit | B1, B2, B12. |\n156\t| NFR-5 mui-mcp | Dev-phase hard gate (NFR-5 row). The mui-mcp server is configured in this environment. |\n157\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"197d390e-c577-4a77-aead-08d0e3d6d0a4","uuid":"83945e5c-34b2-4643-a236-c5d7cd171fb0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:17.709Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-6\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`, which covers PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable\n(45 FR and 16 NFR, 61 requirements) at 96% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`,\n> `system-design.md`, `tech-stack-decisions.md`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are **stale SH-4 outputs**.\n> The other sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-6 input, except for\n> `tech-stack-decisions.md` once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-6.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Validation**, **Clash Engine**, **Service**,\n**Admin API**, **Read API**, **Access Control**, **UI: Bell Schedule**, **UI: Editor**,\n**UI: Personal Timetable**, **UI: Tabs/Nav**, **Print**, **Time/TZ**, **Audit**, **Seed**,\n**Concurrency**, **Performance**, **Accessibility**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `prisma/schema.prisma` has no Period, SchoolDay, TimetableSlot or PeriodKind. The latest migration is `20261104120000_notifications_email`. | The new migration needs a later timestamp (for example `20261105000000_timetable`). |\n| B2 | `Room` already has a back-relation `sections Section[]`. `Course` has `enrollments` but no slots relation. | Add `Room.timetableSlots`, `Course.timetableSlots` and `Period.slots`. All are additive. |\n| B3 | `Course.coTeacherIds String[]`, nullable `sectionId`, `archivedAt`, `@@unique([academicYearId, code])`. `Enrollment @@index([studentId, status])`, `onDelete: Cascade` from Course. | The teacher clash check needs `teacherId IN set OR coTeacherIds hasSome set`. The student-overlap check joins Enrollment on both courses. |\n| B4 | `Section.roomId?` (homeroom room) and `Section.homeroomTeacherId?`. `@@unique([academicYearId, name])`. | FR-17 uses `Section.roomId` as the default room. FR-35 checks TEACHER access through `homeroomTeacherId`. |\n| B5 | `ParentStudentLink(parentId, studentId)` with `@@index([studentId])`. `/api/me/children` already exists. | FR-25 and FR-38 can reuse `/api/me/children` for the child selector, so no new endpoint is needed. Parent access goes through `assertCanViewStudent`. |\n| B6 | `SchoolSettings.timezone` (default `'UTC'`) is read by the cached `getSchoolSettings()` in `src/server/services/settings.ts`. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `formatInSchoolTz` (date-fns-tz `formatInTimeZone`). | All \"now\" maths (FR-31, FR-45) uses `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')` and ISO day `'i'`. Plain `HH:MM` string comparison then works. |\n| B7 | SERIALIZABLE precedent: `academicYears.ts` and `terms.ts` use `prisma.$transaction(fn, { isolationLevel: Serializable })` but **do not retry**. There is no P2034 handling in `src/`. | NFR-1 needs a small retry wrapper for P2034 (serialization failure). It is new code, so keep it local to timetable-service unless the design wants to reuse it. |\n| B8 | `http.ts` has `ApiErrorCode` with CONFLICT=409 and FORBIDDEN=403, plus `AppError`, `withHandler` (maps P2002 → CONFLICT, P2025 → NOT_FOUND), `parseBody` and `parseQuery`. | Clashes are thrown as `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })`. The handler shape is already standard. |\n| B9 | `audit({ actorId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, request })` never throws. By convention `action` is `<entity>.create\\|update\\|delete`. | FR-40 actions: `timetableSlot.create\\|update\\|delete`, `period.create\\|update\\|delete\\|reorder`, `schoolDay.update` (metadata includes `deletedSlotCount`). |\n| B10 | Validators live in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` (courses, sections, ...). Feature services live in `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts`. Tabs live in `src/config/course-tabs.ts` and `student-tabs.ts` (`{ key, label, href, roles }`). | FR-39: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`. FR-27 and FR-28 each register one entry. |\n| B11 | API route dirs exist: `rooms`, `sections`, `courses`, `me/*`, `admin/*`. There are no `periods`, `school-days` or `timetable` routes. App admin pages: `admin/courses`, `admin/sections`, `admin/email-log`. | Everything here is new. Nothing gets renamed. |\n| B12 | `package.json` pins `@mui/x-date-pickers 9.5.0`, `date-fns 3.6.0`, `date-fns-tz 3.2.0` and `@prisma/client 5.20.0`. `@dnd-kit/*` is absent. | FR-23 and NFR-6 add exactly one pinned dependency, `@dnd-kit/core`. Reorder (FR-5) uses up/down buttons, so `@dnd-kit/sortable` is not needed. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n### Data model and migration\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | `enum PeriodKind` and `model Period`. Store `startTime`/`endTime` as `String` `HH:MM`. `order Int @unique` affects reorder (see FR-5). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model | `SchoolDay { dayOfWeek Int @id, isTeaching Boolean }` is a 7-row lookup with no relations. Do not add a FK from TimetableSlot to it (the PRD defines `dayOfWeek Int`). |\n| FR-3 | Data Model | Index `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` covers every clash query (all are scoped to year + day + period). `academicYearId` is denormalised from Course. It is set server-side only (FR-37). `periodId` has no cascade, so deletion is guarded by FR-8 in the service. `roomId?` with `onDelete: SetNull` is the safe default, and rooms are archived rather than deleted. |\n| FR-4 | Migration | One additive migration plus the B2 back-relations. `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then review the SQL. It should only contain CREATE TYPE, CREATE TABLE and CREATE INDEX statements. |\n\n### Validation and the clash engine (core domain)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-6 | Validation + Service | Zod handles the `^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$` format and `end > start`. These are plain string comparisons, so no Date parsing is needed. The overlap check against other periods is in the service, because it needs the DB: `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self on update. |\n| FR-9 | Clash Engine | Teacher set T = {teacherId} ∪ coTeacherIds of the new course. Other slots at (year, day, period) whose course has teacherId ∈ T or coTeacherIds overlapping T. The message needs the teacher's display name, so join User. |\n| FR-10 | Clash Engine | Only when roomId ≠ null: same year, day, period and roomId. |\n| FR-11 | Clash Engine | Only when the course's sectionId ≠ null: another slot whose course.sectionId equals it. A cross-section elective (sectionId null) is skipped by this rule but still caught by FR-12. |\n| FR-12 | Clash Engine | One grouped query: count distinct studentIds where Enrollment(ACTIVE) is in the new course and also in course X, for each X in a slot at (year, day, period). Produce one clash per conflicting course with its count N. Use raw SQL or `groupBy`, because this is the costliest rule (NFR-3). |\n| FR-13 | Clash Engine | Precondition rules: Period.kind ≠ CLASS → `Period '<name>' is not a class period.`, and SchoolDay.isTeaching false → non-teaching day. These go into the same clashes[] list. |\n| FR-14 | Clash Engine / Service | `validateSlot({ courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId?, excludeSlotId? })` returns `Clash[]`, collecting **all** clashes. It is a pure-ish function that takes a `tx`, so the transaction (NFR-1) and the availability map (FR-36) can share it. Clash shape: `{ rule: 'TEACHER'\\|'ROOM'\\|'SECTION'\\|'STUDENT'\\|'PERIOD_KIND'\\|'NON_TEACHING_DAY', message }`. |\n| FR-36 | Clash Engine (batch) | Availability for one course covers ≤7 days × ≤12 periods = 84 cells. Do **not** call validateSlot 84 times. Run each rule once as a year-wide query over all slots, then bucket by `day-periodId`. Room rule: the course has no fixed room, so availability uses the default room (the section homeroom) or skips the room rule. **Design decision needed.** Recommendation: skip the room rule in availability, because the room is checked on drop. |\n| NFR-1 | Concurrency | `$transaction(async tx => { clashes = validateSlot(tx,…); if any throw CONFLICT; insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable })`. Retry on P2034 up to 3 times. `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` is a second guard (P2002 → 409 through withHandler). |\n| NFR-11 | Tests | Unit tests for every rule. This argues for keeping message building and the rule predicates pure (input rows → Clash[]), with Prisma calls kept thin so tests can use small fixtures. Testing the timezone current/next calculation needs an injectable `now` and `tz`. |\n| NFR-12 | Tests | Integration test against a real Postgres (docker-compose). Run `Promise.all` with two conflicting POSTs and assert exactly one succeeds. |\n\n### Service functions (exports used by later PRDs)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-30 | Service | `getScheduleForDate(target: { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }, date)`: get the ISO day in the school timezone, return `[]` if the day is not teaching, else that day's slots for the target, ordered by Period.order. Note for PRD-07 (attendance) and PRD-16 (dashboards): holidays are left out (NFR-15). |\n| FR-31 | Service + Time/TZ | `getCurrentSlot(user, now)`: `hhmm = formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'HH:mm')`, then return the slot where `start ≤ hhmm < end`. It reuses the FR-30 query for \"today\". |\n| FR-45 | Time/TZ | Use one helper (`schoolNow(tz, now)` → `{ isoDay, hhmm }`) everywhere: server pages, the service, and the client Today view (pass tz and the server time in props, never the browser timezone). |\n\n### APIs and access control\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-33 | Admin API | Periods CRUD and reorder. GET is open to any authenticated user. |\n| FR-5 (reorder) | Admin API / Data Model | Because `order` is `@unique`, the update must happen in two phases in one transaction: set all to negative temporary values, then to 1..n. The request lists all period ids, so the service validates that the set equals the existing set. |\n| FR-8 | Admin API | DELETE counts slots on the period. If more than 0, return 409 `{ details: { slotCount } }`. |\n| FR-34 + FR-7 | Admin API | GET returns 7 rows plus `slotCount` for each day (for the current academic year), which resolves the intake blocker. PUT `{ days: [{ dayOfWeek, isTeaching }] }`: in one transaction, delete the slots of days being switched off, update the rows, and audit with the deleted count. **Design decision:** should slotCount and the delete be scoped to the current year or to all years? Recommendation: delete across all years, because a non-teaching day makes every slot invalid. Show the count across all years too, so the confirm number matches what gets deleted. |\n| FR-35 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/timetable?view&id&academicYearId`. Run one query with `include` course → subject, teacher, section, and room, then filter by view. The TEACHER rule is: own id for the teacher view; for the section view, homeroom sections (`Section.homeroomTeacherId`) or sections of courses they teach (intake default). Room view is ADMIN only. Anything else is 403. |\n| FR-37 | Admin API | POST/PATCH run NFR-1. PATCH may change day, period and roomId, and validation excludes the slot itself (FR-14). DELETE is a plain delete plus audit. academicYearId comes from Course. Reject archived courses on POST. |\n| FR-21 | Admin API (new) | The intake blocker: no endpoint lists free rooms. Recommendation: **ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId`** returns non-archived rooms that have no slot at that cell. This is one query. The alternative of putting rooms into the availability map adds weight to every drag preload. |\n| FR-38 | Read API + Access Control | `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId`. TEACHER: courses where teacherId = me or coTeacherIds has me. STUDENT: courses with an ACTIVE enrollment. PARENT: studentId must be a linked child (`assertCanViewStudent`). It is optional when there is exactly one child. Other roles (ADMIN) get an empty result or a 400 (design decision). |\n| FR-27 | Read API reuse | The student tab needs another student's timetable. It reuses the FR-38 service by studentId, with access checked by `assertCanViewStudent` on the server page. No new route is needed. |\n| FR-28 | Read API reuse | The course Schedule tab is a server page. It reads `prisma.timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` with Period and Room after `assertCanViewCourse`. No new route is needed. |\n| NFR-7 | Access Control | `requireRole('ADMIN')` on every mutation, availability and free-rooms. `requireUser` plus a per-entity check on reads. Pages use `requirePageRole` / `requirePageUser`. |\n| NFR-8 | Conventions | Thin handlers: `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (FR-39 schemas) → service → `ok()`. A clash is `{ error: { code: 'CONFLICT', message: <first clash or summary>, details: { clashes } } }`. |\n| FR-39 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts`: `periodSchema`, `periodReorderSchema`, `schoolDaysSchema`, `slotCreateSchema`, `slotUpdateSchema`, `timetableQuerySchema`, `availabilityQuerySchema`, `freeRoomsQuerySchema`, `meTimetableQuerySchema`. The `dayOfWeek` type is `int 1..7`. |\n| FR-40 | Audit | Confirming the intake default: audit all slot, period and school-day mutations (see B9). It is cheap, and audit() never throws. |\n\n### UI\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-5 | UI: Bell Schedule | `/admin/timetable/periods`: PageHeader + MUI Table + an add/edit Dialog with TimeField (`@mui/x-date-pickers`, needs a LocalizationProvider with the date-fns adapter; check whether the app already provides one) + up/down reorder IconButtons + ConfirmDialog for delete. Show a 409 slotCount error through useToast. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Bell Schedule | Seven ToggleButtons (multi-select) on the same page. Switching off a day with slotCount > 0 opens a ConfirmDialog with the count before the PUT. |\n| FR-15 | UI: Editor | `/admin/timetable`: view ToggleButtonGroup, entity Autocomplete (sections, teachers via UserPicker or Autocomplete, rooms) and an academic year Select. The selection state goes in URL search params so the view survives a refresh. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Editor | A shared `TimetableGrid` component with editable and read-only modes. It is reused by FR-24, FR-27 and FR-29. Columns are teaching days. BREAK/LUNCH rows are greyed and not droppable. The cell is a Paper with the subject colour, which comes from the existing `Subject.color String @default(\"#4F46E5\")`. Choose the text colour for contrast (`theme.palette.getContrastText`). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Editor | Section view only: a sidebar with the section's non-archived courses and a \"placed N\" Chip. On drop, POST with `roomId = section.roomId`. The teacher and room views are read-only grids with no sidebar. |\n| FR-18 | UI: Editor | Drag a slot to a cell to PATCH it. Drop outside the grid or press Delete to open a ConfirmDialog, then DELETE. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | On drag start, fetch or reuse the cached availability map for the course. Clashing cells get a red tint, an ErrorOutline icon and a Tooltip listing the messages (NFR-4). For a slot being moved, ignore its own cell's clashes. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Editor | Optimistic placement is optional. Simplest approach: render from server state only, so there is nothing to snap back. Show a toast with `details.clashes.map(c => c.message)`. |\n| FR-21 | UI: Editor | Clicking a slot opens a Popover with an Autocomplete fed by free-rooms, then PATCH `{ roomId }`. |\n| FR-22 | UI: Editor + Accessibility | Grid cells get `tabIndex=0`. Enter on an empty cell opens a \"Place course\" Dialog (List of section courses) and the same POST as a drop. Delete on a focused slot opens the FR-18 confirm. |\n| FR-23 | UI: Editor | `@dnd-kit/core` only (DndContext, useDraggable, useDroppable). Use MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip for visuals. Do not use a sortable or calendar library. |\n| FR-24 | UI: Personal Timetable | `/timetable` server page, `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')`. Loads the FR-38 data, settings.tz and server \"now\", and renders the read-only grid with the current-period highlight. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Personal Timetable | The child selector (Select from `/api/me/children` or a server query) updates `?studentId=` in the URL. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Personal Timetable | Week/Today ToggleButtonGroup. The Today view is a List with \"Now\" and \"Next\" Chips (text, NFR-4). It is computed with the B6 helper from server-supplied tz. A client tick (every minute) only advances the server-supplied now. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `studentTabs` adds `{ key: 'timetable', href: /students/[id]/timetable }` and a page that reuses the read-only grid. |\n| FR-28 | UI: Tabs/Nav | `courseTabs` adds `{ key: 'schedule', href: /courses/[id]/schedule }` and a page with a simple Table (day, period, times, room). |\n| FR-32 | UI: Tabs/Nav | Add 3 entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: Timetable, plus Timetable editor and Bell schedule with `group: 'Administration'`. |\n| FR-29 | Print | A Print Button calls `window.print()`. `@media print` (via MUI `GlobalStyles` or `sx`, not a CSS library) hides the nav, sidebar and controls, and sets `@page { size: A4 landscape }`. A print-only header shows the entity name and academic year. NFR-16 requires checking Safari print. |\n| NFR-4 | Accessibility | Covered by FR-19, FR-22 and FR-26. Also give each cell an `aria-label` (\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Room 101\"). |\n| NFR-5 | Conventions (UI) | Dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI/MUI X component used (Table, ToggleButton, Autocomplete, Popover, Dialog, Tooltip, Chip, Paper, TimeField, LocalizationProvider, GlobalStyles). If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a hard blocker. This is a dev-phase gate, not a design element. |\n| NFR-6 | Conventions (deps) | Only `@dnd-kit/core` (pinned exact) is added. The existing ESLint `no-restricted-imports` must stay green. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-41 | Seed | Upsert periods by `order` (1..8). Idempotent. |\n| FR-42 | Seed | Upsert SchoolDay 1..7 (1–5 teaching). |\n| FR-44 | Seed (fixtures) | Intake blocker, using the default. Add minimal idempotent fixtures upserted by email or code: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and a sibling (STUDENT), Pat (PARENT linked to both), sections 7A and 7B (homeroom rooms Room 101 and Room 102), courses `MATH-7A`… (subjects ELA for ENG and SOC for HIST), Robotics Club (ELECTIVE, sectionId null), and enrollments. **Check first:** PRD-03 and PRD-05 seed helpers or users may already exist in another seed file. Reuse them before adding new ones. |\n| FR-43 | Seed | A fixed, hand-written clash-free week (21 class slots per section; 30 = 5 days × 6 class periods). Robotics on Wed P6 with both sections free then. To avoid hidden clashes, the seed should insert through `validateSlot`, or a unit test should assert the seed has zero clashes. Tom teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B, so those courses must never share a cell. |\n\n### Performance, quality and scope\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| NFR-2 | Performance | Section week load (≤84 cells): one indexed query with includes, plus the periods and school days (cached or small). Easily under 400 ms. Avoid N+1 queries for teacher names. |\n| NFR-3 | Performance | Availability under 300 ms means the batch evaluation in FR-36 makes about 4 queries total, not one per cell. The student-overlap rule is a single SQL statement grouped by `(dayOfWeek, periodId, otherCourseId)`. |\n| NFR-9 | Conventions | Reuse http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader and the access helpers. The new service path is `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Do not create a parallel helpers folder. |\n| NFR-10 | Tests | lint, typecheck and test gate. |\n| NFR-13 | Tests | Playwright: drag works through mouse events with dnd-kit's PointerSensor (step-wise `mouse.move`). The keyboard path (FR-22) is a more reliable e2e fallback for placement. |\n| NFR-14 | Conventions | Use `logger` (for example, to log P2034 retries). |\n| NFR-15 | Scope | No solver, no A/B weeks, no substitutes, no holidays. `getScheduleForDate` is the single place PRD-14 will hook holidays later. |\n| NFR-16 | Scope | English only and a single school. Print must be tested across the 4 browsers. |\n\n## Open design decisions handed to `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Free rooms (FR-21):** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` (recommended), or fold rooms into the availability response.\n2. **Availability room rule (FR-36):** skip it (recommended; it is checked on drop), or evaluate against the section homeroom.\n3. **School-day slotCount and cascade scope (FR-7/FR-34):** all years (recommended) or the current year only.\n4. **Archived entities:** exclude archived courses and rooms from the sidebar and pickers. Existing slots of archived courses still count in clash checks (intake default, agreed).\n5. ~~Subject colour (FR-16)~~ Resolved: `Subject.color` already exists in the schema.\n6. **ADMIN on `/api/me/timetable` (FR-38):** return an empty list (recommended) or a 400.\n7. **Serialization retry helper (NFR-1):** a new small `withSerializableRetry` with no existing precedent (B7). Keep it in timetable-service.\n\n## Intake blockers and how this analysis covers them\n\n| Blocker | Covered by |\n|---------|-----------|\n| FR-44 seed fixtures | Seed rows above. Reuse any existing PRD-03/05 fixtures first. |\n| FR-43 ENG/HIST subjects | Reuse ELA/SOC with PRD course codes. |\n| FR-21 free rooms | Decision 1. |\n| FR-7 slot count | GET /api/school-days `slotCount` (FR-34 row), decision 3. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6 migration + dnd-kit | B1, B2, B12. |\n| NFR-5 mui-mcp | Dev-phase hard gate (NFR-5 row). The mui-mcp server is configured in this environment. |\n","numLines":157,"startLine":1,"totalLines":157}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BwgC3U8xWKZw2K8o21Xb4K","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
