{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDKo36QhvLR39vB77Ni","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XBXpiTGG94DxoD5Sm3pji1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).\nBrownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`\nclient (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in\n`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:\n\n1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).\n2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).\n3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31).\n\nAll of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing\nis renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4).\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |\n| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |\n| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |\n| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |\n| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |\n\n### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |\n| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |\n| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |\n| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |\n| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |\n| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |\n| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |\n| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |\n| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)\n\nNew migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only\n`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.\nGenerate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying.\n\n```prisma\nenum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }\n\nmodel Period {\n  id        String          @id @default(cuid())\n  name      String\n  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)\n  order     Int             @unique\n  slots     TimetableSlot[]\n  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel SchoolDay {\n  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun\n  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)\n}\n\nmodel TimetableSlot {\n  id             String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId String\n  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  courseId       String\n  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7\n  periodId       String\n  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service\n  roomId         String?\n  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n}\n```\n\nAdditive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,\n`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`\n(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.\n`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are\nguaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)\n\nThese are shared by the forms and the handlers.\n\n| Schema | Shape |\n|---|---|\n| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |\n| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |\n| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |\n| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |\n| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |\n| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |\n| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |\n| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |\n| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |\n| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |\n| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |\n\n`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37).\n\n### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)\n\n```ts\nexport function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }\n//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }\nexport function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(\n  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }\n```\n\nThe functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view\n(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.\nA 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used.\n\n### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)\n\nThis is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the\nNFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma.\n\n```ts\ntype ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';\ntype Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };\n\ninterface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }\ninterface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }\ninterface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }\n\nfunction clashesForCell(\n  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,\n  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot\n  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students\n): Clash[]\n```\n\nThe rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):\n\n| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |\n| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |\n| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |\n| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |\n| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |\n| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |\n\n`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call.\n\n### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)\n\n`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads.\n\n| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |\n| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |\n| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |\n| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |\n| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |\n| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |\n| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |\n\n### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |\n| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |\n| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |\n| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |\n| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |\n| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |\n\n**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.\nADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`.\n\nThe detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)\n\nThis follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:\n\n```ts\n<TimetableGrid\n  periods days slots\n  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"\n  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period\n  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging\n  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18\n/>\n```\n\n- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).\n- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).\n- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.\n- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.\n- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).\n- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change.\n\n### 3.7 Pages\n\n| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |\n| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |\n| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |\n| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |\n| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |\n\nNavigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`\n(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`\n`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).\n\n### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)\n\nSeeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.\n\n1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).\n2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).\n3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**\n4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.\n   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)\n\n```\ndrag start (course card or slot)\n  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)\n     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored\ndrop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)\n  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }\n  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }\n       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {\n                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]\n                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved\n                 insert / update\n               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }\n  client:\n    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache\n    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)\n          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)\ndrop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)\nclick slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)\n```\n\nConcurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set\nand both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and\nreturns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12).\n\n### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)\n\n`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.\n`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.\nTeaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm\ndialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit\n`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.\n\n### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)\n\n```\n/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)\n  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()\n  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now\n```\n\nClient-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same\naccess rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7).\n\n### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nPRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from\n`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in\n`SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)\n\n`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),\n`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).\n`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-cutting\n\n| Concern | Design | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |\n| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |\n| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |\n| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |\n| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |\n| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |\n| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |\n\n### Tests (ADR-7)\n\n| File | Covers | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |\n| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File Map (new unless marked)\n\n```\nprisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)\nprisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)\nprisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)\npackage.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")\nsrc/lib/validators/timetable.ts\nsrc/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)\nsrc/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts\nsrc/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\nsrc/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/school-days/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts\nsrc/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx\nsrc/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)\napp-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")\ntests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts\ntests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts\ntests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts\n```\n\nDev must confirm the route-group segment (`(app)` or the repo's actual equivalent) against the existing `admin/courses` page location.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |\n| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |\n| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |\n| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |\n| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |\n| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |\n| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |\n| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |\n| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |\n| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |\n| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |\n| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |\n| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |\n| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |\n| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |\n| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |\n| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |\n| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |\n| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |\n| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |\n| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |\n| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |\n| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |\n| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |\n| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |\n| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |\n| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |\n| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |\n| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |\n| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |\n| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |\n| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |\n| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |\n| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |\n| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |\n| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |\n| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |\n| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |\n| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |\n| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |\n| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |\n| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |\n| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |\n| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |\n| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |\n| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |\n| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |\n| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |\n| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |\n| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |\n| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |\n| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |\n| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |\n| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |\n| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1345,"cache_read_input_tokens":57929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1345},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"197d390e-c577-4a77-aead-08d0e3d6d0a4","uuid":"bb9af69f-c9b6-4b6b-b92d-03fcbc901e2f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:18:43.564Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDKnoU1eGsP3AUVDt4W","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XBXpiTGG94DxoD5Sm3pji1":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).\nBrownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`\nclient (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in\n`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:\n\n1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).\n2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).\n3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31).\n\nAll of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing\nis renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4).\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |\n| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |\n| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |\n| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |\n| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |\n\n### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |\n| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |\n| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |\n| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |\n| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |\n| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |\n| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |\n| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |\n| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)\n\nNew migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only\n`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.\nGenerate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying.\n\n```prisma\nenum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }\n\nmodel Period {\n  id        String          @id @default(cuid())\n  name      String\n  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)\n  order     Int             @unique\n  slots     TimetableSlot[]\n  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel SchoolDay {\n  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun\n  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)\n}\n\nmodel TimetableSlot {\n  id             String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId String\n  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  courseId       String\n  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7\n  periodId       String\n  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service\n  roomId         String?\n  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n}\n```\n\nAdditive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,\n`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`\n(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.\n`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are\nguaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)\n\nThese are shared by the forms and the handlers.\n\n| Schema | Shape |\n|---|---|\n| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |\n| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |\n| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |\n| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |\n| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |\n| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |\n| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |\n| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |\n| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |\n| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |\n| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |\n\n`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37).\n\n### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)\n\n```ts\nexport function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }\n//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }\nexport function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(\n  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }\n```\n\nThe functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view\n(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.\nA 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used.\n\n### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)\n\nThis is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the\nNFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma.\n\n```ts\ntype ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';\ntype Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };\n\ninterface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }\ninterface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }\ninterface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }\n\nfunction clashesForCell(\n  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,\n  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot\n  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students\n): Clash[]\n```\n\nThe rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):\n\n| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |\n| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |\n| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |\n| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |\n| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |\n| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |\n\n`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call.\n\n### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)\n\n`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads.\n\n| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |\n| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |\n| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |\n| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |\n| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |\n| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |\n| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |\n\n### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |\n| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |\n| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |\n| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |\n| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |\n| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |\n\n**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.\nADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`.\n\nThe detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)\n\nThis follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:\n\n```ts\n<TimetableGrid\n  periods days slots\n  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"\n  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period\n  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging\n  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18\n/>\n```\n\n- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).\n- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).\n- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.\n- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.\n- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).\n- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change.\n\n### 3.7 Pages\n\n| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |\n| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |\n| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |\n| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |\n| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |\n\nNavigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`\n(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`\n`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).\n\n### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)\n\nSeeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.\n\n1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).\n2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).\n3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**\n4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.\n   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)\n\n```\ndrag start (course card or slot)\n  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)\n     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored\ndrop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)\n  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }\n  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }\n       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {\n                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]\n                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved\n                 insert / update\n               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }\n  client:\n    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache\n    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)\n          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)\ndrop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)\nclick slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)\n```\n\nConcurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set\nand both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and\nreturns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12).\n\n### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)\n\n`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.\n`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.\nTeaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm\ndialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit\n`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.\n\n### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)\n\n```\n/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)\n  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()\n  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now\n```\n\nClient-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same\naccess rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7).\n\n### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nPRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from\n`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in\n`SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)\n\n`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),\n`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).\n`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-cutting\n\n| Concern | Design | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |\n| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |\n| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |\n| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |\n| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |\n| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |\n| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |\n\n### Tests (ADR-7)\n\n| File | Covers | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |\n| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File Map (new unless marked)\n\n```\nprisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)\nprisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)\nprisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)\npackage.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")\nsrc/lib/validators/timetable.ts\nsrc/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)\nsrc/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts\nsrc/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\nsrc/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/school-days/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts\nsrc/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx\nsrc/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)\napp-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")\ntests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts\ntests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts\ntests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts\n```\n\nDev must confirm the route-group segment (`(app)` or the repo's actual equivalent) against the existing `admin/courses` page location.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |\n| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |\n| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |\n| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |\n| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |\n| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |\n| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |\n| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |\n| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |\n| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |\n| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |\n| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |\n| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |\n| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |\n| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |\n| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |\n| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |\n| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |\n| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |\n| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |\n| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |\n| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |\n| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |\n| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |\n| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |\n| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |\n| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |\n| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |\n| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |\n| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |\n| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |\n| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |\n| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |\n| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |\n| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |\n| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |\n| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |\n| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |\n| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |\n| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |\n| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |\n| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |\n| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |\n| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |\n| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |\n| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |\n| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |\n| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |\n| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |\n| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |\n| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |\n| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |\n| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |\n| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |\n| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XBXpiTGG94DxoD5Sm3pji1","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"197d390e-c577-4a77-aead-08d0e3d6d0a4","uuid":"d8c188e6-e321-4c25-8fe2-92c610cf2bea","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:18:43.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub-prds/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).\nBrownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`\nclient (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in\n`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:\n\n1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).\n2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).\n3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31).\n\nAll of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing\nis renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4).\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |\n| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |\n| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |\n| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |\n| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |\n\n### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |\n| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |\n| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |\n| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |\n| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |\n| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |\n| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |\n| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |\n| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)\n\nNew migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only\n`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.\nGenerate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying.\n\n```prisma\nenum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }\n\nmodel Period {\n  id        String          @id @default(cuid())\n  name      String\n  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)\n  order     Int             @unique\n  slots     TimetableSlot[]\n  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel SchoolDay {\n  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun\n  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)\n}\n\nmodel TimetableSlot {\n  id             String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId String\n  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  courseId       String\n  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7\n  periodId       String\n  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service\n  roomId         String?\n  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n}\n```\n\nAdditive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,\n`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`\n(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.\n`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are\nguaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)\n\nThese are shared by the forms and the handlers.\n\n| Schema | Shape |\n|---|---|\n| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |\n| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |\n| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |\n| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |\n| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |\n| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |\n| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |\n| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |\n| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |\n| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |\n| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |\n\n`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37).\n\n### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)\n\n```ts\nexport function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }\n//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }\nexport function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(\n  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }\n```\n\nThe functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view\n(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.\nA 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used.\n\n### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)\n\nThis is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the\nNFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma.\n\n```ts\ntype ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';\ntype Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };\n\ninterface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }\ninterface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }\ninterface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }\n\nfunction clashesForCell(\n  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,\n  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot\n  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students\n): Clash[]\n```\n\nThe rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):\n\n| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |\n| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |\n| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |\n| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |\n| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |\n| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |\n\n`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call.\n\n### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)\n\n`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads.\n\n| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |\n| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |\n| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |\n| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |\n| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |\n| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |\n| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |\n\n### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |\n| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |\n| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |\n| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |\n| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |\n| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |\n\n**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.\nADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`.\n\nThe detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)\n\nThis follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:\n\n```ts\n<TimetableGrid\n  periods days slots\n  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"\n  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period\n  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging\n  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18\n/>\n```\n\n- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).\n- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).\n- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.\n- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.\n- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).\n- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change.\n\n### 3.7 Pages\n\n| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |\n| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |\n| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |\n| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |\n| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |\n\nNavigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`\n(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`\n`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).\n\n### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)\n\nSeeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.\n\n1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).\n2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).\n3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**\n4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.\n   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)\n\n```\ndrag start (course card or slot)\n  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)\n     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored\ndrop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)\n  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }\n  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }\n       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {\n                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]\n                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved\n                 insert / update\n               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }\n  client:\n    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache\n    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)\n          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)\ndrop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)\nclick slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)\n```\n\nConcurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set\nand both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and\nreturns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12).\n\n### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)\n\n`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.\n`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.\nTeaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm\ndialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit\n`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.\n\n### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)\n\n```\n/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)\n  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()\n  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now\n```\n\nClient-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same\naccess rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7).\n\n### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nPRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from\n`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in\n`SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)\n\n`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),\n`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).\n`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-cutting\n\n| Concern | Design | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |\n| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |\n| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |\n| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |\n| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |\n| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |\n| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |\n\n### Tests (ADR-7)\n\n| File | Covers | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |\n| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File Map (new unless marked)\n\n```\nprisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)\nprisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)\nprisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)\npackage.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")\nsrc/lib/validators/timetable.ts\nsrc/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)\nsrc/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts\nsrc/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\nsrc/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/school-days/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts\nsrc/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx\nsrc/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)\napp-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")\ntests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts\ntests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts\ntests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts\n```\n\nDev must confirm the route-group segment (`(app)` or the repo's actual equivalent) against the existing `admin/courses` page location.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |\n| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |\n| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |\n| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |\n| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |\n| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |\n| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |\n| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |\n| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |\n| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |\n| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |\n| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |\n| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |\n| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |\n| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |\n| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |\n| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |\n| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |\n| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |\n| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |\n| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |\n| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |\n| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |\n| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |\n| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |\n| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |\n| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |\n| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |\n| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |\n| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |\n| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |\n| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |\n| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |\n| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |\n| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |\n| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |\n| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |\n| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |\n| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |\n| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |\n| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |\n| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |\n| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |\n| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |\n| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |\n| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |\n| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |\n| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |\n| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |\n| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |\n| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |\n| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |\n| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |\n| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |\n| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":318,"newStart":1,"newLines":444,"lines":["-# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)","+# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)"," ","-Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete","+Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),","-`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),","-`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),","-`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11).","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),","+`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),","+`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),","+`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).","+Brownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`","+client (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in","+`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention."," ","-## Overview","+---"," ","-PRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:","+## 1. Overview"," ","-1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a","-   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.","-2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A","-   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with","-   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport.","+PRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:"," ","-Producers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing","-`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,","-no schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the","-already-declared tables.","+1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).","+2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).","+3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31)."," ","-### Intake blockers and how this design handles them","+All of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing","+is renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4)."," ","+### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)","+"," | Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |","-| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |","-| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |","-| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |","+| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |","+| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |","+| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |","+| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |","+| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |","+| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |"," ","-### New blocker-level finding (B1)","+### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)"," ","-`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless","-`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`","-would never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in","-`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check","-then becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).","+| # | Decision | Reason |","+|---|---|---|","+| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |","+| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |","+| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |","+| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |","+| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |","+| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |","+| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |","+| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |","+| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |"," ","-## Component Breakdown","+---"," ","-### 1. Data layer (FR-1)","+## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)"," ","-- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with","-  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.","-- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`","-  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).","-- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is","-  derived from the registry at query time.","+New migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only","+`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.","+Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying."," ","-### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)","+```prisma","+enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }"," ","-```ts","-export const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;","-export type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];","-type NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;","-  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };","-export const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {","-  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },","-  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },","-  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },","-} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;","-export type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;","-```","+model Period {","+  id        String          @id @default(cuid())","+  name      String","+  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone","+  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone","+  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)","+  order     Int             @unique","+  slots     TimetableSlot[]","+  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())","+  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt","+}"," ","-- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or","-  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).","-- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and","-  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.","-- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API.","+model SchoolDay {","+  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun","+  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)","+}"," ","-### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)","+model TimetableSlot {","+  id             String       @id @default(cuid())","+  academicYearId String","+  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])","+  courseId       String","+  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","+  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7","+  periodId       String","+  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service","+  roomId         String?","+  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)","+  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())","+  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt"," ","-- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`","-  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).","-- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination","-  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.","-- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks","-  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).","-- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`.","+  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])","+  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])","+}","+```"," ","-### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)","+Additive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,","+`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`","+(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.","+`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are","+guaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`."," ","-| File | Exports | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |","-| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |","-| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |","+---"," ","-`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:","+## 3. Component Breakdown"," ","-1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).","-   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).","-2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).","-3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).","-4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.","-5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the","-   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.","-6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**","-   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).","-   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.","-7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc","-   says: \"call after your transaction commits\".","+### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)"," ","-`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,","-passes the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12).","+These are shared by the forms and the handlers."," ","-*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.","-A later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1.","+| Schema | Shape |","+|---|---|","+| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |","+| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |","+| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |","+| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |","+| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |","+| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |","+| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |","+| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |","+| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |","+| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |","+| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |"," ","-### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)","+`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37)."," ","-| File | Responsibility |","-|---|---|","-| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |","-| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |","-| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |","-| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |","-| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |","-| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |","-| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |","-| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |","-| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |","+### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)"," ","-**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.","-It loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.","-The invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`","-to an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift","-from the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.","-The raw link is no longer logged.","+```ts","+export function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }","+//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }","+export function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(","+  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }","+```"," ","-### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)","+The functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view","+(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.","+A 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used."," ","-| Route file | Guard | Service call |","-|---|---|---|","-| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |","-| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |","-| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |","-| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |","-| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |","-| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |","-| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |","-| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |","-| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |","+### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)"," ","-The service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,","-mark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept","-out of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention.","+This is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the","+NFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma."," ","-### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)","+```ts","+type ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';","+type Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };"," ","-`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT","-or SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,","-because only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script.","+interface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }","+interface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }","+interface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }"," ","-### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)","+function clashesForCell(","+  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,","+  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot","+  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students","+): Clash[]","+```"," ","-| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |","+The rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):","+","+| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |"," |---|---|---|","-| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |","-| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |","-| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |","-| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |","+| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |","+| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |","+| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |","+| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |","+| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |","+| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |"," ","-The server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do","-not depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13).","+`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call."," ","-### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)","+### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)"," ","-For each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip","-message, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.","-Otherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread.","+`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads."," ","-### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)","+| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |","+| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |","+| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |","+| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |","+| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |","+| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |","+| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |","+| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |","+| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |","+| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |","+| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |","+| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |","+| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |"," ","-- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,","-  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.","-- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.","-  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls","-  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`","-  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.","-- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a","-  preference, reload and check that it persisted.","+### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)"," ","-## Data Flow","+| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |","+| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |","+| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |","+| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |","+| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |","+| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |","+| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |","+| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |","+| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |","+| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |"," ","-### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)","+**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.","+ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`."," ","-```","-caller service (after its tx commits)","-  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()","-       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18","-       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7","-       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7","-       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10","-       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13","-  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11","+The detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`."," ","-users.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset","-  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16","+### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)","+","+This follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:","+","+```ts","+<TimetableGrid","+  periods days slots","+  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"","+  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period","+  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging","+  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18","+/>"," ```"," ","-### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)","+- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).","+- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).","+- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.","+- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.","+- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).","+- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change."," ","+### 3.7 Pages","+","+| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |","+| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |","+| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |","+| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |","+| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |","+","+Navigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`","+(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`","+`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).","+","+### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)","+","+Seeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.","+","+1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).","+2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).","+3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**","+4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.","+   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.","+","+---","+","+## 4. Data Flow","+","+### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)","+"," ```","-dispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })","- 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5","- 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()","-              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()","-                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)","-              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4","- 3. for each claimed row (sequential):","-      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++","-                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →","-                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18","- 4. return { sent, failed, retried }","+drag start (course card or slot)","+  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)","+     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored","+drop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)","+  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }","+  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }","+       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {","+                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]","+                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved","+                 insert / update","+               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }","+  client:","+    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache","+    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)","+          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)","+drop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)","+click slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)"," ```"," ","-Triggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path","-meets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.","+Concurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set","+and both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and","+returns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12)."," ","-### C. Consumer UI","+### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)"," ","+`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.","+`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.","+Teaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm","+dialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit","+`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.","+","+### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)","+"," ```","-Bell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])","-     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10","-     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)","-     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications","-Prefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)","-Email log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test","+/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)","+  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()","+  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now"," ```"," ","-### D. Housekeeping","+Client-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same","+access rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7)."," ","-The dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process","-(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).","+### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)"," ","-## Files","+PRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from","+`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in","+`SchoolSettings.timezone`."," ","-- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;","-  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;","-  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;","-  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.","-- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`","-  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and","-  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).","-- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.","+### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)"," ","-## Out of scope (NFR-17)","+`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),","+`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).","+`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded."," ","-No SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or","-per-recipient email personalisation.","+---"," ","-## Requirements Traceability","+## 5. Cross-cutting"," ","+| Concern | Design | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |","+| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |","+| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |","+| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |","+| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |","+| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |","+| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |","+| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |","+","+### Tests (ADR-7)","+","+| File | Covers | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |","+| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |","+| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |","+| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |","+| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |","+","+---","+","+## 6. File Map (new unless marked)","+","+```","+prisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)","+prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)","+prisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)","+package.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")","+src/lib/validators/timetable.ts","+src/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)","+src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts","+src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts","+src/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts","+src/app/api/school-days/route.ts","+src/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts","+src/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts","+src/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts","+src/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)","+src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx","+src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx","+src/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx","+src/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx","+src/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx","+src/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)","+app-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")","+tests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts","+tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts","+tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts","+```","+","+Dev must confirm the route-group segment (`(app)` or the repo's actual equivalent) against the existing `admin/courses` page location.","+","+---","+","+## 7. Requirements Traceability","+"," | Req | Design element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |","-| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |","-| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |","-| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |","-| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |","-| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |","-| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |","-| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |","-| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |","-| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |","-| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |","-| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |","-| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |","-| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |","-| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |","-| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |","-| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |","-| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |","-| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |","-| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |","-| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |","-| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |","-| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |","-| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |","-| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |","-| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |","-| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |","-| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |","-| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |","-| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |","-| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |","-| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |","-| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |","-| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |","-| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |","-| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |","-| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |","-| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |","-| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |","-| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |","-| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |","-| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |","-| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |","-| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |","-| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |","-| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |","-| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |","-| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |","-| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |","-| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |","-| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |","-| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |","-| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |","-| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |","-| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |","-| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |","-| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |","-| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |","-| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |","+| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |","+| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |","+| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |","+| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |","+| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |","+| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |","+| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |","+| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |","+| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |","+| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |","+| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |","+| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |","+| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |","+| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |","+| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |","+| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |","+| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |","+| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |","+| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |","+| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |","+| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |","+| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |","+| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |","+| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |","+| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |","+| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |","+| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |","+| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |","+| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |","+| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |","+| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |","+| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |","+| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |","+| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |","+| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |","+| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |","+| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |","+| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |","+| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |","+| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |","+| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |","+| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |","+| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |","+| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |","+| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |","+| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |","+| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |","+| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |","+| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |","+| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |","+| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |","+| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |","+| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |","+| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |","+| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |","+| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |","+| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |","+| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |","+| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |","+| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |","+| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |"]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — ticket SH-4 (PRD-04 Notifications & Email Infrastructure, SCH-004)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-04T12:20:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 18 NFR),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (93% confidence, 4 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..10),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (brownfield facts B1–B11).\n\n## Overview\n\nPRD-04 adds two delivery channels on top of the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 app:\n\n1. **In-app notifications.** These are `Notification` rows, shown by a polling bell in the shell, a\n   `/notifications` page and a `/account/notifications` preferences page.\n2. **Transactional email through a DB outbox.** Requests only *insert* `EmailOutbox` rows. A\n   dispatcher, run from a cron-hit route or a tsx worker loop, claims them with\n   `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` and sends them through Nodemailer or the console transport.\n\nProducers use a single entry point, `notify()`. The only other producer is the existing\n`sendAuthEmail()` seam, which now enqueues instead of logging. **No new dependencies,\nno schema edits and no new infrastructure** are needed. One additive migration creates the\nalready-declared tables.\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design handles them\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1: models declared but no migration | **Resolved.** One migration, `notifications_email`, generated from the unchanged `schema.prisma`. The additive `updatedAt` columns are kept, and `EmailOutbox.updatedAt` is the SENDING timestamp for NFR-5 (ADR-1). |\n| FR-4/FR-16: auth emails bypass notify()? | **Confirmed.** `sendAuthEmail()` renders the template and inserts one `EmailOutbox` row directly, with no Notification row and no preference lookup. `account.invite` and `account.password_reset` are registered as `emailOnly: true` and are hidden from preferences (FR-28, FR-37) and rejected by the PUT (FR-38). Unlike notify(), `sendAuthEmail` **keeps throwing on failure**. Both callers already await it, and a silently lost invite or reset is worse than a 500. |\n| FR-40: seed count ambiguous | **Default accepted:** 3 per user (1 read, 2 unread), linking to `/dashboard`. **New finding (B2):** `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test` do not exist in `prisma/seed.ts`. The seed looks each user up by email and **skips with a log line** if the user is missing. It does not create identity data that another PRD owns. For idempotency, the seed skips a user who already has any `system.test` notification. |\n| NFR-10: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Carried to dev as a precondition.** mui-mcp is reachable at architect time, and dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` per component before writing UI. If mui-mcp is unreachable during dev, that is a hard stop. |\n\n### New blocker-level finding (B1)\n\n`src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for every `/api/*` request without a session unless\n`isPublicPath()` matches. Cron calls carry no cookie, so `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`\nwould never reach its handler. **Add `'/api/internal/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`** in\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`. The trailing slash gives a prefix match. The handler's CRON_SECRET check\nthen becomes the sole gate (NFR-8), so it must be strict (timing-safe, unset secret → 401).\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Data layer (FR-1)\n\n- `prisma/migrations/<ts>_notifications_email/migration.sql` is generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only --name notifications_email` and must sort after `*_auth_reconcile`.\n- The tables are `Notification` (index `[userId, readAt, createdAt]`, cascade FK), `NotificationPreference`\n  (PK `[userId, type]`, cascade FK) and `EmailOutbox` (index `[status, nextAttemptAt]`, no FK to User).\n- `type` stays a plain `String` (ADR-2). Notification has no `category` column, so the category is\n  derived from the registry at query time.\n\n### 2. Notification type registry: `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (FR-2..5)\n\n```ts\nexport const NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES = ['ACCOUNT','ACADEMIC','ATTENDANCE','COMMUNICATION','FINANCE','SYSTEM'] as const;\nexport type NotificationCategory = typeof NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES[number];\ntype NotificationTypeDef = { label; description; category: NotificationCategory; defaultEmail: boolean;\n  mandatoryInApp: boolean; roles: readonly Role[]; emailOnly?: true };\nexport const NOTIFICATION_TYPES = {\n  'account.invite':         { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'account.password_reset': { category: 'ACCOUNT', defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, emailOnly: true, roles: ALL },\n  'system.test':            { category: 'SYSTEM',  defaultEmail: true, mandatoryInApp: false, roles: ALL },\n} as const satisfies Record<string, NotificationTypeDef>;\nexport type NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES;\n```\n\n- The module must stay **client-safe**, with no `prisma` or `env` imports. Role values are imported as a type, or\n  as string literals, so the validators and client pages can import it (ADR-2).\n- Helpers in the same file: `visibleTypesFor(role)` filters `roles.includes(role) && !emailOnly`, and\n  `typesInCategory(cat)` returns keys for the FR-34 filter.\n- Later PRDs add keys to this object. There is no runtime registration API.\n\n### 3. Shared validators: `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` (FR-41, NFR-6, NFR-18)\n\n- `isSafeRelativeLink(s)` returns true only if the string starts with `/`, `s[1]` is not `/` or `\\`, it contains no `\\`\n  anywhere and it has no control characters (ADR-10).\n- `listNotificationsQuery` defines `unread?: 'true'|'false'` and `category?: z.enum(NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES)`. Pagination\n  goes through the existing `parsePagination`.\n- `updatePreferenceBody` is `{ type: z.string(), inApp: z.boolean(), email: z.boolean() }`. The service checks\n  `type` against the registry and the role (see §6).\n- `TITLE_MAX = 140` and `BODY_MAX = 500`.\n\n### 4. Notify service: `src/server/notifications/` (FR-6..12, NFR-1, NFR-18)\n\n| File | Exports | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `preferences.ts` | `resolvePrefs(def, row?) → { inApp, email }` (pure), `getPreferencesFor(user)`, `updatePreference(user, body)` | `inApp = def.mandatoryInApp \\|\\| (row?.inApp ?? true)`; `email = row?.email ?? def.defaultEmail` |\n| `notify.ts` | `notify(input)`, `notifyStudentAndParents(input)`, `expandStudentRecipients(studentIds, links)` (pure) | see flow below |\n| `purge.ts` | `purgeOldNotifications(now)` | `deleteMany({ createdAt: { lt: now − 180d } })` |\n\n`notify({ type, userIds, title, body?, link?, email?: { subject?, template, data } })` works as follows:\n\n1. Normalise the input. Dedupe `userIds`. Truncate the title to 140 characters and the body to 500, with `logger.warn` on truncation (NFR-18).\n   Drop an unsafe `link` (store `null`, `logger.warn`) (NFR-6).\n2. **Round-trip 1:** `user.findMany({ id in, status notIn [DISABLED, ARCHIVED], archivedAt: null })` (FR-7).\n3. **Round-trip 2:** `notificationPreference.findMany({ userId in, type })` (FR-7).\n4. `resolvePrefs` per user gives the in-app and email recipient lists.\n5. **Round-trip 3:** `notification.createMany(inAppRows)` (FR-8). 1,000 rows × about 7 columns is well under the\n   65,535 parameter limit, so there is no chunking.\n6. If any email recipients have `user.email`, fetch `SchoolSettings` once, render the template **once per call**\n   (ADR-6), then **round-trip 4:** `emailOutbox.createMany(rows)` with the shared html/text (FR-9).\n   That makes 2 round-trips for notifications and 3 for emails, within FR-10's limit of 3 each.\n7. The whole body is wrapped in `try/catch → logger.error`. It returns `void` and **never throws** (FR-11). The JSDoc\n   says: \"call after your transaction commits\".\n\n`notifyStudentAndParents({ studentIds, ...rest })` makes one `parentStudentLink.findMany({ studentId in })` call,\npasses the result through `expandStudentRecipients` (students ∪ parents, deduped with a `Set`), then calls `notify` (FR-12).\n\n*Generic emails have no per-recipient greeting.* That is what makes render-once possible and keeps NFR-1 under 2 s.\nA later PRD that wants personalisation must revisit NFR-1.\n\n### 5. Email subsystem: `src/server/email/` (FR-13..21, NFR-3..5, NFR-7, NFR-9)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `templates/BaseLayout.tsx` | Header with logo and name, then content, then a footer with the address, a \"Manage email preferences\" link to `${APP_URL}/account/notifications` and the fixed sentence (FR-14). Props: `school: Pick<SchoolSettings,'name'\\|'shortName'\\|'logoUrl'\\|'addressLine1'\\|'addressLine2'>`. |\n| `templates/Invite.tsx` | Name, school name, accept button and expiry date (FR-15). |\n| `templates/PasswordReset.tsx` | Link plus \"This link expires in 60 minutes.\" (FR-15) |\n| `templates/GenericNotification.tsx` | Title, body (`white-space: pre-line`, as text) and a CTA to `APP_URL + link` (FR-15). |\n| `render.ts` | `TEMPLATES = { invite, 'password-reset', 'generic-notification' }` and `renderEmail(template, data, school) → Promise<{html,text}>`, which awaits both `render()` calls (`@react-email/render` 1.x is async). No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` anywhere (NFR-7). |\n| `outbox.ts` | `enqueueEmail({ toEmail, toName, subject, html, text })` → `emailOutbox.create`. Used by `sendAuthEmail`. `notify()` uses `createMany` directly. |\n| `backoff.ts` | `BACKOFF_MIN = [1,5,15,60,240]`, `nextRetry(attemptsAfterIncrement, now)` → `{status:'PENDING', nextAttemptAt}` or `{status:'FAILED'}` (FR-18). Pure. |\n| `transport.ts` | `sendMail({ to, toName, subject, html, text })`. `if (env.EMAIL_TRANSPORT === 'smtp')` uses a lazily created Nodemailer transport with `from: EMAIL_FROM` and `headers: { 'List-Unsubscribe': '<${APP_URL}/account/notifications>' }`. Otherwise it uses `console.log` of the subject, recipient and text (FR-21, NFR-9, NFR-11). A missing `SMTP_HOST` or `EMAIL_FROM` throws inside `sendMail`, so the dispatcher records it as a retryable failure. |\n| `dispatch.ts` | `dispatchEmails({ batchSize = 50 } = {}) → { sent, failed, retried }` (FR-17). See the data flow below. |\n\n**Auth email seam (FR-16).** In `src/server/auth/email.ts`, only the body of `sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)` changes.\nIt loads SchoolSettings, calls `renderEmail(kind, …)`, then calls `enqueueEmail({ toEmail: user.email, toName: user.firstName, subject: SUBJECTS[kind], … })`.\nThe invite expiry date is `now + INVITE_TTL_DAYS`. Move the literal `{ days: 7 }` in `users.ts:384`\nto an exported `INVITE_TTL = { days: 7 }` in `src/server/auth/tokens.ts`, used by both, so the email cannot drift\nfrom the real token TTL. The signature and both call sites (`users.ts:396`, `auth.ts:54`) stay unchanged.\nThe raw link is no longer logged.\n\n### 6. HTTP API: thin handlers via `withHandler` → Zod → service → `ok` / `paginated` (NFR-8, NFR-11)\n\n| Route file | Guard | Service call |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/notifications/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `listNotifications(me, query, page)`, with `where: { userId: me.id, readAt: unread ? null : undefined, type: category ? { in: typesInCategory(c) } : undefined }` and `orderBy createdAt desc` (FR-34) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/unread-count/route.ts` GET | `requireUser` | `count({ userId, readAt: null })`, which is index-only (FR-35, NFR-2) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/read-all/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ userId, readAt: null }, { readAt: now })` (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/notifications/[id]/read/route.ts` POST, `[id]/unread/route.ts` POST | `requireUser` | `updateMany({ id, userId: me.id })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, so the existence of other users' rows is not revealed (FR-36) |\n| `src/app/api/me/notification-preferences/route.ts` GET / PUT | `requireUser` | GET: `getPreferencesFor(me)` → `visibleTypesFor(me.role)` merged with rows (FR-37). PUT: `updatePreference(me, body)` rejects unknown, emailOnly or role-invisible types and `inApp:false` on mandatory types with `VALIDATION_ERROR`, then upserts on `userId_type` (FR-38) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/route.ts` GET | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | Paginated `emailOutbox.findMany` with an optional `status` filter, ordered by `createdAt desc`, **selecting no html or text** (FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/email-log/[id]/retry/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `updateMany({ id, status: 'FAILED' }, { attempts: 0, status: 'PENDING', nextAttemptAt: now, lastError: null })`. A count of 0 means `NOT_FOUND`, which makes a double click harmless (FR-32, FR-39) |\n| `src/app/api/admin/notifications/test/route.ts` POST | `requireRole('ADMIN')` | `notify({ type: 'system.test', userIds: [me.id], title: 'Test notification', body, link: '/dashboard', email: { template: 'generic-notification', … } })` (FR-33) |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` POST | CRON_SECRET bearer (timing-safe, unset → 401) | `dispatchEmails()`, then the best-effort purge if more than 24 h have passed since the module-level `lastPurgeAt` (FR-19, FR-27). The purge has its own `try/catch` and never fails the response |\n\nThe service functions for the user and admin routes live in `src/server/notifications/service.ts` (list, count,\nmark read/unread, read-all) and `src/server/email/admin.ts` (log list, retry). These are thin Prisma calls, kept\nout of the route files so the routes stay thin, per the NFR-11 convention.\n\n### 7. Background job: `scripts/worker-email.ts` (FR-20, NFR-3)\n\n`while (running) { try { await dispatchEmails() } catch (e) { logger.error } await sleep(15_000) }`. A SIGINT\nor SIGTERM sets `running = false` and disconnects Prisma. The loop calls the service directly. It does not purge,\nbecause only the endpoint runs the purge. It runs through the existing `npm run worker:email` script.\n\n### 8. UI: MUI v9 only, using `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before each component (NFR-10)\n\n| Surface | File(s) | Components and behaviour |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bell (FR-22..25) | `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx` (`'use client'`). In `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, replace the placeholder `Tooltip > IconButton > NotificationsNoneIcon` with `<NotificationBell />` | `IconButton` + `Badge max={9}` gives \"9+\" natively. One `useEffect` runs `setInterval(30s)` while `document.visibilityState === 'visible'`, clears it on hidden and refetches on visible. When the `Popover` opens, it fetches `GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10`. Rows use `List` / `ListItemButton`, with bold text and a dot for unread items, `Typography` with a 2-line `WebkitLineClamp`, and `formatDistanceToNowStrict`. On click: `POST /:id/read` → `router.push(link)` (only if `isSafeRelativeLink`) → close → refetch the count. The footer has \"Mark all as read\" and \"View all\" linking to `/notifications`. |\n| Notifications page (FR-26) | `src/app/(app)/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `NotificationsList.tsx` (client) | `PageHeader`, `Tabs` (All / Unread), a category `Select`, a `List` with a per-row read/unread `IconButton`, `Pagination` with a page size of 20, a bulk \"Mark all as read\" and `EmptyState`. |\n| Preferences (FR-28..30) | `src/app/(app)/account/notifications/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageUser`) + `PreferencesTable.tsx` (client) | A `Table` with one full-width `TableRow` header per category. Columns: label, description, an \"In app\" `Switch` and an \"Email\" `Switch`. Mandatory rows show a disabled Switch inside `<span>` inside `Tooltip \"Required by the school\"`. Changes update local state optimistically, call `PUT`, and revert plus `useToast` error on failure. |\n| Admin email log (FR-31..33) | `src/app/(app)/admin/email-log/page.tsx` (server, `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`) + `EmailLogTable.tsx` (client) | Reuses `src/components/DataTable` (MUI X DataGrid, URL pagination). Columns: created (`formatInSchoolTz`), recipient `toName <toEmail>`, subject, status `Chip`, attempts and last error. A status `Select` filters the list, and FAILED rows get a \"Retry now\" `Button`. The `PageHeader` action is \"Send test notification to me\", which shows a toast on success. |\n\nThe server pages pass `SchoolSettings.timezone` down as a prop for absolute times (NFR-12). Relative times do\nnot depend on the timezone. Navigation entries already exist and are not touched (NFR-13).\n\n### 9. Seed: append to `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-40)\n\nFor each of `student@schoolhub.test` and `parent@schoolhub.test`: run `findUnique`. If the user is missing, `console.log` a skip\nmessage, since the seed is a script and is outside the NFR-11 logger rule. If the user already has `system.test` notifications, skip.\nOtherwise, `createMany` 3 rows linking to `/dashboard`, 1 read and 2 unread.\n\n### 10. Tests (NFR-14..16, ADR-9)\n\n- `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts`: covers `resolvePrefs`, `nextRetry`, `isSafeRelativeLink` (including `//evil`, `/\\evil`,\n  `http://x` and control characters) and `expandStudentRecipients` dedupe.\n- `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts`: uses `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`.\n  Add `'tests/integration/**/*.test.ts'` to `vitest.config.ts` `include`. The cases are 2 concurrent `dispatchEmails()` calls\n  over 10 PENDING rows, with `sendMail` mocked, asserting each id is sent exactly once (AC-4), and a SENDING row with `updatedAt`\n  set to now − 11 min returning to PENDING.\n- `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`: admin test button → bell count +1 → mark all read → count 0. Then toggle a\n  preference, reload and check that it persisted.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n### A. Producer → in-app and outbox (request path, no SMTP; NFR-3)\n\n```\ncaller service (after its tx commits)\n  └─ notify()/notifyStudentAndParents()\n       ├─ normalise (truncate, safe link)          NFR-6, NFR-18\n       ├─ users.findMany (active only)             FR-7\n       ├─ prefs.findMany → resolvePrefs            FR-7\n       ├─ notification.createMany                  FR-8, FR-10\n       └─ renderEmail once → emailOutbox.createMany FR-9, FR-13\n  errors → logger.error, never thrown             FR-11\n\nusers.ts sendInvite / auth.ts requestPasswordReset\n  └─ sendAuthEmail(user, kind, link)  → renderEmail(invite|password-reset) → emailOutbox.create   FR-16\n```\n\n### B. Dispatcher (cron route or worker; FR-17, FR-18, NFR-4, NFR-5)\n\n```\ndispatchEmails({ batchSize: 50 })\n 1. recover:  updateMany SENDING & updatedAt < now-10m → PENDING (attempts unchanged)     NFR-5\n 2. claim:    $queryRaw`UPDATE \"EmailOutbox\" SET status='SENDING'::\"EmailStatus\", \"updatedAt\"=now()\n              WHERE id IN (SELECT id FROM \"EmailOutbox\" WHERE status='PENDING' AND \"nextAttemptAt\"<=now()\n                           ORDER BY \"nextAttemptAt\" LIMIT ${batchSize} FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)\n              RETURNING *`        -- single autocommit stmt; no lock held during SMTP     NFR-4\n 3. for each claimed row (sequential):\n      sendMail(row)  ok   → update { status: SENT, sentAt: now }                 → sent++\n                     err  → attempts+1, lastError=msg.slice(0,1000), nextRetry() →\n                              PENDING + nextAttemptAt (retried++) | FAILED (failed++)   FR-18\n 4. return { sent, failed, retried }\n```\n\nTriggers: the `worker:email` 15 s loop, **or** cron calling `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` at least once a minute. Either path\nmeets NFR-3's 60 s delivery limit. A crash mid-send leaves the row SENDING, and step 1 recovers it, giving at-least-once delivery on crash.\n\n### C. Consumer UI\n\n```\nBell ──30s poll (visible only)──► GET /api/notifications/unread-count  (index [userId, readAt, createdAt])\n     ──open──► GET /api/notifications?pageSize=10\n     ──click──► POST /api/notifications/:id/read → router.push(link)\n     ──footer──► POST /api/notifications/read-all | Link /notifications\nPrefs page ──► GET/PUT /api/me/notification-preferences (optimistic, rollback + toast)\nEmail log  ──► GET /api/admin/email-log?status= | POST /:id/retry | POST /api/admin/notifications/test\n```\n\n### D. Housekeeping\n\nThe dispatch route runs `purgeOldNotifications()` at most once per 24 h per process\n(`// ponytail: in-memory lastPurgeAt, move to a DB row if purge cost matters`) (FR-27).\n\n## Files\n\n- **New:** the migration; `src/server/notifications/{types,notify,preferences,service,purge}.ts`;\n  `src/server/email/{render,outbox,backoff,transport,dispatch,admin}.ts`; `src/server/email/templates/{BaseLayout,Invite,PasswordReset,GenericNotification}.tsx`;\n  `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts`; the 9 route files in §6; `src/components/NotificationBell/NotificationBell.tsx`;\n  the 3 pages plus their client components in §8; `scripts/worker-email.ts`; and the tests in §10.\n- **Modified:** `src/server/auth/email.ts` (body only); `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` (+`INVITE_TTL`) and `src/server/services/users.ts:384`\n  (use it); `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (the bell); `src/config/public-routes.ts` (+`'/api/internal/'`); `prisma/seed.ts` (append); and\n  `vitest.config.ts` (+integration glob).\n- **Untouched:** `prisma/schema.prisma`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `.env.example`, `src/config/navigation.ts` and `package.json`.\n\n## Out of scope (NFR-17)\n\nNo SMS, push, websockets, digests, channel abstraction, queue library, rate limit on the test button or\nper-recipient email personalisation.\n\n## Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §1 migration `notifications_email` (ADR-1) |\n| FR-2 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `src/server/notifications/types.ts` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `NOTIFICATION_CATEGORIES` / `NotificationCategory` |\n| FR-4 | §2 `account.invite`, `account.password_reset` (`emailOnly`), `system.test` |\n| FR-5 | §2 `NotificationType = keyof typeof NOTIFICATION_TYPES` |\n| FR-6 | §4 `notify()` in `notify.ts` |\n| FR-7 | §4 steps 2–4, `resolvePrefs` in `preferences.ts` |\n| FR-8 | §4 step 5, `notification.createMany` |\n| FR-9 | §4 step 6, `emailOutbox.createMany` |\n| FR-10 | §4 round-trip budget (2 notification, 3 email) |\n| FR-11 | §4 step 7 try/catch, never throws |\n| FR-12 | §4 `notifyStudentAndParents` + `expandStudentRecipients` |\n| FR-13 | §5 `templates/*.tsx` + `render.ts` |\n| FR-14 | §5 `BaseLayout.tsx` |\n| FR-15 | §5 `Invite`, `PasswordReset`, `GenericNotification` |\n| FR-16 | §5 auth email seam (`sendAuthEmail` body → `enqueueEmail`) |\n| FR-17 | §5 `dispatch.ts`, Data Flow B |\n| FR-18 | §5 `backoff.ts` `nextRetry`, Data Flow B step 3 |\n| FR-19 | §6 `api/internal/email/dispatch` route, B1 allowlist |\n| FR-20 | §7 `scripts/worker-email.ts` |\n| FR-21 | §5 `transport.ts` |\n| FR-22 | §8 Bell, `Badge max={9}`, shell.tsx replacement |\n| FR-23 | §8 Bell visibility-gated 30 s poll |\n| FR-24 | §8 Bell Popover list |\n| FR-25 | §8 Bell click and footer actions |\n| FR-26 | §8 Notifications page |\n| FR-27 | §5/§6 `purge.ts`, Data Flow D |\n| FR-28 | §8 Preferences table, `visibleTypesFor` (§2) |\n| FR-29 | §8 disabled Switch + Tooltip \"Required by the school\" |\n| FR-30 | §8 optimistic PUT + rollback toast |\n| FR-31 | §8 Admin email log |\n| FR-32 | §6 retry route, §8 \"Retry now\" |\n| FR-33 | §6 admin test route, §8 header button |\n| FR-34 | §6 `GET /api/notifications` |\n| FR-35 | §6 `GET /api/notifications/unread-count` |\n| FR-36 | §6 `[id]/read`, `[id]/unread`, `read-all` |\n| FR-37 | §6 `GET /api/me/notification-preferences` |\n| FR-38 | §6 `PUT /api/me/notification-preferences`, §3 `updatePreferenceBody` |\n| FR-39 | §6 admin email-log GET + retry |\n| FR-40 | §9 seed (lookup-or-skip, idempotent) |\n| FR-41 | §3 `src/lib/validators/notifications.ts` |\n| NFR-1 | §4 render-once + `createMany`, Overview note on personalisation |\n| NFR-2 | §6 unread-count on `[userId, readAt, createdAt]` index |\n| NFR-3 | Data Flow A (enqueue only), §7 15 s worker / ≤1 min cron |\n| NFR-4 | Data Flow B step 2 `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` claim |\n| NFR-5 | Data Flow B step 1 stuck-SENDING recovery via `updatedAt` |\n| NFR-6 | §3 `isSafeRelativeLink`, §4 step 1, §8 bell `router.push` guard |\n| NFR-7 | §5 JSX escaping, no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` |\n| NFR-8 | §6 guard column; Overview B1 + timing-safe CRON_SECRET |\n| NFR-9 | §5 `transport.ts` html + text + `List-Unsubscribe` |\n| NFR-10 | §8 MUI-only, mui-mcp precondition (Overview blockers) |\n| NFR-11 | §6 thin handlers, services under `src/server/{notifications,email}`, logger |\n| NFR-12 | §8 `formatInSchoolTz` with timezone prop |\n| NFR-13 | Files section: untouched list, additive changes only |\n| NFR-14 | §10 unit tests |\n| NFR-15 | §10 integration tests (gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`) |\n| NFR-16 | §10 Playwright spec |\n| NFR-17 | Out of scope section |\n| NFR-18 | §3 `TITLE_MAX` / `BODY_MAX`, §4 step 1 truncation |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XBXpiTGG94DxoD5Sm3pji1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
