{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKdaXxvxJCiwxg8d4ge","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BrcqpKibzozx6cv9NBz2Ge","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","description":"Read upstream architect research outputs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12607,"cache_read_input_tokens":26168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12607},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd66918-c044-496c-9910-9e27b9148ea6","uuid":"a8d296e7-8975-4a09-a63b-6448e892c20c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:39:10.776Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKdaJLQZUGsdNbKYUz9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BrcqpKibzozx6cv9NBz2Ge":{"command":"cd /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub && cat artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","description":"Read upstream architect research outputs"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01BrcqpKibzozx6cv9NBz2Ge":{"cwd":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BrcqpKibzozx6cv9NBz2Ge","type":"tool_result","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T11:45:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0,\nMUI 9.5.0 with emotion, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0.\nThe stack fits every FR and NFR. **This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13). The ADRs below\nrecord only the choices the requirements force for the gaps intake listed: the auth pages, the shell\nwiring, the seed, the index migration and the tests.\n\n**Workspace facts I checked** (they confirm intake or add detail to it):\n\n- `src/server/auth/credentials.ts`: `AuthError extends CredentialsSignin` and sets `.code` to one of `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited` or `locked:<N>`. A `DUMMY_HASH` compare runs on every path, so NFR-3 is already met.\n- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` exports `handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update`. `auth.config.ts` already sanitises redirects through `safeCallbackUrl` and sets `pages.signIn = '/login'`. The cookies are the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, `__Secure-` prefix in production (NFR-2).\n- **No `SessionProvider`, `useSession` or `next-auth/react` import exists anywhere in `src/`.** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component, and it renders the client `AppShell` from `shell.tsx`, which still contains `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`.\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `acceptInviteSchema`, `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES` and `safeCallbackUrl`. These cover every form.\n- `src/server/auth/email.ts` exports `authLink(kind, rawToken)`. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues to EmailOutbox and never logs the link.\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: `AuditLog.ip String?`. `User` has `@@index([lastName, firstName, email])` and does not have `@@index([role, status])`. The latest migration is `20261105000000_timetable`.\n- Tests: the unit tests for tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy and auth-validators exist. `tests/integration/` has the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent `email-dispatch.test.ts`. `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec. `playwright.config.ts` runs `npm run start` against `APP_URL`.\n- The `mui-mcp` server is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear for now. Dev must still call it before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 requires no scope expansion and no rebuild of the existing auth modules. NFR-7 bans\nextra UI libraries. Every backend piece the gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12,\nFR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` as it is. Do not add an OTP/2FA library, a password-strength library\nsuch as zxcvbn, a form wizard, or a toast library. The strength checklist comes from the existing\n`passwordChecks()` and `PASSWORD_RULES` (FR-16). Toasts use the existing `useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** The lockfile does not change. All new code is pages, shell wiring, the seed, one\nmigration and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: Sign-in uses the client `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, with errors mapped from `result.code`\n\n**Context.** FR-2 requires a `/login` form that submits through Auth.js `signIn('credentials')`.\nFR-4 and FR-6 need the server's specific messages (locked N minutes, disabled, rate-limited) shown\nin an Alert. FR-7 requires the callbackUrl to be sanitised. NFR-5 requires aria-live errors and focus\non the first invalid field. NFR-11 requires RHF with `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. NFR-2 requires CSRF.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `/login/page.tsx` is a Server Component that reads `searchParams` and renders a client `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm` calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`. In beta.25 the result carries `code` from `AuthError`. A small pure function, `loginErrorMessage(code)`, maps the codes. `locked:N` becomes \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" `disabled` becomes the disabled message. `rate_limited` becomes \"Too many attempts…\". Every other code becomes \"Email or password is incorrect.\" (FR-4, FR-6). Keep the function in the form file and export it for a unit test.\n- On success, call `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(searchParams.callbackUrl))` and then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The function already exists, and the server `redirect` callback enforces the same rule a second time.\n- The client `signIn` fetches the Auth.js CSRF token itself (NFR-2). There is no hand-rolled CSRF.\n- Do **not** use a Server Action with the server `signIn`. In beta.25 that throws `CredentialsSignin` through `redirect` plumbing, and the error is harder to surface. The client path is the documented way to show credential errors.\n\n**Consequences.** `next-auth/react` is part of the installed `next-auth`, so nothing is added. The client\ncall does not need a `SessionProvider`, because `signIn` and `signOut` from `next-auth/react` work\nwithout one.\n\n## ADR-3: The shell gets the current user from the server `auth()` through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 says to delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keep exactly one source of \"current user\".\nFR-26 needs the name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the\nsession role. NFR-9 requires server enforcement. `getCurrentUser()` / `requirePageUser()` already exist (FR-23).\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (already an async Server Component) calls `requirePageUser()`, which redirects to `/login` when there is no session. The middleware already handles that case (FR-11), so this is a second guard. The layout passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes a `user` prop, uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and shows initials, the name and a role `Chip`. Its menu has an \"Account security\" `MenuItem` that links to `/account/security` (FR-21) and a \"Sign out\" item that calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react` (FR-26).\n- Do **not** add a `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would create a second \"current user\" source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** The user is read once per navigation on the server, where a JWT decode costs almost\nnothing. Role or name changes appear after the next 5-minute recheck (FR-10), which is the same\nfreshness the JWT already has. Any shell test has to pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-4: The token pages verify on the server first; set-password forms are client RHF forms that post to the existing JSON APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says `/invite/[token]` must show the invalid-link message, or the name and email\nread-only. FR-14 says that after acceptance the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19\ncovers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login` with a success toast. FR-20 covers `/account/security`\n→ \"Password updated\", or a field error on a wrong current password. FR-17 covers `/forgot-password`\nwith a constant message. FR-12 and NFR-1 say tokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts` without consuming the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link Alert. Otherwise they render a client form with the user's email (and name, for invites). The raw token is passed only as a prop. It is never logged and never put in audit metadata (NFR-8).\n- Forms use RHF with `zodResolver(setPasswordSchema(email))` or `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, so client and server share one schema (NFR-11). They `fetch` the existing routes: `POST /api/auth/accept-invite`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/forgot-password` and `/api/account/password`. Server `VALIDATION_ERROR` `details` are mapped back with `setError` (FR-20 \"Current password is incorrect.\").\n- Invite success: call `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service already consumed the token, so a later visit shows the invalid-link message.\n- Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `LoginForm` shows `useToast` \"Password updated, sign in with your new password\" once on mount when `reset=1` is present (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` always shows the same success Alert after any 2xx or 429 response, so there is no enumeration (FR-17).\n- One shared client component, `PasswordChecklist({ password, email })`, renders `PASSWORD_RULES` as an MUI `List` with CheckCircle and RadioButtonUnchecked icons plus text. Colour is never the only signal. It is used under every new-password field (FR-16).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert role=\"alert\"` / `aria-live=\"polite\"` region per form. Field helperText comes from RHF. RHF's default `shouldFocusError: true` moves focus to the first invalid field (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes and no new services. Only pages and client forms are added.\nVerifying the token on the server before render means that an expired link never shows the form.\n\n## ADR-5: Seed users are upserted with bcrypt cost 12; the invite link is logged through the logger\n\n**Context.** FR-28 requires six ACTIVE users with password `SchoolHub123!`, created idempotently. FR-29\nand FR-30 require one INVITED user whose invite link is logged. FR-31 says not to change `sendAuthEmail`.\nNFR-12 bans `console.log`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- In `prisma/seed.ts`, add a users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notification block, which skips users that don't exist. Hash once with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`. Then call `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email }, create: {..., status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for each user. `update: {}` keeps re-runs idempotent and leaves edited users alone.\n- `invited@schoolhub.test`: upsert with `status: 'INVITED'` and `passwordHash: null`. Then call `createInviteToken(user.id)` from `services/users.ts` (it invalidates older invites) and `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. Call these only while the user is still INVITED. Do not call `sendAuthEmail`.\n\n**Consequences.** Each re-seed issues a fresh invite link and invalidates the previous one, which is the\nexpected dev behaviour. The bcrypt hash adds about 250 ms to the seed run.\n\n## ADR-6: Add `@@index([role, status])` in a new additive migration; keep `AuditLog.ip`\n\n**Context.** FR-33 says the PRD's User model declares `@@index([role, status])`. FR-32 says not to rename\nexisting fields, so `ip` stays. NFR-13 requires no renames.\n\n**Decision.** Add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`, and generate\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/` with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`.\nIt contains a single `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` does not change. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** The migration is additive and does not touch existing data. Use a migration\ntimestamp later than `20261105000000_timetable`.\n\n## ADR-7: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 asks for integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and\nchange-password, plus Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset.\nNFR-5 covers accessibility. NFR-13 requires `lint`, `typecheck` and `test` to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, the same as `email-dispatch.test.ts`. It calls `authorizeCredentials` and the services directly with a stub `Request`, covering each branch (invalid, disabled, locked:N, lockout at 5, rate_limited, success resets the count) and each service's happy path and token reuse. Call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`: covers the `loginErrorMessage` code map from ADR-2.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: covers sign-in as the seed admin, sign-out, the wrong-password message, and the redirect for an unauthenticated `/dashboard`. For forgot → reset, the spec reads the newest `EmailOutbox` row for the address through `@prisma/client` in the test process and extracts the `/reset-password/…` URL from the body. That way it needs no test-only API route in the app. Run `@axe-core/playwright` `AxeBuilder` once on `/login` (NFR-5).\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed (ADR-5) and on `DATABASE_URL`\nbeing visible to the Playwright process. Because the specs change shared users (password reset,\nlockout), mark `auth.spec.ts` as `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`. The\nreset flow should use `student2@` so that admin sign-in in parallel specs is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Intake blockers that system-design must surface: the brownfield \"design gaps only\" rule, FR-32 (`ip`, LOW confidence), FR-33 (additive index), FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link, `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is) and NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory).\n- No new API endpoints are implied. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not modify `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are **stale outputs from an earlier ticket**, and the other\n> sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-1 input, with one exception: `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n> once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-1.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI + seed + tests** ticket. Every backend module and API route already exists.\nThe design must add pages and wire them to existing code, not add services or endpoints.\n**No new API endpoint is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` should document the 5 existing routes as-is.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**,\n**UI: Auth Pages**, **UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**,\n**Seed**, **Accessibility**, **UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred `Card` shell (SchoolHub logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"`). | Auth pages render **only the card body**, with no Card or Container of their own. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Nothing imports them yet. | FR-16 checklist and the invite/reset forms **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` and `/login` reuse `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |\n| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |\n| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |\n| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |\n| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |\n| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |\n| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |\n| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |\n| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |\n| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |\n| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |\n| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |\n| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |\n| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |\n| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |\n| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## New files (expected) vs modified files\n\n**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec\n(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites).\n\n**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`.\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip`.\n2. FR-33: add the index.\n3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.\n4. Ticket id is SH-1.\n5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd66918-c044-496c-9910-9e27b9148ea6","uuid":"3829ccda-a963-40e4-876f-6017432fc79e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:39:10.884Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T11:45:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0,\nMUI 9.5.0 with emotion, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0.\nThe stack fits every FR and NFR. **This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13). The ADRs below\nrecord only the choices the requirements force for the gaps intake listed: the auth pages, the shell\nwiring, the seed, the index migration and the tests.\n\n**Workspace facts I checked** (they confirm intake or add detail to it):\n\n- `src/server/auth/credentials.ts`: `AuthError extends CredentialsSignin` and sets `.code` to one of `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited` or `locked:<N>`. A `DUMMY_HASH` compare runs on every path, so NFR-3 is already met.\n- `src/server/auth/auth.ts` exports `handlers, auth, signIn, signOut, unstable_update`. `auth.config.ts` already sanitises redirects through `safeCallbackUrl` and sets `pages.signIn = '/login'`. The cookies are the Auth.js defaults: HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, `__Secure-` prefix in production (NFR-2).\n- **No `SessionProvider`, `useSession` or `next-auth/react` import exists anywhere in `src/`.** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component, and it renders the client `AppShell` from `shell.tsx`, which still contains `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`.\n- `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` exports `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `acceptInviteSchema`, `resetPasswordSchema`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES` and `safeCallbackUrl`. These cover every form.\n- `src/server/auth/email.ts` exports `authLink(kind, rawToken)`. `sendAuthEmail` enqueues to EmailOutbox and never logs the link.\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: `AuditLog.ip String?`. `User` has `@@index([lastName, firstName, email])` and does not have `@@index([role, status])`. The latest migration is `20261105000000_timetable`.\n- Tests: the unit tests for tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy and auth-validators exist. `tests/integration/` has the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent `email-dispatch.test.ts`. `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec. `playwright.config.ts` runs `npm run start` against `APP_URL`.\n- The `mui-mcp` server is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear for now. Dev must still call it before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 requires no scope expansion and no rebuild of the existing auth modules. NFR-7 bans\nextra UI libraries. Every backend piece the gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12,\nFR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` as it is. Do not add an OTP/2FA library, a password-strength library\nsuch as zxcvbn, a form wizard, or a toast library. The strength checklist comes from the existing\n`passwordChecks()` and `PASSWORD_RULES` (FR-16). Toasts use the existing `useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** The lockfile does not change. All new code is pages, shell wiring, the seed, one\nmigration and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: Sign-in uses the client `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, with errors mapped from `result.code`\n\n**Context.** FR-2 requires a `/login` form that submits through Auth.js `signIn('credentials')`.\nFR-4 and FR-6 need the server's specific messages (locked N minutes, disabled, rate-limited) shown\nin an Alert. FR-7 requires the callbackUrl to be sanitised. NFR-5 requires aria-live errors and focus\non the first invalid field. NFR-11 requires RHF with `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. NFR-2 requires CSRF.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `/login/page.tsx` is a Server Component that reads `searchParams` and renders a client `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm` calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`. In beta.25 the result carries `code` from `AuthError`. A small pure function, `loginErrorMessage(code)`, maps the codes. `locked:N` becomes \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" `disabled` becomes the disabled message. `rate_limited` becomes \"Too many attempts…\". Every other code becomes \"Email or password is incorrect.\" (FR-4, FR-6). Keep the function in the form file and export it for a unit test.\n- On success, call `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(searchParams.callbackUrl))` and then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The function already exists, and the server `redirect` callback enforces the same rule a second time.\n- The client `signIn` fetches the Auth.js CSRF token itself (NFR-2). There is no hand-rolled CSRF.\n- Do **not** use a Server Action with the server `signIn`. In beta.25 that throws `CredentialsSignin` through `redirect` plumbing, and the error is harder to surface. The client path is the documented way to show credential errors.\n\n**Consequences.** `next-auth/react` is part of the installed `next-auth`, so nothing is added. The client\ncall does not need a `SessionProvider`, because `signIn` and `signOut` from `next-auth/react` work\nwithout one.\n\n## ADR-3: The shell gets the current user from the server `auth()` through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 says to delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keep exactly one source of \"current user\".\nFR-26 needs the name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the\nsession role. NFR-9 requires server enforcement. `getCurrentUser()` / `requirePageUser()` already exist (FR-23).\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (already an async Server Component) calls `requirePageUser()`, which redirects to `/login` when there is no session. The middleware already handles that case (FR-11), so this is a second guard. The layout passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes a `user` prop, uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and shows initials, the name and a role `Chip`. Its menu has an \"Account security\" `MenuItem` that links to `/account/security` (FR-21) and a \"Sign out\" item that calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react` (FR-26).\n- Do **not** add a `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would create a second \"current user\" source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** The user is read once per navigation on the server, where a JWT decode costs almost\nnothing. Role or name changes appear after the next 5-minute recheck (FR-10), which is the same\nfreshness the JWT already has. Any shell test has to pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-4: The token pages verify on the server first; set-password forms are client RHF forms that post to the existing JSON APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says `/invite/[token]` must show the invalid-link message, or the name and email\nread-only. FR-14 says that after acceptance the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19\ncovers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login` with a success toast. FR-20 covers `/account/security`\n→ \"Password updated\", or a field error on a wrong current password. FR-17 covers `/forgot-password`\nwith a constant message. FR-12 and NFR-1 say tokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts` without consuming the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link Alert. Otherwise they render a client form with the user's email (and name, for invites). The raw token is passed only as a prop. It is never logged and never put in audit metadata (NFR-8).\n- Forms use RHF with `zodResolver(setPasswordSchema(email))` or `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, so client and server share one schema (NFR-11). They `fetch` the existing routes: `POST /api/auth/accept-invite`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/forgot-password` and `/api/account/password`. Server `VALIDATION_ERROR` `details` are mapped back with `setError` (FR-20 \"Current password is incorrect.\").\n- Invite success: call `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service already consumed the token, so a later visit shows the invalid-link message.\n- Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `LoginForm` shows `useToast` \"Password updated, sign in with your new password\" once on mount when `reset=1` is present (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` always shows the same success Alert after any 2xx or 429 response, so there is no enumeration (FR-17).\n- One shared client component, `PasswordChecklist({ password, email })`, renders `PASSWORD_RULES` as an MUI `List` with CheckCircle and RadioButtonUnchecked icons plus text. Colour is never the only signal. It is used under every new-password field (FR-16).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert role=\"alert\"` / `aria-live=\"polite\"` region per form. Field helperText comes from RHF. RHF's default `shouldFocusError: true` moves focus to the first invalid field (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes and no new services. Only pages and client forms are added.\nVerifying the token on the server before render means that an expired link never shows the form.\n\n## ADR-5: Seed users are upserted with bcrypt cost 12; the invite link is logged through the logger\n\n**Context.** FR-28 requires six ACTIVE users with password `SchoolHub123!`, created idempotently. FR-29\nand FR-30 require one INVITED user whose invite link is logged. FR-31 says not to change `sendAuthEmail`.\nNFR-12 bans `console.log`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- In `prisma/seed.ts`, add a users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notification block, which skips users that don't exist. Hash once with `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`. Then call `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email }, create: {..., status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for each user. `update: {}` keeps re-runs idempotent and leaves edited users alone.\n- `invited@schoolhub.test`: upsert with `status: 'INVITED'` and `passwordHash: null`. Then call `createInviteToken(user.id)` from `services/users.ts` (it invalidates older invites) and `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. Call these only while the user is still INVITED. Do not call `sendAuthEmail`.\n\n**Consequences.** Each re-seed issues a fresh invite link and invalidates the previous one, which is the\nexpected dev behaviour. The bcrypt hash adds about 250 ms to the seed run.\n\n## ADR-6: Add `@@index([role, status])` in a new additive migration; keep `AuditLog.ip`\n\n**Context.** FR-33 says the PRD's User model declares `@@index([role, status])`. FR-32 says not to rename\nexisting fields, so `ip` stays. NFR-13 requires no renames.\n\n**Decision.** Add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`, and generate\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/` with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`.\nIt contains a single `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` does not change. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** The migration is additive and does not touch existing data. Use a migration\ntimestamp later than `20261105000000_timetable`.\n\n## ADR-7: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 asks for integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and\nchange-password, plus Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset.\nNFR-5 covers accessibility. NFR-13 requires `lint`, `typecheck` and `test` to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` and `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, the same as `email-dispatch.test.ts`. It calls `authorizeCredentials` and the services directly with a stub `Request`, covering each branch (invalid, disabled, locked:N, lockout at 5, rate_limited, success resets the count) and each service's happy path and token reuse. Call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`: covers the `loginErrorMessage` code map from ADR-2.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: covers sign-in as the seed admin, sign-out, the wrong-password message, and the redirect for an unauthenticated `/dashboard`. For forgot → reset, the spec reads the newest `EmailOutbox` row for the address through `@prisma/client` in the test process and extracts the `/reset-password/…` URL from the body. That way it needs no test-only API route in the app. Run `@axe-core/playwright` `AxeBuilder` once on `/login` (NFR-5).\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed (ADR-5) and on `DATABASE_URL`\nbeing visible to the Playwright process. Because the specs change shared users (password reset,\nlockout), mark `auth.spec.ts` as `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`. The\nreset flow should use `student2@` so that admin sign-in in parallel specs is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Intake blockers that system-design must surface: the brownfield \"design gaps only\" rule, FR-32 (`ip`, LOW confidence), FR-33 (additive index), FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link, `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is) and NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory).\n- No new API endpoints are implied. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not modify `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nSupporting document for `arch-design-system` (not a primary phase output).\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are **stale outputs from an earlier ticket**, and the other\n> sub-tasks overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-1 input, with one exception: `tech-stack-decisions.md`\n> once `arch-research-stack` has rewritten it for SH-1.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI + seed + tests** ticket. Every backend module and API route already exists.\nThe design must add pages and wire them to existing code, not add services or endpoints.\n**No new API endpoint is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` should document the 5 existing routes as-is.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Migration**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**,\n**UI: Auth Pages**, **UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**,\n**Seed**, **Accessibility**, **UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk (these confirm or add to intake)\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred `Card` shell (SchoolHub logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"`). | Auth pages render **only the card body**, with no Card or Container of their own. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Nothing imports them yet. | FR-16 checklist and the invite/reset forms **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` and `/login` reuse `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`. Do not write a second checklist or fetch helper. |\n| B3 | `credentials.ts` throws `AuthError(code)` (a `CredentialsSignin` subclass). Codes: `invalid`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `locked:<N>`. | `/login` calls `signIn('credentials', { redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react` and maps `result.code` to the FR-4 and FR-6 copy. That mapping is a pure function and should get one unit test. |\n| B4 | `auth.ts` exports `signIn`, `signOut` and `unstable_update`. The `jwt` callback handles `trigger==='update' && session.reauth`. `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({reauth:true})`. | FR-20 \"re-issue current session\" is **already done server-side**. The page only POSTs and shows a toast. |\n| B5 | `app/providers.tsx` has **no `SessionProvider`**. | Client `signIn`/`signOut` from `next-auth/react` work without it. The shell gets the user as a **prop from the server layout**, so no provider and no `useSession` are needed. |\n| B6 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders the client `AppShell({ schoolShortName })`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user` (`id`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `role`) to `AppShell`. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (FR-25/26/27) and gives one source of the current user. |\n| B7 | `shell.tsx` already imports `LogoutIcon`, `PersonOutlineIcon`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `Chip` and `UserAvatar`. | FR-21/FR-26 only change menu items. Add the `Account security` link and an `onClick={() => signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })}` handler. |\n| B8 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** sign the user in. Its error copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | FR-14: after a successful POST, the client calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` and then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. The FR-13 copy is rendered by the **page** when the server-side `verifyToken()` fails, and is reused when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. |\n| B9 | `tokens.ts` exports `verifyToken(raw, type)`, which is read-only and does not consume the token. | `/invite/[token]/page.tsx` is a server component that calls `verifyToken(token, 'INVITE')` to show the name and email (FR-13). `/reset-password/[token]` can do the same up front. Neither needs a new endpoint. |\n| B10 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN', …)` is a code **outside** the NFR-10 code list. | This is existing behaviour; keep it (NFR-13). The UI must handle the `INVALID_TOKEN` code. Flag it for `arch-api-contracts` to document. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | FR-11 and NFR-14 are satisfied. Middleware needs no change. |\n| B12 | `prisma/seed.ts` already looks up `student@` and `parent@` to attach PRD-04 notifications, and **skips them if missing**. It uses `console.log`. | FR-28 user upserts must run **before** the notifications block. New seed code uses `logger` (NFR-12). The existing `console.log` lines are out of scope (NFR-13). |\n| B13 | Existing tests: unit `tokens`, `lockout`, `rate-limit`, `password-policy`, `auth-validators`. Integration has no auth tests. E2E has no auth specs. | FR-34 adds 4 integration files and 1–2 Playwright specs. Unit tests are already done. |\n| B14 | The existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) hit `(app)` pages. Once a real session is required, they redirect to `/login`. | **Regression risk (NFR-13):** the e2e suite needs a shared sign-in helper or `storageState` using the seed users. Check whether these specs currently pass without auth. |\n| B15 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. | `/forgot-password` displays the API's `data.message`, or imports this constant, rather than retyping the string. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Already present; no change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, a thin server wrapper that reads `callbackUrl` plus a client `LoginForm`. It uses RHF + `signInSchema`, `TextField`, a show-password `InputAdornment`/`IconButton` (reuse `passwordInputSlot`) and an `Alert`. It links to `/forgot-password`. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`; verify only. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Pure `loginErrorMessage(code)` maps `invalid`, `disabled` and `locked:N` to the PRD copy. The locked message reads \"Try again in N minutes.\" |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`); covered by the integration test. |\n| FR-6 | UI: Auth Pages | Limiter present. Map `rate_limited` to \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` after `signIn` succeeds. Reuse the validator. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Already emitted by `authorizeCredentials`; integration test asserts the rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present; no change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`). The `reauth` path keeps the changing session alive. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present in `middleware.ts` and `public-routes.ts` (B11). |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. UI pages call `verifyToken` server-side (B9) and never hash anything themselves. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name and email. Invalid: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. Uses `verifyToken`, not consume. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client POSTs `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials')`, then `/dashboard` (B8). Service and audit already present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is server-only and surfaces through `fieldErrors.password`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth Pages / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` on invite, reset and change forms (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`. RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password')`. Always shows the success `Alert` and handles `RATE_LIMITED`. API, limiter and service are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` + `sendAuthEmail`); integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | New `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`. Uses `SetPasswordForm`, then `/login?reset=1`, where `LoginForm` fires `useToast` once on mount. The query param is the lazy channel; there is no shared state. |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | New `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form (current/new/confirm, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`). On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show the field error. On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form. Session re-issue is already server-side (B4). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` \"Account security\" item to the user menu. |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present; verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present; `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` are used by the new pages. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`; `AppShell` takes a `user` prop (B6). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name = `firstName lastName`, role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | `prisma.user.upsert` × 6 by email, `bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)`, status ACTIVE and `passwordChangedAt` set. Idempotent with `update: {}`. Place before the notifications block (B12). |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Upsert `invited@schoolhub.test` (INVITED, no `passwordHash`). |\n| FR-30 | Seed | `createInviteToken(user.id)` (which invalidates older invites on rerun) and `logger.info(authLink('invite', raw))`. Do not use `sendAuthEmail`. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip`; no rename (default per intake). |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Add a new additive migration with `@@index([role, status])` on `User` (default per intake). |\n| FR-34 | Tests | Integration files `auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`) run against the test DB. The e2e `auth.spec.ts` covers sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus a unit test for `loginErrorMessage`. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` fetches the CSRF token automatically. JSON POST routes are same-origin and SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt is about 250 ms, so this is met. Nothing new to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every form has an `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"`, and RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default) focuses the first invalid field. `applyFieldErrors` already focuses the first server-reported field. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate:** dev must call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev blocks and does not guess. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. `tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts` already guards banned imports. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | Existing metadata is `{ email, reason }`, which is safe. New code adds no audit calls. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers already conform (B10 notes the one extra code). |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | All forms use RHF + `zodResolver` with the shared `auth.ts` schemas. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger` (seed included). |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | No edits to `course-access.ts`/`student-access.ts` or any existing auth module. Watch B14 so e2e does not regress. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page; `/login` has no \"create account\" link. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI, English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## New files (expected) vs modified files\n\n**New:** `(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`, `(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + client form, one additive migration, 4 integration tests, 1 e2e spec\n(+ e2e sign-in helper if B14 bites).\n\n**Modified:** `(app)/layout.tsx` (session user → prop), `(app)/shell.tsx` (drop placeholder, menu items),\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (index), `prisma/seed.ts` (users + invite).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts` and `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`.\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip`.\n2. FR-33: add the index.\n3. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`.\n4. Ticket id is SH-1.\n5. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a dev-phase hard gate.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BrcqpKibzozx6cv9NBz2Ge","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
