{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKeLwCEoereW8mPCU66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2674,"cache_read_input_tokens":52207,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2674},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd66918-c044-496c-9910-9e27b9148ea6","uuid":"b9ce922e-1331-4ffe-b1ea-e6b87f0d0bd9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:39:23.419Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKeLi3uA54XpU4mGVe5","thinking_duration_ms":3819,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKeLwCEoereW8mPCU66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LpbthVXZpgtbkJ3ejAMXnB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n\n- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.\n  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.\n  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and\n  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).\n- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,\n  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string\n  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.\n- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour\n  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.\n- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not\n  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture at a glance\n\n```\nBrowser\n ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages\n │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]\n │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)\n │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes\n ├─ (app) route group — protected\n │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED\n │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page\n ▼\nmiddleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401\n ▼\nAPI routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)\n /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password\n /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password\n ▼\nServer modules (existing, untouched)\n auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts\n services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts\n ▼\nPrisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)\n```\n\n**Patterns**\n\n- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components\n  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when\n  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).\n- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes\n  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).\n- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).\n- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,\n  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages\n  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |\n| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |\n| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |\n| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |\n| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |\n\n### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)\n\nEvery page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).\nEvery form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default\n`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid\nfield (NFR-5).\n\n**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14\n- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with\n  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No\n  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).\n- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`\n  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).\n- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:\n\n  | `code` | Message |\n  |---|---|\n  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |\n  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |\n  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |\n\n- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server\n  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.\n- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19).\n\n**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11\n- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.\n- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.\n  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field\n  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`.\n\n**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to\n  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by\n  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.\n  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.\n- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata.\n\n**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\n  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).\n- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,\n  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.\n  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it.\n\n### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)\n\n**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11\n- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.\n- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using\n  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".\n- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →\n  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and\n  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server\n  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10).\n\n### 3.4 Modified — app shell\n\n**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9\n- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass\n  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup.\n\n**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27\n- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.\n- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);\n  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.\n- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}\n  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from\n  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).\n- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check).\n\n### 3.5 Data and seed\n\n**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12\n- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).\n- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },\n  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:\n\n  | Email | Name | Role |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |\n  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |\n  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |\n  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |\n  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |\n  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |\n\n- `invited@schoolhub.test` (Ivy Invited, role TEACHER — PRD does not fix name/role; pick and note it):\n  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,\n  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and\n  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).\n- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope).\n\n**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.\n- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged.\n\n### 3.6 Tests\n\n**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13\n\n| File | Kind | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |\n| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |\n\nIntegration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores\n`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**\n1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.\n2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches\n   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →\n   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).\n3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).\n4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`\n   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`.\n\n**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**\n1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.\n2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).\n4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert.\n\n**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →\n   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI\n   shows the same message either way.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`\n   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10).\n\n**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`\n→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min.\n\n**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**\n`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.\n\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |\n| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |\n| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |\n| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |\n| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |\n| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |\n| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |\n| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |\n| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |\n| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |\n| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |\n| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |\n| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |\n| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |\n| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |\n| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |\n| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |\n| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |\n| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |\n| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |\n| FR-34 | C12 test files |\n| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |\n| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |\n| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |\n| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |\n| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |\n| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |\n| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |\n| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |\n| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |\n| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)\n\n**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,\n`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,\n`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n\nToken pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because\n`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it\n`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,\n`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2674,"cache_read_input_tokens":52207,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2674},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd66918-c044-496c-9910-9e27b9148ea6","uuid":"347c3928-4a73-494e-8f6e-ca5a200e0ed4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:40:50.566Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKeLi3uA54XpU4mGVe5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LpbthVXZpgtbkJ3ejAMXnB":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n\n- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.\n  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.\n  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and\n  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).\n- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,\n  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string\n  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.\n- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour\n  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.\n- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not\n  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture at a glance\n\n```\nBrowser\n ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages\n │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]\n │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)\n │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes\n ├─ (app) route group — protected\n │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED\n │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page\n ▼\nmiddleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401\n ▼\nAPI routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)\n /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password\n /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password\n ▼\nServer modules (existing, untouched)\n auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts\n services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts\n ▼\nPrisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)\n```\n\n**Patterns**\n\n- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components\n  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when\n  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).\n- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes\n  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).\n- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).\n- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,\n  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages\n  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |\n| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |\n| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |\n| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |\n| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |\n\n### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)\n\nEvery page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).\nEvery form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default\n`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid\nfield (NFR-5).\n\n**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14\n- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with\n  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No\n  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).\n- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`\n  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).\n- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:\n\n  | `code` | Message |\n  |---|---|\n  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |\n  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |\n  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |\n\n- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server\n  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.\n- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19).\n\n**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11\n- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.\n- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.\n  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field\n  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`.\n\n**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to\n  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by\n  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.\n  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.\n- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata.\n\n**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\n  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).\n- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,\n  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.\n  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it.\n\n### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)\n\n**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11\n- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.\n- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using\n  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".\n- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →\n  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and\n  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server\n  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10).\n\n### 3.4 Modified — app shell\n\n**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9\n- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass\n  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup.\n\n**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27\n- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.\n- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);\n  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.\n- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}\n  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from\n  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).\n- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check).\n\n### 3.5 Data and seed\n\n**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12\n- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).\n- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },\n  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:\n\n  | Email | Name | Role |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |\n  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |\n  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |\n  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |\n  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |\n  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |\n\n- `invited@schoolhub.test` (Ivy Invited, role TEACHER — PRD does not fix name/role; pick and note it):\n  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,\n  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and\n  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).\n- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope).\n\n**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.\n- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged.\n\n### 3.6 Tests\n\n**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13\n\n| File | Kind | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |\n| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |\n\nIntegration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores\n`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**\n1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.\n2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches\n   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →\n   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).\n3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).\n4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`\n   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`.\n\n**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**\n1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.\n2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).\n4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert.\n\n**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →\n   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI\n   shows the same message either way.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`\n   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10).\n\n**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`\n→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min.\n\n**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**\n`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.\n\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |\n| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |\n| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |\n| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |\n| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |\n| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |\n| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |\n| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |\n| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |\n| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |\n| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |\n| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |\n| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |\n| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |\n| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |\n| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |\n| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |\n| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |\n| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |\n| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |\n| FR-34 | C12 test files |\n| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |\n| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |\n| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |\n| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |\n| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |\n| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |\n| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |\n| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |\n| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |\n| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)\n\n**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,\n`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,\n`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n\nToken pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because\n`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it\n`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,\n`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LpbthVXZpgtbkJ3ejAMXnB","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd66918-c044-496c-9910-9e27b9148ea6","uuid":"126a382a-a320-42eb-acc8-ed51afa2a676","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:40:50.669Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n\n- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.\n  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.\n  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and\n  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).\n- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,\n  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string\n  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.\n- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour\n  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.\n- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not\n  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture at a glance\n\n```\nBrowser\n ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages\n │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]\n │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)\n │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes\n ├─ (app) route group — protected\n │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED\n │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page\n ▼\nmiddleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401\n ▼\nAPI routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)\n /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password\n /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password\n ▼\nServer modules (existing, untouched)\n auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts\n services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts\n ▼\nPrisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)\n```\n\n**Patterns**\n\n- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components\n  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when\n  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).\n- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes\n  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).\n- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).\n- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,\n  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages\n  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |\n| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |\n| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |\n| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |\n| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |\n\n### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)\n\nEvery page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).\nEvery form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default\n`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid\nfield (NFR-5).\n\n**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14\n- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with\n  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No\n  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).\n- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`\n  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).\n- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:\n\n  | `code` | Message |\n  |---|---|\n  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |\n  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |\n  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |\n\n- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server\n  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.\n- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19).\n\n**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11\n- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.\n- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.\n  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field\n  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`.\n\n**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to\n  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by\n  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.\n  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.\n- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata.\n\n**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\n  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).\n- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,\n  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.\n  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it.\n\n### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)\n\n**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11\n- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.\n- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using\n  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".\n- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →\n  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and\n  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server\n  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10).\n\n### 3.4 Modified — app shell\n\n**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9\n- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass\n  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup.\n\n**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27\n- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.\n- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);\n  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.\n- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}\n  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from\n  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).\n- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check).\n\n### 3.5 Data and seed\n\n**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12\n- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).\n- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },\n  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:\n\n  | Email | Name | Role |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |\n  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |\n  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |\n  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |\n  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |\n  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |\n\n- `invited@schoolhub.test` (Ivy Invited, role TEACHER — PRD does not fix name/role; pick and note it):\n  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,\n  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and\n  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).\n- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope).\n\n**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.\n- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged.\n\n### 3.6 Tests\n\n**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13\n\n| File | Kind | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |\n| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |\n\nIntegration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores\n`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**\n1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.\n2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches\n   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →\n   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).\n3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).\n4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`\n   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`.\n\n**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**\n1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.\n2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).\n4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert.\n\n**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →\n   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI\n   shows the same message either way.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`\n   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10).\n\n**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`\n→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min.\n\n**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**\n`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.\n\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |\n| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |\n| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |\n| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |\n| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |\n| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |\n| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |\n| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |\n| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |\n| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |\n| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |\n| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |\n| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |\n| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |\n| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |\n| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |\n| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |\n| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |\n| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |\n| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |\n| FR-34 | C12 test files |\n| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |\n| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |\n| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |\n| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |\n| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |\n| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |\n| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |\n| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |\n| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |\n| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)\n\n**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,\n`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,\n`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n\nToken pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because\n`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it\n`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,\n`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":444,"newStart":1,"newLines":341,"lines":["-# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)","+# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)"," ","-Phase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,","+`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).","+Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),","-`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),","-`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),","-`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).","-Brownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`","-client (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in","-`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention.","-"," ---"," "," ## 1. Overview"," ","-PRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:","+SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,","+Auth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,","+credentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate","+limiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +","+tests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new","+API endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13)."," ","-1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).","-2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).","-3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31).","+### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)"," ","-All of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing","-is renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4).","+| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |","+|---|---|---|","+| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |","+| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |","+| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |","+| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |","+| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |","+| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |"," ","-### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)","+Additional risks found during design (not in intake):"," ","-| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |","-|---|---|","-| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |","-| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |","-| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |","-| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |","-| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |","-| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |","+- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.","+  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.","+  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and","+  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).","+- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,","+  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string","+  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.","+- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour","+  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.","+- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not","+  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`."," ","-### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)","-","-| # | Decision | Reason |","-|---|---|---|","-| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |","-| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |","-| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |","-| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |","-| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |","-| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |","-| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |","-| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |","-| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |","-"," ---"," ","-## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)","+## 2. Architecture at a glance"," ","-New migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only","-`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.","-Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying.","-","-```prisma","-enum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }","-","-model Period {","-  id        String          @id @default(cuid())","-  name      String","-  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone","-  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone","-  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)","-  order     Int             @unique","-  slots     TimetableSlot[]","-  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())","-  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt","-}","-","-model SchoolDay {","-  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun","-  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)","-}","-","-model TimetableSlot {","-  id             String       @id @default(cuid())","-  academicYearId String","-  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])","-  courseId       String","-  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7","-  periodId       String","-  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service","-  roomId         String?","-  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)","-  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())","-  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt","-","-  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])","-  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])","-}"," ```","+Browser","+ ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages","+ │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]","+ │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)","+ │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes","+ ├─ (app) route group — protected","+ │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED","+ │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page","+ ▼","+middleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401","+ ▼","+API routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)","+ /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password","+ /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password","+ ▼","+Server modules (existing, untouched)","+ auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts","+ services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts","+ ▼","+Prisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)","+```"," ","-Additive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,","-`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`","-(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.","-`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are","-guaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`.","+**Patterns**"," ","+- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components","+  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when","+  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).","+- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes","+  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).","+- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from","+  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).","+- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,","+  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages","+  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.","+"," ---"," "," ## 3. Component Breakdown"," ","-### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)","+### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)"," ","-These are shared by the forms and the handlers.","+| Module | Provides | Req |","+|---|---|---|","+| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |","+| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |","+| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |","+| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |","+| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |","+| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |","+| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |","+| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |","+| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |","+| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |","+| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |","+| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |","+| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |","+| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |","+| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |","+| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |","+| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |"," ","-| Schema | Shape |","-|---|---|","-| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |","-| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |","-| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |","-| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |","-| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |","-| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |","-| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |","-| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |","-| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |","-| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |","-| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |","+### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)"," ","-`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37).","+Every page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).","+Every form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default","+`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid","+field (NFR-5)."," ","-### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)","+**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14","+- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.","+- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with","+  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No","+  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).","+- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`","+  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).","+- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:"," ","-```ts","-export function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }","-//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }","-export function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(","-  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }","-```","+  | `code` | Message |","+  |---|---|","+  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |","+  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |","+  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |","+  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |"," ","-The functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view","-(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.","-A 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used.","+- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server","+  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.","+- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19)."," ","-### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)","+**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11","+- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.","+- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.","+  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field","+  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`."," ","-This is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the","-NFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma.","+**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8","+- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to","+  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by","+  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).","+- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.","+  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.","+- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata."," ","-```ts","-type ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';","-type Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };","+**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1","+- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.","+  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).","+- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.","+- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,","+  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.","+  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it."," ","-interface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }","-interface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }","-interface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }","+### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)"," ","-function clashesForCell(","-  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,","-  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot","-  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students","-): Clash[]","-```","+**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11","+- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.","+- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using","+  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".","+- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →","+  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and","+  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server","+  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10)."," ","-The rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):","+### 3.4 Modified — app shell"," ","-| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |","-|---|---|---|","-| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |","-| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |","-| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |","-| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |","-| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |","-| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |","+**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9","+- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass","+  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup."," ","-`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call.","+**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27","+- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.","+- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);","+  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.","+- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}","+  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from","+  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).","+- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check)."," ","-### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)","+### 3.5 Data and seed"," ","-`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads.","+**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12","+- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).","+- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },","+  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:"," ","-| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |","-| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |","-| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |","-| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |","-| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |","-| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |","-| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |","-| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |","-| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |","-| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |","-| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |","-| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |","-| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |","+  | Email | Name | Role |","+  |---|---|---|","+  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |","+  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |","+  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |","+  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |","+  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |","+  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |"," ","-### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)","+- `invited@schoolhub.test` (Ivy Invited, role TEACHER — PRD does not fix name/role; pick and note it):","+  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,","+  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and","+  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).","+- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope)."," ","-| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |","-| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |","-| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |","-| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |","-| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |","-| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |","-| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |","-| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |","-| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |","-| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |","+**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32","+- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.","+- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with","+  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged."," ","-**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.","-ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`.","+### 3.6 Tests"," ","-The detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.","+**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13"," ","-### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)","+| File | Kind | Covers |","+|---|---|---|","+| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |","+| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |","+| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |","+| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |","+| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |","+| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |","+| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |","+| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |"," ","-This follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:","+Integration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores","+`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected."," ","-```ts","-<TimetableGrid","-  periods days slots","-  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"","-  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period","-  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging","-  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18","-/>","-```","-","-- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).","-- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).","-- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.","-- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.","-- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).","-- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change.","-","-### 3.7 Pages","-","-| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |","-| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |","-| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |","-| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |","-| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |","-","-Navigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`","-(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`","-`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).","-","-### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)","-","-Seeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.","-","-1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).","-2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).","-3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**","-4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.","-   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.","-"," ---"," "," ## 4. Data Flow"," ","-### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)","+**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**","+1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.","+2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches","+   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →","+   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).","+3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).","+4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`","+   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`."," ","-```","-drag start (course card or slot)","-  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)","-     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored","-drop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)","-  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }","-  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }","-       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {","-                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]","-                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved","-                 insert / update","-               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }","-  client:","-    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache","-    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)","-          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)","-drop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)","-click slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)","-```","+**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**","+1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.","+2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).","+3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).","+4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert."," ","-Concurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set","-and both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and","-returns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12).","+**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**","+1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →","+   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI","+   shows the same message either way.","+2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`","+   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.","+3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10)."," ","-### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)","+**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**","+`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`","+→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min."," ","-`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.","-`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.","-Teaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm","-dialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit","-`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.","+**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**","+`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.","+\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`."," ","-### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)","-","-```","-/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)","-  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()","-  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now","-```","-","-Client-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same","-access rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7).","-","-### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)","-","-PRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from","-`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in","-`SchoolSettings.timezone`.","-","-### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)","-","-`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),","-`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).","-`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded.","-"," ---"," ","-## 5. Cross-cutting","+## 5. Requirements Traceability"," ","-| Concern | Design | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |","-| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |","-| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |","-| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |","-| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |","-| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |","-| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |","-| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |","+| Req | Design element(s) |","+|---|---|","+| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |","+| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |","+| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |","+| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |","+| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |","+| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |","+| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |","+| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |","+| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |","+| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |","+| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |","+| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |","+| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |","+| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |","+| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |","+| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |","+| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |","+| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |","+| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |","+| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |","+| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |","+| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |","+| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |","+| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |","+| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |","+| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |","+| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |","+| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |","+| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |","+| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |","+| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |","+| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |","+| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |","+| FR-34 | C12 test files |","+| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |","+| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |","+| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |","+| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |","+| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |","+| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |","+| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |","+| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |","+| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |","+| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |","+| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |","+| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |","+| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |","+| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |","+| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |"," ","-### Tests (ADR-7)","-","-| File | Covers | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |","-| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |","-| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |","-| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |","-| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |","-"," ---"," ","-## 6. File Map (new unless marked)","+## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)"," ","-```","-prisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)","-prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)","-prisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)","-package.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")","-src/lib/validators/timetable.ts","-src/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)","-src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts","-src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts","-src/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts","-src/app/api/school-days/route.ts","-src/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts","-src/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts","-src/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts","-src/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)","-src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx","-src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx","-src/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx","-src/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx","-src/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx","-src/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)","-app-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")","-tests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts","-tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts","-tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts","-```","+**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,","+`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,","+`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,","+`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,","+`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,","+`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,","+`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`."," ","-The `(app)` route group was checked on disk: `src/app/(app)/admin` already exists.","+Token pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because","+`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it","+`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder."," ","----","+**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,","+`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional)."," ","-## 7. Requirements Traceability","-","-| Req | Design element |","-|---|---|","-| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |","-| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |","-| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |","-| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |","-| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |","-| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |","-| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |","-| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |","-| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |","-| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |","-| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |","-| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |","-| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |","-| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |","-| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |","-| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |","-| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |","-| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |","-| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |","-| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |","-| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |","-| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |","-| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |","-| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |","-| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |","-| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |","-| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |","-| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |","-| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |","-| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |","-| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |","-| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |","-| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |","-| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |","-| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |","-| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |","-| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |","-| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |","-| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |","-| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |","-| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |","-| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |","-| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |","-| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |","-| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |","-| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |","-| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |","-| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |","-| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |","-| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |","-| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |","-| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |","-| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |","-| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |","-| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |","-| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |","-| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |","-| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |","-| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |","-| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |","-| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |","+**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,","+`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`."]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — ticket SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable, SCH-006)\n\nPhase: architect (`arch-design-system`) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (45 FR + 16 NFR, 96% confidence),\n`artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..7, SH-6),\n`artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md` (SH-6, 7 open decisions).\nBrownfield signatures were re-checked on disk: `audit()` writes through the global `prisma`\nclient (it takes no `tx`), `LocalizationProvider` + `AdapterDateFns` are already mounted in\n`src/app/providers.tsx`, `Subject.color` exists, and `tokens.ts` uses the `type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` convention.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-06 adds a single repeating weekly timetable (NFR-15). It has three parts:\n\n1. **Bell schedule**: ordered `Period` rows plus 7 `SchoolDay` rows, edited by ADMIN (FR-1, FR-2, FR-5–FR-8).\n2. **Timetable editor**: ADMIN places `Course`s into (day, period) cells by drag-and-drop or keyboard. A server-side clash engine guards every write (FR-9–FR-23).\n3. **Read-only timetables**: personal `/timetable`, the student tab, the course Schedule tab, print, plus two exported service functions for later PRDs (FR-24–FR-31).\n\nAll of it goes into the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI app as additive code (NFR-9). Nothing\nis renamed. The one new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core@6.3.1` (ADR-1). There is one new migration (FR-4).\n\n### Intake blockers and how this design resolves them (Compliance rule 5)\n\n| Blocker (handoff-to-architect.json) | Resolution |\n|---|---|\n| FR-44: seed has no users, sections, courses or enrollments | **Accepted default.** `prisma/seed.ts` gains an idempotent `seedTimetableFixtures()` that upserts Tom, Sam + sibling, Pat, sections 7A/7B (homerooms Room 101/102), the courses and Robotics Club (§3.8). |\n| FR-43: ENG/HIST subjects do not exist | **Accepted default.** Reuse subjects `ELA` and `SOC`. Course codes follow the PRD (`ENG-7A`, `HIST-7A`, …). |\n| FR-21: no API returns free rooms | **Decision D1:** add ADMIN `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?dayOfWeek&periodId&academicYearId` (§3.5). |\n| FR-7: slot count for the confirm dialog | **Decision D3:** `GET /api/school-days` returns `slotCount` per day, counted across **all** academic years. The PUT cascade deletes across all years too, so the number shown is the number deleted. |\n| FR-4/NFR-6: migration + `@dnd-kit/core` | One additive migration `20261105000000_timetable` (§2). Exact-pinned `@dnd-kit/core` (ADR-1). |\n| NFR-5: mui-mcp must be reachable | **Dev-phase hard gate, not a design element.** mui-mcp is configured in this environment. Dev must call `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` for every MUI component listed in §3.6–3.7 before writing it. |\n\n### Design decisions taken here (the open items from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | New ADMIN endpoint `GET /api/timetable/free-rooms` | One query. Keeps the drag preload (availability) small (FR-21, NFR-3). |\n| D2 | `GET /api/timetable/availability` takes an **optional `roomId`**. When given, the room rule is evaluated for that room. When omitted, the room rule is skipped. The client passes `section.roomId` for a new placement and `slot.roomId` for a move. The client cache key is `courseId:roomId`. | The tinted cells then match exactly what the drop will do (FR-17, FR-19). It costs nothing extra: the room check runs in memory over rows already loaded. |\n| D3 | School-day `slotCount` and the cascade delete cover all academic years | A non-teaching day makes every slot on it invalid, whatever the year (FR-7, FR-13). |\n| D4 | Archived courses and rooms are excluded from the sidebar, the Place-course dialog and free-rooms. Existing slots of archived courses **still count** in clash checks. POST/PATCH of a slot for an archived course → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. An archived `roomId` → 400. | Intake default. It keeps the DB truthful. |\n| D5 | ADMIN calling `GET /api/me/timetable` gets `{ data: { slots: [] } }`, not an error | The ADMIN has no personal timetable, and the nav does not link ADMIN there (FR-32, FR-38). |\n| D6 | The serialization-retry wrapper `withSerializableRetry` is local to `timetable-service.ts` | It has no second caller yet (ADR-3, NFR-9). |\n| D7 | Audit is **confirmed** for every slot, period and school-day mutation (FR-40). `audit()` is called **after** the transaction commits. | `audit()` uses the global client and never throws (B9), so a rolled-back write is never audited. |\n| D8 | TEACHER section access (FR-35) = sections where `homeroomTeacherId = me`, **or** sections of a non-archived course they teach or co-teach | Intake default. It matches `getAccessibleStudentIds` semantics. |\n| D9 | Period `order` is display order only. It is not forced to be chronological. Reorder sends the full id list. | Intake default for FR-5. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1–FR-4)\n\nNew migration `prisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/migration.sql`. It contains only\n`CREATE TYPE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `CREATE INDEX` and `ADD CONSTRAINT … FOREIGN KEY` statements.\nGenerate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and review it before applying.\n\n```prisma\nenum PeriodKind { CLASS BREAK LUNCH ASSEMBLY }\n\nmodel Period {\n  id        String          @id @default(cuid())\n  name      String\n  startTime String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  endTime   String          // 'HH:MM', school timezone\n  kind      PeriodKind      @default(CLASS)\n  order     Int             @unique\n  slots     TimetableSlot[]\n  createdAt DateTime        @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime        @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel SchoolDay {\n  dayOfWeek  Int     @id          // ISO 1=Mon … 7=Sun\n  isTeaching Boolean @default(true)\n}\n\nmodel TimetableSlot {\n  id             String       @id @default(cuid())\n  academicYearId String\n  academicYear   AcademicYear @relation(fields: [academicYearId], references: [id])\n  courseId       String\n  course         Course       @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  dayOfWeek      Int          // 1–7\n  periodId       String\n  period         Period       @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])   // Restrict; FR-8 guards in service\n  roomId         String?\n  room           Room?        @relation(fields: [roomId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  createdAt      DateTime     @default(now())\n  updatedAt      DateTime     @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n  @@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])\n}\n```\n\nAdditive back-relations (FR-4): `Course.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`,\n`Room.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`, and `AcademicYear.timetableSlots TimetableSlot[]`\n(needed because the FR-3 `academicYearId` is a relation). No existing field is changed.\n`SchoolDay` has no FK from `TimetableSlot` (FR-2/FR-3 define a plain `Int`). Days 1–7 are\nguaranteed by the seed (FR-42) and by Zod `int().min(1).max(7)`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Validators: `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` (FR-39, FR-6)\n\nThese are shared by the forms and the handlers.\n\n| Schema | Shape |\n|---|---|\n| `hhmm` | `z.string().regex(/^([01]\\d\\|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d$/)` |\n| `periodSchema` | `{ name: string.trim.min(1).max(50), startTime: hhmm, endTime: hhmm, kind: PeriodKind }`, refined with `endTime > startTime` (string comparison, ADR-2) |\n| `periodUpdateSchema` | `periodSchema.partial()`, with the same refine applied when both times are present. The service re-checks against the merged row. |\n| `periodReorderSchema` | `{ periodIds: string[].min(1) }`, with no duplicates |\n| `schoolDaysSchema` | `{ days: { dayOfWeek: 1..7, isTeaching: boolean }[].length(7) }`, with unique days |\n| `slotCreateSchema` | `{ courseId: string, dayOfWeek: 1..7, periodId: string, roomId?: string \\| null }` |\n| `slotUpdateSchema` | `{ dayOfWeek?, periodId?, roomId?: string \\| null }`, refined to require at least one key |\n| `timetableQuerySchema` | `{ view: 'section'\\|'teacher'\\|'room', id: string, academicYearId: string }` |\n| `availabilityQuerySchema` | `{ courseId: string, roomId?: string }` |\n| `freeRoomsQuerySchema` | `{ dayOfWeek: coerce 1..7, periodId: string, academicYearId: string, excludeSlotId?: string }` |\n| `meTimetableQuerySchema` | `{ studentId?: string, academicYearId?: string }` |\n\n`academicYearId` is never accepted on slot writes. It is derived from the course (FR-37).\n\n### 3.2 Time helpers: added to the existing `src/lib/dates.ts` (FR-45, ADR-2)\n\n```ts\nexport function schoolNow(now: Date, tz: string): { isoDay: number; hhmm: string }\n//  = { isoDay: Number(formatInSchoolTz(now, 'i', tz)), hhmm: formatInSchoolTz(now, 'HH:mm', tz) }\nexport function nowAndNext<P extends { startTime: string; endTime: string }>(\n  periods: P[], hhmm: string): { now: P | null; next: P | null }\n```\n\nThe functions are pure and isomorphic. Server pages, the service and the client Today view\n(FR-26) all call them. The client receives `tz` and the server's `now` ISO string as props.\nA 60 s `setInterval` advances that `now`. The browser timezone is never used.\n\n### 3.3 Clash engine: pure rules in `src/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts` (FR-9–FR-14)\n\nThis is the one extra file next to the mandated service. It holds the pure functions, so the\nNFR-11 unit tests need no DB (ADR-4). It does not import Prisma.\n\n```ts\ntype ClashRule = 'TEACHER' | 'ROOM' | 'SECTION' | 'STUDENT' | 'PERIOD_KIND' | 'NON_TEACHING_DAY';\ntype Clash = { rule: ClashRule; message: string };\n\ninterface CandidateCourse { id; code; teacherId; coTeacherIds: string[]; sectionId: string | null; subjectName }\ninterface OtherSlot { id; course: CandidateCourse & { teacherName; sectionName? }; roomId; roomName? }\ninterface CellCtx { dayLabel: string; period: { name; kind }; isTeaching: boolean }\n\nfunction clashesForCell(\n  course: CandidateCourse, roomId: string | null, cell: CellCtx,\n  others: OtherSlot[],                         // slots at the same year/day/period, excluding the moving slot\n  overlapByCourseId: Map<string, number>,      // courseId → # shared ACTIVE students\n): Clash[]\n```\n\nThe rules run in this order, and **every** one runs (FR-14 collects all clashes):\n\n| Rule | Predicate | Message (exact, from FR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| PERIOD_KIND (FR-13) | `period.kind !== 'CLASS'` | `Period '<name>' is not a class period.` |\n| NON_TEACHING_DAY (FR-13) | `!isTeaching` | `<Day> is not a teaching day.` |\n| TEACHER (FR-9) | `T = {teacherId, ...coTeacherIds}`. For each other slot, `{o.teacherId, ...o.coTeacherIds} ∩ T ≠ ∅` | `Clash: <Teacher> already teaches <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` One message per (teacher, other course). `<Teacher>` is the clashing teacher, who may be a co-teacher. |\n| ROOM (FR-10) | `roomId != null && o.roomId === roomId` | `Clash: <Room> is used by <Course> on <Day>, <Period>.` |\n| SECTION (FR-11) | `course.sectionId != null && o.course.sectionId === course.sectionId` | `Clash: <Section> already has <Subject> on <Day>, <Period>.` (Subject = the other course's subject) |\n| STUDENT (FR-12) | `overlapByCourseId.get(o.course.id) > 0` | `Clash: N students in <Course> also take <Other> at this time.` |\n\n`<Course>` is the course code. Co-teacher names are resolved by one `user.findMany({ id in teacherIds })` per call.\n\n### 3.4 Service: `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` (FR-14, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-1)\n\n`type Tx = Prisma.TransactionClient` follows the `tokens.ts` convention. Every function takes `db: Tx = prisma` where it reads.\n\n| Function | Behaviour | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `listPeriods()` / `createPeriod` / `updatePeriod` / `deletePeriod` / `reorderPeriods(ids)` | Overlap check: the new/merged `[start,end)` against every other period, using `a.start < b.end && b.start < a.end`, excluding self. Failure → `AppError('VALIDATION_ERROR', \"Overlaps '<name>' (<s>–<e>).\")`. A new period gets `order = max+1`. Delete: `count` slots, and if >0 → `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Period has N timetable slots…', { slotCount })`. Reorder: one tx. Verify the id set equals the existing set, else 400. Two-phase write: `order = -(i+1)`, then `i+1`. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `listSchoolDays()` | 7 rows + `slotCount` from `timetableSlot.groupBy({ by: ['dayOfWeek'], _count })` over all years (D3) | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `updateSchoolDays(days)` | One tx: for days switching true→false, `deleteMany({ dayOfWeek in off })`, then update the rows. Returns `{ days, deletedSlotCount }`. | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `validateSlot(input, db = prisma)` | `input = { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, excludeSlotId? }`. Loads the course, period, SchoolDay and other slots at `(yearId, day, periodId, id ≠ excludeSlotId)` with course/teacher/section/subject/room includes. Then one `enrollment.groupBy({ by: ['courseId'], where: { status: 'ACTIVE', courseId: { in: otherIds }, studentId: { in: newCourseActiveIds } } })`. Calls `clashesForCell` and returns `Clash[]`. | FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `createSlot(input, actor)` / `moveSlot(id, patch, actor)` | `withSerializableRetry(() => prisma.$transaction(async tx => { … validateSlot(…, tx); if clashes.length → throw AppError('CONFLICT', clashes[0].message + (n>1 ? ` (+${n-1} more)` : ''), { clashes }); insert/update }, { isolationLevel: Serializable }))`. Move merges the patch over the existing slot and passes `excludeSlotId = id` (FR-14). A room-only PATCH (FR-21) goes through the same path. `academicYearId = course.academicYearId`. After commit, call `audit()` (D7). | FR-14, FR-17, FR-18, FR-21, FR-37, NFR-1 |\n| `deleteSlot(id, actor)` | Delete (404 if missing), then audit | FR-18, FR-37 |\n| `withSerializableRetry(fn, attempts = 3)` | Retries on `PrismaClientKnownRequestError` code `P2034` and logs each retry with `logger.warn`. Rethrows on the last attempt. The `P2002` that the `@@unique` backstop can raise is already mapped to 409 by `withHandler`. | NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n| `getAvailability(courseId, roomId?)` | A fixed number of queries (ADR-4, NFR-3): the course; periods; school days; **all** slots in the course's year (minus the course's own slots, so the course never clashes with itself) with includes; the new course's ACTIVE student ids; ACTIVE enrollments of those students grouped by courseId. Bucket the slots by `${day}-${periodId}`. For each teaching-day × period cell, call `clashesForCell`. Return only the cells with clashes: `Record<string, string[]>`. | FR-19, FR-36, D2 |\n| `getFreeRooms({ dayOfWeek, periodId, academicYearId, excludeSlotId? })` | `room.findMany({ archivedAt: null, timetableSlots: { none: { academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId, id: { not: excludeSlotId } } } })`, ordered by name. `excludeSlotId` keeps the slot's own current room in the list. | FR-21, D1 |\n| `getTimetable(view, id, academicYearId)` | One `timetableSlot.findMany` with `include: { course: { include: { subject, teacher: {select names}, section } }, room, period }`. The where clause depends on the view: section → `course.sectionId = id`; teacher → `course: { OR: [{ teacherId: id }, { coTeacherIds: { has: id } }] }`; room → `roomId = id`. Returns `{ periods, days, slots }` so the grid renders from one response (NFR-2). | FR-15, FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `getPersonalTimetable(target, academicYearId?)` | `target = { kind: 'teacher', userId } \\| { kind: 'student', studentId }`. Teacher: as above. Student: `course.enrollments.some({ studentId, status: 'ACTIVE' })`. The year defaults to the current `AcademicYear` (`isCurrent`, existing precedent). | FR-24, FR-27, FR-38 |\n| `getScheduleForDate(target, date)` | `target = { userId, role } \\| { sectionId }`. Takes `isoDay` from `schoolNow(date, tz)`. Returns `[]` if `!SchoolDay.isTeaching`. Otherwise returns that day's slots for the target, ordered by `period.order`, mapped to `{ period, course, room }[]`. A PARENT target resolves to `[]` (the parent has no own schedule; callers pass the student). **This is the single place where PRD-14 holidays will hook in.** | FR-30, NFR-15 |\n| `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` | `getScheduleForDate(user, now).find(s => s.period.startTime <= hhmm && hhmm < s.period.endTime) ?? null` | FR-31, FR-45 |\n\n### 3.5 API route handlers (thin: `withHandler` → `requireRole`/`requireUser` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` → service → `ok()`) (NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n| Route file (`src/app/api/…/route.ts`) | Methods | Auth | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `periods` | GET / POST | GET `requireUser`; POST `requireRole('ADMIN')` | FR-33 |\n| `periods/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-6, FR-8, FR-33 |\n| `periods/reorder` | POST | ADMIN | FR-5, FR-33 |\n| `school-days` | GET / PUT | GET any user; PUT ADMIN | FR-7, FR-34 |\n| `timetable` | GET | `requireUser` + `assertCanViewTimetable` (below) | FR-35 |\n| `timetable/availability` | GET | ADMIN | FR-36 |\n| `timetable/free-rooms` | GET | ADMIN | FR-21 (D1) |\n| `timetable/slots` | POST | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `timetable/slots/[id]` | PATCH / DELETE | ADMIN | FR-37 |\n| `me/timetable` | GET | `requireUser`. TEACHER → own. STUDENT → self (a `studentId` other than self → 403). PARENT → `studentId` required when there are >1 links, defaults to the only child when there is 1, and must pass `assertCanViewStudent`, else 403. ADMIN → empty (D5). | FR-38, FR-25 |\n\n**`assertCanViewTimetable(user, view, id)`** lives in `timetable-service.ts`, next to its only caller. It is not a new access module.\nADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use `teacher` only when `id === user.id`, and `section` only per D8. Every other case (including the `room` view for non-ADMIN users, and STUDENT/PARENT users) → `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`.\n\nThe detailed request and response shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 3.6 UI: shared grid `src/components/TimetableGrid/` (FR-16, FR-23, FR-24, FR-29, NFR-4)\n\nThis follows the existing `src/components/<Name>/` convention. One component with two modes:\n\n```ts\n<TimetableGrid\n  periods days slots\n  mode=\"read\" | \"edit\"\n  highlight?: { isoDay: number; periodId: string }   // FR-24 current period\n  clashMap?: Record<string, string[]>                // FR-19, edit mode while dragging\n  onCellActivate?(day, periodId) / onSlotActivate?(slot) / onSlotDelete?(slot)   // FR-21, FR-22, FR-18\n/>\n```\n\n- Layout: CSS-grid `Box`. The columns are teaching days only and the rows are periods by `order`. BREAK/LUNCH/ASSEMBLY rows span the full width, are greyed with `action.disabledBackground`, and are not droppable (FR-16).\n- Cell: MUI `Paper`, `tabIndex=0`, with `aria-label=\"Monday, Period 2: MATH-7A, Mr Smith, Room 101\"` or `\"…: empty\"`. A filled cell shows the background from `subject.color`, text from `theme.palette.getContrastText`, the course code, the teacher surname and a room `Chip` (FR-16).\n- Edit mode only: cells call `useDroppable({ id: `${day}-${periodId}`, disabled })` and slots call `useDraggable`. The `DndContext` lives in the editor page, not in the grid, so read mode adds no dnd-kit runtime.\n- Clash tint (FR-19, NFR-4): `error.light` background + `ErrorOutline` icon + `Tooltip` with the messages joined by newlines.\n- Highlight (FR-24): `outline: 2px solid primary.main` + a \"Now\" `Chip` (text, NFR-4).\n- Print (FR-29, ADR-6): `<TimetablePrintStyles />` (MUI `GlobalStyles`): `@page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 10mm }`. Under `@media print`, everything marked `data-print=\"hide\"` (app shell, sidebar, toggles, buttons) is hidden and `.print-only` is shown. The print header is `<Typography className=\"print-only\">{entityName} — {academicYearName}</Typography>`. Cells get `break-inside: avoid; print-color-adjust: exact`. A `PrintButton` calls `window.print()`. The app-shell nav/app bar get `data-print=\"hide\"` in the existing layout component. That is a one-attribute additive change.\n\n### 3.7 Pages\n\n| Route (`src/app/(app)/…`) | Server guard | Composition | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | `PageHeader`. MUI `Table` of periods with an up/down `IconButton` reorder (no sortable, ADR-1), edit/delete. Add/edit `Dialog` with `TimeField` (the LocalizationProvider already exists; the value is converted with `format`/`parse` `'HH:mm'`). Delete → `ConfirmDialog`. A 409 → `showToast` with the slot count. A **Teaching days** section has 7 `ToggleButton`s. Switching off a day with `slotCount>0` → a `ConfirmDialog` \"Remove N slots on <Day>?\", then PUT. | FR-5, FR-6, FR-7, FR-8 |\n| `admin/timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')` | The client `TimetableEditor`. State is in URL search params `?view=section&id=&year=` (FR-15). Contents: view `ToggleButtonGroup`, entity `Autocomplete` (sections / `UserPicker` filtered to TEACHER / rooms), year `Select`. Section view: a `DndContext(PointerSensor, distance 5)` wraps a **sidebar** of non-archived section courses as draggable `Card`s with a \"placed N\" `Chip` (FR-17), plus the grid in edit mode and a `DragOverlay` `Paper`. Teacher and room views: grid in `read` mode (placement is section-driven). | FR-15–FR-23 |\n| `timetable/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('TEACHER','STUDENT','PARENT')` | The server loads `getPersonalTimetable`, `tz`, `now` and (for PARENT) the linked children. The client renders `Week` / `Today` `ToggleButtonGroup`s. The PARENT child `Select` (shown when there are >1 children) sets `?studentId=` (FR-25). Week = read grid + highlight. Today = MUI `List` of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus `Chip`s \"Now\" and \"Next\" from `nowAndNext` (FR-26). | FR-24, FR-25, FR-26, FR-45 |\n| `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` + `student-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'timetable', label: 'Timetable' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewStudent` | Read grid from `getPersonalTimetable({ kind: 'student', studentId })` | FR-27 |\n| `courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx` + `course-tabs.ts` entry `{ key: 'schedule', label: 'Schedule' }` | `requirePageUser` + `assertCanViewCourse` | MUI `Table`: day, period, start–end, room, from `timetableSlot.findMany({ courseId })` ordered by day and `period.order` | FR-28 |\n\nNavigation (FR-32), additive entries in `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Timetable` `/timetable`\n(roles TEACHER, STUDENT, PARENT); `Timetable editor` `/admin/timetable` and `Bell schedule`\n`/admin/timetable/periods` (ADMIN, `group: 'Administration'`).\n\n### 3.8 Seed: `prisma/seed.ts` (FR-41–FR-44)\n\nSeeding runs in this order. Everything upserts on a natural key, so a re-run is a no-op.\n\n1. `seedPeriods()`: upsert by `order` 1–8 with the FR-41 times. Break = order 3 (BREAK), Lunch = order 6 (LUNCH).\n2. `seedSchoolDays()`: upsert days 1–7. Days 1–5 are teaching (FR-42).\n3. `seedTimetableFixtures()` (FR-44): upsert by email: Tom (TEACHER), Sam and Sara (STUDENT, both in 7A), and Pat (PARENT, linked to both, which satisfies FR-25). A second teacher handles the courses Tom does not teach. Sections 7A/7B (homeroom Room 101/102) are upserted by `[academicYearId, name]`. Courses `MATH|ENG|SCI|HIST|PE|ART-7A/7B` (ENG→ELA, HIST→SOC) and `ROBOTICS` (ELECTIVE, sectionId null) are upserted by `[academicYearId, code]`. Enrollments are ACTIVE: 7A students in the 7A courses, Sam also in ROBOTICS. **First check for any PRD-03/05 fixture seed in the repo and reuse it.**\n4. `seedTimetableWeek()` (FR-43): a hand-written constant array with 21 class slots per section (MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2, ART 2), plus ROBOTICS on Wed (3) P6, with 7A and 7B both free then. Inserted with `upsert` on the `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` key.\n   A **unit test** (`tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts`) runs `clashesForCell` over the constant and asserts zero clashes. This also guarantees that MATH-7A and MATH-7B (both taught by Tom) never share a cell.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Place or move a slot (editor, FR-17–FR-20, NFR-1)\n\n```\ndrag start (course card or slot)\n  └─ client: clashMap = cache[`${courseId}:${roomId}`] ?? GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId&roomId   (D2)\n     grid tints clashing cells (red + icon + Tooltip)  — the moving slot's own cell is ignored\ndrop on cell (day, periodId)    | Enter on empty cell → \"Place course\" Dialog → same call (FR-22)\n  ├─ new card    → POST  /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId: section.roomId }\n  └─ existing    → PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id { dayOfWeek, periodId }\n       server: withSerializableRetry( $transaction(Serializable) {\n                 validateSlot(tx, …, excludeSlotId) → Clash[]\n                 clashes? throw AppError CONFLICT { clashes }   → rollback, nothing saved\n                 insert / update\n               }) → audit() → 201/200 { data: slot }\n  client:\n    2xx → refetch GET /api/timetable (section view), clear the clash cache\n    409 → grid untouched (pessimistic, ADR-5, so the card \"snaps back\" for free)\n          showToast({ severity: 'error', message: details.clashes.map(c => c.message).join('\\n') })   (FR-20)\ndrop outside the grid | Delete key on a focused slot → ConfirmDialog → DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id   (FR-18)\nclick slot → Popover → GET /api/timetable/free-rooms?…&excludeSlotId → Autocomplete → PATCH { roomId }   (FR-21)\n```\n\nConcurrency: two SERIALIZABLE transactions that both read the same (year, day, period) slot set\nand both insert will conflict on commit. One gets `P2034`, retries, now sees the other's row, and\nreturns 409. Exactly one success (NFR-1, NFR-12).\n\n### 4.2 Bell-schedule changes (FR-5–FR-8)\n\n`POST/PATCH /api/periods` → Zod (format, end>start) → service overlap check → write → audit.\n`DELETE` → slot count → 409 `{ slotCount }` or delete. Reorder → two-phase tx.\nTeaching days: the page shows `slotCount` from GET. Turning a day off with slots → confirm\ndialog with N → `PUT /api/school-days` → one tx (deleteMany + update) → audit\n`schoolDay.update { changed, deletedSlotCount }`.\n\n### 4.3 Personal timetable (FR-24–FR-26, FR-45)\n\n```\n/timetable (server) → requirePageRole → resolve target (teacher self | student self | parent's child)\n  → getPersonalTimetable + getSchoolSettings().timezone + new Date()\n  → client: schoolNow(now, tz) → highlight / nowAndNext ; setInterval(60s) advances now\n```\n\nClient-side refetches (child switch) use `GET /api/me/timetable?studentId=`. The same\naccess rules are enforced on the server page and on the API (NFR-7).\n\n### 4.4 Exports for later PRDs (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nPRD-07 attendance and PRD-16 dashboards import `getScheduleForDate` and `getCurrentSlot` from\n`src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`. Both compute the weekday and time in\n`SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n### 4.5 Audit actions (FR-40, D7)\n\n`timetableSlot.create|update|delete` (metadata: courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId, and from/to on a move),\n`period.create|update|delete|reorder`, and `schoolDay.update` (metadata: `{ changed, deletedSlotCount }`).\n`audit()` is always called after commit, with `request` passed so the IP is recorded.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Cross-cutting\n\n| Concern | Design | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Errors | `AppError('CONFLICT', msg, { clashes })` for clashes. `{ slotCount }` for period delete. `VALIDATION_ERROR` for overlap, archived entities and a bad reorder set. `FORBIDDEN` from the access checks. All responses use the existing `{ error: { code, message, details } }` shape. | NFR-8 |\n| Performance | One indexed `findMany` per grid view (NFR-2). Availability makes 6 queries regardless of grid size, with in-memory rules (NFR-3, ADR-4). `// ponytail: in-memory clash map; move to SQL aggregation near ~50k slots/year.` | NFR-2, NFR-3 |\n| Accessibility | Keyboard placement Dialog, Delete key, focusable cells with aria-labels, icon + tooltip on clash, text Now/Next chips | NFR-4, FR-22 |\n| UI rules | MUI / MUI X only. Every component is looked up via mui-mcp. Only `@dnd-kit/core` is added. The ESLint ban list is unchanged. | NFR-5, NFR-6, FR-23 |\n| Logging | `logger.warn` on P2034 retry. No `console.log`. | NFR-14 |\n| Scope | No solver, A/B weeks, substitutes or holidays. A single week. | NFR-15 |\n| Browser/print | Native `@media print`, checked in Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari | NFR-16, FR-29 |\n| Quality gate | `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` | NFR-10 |\n\n### Tests (ADR-7)\n\n| File | Covers | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts` | Each rule in `clashesForCell` (incl. co-teacher↔teacher, co-teacher↔co-teacher, student overlap count, null section skip, null room skip), PERIOD_KIND, NON_TEACHING_DAY, the all-clashes-returned case, and excluding a self slot | NFR-11, FR-9–FR-14 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts` | Period overlap predicate, end>start, `schoolNow` + `nowAndNext` under UTC / America/Los_Angeles / Asia/Kolkata, including a date-line case where the UTC and school weekdays differ | NFR-11, FR-6, FR-31, FR-45 |\n| `tests/unit/timetable-seed.test.ts` | The seed week constant has zero clashes, 21 slots per section, and Robotics on Wed P6 | FR-43 |\n| `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` | `Promise.allSettled` of two conflicting `createSlot` calls → exactly one fulfilled. Gated on `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. | NFR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` | Drag a course into a cell (stepwise `mouse.move`), a conflicting drop → error snackbar, the student (Sam) Today view showing Now/Next | NFR-13 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File Map (new unless marked)\n\n```\nprisma/schema.prisma                                  (edit: 3 models, 1 enum, 3 back-relations)\nprisma/migrations/20261105000000_timetable/           (new)\nprisma/seed.ts                                        (edit: periods, days, fixtures, week)\npackage.json                                          (edit: \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"6.3.1\")\nsrc/lib/validators/timetable.ts\nsrc/lib/dates.ts                                      (edit: schoolNow, nowAndNext)\nsrc/server/timetable/clash-rules.ts\nsrc/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts\nsrc/app/api/periods/route.ts, periods/[id]/route.ts, periods/reorder/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/school-days/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/route.ts, availability/route.ts, free-rooms/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/timetable/slots/route.ts, slots/[id]/route.ts\nsrc/app/api/me/timetable/route.ts\nsrc/components/TimetableGrid/ (TimetableGrid.tsx, TimetablePrintStyles.tsx, PrintButton.tsx, index.ts)\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx + TimetableEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx + BellScheduleEditor.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx + PersonalTimetable.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx\nsrc/app/(app)/courses/[id]/schedule/page.tsx\nsrc/config/navigation.ts, student-tabs.ts, course-tabs.ts   (edit: one entry each / three nav entries)\napp-shell layout component                                  (edit: data-print=\"hide\")\ntests/unit/timetable-{clash,time,seed}.test.ts\ntests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts\ntests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts\n```\n\nThe `(app)` route group was checked on disk: `src/app/(app)/admin` already exists.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 `enum PeriodKind`, `model Period` |\n| FR-2 | §2 `model SchoolDay` |\n| FR-3 | §2 `model TimetableSlot` + unique/index |\n| FR-4 | §2 migration `20261105000000_timetable` + back-relations |\n| FR-5 | §3.7 periods page; §3.4 `reorderPeriods`; D9 |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `periodSchema`; §3.4 overlap check |\n| FR-7 | §3.7 teaching-days toggles; §3.4 `listSchoolDays`/`updateSchoolDays`; D3 |\n| FR-8 | §3.4 `deletePeriod` 409 `{ slotCount }` |\n| FR-9 | §3.3 TEACHER rule |\n| FR-10 | §3.3 ROOM rule |\n| FR-11 | §3.3 SECTION rule |\n| FR-12 | §3.3 STUDENT rule; §3.4 enrollment groupBy |\n| FR-13 | §3.3 PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY |\n| FR-14 | §3.4 `validateSlot` (all clashes, `excludeSlotId`) |\n| FR-15 | §3.7 editor selectors + URL state |\n| FR-16 | §3.6 TimetableGrid layout/cell |\n| FR-17 | §3.7 section sidebar; §4.1 POST with `section.roomId` |\n| FR-18 | §4.1 move (PATCH) / delete with ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-19 | §3.6 clash tint; §3.4 `getAvailability`; D2 |\n| FR-20 | §4.1 pessimistic update + toast |\n| FR-21 | §3.4 `getFreeRooms`; §3.5 free-rooms route; D1 |\n| FR-22 | §3.6 focusable cells; §4.1 Place-course Dialog |\n| FR-23 | §3.6/§3.7 `@dnd-kit/core` + MUI Paper/Card/Chip/Tooltip |\n| FR-24 | §3.7 `/timetable`; §3.6 highlight |\n| FR-25 | §3.7 parent child Select; §3.5 me/timetable studentId |\n| FR-26 | §3.7 Week/Today; §3.2 `nowAndNext` |\n| FR-27 | §3.7 student tab page + `student-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-28 | §3.7 course Schedule tab + `course-tabs.ts` |\n| FR-29 | §3.6 print styles + PrintButton |\n| FR-30 | §3.4 `getScheduleForDate`; §4.4 |\n| FR-31 | §3.4 `getCurrentSlot`; §4.4 |\n| FR-32 | §3.7 navigation entries |\n| FR-33 | §3.5 periods routes |\n| FR-34 | §3.5 school-days route |\n| FR-35 | §3.5 timetable route + `assertCanViewTimetable`; D8 |\n| FR-36 | §3.5 availability route; §3.4 `getAvailability` |\n| FR-37 | §3.5 slots routes; §3.4 `createSlot`/`moveSlot`/`deleteSlot` |\n| FR-38 | §3.5 me/timetable; D5 |\n| FR-39 | §3.1 `src/lib/validators/timetable.ts` |\n| FR-40 | §4.5 audit actions; D7 |\n| FR-41 | §3.8 `seedPeriods` |\n| FR-42 | §3.8 `seedSchoolDays` |\n| FR-43 | §3.8 `seedTimetableWeek` + seed clash test |\n| FR-44 | §3.8 `seedTimetableFixtures` |\n| FR-45 | §3.2 `schoolNow`; §4.3 |\n| NFR-1 | §3.4 Serializable tx + `withSerializableRetry`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | §3.4 `getTimetable` single query; §5 |\n| NFR-3 | §3.4 `getAvailability` fixed queries; §5 |\n| NFR-4 | §3.6 icon/tooltip/aria; §3.7 text chips; FR-22 path |\n| NFR-5 | §1 blockers (dev gate); §5 UI rules |\n| NFR-6 | ADR-1; §6 package.json |\n| NFR-7 | §3.5 auth column; §3.7 server guards |\n| NFR-8 | §3.5 thin handlers; §5 errors |\n| NFR-9 | §3 reuse of http.ts/audit/useToast/ConfirmDialog/PageHeader/UserPicker; mandated service path |\n| NFR-10 | §5 quality gate |\n| NFR-11 | §5 unit tests |\n| NFR-12 | §5 integration test |\n| NFR-13 | §5 e2e test |\n| NFR-14 | §3.4 logger on retry |\n| NFR-15 | §1 scope; §3.4 `getScheduleForDate` holiday hook point |\n| NFR-16 | §3.6 native print; §5 |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LpbthVXZpgtbkJ3ejAMXnB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
