{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjKn5ErGNw16pjtaKLmi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-1. A script check confirmed it cites all 49 requirement ids (FR-1 to FR-34, NFR-1 to NFR-15) and no id that isn't in `requirements.json`. I didn't touch any other sub-task's files, including `api-contracts.json` and the handoff, which are still left over from an earlier run.\n\n**What the design covers:** almost all of the PRD-01 backend already exists, so this ticket is mostly UI, wiring, seed data and tests. It adds no new API endpoints, services or dependencies.\n- **New pages:** `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]` and `/account/security`. They reuse the form components already in `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`, which nothing imports yet.\n- **App shell:** the layout reads the signed-in user on the server and passes it to the shell. That lets us delete the placeholder user. The menu gains an \"Account security\" item and a working \"Sign out\".\n- **Seed and migration:** six active seed users, one invited user whose invite link is written to the log, and a new migration adding an index on user role and status.\n- **Tests:** four integration test files, one end-to-end auth test file, and one unit test for the login error messages.\n- **Overview section:** lists all six blockers from intake, as the architect rules require.\n\n**Things I found that intake didn't flag:**\n- **An existing test will break:** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` opens `/dashboard` without signing in, so it will be redirected to `/login`. The design moves the sign-in code from `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and uses it in the dashboard test.\n- **Wrong error text on invite links:** the server says \"This link is invalid or has expired.\", but FR-13 needs the invitation-specific wording. The invite page will show the FR-13 text itself, so the server code stays unchanged.\n- **Non-standard error code:** the server already returns `INVALID_TOKEN`, which isn't in the standard list of error codes. It stays as is, but `arch-api-contracts` needs to document it.\n- **Sign-out option name:** `tech-stack-decisions.md` says to call `signOut` with `callbackUrl`. In this version of next-auth the option is `redirectTo`, so the design uses that.\n\n**Decisions for you:**\n- **Invited seed user's name and role:** intake doesn't give either, and I couldn't find the PRD on disk. I used \"Ivy Invited\" as a TEACHER; change it if the PRD's seed table says otherwise.\n- **Audit log IP column (FR-32, low confidence):** it keeps its current name `ip` rather than the PRD's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing fields isn't allowed. This still needs a person to approve it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":287,"cache_read_input_tokens":67505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":287},"output_tokens":697,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcd66918-c044-496c-9910-9e27b9148ea6","uuid":"64ad0b58-aeff-4783-bfc1-c34409a6c462","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:41:12.524Z","request_id":"req_011CgjKn4zxgW7f2ZtfrF5Ba"}
