{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KNkUnbC4ahkE4FZwXmVTfk","type":"tool_result","content":"total 144\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  5 21:28 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  12797 Nov  5 11:42 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1690 Nov  5 11:42 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  11982 Nov  5 21:28 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  23333 Nov  5 11:41 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  10155 Nov  5 21:27 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    374 Nov  5 11:42 threat-model-notes.json\n# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\nVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n\nThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\ncover only the remaining gaps.\n\n**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n\n- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\npiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\nor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\nthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\nneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\nfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\non success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\nFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\ntokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are\nadded. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.\n\n## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,\nand Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.\nNFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:\n  - seed admin signs in and signs out\n  - wrong-password message\n  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`\n  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)\n  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`\n\n  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the\nPlaywright process.\n\n## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept\n\n**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already\nmigrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.\n\n**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they\nare. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z) for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 5 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces an earlier SH-1 notes file. That version listed `/login`, the seed users and the role/status\n> migration as new work. All three are now **present** on disk.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI-gap + tests** ticket. The backend, every API route, `/login`, the seed and the\nmigration already exist. The design adds **4 pages**, rewires the **shell**, and adds **tests**.\n**No new endpoint, service, model or migration is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` documents the 5 existing routes as they are.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**, **UI: Auth Pages**,\n**UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**, **Seed**, **Accessibility**,\n**UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred Card shell. | New auth pages render only the card body. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Today only `LoginForm` imports any of them. | Invite and reset pages **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` reuses `PasswordChecklist`, `passwordInputSlot`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors`. Do not add a second fetch or checklist helper. |\n| B3 | `SetPasswordForm` **requires `email`**, because the policy rejects a password equal to the email. | `/reset-password/[token]` must also call `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` server-side, to get the email and to show the invalid-link state before the form renders. |\n| B4 | `tokens.ts` `verifyToken(raw, type)` is read-only. `consumeToken` throws `INVALID_TOKEN` on a double submit. | The token pages are **server components** that call `verifyToken`. They show user data or the invalid-link `Alert`. No new endpoint. |\n| B5 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` maps to **410**, a code outside the NFR-10 list. The service copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | Keep this (NFR-13). The UI handles 410 `INVALID_TOKEN` by switching to the page's invalid-link copy. `arch-api-contracts` should document the 410. |\n| B6 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** create a session. | FR-14 flow on the client: POST `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. |\n| B7 | `/login` already exists. `LoginForm({ callbackUrl, reset })` fires a `useToast` once when `reset` is set, and exports `loginErrorMessage` (unit-tested). | FR-19 redirects to `/login?reset=1`. **Do not touch `/login`.** FR-2, FR-4, FR-6 and FR-7 only need verification. Intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date: `loginErrorMessage` covers `rate_limited`. Dev should verify this. |\n| B8 | `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`. The `jwt` callback keeps the current session alive on `reauth`. | FR-20 \"re-issue the current session\" is done server-side. The page only POSTs, then shows a toast and resets the form. |\n| B9 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders `<AppShell schoolShortName>` and does no auth. `providers.tsx` has no `SessionProvider`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user: SessionUser` (`id`, `role`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`) to `AppShell`. **Prop, not `useSession`**, so no provider is needed. This is the one source of the current user (FR-25). |\n| B10 | `shell.tsx` uses `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167). Its menu has 2 `MenuItem`s that only close the menu, and there is no `signOut`. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26 and FR-27 are all in this one file plus the layout. Sign out is `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | Middleware needs no change (FR-11, NFR-14). |\n| B12 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. `requestPasswordReset` throws `RATE_LIMITED`. | `/forgot-password` shows `data.message` from the API rather than retyping the string, and shows an error `Alert` on 429. |\n| B13 | `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` exists. | `requirePageRole` → `/forbidden` is already wired (FR-23). |\n| B14 | Existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) call `page.goto('/dashboard')` with no sign-in. The middleware already requires a session. | **Regression risk (NFR-13).** These specs are probably already failing, or will once the layout calls `requirePageUser`. Add one shared e2e sign-in helper using the seed users and reuse it in the existing specs. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Present. No change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | `/login` is present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`. Verify via the integration test. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`loginErrorMessage`). Verify only. |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`). Covered by the authorize integration test. |\n| FR-6 | Auth Core / UI | Limiter and message are both present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`safeCallbackUrl` in `LoginForm`). Verify only. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Emitted by `authorize`. The integration test asserts the AuditLog rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present. No change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`, `reauth`). The change-password integration test covers `passwordChangedAt`. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present (B11). No change. |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. Pages call `verifyToken` only and never hash anything (B4). |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: read-only name and email + `SetPasswordForm`. Invalid, used or expired: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client flow from B6. A 410 response switches to the invalid-link copy. Service and audit are present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is enforced server-side and comes back through `fieldErrors.password` → `applyFieldErrors`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` (inside `SetPasswordForm`) on the invite, reset and security pages (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + a client form (RHF + the shared forgot-password schema, `postJson`). Always shows the success `Alert`. Handles 429. API and limiter are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` → `sendAuthEmail`). Integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server, `verifyToken` for the email, B3) + `SetPasswordForm` → POST `/api/auth/reset-password` → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')` (B7 toast). |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | **New** `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form with current, new and confirm fields, the shared change-password schema, `PasswordChecklist` and `passwordInputSlot`. On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show \"Current password is incorrect.\" On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form (B8). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` item labelled \"Account security\" (B10). |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present. Verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present (B13). New pages use `requirePageUser`. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. The layout passes `user` to `AppShell` (B9). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name is `firstName lastName`, with a role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), and Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-30 | Seed | Present (`createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))`). No change. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `src/server/auth/email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip` (intake default). No rename. |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Present (`20261106000000_user_role_status_index`). No change. |\n| FR-34 | Tests | **New** integration files `tests/integration/auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`), run against the test DB. **New** `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: sign-in/out, the failed-login message, and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus the shared e2e sign-in helper (B14). The unit tests already exist. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` handles CSRF. The JSON routes are same-origin with SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt, so this is met. Nothing to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every new form has an error `Alert` in an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, and RHF `shouldFocusError` is on. `SetPasswordForm` and `applyFieldErrors` already do this. The security form must match. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate for dev:** call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev is blocked. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. The existing banned-import lint test guards this. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | The new UI code adds no audit calls. Existing metadata is safe. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`, and the `(app)` layout now does too. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers conform, apart from the B5 `INVALID_TOKEN` 410. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`. Add no new schemas unless one is missing. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger`. The existing seed `console.log` (line 148) is out of scope. |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | Leave `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `middleware.ts`, `/login`, the seed and the schema alone. Watch B14. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI and English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## Change footprint\n\n**New (6 source files + tests):** `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (+ a client form), `(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (+ a client form), 4 integration tests,\n`tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` and the e2e sign-in helper.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (`requirePageUser`, then the `user` prop), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (drop the placeholder, real\nuser, sign out, Account security item), and the existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) to use the sign-in helper.\n\n**Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n`src/lib/validators/auth.ts` (unless a form schema is genuinely missing).\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip` (LOW confidence, default applied).\n2. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`. `sendAuthEmail` is unchanged.\n3. The ticket id is SH-1.\n4. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a hard gate for the dev phase.\n5. New: intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" looks out of date (B7). Verify, don't build.\n6. New: existing e2e specs may already be failing without auth (B14).\n# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"reason\": \"Approved by user\",\n  \"reviewer\": \"ikramaansari\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T06:45:44.672Z\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b447f845-727b-4a62-ae8d-232a33ab6037","uuid":"c5481a7d-f748-44bf-9fe6-826418eda299","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:28:47.054Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 144\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  5 21:28 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  12797 Nov  5 11:42 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1690 Nov  5 11:42 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  11982 Nov  5 21:28 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  23333 Nov  5 11:41 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  10155 Nov  5 21:27 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    374 Nov  5 11:42 threat-model-notes.json\n# Tech Stack Decisions — PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json`\nconfirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL,\nnext-auth 5.0.0-beta.25 (Credentials, JWT), bcrypt ^6, zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0 with\n@hookform/resolvers 3.9.0, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs and the X packages) with emotion,\nVitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 and @axe-core/playwright 4.10.0. The stack fits every FR and NFR.\n**This ticket adds no dependency** (NFR-7, NFR-13).\n\nThis file replaces the earlier SH-1 stack ADR. The workspace has moved on since then, and the ADRs now\ncover only the remaining gaps.\n\n**Workspace facts checked on 2026-11-05 (re-run):**\n\n- DONE, do not rebuild: `/login` (`src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` + `LoginForm.tsx`, using client `signIn` from `next-auth/react`, an exported `loginErrorMessage`, and a `reset=1` → `useToast` hook); seed users (FR-28/29); migration `20261106000000_user_role_status_index` (FR-33); `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`.\n- **Reusable and not yet used by any page:** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/index.ts` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, checklist, `setPasswordSchema`), `postJson(url, body)` → `{data}|{error: ApiFailure}`, `applyFieldErrors` and `passwordInputSlot`.\n- `requireRole.ts` exports `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser` and `requirePageRole`, and `SessionUser`.\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` is an async Server Component that only reads `schoolSettings`. It does not pass a user to `AppShell`. `shell.tsx` still has `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167).\n- `next-auth/react` is imported only in `LoginForm.tsx`. There is no `SessionProvider` anywhere.\n- Existing API routes: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`. `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does not sign the user in.\n- Missing pages: `src/app/(auth)/{forgot-password,reset-password/[token],invite/[token]}` and `src/app/(app)/account/security`.\n- Tests: `tests/integration/` has only `email-dispatch` and `timetable-concurrency` (the `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated precedent). `tests/e2e/` has no auth spec.\n- `mui-mcp` is connected in this environment, so the NFR-6 blocker is clear right now. Dev must still call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` before writing UI.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the declared stack unchanged and add no dependency\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 rules out scope expansion and rebuilds. NFR-7 bans extra UI libraries. Every backend\npiece the remaining gaps need already exists (FR-1, FR-3, FR-5, FR-9–FR-12, FR-15, FR-18, FR-22–FR-24).\n\n**Decision.** Keep `package.json` and the lockfile unchanged. Do not add a password-strength, toast, form-wizard\nor session library. The strength checklist is the existing `PasswordChecklist` (FR-16). Toasts use\n`useToast()` (NFR-6).\n\n**Consequences.** All new code is pages, shell wiring and tests.\n\n## ADR-2: The shell gets the user from the server session through a prop; there is no `SessionProvider`\n\n**Context.** FR-25 requires deleting `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and keeping one source of \"current user\". FR-26 needs\nthe name, role badge, initials and Sign out. FR-27 needs `navigationForRole` to use the session role. FR-21\nneeds an \"Account security\" menu item. NFR-9 requires server enforcement.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` calls `requirePageUser()` (FR-23), a second guard behind the middleware (FR-11). It passes `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, email, role }}` to `AppShell`.\n- `AppShell` takes `user: SessionUser`, calls `navigationForRole(user.role)`, and renders `UserAvatar` with the initials, the full name and a role `Chip`. The user menu gets `MenuItem`s for \"Account security\" (`href=\"/account/security\"`) and \"Sign out\", which calls `signOut({ callbackUrl: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`.\n- Do **not** add `SessionProvider` or `useSession`. That would be a second user source with its own polling and would go against FR-25.\n\n**Consequences.** One JWT decode per navigation on the server, which is negligible. Name and role freshness\nfollows the existing 5-minute recheck (FR-10). Shell tests pass a `user` prop instead of mocking a session.\n\n## ADR-3: Token pages verify on the server, then reuse `SetPasswordForm` and `postJson` against the existing APIs\n\n**Context.** FR-13 and FR-14 cover `/invite/[token]`: the invalid-link message, or the name and email read-only;\non success the user is signed in and sent to `/dashboard`. FR-19 covers `/reset-password/[token]` → `/login?reset=1`.\nFR-17 covers `/forgot-password` with a constant message. FR-20 covers `/account/security`. FR-12 and NFR-1 say\ntokens are only touched through `tokens.ts`. NFR-10 requires thin handlers. NFR-11 requires a shared Zod schema.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `invite/[token]/page.tsx` and `reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` are Server Components. They call `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE' | 'PASSWORD_RESET')` from `tokens.ts`. This read does not consume the token. If it returns null, they render the invalid-link `Alert`. Otherwise they render a thin client wrapper around the existing `SetPasswordForm` (name + email for invites, email only for resets). The raw token goes only into a prop. It is never logged or audited (NFR-8).\n- The wrapper's `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite' | '/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })` and maps failures with `applyFieldErrors`.\n  - Invite success: `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')` (FR-14). The service has already consumed the token, so a reused link shows the invalid message.\n  - Reset success: `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. The existing `LoginForm` toast handles the rest (FR-19).\n- `/forgot-password` is a client RHF form using `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField`. After **any** response (2xx or 429), it shows the same success `Alert`, so there is no enumeration (FR-17). The 3-per-email and 10-per-IP limits are already enforced on the server.\n- `/account/security` is a server page that calls `requirePageUser()` and renders a client form with RHF, `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(user.email))`, three password fields with `passwordInputSlot`, and `PasswordChecklist`. It sends `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A `VALIDATION_ERROR` on `currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors` → \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows `useToast` \"Password updated\" and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })` (FR-20, FR-10).\n- Accessibility: one `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"` per form, RHF `shouldFocusError` (the default), and field `helperText` (NFR-5). No extra code is needed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new API routes, services or form components. Only four pages and small client wrappers are\nadded. Verifying on the server before render means an expired link never shows a form.\n\n## ADR-4: Tests use the existing Vitest and Playwright setup; e2e reads reset links from EmailOutbox\n\n**Context.** FR-34 requires integration tests for authorize, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password,\nand Playwright tests for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset. NFR-5 covers accessibility.\nNFR-13 requires lint, typecheck and test to stay green.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`: `// @vitest-environment node` plus `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. It calls `authorize` and the services in `services/auth.ts` directly. It covers invalid, disabled, `locked:N`, lockout at 5, `rate_limited`, a success that resets the count, each service's happy path, token reuse → invalid, and a wrong current password. Reset the rate limiter in `beforeEach`.\n- `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`, run with `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })`:\n  - seed admin signs in and signs out\n  - wrong-password message\n  - unauthenticated `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=`\n  - forgot → reset for `student2@`, reading the newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only route in the app)\n  - one `AxeBuilder` scan on `/login`\n\n  Use `student2@` so parallel specs that sign in as admin are not disturbed.\n\n**Consequences.** No new tooling. The e2e tests depend on the seed and on `DATABASE_URL` being visible to the\nPlaywright process.\n\n## ADR-5: Data layer stays as-is; `AuditLog.ip` is kept\n\n**Context.** FR-32 (LOW confidence) is about the PRD's `ipAddress` vs the existing `ip`. FR-33's index is already\nmigrated. NFR-13 forbids renames.\n\n**Decision.** No schema change and no migration in this run. `AuditLog.ip` and its existing indexes stay as they\nare. FR-32 remains flagged for human sign-off.\n\n**Consequences.** Prisma does not change. If the human decides to rename, that is a separate, explicit migration.\n\n---\n\n## Downstream notes for `arch-design-system`\n\n- Surface the intake blockers in the Overview: brownfield \"design only the gaps\"; FR-32 (`ip`, LOW); FR-30/FR-31 (the seed logs the link and `sendAuthEmail` stays as it is); NFR-6 (the mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI work).\n- Remaining build scope: 4 pages (`/forgot-password`, `/reset-password/[token]`, `/invite/[token]`, `/account/security`), the shell and layout wiring (FR-21, FR-25–FR-27), `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- No new API endpoints. `api-contracts` should list the existing routes the new pages consume: `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `/api/auth/forgot-password`, `/api/auth/reset-password`, `/api/auth/accept-invite` and `/api/account/password`.\n- Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-1\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z) for PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001).\nIt has 34 FRs and 15 NFRs (49 requirements) at 97% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 5 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces an earlier SH-1 notes file. That version listed `/login`, the seed users and the role/status\n> migration as new work. All three are now **present** on disk.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **UI-gap + tests** ticket. The backend, every API route, `/login`, the seed and the\nmigration already exist. The design adds **4 pages**, rewires the **shell**, and adds **tests**.\n**No new endpoint, service, model or migration is needed.** `arch-api-contracts` documents the 5 existing routes as they are.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Auth Core**, **Service**, **API (existing)**, **UI: Auth Pages**,\n**UI: Account**, **UI: Shell**, **Access Control**, **Security**, **Audit**, **Seed**, **Accessibility**,\n**UI Rules**, **Conventions**, **Tests**, **Scope**.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Design implication |\n|---|------|--------------------|\n| B1 | `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` already renders the centred Card shell. | New auth pages render only the card body. |\n| B2 | `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` exports `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({ name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit })`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure`. Today only `LoginForm` imports any of them. | Invite and reset pages **reuse `SetPasswordForm`**. `/account/security` reuses `PasswordChecklist`, `passwordInputSlot`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors`. Do not add a second fetch or checklist helper. |\n| B3 | `SetPasswordForm` **requires `email`**, because the policy rejects a password equal to the email. | `/reset-password/[token]` must also call `verifyToken(token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` server-side, to get the email and to show the invalid-link state before the form renders. |\n| B4 | `tokens.ts` `verifyToken(raw, type)` is read-only. `consumeToken` throws `INVALID_TOKEN` on a double submit. | The token pages are **server components** that call `verifyToken`. They show user data or the invalid-link `Alert`. No new endpoint. |\n| B5 | `AppError('INVALID_TOKEN')` maps to **410**, a code outside the NFR-10 list. The service copy is \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" | Keep this (NFR-13). The UI handles 410 `INVALID_TOKEN` by switching to the page's invalid-link copy. `arch-api-contracts` should document the 410. |\n| B6 | `acceptInvite()` returns `{ email }` and does **not** create a session. | FR-14 flow on the client: POST `/api/auth/accept-invite`, then `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. |\n| B7 | `/login` already exists. `LoginForm({ callbackUrl, reset })` fires a `useToast` once when `reset` is set, and exports `loginErrorMessage` (unit-tested). | FR-19 redirects to `/login?reset=1`. **Do not touch `/login`.** FR-2, FR-4, FR-6 and FR-7 only need verification. Intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date: `loginErrorMessage` covers `rate_limited`. Dev should verify this. |\n| B8 | `POST /api/account/password` already calls `unstable_update({ reauth: true })`. The `jwt` callback keeps the current session alive on `reauth`. | FR-20 \"re-issue the current session\" is done server-side. The page only POSTs, then shows a toast and resets the form. |\n| B9 | `(app)/layout.tsx` is a server component that renders `<AppShell schoolShortName>` and does no auth. `providers.tsx` has no `SessionProvider`. | The layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `user: SessionUser` (`id`, `role`, `firstName`, `lastName`, `email`) to `AppShell`. **Prop, not `useSession`**, so no provider is needed. This is the one source of the current user (FR-25). |\n| B10 | `shell.tsx` uses `PLACEHOLDER_USER` (lines 40, 78, 162–167). Its menu has 2 `MenuItem`s that only close the menu, and there is no `signOut`. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26 and FR-27 are all in this one file plus the layout. Sign out is `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`. |\n| B11 | `public-routes.ts` already lists `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/` and `/reset-password/`, and has no sign-up route. | Middleware needs no change (FR-11, NFR-14). |\n| B12 | `services/auth.ts` exports `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`. `requestPasswordReset` throws `RATE_LIMITED`. | `/forgot-password` shows `data.message` from the API rather than retyping the string, and shows an error `Alert` on 429. |\n| B13 | `src/app/forbidden/page.tsx` exists. | `requirePageRole` → `/forbidden` is already wired (FR-23). |\n| B14 | Existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) call `page.goto('/dashboard')` with no sign-in. The middleware already requires a session. | **Regression risk (NFR-13).** These specs are probably already failing, or will once the layout calls `requirePageUser`. Add one shared e2e sign-in helper using the seed users and reuse it in the existing specs. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | Present. No change. |\n| FR-2 | UI: Auth Pages | `/login` is present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-3 | Auth Core | Present in `credentials.ts`. Verify via the integration test. |\n| FR-4 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`loginErrorMessage`). Verify only. |\n| FR-5 | Auth Core | Present (`computeLockout`). Covered by the authorize integration test. |\n| FR-6 | Auth Core / UI | Limiter and message are both present (B7). Verify only. |\n| FR-7 | UI: Auth Pages | Present (`safeCallbackUrl` in `LoginForm`). Verify only. |\n| FR-8 | Audit | Emitted by `authorize`. The integration test asserts the AuditLog rows. |\n| FR-9 | Auth Core | Present. No change. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Core | Present (`RECHECK_MS`, `reauth`). The change-password integration test covers `passwordChangedAt`. |\n| FR-11 | Access Control | Present (B11). No change. |\n| FR-12 | Auth Core | Present. Pages call `verifyToken` only and never hash anything (B4). |\n| FR-13 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). Valid token: read-only name and email + `SetPasswordForm`. Invalid, used or expired: an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy. |\n| FR-14 | UI: Auth Pages | Client flow from B6. A 410 response switches to the invalid-link copy. Service and audit are present. |\n| FR-15 | Validation | Present. The common-password rule is enforced server-side and comes back through `fieldErrors.password` → `applyFieldErrors`. |\n| FR-16 | UI: Auth / Account | Reuse `PasswordChecklist` (inside `SetPasswordForm`) on the invite, reset and security pages (B2). |\n| FR-17 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + a client form (RHF + the shared forgot-password schema, `postJson`). Always shows the success `Alert`. Handles 429. API and limiter are present. |\n| FR-18 | Service | Present (`requestPasswordReset` → `sendAuthEmail`). Integration test only. |\n| FR-19 | UI: Auth Pages | **New** `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server, `verifyToken` for the email, B3) + `SetPasswordForm` → POST `/api/auth/reset-password` → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')` (B7 toast). |\n| FR-20 | UI: Account | **New** `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (`requirePageUser`) + a client form with current, new and confirm fields, the shared change-password schema, `PasswordChecklist` and `passwordInputSlot`. On 400 `fieldErrors.currentPassword`, show \"Current password is incorrect.\" On success, show the \"Password updated\" toast and reset the form (B8). |\n| FR-21 | UI: Shell | Add a `MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"` item labelled \"Account security\" (B10). |\n| FR-22 | Service | Present. Verify only. |\n| FR-23 | Access Control | Present (B13). New pages use `requirePageUser`. |\n| FR-24 | Audit | Present. |\n| FR-25 | UI: Shell | Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. The layout passes `user` to `AppShell` (B9). |\n| FR-26 | UI: Shell | Name is `firstName lastName`, with a role `Chip`, `UserAvatar` (initials), and Sign out → `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`. |\n| FR-27 | UI: Shell | `navigationForRole(user.role)`. |\n| FR-28 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-29 | Seed | Present. No change. |\n| FR-30 | Seed | Present (`createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))`). No change. |\n| FR-31 | Scope | Do not touch `src/server/auth/email.ts`. |\n| FR-32 | Data Model | Keep `AuditLog.ip` (intake default). No rename. |\n| FR-33 | Migration | Present (`20261106000000_user_role_status_index`). No change. |\n| FR-34 | Tests | **New** integration files `tests/integration/auth-authorize`, `auth-accept-invite`, `auth-reset-password` and `auth-change-password` (`.test.ts`), run against the test DB. **New** `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`: sign-in/out, the failed-login message, and forgot → reset, reading the link from `EmailOutbox`. Plus the shared e2e sign-in helper (B14). The unit tests already exist. |\n| NFR-1 | Security | Present in `tokens.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | Security | Auth.js defaults. `signIn` from `next-auth/react` handles CSRF. The JSON routes are same-origin with SameSite=Lax. |\n| NFR-3 | Security | Present (`DUMMY_HASH`). |\n| NFR-4 | Performance | One bcrypt-12 compare per attempt, so this is met. Nothing to design. |\n| NFR-5 | Accessibility | Every new form has an error `Alert` in an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region, and RHF `shouldFocusError` is on. `SetPasswordForm` and `applyFieldErrors` already do this. The security form must match. |\n| NFR-6 | UI Rules | **Hard gate for dev:** call mui-mcp `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before writing JSX. If it is unreachable, dev is blocked. |\n| NFR-7 | UI Rules | MUI only. The existing banned-import lint test guards this. |\n| NFR-8 | Audit | The new UI code adds no audit calls. Existing metadata is safe. |\n| NFR-9 | Access Control | `/account/security` uses `requirePageUser()`, and the `(app)` layout now does too. The API already calls `requireUser()`. |\n| NFR-10 | Conventions | Existing handlers conform, apart from the B5 `INVALID_TOKEN` 410. |\n| NFR-11 | Conventions | RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas in `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`. Add no new schemas unless one is missing. |\n| NFR-12 | Conventions | New code uses `logger`. The existing seed `console.log` (line 148) is out of scope. |\n| NFR-13 | Scope | Leave `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `middleware.ts`, `/login`, the seed and the schema alone. Watch B14. |\n| NFR-14 | Scope | No sign-up page. |\n| NFR-15 | UI Rules | Stock MUI and English copy. Nothing to design. |\n\n## Change footprint\n\n**New (6 source files + tests):** `(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (+ a client form), `(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (+ a client form), 4 integration tests,\n`tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` and the e2e sign-in helper.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (`requirePageUser`, then the `user` prop), `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (drop the placeholder, real\nuser, sign out, Account security item), and the existing e2e specs (`dashboard`, `notifications`) to use the sign-in helper.\n\n**Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n`src/lib/validators/auth.ts` (unless a form schema is genuinely missing).\n\n## Open items carried from intake\n\n1. FR-32: keep `ip` (LOW confidence, default applied).\n2. FR-30/31: the seed logs the invite link through `logger`. `sendAuthEmail` is unchanged.\n3. The ticket id is SH-1.\n4. NFR-6: mui-mcp availability is a hard gate for the dev phase.\n5. New: intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" looks out of date (B7). Verify, don't build.\n6. New: existing e2e specs may already be failing without auth (B14).\n# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"phase\": \"architect\",\n  \"approved\": true,\n  \"reason\": \"Approved by user\",\n  \"reviewer\": \"ikramaansari\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T06:45:44.672Z\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KNkUnbC4ahkE4FZwXmVTfk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
