{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk6ccWFj91C9LARetqgn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013iBEoK2jfTpB3Qbe8wM2Em","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),\n`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and\n`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status\n> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5\nCredentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`\n(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate\nlimiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.\n\n**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the\n`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**\n(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |\n| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |\n\n### Additional risks found during design\n\n- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the\n  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`\n  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.\n- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept\n  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.\n- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).\n  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |\n| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |\n\nDo not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 New and modified components\n\n| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |\n| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |\n\n**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,\n`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and\n`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).\nCopy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n```\n/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox\nlink ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state\n```\n\n**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**\n```\n/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\nC4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n```\n\n**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n```\n/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword\n   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min\n   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error\n```\n\n**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**\n```\nrequest ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),\n           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions\n\n1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server\n   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).\n   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).\n2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context\n   (FR-25, ADR-2).\n3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).\n   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.\n4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`\n   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The\n   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).\n6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |\n| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |\n| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |\n| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |\n| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |\n| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n| FR-13 | C3 |\n| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-17 | C1 |\n| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |\n| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n| FR-20 | C5; C8 |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |\n| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |\n| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |\n| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |\n| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |\n| FR-34 | C8, C9 |\n| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |\n| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |\n| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |\n| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |\n| NFR-12 | §4.6 |\n| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |\n| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Change Footprint\n\n- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,\n  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.\n- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1027,"cache_read_input_tokens":52795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1027},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b447f845-727b-4a62-ae8d-232a33ab6037","uuid":"28098086-0805-4534-b704-99424b21874e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:30:11.396Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk6cc5x9tfg8RPYMdMEj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013iBEoK2jfTpB3Qbe8wM2Em":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),\n`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and\n`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status\n> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5\nCredentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`\n(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate\nlimiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.\n\n**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the\n`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**\n(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |\n| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |\n\n### Additional risks found during design\n\n- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the\n  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`\n  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.\n- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept\n  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.\n- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).\n  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |\n| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |\n\nDo not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 New and modified components\n\n| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |\n| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |\n\n**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,\n`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and\n`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).\nCopy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n```\n/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox\nlink ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state\n```\n\n**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**\n```\n/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\nC4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n```\n\n**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n```\n/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword\n   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min\n   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error\n```\n\n**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**\n```\nrequest ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),\n           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions\n\n1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server\n   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).\n   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).\n2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context\n   (FR-25, ADR-2).\n3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).\n   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.\n4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`\n   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The\n   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).\n6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |\n| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |\n| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |\n| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |\n| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |\n| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n| FR-13 | C3 |\n| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-17 | C1 |\n| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |\n| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n| FR-20 | C5; C8 |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |\n| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |\n| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |\n| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |\n| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |\n| FR-34 | C8, C9 |\n| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |\n| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |\n| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |\n| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |\n| NFR-12 | §4.6 |\n| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |\n| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Change Footprint\n\n- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,\n  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.\n- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013iBEoK2jfTpB3Qbe8wM2Em","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b447f845-727b-4a62-ae8d-232a33ab6037","uuid":"f60851ce-a89c-40d4-9d58-9af35b712e3c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:30:11.657Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),\n`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and\n`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status\n> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5\nCredentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`\n(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate\nlimiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.\n\n**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the\n`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**\n(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |\n| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |\n\n### Additional risks found during design\n\n- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the\n  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`\n  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.\n- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept\n  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.\n- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).\n  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |\n| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |\n\nDo not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 New and modified components\n\n| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |\n| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |\n\n**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,\n`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and\n`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).\nCopy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n```\n/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox\nlink ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state\n```\n\n**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**\n```\n/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\nC4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n```\n\n**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n```\n/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword\n   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min\n   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error\n```\n\n**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**\n```\nrequest ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),\n           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions\n\n1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server\n   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).\n   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).\n2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context\n   (FR-25, ADR-2).\n3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).\n   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.\n4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`\n   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The\n   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).\n6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |\n| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |\n| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |\n| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |\n| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |\n| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n| FR-13 | C3 |\n| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-17 | C1 |\n| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |\n| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n| FR-20 | C5; C8 |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |\n| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |\n| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |\n| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |\n| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |\n| FR-34 | C8, C9 |\n| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |\n| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |\n| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |\n| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |\n| NFR-12 | §4.6 |\n| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |\n| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Change Footprint\n\n- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,\n  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.\n- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":341,"newStart":1,"newLines":197,"lines":[" # System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)"," ","-Ticket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,","-`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).","-Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Ticket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),","+`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and","+`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","+> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status","+> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.","+"," ---"," "," ## 1. Overview"," ","-SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,","-Auth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,","-credentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate","-limiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +","-tests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new","-API endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).","+SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5","+Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`","+(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate","+limiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index."," ","-### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)","+**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the","+`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**","+(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13)."," ","-| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |","+### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)","+","+| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |"," |---|---|---|","-| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |","-| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |","-| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |","-| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |","-| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |","-| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |","+| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |","+| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |","+| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |","+| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |","+| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |"," ","-Additional risks found during design (not in intake):","+### Additional risks found during design"," ","-- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.","-  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.","-  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and","-  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).","-- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,","-  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string","-  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.","-- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour","-  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.","-- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not","-  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`.","+- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the","+  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`","+  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.","+- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept","+  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.","+- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).","+  Dev verifies this and builds nothing."," "," ---"," ","-## 2. Architecture at a glance","+## 2. Component Breakdown"," ","-```","-Browser","- ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages","- │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]","- │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)","- │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes","- ├─ (app) route group — protected","- │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED","- │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page","- ▼","-middleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401","- ▼","-API routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)","- /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password","- /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password","- ▼","-Server modules (existing, untouched)","- auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts","- services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts","- ▼","-Prisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)","-```","+### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)"," ","-**Patterns**","-","-- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components","-  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when","-  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).","-- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes","-  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).","-- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from","-  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).","-- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,","-  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages","-  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.","-","----","-","-## 3. Component Breakdown","-","-### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)","-","-| Module | Provides | Req |","+| Module | Provides | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|","-| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |","-| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |","-| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |","-| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |","-| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |","-| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |","-| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |","-| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |","-| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |","-| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |","-| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |","-| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |","-| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |","-| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |","-| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |","-| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |","-| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |","+| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |","+| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |","+| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |","+| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |","+| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |","+| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |","+| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |","+| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |","+| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |"," ","-### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)","+Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13)."," ","-Every page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).","-Every form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default","-`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid","-field (NFR-5).","+### 2.2 New and modified components"," ","-**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14","-- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.","-- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with","-  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No","-  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).","-- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`","-  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).","-- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:","+| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |","+| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |","+| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |","+| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |","+| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |","+| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |","+| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |","+| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |","+| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |"," ","-  | `code` | Message |","-  |---|---|","-  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |","-  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |","-  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |","-  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |","+**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,","+`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and","+`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).","+Copy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15)."," ","-- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server","-  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.","-- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19).","+---"," ","-**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11","-- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.","-- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.","-  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field","-  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`.","+## 3. Data Flow"," ","-**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8","-- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to","-  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by","-  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).","-- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.","-  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.","-- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata.","+**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**","+```","+/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)","+       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox","+link ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)","+C4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)","+       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state","+```"," ","-**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1","-- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.","-  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).","-- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.","-- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,","-  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.","-  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it.","+**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**","+```","+/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)","+C4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}","+C4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')","+```"," ","-### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)","+**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**","+```","+/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword","+   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min","+   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error","+```"," ","-**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11","-- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.","-- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using","-  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".","-- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →","-  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and","-  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server","-  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10).","+**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**","+```","+request ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),","+           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})","+```"," ","-### 3.4 Modified — app shell","-","-**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9","-- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass","-  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup.","-","-**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27","-- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.","-- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);","-  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.","-- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}","-  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from","-  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).","-- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check).","-","-### 3.5 Data and seed","-","-**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12","-- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).","-- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },","-  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:","-","-  | Email | Name | Role |","-  |---|---|---|","-  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |","-  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |","-  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |","-  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |","-  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |","-  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |","-","-- `invited@schoolhub.test` (intake FR-29 gives no name or role. **Architect default:** Ivy Invited, TEACHER. Dev may change it if the PRD seed table says otherwise):","-  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,","-  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and","-  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).","-- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope).","-","-**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32","-- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.","-- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with","-  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged.","-","-### 3.6 Tests","-","-**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13","-","-| File | Kind | Covers |","-|---|---|---|","-| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |","-| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |","-| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |","-| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |","-| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |","-| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |","-| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |","-| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |","-","-Integration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores","-`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected.","-"," ---"," ","-## 4. Data Flow","+## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions"," ","-**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**","-1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.","-2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches","-   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →","-   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).","-3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).","-4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`","-   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`.","+1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server","+   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).","+   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).","+2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context","+   (FR-25, ADR-2).","+3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).","+   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.","+4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`","+   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.","+5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The","+   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).","+6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12)."," ","-**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**","-1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.","-2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).","-3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).","-4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert.","-","-**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**","-1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →","-   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI","-   shows the same message either way.","-2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`","-   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.","-3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10).","-","-**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**","-`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`","-→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min.","-","-**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**","-`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.","-\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`.","-"," ---"," "," ## 5. Requirements Traceability"," ","-| Req | Design element(s) |","+| Req | Design element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |","-| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |","-| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |","-| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |","-| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |","-| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |","-| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |","-| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |","-| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |","-| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |","-| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |","-| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |","-| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |","-| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |","-| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |","-| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |","-| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |","-| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |","-| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |","-| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |","-| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |","-| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |","-| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |","-| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |","-| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |","-| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |","+| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |","+| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |","+| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |","+| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |","+| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |","+| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |","+| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |","+| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |","+| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |","+| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |","+| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |","+| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |","+| FR-13 | C3 |","+| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |","+| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |","+| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |","+| FR-17 | C1 |","+| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |","+| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |","+| FR-20 | C5; C8 |","+| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |","+| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |","+| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |","+| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |","+| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |","+| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |"," | FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |","-| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |","-| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |","-| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |","-| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |","-| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |","-| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |","-| FR-34 | C12 test files |","-| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |","-| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |","-| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |","-| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |","-| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |","-| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |","-| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |","-| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |","-| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |","-| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |","-| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |","-| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |","-| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |","-| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |","-| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |","+| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |","+| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |","+| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |","+| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |","+| FR-34 | C8, C9 |","+| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |","+| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |","+| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |","+| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |","+| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |","+| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |","+| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |","+| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |","+| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |","+| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |","+| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |","+| NFR-12 | §4.6 |","+| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |","+| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |","+| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |"," "," ---"," ","-## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)","+## 6. Change Footprint"," ","-**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,","-`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,","-`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,","-`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,","-`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,","-`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,","-`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.","-","-Token pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because","-`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it","-`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder.","-","-**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,","-`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional).","-","-**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,","-`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`.","+- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,","+  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,","+  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,","+  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.","+- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.","+- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,","+  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`."]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T12:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%), `handoff-to-architect.json`,\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-7) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B15).\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL,\nAuth.js v5 Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The PRD-01 **backend already exists**: data model, tokens,\ncredentials authorize with lockout, the JWT session with the passwordChanged recheck, middleware, rate\nlimiting, audit, validators, services and all five API routes. This ticket is a **UI + wiring + seed +\ntests** ticket. It adds pages and connects them to existing code, and it adds **no new service, no new\nAPI endpoint and no new dependency** (ADR-1, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers and open decisions (surfaced per compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker from `handoff-to-architect.json` | Design resolution |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: most of the PRD-01 backend exists; design only the gaps. | §3 lists every existing module as **Reuse, do not modify**. New work is limited to §3.2–§3.6. |\n| 2 | GAPS: auth pages, `/account/security`, shell placeholder removal, seed users, integration and e2e tests. | Covered by components C1–C12 below. |\n| 3 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip`; no rename (NFR-13). **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 4 | **FR-33 (MEDIUM):** `User` lacks `@@index([role, status])`. | Add it in a new additive migration (C11, ADR-6). |\n| 5 | **FR-30/FR-31 (MEDIUM):** `sendAuthEmail` already enqueues to EmailOutbox. | Leave `email.ts` alone. The seed logs the invite link through `logger` + `authLink` (C10). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6:** mui-mcp lookup is mandatory before UI code. | **Hard gate for dev.** Every MUI component in §3 must be looked up through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0) before JSX is written. If the server is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker; it does not guess. |\n\nAdditional risks found during design (not in intake):\n\n- **R1: e2e regression (NFR-13).** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` visits `/dashboard` with no session.\n  Middleware (FR-11) and the new `requirePageUser()` in the layout redirect it to `/login`, so it fails.\n  The design extracts the cookie sign-in already used by `notifications.spec.ts` into a shared helper and\n  uses it in `dashboard.spec.ts` (C12).\n- **R2: copy mismatch.** `services/auth.ts` returns `INVALID_LINK = \"This link is invalid or has expired.\"`,\n  but FR-13 requires the invite-specific copy. The **page owns the copy**: it renders the FR-13 string\n  both when `verifyToken` fails up front and when the POST returns `INVALID_TOKEN`. The service is not changed.\n- **R3: non-standard error code.** `INVALID_TOKEN` (400) is outside the NFR-10 list. It is existing behaviour\n  and stays as-is; `arch-api-contracts` documents it.\n- **R4: `signOut` signature.** In next-auth v5 `next-auth/react`, the option is `redirectTo`, not\n  `callbackUrl` (ADR-3 wording). Use `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture at a glance\n\n```\nBrowser\n ├─ (auth) route group — public (public-routes.ts)        ← NEW pages\n │    /login  /forgot-password  /reset-password/[token]  /invite/[token]\n │        │ client signIn()/signOut()  (next-auth/react; CSRF fetched by Auth.js)\n │        │ postJson() → existing JSON routes\n ├─ (app) route group — protected\n │    layout.tsx (server) ── requirePageUser() ──► AppShell({ user })   ← MODIFIED\n │    /account/security                                                  ← NEW page\n ▼\nmiddleware.ts (FR-11)  ── unauth page → /login?callbackUrl= ; unauth /api → 401\n ▼\nAPI routes (existing, thin: Zod → service → envelope)\n /api/auth/[...nextauth]  /api/auth/forgot-password  /api/auth/reset-password\n /api/auth/accept-invite  /api/account/password\n ▼\nServer modules (existing, untouched)\n auth.ts / auth.config.ts · credentials.ts · tokens.ts · rate-limit.ts · audit.ts\n services/auth.ts · services/users.ts · email.ts (EmailOutbox) · requireRole.ts\n ▼\nPrisma / PostgreSQL — User, AuthToken, AuditLog, EmailOutbox (+ new index)\n```\n\n**Patterns**\n\n- **Server-first page guard + client form.** Token pages and `/account/security` are Server Components\n  that do the authoritative check (`verifyToken`, `requirePageUser`) and render a client form only when\n  it is allowed (ADR-4, NFR-9).\n- **One current-user source.** The `(app)` layout reads the session with `requirePageUser()` and passes\n  `user` to `AppShell` as a prop. No `SessionProvider` and no `useSession` (ADR-3, FR-25).\n- **Shared schemas.** Every form uses RHF + `zodResolver` with the schemas already exported from\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, which the API routes use too (NFR-11).\n- **Reuse the existing form kit.** `src/components/PasswordChecklist/` already exports `PasswordChecklist`,\n  `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` and `ApiFailure` (B2). New pages\n  compose these; nothing is re-implemented.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Existing — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` (User, AuthToken, AuditLog, enums) | Data model | FR-1, FR-32 |\n| `src/server/auth/credentials.ts` | `authorizeCredentials`, lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`, `AuthError` codes `invalid` / `disabled` / `rate_limited` / `locked:<N>`, login audits | FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8, NFR-3, NFR-4 |\n| `src/server/auth/auth.ts`, `auth.config.ts` | JWT 8h, 5-min recheck, `reauth` update, `pages.signIn='/login'`, redirect sanitising, cookie defaults | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-2 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Page redirect / API 401, public paths, no sign-up route | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/auth/tokens.ts` | `createToken` / `verifyToken` / `consumeToken`, SHA-256, constant-time | FR-12, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/rate-limit.ts` | Sliding window, `__resetRateLimits()` | FR-6, FR-17 |\n| `src/server/audit.ts` | `audit()`, never throws, `ip` column | FR-24, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `signInSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `passwordChecks`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/server/services/auth.ts` | `acceptInvite`, `requestPasswordReset`, `resetPassword`, `changePassword`, `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE` | FR-14, FR-17–FR-20 |\n| `src/server/services/users.ts` | `createUser`, `createInviteToken`, `sendInvite`, `setUserStatus`, `unlockUser` | FR-22, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/auth/email.ts` | `sendAuthEmail` (EmailOutbox), `authLink(kind, raw)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-31 |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | `getCurrentUser`, `requireUser`, `requireRole`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| API routes `/api/auth/[...nextauth]`, `forgot-password`, `reset-password`, `accept-invite`, `/api/account/password` | Thin handlers, envelope, `unstable_update({reauth:true})` on change | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx` | Centred Card + logo, `Container maxWidth=\"xs\"` | FR-2 (B1) |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist/*` | Checklist, `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot` | FR-16, NFR-5 |\n| `useToast()` | Snackbar + Alert toasts | FR-19, FR-20, NFR-6 |\n| `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | Out of scope; must not be touched | NFR-13 |\n\n### 3.2 New — auth pages (route group `(auth)`, public)\n\nEvery page renders **only the card body**; the existing `(auth)/layout.tsx` provides Card/Container (B1).\nEvery form has one error `Alert` inside a `Box aria-live=\"polite\"` and relies on RHF's default\n`shouldFocusError` (client errors) plus `applyFieldErrors` (server errors) to focus the first invalid\nfield (NFR-5).\n\n**C1 · `/login`** — `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx` (server) + `LoginForm.tsx` (client). FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19, NFR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11, NFR-14\n- Page reads `searchParams.callbackUrl` and `searchParams.reset` and passes them to `LoginForm`.\n- `LoginForm`: RHF + `zodResolver(signInSchema)`. Email `TextField`, password `TextField` with\n  `passwordInputSlot` (show/hide `IconButton`), submit `Button`, link to `/forgot-password`. No\n  \"create account\" link (NFR-14).\n- Submit calls `signIn('credentials', { email, password, redirect: false })` from `next-auth/react`\n  (ADR-2; CSRF is handled by Auth.js, NFR-2).\n- Error: `loginErrorMessage(result.code)` — an exported pure function in `LoginForm.tsx`:\n\n  | `code` | Message |\n  |---|---|\n  | `locked:<N>` | \"This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.\" |\n  | `disabled` | \"This account is disabled. Contact the school office.\" |\n  | `rate_limited` | \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" |\n  | anything else | \"Email or password is incorrect.\" |\n\n- Success: `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl(callbackUrl))` then `router.refresh()` (FR-7). The server\n  `redirect` callback sanitises the same value again.\n- `reset=1`: one `useToast` success toast on mount (\"Password updated. Sign in with your new password.\") (FR-19).\n\n**C2 · `/forgot-password`** — `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` (client form inside). FR-17, NFR-5, NFR-11\n- RHF + `forgotPasswordSchema`, email field, `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', { email })`.\n- On a 2xx **or** `RATE_LIMITED`, replace the form with a success `Alert` showing `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`.\n  The screen is the same whether the user exists or not (no enumeration). Only `VALIDATION_ERROR` field\n  errors are shown inline. Link back to `/login`.\n\n**C3 · `/reset-password/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-1, NFR-8\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')` (read-only). `null` → invalid-link `Alert` + link to\n  `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `SetPasswordForm` with the user's email (needed by\n  `setPasswordSchema(email)` and `PasswordChecklist`).\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/reset-password', { token, password, confirmPassword })`.\n  Success → `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`. `INVALID_TOKEN` → swap to the invalid-link `Alert`.\n- The raw token is only a prop. It is never logged or put into audit metadata.\n\n**C4 · `/invite/[token]`** — `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` (server). FR-12, FR-13, FR-14, FR-16, NFR-1\n- `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. `null` → `Alert`: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired.\n  Ask the school office to send a new one.\" (page-owned copy, R2).\n- Valid → `SetPasswordForm` with read-only name (`firstName lastName`) and email, `submitLabel=\"Activate account\"`.\n- `onSubmit` → `postJson('/api/auth/accept-invite', …)`; on success `signIn('credentials', { email,\n  password, redirect: false })` with the password just set, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`.\n  `INVALID_TOKEN` → the FR-13 Alert. Reusing the link later fails `verifyToken` because the service consumed it.\n\n### 3.3 New — account page (route group `(app)`, protected)\n\n**C5 · `/account/security`** — `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` (server) + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` (client). FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11\n- Page: `const user = await requirePageUser()` (NFR-9); renders `ChangePasswordForm email={user.email}`.\n- Form: RHF + `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`. Current / new / confirm fields using\n  `passwordInputSlot`, `PasswordChecklist` under \"new\".\n- `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. `VALIDATION_ERROR` with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` →\n  `applyFieldErrors` shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success → `useToast` \"Password updated\" and\n  `reset()`. Re-issuing the current session and invalidating other sessions already happen on the server\n  (`unstable_update({reauth:true})` + `passwordChangedAt`, FR-10).\n\n### 3.4 Modified — app shell\n\n**C6 · `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`** — FR-25, FR-27, NFR-9\n- Add `const user = await requirePageUser()` (second guard behind middleware) and pass\n  `user={{ id, firstName, lastName, role }}` to `AppShell`. Keep the existing `schoolSettings` lookup.\n\n**C7 · `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`** — FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27\n- Delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`. Add a `user` prop to `AppShellProps`.\n- `navigationForRole(user.role)`; `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials);\n  menu header shows `fullName` and a role `Chip`.\n- Menu items: keep existing \"Profile\"; add **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link}\n  href=\"/account/security\"`, FR-21); \"Sign out\" calls `signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from\n  `next-auth/react` (FR-26, R4).\n- After this change, `grep -r PLACEHOLDER_USER src` returns nothing (FR-25 check).\n\n### 3.5 Data and seed\n\n**C10 · `prisma/seed.ts`** — FR-28, FR-29, FR-30, FR-31, NFR-12\n- New users block **before** the existing PRD-04 notifications block (which looks up `student@` / `parent@`).\n- `const hash = await bcrypt.hash('SchoolHub123!', 12)` once, then `prisma.user.upsert({ where: { email },\n  create: { …, role, status: 'ACTIVE', passwordHash: hash, passwordChangedAt: now }, update: {} })` for:\n\n  | Email | Name | Role |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | admin@schoolhub.test | Alice Admin | ADMIN |\n  | teacher@schoolhub.test | Tom Teacher | TEACHER |\n  | teacher2@schoolhub.test | Tina Tutor | TEACHER |\n  | student@schoolhub.test | Sam Student | STUDENT |\n  | student2@schoolhub.test | Sara Scholar | STUDENT |\n  | parent@schoolhub.test | Pat Parent | PARENT |\n\n- `invited@schoolhub.test` (intake FR-29 gives no name or role. **Architect default:** Ivy Invited, TEACHER. Dev may change it if the PRD seed table says otherwise):\n  upsert with `status: 'INVITED'`, `passwordHash: null`, `update: {}`. If the row is still INVITED,\n  `const { raw } = await createInviteToken(user.id)` and\n  `logger.info({ link: authLink('invite', raw) }, 'seed invite link')`. **Do not** call `sendAuthEmail` (FR-31).\n- New seed lines use `logger`; the existing `console.log` lines stay (out of scope).\n\n**C11 · Migration** — FR-33, FR-32\n- `prisma/schema.prisma`: add `@@index([role, status])` to `User`.\n- `prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`, generated with\n  `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, containing one `CREATE INDEX`. `AuditLog.ip` unchanged.\n\n### 3.6 Tests\n\n**C12 · Tests** — FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13\n\n| File | Kind | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts` | Vitest unit | `loginErrorMessage`: `locked:7`, `disabled`, `rate_limited`, `invalid`, unknown/undefined (FR-4, FR-6) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-authorize.test.ts` | Vitest, `TEST_DATABASE_URL`-gated, `@vitest-environment node` | unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked:N, 5th failure sets lockout + `auth.lockout` audit, rate limit, success resets count + `lastLoginAt` + `auth.login.success` (FR-3, FR-5, FR-6, FR-8) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-accept-invite.test.ts` | same | happy path → ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, token consumed, `auth.invite.accepted`; reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`; policy violation (FR-13, FR-14, FR-15) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-reset-password.test.ts` | same | request for unknown email creates no token; ACTIVE user gets token + EmailOutbox row; older tokens invalidated; reset clears lockout, consumes token, audits (FR-17, FR-18, FR-19) |\n| `tests/integration/auth-change-password.test.ts` | same | wrong current password → `fieldErrors.currentPassword`; success updates hash + `passwordChangedAt` (FR-20) |\n| `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` | Playwright helper | `signInAs(page, email, password)`: the CSRF + `/api/auth/callback/credentials` cookie flow lifted from `notifications.spec.ts` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (modified) | Playwright | Calls `signInAs` with the seed admin before visiting `/dashboard` (R1) |\n| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` | Playwright, `mode: 'serial'` | UI sign-in as admin → `/dashboard` with real name in the menu; sign out → `/login`; wrong password message; unauth `/dashboard` → `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`; forgot → reset for `student2@` (reads newest `EmailOutbox` row through `@prisma/client`, extracts `/reset-password/…`), then sign in with the new password; one `AxeBuilder` run on `/login` (FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, NFR-5) |\n\nIntegration tests call `__resetRateLimits()` in `beforeEach`. The forgot → reset e2e test restores\n`student2@`'s password to `SchoolHub123!` in `afterAll` so reruns are not affected.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n**D1 · Sign-in (FR-2–FR-8, FR-11)**\n1. Unauth request to `/grades` → middleware → `302 /login?callbackUrl=%2Fgrades`.\n2. `LoginForm` validates with `signInSchema` → `signIn('credentials', { redirect:false })` → Auth.js fetches\n   CSRF → `POST /api/auth/callback/credentials` → `authorizeCredentials` (rate limit → user lookup →\n   bcrypt / `DUMMY_HASH` → status / lock checks → counter update → audit).\n3. Failure → `{ ok:false, code }` → `loginErrorMessage(code)` → `Alert` (aria-live).\n4. Success → session cookie set → `router.replace(safeCallbackUrl('/grades'))` → `(app)/layout`\n   `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })`.\n\n**D2 · Invite acceptance (FR-12–FR-16)**\n1. Admin `sendInvite` (existing) → EmailOutbox → link `/invite/<raw>`.\n2. Page server-side `verifyToken(raw,'INVITE')` → invalid → FR-13 Alert; valid → `SetPasswordForm` (name, email read-only, checklist).\n3. `POST /api/auth/accept-invite` → `acceptInvite` (policy, hash, ACTIVE, `passwordChangedAt`, consume, audit).\n4. Client `signIn('credentials')` with the new password → `/dashboard`. A revisit → `verifyToken` null → FR-13 Alert.\n\n**D3 · Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n1. `/forgot-password` → `POST /api/auth/forgot-password` → rate limits (3/email/h, 10/IP/h) →\n   `requestPasswordReset` (ACTIVE only: invalidate old, `createToken` 60 min, `sendAuthEmail`). The UI\n   shows the same message either way.\n2. `/reset-password/<raw>` → `verifyToken` → form → `POST /api/auth/reset-password` → `resetPassword`\n   (hash, `passwordChangedAt`, clear lockout, consume, audit) → `/login?reset=1` → toast.\n3. Any other session for the user dies within 5 min through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck (FR-10).\n\n**D4 · Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n`/account/security` (`requirePageUser`) → `POST /api/account/password` (`requireUser`) → `changePassword`\n→ `unstable_update({reauth:true})` keeps this session valid → toast. Other devices are signed out within 5 min.\n\n**D5 · Shell and sign-out (FR-25–FR-27)**\n`(app)/layout` → `requirePageUser()` → `AppShell({ user })` → `navigationForRole(user.role)` and the menu.\n\"Sign out\" → `signOut({ redirectTo:'/login' })` → cookie cleared → `/login`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §3.1 schema (existing, unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | C1 `/login` page + `LoginForm` |\n| FR-3 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-4 | C1 `loginErrorMessage`; C12 unit test + e2e wrong-password |\n| FR-5 | §3.1 `credentials.ts`; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-6 | §3.1 `rate-limit.ts`; C1 `rate_limited` mapping; C12 |\n| FR-7 | C1 `safeCallbackUrl` redirect; D1; C12 e2e callbackUrl |\n| FR-8 | §3.1 `credentials.ts` audits; C12 `auth-authorize.test.ts` |\n| FR-9 | §3.1 `auth.ts` (existing) |\n| FR-10 | §3.1 `auth.ts` recheck; D3 step 3, D4 |\n| FR-11 | §3.1 middleware; D1 step 1; C12 e2e unauth redirect |\n| FR-12 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3, C4 server-side `verifyToken` |\n| FR-13 | C4 `/invite/[token]`; R2 page-owned copy |\n| FR-14 | C4 accept → `signIn` → `/dashboard`; D2; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` |\n| FR-15 | §3.1 validators; C12 `auth-accept-invite.test.ts` policy case |\n| FR-16 | Existing `PasswordChecklist` used in C3, C4, C5 |\n| FR-17 | C2 `/forgot-password`; D3 step 1; C12 |\n| FR-18 | §3.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C12 `auth-reset-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-19 | C3 `/reset-password/[token]`; C1 `reset=1` toast; D3; C12 e2e forgot → reset |\n| FR-20 | C5 `/account/security`; D4; C12 `auth-change-password.test.ts` |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" menu item |\n| FR-22 | §3.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only); C10 uses `createInviteToken` |\n| FR-23 | §3.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 use `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §3.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6 + C7 delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`, user prop |\n| FR-26 | C7 name, role Chip, initials, `signOut`; D5; C12 e2e sign-out |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28 | C10 six ACTIVE upserts |\n| FR-29 | C10 INVITED user |\n| FR-30 | C10 `createInviteToken` + `logger.info(authLink(...))` |\n| FR-31 | §3.1 `email.ts` untouched; C10 avoids `sendAuthEmail` |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 3; C11 keeps `AuditLog.ip` |\n| FR-33 | C11 additive migration |\n| FR-34 | C12 test files |\n| NFR-1 | §3.1 `tokens.ts`; C3/C4 raw token only as prop |\n| NFR-2 | §3.1 cookie defaults; C1 client `signIn` CSRF |\n| NFR-3 | §3.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 one bcrypt-12 compare per attempt; no new work on the sign-in path |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 form pattern (aria-live Alert, focus first invalid); C12 axe on `/login` |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 6 mui-mcp gate; `useToast` in C1, C5 |\n| NFR-7 | All UI in C1–C7 is MUI only; existing banned-import test |\n| NFR-8 | C3/C4 never log the token; no new audit calls |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6 `requirePageUser`; existing `requireUser` in API |\n| NFR-10 | §3.1 existing handlers; R3 `INVALID_TOKEN` documented |\n| NFR-11 | C1–C5 RHF + shared Zod schemas |\n| NFR-12 | C10 uses `logger`; no `console.log` in new code |\n| NFR-13 | §3.1 untouched list; R1 e2e regression fix; no new deps (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-14 | C1 no sign-up link; `public-routes.ts` has no sign-up route |\n| NFR-15 | Stock MUI, English copy throughout C1–C7 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. File change summary (for dev-planning)\n\n**New:** `src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/LoginForm.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx`,\n`src/app/(app)/account/security/ChangePasswordForm.tsx`,\n`prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index/migration.sql`,\n`tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts`, `tests/integration/auth-{authorize,accept-invite,reset-password,change-password}.test.ts`,\n`tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n\nToken pages may need a small client wrapper file next to them (for `onSubmit` + `router`) because\n`SetPasswordForm` takes an `onSubmit` callback, which a Server Component cannot pass. Name it\n`InviteClient.tsx` / `ResetClient.tsx` in the same folder.\n\n**Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `prisma/schema.prisma`,\n`prisma/seed.ts`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` (and `notifications.spec.ts` may switch to the shared helper; optional).\n\n**Untouched:** everything under `src/server/`, `src/app/api/`, `src/middleware.ts`,\n`src/config/public-routes.ts`, `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `src/components/PasswordChecklist/`.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013iBEoK2jfTpB3Qbe8wM2Em","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
