{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk6hisNtzpJXarrFAse3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-1 (`arch-design-system`). It replaces the older design from 11:41, which still listed the seed users, the role/status migration and `/login` as new work. All three already exist in the code, so I took them out of scope.\n\n**What the ticket needs:** 4 new pages, a fix to how the app shell gets the signed-in user, and tests. No new API route, service, schema change, migration or dependency.\n\n- **C1:** `/forgot-password`. It always shows the server's \"if an account exists\" message, so it doesn't reveal which emails have accounts, and it handles the \"too many attempts\" (429) response.\n- **C2, C3, C4:** `/reset-password/[token]` and `/invite/[token]`. They check the token on the server before showing anything, so an expired link never renders a form. Both use one shared client form built on the existing `SetPasswordForm`.\n  - **Invite:** after the user sets a password, it signs them in and goes to `/dashboard`.\n  - **Reset:** it goes to `/login?reset=1`, where the existing success toast fires.\n  - **Bad link:** a \"link invalid\" response from the API switches the page to the invalid-link message.\n- **C5:** `/account/security`, using the existing schemas and the `/api/account/password` route.\n- **C6, C7:** the `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` and passes the user to the shell. This removes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wires up the real name, role badge and initials, the sidebar filtered by role, the \"Account security\" menu item and Sign out. There is no `SessionProvider`, so there is only one source of the current user.\n- **C8, C9:** one integration test file, one Playwright auth spec, and a shared sign-in helper for the e2e tests.\n\n**Things the next steps should know:**\n- **Needs your sign-off:** the audit log keeps its existing `ip` column rather than the PRD's `ipAddress` (FR-32).\n- **Existing test will break:** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` opens `/dashboard` without signing in. Once the layout requires a user, it will fail unless it uses the new sign-in helper.\n- **One gap is already closed:** intake listed the \"too many attempts\" message on `/login` as missing (FR-6), but it's already there. Dev should check it, not build it.\n- **Hard gate before any UI code:** dev must look up every MUI component through the mui-mcp server. It was connected while I wrote this.\n- **Stale files in `artifacts/architect/`:** `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` are left over from the earlier run. The `arch-api-contracts` step needs to regenerate both; I didn't touch them.\n\nEvery requirement ID cited in the design exists in `requirements.json`, and the traceability table covers all 34 FRs and 15 NFRs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8401,"cache_read_input_tokens":53822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8401},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b447f845-727b-4a62-ae8d-232a33ab6037","uuid":"7d062c0a-4a2b-4bd1-bd20-33f0c8768318","timestamp":"2026-11-05T16:30:24.398Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk6hiTpZQUtM2ksn5BbZ"}
