{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K2YnefLgbNC5Jic4CVoGgN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2. Nothing in the requirements needs a different stack, so the decisions below cover how this feature uses the stack that is already there.\n6\t\n7\tThis file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) version that was in this folder.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no new dependencies\n12\t\n13\t**Context.** The feature needs a register UI with exclusive toggles (FR-9), a calendar with a custom day slot (FR-26), a scrollable matrix (FR-29), date pickers that block future dates (FR-8), CSV export (FR-32), timezone-aware \"today\" logic (FR-31, NFR-8), and shared validation (FR-36). NFR-6 allows MUI only, and NFR-10 asks for brownfield safety.\n14\t\n15\t**Decision.** Use only installed packages:\n16\t- UI: `@mui/material` `ToggleButtonGroup`, `Paper` (sticky save bar), `Tooltip` and `Badge`; `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate`) and `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot; `@mui/x-data-grid` `DataGrid` for the course matrix and the admin report.\n17\t- Validation: `zod`, in `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`.\n18\t- Dates: `date-fns` and `date-fns-tz`, through the existing `src/lib/dates.ts`.\n19\t- CSV: the existing `toCsv()`/`escapeCsvCell()` in `src/server/csv.ts`. `papaparse` is not needed for export.\n20\t\n21\tBefore writing any component, Dev must look it up through the mui-mcp server (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0). The server was reachable in this session.\n22\t\n23\t**Consequences.** There are no lockfile changes and no banned imports for QA to catch. The free (MIT) `DataGrid` has no column pinning and caps pages at 100 rows. That is acceptable: the matrix scrolls horizontally (FR-29) and pagination is capped at 100 anyway (NFR-8). Do not use `DataGridPro` features.\n24\t\n25\tDrivers: FR-8, FR-9, FR-26, FR-29, FR-32, FR-36, NFR-6, NFR-8, NFR-10.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## ADR-2: Use a Prisma schema plus hand-written SQL in one migration for constraints Prisma can't express\n30\t\n31\t**Context.** FR-1 specifies the `AttendanceStatus` enum and the `AttendanceSession`/`AttendanceRecord` models. FR-2 needs \"exactly one of courseId/sectionId\". FR-3 needs two partial unique indexes. Prisma 5.20 cannot express CHECK constraints or partial (`WHERE`) indexes. FR-4 adds two `SchoolSettings` columns. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n32\t\n33\t**Decision.** Create one new migration, `20261107000000_attendance` or any timestamp later than the latest one. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then append the following raw SQL by hand:\n34\t- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)`\n35\t- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL`\n36\t- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL`\n37\t\n38\t`SchoolSettings` gains an `AttendanceMode` enum column `attendanceMode` (default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. `date` is stored as `@db.Date`.\n39\t\n40\t**Consequences.** `prisma db push` and any schema drift check will not see these SQL objects, so tests must run `prisma migrate reset`/`deploy` and must not use `db push`. The service also checks the one-of rule (FR-2), so callers get a clean `VALIDATION_ERROR` before the database rejects the row. Prisma cannot `upsert` on a partial index (see ADR-3).\n41\t\n42\tDrivers: FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-40, NFR-8.\n43\t\n44\t---\n45\t\n46\t## ADR-3: Save a register in one interactive transaction that only writes changed rows\n47\t\n48\t**Context.** FR-14 requires an atomic create-or-update of the session and all its records. NFR-1 requires a 35-student save to finish in under 500 ms. FR-18 requires an audit entry for each changed status, and FR-21/22 need the previous status to detect changes. A partial unique index cannot be used as an upsert target.\n49\t\n50\t**Decision.** `saveRegister()` in `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` uses `prisma.$transaction(async tx => …)` and runs these steps:\n51\t1. `findFirst` the session by (courseId, date, periodId) or (sectionId, date). Create it if it does not exist. If the create fails with `P2002`, a concurrent first save won the race: re-read the session and continue.\n52\t2. Load the existing records for the session in a single query to get the previous statuses.\n53\t3. Insert new students with `createMany`. Update only the rows whose status, minutesLate or note actually changed; `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` makes these targeted updates.\n54\t4. Validate the roster (NFR-3) against ACTIVE enrollments on that date, or section members for a daily register, in one query before writing.\n55\t5. Return the diff `{studentId, prev, next}[]`. Write `audit()` entries for changed records inside the transaction, or right after commit if `audit()` cannot take `tx`. Dev should check `src/server/audit.ts`.\n56\t\n57\t**Consequences.** About 5 to 40 statements run per save, which fits easily in 500 ms. The diff is computed by a pure function (`diffRecords(prev, next)`) that unit tests can cover (FR-39). No raw `INSERT … ON CONFLICT` is needed.\n58\t\n59\tDrivers: FR-14, FR-18, FR-21, FR-22, FR-39, FR-40, NFR-1, NFR-3.\n60\t\n61\t---\n62\t\n63\t## ADR-4: Send notifications synchronously after commit through the existing notify pipeline, with no new job queue\n64\t\n65\t**Context.** FR-20 to FR-23 add four notification types. NFR-5 requires delivery within 5 minutes, with in-app notifications immediate and email through `EmailOutbox`. `notifyStudentAndParents()`/`notify()` already exist and never throw. There is no job runner or cron in `src/server`.\n66\t\n67\t**Decision.** After the transaction commits, loop over the diff and call `notifyStudentAndParents()` when:\n68\t- a status changes from something other than ABSENT to ABSENT (`attendance.absent`);\n69\t- a status changes from something other than LATE to LATE (`attendance.late`);\n70\t- a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT (`attendance.corrected`).\n71\t\n72\tRe-saving an unchanged register produces no diff and therefore no notifications, which covers the dedupe rule in FR-22. Register all four keys in `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`, using intake's FR-23 defaults for `corrected`/`register_missing`. For daily registers, the body is `<Section> daily register, <date>`, following the clarification default.\n73\t\n74\t**Consequences.** There is no worker or queue infrastructure. Emails go through the existing outbox, so the 5-minute target depends on the existing outbox drain. Save latency grows by about one insert per notified student, which is fine at class size. If the notification loop ever pushes saves past NFR-1, move it to a fire-and-forget call after the response is sent.\n75\t\n76\tDrivers: FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-5.\n77\t\n78\t---\n79\t\n80\t## ADR-5: Compute missing registers and \"today\" on demand in the school timezone, with no scheduler\n81\t\n82\t**Context.** FR-31 flags a register as missing if it is still not taken 15 minutes after the period starts, in the school timezone. FR-6, FR-8 and FR-19 depend on \"today\" and on 14-day windows. `Period.startTime` is a string, and `SchoolSettings.timezone` exists. `src/lib/dates.ts` already wraps `formatInTimeZone`.\n83\t\n84\t**Decision.**\n85\t- Compute `schoolToday()` as `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'yyyy-MM-dd')`. Every date-only comparison (future-date refusal, 14-day open/edit window, current period) uses this school-local date string compared with `@db.Date`. Never use server-local `new Date()`.\n86\t- `GET /api/admin/attendance/overview` computes the missing list when it is requested. It expands `getScheduleForDate()` for each course meeting today, filters to meetings where `startTime + 15 min < now` in the school timezone, and subtracts the sessions that exist. \"Remind teacher\" is a manual POST.\n87\t- Put the edit-window rule in a pure function, `canEdit(role, registerDate, today)` (FR-39).\n88\t\n89\t**Consequences.** No cron and no stored \"missing\" state. The overview always reflects reality. Automatic reminders are out of scope; add a scheduler only if the PRD later asks for automatic sending.\n90\t\n91\tDrivers: FR-6, FR-8, FR-19, FR-30, FR-31, FR-39, NFR-8.\n92\t\n93\t---\n94\t\n95\t## ADR-6: Aggregate per student in TypeScript and school-wide with Prisma `groupBy`\n96\t\n97\t**Context.** NFR-1 requires the student tab to load in under 400 ms with 1,200 records. FR-25/26/27 need the summary, the calendar and the table from the same data. FR-28 defines the rate formula and the mode-dependent record set. FR-32/33 aggregate across all students for up to 366 days.\n98\t\n99\t**Decision.**\n100\t- **Student tab**: run one `findMany` over records joined to the session date and period, filtered by date range and by the mode's session kind (`courseId != null` for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, `sectionId != null` for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure functions then compute the term and year summaries (`attendanceRate()`), the per-day calendar colours and the table rows. 1,200 narrow rows is a few milliseconds of work.\n101\t- **Report and below-threshold**: use `prisma.attendanceRecord.groupBy({ by: ['studentId','status'], where: { session: { date range, kind } } , _count })` and fold the result into per-student rows in TypeScript. If that turns out slow in practice, fall back to a single `$queryRaw` with `GROUP BY`.\n102\t- Records from DROPPED enrollments are never filtered out (FR-28).\n103\t- `attendanceRate()` lives in one place and is shared by the tab, matrix, report and threshold views (FR-39).\n104\t\n105\t**Consequences.** There are no materialised views or cached counters, and no index beyond FR-1's `[studentId, createdAt]` plus the session indexes. Notes are stripped in the service according to role (FR-27), not in the UI.\n106\t\n107\tDrivers: FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-32, FR-33, FR-39, NFR-1.\n108\t\n109\t---\n110\t\n111\t## ADR-7: Keep offline resilience to localStorage drafts, with no service worker or IndexedDB\n112\t\n113\t**Context.** NFR-2 requires that unsaved marks survive a network failure and that the next visit offers a restore. The app already uses `window.localStorage` (`src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`).\n114\t\n115\t**Decision.** The register's client component writes its draft to `localStorage` under the key `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>` when a save fails. On mount it shows a \"Restore unsaved attendance\" action if a draft exists, and it clears the draft after a successful save.\n116\t\n117\t**Consequences.** This is not offline-first. The page itself must still load. That is all NFR-2 asks for. Add a service worker only if a full offline mode is requested.\n118\t\n119\tDrivers: NFR-2, NFR-4.\n120\t\n121\t---\n122\t\n123\t## ADR-8: Reuse the existing auth, settings and config extension points\n124\t\n125\t**Context.** NFR-7 requires server-side access control everywhere. FR-5 needs an admin editor for settings, but there is no settings page and `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty. FR-24, FR-29 and FR-34 extend the tab and nav configuration.\n126\t\n127\t**Decision.**\n128\t- **Access.** Use `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `assertCanManageCourse`/`assertCanViewCourse` and `assertCanViewStudent`/`getAccessibleStudentIds` as they are. The one new check, homeroom access (`section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id || ADMIN`) for FR-15, is a short function in the attendance service. EXCUSED is rejected server-side for anyone who is not an admin (FR-10).\n129\t- **Settings (FR-5).** Use the smallest option. Extend `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` with the two new fields and add `PATCH /api/settings/school`, which is ADMIN only, Zod-validated (threshold 0–100) and calls `audit()`. The editor is an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. A general settings page is out of scope.\n130\t- **Tabs and nav.** Add entries to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts` and `navigation.ts`. Do not move or rename existing entries.\n131\t- **Daily register route (FR-16).** Use `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=`, rendering the same register client component as the course route.\n132\t\n133\t**Consequences.** No new auth abstraction is needed. The FR-5 and FR-16 defaults are open for the user to override (see blockers in the intake handoff).\n134\t\n135\tDrivers: FR-5, FR-10, FR-15, FR-16, FR-24, FR-29, FR-34, FR-35, NFR-7, NFR-10.\n136\t\n137\t---\n138\t\n139\t## ADR-9: Test with the existing Vitest and Playwright setups\n140\t\n141\t**Context.** FR-39 to FR-41 define the tests. Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2 are installed.\n142\t\n143\t**Decision.**\n144\t- **Unit (Vitest).** Cover the pure functions `attendanceRate`, `canEdit` and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`.\n145\t- **Integration (Vitest against a migrated test database).** Cover `saveRegister` atomicity, NFR-3 roster rejection, and violations of the CHECK constraint and both partial indexes. The database must be created through migrations, per ADR-2.\n146\t- **End-to-end (Playwright).** Run the take-attendance flow at a 375×667 viewport, and a parent's notification plus the calendar absence.\n147\t- **Seed (FR-38).** Use a small seeded PRNG (mulberry32, a few lines) in the seed script rather than adding a dependency.\n148\t\n149\t**Consequences.** No new test tooling is added.\n150\t\n151\tDrivers: FR-38, FR-39, FR-40, FR-41, NFR-10.\n152\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90141260-d1a7-451a-8239-c83fc1554359","uuid":"af432e42-bde0-42d1-8854-57de649ab129","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:32:36.511Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js (next-auth 5.0.0-beta.25), Zod 3.23.8, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2. Nothing in the requirements needs a different stack, so the decisions below cover how this feature uses the stack that is already there.\n\nThis file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) version that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no new dependencies\n\n**Context.** The feature needs a register UI with exclusive toggles (FR-9), a calendar with a custom day slot (FR-26), a scrollable matrix (FR-29), date pickers that block future dates (FR-8), CSV export (FR-32), timezone-aware \"today\" logic (FR-31, NFR-8), and shared validation (FR-36). NFR-6 allows MUI only, and NFR-10 asks for brownfield safety.\n\n**Decision.** Use only installed packages:\n- UI: `@mui/material` `ToggleButtonGroup`, `Paper` (sticky save bar), `Tooltip` and `Badge`; `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate`) and `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot; `@mui/x-data-grid` `DataGrid` for the course matrix and the admin report.\n- Validation: `zod`, in `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`.\n- Dates: `date-fns` and `date-fns-tz`, through the existing `src/lib/dates.ts`.\n- CSV: the existing `toCsv()`/`escapeCsvCell()` in `src/server/csv.ts`. `papaparse` is not needed for export.\n\nBefore writing any component, Dev must look it up through the mui-mcp server (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0). The server was reachable in this session.\n\n**Consequences.** There are no lockfile changes and no banned imports for QA to catch. The free (MIT) `DataGrid` has no column pinning and caps pages at 100 rows. That is acceptable: the matrix scrolls horizontally (FR-29) and pagination is capped at 100 anyway (NFR-8). Do not use `DataGridPro` features.\n\nDrivers: FR-8, FR-9, FR-26, FR-29, FR-32, FR-36, NFR-6, NFR-8, NFR-10.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Use a Prisma schema plus hand-written SQL in one migration for constraints Prisma can't express\n\n**Context.** FR-1 specifies the `AttendanceStatus` enum and the `AttendanceSession`/`AttendanceRecord` models. FR-2 needs \"exactly one of courseId/sectionId\". FR-3 needs two partial unique indexes. Prisma 5.20 cannot express CHECK constraints or partial (`WHERE`) indexes. FR-4 adds two `SchoolSettings` columns. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n\n**Decision.** Create one new migration, `20261107000000_attendance` or any timestamp later than the latest one. Generate it with `prisma migrate dev --create-only`, then append the following raw SQL by hand:\n- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)`\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL`\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ... ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL`\n\n`SchoolSettings` gains an `AttendanceMode` enum column `attendanceMode` (default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. `date` is stored as `@db.Date`.\n\n**Consequences.** `prisma db push` and any schema drift check will not see these SQL objects, so tests must run `prisma migrate reset`/`deploy` and must not use `db push`. The service also checks the one-of rule (FR-2), so callers get a clean `VALIDATION_ERROR` before the database rejects the row. Prisma cannot `upsert` on a partial index (see ADR-3).\n\nDrivers: FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, FR-40, NFR-8.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Save a register in one interactive transaction that only writes changed rows\n\n**Context.** FR-14 requires an atomic create-or-update of the session and all its records. NFR-1 requires a 35-student save to finish in under 500 ms. FR-18 requires an audit entry for each changed status, and FR-21/22 need the previous status to detect changes. A partial unique index cannot be used as an upsert target.\n\n**Decision.** `saveRegister()` in `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` uses `prisma.$transaction(async tx => …)` and runs these steps:\n1. `findFirst` the session by (courseId, date, periodId) or (sectionId, date). Create it if it does not exist. If the create fails with `P2002`, a concurrent first save won the race: re-read the session and continue.\n2. Load the existing records for the session in a single query to get the previous statuses.\n3. Insert new students with `createMany`. Update only the rows whose status, minutesLate or note actually changed; `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` makes these targeted updates.\n4. Validate the roster (NFR-3) against ACTIVE enrollments on that date, or section members for a daily register, in one query before writing.\n5. Return the diff `{studentId, prev, next}[]`. Write `audit()` entries for changed records inside the transaction, or right after commit if `audit()` cannot take `tx`. Dev should check `src/server/audit.ts`.\n\n**Consequences.** About 5 to 40 statements run per save, which fits easily in 500 ms. The diff is computed by a pure function (`diffRecords(prev, next)`) that unit tests can cover (FR-39). No raw `INSERT … ON CONFLICT` is needed.\n\nDrivers: FR-14, FR-18, FR-21, FR-22, FR-39, FR-40, NFR-1, NFR-3.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Send notifications synchronously after commit through the existing notify pipeline, with no new job queue\n\n**Context.** FR-20 to FR-23 add four notification types. NFR-5 requires delivery within 5 minutes, with in-app notifications immediate and email through `EmailOutbox`. `notifyStudentAndParents()`/`notify()` already exist and never throw. There is no job runner or cron in `src/server`.\n\n**Decision.** After the transaction commits, loop over the diff and call `notifyStudentAndParents()` when:\n- a status changes from something other than ABSENT to ABSENT (`attendance.absent`);\n- a status changes from something other than LATE to LATE (`attendance.late`);\n- a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT (`attendance.corrected`).\n\nRe-saving an unchanged register produces no diff and therefore no notifications, which covers the dedupe rule in FR-22. Register all four keys in `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`, using intake's FR-23 defaults for `corrected`/`register_missing`. For daily registers, the body is `<Section> daily register, <date>`, following the clarification default.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no worker or queue infrastructure. Emails go through the existing outbox, so the 5-minute target depends on the existing outbox drain. Save latency grows by about one insert per notified student, which is fine at class size. If the notification loop ever pushes saves past NFR-1, move it to a fire-and-forget call after the response is sent.\n\nDrivers: FR-20, FR-21, FR-22, FR-23, NFR-5.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Compute missing registers and \"today\" on demand in the school timezone, with no scheduler\n\n**Context.** FR-31 flags a register as missing if it is still not taken 15 minutes after the period starts, in the school timezone. FR-6, FR-8 and FR-19 depend on \"today\" and on 14-day windows. `Period.startTime` is a string, and `SchoolSettings.timezone` exists. `src/lib/dates.ts` already wraps `formatInTimeZone`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Compute `schoolToday()` as `formatInTimeZone(now, tz, 'yyyy-MM-dd')`. Every date-only comparison (future-date refusal, 14-day open/edit window, current period) uses this school-local date string compared with `@db.Date`. Never use server-local `new Date()`.\n- `GET /api/admin/attendance/overview` computes the missing list when it is requested. It expands `getScheduleForDate()` for each course meeting today, filters to meetings where `startTime + 15 min < now` in the school timezone, and subtracts the sessions that exist. \"Remind teacher\" is a manual POST.\n- Put the edit-window rule in a pure function, `canEdit(role, registerDate, today)` (FR-39).\n\n**Consequences.** No cron and no stored \"missing\" state. The overview always reflects reality. Automatic reminders are out of scope; add a scheduler only if the PRD later asks for automatic sending.\n\nDrivers: FR-6, FR-8, FR-19, FR-30, FR-31, FR-39, NFR-8.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Aggregate per student in TypeScript and school-wide with Prisma `groupBy`\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires the student tab to load in under 400 ms with 1,200 records. FR-25/26/27 need the summary, the calendar and the table from the same data. FR-28 defines the rate formula and the mode-dependent record set. FR-32/33 aggregate across all students for up to 366 days.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Student tab**: run one `findMany` over records joined to the session date and period, filtered by date range and by the mode's session kind (`courseId != null` for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, `sectionId != null` for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure functions then compute the term and year summaries (`attendanceRate()`), the per-day calendar colours and the table rows. 1,200 narrow rows is a few milliseconds of work.\n- **Report and below-threshold**: use `prisma.attendanceRecord.groupBy({ by: ['studentId','status'], where: { session: { date range, kind } } , _count })` and fold the result into per-student rows in TypeScript. If that turns out slow in practice, fall back to a single `$queryRaw` with `GROUP BY`.\n- Records from DROPPED enrollments are never filtered out (FR-28).\n- `attendanceRate()` lives in one place and is shared by the tab, matrix, report and threshold views (FR-39).\n\n**Consequences.** There are no materialised views or cached counters, and no index beyond FR-1's `[studentId, createdAt]` plus the session indexes. Notes are stripped in the service according to role (FR-27), not in the UI.\n\nDrivers: FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-32, FR-33, FR-39, NFR-1.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Keep offline resilience to localStorage drafts, with no service worker or IndexedDB\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 requires that unsaved marks survive a network failure and that the next visit offers a restore. The app already uses `window.localStorage` (`src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** The register's client component writes its draft to `localStorage` under the key `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>` when a save fails. On mount it shows a \"Restore unsaved attendance\" action if a draft exists, and it clears the draft after a successful save.\n\n**Consequences.** This is not offline-first. The page itself must still load. That is all NFR-2 asks for. Add a service worker only if a full offline mode is requested.\n\nDrivers: NFR-2, NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Reuse the existing auth, settings and config extension points\n\n**Context.** NFR-7 requires server-side access control everywhere. FR-5 needs an admin editor for settings, but there is no settings page and `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty. FR-24, FR-29 and FR-34 extend the tab and nav configuration.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Access.** Use `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `assertCanManageCourse`/`assertCanViewCourse` and `assertCanViewStudent`/`getAccessibleStudentIds` as they are. The one new check, homeroom access (`section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id || ADMIN`) for FR-15, is a short function in the attendance service. EXCUSED is rejected server-side for anyone who is not an admin (FR-10).\n- **Settings (FR-5).** Use the smallest option. Extend `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` with the two new fields and add `PATCH /api/settings/school`, which is ADMIN only, Zod-validated (threshold 0–100) and calls `audit()`. The editor is an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. A general settings page is out of scope.\n- **Tabs and nav.** Add entries to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts` and `navigation.ts`. Do not move or rename existing entries.\n- **Daily register route (FR-16).** Use `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=`, rendering the same register client component as the course route.\n\n**Consequences.** No new auth abstraction is needed. The FR-5 and FR-16 defaults are open for the user to override (see blockers in the intake handoff).\n\nDrivers: FR-5, FR-10, FR-15, FR-16, FR-24, FR-29, FR-34, FR-35, NFR-7, NFR-10.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Test with the existing Vitest and Playwright setups\n\n**Context.** FR-39 to FR-41 define the tests. Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2 are installed.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Unit (Vitest).** Cover the pure functions `attendanceRate`, `canEdit` and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`.\n- **Integration (Vitest against a migrated test database).** Cover `saveRegister` atomicity, NFR-3 roster rejection, and violations of the CHECK constraint and both partial indexes. The database must be created through migrations, per ADR-2.\n- **End-to-end (Playwright).** Run the take-attendance flow at a 375×667 viewport, and a parent's notification plus the calendar absence.\n- **Seed (FR-38).** Use a small seeded PRNG (mulberry32, a few lines) in the seed script rather than adding a dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling is added.\n\nDrivers: FR-38, FR-39, FR-40, FR-41, NFR-10.\n","numLines":152,"startLine":1,"totalLines":152}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K2YnefLgbNC5Jic4CVoGgN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
