{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FpDMGZMFsmCD4PFj97piBD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7\n2\t\n3\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).\n5\tIt has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\n6\tRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n7\t\n8\t> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before.\n9\t\n10\t**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the\n11\tmodels, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,\n12\t2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:\n13\t\n14\t| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |\n15\t|---|---|---|\n16\t| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |\n17\t| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |\n18\t| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |\n19\t| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |\n20\t| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |\n21\t| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |\n22\t| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |\n23\t| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |\n24\t\n25\tGaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,\n26\t`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n27\t\n28\tConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,\n29\t**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**.\n30\t\n31\t## Requirement → Concern table\n32\t\n33\t| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n34\t|---|---|---|\n35\t| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |\n36\t| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |\n37\t| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |\n38\t| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |\n39\t| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |\n40\t| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |\n41\t| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |\n42\t| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |\n43\t| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |\n44\t| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |\n45\t| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |\n46\t| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |\n47\t| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |\n48\t| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |\n49\t| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |\n50\t| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |\n51\t| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |\n52\t| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |\n53\t| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n54\t| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |\n55\t| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |\n56\t| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n57\t| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |\n58\t| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |\n59\t| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |\n60\t| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |\n61\t| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |\n62\t| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |\n63\t| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |\n64\t| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |\n65\t| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |\n66\t| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n67\t| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |\n68\t| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |\n69\t| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |\n70\t| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |\n71\t| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |\n72\t| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |\n73\t| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |\n74\t| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |\n75\t| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |\n76\t| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |\n77\t| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |\n78\t| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |\n79\t| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |\n80\t| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |\n81\t| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |\n82\t| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |\n83\t| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |\n84\t| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |\n85\t| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |\n86\t\n87\t## Open points for `arch-design-system`\n88\t\n89\t1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.\n90\t2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.\n91\t3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.\n92\t4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.\n93\t5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.\n94\t6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted.\n95\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90141260-d1a7-451a-8239-c83fc1554359","uuid":"2fcd3011-2f31-49aa-9bc5-6b954dadf8bc","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:32:37.008Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-7\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T05:29:02Z), PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007).\nIt has 41 FRs and 10 NFRs (51 requirements) at 94% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 6 blockers.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 notes that were here before.\n\n**Headline:** this is a **greenfield feature inside a brownfield app**. Everything attendance-related is new: the\nmodels, migration, service, validators, 10 API routes (9 from FR-35 plus PATCH settings from FR-5), 4 page areas,\n2 tabs, nav entries, seed data and tests. It builds on these existing exports. I checked each one on disk:\n\n| Reuse | Location | Verified signature / note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Schedule | `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts:542` | `getScheduleForDate(target: {userId, role} \\| {sectionId}, date)` → `{period, course, room}[]`. Returns `[]` for ADMIN/PARENT and on non-teaching days. Has the PRD-14 holiday hook comment. `getCurrentSlot(user, now)` at :565 already finds the running period, so use it for the FR-6 highlight. |\n| Notify | `src/server/notifications/notify.ts:98` | `notifyStudentAndParents({...NotifyInput minus userIds, studentIds})` never throws. Title and body are per student, so call it **once per student** (FR-21). |\n| Notif types | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` map + `NotificationTypeDef {label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. The `ATTENDANCE` category already exists. |\n| Access | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | `assertCanManageCourse`, `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanViewStudent`, `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`'ALL' \\| string[]`). |\n| Settings | `src/server/services/settings.ts` | `getSchoolSettings()` (singleton upsert, `cache`d) and `updateSchoolSettings(input)`. **`UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` must gain** `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?`. |\n| Misc | `src/server/audit.ts`, `src/server/csv.ts`, `src/server/http.ts` | `audit(input)`, `toCsv(columns, rows)`, response helpers. |\n| UI | `src/components/<Name>/` | DataTable, StatCard, UserAvatar, PageHeader, EmptyState, ConfirmDialog, DateDisplay, LoadingSkeleton, Toast/useToast. They are **not** in `components/shared/`. |\n| Extension points | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | Arrays of `{key, label, href(id), roles}`. Append entries to them. |\n\nGaps confirmed on disk: `src/app/api/settings/school/` is empty and `src/app/(app)/admin/` has only `courses`,\n`email-log` and `sections`, with no settings page. The latest migration is `20261106000000_user_role_status_index`.\n\nConcern buckets: **Data Model**, **Service**, **Validation**, **API**, **Auth Boundary**, **Notifications**,\n**UI: Register**, **UI: Tabs**, **UI: Admin**, **Config/Nav**, **Seed**, **Tests**, **Cross-cutting**.\n\n## Requirement → Concern table\n\n| Req | Architectural concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | Data Model | New `AttendanceStatus` enum and `AttendanceSession` / `AttendanceRecord` models. Records use `@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` and `@@index([studentId, createdAt])`. `date` is `@db.Date` (NFR-8). The session needs a `takenById`/`updatedById` + `updatedAt` for FR-6/FR-14. Records need `minutesLate Int?` and `note String?` (FR-12). |\n| FR-2 | Data Model + Service | XOR courseId/sectionId: raw SQL `CHECK ((courseId IS NULL) <> (sectionId IS NULL))` in the migration, and a guard in the service before insert. |\n| FR-3 | Data Model (migration SQL) | Two partial unique indexes: `(courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL` and `(sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL`. Prisma can't express these, so they go in hand-written SQL in the migration after `20261106000000`. **Consequence:** `upsert` cannot target them. The service must use `findFirst` + create/update inside the transaction, and catch P2002 on a race. |\n| FR-4 | Data Model | `SchoolSettings.attendanceMode` (new enum `AttendanceMode`, default `PER_PERIOD`) and `attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)`. Same migration. |\n| FR-5 | API + UI: Admin (MEDIUM) | No settings page exists. Smallest fix: `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN, Zod-validated, calls the extended `updateSchoolSettings`) and an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance`. That avoids a new page. |\n| FR-6 | Service + UI: Register | `GET /api/attendance/today` → `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` joined with today's sessions to show \"Taken HH:mm by name\". Highlight comes from `getCurrentSlot`. Times are shown in the school tz. |\n| FR-7 | Service + UI | If mode ∈ {DAILY_HOMEROOM, BOTH}, add entries for `Section.homeroomTeacherId = user` to `/today`. |\n| FR-8 | Validation + Auth Boundary | Shared date rule in the validators: no future date (school tz). Teachers can go back 14 days, admins any date. The same rule runs on the client and the server. |\n| FR-9 | Service + UI: Register | Course roster = `Enrollment` where status ACTIVE on the date, sorted by last name. Use the MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` (exclusive). Initial state is null for a new register. |\n| FR-10 | Auth Boundary + Validation | The server rejects `EXCUSED` from non-ADMIN with 403/VALIDATION_ERROR. The UI disables it for teachers. |\n| FR-11 | UI: Register | Client-only: fill nulls with PRESENT. |\n| FR-12 | Validation + UI | `minutesLate` 1–240 is required iff LATE (Zod `superRefine`) and defaults to 5 in the UI. `note` max 500. |\n| FR-13 | UI: Register | Derived counters. Save is disabled while any row is unmarked. The server also requires a full roster (or at least one valid record per student sent). |\n| FR-14 | Service | One `prisma.$transaction`: find/create the session, then upsert the records (`@@unique([sessionId, studentId])` works for `upsert`). Set `updatedById` on the session. The GET returns last-changed-by/at. |\n| FR-15 | Service + Auth Boundary | Section variant: roster = `SectionMember` for the current academic year. Access = `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` or ADMIN. No existing `assertCanManageSection` helper, so add a small one in the attendance service (or `auth/`). |\n| FR-16 | UI: Register (LOW) | Route `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` component with a section-scoped GET/PUT. |\n| FR-17 | UI: Register | Mobile: rows ≥ 48 px, toggles ≥ 44×44, sticky `Paper` save bar. Use theme `sx` only. |\n| FR-18 | Service + Audit | Inside the save, diff old vs new per student. For changed existing records call `audit({action:'attendance.record.update', before, after, actor, note})`. |\n| FR-19 | Service + Auth Boundary | Pure function `canEdit(user, sessionDate, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today - date ≤ 14 days`. The GET returns `readOnly` + `readOnlyReason`. The PUT returns 403. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-20 | Notifications | Add `attendance.absent` (ATTENDANCE, email true, mandatoryInApp true, PARENT+STUDENT) and `attendance.late` (email false). |\n| FR-21 | Notifications + Service | After commit (outside the tx), call `notifyStudentAndParents` per changed student. Daily-register body: `<Section> daily register, <date>` (intake default). Link `/students/<id>/attendance`. |\n| FR-22 | Notifications + Service | Pure `diffForNotifications(prev, next)` → `{absent[], late[], corrected[]}`. Only a transition *into* ABSENT/LATE sends a notice, so re-saving with the same status sends nothing. ABSENT→PRESENT sends `attendance.corrected`. Unit-tested (FR-39). |\n| FR-23 | Notifications (LOW) | `attendance.corrected` (ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false), `attendance.register_missing` (ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false). |\n| FR-24 | Config | Append `{key:'attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}` to `studentTabs`. |\n| FR-25 | Service + UI: Tabs | Term = the Term containing today, else the most recent ended term (intake default). Use `StatCard` ×4 for term and year. |\n| FR-26 | UI: Tabs | MUI X `DateCalendar` read-only with a custom `day` slot coloured from per-day aggregates and a `Tooltip`. Month change refetches or filters `?from=&to=`. |\n| FR-27 | API + Auth Boundary | `GET /api/students/:id/attendance` → `assertCanViewStudent`. **Strip `note`** for STUDENT/PARENT on the server (AC-8). The table uses `DataTable`. |\n| FR-28 | Service (pure) | `attendanceRate(records)` = (P+L+E)/total×100, rounded to 1 dp; empty → null. Include DROPPED enrollments (filter on student, not enrollment). Mode chooses the source: course sessions (PER_PERIOD/BOTH) or section sessions (DAILY_HOMEROOM). Unit-tested. |\n| FR-29 | API + UI: Tabs + Config | `GET /api/courses/:id/attendance` (`assertCanManageCourse`) → last 20 sessions × enrolled students. Use MUI X DataGrid with dynamic columns. The header click links to the register. Course tab roles: ADMIN, TEACHER. |\n| FR-30 | Service + UI: Admin | Overview: expected = all timetable slots for today (all teachers) + sections if the mode includes daily; taken = sessions today; rate today. ADMIN gets `[]` from `getScheduleForDate`, so it **needs a school-wide slot query** (a direct `timetableSlot.findMany` by `dayOfWeek`, or a new helper next to `getScheduleForDate`). |\n| FR-31 | Service + API + Notifications | Missing = expected meetings with no session and `now ≥ period.startTime + 15 min` (school tz). `POST /api/admin/attendance/remind` → `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[teacherId]})`. |\n| FR-32 | Service + API + Validation | Report filters (range ≤ 366 days, grade, section, course, status) go into a per-student aggregate (use a SQL `groupBy` for performance). `?format=csv` → `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| FR-33 | Service + API | YTD rate per student < threshold, sorted ascending. Reuses the same aggregate as FR-32 with the year's date range. |\n| FR-34 | Config/Nav | `navigation.ts`: TEACHER → `/attendance/take`, ADMIN → `/admin/attendance`. |\n| FR-35 | API | The 9 listed routes, plus PATCH settings from FR-5. Every handler starts with `requireUser`/`requireRole` and then the resource assert. They use the `http.ts` helpers. |\n| FR-36 | Validation | `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts`: `registerQuery`, `registerPutBody`, `studentAttendanceQuery`, `reportFilters`, `remindBody`, `attendanceSettingsPatch`. The register form imports them too. |\n| FR-37 | Service | `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts`. Keep the pure helpers (`attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`) in the same file or a sibling `attendance-rules.ts` so the tests need no DB. |\n| FR-38 | Seed | Extend the existing seed. Use a seeded RNG, 15 teaching days before the run date, 7A and 7B, a 94/3/3 split, and two Grade 7 students forced below 85%. Respect the existing school-day config. |\n| FR-39 | Tests (unit) | `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`, `diffForNotifications`. |\n| FR-40 | Tests (integration) | The save transaction, non-enrolled rejection (NFR-3), and the partial unique indexes (a duplicate insert raises). |\n| FR-41 | Tests (e2e) | Playwright: the 375 px take flow, and a parent seeing the notification plus the calendar absence. |\n| NFR-1 | Performance | Save: one tx with batched upserts (≈35). Avoid N+1 by loading existing records in one query. Student tab: one indexed query on `[studentId, createdAt]` (consider filtering on `session.date` and adding an index if needed). Aggregate in memory (1,200 rows is fine). |\n| NFR-2 | UI: Register (client) | localStorage key `attendance:<course\\|section>:<id>:<date>:<periodId\\|daily>`. Write it on a network failure, clear it on success, and offer a restore banner when it is present. |\n| NFR-3 | Service (integrity) | Validate every `studentId` against the ACTIVE enrollment on the date (`enrolledAt ≤ date` and not dropped before it) or the section membership. Any miss → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR and the whole save is rejected. |\n| NFR-4 | UI: Register | Satisfied by FR-11 + FR-17 (mark all present, then fix the exceptions). |\n| NFR-5 | Notifications | `notify()` writes in-app notifications immediately and queues EmailOutbox. Call it post-commit without blocking the response on email. |\n| NFR-6 | Cross-cutting (UI) | MUI only. Dev must use mui-mcp docs for 9.5.0 (ToggleButtonGroup, DateCalendar day slot, DataGrid, Paper sticky). **Hard blocker if unreachable.** |\n| NFR-7 | Auth Boundary | Server-side checks on every handler and server page. Per-role scope is listed above. Teachers also get their homeroom sections. |\n| NFR-8 | Cross-cutting | `@db.Date`, cuid IDs, UTC storage with display in school tz (`date-fns-tz`, already installed), the logger, `audit()` for edits to records owned by others, and pageSize ≤ 100 on the report and student records. |\n| NFR-9 | UI accessibility | `aria-label` on each toggle (\"Mark <name> present\"), 44 px targets. |\n| NFR-10 | Cross-cutting | Reuse the helpers above, add no new deps, rename nothing. Holidays (PRD-14) and the EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) are out of scope beyond the admin-only option. |\n\n## Open points for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **Intake blockers (for the Overview):** FR-5 (MEDIUM), FR-16 (LOW), FR-23 (LOW) and the NFR-6 mui-mcp hard dependency. The defaults are listed above.\n2. **Partial unique indexes vs Prisma upsert (FR-3/FR-14):** sessions can't be `upsert`ed via Prisma. Use find + create in the tx and catch P2002 → retry as an update.\n3. **Admin school-wide schedule (FR-30/31):** `getScheduleForDate` returns `[]` for ADMIN. It needs a school-wide slot query. Prefer a small exported helper in `timetable-service.ts` over duplicating `slotInclude` logic.\n4. **Section access helper (FR-15):** none exists today. Add one small function and don't generalise it.\n5. **\"ACTIVE on date\" (NFR-3):** `Enrollment` has `enrolledAt`/`droppedAt`. Define the rule as `enrolledAt ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt > date)`. For back-dated registers, the roster should use the same rule.\n6. **Rate source by mode (FR-28):** in BOTH mode, rates use the per-period records only. Daily records are stored but not counted.\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1,"totalLines":95}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FpDMGZMFsmCD4PFj97piBD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
