{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8P8cqcx8nGb8x6VFvi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1648,"cache_read_input_tokens":57800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1648},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90141260-d1a7-451a-8239-c83fc1554359","uuid":"1b5a4025-5700-41af-9c58-75d588ac4227","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:32:51.232Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8P8AJ6RMvECKUn2fFs","thinking_duration_ms":1485,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8P8cqcx8nGb8x6VFvi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011vT6DBPfhH3vCoRCQSRhDw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5\nand MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet\n(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is\nbuilt around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages\nsits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,\nsettings, and the tab and nav configs.\n\n**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas\n(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.\n**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |\n| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |\n| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |\n| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |\n| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)\n\n| Module | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |\n| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |\n| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |\n| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |\n| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |\n| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |\n| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |\n| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |\n\n### 2.2 New components\n\n#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)\n\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):\n\n```prisma\nenum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }\nenum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }\n\nmodel AttendanceSession {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)\n  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  sectionId   String?\n  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily\n  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])\n  date        DateTime @db.Date\n  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"\n  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])\n  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"\n  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n  records     AttendanceRecord[]\n\n  @@index([date])\n}\n\nmodel AttendanceRecord {\n  id          String            @id @default(cuid())\n  sessionId   String\n  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  status      AttendanceStatus\n  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE\n  note        String?           // ≤ 500\n  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId, createdAt])\n}\n// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)\n```\n\nBack-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).\n\nThe migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):\n- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n\nThe test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.\n\n#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nAdd one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It\nfollows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current\nyear, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which\nthe overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.\n\n#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)\n\nThis file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.\n- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.\n- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).\n- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.\n- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.\n- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.\n- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).\n- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).\n\n#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)\n\n| Function | Reqs | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |\n| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |\n| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |\n| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |\n| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |\n| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |\n| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |\n| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |\n| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |\n\n**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**\n- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.\n- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year.\n\n**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default).\n\n#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)\n\n| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |\n\n#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)\n\nThese schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:\n- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).\n- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.\n- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.\n- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.\n- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.\n- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.\n\nRole-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the\nuser, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.\n\n#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)\n\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):\n  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.\n  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.\n  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.\n  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".\n  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).\n  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.\n\n#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)\n\n`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:\n- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.\n- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.\n- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.\n\n#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)\n\n`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:\n- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).\n- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.\n- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.\n- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).\n\nOne page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.\n\n#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)\n\n`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20\ndynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to\n`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.\n\n#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)\n\n- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.\n- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.\n- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.\n\n#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)\n\n- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.\n- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.\n- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.\n- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response.\n\n### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)\n\n```\nRegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)\n  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection\n  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).\n  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).\n  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {\n       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).\n       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).\n       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).\n       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.\n       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).\n       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).\n       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).\n     })\n  5. After commit:\n       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)\n       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)\n         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"\n         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"\n         link  /students/<id>/attendance\n  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET).\n```\n\nBrand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies\nonce. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).\n\n### 3.3 Read flows\n\n- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).\n- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.\n- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.\n- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.\n\n### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)\n\nAll \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`\nvalues. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.\n\n---\n\n## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)\n\n| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |\n| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |\n| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |\n| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |\n| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |\n| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |\n| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |\n\nAll 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |\n| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |\n| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |\n| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |\n| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |\n| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |\n| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |\n| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |\n| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |\n| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |\n| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |\n| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |\n| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |\n| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |\n| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |\n| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |\n| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |\n| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |\n| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |\n| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |\n| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |\n| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |\n| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |\n| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |\n| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |\n| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |\n| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |\n| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |\n| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |\n| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |\n| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |\n| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |\n| FR-35 | §4 route table |\n| FR-36 | C6 validators |\n| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |\n| FR-38 | C12 seed |\n| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |\n| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |\n| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |\n| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |\n| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |\n| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |\n| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |\n| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |\n| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |\n| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |\n| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out of scope\n\nHoliday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),\nautomatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first\nservice workers (ADR-7).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1648,"cache_read_input_tokens":57800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1648},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90141260-d1a7-451a-8239-c83fc1554359","uuid":"e9b3b1a9-daac-44bd-84b3-f3ccd5beb0d4","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:34:21.033Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8P8AJ6RMvECKUn2fFs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011vT6DBPfhH3vCoRCQSRhDw":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5\nand MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet\n(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is\nbuilt around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages\nsits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,\nsettings, and the tab and nav configs.\n\n**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas\n(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.\n**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |\n| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |\n| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |\n| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |\n| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)\n\n| Module | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |\n| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |\n| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |\n| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |\n| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |\n| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |\n| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |\n| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |\n\n### 2.2 New components\n\n#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)\n\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):\n\n```prisma\nenum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }\nenum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }\n\nmodel AttendanceSession {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)\n  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  sectionId   String?\n  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily\n  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])\n  date        DateTime @db.Date\n  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"\n  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])\n  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"\n  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n  records     AttendanceRecord[]\n\n  @@index([date])\n}\n\nmodel AttendanceRecord {\n  id          String            @id @default(cuid())\n  sessionId   String\n  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  status      AttendanceStatus\n  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE\n  note        String?           // ≤ 500\n  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId, createdAt])\n}\n// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)\n```\n\nBack-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).\n\nThe migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):\n- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n\nThe test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.\n\n#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nAdd one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It\nfollows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current\nyear, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which\nthe overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.\n\n#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)\n\nThis file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.\n- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.\n- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).\n- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.\n- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.\n- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.\n- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).\n- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).\n\n#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)\n\n| Function | Reqs | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |\n| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |\n| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |\n| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |\n| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |\n| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |\n| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |\n| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |\n| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |\n\n**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**\n- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.\n- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year.\n\n**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default).\n\n#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)\n\n| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |\n\n#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)\n\nThese schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:\n- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).\n- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.\n- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.\n- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.\n- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.\n- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.\n\nRole-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the\nuser, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.\n\n#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)\n\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):\n  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.\n  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.\n  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.\n  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".\n  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).\n  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.\n\n#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)\n\n`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:\n- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.\n- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.\n- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.\n\n#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)\n\n`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:\n- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).\n- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.\n- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.\n- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).\n\nOne page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.\n\n#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)\n\n`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20\ndynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to\n`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.\n\n#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)\n\n- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.\n- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.\n- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.\n\n#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)\n\n- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.\n- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.\n- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.\n- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response.\n\n### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)\n\n```\nRegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)\n  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection\n  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).\n  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).\n  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {\n       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).\n       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).\n       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).\n       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.\n       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).\n       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).\n       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).\n     })\n  5. After commit:\n       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)\n       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)\n         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"\n         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"\n         link  /students/<id>/attendance\n  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET).\n```\n\nBrand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies\nonce. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).\n\n### 3.3 Read flows\n\n- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).\n- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.\n- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.\n- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.\n\n### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)\n\nAll \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`\nvalues. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.\n\n---\n\n## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)\n\n| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |\n| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |\n| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |\n| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |\n| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |\n| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |\n| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |\n\nAll 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |\n| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |\n| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |\n| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |\n| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |\n| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |\n| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |\n| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |\n| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |\n| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |\n| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |\n| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |\n| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |\n| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |\n| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |\n| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |\n| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |\n| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |\n| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |\n| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |\n| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |\n| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |\n| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |\n| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |\n| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |\n| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |\n| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |\n| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |\n| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |\n| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |\n| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |\n| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |\n| FR-35 | §4 route table |\n| FR-36 | C6 validators |\n| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |\n| FR-38 | C12 seed |\n| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |\n| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |\n| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |\n| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |\n| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |\n| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |\n| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |\n| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |\n| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |\n| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |\n| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out of scope\n\nHoliday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),\nautomatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first\nservice workers (ADR-7).\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011vT6DBPfhH3vCoRCQSRhDw","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90141260-d1a7-451a-8239-c83fc1554359","uuid":"7cdad3b6-45d7-4db4-9bf3-bb587d3c0fa9","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:34:21.159Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5\nand MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet\n(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is\nbuilt around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages\nsits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,\nsettings, and the tab and nav configs.\n\n**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas\n(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.\n**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |\n| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |\n| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |\n| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |\n| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)\n\n| Module | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |\n| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |\n| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |\n| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |\n| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |\n| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |\n| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |\n| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |\n\n### 2.2 New components\n\n#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)\n\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):\n\n```prisma\nenum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }\nenum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }\n\nmodel AttendanceSession {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)\n  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  sectionId   String?\n  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily\n  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])\n  date        DateTime @db.Date\n  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"\n  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])\n  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"\n  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n  records     AttendanceRecord[]\n\n  @@index([date])\n}\n\nmodel AttendanceRecord {\n  id          String            @id @default(cuid())\n  sessionId   String\n  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  status      AttendanceStatus\n  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE\n  note        String?           // ≤ 500\n  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId, createdAt])\n}\n// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)\n```\n\nBack-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).\n\nThe migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):\n- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n\nThe test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.\n\n#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nAdd one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It\nfollows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current\nyear, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which\nthe overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.\n\n#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)\n\nThis file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.\n- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.\n- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).\n- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.\n- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.\n- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.\n- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).\n- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).\n\n#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)\n\n| Function | Reqs | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |\n| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |\n| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |\n| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |\n| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |\n| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |\n| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |\n| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |\n| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |\n\n**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**\n- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.\n- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year.\n\n**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default).\n\n#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)\n\n| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |\n\n#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)\n\nThese schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:\n- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).\n- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.\n- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.\n- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.\n- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.\n- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.\n\nRole-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the\nuser, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.\n\n#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)\n\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):\n  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.\n  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.\n  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.\n  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".\n  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).\n  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.\n\n#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)\n\n`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:\n- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.\n- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.\n- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.\n\n#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)\n\n`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:\n- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).\n- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.\n- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.\n- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).\n\nOne page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.\n\n#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)\n\n`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20\ndynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to\n`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.\n\n#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)\n\n- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.\n- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.\n- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.\n\n#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)\n\n- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.\n- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.\n- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.\n- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response.\n\n### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)\n\n```\nRegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)\n  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection\n  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).\n  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).\n  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {\n       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).\n       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).\n       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).\n       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.\n       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).\n       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).\n       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).\n     })\n  5. After commit:\n       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)\n       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)\n         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"\n         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"\n         link  /students/<id>/attendance\n  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET).\n```\n\nBrand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies\nonce. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).\n\n### 3.3 Read flows\n\n- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).\n- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.\n- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.\n- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.\n\n### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)\n\nAll \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`\nvalues. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.\n\n---\n\n## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)\n\n| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |\n| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |\n| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |\n| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |\n| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |\n| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |\n| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |\n\nAll 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |\n| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |\n| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |\n| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |\n| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |\n| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |\n| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |\n| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |\n| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |\n| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |\n| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |\n| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |\n| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |\n| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |\n| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |\n| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |\n| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |\n| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |\n| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |\n| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |\n| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |\n| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |\n| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |\n| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |\n| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |\n| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |\n| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |\n| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |\n| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |\n| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |\n| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |\n| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |\n| FR-35 | §4 route table |\n| FR-36 | C6 validators |\n| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |\n| FR-38 | C12 seed |\n| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |\n| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |\n| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |\n| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |\n| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |\n| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |\n| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |\n| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |\n| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |\n| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |\n| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out of scope\n\nHoliday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),\nautomatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first\nservice workers (ADR-7).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":197,"newStart":1,"newLines":353,"lines":["-# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)","+# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)"," ","-Ticket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),","-`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and","-`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Ticket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),","+`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status","-> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.","+> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder."," "," ---"," "," ## 1. Overview"," ","-SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5","-Credentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`","-(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate","-limiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.","+SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5","+and MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet","+(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is","+built around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages","+sits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,","+settings, and the tab and nav configs."," ","-**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the","-`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**","-(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).","+**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas","+(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.","+**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8)."," "," ### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)"," "," | # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |"," |---|---|---|","-| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |","-| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |","-| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |","-| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |","-| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |","+| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |","+| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |","+| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |","+| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |","+| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |","+| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |"," ","-### Additional risks found during design","-","-- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the","-  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`","-  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.","-- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept","-  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.","-- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).","-  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.","-"," ---"," "," ## 2. Component Breakdown"," ","-### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)","+### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)"," ","-| Module | Provides | Reqs |","+| Module | Used for |","+|---|---|","+| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |","+| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |","+| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |","+| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |","+| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |","+| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |","+| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |","+| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |","+| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |","+| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |","+| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |","+","+### 2.2 New components","+","+#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)","+","+`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):","+","+```prisma","+enum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }","+enum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }","+","+model AttendanceSession {","+  id          String   @id @default(cuid())","+  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)","+  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","+  sectionId   String?","+  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","+  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily","+  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])","+  date        DateTime @db.Date","+  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"","+  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])","+  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"","+  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])","+  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())","+  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt","+  records     AttendanceRecord[]","+","+  @@index([date])","+}","+","+model AttendanceRecord {","+  id          String            @id @default(cuid())","+  sessionId   String","+  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","+  studentId   String","+  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])","+  status      AttendanceStatus","+  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE","+  note        String?           // ≤ 500","+  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())","+  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt","+","+  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])","+  @@index([studentId, createdAt])","+}","+// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)","+```","+","+Back-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).","+","+The migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):","+- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)","+- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)","+- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)","+","+The test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.","+","+#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)","+","+Add one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It","+follows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current","+year, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which","+the overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.","+","+#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)","+","+This file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.","+- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.","+- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).","+- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.","+- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.","+- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.","+- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).","+- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).","+","+#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)","+","+| Function | Reqs | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |","-| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |","-| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |","-| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |","-| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |","-| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |","-| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |","-| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |","-| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |","+| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |","+| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |","+| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |","+| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |","+| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |","+| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |","+| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |","+| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |","+| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |","+| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |"," ","-Do not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).","+**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**","+- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.","+- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year."," ","-### 2.2 New and modified components","+**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default)."," ","-| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |","+#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)","+","+| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |"," |---|---|---|---|---|","-| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |","-| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |","-| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |","-| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |","-| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |","-| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |","-| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |","-| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |","-| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |","+| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |","+| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |","+| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |","+| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |"," ","-**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,","-`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and","-`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).","-Copy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).","+#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)"," ","+These schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:","+- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.","+- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).","+- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.","+- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.","+- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.","+- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.","+- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.","+","+Role-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the","+user, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.","+","+#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)","+","+- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.","+- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.","+- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):","+  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.","+  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.","+  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.","+  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".","+  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).","+  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.","+","+#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)","+","+`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:","+- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.","+- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.","+- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.","+","+#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)","+","+`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:","+- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).","+- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.","+- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.","+- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).","+","+One page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.","+","+#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)","+","+`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20","+dynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to","+`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.","+","+#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)","+","+- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.","+- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.","+- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.","+","+#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)","+","+- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.","+- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.","+- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.","+- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.","+"," ---"," "," ## 3. Data Flow"," ","-**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**","-```","-/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)","-       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox","-link ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)","-C4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)","-       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state","-```","+### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)"," ","-**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**","-```","-/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)","-C4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}","-C4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')","-```","+`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response."," ","-**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**","-```","-/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword","-   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min","-   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error","-```","+### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)"," ","-**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**"," ```","-request ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),","-           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})","+RegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)","+  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection","+  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).","+  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).","+  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {","+       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).","+       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).","+       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).","+       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.","+       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).","+       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).","+       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).","+     })","+  5. After commit:","+       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)","+       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)","+         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"","+         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"","+         link  /students/<id>/attendance","+  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET)."," ```"," ","+Brand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies","+once. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).","+","+### 3.3 Read flows","+","+- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).","+- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.","+- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.","+- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.","+","+### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)","+","+All \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`","+values. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.","+"," ---"," ","-## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions","+## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)"," ","-1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server","-   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).","-   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).","-2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context","-   (FR-25, ADR-2).","-3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).","-   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.","-4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`","-   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.","-5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The","-   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).","-6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).","+| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |","+| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |","+| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |","+| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |","+| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |","+| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |","+| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |","+| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |","+| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |","+| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |"," ","+All 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).","+"," ---"," "," ## 5. Requirements Traceability"," "," | Req | Design element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |","-| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |","-| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |","-| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |","-| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |","-| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |","-| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |","-| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |","-| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |","-| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |","-| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |","-| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |","-| FR-13 | C3 |","-| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |","-| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |","-| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |","-| FR-17 | C1 |","-| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |","-| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |","-| FR-20 | C5; C8 |","-| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |","-| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |","-| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |","-| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |","-| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |","-| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |","-| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |","-| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |","-| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |","-| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |","-| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |","-| FR-34 | C8, C9 |","-| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |","-| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |","-| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |","-| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |","-| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |","-| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |","-| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |","-| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |","-| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |","-| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |","-| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |","-| NFR-12 | §4.6 |","-| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |","-| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |","-| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |","+| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |","+| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |","+| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |","+| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |","+| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |","+| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |","+| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |","+| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |","+| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |","+| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |","+| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |","+| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |","+| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |","+| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |","+| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |","+| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |","+| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |","+| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |","+| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |","+| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |","+| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |","+| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |","+| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |","+| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |","+| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |","+| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |","+| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |","+| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |","+| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |","+| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |","+| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |","+| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |","+| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |","+| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |","+| FR-35 | §4 route table |","+| FR-36 | C6 validators |","+| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |","+| FR-38 | C12 seed |","+| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |","+| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |","+| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |","+| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |","+| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |","+| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |","+| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |","+| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |","+| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |","+| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |","+| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |","+| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |","+| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |"," "," ---"," ","-## 6. Change Footprint","+## 6. Out of scope"," ","-- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,","-  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,","-  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,","-  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.","-- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.","-- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,","-  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.","+Holiday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),","+automatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first","+service workers (ADR-7)."]}],"originalFile":"# System Design — SH-1 · PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC (SCH-001)\n\nTicket: SH-1 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (re-run 2026-11-05T16:26:09Z; 34 FR + 15 NFR, 97%),\n`handoff-to-architect.json` (5 blockers), `tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1…ADR-5) and\n`requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1…B14). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the earlier SH-1 design (11:41). That version planned the seed users, the role/status\n> migration and `/login` as new work. All three are now on disk, so they have been removed from scope.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL, Auth.js v5\nCredentials + JWT, MUI 9.5). The whole PRD-01 backend already exists: models, `tokens.ts`, `credentials.ts`\n(lockout, `DUMMY_HASH`), the JWT session with its 5-minute `passwordChangedAt` recheck, middleware, the rate\nlimiter, audit, validators, services, all five API routes, `/login`, the seed and the `[role, status]` index.\n\n**This ticket covers UI gaps, shell wiring and tests.** It adds 4 pages and 3 small client forms, rewires the\n`(app)` layout and shell, and adds tests. It adds **no API endpoint, service, model, migration or dependency**\n(ADR-1, ADR-5, NFR-13).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | BROWNFIELD: design only the gaps. | §2.1 lists the existing modules as **reuse, do not modify**. New work is C1–C9 only. |\n| 2 | GAPS: 3 `(auth)` pages, `/account/security`, removing `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and wiring the user, badge, initials, signOut and menu item, plus integration and e2e tests. | C1–C9. |\n| 3 | REUSE: TextFormField, PasswordChecklist/passwordInputSlot, useToast, safeCallbackUrl, the existing API routes. | Every new component below is built from these. It also reuses `SetPasswordForm`, `postJson` and `applyFieldErrors` (B2). |\n| 4 | **FR-32 (LOW):** `AuditLog.ip` vs the PRD's `ipAddress`. | Keep `ip` and the existing indexes. No migration. **Needs human sign-off.** |\n| 5 | **NFR-6:** dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. | **Hard gate.** Before writing JSX, dev looks up every MUI component named in §2 with `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` (@mui/material@9.5.0). If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports it; no guessing. mui-mcp was connected when this design was written. |\n\n### Additional risks found during design\n\n- **R1 (B14):** `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts` calls `page.goto('/dashboard')` without signing in. Once the\n  `(app)` layout calls `requirePageUser()` (C6), that spec has to sign in first. `notifications.spec.ts`\n  already has a local `signIn(page)` helper. C9 moves it into a shared helper, and both specs use that.\n- **R2 (B5):** an invalid token returns `410 INVALID_TOKEN`, which is not in the NFR-10 code list. This is kept\n  as-is (NFR-13). The token forms treat a 410 as \"link invalid\" and switch to that state.\n- **R3:** intake's FR-6 \"UI message MISSING\" is out of date. `loginErrorMessage` already maps `rate_limited` (B7).\n  Dev verifies this and builds nothing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules — reuse, do not modify (NFR-13)\n\n| Module | Provides | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `prisma/schema.prisma`, migrations, `prisma/seed.ts` | Models, enums, `[role,status]` index, 6 ACTIVE + 1 INVITED seed user | FR-1, FR-28–FR-30, FR-32, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/auth/{auth,auth.config,credentials,tokens,requireRole}.ts` | Auth.js, authorize/lockout/dummy hash, JWT 8h + recheck, token hashing, `getCurrentUser`/`requireUser`/`requireRole`/`requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`, `SessionUser` | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8–FR-10, FR-12, FR-23, NFR-1–NFR-3 |\n| `src/middleware.ts`, `src/config/public-routes.ts` | Redirect to `/login?callbackUrl=`, 401 JSON; the `(auth)` paths are already public | FR-11, NFR-14 |\n| `src/server/{rate-limit,audit}.ts`, `src/server/services/{auth,users}.ts`, `src/server/auth/email.ts` | Limiter, `audit()`, `acceptInvite`/`requestPasswordReset`/`resetPassword`/`changePassword`, user services, `sendAuthEmail` → EmailOutbox | FR-6, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-22, FR-24, FR-31, NFR-8 |\n| `src/app/api/auth/**`, `src/app/api/account/password` | The 5 routes (see `api-contracts.json`) | FR-14, FR-17, FR-19, FR-20, NFR-10 |\n| `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` | `forgotPasswordSchema`, `setPasswordSchema(email)`, `changePasswordFormSchema(email)`, `PASSWORD_RULES`, `safeCallbackUrl` | FR-7, FR-15, NFR-11 |\n| `src/app/(auth)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**` | Centred Card shell; login page with the `?reset=1` toast | FR-2, FR-4, FR-6, FR-7, FR-19 |\n| `src/components/PasswordChecklist` | `PasswordChecklist`, `SetPasswordForm({name?, email, submitLabel?, onSubmit})`, `postJson`, `applyFieldErrors`, `passwordInputSlot`, `ApiFailure` | FR-16, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/components/FormField` (`TextFormField`), `src/components/Toast/useToast`, `src/components/UserAvatar` | RHF text field, Snackbar+Alert toast, initials avatar | FR-17, FR-20, FR-26, NFR-6 |\n\nDo not touch `course-access.ts` or `student-access.ts` (NFR-13).\n\n### 2.2 New and modified components\n\n| Id | File | Kind | What it does | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **C1** | `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/page.tsx` + `ForgotPasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | RHF with `zodResolver(forgotPasswordSchema)` and `TextFormField` for email. Submits with `postJson('/api/auth/forgot-password', {email})`. A 2xx shows a success `Alert` with `data.message` (the server's `RESET_REQUESTED_MESSAGE`, so the copy is never retyped). A 429 shows an error `Alert` with \"Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.\" Known and unknown emails always get the same success copy, so the page reveals nothing about which accounts exist. Includes a \"Back to sign in\" link. | FR-17, FR-18, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| **C2** | `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'PASSWORD_RESET')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with \"This link is invalid or has expired.\" and a link to `/forgot-password`. Otherwise render `TokenPasswordForm` (C4) with `mode=\"reset\"` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-19, NFR-1 |\n| **C3** | `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx` | Server page | `verifyToken(params.token, 'INVITE')`. If it returns null, show an `Alert` with the FR-13 copy: \"This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.\" Otherwise render C4 with `mode=\"invite\"`, `name = firstName + ' ' + lastName` and `email`. | FR-12, FR-13, NFR-1 |\n| **C4** | `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx` | Client form (shared by C2 and C3) | Wraps `SetPasswordForm` (read-only name/email, new + confirm password, `PasswordChecklist`). `onSubmit` calls `postJson('/api/auth/{accept-invite\\|reset-password}', {token, password, confirmPassword})`. On **410** it switches to the page's invalid-link `Alert` (R2). Any other failure is returned so `SetPasswordForm` can call `applyFieldErrors`. **Invite success:** `signIn('credentials', {email, password, redirect: false})`, then `router.replace('/dashboard')`. **Reset success:** `router.replace('/login?reset=1')`, and the existing LoginForm toast fires. The raw token is only ever a prop; it is never logged. | FR-14, FR-15, FR-16, FR-19, NFR-5, NFR-8 |\n| **C5** | `src/app/(app)/account/security/page.tsx` + `ChangePasswordForm.tsx` | Server page + client form | The page calls `requirePageUser()` and passes `email`. The form uses RHF with `zodResolver(changePasswordFormSchema(email))`: three password `TextField`s with `passwordInputSlot`, a `PasswordChecklist` under the new password, and an `Alert` with `aria-live=\"polite\"`. It submits with `postJson('/api/account/password', …)`. A 400 with `fieldErrors.currentPassword` goes through `applyFieldErrors`, which shows \"Current password is incorrect.\" Success shows the `useToast` toast \"Password updated\", resets the form and calls `router.refresh()`. The route already re-issues the session (`unstable_update({reauth:true})`), and other devices drop off within 5 minutes through the `passwordChangedAt` recheck. | FR-10, FR-16, FR-20, NFR-5, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| **C6** | `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx` (modify) | Server layout | Adds `const user = await requirePageUser()`, a second guard behind the middleware. Passes `user={{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}}` to `AppShell`. This prop is the **only** source of the current user. There is no `SessionProvider` or `useSession` (ADR-2). | FR-23, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| **C7** | `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx` (modify) | Client shell | Deletes `PLACEHOLDER_USER` and adds `user: SessionUser` to `AppShellProps` (imported as `import type`). Uses `navigationForRole(user.role)`. The top bar shows `UserAvatar userId={user.id} name={fullName}` (initials), the full name in `Typography` and the role in a `Chip`. The menu items are **\"Account security\"** (`MenuItem component={Link} href=\"/account/security\"`) and **\"Sign out\"** (`signOut({ redirectTo: '/login' })` from `next-auth/react`). Any other existing menu items that are placeholders and only close the menu get one of these two actions. | FR-21, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27 |\n| **C8** | `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` | Vitest, node env | `describe.runIf(process.env.TEST_DATABASE_URL)`, following the `email-dispatch.test.ts` precedent. Resets the limiter in `beforeEach`. **authorize:** unknown email, wrong password, disabled, archived, locked → `locked:N`, 5th failure locks and writes `auth.lockout`, rate limited, success resets the count and sets `lastLoginAt` and `auth.login.success`. **acceptInvite:** ACTIVE status, `passwordChangedAt` set, token consumed, reuse → `INVALID_TOKEN`. **reset:** a known email creates a token and an EmailOutbox row; an unknown email creates no token; reset clears the lockout fields and the token can't be reused. **changePassword:** a wrong current password returns a field error; success bumps `passwordChangedAt`. Also asserts that no audit metadata contains `password` or `token`. One file, so there is no extra fixture plumbing. | FR-3, FR-5, FR-8, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-20, FR-34, NFR-8 |\n| **C9** | `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts` + `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`; modify `dashboard.spec.ts` and `notifications.spec.ts` | Playwright | The helper `signInAs(page, email, password = 'SchoolHub123!')` is moved out of `notifications.spec.ts`. **`auth.spec.ts`** (serial): admin signs in, the user menu shows \"Alice Admin\" and ADMIN, signs out and lands on `/login`. A wrong password shows \"Email or password is incorrect.\" An unauthenticated `/dashboard` goes to `/login?callbackUrl=%2Fdashboard`. Forgot → reset for `student2@`: the test reads the newest EmailOutbox row via `@prisma/client` in the test process (no test-only app route), opens the link, sets a new password, sees the `/login` toast and signs in with it. One `AxeBuilder` scan of `/login` and `/forgot-password`. `dashboard.spec.ts` signs in first (R1). | FR-2, FR-4, FR-7, FR-11, FR-17, FR-19, FR-26, FR-34, NFR-5, NFR-13 |\n\n**MUI components used** (all need an NFR-6 lookup first): `Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `TextField`, `Button`,\n`Alert`, `Link` (MUI, `component={NextLink}`), `Chip`, `Menu`, `MenuItem`, `ListItemIcon`, `InputAdornment` and\n`IconButton` (via `passwordInputSlot`), plus `@mui/icons-material` `LockOutlined`/`Logout`. No banned libraries (NFR-7).\nCopy is English only, on stock MUI (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Forgot → reset (FR-17–FR-19)**\n```\n/forgot-password (C1) ──POST /api/auth/forgot-password──► requestPasswordReset ──► createToken(PASSWORD_RESET, 60m)\n       ◄── 200 {data:{message}} or 429 ─────────────────            └─► sendAuthEmail ──► EmailOutbox\nlink ► /reset-password/[t] (C2, server) ──verifyToken──► null? invalid Alert : C4(email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/reset-password──► resetPassword (hash, passwordChangedAt, clear lockout, consume, audit)\n       ◄── 200 → router.replace('/login?reset=1') → LoginForm toast   │ 410 → invalid-link state\n```\n\n**Invite (FR-13, FR-14)**\n```\n/invite/[t] (C3, server) ──verifyToken(INVITE)──► null? FR-13 Alert : C4(name, email)\nC4 ──POST /api/auth/accept-invite──► acceptInvite (ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt, consume, audit) ── 200 {email}\nC4 ──signIn('credentials', {email,password,redirect:false})──► /api/auth/callback ──► router.replace('/dashboard')\n```\n\n**Change password (FR-20, FR-10)**\n```\n/account/security (C5; requirePageUser) ──POST /api/account/password──► requireUser → changePassword\n   ──► passwordChangedAt=now ──► unstable_update({reauth}) keeps this session; other JWTs fail recheck ≤5 min\n   ◄── 200 → toast \"Password updated\" │ 400 fieldErrors.currentPassword → field error\n```\n\n**Current user (FR-25–FR-27)**\n```\nrequest ─► middleware (FR-11) ─► (app)/layout.tsx: requirePageUser() ─► <AppShell user> ─► navigationForRole(user.role),\n           avatar/name/Chip, menu: Account security → /account/security, Sign out → signOut({redirectTo:'/login'})\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Patterns and Decisions\n\n1. **Verify on the server, mutate through the API.** The token pages call `verifyToken` (a read-only call) in a Server\n   Component, so an expired link never renders a form. Mutations go through the existing thin routes (NFR-10).\n   Only `tokens.ts` touches token hashes (FR-12, NFR-1).\n2. **One user source.** The layout passes the user to the shell as a prop. The design adds no session context\n   (FR-25, ADR-2).\n3. **Shared schemas.** Client forms use the same `src/lib/validators/auth.ts` schemas as the routes (NFR-11).\n   Server field errors come back through `applyFieldErrors`.\n4. **Accessibility comes from reuse.** Every form has one `aria-live=\"polite\"` `Alert`, RHF `shouldFocusError`\n   and `helperText` (NFR-5). `SetPasswordForm` already does this, and C1 and C5 copy the same pattern.\n5. **Server-side enforcement.** `/account/security` and the whole `(app)` group call `requirePageUser`. The\n   API calls `requireUser`. Hiding a menu item is never the only protection (NFR-9).\n6. **Logging.** New code uses `logger` only and never logs tokens or passwords (NFR-8, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 schema (unchanged) |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `/login` (verify only); C9 e2e |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `credentials.ts`; C8 |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `loginErrorMessage`; C9 wrong-password test |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `computeLockout`; C8 |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 limiter + `loginErrorMessage` (R3, verify); C8 rate-limit case |\n| FR-7 | §2.1 `safeCallbackUrl`; C9 callbackUrl test |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 authorize audit; C8 AuditLog asserts |\n| FR-9 | §2.1 `auth.config.ts` (unchanged); C6 passes the session fields |\n| FR-10 | §2.1 recheck; C5 flow; C8 changePassword |\n| FR-11 | §2.1 middleware; C9 unauthenticated redirect |\n| FR-12 | C2, C3 use `verifyToken` only |\n| FR-13 | C3 |\n| FR-14 | C4 invite branch; C8 acceptInvite |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 validators; C4/C5 `applyFieldErrors` |\n| FR-16 | C4 (via `SetPasswordForm`), C5 `PasswordChecklist` |\n| FR-17 | C1 |\n| FR-18 | §2.1 `requestPasswordReset`; C8 |\n| FR-19 | C2, C4 reset branch; C8; C9 forgot→reset |\n| FR-20 | C5; C8 |\n| FR-21 | C7 \"Account security\" item |\n| FR-22 | §2.1 `services/users.ts` (verify only) |\n| FR-23 | §2.1 `requireRole.ts`; C5, C6 `requirePageUser` |\n| FR-24 | §2.1 `audit.ts` |\n| FR-25 | C6, C7 (delete `PLACEHOLDER_USER`) |\n| FR-26 | C7 avatar/name/Chip/Sign out; C9 sign-out test |\n| FR-27 | C7 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |\n| FR-28, FR-29, FR-30 | §2.1 seed (unchanged); C9 uses the seed users |\n| FR-31 | §2.1 `email.ts` (unchanged); C9 reads EmailOutbox |\n| FR-32 | §1 blocker 4: keep `ip` |\n| FR-33 | §2.1 migration (present) |\n| FR-34 | C8, C9 |\n| NFR-1 | C2, C3 via `tokens.ts`; §4.1 |\n| NFR-2 | Auth.js defaults; C4 uses `next-auth/react` `signIn` (CSRF) |\n| NFR-3 | §2.1 `DUMMY_HASH` |\n| NFR-4 | Unchanged authorize path (one bcrypt-12 compare) |\n| NFR-5 | C1, C4, C5 (§4.4); C9 axe scan |\n| NFR-6 | §1 blocker 5; §2.2 MUI list |\n| NFR-7 | §2.2 MUI-only; no new dependency (ADR-1) |\n| NFR-8 | C4 token prop only; C8 metadata assert; §4.6 |\n| NFR-9 | C5, C6; §4.5 |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 existing routes; R2 |\n| NFR-11 | C1, C4, C5; §4.3 |\n| NFR-12 | §4.6 |\n| NFR-13 | §2.1 do-not-modify list; R1; lint, typecheck and test stay green |\n| NFR-14 | §2.1 public routes have no sign-up; no sign-up page is added |\n| NFR-15 | §2.2 English copy, stock MUI |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Change Footprint\n\n- **New:** `src/app/(auth)/forgot-password/{page,ForgotPasswordForm}.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/reset-password/[token]/page.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx`, `src/app/(auth)/TokenPasswordForm.tsx`,\n  `src/app/(app)/account/security/{page,ChangePasswordForm}.tsx`, `tests/integration/auth.test.ts`,\n  `tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts`, `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`.\n- **Modified:** `src/app/(app)/layout.tsx`, `src/app/(app)/shell.tsx`, `tests/e2e/dashboard.spec.ts`, `tests/e2e/notifications.spec.ts`.\n- **Untouched:** `src/server/**`, `src/app/api/**`, `src/middleware.ts`, `src/app/(auth)/login/**`, `prisma/**`,\n  `src/lib/validators/auth.ts`, `package.json`.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011vT6DBPfhH3vCoRCQSRhDw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
