{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8W95pAacEcSW4Hktpp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the SH-7 system design to `artifacts/architect/system-design.md`. It replaces an old design for a different ticket (SH-1) that was still in that file. I checked the requirement IDs: every one it cites exists in intake's list, and all 51 requirements are covered.\n\n**What it designs:**\n- **Data and code:** one database migration, one main code file for attendance, one file of small rules, and one file of shared input checks. The checks are used by both the forms and the server.\n- **Endpoints and pages:** 10 API endpoints, and pages for taking attendance, the student and course Attendance tabs, and an admin page.\n- **Nothing new to install or run:** no new libraries, no background jobs and no scheduled tasks.\n- **Saving a register:** all marks are saved together in one database transaction. The audit entries and the parent/student notifications are sent after the save succeeds, never before. Re-saving a register without changes sends no duplicate notifications, because only real status changes trigger them.\n- **Small changes to existing code:** one new function in the timetable code. The existing schedule function returns nothing for admins, and the admin overview needs the whole school's schedule for the day. Everything else is only added: four new notification types, two new school settings, and new tab and navigation entries.\n\n**Open questions from intake.** I used these defaults; tell me if you want any changed:\n- **School settings page (medium confidence):** none exists, so admins edit the attendance mode and alert threshold in a small settings tab on `/admin/attendance`. A new endpoint, `PATCH /api/settings/school`, saves them.\n- **Daily homeroom register route (low confidence):** the PRD doesn't name one, so it uses `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` and the same register screen as courses.\n- **Two notification types (low confidence):** the PRD doesn't say who gets them. \"Attendance corrected\" goes to parents and students; \"register missing\" goes to the teacher. Neither sends email.\n\n**Still a hard blocker for dev:** the PRD requires every MUI component to be looked up through the mui-mcp server first. If it's unreachable during development, UI work has to stop.\n\nNext is `arch-api-contracts`. It writes `api-contracts.json` and then the handoff file. The copies of both in the folder now are left over from SH-1 and will be replaced."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297,"cache_read_input_tokens":70919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":297},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"90141260-d1a7-451a-8239-c83fc1554359","uuid":"89460db4-4510-46b3-b9e4-a56ebdd34683","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:34:32.606Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8W8qfiotPB4ThmPuhH"}
