--   1 ikramaansari  staff   5584 Nov  6 11:40 uiv-raw.json\n72\t{\n73\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n74\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n75\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n76\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n77\t  \"prd\": \"PRD-08: File Storage & Course Content (Modules and Lessons) (SCH-008)\",\n78\t  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n79\t  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n80\t    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-8 and the PRD header says SCH-008. All artifacts use SH-8. The artifacts/intake files that were there before belonged to SH-7 and are overwritten.\",\n81\t    \"GREENFIELD FEATURE: the workspace has no file storage or course content code yet. There are no FileObject/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress models, no ContentStatus enum, no src/server/storage.ts, no src/server/files/, no content routes or pages, and no UPLOAD_DIR/MAX_UPLOAD_MB entries in .env.example.\",\n82\t    \"MISSING DEPENDENCIES: the PRD needs file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable, and none of them are in package.json. @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 is installed. All of these are on the PRD's allowed list of non-visual libraries.\",\n83\t    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse()/assertCanManageCourse() in src/server/auth/course-access.ts, assertCanViewStudent()/getAccessibleStudentIds() in src/server/auth/student-access.ts, and requireUser()/requireRole() in src/server/auth/requireRole.ts.\",\n84\t    \"REUSE: rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) in src/server/rate-limit.ts (a per-process sliding window) for the 60 uploads/hour limit. audit() comes from src/server/audit.ts, notify() from src/server/notifications/notify.ts, and the type keys live in NOTIFICATION_TYPES in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n85\t    \"REUSE: the course tab registry src/config/course-tabs.ts (currently overview, roster and attendance) and the student tab registry src/config/student-tabs.ts (currently courses and attendance). The 'Content' and 'Learning' tabs are added there.\",\n86\t    \"DAILY MAINTENANCE HOOK: PRD-04's 'daily maintenance run' is the once-per-day purgeOldNotifications() call inside src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, which is gated by an in-memory lastPurgeAt. purgeOrphanFiles() should be called next to it.\",\n87\t    \"LOGO: SchoolSettings.logoUrl (String?) is in prisma/schema.prisma:195 and in UpdateSchoolSettingsInput (src/server/services/settings.ts), the email BaseLayout and render.ts use it, and PATCH /api/settings/school exists. However, there is NO /admin/settings/school page in src/app/(app)/admin/, so FR-9's 'replace the logo URL field' has no field to replace.\",\n88\t    \"SHARED COMPONENTS: they live in src/components/<Name>/ (DataTable, ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, FormField, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker...), not in src/components/shared/. New shared components (FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView) should follow the existing src/components/<Name>/ layout.\",\n89\t    \"No .gitignore was found at the workspace root. UPLOAD_DIR (./uploads) must be git-ignored, so either create one or add the entry if a .gitignore exists elsewhere.\",\n90\t    \"VERIFIED: assertCanViewCourse already allows PARENT when a linked student has an ACTIVE enrollment, and STUDENT only when ACTIVE-enrolled. Use it unchanged.\"\n91\t  ],\n92\t  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n93\t    {\n94\t      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n95\t      \"description\": \"Add the FileObject Prisma model (ownerId→User, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, unique storageKey '<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>', sha256, context, nullable contextId, createdAt, index on [context, contextId]) with a migration.\",\n96\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n97\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 File storage (Prisma block)\"\n98\t    },\n99\t    {\n100\t      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n101\t      \"description\": \"Create src/server/storage.ts exposing saveFile(stream, meta), readFile(storageKey) and deleteFile(storageKey). It writes under UPLOAD_DIR (new env var, default ./uploads, git-ignored) and never inside public/.\",\n102\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n103\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.1\"\n104\t    },\n105\t    {\n106\t      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n107\t      \"description\": \"POST /api/files (multipart, any signed-in user) accepts one file plus context and creates a FileObject with contextId null.\",\n108\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n109\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.2; API table\"\n110\t    },\n111\t    {\n112\t      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n113\t      \"description\": \"Enforce a per-file size limit of MAX_UPLOAD_MB (env, default 25). Oversize uploads are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'\",\n114\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n115\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.2\"\n116\t    },\n117\t    {\n118\t      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n119\t      \"description\": \"Allow only pdf, doc, docx, xls, xlsx, ppt, pptx, txt, csv, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4 and zip, validated by extension AND by magic-number sniffing with the file-type package. Anything else is rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR 'File type .<ext> is not allowed.'\",\n120\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n121\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.2; Acceptance Criterion 4\"\n122\t    },\n123\t    {\n124\t      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n125\t      \"description\": \"Text formats with no magic number (txt, csv) and Office OOXML formats that sniff as zip (docx/xlsx/pptx) are accepted when the sniffed type is absent or consistent with the extension. Executable or mismatched signatures are rejected.\",\n126\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n127\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.2 (inferred: file-type cannot detect txt/csv; OOXML sniffs as zip container)\"\n128\t    },\n129\t    {\n130\t      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n131\t      \"description\": \"Sanitise filenames: strip path separators and control characters and cap the length at 150 characters, then store the result as originalName.\",\n132\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n133\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.3\"\n134\t    },\n135\t    {\n136\t      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n137\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/files/:id streams the file with the stored MIME type, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, and Content-Disposition: attachment. It uses inline for images and PDFs only when ?inline=1.\",\n138\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n139\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.4; API table\"\n140\t    },\n141\t    {\n142\t      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n143\t      \"description\": \"Add a file access resolver registry src/server/files/access.ts with registerFileAccess(context, (user, file) => boolean | Promise<boolean>). An unknown context allows only the owner and ADMIN. Denied requests return 404/403 without streaming any bytes.\",\n144\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n145\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.4; Acceptance Criterion 3\"\n146\t    },\n147\t    {\n148\t      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n149\t      \"description\": \"Register the 'lesson' file context (allowed when the user can view the lesson under the visibility rules) and the 'logo' context (public, including unauthenticated users).\",\n150\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n151\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.4\"\n152\t    },\n153\t    {\n154\t      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n155\t      \"description\": \"DELETE /api/files/:id is allowed for the owner or ADMIN, only while the file is unattached (contextId null). It removes both the row and the stored bytes.\",\n156\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n157\t      \"source\": \"API table\"\n158\t    },\n159\t    {\n160\t      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n161\t      \"description\": \"purgeOrphanFiles() deletes FileObjects with contextId null that are older than 24 hours, together with their stored bytes. It is called from PRD-04's daily maintenance run.\",\n162\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n163\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.5\"\n164\t    },\n165\t    {\n166\t      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n167\t      \"description\": \"Add a reusable MUI FileUpload component: a Paper drop zone with a dashed border, Button component='label' with a visually hidden input, multiple files, a per-file LinearProgress driven by XHR upload progress, and a List of files showing name, size, type icon and a remove button.\",\n168\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n169\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"\n170\t    },\n171\t    {\n172\t      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n173\t      \"description\": \"Add a FileList component that shows attached files with download links to /api/files/:id.\",\n174\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n175\t      \"source\": \"FR-1.6\"\n176\t    },\n177\t    {\n178\t      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n179\t      \"description\": \"Add the ContentStatus enum (DRAFT, SCHEDULED, PUBLISHED) and the Module, Lesson, LessonAttachment, LessonLink and LessonProgress models exactly as specified, including the cascade deletes and the composite PK [lessonId, studentId] on LessonProgress.\",\n180\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n181\t      \"source\": \"FR-2 Content data model\"\n182\t    },\n183\t    {\n184\t      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n185\t      \"description\": \"Validate content fields with Zod in src/lib/validators/content.ts: module title ≤120, lesson title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100,000 chars, estimatedMinutes 1–600, link URLs http(s) only, and videoUrl YouTube/Vimeo only.\",\n186\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n187\t      \"source\": \"FR-2 field comments; Code layout (validators)\"\n188\t    },\n189\t    {\n190\t      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n191\t      \"description\": \"Attaching a file to a lesson sets FileObject.context='lesson' and contextId=lessonId. Only files owned by the caller (or any file, for ADMIN) that are still unattached can be attached.\",\n192\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n193\t      \"source\": \"FR-1 (contextId 'id of the owning record once attached'); FR-5.2\"\n194\t    },\n195\t    {\n196\t      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n197\t      \"description\": \"Visibility rule: a lesson is visible to STUDENT/PARENT only when both the lesson and its module are PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt <= now. This is evaluated at read time with no background job.\",\n198\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n199\t      \"source\": \"FR-3.1; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n200\t    },\n201\t    {\n202\t      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n203\t      \"description\": \"TEACHER (managing the course) and ADMIN see all modules and lessons with a status badge: Draft grey, Scheduled blue with date, Published green.\",\n204\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n205\t      \"source\": \"FR-3.2\"\n206\t    },\n207\t    {\n208\t      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n209\t      \"description\": \"Register a 'Content' course tab for every role that can view the course. It shows modules as ordered MUI Accordions, each listing lessons with title, estimated minutes, attachment count and, for students, a completion check.\",\n210\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n211\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.1\"\n212\t    },\n213\t    {\n214\t      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n215\t      \"description\": \"Students see a per-module progress bar ('3 of 5 complete'), a course-level progress bar and a 'Continue' button that opens the first incomplete visible lesson.\",\n216\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n217\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.2; Acceptance Criterion 5\"\n218\t    },\n219\t    {\n220\t      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n221\t      \"description\": \"Teacher controls on the Content tab: 'Add module', a per-module menu (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down) and 'Add lesson' per module.\",\n222\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n223\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.3\"\n224\t    },\n225\t    {\n226\t      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n227\t      \"description\": \"Lessons can be reordered within and across modules with @dnd-kit/sortable drag handles on MUI Accordion/List items, with up/down IconButtons as the keyboard alternative. The order persists through POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder with the full ordering { modules: [{ id, lessonIds: [] }] }.\",\n228\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n229\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.3; API table; Acceptance Criterion 7\"\n230\t    },\n231\t    {\n232\t      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n233\t      \"description\": \"Deleting a module that contains lessons requires typing the module title in a confirmation Dialog.\",\n234\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n235\t      \"source\": \"FR-4.4\"\n236\t    },\n237\t    {\n238\t      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n239\t      \"description\": \"Lesson editor page /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL, plus an MUI Markdown editor: Tabs Write/Preview, a multiline TextField, and a toolbar for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image.\",\n240\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n241\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.1\"\n242\t    },\n243\t    {\n244\t      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n245\t      \"description\": \"Toolbar image insert uploads through POST /api/files (context 'lesson') and inserts ![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1). The editor shows a warning when alt text is missing.\",\n246\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n247\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.1; NFR Accessibility\"\n248\t    },\n249\t    {\n250\t      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n251\t      \"description\": \"The lesson editor has an attachments section (FileUpload with reorder) and a links section (title + URL rows). Both are saved via PATCH /api/lessons/:id as attachments and links arrays.\",\n252\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n253\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.2; API table\"\n254\t    },\n255\t    {\n256\t      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n257\t      \"description\": \"Lesson status controls are Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule. Schedule uses an MUI date-time picker in the school timezone and the time must be in the future.\",\n258\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n259\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.3\"\n260\t    },\n261\t    {\n262\t      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n263\t      \"description\": \"Autosave the draft every 10 seconds while there are unsaved changes, show a 'Saved HH:mm' indicator, and warn on navigation away when changes are unsaved.\",\n264\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n265\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.4\"\n266\t    },\n267\t    {\n268\t      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n269\t      \"description\": \"Video URL parser: accept youtube.com/watch?v=, youtu.be/ and vimeo.com/<id> and store the URL as entered. Render it as a privacy-enhanced embed (youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>, player.vimeo.com/video/<id>) in a 16:9 responsive iframe with a title attribute.\",\n270\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n271\t      \"source\": \"FR-5.5; Acceptance Criterion 1\"\n272\t    },\n273\t    {\n274\t      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n275\t      \"description\": \"Add a shared MarkdownView component that uses react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema plus img from same origin only) and maps every element to MUI (Typography, Link, Table*, Divider, List/ListItem, Box component='pre'). External links open in a new tab with rel='noopener noreferrer'.\",\n276\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n277\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n278\t    },\n279\t    {\n280\t      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n281\t      \"description\": \"Lesson viewer /courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId] shows the video embed, attachment list, links, estimated time and Previous/Next navigation across modules, limited to lessons visible to the caller.\",\n282\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n283\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.2\"\n284\t    },\n285\t    {\n286\t      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n287\t      \"description\": \"For students, the first lesson view upserts LessonProgress.firstViewedAt, and a 'Mark as complete' button toggles completedAt via POST /api/lessons/:id/progress { completed }. Only ACTIVE enrolled students may do this.\",\n288\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n289\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.3; API table\"\n290\t    },\n291\t    {\n292\t      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n293\t      \"description\": \"Teachers get a 'Progress' Drawer on the lesson viewer that lists enrolled students with Viewed/Completed status and dates, served by GET /api/lessons/:id/progress (manage).\",\n294\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n295\t      \"source\": \"FR-6.4; API table\"\n296\t    },\n297\t    {\n298\t      \"id\": \"FR-35\",\n299\t      \"description\": \"Register a 'Learning' student tab showing per-course content progress (course, lessons completed / visible, percentage, last activity) via GET /api/students/:id/learning (assertCanViewStudent).\",\n300\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n301\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.1; API table\"\n302\t    },\n303\t    {\n304\t      \"id\": \"FR-36\",\n305\t      \"description\": \"Parents can open linked children's course content and lessons read-only, with no 'Mark as complete' button.\",\n306\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n307\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"\n308\t    },\n309\t    {\n310\t      \"id\": \"FR-37\",\n311\t      \"description\": \"Parents can view a course's Content tab only when a linked student is ACTIVE-enrolled. The existing assertCanViewCourse already enforces this (verified in src/server/auth/course-access.ts PARENT branch), so reuse it as is.\",\n312\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n313\t      \"source\": \"FR-7.2; Roles (parents see data for linked students)\"\n314\t    },\n315\t    {\n316\t      \"id\": \"FR-38\",\n317\t      \"description\": \"Register the notification type content.lesson_published (category ACADEMIC, default email false). 'Publish now' that makes a lesson visible notifies ACTIVE enrolled students.\",\n318\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n319\t      \"source\": \"FR-8.1\"\n320\t    },\n321\t    {\n322\t      \"id\": \"FR-39\",\n323\t      \"description\": \"Scheduled lessons send no notification when publishAt passes. The Schedule control shows the tooltip 'Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.'\",\n324\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n325\t      \"source\": \"FR-8.2\"\n326\t    },\n327\t    {\n328\t      \"id\": \"FR-40\",\n329\t      \"description\": \"Logo upload: the school settings page uses FileUpload (single image, PNG/JPG/WebP/SVG, max 2 MB, context 'logo') instead of a logo URL field, and stores the resulting /api/files/<id> URL in SchoolSettings.logoUrl.\",\n330\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n331\t      \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (storage of the URL in logoUrl inferred; existing column reused, no rename)\"\n332\t    },\n333\t    {\n334\t      \"id\": \"FR-41\",\n335\t      \"description\": \"SVG is allowed only for context 'logo'. SVG logo files are served with Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'.\",\n336\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n337\t      \"source\": \"FR-9.1\"\n338\t    },\n339\t    {\n340\t      \"id\": \"FR-42\",\n341\t      \"description\": \"/admin/settings/school does not exist in the workspace. Create a minimal ADMIN page there that uses the existing PATCH /api/settings/school, holds the logo FileUpload, and adds an nav entry if none exists.\",\n342\t      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n343\t      \"source\": \"FR-9.1 (references a page from PRD-02 not found in src/app/(app)/admin/)\"\n344\t    },\n345\t    {\n346\t      \"id\": \"FR-43\",\n347\t      \"description\": \"Content API: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/modules (GET filters by visibility per role and includes lessons and the caller's progress), PATCH/DELETE /api/modules/:id, POST /api/modules/:id/lessons, GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/lessons/:id, using the PRD response/error envelope and the access checks in the API table.\",\n348\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n349\t      \"source\": \"API table; Code layout (response shape)\"\n350\t    },\n351\t    {\n352\t      \"id\": \"FR-44\",\n353\t      \"description\": \"GET /api/lessons/:id returns NOT_FOUND to STUDENT/PARENT callers when the lesson is not visible under the visibility rules.\",\n354\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n355\t      \"source\": \"API table ('view (visibility rules)'); FR-3.1\"\n356\t    },\n357\t    {\n358\t      \"id\": \"FR-45\",\n359\t      \"description\": \"Content business logic lives in src/server/content/content-service.ts and file logic in src/server/files/. Route handlers stay thin (Zod → service → JSON).\",\n360\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n361\t      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (feature-named subdirectory precedent)\"\n362\t    },\n363\t    {\n364\t      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n365\t      \"description\": \"Teacher/admin mutations on content owned by another user (for example an admin editing a teacher's lesson, or deleting someone else's file) write an AuditLog row via audit().\",\n366\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n367\t      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (AuditLog rule)\"\n368\t    },\n369\t    {\n370\t      \"id\": \"FR-47\",\n371\t      \"description\": \"Seed data: MATH-7A gets 3 modules ('Number Sense', 'Fractions', 'Geometry Basics') with 3 published lessons each of realistic Markdown, one with a YouTube video and one with a seeded PDF from prisma/seed-assets/, plus one draft lesson and one lesson scheduled 7 days ahead. ENG-7A gets 2 modules × 2 lessons. Sam has completed 4 MATH-7A lessons.\",\n372\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n373\t      \"source\": \"Seed Data\"\n374\t    },\n375\t    {\n376\t      \"id\": \"FR-48\",\n377\t      \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for the filename sanitiser, video URL parser, visibility rule and access registry dispatch; integration tests for upload → attach → download with access checks and for the orphan purge; a Playwright test where a teacher creates and publishes a lesson with an attachment and a student completes it.\",\n378\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n379\t      \"source\": \"Test Requirements\"\n380\t    }\n381\t  ],\n382\t  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n383\t    {\n384\t      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n385\t      \"description\": \"Stored files are never served from a static path, and every download goes through the access registry.\",\n386\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n387\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1 (Security); FR-1.1\"\n388\t    },\n389\t    {\n390\t      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n391\t      \"description\": \"Markdown output is sanitised (rehype-sanitize) and javascript: URLs are stripped, so no script executes from lesson content.\",\n392\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n393\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n394\t    },\n395\t    {\n396\t      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n397\t      \"description\": \"POST /api/files is rate limited to 60 uploads per user per hour (RATE_LIMITED 429), reusing rateLimit() from src/server/rate-limit.ts.\",\n398\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n399\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n400\t    },\n401\t    {\n402\t      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n403\t      \"description\": \"The Content tab for a course with 20 modules × 10 lessons renders in under 600 ms. This means no N+1 queries: modules, lessons, attachment counts and progress are loaded in a bounded number of queries.\",\n404\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n405\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2 (Performance)\"\n406\t    },\n407\t    {\n408\t      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n409\t      \"description\": \"Uploads stream to disk and the sha256 is computed while streaming, without buffering whole files in memory. The size limit is enforced during the stream.\",\n410\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n411\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 2\"\n412\t    },\n413\t    {\n414\t      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n415\t      \"description\": \"Accessibility: embedded video iframes have a title, the editor warns when an image has no alt text, and drag reordering has keyboard up/down IconButton alternatives.\",\n416\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n417\t      \"source\": \"Non-Functional Requirements 3; FR-4.3\"\n418\t    },\n419\t    {\n420\t      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n421\t      \"description\": \"UI component rule: only @mui/material, @mui/icons-material and the listed MUI X packages are used. Every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for the installed 9.5.0) before use. Banned libraries are never imported, and Markdown elements map to MUI via the components prop. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented.\",\n422\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n423\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 requires intake to record it)\"\n424\t    },\n425\t    {\n426\t      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n427\t      \"description\": \"Every content and file handler and every server page enforces access server-side (assertCanViewCourse/assertCanManageCourse/assertCanViewStudent/access registry). Hiding a button is never the only protection.\",\n428\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n429\t      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts)\"\n430\t    },\n431\t    {\n432\t      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n433\t      \"description\": \"Brownfield constraint: do not re-scaffold, rename existing routes/models or duplicate helpers. Keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test passing. New dependencies are limited to the PRD-allowed set (file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable).\",\n434\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n435\t      \"source\": \"Platform Context; Assumptions and constraints\"\n436\t    },\n437\t    {\n438\t      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n439\t      \"description\": \"Dates (publishAt, progress dates, 'Saved' indicator) are stored in UTC and displayed in SchoolSettings.timezone. The schedule picker interprets input in the school timezone.\",\n440\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n441\t      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions (timestamps); FR-5.3\"\n442\t    },\n443\t    {\n444\t      \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n445\t      \"description\": \"Out of scope: S3/cloud storage (the storage module has a single local-disk implementation), SCORM/H5P/live video, and copying content between courses.\",\n446\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n447\t      \"source\": \"Out of Scope\"\n448\t    },\n449\t    {\n450\t      \"id\": \"NFR-12\",\n451\t      \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code. Use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. .env.example documents UPLOAD_DIR and MAX_UPLOAD_MB.\",\n452\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n453\t      \"source\": \"Code layout and conventions; Fixed technology decisions (.env.example)\"\n454\t    }\n455\t  ],\n456\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n457\t  \"clarificationLog\": [\n458\t    {\n459\t      \"round\": 1,\n460\t      \"questions\": [\n461\t        \"FR-42: /admin/settings/school (said to come from PRD-02) does not exist in the workspace. Should intake create a minimal school settings page to host the logo upload?\",\n462\t        \"FR-6: How should txt/csv (no magic number) and docx/xlsx/pptx (sniff as zip) pass magic-number validation?\",\n463\t        \"FR-40: Should SchoolSettings.logoUrl store '/api/files/<id>', or should a new logoFileId column be added?\"\n464\t      ],\n465\t      \"unresolved\": [\n466\t        \"FR-42 default: create a minimal ADMIN /admin/settings/school page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school.\",\n467\t        \"FR-6 default: accept text types when no signature is detected, accept OOXML when the sniffed type is zip or the matching OOXML mime, and reject everything else that mismatches.\",\n468\t        \"FR-40 default: store '/api/files/<id>' in the existing logoUrl column, with no schema change. Email templates then need an absolute URL (APP_URL prefix).\"\n469\t      ]\n470\t    }\n471\t  ],\n472\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n473\t}{\n474\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n475\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n476\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n477\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n478\t  \"status\": \"complete\",\n479\t  \"requirementsCount\": 60,\n480\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 93,\n481\t  \"blockers\": [\n482\t    \"GREENFIELD within brownfield: there is no file storage or content code yet. Design the FileObject/ContentStatus/Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress migration, src/server/storage.ts, src/server/files/ (access registry, purge), src/server/content/content-service.ts, src/lib/validators/content.ts, the 15 API endpoints, the Content course tab, the lesson editor and viewer pages, the Learning student tab, the FileUpload/FileList/MarkdownView components, seed data plus prisma/seed-assets PDF, and the tests.\",\n483\t    \"NEW DEPS required (all PRD-allowed): file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize, @dnd-kit/sortable.\",\n484\t    \"REUSE: assertCanViewCourse (already handles PARENT via linked ACTIVE enrollment), assertCanManageCourse, assertCanViewStudent, rateLimit(), audit(), notify() + NOTIFICATION_TYPES, the courseTabs/studentTabs registries, updateSchoolSettings(), and the components in src/components/<Name>/ (ConfirmDialog, EmptyState, PageHeader, Toast/useToast).\",\n485\t    \"FR-12: hook purgeOrphanFiles() into the once-daily purge block in src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts, next to purgeOldNotifications().\",\n486\t    \"FR-42 (LOW): /admin/settings/school does not exist. Default: create a minimal ADMIN page on the existing PATCH /api/settings/school. FR-40 stores '/api/files/<id>' in the existing SchoolSettings.logoUrl, and email templates need an APP_URL-absolute URL.\",\n487\t    \"FR-6 (MEDIUM): define sniffing rules for txt/csv (no signature) and OOXML (zip signature).\",\n488\t    \"No root .gitignore was found. Ensure ./uploads is git-ignored.\",\n489\t    \"NFR-7: Dev must reach the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\"\n490\t  ],\n491\t  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n492\t}\n493\t{\n494\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-8\",\n495\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:00:00Z\",\n496\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n497\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n498\t  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n499\t  \"confidencePct\": 100,\n500\t  \"detectionNotes\": \"The run mode declares '--tech-stack react', and the workspa