{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gaf27VGXgrwd7Vzvarindk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict (`moduleResolution: bundler`), Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5 beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers with `AdapterDateFns` already in `src/app/providers.tsx`, x-charts), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1, date-fns/date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `package.json` declares `engines.node >=18.18.0`, and local Node is 24.11.1. Nothing in the requirements calls for a different stack. The ADRs below cover how this feature fits into the existing stack and pin the new dependencies.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions\n10\t\n11\t**Context.** NFR-9 limits new dependencies to file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable. The latest file-type (22.x) declares `engines.node >=22` and 21.x declares `>=20`. Either would break the repo's `>=18.18.0` engine contract. All five packages are ESM-only.\n12\t\n13\t**Decision.** Install these exact pins:\n14\t| Package | Version | Why this version |\n15\t|---|---|---|\n16\t| `file-type` | `20.5.0` | Newest line with `engines.node >=18`. Use `fileTypeFromBuffer` (FR-5, FR-6). |\n17\t| `react-markdown` | `10.1.0` | Peer is `react >=18` (FR-31). |\n18\t| `remark-gfm` | `4.0.1` | Supports tables and strikethrough for FR-25 and FR-31. |\n19\t| `rehype-sanitize` | `6.0.0` | Provides NFR-2 sanitisation. |\n20\t| `@dnd-kit/sortable` | `10.0.0` | Peer is `@dnd-kit/core ^6.3.0`, which matches the installed 6.3.1 (FR-23). |\n21\t\n22\tESM-only packages import cleanly into App Router server and client code under `moduleResolution: bundler`, so `transpilePackages` is not needed. Add it only if `next build` complains.\n23\t\n24\t**Consequences.** No engine bump is needed. Do not upgrade file-type past 20.x without also raising `engines.node`. NFR-11 (single local-disk storage, no S3 SDK) means no cloud dependency is added.\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## ADR-2: Parse multipart uploads with `busboy` (already installed via Next.js), not `request.formData()`\n29\t\n30\t**Context.** NFR-5 requires uploads to stream to disk, with sha256 computed and the size limit enforced during the stream. In Next 14, `Request.formData()` buffers the whole body in memory, which violates NFR-5 for 25 MB files (FR-4). `busboy@1.6.0` is already in `node_modules` as a direct dependency of `next@14.2.18` (`npm ls busboy`). Adding another parser would break NFR-9.\n31\t\n32\t**Decision.** `POST /api/files` (FR-3) runs on the Node runtime (`export const runtime = 'nodejs'`). It pipes `Readable.fromWeb(req.body)` into `busboy({ headers, limits: { files: 1, fileSize: MAX_UPLOAD_MB*1024*1024 } })`. The file stream goes through a `crypto.createHash('sha256')` tap and into `storage.saveFile()` (FR-2), which writes to a temp path under `UPLOAD_DIR` and then `rename`s it to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>` (FR-1). Busboy's `limit` event aborts the upload, deletes the temp file and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'` (FR-4). Type sniffing (ADR-3) runs on the first chunk(s) before the write is committed. The `context` field must come before the file part in the multipart body because the logo rules (FR-40, FR-41) depend on it. FileUpload (FR-13) appends `context` first.\n33\t\n34\t**Consequences.** busboy is a transitive dependency, so `@types/busboy` is not available. Declare a minimal local type or accept `any` at that one call site, with a `ponytail:` comment explaining it. If a Next upgrade drops busboy, add `busboy` explicitly at that point. The intake handoff should note this as the only deviation from the dependency list, and it is a zero-install one. The rate limit check (NFR-3, `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` from `src/server/rate-limit.ts`) runs before any bytes are read.\n35\t\n36\t---\n37\t\n38\t## ADR-3: Validate file types with an extension allowlist plus `file-type` sniffing of the head buffer, using an explicit table\n39\t\n40\t**Context.** FR-5 requires checks on both the extension and the magic number. FR-6 notes that txt/csv have no signature and that docx/xlsx/pptx can sniff as `zip`. FR-41 allows SVG only for `logo`, and SVG is text, so file-type cannot detect it reliably. The Vitest environment is `jsdom`, so file-type's `\"node\"` export condition may not resolve there, while `fileTypeFromBuffer` exists in both the node and core entries.\n41\t\n42\t**Decision.** In `src/server/files/validate.ts`, keep one `ALLOWED: Record<ext, { mimes: string[]; sniff: 'required' | 'none' | 'zip-or-ooxml' }>` table:\n43\t- Binary types (pdf, doc, xls, ppt, png, jpg/jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4, zip): the sniffed mime must be in `mimes`. doc/xls/ppt sniff as `application/x-cfb`.\n44\t- docx/xlsx/pptx: the sniffed type is `application/zip` or the matching OOXML mime.\n45\t- txt/csv and svg (logo only): sniffing must return `undefined`. If any signature is detected (for example an ELF, PE or zip disguised as .csv), the file is rejected. SVG also requires the head to contain `<svg`, and is limited to 2 MB under context `logo` (FR-40). The logo context also limits extensions to png, jpg, jpeg, webp and svg.\n46\t- The stored `mimeType` comes from the table, not from the client's Content-Type header.\n47\t- Call `fileTypeFromBuffer(head)` on the first 4100 bytes collected from the stream. `head` is a tee of the first chunks, not a re-read.\n48\t\n49\t**Consequences.** The rules are deterministic and testable as a pure function (FR-48). Integration tests that touch busboy or the filesystem add `// @vitest-environment node`. Errors use the FR-5 message `File type .<ext> is not allowed.`\n50\t\n51\t---\n52\t\n53\t## ADR-4: Store files on local disk outside `public/`, serve them only through a Node route handler, and set headers per response\n54\t\n55\t**Context.** NFR-1 says files are never served from a static path. FR-8 sets nosniff, attachment and inline rules. FR-41 sets a CSP for SVG logos. FR-10 requires `logo` to be readable without a session. `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/` path that is not in `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (`src/config/public-routes.ts`). `next.config.js` already sends a site-wide `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a CSP of `default-src 'self'` on `/:path*`.\n56\t\n57\t**Decision.**\n58\t- `src/server/storage.ts` uses `node:fs/promises` and `node:stream/promises` only. `UPLOAD_DIR` is resolved with `path.resolve` and defaults to `./uploads`. Every storage key is checked to stay under `UPLOAD_DIR` after resolution, as a path-traversal guard. This is the only implementation (NFR-11).\n59\t- `GET /api/files/:id` runs on `runtime = 'nodejs'` and returns `new Response(Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream(...)))` with `Content-Type` set to the stored mime, `Content-Length` set to `sizeBytes`, `nosniff`, and `Content-Disposition` set to `attachment` (or `inline` only for image/* or pdf with `?inline=1`) plus an RFC 5987 `filename*`. SVG responses also set `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. If next.config's global CSP is also sent, browsers enforce the stricter intersection, so no config change is needed for this route.\n60\t- Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` so unauthenticated logo fetches reach the handler. The handler then runs the access registry (FR-9) for every request: `auth()` returns `null` for anonymous users, and only the `logo` resolver accepts a null user. Every other context returns 404 without reading bytes (NFR-8).\n61\t- `.gitignore`: create one at the repo root containing `uploads/`, plus `node_modules`, `.next` and `.env` if missing. `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (NFR-12).\n62\t\n63\t**Consequences.** Opening the middleware gate moves the auth decision into the handler, so the access registry must deny by default (FR-9: an unknown context is owner/ADMIN only, and an anonymous user is denied). Integration tests must cover anonymous requests for a lesson file (expect 404) and for a logo (expect 200).\n64\t\n65\t---\n66\t\n67\t## ADR-5: Allow the video-embed origins in the site CSP via `frame-src`\n68\t\n69\t**Context.** FR-30 embeds `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` and `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` iframes. The current CSP has `default-src 'self'` and no `frame-src`, so the browser would block both embeds.\n70\t\n71\t**Decision.** Add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com;` to the CSP string in `next.config.js`. The URL parser lives in `src/lib/video.ts` as a pure function shared by the Zod validator (FR-16) and the viewer (FR-32). It only emits those two origins.\n72\t\n73\t**Consequences.** This is a one-line config change. The `X-Frame-Options: DENY` header only stops other sites from framing SchoolHub, so it does not affect these embeds. Playwright should check that the iframe loads (it is not CSP-blocked) on the seeded YouTube lesson (FR-47).\n74\t\n75\t---\n76\t\n77\t## ADR-6: Render Markdown with react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize, map every element to MUI, and restrict images to same origin\n78\t\n79\t**Context.** FR-31 and NFR-2 require sanitised Markdown with `img` allowed from same origin only and MUI element mapping (NFR-7). The current CSP has `img-src 'self' data:`.\n80\t\n81\t**Decision.** `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` is a client-safe component (no hooks, so it also renders on the server) with `remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}` and `rehypePlugins={[[rehypeSanitize, schema]]}`. `schema` extends `defaultSchema` and limits `img` `src` to relative paths: `protocols.src: []` plus a check that the value starts with `/`. The default schema already drops `javascript:` hrefs. A `components` map converts h1–h6, p, a, ul/ol/li, table/thead/tbody/tr/th/td, hr, blockquote, code and pre into MUI Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External `a` elements get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`. The editor Preview tab (FR-25) uses the same component.\n82\t\n83\t**Consequences.** One renderer is used everywhere, so a sanitisation regression shows up in one unit test with `<script>`, `javascript:` and off-origin `img` cases (FR-48). No CSP change is needed for images.\n84\t\n85\t---\n86\t\n87\t## ADR-7: Implement reordering with @dnd-kit/sortable, persist the whole order in one transaction, and provide keyboard IconButtons\n88\t\n89\t**Context.** FR-23 covers drag within and across modules, with the full ordering sent to `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder`. NFR-6 requires a keyboard alternative. @dnd-kit/core is already installed.\n90\t\n91\t**Decision.** Each module's lesson List is a `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`, all inside one `DndContext`, and cross-container moves are handled in `onDragOver`. Up/down `IconButton`s modify the same client order array. The server validates that every submitted module and lesson id belongs to the course and that the set equals the existing set. It then writes `position`/`moduleId` for all rows inside one `prisma.$transaction`. A course has at most about 200 lessons (NFR-4), so updating every row is acceptable.\n92\t\n93\t**Consequences.** Reorder is a single idempotent call with no partial states. The update count is O(n) per reorder, which is fine at this scale.\n94\t\n95\t---\n96\t\n97\t## ADR-8: Read content with a bounded number of Prisma queries and compute visibility in TypeScript\n98\t\n99\t**Context.** NFR-4 requires the Content tab to render 20×10 lessons in under 600 ms with no N+1 queries. FR-18 evaluates visibility at read time, with no background job.\n100\t\n101\t**Decision.** `GET /api/courses/:id/modules` and the Content tab server component call `content-service.listCourseContent(user, courseId)`. That function makes one `module.findMany` with `include: { lessons: { include: { _count: { select: { attachments: true } } } } }` ordered by position, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany` for the student's lessons in that course when the caller is a STUDENT. That is two queries in total. `isVisible(entity, now)` is a pure function in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` and is unit tested (FR-48). Both module and lesson must be visible. Add an `@@index([courseId, position])` on Module and an `@@index([moduleId, position])` on Lesson.\n102\t\n103\t**Consequences.** Visibility is not pushed into SQL. At 200 rows per course, filtering in memory costs nothing, and having the rule in one place means the viewer (FR-32), the Learning tab (FR-35) and FR-44 all agree.\n104\t\n105\t---\n106\t\n107\t## ADR-9: Use existing stack pieces for scheduling, timezones, autosave and notifications\n108\t\n109\t**Context.** FR-28, NFR-10, FR-29, FR-38/39 and FR-12 all match existing infrastructure.\n110\t\n111\t**Decision.**\n112\t- Schedule picker: use the `DateTimePicker` from `@mui/x-date-pickers` (already wrapped in `src/components/FormField`). Convert school-timezone input to UTC with `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime(SchoolSettings.timezone)`. Zod rejects `publishAt <= now` (FR-28, NFR-10).\n113\t- Autosave (FR-29): a `setInterval` of 10 s plus a dirty flag in the editor, a `beforeunload` listener, and `PATCH /api/lessons/:id`. No new library.\n114\t- Notifications: add `content.lesson_published` to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` and call `notify()` only from the publish-now path (FR-38, FR-39).\n115\t- Orphan purge (FR-12): call `purgeOrphanFiles()` next to `purgeOldNotifications()` inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` daily block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`.\n116\t- Logging (NFR-12): use `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`. Rate limit (NFR-3): use the existing `rateLimit()`, which is per-process. That limitation is already marked with a ponytail comment.\n117\t\n118\t**Consequences.** No scheduler, queue or cron is added. Scheduled lessons appear automatically when read after `publishAt`, and no notification is sent for them, as FR-39 requires.\n119\t\n120\t---\n121\t\n122\t## Open risks carried forward\n123\t1. **NFR-7:** `mui-mcp` tools (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`) were visible in this session's tool list. Dev must still look up every MUI component against 9.5.0 before using it. If the server is unreachable, that is a hard blocker.\n124\t2. **ADR-2:** depending on Next's transitive busboy is a small fragility (see the Consequences of ADR-2).\n125\t3. **FR-40/42 (LOW confidence):** logo URLs stored as `/api/files/<id>` need an `APP_URL` prefix in email templates. The new `/admin/settings/school` page is a minimal page built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`.\n126\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8\n127\t\n128\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n129\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).\n130\tIt has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview.\n131\t\n132\t> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input.\n133\t\n134\t## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)\n135\t\n136\t| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |\n137\t|---|---|---|---|\n138\t| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n139\t| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |\n140\t| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |\n141\t| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |\n142\t| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |\n143\t| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |\n144\t| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |\n145\t| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |\n146\t\n147\t## Requirement → architectural concern\n148\t\n149\tConcern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**\n150\t\n151\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n152\t|---|---|---|\n153\t| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |\n154\t| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |\n155\t| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |\n156\t| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |\n157\t| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |\n158\t| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |\n159\t| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |\n160\t| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |\n161\t| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |\n162\t| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |\n163\t| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |\n164\t| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |\n165\t| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |\n166\t| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |\n167\t| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |\n168\t| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |\n169\t| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |\n170\t| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |\n171\t| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |\n172\t| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |\n173\t| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |\n174\t| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |\n175\t| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |\n176\t| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |\n177\t| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |\n178\t| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |\n179\t| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |\n180\t| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |\n181\t| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |\n182\t| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |\n183\t| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |\n184\t| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |\n185\t| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |\n186\t| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |\n187\t| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |\n188\t| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |\n189\t| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |\n190\t| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |\n191\t| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |\n192\t| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |\n193\t| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |\n194\t| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |\n195\t| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |\n196\t| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |\n197\t| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |\n198\t| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |\n199\t| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |\n200\t| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |\n201\t| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |\n202\t| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |\n203\t| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |\n204\t| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |\n205\t| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |\n206\t| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |\n207\t| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |\n208\t| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |\n209\t| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |\n210\t| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |\n211\t| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |\n212\t| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |\n213\t\n214\t## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`\n215\t\n216\t1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.\n217\t2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.\n218\t3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.\n219\t4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.\n220\t5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.\n221\t6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.\n222\t7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve.\n223\t# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n224\t\n225\tTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\n226\tInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n227\t`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n228\t\n229\t> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n230\t\n231\t---\n232\t\n233\t## 1. Overview\n234\t\n235\tSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on Post"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02965cf6-bb96-4d6d-ae8a-a3708e17396e","uuid":"9d11ed08-f596-4dcf-a96c-de270f08d51c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:52:21.813Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-forge-schoolhub/02965cf6-bb96-4d6d-ae8a-a3708e17396e/tool-results/bry5wq630.txt","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack.** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and the workspace confirms it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict (`moduleResolution: bundler`), Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5 beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers with `AdapterDateFns` already in `src/app/providers.tsx`, x-charts), @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1, date-fns/date-fns-tz, Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `package.json` declares `engines.node >=18.18.0`, and local Node is 24.11.1. Nothing in the requirements calls for a different stack. The ADRs below cover how this feature fits into the existing stack and pin the new dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add only the five PRD-allowed dependencies, with pinned versions\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 limits new dependencies to file-type, react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize and @dnd-kit/sortable. The latest file-type (22.x) declares `engines.node >=22` and 21.x declares `>=20`. Either would break the repo's `>=18.18.0` engine contract. All five packages are ESM-only.\n\n**Decision.** Install these exact pins:\n| Package | Version | Why this version |\n|---|---|---|\n| `file-type` | `20.5.0` | Newest line with `engines.node >=18`. Use `fileTypeFromBuffer` (FR-5, FR-6). |\n| `react-markdown` | `10.1.0` | Peer is `react >=18` (FR-31). |\n| `remark-gfm` | `4.0.1` | Supports tables and strikethrough for FR-25 and FR-31. |\n| `rehype-sanitize` | `6.0.0` | Provides NFR-2 sanitisation. |\n| `@dnd-kit/sortable` | `10.0.0` | Peer is `@dnd-kit/core ^6.3.0`, which matches the installed 6.3.1 (FR-23). |\n\nESM-only packages import cleanly into App Router server and client code under `moduleResolution: bundler`, so `transpilePackages` is not needed. Add it only if `next build` complains.\n\n**Consequences.** No engine bump is needed. Do not upgrade file-type past 20.x without also raising `engines.node`. NFR-11 (single local-disk storage, no S3 SDK) means no cloud dependency is added.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Parse multipart uploads with `busboy` (already installed via Next.js), not `request.formData()`\n\n**Context.** NFR-5 requires uploads to stream to disk, with sha256 computed and the size limit enforced during the stream. In Next 14, `Request.formData()` buffers the whole body in memory, which violates NFR-5 for 25 MB files (FR-4). `busboy@1.6.0` is already in `node_modules` as a direct dependency of `next@14.2.18` (`npm ls busboy`). Adding another parser would break NFR-9.\n\n**Decision.** `POST /api/files` (FR-3) runs on the Node runtime (`export const runtime = 'nodejs'`). It pipes `Readable.fromWeb(req.body)` into `busboy({ headers, limits: { files: 1, fileSize: MAX_UPLOAD_MB*1024*1024 } })`. The file stream goes through a `crypto.createHash('sha256')` tap and into `storage.saveFile()` (FR-2), which writes to a temp path under `UPLOAD_DIR` and then `rename`s it to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>` (FR-1). Busboy's `limit` event aborts the upload, deletes the temp file and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR 'File exceeds 25 MB.'` (FR-4). Type sniffing (ADR-3) runs on the first chunk(s) before the write is committed. The `context` field must come before the file part in the multipart body because the logo rules (FR-40, FR-41) depend on it. FileUpload (FR-13) appends `context` first.\n\n**Consequences.** busboy is a transitive dependency, so `@types/busboy` is not available. Declare a minimal local type or accept `any` at that one call site, with a `ponytail:` comment explaining it. If a Next upgrade drops busboy, add `busboy` explicitly at that point. The intake handoff should note this as the only deviation from the dependency list, and it is a zero-install one. The rate limit check (NFR-3, `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` from `src/server/rate-limit.ts`) runs before any bytes are read.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Validate file types with an extension allowlist plus `file-type` sniffing of the head buffer, using an explicit table\n\n**Context.** FR-5 requires checks on both the extension and the magic number. FR-6 notes that txt/csv have no signature and that docx/xlsx/pptx can sniff as `zip`. FR-41 allows SVG only for `logo`, and SVG is text, so file-type cannot detect it reliably. The Vitest environment is `jsdom`, so file-type's `\"node\"` export condition may not resolve there, while `fileTypeFromBuffer` exists in both the node and core entries.\n\n**Decision.** In `src/server/files/validate.ts`, keep one `ALLOWED: Record<ext, { mimes: string[]; sniff: 'required' | 'none' | 'zip-or-ooxml' }>` table:\n- Binary types (pdf, doc, xls, ppt, png, jpg/jpeg, gif, webp, mp3, mp4, zip): the sniffed mime must be in `mimes`. doc/xls/ppt sniff as `application/x-cfb`.\n- docx/xlsx/pptx: the sniffed type is `application/zip` or the matching OOXML mime.\n- txt/csv and svg (logo only): sniffing must return `undefined`. If any signature is detected (for example an ELF, PE or zip disguised as .csv), the file is rejected. SVG also requires the head to contain `<svg`, and is limited to 2 MB under context `logo` (FR-40). The logo context also limits extensions to png, jpg, jpeg, webp and svg.\n- The stored `mimeType` comes from the table, not from the client's Content-Type header.\n- Call `fileTypeFromBuffer(head)` on the first 4100 bytes collected from the stream. `head` is a tee of the first chunks, not a re-read.\n\n**Consequences.** The rules are deterministic and testable as a pure function (FR-48). Integration tests that touch busboy or the filesystem add `// @vitest-environment node`. Errors use the FR-5 message `File type .<ext> is not allowed.`\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Store files on local disk outside `public/`, serve them only through a Node route handler, and set headers per response\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 says files are never served from a static path. FR-8 sets nosniff, attachment and inline rules. FR-41 sets a CSP for SVG logos. FR-10 requires `logo` to be readable without a session. `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/` path that is not in `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` (`src/config/public-routes.ts`). `next.config.js` already sends a site-wide `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and a CSP of `default-src 'self'` on `/:path*`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `src/server/storage.ts` uses `node:fs/promises` and `node:stream/promises` only. `UPLOAD_DIR` is resolved with `path.resolve` and defaults to `./uploads`. Every storage key is checked to stay under `UPLOAD_DIR` after resolution, as a path-traversal guard. This is the only implementation (NFR-11).\n- `GET /api/files/:id` runs on `runtime = 'nodejs'` and returns `new Response(Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream(...)))` with `Content-Type` set to the stored mime, `Content-Length` set to `sizeBytes`, `nosniff`, and `Content-Disposition` set to `attachment` (or `inline` only for image/* or pdf with `?inline=1`) plus an RFC 5987 `filename*`. SVG responses also set `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. If next.config's global CSP is also sent, browsers enforce the stricter intersection, so no config change is needed for this route.\n- Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` so unauthenticated logo fetches reach the handler. The handler then runs the access registry (FR-9) for every request: `auth()` returns `null` for anonymous users, and only the `logo` resolver accepts a null user. Every other context returns 404 without reading bytes (NFR-8).\n- `.gitignore`: create one at the repo root containing `uploads/`, plus `node_modules`, `.next` and `.env` if missing. `.env.example` documents `UPLOAD_DIR` and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (NFR-12).\n\n**Consequences.** Opening the middleware gate moves the auth decision into the handler, so the access registry must deny by default (FR-9: an unknown context is owner/ADMIN only, and an anonymous user is denied). Integration tests must cover anonymous requests for a lesson file (expect 404) and for a logo (expect 200).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Allow the video-embed origins in the site CSP via `frame-src`\n\n**Context.** FR-30 embeds `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` and `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` iframes. The current CSP has `default-src 'self'` and no `frame-src`, so the browser would block both embeds.\n\n**Decision.** Add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com;` to the CSP string in `next.config.js`. The URL parser lives in `src/lib/video.ts` as a pure function shared by the Zod validator (FR-16) and the viewer (FR-32). It only emits those two origins.\n\n**Consequences.** This is a one-line config change. The `X-Frame-Options: DENY` header only stops other sites from framing SchoolHub, so it does not affect these embeds. Playwright should check that the iframe loads (it is not CSP-blocked) on the seeded YouTube lesson (FR-47).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Render Markdown with react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize, map every element to MUI, and restrict images to same origin\n\n**Context.** FR-31 and NFR-2 require sanitised Markdown with `img` allowed from same origin only and MUI element mapping (NFR-7). The current CSP has `img-src 'self' data:`.\n\n**Decision.** `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` is a client-safe component (no hooks, so it also renders on the server) with `remarkPlugins={[remarkGfm]}` and `rehypePlugins={[[rehypeSanitize, schema]]}`. `schema` extends `defaultSchema` and limits `img` `src` to relative paths: `protocols.src: []` plus a check that the value starts with `/`. The default schema already drops `javascript:` hrefs. A `components` map converts h1–h6, p, a, ul/ol/li, table/thead/tbody/tr/th/td, hr, blockquote, code and pre into MUI Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External `a` elements get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`. The editor Preview tab (FR-25) uses the same component.\n\n**Consequences.** One renderer is used everywhere, so a sanitisation regression shows up in one unit test with `<script>`, `javascript:` and off-origin `img` cases (FR-48). No CSP change is needed for images.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Implement reordering with @dnd-kit/sortable, persist the whole order in one transaction, and provide keyboard IconButtons\n\n**Context.** FR-23 covers drag within and across modules, with the full ordering sent to `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder`. NFR-6 requires a keyboard alternative. @dnd-kit/core is already installed.\n\n**Decision.** Each module's lesson List is a `SortableContext` with `verticalListSortingStrategy`, all inside one `DndContext`, and cross-container moves are handled in `onDragOver`. Up/down `IconButton`s modify the same client order array. The server validates that every submitted module and lesson id belongs to the course and that the set equals the existing set. It then writes `position`/`moduleId` for all rows inside one `prisma.$transaction`. A course has at most about 200 lessons (NFR-4), so updating every row is acceptable.\n\n**Consequences.** Reorder is a single idempotent call with no partial states. The update count is O(n) per reorder, which is fine at this scale.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Read content with a bounded number of Prisma queries and compute visibility in TypeScript\n\n**Context.** NFR-4 requires the Content tab to render 20×10 lessons in under 600 ms with no N+1 queries. FR-18 evaluates visibility at read time, with no background job.\n\n**Decision.** `GET /api/courses/:id/modules` and the Content tab server component call `content-service.listCourseContent(user, courseId)`. That function makes one `module.findMany` with `include: { lessons: { include: { _count: { select: { attachments: true } } } } }` ordered by position, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany` for the student's lessons in that course when the caller is a STUDENT. That is two queries in total. `isVisible(entity, now)` is a pure function in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` and is unit tested (FR-48). Both module and lesson must be visible. Add an `@@index([courseId, position])` on Module and an `@@index([moduleId, position])` on Lesson.\n\n**Consequences.** Visibility is not pushed into SQL. At 200 rows per course, filtering in memory costs nothing, and having the rule in one place means the viewer (FR-32), the Learning tab (FR-35) and FR-44 all agree.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Use existing stack pieces for scheduling, timezones, autosave and notifications\n\n**Context.** FR-28, NFR-10, FR-29, FR-38/39 and FR-12 all match existing infrastructure.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Schedule picker: use the `DateTimePicker` from `@mui/x-date-pickers` (already wrapped in `src/components/FormField`). Convert school-timezone input to UTC with `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime(SchoolSettings.timezone)`. Zod rejects `publishAt <= now` (FR-28, NFR-10).\n- Autosave (FR-29): a `setInterval` of 10 s plus a dirty flag in the editor, a `beforeunload` listener, and `PATCH /api/lessons/:id`. No new library.\n- Notifications: add `content.lesson_published` to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` and call `notify()` only from the publish-now path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Orphan purge (FR-12): call `purgeOrphanFiles()` next to `purgeOldNotifications()` inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` daily block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`.\n- Logging (NFR-12): use `logger` from `src/lib/logger.ts`. Rate limit (NFR-3): use the existing `rateLimit()`, which is per-process. That limitation is already marked with a ponytail comment.\n\n**Consequences.** No scheduler, queue or cron is added. Scheduled lessons appear automatically when read after `publishAt`, and no notification is sent for them, as FR-39 requires.\n\n---\n\n## Open risks carried forward\n1. **NFR-7:** `mui-mcp` tools (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`) were visible in this session's tool list. Dev must still look up every MUI component against 9.5.0 before using it. If the server is unreachable, that is a hard blocker.\n2. **ADR-2:** depending on Next's transitive busboy is a small fragility (see the Consequences of ADR-2).\n3. **FR-40/42 (LOW confidence):** logo URLs stored as `/api/files/<id>` need an `APP_URL` prefix in email templates. The new `/admin/settings/school` page is a minimal page built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`.\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-8\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-06T06:00:00Z), PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008).\nIt has 48 FRs and 12 NFRs (60 requirements) at 93% confidence. `handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers, and they must be surfaced in `system-design.md` Overview.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are still **SH-7** leftovers at the time of writing. Downstream sub-tasks own them and must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-8 input.\n\n## Brownfield findings verified on disk (arch-research-reqs)\n\n| # | Finding | Evidence | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **Middleware blocks unauthenticated `/api/files/:id`.** `src/middleware.ts` returns 401 for any `/api/*` not matched by `isPublicPath()`. `PUBLIC_API_PATHS` in `src/config/public-routes.ts` is `['/api/health','/api/auth/','/api/internal/']`. | middleware.ts L36-40, public-routes.ts L7 | FR-10's public `logo` context cannot work (login page, emails) unless `/api/files/` is made public. **Recommended:** add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. Then the GET handler resolves the session itself (optional user → access registry), and POST/DELETE **must** call `requireUser()` explicitly, because middleware no longer guards them. This is a security-critical design point (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| B2 | Daily hook exists: `lastPurgeAt` + `purgeOldNotifications()` in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` L11-31. | grep | FR-12 adds a second call in the same `if` block. No new scheduler. |\n| B3 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs) → {ok, retryAfterMs}` is a per-process sliding window. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-3: `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)`. |\n| B4 | `logoUrl` consumers: `BaseLayout.tsx` L28 uses `<Img src={school.logoUrl}>` raw, and `render.ts` already passes `appUrl`. | grep | FR-40 stores a relative `/api/files/<id>`, so BaseLayout must prefix `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. Combined with B1, that makes the logo fetchable from mail clients. |\n| B5 | No `.gitignore` at the repo root. | `ls` | Create one with `uploads/` (plus `node_modules`, `.next`, `.env` if missing). |\n| B6 | No `src/server/files/` and no content code. | ls | Confirms greenfield. |\n| B7 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are arrays of `CourseTab`/`StudentTab` in `src/config/`. | grep | FR-20 / FR-35 append one entry each. |\n| B8 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object in `src/server/notifications/types.ts`, and `ACADEMIC` is a valid category. | grep | FR-38 adds one key. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = server service/module · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = background/maintenance · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = config/env/registry · **TEST**\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | `FileObject` + `@@index([context, contextId])`, unique `storageKey`. `context` is a plain String (registry keys), not an enum, so new contexts need no migration. One migration together with FR-15. |\n| FR-2 | SVC, CFG | `src/server/storage.ts`: `saveFile`/`readFile`/`deleteFile`. Resolve paths with `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR, key)` and assert they stay under UPLOAD_DIR (traversal guard). Add env `UPLOAD_DIR` to the env schema. Single local-disk impl, no interface (NFR-11). |\n| FR-3 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/files` multipart. Use `request.formData()`? It buffers, which conflicts with NFR-5. Use `busboy`-free streaming via `req.body` + the Web `Request` multipart parser? **Design must pick.** Next.js route handlers expose `request.body` (a ReadableStream), but a multipart parser isn't in the allowed deps. Practical option: `formData()` is acceptable only if the size cap is pre-checked via `Content-Length` (≤ MAX_UPLOAD_MB + overhead) before parsing, then `File.stream()` → disk with sha256. Flag as a NFR-5 trade-off for design. |\n| FR-4 | VAL, CFG | `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` env (default 25). Enforce with a byte counter in the write stream (abort and unlink the partial file), plus an early `Content-Length` reject. Logo override: 2 MB (FR-40). Make the limit per-context: `{ logo: 2 }`, default env. |\n| FR-5 | VAL | Extension allowlist + `fileTypeFromBuffer` on the first ~4100 bytes (peek before or while writing). New dep `file-type` (ESM-only, so check the Next server bundling). |\n| FR-6 | VAL | Rule table: txt/csv → sniff must be `undefined`. docx/xlsx/pptx → sniff ∈ {zip, matching OOXML mime}. zip → zip. Others → sniff ext must match the declared ext (jpg≡jpeg). Pure function, unit-testable (FR-48). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `sanitizeFilename()`: strip `/ \\ ` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trim, and cap at 150 while preserving the extension. Pure function and unit test. |\n| FR-8 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/files/:id`: registry check **before** `readFile`. Headers: stored mime, `nosniff`, `attachment; filename*=UTF-8''…`, and `inline` only if `?inline=1` and mime is image/* or application/pdf. Stream via `Readable.toWeb(fs.createReadStream)`. |\n| FR-9 | SVC, AUTH, CFG | `src/server/files/access.ts`: a `Map<string, resolver>`. Default: owner or ADMIN. Return **404** for denied (don't leak existence) and 401 for unauthenticated non-public. Contexts are registered via side-effect import, so the GET handler must import the module that registers `lesson`/`logo` (avoid a lazy-registration bug). |\n| FR-10 | AUTH | `lesson` resolver: load lesson+module+course, then `assertCanViewCourse` + visibility rule (FR-18) for STUDENT/PARENT, while managers see drafts. `logo`: `() => true` incl. `user=null`. Depends on B1. Unattached files (contextId null) fall to the owner/ADMIN check even within the 'lesson' context, which lets editor previews work before attach. |\n| FR-11 | EP, AUTH | `DELETE /api/files/:id`: owner/ADMIN, `contextId === null`, else CONFLICT/VALIDATION_ERROR. Delete the row, then the bytes (log on bytes failure, since orphan bytes are harmless). Audit when ADMIN deletes another user's file (FR-46). |\n| FR-12 | JOB | `purgeOrphanFiles()` in `src/server/files/purge.ts`, hooked at B2. Batch `findMany` where contextId null and createdAt < now-24h, delete bytes then rows. **Caveat:** the logo is \"attached\" how? FR-40 stores a URL in logoUrl but contextId stays null, so the logo gets purged after 24h. **Design must set `contextId` for logo** (e.g. the SchoolSettings id/`'school'`) when settings are saved. |\n| FR-13 | UI | `src/components/FileUpload/`. XHR (not fetch) for `upload.onprogress`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`/`onChange` (FileObject summaries), and optional reorder (FR-27). MUI only (NFR-7). |\n| FR-14 | UI | `src/components/FileList/`: read-only list, links `/api/files/:id`. |\n| FR-15 | DM | `ContentStatus` enum, Module(courseId, title, position, status, publishAt), Lesson(moduleId, title, position, status, publishAt, contentMarkdown, estimatedMinutes, videoUrl, createdById?), LessonAttachment(lessonId, fileId, position), LessonLink(lessonId, title, url, position), and LessonProgress PK [lessonId, studentId]. Cascades: Course→Module→Lesson→Attachment/Link/Progress. Add back-relations on Course/User/StudentProfile. Index `[courseId, position]`, `[moduleId, position]`. Follow the PRD's exact field list. |\n| FR-16 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/content.ts` (Zod), shared by client and server. URL refinements reuse the FR-30 parser for videoUrl. |\n| FR-17 | SVC, AUTH | Inside the PATCH lesson transaction: verify each fileId is (owner==caller or ADMIN) and (contextId null or already == this lessonId), then `updateMany` context/contextId. Removed attachments should be detached (contextId → null), which leaves them purgeable in 24h. Decide explicitly. |\n| FR-18 | SVC | Pure `isVisible(entity, now)` + Prisma `where` fragment `visibleWhere(now)` = `OR[{status:PUBLISHED},{status:SCHEDULED, publishAt:{lte:now}}]` applied to both module and lesson. One source of truth used by list, get, prev/next, files, progress and learning. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Status Chip (grey/blue+date/green). Manager view = no visibility filter. |\n| FR-20 | UI, CFG | `courseTabs` entry `content`, all roles. A server component loads via content-service (not via HTTP). |\n| FR-21 | UI, SVC | Progress is computed over **visible** lessons only. \"Continue\" = first visible lesson in (module.position, lesson.position) order without completedAt. |\n| FR-22 | UI, EP | Menu actions map to PATCH /api/modules/:id (status/publishAt/title), DELETE, and reorder (move up/down reuses the reorder endpoint). |\n| FR-23 | EP, SVC, UI | `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder` with the full tree. Server validates that the set of module ids == the course's modules and the set of lesson ids == all the course's lessons (no foreign ids, no omissions), then rewrites positions + moduleId in one transaction. New dep `@dnd-kit/sortable`. |\n| FR-24 | UI | Type-to-confirm Dialog. Can ConfirmDialog be extended or does it need a local Dialog? Server DELETE cascades regardless. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Page `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` (manage). Client editor with Tabs Write/Preview (Preview = MarkdownView). Toolbar inserts text at the selection. |\n| FR-26 | UI | Image insert → FileUpload context `lesson` → `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. The file must then be attached (FR-17) or it gets purged. **Design:** on save, parse `/api/files/<id>` refs in markdown and attach them as context=lesson (not as LessonAttachment rows), or require explicit attach. |\n| FR-27 | EP, UI | PATCH /api/lessons/:id with `attachments: [{fileId}]` (order = position) and `links: [{title,url}]`. Replace-all semantics in a transaction. |\n| FR-28 | UI, VAL | Schedule: MUI X DateTimePicker (check the MUI X pickers package is installed and allowed, NFR-7). Convert school-tz → UTC on the client or server (NFR-10). Server rejects `publishAt <= now`. |\n| FR-29 | UI | Client timer + dirty flag, `beforeunload` + in-app navigation guard. PATCH with `status` untouched. |\n| FR-30 | SVC | `src/lib/video.ts` `parseVideoUrl(url) → {provider,id}|null`, shared by validator and renderer. Pure, unit test. |\n| FR-31 | UI | `src/components/MarkdownView/`. rehype-sanitize schema: default + `img.src` restricted to `/`-relative (same origin). New deps react-markdown, remark-gfm, rehype-sanitize. Client or server component is fine (react-markdown works in RSC). |\n| FR-32 | UI, SVC | Viewer page. Prev/next computed over the ordered visible-lesson list of the course (service helper reusing FR-18). |\n| FR-33 | EP, SVC, AUTH | First view: an upsert in the viewer page's server load for STUDENT with ACTIVE enrollment (set `firstViewedAt` only on create). `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress {completed}` sets/clears completedAt. Reject PARENT/TEACHER with FORBIDDEN, and a non-visible lesson → NOT_FOUND. |\n| FR-34 | EP, UI | `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` (assertCanManageCourse): ACTIVE enrollments left-joined with progress. 2 queries. |\n| FR-35 | EP, UI, CFG | `studentTabs` entry `learning`, `GET /api/students/:id/learning` (assertCanViewStudent). Per course of ACTIVE enrollments: visible lesson count, completed count, max(updatedAt/completedAt). Avoid per-course N+1 (group queries). |\n| FR-36 | UI, AUTH | Parent read-only: hide the button **and** the server rejects (FR-33). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | Reuse `assertCanViewCourse` unchanged. |\n| FR-38 | CFG, SVC | `content.lesson_published` in NOTIFICATION_TYPES. Fire only on the transition to visible via \"Publish now\" (lesson PUBLISHED **and** module currently visible). Recipients = ACTIVE enrolled students, using notify() with a batch/loop. |\n| FR-39 | UI | Tooltip only. No job (consistent with FR-18). |\n| FR-40 | UI, SVC | Logo FileUpload, context `logo`, size cap 2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg. On settings save, set FileObject.contextId (see FR-12 caveat) and logoUrl = `/api/files/<id>`. Fix the BaseLayout absolute URL (B4). |\n| FR-41 | VAL, EP | Allowlist is context-aware: `svg` is only in `logo`. file-type can't sniff SVG (it's text), so validate that it's text and contains `<svg`. On GET, add `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` when mime is image/svg+xml. |\n| FR-42 | UI | New `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` (requireRole ADMIN) + a nav entry. LOW confidence, accepted default. |\n| FR-43 | EP | 15 endpoints total (files ×3, modules ×4 incl. POST lessons, lessons ×3, reorder, progress ×2, learning). Use the existing response/error envelope and `{error:{code,message}}`. |\n| FR-44 | EP, AUTH | STUDENT/PARENT get NOT_FOUND (not FORBIDDEN) for hidden lessons. Same rule for files under FR-10. |\n| FR-45 | SVC | Layout: `src/server/content/content-service.ts`, `src/server/files/{access,service,purge,validate}.ts`, `src/server/storage.ts`. Thin routes. |\n| FR-46 | SVC | `audit()` when actor ≠ lesson/module creator. Needs a `createdById` on Module/Lesson, or always audit ADMIN mutations. Check whether FR-15's exact schema includes a creator field. If not, audit when the actor is ADMIN. |\n| FR-47 | DM (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. Add `prisma/seed-assets/*.pdf` copied into UPLOAD_DIR by the seed via `saveFile`. Sam = the existing seeded student. |\n| FR-48 | TEST | Unit: sanitizer, video parser, visibility, registry dispatch, sniff rules (FR-6). Integration: upload→attach→download + purge (a temp UPLOAD_DIR). One Playwright e2e. |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH | No files under `public/`, and every read goes through FR-9. Watch B1: making `/api/files/` public must not skip the registry. |\n| NFR-2 | UI | rehype-sanitize strips `javascript:`. Also apply link `href` protocol check in the `a` mapper (defence in depth). Unit/e2e with `[x](javascript:alert(1))`. |\n| NFR-3 | EP | B3. Return 429 RATE_LIMITED with `Retry-After`. Note the ceiling: per-process. |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | Content tab: ≤4 queries (modules with lessons ordered + `_count.attachments` + caller progress `where lessonId in`). Add DB indexes (FR-15). |\n| NFR-5 | SVC | Stream → hash → disk, with the byte cap during the stream. See the FR-3 multipart trade-off. Write to a temp name, then rename on success (no partial files under the final key). |\n| NFR-6 | UI | iframe `title`, alt-text warning, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | Dev must use mui-mcp docs before UI work. Blocker if unreachable. Includes the DateTimePicker (FR-28) package choice. |\n| NFR-8 | AUTH | Every route/page calls the assert helpers. Especially relevant for POST/DELETE /api/files if B1 is applied. |\n| NFR-9 | CFG | 5 new deps only. No renames. lint/typecheck/test green. |\n| NFR-10 | UI, SVC | UTC in the DB. Display via SchoolSettings.timezone (reuse the existing tz formatting helper if present). |\n| NFR-11 | — | No storage interface/S3 abstraction. No content copy. |\n| NFR-12 | CFG | Use the logger instead of console.log. Add `UPLOAD_DIR`, `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` to `.env.example` and the env schema. |\n\n## Open design decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n1. **B1 public files path**: either add `/api/files/` to PUBLIC_API_PATHS with explicit `requireUser()` on POST/DELETE (recommended), or special-case GET in middleware.\n2. **Logo orphan purge (FR-12 × FR-40)**: give logo files a non-null `contextId` on save, or they get deleted after 24h.\n3. **Inline markdown images (FR-26 × FR-12)**: attach images referenced in `contentMarkdown` on save, or they get purged.\n4. **Multipart vs streaming (FR-3 × NFR-5)**: `formData()` + a Content-Length pre-check, or a hand-rolled stream parser. No multipart dep is allowed.\n5. **Detach semantics (FR-17/FR-27)**: removing an attachment either nulls contextId (purged later) or deletes immediately.\n6. **Audit trigger (FR-46)**: either add a creator field or audit all ADMIN mutations on content.\n7. **SVG validation (FR-41)**: text sniff for `<svg`, logo context only, CSP header on serve.\n# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. 