{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnBqKmsL7WfbQjCnNNms","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have everything I need. Writing `system-design.md` now. The PRD uses `order` rather than `position`, and it has no creator field, so both choices get recorded in the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":67772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02965cf6-bb96-4d6d-ae8a-a3708e17396e","uuid":"6794bbba-aafd-4ca0-accb-dca937ce57ff","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:58:43.580Z","request_id":"req_011CgnBqKYyrooU9ULKwCC7w"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnBqKmsL7WfbQjCnNNms","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WGqUXiZZX1EzVp6f3k4fKC","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\n| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |\n| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |\n\n### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |\n| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |\n| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |\n| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |\n| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |\n| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |\n\n### 1.3 Schema note\n\nThe PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)\n\n- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.\n- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.\n- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.\n- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.\n\n### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |\n| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |\n\n**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.\n\n**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.\n\n### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |\n| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |\n| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |\n\n`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):\n\n- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.\n- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).\n- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.\n- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.\n- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.\n- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).\n- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).\n- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).\n- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).\n- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).\n- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).\n- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).\n\n### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)\n\n| Existing | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |\n| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |\n| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |\n| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |\n| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |\n| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |\n| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |\n\n### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\n| File | Methods | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |\n| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |\n\nThat is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)\n\n| File | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |\n| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |\n| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |\n| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |\n\n### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits\n\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).\n- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).\n- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.\n- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).\n- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)\n```\nFileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy\n   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)\n   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}\nLessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse\n   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach\nViewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile\n   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)\n   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN\n   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)\n```\n\n### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)\n```\nrequest ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?\n   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now\n```\nNo job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).\n\n### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)\n`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.\n\n### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)\nViewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.\n\n### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)\ndnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.\n\n### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)\nThe email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.\n\n### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)\nThe admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)\n\n- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.\n- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).\n- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).\n- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.\n- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.\n- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.\n- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.\n\n## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)\n\n- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).\n- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.\n- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.\n- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |\n| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |\n| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |\n| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |\n| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |\n| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |\n| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |\n| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |\n| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |\n| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |\n| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |\n| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |\n| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |\n| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |\n| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |\n| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |\n| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |\n| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |\n| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |\n| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |\n| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |\n| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |\n| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |\n| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |\n| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |\n| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |\n| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |\n| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |\n| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |\n| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |\n| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |\n| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |\n| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |\n| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |\n| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |\n| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |\n| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |\n| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |\n| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |\n| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |\n| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |\n| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |\n| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |\n| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |\n| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |\n| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |\n| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |\n| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |\n| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |\n| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |\n| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |\n| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |\n| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |\n| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":67772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":676},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02965cf6-bb96-4d6d-ae8a-a3708e17396e","uuid":"bbc856a0-1e66-49a6-9659-9e78c6f952fd","timestamp":"2026-11-06T19:00:48.265Z","request_id":"req_011CgnBqKYyrooU9ULKwCC7w","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WGqUXiZZX1EzVp6f3k4fKC":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\n| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |\n| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |\n\n### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |\n| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |\n| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |\n| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |\n| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |\n| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |\n\n### 1.3 Schema note\n\nThe PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)\n\n- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.\n- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.\n- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.\n- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.\n\n### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |\n| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |\n\n**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.\n\n**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.\n\n### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |\n| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |\n| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |\n\n`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):\n\n- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.\n- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).\n- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.\n- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.\n- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.\n- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).\n- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).\n- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).\n- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).\n- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).\n- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).\n- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).\n\n### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)\n\n| Existing | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |\n| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |\n| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |\n| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |\n| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |\n| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |\n| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |\n\n### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\n| File | Methods | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |\n| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |\n\nThat is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)\n\n| File | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |\n| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |\n| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |\n| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |\n\n### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits\n\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).\n- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).\n- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.\n- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).\n- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)\n```\nFileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy\n   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)\n   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}\nLessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse\n   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach\nViewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile\n   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)\n   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN\n   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)\n```\n\n### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)\n```\nrequest ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?\n   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now\n```\nNo job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).\n\n### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)\n`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.\n\n### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)\nViewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.\n\n### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)\ndnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.\n\n### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)\nThe email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.\n\n### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)\nThe admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)\n\n- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.\n- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).\n- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).\n- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.\n- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.\n- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.\n- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.\n\n## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)\n\n- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).\n- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.\n- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.\n- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |\n| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |\n| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |\n| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |\n| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |\n| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |\n| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |\n| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |\n| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |\n| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |\n| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |\n| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |\n| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |\n| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |\n| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |\n| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |\n| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |\n| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |\n| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |\n| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |\n| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |\n| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |\n| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |\n| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |\n| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |\n| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |\n| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |\n| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |\n| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |\n| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |\n| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |\n| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |\n| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |\n| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |\n| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |\n| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |\n| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |\n| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |\n| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |\n| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |\n| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |\n| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |\n| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |\n| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |\n| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |\n| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |\n| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |\n| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |\n| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |\n| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |\n| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |\n| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |\n| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |\n| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WGqUXiZZX1EzVp6f3k4fKC","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02965cf6-bb96-4d6d-ae8a-a3708e17396e","uuid":"d6a50a25-3c61-4f4b-ac7a-297894d145bb","timestamp":"2026-11-06T19:00:48.457Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\n| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |\n| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |\n\n### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |\n| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |\n| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |\n| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |\n| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |\n| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |\n\n### 1.3 Schema note\n\nThe PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)\n\n- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.\n- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.\n- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.\n- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.\n\n### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |\n| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |\n\n**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.\n\n**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.\n\n### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |\n| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |\n| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |\n\n`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):\n\n- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.\n- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).\n- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.\n- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.\n- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.\n- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).\n- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).\n- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).\n- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).\n- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).\n- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).\n- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).\n\n### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)\n\n| Existing | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |\n| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |\n| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |\n| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |\n| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |\n| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |\n| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |\n\n### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\n| File | Methods | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |\n| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |\n\nThat is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)\n\n| File | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |\n| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |\n| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |\n| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |\n\n### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits\n\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).\n- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).\n- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.\n- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).\n- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)\n```\nFileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy\n   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)\n   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}\nLessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse\n   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach\nViewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile\n   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)\n   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN\n   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)\n```\n\n### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)\n```\nrequest ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?\n   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now\n```\nNo job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).\n\n### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)\n`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.\n\n### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)\nViewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.\n\n### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)\ndnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.\n\n### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)\nThe email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.\n\n### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)\nThe admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)\n\n- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.\n- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).\n- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).\n- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.\n- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.\n- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.\n- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.\n\n## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)\n\n- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).\n- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.\n- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.\n- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |\n| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |\n| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |\n| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |\n| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |\n| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |\n| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |\n| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |\n| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |\n| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |\n| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |\n| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |\n| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |\n| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |\n| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |\n| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |\n| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |\n| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |\n| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |\n| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |\n| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |\n| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |\n| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |\n| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |\n| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |\n| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |\n| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |\n| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |\n| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |\n| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |\n| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |\n| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |\n| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |\n| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |\n| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |\n| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |\n| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |\n| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |\n| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |\n| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |\n| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |\n| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |\n| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |\n| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |\n| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |\n| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |\n| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |\n| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |\n| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |\n| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |\n| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |\n| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |\n| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |\n| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":353,"newStart":1,"newLines":281,"lines":["-# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)","+# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)"," ","-Ticket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),","-`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Ticket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),","+`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.","+> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder."," "," ---"," "," ## 1. Overview"," ","-SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5","-and MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet","-(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is","-built around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages","-sits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,","-settings, and the tab and nav configs.","+SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).","+SH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:"," ","-**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas","-(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.","-**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8).","+1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.","+2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification."," ","-### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)","+The design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2)."," ","-| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |","+### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)","+","+| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |"," |---|---|---|","-| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |","-| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |","-| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |","-| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |","-| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |","-| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |","+| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |","+| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |","+| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |","+| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |","+| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |","+| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |","+| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |","+| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |"," ","----","+### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)"," ","-## 2. Component Breakdown","-","-### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)","-","-| Module | Used for |","+| # | Decision |"," |---|---|","-| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |","-| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |","-| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |","-| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |","-| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |","-| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |","-| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |","-| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |","-| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |","-| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |","-| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |","+| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |","+| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |","+| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |","+| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |","+| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |","+| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |","+| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |"," ","-### 2.2 New components","+### 1.3 Schema note"," ","-#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)","+The PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students."," ","-`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):","+---"," ","-```prisma","-enum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }","-enum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }","+## 2. Component Breakdown"," ","-model AttendanceSession {","-  id          String   @id @default(cuid())","-  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)","-  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  sectionId   String?","-  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily","-  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])","-  date        DateTime @db.Date","-  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"","-  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])","-  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"","-  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])","-  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())","-  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt","-  records     AttendanceRecord[]","+### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)"," ","-  @@index([date])","-}","+- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.","+- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.","+- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.","+- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey."," ","-model AttendanceRecord {","-  id          String            @id @default(cuid())","-  sessionId   String","-  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  studentId   String","-  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])","-  status      AttendanceStatus","-  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE","-  note        String?           // ≤ 500","-  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())","-  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt","+### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`"," ","-  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])","-  @@index([studentId, createdAt])","-}","-// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)","-```","+| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |","+| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |","+| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |","+| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |","+| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |","+| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |","+| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |"," ","-Back-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).","+**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory."," ","-The migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):","-- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)","-- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)","-- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)","+**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`."," ","-The test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.","+### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`"," ","-#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)","-","-Add one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It","-follows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current","-year, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which","-the overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.","-","-#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)","-","-This file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.","-- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.","-- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).","-- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.","-- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.","-- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.","-- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).","-- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).","-","-#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)","-","-| Function | Reqs | Notes |","+| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|","-| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |","-| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |","-| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |","-| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |","-| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |","-| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |","-| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |","-| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |","-| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |","-| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |","+| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |","+| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |","+| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |","+| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |"," ","-**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**","-- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.","-- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year.","+`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):"," ","-**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default).","+- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.","+- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).","+- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.","+- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.","+- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.","+- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).","+- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).","+- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).","+- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).","+- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).","+- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).","+- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).","+- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46)."," ","-#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)","+### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)"," ","-| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |","-| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |","-| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |","-| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |","+| Existing | Used for |","+|---|---|","+| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |","+| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |","+| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |","+| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |","+| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |","+| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |","+| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |","+| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |","+| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |","+| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |","+| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |"," ","-#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)","+### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)"," ","-These schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:","-- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.","-- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).","-- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.","-- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.","-- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.","-- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.","-- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.","+| File | Methods | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |","+| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |","+| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |","+| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |","+| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |","+| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |","+| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |","+| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |","+| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |"," ","-Role-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the","-user, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.","+That is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`."," ","-#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)","+### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)"," ","-- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.","-- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.","-- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):","-  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.","-  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.","-  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.","-  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".","-  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).","-  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.","+| File | Notes | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |","+| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |","+| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |","+| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |","+| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |","+| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |","+| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |","+| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |","+| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |","+| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |"," ","-#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)","+### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits"," ","-`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:","-- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.","-- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.","-- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.","+- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).","+- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).","+- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).","+- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.","+- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).","+- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12)."," ","-#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)","-","-`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:","-- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).","-- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.","-- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.","-- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).","-","-One page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.","-","-#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)","-","-`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20","-dynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to","-`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.","-","-#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)","-","-- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.","-- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.","-- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.","-","-#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)","-","-- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.","-- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.","-- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.","-- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.","-"," ---"," "," ## 3. Data Flow"," ","-### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)","+### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)","+```","+FileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy","+   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)","+   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}","+LessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse","+   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach","+Viewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile","+   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)","+   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN","+   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)","+```"," ","-`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response.","-","-### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)","-","+### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)"," ```","-RegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)","-  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection","-  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).","-  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).","-  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {","-       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).","-       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).","-       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).","-       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.","-       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).","-       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).","-       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).","-     })","-  5. After commit:","-       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)","-       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)","-         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"","-         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"","-         link  /students/<id>/attendance","-  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET).","+request ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?","+   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now"," ```","+No job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39)."," ","-Brand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies","-once. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).","+### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)","+`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`."," ","-### 3.3 Read flows","+### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)","+Viewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course."," ","-- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).","-- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.","-- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.","-- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.","+### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)","+dnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast."," ","-### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)","+### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)","+The email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos."," ","-All \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`","-values. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.","+### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)","+The admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver."," "," ---"," ","-## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)","+## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)"," ","-| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |","-| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |","-| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |","-| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |","-| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |","-| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |","-| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |","-| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |","-| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |","-| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |","+- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.","+- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).","+- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).","+- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.","+- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.","+- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.","+- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts."," ","-All 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).","+## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)"," ","+- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).","+- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.","+- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.","+- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).","+"," ---"," ","-## 5. Requirements Traceability","+## 6. Requirements Traceability"," "," | Req | Design element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |","-| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |","-| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |","-| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |","-| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |","-| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |","-| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |","-| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |","-| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |","-| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |","-| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |","-| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |","-| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |","-| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |","-| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |","-| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |","-| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |","-| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |","-| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |","-| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |","-| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |","-| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |","-| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |","-| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |","-| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |","-| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |","-| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |","-| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |","-| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |","-| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |","-| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |","-| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |","-| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |","-| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |","-| FR-35 | §4 route table |","-| FR-36 | C6 validators |","-| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |","-| FR-38 | C12 seed |","-| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |","-| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |","-| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |","-| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |","-| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |","-| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |","-| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |","-| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |","-| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |","-| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |","-| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |","-| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |","-| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |","-","----","-","-## 6. Out of scope","-","-Holiday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),","-automatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first","-service workers (ADR-7).","+| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |","+| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |","+| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |","+| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |","+| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |","+| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |","+| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |","+| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |","+| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |","+| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |","+| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |","+| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |","+| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |","+| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |","+| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |","+| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |","+| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |","+| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |","+| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |","+| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |","+| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |","+| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |","+| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |","+| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |","+| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |","+| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |","+| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |","+| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |","+| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |","+| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |","+| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |","+| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |","+| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |","+| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |","+| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |","+| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |","+| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |","+| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |","+| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |","+| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |","+| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |","+| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |","+| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |","+| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |","+| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |","+| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |","+| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |","+| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |","+| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |","+| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |","+| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |","+| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |","+| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |","+| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |","+| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |","+| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |","+| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |","+| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |","+| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |","+| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |"]}],"originalFile":"# System Design: SH-7 · PRD-07 Attendance Tracking (SCH-007)\n\nTicket: SH-7 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T06:30:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (41 FR + 10 NFR, 94%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (6 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-9) and `requirements-analysis-notes.md`. Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-1 (PRD-01) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith: React 18, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5\nand MUI 9.5. Attendance is a **new feature inside a brownfield app**. Nothing attendance-related exists on disk yet\n(`src/server/attendance/` and `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` are both absent, which I verified). The feature is\nbuilt around a single service module and a single shared validator module. A thin set of route handlers and pages\nsits on top, and it plugs into existing extension points: the timetable, notify, access helpers, audit, csv,\nsettings, and the tab and nav configs.\n\n**Shape:** 1 migration · 1 service file + 1 pure rules file · 1 validator file · 10 API routes · 4 page areas\n(take, register, admin, 2 tabs) · 1 shared register client component · config entries · seed extension · tests.\n**No new dependencies, no job queue, no cron, no new auth abstraction** (ADR-1, ADR-4, ADR-5, ADR-8).\n\n### Intake blockers (compliance rule 5)\n\n| # | Blocker (`handoff-to-architect.json`) | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield within brownfield: models, migration, service, validators, 10 routes, pages, tabs, nav, seed, tests. | Components C1 to C12 below. |\n| 2 | Reuse getScheduleForDate, notify, the access asserts, audit, toCsv, settings and `src/components/<Name>/` (not `shared/`). | §2.1 lists the reused modules. C2 adds **one** additive export to the timetable service (school-wide schedule); everything else is consumed unchanged. |\n| 3 | **FR-5 (MEDIUM)**: there is no school settings page or route. | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (ADMIN) plus an \"Attendance settings\" card on `/admin/attendance` (C9). The user can override this. |\n| 4 | **FR-16 (LOW)**: the daily register route is unspecified. | `/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=` renders the same `RegisterForm` (C7). The user can override this. |\n| 5 | **FR-23 (LOW)**: metadata for corrected and register_missing is unspecified. | `attendance.corrected`: ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false. `attendance.register_missing`: ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false (C5). |\n| 6 | **NFR-6**: mui-mcp must be reachable before UI work, or it is a hard blocker. | Carried forward to dev. Every MUI component in C7 to C10 must be looked up via `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` for 9.5.0 first. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Existing modules reused (consumed only; not modified unless noted)\n\n| Module | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts`: `getScheduleForDate`, `getCurrentSlot`, `slotInclude` | FR-6/7 teacher landing, current-period highlight. **Additive change:** a new export, `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` (C2). |\n| `src/server/notifications/notify.ts`: `notifyStudentAndParents`, `notify` | FR-21/22/31. Both never throw. |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | **Additive:** 4 new keys (C5). |\n| `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`, `course-access.ts`, `student-access.ts` | NFR-7 in every handler and server page. |\n| `src/server/audit.ts`: `audit()` | FR-18. Uses the global `prisma` (no `tx` param) and never throws, so it is called **after commit**. |\n| `src/server/http.ts`: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` | Every route (NFR-8). |\n| `src/server/csv.ts`: `toCsv` | FR-32 CSV export. |\n| `src/server/services/settings.ts` | **Additive:** `UpdateSchoolSettingsInput` gains `attendanceMode?` and `attendanceAlertThreshold?` (FR-4/5). |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts`: `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | Every school-timezone computation (ADR-5). |\n| `src/components/{DataTable,StatCard,UserAvatar,PageHeader,EmptyState,DateDisplay,LoadingSkeleton,Toast}` | UI. Reuse in place; do not move or copy. |\n| `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | **Additive:** entries for FR-24/29/34. |\n\n### 2.2 New components\n\n#### C1 Data model and migration (FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, FR-4, NFR-8)\n\n`prisma/schema.prisma` (additive):\n\n```prisma\nenum AttendanceStatus { PRESENT ABSENT LATE EXCUSED }\nenum AttendanceMode   { PER_PERIOD DAILY_HOMEROOM BOTH }\n\nmodel AttendanceSession {\n  id          String   @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String?                     // exactly one of courseId / sectionId (CHECK)\n  course      Course?  @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  sectionId   String?\n  section     Section? @relation(fields: [sectionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  periodId    String?                     // set for course sessions, null for daily\n  period      Period?  @relation(fields: [periodId], references: [id])\n  date        DateTime @db.Date\n  takenById   String                      // FR-6 \"Taken HH:mm by <name>\"\n  takenBy     User     @relation(\"AttendanceTakenBy\", fields: [takenById], references: [id])\n  updatedById String                      // FR-14 \"last changed by\"\n  updatedBy   User     @relation(\"AttendanceUpdatedBy\", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])\n  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt\n  records     AttendanceRecord[]\n\n  @@index([date])\n}\n\nmodel AttendanceRecord {\n  id          String            @id @default(cuid())\n  sessionId   String\n  session     AttendanceSession @relation(fields: [sessionId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  student     User              @relation(fields: [studentId], references: [id])\n  status      AttendanceStatus\n  minutesLate Int?              // 1..240, required iff LATE\n  note        String?           // ≤ 500\n  createdAt   DateTime          @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime          @updatedAt\n\n  @@unique([sessionId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId, createdAt])\n}\n// SchoolSettings += attendanceMode AttendanceMode @default(PER_PERIOD), attendanceAlertThreshold Int @default(90)\n```\n\nBack-relations are added on `Course`, `Section`, `Period` and `User`. These are additive fields only, with no renames (NFR-10).\n\nThe migration is `prisma/migrations/20261107000000_attendance/`. Generate it with `--create-only`, then append the following by hand (ADR-2):\n- `CHECK (((\"courseId\" IS NOT NULL)::int + (\"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL)::int) = 1)` (FR-2)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_course_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"courseId\",\"date\",\"periodId\") WHERE \"courseId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n- `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX attendance_session_section_uq ON \"AttendanceSession\"(\"sectionId\",\"date\") WHERE \"sectionId\" IS NOT NULL` (FR-3)\n\nThe test database is built with `migrate reset`/`deploy`, never `db push`.\n\n#### C2 School-wide schedule helper (FR-30, FR-31)\n\nAdd one exported function to `timetable-service.ts`: `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date): Promise<ScheduleEntry[]>`. It\nfollows the same steps as `getScheduleForDate`: school-day check, **the PRD-14 holiday hook comment**, the current\nyear, and `slotInclude`, but with no target filter. `slotInclude.course` already carries `teacher` and `section`, which\nthe overview and remind features need. Existing functions are not changed.\n\n#### C3 Pure rules: `src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts` (FR-8, FR-19, FR-22, FR-28, FR-39)\n\nThis file has no DB imports, so unit tests need no database.\n- `schoolToday(now, tz): string`: `yyyy-MM-dd` in the school timezone.\n- `canOpen(role, date, today)`: refuses future dates. ADMIN can open any past date; TEACHER only dates where `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-8).\n- `canEdit(role, date, today)`: ADMIN always; TEACHER when `today − date ≤ 14` days (FR-19). Returns `{ ok, reason? }`; `reason` drives the read-only explanation.\n- `diffRecords(prev: Map<studentId, Rec>, next: Rec[])` → `{ created[], changed[{studentId, prev, next}] }`. This drives the writes, FR-18 audit and notifications.\n- `notificationsFor(diff)` → `{ absent[], late[], corrected[] }`: notifies on a transition *into* ABSENT, a transition *into* LATE, and ABSENT→PRESENT (corrected). Unchanged statuses produce nothing, which is the FR-22 dedupe.\n- `attendanceRate(counts)`: `(P+L+E)/total×100`, rounded to 1 dp, or `null` when total is 0 (FR-28).\n- `dayColour(statuses[])`: error if any ABSENT, else warning if any LATE, else success, or default when there is no data (FR-26).\n\n#### C4 Service: `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (FR-37)\n\n| Function | Reqs | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `getToday(user)` | FR-6, FR-7 | `getScheduleForDate({userId, role})` for today, joined with today's sessions (`takenBy`, `createdAt`). `getCurrentSlot` gives the highlighted entry. If the mode is DAILY_HOMEROOM or BOTH, it appends sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. |\n| `getRegister(user, key)` | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19, NFR-3 | `key` is `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`. Access: `assertCanManageCourse` (course) or `assertCanManageSection` (section). Runs `canOpen`. The roster is students active on the date (rule below), sorted by last name. Returns the existing records, `updatedBy`/`updatedAt`, `readOnly` and `readOnlyReason`, plus header labels (course, section, period, date). |\n| `saveRegister(user, key, records)` | FR-2, FR-10, FR-14, FR-18, FR-19, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3 | See §3.2. |\n| `assertCanManageSection(user, sectionId)` | FR-15, NFR-7 | ADMIN, or `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Otherwise it throws `AppError('FORBIDDEN')`. This is the only new access helper and stays private to this module. |\n| `getStudentAttendance(user, studentId, {from,to})` | FR-25 to FR-28, NFR-1 | `assertCanViewStudent`. Runs one `findMany` filtered by `session.date` and by the session kind for the mode (course sessions for PER_PERIOD/BOTH, section sessions for DAILY_HOMEROOM). Pure folds then produce the term and year summaries, the per-day calendar map and the table rows. **`note` is stripped when the role is STUDENT or PARENT** (FR-27). |\n| `getCourseMatrix(user, courseId)` | FR-29 | `assertCanManageCourse`. Loads the last 20 sessions by date and the students enrolled (ACTIVE plus DROPPED students who have records) with a P/A/L/E cell map and a per-student `attendanceRate`. |\n| `getOverview(date)` | FR-30, FR-31 | Expected = `getSchoolScheduleForDate(date)` plus sections, if the mode includes daily. Taken = sessions on that date. Missing = expected meetings with no session where `period.startTime + 15 min ≤ now` (school tz, only when `date` is today). Also returns the school-wide rate for the day. |\n| `remindTeacher(admin, {courseId, periodId, date})` | FR-31 | `notify({type:'attendance.register_missing', userIds:[course.teacherId], link:/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=})`, then `audit`. |\n| `getReport(filters)` | FR-32, NFR-8 | `groupBy(['studentId','status'])` over records filtered by session date range (≤ 366 days), grade, section, course and status, folded into per-student rows. The JSON response is paginated (pageSize ≤ 100); `?format=csv` returns all rows through `toCsv` with the same columns. |\n| `getBelowThreshold()` | FR-33 | The same aggregate over the current academic year (start to today), filtered to `rate < settings.attendanceAlertThreshold` and sorted ascending. |\n\n**Active-on-date rule (NFR-3, FR-9):**\n- Course: `Enrollment.courseId = X AND enrolledAt::date ≤ date AND (status = ACTIVE OR droppedAt::date > date)`.\n- Section: `SectionMember.sectionId = X` for the section's academic year.\n\n**Current term (FR-25):** the `Term` of the current year whose date range contains today; otherwise the latest ended term (intake default).\n\n#### C5 Notification types (FR-20, FR-23): `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (additive)\n\n| Key | category | defaultEmail | mandatoryInApp | roles |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `attendance.absent` | ATTENDANCE | true | true | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.late` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.corrected` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | PARENT, STUDENT |\n| `attendance.register_missing` | ATTENDANCE | false | false | TEACHER |\n\n#### C6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/attendance.ts` (FR-36)\n\nThese schemas are shared by `RegisterForm` and every handler:\n- `registerQuery`: either `{courseId, date, periodId}` or `{sectionId, date}`, as a Zod union. `date` uses `yyyy-MM-dd`.\n- `registerRecord`: `{studentId, status, minutesLate?, note?}`. A `superRefine` requires `minutesLate` 1–240 when the status is LATE and forbids it otherwise. `note` is at most 500 characters (FR-12).\n- `registerPutBody`: `registerQuery & { records: registerRecord[] }`. It has at least one record, and `studentId`s must be unique.\n- `studentAttendanceQuery {from?, to?}`, `courseMatrixQuery`, `overviewQuery {date?}`.\n- `reportFilters {from, to, gradeLevelId?, sectionId?, courseId?, status?, format?: 'csv'}`: a refine rejects ranges over 366 days or with `to < from`.\n- `remindBody {courseId, periodId, date}`.\n- `attendanceSettingsPatch {attendanceMode?, attendanceAlertThreshold?: int 0–100}`.\n\nRole-dependent rules (EXCUSED only for ADMIN, the 14-day window, future dates) are checked in the service against the\nuser, not in Zod. The client imports the same pure `canOpen` rule from C3 for the date picker's `minDate`/`disableFuture`.\n\n#### C7 Register UI (FR-6 to FR-17, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-9)\n\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/page.tsx` (server): calls `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` and `getToday`. Lists the meetings with their status, gives the current one a primary \"Take attendance\" button, shows \"Daily register – <section>\" entries, and has a `DatePicker` (`disableFuture`, `minDate` = today − 14 days for teachers) that navigates to the chosen date.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/[courseId]/page.tsx` and `.../take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx` (server): run `getRegister`, then render the same client component.\n- `src/app/(app)/attendance/take/RegisterForm.tsx` (client, the only register component):\n  - One row per student at least 48 px tall: `UserAvatar`, the name, and an exclusive `ToggleButtonGroup` P/A/L/E with targets at least 44×44 px, palette colours and an `aria-label` such as \"Mark <name> absent\". E is disabled unless the user is an ADMIN.\n  - Choosing L reveals a minutes input that defaults to 5. A note icon opens an optional note field.\n  - The header shows counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked) and \"Mark all present\", which fills only unset rows.\n  - A sticky `Paper` save bar has Save, disabled while any row is unmarked or the register is `readOnly`. When read-only, the form shows the reason and \"last changed by X at Y\".\n  - It PUTs to `/api/attendance/register`. On a network failure it writes a draft to `localStorage` under `attendance-draft:<courseId|section:sectionId>:<date>:<periodId|daily>`. On mount it offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" when a draft exists, and it clears the draft on success (NFR-2, ADR-7).\n  - Validation uses the C6 schemas.\n\n#### C8 Student Attendance tab (FR-24 to FR-28)\n\n`src/app/(app)/students/[studentId]/attendance/page.tsx` shows:\n- 2×4 `StatCard`s: term and year rate %, absent, late and excused counts.\n- A read-only `DateCalendar` with a custom `day` slot coloured by `dayColour`, a `Tooltip` per-day summary, and month navigation that refetches `?from=&to=`.\n- A `DataTable` with filters showing date, period, course, status, minutes late and note. Notes are already stripped server-side for STUDENT/PARENT.\n\n#### C9 Admin pages (FR-5, FR-30 to FR-33)\n\n`src/app/(app)/admin/attendance/page.tsx`, protected by `requireRole('ADMIN')`. It is a single page with MUI `Tabs`:\n- **Today**: expected vs taken, today's rate, and a \"Missing registers\" list with a \"Remind teacher\" button (POSTs to remind, then a toast).\n- **Report**: a filter form, a `DataGrid` with per-student rows, and an \"Export CSV\" link to `?format=csv`.\n- **Below threshold**: a list sorted ascending, each row linked to `/students/<id>/attendance`.\n- **Settings**: a card editing `attendanceMode` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` via `PATCH /api/settings/school` (FR-5).\n\nOne page with tabs instead of four routes keeps the file count down.\n\n#### C10 Course Attendance tab (FR-29)\n\n`src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/attendance/page.tsx` is a `DataGrid` with one row per student. It has up to 20\ndynamic date columns that scroll horizontally, with coloured cells, plus a rate column. Each column header links to\n`/attendance/take/<courseId>?date=&periodId=`.\n\n#### C11 Config and nav (FR-24, FR-29, FR-34)\n\n- `student-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', label:'Attendance', href: id => /students/${id}/attendance, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. Page access still goes through `assertCanViewStudent`.\n- `course-tabs.ts`: add `{key:'attendance', …, roles:['TEACHER','ADMIN']}`.\n- `navigation.ts`: add \"Attendance\" for TEACHER → `/attendance/take` and \"Attendance\" for ADMIN in the main group → `/admin/attendance`.\n\n#### C12 Seed and tests (FR-38 to FR-41)\n\n- **Seed:** extend the existing seed with a mulberry32 RNG using a fixed seed. Generate 7A/7B course sessions for each timetable slot over the 15 teaching days before the run date, using `SchoolDay`. Records are about 94% P, 3% L (minutes 5–20) and 3% A. Force two named Grade 7 students below 85%. Make the seed idempotent: delete the attendance rows for that window first.\n- **Unit:** `attendance-rules.test.ts` covers `attendanceRate`, `canEdit`/`canOpen` at the 14/15-day edges, and `diffRecords`/`notificationsFor`, including re-saving with no changes and ABSENT→PRESENT.\n- **Integration:** `attendance-service.int.test.ts` covers atomic save (a failing record means no session row), NFR-3 rejection, the CHECK constraint, both partial unique indexes, EXCUSED rejected for a teacher, and the edit window returning 403.\n- **E2E:** `attendance.spec.ts` at 375×667 takes a register (mark all present, one absent, one late, save), then logs in as the parent and sees the notification and a red day on the calendar.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Request pipeline (every route, NFR-7, NFR-8)\n\n`withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → `parseQuery`/`parseBody` (C6) → resource assert → service (C4) → `ok`/`paginated` or `AppError` → response.\n\n### 3.2 Save register: `PUT /api/attendance/register` (FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-5)\n\n```\nRegisterForm ──PUT {key, records[]}──► route ─► saveRegister(user, key, records)\n  1. Access: assertCanManageCourse | assertCanManageSection\n  2. canOpen(date) else 400. canEdit(role, date, today) else 403 FORBIDDEN (FR-19).\n  3. Any EXCUSED and role ≠ ADMIN → 403 (FR-10).\n  4. prisma.$transaction(async tx => {\n       roster = active-on-date ids (one query). Any record.studentId ∉ roster → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR (NFR-3).\n       Records must cover the whole roster → else 400 (FR-13 server-side mirror).\n       session = findFirst(key) ?? create(...). On P2002, re-read (ADR-3, partial idx race).\n       prev = findMany({sessionId}) → Map.\n       diff = diffRecords(prev, records).\n       createMany(diff.created). update each diff.changed row (≤ roster size).\n       session.update({updatedById: user.id}).\n     })\n  5. After commit:\n       for c of diff.changed where status changed → audit('attendance.record.update', {old, new, note}, actor)  (FR-18)\n       for n of notificationsFor(diff) → notifyStudentAndParents (one call per student)  (FR-21/22)\n         title \"X was marked absent\" | \"X was marked late (N min)\" | \"Attendance corrected: X was present\"\n         body  \"<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <EEEE d MMM yyyy>\" | \"<Section> daily register, <date>\"\n         link  /students/<id>/attendance\n  6. Return the fresh register (same shape as GET).\n```\n\nBrand-new records count as transitions from \"nothing\", so the first save that marks a student ABSENT notifies\nonce. A re-save with the same status produces no diff and sends nothing (FR-22).\n\n### 3.3 Read flows\n\n- **Teacher landing:** `/attendance/take` → `getToday` → timetable + sessions (+ homeroom sections).\n- **Student tab:** `GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=` → one indexed query → pure folds (rate, calendar, rows), with notes stripped by role.\n- **Admin overview:** `getSchoolScheduleForDate(today)` minus today's sessions, filtered by the `startTime + 15 min` rule in the school timezone.\n- **Report / below threshold:** `groupBy` on (studentId, status) → per-student rows → JSON page or CSV.\n\n### 3.4 Time handling (ADR-5)\n\nAll \"today\", future-date and 14-day comparisons use `schoolToday(now, settings.timezone)` against `@db.Date`\nvalues. Times are shown with `formatInSchoolTz`. Server-local `new Date()` is never used for date-only logic.\n\n---\n\n## 4. API surface (detailed in `api-contracts.json` by arch-api-contracts)\n\n| Method | Path | Guard | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| GET | `/api/attendance/today` | TEACHER, ADMIN | FR-6, FR-7 |\n| GET | `/api/attendance/register?courseId&date&periodId` or `?sectionId&date` | manage course / homeroom or ADMIN | FR-8, FR-9, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19 |\n| PUT | `/api/attendance/register` | same, plus edit window and EXCUSED rule | FR-10, FR-14, FR-18 to FR-22, NFR-3 |\n| GET | `/api/students/:id/attendance?from&to` | `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-25 to FR-28 |\n| GET | `/api/courses/:id/attendance` | `assertCanManageCourse` | FR-29 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/overview?date` | ADMIN | FR-30, FR-31 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/report?…&format=csv` | ADMIN | FR-32 |\n| GET | `/api/admin/attendance/below-threshold` | ADMIN | FR-33 |\n| POST | `/api/admin/attendance/remind` | ADMIN | FR-31 |\n| PATCH | `/api/settings/school` | ADMIN, with audit | FR-4, FR-5 |\n\nAll 10 are listed under FR-35. Error codes come from `http.ts` (`VALIDATION_ERROR` 400, `FORBIDDEN` 403, `NOT_FOUND` 404).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | C1 models and enum |\n| FR-2 | C1 CHECK; C4 `saveRegister` key shape (C6 union) |\n| FR-3 | C1 partial unique indexes; §3.2 P2002 re-read |\n| FR-4 | C1 SchoolSettings columns; settings service input |\n| FR-5 | C9 Settings tab; `PATCH /api/settings/school` |\n| FR-6 | C4 `getToday`; C7 landing |\n| FR-7 | C4 `getToday` homeroom entries; C7 |\n| FR-8 | C3 `canOpen`; C7 DatePicker |\n| FR-9 | C4 roster rule; C7 `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-10 | §3.2 step 3; C7 E disabled |\n| FR-11 | C7 \"Mark all present\" |\n| FR-12 | C6 `registerRecord`; C7 minutes and note inputs |\n| FR-13 | C7 counters and Save disabled; §3.2 full-roster check |\n| FR-14 | §3.2 transaction; `updatedBy`/`updatedAt` |\n| FR-15 | C4 `assertCanManageSection`; section roster |\n| FR-16 | C7 section route reusing `RegisterForm` |\n| FR-17 | C7 48 px rows, 44 px toggles, sticky Paper |\n| FR-18 | §3.2 step 5 audit |\n| FR-19 | C3 `canEdit`; §3.2 step 2; C7 read-only mode |\n| FR-20 | C5 absent and late types |\n| FR-21 | §3.2 step 5 notify; C3 `notificationsFor` |\n| FR-22 | C3 `notificationsFor` (transition-only, corrected) |\n| FR-23 | C5 corrected and register_missing types |\n| FR-24 | C11 student tab; C8 page |\n| FR-25 | C4 `getStudentAttendance`; C8 StatCards |\n| FR-26 | C3 `dayColour`; C8 DateCalendar day slot |\n| FR-27 | C4 note stripping; C8 DataTable |\n| FR-28 | C3 `attendanceRate`; C4 mode-based session kind |\n| FR-29 | C4 `getCourseMatrix`; C10; C11 course tab |\n| FR-30 | C2 `getSchoolScheduleForDate`; C4 `getOverview`; C9 Today |\n| FR-31 | C4 missing rule and `remindTeacher`; C9 Remind button |\n| FR-32 | C4 `getReport`; C6 `reportFilters`; C9 Report and CSV |\n| FR-33 | C4 `getBelowThreshold`; C9 Below threshold |\n| FR-34 | C11 navigation entries |\n| FR-35 | §4 route table |\n| FR-36 | C6 validators |\n| FR-37 | C4 service path (+ C3 sibling rules file) |\n| FR-38 | C12 seed |\n| FR-39 | C12 unit tests on C3 |\n| FR-40 | C12 integration tests |\n| FR-41 | C12 Playwright |\n| NFR-1 | §3.2 single tx with batched writes; C4 single-query student tab |\n| NFR-2 | C7 localStorage draft and restore |\n| NFR-3 | C4 active-on-date rule; §3.2 roster check |\n| NFR-4 | C7 mark-all-present plus mobile layout |\n| NFR-5 | §3.2 post-commit `notifyStudentAndParents` (in-app immediate, EmailOutbox) |\n| NFR-6 | C7 to C10 MUI only, with mui-mcp lookups (Overview blocker 6) |\n| NFR-7 | §3.1 pipeline; C4 asserts; note stripping |\n| NFR-8 | C1 cuid and `@db.Date`; §3.4 timezone; §4 http helpers; pagination ≤ 100 |\n| NFR-9 | C7 `aria-label`s and 44 px targets |\n| NFR-10 | §2.1 reuse in place, only additive changes, no new deps, holidays (PRD-14) and EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15) excluded |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out of scope\n\nHoliday handling (PRD-14, which stays at the existing hook comment), the absence-note/EXCUSED workflow (PRD-15),\nautomatic missing-register reminders (no scheduler; ADR-5), a general school settings page, and offline-first\nservice workers (ADR-7).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WGqUXiZZX1EzVp6f3k4fKC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
