{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnCZKH39QZAZ5wW4obW2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-8, replacing an old SH-7 design that was in the folder. I checked every requirement ID it cites against `requirements.json`. All 60 requirements (48 functional, 12 non-functional) are cited and none of the cited IDs are invalid.\n\nThe document covers the overview, the component breakdown, data flows, security boundaries, the test plan and a traceability table. The Overview lists intake's 8 blockers and how each is handled. It also settles the 7 open questions from the research notes:\n\n- **Public file route:** `/api/files/` gets added to the middleware's public list so logos load without a session. Upload and delete therefore have to check the session themselves with `requireUser()`. Downloads still go through the access registry, which allows only logos for signed-out users.\n- **Logo vs. orphan purge:** a saved logo is marked as attached to the school settings, so the 24-hour orphan purge won't delete it. The previous logo is marked unattached and gets purged.\n- **Images inside lesson text:** saving a lesson finds `/api/files/<id>` links in the Markdown and attaches those files. Without this, the purge would delete them after 24 hours.\n- **Removing files:** a file removed from a lesson is marked unattached and purged 24 hours later. Deleting a lesson or module does the same for its files first, so they aren't left behind forever.\n- **Uploads:** they stream to disk using `busboy`, which Next.js already installs, so no new dependency is needed.\n- **Audit log:** the PRD's schema has no \"created by\" field, so the rule is to audit every content change made by an admin who isn't teaching the course, and every deletion of someone else's file.\n- **SVG:** allowed only for logos, checked for `<svg` in the file's opening bytes, and served with a locked-down security header.\n\nThree things differ from what intake or the research notes assumed:\n- The PRD names the ordering column `order`, not `position` as the research notes said. The design uses `order`.\n- The delete confirmation where you type the module title needs a new optional `confirmText` prop on the existing `ConfirmDialog`. It's an addition, so existing uses aren't affected.\n- The settings update (`PATCH /api/settings/school`) gains an optional `logoFileId` field.\n\n`api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in that folder are still SH-7 leftovers. Writing them is `arch-api-contracts`' job, so I didn't touch them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":276,"cache_read_input_tokens":83792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":276},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02965cf6-bb96-4d6d-ae8a-a3708e17396e","uuid":"84e1faf3-c365-4392-9bac-3dd3f05138f8","timestamp":"2026-11-06T19:08:19.909Z","request_id":"req_011CgnCZJzv3wEydZudoZ4k5"}
