{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Y9LPYzGSgLTLTwa3SUhX5","type":"tool_result","content":"artifacts/architect:\ntotal 216\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  9 10:26 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16669 Nov  6 10:35 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1572 Nov  6 10:36 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  28433 Nov  9 10:26 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  33679 Nov  7 00:00 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  12704 Nov  9 10:25 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    396 Nov  7 01:31 threat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\ntotal 104\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 10:23 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   2374 Nov  9 10:23 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  31946 Nov  9 10:22 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1104 Nov  9 10:23 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   8749 Nov  9 10:23 user-stories.md\n?? ../../../.CFUserTextEncoding\n?? ../../../.anaconda/\n?? ../../../.android/\n?? ../../../.aws/\n?? ../../../.bash_profile\n?? ../../../.cache/\n?? ../../../.claude.json\n?? ../../../.claude.json.backup\n?? ../../../.claude/\n?? ../../../.cocoapods/\n?? ../../../.conda/\n?? ../../../.config/\n?? ../../../.cups/\n?? ../../../.cursor/\n?? ../../../.emulator_console_auth_token\n?? ../../../.eslintrc\n?? ../../../.gem/\n?? ../../../.gitconfig\n?? ../../../.gitignore\n?? ../../../.gradle/\ndd8bf49 cursor: empty commit to allow worktree creation\n# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\nartifacts/architect/api-contracts.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-7\"\nartifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-7\"\nartifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"\nartifacts/dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"\nartifacts/dev-planning/implementation-plan.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"\nartifacts/dev-planning/module-dependencies.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a7b6583-29f5-43b3-9f4e-72722e4e3a4f","uuid":"9791146e-2aa0-4372-8a6c-d218e88a5dca","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:26:46.475Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"artifacts/architect:\ntotal 216\ndrwxr-xr-x   8 ikramaansari  staff    256 Nov  9 10:26 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  16669 Nov  6 10:35 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1572 Nov  6 10:36 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  28433 Nov  9 10:26 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  33679 Nov  7 00:00 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  12704 Nov  9 10:25 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    396 Nov  7 01:31 threat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/intake:\ntotal 104\ndrwxr-xr-x   6 ikramaansari  staff    192 Nov  9 10:23 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   2374 Nov  9 10:23 handoff-to-architect.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  31946 Nov  9 10:22 requirements.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   1104 Nov  9 10:23 tech-stack.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   8749 Nov  9 10:23 user-stories.md\n?? ../../../.CFUserTextEncoding\n?? ../../../.anaconda/\n?? ../../../.android/\n?? ../../../.aws/\n?? ../../../.bash_profile\n?? ../../../.cache/\n?? ../../../.claude.json\n?? ../../../.claude.json.backup\n?? ../../../.claude/\n?? ../../../.cocoapods/\n?? ../../../.conda/\n?? ../../../.config/\n?? ../../../.cups/\n?? ../../../.cursor/\n?? ../../../.emulator_console_auth_token\n?? ../../../.eslintrc\n?? ../../../.gem/\n?? ../../../.gitconfig\n?? ../../../.gitignore\n?? ../../../.gradle/\ndd8bf49 cursor: empty commit to allow worktree creation\n# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\nartifacts/architect/api-contracts.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-7\"\nartifacts/architect/handoff-to-dev-planning.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-7\"\nartifacts/architect/threat-model-notes.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"\nartifacts/dev-planning/file-ownership-matrix.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"\nartifacts/dev-planning/implementation-plan.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"\nartifacts/dev-planning/module-dependencies.json:\"ticketId\": \"SH-8\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017Y9LPYzGSgLTLTwa3SUhX5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
