{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FMdcmoUhcFaWefA34fLY5a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n6\t\n7\tNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n8\t\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n12\t\n13\t**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n14\t\n15\t**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n16\t| Need | Use | Req |\n17\t|---|---|---|\n18\t| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n19\t| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n20\t| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n21\t| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n22\t| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n23\t| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n24\t\n25\t**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n30\t\n31\t**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n32\t\n33\t**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n34\t\n35\t**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n40\t\n41\t**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n42\t\n43\t**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n44\t\n45\t**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n46\t\n47\t---\n48\t\n49\t## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n50\t\n51\t**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n52\t\n53\t**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n54\t\n55\t**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n60\t\n61\t**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n62\t\n63\t**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n64\t- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n65\t- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n66\t- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n67\t- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n68\t\n69\tUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n70\t\n71\t**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n76\t\n77\t**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n78\t\n79\t**Decision.**\n80\t- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n81\t- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n82\t- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n83\t\n84\t**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n85\t\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n89\t\n90\t**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n91\t\n92\t**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n93\t\n94\t**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n95\t\n96\t---\n97\t\n98\t## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n99\t\n100\t**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n101\t\n102\t**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n103\t\n104\t**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n105\t\n106\t---\n107\t\n108\t## Blockers carried forward\n109\t\n110\t1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n111\t2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n112\t3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n113\t4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a7b6583-29f5-43b3-9f4e-72722e4e3a4f","uuid":"048e3f9e-58e9-41ad-b8a7-a367ad34d4de","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:26:49.109Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T09:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (confirmed against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript 5.5.4 strict, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, and MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Also installed: @dnd-kit/core 6.3.1 + @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0, date-fns 3.6.0 / date-fns-tz 3.2.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, file-type 20.5.0, decimal.js 10.6.0 (via Prisma), Vitest 2.1.1 (jsdom) and Playwright 1.47.2. `engines.node >=18.18.0`.\n\nNone of the FR/NFRs needs a different stack. There is no latency target beyond NFR-3, no offline requirement and no realtime requirement. **Overall decision: add no new dependencies.** The ADRs below record how PRD-09 fits into this stack and how to resolve the environment blockers that intake reported.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add zero dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-11 forbids re-scaffolding or duplicating helpers. NFR-6 allows UI only from MUI v9.5.0 and MUI X. Every library that PRD-09 needs is already a direct dependency: Markdown (NFR-10), drag-to-reorder for rubric criteria (FR-11, @dnd-kit/sortable), date/timezone maths (FR-10, FR-23, NFR-9, date-fns-tz), Decimal maths (NFR-1, decimal.js via Prisma), forms and validation (FR-7, react-hook-form + Zod), and the date-time picker (FR-9, @mui/x-date-pickers, with the `AdapterDateFns` provider already in `src/app/providers.tsx`).\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Use the following:\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Score maths | `Prisma.Decimal` (from `@prisma/client`). Never import `decimal.js` directly, so the version cannot drift from Prisma's. | FR-31, FR-36, NFR-1 |\n| Markdown render | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, with components mapped to MUI | FR-19, FR-29, NFR-10 |\n| Rubric criterion reorder | @dnd-kit/sortable (Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, NFR-17) | FR-11 |\n| Forms | react-hook-form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with the shared schemas in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | FR-7, FR-9 |\n| Due date-time input | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DateTimePicker` | FR-9, FR-12 |\n| File sniffing | Already done server-side by the existing files service (file-type 20.5.0). Nothing new in PRD-09. | FR-47, FR-53 |\n\n**Consequences.** No lockfile churn from new packages. Anything outside this list that dev reaches for is a scope smell. ESLint `no-restricted-imports` (NFR-6) still guards the UI side.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Fix the MUI X break by pinning `@mui/x-internals` to 9.1.0 through `overrides`\n\n**Context.** FR-17 (teacher assignments table) and the existing `src/components/DataTable/DataTable.tsx` both use `@mui/x-data-grid`. In `package-lock.json`, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers and x-charts 9.5.0 each declare `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"^9.1.0\"`. npm resolved that range to **9.15.0**, which no longer provides an export the 9.5.0 packages import, so every DataGrid page fails to compile. The npm registry has no `@mui/x-internals@9.5.0`: the published versions jump from 9.1.0 to 9.6.0. So **9.1.0** is the version that was current when the 9.5.0 X packages shipped. `package.json` already uses `overrides` for `react-is` and `playwright-core`, so the pattern is established.\n\n**Decision.** Add `\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\"` to `package.json` `overrides`, run `npm install`, and confirm with `npm ls @mui/x-internals` (every entry must show 9.1.0) and with a compile of an existing DataTable page. Do not upgrade the MUI X packages themselves, because NFR-6 pins MUI X at 9.5.0. **Fallback** (only if 9.1.0 also fails to compile): render the FR-17 table with MUI `Table` (the course list is small and unpaginated), and file the DataGrid fix as a separate ticket.\n\n**Consequences.** This also repairs every earlier DataTable page (a side benefit, with no behaviour change). The X packages must not be bumped without lifting or adjusting this override. It is one line in `package.json` plus the lockfile.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Fix the Vitest config import instead of keeping a temporary config\n\n**Context.** NFR-13 needs `npm run test` to pass, and NFR-14 adds unit and integration tests. `vitest.config.ts` imports `'vitest/config.js'`, which does not resolve. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` differs from it **only** in that import line (`'vitest/config'`).\n\n**Decision.** Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`. `npm run test` (`vitest run`) then works with no flags.\n\n**Consequences.** There is one config, and CI and local runs agree. This is a one-line fix plus one file deletion, with no test behaviour change.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Keep the production CSP and use `bypassCSP` only in the PRD-09 e2e spec\n\n**Context.** `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`. That blocks Next 14's inline hydration scripts in a real browser. NFR-14 requires a Playwright e2e of the create → submit → grade → return → view flow. Fixing CSP properly (per-request nonces through middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`) is a platform-wide security change. That belongs outside the PRD-09 scope (NFR-15: do not change behaviour that other PRDs own), and loosening it would weaken security.\n\n**Decision.** Do not touch `next.config.js` in this ticket. The PRD-09 e2e spec sets `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })`, as earlier e2e runs did. Record the CSP nonce work as a follow-up blocker in the handoff.\n\n**Consequences.** The e2e passes without weakening production headers. Hydration in a real browser stays broken platform-wide until the nonce fix ships, so manual UI verification needs the same bypass. This is a known, pre-existing issue, not one this ticket introduces.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Build the minimal missing PRD-08 UI components in `src/components/` inside this ticket\n\n**Context.** SH-8 failed QA. Its file backend exists (POST /api/files with a `context` field, GET /api/files/[id]?inline=1, `registerFileAccess`/contexts, files-service), but `FileUpload`, `FileList`, `MarkdownView` and a Markdown editor do not. FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29 and FR-30 cannot render without them. NFR-11 says do not duplicate. Because nothing exists yet, building them once as shared components is not duplication.\n\n**Decision.** Add these components, one folder each, following the existing `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` convention:\n- `MarkdownView`: react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema), with elements mapped to MUI `Typography`/`Link`/`Table`/etc. (NFR-10).\n- `MarkdownEditor`: an MUI `TextField multiline` with Write/Preview `Tabs`, where Preview renders `MarkdownView`. No rich-text editor library (ADR-1). It is used for instructions (FR-9), submission text (FR-20) and feedback (FR-30).\n- `FileUpload`: an MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`, POSTing each file to `/api/files` with `context` (`'assignment'` | `'submission'`), plus a `max` count prop (FR-20 maxFileCount). It returns `fileId[]` and shows a `LinearProgress` per file.\n- `FileList`: an MUI `List` of file links to `/api/files/:id`, with an optional inline preview (`<img>`/`<iframe>` to `?inline=1`) for images and PDFs (FR-29).\n\nUse the native file input rather than a dropzone library. Drag-and-drop onto the button is optional and needs no dependency.\n\n**Consequences.** PRD-08's remaining UI can later reuse these components instead of recreating them. The scope stays limited to what PRD-09 needs, so other PRD-08 features (course content pages, etc.) stay out (NFR-15).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Time and deadline maths in UTC, with `date-fns-tz` only for school-timezone rendering and defaults\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 and NFR-9 require server time only, UTC storage, and correct late-day counts across DST and on the exact 24 h boundary. FR-23 defines `lateDays = ceil((submittedAt − dueAt) / 24h)`. That is a pure UTC millisecond difference, so DST cannot affect it: elapsed time is elapsed time. FR-10 (next teaching day at 23:59 school time) and FR-25 (receipt in school timezone) are the only operations that depend on the timezone. `src/lib/dates.ts` already exports `formatInSchoolTz` and `schoolNow`.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `lateDays = Math.ceil((submittedAt.getTime() − dueAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000)` when `isLate`, otherwise 0, computed from `new Date()` on the server. Exactly 24 h late gives 1. Put this function and the penalty/final-score helpers in a small pure module, `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts`, so the NFR-14 unit tests need no DB.\n- FR-10 default due time: walk forward from tomorrow in `SchoolSettings.timezone` until `SchoolDay.isTeaching`, take 23:59 local, and convert it with `fromZonedTime` (date-fns-tz). Add this as a new helper in `src/lib/dates.ts`, next to the existing ones. Do not create a new dates module.\n- All displays use the existing `formatInSchoolTz`.\n\n**Consequences.** DST correctness comes from doing the arithmetic in UTC, not from special-case code. The NFR-14 DST test asserts that, for example, a deadline at 23:59 the night before a spring-forward plus 23 wall-clock hours still counts as 1 late day.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Decimal arithmetic with `Prisma.Decimal`, using ROUND_HALF_UP to 2 dp, computed server-side only\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 and FR-31 require `finalScore = rawScore × (1 − penaltyPercent/100)`, rounded half-up to 2 dp, with no JS floats. FR-30 also requires a live preview in the grading form. The schema uses `Decimal(6,2)` columns (FR-2, FR-3, FR-4).\n\n**Decision.** The server computes the stored `finalScore` with `Prisma.Decimal`: `raw.mul(new Decimal(100).minus(pct)).div(100).toDecimalPlaces(2, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`. The penalty pre-fill is `Decimal.min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)` (FR-30). The client preview may import `Decimal` from `decimal.js` through the same helper module (`grading-math.ts` is pure and isomorphic), but the server value is authoritative (NFR-2). Decimals cross the API boundary as **strings** (for example `\"14.40\"`), never as JSON numbers.\n\n**Consequences.** The preview and the stored value agree because they share one function. API contracts must type score fields as decimal strings, and `arch-api-contracts` should follow this. Note: importing `decimal.js` in client code relies on Prisma's transitive install. If that worries anyone, the client preview can instead call the server function through the form's submit path. Default: share the module.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: No background job, queue or cron. Reminders run inside the existing PRD-04 dispatcher\n\n**Context.** FR-13 says visibility is computed at read time, with no status-flip job. FR-42 says `assignment.published` for SCHEDULED assignments fires on the first student list load after `availableFrom`, deduplicated by an atomic `notifiedAt` set. FR-43 and FR-45 say `sendDueReminders()` runs on every call to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, deduplicated by the `AssignmentReminder` unique key (FR-6).\n\n**Decision.** Add no scheduler, queue library or new worker. Visibility is a single predicate, `status = PUBLISHED OR (status = SCHEDULED AND availableFrom <= now())`, also requiring `archivedAt IS NULL` for students and parents (FR-52). It lives in one place in `assignments-service.ts`. Once-only sends use a conditional write: `updateMany({ where: { id, notifiedAt: null }, data: { notifiedAt: now } })` and send only when `count === 1` (FR-42). Reminders use `createMany({ skipDuplicates: true })` against the `(assignmentId, studentId, kind)` unique key and notify only the rows actually inserted (FR-43, FR-45). Alternatively, insert per row and catch P2002.\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency is enforced by Postgres constraints, not by application locks, so it is safe under concurrent dispatcher calls. Reminder latency is bounded by how often the dispatcher runs. That is acceptable, because the PRD ties reminders to that dispatcher.\n\n---\n\n## Blockers carried forward\n\n1. ADR-2 depends on `@mui/x-internals@9.1.0` compiling against X 9.5.0. Dev must verify. The fallback is defined.\n2. ADR-4: the platform CSP nonce fix is out of scope. Real-browser hydration stays broken until a dedicated ticket fixes it.\n3. NFR-6: dev must reach mui-mcp before writing UI. If it is unreachable, that is a hard blocker per the PRD.\n4. FR-41: `studentTabs` has no renderer, so the tab is registered but not visible. This is not a stack issue and is left to `arch-design-system`.\n","numLines":114,"startLine":1,"totalLines":114}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FMdcmoUhcFaWefA34fLY5a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgroMA8NTLqADWa1PTL4P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011PcCzrE5QaKo7qqESv9wgX","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2527,"cache_read_input_tokens":28320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2527},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a7b6583-29f5-43b3-9f4e-72722e4e3a4f","uuid":"93762770-a950-4cdd-b13f-a0d37fea97ae","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:26:49.584Z","request_id":"req_011CgroM9wxf9xi583mX3Fxc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011PcCzrE5QaKo7qqESv9wgX":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011PcCzrE5QaKo7qqESv9wgX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9\n2\t\n3\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n5\t`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them.\n6\t\n7\t> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input.\n8\t\n9\t## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n10\t\n11\t| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |\n12\t|---|---|---|---|\n13\t| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |\n14\t| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |\n15\t| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |\n16\t| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |\n17\t| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |\n18\t| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |\n19\t| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |\n20\t| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |\n21\t| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |\n22\t| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |\n23\t| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |\n24\t| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |\n25\t| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |\n26\t| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |\n27\t| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |\n28\t| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |\n29\t\n30\t## Requirement → architectural concern\n31\t\n32\tLegend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data\n33\t\n34\t### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)\n35\t\n36\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n37\t|---|---|---|\n38\t| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |\n39\t| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |\n40\t| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |\n41\t| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |\n42\t| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |\n43\t| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |\n44\t| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |\n45\t| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |\n46\t\n47\t### Assignment authoring (teacher)\n48\t\n49\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n50\t|---|---|---|\n51\t| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |\n52\t| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |\n53\t| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |\n54\t| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |\n55\t| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |\n56\t| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |\n57\t| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |\n58\t\n59\t### Lists and navigation\n60\t\n61\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n62\t|---|---|---|\n63\t| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |\n64\t| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |\n65\t| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |\n66\t| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |\n67\t| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |\n68\t| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |\n69\t| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |\n70\t| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |\n71\t| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |\n72\t| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |\n73\t| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |\n74\t| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |\n75\t| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |\n76\t| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |\n77\t\n78\t### Submission (student)\n79\t\n80\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n81\t|---|---|---|\n82\t| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |\n83\t| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |\n84\t| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |\n85\t| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |\n86\t\n87\t### Grading (teacher)\n88\t\n89\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n90\t|---|---|---|\n91\t| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |\n92\t| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |\n93\t| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |\n94\t| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |\n95\t| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |\n96\t| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |\n97\t| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |\n98\t| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |\n99\t| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |\n100\t| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |\n101\t| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |\n102\t| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |\n103\t| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |\n104\t\n105\t### Assignment API\n106\t\n107\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n108\t|---|---|---|\n109\t| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |\n110\t| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |\n111\t| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |\n112\t| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |\n113\t| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |\n114\t| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |\n115\t| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |\n116\t\n117\t### Notifications and maintenance\n118\t\n119\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n120\t|---|---|---|\n121\t| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |\n122\t| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |\n123\t| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |\n124\t| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |\n125\t| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |\n126\t| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |\n127\t\n128\t### Seed\n129\t\n130\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n131\t|---|---|---|\n132\t| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |\n133\t| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |\n134\t\n135\t### Non-functional\n136\t\n137\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n138\t|---|---|---|\n139\t| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |\n140\t| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |\n141\t| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |\n142\t| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |\n143\t| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |\n144\t| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |\n145\t| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |\n146\t| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |\n147\t| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |\n148\t| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |\n149\t| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |\n150\t| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |\n151\t| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |\n152\t| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |\n153\t| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |\n154\t| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |\n155\t| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |\n156\t\n157\t## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)\n158\t\n159\t| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |\n160\t|---|---|---|\n161\t| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |\n162\t| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 **is installed** (package.json L34). It very likely has the same `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 mismatch, so FR-9's DateTimePicker is also at risk. That makes aligning the versions the real fix, rather than a Table workaround. |\n163\t| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |\n164\t| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |\n165\t| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |\n166\t| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |\n167\t| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |\n168\t| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |\n169\t| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |\n170\t| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |\n171\t\n172\t## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)\n173\t\n174\t`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4).\n175\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a7b6583-29f5-43b3-9f4e-72722e4e3a4f","uuid":"8478a18c-35f8-4448-ae66-f401868ee60b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:26:49.884Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-9\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T09:00:00Z), PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009). It has 61 FRs and 17 NFRs (78 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists 8 blockers. They must be surfaced in the `system-design.md` Overview (compliance rule 5). Decisions D1–D4 below answer them.\n\n> The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json, system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md) are **SH-8 leftovers** as of this writing. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them. Do not read them as SH-9 input.\n\n## Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-9 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` sets `context` and `contextId` on unattached files owned by the caller (any file for ADMIN). It does **not** check the file's upload context. `detachFiles` sets `contextId = null`, and `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes those files after 24 h. | src/server/files/files-service.ts L215-245, purge.ts | FR-53 requires uploads with context `'submission'`. The service must check `context === 'submission'` before calling attachFiles. On resubmission, **never detach the previous attempt's files**: `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` points at them, and detaching would let the purge delete history bytes. Keep them attached to the same submission id. |\n| B2 | `FileObject.storageKey` is `@unique`, and a FileObject holds a single `(context, contextId)`. `storage.ts` exports `saveFile(stream)`, `readFile(key)` and `deleteFile`. | schema L564-578, storage.ts | FR-15 duplicate **cannot share** attachment rows. For each target course, copy the bytes (`readFile` → `saveFile`), create a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), then attach it. |\n| B3 | `FileObject` has a back-relation `lessonAttachments LessonAttachment[]`. | schema L577 | FR-3/FR-4 add back-relations `assignmentAttachments` and `submissionFiles` to FileObject. This is an additive edit to an existing model, so NFR-11 allows it. |\n| B4 | `canAccessFile` order: unattached → owner/ADMIN; registered resolver; unknown context → owner/ADMIN. Resolver errors deny. `registerBuiltInContexts` currently registers `lesson` and `logo`. | access.ts L35-50, contexts.ts L36-39 | FR-47 adds `assignmentResolver` (contextId = assignmentId) and `submissionResolver` (contextId = submissionId) in contexts.ts. Before submit, a student's own upload is unattached, so it is already readable by owner/ADMIN only. |\n| B5 | `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` in `src/server/content/visibility.ts` is a pure read-time check: PUBLISHED, or SCHEDULED with publishAt ≤ now. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` covers ADMIN, teacher and co-teacher. | visibility.ts | FR-13 can reuse both by mapping `availableFrom → publishAt`. Widen the `Publishable.status` type to accept `AssignmentStatus`, which has the same string values, rather than writing a second helper (NFR-11). |\n| B6 | `assertCanViewCourse` allows ADMIN, the teacher/co-teacher, an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT, and a PARENT with an ACTIVE-enrolled linked child (`studentLinks`). `assertCanManageCourse` allows ADMIN and the teacher/co-teacher. Errors are `AppError` NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts | These already provide all of NFR-5's course checks. A parent who views a course still needs to be scoped to *which* child (FR-18, FR-38). |\n| B7 | `ParentStudentLink {parentId, studentId}`. `notifyStudentAndParents({studentIds, ...})` never throws. | notify.ts L98-117 | FR-44 uses it as-is. For FR-45 (parents only), call `notify()` with the parent ids from `parentStudentLink`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance route calls `dispatchEmails` **on every call**. Purges run in a once-per-day `if` (`lastPurgeAt`, in memory). | src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-43/FR-45: call `sendDueReminders(now)` on **every** call, outside the daily block (due_soon has a 24 h window, so daily would miss it). Wrap it in its own try/catch + logger, like the purges. |\n| B9 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a const object with `{label, description, category, defaultEmail, mandatoryInApp, roles}`. `content.lesson_published` is the closest precedent. | types.ts L33, L90-100 | FR-46: add four keys. Roles: `published` [STUDENT]; `due_soon` [STUDENT]; `returned` [STUDENT, PARENT]; `missing` [PARENT], with defaultEmail true. |\n| B10 | `formatInSchoolTz(date, pattern, tz)` and `schoolNow(now, tz)` live in `src/lib/dates.ts`, using date-fns-tz, which is already installed. | dates.ts | FR-10 next-teaching-day 23:59 and FR-25 receipt formatting. Convert wall time to UTC with date-fns-tz `fromZonedTime` (NFR-9 DST). |\n| B11 | `SchoolDay {dayOfWeek 1-7, isTeaching}` is seeded with all 7 rows. | schema L477-480 | FR-10 loops forward at most 7 days. If no day is teaching, fall back to tomorrow. |\n| B12 | `courseTabs` = overview, roster, attendance (there is **no content tab**: PRD-08 UI is missing). It is rendered by `CourseTabs.tsx`. `src/app/(app)/students/[id]/` has `attendance/` and `courses/` but no tab bar. | course-tabs.ts, ls | FR-16: append one entry with ALL_ROLES. FR-41: register the entry plus the page `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. It stays unreachable through tabs (blocker 5), but direct URLs work. |\n| B13 | `navigation.ts` entries are `{label, href, icon, roles, group?}`. | navigation.ts L31-38 | FR-40: one entry with roles [STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER]. Default ADMIN to the \"To grade\" view through the API (clarification). Add ADMIN to the nav only if design adopts that default. |\n| B14 | `src/server/assignments/` and `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` do not exist. Validator precedent: `src/lib/validators/content.ts`. HTTP helpers: `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination` and `AppError` in `src/server/http.ts`. | ls, grep | Greenfield feature folder (NFR-8). Route handlers follow NFR-7 using the existing helpers. |\n| B15 | Existing components: ConfirmDialog, DataTable, DateDisplay, EmptyState, FormField, LoadingSkeleton, PageHeader, Toast/useToast, UserPicker. **There is no** FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView or MarkdownEditor. | ls src/components | Blocker 1, see D1. |\n| B16 | Tests live in `tests/{unit,integration,e2e}`. | ls | NFR-14 placement. |\n\n## Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: **DM** = data model/migration · **SVC** = service logic · **EP** = API endpoint · **UI** = page/component · **AUTH** = access boundary · **JOB** = maintenance pass · **VAL** = validation · **CFG** = registry/config · **NOTIF** = notification · **TEST** = test · **SEED** = seed data\n\n### Data model (one migration: FR-1…FR-6)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums `SubmissionType`, `AssignmentStatus`, `SubmissionStatus`. Do not reuse `ContentStatus`, because the PRD names a new enum (the values happen to match, and B5 relies on that). |\n| FR-2 | DM | `Assignment` with `allowExtraCredit`, `notifiedAt?`, `archivedAt?`, `rubricId String? @unique`, Course relation with Cascade, and `@@index([courseId, dueAt])`. Add the back-relation `assignments Assignment[]` on Course. |\n| FR-3 | DM | `AssignmentAttachment` (join to FileObject, back-relation per B3), `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` (`maxPoints Decimal(6,2)`, `order Int`, `levels Json`). A 1:1 Rubric↔Assignment via `rubricId @unique` means a rubric is never shared, so delete it together with the assignment. |\n| FR-4 | DM | `Submission @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])`, which means one row per student. Attempts live in `SubmissionHistory`. The Decimal fields are `rawScore`, `penaltyPercent` and `finalScore`. `rubricScores Json`. `SubmissionFile` join, back-relation per B3. `SubmissionHistory.fileIds String[]` has no FK, so the files must not be purged (B1). |\n| FR-5 | DM | `GradeExemption @@id([assignmentId, studentId])`. Cascade on assignment delete. |\n| FR-6 | DM | `AssignmentReminder @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])`. `kind` is a String ('due_soon' / 'missing'). Insert with `createMany({skipDuplicates:true})`, or catch P2002, and send only for the rows actually inserted (idempotent under concurrent dispatchers). |\n| FR-7 | VAL | `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by client forms and route handlers. Cross-field rules (`lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum) use `.superRefine`. Decimal inputs come in as number/string and the service converts them to `Prisma.Decimal` (NFR-1). |\n| FR-8 | SVC, DM | Offline marker: `attemptNumber = 0`, `text = null`, no files, `submittedAt = gradedAt`. **Edge case for design:** a student may later submit online against an offline-graded row (`status = SUBMITTED`, unique row). Recommend allowing it and treating it as a resubmission (move the attempt-0 grade into history and clear the grade), unless it is already RETURNED. |\n\n### Assignment authoring (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-9 | UI | `/courses/[courseId]/assignments/new` and an edit route (`[assignmentId]/edit`). MUI DateTimePicker (MUI X pickers, same version-alignment risk as D2) in the school timezone. It depends on D1 (FileUpload, MarkdownEditor). |\n| FR-10 | SVC | `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz)`: a pure helper next to `schoolNow` in `src/lib/dates.ts`. Computed server-side and passed as a default prop (NFR-2). |\n| FR-11 | UI, VAL | The rubric builder uses `@dnd-kit/sortable`, which is already installed, for reorder. The rubric-sum check is in the Zod schema (shared), using Decimal sum, so the server rejects with VALIDATION_ERROR. The exact message string is required. |\n| FR-12 | UI, VAL | The status comes from the button. SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > serverNow`, checked in the service, not only in Zod (Zod has no server clock guarantee). |\n| FR-13 | SVC | `isAssignmentVisible(a, now) = !archivedAt && isVisible({status, publishAt: availableFrom}, now)`. Use it in **every** student/parent read path, the file resolver, submission rules and reminders. It is the single source of truth. |\n| FR-14 | UI | Show the warning when the assignment is published and `submissionCount > 0`, and the dueAt or maxPoints changes. No recalculation happens on the server. Keep a `maxPointsChangedAt` banner? Simplest is a client-side banner on save success. **Design should pick one, and not add a column unless needed.** |\n| FR-15 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/duplicate {courseIds}`. Check `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target. Make it one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows (1:1), and copy the attachment bytes per B2. Status DRAFT, `notifiedAt` null. LOW confidence default: identical dueAt plus the availableFrom/lateCutoffAt offsets. |\n\n### Lists and navigation\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-16 | CFG | Append `{key:'assignments', href:/courses/:id/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES}`. |\n| FR-17 | UI, EP | The teacher table depends on D2 (DataTable compile break). The counts come from FR-48's manager shape using `groupBy` aggregates, not N+1 queries. |\n| FR-18 | UI, AUTH | Student groups: Upcoming / Past due (missing) / Submitted / Returned. A parent viewing a course needs a child context: use `?studentId=`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` **and** active enrollment in this course. Default to the only linked child enrolled. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Assignment page: sanitised Markdown (D1 MarkdownView), late-policy summary, rubric, and a countdown under 48 h. Compute the countdown client-side from a server-provided `serverNow` offset, so a skewed client clock doesn't show a wrong countdown. It is display-only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-20 | UI | The panel switches on submissionType. Draft autosave to `localStorage` keyed by `assignmentId:userId`. Clear it after a successful submit. |\n| FR-21 | UI | Reuse `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | UI | Receipt formatted with `formatInSchoolTz(submittedAt, \"EEE d MMM yyyy, HH:mm\", tz)` plus the attempt number. |\n| FR-26 | UI, AUTH | Grading fields appear only when `status = RETURNED` (FR-27). |\n| FR-27 | AUTH, SVC | **Response-shaping boundary.** One serializer `toStudentSubmission(sub)` removes `rawScore/penaltyPercent/finalScore/feedback/rubricScores/gradedAt/gradedById` unless the status is RETURNED. Every student/parent path uses it: FR-48, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58 when the viewer is the student or parent. This covers NFR-4. |\n| FR-37 | UI, EP | `/assignments` STUDENT: 4 tabs plus a course filter, across ACTIVE enrollments. Missing = visible, not archived, `dueAt < now`, no submission, not exempt, `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (FR-60). Define one Prisma `where` builder `missingFilter(now)` and share it with the reminders (FR-43/45) and the counts. |\n| FR-38 | UI, AUTH | PARENT: a child selector using linked students only. The server validates `studentId` against `ParentStudentLink`. The view is read-only, so the submit panel is not rendered **and** the API rejects it (FR-53 is STUDENT-only). |\n| FR-39 | UI, EP | TEACHER \"To grade\": `status = SUBMITTED AND gradedAt IS NULL` in courses where `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`, ordered by `submittedAt asc`. ADMIN gets the same list across all courses (clarification default). |\n| FR-40 | CFG | One nav entry (B13). |\n| FR-41 | CFG, UI | studentTabs entry plus a page. It is invisible until a tab bar exists (blocker 5). Out of scope to build one here: do not add a tab-bar renderer just for this (NFR-15 scope / YAGNI), and surface it as a known gap. |\n\n### Submission (student)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-22 | SVC, AUTH | Rule order: (1) the assignment is visible and not archived; (2) `role = STUDENT` and ACTIVE-enrolled; (3) not exempt; (4) `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` (implied); (5) deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)`. The exact error string is required. `now = new Date()` on the server only (NFR-2). |\n| FR-23 | SVC, TEST | Pure `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt) = ceil((s − d) / 86_400_000)` for `s > d`, else 0. Use UTC milliseconds, so DST cannot affect it (NFR-9: a 24 h wall day across DST is 23/25 h of real time, and the PRD defines late days in 24 h units). Exactly 24 h gives 1. This is unit-test territory (NFR-14). |\n| FR-24 | SVC, DM | In one transaction: if a row exists, require `status = SUBMITTED` (RETURNED gives a VALIDATION/CONFLICT error), insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear the grade fields, replace the `SubmissionFile` rows, and attach the new files. Do not detach the old files (B1). Concurrency: two concurrent first submits hit the unique key. Catch P2002 and retry as a resubmit, or `upsert`. |\n| FR-53 | EP, VAL, AUTH | `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text?, fileIds[]}`. Validation: `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`; the content matches submissionType (text required for ONLINE_TEXT, files for FILE_UPLOAD, at least one for TEXT_AND_FILE); each file is `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'` and unattached, or already on this submission (B1). |\n\n### Grading (teacher)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-28 | UI, EP | The left panel is fed by FR-54. Status chip derivation is a pure function: Exempt > Returned > Graded > Late > Submitted > Not submitted. Shared by the server (FR-54) and tests. |\n| FR-29 | UI | `<img>`/`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">`. **CSP check for design:** confirm that `next.config.js` `frame-src`/`img-src` allow `'self'`. The CSP `script-src` issue is blocker 4. The history dropdown reads FR-55 (manager-only history). |\n| FR-30 | UI, SVC | Rubric ToggleButtonGroup with an auto-sum. Penalty prefill `min(lateDays × perDay, maxPenalty)`. The live final score uses decimal.js on the client too, so the preview and server values agree (NFR-1). The prefill is display-only. The server stores what is submitted, after FR-36 validation. |\n| FR-31 | SVC, TEST | `finalScore = raw × (1 − p/100)`, computed with `Decimal`, `toDecimalPlaces(2, ROUND_HALF_UP)`. One pure function in the service, unit-tested (18 at 20 % = 14.40). |\n| FR-32 | EP, SVC, NOTIF | \"Save\" = `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade`. \"Save & return\" = the same call with `{return:true}`, or grade followed by return. **Design should pick a single round trip.** The bulk route is `POST /api/assignments/:id/return {submissionIds?}`, with the default `gradedAt not null AND status ≠ RETURNED`. Each return sets RETURNED and returnedAt, fires FR-44, and writes an audit (FR-59). |\n| FR-33 | UI | A keydown listener on the grading page. Ignore J/K when `event.target` is an input, textarea or contenteditable. Ctrl/Cmd+Enter always works. Accessibility: show the shortcuts in a help hint (NFR-17). |\n| FR-34 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/assignments/:id/grade-offline {studentId, rawScore, feedback}`. The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. Reject it if a submission already exists (grade that one instead). Creates the FR-8 row with the grade fields set, penalty 0, and an audit row. |\n| FR-35 | EP, SVC | `PUT/DELETE /api/assignments/:id/exemptions/:studentId`. Idempotent (`upsert` / `deleteMany`). Writes an audit row. Its effects come through `missingFilter` and the FR-22 rule. A PRD-11 exclusion flag = the GradeExemption row itself, so no extra column. |\n| FR-36 | VAL, SVC | Server-side, Decimal-based: `0 ≤ raw ≤ maxPoints` (×1.2 if allowExtraCredit). Each rubric score `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints` (extra credit is raw-only, per the clarification), and each `criterionId` belongs to this rubric. `0 ≤ penalty ≤ 100`. With a rubric, should raw equal the sum of the rubric points? The PRD says it auto-sums but stays overridable only via the penalty. **Recommend the server enforces raw = Σ rubric points when rubricScores are given.** |\n| FR-54 | EP | `GET /api/assignments/:id/submissions` (manage). LEFT JOIN of ACTIVE enrollments × submissions × exemptions. Paginate per NFR-7, but grading needs all students for J/K: allow `pageSize` up to 100 and document the limit. |\n| FR-55 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/submissions/:id`: the submitter, linked parents or course managers. History only for managers. Grade fields go through the FR-27 serializer for the student and parent. Also needed by NFR-3 prefetch. |\n| FR-56 | EP, SVC | Sets `gradedById`, `gradedAt` and the computed `finalScore`. Does not change status (it stays SUBMITTED until return). Writes an audit row. |\n| FR-59 | SVC | `audit()` on grade, return (one row per submission, or one bulk row with the ids; **design should pick**), exempt/unexempt and offline grade. |\n\n### Assignment API\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-48 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/courses/:id/assignments`. Two response shapes depending on `canSeeDrafts`. Students and parents get FR-13-visible, non-archived assignments plus their own submission state (via the FR-27 serializer). |\n| FR-49 | EP, SVC | `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments`. One transaction: rubric and criteria, assignment, attachments (`attachFiles` with `'assignment'`, contextId = assignment.id), and on PUBLISHED the FR-42 notify after commit. |\n| FR-50 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/assignments/:id`. A non-manager on an invisible/archived assignment gets NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so existence is not leaked. Includes `serverNow` for FR-19. |\n| FR-51 | EP, SVC | PATCH: re-validate the rubric sum against maxPoints. Diff the attachments (detach the removed ones, which are then purged after 24 h per B1; that is fine for assignment attachments). DRAFT→PUBLISHED triggers FR-42. DELETE: hard delete if there are 0 submissions (cascade; the attachment files are detached first so the purge reclaims them), else set `archivedAt`. |\n| FR-52 | AUTH, SVC | Covered by `isAssignmentVisible` (FR-13), which includes `!archivedAt`. One check, applied everywhere. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-57 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/me/assignments?studentId=&tab=`. Role switch: STUDENT gets its own data; PARENT requires a linked `studentId`; TEACHER/ADMIN get To grade. `tab ∈ upcoming/missing/submitted/returned`. |\n| FR-58 | EP, AUTH | `GET /api/students/:id/assignments` → `assertCanViewStudent`, then the same query as the FR-57 student view, built with a shared service function. A student or parent viewer gets the FR-27 serializer. Teachers and admins see grades? The PRD says \"same per-student data\", so **recommend the same serializer for all non-managers and full fields for the student's course managers.** Design should confirm. |\n\n### Notifications and maintenance\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-42 | NOTIF, SVC | Exactly once: `UPDATE assignment SET notifiedAt = now WHERE id = ? AND notifiedAt IS NULL` (`updateMany`, count = 1 → send). Triggered on publish (FR-49/51), and for SCHEDULED assignments in the student list read path (FR-48/57) when visible and `notifiedAt` is null. **A side effect on GET:** keep it fire-and-forget after the response data is built, and never fail the read. Design may also add it to `sendDueReminders` as a safety net, but must not do both without the atomic guard (the guard makes both safe). |\n| FR-43 | JOB, NOTIF | `sendDueReminders(now)` in `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`, called on every dispatcher call (B8). The window is `dueAt − 24h ≤ now < dueAt`. Targets: ACTIVE-enrolled, no submission, not exempt, visible, not archived, not NO_SUBMISSION. Idempotent via FR-6. Bound the query (only assignments with `dueAt` in [now, now+24h]). |\n| FR-44 | NOTIF | On return: `notifyStudentAndParents` with a body like `\"{course}: {title} — {finalScore}/{maxPoints}\"`. Bulk return sends one notify per student. |\n| FR-45 | JOB, NOTIF | In the same pass: `now ≥ dueAt + 24h`, with the `missingFilter` targets. Parents only (`notify` to the linked parent ids). FR-6 kind 'missing'. Bound the query to avoid scanning all history, e.g. `dueAt` in [now − 8 d, now − 24 h], with a `ponytail:` note on that window. |\n| FR-46 | CFG | Four keys (B9). |\n| FR-47 | AUTH | `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course, then `assertCanViewCourse`, then `canSeeDrafts \\|\\| isAssignmentVisible`. `submissionResolver`: load the submission; allow the submitting student, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`) or `canSeeDrafts(course)` (managers/ADMIN). Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10). Integration test needed. |\n\n### Seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-60 | SVC | Exclude NO_SUBMISSION in `missingFilter` and the reminder targets. The submission panel is hidden and FR-53 rejects. LOW confidence default. |\n| FR-61 | SEED | Idempotent: look up the courses by code and skip if they are missing. Upsert the assignments by `(courseId, title)`. Seed Decimal scores via strings. Seeded attachments/files are not required, so skip byte storage. |\n\n### Non-functional\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | SVC, VAL | Decimal end to end: Prisma `Decimal(6,2)` columns, `Prisma.Decimal` in the service, decimal.js in the client preview. Serialize Decimals in API responses as **strings**, to avoid float loss in JSON. Design must state this convention for api-contracts. |\n| NFR-2 | SVC | Every deadline, visibility or reminder check uses `new Date()` on the server. There is no client timestamp field in any request schema. |\n| NFR-3 | UI, EP | Prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id` into a client cache keyed by id (a plain `Map` in the grading page; no data-fetching library added). The <300 ms target is a client switch from cache. |\n| NFR-4 | AUTH | Enforced at three boundaries: the FR-27 serializer, the FR-47 file resolvers, and query scoping (a student only ever queries `studentId = me`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Every route: `requireUser`/`requireRole`, then assertCan*. Every page: `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole`. |\n| NFR-6 | UI | MUI 9.5.0 + MUI X only, with mui-mcp lookups before use. Components needed: List, Chip, ToggleButtonGroup, Dialog, Tabs, DataGrid (D2), DateTimePicker, Autocomplete, Snackbar. Hard blocker if mui-mcp is unreachable (blocker 8). |\n| NFR-7 | EP | Thin handlers. `{data}` / paginated / `{error}` envelopes via the http.ts helpers. |\n| NFR-8 | CFG | `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts`, plus `reminders.ts` and pure `scoring.ts` (lateDays, penalty, finalScore, chip status) for unit tests. Validators in `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`. |\n| NFR-9 | SVC, TEST | Store UTC. Display via formatInSchoolTz. Late days in UTC ms (FR-23). The FR-10 default uses `fromZonedTime`. |\n| NFR-10 | UI | react-markdown, remark-gfm and rehype-sanitize are installed, with MUI component mapping (D1). |\n| NFR-11 | — | Reuse list: B1–B10, B15. |\n| NFR-12 | — | Use the logger, never console.log. |\n| NFR-13 | TEST, CFG | Blocker 3: fix the `vitest.config.ts` import to `'vitest/config'` (a one-line fix, in scope because NFR-13 requires a working `npm test`). |\n| NFR-14 | TEST | Unit: scoring.ts. Integration: resubmit history, return, reminder idempotency, exemption vs missing, and the file resolvers (AC-10). E2E: the full flow plus the parent missing list (needs bypassCSP, blocker 4). |\n| NFR-15 | — | No gradebook, peer review, group work or annotation. FR-35 stores the exemption only, and PRD-11 consumes it. |\n| NFR-16 | UI | Two-minute publish: sensible defaults (FR-10 due date, max points 100?, submissionType FILE_UPLOAD?). **Design should set the form defaults.** 30-submission keyboard grading via FR-33 + NFR-3. |\n| NFR-17 | UI | Labelled inputs and keyboard-operable controls: the ToggleButtonGroup and the J/K help hint. |\n\n## Decisions arch-design-system must make (answers to the intake blockers)\n\n| # | Blocker / gap | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Blocker 1: PRD-08 UI components are missing. | Build the **minimum** shared components in this ticket: `src/components/MarkdownView` (react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize, mapped to MUI), `src/components/MarkdownEditor` (MUI TextField multiline + a Write/Preview Tabs toggle using MarkdownView; no new editor dependency), `src/components/FileUpload` (input type=file → `POST /api/files` with the context field, list with remove, `maxFiles` prop) and `FileList` (links to `/api/files/:id`). Shape them so PRD-08 can adopt them later. Do not build PRD-08's remaining scope. |\n| D2 | Blocker 2: the MUI X DataGrid compile break. | Preferred: align `@mui/x-*` versions in package.json/lockfile (it also unblocks the DateTimePicker from `@mui/x-date-pickers`, if that package shares the internals). Fallback for FR-17: an MUI `Table`, which needs no DataGrid. `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0 **is installed** (package.json L34). It very likely has the same `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 mismatch, so FR-9's DateTimePicker is also at risk. That makes aligning the versions the real fix, rather than a Table workaround. |\n| D3 | Blockers 3/4: vitest import and CSP. | vitest: one-line import fix. CSP: keep `bypassCSP` in Playwright as before. A CSP fix is outside the PRD scope (NFR-15). Note the FR-29 iframe/img `'self'` dependency. |\n| D4 | Blocker 5: the studentTabs renderer. | Register the tab and build the page. Do not build a tab bar. Report it as a known gap. |\n| D5 | Decimal JSON serialization | Decimal fields are strings in API responses (NFR-1). |\n| D6 | The \"Save & return\" round trip | `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with an optional `return: true` gives one transaction. |\n| D7 | Rubric raw score | When rubricScores are present, the server sets or enforces `rawScore = Σ points`. |\n| D8 | Teacher/admin view of FR-58 grade fields | Course managers get full fields. Other viewers get the FR-27 serializer. |\n| D9 | Offline-graded row followed by an online submit | Treat it as a resubmission while it is not RETURNED. |\n| D10 | Missing-reminder query window | Bound it (e.g. dueAt within the last 8 days), marked with a `ponytail:` note. |\n\n## Shared pure functions (single source of truth; unit-test targets)\n\n`isAssignmentVisible`, `missingFilter(now)` (Prisma where), `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `rubricTotal`, `submissionChipStatus`, `nextTeachingDayDueAt`, `toStudentSubmission` (serializer). Each of these is used by two or more call sites listed above. Keeping one copy of each prevents the drift that leads to privacy and correctness bugs (NFR-1, NFR-4).\n","numLines":175,"startLine":1,"totalLines":175}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011PcCzrE5QaKo7qqESv9wgX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
