{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MwXWtuFqrra4hf9AyNk5Wz","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a7b6583-29f5-43b3-9f4e-72722e4e3a4f","uuid":"3d3098fb-f7c7-44a7-8579-c4e19cae9050","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:29:17.720Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-9 · PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009)\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T10:40:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (61 FR + 17 NFR, 95%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B16, D1–D10). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-8 design that was in this folder. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`\n> and `threat-model-notes.json` in this folder are also leftovers from earlier tickets. `arch-api-contracts` overwrites the first two.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-9 adds **assignments**: teacher authoring with an optional rubric, student submission with resubmission history,\na keyboard-driven grading screen, return flow, exemptions, offline grading, a cross-course `/assignments` page per role,\nfour notifications, and two reminder passes.\n\nShape of the change:\n\n- **One migration**, `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6).\n- **One feature folder**, `src/server/assignments/`, with three files: `assignments-service.ts` (all DB logic),\n  `grading-math.ts` (pure, isomorphic, unit-tested), `reminders.ts` (maintenance pass).\n- **One validator file**, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by forms and handlers.\n- Thin route handlers under `src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…` (NFR-7, NFR-8).\n- Pages under `src/app/(app)/…`, plus the four PRD-08 shared components that were never built (D1).\n- **No new dependencies, services, queues, or cron** (ADR-1, ADR-8). Reminders hook into the existing dispatcher.\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PRD-08 UI is missing: FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor | Build the minimum of all four in `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` (ADR-5, §2.5). No other PRD-08 scope. |\n| 2 | MUI X break: `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 vs X 9.5.0 | `package.json` `overrides: { \"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\" }` (ADR-2). This fixes both DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9). Fallback: FR-17 uses an MUI `Table`, and FR-9 uses `TextField type=\"datetime-local\"`. Dev verifies with `npm ls` plus a compile **before** building UI. |\n| 3 | vitest import break | Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (ADR-3). |\n| 4 | CSP `script-src 'self'` breaks hydration | Leave it alone. The e2e spec uses `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })` (ADR-4). The platform nonce fix is a follow-up ticket. |\n| 5 | `studentTabs` has no renderer | Register the FR-41 tab and build `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. The page works by direct URL. **No tab bar is built** (NFR-15). This is a known gap and is carried to the handoff. |\n| 6 | LOW-confidence defaults FR-15, FR-52, FR-60 | Adopt intake's defaults as written (§5). Each one is a single predicate or a single copy rule, so it is cheap to change later. |\n| 7 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-11). |\n| 8 | mui-mcp must be reachable (NFR-6) | This is a hard gate on the dev phase. Dev looks up every MUI component through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before using it. If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker. |\n\n### 1.2 New finding from this sub-task (not in intake)\n\n`next.config.js` sends **`X-Frame-Options: DENY`** on `/:path*`. That blocks the same-origin\n`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">` PDF preview required by FR-29. CSP `default-src 'self'` already allows same-origin frames,\nso the X-Frame-Options header is the only thing blocking it. `<img>` previews are not affected.\n\n**Decision D11:** in `next.config.js`, split the header rule:\n- `source: '/((?!api/files/).*)'` keeps the existing headers, with `DENY`.\n- `source: '/api/files/:id'` gets the same headers, but with `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` and `frame-ancestors 'self'` appended to the CSP.\n\nThe file route already enforces access (`canAccessFile`) and sniffs types (`nosniff`), so letting our own pages frame it adds no exposure.\n**Fallback**, if the dev wants zero header changes: show PDFs as an \"Open\" link (`target=\"_blank\"`) instead of an iframe. Images still preview inline.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data model: migration `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6)\n\nAll additive. Existing models get back-relations only (NFR-11).\n\n```\nenum SubmissionType   { ONLINE_TEXT FILE_UPLOAD TEXT_AND_FILE NO_SUBMISSION }   // FR-1\nenum AssignmentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }                              // FR-1\nenum SubmissionStatus { SUBMITTED RETURNED }                                     // FR-1\n\nAssignment (FR-2)\n  id, courseId → Course (Cascade), title, instructions (Text), submissionType, maxPoints Decimal(6,2),\n  dueAt, availableFrom?, allowLate, lateCutoffAt?, latePenaltyPercentPerDay Decimal(5,2),\n  maxLatePenaltyPercent Decimal(5,2), maxFileCount Int, allowExtraCredit Boolean @default(false),\n  status AssignmentStatus, rubricId String? @unique → Rubric, notifiedAt?, archivedAt?,\n  createdById, createdAt, updatedAt\n  @@index([courseId, dueAt])\n\nAssignmentAttachment (FR-3)  assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([assignmentId, fileId])\nRubric (FR-3)                id, criteria RubricCriterion[]\nRubricCriterion (FR-3)       id, rubricId → Rubric (Cascade), title, description?, maxPoints Decimal(6,2), order Int,\n                             levels Json  // [{label, points, description}]\n\nSubmission (FR-4)\n  id, assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId → User, status SubmissionStatus, text?,\n  attemptNumber Int, submittedAt, isLate Boolean, lateDays Int,\n  rawScore Decimal(6,2)?, penaltyPercent Decimal(5,2)?, finalScore Decimal(6,2)?,\n  rubricScores Json?  // [{criterionId, points, comment}]\n  feedback?, gradedById?, gradedAt?, returnedAt?\n  @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])\nSubmissionFile (FR-4)        submissionId → Submission (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([submissionId, fileId])\nSubmissionHistory (FR-4)     id, submissionId → Submission (Cascade), attemptNumber, text?, fileIds String[], submittedAt\n\nGradeExemption (FR-5)        assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, reason?, createdAt; @@id([assignmentId, studentId])\nAssignmentReminder (FR-6)    assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, kind String ('due_soon'|'missing'), createdAt\n                             @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])\n```\n\nBack-relations added: `Course.assignments`, `FileObject.assignmentAttachments`, `FileObject.submissionFiles`, `User.submissions`.\n\nModel decisions:\n- **One Submission row per student.** Earlier attempts live in `SubmissionHistory` (FR-24).\n- `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` has no FK. Old attempt files **stay attached** to the same submission id and are never detached. Detaching them would let `purgeOrphanFiles` delete history bytes (B1).\n- Offline grade (FR-8, FR-34) = a Submission with `attemptNumber 0`, `text null`, no files, and `submittedAt = gradedAt`.\n- A Rubric is 1:1 with an Assignment (`rubricId @unique`). Delete the rubric in the same transaction as a hard-deleted assignment.\n- FR-14: **no column added.** The \"review grades\" banner is client-side, shown after a successful PATCH that changed `maxPoints` while `submissionCount > 0`.\n\n### 2.2 Server: `src/server/assignments/` (NFR-8)\n\n| File | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `grading-math.ts` | **Pure and isomorphic** (no Prisma client import; `Decimal` from `decimal.js`, the same package Prisma uses). `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt)`, `defaultPenalty(lateDays, perDay, max)`, `computeFinalScore(raw, pct)`, `rubricTotal(criteria)`, `maxRawScore(maxPoints, allowExtraCredit)`, `submissionChipStatus(row)` | FR-23, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-28, NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n| `assignments-service.ts` | All DB logic: visibility, CRUD, duplicate, submit, grade, return, exempt, offline grade, role-shaped lists, the serializer, and notify triggers. | FR-8, FR-12..15, FR-22, FR-24, FR-32, FR-34, FR-35, FR-42, FR-44, FR-48..58, FR-59 |\n| `reminders.ts` | `sendDueReminders(now)`: due_soon and missing passes. | FR-43, FR-45, FR-60 |\n\n`grading-math.ts` imports only `decimal.js`. The service wraps values as `Prisma.Decimal` (same class). This keeps one function for the client preview and the server value (ADR-7).\n\n#### Single-source helpers (inside `assignments-service.ts` unless noted)\n\n| Helper | Definition | Used by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `isAssignmentVisible(a, now)` | `!a.archivedAt && isVisible({ status: a.status, publishAt: a.availableFrom }, now)`. Reuses `src/server/content/visibility.ts`: widen `Publishable.status` to `ContentStatus \\| AssignmentStatus` (same string values). | FR-13, FR-22, FR-47, FR-48, FR-50, FR-52, FR-57, FR-58, reminders |\n| `visibleWhere(now)` | The Prisma `where` equivalent: `{ archivedAt: null, OR: [{status:'PUBLISHED'}, {status:'SCHEDULED', availableFrom:{lte:now}}] }` | list queries, reminders |\n| `missingWhere(now)` | visible ∧ `dueAt < now` ∧ `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION`; per student: no Submission and no GradeExemption | FR-37, FR-35, FR-45, FR-60 |\n| `toStudentSubmission(sub)` | Removes `rawScore, penaltyPercent, finalScore, feedback, rubricScores, gradedById, gradedAt` unless `status === 'RETURNED'`. Always removes history. | FR-27, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58, NFR-4 |\n| `serializeDecimals` | Prisma.Decimal → `string` (\"14.40\") on the way out | NFR-1 (D5) |\n| `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` | **Reused** from `visibility.ts`: ADMIN, teacher or co-teacher = \"manager\" | everywhere |\n| `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz, teachingDays)` | **In `src/lib/dates.ts`**, next to `schoolNow`. Walk from tomorrow (≤7 days) to the first `isTeaching` weekday, take 23:59 local, convert with `fromZonedTime`. If no day is teaching, use tomorrow. | FR-10, NFR-9 |\n| `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` | STUDENT → self. PARENT → `studentId` must be in `ParentStudentLink`; it defaults to the only linked child. Otherwise FORBIDDEN. | FR-18, FR-38, FR-57 |\n\n#### Key service flows\n\n**Create / update (FR-49, FR-51, FR-11, FR-12, FR-42).** One transaction: Zod parse → if a rubric is given, `rubricTotal == maxPoints`, otherwise\nVALIDATION_ERROR `Rubric totals {sum} points but the assignment is worth {maxPoints}.` → SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > new Date()` (checked in the service,\nbecause Zod has no server clock, NFR-2) → upsert rubric and criteria → write the assignment → `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, 'assignment', id)`. On PATCH,\ndiff the attachments: removed files are `detachFiles` (the purge reclaims them). **After commit**, if the assignment is now visible → `publishOnce(id)`.\n\n**`publishOnce(id)` (FR-42).** `updateMany({ where:{ id, notifiedAt:null }, data:{ notifiedAt: now } })`. Only when `count === 1`, call `notify()` for\n`assignment.published` to ACTIVE-enrolled students. Called from: create/PATCH after commit, and from the student/parent list read paths (FR-48, FR-57)\nfor SCHEDULED assignments that have become visible with `notifiedAt` null. On GET it is fire-and-forget (`void publishOnce(id).catch(logger.error)`) and never fails the read.\n\n**Delete (FR-51).** If there are 0 submissions → detach the attachments, then delete the assignment and its rubric (cascade). Otherwise → set `archivedAt = now`. Audit `assignment.delete|archive`.\n\n**Duplicate (FR-15).** `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target course, then one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows.\nAttachments: `readFile` → `saveFile` → a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), because FileObject holds one context (B2). Status is DRAFT and `notifiedAt` is null.\nSame `dueAt`; `availableFrom` and `lateCutoffAt` keep their offsets from dueAt (FR-15 default).\n\n**Submit (FR-22..FR-24, FR-53, FR-60).** `now = new Date()` on the server. Checks, in order (first failure wins):\n1. Assignment exists and `isAssignmentVisible` → otherwise NOT_FOUND.\n2. `role === 'STUDENT'` and ACTIVE-enrolled in the course → otherwise FORBIDDEN.\n3. Not exempt; `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR.\n4. Deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR `The deadline has passed and late submissions are closed.`\n5. Content matches the type: text for ONLINE_TEXT, ≥1 file for FILE_UPLOAD, ≥1 of either for TEXT_AND_FILE. Also `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`.\n6. Each file has `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'`, and is unattached **or** already attached to this submission. The service checks `context` before calling `attachFiles`, because `attachFiles` does not (B1).\n\nThen, in one transaction:\n- **No row:** create the Submission (`attemptNumber 1`, `isLate`, `lateDays` from `grading-math`).\n- **Row with `status = SUBMITTED`**, including an attempt-0 offline row (D9): insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear all grade fields, and replace the `SubmissionFile` rows. Old files stay attached.\n- **Row with `RETURNED`:** CONFLICT `This submission has been returned and can no longer be changed.`\n\n`attachFiles(tx, user, newFileIds, 'submission', submission.id)`. A P2002 from two concurrent first submits → retry once as a resubmit.\n\n**Grade (FR-56, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-32 \"Save & return\").** `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade { rawScore?, penaltyPercent, feedback?, rubricScores?, return?: boolean }`.\n- If the assignment has a rubric: `rubricScores` are required, every criterion must be scored exactly once, `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints`, and **the server sets `rawScore = Σ points`** (any client raw value is ignored, D7).\n- Otherwise: `0 ≤ rawScore ≤ maxRawScore` (×1.2 when `allowExtraCredit`). Extra credit applies to rawScore only.\n- `0 ≤ penaltyPercent ≤ 100`. `finalScore = computeFinalScore`. Set `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. The status stays SUBMITTED.\n- `return: true` → in the same transaction, set `status RETURNED`, `returnedAt`, then notify after commit (D6: a single round trip). Audit `submission.grade` (+ `submission.return`).\n\n**Bulk return (FR-32).** `POST /api/assignments/:id/return { submissionIds? }`. The default set is `gradedAt != null AND status = SUBMITTED`. A supplied id that is ungraded is\nskipped and reported in the response (`{returned, skipped}`). One `updateMany`, then one `notifyStudentAndParents` per student (FR-44), plus **one audit row per submission** (FR-59), so\na per-record audit trail is possible.\n\n**Offline grade (FR-34, FR-8).** The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. If a submission already exists → CONFLICT (grade that one instead). Create the attempt-0 row\nwith the grade fields and penalty 0, using the same validation as Grade. Audit `submission.grade_offline`.\n\n**Exempt (FR-35).** PUT = `upsert` GradeExemption, DELETE = `deleteMany` (both idempotent). Audit `assignment.exempt|unexempt`. The effects come only through\n`missingWhere`, the submit rule 3, and reminders. The PRD-11 \"exclude\" flag **is** the row itself (NFR-15).\n\n### 2.3 Maintenance: `reminders.ts` (FR-43, FR-45, FR-60)\n\n`sendDueReminders(now)` is called on **every** request to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, outside the daily `lastPurgeAt` block, in its own try/catch with logger (B8).\n\n| Pass | Assignment window | Targets | Notify |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| due_soon | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ (now, now+24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | ACTIVE-enrolled, no Submission, no GradeExemption | `assignment.due_soon` → student |\n| missing | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ [now−8d, now−24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | same | `assignment.missing` → linked parents only, via `notify()` |\n\nIdempotency: `createMany({ data: candidates, skipDuplicates: true })` cannot report *which* rows were inserted, so **insert per (assignment, student) with `create` and catch P2002**,\nand notify only on success. The Postgres unique key makes this safe across concurrent dispatchers. Candidate counts are small (one course × roster).\n`// ponytail: missing pass only looks back 8 days; widen or add a cursor if the dispatcher can be down longer.`\n\n### 2.4 Reuse map (NFR-11)\n\n| Existing | Where | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` | `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | every handler and page (NFR-5) |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` | course-scoped routes |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-58 |\n| `isVisible`, `canSeeDrafts` | `src/server/content/visibility.ts` (type widened) | FR-13, manager checks |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination`, `AppError` | `src/server/http.ts` | NFR-7 envelopes and errors |\n| `audit()` | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-59 |\n| `notify()`, `notifyStudentAndParents()`, `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | `src/server/notifications/` | FR-42..FR-46 |\n| `attachFiles`, `detachFiles`, `POST /api/files`, `GET /api/files/:id?inline=1`, `registerBuiltInContexts`, `storage.ts` | `src/server/files/`, `src/server/storage.ts` | FR-9, FR-15, FR-20, FR-29, FR-47, FR-53 |\n| `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | `src/lib/dates.ts` | FR-19, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `DataTable`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `useToast`, `FormField`, `DateDisplay` | `src/components/` | FR-17, FR-21, lists, forms |\n| `courseTabs`, `studentTabs`, `navigation` | `src/config/` | FR-16, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `logger` | `src/lib/logger.ts` | NFR-12 |\n\n### 2.5 New shared UI components (blocker 1, ADR-5)\n\n| Component | Build | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `MarkdownView` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema). Elements map to MUI `Typography`, `Link`, `Table*`, `List*`, `Box component=\"pre\"`. | NFR-10, FR-19, FR-29, FR-26 |\n| `MarkdownEditor` | MUI `TextField multiline` + `Tabs` (Write / Preview → `MarkdownView`). Controlled `value`/`onChange`, plus `maxLength`. | FR-9, FR-20, FR-30 |\n| `FileUpload` | MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`. POSTs each file to `/api/files` with `context`. Props `{context, max, value: FileRef[], onChange}`. A `LinearProgress` per file, plus remove. | FR-9, FR-20 |\n| `FileList` | MUI `List` of links to `/api/files/:id`. Optional `preview` prop: `<img>` for `image/*`, `<iframe>` for `application/pdf`, both via `?inline=1` (D11). | FR-19, FR-25, FR-29 |\n\n### 2.6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` (FR-7)\n\n`assignmentInput` (FR-7 limits; `.superRefine`: `lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum = maxPoints using `rubricTotal`), `rubricCriterionInput`,\n`submissionInput {text? ≤50k, fileIds ≤10}`, `gradeInput {rawScore?, penaltyPercent 0–100, feedback? ≤10k, rubricScores?, return?}`,\n`offlineGradeInput`, `bulkReturnInput`, `duplicateInput {courseIds min 1}`, `meAssignmentsQuery {studentId?, tab?, courseId?}`.\nDecimals are accepted as `z.union([z.number(), z.string()])` and converted to Decimal in the service. No request schema has a timestamp field except\n`dueAt`/`availableFrom`/`lateCutoffAt`, which are authoring data, not \"now\" (NFR-2).\n\n### 2.7 Route handlers (thin: Zod → service → envelope; NFR-7)\n\n| Route | Auth | Service fn | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | user + view course | `listCourseAssignments` (manager shape with `groupBy` counts / student shape) | FR-48, FR-17, FR-18 |\n| `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | manage course | `createAssignment` | FR-49 |\n| `GET /api/assignments/[id]` | view (NOT_FOUND for invisible to non-manager) | `getAssignment` (+ own submission, `serverNow`) | FR-50, FR-19 |\n| `PATCH` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]` | manage | `updateAssignment` / `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | FR-51, FR-14 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/duplicate` | manage source + each target | `duplicateAssignment` | FR-15 |\n| `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | manage | `listGradingRoster` (every ACTIVE enrollee; `pageSize` ≤100) | FR-54, FR-28 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | STUDENT | `submit` | FR-53, FR-22..24 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/return` | manage | `bulkReturn` | FR-32, FR-44 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/grade-offline` | manage | `gradeOffline` | FR-34, FR-8 |\n| `PUT` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]/exemptions/[studentId]` | manage | `setExemption` | FR-35 |\n| `GET /api/submissions/[id]` | submitter, linked parent, or manager; history for managers only | `getSubmission` | FR-55, FR-29, NFR-3 |\n| `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade` | manage | `gradeSubmission` | FR-56, FR-30..32, FR-36 |\n| `GET /api/me/assignments` | any user; role switch | `listMyAssignments` | FR-57, FR-37..39 |\n| `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments` | `assertCanViewStudent` | `listStudentAssignments` | FR-58, FR-41 |\n\nShared response conventions for `arch-api-contracts`: Decimals are **strings**. Timestamps are ISO UTC strings. Student/parent submission objects\nalways pass through `toStudentSubmission`. FR-58: a viewer who manages the course gets the full fields, everyone else gets the serializer (D8).\n`/api/me/assignments` for ADMIN = \"To grade\" across all courses (intake default).\n\n### 2.8 Pages (`src/app/(app)/…`)\n\n| Page | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/page.tsx` | Manager: `DataTable` (title, due, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted, Grade button; Archived chip). Student/parent: grouped `List` (Upcoming / Past due / Submitted / Returned). Parent child selector when more than one linked child is enrolled. | FR-16..18, FR-52 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/new/page.tsx` + `[assignmentId]/edit/page.tsx` | One shared `AssignmentForm` (react-hook-form + the Zod schema). Defaults: dueAt = `nextTeachingDayDueAt` (computed server-side, passed as a prop), maxPoints 100, FILE_UPLOAD, maxFileCount 3, allowLate off (NFR-16). Rubric builder: `@dnd-kit/sortable` with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, and a live sum error. Buttons: Save draft / Publish / Schedule. Edit warns per FR-14. \"Duplicate to other courses\" dialog with an `Autocomplete` of managed courses. | FR-9..15 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/page.tsx` | MarkdownView instructions, FileList, due and late-policy summary, rubric table, countdown under 48 h (offset from `serverNow`, display only). Submission panel by type, `localStorage` draft key `assignment:{id}:{userId}` (cleared on success), ConfirmDialog before POST, receipt via `formatInSchoolTz`, returned results, or \"Submitted — awaiting grading\". Parent: read-only, no panel. | FR-19..27 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/page.tsx` | Left: `List` + status `Chip`s from `submissionChipStatus`, filter, sort by name or time. Main: MarkdownView text, FileList with preview, history `Select`. Form: rubric `ToggleButtonGroup`s that auto-sum, prefilled penalty (`defaultPenalty`), live final score (`computeFinalScore`), MarkdownEditor feedback. Buttons Save / Save & return / Return all graded / Grade without submission / Exempt toggle. J/K/Ctrl+Enter keydown handler that skips J/K in input/textarea/contenteditable, with a visible shortcut hint. **NFR-3:** a plain `Map<id, Submission>` cache; after each selection, prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id`. | FR-28..36, NFR-3, NFR-16, NFR-17 |\n| `assignments/page.tsx` | STUDENT: `Tabs` Upcoming/Missing/Submitted/Returned + course filter. PARENT: child selector, same view, read-only. TEACHER/ADMIN: \"To grade\" list, oldest first. | FR-37..39 |\n| `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx` | Per-student list (FR-58). Reachable by URL only (blocker 5). | FR-41 |\n\n### 2.9 Config and registrations\n\n- `src/config/course-tabs.ts`: `{ key:'assignments', label:'Assignments', href: id => /courses/${id}/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES }` (FR-16).\n- `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Assignments` → `/assignments`, roles `[STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER, ADMIN]` (FR-40; ADMIN added because the To-grade default applies to ADMIN).\n- `src/config/student-tabs.ts`: `assignments` entry (FR-41).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: four keys, category ACADEMIC (FR-46):\n  `assignment.published` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.due_soon` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.returned` [STUDENT, PARENT] email false · `assignment.missing` [PARENT] email **true**.\n- `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (FR-47), registered in `registerBuiltInContexts`:\n  - `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course → `assertCanViewCourse` → `canSeeDrafts || isAssignmentVisible`.\n  - `submissionResolver`: load the submission and course → allow `studentId === user.id`, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), or `canSeeDrafts`. Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10).\n- `next.config.js`: D11 header split.\n- `package.json`: `overrides[\"@mui/x-internals\"] = \"9.1.0\"` (ADR-2). `vitest.config.ts` import fix (ADR-3).\n- `prisma/seed.ts`: FR-61 block, idempotent: look up courses by code (skip if missing), upsert by `(courseId, title)`, Decimals as strings, no file bytes.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Author → publish.** Teacher form → `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments` → validate (Zod + rubric sum + schedule time) → tx (rubric, assignment, attachments) → commit → `publishOnce` → `notify(assignment.published)` to enrolled students.\n\n**Scheduled becomes visible.** No job. A student/parent list read evaluates `visibleWhere(now)`. Any newly visible assignment with `notifiedAt` null → fire-and-forget `publishOnce` (the atomic guard sends exactly once).\n\n**Submit.** Student uploads files → `POST /api/files {context:'submission'}` (unattached, owner-only readable) → `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text, fileIds}` → the six checks in order → tx (history snapshot if resubmitting, upsert submission, file rows, `attachFiles` → contextId = submission.id) → receipt.\nFrom then on, the files are readable through `submissionResolver` only by the student, their parents, and course managers.\n\n**Grade → return.** Grader page loads the roster (FR-54) → selects a student → `GET /api/submissions/:id` (cached; next and previous prefetched) → form computes the preview with `grading-math` → `PUT …/grade {…, return?}` → server recomputes everything authoritatively → tx → audit → (if return) `notifyStudentAndParents(assignment.returned, \"Course: Title — 18/20\")`.\nStudent `GET` now gets the grade fields, because the serializer unlocks on RETURNED.\n\n**Reminders.** The external caller hits `/api/internal/email/dispatch` → `dispatchEmails` → `sendDueReminders(now)` → due_soon and missing candidate queries → per-row `AssignmentReminder.create` (P2002 = already sent) → `notify`.\n\n**Privacy boundaries (NFR-4), three layers:** (1) query scoping: student and parent paths always filter `studentId ∈ resolveViewedStudent`; (2) `toStudentSubmission` serializer; (3) the file resolvers for `/api/files/:id`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Testing layout (NFR-13, NFR-14)\n\n- `tests/unit/assignments/grading-math.test.ts`: lateDays (exactly 24 h = 1, 24 h + 1 ms = 2, across spring-forward and fall-back in `Europe/London`), penalty cap, final score (18 @ 20 % = \"14.40\", half-up at .005), rubric sum, chip status. Also `nextTeachingDayDueAt` across DST.\n- `tests/integration/assignments/*.test.ts`: resubmission history (files kept attached), RETURNED refuses resubmit, return flow plus serializer unlock, reminder idempotency (call twice → one notification), exemption removes from missing and blocks submit, NO_SUBMISSION excluded, file resolver denies another student (AC-10).\n- `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` (`bypassCSP: true`): teacher creates → student submits a file → teacher grades with a rubric and returns → student sees feedback; parent sees the missing list.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions log\n\n| # | Decision | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Build the minimal MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor, FileUpload and FileList in `src/components/` | FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29, FR-30 |\n| D2 | Pin `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 via overrides; fallbacks are MUI `Table` and `datetime-local` | FR-17, FR-9 |\n| D3 | Fix the vitest import; e2e uses bypassCSP | NFR-13, NFR-14 |\n| D4 | Register the student tab and page; no tab bar | FR-41 |\n| D5 | Decimals are strings in JSON | NFR-1 |\n| D6 | \"Save & return\" = `PUT …/grade {return:true}`, one transaction | FR-32 |\n| D7 | With a rubric, the server sets `rawScore = Σ rubric points` | FR-30, FR-36 |\n| D8 | FR-58: managers get the full fields, other viewers get the serializer | FR-58, FR-27 |\n| D9 | An online submit over an unreturned offline grade = a resubmission | FR-8, FR-24 |\n| D10 | The missing pass looks back 8 days (`ponytail:` note) | FR-45 |\n| D11 | `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` only for `/api/files/:id`, so PDF iframes work | FR-29 |\n| D12 | Intake defaults adopted: FR-15 same dueAt plus offsets; FR-52 archived = hidden from students/parents, closed, no reminders, visible to managers; FR-60 NO_SUBMISSION never missing or reminded; FR-10 weekdays only; FR-36 extra credit raw-only; ADMIN /assignments = To grade | FR-10, FR-15, FR-36, FR-39, FR-52, FR-60 |\n| D13 | Resubmission after RETURNED → CONFLICT (409). Deadline and content failures → VALIDATION_ERROR | FR-22, FR-24 |\n| D14 | One audit row per affected submission, including bulk return | FR-59 |\n| D15 | FR-14 banner is client-side; no schema column | FR-14 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 enums in migration `add_assignments` |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `Assignment` (+allowExtraCredit, notifiedAt, archivedAt, rubricId @unique, index) |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `AssignmentAttachment`, `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `Submission`, `SubmissionFile`, `SubmissionHistory` |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `GradeExemption` |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 `AssignmentReminder`; §2.3 idempotency |\n| FR-7 | §2.6 `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 attempt-0 row; §2.2 Offline grade; D9 |\n| FR-9 | §2.8 `AssignmentForm`; §2.5 MarkdownEditor, FileUpload; D2 |\n| FR-10 | §2.2 `nextTeachingDayDueAt` in `src/lib/dates.ts` |\n| FR-11 | §2.8 rubric builder; §2.2 Create (server rubric-sum check); §2.6 superRefine |\n| FR-12 | §2.8 three buttons; §2.2 Create (SCHEDULED future check) |\n| FR-13 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` / `visibleWhere` (read-time, no job) |\n| FR-14 | §2.8 edit warning; D15 |\n| FR-15 | §2.2 Duplicate; §2.7 duplicate route |\n| FR-16 | §2.9 courseTabs entry |\n| FR-17 | §2.8 manager DataTable; §2.7 FR-48 manager shape; D2 |\n| FR-18 | §2.8 student/parent grouped list; `resolveViewedStudent` |\n| FR-19 | §2.8 assignment page; §2.5 MarkdownView, FileList |\n| FR-20 | §2.8 submission panel (localStorage draft); §2.5 FileUpload |\n| FR-21 | §2.8 ConfirmDialog before POST |\n| FR-22 | §2.2 Submit checks 1–4 |\n| FR-23 | §2.2 `grading-math.lateDays` |\n| FR-24 | §2.2 Submit transaction (history, clear grade, files kept) |\n| FR-25 | §2.8 receipt via `formatInSchoolTz` |\n| FR-26 | §2.8 returned results view |\n| FR-27 | §2.2 `toStudentSubmission` serializer |\n| FR-28 | §2.8 grading left panel; `submissionChipStatus` |\n| FR-29 | §2.8 grading main panel; §2.5 FileList preview; D11 |\n| FR-30 | §2.8 grading form; `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`; D7 |\n| FR-31 | §2.2 `grading-math.computeFinalScore` (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP) |\n| FR-32 | §2.2 Grade (`return:true`) and Bulk return; D6 |\n| FR-33 | §2.8 keydown handler |\n| FR-34 | §2.2 Offline grade; §2.7 grade-offline route |\n| FR-35 | §2.2 Exempt; `missingWhere`; Submit check 3 |\n| FR-36 | §2.2 Grade validation; `maxRawScore` |\n| FR-37 | §2.8 `/assignments` STUDENT; `missingWhere` |\n| FR-38 | §2.8 `/assignments` PARENT; `resolveViewedStudent` |\n| FR-39 | §2.8 `/assignments` TEACHER/ADMIN To grade |\n| FR-40 | §2.9 navigation entry |\n| FR-41 | §2.9 studentTabs entry; §2.8 students page; blocker 5 |\n| FR-42 | §2.2 `publishOnce` (atomic notifiedAt) |\n| FR-43 | §2.3 due_soon pass |\n| FR-44 | §2.2 Grade/Bulk return → `notifyStudentAndParents` |\n| FR-45 | §2.3 missing pass (parents only) |\n| FR-46 | §2.9 NOTIFICATION_TYPES keys |\n| FR-47 | §2.9 `assignmentResolver`, `submissionResolver` |\n| FR-48 | §2.7 `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` |\n| FR-49 | §2.7 `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments`; §2.2 Create |\n| FR-50 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]` |\n| FR-51 | §2.7 PATCH/DELETE; §2.2 Delete |\n| FR-52 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` (`!archivedAt`); D12 |\n| FR-53 | §2.7 POST submissions; §2.2 Submit checks 5–6 |\n| FR-54 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` |\n| FR-55 | §2.7 `GET /api/submissions/[id]` |\n| FR-56 | §2.7 `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade`; §2.2 Grade |\n| FR-57 | §2.7 `GET /api/me/assignments` |\n| FR-58 | §2.7 `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments`; D8 |\n| FR-59 | §2.2 audit calls; D14 |\n| FR-60 | §2.2 `missingWhere`, Submit check 3; §2.3 filters; D12 |\n| FR-61 | §2.9 seed block |\n| NFR-1 | §2.2 `grading-math` (Decimal); D5 strings in JSON |\n| NFR-2 | §2.2 server `now` everywhere; §2.6 no client clock fields |\n| NFR-3 | §2.8 grading `Map` cache plus next/prev prefetch |\n| NFR-4 | §3 privacy boundaries (scoping, serializer, resolvers) |\n| NFR-5 | §2.7 auth column; §2.4 reuse of require*/assertCan* |\n| NFR-6 | §1.1 blocker 8; §2.5/§2.8 MUI-only components |\n| NFR-7 | §2.7 thin handlers via `http.ts` helpers |\n| NFR-8 | §2.2 `src/server/assignments/`; §2.6; §2.7; §2.8 |\n| NFR-9 | §2.2 UTC lateDays, `fromZonedTime` default; §4 DST tests |\n| NFR-10 | §2.5 MarkdownView |\n| NFR-11 | §2.4 reuse map |\n| NFR-12 | §2.3 / §2.2 `logger` in catch paths |\n| NFR-13 | §1.1 blockers 2–3; ADR-2, ADR-3 |\n| NFR-14 | §4 testing layout |\n| NFR-15 | §1.1 blockers 4–5 (no CSP or tab-bar work); D12; exemption = row only |\n| NFR-16 | §2.8 form defaults; keyboard grading |\n| NFR-17 | §2.8 dnd-kit Up/Down fallback, shortcut hint, labelled inputs |\n\n## 7. Open items carried to handoff\n\n1. ADR-2 override must compile. Otherwise use the D2 fallbacks.\n2. Platform CSP nonce fix (real-browser hydration) is out of scope.\n3. The `studentTabs` renderer is missing, so the FR-41 tab is not visible.\n4. mui-mcp reachability is a hard gate for dev (NFR-6).\n5. D11 changes a security header (narrowly). Reviewer sign-off is recommended; the fallback is a PDF \"Open\" link.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":281,"newStart":1,"newLines":410,"lines":["-# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)","+# System Design: SH-9 · PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009)"," ","-Ticket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),","-`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Ticket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T10:40:00Z · Status: complete","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (61 FR + 17 NFR, 95%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),","+`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B16, D1–D10). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.","+> This file replaces the stale SH-8 design that was in this folder. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`","+> and `threat-model-notes.json` in this folder are also leftovers from earlier tickets. `arch-api-contracts` overwrites the first two."," "," ---"," "," ## 1. Overview"," "," SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).","-SH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:","+SH-9 adds **assignments**: teacher authoring with an optional rubric, student submission with resubmission history,","+a keyboard-driven grading screen, return flow, exemptions, offline grading, a cross-course `/assignments` page per role,","+four notifications, and two reminder passes."," ","-1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.","-2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.","+Shape of the change:"," ","-The design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).","+- **One migration**, `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6).","+- **One feature folder**, `src/server/assignments/`, with three files: `assignments-service.ts` (all DB logic),","+  `grading-math.ts` (pure, isomorphic, unit-tested), `reminders.ts` (maintenance pass).","+- **One validator file**, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by forms and handlers.","+- Thin route handlers under `src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…` (NFR-7, NFR-8).","+- Pages under `src/app/(app)/…`, plus the four PRD-08 shared components that were never built (D1).","+- **No new dependencies, services, queues, or cron** (ADR-1, ADR-8). Reminders hook into the existing dispatcher."," "," ### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)"," "," | # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |"," |---|---|---|","-| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |","-| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |","-| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |","-| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |","-| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |","-| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |","-| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |","-| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |","+| 1 | PRD-08 UI is missing: FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor | Build the minimum of all four in `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` (ADR-5, §2.5). No other PRD-08 scope. |","+| 2 | MUI X break: `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 vs X 9.5.0 | `package.json` `overrides: { \"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\" }` (ADR-2). This fixes both DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9). Fallback: FR-17 uses an MUI `Table`, and FR-9 uses `TextField type=\"datetime-local\"`. Dev verifies with `npm ls` plus a compile **before** building UI. |","+| 3 | vitest import break | Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (ADR-3). |","+| 4 | CSP `script-src 'self'` breaks hydration | Leave it alone. The e2e spec uses `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })` (ADR-4). The platform nonce fix is a follow-up ticket. |","+| 5 | `studentTabs` has no renderer | Register the FR-41 tab and build `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. The page works by direct URL. **No tab bar is built** (NFR-15). This is a known gap and is carried to the handoff. |","+| 6 | LOW-confidence defaults FR-15, FR-52, FR-60 | Adopt intake's defaults as written (§5). Each one is a single predicate or a single copy rule, so it is cheap to change later. |","+| 7 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-11). |","+| 8 | mui-mcp must be reachable (NFR-6) | This is a hard gate on the dev phase. Dev looks up every MUI component through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before using it. If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker. |"," ","-### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)","+### 1.2 New finding from this sub-task (not in intake)"," ","-| # | Decision |","-|---|---|","-| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |","-| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |","-| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |","-| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |","-| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |","-| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |","-| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |","+`next.config.js` sends **`X-Frame-Options: DENY`** on `/:path*`. That blocks the same-origin","+`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">` PDF preview required by FR-29. CSP `default-src 'self'` already allows same-origin frames,","+so the X-Frame-Options header is the only thing blocking it. `<img>` previews are not affected."," ","-### 1.3 Schema note","+**Decision D11:** in `next.config.js`, split the header rule:","+- `source: '/((?!api/files/).*)'` keeps the existing headers, with `DENY`.","+- `source: '/api/files/:id'` gets the same headers, but with `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` and `frame-ancestors 'self'` appended to the CSP."," ","-The PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.","+The file route already enforces access (`canAccessFile`) and sniffs types (`nosniff`), so letting our own pages frame it adds no exposure.","+**Fallback**, if the dev wants zero header changes: show PDFs as an \"Open\" link (`target=\"_blank\"`) instead of an iframe. Images still preview inline."," "," ---"," "," ## 2. Component Breakdown"," ","-### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)","+### 2.1 Data model: migration `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6)"," ","-- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.","-- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.","-- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.","-- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.","+All additive. Existing models get back-relations only (NFR-11)."," ","-### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`","+```","+enum SubmissionType   { ONLINE_TEXT FILE_UPLOAD TEXT_AND_FILE NO_SUBMISSION }   // FR-1","+enum AssignmentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }                              // FR-1","+enum SubmissionStatus { SUBMITTED RETURNED }                                     // FR-1"," ","-| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |","-| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |","-| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |","-| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |","-| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |","-| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |","-| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |","+Assignment (FR-2)","+  id, courseId → Course (Cascade), title, instructions (Text), submissionType, maxPoints Decimal(6,2),","+  dueAt, availableFrom?, allowLate, lateCutoffAt?, latePenaltyPercentPerDay Decimal(5,2),","+  maxLatePenaltyPercent Decimal(5,2), maxFileCount Int, allowExtraCredit Boolean @default(false),","+  status AssignmentStatus, rubricId String? @unique → Rubric, notifiedAt?, archivedAt?,","+  createdById, createdAt, updatedAt","+  @@index([courseId, dueAt])"," ","-**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.","+AssignmentAttachment (FR-3)  assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([assignmentId, fileId])","+Rubric (FR-3)                id, criteria RubricCriterion[]","+RubricCriterion (FR-3)       id, rubricId → Rubric (Cascade), title, description?, maxPoints Decimal(6,2), order Int,","+                             levels Json  // [{label, points, description}]"," ","-**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.","+Submission (FR-4)","+  id, assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId → User, status SubmissionStatus, text?,","+  attemptNumber Int, submittedAt, isLate Boolean, lateDays Int,","+  rawScore Decimal(6,2)?, penaltyPercent Decimal(5,2)?, finalScore Decimal(6,2)?,","+  rubricScores Json?  // [{criterionId, points, comment}]","+  feedback?, gradedById?, gradedAt?, returnedAt?","+  @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])","+SubmissionFile (FR-4)        submissionId → Submission (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([submissionId, fileId])","+SubmissionHistory (FR-4)     id, submissionId → Submission (Cascade), attemptNumber, text?, fileIds String[], submittedAt"," ","-### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`","+GradeExemption (FR-5)        assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, reason?, createdAt; @@id([assignmentId, studentId])","+AssignmentReminder (FR-6)    assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, kind String ('due_soon'|'missing'), createdAt","+                             @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])","+```"," ","-| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |","+Back-relations added: `Course.assignments`, `FileObject.assignmentAttachments`, `FileObject.submissionFiles`, `User.submissions`.","+","+Model decisions:","+- **One Submission row per student.** Earlier attempts live in `SubmissionHistory` (FR-24).","+- `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` has no FK. Old attempt files **stay attached** to the same submission id and are never detached. Detaching them would let `purgeOrphanFiles` delete history bytes (B1).","+- Offline grade (FR-8, FR-34) = a Submission with `attemptNumber 0`, `text null`, no files, and `submittedAt = gradedAt`.","+- A Rubric is 1:1 with an Assignment (`rubricId @unique`). Delete the rubric in the same transaction as a hard-deleted assignment.","+- FR-14: **no column added.** The \"review grades\" banner is client-side, shown after a successful PATCH that changed `maxPoints` while `submissionCount > 0`.","+","+### 2.2 Server: `src/server/assignments/` (NFR-8)","+","+| File | Contents | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|","-| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |","-| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |","-| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |","-| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |","+| `grading-math.ts` | **Pure and isomorphic** (no Prisma client import; `Decimal` from `decimal.js`, the same package Prisma uses). `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt)`, `defaultPenalty(lateDays, perDay, max)`, `computeFinalScore(raw, pct)`, `rubricTotal(criteria)`, `maxRawScore(maxPoints, allowExtraCredit)`, `submissionChipStatus(row)` | FR-23, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-28, NFR-1, NFR-14 |","+| `assignments-service.ts` | All DB logic: visibility, CRUD, duplicate, submit, grade, return, exempt, offline grade, role-shaped lists, the serializer, and notify triggers. | FR-8, FR-12..15, FR-22, FR-24, FR-32, FR-34, FR-35, FR-42, FR-44, FR-48..58, FR-59 |","+| `reminders.ts` | `sendDueReminders(now)`: due_soon and missing passes. | FR-43, FR-45, FR-60 |"," ","-`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):","+`grading-math.ts` imports only `decimal.js`. The service wraps values as `Prisma.Decimal` (same class). This keeps one function for the client preview and the server value (ADR-7)."," ","-- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.","-- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).","-- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.","-- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.","-- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.","-- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).","-- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).","-- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).","-- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).","-- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).","-- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).","-- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).","-- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).","+#### Single-source helpers (inside `assignments-service.ts` unless noted)"," ","-### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)","+| Helper | Definition | Used by |","+|---|---|---|","+| `isAssignmentVisible(a, now)` | `!a.archivedAt && isVisible({ status: a.status, publishAt: a.availableFrom }, now)`. Reuses `src/server/content/visibility.ts`: widen `Publishable.status` to `ContentStatus \\| AssignmentStatus` (same string values). | FR-13, FR-22, FR-47, FR-48, FR-50, FR-52, FR-57, FR-58, reminders |","+| `visibleWhere(now)` | The Prisma `where` equivalent: `{ archivedAt: null, OR: [{status:'PUBLISHED'}, {status:'SCHEDULED', availableFrom:{lte:now}}] }` | list queries, reminders |","+| `missingWhere(now)` | visible ∧ `dueAt < now` ∧ `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION`; per student: no Submission and no GradeExemption | FR-37, FR-35, FR-45, FR-60 |","+| `toStudentSubmission(sub)` | Removes `rawScore, penaltyPercent, finalScore, feedback, rubricScores, gradedById, gradedAt` unless `status === 'RETURNED'`. Always removes history. | FR-27, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58, NFR-4 |","+| `serializeDecimals` | Prisma.Decimal → `string` (\"14.40\") on the way out | NFR-1 (D5) |","+| `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` | **Reused** from `visibility.ts`: ADMIN, teacher or co-teacher = \"manager\" | everywhere |","+| `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz, teachingDays)` | **In `src/lib/dates.ts`**, next to `schoolNow`. Walk from tomorrow (≤7 days) to the first `isTeaching` weekday, take 23:59 local, convert with `fromZonedTime`. If no day is teaching, use tomorrow. | FR-10, NFR-9 |","+| `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` | STUDENT → self. PARENT → `studentId` must be in `ParentStudentLink`; it defaults to the only linked child. Otherwise FORBIDDEN. | FR-18, FR-38, FR-57 |"," ","-| Existing | Used for |","-|---|---|","-| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |","-| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |","-| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |","-| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |","-| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |","-| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |","-| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |","-| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |","-| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |","-| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |","-| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |","+#### Key service flows"," ","-### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)","+**Create / update (FR-49, FR-51, FR-11, FR-12, FR-42).** One transaction: Zod parse → if a rubric is given, `rubricTotal == maxPoints`, otherwise","+VALIDATION_ERROR `Rubric totals {sum} points but the assignment is worth {maxPoints}.` → SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > new Date()` (checked in the service,","+because Zod has no server clock, NFR-2) → upsert rubric and criteria → write the assignment → `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, 'assignment', id)`. On PATCH,","+diff the attachments: removed files are `detachFiles` (the purge reclaims them). **After commit**, if the assignment is now visible → `publishOnce(id)`."," ","-| File | Methods | Reqs |","+**`publishOnce(id)` (FR-42).** `updateMany({ where:{ id, notifiedAt:null }, data:{ notifiedAt: now } })`. Only when `count === 1`, call `notify()` for","+`assignment.published` to ACTIVE-enrolled students. Called from: create/PATCH after commit, and from the student/parent list read paths (FR-48, FR-57)","+for SCHEDULED assignments that have become visible with `notifiedAt` null. On GET it is fire-and-forget (`void publishOnce(id).catch(logger.error)`) and never fails the read.","+","+**Delete (FR-51).** If there are 0 submissions → detach the attachments, then delete the assignment and its rubric (cascade). Otherwise → set `archivedAt = now`. Audit `assignment.delete|archive`.","+","+**Duplicate (FR-15).** `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target course, then one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows.","+Attachments: `readFile` → `saveFile` → a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), because FileObject holds one context (B2). Status is DRAFT and `notifiedAt` is null.","+Same `dueAt`; `availableFrom` and `lateCutoffAt` keep their offsets from dueAt (FR-15 default).","+","+**Submit (FR-22..FR-24, FR-53, FR-60).** `now = new Date()` on the server. Checks, in order (first failure wins):","+1. Assignment exists and `isAssignmentVisible` → otherwise NOT_FOUND.","+2. `role === 'STUDENT'` and ACTIVE-enrolled in the course → otherwise FORBIDDEN.","+3. Not exempt; `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR.","+4. Deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR `The deadline has passed and late submissions are closed.`","+5. Content matches the type: text for ONLINE_TEXT, ≥1 file for FILE_UPLOAD, ≥1 of either for TEXT_AND_FILE. Also `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`.","+6. Each file has `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'`, and is unattached **or** already attached to this submission. The service checks `context` before calling `attachFiles`, because `attachFiles` does not (B1).","+","+Then, in one transaction:","+- **No row:** create the Submission (`attemptNumber 1`, `isLate`, `lateDays` from `grading-math`).","+- **Row with `status = SUBMITTED`**, including an attempt-0 offline row (D9): insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear all grade fields, and replace the `SubmissionFile` rows. Old files stay attached.","+- **Row with `RETURNED`:** CONFLICT `This submission has been returned and can no longer be changed.`","+","+`attachFiles(tx, user, newFileIds, 'submission', submission.id)`. A P2002 from two concurrent first submits → retry once as a resubmit.","+","+**Grade (FR-56, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-32 \"Save & return\").** `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade { rawScore?, penaltyPercent, feedback?, rubricScores?, return?: boolean }`.","+- If the assignment has a rubric: `rubricScores` are required, every criterion must be scored exactly once, `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints`, and **the server sets `rawScore = Σ points`** (any client raw value is ignored, D7).","+- Otherwise: `0 ≤ rawScore ≤ maxRawScore` (×1.2 when `allowExtraCredit`). Extra credit applies to rawScore only.","+- `0 ≤ penaltyPercent ≤ 100`. `finalScore = computeFinalScore`. Set `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. The status stays SUBMITTED.","+- `return: true` → in the same transaction, set `status RETURNED`, `returnedAt`, then notify after commit (D6: a single round trip). Audit `submission.grade` (+ `submission.return`).","+","+**Bulk return (FR-32).** `POST /api/assignments/:id/return { submissionIds? }`. The default set is `gradedAt != null AND status = SUBMITTED`. A supplied id that is ungraded is","+skipped and reported in the response (`{returned, skipped}`). One `updateMany`, then one `notifyStudentAndParents` per student (FR-44), plus **one audit row per submission** (FR-59), so","+a per-record audit trail is possible.","+","+**Offline grade (FR-34, FR-8).** The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. If a submission already exists → CONFLICT (grade that one instead). Create the attempt-0 row","+with the grade fields and penalty 0, using the same validation as Grade. Audit `submission.grade_offline`.","+","+**Exempt (FR-35).** PUT = `upsert` GradeExemption, DELETE = `deleteMany` (both idempotent). Audit `assignment.exempt|unexempt`. The effects come only through","+`missingWhere`, the submit rule 3, and reminders. The PRD-11 \"exclude\" flag **is** the row itself (NFR-15).","+","+### 2.3 Maintenance: `reminders.ts` (FR-43, FR-45, FR-60)","+","+`sendDueReminders(now)` is called on **every** request to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, outside the daily `lastPurgeAt` block, in its own try/catch with logger (B8).","+","+| Pass | Assignment window | Targets | Notify |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| due_soon | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ (now, now+24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | ACTIVE-enrolled, no Submission, no GradeExemption | `assignment.due_soon` → student |","+| missing | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ [now−8d, now−24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | same | `assignment.missing` → linked parents only, via `notify()` |","+","+Idempotency: `createMany({ data: candidates, skipDuplicates: true })` cannot report *which* rows were inserted, so **insert per (assignment, student) with `create` and catch P2002**,","+and notify only on success. The Postgres unique key makes this safe across concurrent dispatchers. Candidate counts are small (one course × roster).","+`// ponytail: missing pass only looks back 8 days; widen or add a cursor if the dispatcher can be down longer.`","+","+### 2.4 Reuse map (NFR-11)","+","+| Existing | Where | Used for |"," |---|---|---|","-| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |","-| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |","-| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |","-| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |","-| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |","-| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |","-| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |","-| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |","-| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |","+| `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` | `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | every handler and page (NFR-5) |","+| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` | course-scoped routes |","+| `assertCanViewStudent` | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-58 |","+| `isVisible`, `canSeeDrafts` | `src/server/content/visibility.ts` (type widened) | FR-13, manager checks |","+| `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination`, `AppError` | `src/server/http.ts` | NFR-7 envelopes and errors |","+| `audit()` | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-59 |","+| `notify()`, `notifyStudentAndParents()`, `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | `src/server/notifications/` | FR-42..FR-46 |","+| `attachFiles`, `detachFiles`, `POST /api/files`, `GET /api/files/:id?inline=1`, `registerBuiltInContexts`, `storage.ts` | `src/server/files/`, `src/server/storage.ts` | FR-9, FR-15, FR-20, FR-29, FR-47, FR-53 |","+| `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | `src/lib/dates.ts` | FR-19, FR-25, NFR-9 |","+| `ConfirmDialog`, `DataTable`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `useToast`, `FormField`, `DateDisplay` | `src/components/` | FR-17, FR-21, lists, forms |","+| `courseTabs`, `studentTabs`, `navigation` | `src/config/` | FR-16, FR-40, FR-41 |","+| `logger` | `src/lib/logger.ts` | NFR-12 |"," ","-That is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.","+### 2.5 New shared UI components (blocker 1, ADR-5)"," ","-### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)","+| Component | Build | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `MarkdownView` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema). Elements map to MUI `Typography`, `Link`, `Table*`, `List*`, `Box component=\"pre\"`. | NFR-10, FR-19, FR-29, FR-26 |","+| `MarkdownEditor` | MUI `TextField multiline` + `Tabs` (Write / Preview → `MarkdownView`). Controlled `value`/`onChange`, plus `maxLength`. | FR-9, FR-20, FR-30 |","+| `FileUpload` | MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`. POSTs each file to `/api/files` with `context`. Props `{context, max, value: FileRef[], onChange}`. A `LinearProgress` per file, plus remove. | FR-9, FR-20 |","+| `FileList` | MUI `List` of links to `/api/files/:id`. Optional `preview` prop: `<img>` for `image/*`, `<iframe>` for `application/pdf`, both via `?inline=1` (D11). | FR-19, FR-25, FR-29 |"," ","-| File | Notes | Reqs |","+### 2.6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` (FR-7)","+","+`assignmentInput` (FR-7 limits; `.superRefine`: `lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum = maxPoints using `rubricTotal`), `rubricCriterionInput`,","+`submissionInput {text? ≤50k, fileIds ≤10}`, `gradeInput {rawScore?, penaltyPercent 0–100, feedback? ≤10k, rubricScores?, return?}`,","+`offlineGradeInput`, `bulkReturnInput`, `duplicateInput {courseIds min 1}`, `meAssignmentsQuery {studentId?, tab?, courseId?}`.","+Decimals are accepted as `z.union([z.number(), z.string()])` and converted to Decimal in the service. No request schema has a timestamp field except","+`dueAt`/`availableFrom`/`lateCutoffAt`, which are authoring data, not \"now\" (NFR-2).","+","+### 2.7 Route handlers (thin: Zod → service → envelope; NFR-7)","+","+| Route | Auth | Service fn | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | user + view course | `listCourseAssignments` (manager shape with `groupBy` counts / student shape) | FR-48, FR-17, FR-18 |","+| `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | manage course | `createAssignment` | FR-49 |","+| `GET /api/assignments/[id]` | view (NOT_FOUND for invisible to non-manager) | `getAssignment` (+ own submission, `serverNow`) | FR-50, FR-19 |","+| `PATCH` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]` | manage | `updateAssignment` / `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | FR-51, FR-14 |","+| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/duplicate` | manage source + each target | `duplicateAssignment` | FR-15 |","+| `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | manage | `listGradingRoster` (every ACTIVE enrollee; `pageSize` ≤100) | FR-54, FR-28 |","+| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | STUDENT | `submit` | FR-53, FR-22..24 |","+| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/return` | manage | `bulkReturn` | FR-32, FR-44 |","+| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/grade-offline` | manage | `gradeOffline` | FR-34, FR-8 |","+| `PUT` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]/exemptions/[studentId]` | manage | `setExemption` | FR-35 |","+| `GET /api/submissions/[id]` | submitter, linked parent, or manager; history for managers only | `getSubmission` | FR-55, FR-29, NFR-3 |","+| `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade` | manage | `gradeSubmission` | FR-56, FR-30..32, FR-36 |","+| `GET /api/me/assignments` | any user; role switch | `listMyAssignments` | FR-57, FR-37..39 |","+| `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments` | `assertCanViewStudent` | `listStudentAssignments` | FR-58, FR-41 |","+","+Shared response conventions for `arch-api-contracts`: Decimals are **strings**. Timestamps are ISO UTC strings. Student/parent submission objects","+always pass through `toStudentSubmission`. FR-58: a viewer who manages the course gets the full fields, everyone else gets the serializer (D8).","+`/api/me/assignments` for ADMIN = \"To grade\" across all courses (intake default).","+","+### 2.8 Pages (`src/app/(app)/…`)","+","+| Page | Notes | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|","-| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |","-| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |","-| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |","-| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |","-| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |","-| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |","-| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |","-| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |","-| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |","-| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/page.tsx` | Manager: `DataTable` (title, due, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted, Grade button; Archived chip). Student/parent: grouped `List` (Upcoming / Past due / Submitted / Returned). Parent child selector when more than one linked child is enrolled. | FR-16..18, FR-52 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/new/page.tsx` + `[assignmentId]/edit/page.tsx` | One shared `AssignmentForm` (react-hook-form + the Zod schema). Defaults: dueAt = `nextTeachingDayDueAt` (computed server-side, passed as a prop), maxPoints 100, FILE_UPLOAD, maxFileCount 3, allowLate off (NFR-16). Rubric builder: `@dnd-kit/sortable` with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, and a live sum error. Buttons: Save draft / Publish / Schedule. Edit warns per FR-14. \"Duplicate to other courses\" dialog with an `Autocomplete` of managed courses. | FR-9..15 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/page.tsx` | MarkdownView instructions, FileList, due and late-policy summary, rubric table, countdown under 48 h (offset from `serverNow`, display only). Submission panel by type, `localStorage` draft key `assignment:{id}:{userId}` (cleared on success), ConfirmDialog before POST, receipt via `formatInSchoolTz`, returned results, or \"Submitted — awaiting grading\". Parent: read-only, no panel. | FR-19..27 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/page.tsx` | Left: `List` + status `Chip`s from `submissionChipStatus`, filter, sort by name or time. Main: MarkdownView text, FileList with preview, history `Select`. Form: rubric `ToggleButtonGroup`s that auto-sum, prefilled penalty (`defaultPenalty`), live final score (`computeFinalScore`), MarkdownEditor feedback. Buttons Save / Save & return / Return all graded / Grade without submission / Exempt toggle. J/K/Ctrl+Enter keydown handler that skips J/K in input/textarea/contenteditable, with a visible shortcut hint. **NFR-3:** a plain `Map<id, Submission>` cache; after each selection, prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id`. | FR-28..36, NFR-3, NFR-16, NFR-17 |","+| `assignments/page.tsx` | STUDENT: `Tabs` Upcoming/Missing/Submitted/Returned + course filter. PARENT: child selector, same view, read-only. TEACHER/ADMIN: \"To grade\" list, oldest first. | FR-37..39 |","+| `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx` | Per-student list (FR-58). Reachable by URL only (blocker 5). | FR-41 |"," ","-### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits","+### 2.9 Config and registrations"," ","-- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).","-- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).","-- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).","-- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.","-- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).","-- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).","+- `src/config/course-tabs.ts`: `{ key:'assignments', label:'Assignments', href: id => /courses/${id}/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES }` (FR-16).","+- `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Assignments` → `/assignments`, roles `[STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER, ADMIN]` (FR-40; ADMIN added because the To-grade default applies to ADMIN).","+- `src/config/student-tabs.ts`: `assignments` entry (FR-41).","+- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: four keys, category ACADEMIC (FR-46):","+  `assignment.published` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.due_soon` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.returned` [STUDENT, PARENT] email false · `assignment.missing` [PARENT] email **true**.","+- `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (FR-47), registered in `registerBuiltInContexts`:","+  - `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course → `assertCanViewCourse` → `canSeeDrafts || isAssignmentVisible`.","+  - `submissionResolver`: load the submission and course → allow `studentId === user.id`, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), or `canSeeDrafts`. Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10).","+- `next.config.js`: D11 header split.","+- `package.json`: `overrides[\"@mui/x-internals\"] = \"9.1.0\"` (ADR-2). `vitest.config.ts` import fix (ADR-3).","+- `prisma/seed.ts`: FR-61 block, idempotent: look up courses by code (skip if missing), upsert by `(courseId, title)`, Decimals as strings, no file bytes."," "," ---"," "," ## 3. Data Flow"," ","-### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)","-```","-FileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy","-   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)","-   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}","-LessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse","-   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach","-Viewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile","-   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)","-   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN","-   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)","-```","+**Author → publish.** Teacher form → `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments` → validate (Zod + rubric sum + schedule time) → tx (rubric, assignment, attachments) → commit → `publishOnce` → `notify(assignment.published)` to enrolled students."," ","-### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)","-```","-request ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?","-   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now","-```","-No job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).","+**Scheduled becomes visible.** No job. A student/parent list read evaluates `visibleWhere(now)`. Any newly visible assignment with `notifiedAt` null → fire-and-forget `publishOnce` (the atomic guard sends exactly once)."," ","-### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)","-`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.","+**Submit.** Student uploads files → `POST /api/files {context:'submission'}` (unattached, owner-only readable) → `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text, fileIds}` → the six checks in order → tx (history snapshot if resubmitting, upsert submission, file rows, `attachFiles` → contextId = submission.id) → receipt.","+From then on, the files are readable through `submissionResolver` only by the student, their parents, and course managers."," ","-### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)","-Viewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.","+**Grade → return.** Grader page loads the roster (FR-54) → selects a student → `GET /api/submissions/:id` (cached; next and previous prefetched) → form computes the preview with `grading-math` → `PUT …/grade {…, return?}` → server recomputes everything authoritatively → tx → audit → (if return) `notifyStudentAndParents(assignment.returned, \"Course: Title — 18/20\")`.","+Student `GET` now gets the grade fields, because the serializer unlocks on RETURNED."," ","-### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)","-dnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.","+**Reminders.** The external caller hits `/api/internal/email/dispatch` → `dispatchEmails` → `sendDueReminders(now)` → due_soon and missing candidate queries → per-row `AssignmentReminder.create` (P2002 = already sent) → `notify`."," ","-### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)","-The email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.","+**Privacy boundaries (NFR-4), three layers:** (1) query scoping: student and parent paths always filter `studentId ∈ resolveViewedStudent`; (2) `toStudentSubmission` serializer; (3) the file resolvers for `/api/files/:id`."," ","-### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)","-The admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.","-"," ---"," ","-## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)","+## 4. Testing layout (NFR-13, NFR-14)"," ","-- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.","-- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).","-- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).","-- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.","-- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.","-- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.","-- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.","+- `tests/unit/assignments/grading-math.test.ts`: lateDays (exactly 24 h = 1, 24 h + 1 ms = 2, across spring-forward and fall-back in `Europe/London`), penalty cap, final score (18 @ 20 % = \"14.40\", half-up at .005), rubric sum, chip status. Also `nextTeachingDayDueAt` across DST.","+- `tests/integration/assignments/*.test.ts`: resubmission history (files kept attached), RETURNED refuses resubmit, return flow plus serializer unlock, reminder idempotency (call twice → one notification), exemption removes from missing and blocks submit, NO_SUBMISSION excluded, file resolver denies another student (AC-10).","+- `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` (`bypassCSP: true`): teacher creates → student submits a file → teacher grades with a rubric and returns → student sees feedback; parent sees the missing list."," ","-## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)","+---"," ","-- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).","-- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.","-- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.","-- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).","+## 5. Decisions log"," ","+| # | Decision | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| D1 | Build the minimal MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor, FileUpload and FileList in `src/components/` | FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29, FR-30 |","+| D2 | Pin `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 via overrides; fallbacks are MUI `Table` and `datetime-local` | FR-17, FR-9 |","+| D3 | Fix the vitest import; e2e uses bypassCSP | NFR-13, NFR-14 |","+| D4 | Register the student tab and page; no tab bar | FR-41 |","+| D5 | Decimals are strings in JSON | NFR-1 |","+| D6 | \"Save & return\" = `PUT …/grade {return:true}`, one transaction | FR-32 |","+| D7 | With a rubric, the server sets `rawScore = Σ rubric points` | FR-30, FR-36 |","+| D8 | FR-58: managers get the full fields, other viewers get the serializer | FR-58, FR-27 |","+| D9 | An online submit over an unreturned offline grade = a resubmission | FR-8, FR-24 |","+| D10 | The missing pass looks back 8 days (`ponytail:` note) | FR-45 |","+| D11 | `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` only for `/api/files/:id`, so PDF iframes work | FR-29 |","+| D12 | Intake defaults adopted: FR-15 same dueAt plus offsets; FR-52 archived = hidden from students/parents, closed, no reminders, visible to managers; FR-60 NO_SUBMISSION never missing or reminded; FR-10 weekdays only; FR-36 extra credit raw-only; ADMIN /assignments = To grade | FR-10, FR-15, FR-36, FR-39, FR-52, FR-60 |","+| D13 | Resubmission after RETURNED → CONFLICT (409). Deadline and content failures → VALIDATION_ERROR | FR-22, FR-24 |","+| D14 | One audit row per affected submission, including bulk return | FR-59 |","+| D15 | FR-14 banner is client-side; no schema column | FR-14 |","+"," ---"," "," ## 6. Requirements Traceability"," "," | Req | Design element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |","-| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |","-| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |","-| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |","-| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |","-| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |","-| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |","-| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |","-| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |","-| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |","-| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |","-| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |","-| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |","-| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |","-| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |","-| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |","-| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |","-| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |","-| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |","-| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |","-| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |","-| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |","-| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |","-| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |","-| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |","-| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |","-| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |","-| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |","-| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |","-| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |","-| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |","-| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |","-| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |","-| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |","-| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |","-| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |","-| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |","-| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |","-| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |","-| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |","-| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |","-| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |","-| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |","-| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |","-| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |","-| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |","-| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |","-| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |","-| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |","-| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |","-| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |","-| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |","-| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |","-| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |","-| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |","-| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |","-| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |","-| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |","-| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |","-| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |","+| FR-1 | §2.1 enums in migration `add_assignments` |","+| FR-2 | §2.1 `Assignment` (+allowExtraCredit, notifiedAt, archivedAt, rubricId @unique, index) |","+| FR-3 | §2.1 `AssignmentAttachment`, `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` |","+| FR-4 | §2.1 `Submission`, `SubmissionFile`, `SubmissionHistory` |","+| FR-5 | §2.1 `GradeExemption` |","+| FR-6 | §2.1 `AssignmentReminder`; §2.3 idempotency |","+| FR-7 | §2.6 `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` |","+| FR-8 | §2.1 attempt-0 row; §2.2 Offline grade; D9 |","+| FR-9 | §2.8 `AssignmentForm`; §2.5 MarkdownEditor, FileUpload; D2 |","+| FR-10 | §2.2 `nextTeachingDayDueAt` in `src/lib/dates.ts` |","+| FR-11 | §2.8 rubric builder; §2.2 Create (server rubric-sum check); §2.6 superRefine |","+| FR-12 | §2.8 three buttons; §2.2 Create (SCHEDULED future check) |","+| FR-13 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` / `visibleWhere` (read-time, no job) |","+| FR-14 | §2.8 edit warning; D15 |","+| FR-15 | §2.2 Duplicate; §2.7 duplicate route |","+| FR-16 | §2.9 courseTabs entry |","+| FR-17 | §2.8 manager DataTable; §2.7 FR-48 manager shape; D2 |","+| FR-18 | §2.8 student/parent grouped list; `resolveViewedStudent` |","+| FR-19 | §2.8 assignment page; §2.5 MarkdownView, FileList |","+| FR-20 | §2.8 submission panel (localStorage draft); §2.5 FileUpload |","+| FR-21 | §2.8 ConfirmDialog before POST |","+| FR-22 | §2.2 Submit checks 1–4 |","+| FR-23 | §2.2 `grading-math.lateDays` |","+| FR-24 | §2.2 Submit transaction (history, clear grade, files kept) |","+| FR-25 | §2.8 receipt via `formatInSchoolTz` |","+| FR-26 | §2.8 returned results view |","+| FR-27 | §2.2 `toStudentSubmission` serializer |","+| FR-28 | §2.8 grading left panel; `submissionChipStatus` |","+| FR-29 | §2.8 grading main panel; §2.5 FileList preview; D11 |","+| FR-30 | §2.8 grading form; `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`; D7 |","+| FR-31 | §2.2 `grading-math.computeFinalScore` (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP) |","+| FR-32 | §2.2 Grade (`return:true`) and Bulk return; D6 |","+| FR-33 | §2.8 keydown handler |","+| FR-34 | §2.2 Offline grade; §2.7 grade-offline route |","+| FR-35 | §2.2 Exempt; `missingWhere`; Submit check 3 |","+| FR-36 | §2.2 Grade validation; `maxRawScore` |","+| FR-37 | §2.8 `/assignments` STUDENT; `missingWhere` |","+| FR-38 | §2.8 `/assignments` PARENT; `resolveViewedStudent` |","+| FR-39 | §2.8 `/assignments` TEACHER/ADMIN To grade |","+| FR-40 | §2.9 navigation entry |","+| FR-41 | §2.9 studentTabs entry; §2.8 students page; blocker 5 |","+| FR-42 | §2.2 `publishOnce` (atomic notifiedAt) |","+| FR-43 | §2.3 due_soon pass |","+| FR-44 | §2.2 Grade/Bulk return → `notifyStudentAndParents` |","+| FR-45 | §2.3 missing pass (parents only) |","+| FR-46 | §2.9 NOTIFICATION_TYPES keys |","+| FR-47 | §2.9 `assignmentResolver`, `submissionResolver` |","+| FR-48 | §2.7 `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` |","+| FR-49 | §2.7 `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments`; §2.2 Create |","+| FR-50 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]` |","+| FR-51 | §2.7 PATCH/DELETE; §2.2 Delete |","+| FR-52 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` (`!archivedAt`); D12 |","+| FR-53 | §2.7 POST submissions; §2.2 Submit checks 5–6 |","+| FR-54 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` |","+| FR-55 | §2.7 `GET /api/submissions/[id]` |","+| FR-56 | §2.7 `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade`; §2.2 Grade |","+| FR-57 | §2.7 `GET /api/me/assignments` |","+| FR-58 | §2.7 `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments`; D8 |","+| FR-59 | §2.2 audit calls; D14 |","+| FR-60 | §2.2 `missingWhere`, Submit check 3; §2.3 filters; D12 |","+| FR-61 | §2.9 seed block |","+| NFR-1 | §2.2 `grading-math` (Decimal); D5 strings in JSON |","+| NFR-2 | §2.2 server `now` everywhere; §2.6 no client clock fields |","+| NFR-3 | §2.8 grading `Map` cache plus next/prev prefetch |","+| NFR-4 | §3 privacy boundaries (scoping, serializer, resolvers) |","+| NFR-5 | §2.7 auth column; §2.4 reuse of require*/assertCan* |","+| NFR-6 | §1.1 blocker 8; §2.5/§2.8 MUI-only components |","+| NFR-7 | §2.7 thin handlers via `http.ts` helpers |","+| NFR-8 | §2.2 `src/server/assignments/`; §2.6; §2.7; §2.8 |","+| NFR-9 | §2.2 UTC lateDays, `fromZonedTime` default; §4 DST tests |","+| NFR-10 | §2.5 MarkdownView |","+| NFR-11 | §2.4 reuse map |","+| NFR-12 | §2.3 / §2.2 `logger` in catch paths |","+| NFR-13 | §1.1 blockers 2–3; ADR-2, ADR-3 |","+| NFR-14 | §4 testing layout |","+| NFR-15 | §1.1 blockers 4–5 (no CSP or tab-bar work); D12; exemption = row only |","+| NFR-16 | §2.8 form defaults; keyboard grading |","+| NFR-17 | §2.8 dnd-kit Up/Down fallback, shortcut hint, labelled inputs |","+","+## 7. Open items carried to handoff","+","+1. ADR-2 override must compile. Otherwise use the D2 fallbacks.","+2. Platform CSP nonce fix (real-browser hydration) is out of scope.","+3. The `studentTabs` renderer is missing, so the FR-41 tab is not visible.","+4. mui-mcp reachability is a hard gate for dev (NFR-6).","+5. D11 changes a security header (narrowly). Reviewer sign-off is recommended; the fallback is a PDF \"Open\" link."]}],"originalFile":"# System Design: SH-8 · PRD-08 File Storage & Course Content (SCH-008)\n\nTicket: SH-8 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-06T07:00:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (48 FR + 12 NFR, 93%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-9), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B8, 7 open decisions). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-7 (PRD-07) design that was in this folder.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-8 adds two features that are greenfield within the brownfield codebase:\n\n1. **File storage**: a generic `FileObject` table, a local-disk `storage.ts`, a context-keyed **access registry**, three `/api/files` endpoints, an orphan purge, and the `FileUpload`/`FileList` components.\n2. **Course content**: Module → Lesson (Markdown, video, attachments, links) with DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED status evaluated at read time, a Content course tab, a lesson editor and viewer, student progress, a Learning student tab, and the `content.lesson_published` notification.\n\nThe design adds no new runtime services, queues, schedulers or storage abstraction (NFR-11). Everything runs in the existing Next process. The only new dependencies are the five pinned in ADR-1. Multipart parsing reuses Next's transitive `busboy` (ADR-2).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Greenfield file and content code | §2 component breakdown lists every new file. There is one migration, `add_files_and_content` (§2.1). |\n| 2 | New deps | ADR-1 pins: file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown 10.1.0, remark-gfm 4.0.1, rehype-sanitize 6.0.0, @dnd-kit/sortable 10.0.0. busboy is transitive, so nothing is installed for it (ADR-2). |\n| 3 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-9). |\n| 4 | FR-12 hook | `purgeOrphanFiles()` is called inside the existing `lastPurgeAt` block in `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, next to `purgeOldNotifications()`. |\n| 5 | FR-42/FR-40 (LOW) | A minimal ADMIN page `/admin/settings/school` is built on the existing `PATCH /api/settings/school`. `logoUrl` stores `/api/files/<id>`. Email `BaseLayout` prefixes `appUrl` when the value starts with `/`. The logo file is **attached** (`contextId='singleton'`) so the purge never deletes it (D2). |\n| 6 | FR-6 sniff rules | ADR-3 table in `src/server/files/validate.ts` (§2.2). |\n| 7 | No `.gitignore` | A root `.gitignore` is created with `uploads/`, `node_modules/`, `.next/` and `.env`. |\n| 8 | NFR-7 mui-mcp | Dev must call `useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs` (9.5.0) for every MUI component before writing UI. If the MCP is unreachable, that is a **hard blocker** and dev stops. The mui-mcp tools were listed as available in this session. |\n\n### 1.2 Resolved open design decisions (from requirements-analysis-notes)\n\n| # | Decision |\n|---|---|\n| D1 Public `/api/files/` (B1) | Add `'/api/files/'` to `PUBLIC_API_PATHS`. GET resolves the user with `getCurrentUser()` (nullable) and runs the registry. **POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` first**, because middleware no longer guards them (NFR-1, NFR-8). |\n| D2 Logo vs purge | Saving settings with a logo sets `context='logo', contextId='singleton'` on the new file and sets the previous logo file's `contextId` back to null, so it is purged 24 h later. |\n| D3 Inline Markdown images | On every lesson PATCH that includes `contentMarkdown`, the service extracts `/api/files/<id>` refs with a regex and attaches eligible files (`context='lesson', contextId=lessonId`). They do **not** get LessonAttachment rows. Refs that were removed are detached (contextId null) unless the file is still a LessonAttachment. |\n| D4 Multipart | busboy streaming (ADR-2). `formData()` is not used anywhere. |\n| D5 Detach semantics | A file removed from `attachments[]` gets `contextId=null`, and the orphan purge deletes it after 24 h. This gives one cleanup path and allows undo within a day. Deleting a lesson or module detaches its files in the same transaction before the cascade. Otherwise they would keep a dangling contextId and never be purged. |\n| D6 Audit (FR-46) | The PRD schema has no creator field and we keep it exactly as specified (FR-15). Rule: **every content or file mutation by an ADMIN** (who is not the course's `teacherId`/`coTeacherIds`) and every deletion of a file whose owner is not the actor writes `audit()`. |\n| D7 SVG | Allowed only when `context==='logo'`. It must have no sniffed signature and contain `<svg` in the head. It is served with `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'` (FR-41). |\n\n### 1.3 Schema note\n\nThe PRD names the ordering column **`order`** (not `position`). Every ordering in this document uses `order`. Additive indexes `@@index([courseId, order])` on Module and `@@index([moduleId, order])` on Lesson (NFR-4) are the only additions to the PRD's block, along with the back-relations Prisma requires (`Course.modules`, `User.files`, `FileObject.lessonAttachments`). `LessonProgress.studentId` stays a plain String as specified, and the service only writes ids of ACTIVE-enrolled students.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration `add_files_and_content` (FR-1, FR-15)\n\n- `FileObject` exactly as specified (FR-1). `context` is a String, so later PRDs add contexts without a migration.\n- `enum ContentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }`, plus `Module`, `Lesson`, `LessonAttachment`, `LessonLink` and `LessonProgress` exactly as specified (FR-15). Cascade path: Course → Module → Lesson → Attachment/Link/Progress.\n- `LessonAttachment.file` has no cascade, which means Restrict. A file can't be hard-deleted while it is a LessonAttachment, and that backs up the FR-11 `contextId===null` check at the database level.\n- Seed (FR-47): extend `prisma/seed.ts` and add `prisma/seed-assets/fractions-worksheet.pdf`, which is copied through `saveFile()` so the stored row has a real sha256 and storageKey.\n\n### 2.2 File storage: `src/server/storage.ts`, `src/server/files/*`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/storage.ts` | `saveFile(stream, { ext })` → `{ storageKey, sizeBytes, sha256 }`. It writes to `UPLOAD_DIR/.tmp/<cuid>` while hashing and counting bytes, then `rename`s to `<yyyy>/<mm>/<cuid>.<ext>`. `readFile(key)` returns a Node `Readable`. `deleteFile(key)` ignores ENOENT. `resolveKey()` asserts the resolved path stays under `path.resolve(UPLOAD_DIR)` (traversal guard). Single implementation with no interface. | FR-2, NFR-5, NFR-11 |\n| `src/lib/env.ts` (edit) | Add `UPLOAD_DIR` (default `./uploads`) and `MAX_UPLOAD_MB` (coerce int, default 25). Document both in `.env.example`. | FR-2, FR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `src/server/files/validate.ts` | Pure functions. `sanitizeFilename(name)` strips `/`, `\\` and `\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f`, trims, and caps at 150 characters while keeping the extension. `ALLOWED` is the ext → `{ mime, sniff }` table. `checkType(ext, sniffed, context, head)` returns `{ ok, mime } \\| { error }`. `maxBytesFor(context)` returns 2 MB for `logo`, otherwise `MAX_UPLOAD_MB`. The logo context allows png/jpg/jpeg/webp/svg only. | FR-4–FR-7, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/files/access.ts` | `registerFileAccess(context, resolver)` and `canAccessFile(user \\| null, file)`. Dispatch order: (1) unattached file (`contextId===null`): owner or ADMIN only. (2) A registered resolver gets `(user, file)`. (3) An unknown context allows owner or ADMIN. An anonymous user is denied in every case except a resolver that explicitly accepts null. | FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | Side-effect module that registers `lesson` and `logo`. `lesson`: load the lesson and its module and course, run `assertCanViewCourse` (catch the error and return false), and for STUDENT/PARENT also require `isLessonVisible`. `logo`: `() => true`. It is imported **by `access.ts` itself** at the bottom, so any caller of `canAccessFile` gets the registrations and no handler can forget the import. | FR-10, FR-18 |\n| `src/server/files/files-service.ts` | `uploadFile(user, req)`: busboy pipeline. The `context` field must arrive before the file part. Peek the first 4100 bytes, run `fileTypeFromBuffer` and `checkType`, then stream to `saveFile`, and create the FileObject with `contextId=null`. `getFileForDownload(user, id)`: `findUnique`, then `canAccessFile`, and throws `NOT_FOUND` when denied, before any bytes are read. `deleteUnattachedFile(user, id)`: owner/ADMIN, contextId null, otherwise CONFLICT. Deletes the row, then the bytes, and audits when owner ≠ actor. `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, context, contextId)` and `detachFiles(tx, ids)` are shared by the content service and the settings service. | FR-3, FR-8, FR-11, FR-17, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/purge.ts` | `purgeOrphanFiles(now)`: `findMany({ contextId: null, createdAt < now-24h }, take 500)`. For each file, `deleteFile`, then `deleteMany` the rows. Logs a count with `logger`. | FR-12 |\n\n**Upload pipeline (NFR-5):** `rateLimit('upload:'+userId, 60, 3_600_000)` runs first and returns 429 `RATE_LIMITED` with `Retry-After` (NFR-3). Next, an early reject happens if `Content-Length` is more than `maxBytes + 64 KB`. Then busboy runs with `limits.fileSize = maxBytes`. busboy's `'limit'` event destroys the stream, `saveFile` unlinks the tmp file, and the server returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File exceeds 25 MB.\"` (the number comes from config). A sniff failure also aborts before rename and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR \"File type .<ext> is not allowed.\"`. No path ever buffers more than the 4100-byte head in memory.\n\n**Download headers (FR-8, FR-41):** `Content-Type` is the stored mime. The response also sends `Content-Length`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename*=UTF-8''<enc>`. The disposition is `inline` only when `?inline=1` and the mime is `image/*` or `application/pdf`. For `image/svg+xml` the response adds `Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'`. `Cache-Control: private, no-store` is sent for everything except `logo`, which gets `public, max-age=3600`. All handlers use `runtime='nodejs'`.\n\n### 2.3 Content: `src/server/content/*`, `src/lib/validators/content.ts`, `src/lib/video.ts`\n\n| Module | Responsibility | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/content/visibility.ts` | Pure functions. `isVisible({status, publishAt}, now)` returns true for PUBLISHED, or for SCHEDULED with `publishAt <= now`. `isLessonVisible(lesson, module, now)` requires both to be visible. `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` is true for ADMIN and for the course's teacher or co-teacher. This is the single source of truth for list, get, prev/next, file access, progress and learning. | FR-18, FR-19, FR-44 |\n| `src/lib/video.ts` | `parseVideoUrl(url)` returns `{ provider: 'youtube'\\|'vimeo', id } \\| null` for `youtube.com/watch?v=`, `youtu.be/` and `vimeo.com/<id>`. `embedUrl(parsed)` returns the `youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>` or `player.vimeo.com/video/<id>` URL. Shared by the client and the server. | FR-30 |\n| `src/lib/validators/content.ts` | Zod schemas. `moduleCreate/Update` (title ≤120, description, status, publishAt). `lessonCreate/Update` (title ≤150, contentMarkdown ≤100 000, estimatedMinutes 1–600, videoUrl refined with `parseVideoUrl`, `attachments: [{fileId}]`, `links: [{title, url (http/https only)}]`, status, publishAt). `reorder` (`{ modules: [{ id, lessonIds[] }] }`). `progress` (`{ completed: boolean }`). A `SCHEDULED` status requires `publishAt > now` (FR-28). | FR-16, FR-23, FR-27, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `src/server/content/content-service.ts` | All content logic. Route handlers stay thin (FR-45). See the function list below. | FR-17–FR-24, FR-27, FR-32–FR-35, FR-38, FR-43–FR-46 |\n\n`content-service.ts` functions (each starts with the listed access check):\n\n- `listCourseContent(user, courseId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. It runs **2 queries**: one `module.findMany({ courseId, orderBy: order, include: { lessons: { orderBy: order, select: …, _count: { attachments } } } })`, plus one `lessonProgress.findMany({ studentId: user.id, lessonId in … })` when the caller is a STUDENT. For non-managers it filters in TypeScript with `isLessonVisible`. It returns modules with lessons, `attachmentCount`, the caller's `progress`, and the student's per-module/course counts plus `continueLessonId` (the first visible lesson without `completedAt`). This covers FR-20, FR-21, FR-43 and NFR-4.\n- `createModule` and `updateModule` use `assertCanManageCourse`. A new module gets `order = max+1`. `updateModule` handles the menu actions publish now (PUBLISHED), schedule (SCHEDULED + publishAt), unpublish (DRAFT) and edit. When a module becomes visible through publish now, its already-PUBLISHED lessons do **not** notify. Only the lesson-level publish-now path notifies (FR-38).\n- `deleteModule` uses manage. Inside a transaction it first detaches every file with `context='lesson'` and a `contextId` in the module's lessons, then deletes the module, and the cascade removes the rest (D5). The type-the-title confirmation is client-side only (FR-24). The server deletes regardless.\n- `reorderContent(user, courseId, tree)` uses manage. It validates that the submitted module-id set equals the course's module set and that the lesson-id set equals the course's lesson set, each with no duplicates, and returns `VALIDATION_ERROR` otherwise. Then one `$transaction` rewrites `order` for every module, and `moduleId` and `order` for every lesson (FR-23, ADR-7). The up/down moves in the module menu also go through this function.\n- `createLesson(user, moduleId, input)` uses manage. It appends with `order = max+1` and starts as DRAFT.\n- `getLesson(user, lessonId)` uses `assertCanViewCourse`. If the caller can't see drafts and the lesson is not visible, it throws `NOT_FOUND`, which hides existence (FR-44). The payload includes the lesson with attachments (FileObject summaries), links, `embedUrl`, and the prev/next lesson ids computed over the course's ordered list of lessons visible to the caller (one extra `findMany` of `id, order, status, publishAt` for the course). For an ACTIVE-enrolled STUDENT it upserts `LessonProgress` with `create: { firstViewedAt: now }, update: {}` (FR-32, FR-33).\n- `updateLesson(user, lessonId, input)` uses manage. In one transaction it updates the scalar fields. When `attachments` is present it replaces all of them: it computes the old and new fileId sets, calls `attachFiles` for the new ones (eligible if `ownerId===user.id` or the user is ADMIN, and `contextId` is null or already equals this lessonId, otherwise `VALIDATION_ERROR`), calls `detachFiles` for the removed ones, then runs `deleteMany` and `createMany` on LessonAttachment with `order` = array index. When `links` is present it replaces all of them in the same way. When `contentMarkdown` is present it attaches and detaches the inline image refs (D3). After commit, if the status went from not-visible to visible via `PUBLISHED` and the module is visible, it calls `notifyLessonPublished` (FR-17, FR-27, FR-38). Autosave sends the same PATCH without `status` (FR-29).\n- `deleteLesson` uses manage. It detaches the lesson's files and then deletes the lesson (D5).\n- `setLessonProgress(user, lessonId, completed)` requires `user.role==='STUDENT'` with an ACTIVE Enrollment in the course, and returns `FORBIDDEN` otherwise, which also blocks PARENT (FR-36). The lesson must be visible, otherwise `NOT_FOUND`. It upserts and sets `completedAt` to now or null (FR-33).\n- `listLessonProgress(user, lessonId)` uses manage. It loads the ACTIVE enrollments with the student user, plus `lessonProgress.findMany({ lessonId })`, and merges them in memory. Two queries (FR-34).\n- `getStudentLearning(user, studentId)` uses `assertCanViewStudent`. It loads the student's ACTIVE enrollments with the course, then all modules and lessons for those courses (one query with a `select` of status, publishAt and order), then the student's LessonProgress rows for those lessons. That is 3 queries, aggregated per course in memory: visible count, completed count, percentage, and last activity = max(firstViewedAt, completedAt) (FR-35).\n- `notifyLessonPublished(lesson, course)` loads the ACTIVE enrolled studentIds and calls `notify()` with type `content.lesson_published` (category ACADEMIC, `defaultEmail: false`), linking to `/courses/<courseId>/lessons/<lessonId>`. Scheduled lessons never reach this path (FR-38, FR-39).\n- Audit: every mutation above calls `audit({ actorId, action: 'content.<entity>.<verb>', entityId, … })` when `user.role==='ADMIN'` and the user is not on the course's teaching staff (D6, FR-46).\n\n### 2.4 Reused brownfield pieces (no duplicates, NFR-9)\n\n| Existing | Used for |\n|---|---|\n| `requireUser`, `getCurrentUser`, `requirePageUser`, `requirePageRole` (`src/server/auth/requireRole.ts`) | All routes and pages. GET `/api/files/:id` uses the nullable `getCurrentUser`. |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` (`course-access.ts`) | Every content handler and page, plus the `lesson` file resolver. The PARENT branch is reused unchanged (FR-37). |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` (`student-access.ts`) | `GET /api/students/:id/learning` and the Learning tab. |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `apiError`, `AppError`, `parseBody` (`src/server/http.ts`) | Response and error envelope for all 15 endpoints. The error codes already exist: VALIDATION_ERROR, NOT_FOUND, CONFLICT, RATE_LIMITED, UNAUTHENTICATED, FORBIDDEN. |\n| `rateLimit` (`src/server/rate-limit.ts`) | NFR-3. |\n| `audit` (`src/server/audit.ts`), `notify` + `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | FR-46, FR-38. |\n| `formatInSchoolTz` (`src/lib/dates.ts`), `date-fns-tz` `fromZonedTime` | NFR-10 display and schedule input. |\n| `logger` (`src/lib/logger.ts`) | NFR-12. |\n| `courseTabs`/`studentTabs` registries (`src/config/`) | FR-20, FR-35. |\n| `updateSchoolSettings` (`src/server/services/settings.ts`), `PATCH /api/settings/school` | FR-40, FR-42. Extended to take an optional `logoFileId`. The service attaches or detaches the file and writes `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` (D2). |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `Toast/useToast`, `FormField` (DateTimePicker) | UI. FR-24's type-to-confirm needs a text field, which ConfirmDialog lacks. Add an optional `confirmText?: string` prop to ConfirmDialog. Confirm stays disabled until the typed value matches. This is additive and backwards compatible. |\n\n### 2.5 API layer: route handlers (thin: Zod → service → `ok()`)\n\n| File | Methods | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/api/files/route.ts` | POST | FR-3–FR-7, NFR-3, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/files/[id]/route.ts` | GET, DELETE | FR-8–FR-11, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/modules/route.ts` | GET, POST | FR-43, FR-20–FR-22 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | FR-22, FR-24, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/modules/[id]/lessons/route.ts` | POST | FR-22, FR-43 |\n| `src/app/api/courses/[id]/content/reorder/route.ts` | POST | FR-23 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/route.ts` | GET, PATCH, DELETE | FR-25–FR-30, FR-43, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/lessons/[id]/progress/route.ts` | POST, GET | FR-33, FR-34 |\n| `src/app/api/students/[id]/learning/route.ts` | GET | FR-35 |\n\nThat is 15 endpoints in total, matching the PRD API table. The exact shapes are owned by `arch-api-contracts`.\n\n### 2.6 UI layer (MUI only, every component looked up via mui-mcp first, NFR-7)\n\n| File | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/components/FileUpload/FileUpload.tsx` | Client component. A `Paper` drop zone (dashed border via `sx`) and `Button component=\"label\"` with a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">`. Uses XHR `upload.onprogress` to drive a per-file `LinearProgress`. Appends `context` **before** `file` in the FormData (ADR-2). Shows a `List` with name, size, type icon and a remove `IconButton`. Removing a file before save calls `DELETE /api/files/:id`. Props: `context`, `accept`, `maxSizeMb`, `multiple`, `value`, `onChange`, `reorderable` (up/down IconButtons, used in FR-27). | FR-13, NFR-6 |\n| `src/components/FileList/FileList.tsx` | Read-only `List` with links to `/api/files/:id`. | FR-14 |\n| `src/components/MarkdownView/MarkdownView.tsx` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize. The schema is the default plus `img` restricted to `/`-relative `src`. The `components` map renders Typography, Link, List/ListItem, Table*, Divider and `Box component=\"pre\"`. External links get `target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`, and the `a` mapper also drops any non-http(s)/relative href. It has no hooks, so it renders both on the server and in the editor Preview. | FR-31, NFR-2 |\n| `src/components/content/StatusChip.tsx` | `Chip`: Draft is `default`, Scheduled is `info` with a formatted date in the school timezone, Published is `success`. | FR-19, NFR-10 |\n| `src/components/content/VideoEmbed.tsx` | A 16:9 `Box` (`aspectRatio: '16/9'`) containing an `iframe` with a `title` attribute and the `embedUrl`. | FR-30, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/content/…` registered as `courseTabs` entry `content` | A server component calls `listCourseContent` directly (no HTTP round-trip). The client `ContentOutline` shows module `Accordion`s, lesson `List`s, a check icon for students, per-module and course `LinearProgress` with the \"3 of 5 complete\" label, and a Continue `Button`. Teacher mode adds Add module/Add lesson, a module `Menu` (edit, publish now, schedule, unpublish, delete, move up/down), dnd-kit `DndContext` with a `SortableContext` per module and drag handles, up/down IconButtons with aria-labels, and the type-to-confirm delete. | FR-19–FR-24, NFR-4, NFR-6 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/edit/page.tsx` + `LessonEditor.tsx` | The page does `requirePageUser` + `assertCanManageCourse`. The editor has fields for title, estimated minutes and video URL. The Markdown editor has `Tabs` Write/Preview, a multiline `TextField`, and a toolbar (`ToggleButtonGroup`/`IconButton`s) for bold, italic, headings, lists, link, code, quote, table and image that inserts at the selection. Image insert opens FileUpload with `context='lesson'` and inserts `![alt](/api/files/<id>?inline=1)`. An `Alert` warns when any image has empty alt text. The attachments section uses FileUpload (reorderable), and the links section has title + URL rows. The status bar has Save draft, Publish now, and Schedule (`DateTimePicker`, school timezone → UTC, future only, with the `Tooltip` \"Scheduled lessons appear automatically without a notification.\"). Autosave runs every 10 s when dirty and shows \"Saved HH:mm\". `beforeunload` plus a link-click guard warn when there are unsaved changes. | FR-25–FR-29, FR-39, NFR-6, NFR-10 |\n| `src/app/(app)/courses/[courseId]/lessons/[lessonId]/page.tsx` | Calls `getLesson`, which handles visibility and the first-view upsert. Shows VideoEmbed, MarkdownView, FileList, links, estimated time and Previous/Next. Students get a \"Mark as complete\" `Button` that POSTs progress. Parents get no button (FR-36). Managers get a \"Progress\" `Drawer` that fetches `GET /api/lessons/:id/progress` and shows a list of students with Viewed/Completed and dates. | FR-32–FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `studentTabs` entry `learning` | A server component calls `getStudentLearning`. It shows a `Table` with course, completed/visible, a `LinearProgress` percentage, and last activity. | FR-35 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/settings/school/page.tsx` + nav entry in `src/config/navigation.ts` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. A minimal form for the existing settings fields, plus the logo FileUpload (single file, png/jpg/webp/svg, 2 MB, `context='logo'`). Saves through `PATCH /api/settings/school` with `logoFileId`. | FR-40–FR-42 |\n\n### 2.7 Config and infrastructure edits\n\n- `src/config/public-routes.ts`: add `'/api/files/'` (D1).\n- `next.config.js` CSP: add `frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com` (ADR-5).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: add `content.lesson_published` (ACADEMIC, email off).\n- `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`: call `purgeOrphanFiles(new Date())` in the daily block.\n- `src/server/email/…/BaseLayout.tsx`: when `logoUrl` starts with `/`, render `appUrl + logoUrl` (B4).\n- Root `.gitignore` and `.env.example` (blockers 7, NFR-12).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Upload → attach → download (FR-3, FR-17, FR-8)\n```\nFileUpload (XHR, context first) ──POST /api/files──► requireUser ─► rateLimit ─► busboy\n   ─► head 4100B ─► fileTypeFromBuffer + checkType(ext, sniff, context) ─► sha256+count tap ─► saveFile(tmp→rename)\n   ─► FileObject{contextId:null} ─► 201 {id, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes}\nLessonEditor save ──PATCH /api/lessons/:id {attachments:[{fileId}], contentMarkdown}──► assertCanManageCourse\n   ─► $transaction: attachFiles(new) / detachFiles(removed) / replace LessonAttachment+LessonLink / inline-image attach\nViewer/FileList ──GET /api/files/:id[?inline=1]──► getCurrentUser (nullable) ─► canAccessFile\n   ├─ contextId null → owner|ADMIN       ├─ 'lesson' → assertCanViewCourse + isLessonVisible (non-managers)\n   ├─ 'logo' → true (anonymous OK)        └─ unknown → owner|ADMIN\n   denied → 404 (no bytes read) · allowed → readFile stream + headers (nosniff, disposition, SVG CSP)\n```\n\n### 3.2 Visibility at read time (FR-18, FR-44)\n```\nrequest ─► assertCanViewCourse ─► load modules+lessons (1 query) ─► canSeeDrafts(user, course)?\n   yes → all items + StatusChip      no → keep lesson iff isVisible(module) && isVisible(lesson) at now\n```\nNo job runs at `publishAt`. The next read simply includes the item, and no notification is sent (FR-39).\n\n### 3.3 Publish now → notification (FR-38)\n`PATCH /api/lessons/:id {status:'PUBLISHED'}` → commit → if the lesson was not visible before, is visible now, and its module is visible → `notify()` each ACTIVE enrolled student with `content.lesson_published`.\n\n### 3.4 Student progress (FR-21, FR-33, FR-35)\nViewer load upserts `firstViewedAt` → \"Mark as complete\" `POST /api/lessons/:id/progress` sets or clears `completedAt` → the Content tab recomputes per-module and course counts plus Continue over **visible** lessons only → the Learning tab aggregates per ACTIVE course.\n\n### 3.5 Reorder (FR-23)\ndnd-kit `onDragOver`/`onDragEnd` or the up/down IconButtons change the client tree optimistically → `POST /api/courses/:id/content/reorder {modules:[{id, lessonIds}]}` → set-equality validation → one transaction rewrites `order` and `moduleId` → on error, revert to the server state and show a toast.\n\n### 3.6 Orphan purge (FR-12)\nThe email dispatcher tick runs. If 24 h have passed since `lastPurgeAt`, it runs `purgeOldNotifications()` and `purgeOrphanFiles()`, which removes files with contextId null older than 24 h (bytes, then rows, batch 500). The files it catches are abandoned uploads, detached attachments, removed inline images, and replaced logos.\n\n### 3.7 Logo (FR-40–FR-42)\nThe admin settings page uploads with FileUpload `context='logo'` (2 MB, png/jpg/webp/svg) → `PATCH /api/settings/school {logoFileId}` → `updateSchoolSettings` attaches the new file (`contextId='singleton'`), detaches the old one, and sets `logoUrl='/api/files/<id>'` → the app shell, the login page and emails (`appUrl`-prefixed) fetch it anonymously through the `logo` resolver.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Security Boundaries (NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-8)\n\n- Bytes live only in `UPLOAD_DIR` (outside `public/`) and are reached only through `GET /api/files/:id` → `canAccessFile`. Storage keys are generated server-side, and `resolveKey` guards against traversal.\n- `/api/files/` is public at the middleware level, so POST and DELETE call `requireUser()` explicitly. Integration tests cover anonymous POST (401), anonymous lesson-file GET (404) and anonymous logo GET (200).\n- Denials on hidden content return 404, not 403, for both lessons and files (FR-44, FR-9).\n- The type check is server-side (extension + magic number). The stored mime comes from the allowlist table and never from the client. Every download sends nosniff. SVG is limited to logo and gets a sandboxing CSP.\n- Markdown goes through rehype-sanitize, images are same-origin only, and the `a` mapper drops non-http(s) hrefs.\n- Every page and handler calls an assert helper. Hidden buttons are cosmetic only.\n- `rateLimit` is per-process. That ceiling is already noted in rate-limit.ts.\n\n## 5. Testing Strategy (FR-48)\n\n- Unit (Vitest): `sanitizeFilename`, `parseVideoUrl`/`embedUrl`, `isVisible`/`isLessonVisible` (including the SCHEDULED past/future boundary), `canAccessFile` dispatch (unattached, registered, unknown, anonymous), `checkType` (exe renamed to .pdf, ELF renamed to .csv, docx-as-zip, svg outside logo), and the MarkdownView sanitiser (`<script>`, `javascript:`, off-origin img).\n- Integration (`// @vitest-environment node`, temp `UPLOAD_DIR`): upload → attach via PATCH → download as student (200), as an unenrolled student (404) and anonymous (404). Oversize → 400. Rate limit → 429. `purgeOrphanFiles` deletes old unattached files and keeps attached ones and the logo.\n- E2E (Playwright): a teacher creates a module and lesson with an attachment and publishes it, then a student sees it, downloads the attachment, marks it complete, and the progress bar updates. The seeded YouTube iframe is not CSP-blocked.\n- Gate: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` (NFR-9). QA greps for banned UI imports (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 `FileObject` model, migration `add_files_and_content` |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 `src/server/storage.ts`, `env.ts` UPLOAD_DIR |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `files-service.uploadFile`, §2.5 `POST /api/files`, §3.1 |\n| FR-4 | §2.2 `maxBytesFor`, busboy `fileSize` limit, Content-Length pre-check |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `validate.ts` ALLOWED table + `fileTypeFromBuffer` |\n| FR-6 | §2.2 `checkType` sniff modes (none / zip-or-ooxml / required) |\n| FR-7 | §2.2 `sanitizeFilename` |\n| FR-8 | §2.2 download headers, §2.5 `GET /api/files/:id` |\n| FR-9 | §2.2 `files/access.ts` registry + dispatch order |\n| FR-10 | §2.2 `files/contexts.ts` lesson + logo resolvers |\n| FR-11 | §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile`, §2.1 Restrict FK |\n| FR-12 | §2.2 `files/purge.ts`, §2.7 dispatcher hook, §3.6 |\n| FR-13 | §2.6 `FileUpload` |\n| FR-14 | §2.6 `FileList` |\n| FR-15 | §2.1 ContentStatus + Module/Lesson/LessonAttachment/LessonLink/LessonProgress, §1.3 |\n| FR-16 | §2.3 `validators/content.ts` |\n| FR-17 | §2.2 `attachFiles` eligibility, §2.3 `updateLesson` |\n| FR-18 | §2.3 `visibility.ts`, §3.2 |\n| FR-19 | §2.3 `canSeeDrafts`, §2.6 `StatusChip` |\n| FR-20 | §2.6 `content` course tab, §2.3 `listCourseContent` |\n| FR-21 | §2.3 `listCourseContent` counts + `continueLessonId`, §2.6 progress bars |\n| FR-22 | §2.3 `createModule`/`updateModule`/`createLesson`, §2.6 module Menu |\n| FR-23 | §2.3 `reorderContent`, §2.6 dnd-kit, §3.5 |\n| FR-24 | §2.4 ConfirmDialog `confirmText`, §2.3 `deleteModule` |\n| FR-25 | §2.6 lesson editor page + Markdown editor |\n| FR-26 | §2.6 image insert, §1.2 D3 inline-image attach |\n| FR-27 | §2.6 attachments/links sections, §2.3 `updateLesson` replace-all |\n| FR-28 | §2.6 Schedule DateTimePicker, §2.3 Zod future check |\n| FR-29 | §2.6 autosave + unsaved-changes guard |\n| FR-30 | §2.3 `src/lib/video.ts`, §2.6 `VideoEmbed`, §2.7 CSP frame-src |\n| FR-31 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` |\n| FR-32 | §2.6 lesson viewer, §2.3 `getLesson` prev/next |\n| FR-33 | §2.3 `getLesson` first-view upsert + `setLessonProgress` |\n| FR-34 | §2.3 `listLessonProgress`, §2.6 Progress Drawer |\n| FR-35 | §2.3 `getStudentLearning`, §2.6 `learning` student tab |\n| FR-36 | §2.3 `setLessonProgress` STUDENT-only, §2.6 viewer hides the button |\n| FR-37 | §2.4 `assertCanViewCourse` reused unchanged |\n| FR-38 | §2.3 `notifyLessonPublished`, §2.7 NOTIFICATION_TYPES, §3.3 |\n| FR-39 | §3.2 no job, §2.6 Schedule tooltip |\n| FR-40 | §2.6 admin settings logo FileUpload, §2.4 `updateSchoolSettings` + logoFileId, §3.7 |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 SVG logo-only + CSP header, §1.2 D7 |\n| FR-42 | §2.6 `/admin/settings/school` page + nav entry |\n| FR-43 | §2.5 route table (15 endpoints), §2.3 service functions |\n| FR-44 | §2.3 `getLesson` NOT_FOUND for hidden lessons |\n| FR-45 | §2.3 `content-service.ts`, §2.2 `src/server/files/`, thin handlers §2.5 |\n| FR-46 | §1.2 D6, §2.3 audit rule, §2.2 `deleteUnattachedFile` audit |\n| FR-47 | §2.1 seed + `prisma/seed-assets/` |\n| FR-48 | §5 Testing Strategy |\n| NFR-1 | §2.2 storage outside public + registry, §4 |\n| NFR-2 | §2.6 `MarkdownView` sanitize + `a` mapper, §4 |\n| NFR-3 | §2.2 upload pipeline `rateLimit` |\n| NFR-4 | §2.3 2-query `listCourseContent`, §1.3 order indexes |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 busboy streaming + hash/count tap + tmp→rename |\n| NFR-6 | §2.6 iframe title, alt-text Alert, up/down IconButtons |\n| NFR-7 | §1.1 blocker 8, §2.6 MUI-only + mui-mcp lookup |\n| NFR-8 | §2.3 per-function access checks, §1.2 D1, §4 |\n| NFR-9 | §2.4 reuse table, ADR-1 deps, §5 gate |\n| NFR-10 | §2.6 StatusChip/Schedule school timezone, `formatInSchoolTz`, `fromZonedTime` |\n| NFR-11 | §1 single local-disk storage, no abstraction |\n| NFR-12 | §2.2 `logger`, §2.7 `.env.example` |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MwXWtuFqrra4hf9AyNk5Wz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
