{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgroYYaYNUYwbNSGEKEYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-9 (status: complete). The file that was there was left over from SH-8, so I replaced it. Every requirement id it cites exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**What the design adds:**\n- **Database:** one migration, `add_assignments`. It adds the three enums and eight models, with only back-relations added to existing models.\n- **Server code:** `src/server/assignments/` holds three files:\n  - `assignments-service.ts` for all the database logic.\n  - `grading-math.ts` for the score and late-day maths, with no database access so it can be unit-tested and reused by the grading form's live preview.\n  - `reminders.ts`, which the existing email dispatcher calls on every run.\n- **Validation:** all form and request checks live in one shared file, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`.\n- **API and pages:** 14 thin route handlers and 6 pages.\n- **Missing PRD-08 components:** I added the four that SH-9 needs (`MarkdownView`, `MarkdownEditor`, `FileUpload`, `FileList`).\n- No new dependencies, background jobs or queues.\n\n**Intake's 8 blockers** are listed in the Overview with how each is resolved, following ADR-2 to ADR-5 in the stack decisions.\n\n**Something intake missed:** `next.config.js` sends `X-Frame-Options: DENY` on every path. That blocks the PDF preview the grading screen needs (FR-29), because it shows PDFs in an iframe. I proposed relaxing it to `SAMEORIGIN` for `/api/files/:id` only (decision D11). This is a security-header change, so it needs a reviewer to approve it. If you'd rather not change the header, the alternative is an \"Open\" link for PDFs; images still preview either way.\n\n**Decisions `arch-api-contracts` must follow:**\n- Score values are sent as strings in API responses, never as JSON numbers.\n- \"Save & return\" is a single call: `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade` with `return: true`.\n- When an assignment has a rubric, the server sets the raw score to the sum of the rubric points.\n- Students and parents never get score, feedback or rubric fields until the work is returned.\n\n**Still open:**\n- The `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 pin still has to be confirmed to compile. If it doesn't, the design falls back to a plain MUI table and a native date-time input.\n- The site-wide CSP fix for real-browser loading is out of scope; the end-to-end test bypasses CSP instead.\n- The student Assignments tab works by direct URL but won't show up, because student pages have no tab bar yet.\n- The dev phase can't start UI work unless mui-mcp is reachable.\n\n`api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` are still from SH-7. I didn't touch them; the `arch-api-contracts` sub-task overwrites them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":259,"cache_read_input_tokens":86872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":259},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a7b6583-29f5-43b3-9f4e-72722e4e3a4f","uuid":"4eac694d-2254-41a7-a48e-1eac0bb60ba8","timestamp":"2026-11-09T05:29:31.400Z","request_id":"req_011CgroYYN9Nr22odqeCah2Q"}
