{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgrvmrgu9HmrLSdALNXp3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012Bk8pTEdwsgWRYhDNnXCzy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-10 · PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010)\n\nTicket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:45:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 FR + 10 NFR, 96%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (no blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B15, D1–D5), PRD `10-quizzes.md` FR-1 schema.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-10 adds teacher-built quizzes to courses: students take timed, autosaved attempts, the server grades them automatically where it can, teachers grade essays and flagged short answers by hand, and results are released according to a per-quiz visibility rule. The feature is a new vertical slice in the existing Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/Postgres app. It follows the PRD-09 assignments layout exactly:\n\n- `src/server/quiz/` holds the domain logic\n- `src/app/api/...` holds thin route handlers\n- `src/app/(app)/...` holds server pages with MUI client components\n\nThere is no new infrastructure and no new dependency (ADR-1). All background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher (ADR-6).\n\n**Design principles**\n1. **The server owns time and truth.** `deadlineAt` is frozen at start and checked only on the server. The client timer is display-only (FR-13, FR-16, ADR-4).\n2. **One path per state transition.** Manual submit, the deadline rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call a single `submitAttempt()`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` guard makes it idempotent (FR-17, FR-18, FR-35).\n3. **One visibility predicate.** `resultsVisible()` gates scores, correct answers and parent access (FR-20, FR-21, NFR-1).\n4. **Allow-listed student output.** Students only ever receive output from `serializers.ts` (NFR-1, ADR-5).\n5. **Pure core, thin I/O shell.** Grading, deadline, scoring, shuffle and publish checks are pure and unit-tested (NFR-8, ADR-3).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`**. Nothing blocks design or dev.\n\n### 1.2 Assumptions carried forward (flagged by intake, resolved here)\n| # | Req | Assumption / decision |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-37 (LOW) | **No sidebar entry.** Quizzes are reached through the course \"Quizzes\" tab and direct routes. FR-37 produces no code. |\n| A2 | FR-11 | \"Missed\" means the quiz is past `availableUntil` and the student has zero attempts. |\n| A3 | FR-10 | Regrade runs only through the explicit `POST /regrade`. Editing accepted answers does not trigger an automatic regrade. |\n| A4 | FR-33 | Practice quizzes count toward attempts, analytics and the teacher list. They are excluded only from the gradebook: `getStudentQuizScore` returns `isPractice` and PRD-11 filters on it. |\n| A5 | FR-29, FR-30 | `quiz.published` has defaultEmail = false (PRD). `quiz.results_released` has defaultEmail = true, matching `assignment.graded`; the PRD doesn't say. |\n| A6 | FR-30 | **No new column.** The \"sent once\" marker for AFTER_CLOSE results is the existing `Quiz.resultsReleasedAt`, which the maintenance pass claims atomically for AFTER_CLOSE quizzes (§4.5). This keeps FR-1's model list exact. The research notes' `resultsNotifiedAt` and claim-table options are therefore not needed. |\n| A7 | FR-28 | Accommodation changes apply only to attempts started after the change, because `deadlineAt` is frozen at start. The settings UI says so. |\n| A8 | FR-17, FR-25 | FR-1 has no `flagged` or `manuallyGraded` column. Both are **derived**: an answer is *manually graded* when `gradedById != null`, and it *needs review* when it is an ESSAY with `gradedById = null`, or a SHORT_ANSWER with `isCorrect = false` and `gradedById = null`. A pure `needsReview()` implements this rule. |\n| A9 | FR-29 | Status transitions are **DRAFT → PUBLISHED → CLOSED** only. There is no unpublish, so `quiz.published` fires exactly once, on the conditional DRAFT→PUBLISHED update. |\n| A10 | FR-8 | Preview mode reuses the player with `mode=\"preview\"`. Saves and submit are no-ops, nothing is graded, and nothing is sent to attempt endpoints. |\n\n### 1.3 Scope fence (NFR-10)\nOut of scope: lockdown browser, webcam proctoring, question banks, random pools and LaTeX. Nothing in this design anticipates them.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1, FR-2)\n\nThe model is one migration, `prisma/migrations/20261110000000_add_quizzes/`, created with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and hand-edited (ADR-2). The fields are **exactly as in PRD FR-1**. This design adds only relations and indexes, never new columns:\n\n| Model | Additions beyond the PRD listing | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Quiz | `createdBy User @relation(\"QuizCreatedBy\")`; `@@index([courseId, status])` | FK integrity; course tab list (FR-11) |\n| Question | `answers QuizAnswer[]`; `@@index([quizId, order])` | ordered load (FR-7, FR-31) |\n| QuizAttempt | `@@index([quizId, status])`, `@@index([status, deadlineAt])` | teacher list/needs-grading count (FR-11); maintenance sweep (FR-18) |\n| QuizAnswer | `question Question @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `gradedBy User? @relation(\"QuizAnswerGradedBy\")` | FK integrity; grading audit (FR-24) |\n| QuizAccommodation | `quiz Quiz @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `student User @relation(...)`, plus `accommodations QuizAccommodation[]` on Quiz | FK integrity (FR-28) |\n| Course | `quizzes Quiz[]` | FR-1 back-relation |\n| User | `quizzesCreated`, `quizAttempts`, `quizAccommodations`, `quizAnswersGraded` | FR-1 back-relations |\n\n**Raw SQL appended to the migration (FR-19, ADR-2):**\n```sql\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\"\n  ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';\n```\nA `schema.prisma` comment on QuizAttempt points to it, following the attendance-migration precedent. `prisma db push` would drop it, so dev and CI must use `migrate`.\n\n**JSON shapes** follow the PRD FR-2 table and are typed by the Zod discriminated union in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`:\n- `options`: `[{id,text}]`. Option ids are short cuids generated client-side and stable across edits.\n- `correct` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}`, `{accepted}` or `{guidance?}`.\n- `response` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}` or `{text}`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Server domain: `src/server/quiz/` (NFR-7)\n\n| File | Kind | Exports | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `grading.ts` | **pure**, isomorphic, no Prisma client | `gradeAnswer(question, response) → {pointsAwarded: Decimal\\|null, isCorrect: boolean\\|null}`, `needsReview(question, answer)`, `normalizeShortAnswer(s)`, `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)`, `attemptLimit(maxAttempts, extraAttempts)`, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`, `canPublish(questions) → string[]`, `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)`, `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (string hash + mulberry32), `ANSWER_GRACE_MS = 30_000` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-9, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-28 |\n| `serializers.ts` | pure | `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt`, `toStudentResult`. They are built by explicit allow-list, never spread-then-delete. | NFR-1, FR-21, FR-11 |\n| `access.ts` | I/O | `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt, {write})`: the owner (write allowed), a manager via `assertCanManageCourse`, or a linked PARENT (read-only, and only when `resultsVisible`). Otherwise it throws NOT_FOUND. | FR-34, NFR-5 |\n| `quiz-service.ts` | I/O | `listCourseQuizzes(user, courseId, page)` (role-shaped), `createQuiz`, `getQuizForManager`, `getQuizForStudent`, `updateQuiz` (settings + status transition + publish check + FR-29 notify), `deleteQuiz` (CONFLICT if any attempt exists), `addQuestion`, `updateQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions` (all through the **edit lock**), `regradeQuiz`, `releaseResults`, `upsertAccommodation` | FR-6..FR-11, FR-20, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31, FR-38 |\n| `attempt-service.ts` | I/O | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `getAttempt` (calls `ensureNotExpired`), `saveAnswer` (hot path), `submitAttempt(attemptId, {auto})`, `ensureNotExpired(attempt)`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`, `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` | FR-12..FR-19, FR-22..FR-25, FR-32, FR-33, FR-38 |\n| `analytics.ts` | I/O + pure aggregation | `getQuizAnalytics(quizId)` returns summary stats, a 10-bucket histogram and per-question stats. `analyticsCsv(quizId)` uses `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts`. | FR-26, FR-27 |\n| `maintenance.ts` | I/O | `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`, `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |\n\nReused as-is: `dec`/`fixed2`/`Decimal` from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` (imported, not copied); `withHandler`/`ok`/`paginated`/`AppError` (`src/server/http.ts`); `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`); `notify`/`notifyStudentAndParents`; `audit`; `logger`; `toCsv`; `getSchoolTimezone` (NFR-7).\n\n**Edit lock (FR-10).** `quiz-service` checks `_count.attempts > 0` before every question mutation. When attempts exist:\n- `updateQuestion` accepts only `prompt`, `explanation`, and (for SHORT_ANSWER) `correct.accepted` / `caseSensitive`.\n- `addQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions`, and changes to `type`/`points`/options/choice `correct` throw `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Quiz has attempts — only text, explanation and accepted answers can change. Use Regrade after editing accepted answers.')`.\n- The same check sits behind the builder's disabled controls and their tooltip.\n\n**Regrade (FR-10, FR-38).** One `$transaction`:\n1. For every submitted attempt, re-run `gradeAnswer` on answers with `gradedById = null` (a manual grade always wins, per A8).\n2. `recomputeAttempt` each attempt.\n3. Write `audit('quiz.regrade', {attemptCount})`.\n\n`recomputeAttempt` (FR-25): sets `score = Σ pointsAwarded` (fixed2) and sets status to `NEEDS_GRADING` if any `needsReview`, otherwise `GRADED`. Only submitted attempts are touched.\n\n### 3.2 Validators: `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` (FR-2, NFR-6)\nThese are client-safe Zod schemas shared by the builder forms and the route handlers:\n- `quizSettingsSchema` uses `.superRefine`: `availableUntil > availableFrom`, and `timeLimitMinutes ≤ window minutes` (FR-6). Limits: timeLimit 1–300 or null, maxAttempts 1–10.\n- `questionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', …)`: points 0.5–100, 2–8 options, ≥1 correct option for MULTIPLE_CHOICE, 1–10 accepted answers, prompt as non-empty Markdown.\n- `answerResponseSchema` is a type-agnostic union, so the hot path doesn't load the Question (NFR-2). ESSAY/SHORT text is ≤ 10,000 characters.\n- `manualGradeSchema` is `{points: 0..∞ step 0.5, feedback?}`. The upper bound (question points) is checked in the service.\n- `accommodationSchema`: extraTime 0–300, extraAttempts 0–5.\n- `reorderSchema`: `{questionIds: string[]}`.\n\n### 3.3 API route handlers (FR-31, FR-32, NFR-5, NFR-6)\nEvery handler is `withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → Zod parse → one service call → `ok`/`paginated`. There is no logic in the handlers. `api-contracts.json` (the next sub-task) owns the exact shapes.\n\n| Route file | Methods | Access | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `api/courses/[id]/quizzes/route.ts` | GET (role-shaped, paginated), POST | view / manage | FR-11, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/route.ts` | GET (manager: full; student/parent: `toStudentQuiz`), PATCH, DELETE | view / manage | FR-6, FR-9, FR-29, FR-31, NFR-1 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-31 |\n| `api/questions/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/attempts/route.ts` | POST (start/resume) | STUDENT + view | FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-32 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/route.ts` | GET | owner / linked parent / manager | FR-18, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-1 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/route.ts` | PUT | owner | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/submit/route.ts` | POST | owner | FR-17 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/grade/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-24, FR-25, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/regrade/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-10, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/release-results/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-20, FR-30, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/analytics/route.ts` | GET (`?format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | FR-26, FR-27 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/accommodations/[studentId]/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-28, FR-38 |\n\nError mapping: CONFLICT (409) covers writing after the deadline, the edit lock, deleting with attempts, the attempt limit, and a quiz that isn't open. VALIDATION_ERROR (400) is for Zod failures. NOT_FOUND hides resources the user can't access (NFR-5, NFR-6).\n\n### 3.4 Pages and UI: `src/app/(app)/...` (NFR-4: MUI only, mui-mcp lookup before each component)\n\n| Route / file | Server/client | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/config/course-tabs.ts` | config | One entry, `{key:'quizzes', label:'Quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES}` | FR-11 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/page.tsx` + `CourseQuizzesView.tsx` | server + client | Teacher: DataTable (status, window, attempts, avg, Needs grading) + \"New quiz\". Student: four sections (Upcoming / Available now (Start/Resume) / Completed (score if visible) / Missed). Parent: completed results, read-only, per linked child. | FR-11, FR-33 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/new/page.tsx` | server | Creates a DRAFT quiz with defaults and redirects to edit (no separate form) | FR-6 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/page.tsx` + `QuizBuilder.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx`, `QuestionList.tsx`, `QuestionEditor.tsx` | server + client | Settings (DateTimePicker, Switch, Select, TextField). The question list is a dnd-kit `SortableContext` of MUI Cards, with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback. Each type has its own editor (options with a correct Radio/Checkbox, an accepted-answers list, guidance). A running points total. Publish button with `canPublish` errors. Lock banner + disabled controls when attempts exist, plus a Regrade button. Accommodations section (DataTable of enrolled students). The prompt uses MarkdownEditor + FileUpload with context `'quiz'`. | FR-6..FR-10, FR-28, FR-39, NFR-9 |\n| `quizzes/[quizId]/take/page.tsx` + `QuizPlayer.tsx`, `useAutosave.ts` | server + client | Start screen (instructions, counts, points, limit, attempts used/allowed, ConfirmDialog on Start). The player has a sticky header (title, mm:ss timer from `deadlineAt`, red under 2 min, `aria-live=\"assertive\"` announcing at 5:00 and 1:00), a Chip status pill, LinearProgress, and RadioGroup/FormGroup+Checkbox/TextField per type. Layout is all-on-one-page, or one question per page with a navigator Button grid (answered / unanswered / flagged; flags stored client-side only). Submit uses ConfirmDialog showing the unanswered count. `mode=\"preview\"` is used by the builder. | FR-8, FR-12..FR-17, FR-19, NFR-3 |\n| `quizzes/[quizId]/attempts/[attemptId]/page.tsx` | server | Result view built from `toStudentResult`: score, %, per-question correctness, response and feedback, plus correct answers/explanations if allowed. Otherwise it shows \"Submitted — results will be available later.\" Also used by parents and teachers. | FR-20, FR-21 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/grade/page.tsx` + `QuizGradingWorkspace.tsx` | server + client | Tabs: By student / By question. Points TextField (step 0.5, max = question points) + feedback, with override allowed on auto-graded answers. | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/analytics/page.tsx` + `QuizAnalytics.tsx` | server + client | StatCards (attempts, avg, median, high, low, avg time), x-charts `BarChart` with 10 buckets, a per-question DataTable with option distribution (most-chosen wrong option highlighted), and a CSV link | FR-26, FR-27 |\n\nServer pages call `requirePageRole` and the course/attempt access helpers before fetching (NFR-5). They pass only serializer output to client components (NFR-1).\n\n**`useAutosave(attemptId, mode)` (FR-15, ADR-4).**\n- Each question gets an 800 ms `setTimeout` debounce, then `PUT /answers/:questionId`.\n- On network failure or 5xx, the latest response per question is written to the `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` map, and a 5 s `setInterval` drains it.\n- A 409 stops the queue, clears storage and routes to the result page. A 2xx removes that key.\n- The status pill reads `Saving…`, `All answers saved`, or `Offline — answers saved on this device` (shown when the queue is non-empty).\n- On mount, any queued answers are merged over server answers before rendering, so a reload loses nothing (FR-19, AC-2).\n\n### 3.5 Integrations into existing modules\n\n| Existing file | Change | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT, defaultEmail false) and `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT + PARENT, defaultEmail true, A5) | FR-29, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | `register('quiz', quizResolver)`. The resolver allows a course manager, or a course viewer when the quiz is PUBLISHED (images sit only in prompts, which students already see) | FR-39, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | After `sendDueReminders(now)`, add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)`, each in its own try/catch + `logger.error`, on every call | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` | Three seed quizzes, idempotent by (courseId, title). Scores are computed with `grading.ts` | FR-36 |\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration | §2 | FR-1, FR-19 |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Build and publish (FR-6..FR-9, FR-29)\n1. Teacher opens New. The server creates a DRAFT quiz and redirects to `/edit`.\n2. Settings and question edits go through PATCH/POST. Each is Zod-validated on both client and server, and question mutations pass the edit-lock check.\n3. On Publish, the client sends `PATCH {status:'PUBLISHED'}`. The service runs `canPublish(questions)` and throws VALIDATION_ERROR with the list of problems if any. Otherwise it runs `updateMany({where:{id, status:'DRAFT'}, data:{status:'PUBLISHED'}})`.\n4. If that update changed a row (count = 1), the service calls `notify('quiz.published')` for ACTIVE enrollees after commit (A9).\n\n### 4.2 Start or resume (FR-12, FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-28)\n```\nPOST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts  (STUDENT)\n  assertCanViewCourse → quiz PUBLISHED && availableFrom ≤ now < availableUntil, else CONFLICT\n  existing IN_PROGRESS? → ensureNotExpired → still IN_PROGRESS ? return it (resume)\n  count(attempts) ≥ attemptLimit(maxAttempts, accommodation.extraAttempts) → CONFLICT\n  $transaction:\n    id = cuid()                         // generated up front so the shuffle seed is known\n    order = shuffleQuestions ? seededShuffle(questionIds, id) : questionIds by `order`\n    deadlineAt = computeDeadline(now, timeLimitMinutes, accommodation.extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)\n    create {id, attemptNumber: count+1, questionOrder: order, deadlineAt, maxScore: Σ points}\n  on P2002 (partial index or attemptNumber unique) → re-read IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it\n→ toStudentAttempt(attempt, questions with seededShuffle(options, attempt.id) if shuffleOptions)\n```\nOption order isn't stored. It is recomputed from the `attempt.id` seed on every load, which makes it deterministic (FR-13). Two tabs get the same attempt id (FR-19).\n\n### 4.3 Autosave hot path (FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2)\n```\nPUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId   body {response}\n  1 query : attempt {studentId, status, deadlineAt, questionOrder}     (no Quiz/Question load)\n  studentId ≠ user → NOT_FOUND;  questionId ∉ questionOrder → NOT_FOUND\n  status ≠ IN_PROGRESS → CONFLICT\n  now > deadlineAt + 30s → submitAttempt(id,{auto:true}); throw CONFLICT('Time is up')\n  1 query : quizAnswer.upsert({attemptId_questionId}, {response})\n→ { data: { questionId, savedAt } }      // no grading data (NFR-1)\n```\nThe path is two indexed statements, well under the 50 ms budget at 300 concurrent students. It is idempotent, so localStorage replays are safe.\n\n### 4.4 Submit, auto-submit and grading (FR-17, FR-18, FR-24, FR-25)\n```\nsubmitAttempt(attemptId, {auto}):   $transaction\n  claimed = updateMany({id, status:'IN_PROGRESS'} → {status:'SUBMITTED', submittedAt: now, autoSubmitted: auto})\n  claimed.count = 0 → return current attempt (already submitted: idempotent, race-safe)\n  load questions + answers; for every questionId in questionOrder:\n     answer missing → create {response:null}\n     {pointsAwarded,isCorrect} = gradeAnswer(question, response)     // ESSAY → null,null; unanswered → 0,false\n  recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)   → score = Σ, status = NEEDS_GRADING | GRADED\n```\nCallers:\n- the submit POST (`auto:false`)\n- the deadline branch of saveAnswer\n- `ensureNotExpired` on GET attempt, start/resume, the player page and the teacher grade/list loads (FR-18, lazy)\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` (FR-18, batch)\n\nAn unanswered ESSAY gets `pointsAwarded = 0` and still needs review: the A8 predicate keys on `gradedById`, so the teacher confirms it.\n\nManual grading:\n1. `PUT …/grade` validates `points ≤ question.points` and `points % 0.5 = 0`, then sets `pointsAwarded`, `isCorrect = points == question.points`, `feedback` and `gradedById`.\n2. It runs `recomputeAttempt`, which sets GRADED when nothing still needs review (FR-25), and writes `audit('quizAnswer.grade')` after commit (FR-38).\n3. If the attempt became GRADED and the quiz is IMMEDIATELY, nothing is sent (FR-30).\n\n### 4.5 Results visibility and notification (FR-20, FR-21, FR-30)\n`resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`:\n- the attempt must be submitted\n- **IMMEDIATELY**: true\n- **AFTER_CLOSE**: `now ≥ availableUntil`\n- **MANUAL**: `resultsReleasedAt != null`\n\nScores also need status GRADED to display a final score. A NEEDS_GRADING attempt shows \"awaiting grading\" for the pending questions.\n\n- **MANUAL release:** `POST /release-results` runs `updateMany({id, resultsVisibility:'MANUAL', resultsReleasedAt:null} → now)`. If count = 1, it calls `notifyStudentAndParents` for students with a submitted attempt, then `audit('quiz.release_results')`. A repeat call is a no-op.\n- **AFTER_CLOSE (maintenance):** `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` finds quizzes where `resultsVisibility = AFTER_CLOSE AND availableUntil ≤ now AND resultsReleasedAt IS NULL`. For each one it claims with `updateMany(... resultsReleasedAt: null → now)`, and only when count = 1 does it notify. That makes it idempotent across concurrent cron calls (A6, FR-35).\n- **IMMEDIATELY:** no notification.\n\n### 4.6 Maintenance (FR-18, FR-35)\n`autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` finds attempts with `status = IN_PROGRESS AND deadlineAt < now − 30s`, takes up to 200 per call, and runs `submitAttempt(id, {auto:true})` on each. The per-call cap keeps a cron tick bounded; the next tick and the lazy path cover any remainder.\n\n### 4.7 Score export to PRD-11 (FR-22, FR-33)\n`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` returns `{score, maxScore, percent, isPractice, attemptsCounted} | null`, computed by `applyScoringPolicy` over GRADED attempts only. HIGHEST takes the max percent, LATEST takes the latest `submittedAt`, AVERAGE takes the Decimal mean, all with fixed2. It returns null when there are no GRADED attempts. There is no endpoint; PRD-11 imports it.\n\n### 4.8 Analytics (FR-26, FR-27)\n- **Input:** submitted attempts with their answers, aggregated in memory (class sizes are small).\n- **Summary stats:** count, mean, median, max, min, and mean of `submittedAt − startedAt`.\n- **Histogram:** 10 buckets by percent, with 100% placed in the last bucket.\n- **Per question:** % with `isCorrect = true`, average `pointsAwarded`, and for choice types an option-id count, with the most-chosen wrong option marked.\n- **CSV:** `toCsv` rows of student, attemptNumber, score, then one points column per question in quiz order.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Security and access (NFR-1, NFR-5)\n\n| Actor | Can |\n|---|---|\n| ADMIN / course teacher | All manage routes for their courses, any attempt in those courses |\n| STUDENT (ACTIVE enrolled) | List and take PUBLISHED quizzes; read and write **own** attempts; results only via `toStudentResult` |\n| PARENT (linked to an enrolled student) | Read-only: completed results of linked children, only when `resultsVisible` |\n\n- Student-path Prisma queries never `select` `correct` or `explanation`. The serializers add those fields back only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers` (defence in depth).\n- The answer-PUT response carries no grading data.\n- Inaccessible ids return NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so their existence isn't revealed.\n- Test: a serializer unit test walks the output recursively and asserts no `correct` key exists before visibility (AC-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Testing map (NFR-8, ADR-8)\n\n| Level | Target | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit (Vitest, no DB) | `gradeAnswer` per type, incl. the FR-2 example ({A,B} → 0, {A} → 2) and `' Photosynthesis '`; `needsReview`; `computeDeadline` (timed, untimed, extra time, capped by availableUntil); `attemptLimit`; `applyScoringPolicy` ×3; `seededShuffle` determinism; `resultsVisible` ×3; `canPublish`; serializers (no `correct` key) | FR-3, FR-4, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| Integration (Vitest + test DB) | Autosave returns 409 after deadline + 30 s and the attempt is auto-submitted; GET auto-submits an expired attempt; regrade changes auto-graded answers but not manual ones; concurrent start returns one attempt; double submit is a no-op | FR-16, FR-18, FR-10, FR-19, FR-17 |\n| E2E (Playwright, 1 spec) | Teacher builds a 4-question quiz (incl. an essay) and publishes it → student starts, answers, `page.reload()`, answers persist, submits → teacher grades the essay → student sees results. Includes an axe check on the player | NFR-8, NFR-3, FR-15 |\n\n`npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test` must stay green. QA's banned-import scan covers NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 migration `add_quizzes`; schema models/enums exactly per PRD; relations and indexes only |\n| FR-2 | §3.2 `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` |\n| FR-3 | `grading.ts` `gradeAnswer` (choice rules, partial credit) |\n| FR-4 | `grading.ts` `normalizeShortAnswer` + `needsReview`; manual override §4.4 |\n| FR-5 | `gradeAnswer` ESSAY → null; `correct.guidance` server-only |\n| FR-6 | `/edit` page, `QuizSettingsPanel`, `quizSettingsSchema` superRefine |\n| FR-7 | `QuestionList` (dnd-kit + MUI), `QuestionEditor`, questions/reorder routes |\n| FR-8 | Builder points total; `QuizPlayer mode=\"preview\"` (A10) |\n| FR-9 | `canPublish`; DRAFT→PUBLISHED conditional update §4.1 |\n| FR-10 | Edit lock in `quiz-service`; `regradeQuiz`; `/regrade` route |\n| FR-11 | `course-tabs.ts` entry; `listCourseQuizzes` role-shaped; `CourseQuizzesView`; A2 |\n| FR-12 | `/quizzes/[quizId]/take` start screen + ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-13 | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `seededShuffle`, `computeDeadline` §4.2 |\n| FR-14 | `QuizPlayer` layout, navigator, sticky timer |\n| FR-15 | `useAutosave` hook; answer PUT §4.3 |\n| FR-16 | `saveAnswer` deadline + 30 s → auto-submit + CONFLICT |\n| FR-17 | `submitAttempt` §4.4; submit route |\n| FR-18 | `ensureNotExpired` (lazy) + `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` §4.6 |\n| FR-19 | Partial unique index §2; P2002 resume §4.2; localStorage merge on mount |\n| FR-20 | `resultsVisible`; `releaseResults`; result page placeholder text |\n| FR-21 | `toStudentResult`; result page |\n| FR-22 | `getStudentQuizScore` + `applyScoringPolicy` §4.7 |\n| FR-23 | `attemptLimit`; start CONFLICT §4.2 |\n| FR-24 | `/grade` page, `QuizGradingWorkspace`, grade route |\n| FR-25 | `recomputeAttempt` |\n| FR-26 | `analytics.ts`; `/analytics` page; x-charts BarChart |\n| FR-27 | Per-question stats; `analyticsCsv` via `toCsv` |\n| FR-28 | `upsertAccommodation`; accommodations route; feeds `computeDeadline`/`attemptLimit`; A7 |\n| FR-29 | `types.ts` `quiz.published`; notify on DRAFT→PUBLISHED (A9) |\n| FR-30 | `types.ts` `quiz.results_released`; release + maintenance claim §4.5 (A6) |\n| FR-31 | Quiz/question route files §3.3 |\n| FR-32 | Attempt route files §3.3 |\n| FR-33 | `isPractice` in `getStudentQuizScore`; A4 |\n| FR-34 | Reuse `course-access.ts`; `access.ts` `assertCanAccessAttempt` |\n| FR-35 | Two calls in `internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`; idempotent via status guard and claim |\n| FR-36 | `prisma/seed.ts` three quizzes |\n| FR-37 | No work: no sidebar entry (A1) |\n| FR-38 | `audit()` in grade, regrade, release, accommodation service functions |\n| FR-39 | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView + FileUpload; `'quiz'` file context |\n| NFR-1 | `serializers.ts`, student-path selects, serializer unit test §5 |\n| NFR-2 | Composite PK upsert; 2-query hot path §4.3 |\n| NFR-3 | Native MUI Radio/Checkbox; aria-live at 5/1 min; keyboard reorder fallback; axe in e2e |\n| NFR-4 | MUI-only component list §3.4; mui-mcp lookup is a dev gate (ADR-7) |\n| NFR-5 | requireUser/requirePageRole + course/attempt checks on every handler/page §5 |\n| NFR-6 | `withHandler`/Zod/`ok`/`paginated`; error mapping §3.3; UTC + school tz display |\n| NFR-7 | `src/server/quiz/` layout; reuse list §3.1; zero new deps |\n| NFR-8 | Testing map §6 |\n| NFR-9 | Builder defaults (SINGLE_CHOICE), Enter adds option, Duplicate, inline editing |\n| NFR-10 | Scope fence §1.3 |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2885,"cache_read_input_tokens":58290,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2885,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5aa5ddb-e317-4c7f-b076-47081e553974","uuid":"19987d72-b6b8-4ef1-be3f-1569fd546974","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:06:01.706Z","request_id":"req_011CgrvmrR2JJ2BnDrWgcrWp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012Bk8pTEdwsgWRYhDNnXCzy":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-10 · PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010)\n\nTicket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:45:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 FR + 10 NFR, 96%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (no blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B15, D1–D5), PRD `10-quizzes.md` FR-1 schema.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-10 adds teacher-built quizzes to courses: students take timed, autosaved attempts, the server grades them automatically where it can, teachers grade essays and flagged short answers by hand, and results are released according to a per-quiz visibility rule. The feature is a new vertical slice in the existing Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/Postgres app. It follows the PRD-09 assignments layout exactly:\n\n- `src/server/quiz/` holds the domain logic\n- `src/app/api/...` holds thin route handlers\n- `src/app/(app)/...` holds server pages with MUI client components\n\nThere is no new infrastructure and no new dependency (ADR-1). All background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher (ADR-6).\n\n**Design principles**\n1. **The server owns time and truth.** `deadlineAt` is frozen at start and checked only on the server. The client timer is display-only (FR-13, FR-16, ADR-4).\n2. **One path per state transition.** Manual submit, the deadline rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call a single `submitAttempt()`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` guard makes it idempotent (FR-17, FR-18, FR-35).\n3. **One visibility predicate.** `resultsVisible()` gates scores, correct answers and parent access (FR-20, FR-21, NFR-1).\n4. **Allow-listed student output.** Students only ever receive output from `serializers.ts` (NFR-1, ADR-5).\n5. **Pure core, thin I/O shell.** Grading, deadline, scoring, shuffle and publish checks are pure and unit-tested (NFR-8, ADR-3).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`**. Nothing blocks design or dev.\n\n### 1.2 Assumptions carried forward (flagged by intake, resolved here)\n| # | Req | Assumption / decision |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-37 (LOW) | **No sidebar entry.** Quizzes are reached through the course \"Quizzes\" tab and direct routes. FR-37 produces no code. |\n| A2 | FR-11 | \"Missed\" means the quiz is past `availableUntil` and the student has zero attempts. |\n| A3 | FR-10 | Regrade runs only through the explicit `POST /regrade`. Editing accepted answers does not trigger an automatic regrade. |\n| A4 | FR-33 | Practice quizzes count toward attempts, analytics and the teacher list. They are excluded only from the gradebook: `getStudentQuizScore` returns `isPractice` and PRD-11 filters on it. |\n| A5 | FR-29, FR-30 | `quiz.published` has defaultEmail = false (PRD). `quiz.results_released` has defaultEmail = true, matching `assignment.graded`; the PRD doesn't say. |\n| A6 | FR-30 | **No new column.** The \"sent once\" marker for AFTER_CLOSE results is the existing `Quiz.resultsReleasedAt`, which the maintenance pass claims atomically for AFTER_CLOSE quizzes (§4.5). This keeps FR-1's model list exact. The research notes' `resultsNotifiedAt` and claim-table options are therefore not needed. |\n| A7 | FR-28 | Accommodation changes apply only to attempts started after the change, because `deadlineAt` is frozen at start. The settings UI says so. |\n| A8 | FR-17, FR-25 | FR-1 has no `flagged` or `manuallyGraded` column. Both are **derived**: an answer is *manually graded* when `gradedById != null`, and it *needs review* when it is an ESSAY with `gradedById = null`, or a SHORT_ANSWER with `isCorrect = false` and `gradedById = null`. A pure `needsReview()` implements this rule. |\n| A9 | FR-29 | Status transitions are **DRAFT → PUBLISHED → CLOSED** only. There is no unpublish, so `quiz.published` fires exactly once, on the conditional DRAFT→PUBLISHED update. |\n| A10 | FR-8 | Preview mode reuses the player with `mode=\"preview\"`. Saves and submit are no-ops, nothing is graded, and nothing is sent to attempt endpoints. |\n\n### 1.3 Scope fence (NFR-10)\nOut of scope: lockdown browser, webcam proctoring, question banks, random pools and LaTeX. Nothing in this design anticipates them.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1, FR-2)\n\nThe model is one migration, `prisma/migrations/20261110000000_add_quizzes/`, created with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and hand-edited (ADR-2). The fields are **exactly as in PRD FR-1**. This design adds only relations and indexes, never new columns:\n\n| Model | Additions beyond the PRD listing | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Quiz | `createdBy User @relation(\"QuizCreatedBy\")`; `@@index([courseId, status])` | FK integrity; course tab list (FR-11) |\n| Question | `answers QuizAnswer[]`; `@@index([quizId, order])` | ordered load (FR-7, FR-31) |\n| QuizAttempt | `@@index([quizId, status])`, `@@index([status, deadlineAt])` | teacher list/needs-grading count (FR-11); maintenance sweep (FR-18) |\n| QuizAnswer | `question Question @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `gradedBy User? @relation(\"QuizAnswerGradedBy\")` | FK integrity; grading audit (FR-24) |\n| QuizAccommodation | `quiz Quiz @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `student User @relation(...)`, plus `accommodations QuizAccommodation[]` on Quiz | FK integrity (FR-28) |\n| Course | `quizzes Quiz[]` | FR-1 back-relation |\n| User | `quizzesCreated`, `quizAttempts`, `quizAccommodations`, `quizAnswersGraded` | FR-1 back-relations |\n\n**Raw SQL appended to the migration (FR-19, ADR-2):**\n```sql\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\"\n  ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';\n```\nA `schema.prisma` comment on QuizAttempt points to it, following the attendance-migration precedent. `prisma db push` would drop it, so dev and CI must use `migrate`.\n\n**JSON shapes** follow the PRD FR-2 table and are typed by the Zod discriminated union in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`:\n- `options`: `[{id,text}]`. Option ids are short cuids generated client-side and stable across edits.\n- `correct` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}`, `{accepted}` or `{guidance?}`.\n- `response` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}` or `{text}`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Server domain: `src/server/quiz/` (NFR-7)\n\n| File | Kind | Exports | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `grading.ts` | **pure**, isomorphic, no Prisma client | `gradeAnswer(question, response) → {pointsAwarded: Decimal\\|null, isCorrect: boolean\\|null}`, `needsReview(question, answer)`, `normalizeShortAnswer(s)`, `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)`, `attemptLimit(maxAttempts, extraAttempts)`, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`, `canPublish(questions) → string[]`, `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)`, `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (string hash + mulberry32), `ANSWER_GRACE_MS = 30_000` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-9, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-28 |\n| `serializers.ts` | pure | `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt`, `toStudentResult`. They are built by explicit allow-list, never spread-then-delete. | NFR-1, FR-21, FR-11 |\n| `access.ts` | I/O | `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt, {write})`: the owner (write allowed), a manager via `assertCanManageCourse`, or a linked PARENT (read-only, and only when `resultsVisible`). Otherwise it throws NOT_FOUND. | FR-34, NFR-5 |\n| `quiz-service.ts` | I/O | `listCourseQuizzes(user, courseId, page)` (role-shaped), `createQuiz`, `getQuizForManager`, `getQuizForStudent`, `updateQuiz` (settings + status transition + publish check + FR-29 notify), `deleteQuiz` (CONFLICT if any attempt exists), `addQuestion`, `updateQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions` (all through the **edit lock**), `regradeQuiz`, `releaseResults`, `upsertAccommodation` | FR-6..FR-11, FR-20, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31, FR-38 |\n| `attempt-service.ts` | I/O | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `getAttempt` (calls `ensureNotExpired`), `saveAnswer` (hot path), `submitAttempt(attemptId, {auto})`, `ensureNotExpired(attempt)`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`, `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` | FR-12..FR-19, FR-22..FR-25, FR-32, FR-33, FR-38 |\n| `analytics.ts` | I/O + pure aggregation | `getQuizAnalytics(quizId)` returns summary stats, a 10-bucket histogram and per-question stats. `analyticsCsv(quizId)` uses `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts`. | FR-26, FR-27 |\n| `maintenance.ts` | I/O | `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`, `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |\n\nReused as-is: `dec`/`fixed2`/`Decimal` from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` (imported, not copied); `withHandler`/`ok`/`paginated`/`AppError` (`src/server/http.ts`); `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`); `notify`/`notifyStudentAndParents`; `audit`; `logger`; `toCsv`; `getSchoolTimezone` (NFR-7).\n\n**Edit lock (FR-10).** `quiz-service` checks `_count.attempts > 0` before every question mutation. When attempts exist:\n- `updateQuestion` accepts only `prompt`, `explanation`, and (for SHORT_ANSWER) `correct.accepted` / `caseSensitive`.\n- `addQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions`, and changes to `type`/`points`/options/choice `correct` throw `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Quiz has attempts — only text, explanation and accepted answers can change. Use Regrade after editing accepted answers.')`.\n- The same check sits behind the builder's disabled controls and their tooltip.\n\n**Regrade (FR-10, FR-38).** One `$transaction`:\n1. For every submitted attempt, re-run `gradeAnswer` on answers with `gradedById = null` (a manual grade always wins, per A8).\n2. `recomputeAttempt` each attempt.\n3. Write `audit('quiz.regrade', {attemptCount})`.\n\n`recomputeAttempt` (FR-25): sets `score = Σ pointsAwarded` (fixed2) and sets status to `NEEDS_GRADING` if any `needsReview`, otherwise `GRADED`. Only submitted attempts are touched.\n\n### 3.2 Validators: `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` (FR-2, NFR-6)\nThese are client-safe Zod schemas shared by the builder forms and the route handlers:\n- `quizSettingsSchema` uses `.superRefine`: `availableUntil > availableFrom`, and `timeLimitMinutes ≤ window minutes` (FR-6). Limits: timeLimit 1–300 or null, maxAttempts 1–10.\n- `questionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', …)`: points 0.5–100, 2–8 options, ≥1 correct option for MULTIPLE_CHOICE, 1–10 accepted answers, prompt as non-empty Markdown.\n- `answerResponseSchema` is a type-agnostic union, so the hot path doesn't load the Question (NFR-2). ESSAY/SHORT text is ≤ 10,000 characters.\n- `manualGradeSchema` is `{points: 0..∞ step 0.5, feedback?}`. The upper bound (question points) is checked in the service.\n- `accommodationSchema`: extraTime 0–300, extraAttempts 0–5.\n- `reorderSchema`: `{questionIds: string[]}`.\n\n### 3.3 API route handlers (FR-31, FR-32, NFR-5, NFR-6)\nEvery handler is `withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → Zod parse → one service call → `ok`/`paginated`. There is no logic in the handlers. `api-contracts.json` (the next sub-task) owns the exact shapes.\n\n| Route file | Methods | Access | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `api/courses/[id]/quizzes/route.ts` | GET (role-shaped, paginated), POST | view / manage | FR-11, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/route.ts` | GET (manager: full; student/parent: `toStudentQuiz`), PATCH, DELETE | view / manage | FR-6, FR-9, FR-29, FR-31, NFR-1 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-31 |\n| `api/questions/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/attempts/route.ts` | POST (start/resume) | STUDENT + view | FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-32 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/route.ts` | GET | owner / linked parent / manager | FR-18, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-1 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/route.ts` | PUT | owner | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/submit/route.ts` | POST | owner | FR-17 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/grade/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-24, FR-25, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/regrade/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-10, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/release-results/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-20, FR-30, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/analytics/route.ts` | GET (`?format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | FR-26, FR-27 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/accommodations/[studentId]/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-28, FR-38 |\n\nError mapping: CONFLICT (409) covers writing after the deadline, the edit lock, deleting with attempts, the attempt limit, and a quiz that isn't open. VALIDATION_ERROR (400) is for Zod failures. NOT_FOUND hides resources the user can't access (NFR-5, NFR-6).\n\n### 3.4 Pages and UI: `src/app/(app)/...` (NFR-4: MUI only, mui-mcp lookup before each component)\n\n| Route / file | Server/client | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/config/course-tabs.ts` | config | One entry, `{key:'quizzes', label:'Quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES}` | FR-11 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/page.tsx` + `CourseQuizzesView.tsx` | server + client | Teacher: DataTable (status, window, attempts, avg, Needs grading) + \"New quiz\". Student: four sections (Upcoming / Available now (Start/Resume) / Completed (score if visible) / Missed). Parent: completed results, read-only, per linked child. | FR-11, FR-33 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/new/page.tsx` | server | Creates a DRAFT quiz with defaults and redirects to edit (no separate form) | FR-6 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/page.tsx` + `QuizBuilder.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx`, `QuestionList.tsx`, `QuestionEditor.tsx` | server + client | Settings (DateTimePicker, Switch, Select, TextField). The question list is a dnd-kit `SortableContext` of MUI Cards, with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback. Each type has its own editor (options with a correct Radio/Checkbox, an accepted-answers list, guidance). A running points total. Publish button with `canPublish` errors. Lock banner + disabled controls when attempts exist, plus a Regrade button. Accommodations section (DataTable of enrolled students). The prompt uses MarkdownEditor + FileUpload with context `'quiz'`. | FR-6..FR-10, FR-28, FR-39, NFR-9 |\n| `quizzes/[quizId]/take/page.tsx` + `QuizPlayer.tsx`, `useAutosave.ts` | server + client | Start screen (instructions, counts, points, limit, attempts used/allowed, ConfirmDialog on Start). The player has a sticky header (title, mm:ss timer from `deadlineAt`, red under 2 min, `aria-live=\"assertive\"` announcing at 5:00 and 1:00), a Chip status pill, LinearProgress, and RadioGroup/FormGroup+Checkbox/TextField per type. Layout is all-on-one-page, or one question per page with a navigator Button grid (answered / unanswered / flagged; flags stored client-side only). Submit uses ConfirmDialog showing the unanswered count. `mode=\"preview\"` is used by the builder. | FR-8, FR-12..FR-17, FR-19, NFR-3 |\n| `quizzes/[quizId]/attempts/[attemptId]/page.tsx` | server | Result view built from `toStudentResult`: score, %, per-question correctness, response and feedback, plus correct answers/explanations if allowed. Otherwise it shows \"Submitted — results will be available later.\" Also used by parents and teachers. | FR-20, FR-21 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/grade/page.tsx` + `QuizGradingWorkspace.tsx` | server + client | Tabs: By student / By question. Points TextField (step 0.5, max = question points) + feedback, with override allowed on auto-graded answers. | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/analytics/page.tsx` + `QuizAnalytics.tsx` | server + client | StatCards (attempts, avg, median, high, low, avg time), x-charts `BarChart` with 10 buckets, a per-question DataTable with option distribution (most-chosen wrong option highlighted), and a CSV link | FR-26, FR-27 |\n\nServer pages call `requirePageRole` and the course/attempt access helpers before fetching (NFR-5). They pass only serializer output to client components (NFR-1).\n\n**`useAutosave(attemptId, mode)` (FR-15, ADR-4).**\n- Each question gets an 800 ms `setTimeout` debounce, then `PUT /answers/:questionId`.\n- On network failure or 5xx, the latest response per question is written to the `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` map, and a 5 s `setInterval` drains it.\n- A 409 stops the queue, clears storage and routes to the result page. A 2xx removes that key.\n- The status pill reads `Saving…`, `All answers saved`, or `Offline — answers saved on this device` (shown when the queue is non-empty).\n- On mount, any queued answers are merged over server answers before rendering, so a reload loses nothing (FR-19, AC-2).\n\n### 3.5 Integrations into existing modules\n\n| Existing file | Change | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT, defaultEmail false) and `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT + PARENT, defaultEmail true, A5) | FR-29, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | `register('quiz', quizResolver)`. The resolver allows a course manager, or a course viewer when the quiz is PUBLISHED (images sit only in prompts, which students already see) | FR-39, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | After `sendDueReminders(now)`, add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)`, each in its own try/catch + `logger.error`, on every call | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` | Three seed quizzes, idempotent by (courseId, title). Scores are computed with `grading.ts` | FR-36 |\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration | §2 | FR-1, FR-19 |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Build and publish (FR-6..FR-9, FR-29)\n1. Teacher opens New. The server creates a DRAFT quiz and redirects to `/edit`.\n2. Settings and question edits go through PATCH/POST. Each is Zod-validated on both client and server, and question mutations pass the edit-lock check.\n3. On Publish, the client sends `PATCH {status:'PUBLISHED'}`. The service runs `canPublish(questions)` and throws VALIDATION_ERROR with the list of problems if any. Otherwise it runs `updateMany({where:{id, status:'DRAFT'}, data:{status:'PUBLISHED'}})`.\n4. If that update changed a row (count = 1), the service calls `notify('quiz.published')` for ACTIVE enrollees after commit (A9).\n\n### 4.2 Start or resume (FR-12, FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-28)\n```\nPOST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts  (STUDENT)\n  assertCanViewCourse → quiz PUBLISHED && availableFrom ≤ now < availableUntil, else CONFLICT\n  existing IN_PROGRESS? → ensureNotExpired → still IN_PROGRESS ? return it (resume)\n  count(attempts) ≥ attemptLimit(maxAttempts, accommodation.extraAttempts) → CONFLICT\n  $transaction:\n    id = cuid()                         // generated up front so the shuffle seed is known\n    order = shuffleQuestions ? seededShuffle(questionIds, id) : questionIds by `order`\n    deadlineAt = computeDeadline(now, timeLimitMinutes, accommodation.extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)\n    create {id, attemptNumber: count+1, questionOrder: order, deadlineAt, maxScore: Σ points}\n  on P2002 (partial index or attemptNumber unique) → re-read IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it\n→ toStudentAttempt(attempt, questions with seededShuffle(options, attempt.id) if shuffleOptions)\n```\nOption order isn't stored. It is recomputed from the `attempt.id` seed on every load, which makes it deterministic (FR-13). Two tabs get the same attempt id (FR-19).\n\n### 4.3 Autosave hot path (FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2)\n```\nPUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId   body {response}\n  1 query : attempt {studentId, status, deadlineAt, questionOrder}     (no Quiz/Question load)\n  studentId ≠ user → NOT_FOUND;  questionId ∉ questionOrder → NOT_FOUND\n  status ≠ IN_PROGRESS → CONFLICT\n  now > deadlineAt + 30s → submitAttempt(id,{auto:true}); throw CONFLICT('Time is up')\n  1 query : quizAnswer.upsert({attemptId_questionId}, {response})\n→ { data: { questionId, savedAt } }      // no grading data (NFR-1)\n```\nThe path is two indexed statements, well under the 50 ms budget at 300 concurrent students. It is idempotent, so localStorage replays are safe.\n\n### 4.4 Submit, auto-submit and grading (FR-17, FR-18, FR-24, FR-25)\n```\nsubmitAttempt(attemptId, {auto}):   $transaction\n  claimed = updateMany({id, status:'IN_PROGRESS'} → {status:'SUBMITTED', submittedAt: now, autoSubmitted: auto})\n  claimed.count = 0 → return current attempt (already submitted: idempotent, race-safe)\n  load questions + answers; for every questionId in questionOrder:\n     answer missing → create {response:null}\n     {pointsAwarded,isCorrect} = gradeAnswer(question, response)     // ESSAY → null,null; unanswered → 0,false\n  recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)   → score = Σ, status = NEEDS_GRADING | GRADED\n```\nCallers:\n- the submit POST (`auto:false`)\n- the deadline branch of saveAnswer\n- `ensureNotExpired` on GET attempt, start/resume, the player page and the teacher grade/list loads (FR-18, lazy)\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` (FR-18, batch)\n\nAn unanswered ESSAY gets `pointsAwarded = 0` and still needs review: the A8 predicate keys on `gradedById`, so the teacher confirms it.\n\nManual grading:\n1. `PUT …/grade` validates `points ≤ question.points` and `points % 0.5 = 0`, then sets `pointsAwarded`, `isCorrect = points == question.points`, `feedback` and `gradedById`.\n2. It runs `recomputeAttempt`, which sets GRADED when nothing still needs review (FR-25), and writes `audit('quizAnswer.grade')` after commit (FR-38).\n3. If the attempt became GRADED and the quiz is IMMEDIATELY, nothing is sent (FR-30).\n\n### 4.5 Results visibility and notification (FR-20, FR-21, FR-30)\n`resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`:\n- the attempt must be submitted\n- **IMMEDIATELY**: true\n- **AFTER_CLOSE**: `now ≥ availableUntil`\n- **MANUAL**: `resultsReleasedAt != null`\n\nScores also need status GRADED to display a final score. A NEEDS_GRADING attempt shows \"awaiting grading\" for the pending questions.\n\n- **MANUAL release:** `POST /release-results` runs `updateMany({id, resultsVisibility:'MANUAL', resultsReleasedAt:null} → now)`. If count = 1, it calls `notifyStudentAndParents` for students with a submitted attempt, then `audit('quiz.release_results')`. A repeat call is a no-op.\n- **AFTER_CLOSE (maintenance):** `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` finds quizzes where `resultsVisibility = AFTER_CLOSE AND availableUntil ≤ now AND resultsReleasedAt IS NULL`. For each one it claims with `updateMany(... resultsReleasedAt: null → now)`, and only when count = 1 does it notify. That makes it idempotent across concurrent cron calls (A6, FR-35).\n- **IMMEDIATELY:** no notification.\n\n### 4.6 Maintenance (FR-18, FR-35)\n`autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` finds attempts with `status = IN_PROGRESS AND deadlineAt < now − 30s`, takes up to 200 per call, and runs `submitAttempt(id, {auto:true})` on each. The per-call cap keeps a cron tick bounded; the next tick and the lazy path cover any remainder.\n\n### 4.7 Score export to PRD-11 (FR-22, FR-33)\n`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` returns `{score, maxScore, percent, isPractice, attemptsCounted} | null`, computed by `applyScoringPolicy` over GRADED attempts only. HIGHEST takes the max percent, LATEST takes the latest `submittedAt`, AVERAGE takes the Decimal mean, all with fixed2. It returns null when there are no GRADED attempts. There is no endpoint; PRD-11 imports it.\n\n### 4.8 Analytics (FR-26, FR-27)\n- **Input:** submitted attempts with their answers, aggregated in memory (class sizes are small).\n- **Summary stats:** count, mean, median, max, min, and mean of `submittedAt − startedAt`.\n- **Histogram:** 10 buckets by percent, with 100% placed in the last bucket.\n- **Per question:** % with `isCorrect = true`, average `pointsAwarded`, and for choice types an option-id count, with the most-chosen wrong option marked.\n- **CSV:** `toCsv` rows of student, attemptNumber, score, then one points column per question in quiz order.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Security and access (NFR-1, NFR-5)\n\n| Actor | Can |\n|---|---|\n| ADMIN / course teacher | All manage routes for their courses, any attempt in those courses |\n| STUDENT (ACTIVE enrolled) | List and take PUBLISHED quizzes; read and write **own** attempts; results only via `toStudentResult` |\n| PARENT (linked to an enrolled student) | Read-only: completed results of linked children, only when `resultsVisible` |\n\n- Student-path Prisma queries never `select` `correct` or `explanation`. The serializers add those fields back only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers` (defence in depth).\n- The answer-PUT response carries no grading data.\n- Inaccessible ids return NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so their existence isn't revealed.\n- Test: a serializer unit test walks the output recursively and asserts no `correct` key exists before visibility (AC-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Testing map (NFR-8, ADR-8)\n\n| Level | Target | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit (Vitest, no DB) | `gradeAnswer` per type, incl. the FR-2 example ({A,B} → 0, {A} → 2) and `' Photosynthesis '`; `needsReview`; `computeDeadline` (timed, untimed, extra time, capped by availableUntil); `attemptLimit`; `applyScoringPolicy` ×3; `seededShuffle` determinism; `resultsVisible` ×3; `canPublish`; serializers (no `correct` key) | FR-3, FR-4, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| Integration (Vitest + test DB) | Autosave returns 409 after deadline + 30 s and the attempt is auto-submitted; GET auto-submits an expired attempt; regrade changes auto-graded answers but not manual ones; concurrent start returns one attempt; double submit is a no-op | FR-16, FR-18, FR-10, FR-19, FR-17 |\n| E2E (Playwright, 1 spec) | Teacher builds a 4-question quiz (incl. an essay) and publishes it → student starts, answers, `page.reload()`, answers persist, submits → teacher grades the essay → student sees results. Includes an axe check on the player | NFR-8, NFR-3, FR-15 |\n\n`npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test` must stay green. QA's banned-import scan covers NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 migration `add_quizzes`; schema models/enums exactly per PRD; relations and indexes only |\n| FR-2 | §3.2 `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` |\n| FR-3 | `grading.ts` `gradeAnswer` (choice rules, partial credit) |\n| FR-4 | `grading.ts` `normalizeShortAnswer` + `needsReview`; manual override §4.4 |\n| FR-5 | `gradeAnswer` ESSAY → null; `correct.guidance` server-only |\n| FR-6 | `/edit` page, `QuizSettingsPanel`, `quizSettingsSchema` superRefine |\n| FR-7 | `QuestionList` (dnd-kit + MUI), `QuestionEditor`, questions/reorder routes |\n| FR-8 | Builder points total; `QuizPlayer mode=\"preview\"` (A10) |\n| FR-9 | `canPublish`; DRAFT→PUBLISHED conditional update §4.1 |\n| FR-10 | Edit lock in `quiz-service`; `regradeQuiz`; `/regrade` route |\n| FR-11 | `course-tabs.ts` entry; `listCourseQuizzes` role-shaped; `CourseQuizzesView`; A2 |\n| FR-12 | `/quizzes/[quizId]/take` start screen + ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-13 | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `seededShuffle`, `computeDeadline` §4.2 |\n| FR-14 | `QuizPlayer` layout, navigator, sticky timer |\n| FR-15 | `useAutosave` hook; answer PUT §4.3 |\n| FR-16 | `saveAnswer` deadline + 30 s → auto-submit + CONFLICT |\n| FR-17 | `submitAttempt` §4.4; submit route |\n| FR-18 | `ensureNotExpired` (lazy) + `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` §4.6 |\n| FR-19 | Partial unique index §2; P2002 resume §4.2; localStorage merge on mount |\n| FR-20 | `resultsVisible`; `releaseResults`; result page placeholder text |\n| FR-21 | `toStudentResult`; result page |\n| FR-22 | `getStudentQuizScore` + `applyScoringPolicy` §4.7 |\n| FR-23 | `attemptLimit`; start CONFLICT §4.2 |\n| FR-24 | `/grade` page, `QuizGradingWorkspace`, grade route |\n| FR-25 | `recomputeAttempt` |\n| FR-26 | `analytics.ts`; `/analytics` page; x-charts BarChart |\n| FR-27 | Per-question stats; `analyticsCsv` via `toCsv` |\n| FR-28 | `upsertAccommodation`; accommodations route; feeds `computeDeadline`/`attemptLimit`; A7 |\n| FR-29 | `types.ts` `quiz.published`; notify on DRAFT→PUBLISHED (A9) |\n| FR-30 | `types.ts` `quiz.results_released`; release + maintenance claim §4.5 (A6) |\n| FR-31 | Quiz/question route files §3.3 |\n| FR-32 | Attempt route files §3.3 |\n| FR-33 | `isPractice` in `getStudentQuizScore`; A4 |\n| FR-34 | Reuse `course-access.ts`; `access.ts` `assertCanAccessAttempt` |\n| FR-35 | Two calls in `internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`; idempotent via status guard and claim |\n| FR-36 | `prisma/seed.ts` three quizzes |\n| FR-37 | No work: no sidebar entry (A1) |\n| FR-38 | `audit()` in grade, regrade, release, accommodation service functions |\n| FR-39 | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView + FileUpload; `'quiz'` file context |\n| NFR-1 | `serializers.ts`, student-path selects, serializer unit test §5 |\n| NFR-2 | Composite PK upsert; 2-query hot path §4.3 |\n| NFR-3 | Native MUI Radio/Checkbox; aria-live at 5/1 min; keyboard reorder fallback; axe in e2e |\n| NFR-4 | MUI-only component list §3.4; mui-mcp lookup is a dev gate (ADR-7) |\n| NFR-5 | requireUser/requirePageRole + course/attempt checks on every handler/page §5 |\n| NFR-6 | `withHandler`/Zod/`ok`/`paginated`; error mapping §3.3; UTC + school tz display |\n| NFR-7 | `src/server/quiz/` layout; reuse list §3.1; zero new deps |\n| NFR-8 | Testing map §6 |\n| NFR-9 | Builder defaults (SINGLE_CHOICE), Enter adds option, Duplicate, inline editing |\n| NFR-10 | Scope fence §1.3 |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Bk8pTEdwsgWRYhDNnXCzy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5aa5ddb-e317-4c7f-b076-47081e553974","uuid":"7f6f30bc-d018-4889-908d-dbbca21bf7a1","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:06:01.810Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: SH-10 · PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010)\n\nTicket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:45:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 FR + 10 NFR, 96%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (no blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B15, D1–D5), PRD `10-quizzes.md` FR-1 schema.\nRun mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nPRD-10 adds teacher-built quizzes to courses: students take timed, autosaved attempts, the server grades them automatically where it can, teachers grade essays and flagged short answers by hand, and results are released according to a per-quiz visibility rule. The feature is a new vertical slice in the existing Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/Postgres app. It follows the PRD-09 assignments layout exactly:\n\n- `src/server/quiz/` holds the domain logic\n- `src/app/api/...` holds thin route handlers\n- `src/app/(app)/...` holds server pages with MUI client components\n\nThere is no new infrastructure and no new dependency (ADR-1). All background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher (ADR-6).\n\n**Design principles**\n1. **The server owns time and truth.** `deadlineAt` is frozen at start and checked only on the server. The client timer is display-only (FR-13, FR-16, ADR-4).\n2. **One path per state transition.** Manual submit, the deadline rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call a single `submitAttempt()`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` guard makes it idempotent (FR-17, FR-18, FR-35).\n3. **One visibility predicate.** `resultsVisible()` gates scores, correct answers and parent access (FR-20, FR-21, NFR-1).\n4. **Allow-listed student output.** Students only ever receive output from `serializers.ts` (NFR-1, ADR-5).\n5. **Pure core, thin I/O shell.** Grading, deadline, scoring, shuffle and publish checks are pure and unit-tested (NFR-8, ADR-3).\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`**. Nothing blocks design or dev.\n\n### 1.2 Assumptions carried forward (flagged by intake, resolved here)\n| # | Req | Assumption / decision |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | FR-37 (LOW) | **No sidebar entry.** Quizzes are reached through the course \"Quizzes\" tab and direct routes. FR-37 produces no code. |\n| A2 | FR-11 | \"Missed\" means the quiz is past `availableUntil` and the student has zero attempts. |\n| A3 | FR-10 | Regrade runs only through the explicit `POST /regrade`. Editing accepted answers does not trigger an automatic regrade. |\n| A4 | FR-33 | Practice quizzes count toward attempts, analytics and the teacher list. They are excluded only from the gradebook: `getStudentQuizScore` returns `isPractice` and PRD-11 filters on it. |\n| A5 | FR-29, FR-30 | `quiz.published` has defaultEmail = false (PRD). `quiz.results_released` has defaultEmail = true, matching `assignment.graded`; the PRD doesn't say. |\n| A6 | FR-30 | **No new column.** The \"sent once\" marker for AFTER_CLOSE results is the existing `Quiz.resultsReleasedAt`, which the maintenance pass claims atomically for AFTER_CLOSE quizzes (§4.5). This keeps FR-1's model list exact. The research notes' `resultsNotifiedAt` and claim-table options are therefore not needed. |\n| A7 | FR-28 | Accommodation changes apply only to attempts started after the change, because `deadlineAt` is frozen at start. The settings UI says so. |\n| A8 | FR-17, FR-25 | FR-1 has no `flagged` or `manuallyGraded` column. Both are **derived**: an answer is *manually graded* when `gradedById != null`, and it *needs review* when it is an ESSAY with `gradedById = null`, or a SHORT_ANSWER with `isCorrect = false` and `gradedById = null`. A pure `needsReview()` implements this rule. |\n| A9 | FR-29 | Status transitions are **DRAFT → PUBLISHED → CLOSED** only. There is no unpublish, so `quiz.published` fires exactly once, on the conditional DRAFT→PUBLISHED update. |\n| A10 | FR-8 | Preview mode reuses the player with `mode=\"preview\"`. Saves and submit are no-ops, nothing is graded, and nothing is sent to attempt endpoints. |\n\n### 1.3 Scope fence (NFR-10)\nOut of scope: lockdown browser, webcam proctoring, question banks, random pools and LaTeX. Nothing in this design anticipates them.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Data Model (FR-1, FR-2)\n\nThe model is one migration, `prisma/migrations/20261110000000_add_quizzes/`, created with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and hand-edited (ADR-2). The fields are **exactly as in PRD FR-1**. This design adds only relations and indexes, never new columns:\n\n| Model | Additions beyond the PRD listing | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Quiz | `createdBy User @relation(\"QuizCreatedBy\")`; `@@index([courseId, status])` | FK integrity; course tab list (FR-11) |\n| Question | `answers QuizAnswer[]`; `@@index([quizId, order])` | ordered load (FR-7, FR-31) |\n| QuizAttempt | `@@index([quizId, status])`, `@@index([status, deadlineAt])` | teacher list/needs-grading count (FR-11); maintenance sweep (FR-18) |\n| QuizAnswer | `question Question @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `gradedBy User? @relation(\"QuizAnswerGradedBy\")` | FK integrity; grading audit (FR-24) |\n| QuizAccommodation | `quiz Quiz @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `student User @relation(...)`, plus `accommodations QuizAccommodation[]` on Quiz | FK integrity (FR-28) |\n| Course | `quizzes Quiz[]` | FR-1 back-relation |\n| User | `quizzesCreated`, `quizAttempts`, `quizAccommodations`, `quizAnswersGraded` | FR-1 back-relations |\n\n**Raw SQL appended to the migration (FR-19, ADR-2):**\n```sql\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\"\n  ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';\n```\nA `schema.prisma` comment on QuizAttempt points to it, following the attendance-migration precedent. `prisma db push` would drop it, so dev and CI must use `migrate`.\n\n**JSON shapes** follow the PRD FR-2 table and are typed by the Zod discriminated union in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`:\n- `options`: `[{id,text}]`. Option ids are short cuids generated client-side and stable across edits.\n- `correct` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}`, `{accepted}` or `{guidance?}`.\n- `response` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}` or `{text}`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Component Breakdown\n\n### 3.1 Server domain: `src/server/quiz/` (NFR-7)\n\n| File | Kind | Exports | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `grading.ts` | **pure**, isomorphic, no Prisma client | `gradeAnswer(question, response) → {pointsAwarded: Decimal\\|null, isCorrect: boolean\\|null}`, `needsReview(question, answer)`, `normalizeShortAnswer(s)`, `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)`, `attemptLimit(maxAttempts, extraAttempts)`, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`, `canPublish(questions) → string[]`, `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)`, `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (string hash + mulberry32), `ANSWER_GRACE_MS = 30_000` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-9, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-28 |\n| `serializers.ts` | pure | `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt`, `toStudentResult`. They are built by explicit allow-list, never spread-then-delete. | NFR-1, FR-21, FR-11 |\n| `access.ts` | I/O | `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt, {write})`: the owner (write allowed), a manager via `assertCanManageCourse`, or a linked PARENT (read-only, and only when `resultsVisible`). Otherwise it throws NOT_FOUND. | FR-34, NFR-5 |\n| `quiz-service.ts` | I/O | `listCourseQuizzes(user, courseId, page)` (role-shaped), `createQuiz`, `getQuizForManager`, `getQuizForStudent`, `updateQuiz` (settings + status transition + publish check + FR-29 notify), `deleteQuiz` (CONFLICT if any attempt exists), `addQuestion`, `updateQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions` (all through the **edit lock**), `regradeQuiz`, `releaseResults`, `upsertAccommodation` | FR-6..FR-11, FR-20, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31, FR-38 |\n| `attempt-service.ts` | I/O | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `getAttempt` (calls `ensureNotExpired`), `saveAnswer` (hot path), `submitAttempt(attemptId, {auto})`, `ensureNotExpired(attempt)`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`, `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` | FR-12..FR-19, FR-22..FR-25, FR-32, FR-33, FR-38 |\n| `analytics.ts` | I/O + pure aggregation | `getQuizAnalytics(quizId)` returns summary stats, a 10-bucket histogram and per-question stats. `analyticsCsv(quizId)` uses `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts`. | FR-26, FR-27 |\n| `maintenance.ts` | I/O | `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`, `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |\n\nReused as-is: `dec`/`fixed2`/`Decimal` from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` (imported, not copied); `withHandler`/`ok`/`paginated`/`AppError` (`src/server/http.ts`); `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`); `notify`/`notifyStudentAndParents`; `audit`; `logger`; `toCsv`; `getSchoolTimezone` (NFR-7).\n\n**Edit lock (FR-10).** `quiz-service` checks `_count.attempts > 0` before every question mutation. When attempts exist:\n- `updateQuestion` accepts only `prompt`, `explanation`, and (for SHORT_ANSWER) `correct.accepted` / `caseSensitive`.\n- `addQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions`, and changes to `type`/`points`/options/choice `correct` throw `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Quiz has attempts — only text, explanation and accepted answers can change. Use Regrade after editing accepted answers.')`.\n- The same check sits behind the builder's disabled controls and their tooltip.\n\n**Regrade (FR-10, FR-38).** One `$transaction`:\n1. For every submitted attempt, re-run `gradeAnswer` on answers with `gradedById = null` (a manual grade always wins, per A8).\n2. `recomputeAttempt` each attempt.\n3. Write `audit('quiz.regrade', {attemptCount})`.\n\n`recomputeAttempt` (FR-25): sets `score = Σ pointsAwarded` (fixed2) and sets status to `NEEDS_GRADING` if any `needsReview`, otherwise `GRADED`. Only submitted attempts are touched.\n\n### 3.2 Validators: `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` (FR-2, NFR-6)\nThese are client-safe Zod schemas shared by the builder forms and the route handlers:\n- `quizSettingsSchema` uses `.superRefine`: `availableUntil > availableFrom`, and `timeLimitMinutes ≤ window minutes` (FR-6). Limits: timeLimit 1–300 or null, maxAttempts 1–10.\n- `questionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', …)`: points 0.5–100, 2–8 options, ≥1 correct option for MULTIPLE_CHOICE, 1–10 accepted answers, prompt as non-empty Markdown.\n- `answerResponseSchema` is a type-agnostic union, so the hot path doesn't load the Question (NFR-2). ESSAY/SHORT text is ≤ 10,000 characters.\n- `manualGradeSchema` is `{points: 0..∞ step 0.5, feedback?}`. The upper bound (question points) is checked in the service.\n- `accommodationSchema`: extraTime 0–300, extraAttempts 0–5.\n- `reorderSchema`: `{questionIds: string[]}`.\n\n### 3.3 API route handlers (FR-31, FR-32, NFR-5, NFR-6)\nEvery handler is `withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → Zod parse → one service call → `ok`/`paginated`. There is no logic in the handlers. `api-contracts.json` (the next sub-task) owns the exact shapes.\n\n| Route file | Methods | Access | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `api/courses/[id]/quizzes/route.ts` | GET (role-shaped, paginated), POST | view / manage | FR-11, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/route.ts` | GET (manager: full; student/parent: `toStudentQuiz`), PATCH, DELETE | view / manage | FR-6, FR-9, FR-29, FR-31, NFR-1 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-31 |\n| `api/questions/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/attempts/route.ts` | POST (start/resume) | STUDENT + view | FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-32 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/route.ts` | GET | owner / linked parent / manager | FR-18, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-1 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/route.ts` | PUT | owner | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/submit/route.ts` | POST | owner | FR-17 |\n| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/grade/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-24, FR-25, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/regrade/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-10, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/release-results/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-20, FR-30, FR-38 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/analytics/route.ts` | GET (`?format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | FR-26, FR-27 |\n| `api/quizzes/[id]/accommodations/[studentId]/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-28, FR-38 |\n\nError mapping: CONFLICT (409) covers writing after the deadline, the edit lock, deleting with attempts, the attempt limit, and a quiz that isn't open. VALIDATION_ERROR (400) is for Zod failures. NOT_FOUND hides resources the user can't access (NFR-5, NFR-6).\n\n### 3.4 Pages and UI: `src/app/(app)/...` (NFR-4: MUI only, mui-mcp lookup before each component)\n\n| Route / file | Server/client | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/config/course-tabs.ts` | config | One entry, `{key:'quizzes', label:'Quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES}` | FR-11 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/page.tsx` + `CourseQuizzesView.tsx` | server + client | Teacher: DataTable (status, window, attempts, avg, Needs grading) + \"New quiz\". Student: four sections (Upcoming / Available now (Start/Resume) / Completed (score if visible) / Missed). Parent: completed results, read-only, per linked child. | FR-11, FR-33 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/new/page.tsx` | server | Creates a DRAFT quiz with defaults and redirects to edit (no separate form) | FR-6 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/page.tsx` + `QuizBuilder.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx`, `QuestionList.tsx`, `QuestionEditor.tsx` | server + client | Settings (DateTimePicker, Switch, Select, TextField). The question list is a dnd-kit `SortableContext` of MUI Cards, with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback. Each type has its own editor (options with a correct Radio/Checkbox, an accepted-answers list, guidance). A running points total. Publish button with `canPublish` errors. Lock banner + disabled controls when attempts exist, plus a Regrade button. Accommodations section (DataTable of enrolled students). The prompt uses MarkdownEditor + FileUpload with context `'quiz'`. | FR-6..FR-10, FR-28, FR-39, NFR-9 |\n| `quizzes/[quizId]/take/page.tsx` + `QuizPlayer.tsx`, `useAutosave.ts` | server + client | Start screen (instructions, counts, points, limit, attempts used/allowed, ConfirmDialog on Start). The player has a sticky header (title, mm:ss timer from `deadlineAt`, red under 2 min, `aria-live=\"assertive\"` announcing at 5:00 and 1:00), a Chip status pill, LinearProgress, and RadioGroup/FormGroup+Checkbox/TextField per type. Layout is all-on-one-page, or one question per page with a navigator Button grid (answered / unanswered / flagged; flags stored client-side only). Submit uses ConfirmDialog showing the unanswered count. `mode=\"preview\"` is used by the builder. | FR-8, FR-12..FR-17, FR-19, NFR-3 |\n| `quizzes/[quizId]/attempts/[attemptId]/page.tsx` | server | Result view built from `toStudentResult`: score, %, per-question correctness, response and feedback, plus correct answers/explanations if allowed. Otherwise it shows \"Submitted — results will be available later.\" Also used by parents and teachers. | FR-20, FR-21 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/grade/page.tsx` + `QuizGradingWorkspace.tsx` | server + client | Tabs: By student / By question. Points TextField (step 0.5, max = question points) + feedback, with override allowed on auto-graded answers. | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/analytics/page.tsx` + `QuizAnalytics.tsx` | server + client | StatCards (attempts, avg, median, high, low, avg time), x-charts `BarChart` with 10 buckets, a per-question DataTable with option distribution (most-chosen wrong option highlighted), and a CSV link | FR-26, FR-27 |\n\nServer pages call `requirePageRole` and the course/attempt access helpers before fetching (NFR-5). They pass only serializer output to client components (NFR-1).\n\n**`useAutosave(attemptId, mode)` (FR-15, ADR-4).**\n- Each question gets an 800 ms `setTimeout` debounce, then `PUT /answers/:questionId`.\n- On network failure or 5xx, the latest response per question is written to the `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` map, and a 5 s `setInterval` drains it.\n- A 409 stops the queue, clears storage and routes to the result page. A 2xx removes that key.\n- The status pill reads `Saving…`, `All answers saved`, or `Offline — answers saved on this device` (shown when the queue is non-empty).\n- On mount, any queued answers are merged over server answers before rendering, so a reload loses nothing (FR-19, AC-2).\n\n### 3.5 Integrations into existing modules\n\n| Existing file | Change | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT, defaultEmail false) and `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT + PARENT, defaultEmail true, A5) | FR-29, FR-30 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | `register('quiz', quizResolver)`. The resolver allows a course manager, or a course viewer when the quiz is PUBLISHED (images sit only in prompts, which students already see) | FR-39, NFR-5 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | After `sendDueReminders(now)`, add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)`, each in its own try/catch + `logger.error`, on every call | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` | Three seed quizzes, idempotent by (courseId, title). Scores are computed with `grading.ts` | FR-36 |\n| `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration | §2 | FR-1, FR-19 |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Flow\n\n### 4.1 Build and publish (FR-6..FR-9, FR-29)\n1. Teacher opens New. The server creates a DRAFT quiz and redirects to `/edit`.\n2. Settings and question edits go through PATCH/POST. Each is Zod-validated on both client and server, and question mutations pass the edit-lock check.\n3. On Publish, the client sends `PATCH {status:'PUBLISHED'}`. The service runs `canPublish(questions)` and throws VALIDATION_ERROR with the list of problems if any. Otherwise it runs `updateMany({where:{id, status:'DRAFT'}, data:{status:'PUBLISHED'}})`.\n4. If that update changed a row (count = 1), the service calls `notify('quiz.published')` for ACTIVE enrollees after commit (A9).\n\n### 4.2 Start or resume (FR-12, FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-28)\n```\nPOST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts  (STUDENT)\n  assertCanViewCourse → quiz PUBLISHED && availableFrom ≤ now < availableUntil, else CONFLICT\n  existing IN_PROGRESS? → ensureNotExpired → still IN_PROGRESS ? return it (resume)\n  count(attempts) ≥ attemptLimit(maxAttempts, accommodation.extraAttempts) → CONFLICT\n  $transaction:\n    id = cuid()                         // generated up front so the shuffle seed is known\n    order = shuffleQuestions ? seededShuffle(questionIds, id) : questionIds by `order`\n    deadlineAt = computeDeadline(now, timeLimitMinutes, accommodation.extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)\n    create {id, attemptNumber: count+1, questionOrder: order, deadlineAt, maxScore: Σ points}\n  on P2002 (partial index or attemptNumber unique) → re-read IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it\n→ toStudentAttempt(attempt, questions with seededShuffle(options, attempt.id) if shuffleOptions)\n```\nOption order isn't stored. It is recomputed from the `attempt.id` seed on every load, which makes it deterministic (FR-13). Two tabs get the same attempt id (FR-19).\n\n### 4.3 Autosave hot path (FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2)\n```\nPUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId   body {response}\n  1 query : attempt {studentId, status, deadlineAt, questionOrder}     (no Quiz/Question load)\n  studentId ≠ user → NOT_FOUND;  questionId ∉ questionOrder → NOT_FOUND\n  status ≠ IN_PROGRESS → CONFLICT\n  now > deadlineAt + 30s → submitAttempt(id,{auto:true}); throw CONFLICT('Time is up')\n  1 query : quizAnswer.upsert({attemptId_questionId}, {response})\n→ { data: { questionId, savedAt } }      // no grading data (NFR-1)\n```\nThe path is two indexed statements, well under the 50 ms budget at 300 concurrent students. It is idempotent, so localStorage replays are safe.\n\n### 4.4 Submit, auto-submit and grading (FR-17, FR-18, FR-24, FR-25)\n```\nsubmitAttempt(attemptId, {auto}):   $transaction\n  claimed = updateMany({id, status:'IN_PROGRESS'} → {status:'SUBMITTED', submittedAt: now, autoSubmitted: auto})\n  claimed.count = 0 → return current attempt (already submitted: idempotent, race-safe)\n  load questions + answers; for every questionId in questionOrder:\n     answer missing → create {response:null}\n     {pointsAwarded,isCorrect} = gradeAnswer(question, response)     // ESSAY → null,null; unanswered → 0,false\n  recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)   → score = Σ, status = NEEDS_GRADING | GRADED\n```\nCallers:\n- the submit POST (`auto:false`)\n- the deadline branch of saveAnswer\n- `ensureNotExpired` on GET attempt, start/resume, the player page and the teacher grade/list loads (FR-18, lazy)\n- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` (FR-18, batch)\n\nAn unanswered ESSAY gets `pointsAwarded = 0` and still needs review: the A8 predicate keys on `gradedById`, so the teacher confirms it.\n\nManual grading:\n1. `PUT …/grade` validates `points ≤ question.points` and `points % 0.5 = 0`, then sets `pointsAwarded`, `isCorrect = points == question.points`, `feedback` and `gradedById`.\n2. It runs `recomputeAttempt`, which sets GRADED when nothing still needs review (FR-25), and writes `audit('quizAnswer.grade')` after commit (FR-38).\n3. If the attempt became GRADED and the quiz is IMMEDIATELY, nothing is sent (FR-30).\n\n### 4.5 Results visibility and notification (FR-20, FR-21, FR-30)\n`resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`:\n- the attempt must be submitted\n- **IMMEDIATELY**: true\n- **AFTER_CLOSE**: `now ≥ availableUntil`\n- **MANUAL**: `resultsReleasedAt != null`\n\nScores also need status GRADED to display a final score. A NEEDS_GRADING attempt shows \"awaiting grading\" for the pending questions.\n\n- **MANUAL release:** `POST /release-results` runs `updateMany({id, resultsVisibility:'MANUAL', resultsReleasedAt:null} → now)`. If count = 1, it calls `notifyStudentAndParents` for students with a submitted attempt, then `audit('quiz.release_results')`. A repeat call is a no-op.\n- **AFTER_CLOSE (maintenance):** `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` finds quizzes where `resultsVisibility = AFTER_CLOSE AND availableUntil ≤ now AND resultsReleasedAt IS NULL`. For each one it claims with `updateMany(... resultsReleasedAt: null → now)`, and only when count = 1 does it notify. That makes it idempotent across concurrent cron calls (A6, FR-35).\n- **IMMEDIATELY:** no notification.\n\n### 4.6 Maintenance (FR-18, FR-35)\n`autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` finds attempts with `status = IN_PROGRESS AND deadlineAt < now − 30s`, takes up to 200 per call, and runs `submitAttempt(id, {auto:true})` on each. The per-call cap keeps a cron tick bounded; the next tick and the lazy path cover any remainder.\n\n### 4.7 Score export to PRD-11 (FR-22, FR-33)\n`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` returns `{score, maxScore, percent, isPractice, attemptsCounted} | null`, computed by `applyScoringPolicy` over GRADED attempts only. HIGHEST takes the max percent, LATEST takes the latest `submittedAt`, AVERAGE takes the Decimal mean, all with fixed2. It returns null when there are no GRADED attempts. There is no endpoint; PRD-11 imports it.\n\n### 4.8 Analytics (FR-26, FR-27)\n- **Input:** submitted attempts with their answers, aggregated in memory (class sizes are small).\n- **Summary stats:** count, mean, median, max, min, and mean of `submittedAt − startedAt`.\n- **Histogram:** 10 buckets by percent, with 100% placed in the last bucket.\n- **Per question:** % with `isCorrect = true`, average `pointsAwarded`, and for choice types an option-id count, with the most-chosen wrong option marked.\n- **CSV:** `toCsv` rows of student, attemptNumber, score, then one points column per question in quiz order.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Security and access (NFR-1, NFR-5)\n\n| Actor | Can |\n|---|---|\n| ADMIN / course teacher | All manage routes for their courses, any attempt in those courses |\n| STUDENT (ACTIVE enrolled) | List and take PUBLISHED quizzes; read and write **own** attempts; results only via `toStudentResult` |\n| PARENT (linked to an enrolled student) | Read-only: completed results of linked children, only when `resultsVisible` |\n\n- Student-path Prisma queries never `select` `correct` or `explanation`. The serializers add those fields back only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers` (defence in depth).\n- The answer-PUT response carries no grading data.\n- Inaccessible ids return NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so their existence isn't revealed.\n- Test: a serializer unit test walks the output recursively and asserts no `correct` key exists before visibility (AC-7).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Testing map (NFR-8, ADR-8)\n\n| Level | Target | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unit (Vitest, no DB) | `gradeAnswer` per type, incl. the FR-2 example ({A,B} → 0, {A} → 2) and `' Photosynthesis '`; `needsReview`; `computeDeadline` (timed, untimed, extra time, capped by availableUntil); `attemptLimit`; `applyScoringPolicy` ×3; `seededShuffle` determinism; `resultsVisible` ×3; `canPublish`; serializers (no `correct` key) | FR-3, FR-4, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-9, NFR-1 |\n| Integration (Vitest + test DB) | Autosave returns 409 after deadline + 30 s and the attempt is auto-submitted; GET auto-submits an expired attempt; regrade changes auto-graded answers but not manual ones; concurrent start returns one attempt; double submit is a no-op | FR-16, FR-18, FR-10, FR-19, FR-17 |\n| E2E (Playwright, 1 spec) | Teacher builds a 4-question quiz (incl. an essay) and publishes it → student starts, answers, `page.reload()`, answers persist, submits → teacher grades the essay → student sees results. Includes an axe check on the player | NFR-8, NFR-3, FR-15 |\n\n`npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test` must stay green. QA's banned-import scan covers NFR-4.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2 migration `add_quizzes`; schema models/enums exactly per PRD; relations and indexes only |\n| FR-2 | §3.2 `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` |\n| FR-3 | `grading.ts` `gradeAnswer` (choice rules, partial credit) |\n| FR-4 | `grading.ts` `normalizeShortAnswer` + `needsReview`; manual override §4.4 |\n| FR-5 | `gradeAnswer` ESSAY → null; `correct.guidance` server-only |\n| FR-6 | `/edit` page, `QuizSettingsPanel`, `quizSettingsSchema` superRefine |\n| FR-7 | `QuestionList` (dnd-kit + MUI), `QuestionEditor`, questions/reorder routes |\n| FR-8 | Builder points total; `QuizPlayer mode=\"preview\"` (A10) |\n| FR-9 | `canPublish`; DRAFT→PUBLISHED conditional update §4.1 |\n| FR-10 | Edit lock in `quiz-service`; `regradeQuiz`; `/regrade` route |\n| FR-11 | `course-tabs.ts` entry; `listCourseQuizzes` role-shaped; `CourseQuizzesView`; A2 |\n| FR-12 | `/quizzes/[quizId]/take` start screen + ConfirmDialog |\n| FR-13 | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `seededShuffle`, `computeDeadline` §4.2 |\n| FR-14 | `QuizPlayer` layout, navigator, sticky timer |\n| FR-15 | `useAutosave` hook; answer PUT §4.3 |\n| FR-16 | `saveAnswer` deadline + 30 s → auto-submit + CONFLICT |\n| FR-17 | `submitAttempt` §4.4; submit route |\n| FR-18 | `ensureNotExpired` (lazy) + `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` §4.6 |\n| FR-19 | Partial unique index §2; P2002 resume §4.2; localStorage merge on mount |\n| FR-20 | `resultsVisible`; `releaseResults`; result page placeholder text |\n| FR-21 | `toStudentResult`; result page |\n| FR-22 | `getStudentQuizScore` + `applyScoringPolicy` §4.7 |\n| FR-23 | `attemptLimit`; start CONFLICT §4.2 |\n| FR-24 | `/grade` page, `QuizGradingWorkspace`, grade route |\n| FR-25 | `recomputeAttempt` |\n| FR-26 | `analytics.ts`; `/analytics` page; x-charts BarChart |\n| FR-27 | Per-question stats; `analyticsCsv` via `toCsv` |\n| FR-28 | `upsertAccommodation`; accommodations route; feeds `computeDeadline`/`attemptLimit`; A7 |\n| FR-29 | `types.ts` `quiz.published`; notify on DRAFT→PUBLISHED (A9) |\n| FR-30 | `types.ts` `quiz.results_released`; release + maintenance claim §4.5 (A6) |\n| FR-31 | Quiz/question route files §3.3 |\n| FR-32 | Attempt route files §3.3 |\n| FR-33 | `isPractice` in `getStudentQuizScore`; A4 |\n| FR-34 | Reuse `course-access.ts`; `access.ts` `assertCanAccessAttempt` |\n| FR-35 | Two calls in `internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`; idempotent via status guard and claim |\n| FR-36 | `prisma/seed.ts` three quizzes |\n| FR-37 | No work: no sidebar entry (A1) |\n| FR-38 | `audit()` in grade, regrade, release, accommodation service functions |\n| FR-39 | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView + FileUpload; `'quiz'` file context |\n| NFR-1 | `serializers.ts`, student-path selects, serializer unit test §5 |\n| NFR-2 | Composite PK upsert; 2-query hot path §4.3 |\n| NFR-3 | Native MUI Radio/Checkbox; aria-live at 5/1 min; keyboard reorder fallback; axe in e2e |\n| NFR-4 | MUI-only component list §3.4; mui-mcp lookup is a dev gate (ADR-7) |\n| NFR-5 | requireUser/requirePageRole + course/attempt checks on every handler/page §5 |\n| NFR-6 | `withHandler`/Zod/`ok`/`paginated`; error mapping §3.3; UTC + school tz display |\n| NFR-7 | `src/server/quiz/` layout; reuse list §3.1; zero new deps |\n| NFR-8 | Testing map §6 |\n| NFR-9 | Builder defaults (SINGLE_CHOICE), Enter adds option, Duplicate, inline editing |\n| NFR-10 | Scope fence §1.3 |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":410,"newStart":1,"newLines":336,"lines":["-# System Design: SH-9 · PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009)","+# System Design: SH-10 · PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams (SCH-010)"," ","-Ticket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T10:40:00Z · Status: complete","-Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (61 FR + 17 NFR, 95%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),","-`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B16, D1–D10). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.","+Ticket: SH-10 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T12:45:00Z · Status: complete","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (39 FR + 10 NFR, 96%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (no blockers),","+`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B15, D1–D5), PRD `10-quizzes.md` FR-1 schema.","+Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`."," ","-> This file replaces the stale SH-8 design that was in this folder. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`","-> and `threat-model-notes.json` in this folder are also leftovers from earlier tickets. `arch-api-contracts` overwrites the first two.","-"," ---"," "," ## 1. Overview"," ","-SchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).","-SH-9 adds **assignments**: teacher authoring with an optional rubric, student submission with resubmission history,","-a keyboard-driven grading screen, return flow, exemptions, offline grading, a cross-course `/assignments` page per role,","-four notifications, and two reminder passes.","+PRD-10 adds teacher-built quizzes to courses: students take timed, autosaved attempts, the server grades them automatically where it can, teachers grade essays and flagged short answers by hand, and results are released according to a per-quiz visibility rule. The feature is a new vertical slice in the existing Next.js 14 App Router + Prisma/Postgres app. It follows the PRD-09 assignments layout exactly:"," ","-Shape of the change:","+- `src/server/quiz/` holds the domain logic","+- `src/app/api/...` holds thin route handlers","+- `src/app/(app)/...` holds server pages with MUI client components"," ","-- **One migration**, `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6).","-- **One feature folder**, `src/server/assignments/`, with three files: `assignments-service.ts` (all DB logic),","-  `grading-math.ts` (pure, isomorphic, unit-tested), `reminders.ts` (maintenance pass).","-- **One validator file**, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by forms and handlers.","-- Thin route handlers under `src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…` (NFR-7, NFR-8).","-- Pages under `src/app/(app)/…`, plus the four PRD-08 shared components that were never built (D1).","-- **No new dependencies, services, queues, or cron** (ADR-1, ADR-8). Reminders hook into the existing dispatcher.","+There is no new infrastructure and no new dependency (ADR-1). All background work goes through the existing maintenance dispatcher (ADR-6)."," ","-### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)","+**Design principles**","+1. **The server owns time and truth.** `deadlineAt` is frozen at start and checked only on the server. The client timer is display-only (FR-13, FR-16, ADR-4).","+2. **One path per state transition.** Manual submit, the deadline rejection, lazy load and the maintenance pass all call a single `submitAttempt()`. The `status = IN_PROGRESS` guard makes it idempotent (FR-17, FR-18, FR-35).","+3. **One visibility predicate.** `resultsVisible()` gates scores, correct answers and parent access (FR-20, FR-21, NFR-1).","+4. **Allow-listed student output.** Students only ever receive output from `serializers.ts` (NFR-1, ADR-5).","+5. **Pure core, thin I/O shell.** Grading, deadline, scoring, shuffle and publish checks are pure and unit-tested (NFR-8, ADR-3)."," ","-| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |","+### 1.1 Intake blockers","+`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`**. Nothing blocks design or dev.","+","+### 1.2 Assumptions carried forward (flagged by intake, resolved here)","+| # | Req | Assumption / decision |"," |---|---|---|","-| 1 | PRD-08 UI is missing: FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor | Build the minimum of all four in `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` (ADR-5, §2.5). No other PRD-08 scope. |","-| 2 | MUI X break: `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 vs X 9.5.0 | `package.json` `overrides: { \"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\" }` (ADR-2). This fixes both DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9). Fallback: FR-17 uses an MUI `Table`, and FR-9 uses `TextField type=\"datetime-local\"`. Dev verifies with `npm ls` plus a compile **before** building UI. |","-| 3 | vitest import break | Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (ADR-3). |","-| 4 | CSP `script-src 'self'` breaks hydration | Leave it alone. The e2e spec uses `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })` (ADR-4). The platform nonce fix is a follow-up ticket. |","-| 5 | `studentTabs` has no renderer | Register the FR-41 tab and build `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. The page works by direct URL. **No tab bar is built** (NFR-15). This is a known gap and is carried to the handoff. |","-| 6 | LOW-confidence defaults FR-15, FR-52, FR-60 | Adopt intake's defaults as written (§5). Each one is a single predicate or a single copy rule, so it is cheap to change later. |","-| 7 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-11). |","-| 8 | mui-mcp must be reachable (NFR-6) | This is a hard gate on the dev phase. Dev looks up every MUI component through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before using it. If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker. |","+| A1 | FR-37 (LOW) | **No sidebar entry.** Quizzes are reached through the course \"Quizzes\" tab and direct routes. FR-37 produces no code. |","+| A2 | FR-11 | \"Missed\" means the quiz is past `availableUntil` and the student has zero attempts. |","+| A3 | FR-10 | Regrade runs only through the explicit `POST /regrade`. Editing accepted answers does not trigger an automatic regrade. |","+| A4 | FR-33 | Practice quizzes count toward attempts, analytics and the teacher list. They are excluded only from the gradebook: `getStudentQuizScore` returns `isPractice` and PRD-11 filters on it. |","+| A5 | FR-29, FR-30 | `quiz.published` has defaultEmail = false (PRD). `quiz.results_released` has defaultEmail = true, matching `assignment.graded`; the PRD doesn't say. |","+| A6 | FR-30 | **No new column.** The \"sent once\" marker for AFTER_CLOSE results is the existing `Quiz.resultsReleasedAt`, which the maintenance pass claims atomically for AFTER_CLOSE quizzes (§4.5). This keeps FR-1's model list exact. The research notes' `resultsNotifiedAt` and claim-table options are therefore not needed. |","+| A7 | FR-28 | Accommodation changes apply only to attempts started after the change, because `deadlineAt` is frozen at start. The settings UI says so. |","+| A8 | FR-17, FR-25 | FR-1 has no `flagged` or `manuallyGraded` column. Both are **derived**: an answer is *manually graded* when `gradedById != null`, and it *needs review* when it is an ESSAY with `gradedById = null`, or a SHORT_ANSWER with `isCorrect = false` and `gradedById = null`. A pure `needsReview()` implements this rule. |","+| A9 | FR-29 | Status transitions are **DRAFT → PUBLISHED → CLOSED** only. There is no unpublish, so `quiz.published` fires exactly once, on the conditional DRAFT→PUBLISHED update. |","+| A10 | FR-8 | Preview mode reuses the player with `mode=\"preview\"`. Saves and submit are no-ops, nothing is graded, and nothing is sent to attempt endpoints. |"," ","-### 1.2 New finding from this sub-task (not in intake)","+### 1.3 Scope fence (NFR-10)","+Out of scope: lockdown browser, webcam proctoring, question banks, random pools and LaTeX. Nothing in this design anticipates them."," ","-`next.config.js` sends **`X-Frame-Options: DENY`** on `/:path*`. That blocks the same-origin","-`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">` PDF preview required by FR-29. CSP `default-src 'self'` already allows same-origin frames,","-so the X-Frame-Options header is the only thing blocking it. `<img>` previews are not affected.","-","-**Decision D11:** in `next.config.js`, split the header rule:","-- `source: '/((?!api/files/).*)'` keeps the existing headers, with `DENY`.","-- `source: '/api/files/:id'` gets the same headers, but with `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` and `frame-ancestors 'self'` appended to the CSP.","-","-The file route already enforces access (`canAccessFile`) and sniffs types (`nosniff`), so letting our own pages frame it adds no exposure.","-**Fallback**, if the dev wants zero header changes: show PDFs as an \"Open\" link (`target=\"_blank\"`) instead of an iframe. Images still preview inline.","-"," ---"," ","-## 2. Component Breakdown","+## 2. Data Model (FR-1, FR-2)"," ","-### 2.1 Data model: migration `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6)","+The model is one migration, `prisma/migrations/20261110000000_add_quizzes/`, created with `prisma migrate dev --create-only` and hand-edited (ADR-2). The fields are **exactly as in PRD FR-1**. This design adds only relations and indexes, never new columns:"," ","-All additive. Existing models get back-relations only (NFR-11).","+| Model | Additions beyond the PRD listing | Why |","+|---|---|---|","+| Quiz | `createdBy User @relation(\"QuizCreatedBy\")`; `@@index([courseId, status])` | FK integrity; course tab list (FR-11) |","+| Question | `answers QuizAnswer[]`; `@@index([quizId, order])` | ordered load (FR-7, FR-31) |","+| QuizAttempt | `@@index([quizId, status])`, `@@index([status, deadlineAt])` | teacher list/needs-grading count (FR-11); maintenance sweep (FR-18) |","+| QuizAnswer | `question Question @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `gradedBy User? @relation(\"QuizAnswerGradedBy\")` | FK integrity; grading audit (FR-24) |","+| QuizAccommodation | `quiz Quiz @relation(onDelete: Cascade)`, `student User @relation(...)`, plus `accommodations QuizAccommodation[]` on Quiz | FK integrity (FR-28) |","+| Course | `quizzes Quiz[]` | FR-1 back-relation |","+| User | `quizzesCreated`, `quizAttempts`, `quizAccommodations`, `quizAnswersGraded` | FR-1 back-relations |"," ","+**Raw SQL appended to the migration (FR-19, ADR-2):**","+```sql","+CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \"quiz_attempt_one_in_progress_uq\"","+  ON \"QuizAttempt\"(\"quizId\",\"studentId\") WHERE \"status\" = 'IN_PROGRESS';"," ```","-enum SubmissionType   { ONLINE_TEXT FILE_UPLOAD TEXT_AND_FILE NO_SUBMISSION }   // FR-1","-enum AssignmentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }                              // FR-1","-enum SubmissionStatus { SUBMITTED RETURNED }                                     // FR-1","+A `schema.prisma` comment on QuizAttempt points to it, following the attendance-migration precedent. `prisma db push` would drop it, so dev and CI must use `migrate`."," ","-Assignment (FR-2)","-  id, courseId → Course (Cascade), title, instructions (Text), submissionType, maxPoints Decimal(6,2),","-  dueAt, availableFrom?, allowLate, lateCutoffAt?, latePenaltyPercentPerDay Decimal(5,2),","-  maxLatePenaltyPercent Decimal(5,2), maxFileCount Int, allowExtraCredit Boolean @default(false),","-  status AssignmentStatus, rubricId String? @unique → Rubric, notifiedAt?, archivedAt?,","-  createdById, createdAt, updatedAt","-  @@index([courseId, dueAt])","+**JSON shapes** follow the PRD FR-2 table and are typed by the Zod discriminated union in `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts`:","+- `options`: `[{id,text}]`. Option ids are short cuids generated client-side and stable across edits.","+- `correct` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}`, `{accepted}` or `{guidance?}`.","+- `response` (per type): `{optionId}`, `{optionIds}`, `{value}` or `{text}`."," ","-AssignmentAttachment (FR-3)  assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([assignmentId, fileId])","-Rubric (FR-3)                id, criteria RubricCriterion[]","-RubricCriterion (FR-3)       id, rubricId → Rubric (Cascade), title, description?, maxPoints Decimal(6,2), order Int,","-                             levels Json  // [{label, points, description}]","+---"," ","-Submission (FR-4)","-  id, assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId → User, status SubmissionStatus, text?,","-  attemptNumber Int, submittedAt, isLate Boolean, lateDays Int,","-  rawScore Decimal(6,2)?, penaltyPercent Decimal(5,2)?, finalScore Decimal(6,2)?,","-  rubricScores Json?  // [{criterionId, points, comment}]","-  feedback?, gradedById?, gradedAt?, returnedAt?","-  @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])","-SubmissionFile (FR-4)        submissionId → Submission (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([submissionId, fileId])","-SubmissionHistory (FR-4)     id, submissionId → Submission (Cascade), attemptNumber, text?, fileIds String[], submittedAt","+## 3. Component Breakdown"," ","-GradeExemption (FR-5)        assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, reason?, createdAt; @@id([assignmentId, studentId])","-AssignmentReminder (FR-6)    assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, kind String ('due_soon'|'missing'), createdAt","-                             @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])","-```","+### 3.1 Server domain: `src/server/quiz/` (NFR-7)"," ","-Back-relations added: `Course.assignments`, `FileObject.assignmentAttachments`, `FileObject.submissionFiles`, `User.submissions`.","+| File | Kind | Exports | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `grading.ts` | **pure**, isomorphic, no Prisma client | `gradeAnswer(question, response) → {pointsAwarded: Decimal\\|null, isCorrect: boolean\\|null}`, `needsReview(question, answer)`, `normalizeShortAnswer(s)`, `computeDeadline(startedAt, timeLimitMinutes, extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)`, `attemptLimit(maxAttempts, extraAttempts)`, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`, `canPublish(questions) → string[]`, `applyScoringPolicy(policy, gradedAttempts)`, `seededShuffle(items, seed)` (string hash + mulberry32), `ANSWER_GRACE_MS = 30_000` | FR-3, FR-4, FR-5, FR-9, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-28 |","+| `serializers.ts` | pure | `toStudentQuiz`, `toStudentAttempt`, `toStudentResult`. They are built by explicit allow-list, never spread-then-delete. | NFR-1, FR-21, FR-11 |","+| `access.ts` | I/O | `assertCanAccessAttempt(user, attempt, {write})`: the owner (write allowed), a manager via `assertCanManageCourse`, or a linked PARENT (read-only, and only when `resultsVisible`). Otherwise it throws NOT_FOUND. | FR-34, NFR-5 |","+| `quiz-service.ts` | I/O | `listCourseQuizzes(user, courseId, page)` (role-shaped), `createQuiz`, `getQuizForManager`, `getQuizForStudent`, `updateQuiz` (settings + status transition + publish check + FR-29 notify), `deleteQuiz` (CONFLICT if any attempt exists), `addQuestion`, `updateQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions` (all through the **edit lock**), `regradeQuiz`, `releaseResults`, `upsertAccommodation` | FR-6..FR-11, FR-20, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31, FR-38 |","+| `attempt-service.ts` | I/O | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `getAttempt` (calls `ensureNotExpired`), `saveAnswer` (hot path), `submitAttempt(attemptId, {auto})`, `ensureNotExpired(attempt)`, `gradeAnswerManually`, `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`, `getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` | FR-12..FR-19, FR-22..FR-25, FR-32, FR-33, FR-38 |","+| `analytics.ts` | I/O + pure aggregation | `getQuizAnalytics(quizId)` returns summary stats, a 10-bucket histogram and per-question stats. `analyticsCsv(quizId)` uses `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts`. | FR-26, FR-27 |","+| `maintenance.ts` | I/O | `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)`, `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |"," ","-Model decisions:","-- **One Submission row per student.** Earlier attempts live in `SubmissionHistory` (FR-24).","-- `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` has no FK. Old attempt files **stay attached** to the same submission id and are never detached. Detaching them would let `purgeOrphanFiles` delete history bytes (B1).","-- Offline grade (FR-8, FR-34) = a Submission with `attemptNumber 0`, `text null`, no files, and `submittedAt = gradedAt`.","-- A Rubric is 1:1 with an Assignment (`rubricId @unique`). Delete the rubric in the same transaction as a hard-deleted assignment.","-- FR-14: **no column added.** The \"review grades\" banner is client-side, shown after a successful PATCH that changed `maxPoints` while `submissionCount > 0`.","+Reused as-is: `dec`/`fixed2`/`Decimal` from `@/server/assignments/grading-math` (imported, not copied); `withHandler`/`ok`/`paginated`/`AppError` (`src/server/http.ts`); `assertCanViewCourse`/`assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`); `notify`/`notifyStudentAndParents`; `audit`; `logger`; `toCsv`; `getSchoolTimezone` (NFR-7)."," ","-### 2.2 Server: `src/server/assignments/` (NFR-8)","+**Edit lock (FR-10).** `quiz-service` checks `_count.attempts > 0` before every question mutation. When attempts exist:","+- `updateQuestion` accepts only `prompt`, `explanation`, and (for SHORT_ANSWER) `correct.accepted` / `caseSensitive`.","+- `addQuestion`, `deleteQuestion`, `reorderQuestions`, and changes to `type`/`points`/options/choice `correct` throw `AppError('CONFLICT', 'Quiz has attempts — only text, explanation and accepted answers can change. Use Regrade after editing accepted answers.')`.","+- The same check sits behind the builder's disabled controls and their tooltip."," ","-| File | Contents | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| `grading-math.ts` | **Pure and isomorphic** (no Prisma client import; `Decimal` from `decimal.js`, the same package Prisma uses). `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt)`, `defaultPenalty(lateDays, perDay, max)`, `computeFinalScore(raw, pct)`, `rubricTotal(criteria)`, `maxRawScore(maxPoints, allowExtraCredit)`, `submissionChipStatus(row)` | FR-23, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-28, NFR-1, NFR-14 |","-| `assignments-service.ts` | All DB logic: visibility, CRUD, duplicate, submit, grade, return, exempt, offline grade, role-shaped lists, the serializer, and notify triggers. | FR-8, FR-12..15, FR-22, FR-24, FR-32, FR-34, FR-35, FR-42, FR-44, FR-48..58, FR-59 |","-| `reminders.ts` | `sendDueReminders(now)`: due_soon and missing passes. | FR-43, FR-45, FR-60 |","+**Regrade (FR-10, FR-38).** One `$transaction`:","+1. For every submitted attempt, re-run `gradeAnswer` on answers with `gradedById = null` (a manual grade always wins, per A8).","+2. `recomputeAttempt` each attempt.","+3. Write `audit('quiz.regrade', {attemptCount})`."," ","-`grading-math.ts` imports only `decimal.js`. The service wraps values as `Prisma.Decimal` (same class). This keeps one function for the client preview and the server value (ADR-7).","+`recomputeAttempt` (FR-25): sets `score = Σ pointsAwarded` (fixed2) and sets status to `NEEDS_GRADING` if any `needsReview`, otherwise `GRADED`. Only submitted attempts are touched."," ","-#### Single-source helpers (inside `assignments-service.ts` unless noted)","+### 3.2 Validators: `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` (FR-2, NFR-6)","+These are client-safe Zod schemas shared by the builder forms and the route handlers:","+- `quizSettingsSchema` uses `.superRefine`: `availableUntil > availableFrom`, and `timeLimitMinutes ≤ window minutes` (FR-6). Limits: timeLimit 1–300 or null, maxAttempts 1–10.","+- `questionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', …)`: points 0.5–100, 2–8 options, ≥1 correct option for MULTIPLE_CHOICE, 1–10 accepted answers, prompt as non-empty Markdown.","+- `answerResponseSchema` is a type-agnostic union, so the hot path doesn't load the Question (NFR-2). ESSAY/SHORT text is ≤ 10,000 characters.","+- `manualGradeSchema` is `{points: 0..∞ step 0.5, feedback?}`. The upper bound (question points) is checked in the service.","+- `accommodationSchema`: extraTime 0–300, extraAttempts 0–5.","+- `reorderSchema`: `{questionIds: string[]}`."," ","-| Helper | Definition | Used by |","-|---|---|---|","-| `isAssignmentVisible(a, now)` | `!a.archivedAt && isVisible({ status: a.status, publishAt: a.availableFrom }, now)`. Reuses `src/server/content/visibility.ts`: widen `Publishable.status` to `ContentStatus \\| AssignmentStatus` (same string values). | FR-13, FR-22, FR-47, FR-48, FR-50, FR-52, FR-57, FR-58, reminders |","-| `visibleWhere(now)` | The Prisma `where` equivalent: `{ archivedAt: null, OR: [{status:'PUBLISHED'}, {status:'SCHEDULED', availableFrom:{lte:now}}] }` | list queries, reminders |","-| `missingWhere(now)` | visible ∧ `dueAt < now` ∧ `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION`; per student: no Submission and no GradeExemption | FR-37, FR-35, FR-45, FR-60 |","-| `toStudentSubmission(sub)` | Removes `rawScore, penaltyPercent, finalScore, feedback, rubricScores, gradedById, gradedAt` unless `status === 'RETURNED'`. Always removes history. | FR-27, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58, NFR-4 |","-| `serializeDecimals` | Prisma.Decimal → `string` (\"14.40\") on the way out | NFR-1 (D5) |","-| `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` | **Reused** from `visibility.ts`: ADMIN, teacher or co-teacher = \"manager\" | everywhere |","-| `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz, teachingDays)` | **In `src/lib/dates.ts`**, next to `schoolNow`. Walk from tomorrow (≤7 days) to the first `isTeaching` weekday, take 23:59 local, convert with `fromZonedTime`. If no day is teaching, use tomorrow. | FR-10, NFR-9 |","-| `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` | STUDENT → self. PARENT → `studentId` must be in `ParentStudentLink`; it defaults to the only linked child. Otherwise FORBIDDEN. | FR-18, FR-38, FR-57 |","+### 3.3 API route handlers (FR-31, FR-32, NFR-5, NFR-6)","+Every handler is `withHandler` → `requireUser`/`requireRole` → Zod parse → one service call → `ok`/`paginated`. There is no logic in the handlers. `api-contracts.json` (the next sub-task) owns the exact shapes."," ","-#### Key service flows","+| Route file | Methods | Access | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `api/courses/[id]/quizzes/route.ts` | GET (role-shaped, paginated), POST | view / manage | FR-11, FR-31 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/route.ts` | GET (manager: full; student/parent: `toStudentQuiz`), PATCH, DELETE | view / manage | FR-6, FR-9, FR-29, FR-31, NFR-1 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/questions/reorder/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-7, FR-31 |","+| `api/questions/[id]/route.ts` | PATCH, DELETE | manage | FR-7, FR-10, FR-31 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/attempts/route.ts` | POST (start/resume) | STUDENT + view | FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-32 |","+| `api/attempts/[id]/route.ts` | GET | owner / linked parent / manager | FR-18, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-1 |","+| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/route.ts` | PUT | owner | FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2 |","+| `api/attempts/[id]/submit/route.ts` | POST | owner | FR-17 |","+| `api/attempts/[id]/answers/[questionId]/grade/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-24, FR-25, FR-38 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/regrade/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-10, FR-38 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/release-results/route.ts` | POST | manage | FR-20, FR-30, FR-38 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/analytics/route.ts` | GET (`?format=csv` → `text/csv`) | manage | FR-26, FR-27 |","+| `api/quizzes/[id]/accommodations/[studentId]/route.ts` | PUT | manage | FR-28, FR-38 |"," ","-**Create / update (FR-49, FR-51, FR-11, FR-12, FR-42).** One transaction: Zod parse → if a rubric is given, `rubricTotal == maxPoints`, otherwise","-VALIDATION_ERROR `Rubric totals {sum} points but the assignment is worth {maxPoints}.` → SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > new Date()` (checked in the service,","-because Zod has no server clock, NFR-2) → upsert rubric and criteria → write the assignment → `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, 'assignment', id)`. On PATCH,","-diff the attachments: removed files are `detachFiles` (the purge reclaims them). **After commit**, if the assignment is now visible → `publishOnce(id)`.","+Error mapping: CONFLICT (409) covers writing after the deadline, the edit lock, deleting with attempts, the attempt limit, and a quiz that isn't open. VALIDATION_ERROR (400) is for Zod failures. NOT_FOUND hides resources the user can't access (NFR-5, NFR-6)."," ","-**`publishOnce(id)` (FR-42).** `updateMany({ where:{ id, notifiedAt:null }, data:{ notifiedAt: now } })`. Only when `count === 1`, call `notify()` for","-`assignment.published` to ACTIVE-enrolled students. Called from: create/PATCH after commit, and from the student/parent list read paths (FR-48, FR-57)","-for SCHEDULED assignments that have become visible with `notifiedAt` null. On GET it is fire-and-forget (`void publishOnce(id).catch(logger.error)`) and never fails the read.","+### 3.4 Pages and UI: `src/app/(app)/...` (NFR-4: MUI only, mui-mcp lookup before each component)"," ","-**Delete (FR-51).** If there are 0 submissions → detach the attachments, then delete the assignment and its rubric (cascade). Otherwise → set `archivedAt = now`. Audit `assignment.delete|archive`.","-","-**Duplicate (FR-15).** `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target course, then one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows.","-Attachments: `readFile` → `saveFile` → a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), because FileObject holds one context (B2). Status is DRAFT and `notifiedAt` is null.","-Same `dueAt`; `availableFrom` and `lateCutoffAt` keep their offsets from dueAt (FR-15 default).","-","-**Submit (FR-22..FR-24, FR-53, FR-60).** `now = new Date()` on the server. Checks, in order (first failure wins):","-1. Assignment exists and `isAssignmentVisible` → otherwise NOT_FOUND.","-2. `role === 'STUDENT'` and ACTIVE-enrolled in the course → otherwise FORBIDDEN.","-3. Not exempt; `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR.","-4. Deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR `The deadline has passed and late submissions are closed.`","-5. Content matches the type: text for ONLINE_TEXT, ≥1 file for FILE_UPLOAD, ≥1 of either for TEXT_AND_FILE. Also `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`.","-6. Each file has `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'`, and is unattached **or** already attached to this submission. The service checks `context` before calling `attachFiles`, because `attachFiles` does not (B1).","-","-Then, in one transaction:","-- **No row:** create the Submission (`attemptNumber 1`, `isLate`, `lateDays` from `grading-math`).","-- **Row with `status = SUBMITTED`**, including an attempt-0 offline row (D9): insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear all grade fields, and replace the `SubmissionFile` rows. Old files stay attached.","-- **Row with `RETURNED`:** CONFLICT `This submission has been returned and can no longer be changed.`","-","-`attachFiles(tx, user, newFileIds, 'submission', submission.id)`. A P2002 from two concurrent first submits → retry once as a resubmit.","-","-**Grade (FR-56, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-32 \"Save & return\").** `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade { rawScore?, penaltyPercent, feedback?, rubricScores?, return?: boolean }`.","-- If the assignment has a rubric: `rubricScores` are required, every criterion must be scored exactly once, `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints`, and **the server sets `rawScore = Σ points`** (any client raw value is ignored, D7).","-- Otherwise: `0 ≤ rawScore ≤ maxRawScore` (×1.2 when `allowExtraCredit`). Extra credit applies to rawScore only.","-- `0 ≤ penaltyPercent ≤ 100`. `finalScore = computeFinalScore`. Set `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. The status stays SUBMITTED.","-- `return: true` → in the same transaction, set `status RETURNED`, `returnedAt`, then notify after commit (D6: a single round trip). Audit `submission.grade` (+ `submission.return`).","-","-**Bulk return (FR-32).** `POST /api/assignments/:id/return { submissionIds? }`. The default set is `gradedAt != null AND status = SUBMITTED`. A supplied id that is ungraded is","-skipped and reported in the response (`{returned, skipped}`). One `updateMany`, then one `notifyStudentAndParents` per student (FR-44), plus **one audit row per submission** (FR-59), so","-a per-record audit trail is possible.","-","-**Offline grade (FR-34, FR-8).** The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. If a submission already exists → CONFLICT (grade that one instead). Create the attempt-0 row","-with the grade fields and penalty 0, using the same validation as Grade. Audit `submission.grade_offline`.","-","-**Exempt (FR-35).** PUT = `upsert` GradeExemption, DELETE = `deleteMany` (both idempotent). Audit `assignment.exempt|unexempt`. The effects come only through","-`missingWhere`, the submit rule 3, and reminders. The PRD-11 \"exclude\" flag **is** the row itself (NFR-15).","-","-### 2.3 Maintenance: `reminders.ts` (FR-43, FR-45, FR-60)","-","-`sendDueReminders(now)` is called on **every** request to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, outside the daily `lastPurgeAt` block, in its own try/catch with logger (B8).","-","-| Pass | Assignment window | Targets | Notify |","+| Route / file | Server/client | Contents | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| due_soon | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ (now, now+24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | ACTIVE-enrolled, no Submission, no GradeExemption | `assignment.due_soon` → student |","-| missing | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ [now−8d, now−24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | same | `assignment.missing` → linked parents only, via `notify()` |","+| `src/config/course-tabs.ts` | config | One entry, `{key:'quizzes', label:'Quizzes', href: id => /courses/${id}/quizzes, roles: ALL_ROLES}` | FR-11 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/page.tsx` + `CourseQuizzesView.tsx` | server + client | Teacher: DataTable (status, window, attempts, avg, Needs grading) + \"New quiz\". Student: four sections (Upcoming / Available now (Start/Resume) / Completed (score if visible) / Missed). Parent: completed results, read-only, per linked child. | FR-11, FR-33 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/new/page.tsx` | server | Creates a DRAFT quiz with defaults and redirects to edit (no separate form) | FR-6 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/page.tsx` + `QuizBuilder.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx`, `QuestionList.tsx`, `QuestionEditor.tsx` | server + client | Settings (DateTimePicker, Switch, Select, TextField). The question list is a dnd-kit `SortableContext` of MUI Cards, with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback. Each type has its own editor (options with a correct Radio/Checkbox, an accepted-answers list, guidance). A running points total. Publish button with `canPublish` errors. Lock banner + disabled controls when attempts exist, plus a Regrade button. Accommodations section (DataTable of enrolled students). The prompt uses MarkdownEditor + FileUpload with context `'quiz'`. | FR-6..FR-10, FR-28, FR-39, NFR-9 |","+| `quizzes/[quizId]/take/page.tsx` + `QuizPlayer.tsx`, `useAutosave.ts` | server + client | Start screen (instructions, counts, points, limit, attempts used/allowed, ConfirmDialog on Start). The player has a sticky header (title, mm:ss timer from `deadlineAt`, red under 2 min, `aria-live=\"assertive\"` announcing at 5:00 and 1:00), a Chip status pill, LinearProgress, and RadioGroup/FormGroup+Checkbox/TextField per type. Layout is all-on-one-page, or one question per page with a navigator Button grid (answered / unanswered / flagged; flags stored client-side only). Submit uses ConfirmDialog showing the unanswered count. `mode=\"preview\"` is used by the builder. | FR-8, FR-12..FR-17, FR-19, NFR-3 |","+| `quizzes/[quizId]/attempts/[attemptId]/page.tsx` | server | Result view built from `toStudentResult`: score, %, per-question correctness, response and feedback, plus correct answers/explanations if allowed. Otherwise it shows \"Submitted — results will be available later.\" Also used by parents and teachers. | FR-20, FR-21 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/grade/page.tsx` + `QuizGradingWorkspace.tsx` | server + client | Tabs: By student / By question. Points TextField (step 0.5, max = question points) + feedback, with override allowed on auto-graded answers. | FR-24, FR-25 |","+| `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/analytics/page.tsx` + `QuizAnalytics.tsx` | server + client | StatCards (attempts, avg, median, high, low, avg time), x-charts `BarChart` with 10 buckets, a per-question DataTable with option distribution (most-chosen wrong option highlighted), and a CSV link | FR-26, FR-27 |"," ","-Idempotency: `createMany({ data: candidates, skipDuplicates: true })` cannot report *which* rows were inserted, so **insert per (assignment, student) with `create` and catch P2002**,","-and notify only on success. The Postgres unique key makes this safe across concurrent dispatchers. Candidate counts are small (one course × roster).","-`// ponytail: missing pass only looks back 8 days; widen or add a cursor if the dispatcher can be down longer.`","+Server pages call `requirePageRole` and the course/attempt access helpers before fetching (NFR-5). They pass only serializer output to client components (NFR-1)."," ","-### 2.4 Reuse map (NFR-11)","+**`useAutosave(attemptId, mode)` (FR-15, ADR-4).**","+- Each question gets an 800 ms `setTimeout` debounce, then `PUT /answers/:questionId`.","+- On network failure or 5xx, the latest response per question is written to the `localStorage['quiz-attempt:<id>']` map, and a 5 s `setInterval` drains it.","+- A 409 stops the queue, clears storage and routes to the result page. A 2xx removes that key.","+- The status pill reads `Saving…`, `All answers saved`, or `Offline — answers saved on this device` (shown when the queue is non-empty).","+- On mount, any queued answers are merged over server answers before rendering, so a reload loses nothing (FR-19, AC-2)."," ","-| Existing | Where | Used for |","-|---|---|---|","-| `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` | `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | every handler and page (NFR-5) |","-| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` | course-scoped routes |","-| `assertCanViewStudent` | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-58 |","-| `isVisible`, `canSeeDrafts` | `src/server/content/visibility.ts` (type widened) | FR-13, manager checks |","-| `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination`, `AppError` | `src/server/http.ts` | NFR-7 envelopes and errors |","-| `audit()` | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-59 |","-| `notify()`, `notifyStudentAndParents()`, `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | `src/server/notifications/` | FR-42..FR-46 |","-| `attachFiles`, `detachFiles`, `POST /api/files`, `GET /api/files/:id?inline=1`, `registerBuiltInContexts`, `storage.ts` | `src/server/files/`, `src/server/storage.ts` | FR-9, FR-15, FR-20, FR-29, FR-47, FR-53 |","-| `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | `src/lib/dates.ts` | FR-19, FR-25, NFR-9 |","-| `ConfirmDialog`, `DataTable`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `useToast`, `FormField`, `DateDisplay` | `src/components/` | FR-17, FR-21, lists, forms |","-| `courseTabs`, `studentTabs`, `navigation` | `src/config/` | FR-16, FR-40, FR-41 |","-| `logger` | `src/lib/logger.ts` | NFR-12 |","+### 3.5 Integrations into existing modules"," ","-### 2.5 New shared UI components (blocker 1, ADR-5)","-","-| Component | Build | Reqs |","+| Existing file | Change | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|","-| `MarkdownView` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema). Elements map to MUI `Typography`, `Link`, `Table*`, `List*`, `Box component=\"pre\"`. | NFR-10, FR-19, FR-29, FR-26 |","-| `MarkdownEditor` | MUI `TextField multiline` + `Tabs` (Write / Preview → `MarkdownView`). Controlled `value`/`onChange`, plus `maxLength`. | FR-9, FR-20, FR-30 |","-| `FileUpload` | MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`. POSTs each file to `/api/files` with `context`. Props `{context, max, value: FileRef[], onChange}`. A `LinearProgress` per file, plus remove. | FR-9, FR-20 |","-| `FileList` | MUI `List` of links to `/api/files/:id`. Optional `preview` prop: `<img>` for `image/*`, `<iframe>` for `application/pdf`, both via `?inline=1` (D11). | FR-19, FR-25, FR-29 |","+| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `quiz.published` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT, defaultEmail false) and `quiz.results_released` (ACADEMIC, STUDENT + PARENT, defaultEmail true, A5) | FR-29, FR-30 |","+| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | `register('quiz', quizResolver)`. The resolver allows a course manager, or a course viewer when the quiz is PUBLISHED (images sit only in prompts, which students already see) | FR-39, NFR-5 |","+| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | After `sendDueReminders(now)`, add `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)`, each in its own try/catch + `logger.error`, on every call | FR-18, FR-30, FR-35 |","+| `prisma/seed.ts` | Three seed quizzes, idempotent by (courseId, title). Scores are computed with `grading.ts` | FR-36 |","+| `prisma/schema.prisma` + migration | §2 | FR-1, FR-19 |"," ","-### 2.6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` (FR-7)","+---"," ","-`assignmentInput` (FR-7 limits; `.superRefine`: `lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum = maxPoints using `rubricTotal`), `rubricCriterionInput`,","-`submissionInput {text? ≤50k, fileIds ≤10}`, `gradeInput {rawScore?, penaltyPercent 0–100, feedback? ≤10k, rubricScores?, return?}`,","-`offlineGradeInput`, `bulkReturnInput`, `duplicateInput {courseIds min 1}`, `meAssignmentsQuery {studentId?, tab?, courseId?}`.","-Decimals are accepted as `z.union([z.number(), z.string()])` and converted to Decimal in the service. No request schema has a timestamp field except","-`dueAt`/`availableFrom`/`lateCutoffAt`, which are authoring data, not \"now\" (NFR-2).","+## 4. Data Flow"," ","-### 2.7 Route handlers (thin: Zod → service → envelope; NFR-7)","+### 4.1 Build and publish (FR-6..FR-9, FR-29)","+1. Teacher opens New. The server creates a DRAFT quiz and redirects to `/edit`.","+2. Settings and question edits go through PATCH/POST. Each is Zod-validated on both client and server, and question mutations pass the edit-lock check.","+3. On Publish, the client sends `PATCH {status:'PUBLISHED'}`. The service runs `canPublish(questions)` and throws VALIDATION_ERROR with the list of problems if any. Otherwise it runs `updateMany({where:{id, status:'DRAFT'}, data:{status:'PUBLISHED'}})`.","+4. If that update changed a row (count = 1), the service calls `notify('quiz.published')` for ACTIVE enrollees after commit (A9)."," ","-| Route | Auth | Service fn | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | user + view course | `listCourseAssignments` (manager shape with `groupBy` counts / student shape) | FR-48, FR-17, FR-18 |","-| `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | manage course | `createAssignment` | FR-49 |","-| `GET /api/assignments/[id]` | view (NOT_FOUND for invisible to non-manager) | `getAssignment` (+ own submission, `serverNow`) | FR-50, FR-19 |","-| `PATCH` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]` | manage | `updateAssignment` / `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | FR-51, FR-14 |","-| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/duplicate` | manage source + each target | `duplicateAssignment` | FR-15 |","-| `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | manage | `listGradingRoster` (every ACTIVE enrollee; `pageSize` ≤100) | FR-54, FR-28 |","-| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | STUDENT | `submit` | FR-53, FR-22..24 |","-| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/return` | manage | `bulkReturn` | FR-32, FR-44 |","-| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/grade-offline` | manage | `gradeOffline` | FR-34, FR-8 |","-| `PUT` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]/exemptions/[studentId]` | manage | `setExemption` | FR-35 |","-| `GET /api/submissions/[id]` | submitter, linked parent, or manager; history for managers only | `getSubmission` | FR-55, FR-29, NFR-3 |","-| `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade` | manage | `gradeSubmission` | FR-56, FR-30..32, FR-36 |","-| `GET /api/me/assignments` | any user; role switch | `listMyAssignments` | FR-57, FR-37..39 |","-| `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments` | `assertCanViewStudent` | `listStudentAssignments` | FR-58, FR-41 |","+### 4.2 Start or resume (FR-12, FR-13, FR-19, FR-23, FR-28)","+```","+POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts  (STUDENT)","+  assertCanViewCourse → quiz PUBLISHED && availableFrom ≤ now < availableUntil, else CONFLICT","+  existing IN_PROGRESS? → ensureNotExpired → still IN_PROGRESS ? return it (resume)","+  count(attempts) ≥ attemptLimit(maxAttempts, accommodation.extraAttempts) → CONFLICT","+  $transaction:","+    id = cuid()                         // generated up front so the shuffle seed is known","+    order = shuffleQuestions ? seededShuffle(questionIds, id) : questionIds by `order`","+    deadlineAt = computeDeadline(now, timeLimitMinutes, accommodation.extraTimeMinutes, availableUntil)","+    create {id, attemptNumber: count+1, questionOrder: order, deadlineAt, maxScore: Σ points}","+  on P2002 (partial index or attemptNumber unique) → re-read IN_PROGRESS attempt and return it","+→ toStudentAttempt(attempt, questions with seededShuffle(options, attempt.id) if shuffleOptions)","+```","+Option order isn't stored. It is recomputed from the `attempt.id` seed on every load, which makes it deterministic (FR-13). Two tabs get the same attempt id (FR-19)."," ","-Shared response conventions for `arch-api-contracts`: Decimals are **strings**. Timestamps are ISO UTC strings. Student/parent submission objects","-always pass through `toStudentSubmission`. FR-58: a viewer who manages the course gets the full fields, everyone else gets the serializer (D8).","-`/api/me/assignments` for ADMIN = \"To grade\" across all courses (intake default).","+### 4.3 Autosave hot path (FR-15, FR-16, NFR-2)","+```","+PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId   body {response}","+  1 query : attempt {studentId, status, deadlineAt, questionOrder}     (no Quiz/Question load)","+  studentId ≠ user → NOT_FOUND;  questionId ∉ questionOrder → NOT_FOUND","+  status ≠ IN_PROGRESS → CONFLICT","+  now > deadlineAt + 30s → submitAttempt(id,{auto:true}); throw CONFLICT('Time is up')","+  1 query : quizAnswer.upsert({attemptId_questionId}, {response})","+→ { data: { questionId, savedAt } }      // no grading data (NFR-1)","+```","+The path is two indexed statements, well under the 50 ms budget at 300 concurrent students. It is idempotent, so localStorage replays are safe."," ","-### 2.8 Pages (`src/app/(app)/…`)","+### 4.4 Submit, auto-submit and grading (FR-17, FR-18, FR-24, FR-25)","+```","+submitAttempt(attemptId, {auto}):   $transaction","+  claimed = updateMany({id, status:'IN_PROGRESS'} → {status:'SUBMITTED', submittedAt: now, autoSubmitted: auto})","+  claimed.count = 0 → return current attempt (already submitted: idempotent, race-safe)","+  load questions + answers; for every questionId in questionOrder:","+     answer missing → create {response:null}","+     {pointsAwarded,isCorrect} = gradeAnswer(question, response)     // ESSAY → null,null; unanswered → 0,false","+  recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)   → score = Σ, status = NEEDS_GRADING | GRADED","+```","+Callers:","+- the submit POST (`auto:false`)","+- the deadline branch of saveAnswer","+- `ensureNotExpired` on GET attempt, start/resume, the player page and the teacher grade/list loads (FR-18, lazy)","+- `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` (FR-18, batch)"," ","-| Page | Notes | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/page.tsx` | Manager: `DataTable` (title, due, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted, Grade button; Archived chip). Student/parent: grouped `List` (Upcoming / Past due / Submitted / Returned). Parent child selector when more than one linked child is enrolled. | FR-16..18, FR-52 |","-| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/new/page.tsx` + `[assignmentId]/edit/page.tsx` | One shared `AssignmentForm` (react-hook-form + the Zod schema). Defaults: dueAt = `nextTeachingDayDueAt` (computed server-side, passed as a prop), maxPoints 100, FILE_UPLOAD, maxFileCount 3, allowLate off (NFR-16). Rubric builder: `@dnd-kit/sortable` with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, and a live sum error. Buttons: Save draft / Publish / Schedule. Edit warns per FR-14. \"Duplicate to other courses\" dialog with an `Autocomplete` of managed courses. | FR-9..15 |","-| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/page.tsx` | MarkdownView instructions, FileList, due and late-policy summary, rubric table, countdown under 48 h (offset from `serverNow`, display only). Submission panel by type, `localStorage` draft key `assignment:{id}:{userId}` (cleared on success), ConfirmDialog before POST, receipt via `formatInSchoolTz`, returned results, or \"Submitted — awaiting grading\". Parent: read-only, no panel. | FR-19..27 |","-| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/page.tsx` | Left: `List` + status `Chip`s from `submissionChipStatus`, filter, sort by name or time. Main: MarkdownView text, FileList with preview, history `Select`. Form: rubric `ToggleButtonGroup`s that auto-sum, prefilled penalty (`defaultPenalty`), live final score (`computeFinalScore`), MarkdownEditor feedback. Buttons Save / Save & return / Return all graded / Grade without submission / Exempt toggle. J/K/Ctrl+Enter keydown handler that skips J/K in input/textarea/contenteditable, with a visible shortcut hint. **NFR-3:** a plain `Map<id, Submission>` cache; after each selection, prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id`. | FR-28..36, NFR-3, NFR-16, NFR-17 |","-| `assignments/page.tsx` | STUDENT: `Tabs` Upcoming/Missing/Submitted/Returned + course filter. PARENT: child selector, same view, read-only. TEACHER/ADMIN: \"To grade\" list, oldest first. | FR-37..39 |","-| `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx` | Per-student list (FR-58). Reachable by URL only (blocker 5). | FR-41 |","+An unanswered ESSAY gets `pointsAwarded = 0` and still needs review: the A8 predicate keys on `gradedById`, so the teacher confirms it."," ","-### 2.9 Config and registrations","+Manual grading:","+1. `PUT …/grade` validates `points ≤ question.points` and `points % 0.5 = 0`, then sets `pointsAwarded`, `isCorrect = points == question.points`, `feedback` and `gradedById`.","+2. It runs `recomputeAttempt`, which sets GRADED when nothing still needs review (FR-25), and writes `audit('quizAnswer.grade')` after commit (FR-38).","+3. If the attempt became GRADED and the quiz is IMMEDIATELY, nothing is sent (FR-30)."," ","-- `src/config/course-tabs.ts`: `{ key:'assignments', label:'Assignments', href: id => /courses/${id}/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES }` (FR-16).","-- `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Assignments` → `/assignments`, roles `[STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER, ADMIN]` (FR-40; ADMIN added because the To-grade default applies to ADMIN).","-- `src/config/student-tabs.ts`: `assignments` entry (FR-41).","-- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: four keys, category ACADEMIC (FR-46):","-  `assignment.published` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.due_soon` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.returned` [STUDENT, PARENT] email false · `assignment.missing` [PARENT] email **true**.","-- `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (FR-47), registered in `registerBuiltInContexts`:","-  - `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course → `assertCanViewCourse` → `canSeeDrafts || isAssignmentVisible`.","-  - `submissionResolver`: load the submission and course → allow `studentId === user.id`, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), or `canSeeDrafts`. Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10).","-- `next.config.js`: D11 header split.","-- `package.json`: `overrides[\"@mui/x-internals\"] = \"9.1.0\"` (ADR-2). `vitest.config.ts` import fix (ADR-3).","-- `prisma/seed.ts`: FR-61 block, idempotent: look up courses by code (skip if missing), upsert by `(courseId, title)`, Decimals as strings, no file bytes.","+### 4.5 Results visibility and notification (FR-20, FR-21, FR-30)","+`resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)`:","+- the attempt must be submitted","+- **IMMEDIATELY**: true","+- **AFTER_CLOSE**: `now ≥ availableUntil`","+- **MANUAL**: `resultsReleasedAt != null`"," ","----","+Scores also need status GRADED to display a final score. A NEEDS_GRADING attempt shows \"awaiting grading\" for the pending questions."," ","-## 3. Data Flow","+- **MANUAL release:** `POST /release-results` runs `updateMany({id, resultsVisibility:'MANUAL', resultsReleasedAt:null} → now)`. If count = 1, it calls `notifyStudentAndParents` for students with a submitted attempt, then `audit('quiz.release_results')`. A repeat call is a no-op.","+- **AFTER_CLOSE (maintenance):** `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased(now)` finds quizzes where `resultsVisibility = AFTER_CLOSE AND availableUntil ≤ now AND resultsReleasedAt IS NULL`. For each one it claims with `updateMany(... resultsReleasedAt: null → now)`, and only when count = 1 does it notify. That makes it idempotent across concurrent cron calls (A6, FR-35).","+- **IMMEDIATELY:** no notification."," ","-**Author → publish.** Teacher form → `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments` → validate (Zod + rubric sum + schedule time) → tx (rubric, assignment, attachments) → commit → `publishOnce` → `notify(assignment.published)` to enrolled students.","+### 4.6 Maintenance (FR-18, FR-35)","+`autoSubmitExpiredAttempts(now)` finds attempts with `status = IN_PROGRESS AND deadlineAt < now − 30s`, takes up to 200 per call, and runs `submitAttempt(id, {auto:true})` on each. The per-call cap keeps a cron tick bounded; the next tick and the lazy path cover any remainder."," ","-**Scheduled becomes visible.** No job. A student/parent list read evaluates `visibleWhere(now)`. Any newly visible assignment with `notifiedAt` null → fire-and-forget `publishOnce` (the atomic guard sends exactly once).","+### 4.7 Score export to PRD-11 (FR-22, FR-33)","+`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` returns `{score, maxScore, percent, isPractice, attemptsCounted} | null`, computed by `applyScoringPolicy` over GRADED attempts only. HIGHEST takes the max percent, LATEST takes the latest `submittedAt`, AVERAGE takes the Decimal mean, all with fixed2. It returns null when there are no GRADED attempts. There is no endpoint; PRD-11 imports it."," ","-**Submit.** Student uploads files → `POST /api/files {context:'submission'}` (unattached, owner-only readable) → `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text, fileIds}` → the six checks in order → tx (history snapshot if resubmitting, upsert submission, file rows, `attachFiles` → contextId = submission.id) → receipt.","-From then on, the files are readable through `submissionResolver` only by the student, their parents, and course managers.","+### 4.8 Analytics (FR-26, FR-27)","+- **Input:** submitted attempts with their answers, aggregated in memory (class sizes are small).","+- **Summary stats:** count, mean, median, max, min, and mean of `submittedAt − startedAt`.","+- **Histogram:** 10 buckets by percent, with 100% placed in the last bucket.","+- **Per question:** % with `isCorrect = true`, average `pointsAwarded`, and for choice types an option-id count, with the most-chosen wrong option marked.","+- **CSV:** `toCsv` rows of student, attemptNumber, score, then one points column per question in quiz order."," ","-**Grade → return.** Grader page loads the roster (FR-54) → selects a student → `GET /api/submissions/:id` (cached; next and previous prefetched) → form computes the preview with `grading-math` → `PUT …/grade {…, return?}` → server recomputes everything authoritatively → tx → audit → (if return) `notifyStudentAndParents(assignment.returned, \"Course: Title — 18/20\")`.","-Student `GET` now gets the grade fields, because the serializer unlocks on RETURNED.","-","-**Reminders.** The external caller hits `/api/internal/email/dispatch` → `dispatchEmails` → `sendDueReminders(now)` → due_soon and missing candidate queries → per-row `AssignmentReminder.create` (P2002 = already sent) → `notify`.","-","-**Privacy boundaries (NFR-4), three layers:** (1) query scoping: student and parent paths always filter `studentId ∈ resolveViewedStudent`; (2) `toStudentSubmission` serializer; (3) the file resolvers for `/api/files/:id`.","-"," ---"," ","-## 4. Testing layout (NFR-13, NFR-14)","+## 5. Security and access (NFR-1, NFR-5)"," ","-- `tests/unit/assignments/grading-math.test.ts`: lateDays (exactly 24 h = 1, 24 h + 1 ms = 2, across spring-forward and fall-back in `Europe/London`), penalty cap, final score (18 @ 20 % = \"14.40\", half-up at .005), rubric sum, chip status. Also `nextTeachingDayDueAt` across DST.","-- `tests/integration/assignments/*.test.ts`: resubmission history (files kept attached), RETURNED refuses resubmit, return flow plus serializer unlock, reminder idempotency (call twice → one notification), exemption removes from missing and blocks submit, NO_SUBMISSION excluded, file resolver denies another student (AC-10).","-- `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` (`bypassCSP: true`): teacher creates → student submits a file → teacher grades with a rubric and returns → student sees feedback; parent sees the missing list.","+| Actor | Can |","+|---|---|","+| ADMIN / course teacher | All manage routes for their courses, any attempt in those courses |","+| STUDENT (ACTIVE enrolled) | List and take PUBLISHED quizzes; read and write **own** attempts; results only via `toStudentResult` |","+| PARENT (linked to an enrolled student) | Read-only: completed results of linked children, only when `resultsVisible` |"," ","+- Student-path Prisma queries never `select` `correct` or `explanation`. The serializers add those fields back only when `resultsVisible && showCorrectAnswers` (defence in depth).","+- The answer-PUT response carries no grading data.","+- Inaccessible ids return NOT_FOUND, not FORBIDDEN, so their existence isn't revealed.","+- Test: a serializer unit test walks the output recursively and asserts no `correct` key exists before visibility (AC-7).","+"," ---"," ","-## 5. Decisions log","+## 6. Testing map (NFR-8, ADR-8)"," ","-| # | Decision | Reqs |","+| Level | Target | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|","-| D1 | Build the minimal MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor, FileUpload and FileList in `src/components/` | FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29, FR-30 |","-| D2 | Pin `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 via overrides; fallbacks are MUI `Table` and `datetime-local` | FR-17, FR-9 |","-| D3 | Fix the vitest import; e2e uses bypassCSP | NFR-13, NFR-14 |","-| D4 | Register the student tab and page; no tab bar | FR-41 |","-| D5 | Decimals are strings in JSON | NFR-1 |","-| D6 | \"Save & return\" = `PUT …/grade {return:true}`, one transaction | FR-32 |","-| D7 | With a rubric, the server sets `rawScore = Σ rubric points` | FR-30, FR-36 |","-| D8 | FR-58: managers get the full fields, other viewers get the serializer | FR-58, FR-27 |","-| D9 | An online submit over an unreturned offline grade = a resubmission | FR-8, FR-24 |","-| D10 | The missing pass looks back 8 days (`ponytail:` note) | FR-45 |","-| D11 | `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` only for `/api/files/:id`, so PDF iframes work | FR-29 |","-| D12 | Intake defaults adopted: FR-15 same dueAt plus offsets; FR-52 archived = hidden from students/parents, closed, no reminders, visible to managers; FR-60 NO_SUBMISSION never missing or reminded; FR-10 weekdays only; FR-36 extra credit raw-only; ADMIN /assignments = To grade | FR-10, FR-15, FR-36, FR-39, FR-52, FR-60 |","-| D13 | Resubmission after RETURNED → CONFLICT (409). Deadline and content failures → VALIDATION_ERROR | FR-22, FR-24 |","-| D14 | One audit row per affected submission, including bulk return | FR-59 |","-| D15 | FR-14 banner is client-side; no schema column | FR-14 |","+| Unit (Vitest, no DB) | `gradeAnswer` per type, incl. the FR-2 example ({A,B} → 0, {A} → 2) and `' Photosynthesis '`; `needsReview`; `computeDeadline` (timed, untimed, extra time, capped by availableUntil); `attemptLimit`; `applyScoringPolicy` ×3; `seededShuffle` determinism; `resultsVisible` ×3; `canPublish`; serializers (no `correct` key) | FR-3, FR-4, FR-13, FR-20, FR-22, FR-23, FR-9, NFR-1 |","+| Integration (Vitest + test DB) | Autosave returns 409 after deadline + 30 s and the attempt is auto-submitted; GET auto-submits an expired attempt; regrade changes auto-graded answers but not manual ones; concurrent start returns one attempt; double submit is a no-op | FR-16, FR-18, FR-10, FR-19, FR-17 |","+| E2E (Playwright, 1 spec) | Teacher builds a 4-question quiz (incl. an essay) and publishes it → student starts, answers, `page.reload()`, answers persist, submits → teacher grades the essay → student sees results. Includes an axe check on the player | NFR-8, NFR-3, FR-15 |"," ","+`npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test` must stay green. QA's banned-import scan covers NFR-4.","+"," ---"," ","-## 6. Requirements Traceability","+## 7. Requirements Traceability"," ","-| Req | Design element |","+| Req | Design element(s) |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | §2.1 enums in migration `add_assignments` |","-| FR-2 | §2.1 `Assignment` (+allowExtraCredit, notifiedAt, archivedAt, rubricId @unique, index) |","-| FR-3 | §2.1 `AssignmentAttachment`, `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` |","-| FR-4 | §2.1 `Submission`, `SubmissionFile`, `SubmissionHistory` |","-| FR-5 | §2.1 `GradeExemption` |","-| FR-6 | §2.1 `AssignmentReminder`; §2.3 idempotency |","-| FR-7 | §2.6 `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` |","-| FR-8 | §2.1 attempt-0 row; §2.2 Offline grade; D9 |","-| FR-9 | §2.8 `AssignmentForm`; §2.5 MarkdownEditor, FileUpload; D2 |","-| FR-10 | §2.2 `nextTeachingDayDueAt` in `src/lib/dates.ts` |","-| FR-11 | §2.8 rubric builder; §2.2 Create (server rubric-sum check); §2.6 superRefine |","-| FR-12 | §2.8 three buttons; §2.2 Create (SCHEDULED future check) |","-| FR-13 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` / `visibleWhere` (read-time, no job) |","-| FR-14 | §2.8 edit warning; D15 |","-| FR-15 | §2.2 Duplicate; §2.7 duplicate route |","-| FR-16 | §2.9 courseTabs entry |","-| FR-17 | §2.8 manager DataTable; §2.7 FR-48 manager shape; D2 |","-| FR-18 | §2.8 student/parent grouped list; `resolveViewedStudent` |","-| FR-19 | §2.8 assignment page; §2.5 MarkdownView, FileList |","-| FR-20 | §2.8 submission panel (localStorage draft); §2.5 FileUpload |","-| FR-21 | §2.8 ConfirmDialog before POST |","-| FR-22 | §2.2 Submit checks 1–4 |","-| FR-23 | §2.2 `grading-math.lateDays` |","-| FR-24 | §2.2 Submit transaction (history, clear grade, files kept) |","-| FR-25 | §2.8 receipt via `formatInSchoolTz` |","-| FR-26 | §2.8 returned results view |","-| FR-27 | §2.2 `toStudentSubmission` serializer |","-| FR-28 | §2.8 grading left panel; `submissionChipStatus` |","-| FR-29 | §2.8 grading main panel; §2.5 FileList preview; D11 |","-| FR-30 | §2.8 grading form; `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`; D7 |","-| FR-31 | §2.2 `grading-math.computeFinalScore` (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP) |","-| FR-32 | §2.2 Grade (`return:true`) and Bulk return; D6 |","-| FR-33 | §2.8 keydown handler |","-| FR-34 | §2.2 Offline grade; §2.7 grade-offline route |","-| FR-35 | §2.2 Exempt; `missingWhere`; Submit check 3 |","-| FR-36 | §2.2 Grade validation; `maxRawScore` |","-| FR-37 | §2.8 `/assignments` STUDENT; `missingWhere` |","-| FR-38 | §2.8 `/assignments` PARENT; `resolveViewedStudent` |","-| FR-39 | §2.8 `/assignments` TEACHER/ADMIN To grade |","-| FR-40 | §2.9 navigation entry |","-| FR-41 | §2.9 studentTabs entry; §2.8 students page; blocker 5 |","-| FR-42 | §2.2 `publishOnce` (atomic notifiedAt) |","-| FR-43 | §2.3 due_soon pass |","-| FR-44 | §2.2 Grade/Bulk return → `notifyStudentAndParents` |","-| FR-45 | §2.3 missing pass (parents only) |","-| FR-46 | §2.9 NOTIFICATION_TYPES keys |","-| FR-47 | §2.9 `assignmentResolver`, `submissionResolver` |","-| FR-48 | §2.7 `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` |","-| FR-49 | §2.7 `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments`; §2.2 Create |","-| FR-50 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]` |","-| FR-51 | §2.7 PATCH/DELETE; §2.2 Delete |","-| FR-52 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` (`!archivedAt`); D12 |","-| FR-53 | §2.7 POST submissions; §2.2 Submit checks 5–6 |","-| FR-54 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` |","-| FR-55 | §2.7 `GET /api/submissions/[id]` |","-| FR-56 | §2.7 `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade`; §2.2 Grade |","-| FR-57 | §2.7 `GET /api/me/assignments` |","-| FR-58 | §2.7 `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments`; D8 |","-| FR-59 | §2.2 audit calls; D14 |","-| FR-60 | §2.2 `missingWhere`, Submit check 3; §2.3 filters; D12 |","-| FR-61 | §2.9 seed block |","-| NFR-1 | §2.2 `grading-math` (Decimal); D5 strings in JSON |","-| NFR-2 | §2.2 server `now` everywhere; §2.6 no client clock fields |","-| NFR-3 | §2.8 grading `Map` cache plus next/prev prefetch |","-| NFR-4 | §3 privacy boundaries (scoping, serializer, resolvers) |","-| NFR-5 | §2.7 auth column; §2.4 reuse of require*/assertCan* |","-| NFR-6 | §1.1 blocker 8; §2.5/§2.8 MUI-only components |","-| NFR-7 | §2.7 thin handlers via `http.ts` helpers |","-| NFR-8 | §2.2 `src/server/assignments/`; §2.6; §2.7; §2.8 |","-| NFR-9 | §2.2 UTC lateDays, `fromZonedTime` default; §4 DST tests |","-| NFR-10 | §2.5 MarkdownView |","-| NFR-11 | §2.4 reuse map |","-| NFR-12 | §2.3 / §2.2 `logger` in catch paths |","-| NFR-13 | §1.1 blockers 2–3; ADR-2, ADR-3 |","-| NFR-14 | §4 testing layout |","-| NFR-15 | §1.1 blockers 4–5 (no CSP or tab-bar work); D12; exemption = row only |","-| NFR-16 | §2.8 form defaults; keyboard grading |","-| NFR-17 | §2.8 dnd-kit Up/Down fallback, shortcut hint, labelled inputs |","-","-## 7. Open items carried to handoff","-","-1. ADR-2 override must compile. Otherwise use the D2 fallbacks.","-2. Platform CSP nonce fix (real-browser hydration) is out of scope.","-3. The `studentTabs` renderer is missing, so the FR-41 tab is not visible.","-4. mui-mcp reachability is a hard gate for dev (NFR-6).","-5. D11 changes a security header (narrowly). Reviewer sign-off is recommended; the fallback is a PDF \"Open\" link.","+| FR-1 | §2 migration `add_quizzes`; schema models/enums exactly per PRD; relations and indexes only |","+| FR-2 | §3.2 `src/lib/validators/quiz.ts` |","+| FR-3 | `grading.ts` `gradeAnswer` (choice rules, partial credit) |","+| FR-4 | `grading.ts` `normalizeShortAnswer` + `needsReview`; manual override §4.4 |","+| FR-5 | `gradeAnswer` ESSAY → null; `correct.guidance` server-only |","+| FR-6 | `/edit` page, `QuizSettingsPanel`, `quizSettingsSchema` superRefine |","+| FR-7 | `QuestionList` (dnd-kit + MUI), `QuestionEditor`, questions/reorder routes |","+| FR-8 | Builder points total; `QuizPlayer mode=\"preview\"` (A10) |","+| FR-9 | `canPublish`; DRAFT→PUBLISHED conditional update §4.1 |","+| FR-10 | Edit lock in `quiz-service`; `regradeQuiz`; `/regrade` route |","+| FR-11 | `course-tabs.ts` entry; `listCourseQuizzes` role-shaped; `CourseQuizzesView`; A2 |","+| FR-12 | `/quizzes/[quizId]/take` start screen + ConfirmDialog |","+| FR-13 | `startOrResumeAttempt`, `seededShuffle`, `computeDeadline` §4.2 |","+| FR-14 | `QuizPlayer` layout, navigator, sticky timer |","+| FR-15 | `useAutosave` hook; answer PUT §4.3 |","+| FR-16 | `saveAnswer` deadline + 30 s → auto-submit + CONFLICT |","+| FR-17 | `submitAttempt` §4.4; submit route |","+| FR-18 | `ensureNotExpired` (lazy) + `autoSubmitExpiredAttempts` §4.6 |","+| FR-19 | Partial unique index §2; P2002 resume §4.2; localStorage merge on mount |","+| FR-20 | `resultsVisible`; `releaseResults`; result page placeholder text |","+| FR-21 | `toStudentResult`; result page |","+| FR-22 | `getStudentQuizScore` + `applyScoringPolicy` §4.7 |","+| FR-23 | `attemptLimit`; start CONFLICT §4.2 |","+| FR-24 | `/grade` page, `QuizGradingWorkspace`, grade route |","+| FR-25 | `recomputeAttempt` |","+| FR-26 | `analytics.ts`; `/analytics` page; x-charts BarChart |","+| FR-27 | Per-question stats; `analyticsCsv` via `toCsv` |","+| FR-28 | `upsertAccommodation`; accommodations route; feeds `computeDeadline`/`attemptLimit`; A7 |","+| FR-29 | `types.ts` `quiz.published`; notify on DRAFT→PUBLISHED (A9) |","+| FR-30 | `types.ts` `quiz.results_released`; release + maintenance claim §4.5 (A6) |","+| FR-31 | Quiz/question route files §3.3 |","+| FR-32 | Attempt route files §3.3 |","+| FR-33 | `isPractice` in `getStudentQuizScore`; A4 |","+| FR-34 | Reuse `course-access.ts`; `access.ts` `assertCanAccessAttempt` |","+| FR-35 | Two calls in `internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`; idempotent via status guard and claim |","+| FR-36 | `prisma/seed.ts` three quizzes |","+| FR-37 | No work: no sidebar entry (A1) |","+| FR-38 | `audit()` in grade, regrade, release, accommodation service functions |","+| FR-39 | MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView + FileUpload; `'quiz'` file context |","+| NFR-1 | `serializers.ts`, student-path selects, serializer unit test §5 |","+| NFR-2 | Composite PK upsert; 2-query hot path §4.3 |","+| NFR-3 | Native MUI Radio/Checkbox; aria-live at 5/1 min; keyboard reorder fallback; axe in e2e |","+| NFR-4 | MUI-only component list §3.4; mui-mcp lookup is a dev gate (ADR-7) |","+| NFR-5 | requireUser/requirePageRole + course/attempt checks on every handler/page §5 |","+| NFR-6 | `withHandler`/Zod/`ok`/`paginated`; error mapping §3.3; UTC + school tz display |","+| NFR-7 | `src/server/quiz/` layout; reuse list §3.1; zero new deps |","+| NFR-8 | Testing map §6 |","+| NFR-9 | Builder defaults (SINGLE_CHOICE), Enter adds option, Duplicate, inline editing |","+| NFR-10 | Scope fence §1.3 |"]}],"originalFile":"# System Design: SH-9 · PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions (SCH-009)\n\nTicket: SH-9 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T10:40:00Z · Status: complete\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (61 FR + 17 NFR, 95%), `handoff-to-architect.json` (8 blockers),\n`tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1..ADR-8), `requirements-analysis-notes.md` (B1–B16, D1–D10). Run mode: `--brownfield --tech-stack react`.\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-8 design that was in this folder. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`\n> and `threat-model-notes.json` in this folder are also leftovers from earlier tickets. `arch-api-contracts` overwrites the first two.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSchoolHub is a Next.js 14 App Router monolith (React 18, TS strict, Prisma 5 / PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, MUI 9.5.0).\nSH-9 adds **assignments**: teacher authoring with an optional rubric, student submission with resubmission history,\na keyboard-driven grading screen, return flow, exemptions, offline grading, a cross-course `/assignments` page per role,\nfour notifications, and two reminder passes.\n\nShape of the change:\n\n- **One migration**, `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6).\n- **One feature folder**, `src/server/assignments/`, with three files: `assignments-service.ts` (all DB logic),\n  `grading-math.ts` (pure, isomorphic, unit-tested), `reminders.ts` (maintenance pass).\n- **One validator file**, `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts`, shared by forms and handlers.\n- Thin route handlers under `src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…` (NFR-7, NFR-8).\n- Pages under `src/app/(app)/…`, plus the four PRD-08 shared components that were never built (D1).\n- **No new dependencies, services, queues, or cron** (ADR-1, ADR-8). Reminders hook into the existing dispatcher.\n\n### 1.1 Intake blockers and how they are resolved (Compliance Rule 5)\n\n| # | Intake blocker | Resolution in this design |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PRD-08 UI is missing: FileUpload, FileList, MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor | Build the minimum of all four in `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx` (ADR-5, §2.5). No other PRD-08 scope. |\n| 2 | MUI X break: `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 vs X 9.5.0 | `package.json` `overrides: { \"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.1.0\" }` (ADR-2). This fixes both DataGrid (FR-17) and DateTimePicker (FR-9). Fallback: FR-17 uses an MUI `Table`, and FR-9 uses `TextField type=\"datetime-local\"`. Dev verifies with `npm ls` plus a compile **before** building UI. |\n| 3 | vitest import break | Change the import in `vitest.config.ts` to `'vitest/config'` and delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (ADR-3). |\n| 4 | CSP `script-src 'self'` breaks hydration | Leave it alone. The e2e spec uses `test.use({ bypassCSP: true })` (ADR-4). The platform nonce fix is a follow-up ticket. |\n| 5 | `studentTabs` has no renderer | Register the FR-41 tab and build `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx`. The page works by direct URL. **No tab bar is built** (NFR-15). This is a known gap and is carried to the handoff. |\n| 6 | LOW-confidence defaults FR-15, FR-52, FR-60 | Adopt intake's defaults as written (§5). Each one is a single predicate or a single copy rule, so it is cheap to change later. |\n| 7 | Reuse list | §2.4 maps each reused helper. No helper is duplicated (NFR-11). |\n| 8 | mui-mcp must be reachable (NFR-6) | This is a hard gate on the dev phase. Dev looks up every MUI component through `useMuiDocs` → `fetchDocs` before using it. If mui-mcp is unreachable, dev stops and reports a blocker. |\n\n### 1.2 New finding from this sub-task (not in intake)\n\n`next.config.js` sends **`X-Frame-Options: DENY`** on `/:path*`. That blocks the same-origin\n`<iframe src=\"/api/files/:id?inline=1\">` PDF preview required by FR-29. CSP `default-src 'self'` already allows same-origin frames,\nso the X-Frame-Options header is the only thing blocking it. `<img>` previews are not affected.\n\n**Decision D11:** in `next.config.js`, split the header rule:\n- `source: '/((?!api/files/).*)'` keeps the existing headers, with `DENY`.\n- `source: '/api/files/:id'` gets the same headers, but with `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` and `frame-ancestors 'self'` appended to the CSP.\n\nThe file route already enforces access (`canAccessFile`) and sniffs types (`nosniff`), so letting our own pages frame it adds no exposure.\n**Fallback**, if the dev wants zero header changes: show PDFs as an \"Open\" link (`target=\"_blank\"`) instead of an iframe. Images still preview inline.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data model: migration `add_assignments` (FR-1..FR-6)\n\nAll additive. Existing models get back-relations only (NFR-11).\n\n```\nenum SubmissionType   { ONLINE_TEXT FILE_UPLOAD TEXT_AND_FILE NO_SUBMISSION }   // FR-1\nenum AssignmentStatus { DRAFT SCHEDULED PUBLISHED }                              // FR-1\nenum SubmissionStatus { SUBMITTED RETURNED }                                     // FR-1\n\nAssignment (FR-2)\n  id, courseId → Course (Cascade), title, instructions (Text), submissionType, maxPoints Decimal(6,2),\n  dueAt, availableFrom?, allowLate, lateCutoffAt?, latePenaltyPercentPerDay Decimal(5,2),\n  maxLatePenaltyPercent Decimal(5,2), maxFileCount Int, allowExtraCredit Boolean @default(false),\n  status AssignmentStatus, rubricId String? @unique → Rubric, notifiedAt?, archivedAt?,\n  createdById, createdAt, updatedAt\n  @@index([courseId, dueAt])\n\nAssignmentAttachment (FR-3)  assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([assignmentId, fileId])\nRubric (FR-3)                id, criteria RubricCriterion[]\nRubricCriterion (FR-3)       id, rubricId → Rubric (Cascade), title, description?, maxPoints Decimal(6,2), order Int,\n                             levels Json  // [{label, points, description}]\n\nSubmission (FR-4)\n  id, assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId → User, status SubmissionStatus, text?,\n  attemptNumber Int, submittedAt, isLate Boolean, lateDays Int,\n  rawScore Decimal(6,2)?, penaltyPercent Decimal(5,2)?, finalScore Decimal(6,2)?,\n  rubricScores Json?  // [{criterionId, points, comment}]\n  feedback?, gradedById?, gradedAt?, returnedAt?\n  @@unique([assignmentId, studentId])\nSubmissionFile (FR-4)        submissionId → Submission (Cascade), fileId → FileObject; @@id([submissionId, fileId])\nSubmissionHistory (FR-4)     id, submissionId → Submission (Cascade), attemptNumber, text?, fileIds String[], submittedAt\n\nGradeExemption (FR-5)        assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, reason?, createdAt; @@id([assignmentId, studentId])\nAssignmentReminder (FR-6)    assignmentId → Assignment (Cascade), studentId, kind String ('due_soon'|'missing'), createdAt\n                             @@unique([assignmentId, studentId, kind])\n```\n\nBack-relations added: `Course.assignments`, `FileObject.assignmentAttachments`, `FileObject.submissionFiles`, `User.submissions`.\n\nModel decisions:\n- **One Submission row per student.** Earlier attempts live in `SubmissionHistory` (FR-24).\n- `SubmissionHistory.fileIds` has no FK. Old attempt files **stay attached** to the same submission id and are never detached. Detaching them would let `purgeOrphanFiles` delete history bytes (B1).\n- Offline grade (FR-8, FR-34) = a Submission with `attemptNumber 0`, `text null`, no files, and `submittedAt = gradedAt`.\n- A Rubric is 1:1 with an Assignment (`rubricId @unique`). Delete the rubric in the same transaction as a hard-deleted assignment.\n- FR-14: **no column added.** The \"review grades\" banner is client-side, shown after a successful PATCH that changed `maxPoints` while `submissionCount > 0`.\n\n### 2.2 Server: `src/server/assignments/` (NFR-8)\n\n| File | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `grading-math.ts` | **Pure and isomorphic** (no Prisma client import; `Decimal` from `decimal.js`, the same package Prisma uses). `lateDays(submittedAt, dueAt)`, `defaultPenalty(lateDays, perDay, max)`, `computeFinalScore(raw, pct)`, `rubricTotal(criteria)`, `maxRawScore(maxPoints, allowExtraCredit)`, `submissionChipStatus(row)` | FR-23, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-28, NFR-1, NFR-14 |\n| `assignments-service.ts` | All DB logic: visibility, CRUD, duplicate, submit, grade, return, exempt, offline grade, role-shaped lists, the serializer, and notify triggers. | FR-8, FR-12..15, FR-22, FR-24, FR-32, FR-34, FR-35, FR-42, FR-44, FR-48..58, FR-59 |\n| `reminders.ts` | `sendDueReminders(now)`: due_soon and missing passes. | FR-43, FR-45, FR-60 |\n\n`grading-math.ts` imports only `decimal.js`. The service wraps values as `Prisma.Decimal` (same class). This keeps one function for the client preview and the server value (ADR-7).\n\n#### Single-source helpers (inside `assignments-service.ts` unless noted)\n\n| Helper | Definition | Used by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `isAssignmentVisible(a, now)` | `!a.archivedAt && isVisible({ status: a.status, publishAt: a.availableFrom }, now)`. Reuses `src/server/content/visibility.ts`: widen `Publishable.status` to `ContentStatus \\| AssignmentStatus` (same string values). | FR-13, FR-22, FR-47, FR-48, FR-50, FR-52, FR-57, FR-58, reminders |\n| `visibleWhere(now)` | The Prisma `where` equivalent: `{ archivedAt: null, OR: [{status:'PUBLISHED'}, {status:'SCHEDULED', availableFrom:{lte:now}}] }` | list queries, reminders |\n| `missingWhere(now)` | visible ∧ `dueAt < now` ∧ `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION`; per student: no Submission and no GradeExemption | FR-37, FR-35, FR-45, FR-60 |\n| `toStudentSubmission(sub)` | Removes `rawScore, penaltyPercent, finalScore, feedback, rubricScores, gradedById, gradedAt` unless `status === 'RETURNED'`. Always removes history. | FR-27, FR-50, FR-55, FR-57, FR-58, NFR-4 |\n| `serializeDecimals` | Prisma.Decimal → `string` (\"14.40\") on the way out | NFR-1 (D5) |\n| `canSeeDrafts(user, course)` | **Reused** from `visibility.ts`: ADMIN, teacher or co-teacher = \"manager\" | everywhere |\n| `nextTeachingDayDueAt(now, tz, teachingDays)` | **In `src/lib/dates.ts`**, next to `schoolNow`. Walk from tomorrow (≤7 days) to the first `isTeaching` weekday, take 23:59 local, convert with `fromZonedTime`. If no day is teaching, use tomorrow. | FR-10, NFR-9 |\n| `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` | STUDENT → self. PARENT → `studentId` must be in `ParentStudentLink`; it defaults to the only linked child. Otherwise FORBIDDEN. | FR-18, FR-38, FR-57 |\n\n#### Key service flows\n\n**Create / update (FR-49, FR-51, FR-11, FR-12, FR-42).** One transaction: Zod parse → if a rubric is given, `rubricTotal == maxPoints`, otherwise\nVALIDATION_ERROR `Rubric totals {sum} points but the assignment is worth {maxPoints}.` → SCHEDULED requires `availableFrom > new Date()` (checked in the service,\nbecause Zod has no server clock, NFR-2) → upsert rubric and criteria → write the assignment → `attachFiles(tx, user, fileIds, 'assignment', id)`. On PATCH,\ndiff the attachments: removed files are `detachFiles` (the purge reclaims them). **After commit**, if the assignment is now visible → `publishOnce(id)`.\n\n**`publishOnce(id)` (FR-42).** `updateMany({ where:{ id, notifiedAt:null }, data:{ notifiedAt: now } })`. Only when `count === 1`, call `notify()` for\n`assignment.published` to ACTIVE-enrolled students. Called from: create/PATCH after commit, and from the student/parent list read paths (FR-48, FR-57)\nfor SCHEDULED assignments that have become visible with `notifiedAt` null. On GET it is fire-and-forget (`void publishOnce(id).catch(logger.error)`) and never fails the read.\n\n**Delete (FR-51).** If there are 0 submissions → detach the attachments, then delete the assignment and its rubric (cascade). Otherwise → set `archivedAt = now`. Audit `assignment.delete|archive`.\n\n**Duplicate (FR-15).** `assertCanManageCourse` for **each** target course, then one transaction per target. Copy the rubric and criteria as new rows.\nAttachments: `readFile` → `saveFile` → a new FileObject (context `'assignment'`), because FileObject holds one context (B2). Status is DRAFT and `notifiedAt` is null.\nSame `dueAt`; `availableFrom` and `lateCutoffAt` keep their offsets from dueAt (FR-15 default).\n\n**Submit (FR-22..FR-24, FR-53, FR-60).** `now = new Date()` on the server. Checks, in order (first failure wins):\n1. Assignment exists and `isAssignmentVisible` → otherwise NOT_FOUND.\n2. `role === 'STUDENT'` and ACTIVE-enrolled in the course → otherwise FORBIDDEN.\n3. Not exempt; `submissionType ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR.\n4. Deadline: `now ≤ dueAt`, or `allowLate && (!lateCutoffAt || now ≤ lateCutoffAt)` → otherwise VALIDATION_ERROR `The deadline has passed and late submissions are closed.`\n5. Content matches the type: text for ONLINE_TEXT, ≥1 file for FILE_UPLOAD, ≥1 of either for TEXT_AND_FILE. Also `fileIds.length ≤ maxFileCount`.\n6. Each file has `ownerId = me`, `context = 'submission'`, and is unattached **or** already attached to this submission. The service checks `context` before calling `attachFiles`, because `attachFiles` does not (B1).\n\nThen, in one transaction:\n- **No row:** create the Submission (`attemptNumber 1`, `isLate`, `lateDays` from `grading-math`).\n- **Row with `status = SUBMITTED`**, including an attempt-0 offline row (D9): insert `SubmissionHistory` from the current row, `attemptNumber++`, clear all grade fields, and replace the `SubmissionFile` rows. Old files stay attached.\n- **Row with `RETURNED`:** CONFLICT `This submission has been returned and can no longer be changed.`\n\n`attachFiles(tx, user, newFileIds, 'submission', submission.id)`. A P2002 from two concurrent first submits → retry once as a resubmit.\n\n**Grade (FR-56, FR-30, FR-31, FR-36, FR-32 \"Save & return\").** `PUT /api/submissions/:id/grade { rawScore?, penaltyPercent, feedback?, rubricScores?, return?: boolean }`.\n- If the assignment has a rubric: `rubricScores` are required, every criterion must be scored exactly once, `0 ≤ points ≤ criterion.maxPoints`, and **the server sets `rawScore = Σ points`** (any client raw value is ignored, D7).\n- Otherwise: `0 ≤ rawScore ≤ maxRawScore` (×1.2 when `allowExtraCredit`). Extra credit applies to rawScore only.\n- `0 ≤ penaltyPercent ≤ 100`. `finalScore = computeFinalScore`. Set `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. The status stays SUBMITTED.\n- `return: true` → in the same transaction, set `status RETURNED`, `returnedAt`, then notify after commit (D6: a single round trip). Audit `submission.grade` (+ `submission.return`).\n\n**Bulk return (FR-32).** `POST /api/assignments/:id/return { submissionIds? }`. The default set is `gradedAt != null AND status = SUBMITTED`. A supplied id that is ungraded is\nskipped and reported in the response (`{returned, skipped}`). One `updateMany`, then one `notifyStudentAndParents` per student (FR-44), plus **one audit row per submission** (FR-59), so\na per-record audit trail is possible.\n\n**Offline grade (FR-34, FR-8).** The student must be ACTIVE-enrolled. If a submission already exists → CONFLICT (grade that one instead). Create the attempt-0 row\nwith the grade fields and penalty 0, using the same validation as Grade. Audit `submission.grade_offline`.\n\n**Exempt (FR-35).** PUT = `upsert` GradeExemption, DELETE = `deleteMany` (both idempotent). Audit `assignment.exempt|unexempt`. The effects come only through\n`missingWhere`, the submit rule 3, and reminders. The PRD-11 \"exclude\" flag **is** the row itself (NFR-15).\n\n### 2.3 Maintenance: `reminders.ts` (FR-43, FR-45, FR-60)\n\n`sendDueReminders(now)` is called on **every** request to `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts`, outside the daily `lastPurgeAt` block, in its own try/catch with logger (B8).\n\n| Pass | Assignment window | Targets | Notify |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| due_soon | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ (now, now+24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | ACTIVE-enrolled, no Submission, no GradeExemption | `assignment.due_soon` → student |\n| missing | `visibleWhere` ∧ `dueAt ∈ [now−8d, now−24h]` ∧ `type ≠ NO_SUBMISSION` | same | `assignment.missing` → linked parents only, via `notify()` |\n\nIdempotency: `createMany({ data: candidates, skipDuplicates: true })` cannot report *which* rows were inserted, so **insert per (assignment, student) with `create` and catch P2002**,\nand notify only on success. The Postgres unique key makes this safe across concurrent dispatchers. Candidate counts are small (one course × roster).\n`// ponytail: missing pass only looks back 8 days; widen or add a cursor if the dispatcher can be down longer.`\n\n### 2.4 Reuse map (NFR-11)\n\n| Existing | Where | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| `requireUser`/`requireRole`, `requirePageUser`/`requirePageRole` | `src/server/auth/requireRole.ts` | every handler and page (NFR-5) |\n| `assertCanViewCourse`, `assertCanManageCourse` | `src/server/auth/course-access.ts` | course-scoped routes |\n| `assertCanViewStudent` | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | FR-58 |\n| `isVisible`, `canSeeDrafts` | `src/server/content/visibility.ts` (type widened) | FR-13, manager checks |\n| `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery`, `parsePagination`, `AppError` | `src/server/http.ts` | NFR-7 envelopes and errors |\n| `audit()` | `src/server/audit.ts` | FR-59 |\n| `notify()`, `notifyStudentAndParents()`, `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | `src/server/notifications/` | FR-42..FR-46 |\n| `attachFiles`, `detachFiles`, `POST /api/files`, `GET /api/files/:id?inline=1`, `registerBuiltInContexts`, `storage.ts` | `src/server/files/`, `src/server/storage.ts` | FR-9, FR-15, FR-20, FR-29, FR-47, FR-53 |\n| `formatInSchoolTz`, `schoolNow` | `src/lib/dates.ts` | FR-19, FR-25, NFR-9 |\n| `ConfirmDialog`, `DataTable`, `EmptyState`, `PageHeader`, `useToast`, `FormField`, `DateDisplay` | `src/components/` | FR-17, FR-21, lists, forms |\n| `courseTabs`, `studentTabs`, `navigation` | `src/config/` | FR-16, FR-40, FR-41 |\n| `logger` | `src/lib/logger.ts` | NFR-12 |\n\n### 2.5 New shared UI components (blocker 1, ADR-5)\n\n| Component | Build | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `MarkdownView` | react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-sanitize (default schema). Elements map to MUI `Typography`, `Link`, `Table*`, `List*`, `Box component=\"pre\"`. | NFR-10, FR-19, FR-29, FR-26 |\n| `MarkdownEditor` | MUI `TextField multiline` + `Tabs` (Write / Preview → `MarkdownView`). Controlled `value`/`onChange`, plus `maxLength`. | FR-9, FR-20, FR-30 |\n| `FileUpload` | MUI `Button` + hidden `<input type=\"file\" multiple>`. POSTs each file to `/api/files` with `context`. Props `{context, max, value: FileRef[], onChange}`. A `LinearProgress` per file, plus remove. | FR-9, FR-20 |\n| `FileList` | MUI `List` of links to `/api/files/:id`. Optional `preview` prop: `<img>` for `image/*`, `<iframe>` for `application/pdf`, both via `?inline=1` (D11). | FR-19, FR-25, FR-29 |\n\n### 2.6 Validators: `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` (FR-7)\n\n`assignmentInput` (FR-7 limits; `.superRefine`: `lateCutoffAt > dueAt`, rubric sum = maxPoints using `rubricTotal`), `rubricCriterionInput`,\n`submissionInput {text? ≤50k, fileIds ≤10}`, `gradeInput {rawScore?, penaltyPercent 0–100, feedback? ≤10k, rubricScores?, return?}`,\n`offlineGradeInput`, `bulkReturnInput`, `duplicateInput {courseIds min 1}`, `meAssignmentsQuery {studentId?, tab?, courseId?}`.\nDecimals are accepted as `z.union([z.number(), z.string()])` and converted to Decimal in the service. No request schema has a timestamp field except\n`dueAt`/`availableFrom`/`lateCutoffAt`, which are authoring data, not \"now\" (NFR-2).\n\n### 2.7 Route handlers (thin: Zod → service → envelope; NFR-7)\n\n| Route | Auth | Service fn | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | user + view course | `listCourseAssignments` (manager shape with `groupBy` counts / student shape) | FR-48, FR-17, FR-18 |\n| `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments` | manage course | `createAssignment` | FR-49 |\n| `GET /api/assignments/[id]` | view (NOT_FOUND for invisible to non-manager) | `getAssignment` (+ own submission, `serverNow`) | FR-50, FR-19 |\n| `PATCH` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]` | manage | `updateAssignment` / `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` | FR-51, FR-14 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/duplicate` | manage source + each target | `duplicateAssignment` | FR-15 |\n| `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | manage | `listGradingRoster` (every ACTIVE enrollee; `pageSize` ≤100) | FR-54, FR-28 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` | STUDENT | `submit` | FR-53, FR-22..24 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/return` | manage | `bulkReturn` | FR-32, FR-44 |\n| `POST /api/assignments/[id]/grade-offline` | manage | `gradeOffline` | FR-34, FR-8 |\n| `PUT` / `DELETE /api/assignments/[id]/exemptions/[studentId]` | manage | `setExemption` | FR-35 |\n| `GET /api/submissions/[id]` | submitter, linked parent, or manager; history for managers only | `getSubmission` | FR-55, FR-29, NFR-3 |\n| `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade` | manage | `gradeSubmission` | FR-56, FR-30..32, FR-36 |\n| `GET /api/me/assignments` | any user; role switch | `listMyAssignments` | FR-57, FR-37..39 |\n| `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments` | `assertCanViewStudent` | `listStudentAssignments` | FR-58, FR-41 |\n\nShared response conventions for `arch-api-contracts`: Decimals are **strings**. Timestamps are ISO UTC strings. Student/parent submission objects\nalways pass through `toStudentSubmission`. FR-58: a viewer who manages the course gets the full fields, everyone else gets the serializer (D8).\n`/api/me/assignments` for ADMIN = \"To grade\" across all courses (intake default).\n\n### 2.8 Pages (`src/app/(app)/…`)\n\n| Page | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/page.tsx` | Manager: `DataTable` (title, due, status, submitted/total, graded/submitted, Grade button; Archived chip). Student/parent: grouped `List` (Upcoming / Past due / Submitted / Returned). Parent child selector when more than one linked child is enrolled. | FR-16..18, FR-52 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/new/page.tsx` + `[assignmentId]/edit/page.tsx` | One shared `AssignmentForm` (react-hook-form + the Zod schema). Defaults: dueAt = `nextTeachingDayDueAt` (computed server-side, passed as a prop), maxPoints 100, FILE_UPLOAD, maxFileCount 3, allowLate off (NFR-16). Rubric builder: `@dnd-kit/sortable` with Up/Down buttons as the keyboard fallback, and a live sum error. Buttons: Save draft / Publish / Schedule. Edit warns per FR-14. \"Duplicate to other courses\" dialog with an `Autocomplete` of managed courses. | FR-9..15 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/page.tsx` | MarkdownView instructions, FileList, due and late-policy summary, rubric table, countdown under 48 h (offset from `serverNow`, display only). Submission panel by type, `localStorage` draft key `assignment:{id}:{userId}` (cleared on success), ConfirmDialog before POST, receipt via `formatInSchoolTz`, returned results, or \"Submitted — awaiting grading\". Parent: read-only, no panel. | FR-19..27 |\n| `courses/[courseId]/assignments/[assignmentId]/grade/page.tsx` | Left: `List` + status `Chip`s from `submissionChipStatus`, filter, sort by name or time. Main: MarkdownView text, FileList with preview, history `Select`. Form: rubric `ToggleButtonGroup`s that auto-sum, prefilled penalty (`defaultPenalty`), live final score (`computeFinalScore`), MarkdownEditor feedback. Buttons Save / Save & return / Return all graded / Grade without submission / Exempt toggle. J/K/Ctrl+Enter keydown handler that skips J/K in input/textarea/contenteditable, with a visible shortcut hint. **NFR-3:** a plain `Map<id, Submission>` cache; after each selection, prefetch the next and previous `GET /api/submissions/:id`. | FR-28..36, NFR-3, NFR-16, NFR-17 |\n| `assignments/page.tsx` | STUDENT: `Tabs` Upcoming/Missing/Submitted/Returned + course filter. PARENT: child selector, same view, read-only. TEACHER/ADMIN: \"To grade\" list, oldest first. | FR-37..39 |\n| `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx` | Per-student list (FR-58). Reachable by URL only (blocker 5). | FR-41 |\n\n### 2.9 Config and registrations\n\n- `src/config/course-tabs.ts`: `{ key:'assignments', label:'Assignments', href: id => /courses/${id}/assignments, roles: ALL_ROLES }` (FR-16).\n- `src/config/navigation.ts`: `Assignments` → `/assignments`, roles `[STUDENT, PARENT, TEACHER, ADMIN]` (FR-40; ADMIN added because the To-grade default applies to ADMIN).\n- `src/config/student-tabs.ts`: `assignments` entry (FR-41).\n- `src/server/notifications/types.ts`: four keys, category ACADEMIC (FR-46):\n  `assignment.published` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.due_soon` [STUDENT] email false · `assignment.returned` [STUDENT, PARENT] email false · `assignment.missing` [PARENT] email **true**.\n- `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (FR-47), registered in `registerBuiltInContexts`:\n  - `assignmentResolver`: load the assignment and course → `assertCanViewCourse` → `canSeeDrafts || isAssignmentVisible`.\n  - `submissionResolver`: load the submission and course → allow `studentId === user.id`, a linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), or `canSeeDrafts`. Deny everyone else, including other students (NFR-4, AC-10).\n- `next.config.js`: D11 header split.\n- `package.json`: `overrides[\"@mui/x-internals\"] = \"9.1.0\"` (ADR-2). `vitest.config.ts` import fix (ADR-3).\n- `prisma/seed.ts`: FR-61 block, idempotent: look up courses by code (skip if missing), upsert by `(courseId, title)`, Decimals as strings, no file bytes.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n**Author → publish.** Teacher form → `POST /api/courses/:id/assignments` → validate (Zod + rubric sum + schedule time) → tx (rubric, assignment, attachments) → commit → `publishOnce` → `notify(assignment.published)` to enrolled students.\n\n**Scheduled becomes visible.** No job. A student/parent list read evaluates `visibleWhere(now)`. Any newly visible assignment with `notifiedAt` null → fire-and-forget `publishOnce` (the atomic guard sends exactly once).\n\n**Submit.** Student uploads files → `POST /api/files {context:'submission'}` (unattached, owner-only readable) → `POST /api/assignments/:id/submissions {text, fileIds}` → the six checks in order → tx (history snapshot if resubmitting, upsert submission, file rows, `attachFiles` → contextId = submission.id) → receipt.\nFrom then on, the files are readable through `submissionResolver` only by the student, their parents, and course managers.\n\n**Grade → return.** Grader page loads the roster (FR-54) → selects a student → `GET /api/submissions/:id` (cached; next and previous prefetched) → form computes the preview with `grading-math` → `PUT …/grade {…, return?}` → server recomputes everything authoritatively → tx → audit → (if return) `notifyStudentAndParents(assignment.returned, \"Course: Title — 18/20\")`.\nStudent `GET` now gets the grade fields, because the serializer unlocks on RETURNED.\n\n**Reminders.** The external caller hits `/api/internal/email/dispatch` → `dispatchEmails` → `sendDueReminders(now)` → due_soon and missing candidate queries → per-row `AssignmentReminder.create` (P2002 = already sent) → `notify`.\n\n**Privacy boundaries (NFR-4), three layers:** (1) query scoping: student and parent paths always filter `studentId ∈ resolveViewedStudent`; (2) `toStudentSubmission` serializer; (3) the file resolvers for `/api/files/:id`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Testing layout (NFR-13, NFR-14)\n\n- `tests/unit/assignments/grading-math.test.ts`: lateDays (exactly 24 h = 1, 24 h + 1 ms = 2, across spring-forward and fall-back in `Europe/London`), penalty cap, final score (18 @ 20 % = \"14.40\", half-up at .005), rubric sum, chip status. Also `nextTeachingDayDueAt` across DST.\n- `tests/integration/assignments/*.test.ts`: resubmission history (files kept attached), RETURNED refuses resubmit, return flow plus serializer unlock, reminder idempotency (call twice → one notification), exemption removes from missing and blocks submit, NO_SUBMISSION excluded, file resolver denies another student (AC-10).\n- `tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` (`bypassCSP: true`): teacher creates → student submits a file → teacher grades with a rubric and returns → student sees feedback; parent sees the missing list.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Decisions log\n\n| # | Decision | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | Build the minimal MarkdownView, MarkdownEditor, FileUpload and FileList in `src/components/` | FR-9, FR-19, FR-20, FR-29, FR-30 |\n| D2 | Pin `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 via overrides; fallbacks are MUI `Table` and `datetime-local` | FR-17, FR-9 |\n| D3 | Fix the vitest import; e2e uses bypassCSP | NFR-13, NFR-14 |\n| D4 | Register the student tab and page; no tab bar | FR-41 |\n| D5 | Decimals are strings in JSON | NFR-1 |\n| D6 | \"Save & return\" = `PUT …/grade {return:true}`, one transaction | FR-32 |\n| D7 | With a rubric, the server sets `rawScore = Σ rubric points` | FR-30, FR-36 |\n| D8 | FR-58: managers get the full fields, other viewers get the serializer | FR-58, FR-27 |\n| D9 | An online submit over an unreturned offline grade = a resubmission | FR-8, FR-24 |\n| D10 | The missing pass looks back 8 days (`ponytail:` note) | FR-45 |\n| D11 | `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN` only for `/api/files/:id`, so PDF iframes work | FR-29 |\n| D12 | Intake defaults adopted: FR-15 same dueAt plus offsets; FR-52 archived = hidden from students/parents, closed, no reminders, visible to managers; FR-60 NO_SUBMISSION never missing or reminded; FR-10 weekdays only; FR-36 extra credit raw-only; ADMIN /assignments = To grade | FR-10, FR-15, FR-36, FR-39, FR-52, FR-60 |\n| D13 | Resubmission after RETURNED → CONFLICT (409). Deadline and content failures → VALIDATION_ERROR | FR-22, FR-24 |\n| D14 | One audit row per affected submission, including bulk return | FR-59 |\n| D15 | FR-14 banner is client-side; no schema column | FR-14 |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 enums in migration `add_assignments` |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 `Assignment` (+allowExtraCredit, notifiedAt, archivedAt, rubricId @unique, index) |\n| FR-3 | §2.1 `AssignmentAttachment`, `Rubric`, `RubricCriterion` |\n| FR-4 | §2.1 `Submission`, `SubmissionFile`, `SubmissionHistory` |\n| FR-5 | §2.1 `GradeExemption` |\n| FR-6 | §2.1 `AssignmentReminder`; §2.3 idempotency |\n| FR-7 | §2.6 `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` |\n| FR-8 | §2.1 attempt-0 row; §2.2 Offline grade; D9 |\n| FR-9 | §2.8 `AssignmentForm`; §2.5 MarkdownEditor, FileUpload; D2 |\n| FR-10 | §2.2 `nextTeachingDayDueAt` in `src/lib/dates.ts` |\n| FR-11 | §2.8 rubric builder; §2.2 Create (server rubric-sum check); §2.6 superRefine |\n| FR-12 | §2.8 three buttons; §2.2 Create (SCHEDULED future check) |\n| FR-13 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` / `visibleWhere` (read-time, no job) |\n| FR-14 | §2.8 edit warning; D15 |\n| FR-15 | §2.2 Duplicate; §2.7 duplicate route |\n| FR-16 | §2.9 courseTabs entry |\n| FR-17 | §2.8 manager DataTable; §2.7 FR-48 manager shape; D2 |\n| FR-18 | §2.8 student/parent grouped list; `resolveViewedStudent` |\n| FR-19 | §2.8 assignment page; §2.5 MarkdownView, FileList |\n| FR-20 | §2.8 submission panel (localStorage draft); §2.5 FileUpload |\n| FR-21 | §2.8 ConfirmDialog before POST |\n| FR-22 | §2.2 Submit checks 1–4 |\n| FR-23 | §2.2 `grading-math.lateDays` |\n| FR-24 | §2.2 Submit transaction (history, clear grade, files kept) |\n| FR-25 | §2.8 receipt via `formatInSchoolTz` |\n| FR-26 | §2.8 returned results view |\n| FR-27 | §2.2 `toStudentSubmission` serializer |\n| FR-28 | §2.8 grading left panel; `submissionChipStatus` |\n| FR-29 | §2.8 grading main panel; §2.5 FileList preview; D11 |\n| FR-30 | §2.8 grading form; `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`; D7 |\n| FR-31 | §2.2 `grading-math.computeFinalScore` (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP) |\n| FR-32 | §2.2 Grade (`return:true`) and Bulk return; D6 |\n| FR-33 | §2.8 keydown handler |\n| FR-34 | §2.2 Offline grade; §2.7 grade-offline route |\n| FR-35 | §2.2 Exempt; `missingWhere`; Submit check 3 |\n| FR-36 | §2.2 Grade validation; `maxRawScore` |\n| FR-37 | §2.8 `/assignments` STUDENT; `missingWhere` |\n| FR-38 | §2.8 `/assignments` PARENT; `resolveViewedStudent` |\n| FR-39 | §2.8 `/assignments` TEACHER/ADMIN To grade |\n| FR-40 | §2.9 navigation entry |\n| FR-41 | §2.9 studentTabs entry; §2.8 students page; blocker 5 |\n| FR-42 | §2.2 `publishOnce` (atomic notifiedAt) |\n| FR-43 | §2.3 due_soon pass |\n| FR-44 | §2.2 Grade/Bulk return → `notifyStudentAndParents` |\n| FR-45 | §2.3 missing pass (parents only) |\n| FR-46 | §2.9 NOTIFICATION_TYPES keys |\n| FR-47 | §2.9 `assignmentResolver`, `submissionResolver` |\n| FR-48 | §2.7 `GET /api/courses/[id]/assignments` |\n| FR-49 | §2.7 `POST /api/courses/[id]/assignments`; §2.2 Create |\n| FR-50 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]` |\n| FR-51 | §2.7 PATCH/DELETE; §2.2 Delete |\n| FR-52 | §2.2 `isAssignmentVisible` (`!archivedAt`); D12 |\n| FR-53 | §2.7 POST submissions; §2.2 Submit checks 5–6 |\n| FR-54 | §2.7 `GET /api/assignments/[id]/submissions` |\n| FR-55 | §2.7 `GET /api/submissions/[id]` |\n| FR-56 | §2.7 `PUT /api/submissions/[id]/grade`; §2.2 Grade |\n| FR-57 | §2.7 `GET /api/me/assignments` |\n| FR-58 | §2.7 `GET /api/students/[id]/assignments`; D8 |\n| FR-59 | §2.2 audit calls; D14 |\n| FR-60 | §2.2 `missingWhere`, Submit check 3; §2.3 filters; D12 |\n| FR-61 | §2.9 seed block |\n| NFR-1 | §2.2 `grading-math` (Decimal); D5 strings in JSON |\n| NFR-2 | §2.2 server `now` everywhere; §2.6 no client clock fields |\n| NFR-3 | §2.8 grading `Map` cache plus next/prev prefetch |\n| NFR-4 | §3 privacy boundaries (scoping, serializer, resolvers) |\n| NFR-5 | §2.7 auth column; §2.4 reuse of require*/assertCan* |\n| NFR-6 | §1.1 blocker 8; §2.5/§2.8 MUI-only components |\n| NFR-7 | §2.7 thin handlers via `http.ts` helpers |\n| NFR-8 | §2.2 `src/server/assignments/`; §2.6; §2.7; §2.8 |\n| NFR-9 | §2.2 UTC lateDays, `fromZonedTime` default; §4 DST tests |\n| NFR-10 | §2.5 MarkdownView |\n| NFR-11 | §2.4 reuse map |\n| NFR-12 | §2.3 / §2.2 `logger` in catch paths |\n| NFR-13 | §1.1 blockers 2–3; ADR-2, ADR-3 |\n| NFR-14 | §4 testing layout |\n| NFR-15 | §1.1 blockers 4–5 (no CSP or tab-bar work); D12; exemption = row only |\n| NFR-16 | §2.8 form defaults; keyboard grading |\n| NFR-17 | §2.8 dnd-kit Up/Down fallback, shortcut hint, labelled inputs |\n\n## 7. Open items carried to handoff\n\n1. ADR-2 override must compile. Otherwise use the D2 fallbacks.\n2. Platform CSP nonce fix (real-browser hydration) is out of scope.\n3. The `studentTabs` renderer is missing, so the FR-41 tab is not visible.\n4. mui-mcp reachability is a hard gate for dev (NFR-6).\n5. D11 changes a security header (narrowly). Reviewer sign-off is recommended; the fallback is a PDF \"Open\" link.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012Bk8pTEdwsgWRYhDNnXCzy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
