{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrvvAaeYmLPfrp5ekCcX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-10. It replaces a leftover SH-9 version of the file. I didn't touch any other sub-task's files. Intake reported no blockers, and the Overview says so. Every requirement from FR-1 to FR-39 and NFR-1 to NFR-10 maps to a design element in the traceability table.\n\n**What's in it**\n- **Data model:** the five models and five enums exactly as the PRD lists them. The design only adds relations, indexes, and one hand-written database rule that allows a single in-progress attempt per student per quiz, so two tabs can't start two attempts.\n- **Code layout:** the logic lives in `src/server/quiz/`. Grading, deadlines, scoring, shuffling and the publish checks are plain functions with no database access, so they're easy to unit-test. Students only ever receive data built by `serializers.ts`.\n- **Single paths:** manual submit, the late-save rejection, auto-submit when an attempt is loaded, and the scheduled maintenance run all go through one `submitAttempt()`. Saving an answer is two database queries and never loads the quiz or the questions.\n- **API, pages and tests:** a table of route files with who can access each one, the UI pages (MUI only), and the testing plan.\n\n**Decisions I made that aren't in the PRD**\n- **No new database column for \"results sent\".** For quizzes whose results show after close, the maintenance run marks the existing `resultsReleasedAt` field as it sends the notification. This guarantees it's sent once without adding the `resultsNotifiedAt` column the research notes suggested.\n- **\"Flagged for review\" and \"manually graded\" are worked out, not stored.** An answer counts as manually graded once `gradedById` is set. Essays and unmatched short answers stay flagged until a teacher grades them. Regrade never changes answers a teacher has graded.\n- **No unpublishing.** A quiz only moves from DRAFT to PUBLISHED to CLOSED, so the \"quiz published\" notification fires exactly once.\n- **Preview records nothing at all.** It doesn't call the attempt endpoints or grade answers.\n\nThe design lists ten assumptions (A1–A10) in its Overview, including these four. Next, `arch-api-contracts` should read `system-design.md` and write `api-contracts.json` and the dev-planning handoff. The current versions of both files are still left over from SH-9."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13728,"cache_read_input_tokens":61175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13728,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5aa5ddb-e317-4c7f-b076-47081e553974","uuid":"e712bc88-7930-4f9a-9139-2828a456fd6a","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:06:11.514Z","request_id":"req_011CgrvvA2uSoxeqd33Qme7P"}
