{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UzwBaAosjXvcBPafc82f8z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n6\t\n7\tIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:\n8\t\n9\t- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.\n10\t- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.\n11\t- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.\n12\t\n13\tNone of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n18\t\n19\t**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n20\t\n21\t**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:\n22\t\n23\t| Need | Use | Req |\n24\t|---|---|---|\n25\t| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |\n26\t| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |\n27\t| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |\n28\t| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |\n29\t| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |\n30\t| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |\n31\t| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |\n32\t| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |\n33\t| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |\n34\t| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |\n35\t| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |\n36\t| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n37\t| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |\n38\t| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n39\t| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |\n40\t\n41\t**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7).\n42\t\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions\n46\t\n47\t**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly.\n48\t\n49\t**Decision.**\n50\t- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.\n51\t- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.\n52\t- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).\n53\t- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary.\n54\t\n55\t**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded.\n56\t\n57\t---\n58\t\n59\t## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod\n60\t\n61\t**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own.\n62\t\n63\t**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop.\n64\t\n65\t**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\".\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper\n70\t\n71\t**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing.\n72\t\n73\t**Decision.**\n74\t- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.\n75\t- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).\n76\t- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.\n77\t- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk.\n78\t\n79\t**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\").\n80\t\n81\t---\n82\t\n83\t## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue\n84\t\n85\t**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope.\n86\t\n87\t**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.\n88\t- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).\n89\t- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).\n90\t- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3).\n91\t\n92\t**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions.\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers\n97\t\n98\t**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`.\n99\t\n100\t**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`.\n101\t\n102\t**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event.\n103\t\n104\t---\n105\t\n106\t## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync\n107\t\n108\t**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test.\n109\t\n110\t**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41).\n111\t\n112\t**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion.\n113\t\n114\t---\n115\t\n116\t## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row\n117\t\n118\t**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s.\n119\t\n120\t**Decision.**\n121\t- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.\n122\t- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:\n123\t  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students\n124\t  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses\n125\t  - the scale\n126\t  - one attendance groupBy for the term range\n127\t- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.\n128\t- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`.\n129\t\n130\t**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it.\n131\t\n132\t---\n133\t\n134\t## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library\n135\t\n136\t**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.\n137\t\n138\t**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.\n139\t\n140\t**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.\n141\t\n142\t---\n143\t\n144\t## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone\n145\t\n146\t**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.\n147\t\n148\t**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n149\t\n150\t**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added.\n151\t# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11\n152\t\n153\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n154\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n155\t`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n156\t\n157\t> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input.\n158\t\n159\t## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n160\t\n161\t| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |\n162\t|---|---|---|---|\n163\t| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |\n164\t| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |\n165\t| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |\n166\t| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |\n167\t| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |\n168\t| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |\n169\t| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |\n170\t| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |\n171\t| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |\n172\t| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |\n173\t| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |\n174\t| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |\n175\t| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |\n176\t| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |\n177\t| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |\n178\t| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |\n179\t| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |\n180\t| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |\n181\t| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |\n182\t\n183\t## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n184\t\n185\tConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry.\n186\t\n187\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n188\t|---|---|---|\n189\t| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |\n190\t| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |\n191\t| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |\n192\t| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |\n193\t| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |\n194\t| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |\n195\t| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |\n196\t| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |\n197\t| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |\n198\t| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |\n199\t| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |\n200\t| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |\n201\t| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |\n202\t| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |\n203\t| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |\n204\t| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |\n205\t| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |\n206\t| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |\n207\t| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |\n208\t| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |\n209\t| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |\n210\t| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |\n211\t| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |\n212\t| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |\n213\t| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |\n214\t| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |\n215\t| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |\n216\t| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |\n217\t| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |\n218\t| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |\n219\t| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |\n220\t| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |\n221\t| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |\n222\t| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |\n223\t| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |\n224\t| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |\n225\t| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |\n226\t| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |\n227\t| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |\n228\t| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |\n229\t| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |\n230\t| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |\n231\t| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |\n232\t| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |\n233\t| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |\n234\t| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |\n235\t| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |\n236\t| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |\n237\t| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |\n238\t| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |\n239\t| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |\n240\t| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |\n241\t| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |\n242\t| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |\n243\t| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |\n244\t\n245\t## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`\n246\t\n247\t- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.\n248\t- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.\n249\t- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.\n250\t- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.\n251\t- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.\n252\t- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.\n253\t- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component.\n254\t\n255\t## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)\n256\t\n257\t1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.\n258\t2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".\n259\t3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\n260\t4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.\n261\t5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.\n262\t6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.\n263\t7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT.\n264\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cedb5742-c42c-44c2-b06a-ff50226957e7","uuid":"983c4342-b5d3-4124-9045-35dbf0454af7","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:05:51.161Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/cedb5742-c42c-44c2-b06a-ff50226957e7/tool-results/b3j0xs181.txt","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards\n\nTicket: SH-11 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n**Base stack (checked against the workspace).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 100% confidence, and `package.json` matches it: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, Prisma 5.20.0 (`@prisma/client` 5.20.0) on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, papaparse ^5.4.1, tsx 4.16.2, MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), `@mui/x-internals` overridden to 9.1.0, Vitest 2.1.1 and Playwright 1.47.2.\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`handoff-to-architect.json`, `blockers: []`, confidence 95%). No NFR pushes toward a different stack:\n\n- **NFR-2** (35×80 gradebook in under 800 ms): three indexed queries (items, grades, enrolments), then the pure calculation in memory.\n- **NFR-3** (600 students × 8 courses in under 30 s): batch loading per course and term, then in-memory calculation.\n- **NFR-11** (A4 print): CSS `@media print`.\n\nNone of these needs a cache, a queue, a PDF engine or a grid library. **Overall decision: keep the stack and add no dependencies (NFR-7, NFR-9).**\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-9 forbids re-scaffolding and requires reuse of existing code. NFR-7 limits UI to MUI 9.5.0 and MUI X. Every capability PRD-11 needs is already installed or already in the repo.\n\n**Decision.** Add nothing to `dependencies` or `devDependencies`. Map each need to something that already exists:\n\n| Need | Use | Req |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grade maths | `Decimal`, `dec`, `fixed2` from `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` (Prisma.Decimal). Import them; don't copy them. | FR-10–FR-15, NFR-1 |\n| Validation | Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, shared by the client forms and the route handlers | FR-16, FR-17, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| Gradebook grid | `DataGrid` from `@mui/x-data-grid` (MIT), used directly (see ADR-4) | FR-18–FR-21, FR-24, NFR-8 |\n| Admin lists (scales, report cards) | Existing `src/components/DataTable` | FR-16, FR-29 |\n| Band and category editors | MUI `TextField`, `Select`, `Autocomplete`, `Dialog` | FR-16, FR-17, FR-22, FR-23 |\n| Date and term inputs | `@mui/x-date-pickers` `DatePicker` | FR-22 |\n| CSV export | `toCsv` from `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-25 |\n| Quiz score | `applyScoringPolicy` + `resultsVisible` from `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` (see ADR-6) | FR-7 |\n| Access control | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` (`src/server/auth/course-access.ts`) and `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds` (`src/server/auth/student-access.ts`) | FR-37, FR-39, FR-42, NFR-6 |\n| Term attendance summary | Reuse the `attendance-service.ts` groupBy aggregation, run once per term for the filtered students | FR-30, NFR-3 |\n| Timezone date rules | `schoolToday` (`src/server/attendance/attendance-rules.ts`) with `SchoolSettings.timezone` | FR-3, FR-10, FR-24, NFR-10 |\n| Notifications and audit | `notify()` (`src/server/notifications/notify.ts`, types in `types.ts`) and `audit()` (`src/server/audit.ts`) | FR-34, FR-38, NFR-4 |\n| Confirmations and toasts | Existing `ConfirmDialog` and `Toast`/`useToast` | FR-34, NFR-7 |\n| Printing | `@media print` + `window.print()` | FR-35, NFR-11 |\n| Backfill runner | `tsx` (already a devDependency) | FR-8 |\n\n**Consequences.** `package.json` changes only by one script (ADR-7). There's no lockfile churn or license review, and nothing new for QA's banned-import scan. Every UI component still has to be looked up via mui-mcp before use (NFR-7).\n\n---\n\n## ADR-2: Store grades as Prisma `Decimal` and calculate in pure functions\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires Decimal arithmetic and pure, unit-tested calculation. FR-13 rounds half-up at band edges (89.95 → 90.0), which floating point can get wrong. FR-15 must reproduce 78.0% C+ exactly.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Make `Grade.score`, `GradeItem.maxPoints`, `GradeCategory.weight`, `GradingScale` band `minPercent` and `TermGradeOverride.percent` `Decimal` columns, with precision set by the FR-1 schema spec.\n- Put `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` on plain inputs only: items, grades, categories, scale, override and `now`. It does no Prisma I/O, and it computes everything in `Decimal`.\n- Round the course percent once, at the end, with `toDecimalPlaces(1, Decimal.ROUND_HALF_UP)`, then do the band lookup (FR-13).\n- Convert to `number` or `string` only at the serializer boundary.\n\n**Consequences.** Calculation is deterministic and the Vitest matrix (NFR-1, NFR-12) needs no database. NFR-3 follows from this: batched loading feeds the same pure function. Callers must not round category percents before weighting, because only the final value is rounded.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-3: Store grading scale bands as a JSON column validated by Zod\n\n**Context.** FR-1 says \"exactly as specified\". FR-16 validates bands as a set: strictly descending, lowest minimum 0, unique letters. Bands are always read and written together with their scale, and nothing queries a band on its own.\n\n**Decision.** Follow the PRD's `GradingScale` model as written. If it defines bands as `Json`, keep them as a JSON array of `{ letter, minPercent, gpa?, descriptor? }`. Treat the array as one unit and validate it with a single Zod schema in `gradebook.ts`. Enforce \"exactly one default\" in a service transaction that clears the old default when a new one is set. Add a partial unique index (`WHERE \"isDefault\"`) in the migration SQL as a backstop.\n\n**Consequences.** The band editor saves in one write, and the scale reaches `grade-calc.ts` with no join. GPA is stored only and never computed (NFR-13). If the PRD's FR-1 instead specifies a separate band table, use it; this ADR then reduces to \"validate as a set in Zod\".\n\n---\n\n## ADR-4: Build the gradebook on MIT `DataGrid` directly, not the `DataTable` wrapper\n\n**Context.** FR-18 to FR-21 and FR-24 need `columnGroupingModel`, `processRowUpdate`, custom edit cells, column menu items, row virtualisation (60×120) and a sticky header. NFR-8 forbids Pro and Premium features, so there are no pinned columns. The existing `DataTable` wraps `DataGrid` for URL-paginated, searchable server lists, and its props don't expose grouping or editing.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Use `<DataGrid>` from `@mui/x-data-grid` in a new `src/components/gradebook/GradebookGrid.tsx`.\n- Keep the default row and column virtualisation, and turn off pagination (`hideFooterPagination`).\n- Handle keyboard input (digit, E, M, Delete, Enter or arrow keys) in a custom `renderEditCell` and `onCellKeyDown`, then commit through `processRowUpdate` and `onProcessRowUpdateError` for per-cell error state.\n- Before writing, confirm every prop against the v9.5.0 docs through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs`/`fetchDocs`). This is intake's FR-20 risk.\n\n**Consequences.** One consumer of raw `DataGrid` is justified by needs `DataTable` doesn't cover. Admin lists still use `DataTable` (FR-16, FR-29). Without pinned columns, the student-name column scrolls away horizontally, which the PRD accepts (\"sticky header, no pinned columns\").\n\n---\n\n## ADR-5: Sync with direct service calls inside existing transactions, not events or a queue\n\n**Context.** FR-3 to FR-7 must react to publish, unpublish, archive, delete, return, exemption and quiz-graded events. NFR-5 needs Grade rows to never hold scores that haven't been released. The repo has no event bus. Its only background process is `worker:email`, and it's out of scope.\n\n**Decision.** Add `src/server/gradebook/sync.ts` with idempotent upserts keyed on `(source, sourceId)` and `(gradeItemId, studentId)`. Call it from the existing assignment, quiz, submission-return and exemption services, inside their existing `prisma.$transaction` when there is one.\n- Saving a grade without returning it doesn't call sync (FR-5).\n- Practice quizzes return early (`Quiz.isPractice`).\n- An item with no matching term is skipped and logged with `logger.warn` (intake assumption, FR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** Sync can't drift out of step with the source write. Scores are written only on return or visibility, so privacy holds at the storage layer as well as in serializers. Each hook adds a few ms to the source write, which is fine at this scale. The backfill (ADR-7) reuses the same functions.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-6: Create `getStudentQuizScore` from the existing quiz grading helpers\n\n**Context.** FR-7 names `getStudentQuizScore`, but it doesn't exist. `src/server/quiz/grading.ts` already exports `applyScoringPolicy(policy, attempts)`, which returns `{ score, maxScore, percent }` as fixed2 strings, `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` and `percentOf`.\n\n**Decision.** Add `getStudentQuizScore(quiz, gradedAttempts, now)` next to these helpers in `src/server/quiz/grading.ts`. It filters attempts to GRADED and results-visible, calls `applyScoringPolicy` and returns `score / maxScore × quiz.maxScore` as `Decimal`, or `null`. Sync stores that value as `Grade.score` against `GradeItem.maxPoints = quiz.maxScore`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's one source of truth for the quiz score policy, and PRD-10's helpers stay unchanged. When a quiz uses `AFTER_CLOSE` or `MANUAL` visibility, sync has to run again when results become visible. That means at close and on release; dev-planning should hook the release action. Otherwise the score fills in at backfill or at the next attempt event.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-7: Run the backfill as a `tsx` script that reuses sync\n\n**Context.** FR-8 requires an idempotent `npm run gradebook:backfill`, and the seed must call it. NFR-12 needs an idempotency integration test.\n\n**Decision.** Add `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts`, which exports `backfill()` and has a CLI entry point. The script is a loop over existing published assignments, non-practice quizzes, returned submissions, visible graded attempts and exemptions, calling the ADR-5 sync functions. Add one script line to `package.json`: `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`. `prisma/seed.ts` imports and calls `backfill()` (FR-41).\n\n**Consequences.** Idempotency comes from the upsert keys, so there's no \"already ran\" flag. It follows the `worker:email` pattern. Running it twice gives identical row counts, which is the test assertion.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-8: Freeze report cards as a JSON snapshot on the row\n\n**Context.** FR-30 lists a fixed set of snapshot fields. FR-31 and AC-8 need PUBLISHED cards to stay unchanged when grades are edited or cards are regenerated. NFR-3 requires generating 600 × 8 in under 30 s.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Store `ReportCard.snapshot` as `Json` (per the FR-1 model), typed by a Zod schema in `src/server/report-cards/`.\n- Generation batch-loads per term and does no per-student queries:\n  - courses and enrolments for the filtered students\n  - items, grades, categories and overrides for those courses\n  - the scale\n  - one attendance groupBy for the term range\n- Run `grade-calc.ts` in memory, then `createMany` new cards and `update` existing ones, always filtered with `where: { status: 'DRAFT' }`.\n- Nothing in `src/server/gradebook/` writes to `ReportCard`.\n\n**Consequences.** The print view and student tab read only the snapshot, which is fast and immutable. Unpublishing returns a card to DRAFT, and the next generation can then refresh it (FR-34, with an audit entry). Snapshot JSON is not queryable, which is fine because nothing filters on it.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-9: Build the print view with CSS, not a PDF library\n\n**Context.** FR-35 and NFR-11 need A4 portrait pages, a letterhead, signature lines, a hidden app sidebar and page breaks for \"Print all\". The intake stack notes say no PDF library is needed.\n\n**Decision.** Render `/report-cards/[id]/print` and the bulk print route as server components. Use MUI `Table` and `Typography` styled through `sx` and theme `GlobalStyles` with `@page { size: A4 portrait }` and `@media print` rules that hide the app shell (sidebar, app bar, buttons). Add `break-after: page` per card. A small client `Button` calls `window.print()`.\n\n**Consequences.** There's no new dependency and no server-side rendering farm, and \"Save as PDF\" is the browser's own feature. Print fidelity depends on the browser. The Playwright test (NFR-12) checks the print media, not PDF bytes.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-10: Compare dates in the school timezone\n\n**Context.** NFR-10 says the school timezone is the reference for date rules. Intake's assumption is that \"past due\" means `now > dueAt`, compared as an exact instant.\n\n**Decision.** Compare past-due status as a UTC instant (`now > dueAt`). This applies to FR-10 missing items and the FR-24 \"mark all missing\" action. For term containment (FR-3), convert `dueAt` or `availableUntil` to a school-local date with `schoolToday(date, tz)` and compare it with the term's `startDate` and `endDate`. Show all dates through the existing `DateDisplay` component in `SchoolSettings.timezone`.\n\n**Consequences.** Reusing the same helper as attendance avoids off-by-one-day errors at term boundaries. No date library is added.\n# Requirements Analysis Notes — ticket SH-11\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T12:00:00Z), PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards (SCH-011). It has 42 FRs and 13 NFRs (55 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. Its flagged assumptions (FR-6, FR-7, FR-13, FR-27/33, NFR-10, FR-3 no-term) are restated in §4 so `system-design.md` can carry them forward.\n\n> As of this writing the other files in `artifacts/architect/` (system-design.md, tech-stack-decisions.md, api-contracts.json, handoff-to-dev-planning.json, threat-model-notes.json) are **leftovers from earlier tickets**. Their owning sub-tasks must overwrite them, and none of them is SH-11 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-11 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | **`getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId)` already exists.** It is labelled \"PRD-11 export\". It loads GRADED attempts, applies `applyScoringPolicy(quiz.scoringPolicy, …)`, and returns `{score, maxScore, percent, attemptsCounted, isPractice}` (fixed2 strings) or null. | src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts L355-372 | **This corrects intake** (B-finding 5 and the FR-7 assumption). FR-7 calls it directly, with no new helper. It does **not** check `resultsVisible`, so the sync caller must gate on that (NFR-5). The batch path (FR-8 backfill, NFR-3) should run `applyScoringPolicy` in memory over attempts it has already loaded, rather than calling this per student. |\n| B2 | `resultsVisible(quiz, attempt, now)` covers IMMEDIATELY / AFTER_CLOSE (`now >= availableUntil`) / MANUAL (`resultsReleasedAt != null`). | src/server/quiz/grading.ts L94 | FR-7 / NFR-5 gate. AFTER_CLOSE depends on time, so a GRADED attempt is not syncable until close. See B4. |\n| B3 | Every quiz attempt status change goes through `recomputeAttempt(tx, attemptId)`. It is called from `submitAttempt` (L123, which includes auto-submit), `gradeAnswerManually` (L338) and `regradeQuiz` (quiz-service L435). | attempt-service.ts L73-81 | FR-7 hook. After each caller commits, call `syncQuizGrade(quizId, studentId)`, which no-ops unless GRADED + visible + !isPractice. Making this one function the only quiz sync entry point covers all three callers. |\n| B4 | Results become visible through `releaseResults` (MANUAL, quiz-service L464) and `sendAfterCloseResultsReleased` (AFTER_CLOSE). The latter claims `resultsReleasedAt` with `updateMany` on each maintenance tick. | quiz-service.ts L464; quiz/maintenance.ts L27-40 | FR-7 also needs a **bulk** `syncQuizGrades(quizId)` in both places. Otherwise AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL quizzes never reach the gradebook. The maintenance claim is already idempotent, so put the sync after `count === 1`. |\n| B5 | Quiz lifecycle: `createQuiz`, `updateQuiz` (DRAFT→PUBLISHED and PUBLISHED→CLOSED via guarded `updateMany`, L304-305), `deleteQuiz` (hard delete, L317). Quizzes have **no archive**. | quiz-service.ts L259-317 | FR-3: upsert the item on →PUBLISHED. FR-4: delete the item on deleteQuiz. CLOSED is **not** unpublish, so the item stays visible. Settings edits to a published quiz (title, availableUntil, categoryId, max) re-upsert the item. |\n| B6 | Assignment lifecycle: `createAssignment` / `updateAssignment` (status DRAFT/SCHEDULED/PUBLISHED); `publishOnce` (cron, makes SCHEDULED visible once `availableFrom` passes); `deleteOrArchiveAssignment` (hard delete in a tx, or sets `archivedAt` when submissions exist, L479-492). `isAssignmentVisible` = !archivedAt && published-or-scheduled-reached. | assignments-service.ts L67-74, L292-330, L437-492 | FR-3/FR-4: compute GradeItem.isVisible from `isAssignmentVisible`. Upsert on create/update/publishOnce, set isVisible=false on archive, delete inside the delete tx. **FR-24's teacher hide toggle conflicts with this** (see §3 R2). |\n| B7 | Return paths: `gradeSubmission` (`returning = input.return && status !== 'RETURNED'`; it also re-grades an already-RETURNED submission), `bulkReturn`, and `gradeOffline` (`input.return`). | assignments-service.ts ~L696-800 | FR-5: sync when the submission **is RETURNED after the write**, not only on the transition. Re-grading a returned submission must update Grade.score, and grade-without-return must not sync (AC-3). Use one `syncSubmissionGrade(submissionId)` from all three. |\n| B8 | `setExemption(…, exempt)` upserts or deletes `GradeExemption` (L818/L824) and audits `assignment.exempt` / `assignment.unexempt`. | assignments-service.ts L815-838 | FR-6: call `syncSubmissionGrade` (or a by-(assignment, student) variant) after both branches. Unexempt re-derives the score from a RETURNED submission, else null. |\n| B9 | GradeItem has a polymorphic `source + sourceId` with **no FK**. Assignment and Quiz deletes will not cascade. | FR-1 model spec | FR-4: delete the GradeItem explicitly inside the same transaction as the source delete (and in `deleteQuiz`, which today runs outside a tx). Grade → GradeItem should be `onDelete: Cascade`. |\n| B10 | `Term` has no `isCurrent`. It has `academicYearId`, `startDate`/`endDate` as `@db.Date`, `order`. `AcademicYear.isCurrent` exists. `Course.academicYearId` exists. | schema.prisma L240-252, Course ~L415 | FR-3 term placement: pick the term of **the course's academic year** whose `[startDate, endDate]` contains dueAt, comparing dates in the school timezone (NFR-10). The fallback \"current term\" is the term of that year containing today (tz), else skip + `logger.warn`. Put this in one pure helper `termFor(date, terms, tz)`. |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` is exported from assignments-service. `dec` / `fixed2` / `Decimal` come from grading-math (isomorphic). `percentOf` (1 dp half-up) is in quiz/grading.ts. | assignments-service.ts L57; grading-math.ts L7-15; grading.ts L133 | NFR-1/NFR-10/FR-13 reuse these. `percentOf` rounds to 1 dp on a single value. grade-calc must keep full-precision Decimal until the **final** rounding (FR-13), so it must not round category percents early. |\n| B12 | `assertCanViewCourse` / `assertCanManageCourse` exist. `getAccessibleStudentIds` / `assertCanViewStudent` cover own student, linked parent (`ParentStudentLink`), teacher and admin, with homeroom handled there too. `src/server/quiz/access.ts` has `canManageCourse`. | src/server/auth/course-access.ts, student-access.ts | FR-39 \"manage\"/\"view\" and FR-42 reuse these. FR-37 report-card access is new: ADMIN; teachers of any course on the card or the homeroom teacher; the student or a linked parent only when PUBLISHED. Return NOT_FOUND to everyone else (AC-7). |\n| B13 | Attendance aggregation already exists: `getReport(filters)` → `StudentSummaryRow` (StatusCounts per student) using a single `groupBy(studentId, status)`. It filters by date range, grade level, section and course. | attendance-service.ts L528-582 | FR-30 attendance summary and NFR-3 batching: call `getReport({from: term.start, to: term.end, sectionId/gradeLevelId})` **once** per generate request. Do not loop per student. Rate formula: reuse whatever StatusCounts consumers use. Do not invent a new one. |\n| B14 | `SchoolSettings` singleton: name, shortName, logoUrl, timezone, address fields. Student profile: `admissionNumber`, `gradeLevel`. `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. | schema.prisma L109-113, L198-215 | FR-30 snapshot fields all come from existing models. No schema change beyond FR-1. |\n| B15 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` const already contains assignment.* and quiz.* entries. `notify()` and `notifyStudentAndParents()` never throw. `audit()` never throws. | notifications/types.ts, notify.ts L28/L98, audit.ts L26 | FR-38: add `grade.posted` (ACADEMIC, defaultEmail false, STUDENT+PARENT) and `report_card.published` (defaultEmail true, STUDENT+PARENT). Call them after commit. NFR-4 audit actions: `grade.update`, `termOverride.upsert`, `reportCard.unpublish` (plus `reportCard.publish` and `gradingScale.*` as nice-to-haves). |\n| B16 | `courseTabs` / `studentTabs` are static arrays. `studentTabs` notes \"No tab bar renders studentTabs yet\". `navigation` is a flat array with `roles` and an optional `group: 'Administration'`. | src/config/*.ts | FR-18/28: add course tabs `gradebook` (TEACHER, ADMIN) and `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT). FR-26/36: add student tabs `grades` and `report-cards`. These are reachable by URL only, the same as `assignments`. FR-27/33 + admin pages: nav entries `/grades`, `/report-cards`, `/admin/grading-scales`, `/admin/report-cards`. |\n| B17 | `toCsv(columns, rows)` + `escapeCsvCell` are in src/server/csv.ts. Shared components: DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast (useToast), PageHeader, EmptyState, StatCard, DateDisplay, UserPicker, FormField, LoadingSkeleton. **No existing `@mui/x-data-grid` usage in src.** | src/server/csv.ts; src/components/ | FR-25: export on the server with `toCsv`, building the same columns as the grid. FR-18 is the first DataGrid in the codebase, so its MIT-tier API (columnGroupingModel, processRowUpdate, virtualisation, no pinning) must be looked up via mui-mcp for 9.5.0 (NFR-7/8). FR-29 table → DataTable. |\n| B18 | Scripts: `db:seed` = `tsx prisma/seed.ts`. There is no `gradebook:backfill`. The seed looks up courses by code with `findCourse([...])`. | package.json; prisma/seed.ts | FR-8: add `\"gradebook:backfill\": \"tsx scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts\"`, a thin wrapper over an exported `backfillGradebook()` in src/server/gradebook/ that the seed also calls before the FR-41 data. |\n| B19 | Postgres. Migrations already hand-add raw SQL partial indexes. Prisma 5.20. | prisma/migrations/* | FR-1: one migration. It needs `@@unique([source, sourceId])` on GradeItem (sync and backfill idempotency), `@@unique([gradeItemId, studentId])` on Grade, `@@unique([courseId, termId, studentId])` on TermGradeOverride, and `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on ReportCard. These make the upserts race-safe. A one-default-scale rule can be a partial unique index `WHERE \"isDefault\"` (FR-16). |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern legend: **DM** data model/migration · **SYNC** source→gradebook sync hook · **CALC** pure calculation · **API** REST endpoint · **UI** page/component · **AUTH** access boundary · **JOB** script/batch · **NOTIF** notification · **AUD** audit · **CFG** config registry.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | New enums + 6 models in one `prisma migrate` migration. Use the unique keys from B19. Grade: `score Decimal?`, `excused`, `missing`, `comment`, `gradedById`, `gradedAt`. ReportCard: `status`, `snapshot Json`, `homeroomComment`, `principalComment`, `publishedAt`, `publishedById`. |\n| FR-2 | DM, UI | Nullable `Course.gradingScaleId`, `Assignment.categoryId` and `Quiz.categoryId` with `onDelete: SetNull`. Category deletion via FR-40 must not delete sources. Add one `Select` to the existing assignment and quiz editors, plus the validator fields in assignments.ts / quiz.ts (optional and nullable). Don't change existing behaviour. |\n| FR-3 | SYNC | `upsertGradeItemFromAssignment(id)` / `…FromQuiz(id)` keyed on (source, sourceId). Skip practice quizzes. Term placement via `termFor` (B10). Callers per B5/B6. Keep the GradeItem's term stable after first creation unless the date changes, so grades don't jump terms on unrelated edits. |\n| FR-4 | SYNC | Archive sets isVisible=false. Delete removes the GradeItem in the same tx (B9). Quiz has no archive or unpublish. A practice-toggle after publish should delete or hide the item. |\n| FR-5 | SYNC | `syncSubmissionGrade` from 3 return paths (B7). It writes only when RETURNED. Score = `finalScore`. |\n| FR-6 | SYNC | From `setExemption` (B8). Exemption wins over the score: excused=true and the score is kept. |\n| FR-7 | SYNC | Per-attempt `syncQuizGrade` after `recomputeAttempt` callers (B3). Bulk `syncQuizGrades` on release and AFTER_CLOSE (B4). Score scaled: `score/maxScore × GradeItem.maxPoints`, Decimal. |\n| FR-8 | JOB | `backfillGradebook()`: batch load per course, reuse the same upsert builders as live sync (one code path), idempotent through the unique keys. npm script + seed call (B18). |\n| FR-9 | API, AUTH | The service rejects score/excused/missing edits on non-MANUAL items (`AppError('FORBIDDEN'/'VALIDATION_ERROR')`). Comment stays editable. The grid marks those columns non-editable. |\n| FR-10 | CALC | `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`: pure, Decimal-only, no Prisma client import (types only). Input: items, grades, categories, scale, override, `now`. Counted = visible ∧ ¬excused ∧ (score≠null ∨ (missing ∧ now>dueAt)). |\n| FR-11 | CALC | Drop lowest by item **percentage**, keeping ≥1. Ties are dropped deterministically (by dueAt, then id). |\n| FR-12 | CALC | Implicit \"Uncategorised\" bucket. What weight does it get? The PRD is silent, so see §3 R3. No categories gives a points total. |\n| FR-13 | CALC | `toDecimalPlaces(1, ROUND_HALF_UP)` only at the end. Bands are sorted descending, first `percent >= minPercent`. |\n| FR-14 | CALC | The override is applied after computing. A letter-only override keeps the computed percent. A percent-only override probably re-derives the letter from the scale (unstated, so flag it). |\n| FR-15 | CALC, UI | Golden unit test (78.0 C+). The gradebook and student Grades **must call the same function**, with no client-side recomputation. |\n| FR-16 | API, UI, DM | `/admin/grading-scales` (ADMIN). Band validation lives in a Zod refinement shared by client and server. \"Exactly one default\" uses a tx that clears others + a partial unique index. Deleting a scale in use is either blocked or falls back to the default; decide this. |\n| FR-17 | UI, API | Course settings page. The live weight sum is client-side, with the 100 check repeated server-side in FR-40. Decimal weights: compare with `dec(sum).eq(100)`, not floats. |\n| FR-18 | UI, API, CALC | First DataGrid. The server returns one denormalised payload `{students, items, categories, grades, computed}` for (course, term) in a fixed number of queries (NFR-2). Columns are built client-side from it. Sort by last name on the server. |\n| FR-19 | UI | Pure cell renderer. \"Late\" needs `Submission.isLate`, so the gradebook payload must carry the source submission's isLate. |\n| FR-20 | UI, API | `processRowUpdate` → PATCH a single grade. E/M/Delete need a custom edit cell / `onCellKeyDown` (check mui-mcp). Optimistic update with per-cell error. Audited (NFR-4). Triggers `grade.posted` (FR-38). |\n| FR-21 | UI | The cell click opens a link to the submission grading page or the quiz attempt. The payload needs `submissionId` / `attemptId` per synced grade. |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | POST manual item. Validate that the term belongs to the course's academic year and the category belongs to the course. |\n| FR-23 | API, UI, AUD | PUT override (upsert). Comment ≤1000 chars. Audit with old/new values. |\n| FR-24 | API, UI | Toggle visibility (see R2). Bulk-missing allowed only if `now > dueAt` and only for ungraded rows. Stats come from the computed payload, client-side, over counted scores. |\n| FR-25 | API | Server CSV via `toCsv`, using the same row builder as the grid. \"As displayed\" means EX/M/— markers and the term letter. |\n| FR-26 | UI, API, CFG | Student tab → `GET /api/students/:id/grades?termId`. The colour thresholds come from a single helper reused by FR-27/28. |\n| FR-27 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/grades` reuses the FR-26 component. Parent child selector from `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-28 | UI, CFG | Course tab `grades` (STUDENT, PARENT): same endpoint filtered by courseId. |\n| FR-29 | UI, API | `/admin/report-cards`: list query joins students (grade level, section filters) with ReportCard status for the term. Missing-data warnings are computed in batch (ungraded counted-eligible items, missing TermGradeOverride.comment per course). |\n| FR-30 | JOB, API | `generate`: batch load (NFR-3), compute in memory, write the snapshot JSON (versioned shape, e.g. `snapshot.v = 1`). Teacher comment = `TermGradeOverride.comment`. Attendance via B13. |\n| FR-31 | JOB, DM | `upsert` with `where status = DRAFT` semantics: createMany for new cards, `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})` for existing ones, never touching PUBLISHED. Grade-edit services never import report-cards code. |\n| FR-32 | API, UI, AUTH | PATCH: field-level role check (homeroomComment: homeroom teacher of the student's section or ADMIN; principalComment: ADMIN). Edits are allowed only while DRAFT (implied, so flag it). |\n| FR-33 | UI, CFG, AUTH | `/report-cards` (TEACHER): drafts for sections where `homeroomTeacherId = user.id`. Nav entry. |\n| FR-34 | API, NOTIF, AUD | Publish (one or bulk) with a guarded `updateMany({status:'DRAFT'})`, then notify after commit. Unpublish: ADMIN, reason required, audit, back to DRAFT. |\n| FR-35 | UI | `/report-cards/[id]/print` renders from the **snapshot only**. `@media print` via MUI `GlobalStyles`, hiding the sidebar. Bulk print: one page renders N cards with `break-after: page`. |\n| FR-36 | UI, CFG, API | Student tab \"Report cards\". The list endpoint filters to PUBLISHED for student/parent (NFR-5). |\n| FR-37 | AUTH | New `assertCanViewReportCard`. Non-entitled users get NOT_FOUND, so existence isn't leaked. |\n| FR-38 | NOTIF | Register 2 types (B15). `grade.posted`: only for MANUAL items, only when a score is first entered or changed (one per student per item, so an idempotency marker such as `Grade.notifiedAt` is needed; flag it). |\n| FR-39 | API, AUTH | Thin route handlers using `withHandler`, Zod in `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts`, and services in `src/server/gradebook/` + `src/server/report-cards/`. |\n| FR-40 | API | Replace-all in a tx: delete missing ids (sources → SetNull), upsert the rest. Weights total 100 (Decimal). |\n| FR-41 | JOB | Seed: scale, 7A categories, 'Oral presentation' + grades, draft S1 cards for 7A with MATH/ENG override comments. Run after `backfillGradebook()`. |\n| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Student serializer: visible items only. Grade rows only exist for released scores (sync gating), so the risk is mainly hidden items and MANUAL items with isVisible=false. Still filter explicitly. |\n| NFR-1 | CALC | Decimal throughout. Unit matrix in `grade-calc.test.ts`. |\n| NFR-2 | API | Gradebook: ~5 queries (enrollments, items, grades, categories, scale + override), all indexed by (courseId, termId). The grid virtualises. |\n| NFR-3 | JOB | Generation: per term, `findMany` items/grades/overrides/categories for all courses in scope with `in` filters, then group in memory. One attendance `groupBy`. Chunk the writes. |\n| NFR-4 | AUD | Old/new values in metadata for grade.update, termOverride.upsert and reportCard.unpublish. |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Enforced in 3 layers: sync gating (B2/B7), student serializer (FR-42), report-card guard (FR-37). Integration tests for each. |\n| NFR-6 | AUTH | Every route uses requireUser/requireRole + an entity check (B12). Server pages check too, not just the API. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | MUI only, with mui-mcp lookup. Toast via useToast, confirm via Dialog/ConfirmDialog. |\n| NFR-8 | UI | DataGrid MIT: no `pinnedColumns` and no `@mui/x-data-grid-pro`. Sticky header is the default. |\n| NFR-9 | all | New code only in src/server/gradebook/ and src/server/report-cards/. Hooks into existing services are one-line calls. Use `logger`, no console.log. |\n| NFR-10 | CALC, SYNC | Past-due uses an instant comparison (`now > dueAt`). Term containment uses a tz date comparison (B10). |\n| NFR-11 | UI | A4 portrait `@page` rule. Long course lists may need a 2nd page, with table rows set to `break-inside: avoid`. |\n| NFR-12 | all | Tests per the intake list. Integration tests hit the real sync hooks (B3/B4/B7). |\n| NFR-13 | — | Scope guard: store `gpa`, never compute it. No rank or transcript. |\n\n## 3. Risks / decisions for `arch-design-system`\n\n- **R1 (FR-7 timing):** AFTER_CLOSE and MANUAL visibility arrive later than GRADED. Without the B4 bulk hooks, those quizzes never sync. Syncing early would break NFR-5.\n- **R2 (FR-4 vs FR-24):** the teacher's hide toggle and the source-driven `isVisible` share one column. Re-saving an assignment would silently re-show a teacher-hidden item. Options: (a) source sync writes isVisible only on publish/archive *transitions*; (b) add a separate `hiddenByTeacher` flag and make visible = sourceVisible ∧ ¬hiddenByTeacher. (b) is clearer but adds a column beyond FR-1's \"exactly as specified\". Pick one and state it.\n- **R3 (FR-12 Uncategorised weight):** the PRD doesn't say what weight the implicit bucket carries when real categories exist. A sensible default is weight 0, so it's shown but excluded from the weighted mean, unless it's the only bucket. This affects the FR-15 golden test only if it has uncategorised items (it doesn't). Flag it.\n- **R4 (FR-38 dedupe):** \"one notification per student per item\" needs a marker. A nullable `Grade.notifiedAt` claimed via `updateMany` follows the existing claim pattern.\n- **R5 (FR-3 term drift):** re-deriving the term on every edit can move existing grades between terms. Only recompute it when dueAt/availableUntil changes.\n- **R6 (FR-16 delete):** deleting a scale referenced by courses or by DRAFT snapshots (PUBLISHED ones embed the legend, so they're safe). Recommend blocking the delete with CONFLICT while courses reference the scale.\n- **R7 (first DataGrid):** there is no in-repo precedent. Keyboard E/M/Delete handling within the MIT tier is the main implementation risk (intake keyRisk). The design should keep the grid behind one client component.\n\n## 4. Carried-forward assumptions (from intake, adjusted)\n\n1. FR-6: unexempting clears excused and re-syncs the score from the source.\n2. FR-7: **use the existing `getStudentQuizScore`** (B1) plus a caller-side `resultsVisible` gate. This replaces intake's \"build a new helper\".\n3. FR-13: 89.95 → 90.0 → **A−** under the seed scale. The test asserts 90.0 and the 90-band letter.\n4. FR-27/FR-33: add nav entries per the convention.\n5. NFR-10: past due = `now > dueAt` (exact instant). Term containment is evaluated in the school timezone.\n6. FR-3: no containing term and no current term → skip the item + `logger.warn`.\n7. New and unstated (needs sign-off): FR-14 percent-only override re-derives the letter; FR-32 comments are editable only while DRAFT; FR-34 unpublish returns to DRAFT.\n","numLines":264,"startLine":1,"totalLines":264}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UzwBaAosjXvcBPafc82f8z","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
