{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ckJaMdKYDdBS9FYLzRaTb","type":"tool_result","content":"91\t## Functional Requirements\n92\t\n93\t### FR-1 Data model\n94\t\n95\t```prisma\n96\tenum GradeItemSource { ASSIGNMENT QUIZ MANUAL }\n97\tenum ReportCardStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED }\n98\t\n99\tmodel GradingScale {\n100\t  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n101\t  name      String                     // \"Standard A–F\"\n102\t  isDefault Boolean  @default(false)\n103\t  bands     Json                       // [{ letter: \"A\", minPercent: 90, gpa?: 4.0, descriptor: \"Excellent\" }], sorted desc\n104\t  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n105\t  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n106\t}\n107\t\n108\tmodel GradeCategory {\n109\t  id            String   @id @default(cuid())\n110\t  courseId      String\n111\t  course        Course   @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n112\t  name          String                     // \"Homework\"\n113\t  weightPercent Decimal  @db.Decimal(5, 2) // 0–100; a course's categories total 100\n114\t  dropLowest    Int      @default(0)       // drop N lowest scores in this category per student\n115\t  order         Int\n116\t}\n117\t\n118\tmodel GradeItem {\n119\t  id          String          @id @default(cuid())\n120\t  courseId    String\n121\t  course      Course          @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n122\t  categoryId  String?\n123\t  category    GradeCategory?  @relation(fields: [categoryId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n124\t  termId      String\n125\t  term        Term            @relation(fields: [termId], references: [id])\n126\t  title       String\n127\t  maxPoints   Decimal         @db.Decimal(6, 2)\n128\t  dueAt       DateTime?\n129\t  source      GradeItemSource\n130\t  sourceId    String?         @unique       // assignmentId or quizId\n131\t  isVisible   Boolean         @default(true) // hidden items do not show to students/parents and do not count\n132\t  createdAt   DateTime        @default(now())\n133\t  updatedAt   DateTime        @updatedAt\n134\t  grades      Grade[]\n135\t}\n136\t\n137\tmodel Grade {\n138\t  gradeItemId String\n139\t  gradeItem   GradeItem @relation(fields: [gradeItemId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n140\t  studentId   String\n141\t  score       Decimal?  @db.Decimal(6, 2)  // null = not graded yet\n142\t  excused     Boolean   @default(false)    // excluded from calculation\n143\t  missing     Boolean   @default(false)    // counts as 0 when the item is past due\n144\t  comment     String?\n145\t  updatedById String\n146\t  updatedAt   DateTime  @updatedAt\n147\t  @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])\n148\t  @@index([studentId])\n149\t}\n150\t\n151\tmodel TermGradeOverride {\n152\t  courseId        String\n153\t  termId          String\n154\t  studentId       String\n155\t  percent         Decimal? @db.Decimal(5, 2)\n156\t  letter          String?\n157\t  teacherComment  String?                  // max 1,000, appears on the report card\n158\t  updatedById     String\n159\t  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt\n160\t  @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])\n161\t}\n162\t\n163\tmodel ReportCard {\n164\t  id               String           @id @default(cuid())\n165\t  studentId        String\n166\t  termId           String\n167\t  status           ReportCardStatus @default(DRAFT)\n168\t  snapshot         Json                     // frozen data: courses, grades, attendance, comments\n169\t  homeroomComment  String?\n170\t  principalComment String?\n171\t  generatedAt      DateTime         @default(now())\n172\t  publishedAt      DateTime?\n173\t  publishedById    String?\n174\t  @@unique([studentId, termId])\n175\t}\n176\t```\n177\t\n178\tAlso add `gradingScaleId String?` to `Course` (null = school default) and `categoryId String?` to `Assignment` and `Quiz` with a category select added to their editors.\n179\t\n180\t### FR-2 Sync from assignments and quizzes (`src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts`)\n181\t1. When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a `GradeItem` (title, maxPoints, dueAt, category, term = term containing `dueAt` / `availableUntil`, falling back to the current term). Unpublishing or archiving sets `isVisible = false`; deleting deletes the item.\n182\t2. When a submission is returned, upsert its `Grade` with `score = finalScore`. Saving without returning does not sync (students must not see unreturned scores). Exemptions set `excused = true`.\n183\t3. When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and results are visible, upsert `Grade.score` from `getStudentQuizScore` scaled to the quiz maxScore.\n184\t4. A one-time backfill `npm run gradebook:backfill` creates items and grades for data that existed before this PRD; it is idempotent and runs in the seed.\n185\t5. Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI (edit happens at the source) except `comment`; manual items are fully editable.\n186\t\n187\t### FR-3 Calculation (`src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`, pure functions)\n188\tFor a student, course and term:\n189\t1. Consider visible items in the term whose student grade is not `excused`. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and `missing` (counts as 0). Ungraded, not-missing items are ignored.\n190\t2. Per category: drop the `dropLowest` lowest percentages (never dropping all), then `categoryPercent = Σ score / Σ maxPoints × 100`.\n191\t3. Course percent = weighted mean of category percentages over categories that have at least one counted item, re-normalising weights to the categories present. Items without a category form an implicit \"Uncategorised\" category; if the course has no categories, course percent = total points earned / total possible × 100.\n192\t4. Letter = first band where `percent >= minPercent` in the effective scale. Round percent half-up to 1 decimal place before letter lookup.\n193\t5. `TermGradeOverride` percent/letter replace the computed values when set (letter-only overrides keep the computed percent).\n194\t6. Example: Homework 40 % (scores 18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60 % (scores 70/100): Homework = 27/30 = 90.0 %, Exams = 70.0 %, course = 0.4 × 90 + 0.6 × 70 = 78.0 % → \"C+\" in the seed scale.\n195\t\n196\t### FR-4 Grading scales (`/admin/grading-scales`)\n197\t1. CRUD for scales; band editor with letter, minimum %, optional GPA points and descriptor. Validation: bands strictly descending, lowest band minimum is 0, letters unique. Exactly one default.\n198\t\n199\t### FR-5 Category setup (course \"Gradebook\" settings)\n200\t1. Teacher manages categories: name, weight, drop lowest, order. Weights must total 100 (live sum indicator) before saving. Course grading scale select (defaults to school default).\n201\t\n202\t### FR-6 Gradebook grid (course tab \"Gradebook\", TEACHER/ADMIN)\n203\t1. Term selector. Grid built on MUI X `DataGrid` (MIT: column groups via `columnGroupingModel`, cell editing via `processRowUpdate`; pinned columns are not in the MIT version, so keep the student column first and use the grid's sticky header): first column students (sorted by last name), then items grouped by category (column header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages and the term percent + letter (bold). Horizontally scrollable; the DataGrid's built-in virtualisation handles up to 60 students × 120 items.\n204\t2. Cell content: score, \"EX\" (excused), \"M\" (missing, red), \"—\" (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\n205\t3. Manual items: editable DataGrid cells — type a number, `Enter` / arrow keys move between cells, `E` excuse, `M` missing, `Delete` clears. Changes save on blur with optimistic update and per-cell error state.\n206\t4. Synced cells: clicking opens the source (submission grading page or quiz attempt).\n207\t5. \"Add manual item\" dialog: title, category, max points, date, term.\n208\t6. Student row action: \"Override term grade / comment\" dialog (percent, letter, comment).\n209\t7. Column menu: hide/show item to students, set all ungraded to missing (after due date), view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\n210\t8. \"Export CSV\" exports the grid as displayed.\n211\t\n212\t### FR-7 Student and parent grade views\n213\t1. Register student tab \"Grades\": for the selected term, one card per course with percent, letter and a colour (≥ 80 green, 60–79 amber, < 60 red); expanding shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\n214\t2. `/grades` page for STUDENT and PARENT (child selector) showing the same.\n215\t3. Course tab \"Grades\" for STUDENT/PARENT shows that course's items only.\n216\t\n217\t### FR-8 Report cards (`/admin/report-cards`)\n218\t1. Select term → table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated, Draft, Published) and missing-data warnings (for example \"2 courses have ungraded items\", \"No teacher comment for ENG-7A\").\n219\t2. \"Generate drafts\" for the filtered students builds each `snapshot`: school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year; per course: subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacher comment (from overrides); attendance summary for the term (rate, absences, lates); grading scale legend. Regenerating a draft refreshes the snapshot; published cards are never changed by regeneration.\n220\t3. Review page per card: rendered report card preview with editable homeroom comment (homeroom teacher or admin) and principal comment (admin). Homeroom teachers also get `/report-cards` listing their section's drafts to write comments.\n221\t4. \"Publish\" (per card or bulk for filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED and sends `report_card.published` to student and parents (default email true). \"Unpublish\" (admin only, requires reason, audited).\n222\t5. Print view `/report-cards/[id]/print`: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for principal and homeroom teacher; uses `@media print`; \"Print / Save as PDF\" button calls `window.print()`. Bulk \"Print all\" renders filtered published cards with page breaks.\n223\t6. Register student tab \"Report cards\": list of published cards (students/parents) or all (admin/teacher), each opening the print view.\n224\t\n225\t### FR-9 Notifications\n226\t1. `grade.posted` → student + parents when a manual item grade is entered (default email false; batched: one notification per student per item).\n227\t2. `report_card.published` as above.\n228\t\n229\t## API\n230\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cedb5742-c42c-44c2-b06a-ff50226957e7","uuid":"68bb8463-f936-4145-8592-5bc5fabf2de6","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:06:01.756Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/11-gradebook.md","content":"## Functional Requirements\n\n### FR-1 Data model\n\n```prisma\nenum GradeItemSource { ASSIGNMENT QUIZ MANUAL }\nenum ReportCardStatus { DRAFT PUBLISHED }\n\nmodel GradingScale {\n  id        String   @id @default(cuid())\n  name      String                     // \"Standard A–F\"\n  isDefault Boolean  @default(false)\n  bands     Json                       // [{ letter: \"A\", minPercent: 90, gpa?: 4.0, descriptor: \"Excellent\" }], sorted desc\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt\n}\n\nmodel GradeCategory {\n  id            String   @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId      String\n  course        Course   @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  name          String                     // \"Homework\"\n  weightPercent Decimal  @db.Decimal(5, 2) // 0–100; a course's categories total 100\n  dropLowest    Int      @default(0)       // drop N lowest scores in this category per student\n  order         Int\n}\n\nmodel GradeItem {\n  id          String          @id @default(cuid())\n  courseId    String\n  course      Course          @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  categoryId  String?\n  category    GradeCategory?  @relation(fields: [categoryId], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n  termId      String\n  term        Term            @relation(fields: [termId], references: [id])\n  title       String\n  maxPoints   Decimal         @db.Decimal(6, 2)\n  dueAt       DateTime?\n  source      GradeItemSource\n  sourceId    String?         @unique       // assignmentId or quizId\n  isVisible   Boolean         @default(true) // hidden items do not show to students/parents and do not count\n  createdAt   DateTime        @default(now())\n  updatedAt   DateTime        @updatedAt\n  grades      Grade[]\n}\n\nmodel Grade {\n  gradeItemId String\n  gradeItem   GradeItem @relation(fields: [gradeItemId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  studentId   String\n  score       Decimal?  @db.Decimal(6, 2)  // null = not graded yet\n  excused     Boolean   @default(false)    // excluded from calculation\n  missing     Boolean   @default(false)    // counts as 0 when the item is past due\n  comment     String?\n  updatedById String\n  updatedAt   DateTime  @updatedAt\n  @@id([gradeItemId, studentId])\n  @@index([studentId])\n}\n\nmodel TermGradeOverride {\n  courseId        String\n  termId          String\n  studentId       String\n  percent         Decimal? @db.Decimal(5, 2)\n  letter          String?\n  teacherComment  String?                  // max 1,000, appears on the report card\n  updatedById     String\n  updatedAt       DateTime @updatedAt\n  @@id([courseId, termId, studentId])\n}\n\nmodel ReportCard {\n  id               String           @id @default(cuid())\n  studentId        String\n  termId           String\n  status           ReportCardStatus @default(DRAFT)\n  snapshot         Json                     // frozen data: courses, grades, attendance, comments\n  homeroomComment  String?\n  principalComment String?\n  generatedAt      DateTime         @default(now())\n  publishedAt      DateTime?\n  publishedById    String?\n  @@unique([studentId, termId])\n}\n```\n\nAlso add `gradingScaleId String?` to `Course` (null = school default) and `categoryId String?` to `Assignment` and `Quiz` with a category select added to their editors.\n\n### FR-2 Sync from assignments and quizzes (`src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts`)\n1. When an assignment or non-practice quiz is published, upsert a `GradeItem` (title, maxPoints, dueAt, category, term = term containing `dueAt` / `availableUntil`, falling back to the current term). Unpublishing or archiving sets `isVisible = false`; deleting deletes the item.\n2. When a submission is returned, upsert its `Grade` with `score = finalScore`. Saving without returning does not sync (students must not see unreturned scores). Exemptions set `excused = true`.\n3. When a quiz attempt reaches GRADED and results are visible, upsert `Grade.score` from `getStudentQuizScore` scaled to the quiz maxScore.\n4. A one-time backfill `npm run gradebook:backfill` creates items and grades for data that existed before this PRD; it is idempotent and runs in the seed.\n5. Grades written by sync are read-only in the gradebook UI (edit happens at the source) except `comment`; manual items are fully editable.\n\n### FR-3 Calculation (`src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts`, pure functions)\nFor a student, course and term:\n1. Consider visible items in the term whose student grade is not `excused`. An item counts when it has a score, or when it is past due and `missing` (counts as 0). Ungraded, not-missing items are ignored.\n2. Per category: drop the `dropLowest` lowest percentages (never dropping all), then `categoryPercent = Σ score / Σ maxPoints × 100`.\n3. Course percent = weighted mean of category percentages over categories that have at least one counted item, re-normalising weights to the categories present. Items without a category form an implicit \"Uncategorised\" category; if the course has no categories, course percent = total points earned / total possible × 100.\n4. Letter = first band where `percent >= minPercent` in the effective scale. Round percent half-up to 1 decimal place before letter lookup.\n5. `TermGradeOverride` percent/letter replace the computed values when set (letter-only overrides keep the computed percent).\n6. Example: Homework 40 % (scores 18/20, 9/10) and Exams 60 % (scores 70/100): Homework = 27/30 = 90.0 %, Exams = 70.0 %, course = 0.4 × 90 + 0.6 × 70 = 78.0 % → \"C+\" in the seed scale.\n\n### FR-4 Grading scales (`/admin/grading-scales`)\n1. CRUD for scales; band editor with letter, minimum %, optional GPA points and descriptor. Validation: bands strictly descending, lowest band minimum is 0, letters unique. Exactly one default.\n\n### FR-5 Category setup (course \"Gradebook\" settings)\n1. Teacher manages categories: name, weight, drop lowest, order. Weights must total 100 (live sum indicator) before saving. Course grading scale select (defaults to school default).\n\n### FR-6 Gradebook grid (course tab \"Gradebook\", TEACHER/ADMIN)\n1. Term selector. Grid built on MUI X `DataGrid` (MIT: column groups via `columnGroupingModel`, cell editing via `processRowUpdate`; pinned columns are not in the MIT version, so keep the student column first and use the grid's sticky header): first column students (sorted by last name), then items grouped by category (column header shows title, due date, max points, source icon), then category averages and the term percent + letter (bold). Horizontally scrollable; the DataGrid's built-in virtualisation handles up to 60 students × 120 items.\n2. Cell content: score, \"EX\" (excused), \"M\" (missing, red), \"—\" (ungraded). Late submissions show a small clock icon.\n3. Manual items: editable DataGrid cells — type a number, `Enter` / arrow keys move between cells, `E` excuse, `M` missing, `Delete` clears. Changes save on blur with optimistic update and per-cell error state.\n4. Synced cells: clicking opens the source (submission grading page or quiz attempt).\n5. \"Add manual item\" dialog: title, category, max points, date, term.\n6. Student row action: \"Override term grade / comment\" dialog (percent, letter, comment).\n7. Column menu: hide/show item to students, set all ungraded to missing (after due date), view item statistics (average, median, high, low).\n8. \"Export CSV\" exports the grid as displayed.\n\n### FR-7 Student and parent grade views\n1. Register student tab \"Grades\": for the selected term, one card per course with percent, letter and a colour (≥ 80 green, 60–79 amber, < 60 red); expanding shows each visible item (title, category, score/max, percent, comment, missing/excused flags) and category subtotals.\n2. `/grades` page for STUDENT and PARENT (child selector) showing the same.\n3. Course tab \"Grades\" for STUDENT/PARENT shows that course's items only.\n\n### FR-8 Report cards (`/admin/report-cards`)\n1. Select term → table of students (filter by grade level and section) with report card status (Not generated, Draft, Published) and missing-data warnings (for example \"2 courses have ungraded items\", \"No teacher comment for ENG-7A\").\n2. \"Generate drafts\" for the filtered students builds each `snapshot`: school name/logo, student name, admission number, grade level, section, homeroom teacher, term and year; per course: subject, teacher, percent, letter, descriptor, teacher comment (from overrides); attendance summary for the term (rate, absences, lates); grading scale legend. Regenerating a draft refreshes the snapshot; published cards are never changed by regeneration.\n3. Review page per card: rendered report card preview with editable homeroom comment (homeroom teacher or admin) and principal comment (admin). Homeroom teachers also get `/report-cards` listing their section's drafts to write comments.\n4. \"Publish\" (per card or bulk for filtered list) sets status PUBLISHED and sends `report_card.published` to student and parents (default email true). \"Unpublish\" (admin only, requires reason, audited).\n5. Print view `/report-cards/[id]/print`: A4 portrait, school letterhead, tables, signature lines for principal and homeroom teacher; uses `@media print`; \"Print / Save as PDF\" button calls `window.print()`. Bulk \"Print all\" renders filtered published cards with page breaks.\n6. Register student tab \"Report cards\": list of published cards (students/parents) or all (admin/teacher), each opening the print view.\n\n### FR-9 Notifications\n1. `grade.posted` → student + parents when a manual item grade is entered (default email false; batched: one notification per student per item).\n2. `report_card.published` as above.\n\n## API\n","numLines":140,"startLine":91,"totalLines":278}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014ckJaMdKYDdBS9FYLzRaTb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
