{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsKz2Xk3L5vnSu9fBbgC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've rewritten `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-11 to replace the old copy left from an earlier ticket. All 55 requirement IDs are cited, and every cited ID exists in `requirements.json`. No code was written or run; this sub-task only produces the design document.\n\nIntake reported no blockers, and the Overview says so. Things to know before the next steps:\n\n- **Quiz score helper already exists:** intake said `getStudentQuizScore` didn't exist, but it does, in `src/server/quiz/attempt-service.ts`. The design calls it as is rather than adding one to `grading.ts` as the tech-stack notes proposed. It doesn't check whether quiz results are visible yet, so the sync checks that first.\n- **Delayed quiz results need two extra hooks:** quizzes whose results show after close or on manual release need a bulk sync when results are released and at close. Without these, those quiz grades never reach the gradebook.\n- **Report cards never change after publishing:** report-card generation only updates cards still in DRAFT, and grade-editing code never writes report cards.\n- **Data model is exactly the PRD's:** no extra columns. Three open questions were settled to fit that:\n  - A teacher hiding an item survives later edits, because sync only changes visibility when the assignment or quiz is published or archived.\n  - Items with no category are shown but carry weight 0 in the course percent.\n  - The `grade.posted` notification only fires when a manual grade is first entered, which gives one per student per item.\n- **One endpoint outside the PRD's API table:** `POST /api/grade-items/:id/mark-missing`, for the \"set all ungraded to missing\" column action. It avoids sending one request (and writing one audit row) per student.\n\nFifteen assumptions (A1–A15, listed in §1.2) need product sign-off, but none blocks development. They include treating 89.95 → 90.0 as A− under the seed scale, and allowing report-card comments to be edited only while in DRAFT.\n\n`api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in that folder are still from an earlier ticket. `arch-api-contracts` must overwrite them next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":287,"cache_read_input_tokens":82698,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":287},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cedb5742-c42c-44c2-b06a-ff50226957e7","uuid":"ddc51661-1c92-4dd0-9111-8dd506036448","timestamp":"2026-11-09T12:08:39.749Z","request_id":"req_011CgsKz2JMmCx1THKtNXeMF"}
