{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsgF6WrCBHG5ziZAx2rM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the SH-12 system design to `artifacts/architect/system-design.md`, replacing the older SH-11 file that was there. It has the Overview, Component Breakdown, Data Flow, a test plan and a Requirements Traceability table. Every requirement from intake (FR-1 to FR-36, NFR-1 to NFR-11) maps to at least one design element. Intake reported no blockers, and the Overview says so.\n\n**Decisions made in this step:**\n- **Notifications that need acknowledgement (FR-26):** the notification type list is fixed per type, so \"in-app is mandatory only when acknowledgement is required\" can't be set per announcement. I kept the single `announcement.published` type and added an optional `mandatoryInApp` setting to `notify()`, a one-line change. The alternative was a second notification type, which would have changed the type name the requirement gives.\n- **Response codes:**\n  - Users who aren't in an announcement's audience get 404, so they can't tell it exists.\n  - Teachers who target an audience they aren't allowed to get 403.\n  - A second reminder within 24 hours gets 429, stored in a new nullable `lastRemindedAt` column.\n  - A non-admin editing an archived announcement gets 409.\n- **One set of audience rules:** each user's grades, sections, courses and children are loaded once. The same rules then decide single-user membership, build the database filter for the feed, and (expanded the other way) list all recipients. A test checks that the single-user check and the recipient list agree for every seed user.\n- **Visibility and scheduled sends:** whether an announcement is visible is worked out when it's read, from its publish and expiry times. The scheduled job only sends the publish notification, and it marks `notifiedAt` atomically first so overlapping runs can't send it twice.\n\n**Changes beyond the PRD's data model:** the `lastRemindedAt` column, some indexes for feed speed, and the links Prisma needs back from users and files. All are listed in the Overview. I also assumed one thing the PRD doesn't state: archived courses are left out when working out audiences.\n\nI didn't touch `api-contracts.json` or `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`. They are still the SH-11 versions and get overwritten when `arch-api-contracts` runs next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14859,"cache_read_input_tokens":63655,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14859,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59086f77-7341-496e-add0-8445c854c82b","uuid":"1b7fa06b-113a-4872-adee-ee81e856d7dc","timestamp":"2026-11-09T16:34:22.350Z","request_id":"req_011CgsgF64pZerjrAWUSm7F6"}
