{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pxb78sssCPuhbzWpVDjn8J","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13\n2\t\n3\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n5\t`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4.\n6\t\n7\t> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input.\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n10\t\n11\t| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |\n12\t|---|---|---|---|\n13\t| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |\n14\t| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |\n15\t| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |\n16\t| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |\n17\t| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |\n18\t| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |\n19\t| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |\n20\t| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |\n21\t| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |\n22\t| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |\n23\t| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n24\t| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |\n25\t| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |\n26\t| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |\n27\t| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |\n28\t| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |\n29\t| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |\n30\t| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |\n31\t| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |\n32\t| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |\n33\t\n34\t## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n35\t\n36\tLegend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n37\t\n38\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n39\t|---|---|---|\n40\t| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |\n41\t| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |\n42\t| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |\n43\t| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |\n44\t| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |\n45\t| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |\n46\t| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |\n47\t| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |\n48\t| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |\n49\t| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |\n50\t| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |\n51\t| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |\n52\t| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |\n53\t| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |\n54\t| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |\n55\t| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |\n56\t| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |\n57\t| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |\n58\t| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |\n59\t| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |\n60\t| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |\n61\t| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |\n62\t| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |\n63\t| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |\n64\t| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |\n65\t| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |\n66\t| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |\n67\t| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |\n68\t| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |\n69\t| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |\n70\t| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |\n71\t| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |\n72\t| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |\n73\t| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |\n74\t| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |\n75\t| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |\n76\t| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |\n77\t| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |\n78\t| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |\n79\t| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |\n80\t| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |\n81\t| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |\n82\t| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |\n83\t\n84\t## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)\n85\t\n86\t- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)\n87\t- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)\n88\t- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)\n89\t- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)\n90\t- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)\n91\t\n92\t## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system\n93\t\n94\t| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |\n95\t|---|---|---|---|\n96\t| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |\n97\t| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |\n98\t| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |\n99\t| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |\n100\t| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |\n101\t| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |\n102\t| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |\n103\t| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |\n104\t| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |\n105\t| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |\n106\t| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |\n107\t| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |\n108\t| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |\n109\t| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |\n110\t\n111\t## 5. Risks\n112\t\n113\t- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.\n114\t- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.\n115\t- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.\n116\t- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI.\n117\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f2dd57a-95b5-4614-9b2d-795cabd61e18","uuid":"169052d0-1d85-46b2-b4a6-4d395d812d1c","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:22:07.766Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-13\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:00:00Z), PRD-13 Direct Messaging. It has 32 FRs and 11 NFRs (43 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. The open decisions intake handed to the architect are in §4.\n\n> Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is left over from an earlier ticket (SH-12/SH-11). Its owning sub-task must overwrite it. None of those files is an SH-13 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-13 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no messaging models. The latest migration is `20261111000000_add_gradebook`. `User` has `role`, `status` (default INVITED) and `archivedAt`, with `@@index([role, status])`. `FileObject` back-relations are explicit per attachment table. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-1..4: one new migration (e.g. `20261112000000_add_messaging`). Add back-relations on `User` (participants, sent messages, reports filed/reviewed, settings, pending emails) and on `FileObject` (`messageAttachments`). |\n| B2 | `Notification` has **no entity/context column**: only `userId, type, title, body, link, readAt`, indexed on `(userId, readAt, createdAt)`. | schema L304-317 | FR-19 collapsing: \"replace older unread message.received rows for that conversation\" can only key on `link = /messages/<conversationId>` (plus `type` and `readAt: null`). Recommend `deleteMany({ userId in, type:'message.received', readAt:null, link })` before `notify()`. This is fine for performance because the leading `userId` index column applies. No schema change to Notification is needed. |\n| B3 | `notify()` writes the in-app rows **and enqueues email immediately** (EmailOutbox) when `input.email` is passed. It never throws and dedupes userIds. It filters DISABLED/ARCHIVED users. Preferences come from `resolvePrefs(def, pref)` in `notifications/preferences.ts`. | notify.ts L8-80 | FR-19/20 conflict: message email must be **deferred**. Call `notify()` for `message.received` **without** `email`, so only the in-app row is written. Upsert a `PendingMessageEmail` per recipient whose resolved `prefs.email` is true. The maintenance pass then re-checks `lastReadAt`/quiet hours and enqueues to EmailOutbox using the same `renderEmail('generic-notification')`. **arch-design-system** should define a small exported helper (e.g. `enqueueEmail(userIds, …)` or reuse of `resolvePrefs`) rather than duplicating notify's internals. |\n| B4 | `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const object (no runtime registration). The `COMMUNICATION` category exists. `mandatoryInApp` is a static boolean per type and `roles` is a per-type role list. | notifications/types.ts | FR-19: `message.received` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp false, roles ALL}. FR-26: `message.reported` {COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true, mandatoryInApp true, roles ['ADMIN']}. |\n| B5 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` is a per-process sliding window that returns `{ ok, retryAfterMs }`. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | NFR-4: `rateLimit('msg:'+userId, 30, 60_000)`. On failure, throw `AppError('RATE_LIMITED')` (429) with `details.retryAfterMs`. The limiter is per-process. This is accepted (existing ponytail note). |\n| B6 | `registerFileAccess`: built-ins are registered lazily in `registerBuiltInContexts` (files/contexts.ts). Unattached files (`contextId null`) are owner/ADMIN only. Resolver errors deny. Orphan files are purged after 24 h. | files/access.ts; files/contexts.ts | FR-27: add `register('message', messageResolver)` in `registerBuiltInContexts`. The resolver loads the Message by `file.contextId` (contextId = **messageId**, so a soft-deleted message can still be resolved), then allows a participant (`leftAt` irrelevant? see A7) or `isSafeguardingLead`. Attach files in the send transaction, or they are purged. Note: `FileAccessUser` is `{id, role}` only, so the resolver must query `isSafeguardingLead` itself. |\n| B7 | `SessionUser` = `{id, role, firstName, lastName, email}`. It has **no `isSafeguardingLead`**. | requireRole.ts L14-26 | NFR-1/FR-23..25: add a `requireSafeguardingLead()` helper (in `src/server/messaging/` or auth) that does `requireRole('ADMIN')` plus a DB read of the flag. Do not put the flag in the JWT: a revoked flag must take effect immediately. The page variant redirects to /forbidden (FR-23 says \"others get 403\"). |\n| B8 | Teacher→student reachability already exists: `getAccessibleStudentIds(TEACHER)` = ACTIVE enrollment in courses where `teacherId` or `coTeacherIds has` the teacher, **plus** SectionMember of sections they homeroom. The homeroom branch has **no academic-year filter**. `teaches(user, course)` is in course-access.ts. | student-access.ts L20-55; course-access.ts | FR-5/FR-32: reuse the same predicates (ideally share the Prisma `where` fragments) so contact rules and student-record access never disagree. Decide on the current-year filter for homeroom (A5). The PARENT branch is ParentStudentLink. |\n| B9 | `Enrollment @@unique([courseId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId, status])`. `ParentStudentLink @@unique([parentId, studentId])`, `@@index([studentId])`. `SectionMember @@unique([studentId, academicYearId])` (no `sectionId` index). | schema | FR-5/FR-8 queries are index-backed from the student side. `coTeacherIds has` is not indexable, but a single user's course set is small. |\n| B10 | Maintenance route `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` (CRON_SECRET) runs each job in its own try/catch + logger. The quiz pattern is `findMany(take)` → conditional `updateMany` claim → act if `count===1`. | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts; quiz/maintenance.ts | FR-20: add `sendDueMessageEmails(now)`, isolated in its own try/catch. Process `PendingMessageEmail where dueAt <= now`. If the participant's `lastReadAt >= message time`, drop the row. If now is inside quiet hours, push `dueAt` to the end of quiet hours. Otherwise enqueue and delete the row (delete = claim; `deleteMany` count===1). |\n| B11 | `getSchoolTimezone()` lives in `assignments-service.ts` (precedent: other modules import it). `schoolNow(now, tz)` returns `{isoDay, hhmm}`. `formatInSchoolTz`, and `fromZonedTime` from date-fns-tz, are available. | src/lib/dates.ts; assignments-service.ts L64 | FR-20/21 quiet hours: a pure `isInQuietHours(hhmm, start, end)` with midnight wrap (`start > end`) and `quietHoursEnd(now, tz, end)` → UTC instant. Unit-test both (NFR-10). FR-10 day grouping uses `formatInSchoolTz`. |\n| B12 | `ApiErrorCode` includes `RATE_LIMITED`, `FORBIDDEN`, `NOT_FOUND`, `CONFLICT`, `VALIDATION`. `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `parsePagination`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `audit()` exist. | src/server/http.ts; src/server/audit.ts | FR-28/NFR-6 handler conventions. Recommend returning 404 (not 403) for a non-participant on `GET /api/conversations/:id`, so cuids reveal nothing (NFR-1). FR-6 explicitly mandates 403 for **create** violations. |\n| B13 | **No admin user-edit UI exists.** `src/app/(app)/admin` has only attendance, courses, email-log, grading-scales, report-cards and sections. Users are edited only via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (ADMIN, `updateUserSchema`, audited). | src/app/api/users/[id]/route.ts; src/lib/validators/users.ts L103 | FR-2 resolution (intake's open question): add `isSafeguardingLead: z.boolean().optional()` to `updateUserSchema`. Reject or ignore it when the target role ≠ ADMIN. Audit the change (`user.update` metadata). **No form to extend.** Building a user-admin page is out of scope. |\n| B14 | **`/students/[id]` has no page.tsx or layout.tsx.** There are only sub-pages (attendance, assignments, courses, grades, report-cards), so there is no shared \"student page header\" today. | find src/app/(app)/students | FR-16: arch-design-system must pick the surface. Options: (a) add `students/[id]/layout.tsx` with a PageHeader + actions (affects all sub-pages, minimal per-page edits), or (b) put actions on each sub-page header. Recommend (a), keeping the `[id]` segment (no rename, per the PRD). The actions are client components that call `POST /api/conversations`. |\n| B15 | The course roster page is a **server component** rendering an MUI Table with no selection. PARENT gets notFound and STUDENT sees a name list. | courses/[courseId]/roster/page.tsx | FR-17: extract the TEACHER/ADMIN table into a client component with Checkbox selection and a toolbar button \"Message selected students\". It opens the FR-12 dialog prefilled. Rows carry `enrollmentId`, so the student id needs to be included in `RosterEntry` if it is not already there. |\n| B16 | `NavItem` has no badge field. `NotificationBell` implements a visibility-gated 30 s poll + MUI `Badge`. | src/config/navigation.ts; NotificationBell.tsx L23-73 | FR-18: add `{label:'Messages', href:'/messages', roles: ALL_ROLES}` and an optional `badge?: 'messages'` key. The shell renders a polled Badge from `/api/messaging/unread-count`. Extract the bell's poll loop into a small `usePolling(fn, ms)` hook and reuse it for FR-13's 5 s/30 s polls. |\n| B17 | `/account/notifications` = page.tsx + `PreferencesTable.tsx`. `/api/me/*` routes exist (notification-preferences, profile, …). | src/app/(app)/account/notifications | FR-21: add a `QuietHoursSection` client component under that page, plus `src/app/api/me/messaging-settings/route.ts` (GET/PUT, any role). |\n| B18 | Seed users: Alice Admin, Tom Teacher, Tina Tutor, Sam Student, Sara Scholar and Pat Parent (by email). The seed creates **no ParentStudentLink** and no enrollments. Courses come from elsewhere and `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` skips when missing. | prisma/seed.ts L16-22, L304 | FR-29: set `isSafeguardingLead=true` on Alice. The Pat↔Tom thread \"about Sam's homework\" needs a Pat↔Sam link to satisfy contact rules at runtime. Recommend the seed upsert that link (or skip the thread with a log, like other seeds). The MATH-7A group uses the first 4 ACTIVE enrollments and skips if there are fewer or the course is missing. Seeds write via Prisma directly (bypassing canMessage) but must leave data valid under canMessage. Make it idempotent by checking for existing seeded conversations (subject/participants). |\n| B19 | Shared components: FileUpload, FileList, UserAvatar, UserPicker, ConfirmDialog, Toast, EmptyState, PageHeader, DataTable (in `src/components/<Name>/`). `@mui/x-date-pickers` is installed. | src/components | FR-10/11/12/23/24: reuse FileList/FileUpload (context 'message'), UserAvatar, ConfirmDialog (delete/leave), Toast (report confirmation), DataTable (safeguarding lists). FR-12 recipient picker: UserPicker is a candidate only if it accepts a custom options source (grouped contacts). Otherwise use MUI Autocomplete with `groupBy`. FR-21 time inputs: x-date-pickers TimePicker. |\n| B20 | The mui-mcp server failed to connect in this session (CONNECT_TIMEOUT). | session | NFR-5 requires mui-mcp lookups during dev. The dev phase must retry it. This is not a blocker for architecture. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nLegend: DM = data model/migration, SVC = server service, API = route handler, UI = page/component, JOB = maintenance job, AUTH = authorization boundary, NOTIF = notification, FILE = file access, CFG = config registry, SEED, TEST, XC = cross-cutting rule.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | Conversation, ConversationParticipant (`@@unique([conversationId,userId])`, `@@index([userId])`, per-user `lastReadAt`, `mutedAt`/`archivedAt`, `leftAt`), Message (`@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, which NFR-2 depends on; `editedAt`, `deletedAt`), MessageAttachment (messageId, fileId; cascade on message), MessageReport + `ReportStatus`, MessagingSettings (userId unique, quietStart/End `String? HH:mm`). Add `updatedAt` per convention (A2). |\n| FR-2 | DM, API, AUTH | `User.isSafeguardingLead`. It can only be edited via `PATCH /api/users/:id` (B13) and is meaningful only for ADMIN. |\n| FR-3 | DM, SVC | `MessageRevision(messageId, body, createdAt)`, `@@index([messageId])`. Written in the same tx as the edit (original body before overwrite). Cascade with Message (messages are never hard-deleted anyway, NFR-3). |\n| FR-4 | DM, JOB | `PendingMessageEmail(userId, conversationId, dueAt)`, `@@unique([userId, conversationId])` so repeated sends upsert one row (the first unread message sets dueAt = now+10 min; later sends keep the earliest dueAt). `@@index([dueAt])`. |\n| FR-5 | SVC, AUTH | `canMessage(sender, recipient)` is a pure decision over pre-loaded relationship facts. Expose a batch form `messageableIds(sender, candidateIds)` to avoid N+1 queries for groups (≤25) and contacts (FR-8). Matrix: ADMIN→any, any→ADMIN, TEACHER↔TEACHER, TEACHER→STUDENT (managed course or homeroom, B8), TEACHER→PARENT (via the linked child under the same rule), STUDENT→own teachers, PARENT→linked child's teachers, all others false. Symmetry: student→teacher uses the same relation as teacher→student. Disabled/archived recipients → false. |\n| FR-6 | SVC, AUTH | Create conversation in one tx: participants = creator ∪ recipients (dedupe, exclude self from count rules), 2..25 total. Check `canMessage(creator, each)`. If any STUDENT is present, require ≥1 TEACHER/ADMIN. Any violation → 403 with nothing created. \"Students may reply in staff groups but cannot start student-student\" follows from canMessage(student, student)=false at create, plus the send-time rule (FR-7) being evaluated per-sender against **staff** participants only (A4). |\n| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH, UI | Send-time re-check. Non-staff sender: allowed iff canMessage(sender, p) holds for at least one remaining staff participant (A4). Otherwise 403 with code/reason `RELATIONSHIP_ENDED`. Staff always pass. `GET /api/conversations/:id` returns `canSend: boolean` so the composer shows the disabled message without a failed POST. |\n| FR-8 | SVC, API | `GET /api/messaging/contacts?q=`: role-specific grouped queries (PARENT: per child, \"My child's teachers (<child>)\"; STUDENT: \"My teachers\"; TEACHER: \"Students in <course>\", \"Parents of students in <course>\", homeroom, staff; all: \"School office\" = ADMINs). Status ACTIVE only. `q` filters on name. Cap each group (e.g. 50). |\n| FR-9 | UI, API | `/messages` layout with a two-pane `useMediaQuery(theme.breakpoints.down('md'))`, single pane + back below 768 px (theme `md`=900, so use a custom `down(768)` or confirm breakpoint, A8). List from `GET /api/conversations?archived=&q=` sorted `lastMessageAt desc`, with preview and `unreadCount` per row. Route: `/messages` and `/messages/[conversationId]`. |\n| FR-10 | UI, API | `GET /api/conversations/:id/messages?before=<id>&limit=30` (keyset on `(createdAt,id)`). Deleted messages are returned with `body: null, deleted: true` and attachments stripped for normal users (NFR-3: content is never exposed to non-safeguarding users). Day grouping in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-11 | UI, XC | Composer validation shared by the client and `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts` (body trim 1..5000, ≤5 fileIds). Enter=send / Shift+Enter=newline. Counter shows at >4500. |\n| FR-12 | UI | New-conversation dialog: Autocomplete multi-select grouped by contacts label, subject ≤120, first message. It posts `POST /api/conversations` with `{participantIds, subject?, body, fileIds?}`, creating the conversation + first message atomically. Also opened prefilled from FR-16/FR-17. |\n| FR-13 | UI, API, XC | 5 s poll of `?after=<lastId>` on the visible thread. 30 s poll on the list + nav badge. Gate on `document.visibilityState` (B16). The `after` query must also surface **edits/deletes** of already-loaded messages, or edits only appear on reload (A9). |\n| FR-14 | API, SVC, UI | `POST /api/conversations/:id/read` (sets lastReadAt=now and marks this conversation's unread `message.received` notifications read; deletes the PendingMessageEmail row), `/mute`, `/archive` (toggle body `{archived}`), `/leave`. Leave: set `leftAt`, which blocks further reads/sends for that user. Refuse (409/403) for the creator when `involvesStudent` is true. Group-only: DMs with 2 participants cannot be left (A10). Sending auto-unarchives for other participants? (A11). |\n| FR-15 | SVC, API | `PATCH /api/messages/:id` / `DELETE` (soft: `deletedAt`). Sender only, `now - createdAt ≤ 15 min`, not already deleted. Edit writes a MessageRevision + `editedAt` in one tx. No hard-delete path exists anywhere. |\n| FR-16 | UI | Student page actions (surface per B14). TEACHER/ADMIN \"Message parents\": participants = linked parents (+ creator). Hide the action if there are none or canMessage fails. PARENT \"Message teacher\": picker of the child's teachers (subset of contacts) → dialog. |\n| FR-17 | UI | Roster selection + action (B15). TEACHER only (ADMIN may also be offered, harmless). |\n| FR-18 | CFG, API, UI | Nav entry + badge (B16). `GET /api/messaging/unread-count` = count of the user's non-left participations where `lastMessageAt > coalesce(lastReadAt, epoch)` (count conversations, not messages: cheap, index-friendly). Archived conversations excluded? (A11). |\n| FR-19 | NOTIF, SVC | After the send tx commits: for each other participant not muted and not left, delete older unread `message.received` rows with the same link (B2), then `notify()` in-app only (B3). Title \"New message from <sender>\", body = 200-char plain preview, link `/messages/<id>`. |\n| FR-20 | JOB, DM, NOTIF | Upsert a PendingMessageEmail (dueAt=now+10 min) for recipients whose email pref is on (B3). Job per B10. Quiet hours read from MessagingSettings, evaluated in the school timezone (B11). |\n| FR-21 | UI, API, DM | MessagingSettings GET (defaults: no quiet hours) / PUT, Zod `HH:mm` regex. Both-or-neither validation. start == end is rejected. Applies to all roles (A3). |\n| FR-22 | API, SVC, NOTIF | `POST /api/messages/:id/report {reason ≤1000}`. Participant only. Allowed on own/others' messages (or other people's only? A12). One OPEN report per (message, reporter) to avoid spam (unique or check). Then FR-26 notify. |\n| FR-23 | UI, API, AUTH, XC | `/admin/safeguarding` (tabs Reports / Conversations), gated by `requireSafeguardingLead` (B7). `GET /api/safeguarding/reports?status=` with OPEN first, then createdAt desc. Detail includes the message, ±5 messages (including deleted and with revisions) and participants. `PATCH /api/safeguarding/reports/:id {action: review\\|dismiss, note?}` sets status, reviewedById, reviewedAt and note, then calls `audit()` (NFR-11). The nav entry is shown only to leads (the nav filter is role-based, so either show it to ADMIN and 403 non-leads, or extend NavItem with a predicate, A13). |\n| FR-24 | UI, API, AUTH | `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations?participantId=&from=&to=` with `involvesStudent: true`, paginated. `GET /api/safeguarding/conversations/:id` = read-only full thread with deleted bodies and `revisions[]`. Same lead gate. |\n| FR-25 | XC, AUTH | `audit({action:'safeguarding.conversation.view', entityType:'Conversation', entityId})` on every safeguarding conversation view **and** on report detail views, since they expose conversation context. Done in the service, so both the API and the server page paths are covered. |\n| FR-26 | NOTIF | Notify `User where role=ADMIN, isSafeguardingLead, status ACTIVE` with `message.reported` (email allowed via notify's normal path: no deferral). Link `/admin/safeguarding?report=<id>`. The body must not include the message text (keep emails minimal). |\n| FR-27 | FILE, AUTH | B6. Send validates that each fileId is owned by the sender, unattached, and context 'message', then attaches in the tx (contextId = messageId). |\n| FR-28 | API, XC | All routes under `src/app/api/{conversations,messages,messaging,safeguarding,me/messaging-settings}`. Thin handlers + Zod + services in `src/server/messaging/`. Standard ok/paginated/error shapes. |\n| FR-29 | SEED | B18. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, DM | `involvesStudent` is computed in the create tx and is immutable afterwards (no participant-add API exists, so it stays correct). |\n| FR-31 | SVC | Update `lastMessageAt` in the send tx. `@@index` on ConversationParticipant `(userId)` + Conversation `lastMessageAt` serves the list ordering. Edits/deletes do **not** bump it. |\n| FR-32 | AUTH | B8: `teacherId = me OR coTeacherIds has me`. Resolved as yes (intake default, matches the existing `teaches()`). |\n| NFR-1 | AUTH, XC | Every service entry takes the SessionUser and loads `ConversationParticipant(conversationId, userId, leftAt null)` first. Non-participant → 404. Safeguarding → `requireSafeguardingLead`. File resolver per B6. Contacts never leak non-messageable users. |\n| NFR-2 | DM, API | `after` poll = participant check (unique-index lookup) + `Message where conversationId, (createdAt,id) > cursor` on `@@index([conversationId, createdAt])`, `take 100`. Return `[]` fast. The 30 s list/unread polls use the participant index. Avoid count-per-message aggregation for unread (FR-18). |\n| NFR-3 | DM, SVC, AUTH | No DELETE that removes rows. FK cascades exist only for actual tree cleanup. Deleted/edited originals are exposed only through safeguarding services. |\n| NFR-4 | API, XC | B5. Applies to `POST /api/conversations/:id/messages`. Recommend counting `POST /api/conversations` (it also sends) against the same key. |\n| NFR-5 | UI, XC | MUI only; B19/B20. Badge, Drawer/List, Autocomplete, TimePicker, Tabs, Menu, Chip, TextField. |\n| NFR-6 | XC | `src/lib/validators/messaging.ts`, `src/server/messaging/{contact-rules,conversations,messages,notifications,quiet-hours,safeguarding,maintenance}.ts`, logger, cuid, UTC storage. |\n| NFR-7 | UI | See FR-9 (breakpoint, A8). |\n| NFR-8 | XC | A 5 s poll guarantees ≤ ~5 s + request latency < 6 s. No websockets/SSE. |\n| NFR-9 | XC | There is no reactions, typing or broadcast endpoint. Do not touch announcements (PRD-12 is absent). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | `tests/unit/messaging/contact-rules.test.ts` (matrix incl. co-teacher, homeroom, DROPPED enrollment, group student-needs-staff, 26 participants), `quiet-hours.test.ts` (wrap midnight). `tests/integration/messaging/` (notification collapse, quiet-hours deferral via maintenance job, revision capture, 15-min window, rate limit, non-participant 404, safeguarding 403 + audit). `tests/e2e/messaging.spec.ts` (two browser contexts parent→teacher < 6 s; student→student blocked in the picker and on POST 403). |\n| NFR-11 | XC | Audit report review/dismiss and `isSafeguardingLead` changes. Users' own edits/deletes of their messages are not \"someone else's\" records, so no audit is needed. |\n\n## 3. New surface summary (for traceability)\n\n- **Models:** Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageAttachment, MessageRevision, MessageReport (+ReportStatus), MessagingSettings, PendingMessageEmail. Plus User.isSafeguardingLead. (FR-1..4, FR-30, FR-31)\n- **Services (`src/server/messaging/`):** contact-rules, contacts, conversations, messages, read-state, notifications/pending-email, quiet-hours, safeguarding, maintenance (`sendDueMessageEmails`). (FR-5..8, FR-14, FR-15, FR-19..27)\n- **Routes:** conversations (list/create/get/read/mute/archive/leave), conversation messages (list before/after, send), messages/:id (patch/delete/report), messaging/unread-count, messaging/contacts, me/messaging-settings, safeguarding reports + conversations, and a hook into the internal dispatch route. (FR-28, FR-20)\n- **Pages:** `/messages`, `/messages/[conversationId]`, `/admin/safeguarding`, plus a Quiet hours section on `/account/notifications`, student layout actions and roster selection. (FR-9..18, FR-21, FR-23, FR-24)\n- **Registries:** 2 notification types, 1 file context, 1 nav item (+badge). (FR-18, FR-19, FR-26, FR-27)\n\n## 4. Open decisions for arch-design-system\n\n| # | Question | Recommendation | Drives |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Co-teachers count as \"managing\" a course? | **Yes**: matches `teaches()`/`getAccessibleStudentIds`. | FR-32, FR-5 |\n| A2 | `updatedAt` on new models (the PRD block omits it)? | Add `updatedAt @updatedAt` to Conversation, ConversationParticipant, Message, MessageReport and MessagingSettings (platform convention). Leave it off append-only MessageRevision, MessageAttachment and PendingMessageEmail. Treat the PRD block as the minimum field set. | FR-1, NFR-6 |\n| A3 | Quiet hours for all roles? | **All roles** (the settings endpoint is open to any role). | FR-21, FR-20 |\n| A4 | Send-time rule in groups: what does \"relationship ended\" mean when there are many participants? | Non-staff sender may send iff canMessage(sender, s) for ≥1 staff participant still present. If no staff remain (all left), they are refused. Note that staff can never leave a student group they created (FR-14). | FR-7, FR-6 |\n| A5 | Homeroom teacher reachability: current academic year only? | Filter `section.academicYear.isCurrent = true` for messaging (otherwise last year's homeroom stays reachable). Keep student-access.ts unchanged (do not modify other PRDs' behaviour). | FR-5 |\n| A6 | Where is isSafeguardingLead edited? | API/validator only (no form exists, B13). Document that the flag is set via the seed or the API. | FR-2 |\n| A7 | Does a participant who **left** keep read access to the old thread and attachments? | No: `leftAt` set → treat as non-participant (list hides it, 404 on get). Safeguarding still sees everything. | FR-14, FR-27, NFR-1 |\n| A8 | The 768 px breakpoint does not match MUI default `md` (900). | Use `theme.breakpoints.down(768)` locally, not a theme change. | FR-9, NFR-7 |\n| A9 | How do polling clients learn about edits/deletes? | `after` responses also return `changed[]` = messages in the loaded window with `updatedAt > since` (pass `since` ISO alongside `after`). Alternatively accept staleness until reload. Recommend the former (cheap; same index plus `updatedAt`). | FR-13, FR-15 |\n| A10 | Can a participant leave a 1:1 conversation? | No: \"leave group\" only applies when there are >2 participants. Archive covers 1:1. | FR-14 |\n| A11 | Does a new message unarchive the conversation for recipients, and does the unread badge count archived conversations? | Yes, unarchive for recipients on new message (standard inbox behaviour). Unread count then needs no archive filter. | FR-9, FR-14, FR-18 |\n| A12 | Can a user report their own message, or report the same message twice? | Others' messages only. One OPEN report per (message, reporter): return 409 CONFLICT otherwise. | FR-22 |\n| A13 | Nav visibility for `/admin/safeguarding` (role-only nav filter)? | Show the item to ADMIN only via a new optional `NavItem.requires?: 'safeguardingLead'` evaluated in the shell with the flag loaded server-side. The page still enforces 403. Otherwise leave it out of nav and link from the `message.reported` notification. | FR-23 |\n| A14 | Seed Pat↔Sam link missing (B18). | The seed upserts `ParentStudentLink(Pat, Sam)` if absent before creating the Pat↔Tom thread, and skips the thread if Tom does not teach Sam. | FR-29 |\n\n## 5. Risks\n\n- **Notification collapse via `link` match** (B2) is coupled to the link format. Keep link building in a single helper used by both send and read paths.\n- **Per-process rate limiter and in-memory state** (B5) are not shared across instances. This is accepted per the existing ponytail note.\n- **Email-preference bypass**: deferring email outside `notify()` (B3) must still honour `NotificationPreference` and DISABLED/ARCHIVED filtering. Reuse `resolvePrefs`, and cover it in integration tests.\n- **mui-mcp unavailable** in this session (B20). The dev phase must retry it before writing UI.\n","numLines":117,"startLine":1,"totalLines":117}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pxb78sssCPuhbzWpVDjn8J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
