{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JgoRivRSSG5YnpFj7QiiG6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-14\n2\t\n3\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:10:00Z), PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays. It has 37 FRs and 12 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n5\t`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 3 warnings: PRD-12 is missing, the academic-year page is missing, and new dependencies are needed. The decisions left open are in §3.\n6\t\n7\t> This file replaces a leftover SH-13 version. Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is also left over from SH-13. Its owning sub-task must overwrite it, and none of those files is an SH-14 input.\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n10\t\n11\t| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-14 |\n12\t|---|---|---|---|\n13\t| B1 | The schema has no calendar models and no `AudienceType` enum. There is no `Announcement` model and no `audience.ts`. The latest migration is `20261112000000_add_direct_messaging`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-2/FR-3: add one new migration, e.g. `20261113000000_add_calendar`. `AudienceType` must be defined here (see D1). Add back-relations on `User` for events created, RSVPs and the feed token. |\n14\t| B2 | Audience targets that already exist: `GradeLevel` (Grade 6/7/8 seeded), `Section` (`homeroomTeacherId`, `gradeLevelId`, per year), `SectionMember` (`@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])`), `Course` (`teacherId`, `coTeacherIds String[]`, `sectionId?`), `Enrollment` (ACTIVE/DROPPED, `@@index([studentId,status])`) and `ParentStudentLink`. `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` exists. | schema L115-470 | FR-3: the minimal enum is `SCHOOL`, `GRADE_LEVEL`, `SECTION` and `COURSE`, plus a role filter so the seed's \"Grade 7 parents\" works (see D1). Every type resolves to student ids through existing tables. Parents are added through `ParentStudentLink`. |\n15\t| B3 | `getScheduleForDate` and `getSchoolScheduleForDate` both contain a placeholder comment: `// PRD-14 holidays hook in here: return [] when date is a school holiday.` Both return `ScheduleEntry[]` and have no reason field. A private `schoolTimezone()` exists at L488. | timetable-service.ts L542-583 | FR-17: put the `isSchoolDay` check at those two hooks. **The return type cannot change without touching callers** (`attendance-service.ts` L130 and L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Recommendation: keep `ScheduleEntry[]` and add a sibling, e.g. `getDayInfo(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`, which callers use to show the holiday name. The alternative is a new return shape, which needs every caller updated. |\n16\t| B4 | Both `isSchoolDay` and `getScheduleForDate` apply the teaching-weekday rule `day?.isTeaching ?? isoDay <= 5` from the `SchoolDay` table. | timetable-service.ts L552, L572 | FR-16: reuse `listSchoolDays()` (exported L112) instead of re-implementing the fallback. Watch for import cycles: calendar-service will import from timetable-service, and timetable-service calls back into `isSchoolDay`. Put the pure date→isoDay and holiday lookup in calendar-service with **no** import from timetable-service, or pass teaching days in. |\n17\t| B5 | Attendance teacher landing is `getToday(user, date?)` and admin overview is `getOverview(date?)`. Both are fed by the schedule functions. `RegisterForm.tsx` is the register UI. | attendance-service.ts L122-150, L463-475 | FR-18: `getToday` returns `{noSchoolReason}` alongside its existing fields. Saving a register on a no-school date requires a confirm flag in the save body (e.g. `holidayOverride: true`) and the server checks it. That makes it a server-side rule, not only a dialog. |\n18\t| B6 | The assignment editor is `courses/[courseId]/assignments/AssignmentForm.tsx`, using `DateTimePicker` on `dueAt` with school-tz `toWall/fromWall`. Quiz settings are in `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` (`availableUntil`). | grep | FR-19: both are client components. Fetch `GET /api/school-day?date=` on date change and render a non-blocking MUI `Alert`. Saving is unchanged. |\n19\t| B7 | Notification registry `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const and its `COMMUNICATION`/`ACADEMIC` categories exist. `notify({type,userIds,title,body,link,email})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. `notifyStudentAndParents` / `expandStudentRecipients` add linked parents. | notifications/types.ts; notify.ts L30, L89-120 | FR-23/28/29: add `event.created`, `event.updated` and `event.rsvp_reminder`. **`defaultEmail` is per type, but FR-28 wants it per category** (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email on by default). See D5. Resolve audience → userIds once, then call `notify`. |\n20\t| B8 | The maintenance cron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each job in its own try/catch + logger (reminders, quiz, message emails). | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-23: add `sendRsvpReminders(now)` to its own isolated block. \"Once per event\" needs a claim column: `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?`, claimed with conditional `updateMany` (quiz `resultsReleasedAt` precedent). The PRD model list doesn't include that column. Adding it is a small, justified deviation (flag it). |\n21\t| B9 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` → `{ok, retryAfterMs}`. It is per-process and marked with a `ponytail` note. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | FR-27: `rateLimit('ical:'+tokenHash, 60, 3_600_000)` → 429 `RATE_LIMITED`. Key on the **hash**, not the raw token, so raw tokens never sit in memory maps or logs. |\n22\t| B10 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` with codes incl. `RATE_LIMITED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN` and `VALIDATION_ERROR`. `requireRole`, `requireUser`, `requirePageRole` and `requirePageUser` exist. `audit()` exists. | http.ts; requireRole.ts; audit.ts | NFR-7/8/FR-36. The feed route is the only unauthenticated handler. It returns `text/calendar` and the 404 is a plain response, not JSON. Its token parse failure and token-not-found case return the same 404. |\n23\t| B11 | Access helpers: `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` ('ALL' for admin, own id for students, linked children for parents, enrolled + homeroom students for teachers), `assertCanViewStudent`, `assertCanManageCourse` (course-access.ts L56) and `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` (assignments-service L262). | auth/*.ts | FR-7: teacher create checks are `assertCanManageCourse` for COURSE audiences and `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` for SECTION. FR-11/FR-32 `studentId` param: use `resolveViewedStudent`/`assertCanViewStudent` (404 for other families). |\n24\t| B12 | Deadline data sources already exist: `/api/me/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` and `/api/me/children` routes, `Assignment @@index([courseId, dueAt])`, `Quiz @@index([courseId,status])` with `availableUntil`, and `getPersonalTimetable`. | api/me/*; schema | FR-10/FR-32: the calendar merge should call the existing service functions behind these routes (scoped to a date range), not new queries. A range filter on `dueAt`/`availableUntil` may need adding. Only PUBLISHED assignments/quizzes should be included, matching what the user can open. |\n25\t| B13 | School timezone is read in two places: exported `getSchoolTimezone()` in assignments-service.ts L64 and private `schoolTimezone()` in timetable-service. `getSchoolSettings` (cached) is in services/settings.ts. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `schoolNow`, `formatInSchoolTz` and `ISO_DAY_NAMES`. date-fns-tz 3.2.0 is installed. | grep | NFR-3/FR-4: use `getSchoolTimezone()` and do not add a third copy. All-day ↔ `fromZonedTime(midnight, tz)` conversions belong as pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` (unit-testable, client-safe). |\n26\t| B14 | No `/admin/academic-years` page exists. Only APIs exist: `academic-years/[id]`, `…/set-current`, `…/terms`, `…/terms/generate`, and `terms.ts` service functions. Seed terms: S1 2026-08-17→2027-01-15, S2 2027-01-18→2027-06-11. | ls src/app/(app)/admin; seed.ts L91-94 | FR-20: a host page is needed (see D2). Note that the seed's gap between S1 and S2 is a weekend (Jan 16–17), so \"Add term breaks\" on seed data produces one short break. Winter break is **inside** S1 and is seeded explicitly. |\n27\t| B15 | `navigation.ts` has `NavItem {label, href, icon, roles, group?, badge?, requires?}` and `ALL_ROLES`. The account area has `notifications` and `security` pages only, and no account nav entries. | config/navigation.ts | FR-35: add `{label:'Calendar', href:'/calendar', roles: ALL_ROLES}`. `/account/calendar` is linked from the account area like the other `/account/*` pages; no sidebar entry is needed (D6). |\n28\t| B16 | Shared UI exists: `components/Toast/useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView`, `MarkdownEditor`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState` and `UserPicker`. `react-markdown` 10.1.0 is installed. `components/messaging` exists, but no audience builder. | ls src/components | NFR-1/NFR-9: the drawer uses `MarkdownView` and the editor uses `MarkdownEditor`. Delete confirmation uses `ConfirmDialog`. The RSVP list uses `DataTable`. CSV export reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. A new `components/AudienceBuilder` is the only new shared component (D1). |\n29\t| B17 | `package.json` has MUI 9.5.0 for material, icons, x-charts, x-data-grid and x-date-pickers, plus `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 as an override. There is no `@mui/x-scheduler`, `ics` or `node-ical`. | package.json | FR-1: pin the scheduler with an exact version from MUI MCP, and check its peer range against `@mui/material` 9.5.0 and `@mui/x-internals`. NFR-6: `node-ical` as an exact-pinned devDependency. `ics` is not needed, because a hand-written RFC 5545 builder (about 100 lines, pure) is easier to test for escaping and folding (tech-stack sub-task decides). |\n30\t| B18 | Seed: academic year 2026-2027 is current, Grade 6/7/8 exist, and sections 7A/7B exist. **There is no \"Robotics Club\" course anywhere**, and no Announcement exists. Seeds use the `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` + skip-with-log pattern. | seed.ts; grep | FR-37: the Chess club audience needs a Robotics Club course. Either seed it (an ELECTIVE `Course`, with `CourseKind` available) or skip with a log (D7). Sports day is seeded without an announcement link. |\n31\t| B19 | `Notification` has only `link` for context (no entity column). | schema L313-326 | FR-28/29 links: `/calendar?event=<id>` so the page can open the drawer from a query param. |\n32\t\n33\t## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n34\t\n35\tConcern key: **DM** data model/migration, **SVC** server service, **API** route handler, **UI** page/component, **JOB** cron/maintenance, **AUTH** access boundary, **INT** change to existing module, **NOTIF** notification type, **DEP** dependency, **TEST**, **SEED**.\n36\t\n37\t| Req | Concern | Notes for arch-design-system |\n38\t|---|---|---|\n39\t| FR-1 | DEP | `@mui/x-scheduler` exact pin taken from the MUI MCP `useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`. This comes first in the dev plan. If MCP is unreachable, stop (NFR-2). Check peer deps against 9.5.0 (B17). |\n40\t| FR-2 | DM | Enums `EventCategory`, `Recurrence` (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY), `RsvpResponse` (YES/NO/MAYBE). Models `CalendarEvent`, `EventAudience` (cascade from event), `EventRsvp` (`@@id([eventId,userId])`, cascade) and `CalendarFeedToken` (`userId @unique`, `tokenHash @unique`). Add `@@index([startAt, endAt])` on events. Recurrence widens the read window, so range queries must be `startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR recurrence != NONE AND recurrenceUntil >= from)`. Index use is partial, which is fine at school scale. Possible extra columns: `rsvpReminderSentAt` (B8). |\n41\t| FR-3 | DM, AUTH | Decision D1. The audience resolver (`resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` and `userMatchesAudience(user, audiences)`) is the hub of FR-7/10/21/23/26/28/29/31/32. Build it once, in a form PRD-12 can adopt (e.g. `src/server/audience/audience.ts`). |\n42\t| FR-4 | SVC | Zod in `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (client-safe, shared with the editor dialog). Cross-field rules use `.superRefine`: endAt ≥ startAt; recurrenceUntil required when recurrence ≠ NONE and ≤ startAt + 1 year; guests 0–5. All-day normalisation (school-tz midnight, **exclusive** end) is a server-side transform, because the client sends dates and not instants. Unit-test the exclusive end (NFR-10). |\n43\t| FR-5 | SVC | Default applied in the service when `isNoSchool` is undefined: `category in (HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK)`. Not a DB default (it depends on another column). |\n44\t| FR-6 | AUTH | Service-level check: a non-admin sending `isNoSchool`, `isPublic` or a HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK category gets 403. The editor UI hides these fields, but the server is authoritative. |\n45\t| FR-7 | AUTH | A teacher's audiences must all be COURSE audiences they manage (`assertCanManageCourse`) or SECTION audiences they homeroom. SCHOOL or GRADE_LEVEL gives 403 (AC-7). This also applies on PATCH when audiences change. |\n46\t| FR-8 | AUTH | Edit/delete when `createdById === user.id` or the user is ADMIN. Others get 403 if they can see the event, 404 otherwise. |\n47\t| FR-9 | UI, DEP | Client page `/calendar` (server `page.tsx` does `requirePageUser`, then a client `CalendarView`). The view switches at the 768 px breakpoint via `useMediaQuery`. Agenda \"infinite scroll\" means fetching the next 30-day window on scroll. The range cap is 100 days (FR-32). Fallback components only where the Community scheduler lacks a feature. Record each fallback in system-design with its MCP doc reference. |\n48\t| FR-10 | UI | Chips with localStorage key e.g. `calendar.sources`. Sources map 1:1 to the `sources=` query param. Timetable blocks only in Week view: don't fetch `timetable` unless the Week view is active. Holidays vs School events default: HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` belong to \"Holidays\" only, with no duplicates (intake's default, D3). |\n49\t| FR-11 | UI, AUTH | Parent child filter → `studentId=` (omitted = all children). Server validates via `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Deadline items carry `childName`. Event audience matching for parents uses the union of their children (and the parent's own role for role-filtered audiences). |\n50\t| FR-12 | UI | Right `Drawer`. Data comes from the expanded item plus `GET /api/events/:id` for full detail and RSVP. \"Add to my calendar\" = `<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`. Edit/delete visible when `canEdit` is set; the server computes `canEdit` and returns it. |\n51\t| FR-13 | UI | Deadline items carry an `href` set by the server (`/assignments/<id>` or the quiz route). Clicking navigates; no drawer. |\n52\t| FR-14 | UI | `EventEditorDialog` with React Hook Form + the shared Zod schema. Uses `AudienceBuilder` (D1), the recurrence select + until date, the RSVP switch + deadline, and `MarkdownEditor`. Admin-only fields are rendered only for ADMIN (FR-6). |\n53\t| FR-15 | SVC | Pure `expandOccurrences(event, from, to)` in calendar-service (or `src/lib/calendar/recurrence.ts`). WEEKLY = +7 days **in wall-clock school time** (DST, NFR-3), not +7×24h. MONTHLY-by-date: skip months without that day (e.g. 31st). Document this, because RRULE `BYMONTHDAY=31` also skips, so UI and feed agree. Each occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. Heavily unit-tested. |\n54\t| FR-16 | SVC | `isSchoolDay(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`. Checks the weekday against `SchoolDay` (B4), then SCHOOL-audience `isNoSchool` events covering the date, **including recurring ones** (expand within that day). Reason = `Holiday: <title>` or `Not a teaching day`. A batched variant `noSchoolDays(from, to)` for the month view/landing avoids N queries (NFR-4). |\n55\t| FR-17 | INT | Hook at the two marked lines (B3). Today views use `GET /api/school-day` or the server-side `isSchoolDay`. Keep the `ScheduleEntry[]` signature to avoid caller churn. |\n56\t| FR-18 | INT, AUTH | `getToday` adds the no-school reason. Register save needs the override flag, enforced server-side (B5). Banner + `ConfirmDialog` in `RegisterForm`. |\n57\t| FR-19 | INT, UI | Non-blocking alert in two forms (B6). Only uses FR-34. |\n58\t| FR-20 | UI, SVC | Decision D2. Service `createTermBreaks(academicYearId, actor)`: for each consecutive term pair with a gap of at least one day, create a TERM_BREAK all-day SCHOOL event over the gap (start = day after term end, exclusive end = next term start). Idempotent: skip if an identical TERM_BREAK already exists. ADMIN only + audit. |\n59\t| FR-21 | API, AUTH | `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`. Rules: RSVP enabled, the user is in the audience, now < `rsvpDeadline`, guests > 0 only for PARENT (D4). Deadline violations return 409 `CONFLICT` or `VALIDATION_ERROR` (pick one and document it). Upsert on the composite PK. Recurring events take a single RSVP for the series (edits apply to the whole series; no per-occurrence data). |\n60\t| FR-22 | API, UI | `GET /api/events/:id` includes `myRsvp` + totals `{yes,no,maybe,guests}`. `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv` is creator/ADMIN only and reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. The JSON version uses `DataTable` in the drawer or dialog. |\n61\t| FR-23 | JOB, NOTIF, DM | `event.rsvp_reminder`. The job selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline` within the next 48h, and `rsvpReminderSentAt` null. It claims each event, then notifies audience members with no RSVP row (B8). |\n62\t| FR-24 | UI | `/account/calendar` (requirePageUser). Copy via `navigator.clipboard`. Instructions are static text. Reset uses `ConfirmDialog`. |\n63\t| FR-25 | API, DM, AUTH | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed`: if no token exists, create one and return the URL once. If one exists, **the raw token cannot be shown again** because it is stored hashed. Return `{exists:true, url:null}` and require a reset to see a URL, or create on first GET only. The design must reconcile the \"copy\" UX with hashing (D8). `POST …/reset` replaces the hash. |\n64\t| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `buildIcs(items, tz)`: VCALENDAR + VTIMEZONE (generated from the IANA tz for the covered years; transitions from date-fns-tz offsets), VEVENT with DTSTART;TZID or VALUE=DATE for all-day, RRULE `FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z`, escaping `\\\\ ; , \\n`, and 75-octet line folding. Window is now−30d → now+365d. The items come from the same merge as FR-32 (NFR-5 parity), skipping timetable. Deadlines are 0-duration VEVENTs with a URL. |\n65\t| FR-27 | API, AUTH | `src/app/api/calendar/feed/[token]/route.ts`. The `.ics` suffix arrives inside the param, so strip it and hash with sha256 to look up the row. Rate limit (B9). Headers: `Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8`, `Cache-Control: private, max-age=900`. Disabled or archived user → 404. |\n66\t| FR-28 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.created` when `startAt` is within 30 days (for recurring events, the first occurrence). Email-default-by-category (D5). Recipients come from `resolveAudienceUserIds`, excluding the creator. |\n67\t| FR-29 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.updated` only when `startAt`, `endAt`, `allDay` or `location` changes **and** the event is upcoming. One notify call per PATCH. |\n68\t| FR-30 | SVC, API | `getPublicEvents(from,to)` → `isPublic` events expanded, public-safe fields only (no audience, no creator). The route is unauthenticated and range-capped like FR-32. PRD-18 is the consumer. Consider applying `rateLimit` per IP. |\n69\t| FR-31 | SVC | `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)` reuses the FR-32 merge with sources=events and a 90-day window, takes `limit`. No UI (NFR-11). |\n70\t| FR-32 | API, SVC, AUTH | `getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})` is the core merge. It returns a discriminated union `{kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', …}` with instants in UTC plus `allDay`. Validation rejects `to − from > 100 days`. Performance: one events query + one audience-match pass in memory, and one query per deadline source over all children at once (NFR-4). |\n71\t| FR-33 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/events`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id`, `GET /api/events/:id/ics`. Visibility = the user matches the audience **or** is the creator or ADMIN. Not visible → 404. |\n72\t| FR-34 | API | `src/app/api/school-day/route.ts` (singular, a new folder next to `school-days`, which stays untouched). `date` is `YYYY-MM-DD` in the school tz. Any authenticated user. |\n73\t| FR-35 | INT | Nav entry (B15, D6). |\n74\t| FR-36 | AUTH, SVC | In update/delete: `if (user.role==='ADMIN' && event.createdById !== user.id) audit({action:'event.update'|'event.delete', entityType:'CalendarEvent', entityId, metadata})`. |\n75\t| FR-37 | SEED | An idempotent `seedCalendar()` in `prisma/seed.ts`, matching events by title + startAt. Parent–teacher evening date = seed run date + 14 days, so it is not stable across runs; match it by title only. Robotics Club: D7. Sports day: no announcement link. |\n76\t| NFR-1 | UI, TEST | Lint/QA grep for banned imports. Only MUI + MUI X (incl. the scheduler). |\n77\t| NFR-2 | process | The dev phase must call MUI MCP before using any scheduler API, and system-design should list the doc pages to fetch (Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization). |\n78\t| NFR-3 | SVC, TEST | One concern across expansion (wall-clock stepping), all-day storage (tz midnight), the `VALUE=DATE` / TZID feed, and the scheduler `timezone` prop (check MCP Timezones page). Test a DST week (e.g. the US 2026-11-01 or 2027-03-14 transition, depending on the seed tz). |\n79\t| NFR-4 | SVC | <500 ms for a parent with 3 children in month view. Batch the child/course/section lookups, use one events query with an audience `OR` filter, and avoid per-day `isSchoolDay` calls. Add an index on `EventAudience(type, targetId)` beyond the PRD spec (the PRD's model has the event FK; add `@@index([type, targetId])`). |\n80\t| NFR-5 | AUTH, SVC | `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stored as sha256 hex. The feed reuses `getCalendarItems`, so visibility can't drift. Integration test for parity. |\n81\t| NFR-6 | TEST, DEP | `node-ical` devDependency. Parse `buildIcs` output in a unit test and the feed route output in an integration test. |\n82\t| NFR-7 | AUTH | Every handler uses `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (token auth) and `/api/public/events` (public by design). Per-entity checks live in calendar-service, not in the routes. |\n83\t| NFR-8 | all | `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (+ `ical.ts`, `recurrence.ts` if split). Thin routes. `{data}` responses. `logger`. cuid ids. |\n84\t| NFR-9 | INT | Reuse list: timetable-service (B3/B4), rate-limit (B9), notify (B7), audit, DataTable, useToast, ConfirmDialog, MarkdownView/Editor, csv.ts, the dispatch cron (B8), getSchoolTimezone (B13), and the access helpers (B11). |\n85\t| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: expansion, isSchoolDay, ICS escaping/RRULE/folding, all-day exclusive end, term-break gaps. Integration: merge per role, token reset (old URL 404), RSVP deadline. Playwright: 3 flows. |\n86\t| NFR-11 | scope | No per-occurrence exceptions, no room booking, no two-way sync. PRD-16/18 get only FR-30/31 hooks. |\n87\t| NFR-12 | UI | 768 px breakpoint (FR-9). English only. Evergreen browsers. |\n88\t\n89\t## 3. Decisions for arch-design-system (open items from intake)\n90\t\n91\t- **D1 – AudienceType / audience.ts / builder (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14).** PRD-12 is absent. Recommendation: SH-14 defines `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }`. `EventAudience` gets `type`, `targetId String?` (null for SCHOOL) and `roles Role[] @default([])`, where empty means all roles. `roles` covers \"Grade 7 parents\". Resolver in `src/server/audience/audience.ts`, builder in `src/components/AudienceBuilder/`. Both are named generically so PRD-12 adopts them instead of re-creating them. Membership: SCHOOL = all active users; GRADE_LEVEL = students whose current-year SectionMember section has that grade (or `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`, pick one) plus their parents plus teachers of those sections or courses; SECTION = members + homeroom teacher + parents; COURSE = ACTIVE enrollments + teacher/co-teachers + parents.\n92\t- **D2 – FR-20 host page.** No `/admin/academic-years/[id]` UI exists. The minimal option is a small server page at that exact path that lists the year's terms (read-only) with an \"Add term breaks\" button. Full academic-year CRUD UI is out of scope. Add no nav entry; link to it from the calendar editor or admin, or reach it by URL.\n93\t- **D3 – Holidays vs School events chips.** Use intake's default: no duplication. HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` events appear only under \"Holidays\".\n94\t- **D4 – RSVP guests.** Parents only. The server forces 0 for other roles.\n95\t- **D5 – Email default per category (FR-28).** The registry's `defaultEmail` is per type. Options: (a) two types, `event.created` (defaultEmail false) and `event.holiday_created` (defaultEmail true); or (b) one type that passes `email` only for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK, which ignores the user preference toggle semantics. Recommend (a), because it stays inside the existing preference model with no changes to notify.ts.\n96\t- **D6 – Nav.** Add `/calendar` (all roles). `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, consistent with the existing account pages. It is reached from the account menu and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`.\n97\t- **D7 – Robotics Club course (FR-37).** Not in the seed. Recommend seeding a minimal ELECTIVE course `ROBOTICS` (teacher Tom, current year) only if absent, so the Chess club example works. The alternative is skip-with-log.\n98\t- **D8 – Feed URL display vs hashed storage (FR-24/25, NFR-5).** The raw token is only available at creation or reset. Recommendation: `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `{url}` only when it creates the first token, and `{url:null, createdAt}` otherwise. The page then says \"Reset link to get a new URL\". This needs to be explicit in the API contracts.\n99\t- **D9 – Schema deviations from the PRD's model list** (flag them in system-design): `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt`, `EventAudience.roles`, `@@index([type,targetId])`. Each traces to FR-23, FR-3/FR-37 and NFR-4.\n100\t\n101\t## 4. Risks\n102\t\n103\t- **R1 (high):** `@mui/x-scheduler` is beta. Its API (views, timezone, all-day exclusivity, custom event rendering for chips/colours) is unverified until MCP is consulted. Budget for fallbacks (FR-9).\n104\t- **R2:** The import cycle between timetable-service and calendar-service (B4).\n105\t- **R3:** DST correctness spans four places (FR-15 expansion, FR-4 storage, FR-26 VTIMEZONE, UI). One shared pure helper set in `src/lib/dates.ts` keeps them consistent.\n106\t- **R4:** Audience resolution is the performance hot path (NFR-4) and the security boundary (NFR-5/7). It needs a single implementation, tested per role.\n107\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aebc8821-7772-4638-b1aa-c18e63e97e7e","uuid":"66bdae5b-3592-4404-8801-1780d0fb9bb4","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:50:55.768Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-14\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-09T19:10:00Z), PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays. It has 37 FRs and 12 NFRs (49 requirements) at 96% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 3 warnings: PRD-12 is missing, the academic-year page is missing, and new dependencies are needed. The decisions left open are in §3.\n\n> This file replaces a leftover SH-13 version. Every other file in `artifacts/architect/` is also left over from SH-13. Its owning sub-task must overwrite it, and none of those files is an SH-14 input.\n\n## 1. Brownfield facts verified on disk\n\n| # | Fact | Evidence | Impact on SH-14 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | The schema has no calendar models and no `AudienceType` enum. There is no `Announcement` model and no `audience.ts`. The latest migration is `20261112000000_add_direct_messaging`. | prisma/schema.prisma; prisma/migrations | FR-2/FR-3: add one new migration, e.g. `20261113000000_add_calendar`. `AudienceType` must be defined here (see D1). Add back-relations on `User` for events created, RSVPs and the feed token. |\n| B2 | Audience targets that already exist: `GradeLevel` (Grade 6/7/8 seeded), `Section` (`homeroomTeacherId`, `gradeLevelId`, per year), `SectionMember` (`@@unique([studentId, academicYearId])`), `Course` (`teacherId`, `coTeacherIds String[]`, `sectionId?`), `Enrollment` (ACTIVE/DROPPED, `@@index([studentId,status])`) and `ParentStudentLink`. `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId` exists. | schema L115-470 | FR-3: the minimal enum is `SCHOOL`, `GRADE_LEVEL`, `SECTION` and `COURSE`, plus a role filter so the seed's \"Grade 7 parents\" works (see D1). Every type resolves to student ids through existing tables. Parents are added through `ParentStudentLink`. |\n| B3 | `getScheduleForDate` and `getSchoolScheduleForDate` both contain a placeholder comment: `// PRD-14 holidays hook in here: return [] when date is a school holiday.` Both return `ScheduleEntry[]` and have no reason field. A private `schoolTimezone()` exists at L488. | timetable-service.ts L542-583 | FR-17: put the `isSchoolDay` check at those two hooks. **The return type cannot change without touching callers** (`attendance-service.ts` L130 and L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Recommendation: keep `ScheduleEntry[]` and add a sibling, e.g. `getDayInfo(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`, which callers use to show the holiday name. The alternative is a new return shape, which needs every caller updated. |\n| B4 | Both `isSchoolDay` and `getScheduleForDate` apply the teaching-weekday rule `day?.isTeaching ?? isoDay <= 5` from the `SchoolDay` table. | timetable-service.ts L552, L572 | FR-16: reuse `listSchoolDays()` (exported L112) instead of re-implementing the fallback. Watch for import cycles: calendar-service will import from timetable-service, and timetable-service calls back into `isSchoolDay`. Put the pure date→isoDay and holiday lookup in calendar-service with **no** import from timetable-service, or pass teaching days in. |\n| B5 | Attendance teacher landing is `getToday(user, date?)` and admin overview is `getOverview(date?)`. Both are fed by the schedule functions. `RegisterForm.tsx` is the register UI. | attendance-service.ts L122-150, L463-475 | FR-18: `getToday` returns `{noSchoolReason}` alongside its existing fields. Saving a register on a no-school date requires a confirm flag in the save body (e.g. `holidayOverride: true`) and the server checks it. That makes it a server-side rule, not only a dialog. |\n| B6 | The assignment editor is `courses/[courseId]/assignments/AssignmentForm.tsx`, using `DateTimePicker` on `dueAt` with school-tz `toWall/fromWall`. Quiz settings are in `courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit/QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` (`availableUntil`). | grep | FR-19: both are client components. Fetch `GET /api/school-day?date=` on date change and render a non-blocking MUI `Alert`. Saving is unchanged. |\n| B7 | Notification registry `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` is a static const and its `COMMUNICATION`/`ACADEMIC` categories exist. `notify({type,userIds,title,body,link,email})` dedupes, never throws, and is called after commit. `notifyStudentAndParents` / `expandStudentRecipients` add linked parents. | notifications/types.ts; notify.ts L30, L89-120 | FR-23/28/29: add `event.created`, `event.updated` and `event.rsvp_reminder`. **`defaultEmail` is per type, but FR-28 wants it per category** (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK email on by default). See D5. Resolve audience → userIds once, then call `notify`. |\n| B8 | The maintenance cron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` runs each job in its own try/catch + logger (reminders, quiz, message emails). | internal/email/dispatch/route.ts | FR-23: add `sendRsvpReminders(now)` to its own isolated block. \"Once per event\" needs a claim column: `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?`, claimed with conditional `updateMany` (quiz `resultsReleasedAt` precedent). The PRD model list doesn't include that column. Adding it is a small, justified deviation (flag it). |\n| B9 | `rateLimit(key, limit, windowMs)` → `{ok, retryAfterMs}`. It is per-process and marked with a `ponytail` note. | src/server/rate-limit.ts | FR-27: `rateLimit('ical:'+tokenHash, 60, 3_600_000)` → 429 `RATE_LIMITED`. Key on the **hash**, not the raw token, so raw tokens never sit in memory maps or logs. |\n| B10 | `http.ts` provides `withHandler`, `ok`, `paginated`, `apiError`, `parseBody`, `parseQuery` and `AppError` with codes incl. `RATE_LIMITED`, `NOT_FOUND`, `FORBIDDEN` and `VALIDATION_ERROR`. `requireRole`, `requireUser`, `requirePageRole` and `requirePageUser` exist. `audit()` exists. | http.ts; requireRole.ts; audit.ts | NFR-7/8/FR-36. The feed route is the only unauthenticated handler. It returns `text/calendar` and the 404 is a plain response, not JSON. Its token parse failure and token-not-found case return the same 404. |\n| B11 | Access helpers: `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` ('ALL' for admin, own id for students, linked children for parents, enrolled + homeroom students for teachers), `assertCanViewStudent`, `assertCanManageCourse` (course-access.ts L56) and `resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId?)` (assignments-service L262). | auth/*.ts | FR-7: teacher create checks are `assertCanManageCourse` for COURSE audiences and `section.homeroomTeacherId === user.id` for SECTION. FR-11/FR-32 `studentId` param: use `resolveViewedStudent`/`assertCanViewStudent` (404 for other families). |\n| B12 | Deadline data sources already exist: `/api/me/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` and `/api/me/children` routes, `Assignment @@index([courseId, dueAt])`, `Quiz @@index([courseId,status])` with `availableUntil`, and `getPersonalTimetable`. | api/me/*; schema | FR-10/FR-32: the calendar merge should call the existing service functions behind these routes (scoped to a date range), not new queries. A range filter on `dueAt`/`availableUntil` may need adding. Only PUBLISHED assignments/quizzes should be included, matching what the user can open. |\n| B13 | School timezone is read in two places: exported `getSchoolTimezone()` in assignments-service.ts L64 and private `schoolTimezone()` in timetable-service. `getSchoolSettings` (cached) is in services/settings.ts. `src/lib/dates.ts` has `schoolNow`, `formatInSchoolTz` and `ISO_DAY_NAMES`. date-fns-tz 3.2.0 is installed. | grep | NFR-3/FR-4: use `getSchoolTimezone()` and do not add a third copy. All-day ↔ `fromZonedTime(midnight, tz)` conversions belong as pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` (unit-testable, client-safe). |\n| B14 | No `/admin/academic-years` page exists. Only APIs exist: `academic-years/[id]`, `…/set-current`, `…/terms`, `…/terms/generate`, and `terms.ts` service functions. Seed terms: S1 2026-08-17→2027-01-15, S2 2027-01-18→2027-06-11. | ls src/app/(app)/admin; seed.ts L91-94 | FR-20: a host page is needed (see D2). Note that the seed's gap between S1 and S2 is a weekend (Jan 16–17), so \"Add term breaks\" on seed data produces one short break. Winter break is **inside** S1 and is seeded explicitly. |\n| B15 | `navigation.ts` has `NavItem {label, href, icon, roles, group?, badge?, requires?}` and `ALL_ROLES`. The account area has `notifications` and `security` pages only, and no account nav entries. | config/navigation.ts | FR-35: add `{label:'Calendar', href:'/calendar', roles: ALL_ROLES}`. `/account/calendar` is linked from the account area like the other `/account/*` pages; no sidebar entry is needed (D6). |\n| B16 | Shared UI exists: `components/Toast/useToast`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView`, `MarkdownEditor`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`, `EmptyState` and `UserPicker`. `react-markdown` 10.1.0 is installed. `components/messaging` exists, but no audience builder. | ls src/components | NFR-1/NFR-9: the drawer uses `MarkdownView` and the editor uses `MarkdownEditor`. Delete confirmation uses `ConfirmDialog`. The RSVP list uses `DataTable`. CSV export reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. A new `components/AudienceBuilder` is the only new shared component (D1). |\n| B17 | `package.json` has MUI 9.5.0 for material, icons, x-charts, x-data-grid and x-date-pickers, plus `@mui/x-internals` 9.1.0 as an override. There is no `@mui/x-scheduler`, `ics` or `node-ical`. | package.json | FR-1: pin the scheduler with an exact version from MUI MCP, and check its peer range against `@mui/material` 9.5.0 and `@mui/x-internals`. NFR-6: `node-ical` as an exact-pinned devDependency. `ics` is not needed, because a hand-written RFC 5545 builder (about 100 lines, pure) is easier to test for escaping and folding (tech-stack sub-task decides). |\n| B18 | Seed: academic year 2026-2027 is current, Grade 6/7/8 exist, and sections 7A/7B exist. **There is no \"Robotics Club\" course anywhere**, and no Announcement exists. Seeds use the `findCourse(['MATH-7A'])` + skip-with-log pattern. | seed.ts; grep | FR-37: the Chess club audience needs a Robotics Club course. Either seed it (an ELECTIVE `Course`, with `CourseKind` available) or skip with a log (D7). Sports day is seeded without an announcement link. |\n| B19 | `Notification` has only `link` for context (no entity column). | schema L313-326 | FR-28/29 links: `/calendar?event=<id>` so the page can open the drawer from a query param. |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern key: **DM** data model/migration, **SVC** server service, **API** route handler, **UI** page/component, **JOB** cron/maintenance, **AUTH** access boundary, **INT** change to existing module, **NOTIF** notification type, **DEP** dependency, **TEST**, **SEED**.\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes for arch-design-system |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DEP | `@mui/x-scheduler` exact pin taken from the MUI MCP `useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`. This comes first in the dev plan. If MCP is unreachable, stop (NFR-2). Check peer deps against 9.5.0 (B17). |\n| FR-2 | DM | Enums `EventCategory`, `Recurrence` (NONE/WEEKLY/MONTHLY), `RsvpResponse` (YES/NO/MAYBE). Models `CalendarEvent`, `EventAudience` (cascade from event), `EventRsvp` (`@@id([eventId,userId])`, cascade) and `CalendarFeedToken` (`userId @unique`, `tokenHash @unique`). Add `@@index([startAt, endAt])` on events. Recurrence widens the read window, so range queries must be `startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR recurrence != NONE AND recurrenceUntil >= from)`. Index use is partial, which is fine at school scale. Possible extra columns: `rsvpReminderSentAt` (B8). |\n| FR-3 | DM, AUTH | Decision D1. The audience resolver (`resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)` and `userMatchesAudience(user, audiences)`) is the hub of FR-7/10/21/23/26/28/29/31/32. Build it once, in a form PRD-12 can adopt (e.g. `src/server/audience/audience.ts`). |\n| FR-4 | SVC | Zod in `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (client-safe, shared with the editor dialog). Cross-field rules use `.superRefine`: endAt ≥ startAt; recurrenceUntil required when recurrence ≠ NONE and ≤ startAt + 1 year; guests 0–5. All-day normalisation (school-tz midnight, **exclusive** end) is a server-side transform, because the client sends dates and not instants. Unit-test the exclusive end (NFR-10). |\n| FR-5 | SVC | Default applied in the service when `isNoSchool` is undefined: `category in (HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK)`. Not a DB default (it depends on another column). |\n| FR-6 | AUTH | Service-level check: a non-admin sending `isNoSchool`, `isPublic` or a HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK category gets 403. The editor UI hides these fields, but the server is authoritative. |\n| FR-7 | AUTH | A teacher's audiences must all be COURSE audiences they manage (`assertCanManageCourse`) or SECTION audiences they homeroom. SCHOOL or GRADE_LEVEL gives 403 (AC-7). This also applies on PATCH when audiences change. |\n| FR-8 | AUTH | Edit/delete when `createdById === user.id` or the user is ADMIN. Others get 403 if they can see the event, 404 otherwise. |\n| FR-9 | UI, DEP | Client page `/calendar` (server `page.tsx` does `requirePageUser`, then a client `CalendarView`). The view switches at the 768 px breakpoint via `useMediaQuery`. Agenda \"infinite scroll\" means fetching the next 30-day window on scroll. The range cap is 100 days (FR-32). Fallback components only where the Community scheduler lacks a feature. Record each fallback in system-design with its MCP doc reference. |\n| FR-10 | UI | Chips with localStorage key e.g. `calendar.sources`. Sources map 1:1 to the `sources=` query param. Timetable blocks only in Week view: don't fetch `timetable` unless the Week view is active. Holidays vs School events default: HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` belong to \"Holidays\" only, with no duplicates (intake's default, D3). |\n| FR-11 | UI, AUTH | Parent child filter → `studentId=` (omitted = all children). Server validates via `getAccessibleStudentIds`. Deadline items carry `childName`. Event audience matching for parents uses the union of their children (and the parent's own role for role-filtered audiences). |\n| FR-12 | UI | Right `Drawer`. Data comes from the expanded item plus `GET /api/events/:id` for full detail and RSVP. \"Add to my calendar\" = `<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`. Edit/delete visible when `canEdit` is set; the server computes `canEdit` and returns it. |\n| FR-13 | UI | Deadline items carry an `href` set by the server (`/assignments/<id>` or the quiz route). Clicking navigates; no drawer. |\n| FR-14 | UI | `EventEditorDialog` with React Hook Form + the shared Zod schema. Uses `AudienceBuilder` (D1), the recurrence select + until date, the RSVP switch + deadline, and `MarkdownEditor`. Admin-only fields are rendered only for ADMIN (FR-6). |\n| FR-15 | SVC | Pure `expandOccurrences(event, from, to)` in calendar-service (or `src/lib/calendar/recurrence.ts`). WEEKLY = +7 days **in wall-clock school time** (DST, NFR-3), not +7×24h. MONTHLY-by-date: skip months without that day (e.g. 31st). Document this, because RRULE `BYMONTHDAY=31` also skips, so UI and feed agree. Each occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. Heavily unit-tested. |\n| FR-16 | SVC | `isSchoolDay(date)` → `{isSchoolDay, reason}`. Checks the weekday against `SchoolDay` (B4), then SCHOOL-audience `isNoSchool` events covering the date, **including recurring ones** (expand within that day). Reason = `Holiday: <title>` or `Not a teaching day`. A batched variant `noSchoolDays(from, to)` for the month view/landing avoids N queries (NFR-4). |\n| FR-17 | INT | Hook at the two marked lines (B3). Today views use `GET /api/school-day` or the server-side `isSchoolDay`. Keep the `ScheduleEntry[]` signature to avoid caller churn. |\n| FR-18 | INT, AUTH | `getToday` adds the no-school reason. Register save needs the override flag, enforced server-side (B5). Banner + `ConfirmDialog` in `RegisterForm`. |\n| FR-19 | INT, UI | Non-blocking alert in two forms (B6). Only uses FR-34. |\n| FR-20 | UI, SVC | Decision D2. Service `createTermBreaks(academicYearId, actor)`: for each consecutive term pair with a gap of at least one day, create a TERM_BREAK all-day SCHOOL event over the gap (start = day after term end, exclusive end = next term start). Idempotent: skip if an identical TERM_BREAK already exists. ADMIN only + audit. |\n| FR-21 | API, AUTH | `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`. Rules: RSVP enabled, the user is in the audience, now < `rsvpDeadline`, guests > 0 only for PARENT (D4). Deadline violations return 409 `CONFLICT` or `VALIDATION_ERROR` (pick one and document it). Upsert on the composite PK. Recurring events take a single RSVP for the series (edits apply to the whole series; no per-occurrence data). |\n| FR-22 | API, UI | `GET /api/events/:id` includes `myRsvp` + totals `{yes,no,maybe,guests}`. `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps?format=csv` is creator/ADMIN only and reuses `src/server/csv.ts`. The JSON version uses `DataTable` in the drawer or dialog. |\n| FR-23 | JOB, NOTIF, DM | `event.rsvp_reminder`. The job selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline` within the next 48h, and `rsvpReminderSentAt` null. It claims each event, then notifies audience members with no RSVP row (B8). |\n| FR-24 | UI | `/account/calendar` (requirePageUser). Copy via `navigator.clipboard`. Instructions are static text. Reset uses `ConfirmDialog`. |\n| FR-25 | API, DM, AUTH | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed`: if no token exists, create one and return the URL once. If one exists, **the raw token cannot be shown again** because it is stored hashed. Return `{exists:true, url:null}` and require a reset to see a URL, or create on first GET only. The design must reconcile the \"copy\" UX with hashing (D8). `POST …/reset` replaces the hash. |\n| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `buildIcs(items, tz)`: VCALENDAR + VTIMEZONE (generated from the IANA tz for the covered years; transitions from date-fns-tz offsets), VEVENT with DTSTART;TZID or VALUE=DATE for all-day, RRULE `FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z`, escaping `\\\\ ; , \\n`, and 75-octet line folding. Window is now−30d → now+365d. The items come from the same merge as FR-32 (NFR-5 parity), skipping timetable. Deadlines are 0-duration VEVENTs with a URL. |\n| FR-27 | API, AUTH | `src/app/api/calendar/feed/[token]/route.ts`. The `.ics` suffix arrives inside the param, so strip it and hash with sha256 to look up the row. Rate limit (B9). Headers: `Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=utf-8`, `Cache-Control: private, max-age=900`. Disabled or archived user → 404. |\n| FR-28 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.created` when `startAt` is within 30 days (for recurring events, the first occurrence). Email-default-by-category (D5). Recipients come from `resolveAudienceUserIds`, excluding the creator. |\n| FR-29 | NOTIF, SVC | `event.updated` only when `startAt`, `endAt`, `allDay` or `location` changes **and** the event is upcoming. One notify call per PATCH. |\n| FR-30 | SVC, API | `getPublicEvents(from,to)` → `isPublic` events expanded, public-safe fields only (no audience, no creator). The route is unauthenticated and range-capped like FR-32. PRD-18 is the consumer. Consider applying `rateLimit` per IP. |\n| FR-31 | SVC | `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)` reuses the FR-32 merge with sources=events and a 90-day window, takes `limit`. No UI (NFR-11). |\n| FR-32 | API, SVC, AUTH | `getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})` is the core merge. It returns a discriminated union `{kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', …}` with instants in UTC plus `allDay`. Validation rejects `to − from > 100 days`. Performance: one events query + one audience-match pass in memory, and one query per deadline source over all children at once (NFR-4). |\n| FR-33 | API, AUTH | `POST /api/events`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/events/:id`, `GET /api/events/:id/ics`. Visibility = the user matches the audience **or** is the creator or ADMIN. Not visible → 404. |\n| FR-34 | API | `src/app/api/school-day/route.ts` (singular, a new folder next to `school-days`, which stays untouched). `date` is `YYYY-MM-DD` in the school tz. Any authenticated user. |\n| FR-35 | INT | Nav entry (B15, D6). |\n| FR-36 | AUTH, SVC | In update/delete: `if (user.role==='ADMIN' && event.createdById !== user.id) audit({action:'event.update'|'event.delete', entityType:'CalendarEvent', entityId, metadata})`. |\n| FR-37 | SEED | An idempotent `seedCalendar()` in `prisma/seed.ts`, matching events by title + startAt. Parent–teacher evening date = seed run date + 14 days, so it is not stable across runs; match it by title only. Robotics Club: D7. Sports day: no announcement link. |\n| NFR-1 | UI, TEST | Lint/QA grep for banned imports. Only MUI + MUI X (incl. the scheduler). |\n| NFR-2 | process | The dev phase must call MUI MCP before using any scheduler API, and system-design should list the doc pages to fetch (Quickstart, Views, Events, Timezones, Localization). |\n| NFR-3 | SVC, TEST | One concern across expansion (wall-clock stepping), all-day storage (tz midnight), the `VALUE=DATE` / TZID feed, and the scheduler `timezone` prop (check MCP Timezones page). Test a DST week (e.g. the US 2026-11-01 or 2027-03-14 transition, depending on the seed tz). |\n| NFR-4 | SVC | <500 ms for a parent with 3 children in month view. Batch the child/course/section lookups, use one events query with an audience `OR` filter, and avoid per-day `isSchoolDay` calls. Add an index on `EventAudience(type, targetId)` beyond the PRD spec (the PRD's model has the event FK; add `@@index([type, targetId])`). |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH, SVC | `crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stored as sha256 hex. The feed reuses `getCalendarItems`, so visibility can't drift. Integration test for parity. |\n| NFR-6 | TEST, DEP | `node-ical` devDependency. Parse `buildIcs` output in a unit test and the feed route output in an integration test. |\n| NFR-7 | AUTH | Every handler uses `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (token auth) and `/api/public/events` (public by design). Per-entity checks live in calendar-service, not in the routes. |\n| NFR-8 | all | `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (+ `ical.ts`, `recurrence.ts` if split). Thin routes. `{data}` responses. `logger`. cuid ids. |\n| NFR-9 | INT | Reuse list: timetable-service (B3/B4), rate-limit (B9), notify (B7), audit, DataTable, useToast, ConfirmDialog, MarkdownView/Editor, csv.ts, the dispatch cron (B8), getSchoolTimezone (B13), and the access helpers (B11). |\n| NFR-10 | TEST | Unit: expansion, isSchoolDay, ICS escaping/RRULE/folding, all-day exclusive end, term-break gaps. Integration: merge per role, token reset (old URL 404), RSVP deadline. Playwright: 3 flows. |\n| NFR-11 | scope | No per-occurrence exceptions, no room booking, no two-way sync. PRD-16/18 get only FR-30/31 hooks. |\n| NFR-12 | UI | 768 px breakpoint (FR-9). English only. Evergreen browsers. |\n\n## 3. Decisions for arch-design-system (open items from intake)\n\n- **D1 – AudienceType / audience.ts / builder (FR-3, FR-7, FR-14).** PRD-12 is absent. Recommendation: SH-14 defines `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }`. `EventAudience` gets `type`, `targetId String?` (null for SCHOOL) and `roles Role[] @default([])`, where empty means all roles. `roles` covers \"Grade 7 parents\". Resolver in `src/server/audience/audience.ts`, builder in `src/components/AudienceBuilder/`. Both are named generically so PRD-12 adopts them instead of re-creating them. Membership: SCHOOL = all active users; GRADE_LEVEL = students whose current-year SectionMember section has that grade (or `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId`, pick one) plus their parents plus teachers of those sections or courses; SECTION = members + homeroom teacher + parents; COURSE = ACTIVE enrollments + teacher/co-teachers + parents.\n- **D2 – FR-20 host page.** No `/admin/academic-years/[id]` UI exists. The minimal option is a small server page at that exact path that lists the year's terms (read-only) with an \"Add term breaks\" button. Full academic-year CRUD UI is out of scope. Add no nav entry; link to it from the calendar editor or admin, or reach it by URL.\n- **D3 – Holidays vs School events chips.** Use intake's default: no duplication. HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool` events appear only under \"Holidays\".\n- **D4 – RSVP guests.** Parents only. The server forces 0 for other roles.\n- **D5 – Email default per category (FR-28).** The registry's `defaultEmail` is per type. Options: (a) two types, `event.created` (defaultEmail false) and `event.holiday_created` (defaultEmail true); or (b) one type that passes `email` only for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK, which ignores the user preference toggle semantics. Recommend (a), because it stays inside the existing preference model with no changes to notify.ts.\n- **D6 – Nav.** Add `/calendar` (all roles). `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, consistent with the existing account pages. It is reached from the account menu and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`.\n- **D7 – Robotics Club course (FR-37).** Not in the seed. Recommend seeding a minimal ELECTIVE course `ROBOTICS` (teacher Tom, current year) only if absent, so the Chess club example works. The alternative is skip-with-log.\n- **D8 – Feed URL display vs hashed storage (FR-24/25, NFR-5).** The raw token is only available at creation or reset. Recommendation: `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `{url}` only when it creates the first token, and `{url:null, createdAt}` otherwise. The page then says \"Reset link to get a new URL\". This needs to be explicit in the API contracts.\n- **D9 – Schema deviations from the PRD's model list** (flag them in system-design): `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt`, `EventAudience.roles`, `@@index([type,targetId])`. Each traces to FR-23, FR-3/FR-37 and NFR-4.\n\n## 4. Risks\n\n- **R1 (high):** `@mui/x-scheduler` is beta. Its API (views, timezone, all-day exclusivity, custom event rendering for chips/colours) is unverified until MCP is consulted. Budget for fallbacks (FR-9).\n- **R2:** The import cycle between timetable-service and calendar-service (B4).\n- **R3:** DST correctness spans four places (FR-15 expansion, FR-4 storage, FR-26 VTIMEZONE, UI). One shared pure helper set in `src/lib/dates.ts` keeps them consistent.\n- **R4:** Audience resolution is the performance hot path (NFR-4) and the security boundary (NFR-5/7). It needs a single implementation, tested per role.\n","numLines":107,"startLine":1,"totalLines":107}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JgoRivRSSG5YnpFj7QiiG6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
