{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgsrtA9KuHE3NJkzotQFt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for SH-14. All 37 FRs and 12 NFRs appear in its traceability table, and every requirement id it cites exists in `requirements.json`. I didn't touch any other sub-task's files.\n\nThe two research inputs disagreed in a few places. I checked each against the PRDs and the code and settled them like this:\n\n- **Audience model:** I followed the tech-stack research, because PRD-14's own `EventAudience` model and PRD-12's spec both use that shape. SH-14 adds PRD-12's six-value `AudienceType` enum, its `refId` plus include-flag fields, and the resolver at PRD-12's path, `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`. \"Grade 7 parents\" is a grade-level audience with only parents included, so the `roles[]` column the requirements notes suggested isn't needed.\n- **`getScheduleForDate`:** its return type stays the same, so the attendance code that calls it doesn't change. Its built-in weekday check is deleted and replaced by a call to `isSchoolDay`, which now owns the only copy of that rule. Screens that need the holiday name call `isSchoolDay` directly.\n- **Circular import between timetable and calendar code:** `getCalendarItems` (plus the public-events and upcoming-events helpers) moves to a new `src/server/calendar/sources.ts`. That way imports only run one way and `calendar-service` never imports the timetable service.\n- **Holiday emails on by default:** I added a second notification type, `event.holiday_created`, with email on by default. Users can still turn it off in their preferences, and the shared notification code doesn't change.\n\nThe design departs from the PRD in nine places, labelled D-1 to D-9 in the Overview. The ones a reviewer is most likely to question:\n\n- **D-1:** a `rsvpReminderSentAt` column, so each event's RSVP reminder is sent only once.\n- **D-5:** the agenda view pages 30 days at a time instead of scrolling infinitely, because the free version of the scheduler doesn't support infinite scroll. If QA rejects that, the fallback is already specified.\n- **D-6:** the feed URL is shown only once, when it's created. The token is stored hashed, so after that the user has to reset the link to see a URL again.\n- **D-8:** saving attendance on a holiday needs a `holidayOverride` flag that the server checks, not just a confirmation dialog.\n\nIntake reported no blockers. Its three warnings (PRD-12 missing, no academic-year page, new dependencies) are dealt with in the Overview.\n\n`api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in that folder are still leftovers from SH-13. `arch-api-contracts` needs to rewrite both."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":83755,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":308,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aebc8821-7772-4638-b1aa-c18e63e97e7e","uuid":"2aefd5e7-a2f7-4b8b-8a81-8e70d607cc28","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:53:53.360Z","request_id":"req_011Cgsrt9uwZGxpdnm4PKzp5"}
