eSlot, ConsentForm, ConsentAudience, ConsentResponse exactly as specified, with a migration; reuse existing AudienceType enum (GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE only for consent).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-1 Data model\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"AbsenceNote validation: toDate >= fromDate, span <= 30 days, details <= 1,000 chars, periodIds used only when partialDay; ConferenceEvent.slotMinutes 5–60; ConferenceSlot.parentNote <= 500 chars.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-1 Data model (field comments)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"PARENT users with 2+ linked children see a top-bar child switcher (avatar + first name dropdown); selection stored in cookie sh_child.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"sh_child cookie is validated against ParentStudentLink on every request; an invalid/unlinked value falls back to the first child.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent-facing pages accepting studentId (timetable, assignments, grades, calendar filter) default to the selected child, replacing per-page child selectors; ?studentId= remains an override.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.2; AC-1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents with exactly one child see that child's name in the top bar with no dropdown.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"/my-children replaces the PRD-03 'My children' list: one-child parents redirect to /my-children/[studentId]; multi-child parents see cards with attendance rate this term, missing-assignment count and average grade linking to each overview.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.1; AC-8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Child overview is the default landing page for parents after sign-in (within 2 clicks of sign-in).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3 heading; Goals 1; AC-8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Today' card shows the child's schedule for today or a holiday message (PRD-06/14 data).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Today\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Attendance' card shows term rate, absences and lates this term, last 5 marks and a 'Report an absence' button.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Attendance\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Assignments' card shows missing assignments (red) and those due in the next 7 days.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Assignments\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Recent grades' card shows last 5 returned/visible grades with course and score, plus current percent per course.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Recent grades\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Announcements' card shows the last 3 unread announcements for this child.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Announcements (PRD-12 Announcement model not present in workspace)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Upcoming events' card shows the next 5 calendar items.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Upcoming events\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Teachers' card lists the child's teachers with subject and a 'Message' button (PRD-13 messaging).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Teachers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Action items' card lists pending consent forms and open conference bookings.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Action items\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"description\": \"Each overview card has a 'View all' link to the full page/tab and loads independently via React Suspense streaming.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2, FR-3.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent absence form at /my-children/[studentId]/absence/new: from/to dates (past 14 days to 60 days ahead), whole day or specific periods (checkboxes from bell schedule), reason, details, optional PDF/JPG/PNG upload with file context 'absence-note'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"description\": \"On submit the note is PENDING and notifies the homeroom teacher and admins via notify() type absence_note.submitted (default email false).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents see a list of their absence notes with status.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"description\": \"Review queue /attendance/absence-notes for homeroom TEACHER (own section) and ADMIN (all), filterable by status and date; each note shows student, dates, reason, details, document link and existing attendance records for those dates.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n      \"description\": \"Reviewers can Approve (optional note) or Reject (note required); reviewedById, reviewNote, reviewedAt are recorded.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.3; API POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n      \"description\": \"Approval sets every matching attendance record (dates, and periods if partial) with status ABSENT or no record yet to EXCUSED with note 'Absence note #<id>', writes audit(), and attendance rate recalculates; rejected notes leave records unchanged.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.4; AC-3; AC-4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"description\": \"For future dates an approved note pre-fills students as EXCUSED with an 'Absence note' badge when a register is later taken; teachers may still change it.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.4; AC-2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"description\": \"Teachers may select EXCUSED in the register only when an approved note covers that student/date/period; ADMIN can always set EXCUSED (relaxes current ADMIN-only rule in attendance-service).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent is notified of the review decision including the reviewer's note (absence_note.reviewed, default email true).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.6; AC-4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"description\": \"PRD-07 attendance.absent notifications are suppressed for a student when a PENDING or APPROVED note covers that date/period.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.7; AC-2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n      \"description\": \"Admin creates/edits ConferenceEvent at /admin/conferences (title, date, booking window, slot length, eligible grade levels); teachers teaching eligible students are notified (conference.slots_requested).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.1; API POST/PATCH /api/conferences\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"description\": \"Teacher availability page /conferences/[id]/availability: pick time ranges and location; system regenerates unbooked slots of slotMinutes; teachers can remove unbooked slots and block individual slots.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.2; API PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent booking page /conferences/[id] shows, for each of the selected child's teachers with slots, available slots as time buttons; booking is atomic (UPDATE … WHERE bookedByParentId IS NULL) with an optional note.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"description\": \"Booking rules: max one slot per teacher per child; overlapping bookings with other teachers are rejected with message 'You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.3; AC-6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"description\": \"Reschedule = cancel + book; cancellation allowed until bookingClosesAt (booking only within booking window).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"description\": \"Booking/cancellation notifies parent and teacher (conference.booked, conference.cancelled) with an .ics attachment link.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"description\": \"Teacher day view lists booked slots in order with student, parent and note, and is printable.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-35\",\n      \"description\": \"Booked conference slots appear on both parties' calendars as PRD-14 source 'My meetings'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.7 (PRD-14 calendar UI/aggregation not present in workspace)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-36\",\n      \"description\": \"Admins (any audience) and teachers (courses they manage) create consent forms at /consent-forms/new with title, Markdown description, due date, optional linked CalendarEvent, audience; parents of audience students notified (consent.requested, default email true).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-37\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents see pending consent forms on the child overview and at /consent-forms; responding requires Granted/Declined and a typed signature matching the parent's name case-insensitively, plus optional comment.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.2; AC-7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-38\",\n      \"description\": \"One response per student (any linked parent); responses may be changed until dueAt and every change is audited.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-39\",\n      \"description\": \"Creator/admin tracking page shows per-student status (Granted, Declined, No response) with filters, CSV export (?format=csv), and 'Remind non-responders' throttled to once per 24 hours.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.3; API tracking/remind\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-40\",\n      \"description\": \"Maintenance run sends a reminder 48 hours before dueAt to parents with no response.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-41\",\n      \"description\": \"Register file context 'absence-note' readable by the submitting parent, other linked parents, homeroom teacher and admins.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-7.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-42\",\n      \"description\": \"Navigation entries: Parents — My children, Absence notes, Conferences, Consent forms; Teachers — Absence notes (homeroom only), Conferences; Admins — Conferences, Consent forms, Absence notes.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-8.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-43\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the REST API table (me/children/summary, students/:id/overview, absence-notes CRUD/review, conferences, availability, slots, book/cancel, consent-forms, responses, tracking, remind) with role checks enforced server-side via requireRole/access helpers and the standard response/error shapes.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 API table; Platform Context conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-44\",\n      \"description\": \"Register new notification types absence_note.submitted, absence_note.reviewed, conference.slots_requested, conference.booked, conference.cancelled, consent.requested (and consent reminder) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4/5/6 notify keys; Platform Context notifications rule (reminder key name not specified)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-45\",\n      \"description\": \"Seed data: one pending and one approved absence note for Grade 7; 'Autumn conferences' 3 weeks out for Grade 7 with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 (10 min), two booked; consent form 'Science Museum Trip' for Grade 7 due in 10 days linked to a calendar event with 40% responses.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Seed Data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n      \"description\": \"Tests: unit (absence coverage matching whole-day/periods/multi-day, slot generation, signature match); integration (approval updates/pre-fill, concurrent atomic booking, notification suppression); Playwright (absence note → approve → register EXCUSED; book conference slot; sign consent).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Test Requirements\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Concurrency: two simultaneous bookings of the same slot → exactly one succeeds; the other gets 'That slot was just taken' (409 CONFLICT) and refreshed slots.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-1; AC-5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Performance: child overview first section paints < 1 s; full page < 2 s.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Auditability: absence approvals, consent responses and changes write AuditLog entries including IP address.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"UI component rule: Material UI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X data-grid/date-pickers/charts/scheduler); every component looked up via mui-mcp (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Chakra, lucide-react, notistack, etc.) never imported; toasts via shared useToast(), confirmations via Dialog, pickers via Autocomplete; MCP unreachable = blocker. QA must verify.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 mandates recording as NFR)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Security/access: every handler and server page enforces access server-side; parents only for linked students, homeroom teachers only for their section, consent tracking only creator/admin.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Roles; code conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models/services/components/helpers (audit(), notify(), files contexts, attendance-service, AudienceType/audience.ts, DataTable, FileUpload, MarkdownView, ConfirmDialog, UserAvatar); new services in src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts; no renames, no re-scaffolding.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Code layout and conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"Quality gates: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test stay green; TypeScript strict; Zod validators in src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts shared by forms and handlers; no console.log (use logger).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Constraints; conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Date handling: timestamps stored UTC, displayed and date rules (absence windows, 'today', due dates, 48h reminder) evaluated in SchoolSettings.timezone; date-only fields use @db.Date.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — conventions; Assumptions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Scope: deliver in a single forge run; no payments, pickup/transport, or parent self-registration; do not modify behaviour owned by PRD-16+.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Out of Scope; Constraints\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Lists use standard pagination (?page, ?pageSize ≤100), sorting and ?q search where applicable.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Pagination conventions\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n      ],\n      \"note\": \"No interactive user available; aggregate confidence (95%) exceeds 80% threshold so no further rounds run. Items forwarded to Architect as flagged assumptions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 56,\n  \"functionalCount\": 46,\n  \"nonFunctionalCount\": 10,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [\n    \"SH-14 (PRD-14 Calendar) dev phase failed per artifacts/run-summary.json: CalendarEvent/EventAudience models exist but no calendar API or pages. FR-14, FR-35 ('My meetings'), FR-5 calendar filter and ConsentForm.eventId depend on it.\",\n    \"PRD-12 Announcement model absent (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts) — FR-13 overview Announcements card has no data source.\",\n    \"Shared components live under src/components/<Name>/ not src/components/shared/; student detail route is /students/[id].\",\n    \"Attendance-service currently restricts EXCUSED to ADMIN (attendance-service.ts:219) — FR-25 must relax this for teachers with an approved note; notification send path (attendance-service.ts ~line 299) is where FR-27 suppression hooks in.\",\n    \"ConferenceSlot has no 'blocked' field although FR-29 requires blocking individual slots — Architect to decide.\",\n    \"Previous SH-14 intake artifacts archived to artifacts/intake/.prev-SH-14/.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 98,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"PRD run mode '--brownfield --tech-stack react'; Platform Context fixes Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 + Emotion (no CSS modules/Tailwind), Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, Zod, React Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright. Confirmed in workspace (package.json, prisma/schema.prisma, src/app/(app)). Styling only via MUI theme/sx/styled(), so cssPreprocessor recorded as plain css.\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking)\n\nTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T12:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n> This file replaces the SH-14 version. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`system-design.md`, `requirements-analysis-notes.md`, `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are still from SH-14 until their own sub-tasks rewrite them.\n\n**Base stack (checked against `package.json`).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 98% confidence. The workspace matches:\n\n- Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict\n- Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25\n- MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), @mui/x-scheduler 9.0.0-beta.15 (theme augmentation only)\n- date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse, file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown + rehype-sanitize (behind `MarkdownView`)\n- Vitest 2.1.1, Testing Library, Playwright 1.47.2\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`blockers: []`, 95% confidence). It left six warnings and seven unresolved questions. ADR-11 through ADR-13 cover them.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no new dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-6 says to reuse what exists, with no re-scaffolding. NFR-7 requires lint, typecheck and tests to stay green. NFR-9 limits the work to one forge run. Every PRD-15 feature is covered by something already installed:\n\n- **Forms:** RHF + Zod\n- **Dates:** date-fns-tz\n- **CSV:** `src/server/csv.ts` / papaparse\n- **.ics:** `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`\n- **Markdown:** `MarkdownView` / `MarkdownEditor`\n- **Uploads:** `FileUpload` + `file-type`\n- **Grids:** MUI X DataGrid via `DataTable`\n- **Date inputs:** MUI X DatePicker\n\n**Decision.** No new runtime or dev dependencies. `package.json` stays unchanged.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no new supply-chain surface and no lockfile churn. If dev-planning proposes a package, it needs a new ADR.\n\n## ADR-2: UI is MUI only, and every component is looked up in mui-mcp first\n\n**Context.** NFR-4 requires MUI v9 and MUI X only. Banned libraries are never imported. Toasts go through `useToast()`, confirmations through `Dialog`/`ConfirmDialog`, pickers through `Autocomplete`. The mui-mcp server is connected in this session (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`).\n\n**Decision.** Map each new UI surface to MUI components:\n\n| Surface | Requirements | MUI components |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Child switcher | FR-3, FR-6 | `Select` or `Menu`, with `UserAvatar` |\n| Overview cards | FR-9–FR-17 | `Card`, `List`, `Chip`, `LoadingSkeleton` |\n| Absence form | FR-18 | `DatePicker`, `RadioGroup`, `Checkbox` group, `FileUpload` |\n| Review queue | FR-21, FR-22 | `DataTable`, with `Dialog` for approve/reject |\n| Slot buttons | FR-30 | `ToggleButton` or `Button` grid |\n| Day view | FR-34 | `Table` with print CSS through `sx` and `@media print` |\n| Consent tracking | FR-39 | `DataTable` |\n| Signature field | FR-37 | `TextField` |\n\nDevelopers must call `useMuiDocs` and `fetchDocs` before using each component. If the MCP is unreachable at dev time, that is a blocker, not something to work around.\n\n**Consequences.** QA's banned-import grep stays at zero hits. Printing (FR-34) uses `@media print` styles only, with no print library.\n\n## ADR-3: Data model is one additive Prisma migration, plus three flagged extra columns\n\n**Context.** FR-1 and FR-2 define the enums and models, and reuse `AudienceType` for consent. Consent audiences are limited to GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION and COURSE. Three requirements need persisted state that the PRD field list does not name:\n\n- **FR-29:** block individual slots. Deleting a slot would not work, because the next availability regeneration would recreate it.\n- **FR-39:** \"Remind non-responders\" is limited to once per 24 h. `src/server/rate-limit.ts` is in-memory per process (its own `ponytail:` note says so), so the limit would reset on every deploy or restart.\n- **FR-40:** the 48 h reminder must go out once per form.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Add one migration `…_prd15_parent_portal` with the enums and models as specified. Date-only fields use `@db.Date` (NFR-8).\n- The three extra columns:\n  - `ConferenceSlot.blocked Boolean @default(false)` (FR-29)\n  - `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-39)\n  - `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt DateTime?` (FR-40)\n\n  Both reminders claim their slot atomically with `updateMany({ where: { id, <col>: null | lt cutoff } })` and treat `count === 0` as \"already done\". This is the same pattern as `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt` (D-1).\n- Use one `ConsentResponse` per (formId, studentId) via `@@unique` (FR-38). Changes update the row in place, and each change is audited.\n- Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` enforce the FR-2 limits: span ≤ 30 days, details ≤ 1,000 chars, slotMinutes 5–60, parentNote ≤ 500 chars. Forms and handlers share these schemas (NFR-7).\n\n**Consequences.** The extra columns go beyond \"exactly as specified\". `system-design.md` must list them as a deviation. If the PRD's own model already has an equivalent field, use that field and drop the extra column.\n\n## ADR-4: Conference booking uses a conditional UPDATE plus a partial unique index\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires that exactly one of two concurrent bookings succeeds. The loser gets 409 `That slot was just taken`. FR-31 allows one slot per teacher per child and no overlapping bookings across teachers. FR-30 requires the booking to be atomic.\n\n**Decision.**\n1. Book with `prisma.conferenceSlot.updateMany({ where: { id, bookedByParentId: null, blocked: false }, data: {...} })`. If `count === 0`, throw `AppError('CONFLICT', 'That slot was just taken')`. The client then refetches the slots.\n2. Enforce \"one per teacher per child\" in the database: a raw-SQL partial unique index in the migration on `(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) WHERE bookedForStudentId IS NOT NULL`. A P2002 error maps to a 409 with the FR-31 message. This follows the attendance ADR-3 precedent of a partial unique index plus P2002 handling.\n3. Check for overlaps with the parent's other bookings at that time inside the same `$transaction` before the conditional update. It returns `You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>`.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no advisory lock and no SERIALIZABLE isolation. The FR-46 integration test fires two `Promise.all` bookings and asserts exactly one success. There is a small window in which one parent could double-book overlapping slots with two different teachers in two tabs at once. That is acceptable: it is the same parent, and no data is corrupted.\n\n## ADR-5: Child selection uses an httpOnly cookie that is validated on every request\n\n**Context.** FR-3 to FR-6 require a selection stored in cookie `sh_child`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` on every request, falling back to the first child, with `?studentId=` as an override.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Create one server helper, `getSelectedChild(user, searchParams?)`, in `src/server/parent/selected-child.ts`, wrapped in React `cache()`.\n- It resolves the child in this order: `?studentId=` if linked, then the `sh_child` cookie if linked, then the first l","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/a4eeb429-6a70-48e8-a0ff-b55a8b190b9d/tool-results/bcwa03c30.txt","persistedOutputSize":54736},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AqcJ4uph35E1P7J4eUnnF9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
