{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BfYUt3RhBHXntC5aHYeTe6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tartifacts/approvals/:\n2\tarchitect-approval.json\n3\tdev-planning-approval.json\n4\tintake-approval.json\n5\t\n6\tartifacts/architect/:\n7\tapi-contracts.json\n8\thandoff-to-dev-planning.json\n9\trequirements-analysis-notes.md\n10\tsystem-design.md\n11\ttech-stack-decisions.md\n12\tthreat-model-notes.json\n13\t\n14\tartifacts/dev-planning/:\n15\tfile-ownership-matrix.json\n16\tfile-structure.md\n17\timplementation-plan.json\n18\tmodule-dependencies.json\n19\t\n20\tartifacts/dev/:\n21\tdev-log.md\n22\tdev-rerun-count.json\n23\tsecurity-scan-report.json\n24\ttask-completion-markers.json\n25\t\n26\tartifacts/intake/:\n27\thandoff-to-architect.json\n28\trequirements.json\n29\ttech-stack.json\n30\tuser-stories.md\n31\t\n32\tartifacts/qa/:\n33\tcoverage-report.md\n34\tqa-report.md\n35\t\n36\tartifacts/telemetry/:\n37\tapi-retries.jsonl\n38\tdaemon-handoff.json\n39\tknowledge-log.jsonl\n40\tmetering.jsonl\n41\tphase-sessions.json\n42\t\n43\tartifacts/ui-verification/:\n44\tscreenshots\n45\tscreenshots-sh14\n46\tui-verification-report.json\n47\tui-verification-report.md\n48\tuiv-raw-sh14.log\n49\t{\n50\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n51\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n52\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n53\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n54\t  \"prd\": \"PRD-15 Parent Portal — Child Switcher, Absence Notes & Conference Booking (SCH-015)\",\n55\t  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n56\t    {\n57\t      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n58\t      \"description\": \"Add Prisma enums AbsenceNoteStatus, AbsenceReason, ConsentResponseValue and models AbsenceNote, ConferenceEvent, ConferenceSlot, ConsentForm, ConsentAudience, ConsentResponse exactly as specified, with a migration; reuse existing AudienceType enum (GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE only for consent).\",\n59\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n60\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-1 Data model\"\n61\t    },\n62\t    {\n63\t      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n64\t      \"description\": \"AbsenceNote validation: toDate >= fromDate, span <= 30 days, details <= 1,000 chars, periodIds used only when partialDay; ConferenceEvent.slotMinutes 5–60; ConferenceSlot.parentNote <= 500 chars.\",\n65\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n66\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-1 Data model (field comments)\"\n67\t    },\n68\t    {\n69\t      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n70\t      \"description\": \"PARENT users with 2+ linked children see a top-bar child switcher (avatar + first name dropdown); selection stored in cookie sh_child.\",\n71\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n72\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.1\"\n73\t    },\n74\t    {\n75\t      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n76\t      \"description\": \"sh_child cookie is validated against ParentStudentLink on every request; an invalid/unlinked value falls back to the first child.\",\n77\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n78\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.1\"\n79\t    },\n80\t    {\n81\t      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n82\t      \"description\": \"Parent-facing pages accepting studentId (timetable, assignments, grades, calendar filter) default to the selected child, replacing per-page child selectors; ?studentId= remains an override.\",\n83\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n84\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.2; AC-1\"\n85\t    },\n86\t    {\n87\t      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n88\t      \"description\": \"Parents with exactly one child see that child's name in the top bar with no dropdown.\",\n89\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n90\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.3\"\n91\t    },\n92\t    {\n93\t      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n94\t      \"description\": \"/my-children replaces the PRD-03 'My children' list: one-child parents redirect to /my-children/[studentId]; multi-child parents see cards with attendance rate this term, missing-assignment count and average grade linking to each overview.\",\n95\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n96\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.1; AC-8\"\n97\t    },\n98\t    {\n99\t      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n100\t      \"description\": \"Child overview is the default landing page for parents after sign-in (within 2 clicks of sign-in).\",\n101\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n102\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3 heading; Goals 1; AC-8\"\n103\t    },\n104\t    {\n105\t      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n106\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Today' card shows the child's schedule for today or a holiday message (PRD-06/14 data).\",\n107\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n108\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Today\"\n109\t    },\n110\t    {\n111\t      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n112\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Attendance' card shows term rate, absences and lates this term, last 5 marks and a 'Report an absence' button.\",\n113\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n114\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Attendance\"\n115\t    },\n116\t    {\n117\t      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n118\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Assignments' card shows missing assignments (red) and those due in the next 7 days.\",\n119\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n120\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Assignments\"\n121\t    },\n122\t    {\n123\t      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n124\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Recent grades' card shows last 5 returned/visible grades with course and score, plus current percent per course.\",\n125\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n126\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Recent grades\"\n127\t    },\n128\t    {\n129\t      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n130\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Announcements' card shows the last 3 unread announcements for this child.\",\n131\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n132\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Announcements (PRD-12 Announcement model not present in workspace)\"\n133\t    },\n134\t    {\n135\t      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n136\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Upcoming events' card shows the next 5 calendar items.\",\n137\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n138\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Upcoming events\"\n139\t    },\n140\t    {\n141\t      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n142\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Teachers' card lists the child's teachers with subject and a 'Message' button (PRD-13 messaging).\",\n143\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n144\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Teachers\"\n145\t    },\n146\t    {\n147\t      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n148\t      \"description\": \"Overview 'Action items' card lists pending consent forms and open conference bookings.\",\n149\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n150\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Action items\"\n151\t    },\n152\t    {\n153\t      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n154\t      \"description\": \"Each overview card has a 'View all' link to the full page/tab and loads independently via React Suspense streaming.\",\n155\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n156\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2, FR-3.3\"\n157\t    },\n158\t    {\n159\t      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n160\t      \"description\": \"Parent absence form at /my-children/[studentId]/absence/new: from/to dates (past 14 days to 60 days ahead), whole day or specific periods (checkboxes from bell schedule), reason, details, optional PDF/JPG/PNG upload with file context 'absence-note'.\",\n161\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n162\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.1\"\n163\t    },\n164\t    {\n165\t      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n166\t      \"description\": \"On submit the note is PENDING and notifies the homeroom teacher and admins via notify() type absence_note.submitted (default email false).\",\n167\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n168\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.2\"\n169\t    },\n170\t    {\n171\t      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n172\t      \"description\": \"Parents see a list of their absence notes with status.\",\n173\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n174\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.2\"\n175\t    },\n176\t    {\n177\t      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n178\t      \"description\": \"Review queue /attendance/absence-notes for homeroom TEACHER (own section) and ADMIN (all), filterable by status and date; each note shows student, dates, reason, details, document link and existing attendance records for those dates.\",\n179\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n180\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.3\"\n181\t    },\n182\t    {\n183\t      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n184\t      \"description\": \"Reviewers can Approve (optional note) or Reject (note required); reviewedById, reviewNote, reviewedAt are recorded.\",\n185\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n186\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.3; API POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review\"\n187\t    },\n188\t    {\n189\t      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n190\t      \"description\": \"Approval sets every matching attendance record (dates, and periods if partial) with status ABSENT or no record yet to EXCUSED with note 'Absence note #<id>', writes audit(), and attendance rate recalculates; rejected notes leave records unchanged.\",\n191\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n192\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.4; AC-3; AC-4\"\n193\t    },\n194\t    {\n195\t      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n196\t      \"description\": \"For future dates an approved note pre-fills students as EXCUSED with an 'Absence note' badge when a register is later taken; teachers may still change it.\",\n197\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n198\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.4; AC-2\"\n199\t    },\n200\t    {\n201\t      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n202\t      \"description\": \"Teachers may select EXCUSED in the register only when an approved note covers that student/date/period; ADMIN can always set EXCUSED (relaxes current ADMIN-only rule in attendance-service).\",\n203\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n204\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.5\"\n205\t    },\n206\t    {\n207\t      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n208\t      \"description\": \"Parent is notified of the review decision including the reviewer's note (absence_note.reviewed, default email true).\",\n209\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n210\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.6; AC-4\"\n211\t    },\n212\t    {\n213\t      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n214\t      \"description\": \"PRD-07 attendance.absent notifications are suppressed for a student when a PENDING or APPROVED note covers that date/period.\",\n215\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n216\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.7; AC-2\"\n217\t    },\n218\t    {\n219\t      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n220\t      \"description\": \"Admin creates/edits ConferenceEvent at /admin/conferences (title, date, booking window, slot length, eligible grade levels); teachers teaching eligible students are notified (conference.slots_requested).\",\n221\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n222\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.1; API POST/PATCH /api/conferences\"\n223\t    },\n224\t    {\n225\t      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n226\t      \"description\": \"Teacher availability page /conferences/[id]/availability: pick time ranges and location; system regenerates unbooked slots of slotMinutes; teachers can remove unbooked slots and block individual slots.\",\n227\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n228\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.2; API PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability\"\n229\t    },\n230\t    {\n231\t      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n232\t      \"description\": \"Parent booking page /conferences/[id] shows, for each of the selected child's teachers with slots, available slots as time buttons; booking is atomic (UPDATE … WHERE bookedByParentId IS NULL) with an optional note.\",\n233\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n234\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.3\"\n235\t    },\n236\t    {\n237\t      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n238\t      \"description\": \"Booking rules: max one slot per teacher per child; overlapping bookings with other teachers are rejected with message 'You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>'.\",\n239\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n240\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.3; AC-6\"\n241\t    },\n242\t    {\n243\t      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n244\t      \"description\": \"Reschedule = cancel + book; cancellation allowed until bookingClosesAt (booking only within booking window).\",\n245\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n246\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.4\"\n247\t    },\n248\t    {\n249\t      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n250\t      \"description\": \"Booking/cancellation notifies parent and teacher (conference.booked, conference.cancelled) with an .ics attachment link.\",\n251\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n252\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.5\"\n253\t    },\n254\t    {\n255\t      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n256\t      \"description\": \"Teacher day view lists booked slots in order with student, parent and note, and is printable.\",\n257\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n258\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.6\"\n259\t    },\n260\t    {\n261\t      \"id\": \"FR-35\",\n262\t      \"description\": \"Booked conference slots appear on both parties' calendars as PRD-14 source 'My meetings'.\",\n263\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n264\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.7 (PRD-14 calendar UI/aggregation not present in workspace)\"\n265\t    },\n266\t    {\n267\t      \"id\": \"FR-36\",\n268\t      \"description\": \"Admins (any audience) and teachers (courses they manage) create consent forms at /consent-forms/new with title, Markdown description, due date, optional linked CalendarEvent, audience; parents of audience students notified (consent.requested, default email true).\",\n269\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n270\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.1\"\n271\t    },\n272\t    {\n273\t      \"id\": \"FR-37\",\n274\t      \"description\": \"Parents see pending consent forms on the child overview and at /consent-forms; responding requires Granted/Declined and a typed signature matching the parent's name case-insensitively, plus optional comment.\",\n275\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n276\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.2; AC-7\"\n277\t    },\n278\t    {\n279\t      \"id\": \"FR-38\",\n280\t      \"description\": \"One response per student (any linked parent); responses may be changed until dueAt and every change is audited.\",\n281\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n282\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.2\"\n283\t    },\n284\t    {\n285\t      \"id\": \"FR-39\",\n286\t      \"description\": \"Creator/admin tracking page shows per-student status (Granted, Declined, No response) with filters, CSV export (?format=csv), and 'Remind non-responders' throttled to once per 24 hours.\",\n287\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n288\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.3; API tracking/remind\"\n289\t    },\n290\t    {\n291\t      \"id\": \"FR-40\",\n292\t      \"description\": \"Maintenance run sends a reminder 48 hours before dueAt to parents with no response.\",\n293\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n294\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.4\"\n295\t    },\n296\t    {\n297\t      \"id\": \"FR-41\",\n298\t      \"description\": \"Register file context 'absence-note' readable by the submitting parent, other linked parents, homeroom teacher and admins.\",\n299\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n300\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-7.1\"\n301\t    },\n302\t    {\n303\t      \"id\": \"FR-42\",\n304\t      \"description\": \"Navigation entries: Parents — My children, Absence notes, Conferences, Consent forms; Teachers — Absence notes (homeroom only), Conferences; Admins — Conferences, Consent forms, Absence notes.\",\n305\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n306\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-8.1\"\n307\t    },\n308\t    {\n309\t      \"id\": \"FR-43\",\n310\t      \"description\": \"Implement the REST API table (me/children/summary, students/:id/overview, absence-notes CRUD/review, conferences, availability, slots, book/cancel, consent-forms, responses, tracking, remind) with role checks enforced server-side via requireRole/access helpers and the standard response/error shapes.\",\n311\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n312\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 API table; Platform Context conventions\"\n313\t    },\n314\t    {\n315\t      \"id\": \"FR-44\",\n316\t      \"description\": \"Register new notification types absence_note.submitted, absence_note.reviewed, conference.slots_requested, conference.booked, conference.cancelled, consent.requested (and consent reminder) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n317\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n318\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4/5/6 notify keys; Platform Context notifications rule (reminder key name not specified)\"\n319\t    },\n320\t    {\n321\t      \"id\": \"FR-45\",\n322\t      \"description\": \"Seed data: one pending and one approved absence note for Grade 7; 'Autumn conferences' 3 weeks out for Grade 7 with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 (10 min), two booked; consent form 'Science Museum Trip' for Grade 7 due in 10 days linked to a calendar event with 40% responses.\",\n323\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n324\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Seed Data\"\n325\t    },\n326\t    {\n327\t      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n328\t      \"description\": \"Tests: unit (absence coverage matching whole-day/periods/multi-day, slot generation, signature match); integration (approval updates/pre-fill, concurrent atomic booking, notification suppression); Playwright (absence note → approve → register EXCUSED; book conference slot; sign consent).\",\n329\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n330\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Test Requirements\"\n331\t    }\n332\t  ],\n333\t  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n334\t    {\n335\t      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n336\t      \"description\": \"Concurrency: two simultaneous bookings of the same slot → exactly one succeeds; the other gets 'That slot was just taken' (409 CONFLICT) and refreshed slots.\",\n337\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n338\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-1; AC-5\"\n339\t    },\n340\t    {\n341\t      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n342\t      \"description\": \"Performance: child overview first section paints < 1 s; full page < 2 s.\",\n343\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n344\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-2\"\n345\t    },\n346\t    {\n347\t      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n348\t      \"description\": \"Auditability: absence approvals, consent responses and changes write AuditLog entries including IP address.\",\n349\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n350\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-3\"\n351\t    },\n352\t    {\n353\t      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n354\t      \"description\": \"UI component rule: Material UI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X data-grid/date-pickers/charts/scheduler); every component looked up via mui-mcp (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Chakra, lucide-react, notistack, etc.) never imported; toasts via shared useToast(), confirmations via Dialog, pickers via Autocomplete; MCP unreachable = blocker. QA must verify.\",\n355\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n356\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 mandates recording as NFR)\"\n357\t    },\n358\t    {\n359\t      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n360\t      \"description\": \"Security/access: every handler and server page enforces access server-side; parents only for linked students, homeroom teachers only for their section, consent tracking only creator/admin.\",\n361\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n362\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Roles; code conventions\"\n363\t    },\n364\t    {\n365\t      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n366\t      \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models/services/components/helpers (audit(), notify(), files contexts, attendance-service, AudienceType/audience.ts, DataTable, FileUpload, MarkdownView, ConfirmDialog, UserAvatar); new services in src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts; no renames, no re-scaffolding.\",\n367\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n368\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Code layout and conventions\"\n369\t    },\n370\t    {\n371\t      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n372\t      \"description\": \"Quality gates: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test stay green; TypeScript strict; Zod validators in src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts shared by forms and handlers; no console.log (use logger).\",\n373\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n374\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Constraints; conventions\"\n375\t    },\n376\t    {\n377\t      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n378\t      \"description\": \"Date handling: timestamps stored UTC, displayed and date rules (absence windows, 'today', due dates, 48h reminder) evaluated in SchoolSettings.timezone; date-only fields use @db.Date.\",\n379\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n380\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — conventions; Assumptions\"\n381\t    },\n382\t    {\n383\t      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n384\t      \"description\": \"Scope: deliver in a single forge run; no payments, pickup/transport, or parent self-registration; do not modify behaviour owned by PRD-16+.\",\n385\t      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n386\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Out of Scope; Constraints\"\n387\t    },\n388\t    {\n389\t      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n390\t      \"description\": \"Lists use standard pagination (?page, ?pageSize ≤100), sorting and ?q search where applicable.\",\n391\t      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n392\t      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Pagination conventions\"\n393\t    }\n394\t  ],\n395\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n396\t  \"clarificationLog\": [\n397\t    {\n398\t      \"round\": 1,\n399\t      \"questions\": [\n400\t        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n401\t        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n402\t        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n403\t        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n404\t        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n405\t        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n406\t        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n407\t      ],\n408\t      \"unresolved\": [\n409\t        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n410\t        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n411\t        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n412\t        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n413\t        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n414\t        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n415\t        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n416\t      ],\n417\t      \"note\": \"No interactive user available; aggregate confidence (95%) exceeds 80% threshold so no further rounds run. Items forwarded to Architect as flagged assumptions.\"\n418\t    }\n419\t  ],\n420\t  \"status\": \"complete\"\n421\t}{\n422\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n423\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n424\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n425\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n426\t  \"status\": \"complete\",\n427\t  \"requirementsCount\": 56,\n428\t  \"functionalCount\": 46,\n429\t  \"nonFunctionalCount\": 10,\n430\t  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n431\t  \"blockers\": [],\n432\t  \"warnings\": [\n433\t    \"SH-14 (PRD-14 Calendar) dev phase failed per artifacts/run-summary.json: CalendarEvent/EventAudience models exist but no calendar API or pages. FR-14, FR-35 ('My meetings'), FR-5 calendar filter and ConsentForm.eventId depend on it.\",\n434\t    \"PRD-12 Announcement model absent (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts) — FR-13 overview Announcements card has no data source.\",\n435\t    \"Shared components live under src/components/<Name>/ not src/components/shared/; student detail route is /students/[id].\",\n436\t    \"Attendance-service currently restricts EXCUSED to ADMIN (attendance-service.ts:219) — FR-25 must relax this for teachers with an approved note; notification send path (attendance-service.ts ~line 299) is where FR-27 suppression hooks in.\",\n437\t    \"ConferenceSlot has no 'blocked' field although FR-29 requires blocking individual slots — Architect to decide.\",\n438\t    \"Previous SH-14 intake artifacts archived to artifacts/intake/.prev-SH-14/.\"\n439\t  ],\n440\t  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n441\t}{\n442\t  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n443\t  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n444\t  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n445\t  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n446\t  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n447\t  \"confidencePct\": 98,\n448\t  \"detectionNotes\": \"PRD run mode '--brownfield --tech-stack react'; Platform Context fixes Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 + Emotion (no CSS modules/Tailwind), Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, Zod, React Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright. Confirmed in workspace (package.json, prisma/schema.prisma, src/app/(app)). Styling only via MUI theme/sx/styled(), so cssPreprocessor recorded as plain css.\",\n449\t  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n450\t}# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking)\n451\t\n452\tTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T12:30:00Z · Status: complete\n453\t\n454\t> This file replaces the SH-14 version. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`system-design.md`, `requirements-analysis-notes.md`, `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are still from SH-14 until their own sub-tasks rewrite them.\n455\t\n456\t**Base stack (checked against `package.json`).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 98% confidence. The workspace matches:\n457\t\n458\t- Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict\n459\t- Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25\n460\t- MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), @mui/x-scheduler 9.0.0-beta.15 (theme augmentation only)\n461\t- date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse, file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown + rehype-sanitize (behind `MarkdownView`)\n462\t- Vitest 2.1.1, Testing Library, Playwright 1.47.2\n463\t\n464\tIntake reported no blockers (`blockers: []`, 95% confidence). It left six warnings and seven unresolved questions. ADR-11 through ADR-13 cover them.\n465\t\n466\t---\n467\t\n468\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no new dependencies\n469\t\n470\t**Context.** NFR-6 says to reuse what exists, with no re-scaffolding. NFR-7 requires lint, typecheck and tests to stay green. NFR-9 limits the work to one forge run. Every PRD-15 feature is covered by something already installed:\n471\t\n472\t- **Forms:** RHF + Zod\n473\t- **Dates:** date-fns-tz\n474\t- **CSV:** `src/server/csv.ts` / papaparse\n475\t- **.ics:** `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`\n476\t- **Markdown:** `MarkdownView` / `MarkdownEditor`\n477\t- **Uploads:** `FileUpload` + `file-type`\n478\t- **Grids:** MUI X DataGrid via `DataTable`\n479\t- **Date inputs:** MUI X DatePicker\n480\t\n481\t**Decision.** No new runtime or dev dependencies. `package.json` stays unchanged.\n482\t\n483\t**Consequences.** There is no new supply-chain surface and no lockfile churn. If dev-planning proposes a package, it needs a new ADR.\n484\t\n485\t## ADR-2: UI is MUI only, and every component is looked up in mui-mcp first\n486\t\n487\t**Context.** NFR-4 requires MUI v9 and MUI X only. Banned libraries are never imported. Toasts go through `useToast()`, confirmations through `Dialog`/`ConfirmDialog`, pickers through `Autocomplete`. The mui-mcp server is connected in this session (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`).\n488\t\n489\t**Decision.** Map each new UI surface to MUI components:\n490\t\n491\t| Surface | Requirements | MUI components |\n492\t| --- | --- | --- |\n493\t| Child switcher | FR-3, FR-6 | `Select` or `Menu`, with `UserAvatar` |\n494\t| Overview cards | FR-9–FR-17 | `Card`, `List`, `Chip`, `LoadingSkeleton` |\n495\t| Absence form | FR-18 | `DatePicker`, `RadioGroup`, `Checkbox` group, `FileUpload` |\n496\t| Review queue | FR-21, FR-22 | `DataTable`, with `Dialog` for approve/reject |\n497\t| Slot buttons | FR-30 | `ToggleButton` or `Button` grid |\n498\t| Day view | FR-34 | `Table` with print CSS through `sx` and `@media print` |\n499\t| Consent tracking | FR-39 | `DataTable` |\n500\t| Signature field | FR-37 | `TextField` |\n501\t\n502\tDevelopers must call `useMuiDocs` and `fetchDocs` before using each component. If the MCP is unreachable at dev time, that is a blocker, not something to work around.\n503\t\n504\t**Consequences.** QA's banned-import grep stays at zero hits. Printing (FR-34) uses `@media print` styles only, with no print library.\n505\t\n506\t## ADR-3: Data model is one additive Prisma migration, plus three flagged extra columns\n507\t\n508\t**Context.** FR-1 and FR-2 define the enums and models, and reuse `AudienceType` for consent. Consent audiences are limited to GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION and COURSE. Three requirements need persisted state that the PRD field list does not name:\n509\t\n510\t- **FR-29:** block individual slots. Deleting a slot would not work, because the next availability regeneration would recreate it.\n511\t- **FR-39:** \"Remind non-responders\" is limited to once per 24 h. `src/server/rate-limit.ts` is in-memory per process (its own `ponytail:` note says so), so the limit would reset on every deploy or restart.\n512\t- **FR-40:** the 48 h reminder must go out once per form.\n513\t\n514\t**Decision.**\n515\t- Add one migration `…_prd15_parent_portal` with the enums and models as specified. Date-only fields use `@db.Date` (NFR-8).\n516\t- The three extra columns:\n517\t  - `ConferenceSlot.blocked Boolean @default(false)` (FR-29)\n518\t  - `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-39)\n519\t  - `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt DateTime?` (FR-40)\n520\t\n521\t  Both reminders claim their slot atomically with `updateMany({ where: { id, <col>: null | lt cutoff } })` and treat `count === 0` as \"already done\". This is the same pattern as `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt` (D-1).\n522\t- Use one `ConsentResponse` per (formId, studentId) via `@@unique` (FR-38). Changes update the row in place, and each change is audited.\n523\t- Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` enforce the FR-2 limits: span ≤ 30 days, details ≤ 1,000 chars, slotMinutes 5–60, parentNote ≤ 500 chars. Forms and handlers share these schemas (NFR-7).\n524\t\n525\t**Consequences.** The extra columns go beyond \"exactly as specified\". `system-design.md` must list them as a deviation. If the PRD's own model already has an equivalent field, use that field and drop the extra column.\n526\t\n527\t## ADR-4: Conference booking uses a conditional UPDATE plus a partial unique index\n528\t\n529\t**Context.** NFR-1 requires that exactly one of two concurrent bookings succeeds. The loser gets 409 `That slot was just taken`. FR-31 allows one slot per teacher per child and no overlapping bookings across teachers. FR-30 requires the booking to be atomic.\n530\t\n531\t**Decision.**\n532\t1. Book with `prisma.conferenceSlot.updateMany({ where: { id, bookedByParentId: null, blocked: false }, data: {...} })`. If `count === 0`, throw `AppError('CONFLICT', 'That slot was just taken')`. The client then refetches the slots.\n533\t2. Enforce \"one per teacher per child\" in the database: a raw-SQL partial unique index in the migration on `(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) WHERE bookedForStudentId IS NOT NULL`. A P2002 error maps to a 409 with the FR-31 message. This follows the attendance ADR-3 precedent of a partial unique index plus P2002 handling.\n534\t3. Check for overlaps with the parent's other bookings at that time inside the same `$transaction` before the conditional update. It returns `You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>`.\n535\t\n536\t**Consequences.** There is no advisory lock and no SERIALIZABLE isolation. The FR-46 integration test fires two `Promise.all` bookings and asserts exactly one success. There is a small window in which one parent could double-book overlapping slots with two different teachers in two tabs at once. That is acceptable: it is the same parent, and no data is corrupted.\n537\t\n538\t## ADR-5: Child selection uses an httpOnly cookie that is validated on every request\n539\t\n540\t**Context.** FR-3 to FR-6 require a selection stored in cookie `sh_child`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` on every request, falling back to the first child, with `?studentId=` as an override.\n541\t\n542\t**Decision.**\n543\t- Create one server helper, `getSelectedChild(user, searchParams?)`, in `src/server/parent/selected-child.ts`, wrapped in React `cache()`.\n544\t- It resolves the child in this order: `?studentId=` if linked, then the `sh_child` cookie if linked, then the first linked child ordered by firstName.\n545\t- It reads the cookie with `cookies()` from `next/headers`.\n546\t- Writes go through one small route handler that sets the cookie with `httpOnly`, `sameSite=lax`, `path=/` and a 1-year maxAge, then calls `router.refresh()`. That handler is the existing `withHandler` pattern and gets the existing NFR-8 same-origin check in middleware.\n547\t\n548\t**Consequences.** The cookie value is untrusted input. Every consumer gets it through the helper and never reads the cookie directly (NFR-5). The switcher lives in `shell.tsx`'s top bar.\n549\t\n550\t## ADR-6: The child overview is built from streaming server components\n551\t\n552\t**Context.** NFR-2 requires first paint under 1 s and the full page under 2 s. FR-17 requires each card to load independently through Suspense. FR-8 makes this the parent landing page.\n553\t\n554\t**Decision.**\n555\t- `/my-children/[studentId]` is a server component. It calls `assertCanViewStudent` once, then renders eight async card components (FR-9–FR-16). Each card is wrapped in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` and runs its own service query.\n556\t- No client data-fetching library is used. `GET /api/students/:id/overview` (FR-43) reuses the same service functions for API consumers.\n557\t- Post-sign-in redirect for PARENT → `/my-children` (FR-8).\n558\t\n559\t**Consequences.** Slow cards such as grades do not block fast ones. Each card query must stay index-backed. `AttendanceRecord(studentId, createdAt)` and `CalendarEvent(startAt, endAt)` indexes already exist.\n560\t\n561\t## ADR-7: Absence coverage is one pure module that attendance-service uses in three places\n562\t\n563\t**Context.**\n564\t- FR-23: approval converts ABSENT or missing records to EXCUSED.\n565\t- FR-24: future registers are pre-filled.\n566\t- FR-25: teachers may mark EXCUSED only when a note covers the student. Today `attendance-service.ts:219` restricts EXCUSED to ADMIN.\n567\t- FR-27: absence notifications are suppressed.\n568\t- FR-46 asks for unit tests of whole-day, partial-period and multi-day matching.\n569\t\n570\t**Decision.**\n571\t- Add a pure function `coversRecord(note, { date, periodId })` in `src/server/absence-notes/absence-coverage.ts`, with no Prisma import so it can be unit-tested.\n572\t- `absence-notes-service.ts` loads the relevant notes, and attendance-service uses the function at three points:\n573\t  1. `getRegister`: pre-fill EXCUSED and show a badge.\n574\t  2. `saveRegister` line 219: replace the ADMIN-only check with \"ADMIN, or an APPROVED note covers the record\".\n575\t  3. Before `notifyStudentAndParents` (~line 299): drop `attendance.absent` for students covered by a PENDING or APPROVED note.\n576\t- Approval runs in one `$transaction`. It updates matching ABSENT records with an `updateMany`, and creates missing records for sessions that already exist. Dates with no session yet are handled by the FR-24 pre-fill.\n577\t- After commit, call `audit({ request })` so the IP is stored (NFR-3).\n578\t\n579\t**Consequences.** The rate recalculation needs no code, because `attendanceRate()` reads the records. Daily-homeroom sessions have no `periodId`, so whole-day and partial matching must treat a null `periodId` as matching any note that covers that date.\n580\t\n581\t## ADR-8: Dates and time zones reuse the existing helpers\n582\t\n583\t**Context.** NFR-8 requires UTC storage and school-timezone rules. Several features depend on this:\n584\t\n585\t- FR-18: absence dates from 14 days back to 60 days ahead\n586\t- FR-9: what counts as \"today\"\n587\t- FR-32: the booking window\n588\t- FR-40: the reminder 48 h before the due date\n589\t\n590\t**Decision.** Use `schoolToday`, `addDays` and `daysBetween` from `attendance-rules.ts` and `date-fns-tz`, with the time zone from `SchoolSettings.timezone`. Generate slots (FR-29) with a pure `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` function in `conference-slots.ts`, which FR-46 also unit-tests.\n591\t\n592\t**Consequences.** No new date helpers. Pure functions keep the unit tests free of timezone flakiness.\n593\t\n594\t## ADR-9: Files, notifications and .ics extend the existing registries\n595\t\n596\t**Context.** FR-18 and FR-41 add the `absence-note` file context. FR-19, FR-26, FR-28, FR-33, FR-36 and FR-44 add notification types. FR-33 needs an .ics attachment link.\n597\t\n598\t**Decision.**\n599\t- **Files:** add an `absenceNoteResolver` to `src/server/files/contexts.ts`. It allows any linked parent (including the submitter), the homeroom teacher of the student's section, and ADMIN. Uploads reuse `FileUpload` and `files-service` validation, limited to PDF, JPG and PNG checked by `file-type` magic bytes.\n600\t- **Notifications:** add these keys to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `types.ts`, then send through the existing `notify()` / `notifyStudentAndParents()`:\n601\t\n602\t  | Key | Default email |\n603\t  | --- | --- |\n604\t  | `absence_note.submitted` | false |\n605\t  | `absence_note.reviewed` | true |\n606\t  | `conference.slots_requested` | – |\n607\t  | `conference.booked` | – |\n608\t  | `conference.cancelled` | – |\n609\t  | `consent.requested` | true |\n610\t  | `consent.reminder` | true |\n611\t\n612\t- **.ics:** build it with the existing `buildCalendar` / `vevent` from `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`. Serve it from an authenticated GET per booked slot. The notification links to that URL.\n613\t\n614\t**Consequences.** There is no attachment pipeline. Email links to the .ics URL, which matches FR-33's \"attachment link\" wording.\n615\t\n616\t## ADR-10: Scheduled work goes in the existing cron route\n617\t\n618\t**Context.** FR-40 needs a maintenance run. The only scheduler is `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`, which is protected by `CRON_SECRET` and already runs assignment reminders and quiz maintenance in isolated try-blocks.\n619\t\n620\t**Decision.** Add a `sendConsentDueReminders(now)` call to that route as another isolated try-block. It is idempotent through the `dueReminderSentAt` claim (ADR-3).\n621\t\n622\t**Consequences.** No new cron, worker or script. Reminder precision is limited by the cron interval.\n623\t\n624\t## ADR-11: Unavailable upstream data degrades gracefully\n625\t\n626\t**Context.**\n627\t- FR-13: the PRD-12 `Announcement` model is missing. Only `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` exists.\n628\t- FR-5, FR-14, FR-35: SH-14's dev phase failed. The `CalendarEvent` and `EventAudience` models exist, but there are no calendar pages or API.\n629\t- Building either one would violate NFR-9, which says not to take on another PRD's scope.\n630\t\n631\t**Decision.**\n632\t- **FR-13:** render an `EmptyState` (\"No announcements\") behind a single service function that returns `[]`. Do not add an Announcement model.\n633\t- **FR-14:** query `CalendarEvent` directly with the existing `audienceWhereForUser(user, { studentIds: [child] })` and return the next 5. Expand recurrence with `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts`.\n634\t- **FR-35:** render booked slots inside the overview's Upcoming events and Action items cards as \"My meetings\" items. There is no calendar page to add them to.\n635\t- **FR-5:** the calendar `studentId` filter is not implemented, because there is no calendar page.\n636\t- **ConsentForm.eventId:** an optional FK to `CalendarEvent`, which exists.\n637\t\n638\t**Consequences.** FR-13 and FR-35 are delivered partially. They become complete without schema work once PRD-12 and PRD-14 land. `system-design.md` should record this.\n639\t\n640\t## ADR-12: Answers to intake's open questions\n641\t\n642\t**Context.** Intake forwarded seven unresolved questions. No user is available to answer them.\n643\t\n644\t**Decision.**\n645\t\n646\t| # | Question | Decision |\n647\t| --- | --- | --- |\n648\t| 1 | Announcements | See ADR-11 |\n649\t| 2 | Calendar | See ADR-11 |\n650\t| 3 | Shared component location | Reuse components where they are, under `src/components/<Name>/`. Do not move them (NFR-6). |\n651\t| 4 | Student detail route | `/students/[id]` is the target for \"View all\" links, including `/students/[id]/attendance`. |\n652\t| 5 | Pages that adopt the `sh_child` default (FR-5) | The existing `/assignments`, `/grades` and `/api/me/timetable` consumers, plus the new `/my-children/*`, `/conferences/[id]` and `/consent-forms` pages. |\n653\t| 6 | Reminder notification key | `consent.reminder` for both the 48 h reminder and the manual reminder (FR-44). |\n654\t| 7 | Blocked slots (FR-29) | `ConferenceSlot.blocked` column (ADR-3). |\n655\t\n656\t**Consequences.** All seven are recorded as assumptions. None blocks the work.\n657\t\n658\t## ADR-13: Access control and tests follow the existing patterns\n659\t\n660\t**Context.** NFR-5 requires server-side access control on every handler. NFR-7 sets the quality gates. FR-46 lists the required tests.\n661\t\n662\t**Decision.**\n663\t- **Access control:**\n664\t  - Every handler uses `withHandler` and `requireRole`.\n665\t  - Parent and child scoping uses `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds`.\n666\t  - Homeroom scoping checks section membership against `Section` (teacher's own section).\n667\t  - Consent tracking is limited to the form's creator and ADMIN.\n668\t  - Teachers may target only courses they manage (`canTargetAudience`).\n669\t- **Tests:**\n670\t  - Unit tests in Vitest cover the pure modules: `absence-coverage`, `conference-slots`, and signature matching (`trim().toLowerCase()` equality).\n671\t  - Integration tests in Vitest against the database cover approval/pre-fill, concurrent booking and notification suppression.\n672\t  - Three Playwright specs cover the FR-46 flows.\n673\t- Use `logger`, never `console.log`.\n674\t\n675\t**Consequences.** No new test tooling. Seed data (FR-45) extends `prisma/seed.ts` in place.\n676\t# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-15\n677\t\n678\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n679\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-10T12:00:00Z), PRD-15 Parent Portal: Child Switcher, Absence Notes & Conference Booking. It has 46 FRs and 10 NFRs (56 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n680\t`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 6 warnings, and 7 clarifications are unresolved. §3 proposes a default for each one so that `arch-design-system` can decide.\n681\t\n682\t## 1. Codebase facts verified (2026-11-10)\n683\t\n684\t| Fact | Where | Impact |\n685\t|---|---|---|\n686\t| No `AbsenceNote`/`Conference*`/`Consent*` models; `AudienceType` exists (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE) | `prisma/schema.prisma:1236` | FR-1: one additive migration. Consent can only use 3 of the 6 values, so this must be enforced in Zod, not by a new enum |\n687\t| `Section.homeroomTeacherId` exists; `assertHomeroom`-style check is private to attendance-service | `schema.prisma:397`, `attendance-service.ts:56-60` | FR-21/22/41 \"homeroom teacher\" = `Section.homeroomTeacherId` for the student's current-year `SectionMember` section. Export or duplicate a small helper |\n688\t| EXCUSED is ADMIN-only on save; `canExcuse: user.role === 'ADMIN'` on load | `attendance-service.ts:219`, `:208` | FR-25: replace with a per-record check against approved notes; `getRegister` must return per-student `excusable` + `noteId` for FR-24 badge/pre-fill |\n689\t| Absent/late notifications are sent after commit via `notificationsFor(diff)` → `notifyStudentAndParents` | `attendance-service.ts:~297-310` | FR-27: filter `notes.absent` against PENDING/APPROVED note coverage at this single point |\n690\t| `AttendanceRecord` requires a `sessionId`; there is no sessionless record | `schema.prisma:569-585` | FR-23 \"no record yet\": approval cannot create records without a session. Updates existing ABSENT records; for dates with no session, coverage is applied at register load (FR-24). The same coverage function serves both |\n691\t| `audit()` stores IP only when `request` is passed | `src/server/audit.ts:12,38` | NFR-3: absence review, consent response handlers must pass `request` |\n692\t| Maintenance = passes run on every `/api/internal/email/dispatch` call | `src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts`, `assignments/reminders.ts` | FR-40: add a consent-reminder pass there; idempotency needs a \"reminded48hAt\" marker (field or AuditLog/Notification lookup) |\n693\t| Files: contexts registered in `src/server/files/contexts.ts`, `registerFileAccess` | `src/server/files/access.ts` | FR-41: add `absence-note` context in contexts.ts |\n694\t| Notification types: static map `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-44: add keys only, no runtime API |\n695\t| `GET /api/me/children` exists (PARENT, via `listLinksForParent`) | `src/app/api/me/children/route.ts` | FR-3/4/7: reuse `listLinksForParent` as the sole source for the switcher and cookie validation |\n696\t| Calendar: `CalendarEvent`/`EventAudience` models + `src/server/calendar/{ical,recurrence}.ts`, but no calendar service/API/pages | `schema.prisma:1270`, `src/server/calendar` | FR-14/35/36 and the calendar part of FR-5 have only partial upstream support (see §3 Q2). `ical.ts` is reusable for FR-33 .ics |\n697\t| No Announcement model (only `announcements/audience.ts`) | `src/server/announcements` | FR-13 has no data source (see §3 Q1). `audience.ts` is reusable for FR-36 consent audience resolution |\n698\t| No `/my-children`, `/conferences`, `/consent-forms` routes; parent landing is `/dashboard`; student detail is `/students/[id]` | `src/app/(app)` | FR-7/8: new route group; change the post-sign-in redirect for PARENT |\n699\t| Validators per feature in `src/lib/validators/*.ts` | — | NFR-7: add `absence-notes.ts`, `conferences.ts`, `consent-forms.ts` |\n700\t\n701\t## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n702\t\n703\tConcern keys: **DM** data model · **API** endpoint · **UI** page/surface · **SVC** service logic · **JOB** background/maintenance · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **INT** integration with existing module · **X** cross-cutting\n704\t\n705\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n706\t|---|---|---|\n707\t| FR-1 | DM | 3 enums + 6 models in one migration. `ConsentAudience` reuses `AudienceType`. Index `AbsenceNote(studentId, status, fromDate)`; `ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, startsAt)` unique; `ConsentResponse(formId, studentId)` unique (FR-38) |\n708\t| FR-2 | SVC (Zod) | `src/lib/validators/absence-notes.ts`, `conferences.ts`. Span ≤ 30 days and `periodIds` only when `partialDay` use `.superRefine`. The same schema is used by the form and the handler |\n709\t| FR-3 | UI + X | Top-bar switcher in `shell.tsx` (PARENT only). Writes the `sh_child` cookie via server action or route; MUI `Select`/`Menu` + `UserAvatar` |\n710\t| FR-4 | AUTH + SVC | One `getSelectedChild(parent)` helper (cookie → `ParentStudentLink` check → fallback first child). Called on every parent request. Never trust the cookie alone |\n711\t| FR-5 | INT | Parent pages resolve `studentId = searchParams.studentId ?? getSelectedChild()`, and `?studentId` is still access-checked. Target pages: `/grades`, `/assignments`, timetable (`/api/me/timetable` consumer), calendar (if present) (§3 Q5) |\n712\t| FR-6 | UI | Same component; renders a name only when there is 1 child |\n713\t| FR-7 | UI + API | `/my-children` server page. 1 child → `redirect`. `GET /api/me/children/summary` returns per-child attendance rate (attendance-service term rate), missing count, average grade |\n714\t| FR-8 | INT | Post-sign-in redirect for PARENT → `/my-children` (which redirects to the overview for 1 child) |\n715\t| FR-9 | INT | Reuse timetable service + SchoolDay/holiday data for \"today\" in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (NFR-8) |\n716\t| FR-10 | INT | Reuse `getStudentAttendance` + term counts; button links to FR-18 form |\n717\t| FR-11 | INT | Reuse assignments service (missing = past due, no submission, not exempt) |\n718\t| FR-12 | INT | Reuse gradebook service; only visible/returned grades (respect existing visibility rules) |\n719\t| FR-13 | INT (gap) | No source. Default: empty-state card with no new model (§3 Q1) |\n720\t| FR-14 | INT (gap) | `CalendarEvent` + `EventAudience` query exists at model level. Default: a small read-only query in the overview service (§3 Q2) |\n721\t| FR-15 | INT | Teachers from the student's active `Enrollment`→`Course.teacher` + subject. \"Message\" links to PRD-13 compose with the recipient prefilled |\n722\t| FR-16 | SVC | Pending consent responses for the child + open conference events with no booking for the child |\n723\t| FR-17 | UI + X | Each card is a separate async server component in `<Suspense>` with a `LoadingSkeleton` fallback. Also drives NFR-2 |\n724\t| FR-18 | UI + API | `/my-children/[studentId]/absence/new`. Date window −14/+60 days in school TZ. Period checkboxes come from `Period` (bell schedule). `FileUpload` with context `absence-note` |\n725\t| FR-19 | NOTIF | `absence_note.submitted` → homeroom teacher(s) of the student's section + all ADMINs |\n726\t| FR-20 | UI + API | `GET /api/absence-notes` scoped by role (parent = linked students). Uses DataTable with standard pagination (NFR-10) |\n727\t| FR-21 | UI + API + AUTH | `/attendance/absence-notes` queue. TEACHER limited to homeroom sections, ADMIN sees all. The detail view joins existing `AttendanceRecord`s for the date range |\n728\t| FR-22 | API + SVC | `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review` `{decision, note}`; note required on reject (Zod). Only PENDING notes are reviewable (else 409) |\n729\t| FR-23 | SVC + INT | Inside one transaction, update ABSENT records in sessions matching the dates (+ periodIds if partial) to EXCUSED with note `Absence note #<id>`; `audit()` with request. Rate recalculation is automatic because rates are computed on read. **Core shared function:** `noteCovers(note, date, periodId?)` |\n730\t| FR-24 | INT | `getRegister` computes approved-note coverage for each student/date/period and pre-fills EXCUSED + badge when the record does not exist yet |\n731\t| FR-25 | AUTH + INT | Replace the ADMIN-only guard in `saveRegister` with: ADMIN, or an approved note covers (student, date, period). Use the same coverage function |\n732\t| FR-26 | NOTIF | `absence_note.reviewed` → submitting parent (+ other linked parents?), body includes reviewNote |\n733\t| FR-27 | INT | Filter `notes.absent` in `saveRegister` with a PENDING/APPROVED coverage lookup (batched, one query per save) |\n734\t| FR-28 | UI + API + NOTIF | `/admin/conferences`, `POST/PATCH /api/conferences`. Eligible teachers = teachers of courses with enrolled students in the eligible grade levels. Grade levels are stored on the event (array or join; FR-1 spec decides) |\n735\t| FR-29 | UI + API + SVC | `PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability` replaces the teacher's unbooked slots in a transaction and never touches booked slots. Pure function `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` (unit test FR-46). Blocking: §3 Q7 |\n736\t| FR-30 | UI + API + SVC | `/conferences/[id]` for the selected child's teachers. Booking = `updateMany where {id, bookedByParentId: null}`; count 0 → 409 |\n737\t| FR-31 | SVC | Pre-checks in the same transaction: no existing slot for (teacher, child); no overlapping slot booked by this parent. Use the exact error message text |\n738\t| FR-32 | SVC | Booking/cancel allowed only while `now` is within `[bookingOpensAt, bookingClosesAt]`. Reschedule is client-side cancel + book (no new endpoint) |\n739\t| FR-33 | NOTIF + API | `conference.booked`/`cancelled` → parent + teacher. `.ics` via `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` reusing `src/server/calendar/ical.ts` |\n740\t| FR-34 | UI | Teacher day view with `@media print` CSS. Reads the teacher's booked slots for the event |\n741\t| FR-35 | INT (gap) | No calendar aggregation exists (SH-14 failed). Default: expose `listMyMeetings(user, range)` from the conference service for a future calendar source, and show booked slots on the overview/conference pages (§3 Q2) |\n742\t| FR-36 | UI + API + AUTH + NOTIF | `/consent-forms/new`. TEACHER only for COURSE audiences of courses they teach. Audience is resolved to students via `announcements/audience.ts` and then to linked parents. `eventId` is an optional FK to `CalendarEvent` |\n743\t| FR-37 | UI + API + SVC | `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/responses`. Signature check: `trim().toLowerCase()` equals the parent's full name (pure function, unit test). Only before `dueAt` |\n744\t| FR-38 | DM + SVC | Unique (formId, studentId) upsert; `respondedById` = latest parent. Every create/change → `audit()` with old/new + request |\n745\t| FR-39 | UI + API | `GET /api/consent-forms/:id/tracking` (creator/admin), `?format=csv` via `src/server/csv.ts`. `POST …/remind` throttled by a `lastRemindedAt` field on ConsentForm (24 h) → 429 |\n746\t| FR-40 | JOB | Pass in dispatch maintenance: forms with `dueAt` in (now, now+48h] not yet reminded → notify non-responders and set a marker (e.g. `autoReminderSentAt`) for idempotency |\n747\t| FR-41 | AUTH | `absence-note` context in `files/contexts.ts`: submitting parent, other linked parents, the student's homeroom teacher, ADMIN |\n748\t| FR-42 | UI | Nav config in `shell.tsx`. Teacher \"Absence notes\" only if they are a homeroom teacher (current year) |\n749\t| FR-43 | API + AUTH | ~20 route handlers using `withHandler` / `requireRole` / `ok` from `src/server/http.ts`. Thin handlers call `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts` |\n750\t| FR-44 | NOTIF | Add 6 keys + `consent.reminder` (one key covers both the manual and the 48 h reminder) to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with the PRD's `defaultEmail` values |\n751\t| FR-45 | X (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. The consent form needs a seeded CalendarEvent. Tom/Tina must be teachers of Grade 7 courses |\n752\t| FR-46 | X (tests) | Unit: `noteCovers`, `generateSlots`, `signatureMatches`. Integration: approval, pre-fill, concurrent booking (`Promise.all` of 2 bookings), suppression. 3 Playwright specs |\n753\t| NFR-1 | SVC + DM | Conditional `updateMany` is the guarantee (no app lock). 409 `CONFLICT` \"That slot was just taken\"; the client refetches slots |\n754\t| NFR-2 | X | Suspense per card (FR-17). Each card runs ≤ 2 queries with `select`. Shell + header render first |\n755\t| NFR-3 | X | `audit({…, request})` on review, consent respond/change, conference admin edits |\n756\t| NFR-4 | UI | MUI v9 + X only; mui-mcp lookups are required per component (the tools are available this session). Notable components: Select/Menu (switcher), Card, DataGrid, DatePicker, Checkbox group, ToggleButton (slots), Dialog |\n757\t| NFR-5 | AUTH | Central access helpers: `assertParentOf(user, studentId)`, `assertHomeroomOf(user, studentId)`, `assertConsentOwner(user, form)`. Server pages call them too, not only APIs |\n758\t| NFR-6 | X | New services: `src/server/absence-notes/`, `conferences/`, `consent-forms/`, `parent-portal/` (overview, child selection). No moves or renames |\n759\t| NFR-7 | X | Validators in `src/lib/validators/`; use logger, not console |\n760\t| NFR-8 | X | `@db.Date` for `fromDate`/`toDate`/conference `date`; all windows (−14/+60, today, dueAt−48h) use the existing `schoolToday(now, tz)` |\n761\t| NFR-9 | X | Do not build calendar/announcement subsystems (PRD-12/14 scope); use degrade-gracefully defaults |\n762\t| NFR-10 | API | List endpoints (`absence-notes`, `consent-forms`, `tracking`, admin `conferences`) use the standard `?page&pageSize≤100&sort&q` |\n763\t\n764\t## 3. Open questions: proposed defaults for `arch-design-system`\n765\t\n766\t| # | Question (from intake) | Proposed default | Reqs |\n767\t|---|---|---|---|\n768\t| Q1 | Announcements card has no model | Render the card with an `EmptyState` (\"No announcements\"). Do not add an Announcement model, because it belongs to PRD-12 (NFR-9). Record this as a known gap | FR-13 |\n769\t| Q2 | Calendar API/pages missing (SH-14 failed) | Upcoming events: query `CalendarEvent`+`EventAudience` directly in the overview service (read-only, small). My meetings: expose `listMyMeetings` and list booked meetings on the overview/conference pages; full calendar integration is deferred to PRD-14. `ConsentForm.eventId`: optional FK, picked via Autocomplete over existing events | FR-5, FR-14, FR-35, FR-36 |\n770\t| Q3 | Shared components at `src/components/<Name>/` | Reuse in place; do not move them (NFR-6) | NFR-6 |\n771\t| Q4 | Student route is `/students/[id]` | \"View all\" links target `/students/[id]?tab=…` where tabs exist, otherwise the feature pages (`/grades?studentId=`, `/assignments?studentId=`) | FR-17 |\n772\t| Q5 | Which pages adopt `sh_child` | `/grades`, `/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` consumers, and new SH-15 pages. Calendar only once it exists | FR-5 |\n773\t| Q6 | Reminder notification key | Single key `consent.reminder` (defaultEmail true) for both the manual and the 48 h reminder | FR-39, FR-40, FR-44 |\n774\t| Q7 | Blocking slots: schema has no field | Add `blocked Boolean @default(false)` to `ConferenceSlot`. Deleting a slot would lose it on availability regeneration. Note that this is the only deviation from the PRD's \"exactly as specified\" model (FR-1) | FR-1, FR-29 |\n775\t\n776\tAdditional decisions the design must make:\n777\t- **Homeroom resolution** (FR-19/21/41/42): student → current-year `SectionMember` → `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. Put this in one shared helper.\n778\t- **Throttle/idempotency markers** (FR-39/40): this needs fields not in the PRD model (`lastRemindedAt`, `autoReminderSentAt`). Alternative: query `Notification` rows of type `consent.reminder`. Fields are simpler, so the recommendation is to add them.\n779\t- **FR-23 vs FR-24 split**: approval changes only existing ABSENT records. Future or untaken registers rely on load-time coverage. One `noteCovers` function underpins FR-23/24/25/27, and it is the main unit-test target.\n780\t- **FR-26 recipients**: the submitting parent is required. Notifying other linked parents is optional (recommended, since FR-41 already grants them read access).\n781\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eeb429-6a70-48e8-a0ff-b55a8b190b9d","uuid":"ef790936-e36e-48d4-8b9d-db1c90ac0407","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:16:50.197Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/a4eeb429-6a70-48e8-a0ff-b55a8b190b9d/tool-results/bcwa03c30.txt","content":"artifacts/approvals/:\narchitect-approval.json\ndev-planning-approval.json\nintake-approval.json\n\nartifacts/architect/:\napi-contracts.json\nhandoff-to-dev-planning.json\nrequirements-analysis-notes.md\nsystem-design.md\ntech-stack-decisions.md\nthreat-model-notes.json\n\nartifacts/dev-planning/:\nfile-ownership-matrix.json\nfile-structure.md\nimplementation-plan.json\nmodule-dependencies.json\n\nartifacts/dev/:\ndev-log.md\ndev-rerun-count.json\nsecurity-scan-report.json\ntask-completion-markers.json\n\nartifacts/intake/:\nhandoff-to-architect.json\nrequirements.json\ntech-stack.json\nuser-stories.md\n\nartifacts/qa/:\ncoverage-report.md\nqa-report.md\n\nartifacts/telemetry/:\napi-retries.jsonl\ndaemon-handoff.json\nknowledge-log.jsonl\nmetering.jsonl\nphase-sessions.json\n\nartifacts/ui-verification/:\nscreenshots\nscreenshots-sh14\nui-verification-report.json\nui-verification-report.md\nuiv-raw-sh14.log\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-15 Parent Portal — Child Switcher, Absence Notes & Conference Booking (SCH-015)\",\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Add Prisma enums AbsenceNoteStatus, AbsenceReason, ConsentResponseValue and models AbsenceNote, ConferenceEvent, ConferenceSlot, ConsentForm, ConsentAudience, ConsentResponse exactly as specified, with a migration; reuse existing AudienceType enum (GRADE_LEVEL/SECTION/COURSE only for consent).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-1 Data model\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"AbsenceNote validation: toDate >= fromDate, span <= 30 days, details <= 1,000 chars, periodIds used only when partialDay; ConferenceEvent.slotMinutes 5–60; ConferenceSlot.parentNote <= 500 chars.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-1 Data model (field comments)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"PARENT users with 2+ linked children see a top-bar child switcher (avatar + first name dropdown); selection stored in cookie sh_child.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"sh_child cookie is validated against ParentStudentLink on every request; an invalid/unlinked value falls back to the first child.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent-facing pages accepting studentId (timetable, assignments, grades, calendar filter) default to the selected child, replacing per-page child selectors; ?studentId= remains an override.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.2; AC-1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents with exactly one child see that child's name in the top bar with no dropdown.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-2.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"/my-children replaces the PRD-03 'My children' list: one-child parents redirect to /my-children/[studentId]; multi-child parents see cards with attendance rate this term, missing-assignment count and average grade linking to each overview.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.1; AC-8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Child overview is the default landing page for parents after sign-in (within 2 clicks of sign-in).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3 heading; Goals 1; AC-8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Today' card shows the child's schedule for today or a holiday message (PRD-06/14 data).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Today\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Attendance' card shows term rate, absences and lates this term, last 5 marks and a 'Report an absence' button.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Attendance\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Assignments' card shows missing assignments (red) and those due in the next 7 days.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Assignments\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Recent grades' card shows last 5 returned/visible grades with course and score, plus current percent per course.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Recent grades\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Announcements' card shows the last 3 unread announcements for this child.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Announcements (PRD-12 Announcement model not present in workspace)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Upcoming events' card shows the next 5 calendar items.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Upcoming events\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Teachers' card lists the child's teachers with subject and a 'Message' button (PRD-13 messaging).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Teachers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"description\": \"Overview 'Action items' card lists pending consent forms and open conference bookings.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2 Action items\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"description\": \"Each overview card has a 'View all' link to the full page/tab and loads independently via React Suspense streaming.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-3.2, FR-3.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent absence form at /my-children/[studentId]/absence/new: from/to dates (past 14 days to 60 days ahead), whole day or specific periods (checkboxes from bell schedule), reason, details, optional PDF/JPG/PNG upload with file context 'absence-note'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"description\": \"On submit the note is PENDING and notifies the homeroom teacher and admins via notify() type absence_note.submitted (default email false).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents see a list of their absence notes with status.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"description\": \"Review queue /attendance/absence-notes for homeroom TEACHER (own section) and ADMIN (all), filterable by status and date; each note shows student, dates, reason, details, document link and existing attendance records for those dates.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n      \"description\": \"Reviewers can Approve (optional note) or Reject (note required); reviewedById, reviewNote, reviewedAt are recorded.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.3; API POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n      \"description\": \"Approval sets every matching attendance record (dates, and periods if partial) with status ABSENT or no record yet to EXCUSED with note 'Absence note #<id>', writes audit(), and attendance rate recalculates; rejected notes leave records unchanged.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.4; AC-3; AC-4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"description\": \"For future dates an approved note pre-fills students as EXCUSED with an 'Absence note' badge when a register is later taken; teachers may still change it.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.4; AC-2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"description\": \"Teachers may select EXCUSED in the register only when an approved note covers that student/date/period; ADMIN can always set EXCUSED (relaxes current ADMIN-only rule in attendance-service).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent is notified of the review decision including the reviewer's note (absence_note.reviewed, default email true).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.6; AC-4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"description\": \"PRD-07 attendance.absent notifications are suppressed for a student when a PENDING or APPROVED note covers that date/period.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4.7; AC-2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n      \"description\": \"Admin creates/edits ConferenceEvent at /admin/conferences (title, date, booking window, slot length, eligible grade levels); teachers teaching eligible students are notified (conference.slots_requested).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.1; API POST/PATCH /api/conferences\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"description\": \"Teacher availability page /conferences/[id]/availability: pick time ranges and location; system regenerates unbooked slots of slotMinutes; teachers can remove unbooked slots and block individual slots.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.2; API PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"description\": \"Parent booking page /conferences/[id] shows, for each of the selected child's teachers with slots, available slots as time buttons; booking is atomic (UPDATE … WHERE bookedByParentId IS NULL) with an optional note.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"description\": \"Booking rules: max one slot per teacher per child; overlapping bookings with other teachers are rejected with message 'You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.3; AC-6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"description\": \"Reschedule = cancel + book; cancellation allowed until bookingClosesAt (booking only within booking window).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"description\": \"Booking/cancellation notifies parent and teacher (conference.booked, conference.cancelled) with an .ics attachment link.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"description\": \"Teacher day view lists booked slots in order with student, parent and note, and is printable.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-35\",\n      \"description\": \"Booked conference slots appear on both parties' calendars as PRD-14 source 'My meetings'.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-5.7 (PRD-14 calendar UI/aggregation not present in workspace)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-36\",\n      \"description\": \"Admins (any audience) and teachers (courses they manage) create consent forms at /consent-forms/new with title, Markdown description, due date, optional linked CalendarEvent, audience; parents of audience students notified (consent.requested, default email true).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-37\",\n      \"description\": \"Parents see pending consent forms on the child overview and at /consent-forms; responding requires Granted/Declined and a typed signature matching the parent's name case-insensitively, plus optional comment.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.2; AC-7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-38\",\n      \"description\": \"One response per student (any linked parent); responses may be changed until dueAt and every change is audited.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-39\",\n      \"description\": \"Creator/admin tracking page shows per-student status (Granted, Declined, No response) with filters, CSV export (?format=csv), and 'Remind non-responders' throttled to once per 24 hours.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.3; API tracking/remind\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-40\",\n      \"description\": \"Maintenance run sends a reminder 48 hours before dueAt to parents with no response.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-6.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-41\",\n      \"description\": \"Register file context 'absence-note' readable by the submitting parent, other linked parents, homeroom teacher and admins.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-7.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-42\",\n      \"description\": \"Navigation entries: Parents — My children, Absence notes, Conferences, Consent forms; Teachers — Absence notes (homeroom only), Conferences; Admins — Conferences, Consent forms, Absence notes.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-8.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-43\",\n      \"description\": \"Implement the REST API table (me/children/summary, students/:id/overview, absence-notes CRUD/review, conferences, availability, slots, book/cancel, consent-forms, responses, tracking, remind) with role checks enforced server-side via requireRole/access helpers and the standard response/error shapes.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 API table; Platform Context conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-44\",\n      \"description\": \"Register new notification types absence_note.submitted, absence_note.reviewed, conference.slots_requested, conference.booked, conference.cancelled, consent.requested (and consent reminder) in src/server/notifications/types.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 FR-4/5/6 notify keys; Platform Context notifications rule (reminder key name not specified)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-45\",\n      \"description\": \"Seed data: one pending and one approved absence note for Grade 7; 'Autumn conferences' 3 weeks out for Grade 7 with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 (10 min), two booked; consent form 'Science Museum Trip' for Grade 7 due in 10 days linked to a calendar event with 40% responses.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Seed Data\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-46\",\n      \"description\": \"Tests: unit (absence coverage matching whole-day/periods/multi-day, slot generation, signature match); integration (approval updates/pre-fill, concurrent atomic booking, notification suppression); Playwright (absence note → approve → register EXCUSED; book conference slot; sign consent).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Test Requirements\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Concurrency: two simultaneous bookings of the same slot → exactly one succeeds; the other gets 'That slot was just taken' (409 CONFLICT) and refreshed slots.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-1; AC-5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Performance: child overview first section paints < 1 s; full page < 2 s.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Auditability: absence approvals, consent responses and changes write AuditLog entries including IP address.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 NFR-3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"UI component rule: Material UI only (@mui/material v9, icons, MUI X data-grid/date-pickers/charts/scheduler); every component looked up via mui-mcp (useMuiDocs + fetchDocs) before use; banned libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, Chakra, lucide-react, notistack, etc.) never imported; toasts via shared useToast(), confirmations via Dialog, pickers via Autocomplete; MCP unreachable = blocker. QA must verify.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — UI component rule (item 6 mandates recording as NFR)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Security/access: every handler and server page enforces access server-side; parents only for linked students, homeroom teachers only for their section, consent tracking only creator/admin.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Roles; code conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Brownfield: reuse existing models/services/components/helpers (audit(), notify(), files contexts, attendance-service, AudienceType/audience.ts, DataTable, FileUpload, MarkdownView, ConfirmDialog, UserAvatar); new services in src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts; no renames, no re-scaffolding.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Code layout and conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"Quality gates: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test stay green; TypeScript strict; Zod validators in src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts shared by forms and handlers; no console.log (use logger).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Constraints; conventions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Date handling: timestamps stored UTC, displayed and date rules (absence windows, 'today', due dates, 48h reminder) evaluated in SchoolSettings.timezone; date-only fields use @db.Date.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — conventions; Assumptions\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Scope: deliver in a single forge run; no payments, pickup/transport, or parent self-registration; do not modify behaviour owned by PRD-16+.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Out of Scope; Constraints\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"Lists use standard pagination (?page, ?pageSize ≤100), sorting and ?q search where applicable.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD-15 Platform Context — Pagination conventions\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"clarificationLog\": [\n    {\n      \"round\": 1,\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"PRD-12 Announcement model/read-state is absent from the workspace (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts). Should the overview Announcements card render an empty state, or must SH-15 add a minimal Announcement read model? (FR-13)\",\n        \"PRD-14 dev phase failed (run-summary SH-14 dev failedCount=1): CalendarEvent models exist but no calendar pages/API. How should 'My meetings' (FR-35), 'Upcoming events' (FR-14), calendar studentId filter (FR-5) and ConsentForm.eventId linking be satisfied?\",\n        \"Shared wrappers live under src/components/<Name>/ (e.g. src/components/Toast/useToast.ts), not src/components/shared/ as the PRD states. Confirm reuse in place rather than moving.\",\n        \"Student detail route is /students/[id] (not [studentId]); confirm overview 'View all' links target existing tabs.\",\n        \"No parent timetable/grades page with a child selector found under src/app/(app) (only /grades, /assignments and /api/me/timetable). Which pages must adopt the sh_child default (FR-5)?\",\n        \"Notification key name for the 48h consent reminder and the manual 'Remind non-responders' is not specified (FR-44).\",\n        \"Does 'block individual slots' need a new ConferenceSlot field (schema has none), or is a blocked slot represented by deleting it? (FR-29)\"\n      ],\n      \"note\": \"No interactive user available; aggregate confidence (95%) exceeds 80% threshold so no further rounds run. Items forwarded to Architect as flagged assumptions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"status\": \"complete\"\n}{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"requirementsCount\": 56,\n  \"functionalCount\": 46,\n  \"nonFunctionalCount\": 10,\n  \"overallConfidencePct\": 95,\n  \"blockers\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [\n    \"SH-14 (PRD-14 Calendar) dev phase failed per artifacts/run-summary.json: CalendarEvent/EventAudience models exist but no calendar API or pages. FR-14, FR-35 ('My meetings'), FR-5 calendar filter and ConsentForm.eventId depend on it.\",\n    \"PRD-12 Announcement model absent (only src/server/announcements/audience.ts) — FR-13 overview Announcements card has no data source.\",\n    \"Shared components live under src/components/<Name>/ not src/components/shared/; student detail route is /students/[id].\",\n    \"Attendance-service currently restricts EXCUSED to ADMIN (attendance-service.ts:219) — FR-25 must relax this for teachers with an approved note; notification send path (attendance-service.ts ~line 299) is where FR-27 suppression hooks in.\",\n    \"ConferenceSlot has no 'blocked' field although FR-29 requires blocking individual slots — Architect to decide.\",\n    \"Previous SH-14 intake artifacts archived to artifacts/intake/.prev-SH-14/.\"\n  ],\n  \"nextPhase\": \"architect\"\n}{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-15\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"techStack\": \"react\",\n  \"confidencePct\": 98,\n  \"detectionNotes\": \"PRD run mode '--brownfield --tech-stack react'; Platform Context fixes Next.js 14 App Router, React 18, TypeScript strict, MUI v9 + Emotion (no CSS modules/Tailwind), Prisma/PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js v5, Zod, React Hook Form, Vitest + Playwright. Confirmed in workspace (package.json, prisma/schema.prisma, src/app/(app)). Styling only via MUI theme/sx/styled(), so cssPreprocessor recorded as plain css.\",\n  \"cssPreprocessor\": \"css\"\n}# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking)\n\nTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T12:30:00Z · Status: complete\n\n> This file replaces the SH-14 version. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` (`system-design.md`, `requirements-analysis-notes.md`, `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json`, `threat-model-notes.json`) are still from SH-14 until their own sub-tasks rewrite them.\n\n**Base stack (checked against `package.json`).** `artifacts/intake/tech-stack.json` reports `react` at 98% confidence. The workspace matches:\n\n- Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict\n- Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Zod 3.23.8, react-hook-form 7.53.0, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25\n- MUI 9.5.0 (material, icons-material, material-nextjs, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts), @mui/x-scheduler 9.0.0-beta.15 (theme augmentation only)\n- date-fns 3.6.0, date-fns-tz 3.2.0, papaparse, file-type 20.5.0, react-markdown + rehype-sanitize (behind `MarkdownView`)\n- Vitest 2.1.1, Testing Library, Playwright 1.47.2\n\nIntake reported no blockers (`blockers: []`, 95% confidence). It left six warnings and seven unresolved questions. ADR-11 through ADR-13 cover them.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no new dependencies\n\n**Context.** NFR-6 says to reuse what exists, with no re-scaffolding. NFR-7 requires lint, typecheck and tests to stay green. NFR-9 limits the work to one forge run. Every PRD-15 feature is covered by something already installed:\n\n- **Forms:** RHF + Zod\n- **Dates:** date-fns-tz\n- **CSV:** `src/server/csv.ts` / papaparse\n- **.ics:** `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`\n- **Markdown:** `MarkdownView` / `MarkdownEditor`\n- **Uploads:** `FileUpload` + `file-type`\n- **Grids:** MUI X DataGrid via `DataTable`\n- **Date inputs:** MUI X DatePicker\n\n**Decision.** No new runtime or dev dependencies. `package.json` stays unchanged.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no new supply-chain surface and no lockfile churn. If dev-planning proposes a package, it needs a new ADR.\n\n## ADR-2: UI is MUI only, and every component is looked up in mui-mcp first\n\n**Context.** NFR-4 requires MUI v9 and MUI X only. Banned libraries are never imported. Toasts go through `useToast()`, confirmations through `Dialog`/`ConfirmDialog`, pickers through `Autocomplete`. The mui-mcp server is connected in this session (`useMuiDocs`, `fetchDocs`).\n\n**Decision.** Map each new UI surface to MUI components:\n\n| Surface | Requirements | MUI components |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Child switcher | FR-3, FR-6 | `Select` or `Menu`, with `UserAvatar` |\n| Overview cards | FR-9–FR-17 | `Card`, `List`, `Chip`, `LoadingSkeleton` |\n| Absence form | FR-18 | `DatePicker`, `RadioGroup`, `Checkbox` group, `FileUpload` |\n| Review queue | FR-21, FR-22 | `DataTable`, with `Dialog` for approve/reject |\n| Slot buttons | FR-30 | `ToggleButton` or `Button` grid |\n| Day view | FR-34 | `Table` with print CSS through `sx` and `@media print` |\n| Consent tracking | FR-39 | `DataTable` |\n| Signature field | FR-37 | `TextField` |\n\nDevelopers must call `useMuiDocs` and `fetchDocs` before using each component. If the MCP is unreachable at dev time, that is a blocker, not something to work around.\n\n**Consequences.** QA's banned-import grep stays at zero hits. Printing (FR-34) uses `@media print` styles only, with no print library.\n\n## ADR-3: Data model is one additive Prisma migration, plus three flagged extra columns\n\n**Context.** FR-1 and FR-2 define the enums and models, and reuse `AudienceType` for consent. Consent audiences are limited to GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION and COURSE. Three requirements need persisted state that the PRD field list does not name:\n\n- **FR-29:** block individual slots. Deleting a slot would not work, because the next availability regeneration would recreate it.\n- **FR-39:** \"Remind non-responders\" is limited to once per 24 h. `src/server/rate-limit.ts` is in-memory per process (its own `ponytail:` note says so), so the limit would reset on every deploy or restart.\n- **FR-40:** the 48 h reminder must go out once per form.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Add one migration `…_prd15_parent_portal` with the enums and models as specified. Date-only fields use `@db.Date` (NFR-8).\n- The three extra columns:\n  - `ConferenceSlot.blocked Boolean @default(false)` (FR-29)\n  - `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` (FR-39)\n  - `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt DateTime?` (FR-40)\n\n  Both reminders claim their slot atomically with `updateMany({ where: { id, <col>: null | lt cutoff } })` and treat `count === 0` as \"already done\". This is the same pattern as `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt` (D-1).\n- Use one `ConsentResponse` per (formId, studentId) via `@@unique` (FR-38). Changes update the row in place, and each change is audited.\n- Zod schemas in `src/lib/validators/<feature>.ts` enforce the FR-2 limits: span ≤ 30 days, details ≤ 1,000 chars, slotMinutes 5–60, parentNote ≤ 500 chars. Forms and handlers share these schemas (NFR-7).\n\n**Consequences.** The extra columns go beyond \"exactly as specified\". `system-design.md` must list them as a deviation. If the PRD's own model already has an equivalent field, use that field and drop the extra column.\n\n## ADR-4: Conference booking uses a conditional UPDATE plus a partial unique index\n\n**Context.** NFR-1 requires that exactly one of two concurrent bookings succeeds. The loser gets 409 `That slot was just taken`. FR-31 allows one slot per teacher per child and no overlapping bookings across teachers. FR-30 requires the booking to be atomic.\n\n**Decision.**\n1. Book with `prisma.conferenceSlot.updateMany({ where: { id, bookedByParentId: null, blocked: false }, data: {...} })`. If `count === 0`, throw `AppError('CONFLICT', 'That slot was just taken')`. The client then refetches the slots.\n2. Enforce \"one per teacher per child\" in the database: a raw-SQL partial unique index in the migration on `(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) WHERE bookedForStudentId IS NOT NULL`. A P2002 error maps to a 409 with the FR-31 message. This follows the attendance ADR-3 precedent of a partial unique index plus P2002 handling.\n3. Check for overlaps with the parent's other bookings at that time inside the same `$transaction` before the conditional update. It returns `You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>`.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no advisory lock and no SERIALIZABLE isolation. The FR-46 integration test fires two `Promise.all` bookings and asserts exactly one success. There is a small window in which one parent could double-book overlapping slots with two different teachers in two tabs at once. That is acceptable: it is the same parent, and no data is corrupted.\n\n## ADR-5: Child selection uses an httpOnly cookie that is validated on every request\n\n**Context.** FR-3 to FR-6 require a selection stored in cookie `sh_child`, validated against `ParentStudentLink` on every request, falling back to the first child, with `?studentId=` as an override.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Create one server helper, `getSelectedChild(user, searchParams?)`, in `src/server/parent/selected-child.ts`, wrapped in React `cache()`.\n- It resolves the child in this order: `?studentId=` if linked, then the `sh_child` cookie if linked, then the first linked child ordered by firstName.\n- It reads the cookie with `cookies()` from `next/headers`.\n- Writes go through one small route handler that sets the cookie with `httpOnly`, `sameSite=lax`, `path=/` and a 1-year maxAge, then calls `router.refresh()`. That handler is the existing `withHandler` pattern and gets the existing NFR-8 same-origin check in middleware.\n\n**Consequences.** The cookie value is untrusted input. Every consumer gets it through the helper and never reads the cookie directly (NFR-5). The switcher lives in `shell.tsx`'s top bar.\n\n## ADR-6: The child overview is built from streaming server components\n\n**Context.** NFR-2 requires first paint under 1 s and the full page under 2 s. FR-17 requires each card to load independently through Suspense. FR-8 makes this the parent landing page.\n\n**Decision.**\n- `/my-children/[studentId]` is a server component. It calls `assertCanViewStudent` once, then renders eight async card components (FR-9–FR-16). Each card is wrapped in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` and runs its own service query.\n- No client data-fetching library is used. `GET /api/students/:id/overview` (FR-43) reuses the same service functions for API consumers.\n- Post-sign-in redirect for PARENT → `/my-children` (FR-8).\n\n**Consequences.** Slow cards such as grades do not block fast ones. Each card query must stay index-backed. `AttendanceRecord(studentId, createdAt)` and `CalendarEvent(startAt, endAt)` indexes already exist.\n\n## ADR-7: Absence coverage is one pure module that attendance-service uses in three places\n\n**Context.**\n- FR-23: approval converts ABSENT or missing records to EXCUSED.\n- FR-24: future registers are pre-filled.\n- FR-25: teachers may mark EXCUSED only when a note covers the student. Today `attendance-service.ts:219` restricts EXCUSED to ADMIN.\n- FR-27: absence notifications are suppressed.\n- FR-46 asks for unit tests of whole-day, partial-period and multi-day matching.\n\n**Decision.**\n- Add a pure function `coversRecord(note, { date, periodId })` in `src/server/absence-notes/absence-coverage.ts`, with no Prisma import so it can be unit-tested.\n- `absence-notes-service.ts` loads the relevant notes, and attendance-service uses the function at three points:\n  1. `getRegister`: pre-fill EXCUSED and show a badge.\n  2. `saveRegister` line 219: replace the ADMIN-only check with \"ADMIN, or an APPROVED note covers the record\".\n  3. Before `notifyStudentAndParents` (~line 299): drop `attendance.absent` for students covered by a PENDING or APPROVED note.\n- Approval runs in one `$transaction`. It updates matching ABSENT records with an `updateMany`, and creates missing records for sessions that already exist. Dates with no session yet are handled by the FR-24 pre-fill.\n- After commit, call `audit({ request })` so the IP is stored (NFR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** The rate recalculation needs no code, because `attendanceRate()` reads the records. Daily-homeroom sessions have no `periodId`, so whole-day and partial matching must treat a null `periodId` as matching any note that covers that date.\n\n## ADR-8: Dates and time zones reuse the existing helpers\n\n**Context.** NFR-8 requires UTC storage and school-timezone rules. Several features depend on this:\n\n- FR-18: absence dates from 14 days back to 60 days ahead\n- FR-9: what counts as \"today\"\n- FR-32: the booking window\n- FR-40: the reminder 48 h before the due date\n\n**Decision.** Use `schoolToday`, `addDays` and `daysBetween` from `attendance-rules.ts` and `date-fns-tz`, with the time zone from `SchoolSettings.timezone`. Generate slots (FR-29) with a pure `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` function in `conference-slots.ts`, which FR-46 also unit-tests.\n\n**Consequences.** No new date helpers. Pure functions keep the unit tests free of timezone flakiness.\n\n## ADR-9: Files, notifications and .ics extend the existing registries\n\n**Context.** FR-18 and FR-41 add the `absence-note` file context. FR-19, FR-26, FR-28, FR-33, FR-36 and FR-44 add notification types. FR-33 needs an .ics attachment link.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Files:** add an `absenceNoteResolver` to `src/server/files/contexts.ts`. It allows any linked parent (including the submitter), the homeroom teacher of the student's section, and ADMIN. Uploads reuse `FileUpload` and `files-service` validation, limited to PDF, JPG and PNG checked by `file-type` magic bytes.\n- **Notifications:** add these keys to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` in `types.ts`, then send through the existing `notify()` / `notifyStudentAndParents()`:\n\n  | Key | Default email |\n  | --- | --- |\n  | `absence_note.submitted` | false |\n  | `absence_note.reviewed` | true |\n  | `conference.slots_requested` | – |\n  | `conference.booked` | – |\n  | `conference.cancelled` | – |\n  | `consent.requested` | true |\n  | `consent.reminder` | true |\n\n- **.ics:** build it with the existing `buildCalendar` / `vevent` from `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`. Serve it from an authenticated GET per booked slot. The notification links to that URL.\n\n**Consequences.** There is no attachment pipeline. Email links to the .ics URL, which matches FR-33's \"attachment link\" wording.\n\n## ADR-10: Scheduled work goes in the existing cron route\n\n**Context.** FR-40 needs a maintenance run. The only scheduler is `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch`, which is protected by `CRON_SECRET` and already runs assignment reminders and quiz maintenance in isolated try-blocks.\n\n**Decision.** Add a `sendConsentDueReminders(now)` call to that route as another isolated try-block. It is idempotent through the `dueReminderSentAt` claim (ADR-3).\n\n**Consequences.** No new cron, worker or script. Reminder precision is limited by the cron interval.\n\n## ADR-11: Unavailable upstream data degrades gracefully\n\n**Context.**\n- FR-13: the PRD-12 `Announcement` model is missing. Only `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` exists.\n- FR-5, FR-14, FR-35: SH-14's dev phase failed. The `CalendarEvent` and `EventAudience` models exist, but there are no calendar pages or API.\n- Building either one would violate NFR-9, which says not to take on another PRD's scope.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **FR-13:** render an `EmptyState` (\"No announcements\") behind a single service function that returns `[]`. Do not add an Announcement model.\n- **FR-14:** query `CalendarEvent` directly with the existing `audienceWhereForUser(user, { studentIds: [child] })` and return the next 5. Expand recurrence with `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts`.\n- **FR-35:** render booked slots inside the overview's Upcoming events and Action items cards as \"My meetings\" items. There is no calendar page to add them to.\n- **FR-5:** the calendar `studentId` filter is not implemented, because there is no calendar page.\n- **ConsentForm.eventId:** an optional FK to `CalendarEvent`, which exists.\n\n**Consequences.** FR-13 and FR-35 are delivered partially. They become complete without schema work once PRD-12 and PRD-14 land. `system-design.md` should record this.\n\n## ADR-12: Answers to intake's open questions\n\n**Context.** Intake forwarded seven unresolved questions. No user is available to answer them.\n\n**Decision.**\n\n| # | Question | Decision |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Announcements | See ADR-11 |\n| 2 | Calendar | See ADR-11 |\n| 3 | Shared component location | Reuse components where they are, under `src/components/<Name>/`. Do not move them (NFR-6). |\n| 4 | Student detail route | `/students/[id]` is the target for \"View all\" links, including `/students/[id]/attendance`. |\n| 5 | Pages that adopt the `sh_child` default (FR-5) | The existing `/assignments`, `/grades` and `/api/me/timetable` consumers, plus the new `/my-children/*`, `/conferences/[id]` and `/consent-forms` pages. |\n| 6 | Reminder notification key | `consent.reminder` for both the 48 h reminder and the manual reminder (FR-44). |\n| 7 | Blocked slots (FR-29) | `ConferenceSlot.blocked` column (ADR-3). |\n\n**Consequences.** All seven are recorded as assumptions. None blocks the work.\n\n## ADR-13: Access control and tests follow the existing patterns\n\n**Context.** NFR-5 requires server-side access control on every handler. NFR-7 sets the quality gates. FR-46 lists the required tests.\n\n**Decision.**\n- **Access control:**\n  - Every handler uses `withHandler` and `requireRole`.\n  - Parent and child scoping uses `assertCanViewStudent` / `getAccessibleStudentIds`.\n  - Homeroom scoping checks section membership against `Section` (teacher's own section).\n  - Consent tracking is limited to the form's creator and ADMIN.\n  - Teachers may target only courses they manage (`canTargetAudience`).\n- **Tests:**\n  - Unit tests in Vitest cover the pure modules: `absence-coverage`, `conference-slots`, and signature matching (`trim().toLowerCase()` equality).\n  - Integration tests in Vitest against the database cover approval/pre-fill, concurrent booking and notification suppression.\n  - Three Playwright specs cover the FR-46 flows.\n- Use `logger`, never `console.log`.\n\n**Consequences.** No new test tooling. Seed data (FR-45) extends `prisma/seed.ts` in place.\n# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-15\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-10T12:00:00Z), PRD-15 Parent Portal: Child Switcher, Absence Notes & Conference Booking. It has 46 FRs and 10 NFRs (56 requirements) at 95% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers**. It has 6 warnings, and 7 clarifications are unresolved. §3 proposes a default for each one so that `arch-design-system` can decide.\n\n## 1. Codebase facts verified (2026-11-10)\n\n| Fact | Where | Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| No `AbsenceNote`/`Conference*`/`Consent*` models; `AudienceType` exists (SCHOOL, STAFF, ROLE, GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION, COURSE) | `prisma/schema.prisma:1236` | FR-1: one additive migration. Consent can only use 3 of the 6 values, so this must be enforced in Zod, not by a new enum |\n| `Section.homeroomTeacherId` exists; `assertHomeroom`-style check is private to attendance-service | `schema.prisma:397`, `attendance-service.ts:56-60` | FR-21/22/41 \"homeroom teacher\" = `Section.homeroomTeacherId` for the student's current-year `SectionMember` section. Export or duplicate a small helper |\n| EXCUSED is ADMIN-only on save; `canExcuse: user.role === 'ADMIN'` on load | `attendance-service.ts:219`, `:208` | FR-25: replace with a per-record check against approved notes; `getRegister` must return per-student `excusable` + `noteId` for FR-24 badge/pre-fill |\n| Absent/late notifications are sent after commit via `notificationsFor(diff)` → `notifyStudentAndParents` | `attendance-service.ts:~297-310` | FR-27: filter `notes.absent` against PENDING/APPROVED note coverage at this single point |\n| `AttendanceRecord` requires a `sessionId`; there is no sessionless record | `schema.prisma:569-585` | FR-23 \"no record yet\": approval cannot create records without a session. Updates existing ABSENT records; for dates with no session, coverage is applied at register load (FR-24). The same coverage function serves both |\n| `audit()` stores IP only when `request` is passed | `src/server/audit.ts:12,38` | NFR-3: absence review, consent response handlers must pass `request` |\n| Maintenance = passes run on every `/api/internal/email/dispatch` call | `src/server/quiz/maintenance.ts`, `assignments/reminders.ts` | FR-40: add a consent-reminder pass there; idempotency needs a \"reminded48hAt\" marker (field or AuditLog/Notification lookup) |\n| Files: contexts registered in `src/server/files/contexts.ts`, `registerFileAccess` | `src/server/files/access.ts` | FR-41: add `absence-note` context in contexts.ts |\n| Notification types: static map `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` | `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | FR-44: add keys only, no runtime API |\n| `GET /api/me/children` exists (PARENT, via `listLinksForParent`) | `src/app/api/me/children/route.ts` | FR-3/4/7: reuse `listLinksForParent` as the sole source for the switcher and cookie validation |\n| Calendar: `CalendarEvent`/`EventAudience` models + `src/server/calendar/{ical,recurrence}.ts`, but no calendar service/API/pages | `schema.prisma:1270`, `src/server/calendar` | FR-14/35/36 and the calendar part of FR-5 have only partial upstream support (see §3 Q2). `ical.ts` is reusable for FR-33 .ics |\n| No Announcement model (only `announcements/audience.ts`) | `src/server/announcements` | FR-13 has no data source (see §3 Q1). `audience.ts` is reusable for FR-36 consent audience resolution |\n| No `/my-children`, `/conferences`, `/consent-forms` routes; parent landing is `/dashboard`; student detail is `/students/[id]` | `src/app/(app)` | FR-7/8: new route group; change the post-sign-in redirect for PARENT |\n| Validators per feature in `src/lib/validators/*.ts` | — | NFR-7: add `absence-notes.ts`, `conferences.ts`, `consent-forms.ts` |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern keys: **DM** data model · **API** endpoint · **UI** page/surface · **SVC** service logic · **JOB** background/maintenance · **AUTH** access boundary · **NOTIF** notification · **INT** integration with existing module · **X** cross-cutting\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | DM | 3 enums + 6 models in one migration. `ConsentAudience` reuses `AudienceType`. Index `AbsenceNote(studentId, status, fromDate)`; `ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, startsAt)` unique; `ConsentResponse(formId, studentId)` unique (FR-38) |\n| FR-2 | SVC (Zod) | `src/lib/validators/absence-notes.ts`, `conferences.ts`. Span ≤ 30 days and `periodIds` only when `partialDay` use `.superRefine`. The same schema is used by the form and the handler |\n| FR-3 | UI + X | Top-bar switcher in `shell.tsx` (PARENT only). Writes the `sh_child` cookie via server action or route; MUI `Select`/`Menu` + `UserAvatar` |\n| FR-4 | AUTH + SVC | One `getSelectedChild(parent)` helper (cookie → `ParentStudentLink` check → fallback first child). Called on every parent request. Never trust the cookie alone |\n| FR-5 | INT | Parent pages resolve `studentId = searchParams.studentId ?? getSelectedChild()`, and `?studentId` is still access-checked. Target pages: `/grades`, `/assignments`, timetable (`/api/me/timetable` consumer), calendar (if present) (§3 Q5) |\n| FR-6 | UI | Same component; renders a name only when there is 1 child |\n| FR-7 | UI + API | `/my-children` server page. 1 child → `redirect`. `GET /api/me/children/summary` returns per-child attendance rate (attendance-service term rate), missing count, average grade |\n| FR-8 | INT | Post-sign-in redirect for PARENT → `/my-children` (which redirects to the overview for 1 child) |\n| FR-9 | INT | Reuse timetable service + SchoolDay/holiday data for \"today\" in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (NFR-8) |\n| FR-10 | INT | Reuse `getStudentAttendance` + term counts; button links to FR-18 form |\n| FR-11 | INT | Reuse assignments service (missing = past due, no submission, not exempt) |\n| FR-12 | INT | Reuse gradebook service; only visible/returned grades (respect existing visibility rules) |\n| FR-13 | INT (gap) | No source. Default: empty-state card with no new model (§3 Q1) |\n| FR-14 | INT (gap) | `CalendarEvent` + `EventAudience` query exists at model level. Default: a small read-only query in the overview service (§3 Q2) |\n| FR-15 | INT | Teachers from the student's active `Enrollment`→`Course.teacher` + subject. \"Message\" links to PRD-13 compose with the recipient prefilled |\n| FR-16 | SVC | Pending consent responses for the child + open conference events with no booking for the child |\n| FR-17 | UI + X | Each card is a separate async server component in `<Suspense>` with a `LoadingSkeleton` fallback. Also drives NFR-2 |\n| FR-18 | UI + API | `/my-children/[studentId]/absence/new`. Date window −14/+60 days in school TZ. Period checkboxes come from `Period` (bell schedule). `FileUpload` with context `absence-note` |\n| FR-19 | NOTIF | `absence_note.submitted` → homeroom teacher(s) of the student's section + all ADMINs |\n| FR-20 | UI + API | `GET /api/absence-notes` scoped by role (parent = linked students). Uses DataTable with standard pagination (NFR-10) |\n| FR-21 | UI + API + AUTH | `/attendance/absence-notes` queue. TEACHER limited to homeroom sections, ADMIN sees all. The detail view joins existing `AttendanceRecord`s for the date range |\n| FR-22 | API + SVC | `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review` `{decision, note}`; note required on reject (Zod). Only PENDING notes are reviewable (else 409) |\n| FR-23 | SVC + INT | Inside one transaction, update ABSENT records in sessions matching the dates (+ periodIds if partial) to EXCUSED with note `Absence note #<id>`; `audit()` with request. Rate recalculation is automatic because rates are computed on read. **Core shared function:** `noteCovers(note, date, periodId?)` |\n| FR-24 | INT | `getRegister` computes approved-note coverage for each student/date/period and pre-fills EXCUSED + badge when the record does not exist yet |\n| FR-25 | AUTH + INT | Replace the ADMIN-only guard in `saveRegister` with: ADMIN, or an approved note covers (student, date, period). Use the same coverage function |\n| FR-26 | NOTIF | `absence_note.reviewed` → submitting parent (+ other linked parents?), body includes reviewNote |\n| FR-27 | INT | Filter `notes.absent` in `saveRegister` with a PENDING/APPROVED coverage lookup (batched, one query per save) |\n| FR-28 | UI + API + NOTIF | `/admin/conferences`, `POST/PATCH /api/conferences`. Eligible teachers = teachers of courses with enrolled students in the eligible grade levels. Grade levels are stored on the event (array or join; FR-1 spec decides) |\n| FR-29 | UI + API + SVC | `PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability` replaces the teacher's unbooked slots in a transaction and never touches booked slots. Pure function `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` (unit test FR-46). Blocking: §3 Q7 |\n| FR-30 | UI + API + SVC | `/conferences/[id]` for the selected child's teachers. Booking = `updateMany where {id, bookedByParentId: null}`; count 0 → 409 |\n| FR-31 | SVC | Pre-checks in the same transaction: no existing slot for (teacher, child); no overlapping slot booked by this parent. Use the exact error message text |\n| FR-32 | SVC | Booking/cancel allowed only while `now` is within `[bookingOpensAt, bookingClosesAt]`. Reschedule is client-side cancel + book (no new endpoint) |\n| FR-33 | NOTIF + API | `conference.booked`/`cancelled` → parent + teacher. `.ics` via `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` reusing `src/server/calendar/ical.ts` |\n| FR-34 | UI | Teacher day view with `@media print` CSS. Reads the teacher's booked slots for the event |\n| FR-35 | INT (gap) | No calendar aggregation exists (SH-14 failed). Default: expose `listMyMeetings(user, range)` from the conference service for a future calendar source, and show booked slots on the overview/conference pages (§3 Q2) |\n| FR-36 | UI + API + AUTH + NOTIF | `/consent-forms/new`. TEACHER only for COURSE audiences of courses they teach. Audience is resolved to students via `announcements/audience.ts` and then to linked parents. `eventId` is an optional FK to `CalendarEvent` |\n| FR-37 | UI + API + SVC | `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/responses`. Signature check: `trim().toLowerCase()` equals the parent's full name (pure function, unit test). Only before `dueAt` |\n| FR-38 | DM + SVC | Unique (formId, studentId) upsert; `respondedById` = latest parent. Every create/change → `audit()` with old/new + request |\n| FR-39 | UI + API | `GET /api/consent-forms/:id/tracking` (creator/admin), `?format=csv` via `src/server/csv.ts`. `POST …/remind` throttled by a `lastRemindedAt` field on ConsentForm (24 h) → 429 |\n| FR-40 | JOB | Pass in dispatch maintenance: forms with `dueAt` in (now, now+48h] not yet reminded → notify non-responders and set a marker (e.g. `autoReminderSentAt`) for idempotency |\n| FR-41 | AUTH | `absence-note` context in `files/contexts.ts`: submitting parent, other linked parents, the student's homeroom teacher, ADMIN |\n| FR-42 | UI | Nav config in `shell.tsx`. Teacher \"Absence notes\" only if they are a homeroom teacher (current year) |\n| FR-43 | API + AUTH | ~20 route handlers using `withHandler` / `requireRole` / `ok` from `src/server/http.ts`. Thin handlers call `src/server/<feature>/<feature>-service.ts` |\n| FR-44 | NOTIF | Add 6 keys + `consent.reminder` (one key covers both the manual and the 48 h reminder) to `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` with the PRD's `defaultEmail` values |\n| FR-45 | X (seed) | Extend `prisma/seed.ts`. The consent form needs a seeded CalendarEvent. Tom/Tina must be teachers of Grade 7 courses |\n| FR-46 | X (tests) | Unit: `noteCovers`, `generateSlots`, `signatureMatches`. Integration: approval, pre-fill, concurrent booking (`Promise.all` of 2 bookings), suppression. 3 Playwright specs |\n| NFR-1 | SVC + DM | Conditional `updateMany` is the guarantee (no app lock). 409 `CONFLICT` \"That slot was just taken\"; the client refetches slots |\n| NFR-2 | X | Suspense per card (FR-17). Each card runs ≤ 2 queries with `select`. Shell + header render first |\n| NFR-3 | X | `audit({…, request})` on review, consent respond/change, conference admin edits |\n| NFR-4 | UI | MUI v9 + X only; mui-mcp lookups are required per component (the tools are available this session). Notable components: Select/Menu (switcher), Card, DataGrid, DatePicker, Checkbox group, ToggleButton (slots), Dialog |\n| NFR-5 | AUTH | Central access helpers: `assertParentOf(user, studentId)`, `assertHomeroomOf(user, studentId)`, `assertConsentOwner(user, form)`. Server pages call them too, not only APIs |\n| NFR-6 | X | New services: `src/server/absence-notes/`, `conferences/`, `consent-forms/`, `parent-portal/` (overview, child selection). No moves or renames |\n| NFR-7 | X | Validators in `src/lib/validators/`; use logger, not console |\n| NFR-8 | X | `@db.Date` for `fromDate`/`toDate`/conference `date`; all windows (−14/+60, today, dueAt−48h) use the existing `schoolToday(now, tz)` |\n| NFR-9 | X | Do not build calendar/announcement subsystems (PRD-12/14 scope); use degrade-gracefully defaults |\n| NFR-10 | API | List endpoints (`absence-notes`, `consent-forms`, `tracking`, admin `conferences`) use the standard `?page&pageSize≤100&sort&q` |\n\n## 3. Open questions: proposed defaults for `arch-design-system`\n\n| # | Question (from intake) | Proposed default | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Q1 | Announcements card has no model | Render the card with an `EmptyState` (\"No announcements\"). Do not add an Announcement model, because it belongs to PRD-12 (NFR-9). Record this as a known gap | FR-13 |\n| Q2 | Calendar API/pages missing (SH-14 failed) | Upcoming events: query `CalendarEvent`+`EventAudience` directly in the overview service (read-only, small). My meetings: expose `listMyMeetings` and list booked meetings on the overview/conference pages; full calendar integration is deferred to PRD-14. `ConsentForm.eventId`: optional FK, picked via Autocomplete over existing events | FR-5, FR-14, FR-35, FR-36 |\n| Q3 | Shared components at `src/components/<Name>/` | Reuse in place; do not move them (NFR-6) | NFR-6 |\n| Q4 | Student route is `/students/[id]` | \"View all\" links target `/students/[id]?tab=…` where tabs exist, otherwise the feature pages (`/grades?studentId=`, `/assignments?studentId=`) | FR-17 |\n| Q5 | Which pages adopt `sh_child` | `/grades`, `/assignments`, `/api/me/timetable` consumers, and new SH-15 pages. Calendar only once it exists | FR-5 |\n| Q6 | Reminder notification key | Single key `consent.reminder` (defaultEmail true) for both the manual and the 48 h reminder | FR-39, FR-40, FR-44 |\n| Q7 | Blocking slots: schema has no field | Add `blocked Boolean @default(false)` to `ConferenceSlot`. Deleting a slot would lose it on availability regeneration. Note that this is the only deviation from the PRD's \"exactly as specified\" model (FR-1) | FR-1, FR-29 |\n\nAdditional decisions the design must make:\n- **Homeroom resolution** (FR-19/21/41/42): student → current-year `SectionMember` → `Section.homeroomTeacherId`. Put this in one shared helper.\n- **Throttle/idempotency markers** (FR-39/40): this needs fields not in the PRD model (`lastRemindedAt`, `autoReminderSentAt`). Alternative: query `Notification` rows of type `consent.reminder`. Fields are simpler, so the recommendation is to add them.\n- **FR-23 vs FR-24 split**: approval changes only existing ABSENT records. Future or untaken registers rely on load-time coverage. One `noteCovers` function underpins FR-23/24/25/27, and it is the main unit-test target.\n- **FR-26 recipients**: the submitting parent is required. Notifying other linked parents is optional (recommended, since FR-41 already grants them read access).\n","numLines":781,"startLine":1,"totalLines":781}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BfYUt3RhBHXntC5aHYeTe6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
