{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtXG5iDiMksYAt4MQ62D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing `system-design.md` now. I've confirmed the helpers it builds on: navigation config, the dashboard landing page, the audience helpers and the attendance rules."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":54846,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":459},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eeb429-6a70-48e8-a0ff-b55a8b190b9d","uuid":"d4f019ad-601b-4d31-b40b-bdc569c94312","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:17:01.745Z","request_id":"req_011CgtXG5W4ii3kUcd4nM6YN"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtXG5iDiMksYAt4MQ62D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TFouAbRyaNUFyWffQRAfUf","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking, Consent Forms)\n\nTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-10), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-13), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n> This file replaces the SH-14 version. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` and `threat-model-notes.json` are still from SH-14 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSH-15 adds a parent portal to the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 brownfield app. It has five parts:\n\n1. **Child context:** the `sh_child` cookie, a top-bar switcher, and a default student on parent pages (FR-3 to FR-6).\n2. **Child overview:** `/my-children` and `/my-children/[studentId]`, built from eight streaming cards (FR-7 to FR-17).\n3. **Absence notes:** parents submit notes, teachers and admins review them, and approved notes connect to attendance (FR-18 to FR-27, FR-41).\n4. **Parent–teacher conferences:** admins create events, teachers set availability, and parents book slots atomically (FR-28 to FR-35).\n5. **Consent forms:** staff create forms, parents respond with a typed signature, and creators track responses and send reminders (FR-36 to FR-40).\n\nAll five use the existing building blocks:\n\n- `withHandler`, `requireRole` and `ok`/`AppError` from `src/server/http.ts`\n- `assertCanViewStudent` and `getAccessibleStudentIds` from `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\n- `audit()` and `notify()` / `notifyStudentAndParents()`\n- The file contexts registry\n- The audience helpers in `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`\n- `attendance-rules.ts` (`schoolToday`, `attendanceRate`)\n- `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`\n- The cron route `/api/internal/email/dispatch`\n\nThe design adds **no new dependencies** (ADR-1) and moves or renames nothing (NFR-6).\n\n### Blockers and warnings from intake\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. Its warnings and the seven unresolved questions are settled as follows. Each is an assumption, not a blocker.\n\n| Intake warning / question | Design decision | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| PRD-12 Announcement model absent | The Announcements card renders an `EmptyState`. `listUnreadAnnouncements()` returns `[]`. **FR-13 is partial.** | FR-13 |\n| SH-14 calendar has no API or pages | Upcoming events queries `CalendarEvent` directly through `audienceWhereForUser`. \"My meetings\" appear as overview items. There is no calendar `studentId` filter, because no calendar page exists. **FR-14 is complete. FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 are partial.** | FR-5, FR-14, FR-35 |\n| Shared components live under `src/components/<Name>/` | Reuse them in place. | NFR-6 |\n| Student detail route is `/students/[id]` | \"View all\" links point to `/students/[id]` tabs, `/assignments?studentId=` and `/grades?studentId=`. | FR-17 |\n| Which pages adopt `sh_child` | `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable`, and all new SH-15 parent pages. | FR-5 |\n| Reminder notification key | One key, `consent.reminder`, for both the manual and the 48 h reminder. | FR-44 |\n| `attendance-service.ts:219` allows EXCUSED for ADMIN only | Replace the check: ADMIN, or an APPROVED note covers the record. | FR-25 |\n| Blocked slots | Add a `ConferenceSlot.blocked` column. | FR-29 |\n\n### Deviations from \"exactly as specified\" (FR-1)\n\nThe design adds three columns that the PRD does not list (ADR-3):\n\n| Column | Reqs | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ConferenceSlot.blocked Boolean @default(false)` | FR-29 | A blocked slot survives availability regeneration. |\n| `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` | FR-39 | 24 h throttle that holds across processes. |\n| `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt DateTime?` | FR-40 | Makes the 48 h reminder idempotent. |\n\nThe migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on `ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) WHERE bookedForStudentId IS NOT NULL` (FR-31, ADR-4). If the PRD's model already has an equivalent field, use it and drop the extra column.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: one additive migration `…_prd15_parent_portal` (FR-1, FR-2, NFR-8)\n\n| Model / enum | Key fields and constraints | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `enum AbsenceNoteStatus`, `AbsenceReason`, `ConsentResponseValue` | As specified in the PRD | FR-1 |\n| `AbsenceNote` | `studentId`, `submittedById`, `fromDate`/`toDate @db.Date`, `partialDay`, `periodIds String[]`, `reason`, `details`, `fileId?`, `status`, `reviewedById?`, `reviewNote?`, `reviewedAt?`. Index `(studentId, status, fromDate)` | FR-1, FR-18, FR-22 |\n| `ConferenceEvent` | `title`, `date @db.Date`, `bookingOpensAt`, `bookingClosesAt`, `slotMinutes` (5–60), eligible grade levels, `createdById` | FR-1, FR-28 |\n| `ConferenceSlot` | `eventId`, `teacherId`, `startsAt`, `endsAt`, `location?`, `bookedByParentId?`, `bookedForStudentId?`, `parentNote?` (≤ 500), **`blocked`**. Unique `(eventId, teacherId, startsAt)`, plus the partial unique index above | FR-1, FR-29 to FR-31 |\n| `ConsentForm` | `title`, `description` (Markdown), `dueAt`, `eventId?` FK to `CalendarEvent`, `createdById`, **`lastRemindedAt?`**, **`dueReminderSentAt?`** | FR-1, FR-36, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| `ConsentAudience` | `formId`, `type AudienceType` (GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION or COURSE, enforced in Zod), `refId` | FR-1, FR-36 |\n| `ConsentResponse` | `formId`, `studentId`, `respondedById`, `value`, `signature`, `comment?`. `@@unique([formId, studentId])` | FR-1, FR-38 |\n\nValidators live in `src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts`. Forms and handlers share the same Zod schemas, which enforce the FR-2 limits with `.superRefine`. They also enforce the −14/+60 day window (FR-18) and the rule that a reject requires a note (FR-22). (NFR-7)\n\n### 2.2 Server modules (NFR-6: `src/server/<feature>/`)\n\n| Module | Responsibilities | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/parent/selected-child.ts` | `getSelectedChild(user, searchParams?)`, wrapped in React `cache()`. It resolves in this order: a linked `?studentId=`, then a linked `sh_child` cookie, then the first linked child (`listLinksForParent`). `setSelectedChildCookie(studentId)` validates the link before it writes the cookie (`httpOnly`, `sameSite=lax`, 1 year). | FR-3 to FR-6 |\n| `src/server/parent/overview-service.ts` | One function per card: `getToday`, `getAttendanceSummary`, `getAssignmentsSummary`, `getRecentGrades`, `listUnreadAnnouncements` (returns `[]`), `getUpcomingEvents` (next 5, `CalendarEvent` plus booked meetings), `getTeachers`, `getActionItems` (pending consent plus open conferences). `getChildrenSummary(parent)` builds the `/my-children` cards. Every function reuses the existing timetable, attendance, assignments and gradebook services. | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-coverage.ts` | **Pure, no Prisma.** `coversRecord(note, { date, periodId })`. A whole-day note covers every period on each date in range. A partial note covers only its `periodIds`. A record with a null `periodId` (daily homeroom) is covered by any note for that date. | FR-23 to FR-25, FR-27, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-notes-service.ts` | `submit` (sets PENDING, then `notify('absence_note.submitted')` to the homeroom teacher and ADMINs), `list` (scoped by role, paginated), `getForReview` (joins existing `AttendanceRecord`s), `review` (see §3.2), `findCovering(studentIds, dateRange, statuses)` for attendance-service, `homeroomTeacherOf(studentId)`. | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (changed in place) | `getRegister`: pre-fill EXCUSED and set `noteId`/`excusable` for each student covered by an APPROVED note. `saveRegister:219`: allow EXCUSED for ADMIN, or when an APPROVED note covers the record. `~:299`: before `notifyStudentAndParents`, drop `attendance.absent` for students covered by a PENDING or APPROVED note. | FR-24, FR-25, FR-27 |\n| `src/server/conferences/conference-slots.ts` | **Pure.** `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` and `overlaps(a, b)`. | FR-29, FR-31, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/conferences/conferences-service.ts` | `createEvent`/`updateEvent` (ADMIN), which notifies eligible teachers with `conference.slots_requested`. `setAvailability` uses one transaction to delete the teacher's unbooked, unblocked slots and insert the newly generated ones. Booked and blocked slots are never touched. `setSlotBlocked`, `removeSlot` (unbooked only), `listBookable(event, child)`, `book` and `cancel` (§3.3), `teacherDay(event, teacher)`, `listMyMeetings(user, range)`, `slotIcs(slot, user)`. | FR-28 to FR-35 |\n| `src/server/consent-forms/consent-forms-service.ts` | `create`: checks `canTargetAudience` for each audience row, then notifies parents of the resolved audience students with `consent.requested`. Also `listForParent`, `respond` (§3.4), `tracking` (JSON or CSV through `src/server/csv.ts`), `remind` (24 h claim on `lastRemindedAt`, else 429), and `sendConsentDueReminders(now)` (claims `dueReminderSentAt`). | FR-36 to FR-40 |\n| `src/server/consent-forms/signature.ts` | **Pure.** `signatureMatches(typed, fullName)` compares both values after `trim().toLowerCase()`. | FR-37, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (extended) | `absence-note` resolver grants read access to any linked parent, the homeroom teacher and ADMIN. Uploads allow PDF, JPG and PNG, checked with `file-type`. | FR-18, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (extended) | `absence_note.submitted` (email false), `absence_note.reviewed` (true), `conference.slots_requested`, `conference.booked`, `conference.cancelled`, `consent.requested` (true), `consent.reminder` (true) | FR-19, FR-26, FR-28, FR-33, FR-36, FR-40, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch` (extended) | Adds an isolated try-block that calls `sendConsentDueReminders(now)`. | FR-40 |\n\n**Access helpers (NFR-5).** Every page and handler calls one of these:\n\n- `assertCanViewStudent`, for parent-to-child scoping\n- `assertHomeroomOrAdmin(user, studentId)`, in absence-notes-service, built on `Section.homeroomTeacherId` for the current-year `SectionMember`\n- `assertConsentOwnerOrAdmin(user, form)`\n- `requireRole`\n\nThe `sh_child` cookie is never read except through `getSelectedChild`.\n\n### 2.3 API layer (FR-43)\n\nRoute handlers are thin. They use `withHandler`, then Zod parse, then a service call, then `ok()`, all under `src/app/api/`. Every list endpoint supports `?page&pageSize≤100&sort&q` (NFR-10).\n\n| Area | Routes | Roles | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Child context | `POST /api/me/selected-child` | PARENT | FR-3, FR-4 |\n| Parent summaries | `GET /api/me/children/summary`, `GET /api/students/:id/overview` | PARENT (linked), staff via `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16 |\n| Absence notes | `GET/POST /api/absence-notes`, `GET /api/absence-notes/:id`, `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review` | PARENT (own children), TEACHER (homeroom), ADMIN | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26 |\n| Conferences | `GET/POST /api/conferences`, `GET/PATCH /api/conferences/:id`, `PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability`, `GET /api/conferences/:id/slots`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/conference-slots/:id`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/cancel`, `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` | ADMIN (events), TEACHER (own availability), PARENT (book and cancel for the selected or linked child) | FR-28 to FR-34 |\n| Consent forms | `GET/POST /api/consent-forms`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/responses`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id/tracking[?format=csv]`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/remind` | ADMIN, TEACHER (managed courses), PARENT (respond) | FR-36 to FR-39 |\n\n`arch-api-contracts` will write the exact request and response schemas.\n\n### 2.4 UI layer (NFR-4: MUI v9 only, with an mui-mcp lookup per component)\n\n| Route / surface | Kind | Key components | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `shell.tsx` top bar: `ChildSwitcher` | client | `Select`/`Menu` + `UserAvatar`. With one child it shows a name only. Changing the child POSTs to the selected-child route, then calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-3, FR-6 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | config | Parent: My children, Absence notes, Conferences, Consent forms. Teacher: Absence notes (only if homeroom, via a `homeroom` flag passed like `safeguardingLead`) and Conferences. Admin: Conferences, Consent forms, Absence notes. | FR-42 |\n| `/dashboard` | server | If the role is PARENT, `redirect('/my-children')`. | FR-8 |\n| `/my-children` | server | With one child, `redirect` to the overview. Otherwise show summary `Card`s. | FR-7 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]` | server, streaming | 8 async cards, each in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` with a \"View all\" link | FR-9 to FR-17, NFR-2 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence/new` | client form | RHF + Zod, `DatePicker`, `RadioGroup` (whole day or periods), a `Checkbox` group from `Period`, `FileUpload` (`absence-note`) | FR-18 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence` (parent list) | server + `DataTable` | Status `Chip` | FR-20 |\n| `/attendance/absence-notes` | server + `DataTable` | Status and date filters. The detail `Dialog` shows the note, the document link, existing records, and Approve/Reject (reject requires a note). | FR-21, FR-22 |\n| Attendance register (existing) | changed | EXCUSED pre-fill + an \"Absence note\" `Chip` badge. The EXCUSED option is enabled per `excusable`. | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `/admin/conferences` (list, plus new/edit form) | server + client form | `DataTable`, `DatePicker`/`DateTimePicker`, `Autocomplete` (grade levels) | FR-28 |\n| `/conferences/[id]/availability` | client | Time-range rows, location `TextField`, a slot list with remove and block `IconButton`s | FR-29 |\n| `/conferences/[id]` (parent) | client | One section per teacher of the child, with `Button`/`ToggleButton` slot buttons and an optional note `Dialog`. A 409 shows a toast and refetches. The parent's own booking has Cancel. | FR-30 to FR-32, NFR-1 |\n| `/conferences/[id]/day` (teacher) | server | `Table` of booked slots, with `@media print` through `sx` | FR-34 |\n| `/conferences` | server | Event list for each role | FR-42 |\n| `/consent-forms`, `/consent-forms/new`, `/consent-forms/[id]` | server + client form | `MarkdownEditor`/`MarkdownView`, an audience picker reusing the announcements audience UI pattern, an `Autocomplete` event link, a respond form (`RadioGroup` + signature `TextField` + comment) | FR-36 to FR-38 |\n| `/consent-forms/[id]/tracking` | server + `DataTable` | Status filter, CSV export link, \"Remind non-responders\" `Button` (409 or 429 produces a toast) | FR-39 |\n\nToasts go through `useToast()` and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`. Nothing is imported from the banned list.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Child selection (FR-3 to FR-6)\n\n```\nSwitcher change → POST /api/me/selected-child {studentId}\n  → assert ParentStudentLink → Set-Cookie sh_child (httpOnly) → router.refresh()\nAny parent page → getSelectedChild(user, searchParams)\n  → ?studentId (if linked) ▸ cookie (if linked) ▸ first linked child\n```\n\nThe cookie is untrusted. A stale or tampered value falls back to the first child and never errors.\n\n### 3.2 Absence note lifecycle (FR-18 to FR-27)\n\n```\nParent form ─(Zod)→ POST /api/absence-notes\n  → assertCanViewStudent → create PENDING (+fileId, context absence-note)\n  → notify(absence_note.submitted → homeroom teacher + ADMINs)\n\nReviewer → POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review {decision, note}\n  → assertHomeroomOrAdmin → $transaction:\n       updateMany AbsenceNote where {id, status: PENDING} (count 0 → 409)\n       if APPROVED: load sessions in [fromDate,toDate] for student's sections;\n                    for each covered (date, periodId) via coversRecord:\n                      existing ABSENT record → EXCUSED, note \"Absence note #<id>\"\n                      session exists, no record → create EXCUSED record\n  → after commit: audit({ request }) (IP, NFR-3); notify(absence_note.reviewed → linked parents, incl. reviewNote)\n\nRegister load (getRegister) → findCovering(APPROVED) → pre-fill EXCUSED + badge (future dates, FR-24)\nRegister save (saveRegister) → EXCUSED allowed if ADMIN or APPROVED note covers (FR-25)\n                             → absent notifications filtered by PENDING|APPROVED coverage (FR-27)\n```\n\nAttendance rates recalculate without new code, because `attendanceRate()` counts records when it reads them (FR-23). A rejected note changes no records.\n\n### 3.3 Conference booking (FR-28 to FR-33, NFR-1)\n\n```\nAdmin creates event → notify(conference.slots_requested → teachers of eligible grade levels)\nTeacher PUT availability {ranges, location} → generateSlots → $transaction(delete unbooked&unblocked, insert new)\nParent POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book {studentId, note?}\n  → assertCanViewStudent; now within [bookingOpensAt, bookingClosesAt] else 422\n  → $transaction:\n       overlap check vs parent's other booked slots at that time → 409 \"You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>\"\n       updateMany where {id, bookedByParentId: null, blocked: false} → count 0 → 409 \"That slot was just taken\"\n       P2002 on (eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) → 409 (one per teacher per child)\n  → notify(conference.booked → parent + teacher, link /api/conference-slots/:id/ics)\nCancel → before bookingClosesAt; clear booking fields → notify(conference.cancelled)\nReschedule = cancel + book (client-side, FR-32)\n```\n\n### 3.4 Consent forms (FR-36 to FR-40)\n\n```\nCreate → canTargetAudience per row → insert form+audiences → resolve audience students → linked parents\n       → notify(consent.requested)\nRespond POST …/responses {studentId, value, signature, comment?}\n  → assertCanViewStudent; now < dueAt else 422; signatureMatches(signature, parent full name) else 422\n  → upsert by (formId, studentId) → audit({ before, after, request })\nTracking → audience students × responses → Granted/Declined/No response; ?format=csv\nRemind → updateMany where {id, lastRemindedAt null|< now-24h} count 0 → 429 → notify(consent.reminder → non-responders)\nCron dispatch → forms with dueAt in (now, now+48h], dueReminderSentAt null → claim → notify(consent.reminder)\n```\n\n### 3.5 Overview rendering (FR-7 to FR-17, NFR-2)\n\nThe server page calls `assertCanViewStudent` once. The header and switcher paint first. The eight cards then stream independently, each doing one or two indexed `select` queries in `overview-service`. `GET /api/students/:id/overview` calls the same functions for API consumers. All \"today\", window and due-date evaluation uses `schoolToday(now, SchoolSettings.timezone)` (NFR-8).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Testing and seed data (FR-45, FR-46, NFR-7)\n\n- **Unit tests (Vitest):**\n  - `absence-coverage`: whole day, partial periods, multi-day, and a null `periodId`\n  - `conference-slots`: generation at range boundaries, `slotMinutes` 5 and 60, and overlap\n  - `signature`: case and whitespace\n- **Integration tests (Vitest + DB):**\n  - Approval converts ABSENT to EXCUSED and leaves PRESENT untouched.\n  - Future-register pre-fill.\n  - Two concurrent `book` calls run through `Promise.all`: exactly one succeeds and the other gets 409.\n  - `attendance.absent` is suppressed while a PENDING note covers the student.\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Absence note, then approve, then the register shows EXCUSED.\n  - Book a conference slot.\n  - Sign a consent form.\n- **Seed:** extend `prisma/seed.ts` in place:\n  - Grade 7: one PENDING and one APPROVED absence note.\n  - \"Autumn conferences\" 3 weeks out, with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 at 10 minutes each, two of them booked.\n  - \"Science Museum Trip\" consent form due in 10 days, linked to a seeded `CalendarEvent`, with about 40% of responses in.\n- **Gates:** `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test`. Use `logger`, never `console.log`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 migration `…_prd15_parent_portal`, 3 enums and 6 models, 3 flagged extra columns |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 Zod validators `src/lib/validators/*` with `.superRefine` |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `selected-child.ts`; §2.4 `ChildSwitcher`; `POST /api/me/selected-child` |\n| FR-4 | §3.1 `getSelectedChild` link validation and fallback |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `getSelectedChild` used by `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable` and new pages (calendar filter partial, ADR-11) |\n| FR-6 | §2.4 `ChildSwitcher` single-child mode |\n| FR-7 | §2.4 `/my-children`; `getChildrenSummary`; `GET /api/me/children/summary` |\n| FR-8 | §2.4 `/dashboard` redirects PARENT to `/my-children` |\n| FR-9 | `overview-service.getToday` (timetable + SchoolDay holidays) |\n| FR-10 | `overview-service.getAttendanceSummary` + link to the absence form |\n| FR-11 | `overview-service.getAssignmentsSummary` |\n| FR-12 | `overview-service.getRecentGrades` (visibility rules respected) |\n| FR-13 | `listUnreadAnnouncements` returns `[]` and the card shows an `EmptyState` (**partial**, PRD-12 absent) |\n| FR-14 | `overview-service.getUpcomingEvents` (`CalendarEvent` via `audienceWhereForUser` + recurrence) |\n| FR-15 | `overview-service.getTeachers` + Message link (PRD-13 compose) |\n| FR-16 | `overview-service.getActionItems` |\n| FR-17 | §3.5 Suspense per card + \"View all\" links |\n| FR-18 | §2.4 absence form; `absence-notes-service.submit`; `absence-note` file context |\n| FR-19 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.submitted)` to homeroom teacher + ADMINs |\n| FR-20 | §2.4 parent absence list; `GET /api/absence-notes` |\n| FR-21 | §2.4 `/attendance/absence-notes`; `getForReview`; `assertHomeroomOrAdmin` |\n| FR-22 | §3.2 `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review`, PENDING-only conditional update |\n| FR-23 | §3.2 approval transaction + `coversRecord` + `audit` |\n| FR-24 | §2.2 `getRegister` pre-fill + badge |\n| FR-25 | §2.2 `saveRegister:219` EXCUSED rule |\n| FR-26 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.reviewed)` with reviewNote |\n| FR-27 | §2.2 attendance-service notification filter (~:299) |\n| FR-28 | §2.4 `/admin/conferences`; `createEvent`/`updateEvent`; `conference.slots_requested` |\n| FR-29 | §2.4 availability page; `setAvailability`, `generateSlots`, `blocked` column |\n| FR-30 | §3.3 conditional `updateMany` booking; `/conferences/[id]` |\n| FR-31 | §3.3 overlap check + partial unique index |\n| FR-32 | §3.3 booking-window guard; cancel; reschedule = cancel + book |\n| FR-33 | §3.3 `conference.booked`/`cancelled` + `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` (`ical.ts`) |\n| FR-34 | §2.4 `/conferences/[id]/day`, print CSS |\n| FR-35 | `listMyMeetings`, shown as \"My meetings\" in overview Upcoming events and Action items (**partial**, no PRD-14 calendar page) |\n| FR-36 | §3.4 create + `canTargetAudience` + `consent.requested`; `/consent-forms/new` |\n| FR-37 | §3.4 respond + `signatureMatches`; overview Action items; `/consent-forms` |\n| FR-38 | `ConsentResponse @@unique(formId, studentId)` upsert + `audit` |\n| FR-39 | §3.4 tracking/CSV; remind with a `lastRemindedAt` 24 h claim |\n| FR-40 | §3.4 `sendConsentDueReminders` in the dispatch cron; `dueReminderSentAt` |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 `absence-note` resolver in `files/contexts.ts` |\n| FR-42 | §2.4 `src/config/navigation.ts` entries + homeroom flag |\n| FR-43 | §2.3 route table, `withHandler`/`requireRole`, standard shapes |\n| FR-44 | §2.2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` additions incl. `consent.reminder` |\n| FR-45 | §4 seed extensions |\n| FR-46 | §4 unit, integration and Playwright tests |\n| NFR-1 | §3.3 conditional update → 409 \"That slot was just taken\" + client refetch |\n| NFR-2 | §3.5 streaming cards, indexed `select` queries |\n| NFR-3 | `audit({ request })` on review, consent respond/change, conference admin edits |\n| NFR-4 | §2.4 MUI-only component map, with an mui-mcp lookup required per component |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 access helpers on every page and handler; cookie only via `getSelectedChild` |\n| NFR-6 | §2.2 new `src/server/<feature>/` modules; existing files extended in place |\n| NFR-7 | §2.1 shared Zod validators; §4 gates; `logger` |\n| NFR-8 | `@db.Date` fields; `schoolToday` + `SchoolSettings.timezone` for all date rules |\n| NFR-9 | No Announcement or calendar subsystem built; FR-13, FR-35 and FR-5 calendar part degrade (ADR-11) |\n| NFR-10 | §2.3 list endpoints use standard pagination, sort and `q` |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":54846,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":459},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eeb429-6a70-48e8-a0ff-b55a8b190b9d","uuid":"eaa26eec-0478-41a1-b534-321b813d40f3","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:18:29.236Z","request_id":"req_011CgtXG5W4ii3kUcd4nM6YN","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TFouAbRyaNUFyWffQRAfUf":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking, Consent Forms)\n\nTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-10), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-13), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n> This file replaces the SH-14 version. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` and `threat-model-notes.json` are still from SH-14 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSH-15 adds a parent portal to the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 brownfield app. It has five parts:\n\n1. **Child context:** the `sh_child` cookie, a top-bar switcher, and a default student on parent pages (FR-3 to FR-6).\n2. **Child overview:** `/my-children` and `/my-children/[studentId]`, built from eight streaming cards (FR-7 to FR-17).\n3. **Absence notes:** parents submit notes, teachers and admins review them, and approved notes connect to attendance (FR-18 to FR-27, FR-41).\n4. **Parent–teacher conferences:** admins create events, teachers set availability, and parents book slots atomically (FR-28 to FR-35).\n5. **Consent forms:** staff create forms, parents respond with a typed signature, and creators track responses and send reminders (FR-36 to FR-40).\n\nAll five use the existing building blocks:\n\n- `withHandler`, `requireRole` and `ok`/`AppError` from `src/server/http.ts`\n- `assertCanViewStudent` and `getAccessibleStudentIds` from `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\n- `audit()` and `notify()` / `notifyStudentAndParents()`\n- The file contexts registry\n- The audience helpers in `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`\n- `attendance-rules.ts` (`schoolToday`, `attendanceRate`)\n- `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`\n- The cron route `/api/internal/email/dispatch`\n\nThe design adds **no new dependencies** (ADR-1) and moves or renames nothing (NFR-6).\n\n### Blockers and warnings from intake\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. Its warnings and the seven unresolved questions are settled as follows. Each is an assumption, not a blocker.\n\n| Intake warning / question | Design decision | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| PRD-12 Announcement model absent | The Announcements card renders an `EmptyState`. `listUnreadAnnouncements()` returns `[]`. **FR-13 is partial.** | FR-13 |\n| SH-14 calendar has no API or pages | Upcoming events queries `CalendarEvent` directly through `audienceWhereForUser`. \"My meetings\" appear as overview items. There is no calendar `studentId` filter, because no calendar page exists. **FR-14 is complete. FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 are partial.** | FR-5, FR-14, FR-35 |\n| Shared components live under `src/components/<Name>/` | Reuse them in place. | NFR-6 |\n| Student detail route is `/students/[id]` | \"View all\" links point to `/students/[id]` tabs, `/assignments?studentId=` and `/grades?studentId=`. | FR-17 |\n| Which pages adopt `sh_child` | `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable`, and all new SH-15 parent pages. | FR-5 |\n| Reminder notification key | One key, `consent.reminder`, for both the manual and the 48 h reminder. | FR-44 |\n| `attendance-service.ts:219` allows EXCUSED for ADMIN only | Replace the check: ADMIN, or an APPROVED note covers the record. | FR-25 |\n| Blocked slots | Add a `ConferenceSlot.blocked` column. | FR-29 |\n\n### Deviations from \"exactly as specified\" (FR-1)\n\nThe design adds three columns that the PRD does not list (ADR-3):\n\n| Column | Reqs | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ConferenceSlot.blocked Boolean @default(false)` | FR-29 | A blocked slot survives availability regeneration. |\n| `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` | FR-39 | 24 h throttle that holds across processes. |\n| `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt DateTime?` | FR-40 | Makes the 48 h reminder idempotent. |\n\nThe migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on `ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) WHERE bookedForStudentId IS NOT NULL` (FR-31, ADR-4). If the PRD's model already has an equivalent field, use it and drop the extra column.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: one additive migration `…_prd15_parent_portal` (FR-1, FR-2, NFR-8)\n\n| Model / enum | Key fields and constraints | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `enum AbsenceNoteStatus`, `AbsenceReason`, `ConsentResponseValue` | As specified in the PRD | FR-1 |\n| `AbsenceNote` | `studentId`, `submittedById`, `fromDate`/`toDate @db.Date`, `partialDay`, `periodIds String[]`, `reason`, `details`, `fileId?`, `status`, `reviewedById?`, `reviewNote?`, `reviewedAt?`. Index `(studentId, status, fromDate)` | FR-1, FR-18, FR-22 |\n| `ConferenceEvent` | `title`, `date @db.Date`, `bookingOpensAt`, `bookingClosesAt`, `slotMinutes` (5–60), eligible grade levels, `createdById` | FR-1, FR-28 |\n| `ConferenceSlot` | `eventId`, `teacherId`, `startsAt`, `endsAt`, `location?`, `bookedByParentId?`, `bookedForStudentId?`, `parentNote?` (≤ 500), **`blocked`**. Unique `(eventId, teacherId, startsAt)`, plus the partial unique index above | FR-1, FR-29 to FR-31 |\n| `ConsentForm` | `title`, `description` (Markdown), `dueAt`, `eventId?` FK to `CalendarEvent`, `createdById`, **`lastRemindedAt?`**, **`dueReminderSentAt?`** | FR-1, FR-36, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| `ConsentAudience` | `formId`, `type AudienceType` (GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION or COURSE, enforced in Zod), `refId` | FR-1, FR-36 |\n| `ConsentResponse` | `formId`, `studentId`, `respondedById`, `value`, `signature`, `comment?`. `@@unique([formId, studentId])` | FR-1, FR-38 |\n\nValidators live in `src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts`. Forms and handlers share the same Zod schemas, which enforce the FR-2 limits with `.superRefine`. They also enforce the −14/+60 day window (FR-18) and the rule that a reject requires a note (FR-22). (NFR-7)\n\n### 2.2 Server modules (NFR-6: `src/server/<feature>/`)\n\n| Module | Responsibilities | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/parent/selected-child.ts` | `getSelectedChild(user, searchParams?)`, wrapped in React `cache()`. It resolves in this order: a linked `?studentId=`, then a linked `sh_child` cookie, then the first linked child (`listLinksForParent`). `setSelectedChildCookie(studentId)` validates the link before it writes the cookie (`httpOnly`, `sameSite=lax`, 1 year). | FR-3 to FR-6 |\n| `src/server/parent/overview-service.ts` | One function per card: `getToday`, `getAttendanceSummary`, `getAssignmentsSummary`, `getRecentGrades`, `listUnreadAnnouncements` (returns `[]`), `getUpcomingEvents` (next 5, `CalendarEvent` plus booked meetings), `getTeachers`, `getActionItems` (pending consent plus open conferences). `getChildrenSummary(parent)` builds the `/my-children` cards. Every function reuses the existing timetable, attendance, assignments and gradebook services. | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-coverage.ts` | **Pure, no Prisma.** `coversRecord(note, { date, periodId })`. A whole-day note covers every period on each date in range. A partial note covers only its `periodIds`. A record with a null `periodId` (daily homeroom) is covered by any note for that date. | FR-23 to FR-25, FR-27, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-notes-service.ts` | `submit` (sets PENDING, then `notify('absence_note.submitted')` to the homeroom teacher and ADMINs), `list` (scoped by role, paginated), `getForReview` (joins existing `AttendanceRecord`s), `review` (see §3.2), `findCovering(studentIds, dateRange, statuses)` for attendance-service, `homeroomTeacherOf(studentId)`. | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (changed in place) | `getRegister`: pre-fill EXCUSED and set `noteId`/`excusable` for each student covered by an APPROVED note. `saveRegister:219`: allow EXCUSED for ADMIN, or when an APPROVED note covers the record. `~:299`: before `notifyStudentAndParents`, drop `attendance.absent` for students covered by a PENDING or APPROVED note. | FR-24, FR-25, FR-27 |\n| `src/server/conferences/conference-slots.ts` | **Pure.** `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` and `overlaps(a, b)`. | FR-29, FR-31, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/conferences/conferences-service.ts` | `createEvent`/`updateEvent` (ADMIN), which notifies eligible teachers with `conference.slots_requested`. `setAvailability` uses one transaction to delete the teacher's unbooked, unblocked slots and insert the newly generated ones. Booked and blocked slots are never touched. `setSlotBlocked`, `removeSlot` (unbooked only), `listBookable(event, child)`, `book` and `cancel` (§3.3), `teacherDay(event, teacher)`, `listMyMeetings(user, range)`, `slotIcs(slot, user)`. | FR-28 to FR-35 |\n| `src/server/consent-forms/consent-forms-service.ts` | `create`: checks `canTargetAudience` for each audience row, then notifies parents of the resolved audience students with `consent.requested`. Also `listForParent`, `respond` (§3.4), `tracking` (JSON or CSV through `src/server/csv.ts`), `remind` (24 h claim on `lastRemindedAt`, else 429), and `sendConsentDueReminders(now)` (claims `dueReminderSentAt`). | FR-36 to FR-40 |\n| `src/server/consent-forms/signature.ts` | **Pure.** `signatureMatches(typed, fullName)` compares both values after `trim().toLowerCase()`. | FR-37, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (extended) | `absence-note` resolver grants read access to any linked parent, the homeroom teacher and ADMIN. Uploads allow PDF, JPG and PNG, checked with `file-type`. | FR-18, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (extended) | `absence_note.submitted` (email false), `absence_note.reviewed` (true), `conference.slots_requested`, `conference.booked`, `conference.cancelled`, `consent.requested` (true), `consent.reminder` (true) | FR-19, FR-26, FR-28, FR-33, FR-36, FR-40, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch` (extended) | Adds an isolated try-block that calls `sendConsentDueReminders(now)`. | FR-40 |\n\n**Access helpers (NFR-5).** Every page and handler calls one of these:\n\n- `assertCanViewStudent`, for parent-to-child scoping\n- `assertHomeroomOrAdmin(user, studentId)`, in absence-notes-service, built on `Section.homeroomTeacherId` for the current-year `SectionMember`\n- `assertConsentOwnerOrAdmin(user, form)`\n- `requireRole`\n\nThe `sh_child` cookie is never read except through `getSelectedChild`.\n\n### 2.3 API layer (FR-43)\n\nRoute handlers are thin. They use `withHandler`, then Zod parse, then a service call, then `ok()`, all under `src/app/api/`. Every list endpoint supports `?page&pageSize≤100&sort&q` (NFR-10).\n\n| Area | Routes | Roles | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Child context | `POST /api/me/selected-child` | PARENT | FR-3, FR-4 |\n| Parent summaries | `GET /api/me/children/summary`, `GET /api/students/:id/overview` | PARENT (linked), staff via `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16 |\n| Absence notes | `GET/POST /api/absence-notes`, `GET /api/absence-notes/:id`, `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review` | PARENT (own children), TEACHER (homeroom), ADMIN | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26 |\n| Conferences | `GET/POST /api/conferences`, `GET/PATCH /api/conferences/:id`, `PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability`, `GET /api/conferences/:id/slots`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/conference-slots/:id`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/cancel`, `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` | ADMIN (events), TEACHER (own availability), PARENT (book and cancel for the selected or linked child) | FR-28 to FR-34 |\n| Consent forms | `GET/POST /api/consent-forms`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/responses`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id/tracking[?format=csv]`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/remind` | ADMIN, TEACHER (managed courses), PARENT (respond) | FR-36 to FR-39 |\n\n`arch-api-contracts` will write the exact request and response schemas.\n\n### 2.4 UI layer (NFR-4: MUI v9 only, with an mui-mcp lookup per component)\n\n| Route / surface | Kind | Key components | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `shell.tsx` top bar: `ChildSwitcher` | client | `Select`/`Menu` + `UserAvatar`. With one child it shows a name only. Changing the child POSTs to the selected-child route, then calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-3, FR-6 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | config | Parent: My children, Absence notes, Conferences, Consent forms. Teacher: Absence notes (only if homeroom, via a `homeroom` flag passed like `safeguardingLead`) and Conferences. Admin: Conferences, Consent forms, Absence notes. | FR-42 |\n| `/dashboard` | server | If the role is PARENT, `redirect('/my-children')`. | FR-8 |\n| `/my-children` | server | With one child, `redirect` to the overview. Otherwise show summary `Card`s. | FR-7 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]` | server, streaming | 8 async cards, each in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` with a \"View all\" link | FR-9 to FR-17, NFR-2 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence/new` | client form | RHF + Zod, `DatePicker`, `RadioGroup` (whole day or periods), a `Checkbox` group from `Period`, `FileUpload` (`absence-note`) | FR-18 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence` (parent list) | server + `DataTable` | Status `Chip` | FR-20 |\n| `/attendance/absence-notes` | server + `DataTable` | Status and date filters. The detail `Dialog` shows the note, the document link, existing records, and Approve/Reject (reject requires a note). | FR-21, FR-22 |\n| Attendance register (existing) | changed | EXCUSED pre-fill + an \"Absence note\" `Chip` badge. The EXCUSED option is enabled per `excusable`. | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `/admin/conferences` (list, plus new/edit form) | server + client form | `DataTable`, `DatePicker`/`DateTimePicker`, `Autocomplete` (grade levels) | FR-28 |\n| `/conferences/[id]/availability` | client | Time-range rows, location `TextField`, a slot list with remove and block `IconButton`s | FR-29 |\n| `/conferences/[id]` (parent) | client | One section per teacher of the child, with `Button`/`ToggleButton` slot buttons and an optional note `Dialog`. A 409 shows a toast and refetches. The parent's own booking has Cancel. | FR-30 to FR-32, NFR-1 |\n| `/conferences/[id]/day` (teacher) | server | `Table` of booked slots, with `@media print` through `sx` | FR-34 |\n| `/conferences` | server | Event list for each role | FR-42 |\n| `/consent-forms`, `/consent-forms/new`, `/consent-forms/[id]` | server + client form | `MarkdownEditor`/`MarkdownView`, an audience picker reusing the announcements audience UI pattern, an `Autocomplete` event link, a respond form (`RadioGroup` + signature `TextField` + comment) | FR-36 to FR-38 |\n| `/consent-forms/[id]/tracking` | server + `DataTable` | Status filter, CSV export link, \"Remind non-responders\" `Button` (409 or 429 produces a toast) | FR-39 |\n\nToasts go through `useToast()` and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`. Nothing is imported from the banned list.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Child selection (FR-3 to FR-6)\n\n```\nSwitcher change → POST /api/me/selected-child {studentId}\n  → assert ParentStudentLink → Set-Cookie sh_child (httpOnly) → router.refresh()\nAny parent page → getSelectedChild(user, searchParams)\n  → ?studentId (if linked) ▸ cookie (if linked) ▸ first linked child\n```\n\nThe cookie is untrusted. A stale or tampered value falls back to the first child and never errors.\n\n### 3.2 Absence note lifecycle (FR-18 to FR-27)\n\n```\nParent form ─(Zod)→ POST /api/absence-notes\n  → assertCanViewStudent → create PENDING (+fileId, context absence-note)\n  → notify(absence_note.submitted → homeroom teacher + ADMINs)\n\nReviewer → POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review {decision, note}\n  → assertHomeroomOrAdmin → $transaction:\n       updateMany AbsenceNote where {id, status: PENDING} (count 0 → 409)\n       if APPROVED: load sessions in [fromDate,toDate] for student's sections;\n                    for each covered (date, periodId) via coversRecord:\n                      existing ABSENT record → EXCUSED, note \"Absence note #<id>\"\n                      session exists, no record → create EXCUSED record\n  → after commit: audit({ request }) (IP, NFR-3); notify(absence_note.reviewed → linked parents, incl. reviewNote)\n\nRegister load (getRegister) → findCovering(APPROVED) → pre-fill EXCUSED + badge (future dates, FR-24)\nRegister save (saveRegister) → EXCUSED allowed if ADMIN or APPROVED note covers (FR-25)\n                             → absent notifications filtered by PENDING|APPROVED coverage (FR-27)\n```\n\nAttendance rates recalculate without new code, because `attendanceRate()` counts records when it reads them (FR-23). A rejected note changes no records.\n\n### 3.3 Conference booking (FR-28 to FR-33, NFR-1)\n\n```\nAdmin creates event → notify(conference.slots_requested → teachers of eligible grade levels)\nTeacher PUT availability {ranges, location} → generateSlots → $transaction(delete unbooked&unblocked, insert new)\nParent POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book {studentId, note?}\n  → assertCanViewStudent; now within [bookingOpensAt, bookingClosesAt] else 422\n  → $transaction:\n       overlap check vs parent's other booked slots at that time → 409 \"You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>\"\n       updateMany where {id, bookedByParentId: null, blocked: false} → count 0 → 409 \"That slot was just taken\"\n       P2002 on (eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) → 409 (one per teacher per child)\n  → notify(conference.booked → parent + teacher, link /api/conference-slots/:id/ics)\nCancel → before bookingClosesAt; clear booking fields → notify(conference.cancelled)\nReschedule = cancel + book (client-side, FR-32)\n```\n\n### 3.4 Consent forms (FR-36 to FR-40)\n\n```\nCreate → canTargetAudience per row → insert form+audiences → resolve audience students → linked parents\n       → notify(consent.requested)\nRespond POST …/responses {studentId, value, signature, comment?}\n  → assertCanViewStudent; now < dueAt else 422; signatureMatches(signature, parent full name) else 422\n  → upsert by (formId, studentId) → audit({ before, after, request })\nTracking → audience students × responses → Granted/Declined/No response; ?format=csv\nRemind → updateMany where {id, lastRemindedAt null|< now-24h} count 0 → 429 → notify(consent.reminder → non-responders)\nCron dispatch → forms with dueAt in (now, now+48h], dueReminderSentAt null → claim → notify(consent.reminder)\n```\n\n### 3.5 Overview rendering (FR-7 to FR-17, NFR-2)\n\nThe server page calls `assertCanViewStudent` once. The header and switcher paint first. The eight cards then stream independently, each doing one or two indexed `select` queries in `overview-service`. `GET /api/students/:id/overview` calls the same functions for API consumers. All \"today\", window and due-date evaluation uses `schoolToday(now, SchoolSettings.timezone)` (NFR-8).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Testing and seed data (FR-45, FR-46, NFR-7)\n\n- **Unit tests (Vitest):**\n  - `absence-coverage`: whole day, partial periods, multi-day, and a null `periodId`\n  - `conference-slots`: generation at range boundaries, `slotMinutes` 5 and 60, and overlap\n  - `signature`: case and whitespace\n- **Integration tests (Vitest + DB):**\n  - Approval converts ABSENT to EXCUSED and leaves PRESENT untouched.\n  - Future-register pre-fill.\n  - Two concurrent `book` calls run through `Promise.all`: exactly one succeeds and the other gets 409.\n  - `attendance.absent` is suppressed while a PENDING note covers the student.\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Absence note, then approve, then the register shows EXCUSED.\n  - Book a conference slot.\n  - Sign a consent form.\n- **Seed:** extend `prisma/seed.ts` in place:\n  - Grade 7: one PENDING and one APPROVED absence note.\n  - \"Autumn conferences\" 3 weeks out, with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 at 10 minutes each, two of them booked.\n  - \"Science Museum Trip\" consent form due in 10 days, linked to a seeded `CalendarEvent`, with about 40% of responses in.\n- **Gates:** `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test`. Use `logger`, never `console.log`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 migration `…_prd15_parent_portal`, 3 enums and 6 models, 3 flagged extra columns |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 Zod validators `src/lib/validators/*` with `.superRefine` |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `selected-child.ts`; §2.4 `ChildSwitcher`; `POST /api/me/selected-child` |\n| FR-4 | §3.1 `getSelectedChild` link validation and fallback |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `getSelectedChild` used by `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable` and new pages (calendar filter partial, ADR-11) |\n| FR-6 | §2.4 `ChildSwitcher` single-child mode |\n| FR-7 | §2.4 `/my-children`; `getChildrenSummary`; `GET /api/me/children/summary` |\n| FR-8 | §2.4 `/dashboard` redirects PARENT to `/my-children` |\n| FR-9 | `overview-service.getToday` (timetable + SchoolDay holidays) |\n| FR-10 | `overview-service.getAttendanceSummary` + link to the absence form |\n| FR-11 | `overview-service.getAssignmentsSummary` |\n| FR-12 | `overview-service.getRecentGrades` (visibility rules respected) |\n| FR-13 | `listUnreadAnnouncements` returns `[]` and the card shows an `EmptyState` (**partial**, PRD-12 absent) |\n| FR-14 | `overview-service.getUpcomingEvents` (`CalendarEvent` via `audienceWhereForUser` + recurrence) |\n| FR-15 | `overview-service.getTeachers` + Message link (PRD-13 compose) |\n| FR-16 | `overview-service.getActionItems` |\n| FR-17 | §3.5 Suspense per card + \"View all\" links |\n| FR-18 | §2.4 absence form; `absence-notes-service.submit`; `absence-note` file context |\n| FR-19 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.submitted)` to homeroom teacher + ADMINs |\n| FR-20 | §2.4 parent absence list; `GET /api/absence-notes` |\n| FR-21 | §2.4 `/attendance/absence-notes`; `getForReview`; `assertHomeroomOrAdmin` |\n| FR-22 | §3.2 `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review`, PENDING-only conditional update |\n| FR-23 | §3.2 approval transaction + `coversRecord` + `audit` |\n| FR-24 | §2.2 `getRegister` pre-fill + badge |\n| FR-25 | §2.2 `saveRegister:219` EXCUSED rule |\n| FR-26 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.reviewed)` with reviewNote |\n| FR-27 | §2.2 attendance-service notification filter (~:299) |\n| FR-28 | §2.4 `/admin/conferences`; `createEvent`/`updateEvent`; `conference.slots_requested` |\n| FR-29 | §2.4 availability page; `setAvailability`, `generateSlots`, `blocked` column |\n| FR-30 | §3.3 conditional `updateMany` booking; `/conferences/[id]` |\n| FR-31 | §3.3 overlap check + partial unique index |\n| FR-32 | §3.3 booking-window guard; cancel; reschedule = cancel + book |\n| FR-33 | §3.3 `conference.booked`/`cancelled` + `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` (`ical.ts`) |\n| FR-34 | §2.4 `/conferences/[id]/day`, print CSS |\n| FR-35 | `listMyMeetings`, shown as \"My meetings\" in overview Upcoming events and Action items (**partial**, no PRD-14 calendar page) |\n| FR-36 | §3.4 create + `canTargetAudience` + `consent.requested`; `/consent-forms/new` |\n| FR-37 | §3.4 respond + `signatureMatches`; overview Action items; `/consent-forms` |\n| FR-38 | `ConsentResponse @@unique(formId, studentId)` upsert + `audit` |\n| FR-39 | §3.4 tracking/CSV; remind with a `lastRemindedAt` 24 h claim |\n| FR-40 | §3.4 `sendConsentDueReminders` in the dispatch cron; `dueReminderSentAt` |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 `absence-note` resolver in `files/contexts.ts` |\n| FR-42 | §2.4 `src/config/navigation.ts` entries + homeroom flag |\n| FR-43 | §2.3 route table, `withHandler`/`requireRole`, standard shapes |\n| FR-44 | §2.2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` additions incl. `consent.reminder` |\n| FR-45 | §4 seed extensions |\n| FR-46 | §4 unit, integration and Playwright tests |\n| NFR-1 | §3.3 conditional update → 409 \"That slot was just taken\" + client refetch |\n| NFR-2 | §3.5 streaming cards, indexed `select` queries |\n| NFR-3 | `audit({ request })` on review, consent respond/change, conference admin edits |\n| NFR-4 | §2.4 MUI-only component map, with an mui-mcp lookup required per component |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 access helpers on every page and handler; cookie only via `getSelectedChild` |\n| NFR-6 | §2.2 new `src/server/<feature>/` modules; existing files extended in place |\n| NFR-7 | §2.1 shared Zod validators; §4 gates; `logger` |\n| NFR-8 | `@db.Date` fields; `schoolToday` + `SchoolSettings.timezone` for all date rules |\n| NFR-9 | No Announcement or calendar subsystem built; FR-13, FR-35 and FR-5 calendar part degrade (ADR-11) |\n| NFR-10 | §2.3 list endpoints use standard pagination, sort and `q` |\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TFouAbRyaNUFyWffQRAfUf","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eeb429-6a70-48e8-a0ff-b55a8b190b9d","uuid":"4de2934b-1fba-49bf-acc7-1557c98a9c13","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:18:29.340Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/system-design.md","content":"# System Design: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking, Consent Forms)\n\nTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-10), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-13), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n\n> This file replaces the SH-14 version. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` and `threat-model-notes.json` are still from SH-14 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSH-15 adds a parent portal to the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 brownfield app. It has five parts:\n\n1. **Child context:** the `sh_child` cookie, a top-bar switcher, and a default student on parent pages (FR-3 to FR-6).\n2. **Child overview:** `/my-children` and `/my-children/[studentId]`, built from eight streaming cards (FR-7 to FR-17).\n3. **Absence notes:** parents submit notes, teachers and admins review them, and approved notes connect to attendance (FR-18 to FR-27, FR-41).\n4. **Parent–teacher conferences:** admins create events, teachers set availability, and parents book slots atomically (FR-28 to FR-35).\n5. **Consent forms:** staff create forms, parents respond with a typed signature, and creators track responses and send reminders (FR-36 to FR-40).\n\nAll five use the existing building blocks:\n\n- `withHandler`, `requireRole` and `ok`/`AppError` from `src/server/http.ts`\n- `assertCanViewStudent` and `getAccessibleStudentIds` from `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`\n- `audit()` and `notify()` / `notifyStudentAndParents()`\n- The file contexts registry\n- The audience helpers in `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`\n- `attendance-rules.ts` (`schoolToday`, `attendanceRate`)\n- `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`\n- The cron route `/api/internal/email/dispatch`\n\nThe design adds **no new dependencies** (ADR-1) and moves or renames nothing (NFR-6).\n\n### Blockers and warnings from intake\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. Its warnings and the seven unresolved questions are settled as follows. Each is an assumption, not a blocker.\n\n| Intake warning / question | Design decision | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| PRD-12 Announcement model absent | The Announcements card renders an `EmptyState`. `listUnreadAnnouncements()` returns `[]`. **FR-13 is partial.** | FR-13 |\n| SH-14 calendar has no API or pages | Upcoming events queries `CalendarEvent` directly through `audienceWhereForUser`. \"My meetings\" appear as overview items. There is no calendar `studentId` filter, because no calendar page exists. **FR-14 is complete. FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 are partial.** | FR-5, FR-14, FR-35 |\n| Shared components live under `src/components/<Name>/` | Reuse them in place. | NFR-6 |\n| Student detail route is `/students/[id]` | \"View all\" links point to `/students/[id]` tabs, `/assignments?studentId=` and `/grades?studentId=`. | FR-17 |\n| Which pages adopt `sh_child` | `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable`, and all new SH-15 parent pages. | FR-5 |\n| Reminder notification key | One key, `consent.reminder`, for both the manual and the 48 h reminder. | FR-44 |\n| `attendance-service.ts:219` allows EXCUSED for ADMIN only | Replace the check: ADMIN, or an APPROVED note covers the record. | FR-25 |\n| Blocked slots | Add a `ConferenceSlot.blocked` column. | FR-29 |\n\n### Deviations from \"exactly as specified\" (FR-1)\n\nThe design adds three columns that the PRD does not list (ADR-3):\n\n| Column | Reqs | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ConferenceSlot.blocked Boolean @default(false)` | FR-29 | A blocked slot survives availability regeneration. |\n| `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` | FR-39 | 24 h throttle that holds across processes. |\n| `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt DateTime?` | FR-40 | Makes the 48 h reminder idempotent. |\n\nThe migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on `ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) WHERE bookedForStudentId IS NOT NULL` (FR-31, ADR-4). If the PRD's model already has an equivalent field, use it and drop the extra column.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Data layer: one additive migration `…_prd15_parent_portal` (FR-1, FR-2, NFR-8)\n\n| Model / enum | Key fields and constraints | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `enum AbsenceNoteStatus`, `AbsenceReason`, `ConsentResponseValue` | As specified in the PRD | FR-1 |\n| `AbsenceNote` | `studentId`, `submittedById`, `fromDate`/`toDate @db.Date`, `partialDay`, `periodIds String[]`, `reason`, `details`, `fileId?`, `status`, `reviewedById?`, `reviewNote?`, `reviewedAt?`. Index `(studentId, status, fromDate)` | FR-1, FR-18, FR-22 |\n| `ConferenceEvent` | `title`, `date @db.Date`, `bookingOpensAt`, `bookingClosesAt`, `slotMinutes` (5–60), eligible grade levels, `createdById` | FR-1, FR-28 |\n| `ConferenceSlot` | `eventId`, `teacherId`, `startsAt`, `endsAt`, `location?`, `bookedByParentId?`, `bookedForStudentId?`, `parentNote?` (≤ 500), **`blocked`**. Unique `(eventId, teacherId, startsAt)`, plus the partial unique index above | FR-1, FR-29 to FR-31 |\n| `ConsentForm` | `title`, `description` (Markdown), `dueAt`, `eventId?` FK to `CalendarEvent`, `createdById`, **`lastRemindedAt?`**, **`dueReminderSentAt?`** | FR-1, FR-36, FR-39, FR-40 |\n| `ConsentAudience` | `formId`, `type AudienceType` (GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION or COURSE, enforced in Zod), `refId` | FR-1, FR-36 |\n| `ConsentResponse` | `formId`, `studentId`, `respondedById`, `value`, `signature`, `comment?`. `@@unique([formId, studentId])` | FR-1, FR-38 |\n\nValidators live in `src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts`. Forms and handlers share the same Zod schemas, which enforce the FR-2 limits with `.superRefine`. They also enforce the −14/+60 day window (FR-18) and the rule that a reject requires a note (FR-22). (NFR-7)\n\n### 2.2 Server modules (NFR-6: `src/server/<feature>/`)\n\n| Module | Responsibilities | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/parent/selected-child.ts` | `getSelectedChild(user, searchParams?)`, wrapped in React `cache()`. It resolves in this order: a linked `?studentId=`, then a linked `sh_child` cookie, then the first linked child (`listLinksForParent`). `setSelectedChildCookie(studentId)` validates the link before it writes the cookie (`httpOnly`, `sameSite=lax`, 1 year). | FR-3 to FR-6 |\n| `src/server/parent/overview-service.ts` | One function per card: `getToday`, `getAttendanceSummary`, `getAssignmentsSummary`, `getRecentGrades`, `listUnreadAnnouncements` (returns `[]`), `getUpcomingEvents` (next 5, `CalendarEvent` plus booked meetings), `getTeachers`, `getActionItems` (pending consent plus open conferences). `getChildrenSummary(parent)` builds the `/my-children` cards. Every function reuses the existing timetable, attendance, assignments and gradebook services. | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16, FR-35 |\n| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-coverage.ts` | **Pure, no Prisma.** `coversRecord(note, { date, periodId })`. A whole-day note covers every period on each date in range. A partial note covers only its `periodIds`. A record with a null `periodId` (daily homeroom) is covered by any note for that date. | FR-23 to FR-25, FR-27, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-notes-service.ts` | `submit` (sets PENDING, then `notify('absence_note.submitted')` to the homeroom teacher and ADMINs), `list` (scoped by role, paginated), `getForReview` (joins existing `AttendanceRecord`s), `review` (see §3.2), `findCovering(studentIds, dateRange, statuses)` for attendance-service, `homeroomTeacherOf(studentId)`. | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (changed in place) | `getRegister`: pre-fill EXCUSED and set `noteId`/`excusable` for each student covered by an APPROVED note. `saveRegister:219`: allow EXCUSED for ADMIN, or when an APPROVED note covers the record. `~:299`: before `notifyStudentAndParents`, drop `attendance.absent` for students covered by a PENDING or APPROVED note. | FR-24, FR-25, FR-27 |\n| `src/server/conferences/conference-slots.ts` | **Pure.** `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` and `overlaps(a, b)`. | FR-29, FR-31, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/conferences/conferences-service.ts` | `createEvent`/`updateEvent` (ADMIN), which notifies eligible teachers with `conference.slots_requested`. `setAvailability` uses one transaction to delete the teacher's unbooked, unblocked slots and insert the newly generated ones. Booked and blocked slots are never touched. `setSlotBlocked`, `removeSlot` (unbooked only), `listBookable(event, child)`, `book` and `cancel` (§3.3), `teacherDay(event, teacher)`, `listMyMeetings(user, range)`, `slotIcs(slot, user)`. | FR-28 to FR-35 |\n| `src/server/consent-forms/consent-forms-service.ts` | `create`: checks `canTargetAudience` for each audience row, then notifies parents of the resolved audience students with `consent.requested`. Also `listForParent`, `respond` (§3.4), `tracking` (JSON or CSV through `src/server/csv.ts`), `remind` (24 h claim on `lastRemindedAt`, else 429), and `sendConsentDueReminders(now)` (claims `dueReminderSentAt`). | FR-36 to FR-40 |\n| `src/server/consent-forms/signature.ts` | **Pure.** `signatureMatches(typed, fullName)` compares both values after `trim().toLowerCase()`. | FR-37, FR-46 |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (extended) | `absence-note` resolver grants read access to any linked parent, the homeroom teacher and ADMIN. Uploads allow PDF, JPG and PNG, checked with `file-type`. | FR-18, FR-41 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (extended) | `absence_note.submitted` (email false), `absence_note.reviewed` (true), `conference.slots_requested`, `conference.booked`, `conference.cancelled`, `consent.requested` (true), `consent.reminder` (true) | FR-19, FR-26, FR-28, FR-33, FR-36, FR-40, FR-44 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch` (extended) | Adds an isolated try-block that calls `sendConsentDueReminders(now)`. | FR-40 |\n\n**Access helpers (NFR-5).** Every page and handler calls one of these:\n\n- `assertCanViewStudent`, for parent-to-child scoping\n- `assertHomeroomOrAdmin(user, studentId)`, in absence-notes-service, built on `Section.homeroomTeacherId` for the current-year `SectionMember`\n- `assertConsentOwnerOrAdmin(user, form)`\n- `requireRole`\n\nThe `sh_child` cookie is never read except through `getSelectedChild`.\n\n### 2.3 API layer (FR-43)\n\nRoute handlers are thin. They use `withHandler`, then Zod parse, then a service call, then `ok()`, all under `src/app/api/`. Every list endpoint supports `?page&pageSize≤100&sort&q` (NFR-10).\n\n| Area | Routes | Roles | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Child context | `POST /api/me/selected-child` | PARENT | FR-3, FR-4 |\n| Parent summaries | `GET /api/me/children/summary`, `GET /api/students/:id/overview` | PARENT (linked), staff via `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16 |\n| Absence notes | `GET/POST /api/absence-notes`, `GET /api/absence-notes/:id`, `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review` | PARENT (own children), TEACHER (homeroom), ADMIN | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26 |\n| Conferences | `GET/POST /api/conferences`, `GET/PATCH /api/conferences/:id`, `PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability`, `GET /api/conferences/:id/slots`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/conference-slots/:id`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/cancel`, `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` | ADMIN (events), TEACHER (own availability), PARENT (book and cancel for the selected or linked child) | FR-28 to FR-34 |\n| Consent forms | `GET/POST /api/consent-forms`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/responses`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id/tracking[?format=csv]`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/remind` | ADMIN, TEACHER (managed courses), PARENT (respond) | FR-36 to FR-39 |\n\n`arch-api-contracts` will write the exact request and response schemas.\n\n### 2.4 UI layer (NFR-4: MUI v9 only, with an mui-mcp lookup per component)\n\n| Route / surface | Kind | Key components | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `shell.tsx` top bar: `ChildSwitcher` | client | `Select`/`Menu` + `UserAvatar`. With one child it shows a name only. Changing the child POSTs to the selected-child route, then calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-3, FR-6 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | config | Parent: My children, Absence notes, Conferences, Consent forms. Teacher: Absence notes (only if homeroom, via a `homeroom` flag passed like `safeguardingLead`) and Conferences. Admin: Conferences, Consent forms, Absence notes. | FR-42 |\n| `/dashboard` | server | If the role is PARENT, `redirect('/my-children')`. | FR-8 |\n| `/my-children` | server | With one child, `redirect` to the overview. Otherwise show summary `Card`s. | FR-7 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]` | server, streaming | 8 async cards, each in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` with a \"View all\" link | FR-9 to FR-17, NFR-2 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence/new` | client form | RHF + Zod, `DatePicker`, `RadioGroup` (whole day or periods), a `Checkbox` group from `Period`, `FileUpload` (`absence-note`) | FR-18 |\n| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence` (parent list) | server + `DataTable` | Status `Chip` | FR-20 |\n| `/attendance/absence-notes` | server + `DataTable` | Status and date filters. The detail `Dialog` shows the note, the document link, existing records, and Approve/Reject (reject requires a note). | FR-21, FR-22 |\n| Attendance register (existing) | changed | EXCUSED pre-fill + an \"Absence note\" `Chip` badge. The EXCUSED option is enabled per `excusable`. | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `/admin/conferences` (list, plus new/edit form) | server + client form | `DataTable`, `DatePicker`/`DateTimePicker`, `Autocomplete` (grade levels) | FR-28 |\n| `/conferences/[id]/availability` | client | Time-range rows, location `TextField`, a slot list with remove and block `IconButton`s | FR-29 |\n| `/conferences/[id]` (parent) | client | One section per teacher of the child, with `Button`/`ToggleButton` slot buttons and an optional note `Dialog`. A 409 shows a toast and refetches. The parent's own booking has Cancel. | FR-30 to FR-32, NFR-1 |\n| `/conferences/[id]/day` (teacher) | server | `Table` of booked slots, with `@media print` through `sx` | FR-34 |\n| `/conferences` | server | Event list for each role | FR-42 |\n| `/consent-forms`, `/consent-forms/new`, `/consent-forms/[id]` | server + client form | `MarkdownEditor`/`MarkdownView`, an audience picker reusing the announcements audience UI pattern, an `Autocomplete` event link, a respond form (`RadioGroup` + signature `TextField` + comment) | FR-36 to FR-38 |\n| `/consent-forms/[id]/tracking` | server + `DataTable` | Status filter, CSV export link, \"Remind non-responders\" `Button` (409 or 429 produces a toast) | FR-39 |\n\nToasts go through `useToast()` and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`. Nothing is imported from the banned list.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Child selection (FR-3 to FR-6)\n\n```\nSwitcher change → POST /api/me/selected-child {studentId}\n  → assert ParentStudentLink → Set-Cookie sh_child (httpOnly) → router.refresh()\nAny parent page → getSelectedChild(user, searchParams)\n  → ?studentId (if linked) ▸ cookie (if linked) ▸ first linked child\n```\n\nThe cookie is untrusted. A stale or tampered value falls back to the first child and never errors.\n\n### 3.2 Absence note lifecycle (FR-18 to FR-27)\n\n```\nParent form ─(Zod)→ POST /api/absence-notes\n  → assertCanViewStudent → create PENDING (+fileId, context absence-note)\n  → notify(absence_note.submitted → homeroom teacher + ADMINs)\n\nReviewer → POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review {decision, note}\n  → assertHomeroomOrAdmin → $transaction:\n       updateMany AbsenceNote where {id, status: PENDING} (count 0 → 409)\n       if APPROVED: load sessions in [fromDate,toDate] for student's sections;\n                    for each covered (date, periodId) via coversRecord:\n                      existing ABSENT record → EXCUSED, note \"Absence note #<id>\"\n                      session exists, no record → create EXCUSED record\n  → after commit: audit({ request }) (IP, NFR-3); notify(absence_note.reviewed → linked parents, incl. reviewNote)\n\nRegister load (getRegister) → findCovering(APPROVED) → pre-fill EXCUSED + badge (future dates, FR-24)\nRegister save (saveRegister) → EXCUSED allowed if ADMIN or APPROVED note covers (FR-25)\n                             → absent notifications filtered by PENDING|APPROVED coverage (FR-27)\n```\n\nAttendance rates recalculate without new code, because `attendanceRate()` counts records when it reads them (FR-23). A rejected note changes no records.\n\n### 3.3 Conference booking (FR-28 to FR-33, NFR-1)\n\n```\nAdmin creates event → notify(conference.slots_requested → teachers of eligible grade levels)\nTeacher PUT availability {ranges, location} → generateSlots → $transaction(delete unbooked&unblocked, insert new)\nParent POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book {studentId, note?}\n  → assertCanViewStudent; now within [bookingOpensAt, bookingClosesAt] else 422\n  → $transaction:\n       overlap check vs parent's other booked slots at that time → 409 \"You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>\"\n       updateMany where {id, bookedByParentId: null, blocked: false} → count 0 → 409 \"That slot was just taken\"\n       P2002 on (eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) → 409 (one per teacher per child)\n  → notify(conference.booked → parent + teacher, link /api/conference-slots/:id/ics)\nCancel → before bookingClosesAt; clear booking fields → notify(conference.cancelled)\nReschedule = cancel + book (client-side, FR-32)\n```\n\n### 3.4 Consent forms (FR-36 to FR-40)\n\n```\nCreate → canTargetAudience per row → insert form+audiences → resolve audience students → linked parents\n       → notify(consent.requested)\nRespond POST …/responses {studentId, value, signature, comment?}\n  → assertCanViewStudent; now < dueAt else 422; signatureMatches(signature, parent full name) else 422\n  → upsert by (formId, studentId) → audit({ before, after, request })\nTracking → audience students × responses → Granted/Declined/No response; ?format=csv\nRemind → updateMany where {id, lastRemindedAt null|< now-24h} count 0 → 429 → notify(consent.reminder → non-responders)\nCron dispatch → forms with dueAt in (now, now+48h], dueReminderSentAt null → claim → notify(consent.reminder)\n```\n\n### 3.5 Overview rendering (FR-7 to FR-17, NFR-2)\n\nThe server page calls `assertCanViewStudent` once. The header and switcher paint first. The eight cards then stream independently, each doing one or two indexed `select` queries in `overview-service`. `GET /api/students/:id/overview` calls the same functions for API consumers. All \"today\", window and due-date evaluation uses `schoolToday(now, SchoolSettings.timezone)` (NFR-8).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Testing and seed data (FR-45, FR-46, NFR-7)\n\n- **Unit tests (Vitest):**\n  - `absence-coverage`: whole day, partial periods, multi-day, and a null `periodId`\n  - `conference-slots`: generation at range boundaries, `slotMinutes` 5 and 60, and overlap\n  - `signature`: case and whitespace\n- **Integration tests (Vitest + DB):**\n  - Approval converts ABSENT to EXCUSED and leaves PRESENT untouched.\n  - Future-register pre-fill.\n  - Two concurrent `book` calls run through `Promise.all`: exactly one succeeds and the other gets 409.\n  - `attendance.absent` is suppressed while a PENDING note covers the student.\n- **Playwright:**\n  - Absence note, then approve, then the register shows EXCUSED.\n  - Book a conference slot.\n  - Sign a consent form.\n- **Seed:** extend `prisma/seed.ts` in place:\n  - Grade 7: one PENDING and one APPROVED absence note.\n  - \"Autumn conferences\" 3 weeks out, with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 at 10 minutes each, two of them booked.\n  - \"Science Museum Trip\" consent form due in 10 days, linked to a seeded `CalendarEvent`, with about 40% of responses in.\n- **Gates:** `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test`. Use `logger`, never `console.log`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 migration `…_prd15_parent_portal`, 3 enums and 6 models, 3 flagged extra columns |\n| FR-2 | §2.1 Zod validators `src/lib/validators/*` with `.superRefine` |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `selected-child.ts`; §2.4 `ChildSwitcher`; `POST /api/me/selected-child` |\n| FR-4 | §3.1 `getSelectedChild` link validation and fallback |\n| FR-5 | §2.2 `getSelectedChild` used by `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable` and new pages (calendar filter partial, ADR-11) |\n| FR-6 | §2.4 `ChildSwitcher` single-child mode |\n| FR-7 | §2.4 `/my-children`; `getChildrenSummary`; `GET /api/me/children/summary` |\n| FR-8 | §2.4 `/dashboard` redirects PARENT to `/my-children` |\n| FR-9 | `overview-service.getToday` (timetable + SchoolDay holidays) |\n| FR-10 | `overview-service.getAttendanceSummary` + link to the absence form |\n| FR-11 | `overview-service.getAssignmentsSummary` |\n| FR-12 | `overview-service.getRecentGrades` (visibility rules respected) |\n| FR-13 | `listUnreadAnnouncements` returns `[]` and the card shows an `EmptyState` (**partial**, PRD-12 absent) |\n| FR-14 | `overview-service.getUpcomingEvents` (`CalendarEvent` via `audienceWhereForUser` + recurrence) |\n| FR-15 | `overview-service.getTeachers` + Message link (PRD-13 compose) |\n| FR-16 | `overview-service.getActionItems` |\n| FR-17 | §3.5 Suspense per card + \"View all\" links |\n| FR-18 | §2.4 absence form; `absence-notes-service.submit`; `absence-note` file context |\n| FR-19 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.submitted)` to homeroom teacher + ADMINs |\n| FR-20 | §2.4 parent absence list; `GET /api/absence-notes` |\n| FR-21 | §2.4 `/attendance/absence-notes`; `getForReview`; `assertHomeroomOrAdmin` |\n| FR-22 | §3.2 `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review`, PENDING-only conditional update |\n| FR-23 | §3.2 approval transaction + `coversRecord` + `audit` |\n| FR-24 | §2.2 `getRegister` pre-fill + badge |\n| FR-25 | §2.2 `saveRegister:219` EXCUSED rule |\n| FR-26 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.reviewed)` with reviewNote |\n| FR-27 | §2.2 attendance-service notification filter (~:299) |\n| FR-28 | §2.4 `/admin/conferences`; `createEvent`/`updateEvent`; `conference.slots_requested` |\n| FR-29 | §2.4 availability page; `setAvailability`, `generateSlots`, `blocked` column |\n| FR-30 | §3.3 conditional `updateMany` booking; `/conferences/[id]` |\n| FR-31 | §3.3 overlap check + partial unique index |\n| FR-32 | §3.3 booking-window guard; cancel; reschedule = cancel + book |\n| FR-33 | §3.3 `conference.booked`/`cancelled` + `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` (`ical.ts`) |\n| FR-34 | §2.4 `/conferences/[id]/day`, print CSS |\n| FR-35 | `listMyMeetings`, shown as \"My meetings\" in overview Upcoming events and Action items (**partial**, no PRD-14 calendar page) |\n| FR-36 | §3.4 create + `canTargetAudience` + `consent.requested`; `/consent-forms/new` |\n| FR-37 | §3.4 respond + `signatureMatches`; overview Action items; `/consent-forms` |\n| FR-38 | `ConsentResponse @@unique(formId, studentId)` upsert + `audit` |\n| FR-39 | §3.4 tracking/CSV; remind with a `lastRemindedAt` 24 h claim |\n| FR-40 | §3.4 `sendConsentDueReminders` in the dispatch cron; `dueReminderSentAt` |\n| FR-41 | §2.2 `absence-note` resolver in `files/contexts.ts` |\n| FR-42 | §2.4 `src/config/navigation.ts` entries + homeroom flag |\n| FR-43 | §2.3 route table, `withHandler`/`requireRole`, standard shapes |\n| FR-44 | §2.2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` additions incl. `consent.reminder` |\n| FR-45 | §4 seed extensions |\n| FR-46 | §4 unit, integration and Playwright tests |\n| NFR-1 | §3.3 conditional update → 409 \"That slot was just taken\" + client refetch |\n| NFR-2 | §3.5 streaming cards, indexed `select` queries |\n| NFR-3 | `audit({ request })` on review, consent respond/change, conference admin edits |\n| NFR-4 | §2.4 MUI-only component map, with an mui-mcp lookup required per component |\n| NFR-5 | §2.2 access helpers on every page and handler; cookie only via `getSelectedChild` |\n| NFR-6 | §2.2 new `src/server/<feature>/` modules; existing files extended in place |\n| NFR-7 | §2.1 shared Zod validators; §4 gates; `logger` |\n| NFR-8 | `@db.Date` fields; `schoolToday` + `SchoolSettings.timezone` for all date rules |\n| NFR-9 | No Announcement or calendar subsystem built; FR-13, FR-35 and FR-5 calendar part degrade (ADR-11) |\n| NFR-10 | §2.3 list endpoints use standard pagination, sort and `q` |\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":433,"newStart":1,"newLines":297,"lines":["-# System Design: PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays","+# System Design: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking, Consent Forms)"," ","-Ticket: SH-14 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T23:58:00Z · Status: complete","+Ticket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete"," ","-Inputs:","-- `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`: 37 FR and 12 NFR, 96% confidence","-- `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`","-- `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md`: ADR-1 to ADR-13","-- `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`: B1 to B19, D1 to D9, R1 to R4","+Inputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-10), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-13), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`."," ","-> This replaces the stale SH-13 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still SH-13 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.","+> This file replaces the SH-14 version. `api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` and `threat-model-notes.json` are still from SH-14 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them."," "," ---"," "," ## 1. Overview"," ","-SH-14 adds a school calendar to the existing SchoolHub app (Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma/PostgreSQL, MUI 9). The pieces are:","+SH-15 adds a parent portal to the existing Next.js 14 / Prisma / MUI v9 brownfield app. It has five parts:"," ","-- one Prisma migration","-- one server module, `src/server/calendar/`","-- a shared audience resolver, at the path PRD-12 will use","-- about a dozen thin route handlers","-- two new pages (`/calendar`, `/account/calendar`), plus one small admin page","-- small, targeted edits to timetable, attendance, the assignment and quiz editors, notifications, the cron, navigation and the seed","+1. **Child context:** the `sh_child` cookie, a top-bar switcher, and a default student on parent pages (FR-3 to FR-6).","+2. **Child overview:** `/my-children` and `/my-children/[studentId]`, built from eight streaming cards (FR-7 to FR-17).","+3. **Absence notes:** parents submit notes, teachers and admins review them, and approved notes connect to attendance (FR-18 to FR-27, FR-41).","+4. **Parent–teacher conferences:** admins create events, teachers set availability, and parents book slots atomically (FR-28 to FR-35).","+5. **Consent forms:** staff create forms, parents respond with a typed signature, and creators track responses and send reminders (FR-36 to FR-40)."," ","-Design principles:","+All five use the existing building blocks:"," ","-1. **One read path.** A single function, `getCalendarItems(user, range, sources, studentId?)`, feeds the `/calendar` API, the iCal feed, `getUpcomingEventsForUser`, and (with `sources=['events']`) the single-event visibility check. That way the feed cannot show anything the app hides (NFR-5).","-2. **Recurrence is expanded on the server, at read time.** A recurring event is stored once. Clients and the scheduler only ever receive plain occurrences. The feed emits RRULE (ADR-2, ADR-3).","-3. **One holiday rule.** `isSchoolDay` in calendar-service owns the teaching-weekday rule and the no-school-event rule. Timetable, attendance, the editors and `/api/school-day` all call it (ADR-8).","-4. **Reuse before writing.** The design reuses `rateLimit`, `notify`, `audit`, `hashToken`, `csv.ts`, `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView/Editor`, `useToast`, the dispatch cron, `getSchoolTimezone` and the access helpers (NFR-9).","+- `withHandler`, `requireRole` and `ok`/`AppError` from `src/server/http.ts`","+- `assertCanViewStudent` and `getAccessibleStudentIds` from `src/server/auth/student-access.ts`","+- `audit()` and `notify()` / `notifyStudentAndParents()`","+- The file contexts registry","+- The audience helpers in `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`","+- `attendance-rules.ts` (`schoolToday`, `attendanceRate`)","+- `src/server/calendar/ical.ts`","+- The cron route `/api/internal/email/dispatch`"," ","-### Intake blockers and warnings","+The design adds **no new dependencies** (ADR-1) and moves or renames nothing (NFR-6)."," ","-`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **no blockers** (`blockers: []`). It raises three warnings, resolved as follows:","+### Blockers and warnings from intake"," ","-| Intake warning | Resolution | Ref |","+`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **`blockers: []`** at 95% confidence. Its warnings and the seven unresolved questions are settled as follows. Each is an assumption, not a blocker.","+","+| Intake warning / question | Design decision | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|","-| PRD-12 missing: no `AudienceType`, `audience.ts` or audience builder | SH-14 adds `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }` and `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`, exactly as PRD-12 §FR-1/FR-2 specify. It also adds a minimal MUI `AudienceBuilder`. PRD-12 adopts all three without changes. No Announcement models. | ADR-9, §3.3 |","-| `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page missing | Add a minimal ADMIN server page at that exact route with a read-only term list and an \"Add term breaks\" button. | ADR-10, §3.9 |","-| New dependencies | `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` (exact, installed first) with a scoped `@mui/x-internals` override. `node-ical@0.27.6` as an exact devDependency. Nothing else is added. | ADR-1, ADR-5 |","+| PRD-12 Announcement model absent | The Announcements card renders an `EmptyState`. `listUnreadAnnouncements()` returns `[]`. **FR-13 is partial.** | FR-13 |","+| SH-14 calendar has no API or pages | Upcoming events queries `CalendarEvent` directly through `audienceWhereForUser`. \"My meetings\" appear as overview items. There is no calendar `studentId` filter, because no calendar page exists. **FR-14 is complete. FR-35 and the calendar part of FR-5 are partial.** | FR-5, FR-14, FR-35 |","+| Shared components live under `src/components/<Name>/` | Reuse them in place. | NFR-6 |","+| Student detail route is `/students/[id]` | \"View all\" links point to `/students/[id]` tabs, `/assignments?studentId=` and `/grades?studentId=`. | FR-17 |","+| Which pages adopt `sh_child` | `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable`, and all new SH-15 parent pages. | FR-5 |","+| Reminder notification key | One key, `consent.reminder`, for both the manual and the 48 h reminder. | FR-44 |","+| `attendance-service.ts:219` allows EXCUSED for ADMIN only | Replace the check: ADMIN, or an APPROVED note covers the record. | FR-25 |","+| Blocked slots | Add a `ConferenceSlot.blocked` column. | FR-29 |"," ","-### Conflicts between the research inputs, and how this design settles them","+### Deviations from \"exactly as specified\" (FR-1)"," ","-| Topic | arch-research-stack | arch-research-reqs | **Decision** |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| Audience shape | PRD-12 enum (6 values) with `refId` and `include*` flags | 4-value enum with `targetId` and `roles[]` | **ADR-9.** PRD-14 FR-1 itself defines `EventAudience` with `refId` / `includeStudents` / `includeParents` / `includeTeachers` (verified in `14-calendar.md` L128-137), and PRD-12 L96 defines the 6 values. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with `includeStudents=false, includeTeachers=false`. No `roles[]` column. |","-| Resolver path | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` | `src/server/audience/audience.ts` | **`src/server/announcements/audience.ts`**, the path PRD-12 names, so PRD-12 doesn't need a rename. |","-| `getScheduleForDate` \"reason\" | Add `reason` to its return | Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`; callers fetch the reason separately | **Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`** (no churn for callers: attendance L130/L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Callers that need the holiday name call `isSchoolDay(date)` directly. FR-17's \"reason\" is delivered through `isSchoolDay` and `/api/school-day`. |","-| Email default per category (FR-28) | Not addressed | D5: a second type | **Two registry types:** `event.created` (`defaultEmail: false`) and `event.holiday_created` (`defaultEmail: true`, used for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK). Both keep the per-user preference override, and `notify.ts` is unchanged. This is a deliberate deviation (D-3 below). |","-| RSVP reminder \"once\" | `rsvpReminderSentAt` column | Same, claimed with conditional `updateMany` | Agreed: claim it with `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}})`. |","+The design adds three columns that the PRD does not list (ADR-3):"," ","-### Deviations from the PRD's model and route list (all deliberate)","+| Column | Reqs | Purpose |","+|---|---|---|","+| `ConferenceSlot.blocked Boolean @default(false)` | FR-29 | A blocked slot survives availability regeneration. |","+| `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt DateTime?` | FR-39 | 24 h throttle that holds across processes. |","+| `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt DateTime?` | FR-40 | Makes the 48 h reminder idempotent. |"," ","-| ID | Deviation | Why | Traces to |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| D-1 | `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?` | Stores \"once per event\" for the reminder. Claimed atomically. | FR-23 |","-| D-2 | `EventAudience @@index([eventId])` and `@@index([type, refId])` | Audience filtering in SQL on the hot path. | NFR-4 |","-| D-3 | Extra notification type `event.holiday_created` | Per-category email default, within the existing preference model. | FR-28 |","-| D-4 | Back-relations on `User` (`calendarEvents`, `eventRsvps`, `calendarFeedToken`) and `onDelete: Cascade` FKs on `EventRsvp.userId` / `CalendarFeedToken.userId` | Prisma requires the relations. Cascade matches the \"cascade deletes\" instruction in FR-2. | FR-2 |","-| D-5 | Agenda view: 30-day page with next/prev in Community `EventCalendar`, instead of true infinite scroll | Community has no infinite agenda. If QA rejects this, the fallback is MUI `List` + native `IntersectionObserver` below 768 px, fetching the next 30-day window. Rejection triggers the fallback; it is not built up front. | FR-9, ADR-2 |","-| D-6 | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `url` only when it creates the first token, otherwise `{url:null, hasToken:true, createdAt}`. The page offers \"Reset link\". | The raw token cannot be re-shown because it is stored hashed. | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-5 |","-| D-7 | Seed a minimal ELECTIVE `ROBOTICS` course (teacher Tom, current year) only if it doesn't exist | The Chess club audience needs it, and it is absent from the seed. | FR-37 |","-| D-8 | Register save on a no-school date requires `holidayOverride: true` in the body, enforced on the server | Makes FR-18's extra confirmation a real rule, not only a UI dialog. | FR-18, NFR-7 |","-| D-9 | `GET /api/public/events` is rate limited per IP (`rateLimit('pubcal:'+ip, 120, 3_600_000)`) and range-capped at 100 days | Only unauthenticated JSON route; reuses the existing limiter. | FR-30, NFR-7 |","+The migration also adds a raw-SQL partial unique index on `ConferenceSlot(eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) WHERE bookedForStudentId IS NOT NULL` (FR-31, ADR-4). If the PRD's model already has an equivalent field, use it and drop the extra column."," "," ---"," "," ## 2. Component Breakdown"," ","-### 2.1 Dependencies and config (do first)","+### 2.1 Data layer: one additive migration `…_prd15_parent_portal` (FR-1, FR-2, NFR-8)"," ","-| Change | Ref |","-|---|---|","-| `npm i --save-exact @mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15`. Nested override `\"@mui/x-scheduler\": {\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.17.0\"}`. Verify with `npm ls @mui/x-internals`. If npm doesn't honour the nested override, fall back to a global `9.17.0`. | FR-1, ADR-1 |","-| `import type {} from '@mui/x-scheduler/theme-augmentation'` beside the theme | FR-9, ADR-1 |","-| `npm i -D --save-exact node-ical@0.27.6` | NFR-6 |","-| Before writing scheduler code, the dev phase looks up the Quickstart, Views, Events, Editing, Timezone, Localization and Responsiveness pages via MUI MCP (`useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`). If MCP is unreachable, stop and report a blocker. | NFR-2 |","+| Model / enum | Key fields and constraints | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `enum AbsenceNoteStatus`, `AbsenceReason`, `ConsentResponseValue` | As specified in the PRD | FR-1 |","+| `AbsenceNote` | `studentId`, `submittedById`, `fromDate`/`toDate @db.Date`, `partialDay`, `periodIds String[]`, `reason`, `details`, `fileId?`, `status`, `reviewedById?`, `reviewNote?`, `reviewedAt?`. Index `(studentId, status, fromDate)` | FR-1, FR-18, FR-22 |","+| `ConferenceEvent` | `title`, `date @db.Date`, `bookingOpensAt`, `bookingClosesAt`, `slotMinutes` (5–60), eligible grade levels, `createdById` | FR-1, FR-28 |","+| `ConferenceSlot` | `eventId`, `teacherId`, `startsAt`, `endsAt`, `location?`, `bookedByParentId?`, `bookedForStudentId?`, `parentNote?` (≤ 500), **`blocked`**. Unique `(eventId, teacherId, startsAt)`, plus the partial unique index above | FR-1, FR-29 to FR-31 |","+| `ConsentForm` | `title`, `description` (Markdown), `dueAt`, `eventId?` FK to `CalendarEvent`, `createdById`, **`lastRemindedAt?`**, **`dueReminderSentAt?`** | FR-1, FR-36, FR-39, FR-40 |","+| `ConsentAudience` | `formId`, `type AudienceType` (GRADE_LEVEL, SECTION or COURSE, enforced in Zod), `refId` | FR-1, FR-36 |","+| `ConsentResponse` | `formId`, `studentId`, `respondedById`, `value`, `signature`, `comment?`. `@@unique([formId, studentId])` | FR-1, FR-38 |"," ","-### 2.2 Data model: migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`","+Validators live in `src/lib/validators/{absence-notes,conferences,consent-forms}.ts`. Forms and handlers share the same Zod schemas, which enforce the FR-2 limits with `.superRefine`. They also enforce the −14/+60 day window (FR-18) and the rule that a reject requires a note (FR-22). (NFR-7)"," ","-```prisma","-enum AudienceType  { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }   // PRD-12 values, owned here until PRD-12 lands","-enum EventCategory { HOLIDAY TERM_BREAK EXAM EVENT MEETING TRIP SPORTS DEADLINE OTHER }","-enum Recurrence    { NONE WEEKLY MONTHLY }","-enum RsvpResponse  { YES NO MAYBE }","+### 2.2 Server modules (NFR-6: `src/server/<feature>/`)"," ","-model CalendarEvent {","-  id                 String        @id @default(cuid())","-  title              String","-  description        String?","-  category           EventCategory","-  startAt            DateTime","-  endAt              DateTime","-  allDay             Boolean       @default(false)","-  location           String?","-  roomId             String?","-  recurrence         Recurrence    @default(NONE)","-  recurrenceUntil    DateTime?     @db.Date","-  isNoSchool         Boolean       @default(false)","-  rsvpEnabled        Boolean       @default(false)","-  rsvpDeadline       DateTime?","-  rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?                                  // D-1","-  isPublic           Boolean       @default(false)","-  createdById        String","-  createdBy          User          @relation(\"CalendarEventCreator\", fields: [createdById], references: [id])","-  createdAt          DateTime      @default(now())","-  updatedAt          DateTime      @updatedAt","-  audiences          EventAudience[]","-  rsvps              EventRsvp[]","-  @@index([startAt, endAt])","-}","+| Module | Responsibilities | Reqs |","+|---|---|---|","+| `src/server/parent/selected-child.ts` | `getSelectedChild(user, searchParams?)`, wrapped in React `cache()`. It resolves in this order: a linked `?studentId=`, then a linked `sh_child` cookie, then the first linked child (`listLinksForParent`). `setSelectedChildCookie(studentId)` validates the link before it writes the cookie (`httpOnly`, `sameSite=lax`, 1 year). | FR-3 to FR-6 |","+| `src/server/parent/overview-service.ts` | One function per card: `getToday`, `getAttendanceSummary`, `getAssignmentsSummary`, `getRecentGrades`, `listUnreadAnnouncements` (returns `[]`), `getUpcomingEvents` (next 5, `CalendarEvent` plus booked meetings), `getTeachers`, `getActionItems` (pending consent plus open conferences). `getChildrenSummary(parent)` builds the `/my-children` cards. Every function reuses the existing timetable, attendance, assignments and gradebook services. | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16, FR-35 |","+| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-coverage.ts` | **Pure, no Prisma.** `coversRecord(note, { date, periodId })`. A whole-day note covers every period on each date in range. A partial note covers only its `periodIds`. A record with a null `periodId` (daily homeroom) is covered by any note for that date. | FR-23 to FR-25, FR-27, FR-46 |","+| `src/server/absence-notes/absence-notes-service.ts` | `submit` (sets PENDING, then `notify('absence_note.submitted')` to the homeroom teacher and ADMINs), `list` (scoped by role, paginated), `getForReview` (joins existing `AttendanceRecord`s), `review` (see §3.2), `findCovering(studentIds, dateRange, statuses)` for attendance-service, `homeroomTeacherOf(studentId)`. | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26, FR-41 |","+| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` (changed in place) | `getRegister`: pre-fill EXCUSED and set `noteId`/`excusable` for each student covered by an APPROVED note. `saveRegister:219`: allow EXCUSED for ADMIN, or when an APPROVED note covers the record. `~:299`: before `notifyStudentAndParents`, drop `attendance.absent` for students covered by a PENDING or APPROVED note. | FR-24, FR-25, FR-27 |","+| `src/server/conferences/conference-slots.ts` | **Pure.** `generateSlots(ranges, slotMinutes)` and `overlaps(a, b)`. | FR-29, FR-31, FR-46 |","+| `src/server/conferences/conferences-service.ts` | `createEvent`/`updateEvent` (ADMIN), which notifies eligible teachers with `conference.slots_requested`. `setAvailability` uses one transaction to delete the teacher's unbooked, unblocked slots and insert the newly generated ones. Booked and blocked slots are never touched. `setSlotBlocked`, `removeSlot` (unbooked only), `listBookable(event, child)`, `book` and `cancel` (§3.3), `teacherDay(event, teacher)`, `listMyMeetings(user, range)`, `slotIcs(slot, user)`. | FR-28 to FR-35 |","+| `src/server/consent-forms/consent-forms-service.ts` | `create`: checks `canTargetAudience` for each audience row, then notifies parents of the resolved audience students with `consent.requested`. Also `listForParent`, `respond` (§3.4), `tracking` (JSON or CSV through `src/server/csv.ts`), `remind` (24 h claim on `lastRemindedAt`, else 429), and `sendConsentDueReminders(now)` (claims `dueReminderSentAt`). | FR-36 to FR-40 |","+| `src/server/consent-forms/signature.ts` | **Pure.** `signatureMatches(typed, fullName)` compares both values after `trim().toLowerCase()`. | FR-37, FR-46 |","+| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` (extended) | `absence-note` resolver grants read access to any linked parent, the homeroom teacher and ADMIN. Uploads allow PDF, JPG and PNG, checked with `file-type`. | FR-18, FR-41 |","+| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` (extended) | `absence_note.submitted` (email false), `absence_note.reviewed` (true), `conference.slots_requested`, `conference.booked`, `conference.cancelled`, `consent.requested` (true), `consent.reminder` (true) | FR-19, FR-26, FR-28, FR-33, FR-36, FR-40, FR-44 |","+| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch` (extended) | Adds an isolated try-block that calls `sendConsentDueReminders(now)`. | FR-40 |"," ","-model EventAudience {","-  id              String        @id @default(cuid())","-  eventId         String","-  event           CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  type            AudienceType","-  refId           String?       // gradeLevelId | sectionId | courseId | Role name (ROLE); null for SCHOOL/STAFF","-  includeStudents Boolean       @default(true)","-  includeParents  Boolean       @default(true)","-  includeTeachers Boolean       @default(true)","-  @@index([eventId])","-  @@index([type, refId])                                        // D-2","-}","+**Access helpers (NFR-5).** Every page and handler calls one of these:"," ","-model EventRsvp {","-  eventId   String","-  event     CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  userId    String","-  user      User          @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  response  RsvpResponse","-  guests    Int           @default(0)","-  note      String?","-  createdAt DateTime      @default(now())","-  updatedAt DateTime      @updatedAt","-  @@id([eventId, userId])","-}","+- `assertCanViewStudent`, for parent-to-child scoping","+- `assertHomeroomOrAdmin(user, studentId)`, in absence-notes-service, built on `Section.homeroomTeacherId` for the current-year `SectionMember`","+- `assertConsentOwnerOrAdmin(user, form)`","+- `requireRole`"," ","-model CalendarFeedToken {","-  userId    String   @id","-  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)","-  tokenHash String   @unique","-  createdAt DateTime @default(now())","-}","-```","+The `sh_child` cookie is never read except through `getSelectedChild`."," ","-Exact field lists for `EventRsvp` follow PRD §FR-1. The dev agent copies any field this sketch omits from `14-calendar.md` L139-148. Traces to FR-2, FR-3, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-8.","+### 2.3 API layer (FR-43)"," ","-### 2.3 Server modules","+Route handlers are thin. They use `withHandler`, then Zod parse, then a service call, then `ok()`, all under `src/app/api/`. Every list endpoint supports `?page&pageSize≤100&sort&q` (NFR-10)."," ","-| File | Exports | Notes | Reqs |","+| Area | Routes | Roles | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` (new, PRD-12 path) | `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)`, `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`, `audienceWhereForUser(user)` (Prisma `EventAudience` filter), `canTargetAudience(user, audience)` | Semantics are those of PRD-12 FR-2. `audienceWhereForUser` precomputes the user's keys once: their grade levels, sections and courses, the same for linked children (parents), the courses they teach and the sections they homeroom (teachers), and their role. It returns an `OR` over `{type, refId, include*}` so filtering happens in SQL (NFR-4). `canTargetAudience`: ADMIN → any. TEACHER → `COURSE` passes `assertCanManageCourse`, or `SECTION` where `homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Everything else → false. | FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-28, FR-29, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-7 |","-| `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` (new, pure) | `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` | Steps in school-tz wall clock: +7 days, or +1 month on the same day of month, skipping months that lack the day. Duration is kept in wall-clock terms. Stops at the earlier of `recurrenceUntil` (end of that day, inclusive) and `to`. Occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. | FR-15, FR-4, NFR-3, ADR-3 |","-| `src/server/calendar/ical.ts` (new, pure) | `escapeText`, `foldLine`, `vtimezone(tz, from, to)`, `vevent(item, tz)`, `buildCalendar(items, tz, window)` | All-day events use `VALUE=DATE` with an exclusive `DTEND`. Timed one-off events use UTC `Z`. Recurring events use `TZID` + `RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z` (+`BYMONTHDAY`). Deadlines are zero-duration VEVENTs with `URL`. Lines are CRLF and folded at 75 octets. | FR-12, FR-26, NFR-3, NFR-6, ADR-5 |","-| `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (new) | `getEvent`, `createEvent`, `updateEvent`, `deleteEvent`, `upsertRsvp`, `listRsvps`, `isSchoolDay`, `noSchoolDays(from,to)`, `createTermBreaks(yearId, actor)`, `getOrCreateFeedToken`, `resetFeedToken`, `findUserByFeedToken` | Owns every per-entity check (NFR-7). **Imports nothing from timetable-service** (R2). It reads `prisma.schoolDay` directly, and timetable-service imports *from* it. | FR-5..8, FR-16, FR-20..23, FR-25, FR-33, FR-34, FR-36 |","-| `src/server/calendar/sources.ts` (new) | `getCalendarItems`, `getPublicEvents`, `getUpcomingEventsForUser` | The merge in §3.1. It may import timetable-service, the assignment and quiz services, and calendar-service, because nothing imports it back except routes (R2). | FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-30..32 |","-| `src/server/calendar/maintenance.ts` (new) | `sendRsvpReminders(now)` | Selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline ∈ (now, now+48h]` and `rsvpReminderSentAt = null`. For each, claims it via `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}, data:{rsvpReminderSentAt:now}})`. If `count===1`, resolves the audience minus existing RSVP userIds and calls `notify('event.rsvp_reminder')`. | FR-23, ADR-11 |","-| `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (new, client-safe) | `eventInputSchema`, `eventPatchSchema`, `rsvpSchema`, `calendarQuerySchema`, `schoolDayQuerySchema`, `publicEventsQuerySchema` | Rules: title ≤ 150; description ≤ 5000; `endAt ≥ startAt`; `recurrenceUntil` required for WEEKLY/MONTHLY and ≤ start + 1 year; guests 0–5; range `to − from ≤ 100 days`; `sources ⊆ {events, holidays, assignments, quizzes, timetable}`. All-day input is `yyyy-MM-dd` start and inclusive end. The **server** converts it to `[schoolMidnight(start), schoolMidnight(end+1))`. | FR-4, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-8 |","-| `src/lib/dates.ts` (edit) | add `schoolMidnight(dateStr, tz)`, `schoolDateOf(instant, tz)` | Pure and client-safe. The single source of all-day and date conversions. | FR-4, FR-16, NFR-3, ADR-4 |","+| Child context | `POST /api/me/selected-child` | PARENT | FR-3, FR-4 |","+| Parent summaries | `GET /api/me/children/summary`, `GET /api/students/:id/overview` | PARENT (linked), staff via `assertCanViewStudent` | FR-7, FR-9 to FR-16 |","+| Absence notes | `GET/POST /api/absence-notes`, `GET /api/absence-notes/:id`, `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review` | PARENT (own children), TEACHER (homeroom), ADMIN | FR-18 to FR-23, FR-26 |","+| Conferences | `GET/POST /api/conferences`, `GET/PATCH /api/conferences/:id`, `PUT /api/conferences/:id/availability`, `GET /api/conferences/:id/slots`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/conference-slots/:id`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book`, `POST /api/conference-slots/:id/cancel`, `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` | ADMIN (events), TEACHER (own availability), PARENT (book and cancel for the selected or linked child) | FR-28 to FR-34 |","+| Consent forms | `GET/POST /api/consent-forms`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/responses`, `GET /api/consent-forms/:id/tracking[?format=csv]`, `POST /api/consent-forms/:id/remind` | ADMIN, TEACHER (managed courses), PARENT (respond) | FR-36 to FR-39 |"," ","-### 2.4 Edits to existing modules","+`arch-api-contracts` will write the exact request and response schemas."," ","-| File | Change | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` | At both `// PRD-14 holidays hook` lines, replace the inline `schoolDay` weekday check with `if (!(await isSchoolDay(date)).isSchoolDay) return [];`. The weekday rule now lives only in `isSchoolDay`, so the old check is deleted, not duplicated. The return type is unchanged. | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-9 |","-| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` | `getToday` and `getOverview` add `noSchoolReason: string \\| null` from `isSchoolDay`. The register save path rejects with `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"holidayOverride required\" when the date is not a school day and `holidayOverride !== true` (D-8). | FR-18 |","-| Attendance landing + `RegisterForm.tsx` | Landing shows \"No classes today — <reason>\". The register shows a warning `Alert` banner, and the save button opens `ConfirmDialog` \"Record attendance on a holiday anyway\", which sends `holidayOverride: true`. | FR-18, NFR-1 |","-| Teacher/student/parent Today views (those consuming `getScheduleForDate`) | When `isSchoolDay` is false, show the holiday name instead of the empty class list. | FR-17 |","-| `AssignmentForm.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` | On a `dueAt`/`availableUntil` change, `fetch('/api/school-day?date=')`. If false, show a non-blocking `<Alert severity=\"warning\">This date is a holiday (<title>).</Alert>`. Save is unchanged. | FR-19, FR-34 |","-| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `event.created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail false), `event.holiday_created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true), `event.updated` (COMMUNICATION, false) and `event.rsvp_reminder` (COMMUNICATION, false). All roles. | FR-23, FR-28, FR-29 |","-| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | Add an isolated `try { await sendRsvpReminders(now) } catch (e) { logger.error(...) }` block, matching the quiz-maintenance block. | FR-23, NFR-9 |","-| `src/config/navigation.ts` | `{ label: 'Calendar', href: '/calendar', icon: CalendarMonth, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, as with the other `/account/*` pages. It is reached from the account area and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`. | FR-35 |","-| `prisma/seed.ts` | `seedCalendar()`, idempotent: match by title (+ startAt where it is stable). It seeds the 7 events from FR-37 and the ROBOTICS course if absent (D-7). \"Sports day\" has no announcement link. Grade 6–8 exams use three `GRADE_LEVEL` audiences. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with only `includeParents`. | FR-37 |","+### 2.4 UI layer (NFR-4: MUI v9 only, with an mui-mcp lookup per component)"," ","-### 2.5 Route handlers (thin: requireUser/requireRole → Zod parse → service → `ok`/`apiError`)","-","-| Route | Auth | Service call | Reqs |","+| Route / surface | Kind | Key components | Reqs |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| `GET /api/calendar?from&to&sources&studentId` | any user | `getCalendarItems` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-32, NFR-7 |","-| `POST /api/events` | ADMIN, TEACHER | `createEvent` | FR-5..7, FR-14, FR-28, FR-33 |","-| `GET /api/events/:id` | visible to user | `getEvent` (+`myRsvp`, totals, `canEdit`) | FR-12, FR-22, FR-33 |","-| `PATCH /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `updateEvent` | FR-6..8, FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |","-| `DELETE /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `deleteEvent` | FR-8, FR-33, FR-36 |","-| `GET /api/events/:id/ics` | visible to user | `getEvent` → `buildCalendar([event])` | FR-12, FR-33 |","-| `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` | audience member | `upsertRsvp` | FR-21 |","-| `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps[?format=csv]` | creator, ADMIN | `listRsvps` → JSON or `csv.ts` | FR-22 |","-| `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` | any user | `getOrCreateFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |","-| `POST /api/me/calendar-feed/reset` | any user | `resetFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |","-| `GET /api/calendar/feed/[token]` (`.ics` stripped from param) | token | `findUserByFeedToken` → `rateLimit` → `getCalendarItems` → `buildCalendar` | FR-26, FR-27, NFR-5, NFR-6 |","-| `GET /api/school-day?date=` (new singular folder; `/api/school-days` untouched) | any user | `isSchoolDay` | FR-16, FR-19, FR-34 |","-| `GET /api/public/events?from&to` | public, IP rate limit | `getPublicEvents` | FR-30, D-9 |","-| `POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` | ADMIN | `createTermBreaks` | FR-20 |","+| `shell.tsx` top bar: `ChildSwitcher` | client | `Select`/`Menu` + `UserAvatar`. With one child it shows a name only. Changing the child POSTs to the selected-child route, then calls `router.refresh()`. | FR-3, FR-6 |","+| `src/config/navigation.ts` | config | Parent: My children, Absence notes, Conferences, Consent forms. Teacher: Absence notes (only if homeroom, via a `homeroom` flag passed like `safeguardingLead`) and Conferences. Admin: Conferences, Consent forms, Absence notes. | FR-42 |","+| `/dashboard` | server | If the role is PARENT, `redirect('/my-children')`. | FR-8 |","+| `/my-children` | server | With one child, `redirect` to the overview. Otherwise show summary `Card`s. | FR-7 |","+| `/my-children/[studentId]` | server, streaming | 8 async cards, each in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` with a \"View all\" link | FR-9 to FR-17, NFR-2 |","+| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence/new` | client form | RHF + Zod, `DatePicker`, `RadioGroup` (whole day or periods), a `Checkbox` group from `Period`, `FileUpload` (`absence-note`) | FR-18 |","+| `/my-children/[studentId]/absence` (parent list) | server + `DataTable` | Status `Chip` | FR-20 |","+| `/attendance/absence-notes` | server + `DataTable` | Status and date filters. The detail `Dialog` shows the note, the document link, existing records, and Approve/Reject (reject requires a note). | FR-21, FR-22 |","+| Attendance register (existing) | changed | EXCUSED pre-fill + an \"Absence note\" `Chip` badge. The EXCUSED option is enabled per `excusable`. | FR-24, FR-25 |","+| `/admin/conferences` (list, plus new/edit form) | server + client form | `DataTable`, `DatePicker`/`DateTimePicker`, `Autocomplete` (grade levels) | FR-28 |","+| `/conferences/[id]/availability` | client | Time-range rows, location `TextField`, a slot list with remove and block `IconButton`s | FR-29 |","+| `/conferences/[id]` (parent) | client | One section per teacher of the child, with `Button`/`ToggleButton` slot buttons and an optional note `Dialog`. A 409 shows a toast and refetches. The parent's own booking has Cancel. | FR-30 to FR-32, NFR-1 |","+| `/conferences/[id]/day` (teacher) | server | `Table` of booked slots, with `@media print` through `sx` | FR-34 |","+| `/conferences` | server | Event list for each role | FR-42 |","+| `/consent-forms`, `/consent-forms/new`, `/consent-forms/[id]` | server + client form | `MarkdownEditor`/`MarkdownView`, an audience picker reusing the announcements audience UI pattern, an `Autocomplete` event link, a respond form (`RadioGroup` + signature `TextField` + comment) | FR-36 to FR-38 |","+| `/consent-forms/[id]/tracking` | server + `DataTable` | Status filter, CSV export link, \"Remind non-responders\" `Button` (409 or 429 produces a toast) | FR-39 |"," ","-Error mapping: not visible → 404 `NOT_FOUND`. Visible but not permitted → 403 `FORBIDDEN`. RSVP after the deadline, or with RSVP disabled → 409 `CONFLICT`. Feed token unknown → plain 404. Feed over the limit → 429 `RATE_LIMITED` + `Retry-After`. `arch-api-contracts` defines the exact shapes.","+Toasts go through `useToast()` and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`. Nothing is imported from the banned list."," ","-### 2.6 UI","-","-| Path / component | Contents | Reqs |","-|---|---|---|","-| `src/app/(app)/calendar/page.tsx` (server) → `CalendarView.tsx` (client) | `requirePageUser`. `<EventCalendar>` from `@mui/x-scheduler/event-calendar`: `views={['month','week','agenda']}`, week `startTime:7, endTime:19`, agenda `dayCount:30`, `displayTimezone={tz}`, `readOnly`, `eventCreation={false}`. The default view is month at `useMediaQuery('(min-width:768px)')`, agenda below that. Controlled `events`, refetched on `onVisibleDateChange`/`onViewChange` with plain `fetch` and a small Map cache keyed by `from|to|sources|studentId`. The page opens the drawer when `?event=<id>` is present (notification links). | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-12 |","-| `SourceChips` | MUI `Chip`s: School events · My assignments · My quizzes · My timetable (Week view only) · Holidays. Stored in `localStorage['calendar.sources']`. Holidays = HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool`; School events = everything else, with no overlap. `timetable` is fetched only in Week view. | FR-10 |","-| Child filter (PARENT only) | `Select`: \"All children\" or one child → `studentId`. Deadline titles get the child's name prefixed by the server. | FR-11 |","-| `EventDrawer` | Right-anchored `Drawer`: title, category `Chip`, time in school tz, location, `MarkdownView` description, audience chips, RSVP controls (`ToggleButtonGroup` + guests `TextField` for parents + note; disabled after the deadline), \"Add to my calendar\" (`<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`), and edit/delete when `canEdit` (delete via `ConfirmDialog`). Creator/admin see an RSVP `DataTable` + CSV link. | FR-12, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1 |","-| Deadline click | `onEventEditingStart` → `cancel()` → `router.push(item.href)` | FR-13 |","-| `EventEditorDialog` | \"New event\" button (ADMIN/TEACHER). React Hook Form + `eventInputSchema`. Fields: title, category (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK only for admins), all-day switch, date/time pickers (`@mui/x-date-pickers`), location, `MarkdownEditor`, `AudienceBuilder`, recurrence select + until date, RSVP switch + deadline, and admin-only `isNoSchool`/`isPublic`. Results go through `useToast`. | FR-4..7, FR-14 |","-| `src/components/AudienceBuilder/` (new shared) | Rows of type `Select` + entity `Autocomplete` (grade level / section / course / role) + three include `Checkbox`es. Types are filtered by `canTargetAudience` rules on the client. The server stays authoritative. | FR-3, FR-7, FR-14 |","-| `src/app/(app)/account/calendar/page.tsx` | \"Subscribe\" card: URL `TextField` (read-only) + copy (`navigator.clipboard`), Google/Apple/Outlook instructions as static text, and \"Reset link\" behind `ConfirmDialog`. When `url` is null: \"Reset link to get a new URL\" (D-6). | FR-24, FR-25 |","-| `src/app/(app)/admin/academic-years/[id]/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. Year name, read-only term list (existing terms service), and an \"Add term breaks\" button + `ConfirmDialog` that shows the number of breaks created via toast. | FR-20 |","-"," ---"," "," ## 3. Data Flow"," ","-### 3.1 Calendar read (`GET /api/calendar`, the feed, upcoming events)","+### 3.1 Child selection (FR-3 to FR-6)"," "," ```","-route → calendarQuerySchema (≤100 days) → getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})","-  1. scope   = studentId ? resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId) : getAccessibleStudentIds(user)   (404 for others)","-  2. where   = audienceWhereForUser(user, scope)          // keys computed once","-  3. Promise.all([","-       events:      CalendarEvent where startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR (recurrence≠NONE AND recurrenceUntil ≥ from))","-                    AND (audiences some where) OR createdById=user  (ADMIN: no audience filter)","-                    → expandOccurrences(e, from, to, tz) → split into holidays / events by category+isNoSchool,","-       assignments: existing assignment service, PUBLISHED, dueAt ∈ [from,to), scoped students/courses,","-       quizzes:     existing quiz service, PUBLISHED, availableUntil ∈ [from,to),","-       timetable:   getPersonalTimetable(target) projected onto dates in range, skipping noSchoolDays(from,to)","-     ]) – only for requested sources","-  4. map → CalendarItem union {kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', id, title, start, end, allDay, color, href?, childName?}","+Switcher change → POST /api/me/selected-child {studentId}","+  → assert ParentStudentLink → Set-Cookie sh_child (httpOnly) → router.refresh()","+Any parent page → getSelectedChild(user, searchParams)","+  → ?studentId (if linked) ▸ cookie (if linked) ▸ first linked child"," ```","-The feed calls the same function with `from=now−30d, to=now+365d`, sources minus timetable, and recurring events **unexpanded**. Instead of occurrences it gets the series rows so it can emit RRULE. The 100-day cap is skipped because the call is internal. Traces to FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-4, NFR-5."," ","-### 3.2 Event write","+The cookie is untrusted. A stale or tampered value falls back to the first child and never errors."," ","+### 3.2 Absence note lifecycle (FR-18 to FR-27)","+"," ```","-POST/PATCH → eventInputSchema → createEvent/updateEvent(user, input)","-  - FR-6: non-admin + (isNoSchool | isPublic | HOLIDAY | TERM_BREAK) → 403","-  - FR-7: every audience must pass canTargetAudience(user, a) → else 403","-  - FR-8: PATCH/DELETE requires createdById===user.id or ADMIN","-  - FR-5: isNoSchool ??= category ∈ {HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK}","-  - all-day → schoolMidnight conversion (FR-4)","-  - prisma.$transaction: event + replace audiences","-  - after commit:","-      FR-36 audit() if ADMIN && createdById≠user.id (update/delete)","-      FR-28 create: first occurrence within 30 days → notify(HOLIDAY|TERM_BREAK ? 'event.holiday_created' : 'event.created',","-            resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) − creator, link '/calendar?event=<id>')","-      FR-29 update: startAt|endAt|allDay|location changed AND event upcoming → notify('event.updated') once","-```","+Parent form ─(Zod)→ POST /api/absence-notes","+  → assertCanViewStudent → create PENDING (+fileId, context absence-note)","+  → notify(absence_note.submitted → homeroom teacher + ADMINs)"," ","-### 3.3 Audience resolution (PRD-12 FR-2 semantics)","+Reviewer → POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review {decision, note}","+  → assertHomeroomOrAdmin → $transaction:","+       updateMany AbsenceNote where {id, status: PENDING} (count 0 → 409)","+       if APPROVED: load sessions in [fromDate,toDate] for student's sections;","+                    for each covered (date, periodId) via coversRecord:","+                      existing ABSENT record → EXCUSED, note \"Absence note #<id>\"","+                      session exists, no record → create EXCUSED record","+  → after commit: audit({ request }) (IP, NFR-3); notify(absence_note.reviewed → linked parents, incl. reviewNote)"," ","-| Type | refId | Students (`includeStudents`) | Parents (`includeParents`) | Teachers (`includeTeachers`) |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| SCHOOL | null | all active users | | |","-| STAFF | null | ADMIN + TEACHER | | |","-| ROLE | role name | users with that role | | |","-| GRADE_LEVEL | gradeLevelId | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId = refId` | their `ParentStudentLink` parents | teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade |","-| SECTION | sectionId | current-year `SectionMember`s | their parents | homeroom teacher + teachers of courses in the section |","-| COURSE | courseId | ACTIVE `Enrollment`s | their parents | `teacherId` + `coTeacherIds` |","+Register load (getRegister) → findCovering(APPROVED) → pre-fill EXCUSED + badge (future dates, FR-24)","+Register save (saveRegister) → EXCUSED allowed if ADMIN or APPROVED note covers (FR-25)","+                             → absent notifications filtered by PENDING|APPROVED coverage (FR-27)","+```"," ","-Only ACTIVE, non-archived users count. `isUserInAudience` and `audienceWhereForUser` give the same answer as `resolveAudienceUserIds`. A property-style integration test loops over every seed user to check this (PRD-12 test requirement). Traces to FR-3, FR-7, NFR-7.","+Attendance rates recalculate without new code, because `attendanceRate()` counts records when it reads them (FR-23). A rejected note changes no records."," ","-### 3.4 School-day check","+### 3.3 Conference booking (FR-28 to FR-33, NFR-1)"," "," ```","-isSchoolDay(date) → d = schoolDateOf(date, tz), isoDay","-  1. SchoolDay[isoDay].isTeaching ?? isoDay ≤ 5   → false, reason 'Not a teaching day'","-  2. isNoSchool events with a SCHOOL audience where startAt < midnight(d+1) AND (endAt > midnight(d) OR recurring)","-     → expandOccurrences within that day → first hit → false, reason 'Holiday: <title>'","-  3. → { isSchoolDay: true, reason: null }","-noSchoolDays(from, to) = one query, same rules, returns Map<date, reason> (used by the timetable source; avoids N calls)","+Admin creates event → notify(conference.slots_requested → teachers of eligible grade levels)","+Teacher PUT availability {ranges, location} → generateSlots → $transaction(delete unbooked&unblocked, insert new)","+Parent POST /api/conference-slots/:id/book {studentId, note?}","+  → assertCanViewStudent; now within [bookingOpensAt, bookingClosesAt] else 422","+  → $transaction:","+       overlap check vs parent's other booked slots at that time → 409 \"You already have a meeting with <teacher> at <time>\"","+       updateMany where {id, bookedByParentId: null, blocked: false} → count 0 → 409 \"That slot was just taken\"","+       P2002 on (eventId, teacherId, bookedForStudentId) → 409 (one per teacher per child)","+  → notify(conference.booked → parent + teacher, link /api/conference-slots/:id/ics)","+Cancel → before bookingClosesAt; clear booking fields → notify(conference.cancelled)","+Reschedule = cancel + book (client-side, FR-32)"," ```","-Callers: timetable-service (FR-17), attendance (FR-18), `/api/school-day` (FR-19, FR-34), timetable source in §3.1. Traces to FR-16..19, FR-34."," ","-### 3.5 RSVP","+### 3.4 Consent forms (FR-36 to FR-40)"," ","-`PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` → `rsvpSchema` → `upsertRsvp`:","-1. Check the event is visible and `rsvpEnabled`. Otherwise 404 (not visible) or 409.","-2. Require `isUserInAudience`. Otherwise 403.","-3. Require `now < rsvpDeadline`. Otherwise 409.","-4. If the user is not a PARENT, force `guests = 0`.","-5. Upsert on `(eventId, userId)`.","-","-A recurring event has one RSVP for the whole series. The drawer gets `myRsvp` and totals `{yes, no, maybe, guests}` from `GET /api/events/:id`. Creator and admin read the full list via `/rsvps`, or `?format=csv` via `csv.ts`. Traces to FR-21, FR-22.","-","-### 3.6 Reminder job","-","-Cron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` → `sendRsvpReminders(now)` → claim → audience − responders → `notify('event.rsvp_reminder', link '/calendar?event=<id>')`. Traces to FR-23.","-","-### 3.7 iCal feed","-"," ```","-GET /api/calendar/feed/<token>.ics","-  token = param.replace(/\\.ics$/, '') → hashToken(token) → CalendarFeedToken by tokenHash (unique) → user ACTIVE?","-    no → 404 text/plain","-  rateLimit('calfeed:'+hash, 60, 3_600_000) → !ok → 429 + Retry-After","-  items = getCalendarItems(user, feed window, series mode)","-  body  = buildCalendar(items, tz, window)   // VTIMEZONE for transitions in window, RRULE for series","-  200 text/calendar; charset=utf-8, Cache-Control: private, max-age=900","+Create → canTargetAudience per row → insert form+audiences → resolve audience students → linked parents","+       → notify(consent.requested)","+Respond POST …/responses {studentId, value, signature, comment?}","+  → assertCanViewStudent; now < dueAt else 422; signatureMatches(signature, parent full name) else 422","+  → upsert by (formId, studentId) → audit({ before, after, request })","+Tracking → audience students × responses → Granted/Declined/No response; ?format=csv","+Remind → updateMany where {id, lastRemindedAt null|< now-24h} count 0 → 429 → notify(consent.reminder → non-responders)","+Cron dispatch → forms with dueAt in (now, now+48h], dueReminderSentAt null → claim → notify(consent.reminder)"," ```","-Token lifecycle:","-- `getOrCreateFeedToken` creates the row on first use from `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stores `hashToken(raw)`, and returns the URL once.","-- `resetFeedToken` upserts a new hash, so the old URL returns 404 immediately.","-- No raw token is ever logged."," ","-Traces to FR-24..27, NFR-5, NFR-6, ADR-6, ADR-7.","+### 3.5 Overview rendering (FR-7 to FR-17, NFR-2)"," ","-### 3.8 Public and dashboard hooks","+The server page calls `assertCanViewStudent` once. The header and switcher paint first. The eight cards then stream independently, each doing one or two indexed `select` queries in `overview-service`. `GET /api/students/:id/overview` calls the same functions for API consumers. All \"today\", window and due-date evaluation uses `schoolToday(now, SchoolSettings.timezone)` (NFR-8)."," ","-- `getPublicEvents(from, to)`: `isPublic` events, expanded, returning only public-safe fields (id, title, category, start, end, allDay, location, description). Traces to FR-30.","-- `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)`: `getCalendarItems(user, now..now+90d, ['events','holidays'])`, sorted, then the first `limit` items. No UI. Traces to FR-31, NFR-11.","-","-### 3.9 Term breaks","-","-`POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` (ADMIN) → `createTermBreaks`:","-1. Order the terms by `startDate`.","-2. For each consecutive pair where `next.start > prev.end + 1 day`, create an all-day TERM_BREAK with `isNoSchool=true` and a SCHOOL audience, from `prev.end+1` (inclusive) to `next.start` (exclusive).","-3. Skip any gap that already has a TERM_BREAK with the same span. This makes the call idempotent.","-4. Return `{ created }`.","-5. Write an `audit()` entry.","-","-Traces to FR-20.","-"," ---"," ","-## 4. Cross-cutting","+## 4. Testing and seed data (FR-45, FR-46, NFR-7)"," ","-- **Time (NFR-3, NFR-8).**","-  - Storage is in UTC. Display uses `SchoolSettings.timezone`, read via the existing `getSchoolTimezone()`. No third copy is created.","-  - All-day events run from school-tz midnight with an exclusive end.","-  - Expansion steps in wall-clock time.","-  - The feed uses `VALUE=DATE` for all-day events and `TZID` + VTIMEZONE for series.","-  - The scheduler gets `displayTimezone`.","-  - One DST-week test fixture (America/New_York 2026-11-01, or the seed tz) runs through the expansion, the all-day path and the feed.","-- **Security (NFR-5, NFR-7).**","-  - Every route calls `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (hashed token) and public events (public fields only, IP limit).","-  - Per-entity checks live in calendar-service.","-  - Students see only themselves, and parents only their linked children (`getAccessibleStudentIds` / `resolveViewedStudent`).","-  - A non-visible event returns 404, so its existence doesn't leak.","-- **Performance (NFR-4).**","-  - A parent with 3 children in month view needs about 6 indexed queries, run in parallel.","-  - The audience is filtered in SQL, and holidays are found with one `noSchoolDays` query.","-  - There is no cache layer. Add one only if the Playwright timing or a measurement exceeds 500 ms.","-- **UI rules (NFR-1, NFR-12).**","-  - Only MUI, icons and MUI X (including the scheduler) are used. Toasts go through `useToast`, side panels through `Drawer`, and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`.","-  - English only. The breakpoint is 768 px.","-- **Scope (NFR-11).**","-  - Out of scope: per-occurrence exceptions, room booking (`roomId` is stored and unused), two-way sync, and dashboard or public-site UI.","-- **Tests (NFR-10).**","-  - Unit tests:","-    - `expandOccurrences`: weekly, monthly on the 31st, the until bound, a DST week","-    - `isSchoolDay`: weekday, holiday, recurring no-school","-    - `ical`: escaping `, ; \\ \\n`, folding, RRULE, VALUE=DATE exclusive end, node-ical parse","-    - all-day conversion","-    - term-break gap math","-    - `canTargetAudience`","-  - Integration tests:","-    - calendar merge per role (admin, teacher, student, parent with 3 children)","-    - feed token reset (old URL 404, new URL 200 and node-ical-valid)","-    - RSVP deadline (409) and parent-only guests","-    - audience resolver parity across seed users","-    - teacher SCHOOL create → 403","-  - Playwright:","-    - an admin creates a holiday, and the student's Today view shows the holiday name","-    - a parent RSVPs","-    - the feed URL returns a valid ICS","-  - `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` stays green.","+- **Unit tests (Vitest):**","+  - `absence-coverage`: whole day, partial periods, multi-day, and a null `periodId`","+  - `conference-slots`: generation at range boundaries, `slotMinutes` 5 and 60, and overlap","+  - `signature`: case and whitespace","+- **Integration tests (Vitest + DB):**","+  - Approval converts ABSENT to EXCUSED and leaves PRESENT untouched.","+  - Future-register pre-fill.","+  - Two concurrent `book` calls run through `Promise.all`: exactly one succeeds and the other gets 409.","+  - `attendance.absent` is suppressed while a PENDING note covers the student.","+- **Playwright:**","+  - Absence note, then approve, then the register shows EXCUSED.","+  - Book a conference slot.","+  - Sign a consent form.","+- **Seed:** extend `prisma/seed.ts` in place:","+  - Grade 7: one PENDING and one APPROVED absence note.","+  - \"Autumn conferences\" 3 weeks out, with Tom and Tina slots 15:00–17:00 at 10 minutes each, two of them booked.","+  - \"Science Museum Trip\" consent form due in 10 days, linked to a seeded `CalendarEvent`, with about 40% of responses in.","+- **Gates:** `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test`. Use `logger`, never `console.log`."," ","-### Risks carried forward","-","-| Risk | Mitigation |","-|---|---|","-| R1 Beta scheduler API drift | Exact pin, MCP lookup before use, and the scheduler used only as a read-only display (ADR-2). The D-5 fallback is pre-agreed. |","-| R2 Import cycle between timetable and calendar | The edges run one way: timetable-service → calendar-service, and sources.ts → (timetable, assignments, quizzes, calendar-service). calendar-service reads teaching weekdays via `prisma.schoolDay` and never imports timetable-service. |","-| R3 DST correctness across 4 code paths | Shared pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` plus one shared DST fixture. |","-| R4 Audience is both the hot path and the security boundary | A single implementation plus the parity test. |","-"," ---"," "," ## 5. Requirements Traceability"," ","-| Req | Design element(s) |","+| Req | Design element |"," |---|---|","-| FR-1 | §2.1 exact pin `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` + scoped override (ADR-1) |","-| FR-2 | §2.2 migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`: enums, 4 models, cascades, `[startAt,endAt]` index |","-| FR-3 | §2.2 `AudienceType` (PRD-12 values); §2.3 `announcements/audience.ts`; §3.3 resolution table |","-| FR-4 | §2.3 `validators/calendar.ts` + `schoolMidnight`; §3.2 all-day conversion |","-| FR-5 | §3.2 `isNoSchool ??= HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK` in `createEvent` |","-| FR-6 | §3.2 admin-only field check; §2.6 editor hides admin fields |","-| FR-7 | §2.3 `canTargetAudience`; §3.2 check on create/patch |","-| FR-8 | §3.2 creator/ADMIN guard on PATCH/DELETE |","-| FR-9 | §2.6 `CalendarView` with `EventCalendar` views/viewConfig/breakpoint; D-5 agenda fallback |","-| FR-10 | §2.6 `SourceChips` + localStorage; §3.1 `sources` param, holidays/events split |","-| FR-11 | §2.6 parent child filter; §3.1 `studentId` scope + `childName` |","-| FR-12 | §2.6 `EventDrawer`; §2.5 `GET /api/events/:id`, `/ics` |","-| FR-13 | §2.6 deadline click → `router.push(href)` |","-| FR-14 | §2.6 `EventEditorDialog` + `AudienceBuilder` |","-| FR-15 | §2.3 `recurrence.ts` `expandOccurrences`; §3.1 read-time expansion |","-| FR-16 | §2.3 `isSchoolDay`; §3.4 |","-| FR-17 | §2.4 timetable-service hook + Today views |","-| FR-18 | §2.4 attendance `noSchoolReason`, `holidayOverride` (D-8), `RegisterForm` banner/confirm |","-| FR-19 | §2.4 `AssignmentForm` / `QuizSettingsPanel` warning via `/api/school-day` |","-| FR-20 | §2.6 `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page; §2.5 term-breaks route; §3.9 `createTermBreaks` |","-| FR-21 | §2.5 `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`; §3.5 `upsertRsvp` rules |","-| FR-22 | §2.5 `/rsvps[?format=csv]`; §2.6 drawer totals + `DataTable` |","-| FR-23 | §2.3 `maintenance.ts`; §2.4 cron hook + type; D-1 `rsvpReminderSentAt` |","-| FR-24 | §2.6 `/account/calendar`; §2.5 me/calendar-feed routes |","-| FR-25 | §3.7 token lifecycle with `hashToken`; D-6 |","-| FR-26 | §2.3 `ical.ts`; §3.7 feed build (window, RRULE, VTIMEZONE, escaping) |","-| FR-27 | §2.5 feed route; §3.7 rate limit + Cache-Control |","-| FR-28 | §2.4 types `event.created` + `event.holiday_created` (D-3); §3.2 notify on create |","-| FR-29 | §2.4 type `event.updated`; §3.2 notify on time/location change |","-| FR-30 | §3.8 `getPublicEvents`; §2.5 `/api/public/events` (D-9) |","-| FR-31 | §3.8 `getUpcomingEventsForUser` |","-| FR-32 | §2.5 `GET /api/calendar`; §3.1 `getCalendarItems`; 100-day cap in validator |","-| FR-33 | §2.5 event CRUD + `/ics` routes |","-| FR-34 | §2.5 `GET /api/school-day` (singular, new folder) |","-| FR-35 | §2.4 `navigation.ts` Calendar entry |","-| FR-36 | §3.2 `audit()` on admin edits/deletes of other users' events |","-| FR-37 | §2.4 `seedCalendar()` + ROBOTICS course (D-7) |","-| NFR-1 | §2.6 MUI-only components; §4 UI rules |","-| NFR-2 | §2.1 MCP lookup gate before scheduler use |","-| NFR-3 | §2.3 wall-clock expansion, `dates.ts` helpers, ical VALUE=DATE/TZID; §4 DST fixture |","-| NFR-4 | §3.1 parallel indexed queries, SQL audience filter, D-2 index; §4 performance |","-| NFR-5 | §3.7 32-byte token, SHA-256 hash; §3.1 shared read path |","-| NFR-6 | §2.1 `node-ical` devDep; §4 parse tests |","-| NFR-7 | §2.5 auth column; §3.3; §4 security |","-| NFR-8 | §2.3 module layout under `src/server/calendar/`; thin routes; Zod; UTC storage |","-| NFR-9 | §1 reuse list; §2.4 edits instead of new helpers |","-| NFR-10 | §4 tests |","-| NFR-11 | §4 scope; §3.8 hooks only |","-| NFR-12 | §2.6 768 px breakpoint, English only |","+| FR-1 | §2.1 migration `…_prd15_parent_portal`, 3 enums and 6 models, 3 flagged extra columns |","+| FR-2 | §2.1 Zod validators `src/lib/validators/*` with `.superRefine` |","+| FR-3 | §2.2 `selected-child.ts`; §2.4 `ChildSwitcher`; `POST /api/me/selected-child` |","+| FR-4 | §3.1 `getSelectedChild` link validation and fallback |","+| FR-5 | §2.2 `getSelectedChild` used by `/assignments`, `/grades`, `/api/me/timetable` and new pages (calendar filter partial, ADR-11) |","+| FR-6 | §2.4 `ChildSwitcher` single-child mode |","+| FR-7 | §2.4 `/my-children`; `getChildrenSummary`; `GET /api/me/children/summary` |","+| FR-8 | §2.4 `/dashboard` redirects PARENT to `/my-children` |","+| FR-9 | `overview-service.getToday` (timetable + SchoolDay holidays) |","+| FR-10 | `overview-service.getAttendanceSummary` + link to the absence form |","+| FR-11 | `overview-service.getAssignmentsSummary` |","+| FR-12 | `overview-service.getRecentGrades` (visibility rules respected) |","+| FR-13 | `listUnreadAnnouncements` returns `[]` and the card shows an `EmptyState` (**partial**, PRD-12 absent) |","+| FR-14 | `overview-service.getUpcomingEvents` (`CalendarEvent` via `audienceWhereForUser` + recurrence) |","+| FR-15 | `overview-service.getTeachers` + Message link (PRD-13 compose) |","+| FR-16 | `overview-service.getActionItems` |","+| FR-17 | §3.5 Suspense per card + \"View all\" links |","+| FR-18 | §2.4 absence form; `absence-notes-service.submit`; `absence-note` file context |","+| FR-19 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.submitted)` to homeroom teacher + ADMINs |","+| FR-20 | §2.4 parent absence list; `GET /api/absence-notes` |","+| FR-21 | §2.4 `/attendance/absence-notes`; `getForReview`; `assertHomeroomOrAdmin` |","+| FR-22 | §3.2 `POST /api/absence-notes/:id/review`, PENDING-only conditional update |","+| FR-23 | §3.2 approval transaction + `coversRecord` + `audit` |","+| FR-24 | §2.2 `getRegister` pre-fill + badge |","+| FR-25 | §2.2 `saveRegister:219` EXCUSED rule |","+| FR-26 | §3.2 `notify(absence_note.reviewed)` with reviewNote |","+| FR-27 | §2.2 attendance-service notification filter (~:299) |","+| FR-28 | §2.4 `/admin/conferences`; `createEvent`/`updateEvent`; `conference.slots_requested` |","+| FR-29 | §2.4 availability page; `setAvailability`, `generateSlots`, `blocked` column |","+| FR-30 | §3.3 conditional `updateMany` booking; `/conferences/[id]` |","+| FR-31 | §3.3 overlap check + partial unique index |","+| FR-32 | §3.3 booking-window guard; cancel; reschedule = cancel + book |","+| FR-33 | §3.3 `conference.booked`/`cancelled` + `GET /api/conference-slots/:id/ics` (`ical.ts`) |","+| FR-34 | §2.4 `/conferences/[id]/day`, print CSS |","+| FR-35 | `listMyMeetings`, shown as \"My meetings\" in overview Upcoming events and Action items (**partial**, no PRD-14 calendar page) |","+| FR-36 | §3.4 create + `canTargetAudience` + `consent.requested`; `/consent-forms/new` |","+| FR-37 | §3.4 respond + `signatureMatches`; overview Action items; `/consent-forms` |","+| FR-38 | `ConsentResponse @@unique(formId, studentId)` upsert + `audit` |","+| FR-39 | §3.4 tracking/CSV; remind with a `lastRemindedAt` 24 h claim |","+| FR-40 | §3.4 `sendConsentDueReminders` in the dispatch cron; `dueReminderSentAt` |","+| FR-41 | §2.2 `absence-note` resolver in `files/contexts.ts` |","+| FR-42 | §2.4 `src/config/navigation.ts` entries + homeroom flag |","+| FR-43 | §2.3 route table, `withHandler`/`requireRole`, standard shapes |","+| FR-44 | §2.2 `NOTIFICATION_TYPES` additions incl. `consent.reminder` |","+| FR-45 | §4 seed extensions |","+| FR-46 | §4 unit, integration and Playwright tests |","+| NFR-1 | §3.3 conditional update → 409 \"That slot was just taken\" + client refetch |","+| NFR-2 | §3.5 streaming cards, indexed `select` queries |","+| NFR-3 | `audit({ request })` on review, consent respond/change, conference admin edits |","+| NFR-4 | §2.4 MUI-only component map, with an mui-mcp lookup required per component |","+| NFR-5 | §2.2 access helpers on every page and handler; cookie only via `getSelectedChild` |","+| NFR-6 | §2.2 new `src/server/<feature>/` modules; existing files extended in place |","+| NFR-7 | §2.1 shared Zod validators; §4 gates; `logger` |","+| NFR-8 | `@db.Date` fields; `schoolToday` + `SchoolSettings.timezone` for all date rules |","+| NFR-9 | No Announcement or calendar subsystem built; FR-13, FR-35 and FR-5 calendar part degrade (ADR-11) |","+| NFR-10 | §2.3 list endpoints use standard pagination, sort and `q` |"]}],"originalFile":"# System Design: PRD-14 School Calendar, Events & Holidays\n\nTicket: SH-14 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-09T23:58:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs:\n- `artifacts/intake/requirements.json`: 37 FR and 12 NFR, 96% confidence\n- `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`\n- `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md`: ADR-1 to ADR-13\n- `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`: B1 to B19, D1 to D9, R1 to R4\n\n> This replaces the stale SH-13 `system-design.md`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` in this folder are still SH-13 until `arch-api-contracts` rewrites them.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nSH-14 adds a school calendar to the existing SchoolHub app (Next.js 14 App Router, Prisma/PostgreSQL, MUI 9). The pieces are:\n\n- one Prisma migration\n- one server module, `src/server/calendar/`\n- a shared audience resolver, at the path PRD-12 will use\n- about a dozen thin route handlers\n- two new pages (`/calendar`, `/account/calendar`), plus one small admin page\n- small, targeted edits to timetable, attendance, the assignment and quiz editors, notifications, the cron, navigation and the seed\n\nDesign principles:\n\n1. **One read path.** A single function, `getCalendarItems(user, range, sources, studentId?)`, feeds the `/calendar` API, the iCal feed, `getUpcomingEventsForUser`, and (with `sources=['events']`) the single-event visibility check. That way the feed cannot show anything the app hides (NFR-5).\n2. **Recurrence is expanded on the server, at read time.** A recurring event is stored once. Clients and the scheduler only ever receive plain occurrences. The feed emits RRULE (ADR-2, ADR-3).\n3. **One holiday rule.** `isSchoolDay` in calendar-service owns the teaching-weekday rule and the no-school-event rule. Timetable, attendance, the editors and `/api/school-day` all call it (ADR-8).\n4. **Reuse before writing.** The design reuses `rateLimit`, `notify`, `audit`, `hashToken`, `csv.ts`, `DataTable`, `ConfirmDialog`, `MarkdownView/Editor`, `useToast`, the dispatch cron, `getSchoolTimezone` and the access helpers (NFR-9).\n\n### Intake blockers and warnings\n\n`handoff-to-architect.json` reports **no blockers** (`blockers: []`). It raises three warnings, resolved as follows:\n\n| Intake warning | Resolution | Ref |\n|---|---|---|\n| PRD-12 missing: no `AudienceType`, `audience.ts` or audience builder | SH-14 adds `enum AudienceType { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }` and `src/server/announcements/audience.ts`, exactly as PRD-12 §FR-1/FR-2 specify. It also adds a minimal MUI `AudienceBuilder`. PRD-12 adopts all three without changes. No Announcement models. | ADR-9, §3.3 |\n| `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page missing | Add a minimal ADMIN server page at that exact route with a read-only term list and an \"Add term breaks\" button. | ADR-10, §3.9 |\n| New dependencies | `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` (exact, installed first) with a scoped `@mui/x-internals` override. `node-ical@0.27.6` as an exact devDependency. Nothing else is added. | ADR-1, ADR-5 |\n\n### Conflicts between the research inputs, and how this design settles them\n\n| Topic | arch-research-stack | arch-research-reqs | **Decision** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Audience shape | PRD-12 enum (6 values) with `refId` and `include*` flags | 4-value enum with `targetId` and `roles[]` | **ADR-9.** PRD-14 FR-1 itself defines `EventAudience` with `refId` / `includeStudents` / `includeParents` / `includeTeachers` (verified in `14-calendar.md` L128-137), and PRD-12 L96 defines the 6 values. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with `includeStudents=false, includeTeachers=false`. No `roles[]` column. |\n| Resolver path | `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` | `src/server/audience/audience.ts` | **`src/server/announcements/audience.ts`**, the path PRD-12 names, so PRD-12 doesn't need a rename. |\n| `getScheduleForDate` \"reason\" | Add `reason` to its return | Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`; callers fetch the reason separately | **Keep `ScheduleEntry[]`** (no churn for callers: attendance L130/L472, `getCurrentSlot`). Callers that need the holiday name call `isSchoolDay(date)` directly. FR-17's \"reason\" is delivered through `isSchoolDay` and `/api/school-day`. |\n| Email default per category (FR-28) | Not addressed | D5: a second type | **Two registry types:** `event.created` (`defaultEmail: false`) and `event.holiday_created` (`defaultEmail: true`, used for HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK). Both keep the per-user preference override, and `notify.ts` is unchanged. This is a deliberate deviation (D-3 below). |\n| RSVP reminder \"once\" | `rsvpReminderSentAt` column | Same, claimed with conditional `updateMany` | Agreed: claim it with `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}})`. |\n\n### Deviations from the PRD's model and route list (all deliberate)\n\n| ID | Deviation | Why | Traces to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D-1 | `CalendarEvent.rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?` | Stores \"once per event\" for the reminder. Claimed atomically. | FR-23 |\n| D-2 | `EventAudience @@index([eventId])` and `@@index([type, refId])` | Audience filtering in SQL on the hot path. | NFR-4 |\n| D-3 | Extra notification type `event.holiday_created` | Per-category email default, within the existing preference model. | FR-28 |\n| D-4 | Back-relations on `User` (`calendarEvents`, `eventRsvps`, `calendarFeedToken`) and `onDelete: Cascade` FKs on `EventRsvp.userId` / `CalendarFeedToken.userId` | Prisma requires the relations. Cascade matches the \"cascade deletes\" instruction in FR-2. | FR-2 |\n| D-5 | Agenda view: 30-day page with next/prev in Community `EventCalendar`, instead of true infinite scroll | Community has no infinite agenda. If QA rejects this, the fallback is MUI `List` + native `IntersectionObserver` below 768 px, fetching the next 30-day window. Rejection triggers the fallback; it is not built up front. | FR-9, ADR-2 |\n| D-6 | `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` returns `url` only when it creates the first token, otherwise `{url:null, hasToken:true, createdAt}`. The page offers \"Reset link\". | The raw token cannot be re-shown because it is stored hashed. | FR-24, FR-25, NFR-5 |\n| D-7 | Seed a minimal ELECTIVE `ROBOTICS` course (teacher Tom, current year) only if it doesn't exist | The Chess club audience needs it, and it is absent from the seed. | FR-37 |\n| D-8 | Register save on a no-school date requires `holidayOverride: true` in the body, enforced on the server | Makes FR-18's extra confirmation a real rule, not only a UI dialog. | FR-18, NFR-7 |\n| D-9 | `GET /api/public/events` is rate limited per IP (`rateLimit('pubcal:'+ip, 120, 3_600_000)`) and range-capped at 100 days | Only unauthenticated JSON route; reuses the existing limiter. | FR-30, NFR-7 |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Component Breakdown\n\n### 2.1 Dependencies and config (do first)\n\n| Change | Ref |\n|---|---|\n| `npm i --save-exact @mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15`. Nested override `\"@mui/x-scheduler\": {\"@mui/x-internals\": \"9.17.0\"}`. Verify with `npm ls @mui/x-internals`. If npm doesn't honour the nested override, fall back to a global `9.17.0`. | FR-1, ADR-1 |\n| `import type {} from '@mui/x-scheduler/theme-augmentation'` beside the theme | FR-9, ADR-1 |\n| `npm i -D --save-exact node-ical@0.27.6` | NFR-6 |\n| Before writing scheduler code, the dev phase looks up the Quickstart, Views, Events, Editing, Timezone, Localization and Responsiveness pages via MUI MCP (`useMuiDocs` + `fetchDocs`). If MCP is unreachable, stop and report a blocker. | NFR-2 |\n\n### 2.2 Data model: migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`\n\n```prisma\nenum AudienceType  { SCHOOL STAFF ROLE GRADE_LEVEL SECTION COURSE }   // PRD-12 values, owned here until PRD-12 lands\nenum EventCategory { HOLIDAY TERM_BREAK EXAM EVENT MEETING TRIP SPORTS DEADLINE OTHER }\nenum Recurrence    { NONE WEEKLY MONTHLY }\nenum RsvpResponse  { YES NO MAYBE }\n\nmodel CalendarEvent {\n  id                 String        @id @default(cuid())\n  title              String\n  description        String?\n  category           EventCategory\n  startAt            DateTime\n  endAt              DateTime\n  allDay             Boolean       @default(false)\n  location           String?\n  roomId             String?\n  recurrence         Recurrence    @default(NONE)\n  recurrenceUntil    DateTime?     @db.Date\n  isNoSchool         Boolean       @default(false)\n  rsvpEnabled        Boolean       @default(false)\n  rsvpDeadline       DateTime?\n  rsvpReminderSentAt DateTime?                                  // D-1\n  isPublic           Boolean       @default(false)\n  createdById        String\n  createdBy          User          @relation(\"CalendarEventCreator\", fields: [createdById], references: [id])\n  createdAt          DateTime      @default(now())\n  updatedAt          DateTime      @updatedAt\n  audiences          EventAudience[]\n  rsvps              EventRsvp[]\n  @@index([startAt, endAt])\n}\n\nmodel EventAudience {\n  id              String        @id @default(cuid())\n  eventId         String\n  event           CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  type            AudienceType\n  refId           String?       // gradeLevelId | sectionId | courseId | Role name (ROLE); null for SCHOOL/STAFF\n  includeStudents Boolean       @default(true)\n  includeParents  Boolean       @default(true)\n  includeTeachers Boolean       @default(true)\n  @@index([eventId])\n  @@index([type, refId])                                        // D-2\n}\n\nmodel EventRsvp {\n  eventId   String\n  event     CalendarEvent @relation(fields: [eventId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  userId    String\n  user      User          @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  response  RsvpResponse\n  guests    Int           @default(0)\n  note      String?\n  createdAt DateTime      @default(now())\n  updatedAt DateTime      @updatedAt\n  @@id([eventId, userId])\n}\n\nmodel CalendarFeedToken {\n  userId    String   @id\n  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)\n  tokenHash String   @unique\n  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n}\n```\n\nExact field lists for `EventRsvp` follow PRD §FR-1. The dev agent copies any field this sketch omits from `14-calendar.md` L139-148. Traces to FR-2, FR-3, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-8.\n\n### 2.3 Server modules\n\n| File | Exports | Notes | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/announcements/audience.ts` (new, PRD-12 path) | `resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences)`, `isUserInAudience(user, audiences)`, `audienceWhereForUser(user)` (Prisma `EventAudience` filter), `canTargetAudience(user, audience)` | Semantics are those of PRD-12 FR-2. `audienceWhereForUser` precomputes the user's keys once: their grade levels, sections and courses, the same for linked children (parents), the courses they teach and the sections they homeroom (teachers), and their role. It returns an `OR` over `{type, refId, include*}` so filtering happens in SQL (NFR-4). `canTargetAudience`: ADMIN → any. TEACHER → `COURSE` passes `assertCanManageCourse`, or `SECTION` where `homeroomTeacherId === user.id`. Everything else → false. | FR-3, FR-6, FR-7, FR-28, FR-29, FR-23, NFR-4, NFR-7 |\n| `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` (new, pure) | `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` | Steps in school-tz wall clock: +7 days, or +1 month on the same day of month, skipping months that lack the day. Duration is kept in wall-clock terms. Stops at the earlier of `recurrenceUntil` (end of that day, inclusive) and `to`. Occurrence id = `${eventId}:${occurrenceStartISO}`. | FR-15, FR-4, NFR-3, ADR-3 |\n| `src/server/calendar/ical.ts` (new, pure) | `escapeText`, `foldLine`, `vtimezone(tz, from, to)`, `vevent(item, tz)`, `buildCalendar(items, tz, window)` | All-day events use `VALUE=DATE` with an exclusive `DTEND`. Timed one-off events use UTC `Z`. Recurring events use `TZID` + `RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY|MONTHLY;UNTIL=…Z` (+`BYMONTHDAY`). Deadlines are zero-duration VEVENTs with `URL`. Lines are CRLF and folded at 75 octets. | FR-12, FR-26, NFR-3, NFR-6, ADR-5 |\n| `src/server/calendar/calendar-service.ts` (new) | `getEvent`, `createEvent`, `updateEvent`, `deleteEvent`, `upsertRsvp`, `listRsvps`, `isSchoolDay`, `noSchoolDays(from,to)`, `createTermBreaks(yearId, actor)`, `getOrCreateFeedToken`, `resetFeedToken`, `findUserByFeedToken` | Owns every per-entity check (NFR-7). **Imports nothing from timetable-service** (R2). It reads `prisma.schoolDay` directly, and timetable-service imports *from* it. | FR-5..8, FR-16, FR-20..23, FR-25, FR-33, FR-34, FR-36 |\n| `src/server/calendar/sources.ts` (new) | `getCalendarItems`, `getPublicEvents`, `getUpcomingEventsForUser` | The merge in §3.1. It may import timetable-service, the assignment and quiz services, and calendar-service, because nothing imports it back except routes (R2). | FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-30..32 |\n| `src/server/calendar/maintenance.ts` (new) | `sendRsvpReminders(now)` | Selects events with `rsvpEnabled`, `rsvpDeadline ∈ (now, now+48h]` and `rsvpReminderSentAt = null`. For each, claims it via `updateMany({where:{id, rsvpReminderSentAt:null}, data:{rsvpReminderSentAt:now}})`. If `count===1`, resolves the audience minus existing RSVP userIds and calls `notify('event.rsvp_reminder')`. | FR-23, ADR-11 |\n| `src/lib/validators/calendar.ts` (new, client-safe) | `eventInputSchema`, `eventPatchSchema`, `rsvpSchema`, `calendarQuerySchema`, `schoolDayQuerySchema`, `publicEventsQuerySchema` | Rules: title ≤ 150; description ≤ 5000; `endAt ≥ startAt`; `recurrenceUntil` required for WEEKLY/MONTHLY and ≤ start + 1 year; guests 0–5; range `to − from ≤ 100 days`; `sources ⊆ {events, holidays, assignments, quizzes, timetable}`. All-day input is `yyyy-MM-dd` start and inclusive end. The **server** converts it to `[schoolMidnight(start), schoolMidnight(end+1))`. | FR-4, FR-21, FR-32, NFR-8 |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts` (edit) | add `schoolMidnight(dateStr, tz)`, `schoolDateOf(instant, tz)` | Pure and client-safe. The single source of all-day and date conversions. | FR-4, FR-16, NFR-3, ADR-4 |\n\n### 2.4 Edits to existing modules\n\n| File | Change | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts` | At both `// PRD-14 holidays hook` lines, replace the inline `schoolDay` weekday check with `if (!(await isSchoolDay(date)).isSchoolDay) return [];`. The weekday rule now lives only in `isSchoolDay`, so the old check is deleted, not duplicated. The return type is unchanged. | FR-16, FR-17, NFR-9 |\n| `src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts` | `getToday` and `getOverview` add `noSchoolReason: string \\| null` from `isSchoolDay`. The register save path rejects with `VALIDATION_ERROR` \"holidayOverride required\" when the date is not a school day and `holidayOverride !== true` (D-8). | FR-18 |\n| Attendance landing + `RegisterForm.tsx` | Landing shows \"No classes today — <reason>\". The register shows a warning `Alert` banner, and the save button opens `ConfirmDialog` \"Record attendance on a holiday anyway\", which sends `holidayOverride: true`. | FR-18, NFR-1 |\n| Teacher/student/parent Today views (those consuming `getScheduleForDate`) | When `isSchoolDay` is false, show the holiday name instead of the empty class list. | FR-17 |\n| `AssignmentForm.tsx`, `QuizSettingsPanel.tsx` | On a `dueAt`/`availableUntil` change, `fetch('/api/school-day?date=')`. If false, show a non-blocking `<Alert severity=\"warning\">This date is a holiday (<title>).</Alert>`. Save is unchanged. | FR-19, FR-34 |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | Add `event.created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail false), `event.holiday_created` (COMMUNICATION, defaultEmail true), `event.updated` (COMMUNICATION, false) and `event.rsvp_reminder` (COMMUNICATION, false). All roles. | FR-23, FR-28, FR-29 |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | Add an isolated `try { await sendRsvpReminders(now) } catch (e) { logger.error(...) }` block, matching the quiz-maintenance block. | FR-23, NFR-9 |\n| `src/config/navigation.ts` | `{ label: 'Calendar', href: '/calendar', icon: CalendarMonth, roles: ALL_ROLES }`. `/account/calendar` gets no sidebar entry, as with the other `/account/*` pages. It is reached from the account area and a \"Subscribe\" link on `/calendar`. | FR-35 |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` | `seedCalendar()`, idempotent: match by title (+ startAt where it is stable). It seeds the 7 events from FR-37 and the ROBOTICS course if absent (D-7). \"Sports day\" has no announcement link. Grade 6–8 exams use three `GRADE_LEVEL` audiences. \"Grade 7 parents\" = `GRADE_LEVEL` with only `includeParents`. | FR-37 |\n\n### 2.5 Route handlers (thin: requireUser/requireRole → Zod parse → service → `ok`/`apiError`)\n\n| Route | Auth | Service call | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `GET /api/calendar?from&to&sources&studentId` | any user | `getCalendarItems` | FR-10, FR-11, FR-32, NFR-7 |\n| `POST /api/events` | ADMIN, TEACHER | `createEvent` | FR-5..7, FR-14, FR-28, FR-33 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id` | visible to user | `getEvent` (+`myRsvp`, totals, `canEdit`) | FR-12, FR-22, FR-33 |\n| `PATCH /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `updateEvent` | FR-6..8, FR-29, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `DELETE /api/events/:id` | creator, ADMIN | `deleteEvent` | FR-8, FR-33, FR-36 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id/ics` | visible to user | `getEvent` → `buildCalendar([event])` | FR-12, FR-33 |\n| `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` | audience member | `upsertRsvp` | FR-21 |\n| `GET /api/events/:id/rsvps[?format=csv]` | creator, ADMIN | `listRsvps` → JSON or `csv.ts` | FR-22 |\n| `GET /api/me/calendar-feed` | any user | `getOrCreateFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `POST /api/me/calendar-feed/reset` | any user | `resetFeedToken` | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `GET /api/calendar/feed/[token]` (`.ics` stripped from param) | token | `findUserByFeedToken` → `rateLimit` → `getCalendarItems` → `buildCalendar` | FR-26, FR-27, NFR-5, NFR-6 |\n| `GET /api/school-day?date=` (new singular folder; `/api/school-days` untouched) | any user | `isSchoolDay` | FR-16, FR-19, FR-34 |\n| `GET /api/public/events?from&to` | public, IP rate limit | `getPublicEvents` | FR-30, D-9 |\n| `POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` | ADMIN | `createTermBreaks` | FR-20 |\n\nError mapping: not visible → 404 `NOT_FOUND`. Visible but not permitted → 403 `FORBIDDEN`. RSVP after the deadline, or with RSVP disabled → 409 `CONFLICT`. Feed token unknown → plain 404. Feed over the limit → 429 `RATE_LIMITED` + `Retry-After`. `arch-api-contracts` defines the exact shapes.\n\n### 2.6 UI\n\n| Path / component | Contents | Reqs |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/app/(app)/calendar/page.tsx` (server) → `CalendarView.tsx` (client) | `requirePageUser`. `<EventCalendar>` from `@mui/x-scheduler/event-calendar`: `views={['month','week','agenda']}`, week `startTime:7, endTime:19`, agenda `dayCount:30`, `displayTimezone={tz}`, `readOnly`, `eventCreation={false}`. The default view is month at `useMediaQuery('(min-width:768px)')`, agenda below that. Controlled `events`, refetched on `onVisibleDateChange`/`onViewChange` with plain `fetch` and a small Map cache keyed by `from|to|sources|studentId`. The page opens the drawer when `?event=<id>` is present (notification links). | FR-9, FR-10, NFR-1, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-12 |\n| `SourceChips` | MUI `Chip`s: School events · My assignments · My quizzes · My timetable (Week view only) · Holidays. Stored in `localStorage['calendar.sources']`. Holidays = HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK/`isNoSchool`; School events = everything else, with no overlap. `timetable` is fetched only in Week view. | FR-10 |\n| Child filter (PARENT only) | `Select`: \"All children\" or one child → `studentId`. Deadline titles get the child's name prefixed by the server. | FR-11 |\n| `EventDrawer` | Right-anchored `Drawer`: title, category `Chip`, time in school tz, location, `MarkdownView` description, audience chips, RSVP controls (`ToggleButtonGroup` + guests `TextField` for parents + note; disabled after the deadline), \"Add to my calendar\" (`<a href=\"/api/events/:id/ics\" download>`), and edit/delete when `canEdit` (delete via `ConfirmDialog`). Creator/admin see an RSVP `DataTable` + CSV link. | FR-12, FR-21, FR-22, NFR-1 |\n| Deadline click | `onEventEditingStart` → `cancel()` → `router.push(item.href)` | FR-13 |\n| `EventEditorDialog` | \"New event\" button (ADMIN/TEACHER). React Hook Form + `eventInputSchema`. Fields: title, category (HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK only for admins), all-day switch, date/time pickers (`@mui/x-date-pickers`), location, `MarkdownEditor`, `AudienceBuilder`, recurrence select + until date, RSVP switch + deadline, and admin-only `isNoSchool`/`isPublic`. Results go through `useToast`. | FR-4..7, FR-14 |\n| `src/components/AudienceBuilder/` (new shared) | Rows of type `Select` + entity `Autocomplete` (grade level / section / course / role) + three include `Checkbox`es. Types are filtered by `canTargetAudience` rules on the client. The server stays authoritative. | FR-3, FR-7, FR-14 |\n| `src/app/(app)/account/calendar/page.tsx` | \"Subscribe\" card: URL `TextField` (read-only) + copy (`navigator.clipboard`), Google/Apple/Outlook instructions as static text, and \"Reset link\" behind `ConfirmDialog`. When `url` is null: \"Reset link to get a new URL\" (D-6). | FR-24, FR-25 |\n| `src/app/(app)/admin/academic-years/[id]/page.tsx` | `requirePageRole('ADMIN')`. Year name, read-only term list (existing terms service), and an \"Add term breaks\" button + `ConfirmDialog` that shows the number of breaks created via toast. | FR-20 |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Flow\n\n### 3.1 Calendar read (`GET /api/calendar`, the feed, upcoming events)\n\n```\nroute → calendarQuerySchema (≤100 days) → getCalendarItems(user, {from,to,sources,studentId})\n  1. scope   = studentId ? resolveViewedStudent(user, studentId) : getAccessibleStudentIds(user)   (404 for others)\n  2. where   = audienceWhereForUser(user, scope)          // keys computed once\n  3. Promise.all([\n       events:      CalendarEvent where startAt < to AND (endAt > from OR (recurrence≠NONE AND recurrenceUntil ≥ from))\n                    AND (audiences some where) OR createdById=user  (ADMIN: no audience filter)\n                    → expandOccurrences(e, from, to, tz) → split into holidays / events by category+isNoSchool,\n       assignments: existing assignment service, PUBLISHED, dueAt ∈ [from,to), scoped students/courses,\n       quizzes:     existing quiz service, PUBLISHED, availableUntil ∈ [from,to),\n       timetable:   getPersonalTimetable(target) projected onto dates in range, skipping noSchoolDays(from,to)\n     ]) – only for requested sources\n  4. map → CalendarItem union {kind:'event'|'assignment'|'quiz'|'timetable', id, title, start, end, allDay, color, href?, childName?}\n```\nThe feed calls the same function with `from=now−30d, to=now+365d`, sources minus timetable, and recurring events **unexpanded**. Instead of occurrences it gets the series rows so it can emit RRULE. The 100-day cap is skipped because the call is internal. Traces to FR-10, FR-11, FR-15, FR-26, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-4, NFR-5.\n\n### 3.2 Event write\n\n```\nPOST/PATCH → eventInputSchema → createEvent/updateEvent(user, input)\n  - FR-6: non-admin + (isNoSchool | isPublic | HOLIDAY | TERM_BREAK) → 403\n  - FR-7: every audience must pass canTargetAudience(user, a) → else 403\n  - FR-8: PATCH/DELETE requires createdById===user.id or ADMIN\n  - FR-5: isNoSchool ??= category ∈ {HOLIDAY, TERM_BREAK}\n  - all-day → schoolMidnight conversion (FR-4)\n  - prisma.$transaction: event + replace audiences\n  - after commit:\n      FR-36 audit() if ADMIN && createdById≠user.id (update/delete)\n      FR-28 create: first occurrence within 30 days → notify(HOLIDAY|TERM_BREAK ? 'event.holiday_created' : 'event.created',\n            resolveAudienceUserIds(audiences) − creator, link '/calendar?event=<id>')\n      FR-29 update: startAt|endAt|allDay|location changed AND event upcoming → notify('event.updated') once\n```\n\n### 3.3 Audience resolution (PRD-12 FR-2 semantics)\n\n| Type | refId | Students (`includeStudents`) | Parents (`includeParents`) | Teachers (`includeTeachers`) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SCHOOL | null | all active users | | |\n| STAFF | null | ADMIN + TEACHER | | |\n| ROLE | role name | users with that role | | |\n| GRADE_LEVEL | gradeLevelId | `StudentProfile.gradeLevelId = refId` | their `ParentStudentLink` parents | teachers of current-year courses in sections of that grade |\n| SECTION | sectionId | current-year `SectionMember`s | their parents | homeroom teacher + teachers of courses in the section |\n| COURSE | courseId | ACTIVE `Enrollment`s | their parents | `teacherId` + `coTeacherIds` |\n\nOnly ACTIVE, non-archived users count. `isUserInAudience` and `audienceWhereForUser` give the same answer as `resolveAudienceUserIds`. A property-style integration test loops over every seed user to check this (PRD-12 test requirement). Traces to FR-3, FR-7, NFR-7.\n\n### 3.4 School-day check\n\n```\nisSchoolDay(date) → d = schoolDateOf(date, tz), isoDay\n  1. SchoolDay[isoDay].isTeaching ?? isoDay ≤ 5   → false, reason 'Not a teaching day'\n  2. isNoSchool events with a SCHOOL audience where startAt < midnight(d+1) AND (endAt > midnight(d) OR recurring)\n     → expandOccurrences within that day → first hit → false, reason 'Holiday: <title>'\n  3. → { isSchoolDay: true, reason: null }\nnoSchoolDays(from, to) = one query, same rules, returns Map<date, reason> (used by the timetable source; avoids N calls)\n```\nCallers: timetable-service (FR-17), attendance (FR-18), `/api/school-day` (FR-19, FR-34), timetable source in §3.1. Traces to FR-16..19, FR-34.\n\n### 3.5 RSVP\n\n`PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp` → `rsvpSchema` → `upsertRsvp`:\n1. Check the event is visible and `rsvpEnabled`. Otherwise 404 (not visible) or 409.\n2. Require `isUserInAudience`. Otherwise 403.\n3. Require `now < rsvpDeadline`. Otherwise 409.\n4. If the user is not a PARENT, force `guests = 0`.\n5. Upsert on `(eventId, userId)`.\n\nA recurring event has one RSVP for the whole series. The drawer gets `myRsvp` and totals `{yes, no, maybe, guests}` from `GET /api/events/:id`. Creator and admin read the full list via `/rsvps`, or `?format=csv` via `csv.ts`. Traces to FR-21, FR-22.\n\n### 3.6 Reminder job\n\nCron `POST /api/internal/email/dispatch` → `sendRsvpReminders(now)` → claim → audience − responders → `notify('event.rsvp_reminder', link '/calendar?event=<id>')`. Traces to FR-23.\n\n### 3.7 iCal feed\n\n```\nGET /api/calendar/feed/<token>.ics\n  token = param.replace(/\\.ics$/, '') → hashToken(token) → CalendarFeedToken by tokenHash (unique) → user ACTIVE?\n    no → 404 text/plain\n  rateLimit('calfeed:'+hash, 60, 3_600_000) → !ok → 429 + Retry-After\n  items = getCalendarItems(user, feed window, series mode)\n  body  = buildCalendar(items, tz, window)   // VTIMEZONE for transitions in window, RRULE for series\n  200 text/calendar; charset=utf-8, Cache-Control: private, max-age=900\n```\nToken lifecycle:\n- `getOrCreateFeedToken` creates the row on first use from `randomBytes(32).toString('base64url')`, stores `hashToken(raw)`, and returns the URL once.\n- `resetFeedToken` upserts a new hash, so the old URL returns 404 immediately.\n- No raw token is ever logged.\n\nTraces to FR-24..27, NFR-5, NFR-6, ADR-6, ADR-7.\n\n### 3.8 Public and dashboard hooks\n\n- `getPublicEvents(from, to)`: `isPublic` events, expanded, returning only public-safe fields (id, title, category, start, end, allDay, location, description). Traces to FR-30.\n- `getUpcomingEventsForUser(user, limit)`: `getCalendarItems(user, now..now+90d, ['events','holidays'])`, sorted, then the first `limit` items. No UI. Traces to FR-31, NFR-11.\n\n### 3.9 Term breaks\n\n`POST /api/academic-years/:id/term-breaks` (ADMIN) → `createTermBreaks`:\n1. Order the terms by `startDate`.\n2. For each consecutive pair where `next.start > prev.end + 1 day`, create an all-day TERM_BREAK with `isNoSchool=true` and a SCHOOL audience, from `prev.end+1` (inclusive) to `next.start` (exclusive).\n3. Skip any gap that already has a TERM_BREAK with the same span. This makes the call idempotent.\n4. Return `{ created }`.\n5. Write an `audit()` entry.\n\nTraces to FR-20.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-cutting\n\n- **Time (NFR-3, NFR-8).**\n  - Storage is in UTC. Display uses `SchoolSettings.timezone`, read via the existing `getSchoolTimezone()`. No third copy is created.\n  - All-day events run from school-tz midnight with an exclusive end.\n  - Expansion steps in wall-clock time.\n  - The feed uses `VALUE=DATE` for all-day events and `TZID` + VTIMEZONE for series.\n  - The scheduler gets `displayTimezone`.\n  - One DST-week test fixture (America/New_York 2026-11-01, or the seed tz) runs through the expansion, the all-day path and the feed.\n- **Security (NFR-5, NFR-7).**\n  - Every route calls `requireUser`/`requireRole`, except the feed (hashed token) and public events (public fields only, IP limit).\n  - Per-entity checks live in calendar-service.\n  - Students see only themselves, and parents only their linked children (`getAccessibleStudentIds` / `resolveViewedStudent`).\n  - A non-visible event returns 404, so its existence doesn't leak.\n- **Performance (NFR-4).**\n  - A parent with 3 children in month view needs about 6 indexed queries, run in parallel.\n  - The audience is filtered in SQL, and holidays are found with one `noSchoolDays` query.\n  - There is no cache layer. Add one only if the Playwright timing or a measurement exceeds 500 ms.\n- **UI rules (NFR-1, NFR-12).**\n  - Only MUI, icons and MUI X (including the scheduler) are used. Toasts go through `useToast`, side panels through `Drawer`, and confirmations through `ConfirmDialog`/`Dialog`.\n  - English only. The breakpoint is 768 px.\n- **Scope (NFR-11).**\n  - Out of scope: per-occurrence exceptions, room booking (`roomId` is stored and unused), two-way sync, and dashboard or public-site UI.\n- **Tests (NFR-10).**\n  - Unit tests:\n    - `expandOccurrences`: weekly, monthly on the 31st, the until bound, a DST week\n    - `isSchoolDay`: weekday, holiday, recurring no-school\n    - `ical`: escaping `, ; \\ \\n`, folding, RRULE, VALUE=DATE exclusive end, node-ical parse\n    - all-day conversion\n    - term-break gap math\n    - `canTargetAudience`\n  - Integration tests:\n    - calendar merge per role (admin, teacher, student, parent with 3 children)\n    - feed token reset (old URL 404, new URL 200 and node-ical-valid)\n    - RSVP deadline (409) and parent-only guests\n    - audience resolver parity across seed users\n    - teacher SCHOOL create → 403\n  - Playwright:\n    - an admin creates a holiday, and the student's Today view shows the holiday name\n    - a parent RSVPs\n    - the feed URL returns a valid ICS\n  - `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test` stays green.\n\n### Risks carried forward\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| R1 Beta scheduler API drift | Exact pin, MCP lookup before use, and the scheduler used only as a read-only display (ADR-2). The D-5 fallback is pre-agreed. |\n| R2 Import cycle between timetable and calendar | The edges run one way: timetable-service → calendar-service, and sources.ts → (timetable, assignments, quizzes, calendar-service). calendar-service reads teaching weekdays via `prisma.schoolDay` and never imports timetable-service. |\n| R3 DST correctness across 4 code paths | Shared pure helpers in `src/lib/dates.ts` plus one shared DST fixture. |\n| R4 Audience is both the hot path and the security boundary | A single implementation plus the parity test. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Requirements Traceability\n\n| Req | Design element(s) |\n|---|---|\n| FR-1 | §2.1 exact pin `@mui/x-scheduler@9.0.0-beta.15` + scoped override (ADR-1) |\n| FR-2 | §2.2 migration `20261113000000_add_calendar`: enums, 4 models, cascades, `[startAt,endAt]` index |\n| FR-3 | §2.2 `AudienceType` (PRD-12 values); §2.3 `announcements/audience.ts`; §3.3 resolution table |\n| FR-4 | §2.3 `validators/calendar.ts` + `schoolMidnight`; §3.2 all-day conversion |\n| FR-5 | §3.2 `isNoSchool ??= HOLIDAY/TERM_BREAK` in `createEvent` |\n| FR-6 | §3.2 admin-only field check; §2.6 editor hides admin fields |\n| FR-7 | §2.3 `canTargetAudience`; §3.2 check on create/patch |\n| FR-8 | §3.2 creator/ADMIN guard on PATCH/DELETE |\n| FR-9 | §2.6 `CalendarView` with `EventCalendar` views/viewConfig/breakpoint; D-5 agenda fallback |\n| FR-10 | §2.6 `SourceChips` + localStorage; §3.1 `sources` param, holidays/events split |\n| FR-11 | §2.6 parent child filter; §3.1 `studentId` scope + `childName` |\n| FR-12 | §2.6 `EventDrawer`; §2.5 `GET /api/events/:id`, `/ics` |\n| FR-13 | §2.6 deadline click → `router.push(href)` |\n| FR-14 | §2.6 `EventEditorDialog` + `AudienceBuilder` |\n| FR-15 | §2.3 `recurrence.ts` `expandOccurrences`; §3.1 read-time expansion |\n| FR-16 | §2.3 `isSchoolDay`; §3.4 |\n| FR-17 | §2.4 timetable-service hook + Today views |\n| FR-18 | §2.4 attendance `noSchoolReason`, `holidayOverride` (D-8), `RegisterForm` banner/confirm |\n| FR-19 | §2.4 `AssignmentForm` / `QuizSettingsPanel` warning via `/api/school-day` |\n| FR-20 | §2.6 `/admin/academic-years/[id]` page; §2.5 term-breaks route; §3.9 `createTermBreaks` |\n| FR-21 | §2.5 `PUT /api/events/:id/rsvp`; §3.5 `upsertRsvp` rules |\n| FR-22 | §2.5 `/rsvps[?format=csv]`; §2.6 drawer totals + `DataTable` |\n| FR-23 | §2.3 `maintenance.ts`; §2.4 cron hook + type; D-1 `rsvpReminderSentAt` |\n| FR-24 | §2.6 `/account/calendar`; §2.5 me/calendar-feed routes |\n| FR-25 | §3.7 token lifecycle with `hashToken`; D-6 |\n| FR-26 | §2.3 `ical.ts`; §3.7 feed build (window, RRULE, VTIMEZONE, escaping) |\n| FR-27 | §2.5 feed route; §3.7 rate limit + Cache-Control |\n| FR-28 | §2.4 types `event.created` + `event.holiday_created` (D-3); §3.2 notify on create |\n| FR-29 | §2.4 type `event.updated`; §3.2 notify on time/location change |\n| FR-30 | §3.8 `getPublicEvents`; §2.5 `/api/public/events` (D-9) |\n| FR-31 | §3.8 `getUpcomingEventsForUser` |\n| FR-32 | §2.5 `GET /api/calendar`; §3.1 `getCalendarItems`; 100-day cap in validator |\n| FR-33 | §2.5 event CRUD + `/ics` routes |\n| FR-34 | §2.5 `GET /api/school-day` (singular, new folder) |\n| FR-35 | §2.4 `navigation.ts` Calendar entry |\n| FR-36 | §3.2 `audit()` on admin edits/deletes of other users' events |\n| FR-37 | §2.4 `seedCalendar()` + ROBOTICS course (D-7) |\n| NFR-1 | §2.6 MUI-only components; §4 UI rules |\n| NFR-2 | §2.1 MCP lookup gate before scheduler use |\n| NFR-3 | §2.3 wall-clock expansion, `dates.ts` helpers, ical VALUE=DATE/TZID; §4 DST fixture |\n| NFR-4 | §3.1 parallel indexed queries, SQL audience filter, D-2 index; §4 performance |\n| NFR-5 | §3.7 32-byte token, SHA-256 hash; §3.1 shared read path |\n| NFR-6 | §2.1 `node-ical` devDep; §4 parse tests |\n| NFR-7 | §2.5 auth column; §3.3; §4 security |\n| NFR-8 | §2.3 module layout under `src/server/calendar/`; thin routes; Zod; UTC storage |\n| NFR-9 | §1 reuse list; §2.4 edits instead of new helpers |\n| NFR-10 | §4 tests |\n| NFR-11 | §4 scope; §3.8 hooks only |\n| NFR-12 | §2.6 768 px breakpoint, English only |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TFouAbRyaNUFyWffQRAfUf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
