{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtXNh5dFV2dZEwhkHdDN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the SH-15 version of `artifacts/architect/system-design.md`, replacing the SH-14 file. It has the Overview, Component Breakdown, Data Flow and Requirements Traceability sections. All 56 requirements (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-10) appear in the traceability table, and every id cited exists in `requirements.json`.\n\n**Design calls you should know about:**\n- **Partly delivered:** three requirements depend on features from earlier tickets that aren't in the codebase.\n  - FR-13: the Announcements card shows an empty state, because there's no Announcement model yet (PRD-12).\n  - FR-35: booked conference slots show up as \"My meetings\" only on the child overview, because SH-14 never shipped calendar pages.\n  - FR-5: there's no calendar filter for the selected child, for the same reason.\n\n  None of these needs a schema change later; they fill in once PRD-12 and PRD-14 land.\n- **Not in the PRD's data model:** the design adds three columns it doesn't list. `ConferenceSlot.blocked` lets teachers block a slot without it coming back when they regenerate availability. `ConsentForm.lastRemindedAt` enforces the once-per-24-hours reminder limit. `ConsentForm.dueReminderSentAt` stops the 48-hour reminder going out twice. The migration also adds a database constraint so a child can book only one slot per teacher. All of this is listed as a deviation in the Overview.\n- **Parent landing page:** `/dashboard` now sends parents straight to `/my-children` after sign-in (FR-8).\n\nIntake reported no blockers. Its seven open questions are answered as assumptions in the Overview, following the stack decisions document (ADR-11 and ADR-12).\n\n`api-contracts.json`, `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` and `threat-model-notes.json` in `artifacts/architect/` are still the SH-14 versions. `arch-api-contracts` needs to run next to replace the first two and finish the architect phase. None of the sub-tasks writes `threat-model-notes.json`, so it will stay stale unless someone removes or regenerates it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11178,"cache_read_input_tokens":55305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11178},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eeb429-6a70-48e8-a0ff-b55a8b190b9d","uuid":"80752902-fb00-4b02-9f91-f5ba376284d7","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:18:37.283Z","request_id":"req_011CgtXNgdb6bh2DWW2MmDBY"}
