{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SKEyqutwsmXZcKMNm8aGuy","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (34.6KB). Full output saved to: /Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187/tool-results/b7bf5u2db.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\ntotal 192\ndrwxr-xr-x   9 ikramaansari  staff    288 Nov 10 09:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 ikramaansari  staff     96 Nov 10 09:28 .prev-SH-15\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  25803 Nov 10 08:30 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   2626 Nov 10 08:30 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  20056 Nov 10 09:30 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  24556 Nov 10 08:30 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  14295 Nov 10 09:29 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    397 Nov 10 08:30 threat-model-notes.json\n# System Design: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking, Consent Forms)\n\nTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-10), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-13), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights\n\nTicket: SH-16 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n> This file replaces the SH-15 version. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still from SH-15 until their own sub-tasks rewrite them.\n\n**Summary:** keep intake's detected stack (`react`, 98 %). It meets every FR/NFR. **No new runtime or dev dependencies.** All of the following are already installed and pinned in `package.json`: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, MUI 9.5.0 with `@mui/x-charts`, `@mui/x-data-grid` and `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, date-fns 3.6.0 with date-fns-tz 3.2.0, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 with `@axe-core/playwright` 4.10.0, and tsx 4.16.2.\n\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187","uuid":"d70e11b4-085e-4547-890e-3575383c26d1","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:30:25.115Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 192\ndrwxr-xr-x   9 ikramaansari  staff    288 Nov 10 09:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 ikramaansari  staff    384 Nov  9 16:57 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 ikramaansari  staff     96 Nov 10 09:28 .prev-SH-15\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  25803 Nov 10 08:30 api-contracts.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   2626 Nov 10 08:30 handoff-to-dev-planning.json\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  20056 Nov 10 09:30 requirements-analysis-notes.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  24556 Nov 10 08:30 system-design.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  14295 Nov 10 09:29 tech-stack-decisions.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff    397 Nov 10 08:30 threat-model-notes.json\n# System Design: PRD-15 Parent Portal (Child Switcher, Absence Notes, Conference Booking, Consent Forms)\n\nTicket: SH-15 · Phase: architect (arch-design-system) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\nInputs: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (FR-1 to FR-46, NFR-1 to NFR-10), `artifacts/intake/handoff-to-architect.json`, `artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md` (ADR-1 to ADR-13), `artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md`.\n# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights\n\nTicket: SH-16 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n> This file replaces the SH-15 version. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still from SH-15 until their own sub-tasks rewrite them.\n\n**Summary:** keep intake's detected stack (`react`, 98 %). It meets every FR/NFR. **No new runtime or dev dependencies.** All of the following are already installed and pinned in `package.json`: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, MUI 9.5.0 with `@mui/x-charts`, `@mui/x-data-grid` and `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, date-fns 3.6.0 with date-fns-tz 3.2.0, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 with `@axe-core/playwright` 4.10.0, and tsx 4.16.2.\n\nVerified in the codebase: `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/` do not exist yet. There is no `unstable_cache` or `revalidateTag` usage, no React error boundary, and no `seed:large` script. `@mui/x-charts` is already used in `QuizAnalytics.tsx`. `src/lib/dates.ts` and `src/server/csv.ts` already provide the timezone and CSV helpers.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context:** NFR-8 (brownfield reuse), NFR-4 (MUI-only UI), and NFR-10 (lint/typecheck/test stay green). The new features are dashboards, charts, tables, aggregate queries, a rule engine, caching and a seed script, and the installed stack covers all of them.\n\n**Decision:** Use only installed packages. Do not add charting, error-boundary, faker, cron, cache or date libraries.\n\n**Consequences:** No lockfile churn and no new attack surface. The few small helpers we still need are covered in ADR-4 and ADR-10.\n\n## ADR-2: Use async Server Components for widgets, each in Suspense with a per-widget error boundary\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-2 and NFR-1 (first content in under 1.5 s). Next.js 14's `error.tsx` works at route-segment level, so it cannot isolate one widget's failure. React 18 has no built-in component-level error boundary, and none exists in `src/` yet.\n\n**Decision:**\n- `/dashboard/page.tsx` stays a server component. It checks the role, keeps the PARENT redirect to `/my-children`, and renders one of three role dashboards (FR-1).\n- Each widget is an `async` server component that loads its own data and is wrapped in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` (reuse `src/components/LoadingSkeleton`), so widgets stream independently.\n- Add one small client `WidgetErrorBoundary`: a class component of about 25 lines using `getDerivedStateFromError`. It renders an MUI `Alert` with the text \"This widget could not load\" and a \"Retry\" `Button` that resets its state and calls `router.refresh()`. It lives in `src/components/WidgetErrorBoundary/` and is the only new shared component (FR-2).\n\n**Consequences:** One slow widget, such as at-risk, does not block the others. Widgets read data through server-side services directly, not through `/api/dashboard/*`. The FR-41 GET endpoints are thin JSON wrappers around the same service functions, for API parity and tests.\n\n## ADR-3: Cache aggregates with `unstable_cache`, using role-scoped keys and tags\n\n**Context:** FR-23, FR-24, NFR-1 and NFR-12. Next.js 14.2 provides `unstable_cache(fn, keyParts, { revalidate, tags })` and `revalidateTag()`.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Wrap the expensive reads in `src/server/dashboards/insights.ts`: admin KPIs, the attendance trend, the enrollment and grade distributions, and risk summaries and lists.\n- Use `revalidate: 900` (15 minutes) and `3600` (60 minutes) for at-risk data.\n- Key parts must include the scope: `['admin']`, or `['teacher', teacherId]` for teacher-scoped data. This keeps one teacher's cached data out of another teacher's view (NFR-3).\n- Tags: `dashboard:admin`, `dashboard:teacher`, `dashboard:student` and `insights:at-risk`.\n- `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` (ADMIN only) calls `revalidateTag` for each tag after it triggers the risk recompute (ADR-6).\n- Each cached function returns `{ data, computedAt: ISO string }`, and the widget shows \"Updated N min ago\" from `computedAt` (FR-24).\n\n**Consequences:**\n- `unstable_cache` serializes results to JSON, so cached values must not contain `Date` objects; use ISO strings.\n- The cache lives in each Next.js server process, which is acceptable for a single-node deployment.\n- `ponytail:` ceiling: with several app instances each one has its own cache, and Refresh only clears the instance that handles the request. Add a shared cache handler if the app is scaled out.\n- Per-user student widgets (FR-10 to FR-15) are cheap, single-student queries and are **not** cached. That avoids one cache entry per student.\n\n## ADR-4: Use MUI X Charts, the shared DataTable, and visually hidden data for accessibility\n\n**Context:** FR-15 to FR-19, FR-33 to FR-39, NFR-2, NFR-4 and NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Use `LineChart` (FR-17 and the report trends), `BarChart` (FR-18 stacked by gender, the FR-19 histogram, and the reports) and `Gauge` (FR-15), all from `@mui/x-charts` 9.5.0.\n- Draw the FR-17 threshold with the chart's reference-line component, `ChartsReferenceLine`.\n- All tables use the existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid).\n- Charts are client components that receive serializable props from the server.\n- For NFR-2, every chart gets an `aria-label` summary built on the server, for example \"Attendance trend: 94.2 % average, lowest 88.1 % on 3 Oct\". It also gets a visually hidden MUI `Table` built with the `visuallyHidden` style from `@mui/utils`, which comes with `@mui/material`.\n- Series use labels and distinct marks or patterns, not colour alone.\n- Per NFR-5, the dev phase must look up each component through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` and `fetchDocs`, version 9.5.0) before using it. If MCP is unavailable, that is a blocker.\n\n**Consequences:** No Recharts, Tailwind or shadcn (NFR-4). Each chart duplicates its data once, for the hidden table, which is trivial at these data sizes.\n\n## ADR-5: Implement risk scoring as rule-based pure functions plus a Prisma snapshot with embedded capped history\n\n**Context:** FR-25 to FR-28, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-9 and NFR-11 (no ML). FR-28 is LOW confidence because \"one row per student per term, upserted\" conflicts with the trend arrow and history requirements.\n\n**Decision:**\n- `src/server/dashboards/risk.ts` exports pure, database-free functions `attendanceSignal`, `gradesSignal`, `missingSignal` and `overallLevel`. They take numbers and return `'HIGH' | 'MEDIUM' | null` plus a reason string. That makes the NFR-9 boundary tests plain Vitest tables.\n- A separate loader, `computeRiskInputs(termId, studentIds)`, fetches data in bulk, using a fixed number of queries per run rather than per student.\n- **FR-28 resolution:** keep `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on `StudentRiskSnapshot`. Add `previousLevel RiskLevel?` and `history Json`, a list of `{ level, computedAt, reasons }` capped at the last 10 **level changes**. Unchanged recomputes update `computedAt` only, so hourly runs do not flood the history. The trend arrow compares `level` with `previousLevel`, and the Insights tab renders `history`.\n- Add `highNotifiedAt DateTime?` to enforce the FR-32 rule of at most one notification per 14 days without querying the Notification table.\n- New enum `RiskLevel { MEDIUM HIGH }`. `none` is stored as a `null` level.\n- The \"Missing\" count reuses the definition from `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`: published, due within the last 30 days, no submission, not exempt, and `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION`.\n- A student with no data has no signal.\n\n**Consequences:** One table and one migration, with no separate history table. History is limited to 10 level changes, which is enough for a \"short history\". `ponytail:` add a `StudentRiskSnapshotHistory` table if long-range trend analytics are ever needed.\n\n## ADR-6: Hook the hourly recompute into the existing internal dispatch cron, gated in the database\n\n**Context:** FR-27 and NFR-12. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs the maintenance passes, each in its own try/catch. It currently gates the daily purge with an in-memory `lastPurgeAt`, which does not survive restarts or work across instances.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Add a `recomputeRiskSnapshots()` call in its own try/catch block.\n- Gate it with `max(computedAt)` from `StudentRiskSnapshot` for the current term: skip the run if the latest snapshot is less than 60 minutes old.\n- Admin Refresh bypasses the gate.\n- On completion, call `revalidateTag('insights:at-risk')`.\n- Notifications use the existing `notify()` with the new type `insights.student_high_risk` (default email on). The type is registered wherever notification types and preferences are declared.\n\n**Consequences:** No new scheduler. The \"at most once per hour\" rule holds across restarts and instances because it is gated in the database.\n\n## ADR-7: Use Prisma aggregates first and parameterized `$queryRaw` for time-bucketed reports\n\n**Context:** FR-16 to FR-22, FR-34 to FR-39 and NFR-1 (reports in under 3 s on 600 students over one school year).\n\n**Decision:**\n- Use `groupBy`, `count` and `aggregate` for simple counts.\n- Use tagged-template `prisma.$queryRaw` (parameterized only, never `$queryRawUnsafe`) where Prisma cannot group by date or bucket. That covers the daily attendance rate over 30 school days, the 10 % grade histogram with median (`percentile_cont`), monthly enrollments and archives, and on-time, late and missing rates.\n- Bucket dates in SQL with `AT TIME ZONE $tz` (NFR-7).\n- The attendance report (FR-35) and course percentages (FR-13, FR-19, FR-36) must call the existing `attendance-service.ts` and the gradebook `grade-calc.ts` and `student-grades-service.ts`, so the numbers match the Grades tab.\n- Dev should check with `EXPLAIN` against `seed:large` and add indexes only where a query is slow. `AttendanceRecord @@index([studentId, createdAt])` already exists.\n\n**Consequences:** A small amount of raw SQL, kept in the `src/server/reports/` and `src/server/dashboards/` services and covered by NFR-9 integration tests with known totals.\n\n## ADR-8: Validate with Zod, keep handlers thin, export CSV through the existing helper, and enforce access server-side\n\n**Context:** FR-30, FR-33, FR-41 to FR-44, NFR-3 and NFR-6.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Put the schemas in `src/lib/validators/dashboards.ts` and `src/lib/validators/reports.ts`.\n- `reportKey` is a `z.enum([...6 keys])`, and an unknown key returns a 404 `NOT_FOUND`.\n- Handlers use the existing `withHandler`, `ok` and `AppError` from `src/server/http.ts`.\n- `?format=csv` goes through `toCsv` and `escapeCsvCell` in `src/server/csv.ts`, which already protects against formula injection, using the same column list as the table.\n- Teacher scope = `getAccessibleStudentIds()`. Filters are applied as an intersection with that set, so they can never widen it (FR-42).\n\n**Consequences:** No new HTTP or CSV code.\n\n## ADR-9: Do all date logic in the school timezone with date-fns-tz through `src/lib/dates.ts`\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-4, FR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-17 and NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Reuse `schoolNow`, `schoolDateOf`, `schoolMidnight`, `addDateDays`, `nowAndNext` (for the Now/Next badges) and `formatInSchoolTz`.\n- Add a `greetingFor(now, tz)` helper next to them, and a \"school days\" helper that reads the existing teaching-days and holiday data.\n\n**Consequences:** One timezone source of truth. Timestamps stay in UTC in the database.\n\n## ADR-10: Write a deterministic large seed as a tsx script with an inline PRNG\n\n**Context:** FR-45, FR-46 and NFR-1. The existing seed runs with `tsx prisma/seed.ts` through `db:seed`. Faker is not installed.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Add `prisma/seed-large.ts` and the npm script `\"seed:large\": \"tsx prisma/seed-large.ts\"`.\n- Use an inline mulberry32 PRNG (about 6 lines) with a fixed seed, plus fixed name lists, instead of adding faker.\n- Use `createMany` in batches for 600 students, 40 teachers and 60 school days of attendance, assignments and grades.\n- The default `prisma/seed.ts` stays small but must create at least 3 students at each risk level (High, Medium and none) by planting attendance, grades and missing work that cross the FR-25 thresholds (FR-46).\n\n**Consequences:** Results are reproducible, and there is no new dependency.\n\n## ADR-11: Handle missing upstream data sources with empty states and direct reads instead of fixes outside scope\n\n**Context:** FR-8, FR-14, FR-21 and FR-38. There is no `Announcement` model (PRD-12) and no calendar service (PRD-14). NFR-11 says not to modify other PRDs' behaviour.\n\n**Decision:**\n- **Announcements:** FR-8 and FR-14 render the existing `EmptyState` with the text \"Announcements not available\". FR-38 omits the read-rate metric and its column note says \"not available\". Expose this through one `announcementsAvailable = false` guard in the dashboards service, so it is a one-line change once PRD-12 ships the model.\n- **Events:** FR-21 reads `CalendarEvent` directly with a small Prisma query: school-wide, `start >= now`, ordered by start, `take: 5`. It does not expand recurrences. The existing `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` can be wired in later.\n\n**Consequences:** These requirements are implemented in degraded form, not blocked. This is recorded as a dependency gap for `system-design.md`. Intake reported no blockers.\n\n---\n\n## Requirement → ADR map\n\n| ADR | Requirements |\n|---|---|\n| ADR-1 | NFR-4, NFR-8, NFR-10 |\n| ADR-2 | FR-1, FR-2, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| ADR-3 | FR-23, FR-24, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-12 |\n| ADR-4 | FR-15, FR-16, FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-29, FR-33–FR-39, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-5 |\n| ADR-5 | FR-7, FR-20, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| ADR-6 | FR-24, FR-27, FR-32, NFR-12 |\n| ADR-7 | FR-5, FR-6, FR-12, FR-13, FR-16–FR-22, FR-34–FR-39, NFR-1, NFR-7, NFR-9 |\n| ADR-8 | FR-30, FR-33, FR-40, FR-41–FR-44, NFR-3, NFR-6 |\n| ADR-9 | FR-3, FR-4, FR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n| ADR-10 | FR-45, FR-46, NFR-1, NFR-9 |\n| ADR-11 | FR-8, FR-14, FR-21, FR-38, NFR-11 |\n\nFR-9 (quick-action links) and FR-40 (navigation entries) are plain MUI links and config edits in `src/config/navigation.ts` and `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, and need no stack decision.\n# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-16\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-10T12:00:00Z), PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights. It has 46 FRs and 12 NFRs (58 requirements) at 91% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers** and 7 warnings. §3 proposes a default for each open question so that `arch-design-system` can decide.\nThe previous SH-15 version of this file was moved to `artifacts/architect/.prev-SH-15/`. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still SH-15 outputs until their owning sub-tasks overwrite them.\n\n## 1. Codebase facts verified (2026-11-10)\n\n| Fact | Where | Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| The dashboard page is a placeholder. It already redirects PARENT to `/my-children` | `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` | FR-1: replace the body and keep the redirect line |\n| `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` returns `'ALL'` for ADMIN and `string[]` for TEACHER (active course enrolments + homeroom section members). `assertCanViewStudent` also exists | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | NFR-3, FR-7/29/42/43: one scope source. Students outside a teacher's scope get **FORBIDDEN**, not NOT_FOUND |\n| `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/` do not exist | — | NFR-6: create both as new feature folders |\n| There is no `unstable_cache` or `revalidateTag` anywhere. Next is **14.2.18** | `package.json` | FR-23/24: `unstable_cache` + `revalidateTag` work on 14.2. There is no `'use cache'` |\n| `SchoolSettings.timezone` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` (default 90) exist. `schoolToday(now, tz)` and `addDays` exist | `schema.prisma:222`, `attendance/attendance-rules.ts` | NFR-7, FR-17, FR-25: reuse these. Do not write new date helpers |\n| `getCurrentTerm(date)` exists. `Term` has start and end dates and belongs to an academic year | `src/server/services/academicYears.ts:96` | FR-3, FR-15, FR-25, FR-33: use it as the \"current term\" source |\n| Attendance service exports `getOverview(date)` (registers taken/missing + status counts), `getReport(filters)`, `getBelowThreshold()`, `attendanceRate()` and `countStatuses()` | `attendance/attendance-service.ts`, `attendance-rules.ts` | FR-16 (missing registers, today's rate), FR-17, FR-25 (attendance signal), FR-35: reuse these. Check `getReport` filters before you write new SQL |\n| `computeStudentTerm`, `letterFor` and `isUngradedPastDue` are pure. `getStudentGrades(user, studentId, termId)` is the Grades-tab source | `gradebook/grade-calc.ts`, `student-grades-service.ts` | FR-13 \"consistent with Grades tab\", FR-19, FR-25, FR-36: call the same calc. Calling `getStudentGrades` per student will not scale to 600 students (NFR-1), so use a batch path that runs `computeStudentTerm` |\n| \"Missing\" is derived. `SubmissionStatus` = SUBMITTED \\| RETURNED. `reminders.ts` uses `visibleWhere(now)` + `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION` + no submission + not exempt. Its lookback is 8 days | `assignments/reminders.ts` | FR-11, FR-25, FR-37: extract one shared `missingWhere(window)` predicate. Risk needs a 30-day window |\n| Parent overview service has `getToday` (timetable plus `isNoSchool` holiday check), `getRecentGrades`, `getAssignmentsSummary` and `getUpcomingEvents` (CalendarEvent + `expandOccurrences`). `listUnreadAnnouncements` is a stub that returns `[]` (ADR-11 precedent) | `src/server/parent/overview-service.ts` | FR-10/11/12: student widgets can call these with `studentId = user.id`. FR-14 follows the same stub precedent. FR-21 copies the events query with a school-wide audience and no meetings |\n| `CalendarEvent` (recurrence, `isNoSchool`) and `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` exist. There is still no calendar service or API | `schema.prisma:1281`, `calendar/recurrence.ts` | FR-21: read the model directly and expand recurrences. This removes the warning's \"non-recurring only\" limit |\n| There is no `Announcement` model, only `announcements/audience.ts` | `schema.prisma` | FR-8, FR-14, FR-38: show an empty state or omit the metric |\n| `messaging/conversations.unreadCount(userId)`. `isSafeguardingLead(user)`. `safeguarding.listReports` | `src/server/messaging/` | FR-8 unread count. FR-16 KPI only when `isSafeguardingLead`. For the count, add `count` on open reports. Do not page through the list |\n| `audit({ action: 'auth.login.success' })` is written on login. `User.lastLoginAt` exists. `AuditLog` is indexed on `action` and `[actorId, createdAt]`, but not on `createdAt` alone | `auth/credentials.ts:83`, `schema.prisma:202` | FR-22: filter by action prefix and order by createdAt desc. This may need `@@index([createdAt])` for NFR-1. FR-38 parent sign-ins |\n| `Gender` enum, `Section.homeroomTeacherId`, `TimetableSlot` and `LessonProgress` exist | `schema.prisma` | FR-18, FR-32 (homeroom recipient), FR-39, FR-13/38 |\n| Notification types are a static map `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. `notify()` is in `notify.ts` | `notifications/types.ts`, `notify.ts` | FR-32: add the key `insights.student_high_risk` (ACADEMIC, TEACHER, email default true) |\n| The cron dispatch route runs isolated try/catch passes on every call. The daily purge uses an in-memory `lastPurgeAt` | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | FR-27: add a risk pass. The \"at most once per hour\" rule must be stored in the DB (`max(computedAt)`), not in memory, because there are multiple processes |\n| `csv.ts` exports `escapeCsvCell` and `toCsv(columns, rows)` | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-30, FR-33: reuse these. They already guard against formula injection |\n| `studentTabs` registry, and `navigation` with `roles` + `requires` flags | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | FR-31, FR-40: append entries only |\n| `@mui/material`, `@mui/x-charts` and `@mui/x-data-grid` are 9.5.0. Prisma is 5.20, Zod 3.23 | `package.json` | NFR-4/5: no new dependencies are needed |\n| There is no `seed:large` script. The seed lives in `prisma/seed.ts` | `package.json` | FR-45/46 |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern codes: **UI** = new UI surface, **SVC** = service/query, **API** = endpoint, **DM** = data-model change, **JOB** = background/cron, **AUTH** = auth/scope boundary, **CACHE**, **CFG** = config registry, **XC** = cross-cutting rule.\n\n### Dashboards shell\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | UI, AUTH | `/dashboard` page switches on `getCurrentUser().role`. Keep the PARENT redirect. Use three role components under `src/app/(app)/dashboard/_components/` (or similar) |\n| FR-2 | UI | One async server component per widget inside `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` + a client error boundary with a Retry button (`router.refresh()`). This needs one shared `WidgetCard` wrapper (title, updated-ago, boundary). It is used by ~20 widgets, so the abstraction pays for itself |\n| FR-3 | SVC, XC | Greeting by the hour in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (NFR-7) + `getCurrentTerm().name`. Pure function `greetingFor(now, tz)`, which is unit-testable |\n\n### Teacher widgets (all scoped by `getAccessibleStudentIds` / taught courses, NFR-3)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-4 | SVC, UI | Today's TimetableSlots for the teacher's courses + attendance session existence per (course, period, date). `getToday(user)` in attendance-service probably already covers this. Check it before writing a new query. Now/Next comes from period times in the tz |\n| FR-5 | SVC | Union of ungraded submissions (no grade on the linked GradeItem) and quiz attempts needing manual grading in the teacher's courses. Count + oldest 5 |\n| FR-6 | SVC | Assignments/quizzes due within 7 days. Submission rate = submissions / active enrolments. Use one grouped query, not N+1 |\n| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH | Read `StudentRiskSnapshot` filtered by accessible ids, order High > Medium, take 5. Do not compute live |\n| FR-8 | SVC | `messaging.unreadCount` + announcements empty state (§3 Q1) |\n| FR-9 | UI | Static links. No data. Check that the target routes exist (new announcement route is absent → omit or disable it, §3 Q1) |\n\n### Student widgets (scope = self)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-10 | SVC | Reuse the parent `getToday(user, user.id)`, which already handles `isNoSchool` holidays |\n| FR-11 | SVC | Due in the next 7 days + missing items first. Share the missing predicate with FR-25/37 |\n| FR-12 | SVC | Reuse the parent `getRecentGrades` |\n| FR-13 | SVC | `getStudentGrades` (same as the Grades tab) + LessonProgress ratio + first incomplete visible lesson (`isLessonVisible`) |\n| FR-14 | SVC | Empty state (§3 Q1) |\n| FR-15 | SVC, UI | Term attendance rate via `countStatuses`/`attendanceRate` over the term range. Display with x-charts `Gauge` |\n\n### Admin widgets (ADMIN, cached)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-16 | SVC, CACHE, AUTH | Counts: active students/teachers, `getOverview(today)` rate + missing registers, the same weekday −7 days for the delta, pending absence notes (`absence-notes` service), safeguarding count **only if** `isSafeguardingLead`. The cache key must vary on lead status, or the safeguarding count must be fetched uncached separately |\n| FR-17 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Daily rate for the last 30 **school days**. A school day is a date with ≥1 attendance session. That is simpler and more accurate than combining calendar + weekday logic. One `groupBy` on session date × status. `LineChart` + reference line at the threshold |\n| FR-18 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Active students grouped by current-year section → grade level × gender. Stacked `BarChart` |\n| FR-19 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Batch `computeStudentTerm` for all students in the current term → histogram in 10 % buckets, plus average and median. This is the most expensive admin query. See §4 |\n| FR-20 | SVC | Group snapshots by level and reason. Reads the snapshot table only |\n| FR-21 | SVC | The next 5 school-wide `CalendarEvent` occurrences via `expandOccurrences` (§3 Q2) |\n| FR-22 | SVC | `AuditLog` where `action startsWith user./report_card./settings.`, latest 10, actor joined |\n\n### Caching\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-23 | CACHE | `unstable_cache` wrappers in `src/server/dashboards/insights.ts`. Key = role scope (ADMIN: `'all'`; TEACHER: userId). Tags: `dashboard:admin`, `dashboard:teacher:<id>`, `insights:risk`. `revalidate` 900 s; risk 3600 s. Cached values must be JSON-serialisable, so convert Decimal/Date to number/string |\n| FR-24 | CACHE, API, UI | Return `computedAt` from each cached function → \"Updated N min ago\". `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` → `revalidateTag(...)` + `recomputeRisk({ force: true })`. Audit this admin action |\n| NFR-12 | CACHE, JOB | Satisfied by FR-23 (60 min) + FR-27 (hourly recompute) |\n\n### Early-warning risk\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-25 | SVC | `risk.ts` has two parts. (a) Pure `scoreSignals({ attendancePct, coursePcts, missingCount }, threshold)` → per-signal level. (b) A batch loader that collects the three inputs for all ACTIVE students in the current term in a few grouped queries. Thresholds: attendance `< threshold` → Medium, `< 80` → High. Grades: any `< 60` → Medium, `≥2 < 60` or any `< 50` → High. Missing: 3–4 → Medium, `≥5` → High |\n| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `combine(levels)`: any High or ≥2 Medium → High, exactly 1 Medium → Medium, otherwise none. Keep it in the same pure module as FR-25 for the NFR-9 unit tests |\n| FR-27 | DM, JOB | New model + migration. Unique `(studentId, termId)`. Indexes on `(termId, level)`. Add `RiskLevel` enum (HIGH, MEDIUM, NONE). Hook into the dispatch route as an isolated pass, gated on `max(computedAt) < now − 1h` |\n| FR-28 | DM | Conflicts with the \"one row\" rule. See §3 Q3 |\n| FR-29 | UI, AUTH, SVC | Page `/insights/at-risk` (ADMIN, TEACHER). Server-side scope filter. Use the shared `DataTable`. Reason chips are formatted from `reasons` JSON. \"Message parents\" = link to the existing new-conversation flow (PRD-13) |\n| FR-30 | SVC, API | The same service function serves the table and the CSV (`toCsv`), so their rows match. Filters: level, reason, grade level, section |\n| FR-31 | CFG, UI, AUTH | Add `{ key: 'insights', roles: ['ADMIN','TEACHER'] }` to `studentTabs` + page `/students/[id]/insights` with `assertCanViewStudent` |\n| FR-32 | JOB, XC | On upsert, if prev ∈ {none, MEDIUM} and new = HIGH, and there was no notification for this student in 14 days → `notify()` the homeroom teacher. A `lastHighNotifiedAt` column on the snapshot gives a DB-side 14-day claim, with no Notification table scan. If there is no homeroom teacher, skip and log |\n\n### Reports centre\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-33 | UI, SVC, API | `/admin/reports` with year/term selectors (`x-date-pickers` for ranges) and one sub-route per report. Use a `REPORTS` registry in `src/server/reports/index.ts`: `key → { schema (Zod), run(filters), columns }`. The page, the API and the CSV all use that one registry, which also makes FR-44's 404 for unknown keys trivial |\n| FR-34 | SVC | Enrollment: SectionMember/grade/gender groupings. Monthly new/archived from `createdAt`/`archivedAt` |\n| FR-35 | SVC | Reuse `attendance-service.getReport`/aggregate. Group by grade/section/course + daily trend + bottom 20 |\n| FR-36 | SVC | Batch `computeStudentTerm` grouped by course and subject + `letterFor`. Section comparison within the same grade × subject. Shares the batch loader with FR-19/FR-25 |\n| FR-37 | SVC | On-time/late = submission `submittedAt` vs `dueAt`. Missing = shared predicate. Group by course and teacher |\n| FR-38 | SVC | LessonProgress completion by course. Parent sign-ins = distinct `actorId` on `auth.login.success` in the last 7 and 30 days (and/or `lastLoginAt`). Announcement read rate is omitted (§3 Q1) |\n| FR-39 | SVC | Per teacher: courses, distinct students, TimetableSlot count/week, grading backlog (reuse the FR-5 query) |\n\n### Navigation, API, seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-40 | CFG | Add 'Reports' (ADMIN) and 'At-risk students' (ADMIN, TEACHER) after 'Dashboard' |\n| FR-41 | API, AUTH | `GET /api/dashboard/{teacher,student,admin}` use the same service functions as the widgets, plus `requireRole`. Refresh uses POST, ADMIN only |\n| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Zod query schema. **Intersect** the filtered ids with accessible ids so filters cannot widen scope. `?format=csv` → `text/csv` with a Content-Disposition header |\n| FR-43 | API, AUTH | `assertCanViewStudent`, then the snapshot + current signal values |\n| FR-44 | API | `reportKe","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/ikramaansari/.claude/projects/-Users-ikramaansari-Documents-React-Projects-schoolhub/2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187/tool-results/b7bf5u2db.txt","persistedOutputSize":35478},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SKEyqutwsmXZcKMNm8aGuy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtcrpQmzFNeLESaoBMmd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PN2fte3WX119Pszuz1Cjkc","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1453,"cache_read_input_tokens":38042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1453,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187","uuid":"1986373c-ece5-48e6-9baa-ed7bd6a35731","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:30:26.561Z","request_id":"req_011CgtcrpBd75s9LHmwmKi24","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PN2fte3WX119Pszuz1Cjkc":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PN2fte3WX119Pszuz1Cjkc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights\n2\t\n3\tTicket: SH-16 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n4\t\n5\t> This file replaces the SH-15 version. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still from SH-15 until their own sub-tasks rewrite them.\n6\t\n7\t**Summary:** keep intake's detected stack (`react`, 98 %). It meets every FR/NFR. **No new runtime or dev dependencies.** All of the following are already installed and pinned in `package.json`: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, MUI 9.5.0 with `@mui/x-charts`, `@mui/x-data-grid` and `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, date-fns 3.6.0 with date-fns-tz 3.2.0, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 with `@axe-core/playwright` 4.10.0, and tsx 4.16.2.\n8\t\n9\tVerified in the codebase: `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/` do not exist yet. There is no `unstable_cache` or `revalidateTag` usage, no React error boundary, and no `seed:large` script. `@mui/x-charts` is already used in `QuizAnalytics.tsx`. `src/lib/dates.ts` and `src/server/csv.ts` already provide the timezone and CSV helpers.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n14\t\n15\t**Context:** NFR-8 (brownfield reuse), NFR-4 (MUI-only UI), and NFR-10 (lint/typecheck/test stay green). The new features are dashboards, charts, tables, aggregate queries, a rule engine, caching and a seed script, and the installed stack covers all of them.\n16\t\n17\t**Decision:** Use only installed packages. Do not add charting, error-boundary, faker, cron, cache or date libraries.\n18\t\n19\t**Consequences:** No lockfile churn and no new attack surface. The few small helpers we still need are covered in ADR-4 and ADR-10.\n20\t\n21\t## ADR-2: Use async Server Components for widgets, each in Suspense with a per-widget error boundary\n22\t\n23\t**Context:** FR-1, FR-2 and NFR-1 (first content in under 1.5 s). Next.js 14's `error.tsx` works at route-segment level, so it cannot isolate one widget's failure. React 18 has no built-in component-level error boundary, and none exists in `src/` yet.\n24\t\n25\t**Decision:**\n26\t- `/dashboard/page.tsx` stays a server component. It checks the role, keeps the PARENT redirect to `/my-children`, and renders one of three role dashboards (FR-1).\n27\t- Each widget is an `async` server component that loads its own data and is wrapped in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` (reuse `src/components/LoadingSkeleton`), so widgets stream independently.\n28\t- Add one small client `WidgetErrorBoundary`: a class component of about 25 lines using `getDerivedStateFromError`. It renders an MUI `Alert` with the text \"This widget could not load\" and a \"Retry\" `Button` that resets its state and calls `router.refresh()`. It lives in `src/components/WidgetErrorBoundary/` and is the only new shared component (FR-2).\n29\t\n30\t**Consequences:** One slow widget, such as at-risk, does not block the others. Widgets read data through server-side services directly, not through `/api/dashboard/*`. The FR-41 GET endpoints are thin JSON wrappers around the same service functions, for API parity and tests.\n31\t\n32\t## ADR-3: Cache aggregates with `unstable_cache`, using role-scoped keys and tags\n33\t\n34\t**Context:** FR-23, FR-24, NFR-1 and NFR-12. Next.js 14.2 provides `unstable_cache(fn, keyParts, { revalidate, tags })` and `revalidateTag()`.\n35\t\n36\t**Decision:**\n37\t- Wrap the expensive reads in `src/server/dashboards/insights.ts`: admin KPIs, the attendance trend, the enrollment and grade distributions, and risk summaries and lists.\n38\t- Use `revalidate: 900` (15 minutes) and `3600` (60 minutes) for at-risk data.\n39\t- Key parts must include the scope: `['admin']`, or `['teacher', teacherId]` for teacher-scoped data. This keeps one teacher's cached data out of another teacher's view (NFR-3).\n40\t- Tags: `dashboard:admin`, `dashboard:teacher`, `dashboard:student` and `insights:at-risk`.\n41\t- `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` (ADMIN only) calls `revalidateTag` for each tag after it triggers the risk recompute (ADR-6).\n42\t- Each cached function returns `{ data, computedAt: ISO string }`, and the widget shows \"Updated N min ago\" from `computedAt` (FR-24).\n43\t\n44\t**Consequences:**\n45\t- `unstable_cache` serializes results to JSON, so cached values must not contain `Date` objects; use ISO strings.\n46\t- The cache lives in each Next.js server process, which is acceptable for a single-node deployment.\n47\t- `ponytail:` ceiling: with several app instances each one has its own cache, and Refresh only clears the instance that handles the request. Add a shared cache handler if the app is scaled out.\n48\t- Per-user student widgets (FR-10 to FR-15) are cheap, single-student queries and are **not** cached. That avoids one cache entry per student.\n49\t\n50\t## ADR-4: Use MUI X Charts, the shared DataTable, and visually hidden data for accessibility\n51\t\n52\t**Context:** FR-15 to FR-19, FR-33 to FR-39, NFR-2, NFR-4 and NFR-5.\n53\t\n54\t**Decision:**\n55\t- Use `LineChart` (FR-17 and the report trends), `BarChart` (FR-18 stacked by gender, the FR-19 histogram, and the reports) and `Gauge` (FR-15), all from `@mui/x-charts` 9.5.0.\n56\t- Draw the FR-17 threshold with the chart's reference-line component, `ChartsReferenceLine`.\n57\t- All tables use the existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid).\n58\t- Charts are client components that receive serializable props from the server.\n59\t- For NFR-2, every chart gets an `aria-label` summary built on the server, for example \"Attendance trend: 94.2 % average, lowest 88.1 % on 3 Oct\". It also gets a visually hidden MUI `Table` built with the `visuallyHidden` style from `@mui/utils`, which comes with `@mui/material`.\n60\t- Series use labels and distinct marks or patterns, not colour alone.\n61\t- Per NFR-5, the dev phase must look up each component through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` and `fetchDocs`, version 9.5.0) before using it. If MCP is unavailable, that is a blocker.\n62\t\n63\t**Consequences:** No Recharts, Tailwind or shadcn (NFR-4). Each chart duplicates its data once, for the hidden table, which is trivial at these data sizes.\n64\t\n65\t## ADR-5: Implement risk scoring as rule-based pure functions plus a Prisma snapshot with embedded capped history\n66\t\n67\t**Context:** FR-25 to FR-28, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-9 and NFR-11 (no ML). FR-28 is LOW confidence because \"one row per student per term, upserted\" conflicts with the trend arrow and history requirements.\n68\t\n69\t**Decision:**\n70\t- `src/server/dashboards/risk.ts` exports pure, database-free functions `attendanceSignal`, `gradesSignal`, `missingSignal` and `overallLevel`. They take numbers and return `'HIGH' | 'MEDIUM' | null` plus a reason string. That makes the NFR-9 boundary tests plain Vitest tables.\n71\t- A separate loader, `computeRiskInputs(termId, studentIds)`, fetches data in bulk, using a fixed number of queries per run rather than per student.\n72\t- **FR-28 resolution:** keep `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on `StudentRiskSnapshot`. Add `previousLevel RiskLevel?` and `history Json`, a list of `{ level, computedAt, reasons }` capped at the last 10 **level changes**. Unchanged recomputes update `computedAt` only, so hourly runs do not flood the history. The trend arrow compares `level` with `previousLevel`, and the Insights tab renders `history`.\n73\t- Add `highNotifiedAt DateTime?` to enforce the FR-32 rule of at most one notification per 14 days without querying the Notification table.\n74\t- New enum `RiskLevel { MEDIUM HIGH }`. `none` is stored as a `null` level.\n75\t- The \"Missing\" count reuses the definition from `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`: published, due within the last 30 days, no submission, not exempt, and `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION`.\n76\t- A student with no data has no signal.\n77\t\n78\t**Consequences:** One table and one migration, with no separate history table. History is limited to 10 level changes, which is enough for a \"short history\". `ponytail:` add a `StudentRiskSnapshotHistory` table if long-range trend analytics are ever needed.\n79\t\n80\t## ADR-6: Hook the hourly recompute into the existing internal dispatch cron, gated in the database\n81\t\n82\t**Context:** FR-27 and NFR-12. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs the maintenance passes, each in its own try/catch. It currently gates the daily purge with an in-memory `lastPurgeAt`, which does not survive restarts or work across instances.\n83\t\n84\t**Decision:**\n85\t- Add a `recomputeRiskSnapshots()` call in its own try/catch block.\n86\t- Gate it with `max(computedAt)` from `StudentRiskSnapshot` for the current term: skip the run if the latest snapshot is less than 60 minutes old.\n87\t- Admin Refresh bypasses the gate.\n88\t- On completion, call `revalidateTag('insights:at-risk')`.\n89\t- Notifications use the existing `notify()` with the new type `insights.student_high_risk` (default email on). The type is registered wherever notification types and preferences are declared.\n90\t\n91\t**Consequences:** No new scheduler. The \"at most once per hour\" rule holds across restarts and instances because it is gated in the database.\n92\t\n93\t## ADR-7: Use Prisma aggregates first and parameterized `$queryRaw` for time-bucketed reports\n94\t\n95\t**Context:** FR-16 to FR-22, FR-34 to FR-39 and NFR-1 (reports in under 3 s on 600 students over one school year).\n96\t\n97\t**Decision:**\n98\t- Use `groupBy`, `count` and `aggregate` for simple counts.\n99\t- Use tagged-template `prisma.$queryRaw` (parameterized only, never `$queryRawUnsafe`) where Prisma cannot group by date or bucket. That covers the daily attendance rate over 30 school days, the 10 % grade histogram with median (`percentile_cont`), monthly enrollments and archives, and on-time, late and missing rates.\n100\t- Bucket dates in SQL with `AT TIME ZONE $tz` (NFR-7).\n101\t- The attendance report (FR-35) and course percentages (FR-13, FR-19, FR-36) must call the existing `attendance-service.ts` and the gradebook `grade-calc.ts` and `student-grades-service.ts`, so the numbers match the Grades tab.\n102\t- Dev should check with `EXPLAIN` against `seed:large` and add indexes only where a query is slow. `AttendanceRecord @@index([studentId, createdAt])` already exists.\n103\t\n104\t**Consequences:** A small amount of raw SQL, kept in the `src/server/reports/` and `src/server/dashboards/` services and covered by NFR-9 integration tests with known totals.\n105\t\n106\t## ADR-8: Validate with Zod, keep handlers thin, export CSV through the existing helper, and enforce access server-side\n107\t\n108\t**Context:** FR-30, FR-33, FR-41 to FR-44, NFR-3 and NFR-6.\n109\t\n110\t**Decision:**\n111\t- Put the schemas in `src/lib/validators/dashboards.ts` and `src/lib/validators/reports.ts`.\n112\t- `reportKey` is a `z.enum([...6 keys])`, and an unknown key returns a 404 `NOT_FOUND`.\n113\t- Handlers use the existing `withHandler`, `ok` and `AppError` from `src/server/http.ts`.\n114\t- `?format=csv` goes through `toCsv` and `escapeCsvCell` in `src/server/csv.ts`, which already protects against formula injection, using the same column list as the table.\n115\t- Teacher scope = `getAccessibleStudentIds()`. Filters are applied as an intersection with that set, so they can never widen it (FR-42).\n116\t\n117\t**Consequences:** No new HTTP or CSV code.\n118\t\n119\t## ADR-9: Do all date logic in the school timezone with date-fns-tz through `src/lib/dates.ts`\n120\t\n121\t**Context:** FR-3, FR-4, FR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-17 and NFR-7.\n122\t\n123\t**Decision:**\n124\t- Reuse `schoolNow`, `schoolDateOf`, `schoolMidnight`, `addDateDays`, `nowAndNext` (for the Now/Next badges) and `formatInSchoolTz`.\n125\t- Add a `greetingFor(now, tz)` helper next to them, and a \"school days\" helper that reads the existing teaching-days and holiday data.\n126\t\n127\t**Consequences:** One timezone source of truth. Timestamps stay in UTC in the database.\n128\t\n129\t## ADR-10: Write a deterministic large seed as a tsx script with an inline PRNG\n130\t\n131\t**Context:** FR-45, FR-46 and NFR-1. The existing seed runs with `tsx prisma/seed.ts` through `db:seed`. Faker is not installed.\n132\t\n133\t**Decision:**\n134\t- Add `prisma/seed-large.ts` and the npm script `\"seed:large\": \"tsx prisma/seed-large.ts\"`.\n135\t- Use an inline mulberry32 PRNG (about 6 lines) with a fixed seed, plus fixed name lists, instead of adding faker.\n136\t- Use `createMany` in batches for 600 students, 40 teachers and 60 school days of attendance, assignments and grades.\n137\t- The default `prisma/seed.ts` stays small but must create at least 3 students at each risk level (High, Medium and none) by planting attendance, grades and missing work that cross the FR-25 thresholds (FR-46).\n138\t\n139\t**Consequences:** Results are reproducible, and there is no new dependency.\n140\t\n141\t## ADR-11: Handle missing upstream data sources with empty states and direct reads instead of fixes outside scope\n142\t\n143\t**Context:** FR-8, FR-14, FR-21 and FR-38. There is no `Announcement` model (PRD-12) and no calendar service (PRD-14). NFR-11 says not to modify other PRDs' behaviour.\n144\t\n145\t**Decision:**\n146\t- **Announcements:** FR-8 and FR-14 render the existing `EmptyState` with the text \"Announcements not available\". FR-38 omits the read-rate metric and its column note says \"not available\". Expose this through one `announcementsAvailable = false` guard in the dashboards service, so it is a one-line change once PRD-12 ships the model.\n147\t- **Events:** FR-21 reads `CalendarEvent` directly with a small Prisma query: school-wide, `start >= now`, ordered by start, `take: 5`. It does not expand recurrences. The existing `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` can be wired in later.\n148\t\n149\t**Consequences:** These requirements are implemented in degraded form, not blocked. This is recorded as a dependency gap for `system-design.md`. Intake reported no blockers.\n150\t\n151\t---\n152\t\n153\t## Requirement → ADR map\n154\t\n155\t| ADR | Requirements |\n156\t|---|---|\n157\t| ADR-1 | NFR-4, NFR-8, NFR-10 |\n158\t| ADR-2 | FR-1, FR-2, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n159\t| ADR-3 | FR-23, FR-24, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-12 |\n160\t| ADR-4 | FR-15, FR-16, FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-29, FR-33–FR-39, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-5 |\n161\t| ADR-5 | FR-7, FR-20, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n162\t| ADR-6 | FR-24, FR-27, FR-32, NFR-12 |\n163\t| ADR-7 | FR-5, FR-6, FR-12, FR-13, FR-16–FR-22, FR-34–FR-39, NFR-1, NFR-7, NFR-9 |\n164\t| ADR-8 | FR-30, FR-33, FR-40, FR-41–FR-44, NFR-3, NFR-6 |\n165\t| ADR-9 | FR-3, FR-4, FR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n166\t| ADR-10 | FR-45, FR-46, NFR-1, NFR-9 |\n167\t| ADR-11 | FR-8, FR-14, FR-21, FR-38, NFR-11 |\n168\t\n169\tFR-9 (quick-action links) and FR-40 (navigation entries) are plain MUI links and config edits in `src/config/navigation.ts` and `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, and need no stack decision.\n170\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187","uuid":"ac70a024-89dd-4d7d-83a1-5f23b2f0aa85","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:30:26.591Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/tech-stack-decisions.md","content":"# Tech Stack Decisions: PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights\n\nTicket: SH-16 · Phase: architect (arch-research-stack) · Timestamp: 2026-11-10T13:00:00Z · Status: complete\n\n> This file replaces the SH-15 version. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still from SH-15 until their own sub-tasks rewrite them.\n\n**Summary:** keep intake's detected stack (`react`, 98 %). It meets every FR/NFR. **No new runtime or dev dependencies.** All of the following are already installed and pinned in `package.json`: Next.js 14.2.18 App Router, React 18.3.1, TypeScript strict, MUI 9.5.0 with `@mui/x-charts`, `@mui/x-data-grid` and `@mui/x-date-pickers` 9.5.0, Prisma 5.20.0 on PostgreSQL 16, Auth.js 5.0.0-beta.25, Zod 3.23.8, date-fns 3.6.0 with date-fns-tz 3.2.0, Vitest 2.1.1, Playwright 1.47.2 with `@axe-core/playwright` 4.10.0, and tsx 4.16.2.\n\nVerified in the codebase: `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/` do not exist yet. There is no `unstable_cache` or `revalidateTag` usage, no React error boundary, and no `seed:large` script. `@mui/x-charts` is already used in `QuizAnalytics.tsx`. `src/lib/dates.ts` and `src/server/csv.ts` already provide the timezone and CSV helpers.\n\n---\n\n## ADR-1: Keep the existing stack and add no dependencies\n\n**Context:** NFR-8 (brownfield reuse), NFR-4 (MUI-only UI), and NFR-10 (lint/typecheck/test stay green). The new features are dashboards, charts, tables, aggregate queries, a rule engine, caching and a seed script, and the installed stack covers all of them.\n\n**Decision:** Use only installed packages. Do not add charting, error-boundary, faker, cron, cache or date libraries.\n\n**Consequences:** No lockfile churn and no new attack surface. The few small helpers we still need are covered in ADR-4 and ADR-10.\n\n## ADR-2: Use async Server Components for widgets, each in Suspense with a per-widget error boundary\n\n**Context:** FR-1, FR-2 and NFR-1 (first content in under 1.5 s). Next.js 14's `error.tsx` works at route-segment level, so it cannot isolate one widget's failure. React 18 has no built-in component-level error boundary, and none exists in `src/` yet.\n\n**Decision:**\n- `/dashboard/page.tsx` stays a server component. It checks the role, keeps the PARENT redirect to `/my-children`, and renders one of three role dashboards (FR-1).\n- Each widget is an `async` server component that loads its own data and is wrapped in `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` (reuse `src/components/LoadingSkeleton`), so widgets stream independently.\n- Add one small client `WidgetErrorBoundary`: a class component of about 25 lines using `getDerivedStateFromError`. It renders an MUI `Alert` with the text \"This widget could not load\" and a \"Retry\" `Button` that resets its state and calls `router.refresh()`. It lives in `src/components/WidgetErrorBoundary/` and is the only new shared component (FR-2).\n\n**Consequences:** One slow widget, such as at-risk, does not block the others. Widgets read data through server-side services directly, not through `/api/dashboard/*`. The FR-41 GET endpoints are thin JSON wrappers around the same service functions, for API parity and tests.\n\n## ADR-3: Cache aggregates with `unstable_cache`, using role-scoped keys and tags\n\n**Context:** FR-23, FR-24, NFR-1 and NFR-12. Next.js 14.2 provides `unstable_cache(fn, keyParts, { revalidate, tags })` and `revalidateTag()`.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Wrap the expensive reads in `src/server/dashboards/insights.ts`: admin KPIs, the attendance trend, the enrollment and grade distributions, and risk summaries and lists.\n- Use `revalidate: 900` (15 minutes) and `3600` (60 minutes) for at-risk data.\n- Key parts must include the scope: `['admin']`, or `['teacher', teacherId]` for teacher-scoped data. This keeps one teacher's cached data out of another teacher's view (NFR-3).\n- Tags: `dashboard:admin`, `dashboard:teacher`, `dashboard:student` and `insights:at-risk`.\n- `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` (ADMIN only) calls `revalidateTag` for each tag after it triggers the risk recompute (ADR-6).\n- Each cached function returns `{ data, computedAt: ISO string }`, and the widget shows \"Updated N min ago\" from `computedAt` (FR-24).\n\n**Consequences:**\n- `unstable_cache` serializes results to JSON, so cached values must not contain `Date` objects; use ISO strings.\n- The cache lives in each Next.js server process, which is acceptable for a single-node deployment.\n- `ponytail:` ceiling: with several app instances each one has its own cache, and Refresh only clears the instance that handles the request. Add a shared cache handler if the app is scaled out.\n- Per-user student widgets (FR-10 to FR-15) are cheap, single-student queries and are **not** cached. That avoids one cache entry per student.\n\n## ADR-4: Use MUI X Charts, the shared DataTable, and visually hidden data for accessibility\n\n**Context:** FR-15 to FR-19, FR-33 to FR-39, NFR-2, NFR-4 and NFR-5.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Use `LineChart` (FR-17 and the report trends), `BarChart` (FR-18 stacked by gender, the FR-19 histogram, and the reports) and `Gauge` (FR-15), all from `@mui/x-charts` 9.5.0.\n- Draw the FR-17 threshold with the chart's reference-line component, `ChartsReferenceLine`.\n- All tables use the existing `src/components/DataTable` (x-data-grid).\n- Charts are client components that receive serializable props from the server.\n- For NFR-2, every chart gets an `aria-label` summary built on the server, for example \"Attendance trend: 94.2 % average, lowest 88.1 % on 3 Oct\". It also gets a visually hidden MUI `Table` built with the `visuallyHidden` style from `@mui/utils`, which comes with `@mui/material`.\n- Series use labels and distinct marks or patterns, not colour alone.\n- Per NFR-5, the dev phase must look up each component through mui-mcp (`useMuiDocs` and `fetchDocs`, version 9.5.0) before using it. If MCP is unavailable, that is a blocker.\n\n**Consequences:** No Recharts, Tailwind or shadcn (NFR-4). Each chart duplicates its data once, for the hidden table, which is trivial at these data sizes.\n\n## ADR-5: Implement risk scoring as rule-based pure functions plus a Prisma snapshot with embedded capped history\n\n**Context:** FR-25 to FR-28, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-9 and NFR-11 (no ML). FR-28 is LOW confidence because \"one row per student per term, upserted\" conflicts with the trend arrow and history requirements.\n\n**Decision:**\n- `src/server/dashboards/risk.ts` exports pure, database-free functions `attendanceSignal`, `gradesSignal`, `missingSignal` and `overallLevel`. They take numbers and return `'HIGH' | 'MEDIUM' | null` plus a reason string. That makes the NFR-9 boundary tests plain Vitest tables.\n- A separate loader, `computeRiskInputs(termId, studentIds)`, fetches data in bulk, using a fixed number of queries per run rather than per student.\n- **FR-28 resolution:** keep `@@unique([studentId, termId])` on `StudentRiskSnapshot`. Add `previousLevel RiskLevel?` and `history Json`, a list of `{ level, computedAt, reasons }` capped at the last 10 **level changes**. Unchanged recomputes update `computedAt` only, so hourly runs do not flood the history. The trend arrow compares `level` with `previousLevel`, and the Insights tab renders `history`.\n- Add `highNotifiedAt DateTime?` to enforce the FR-32 rule of at most one notification per 14 days without querying the Notification table.\n- New enum `RiskLevel { MEDIUM HIGH }`. `none` is stored as a `null` level.\n- The \"Missing\" count reuses the definition from `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts`: published, due within the last 30 days, no submission, not exempt, and `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION`.\n- A student with no data has no signal.\n\n**Consequences:** One table and one migration, with no separate history table. History is limited to 10 level changes, which is enough for a \"short history\". `ponytail:` add a `StudentRiskSnapshotHistory` table if long-range trend analytics are ever needed.\n\n## ADR-6: Hook the hourly recompute into the existing internal dispatch cron, gated in the database\n\n**Context:** FR-27 and NFR-12. `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` already runs the maintenance passes, each in its own try/catch. It currently gates the daily purge with an in-memory `lastPurgeAt`, which does not survive restarts or work across instances.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Add a `recomputeRiskSnapshots()` call in its own try/catch block.\n- Gate it with `max(computedAt)` from `StudentRiskSnapshot` for the current term: skip the run if the latest snapshot is less than 60 minutes old.\n- Admin Refresh bypasses the gate.\n- On completion, call `revalidateTag('insights:at-risk')`.\n- Notifications use the existing `notify()` with the new type `insights.student_high_risk` (default email on). The type is registered wherever notification types and preferences are declared.\n\n**Consequences:** No new scheduler. The \"at most once per hour\" rule holds across restarts and instances because it is gated in the database.\n\n## ADR-7: Use Prisma aggregates first and parameterized `$queryRaw` for time-bucketed reports\n\n**Context:** FR-16 to FR-22, FR-34 to FR-39 and NFR-1 (reports in under 3 s on 600 students over one school year).\n\n**Decision:**\n- Use `groupBy`, `count` and `aggregate` for simple counts.\n- Use tagged-template `prisma.$queryRaw` (parameterized only, never `$queryRawUnsafe`) where Prisma cannot group by date or bucket. That covers the daily attendance rate over 30 school days, the 10 % grade histogram with median (`percentile_cont`), monthly enrollments and archives, and on-time, late and missing rates.\n- Bucket dates in SQL with `AT TIME ZONE $tz` (NFR-7).\n- The attendance report (FR-35) and course percentages (FR-13, FR-19, FR-36) must call the existing `attendance-service.ts` and the gradebook `grade-calc.ts` and `student-grades-service.ts`, so the numbers match the Grades tab.\n- Dev should check with `EXPLAIN` against `seed:large` and add indexes only where a query is slow. `AttendanceRecord @@index([studentId, createdAt])` already exists.\n\n**Consequences:** A small amount of raw SQL, kept in the `src/server/reports/` and `src/server/dashboards/` services and covered by NFR-9 integration tests with known totals.\n\n## ADR-8: Validate with Zod, keep handlers thin, export CSV through the existing helper, and enforce access server-side\n\n**Context:** FR-30, FR-33, FR-41 to FR-44, NFR-3 and NFR-6.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Put the schemas in `src/lib/validators/dashboards.ts` and `src/lib/validators/reports.ts`.\n- `reportKey` is a `z.enum([...6 keys])`, and an unknown key returns a 404 `NOT_FOUND`.\n- Handlers use the existing `withHandler`, `ok` and `AppError` from `src/server/http.ts`.\n- `?format=csv` goes through `toCsv` and `escapeCsvCell` in `src/server/csv.ts`, which already protects against formula injection, using the same column list as the table.\n- Teacher scope = `getAccessibleStudentIds()`. Filters are applied as an intersection with that set, so they can never widen it (FR-42).\n\n**Consequences:** No new HTTP or CSV code.\n\n## ADR-9: Do all date logic in the school timezone with date-fns-tz through `src/lib/dates.ts`\n\n**Context:** FR-3, FR-4, FR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-17 and NFR-7.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Reuse `schoolNow`, `schoolDateOf`, `schoolMidnight`, `addDateDays`, `nowAndNext` (for the Now/Next badges) and `formatInSchoolTz`.\n- Add a `greetingFor(now, tz)` helper next to them, and a \"school days\" helper that reads the existing teaching-days and holiday data.\n\n**Consequences:** One timezone source of truth. Timestamps stay in UTC in the database.\n\n## ADR-10: Write a deterministic large seed as a tsx script with an inline PRNG\n\n**Context:** FR-45, FR-46 and NFR-1. The existing seed runs with `tsx prisma/seed.ts` through `db:seed`. Faker is not installed.\n\n**Decision:**\n- Add `prisma/seed-large.ts` and the npm script `\"seed:large\": \"tsx prisma/seed-large.ts\"`.\n- Use an inline mulberry32 PRNG (about 6 lines) with a fixed seed, plus fixed name lists, instead of adding faker.\n- Use `createMany` in batches for 600 students, 40 teachers and 60 school days of attendance, assignments and grades.\n- The default `prisma/seed.ts` stays small but must create at least 3 students at each risk level (High, Medium and none) by planting attendance, grades and missing work that cross the FR-25 thresholds (FR-46).\n\n**Consequences:** Results are reproducible, and there is no new dependency.\n\n## ADR-11: Handle missing upstream data sources with empty states and direct reads instead of fixes outside scope\n\n**Context:** FR-8, FR-14, FR-21 and FR-38. There is no `Announcement` model (PRD-12) and no calendar service (PRD-14). NFR-11 says not to modify other PRDs' behaviour.\n\n**Decision:**\n- **Announcements:** FR-8 and FR-14 render the existing `EmptyState` with the text \"Announcements not available\". FR-38 omits the read-rate metric and its column note says \"not available\". Expose this through one `announcementsAvailable = false` guard in the dashboards service, so it is a one-line change once PRD-12 ships the model.\n- **Events:** FR-21 reads `CalendarEvent` directly with a small Prisma query: school-wide, `start >= now`, ordered by start, `take: 5`. It does not expand recurrences. The existing `src/server/calendar/recurrence.ts` can be wired in later.\n\n**Consequences:** These requirements are implemented in degraded form, not blocked. This is recorded as a dependency gap for `system-design.md`. Intake reported no blockers.\n\n---\n\n## Requirement → ADR map\n\n| ADR | Requirements |\n|---|---|\n| ADR-1 | NFR-4, NFR-8, NFR-10 |\n| ADR-2 | FR-1, FR-2, FR-41, NFR-1 |\n| ADR-3 | FR-23, FR-24, NFR-1, NFR-3, NFR-12 |\n| ADR-4 | FR-15, FR-16, FR-17, FR-18, FR-19, FR-29, FR-33–FR-39, NFR-2, NFR-4, NFR-5 |\n| ADR-5 | FR-7, FR-20, FR-25, FR-26, FR-27, FR-28, FR-29, FR-31, FR-32, NFR-9, NFR-11 |\n| ADR-6 | FR-24, FR-27, FR-32, NFR-12 |\n| ADR-7 | FR-5, FR-6, FR-12, FR-13, FR-16–FR-22, FR-34–FR-39, NFR-1, NFR-7, NFR-9 |\n| ADR-8 | FR-30, FR-33, FR-40, FR-41–FR-44, NFR-3, NFR-6 |\n| ADR-9 | FR-3, FR-4, FR-6, FR-10, FR-11, FR-17, NFR-7 |\n| ADR-10 | FR-45, FR-46, NFR-1, NFR-9 |\n| ADR-11 | FR-8, FR-14, FR-21, FR-38, NFR-11 |\n\nFR-9 (quick-action links) and FR-40 (navigation entries) are plain MUI links and config edits in `src/config/navigation.ts` and `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, and need no stack decision.\n","numLines":170,"startLine":1,"totalLines":170}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PN2fte3WX119Pszuz1Cjkc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtcrpQmzFNeLESaoBMmd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JjYG59fSwyqjpRKJVe8mxz","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1453,"cache_read_input_tokens":38042,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1453,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187","uuid":"75f90983-acab-44c9-9331-3f4605bb53a5","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:30:27.052Z","request_id":"req_011CgtcrpBd75s9LHmwmKi24","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JjYG59fSwyqjpRKJVe8mxz":{"file_path":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JjYG59fSwyqjpRKJVe8mxz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-16\n2\t\n3\tWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\n4\tSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-10T12:00:00Z), PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights. It has 46 FRs and 12 NFRs (58 requirements) at 91% confidence.\n5\t`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers** and 7 warnings. §3 proposes a default for each open question so that `arch-design-system` can decide.\n6\tThe previous SH-15 version of this file was moved to `artifacts/architect/.prev-SH-15/`. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still SH-15 outputs until their owning sub-tasks overwrite them.\n7\t\n8\t## 1. Codebase facts verified (2026-11-10)\n9\t\n10\t| Fact | Where | Impact |\n11\t|---|---|---|\n12\t| The dashboard page is a placeholder. It already redirects PARENT to `/my-children` | `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` | FR-1: replace the body and keep the redirect line |\n13\t| `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` returns `'ALL'` for ADMIN and `string[]` for TEACHER (active course enrolments + homeroom section members). `assertCanViewStudent` also exists | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | NFR-3, FR-7/29/42/43: one scope source. Students outside a teacher's scope get **FORBIDDEN**, not NOT_FOUND |\n14\t| `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/` do not exist | — | NFR-6: create both as new feature folders |\n15\t| There is no `unstable_cache` or `revalidateTag` anywhere. Next is **14.2.18** | `package.json` | FR-23/24: `unstable_cache` + `revalidateTag` work on 14.2. There is no `'use cache'` |\n16\t| `SchoolSettings.timezone` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` (default 90) exist. `schoolToday(now, tz)` and `addDays` exist | `schema.prisma:222`, `attendance/attendance-rules.ts` | NFR-7, FR-17, FR-25: reuse these. Do not write new date helpers |\n17\t| `getCurrentTerm(date)` exists. `Term` has start and end dates and belongs to an academic year | `src/server/services/academicYears.ts:96` | FR-3, FR-15, FR-25, FR-33: use it as the \"current term\" source |\n18\t| Attendance service exports `getOverview(date)` (registers taken/missing + status counts), `getReport(filters)`, `getBelowThreshold()`, `attendanceRate()` and `countStatuses()` | `attendance/attendance-service.ts`, `attendance-rules.ts` | FR-16 (missing registers, today's rate), FR-17, FR-25 (attendance signal), FR-35: reuse these. Check `getReport` filters before you write new SQL |\n19\t| `computeStudentTerm`, `letterFor` and `isUngradedPastDue` are pure. `getStudentGrades(user, studentId, termId)` is the Grades-tab source | `gradebook/grade-calc.ts`, `student-grades-service.ts` | FR-13 \"consistent with Grades tab\", FR-19, FR-25, FR-36: call the same calc. Calling `getStudentGrades` per student will not scale to 600 students (NFR-1), so use a batch path that runs `computeStudentTerm` |\n20\t| \"Missing\" is derived. `SubmissionStatus` = SUBMITTED \\| RETURNED. `reminders.ts` uses `visibleWhere(now)` + `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION` + no submission + not exempt. Its lookback is 8 days | `assignments/reminders.ts` | FR-11, FR-25, FR-37: extract one shared `missingWhere(window)` predicate. Risk needs a 30-day window |\n21\t| Parent overview service has `getToday` (timetable plus `isNoSchool` holiday check), `getRecentGrades`, `getAssignmentsSummary` and `getUpcomingEvents` (CalendarEvent + `expandOccurrences`). `listUnreadAnnouncements` is a stub that returns `[]` (ADR-11 precedent) | `src/server/parent/overview-service.ts` | FR-10/11/12: student widgets can call these with `studentId = user.id`. FR-14 follows the same stub precedent. FR-21 copies the events query with a school-wide audience and no meetings |\n22\t| `CalendarEvent` (recurrence, `isNoSchool`) and `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` exist. There is still no calendar service or API | `schema.prisma:1281`, `calendar/recurrence.ts` | FR-21: read the model directly and expand recurrences. This removes the warning's \"non-recurring only\" limit |\n23\t| There is no `Announcement` model, only `announcements/audience.ts` | `schema.prisma` | FR-8, FR-14, FR-38: show an empty state or omit the metric |\n24\t| `messaging/conversations.unreadCount(userId)`. `isSafeguardingLead(user)`. `safeguarding.listReports` | `src/server/messaging/` | FR-8 unread count. FR-16 KPI only when `isSafeguardingLead`. For the count, add `count` on open reports. Do not page through the list |\n25\t| `audit({ action: 'auth.login.success' })` is written on login. `User.lastLoginAt` exists. `AuditLog` is indexed on `action` and `[actorId, createdAt]`, but not on `createdAt` alone | `auth/credentials.ts:83`, `schema.prisma:202` | FR-22: filter by action prefix and order by createdAt desc. This may need `@@index([createdAt])` for NFR-1. FR-38 parent sign-ins |\n26\t| `Gender` enum, `Section.homeroomTeacherId`, `TimetableSlot` and `LessonProgress` exist | `schema.prisma` | FR-18, FR-32 (homeroom recipient), FR-39, FR-13/38 |\n27\t| Notification types are a static map `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. `notify()` is in `notify.ts` | `notifications/types.ts`, `notify.ts` | FR-32: add the key `insights.student_high_risk` (ACADEMIC, TEACHER, email default true) |\n28\t| The cron dispatch route runs isolated try/catch passes on every call. The daily purge uses an in-memory `lastPurgeAt` | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | FR-27: add a risk pass. The \"at most once per hour\" rule must be stored in the DB (`max(computedAt)`), not in memory, because there are multiple processes |\n29\t| `csv.ts` exports `escapeCsvCell` and `toCsv(columns, rows)` | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-30, FR-33: reuse these. They already guard against formula injection |\n30\t| `studentTabs` registry, and `navigation` with `roles` + `requires` flags | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | FR-31, FR-40: append entries only |\n31\t| `@mui/material`, `@mui/x-charts` and `@mui/x-data-grid` are 9.5.0. Prisma is 5.20, Zod 3.23 | `package.json` | NFR-4/5: no new dependencies are needed |\n32\t| There is no `seed:large` script. The seed lives in `prisma/seed.ts` | `package.json` | FR-45/46 |\n33\t\n34\t## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n35\t\n36\tConcern codes: **UI** = new UI surface, **SVC** = service/query, **API** = endpoint, **DM** = data-model change, **JOB** = background/cron, **AUTH** = auth/scope boundary, **CACHE**, **CFG** = config registry, **XC** = cross-cutting rule.\n37\t\n38\t### Dashboards shell\n39\t\n40\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n41\t|---|---|---|\n42\t| FR-1 | UI, AUTH | `/dashboard` page switches on `getCurrentUser().role`. Keep the PARENT redirect. Use three role components under `src/app/(app)/dashboard/_components/` (or similar) |\n43\t| FR-2 | UI | One async server component per widget inside `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` + a client error boundary with a Retry button (`router.refresh()`). This needs one shared `WidgetCard` wrapper (title, updated-ago, boundary). It is used by ~20 widgets, so the abstraction pays for itself |\n44\t| FR-3 | SVC, XC | Greeting by the hour in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (NFR-7) + `getCurrentTerm().name`. Pure function `greetingFor(now, tz)`, which is unit-testable |\n45\t\n46\t### Teacher widgets (all scoped by `getAccessibleStudentIds` / taught courses, NFR-3)\n47\t\n48\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n49\t|---|---|---|\n50\t| FR-4 | SVC, UI | Today's TimetableSlots for the teacher's courses + attendance session existence per (course, period, date). `getToday(user)` in attendance-service probably already covers this. Check it before writing a new query. Now/Next comes from period times in the tz |\n51\t| FR-5 | SVC | Union of ungraded submissions (no grade on the linked GradeItem) and quiz attempts needing manual grading in the teacher's courses. Count + oldest 5 |\n52\t| FR-6 | SVC | Assignments/quizzes due within 7 days. Submission rate = submissions / active enrolments. Use one grouped query, not N+1 |\n53\t| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH | Read `StudentRiskSnapshot` filtered by accessible ids, order High > Medium, take 5. Do not compute live |\n54\t| FR-8 | SVC | `messaging.unreadCount` + announcements empty state (§3 Q1) |\n55\t| FR-9 | UI | Static links. No data. Check that the target routes exist (new announcement route is absent → omit or disable it, §3 Q1) |\n56\t\n57\t### Student widgets (scope = self)\n58\t\n59\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n60\t|---|---|---|\n61\t| FR-10 | SVC | Reuse the parent `getToday(user, user.id)`, which already handles `isNoSchool` holidays |\n62\t| FR-11 | SVC | Due in the next 7 days + missing items first. Share the missing predicate with FR-25/37 |\n63\t| FR-12 | SVC | Reuse the parent `getRecentGrades` |\n64\t| FR-13 | SVC | `getStudentGrades` (same as the Grades tab) + LessonProgress ratio + first incomplete visible lesson (`isLessonVisible`) |\n65\t| FR-14 | SVC | Empty state (§3 Q1) |\n66\t| FR-15 | SVC, UI | Term attendance rate via `countStatuses`/`attendanceRate` over the term range. Display with x-charts `Gauge` |\n67\t\n68\t### Admin widgets (ADMIN, cached)\n69\t\n70\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n71\t|---|---|---|\n72\t| FR-16 | SVC, CACHE, AUTH | Counts: active students/teachers, `getOverview(today)` rate + missing registers, the same weekday −7 days for the delta, pending absence notes (`absence-notes` service), safeguarding count **only if** `isSafeguardingLead`. The cache key must vary on lead status, or the safeguarding count must be fetched uncached separately |\n73\t| FR-17 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Daily rate for the last 30 **school days**. A school day is a date with ≥1 attendance session. That is simpler and more accurate than combining calendar + weekday logic. One `groupBy` on session date × status. `LineChart` + reference line at the threshold |\n74\t| FR-18 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Active students grouped by current-year section → grade level × gender. Stacked `BarChart` |\n75\t| FR-19 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Batch `computeStudentTerm` for all students in the current term → histogram in 10 % buckets, plus average and median. This is the most expensive admin query. See §4 |\n76\t| FR-20 | SVC | Group snapshots by level and reason. Reads the snapshot table only |\n77\t| FR-21 | SVC | The next 5 school-wide `CalendarEvent` occurrences via `expandOccurrences` (§3 Q2) |\n78\t| FR-22 | SVC | `AuditLog` where `action startsWith user./report_card./settings.`, latest 10, actor joined |\n79\t\n80\t### Caching\n81\t\n82\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n83\t|---|---|---|\n84\t| FR-23 | CACHE | `unstable_cache` wrappers in `src/server/dashboards/insights.ts`. Key = role scope (ADMIN: `'all'`; TEACHER: userId). Tags: `dashboard:admin`, `dashboard:teacher:<id>`, `insights:risk`. `revalidate` 900 s; risk 3600 s. Cached values must be JSON-serialisable, so convert Decimal/Date to number/string |\n85\t| FR-24 | CACHE, API, UI | Return `computedAt` from each cached function → \"Updated N min ago\". `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` → `revalidateTag(...)` + `recomputeRisk({ force: true })`. Audit this admin action |\n86\t| NFR-12 | CACHE, JOB | Satisfied by FR-23 (60 min) + FR-27 (hourly recompute) |\n87\t\n88\t### Early-warning risk\n89\t\n90\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n91\t|---|---|---|\n92\t| FR-25 | SVC | `risk.ts` has two parts. (a) Pure `scoreSignals({ attendancePct, coursePcts, missingCount }, threshold)` → per-signal level. (b) A batch loader that collects the three inputs for all ACTIVE students in the current term in a few grouped queries. Thresholds: attendance `< threshold` → Medium, `< 80` → High. Grades: any `< 60` → Medium, `≥2 < 60` or any `< 50` → High. Missing: 3–4 → Medium, `≥5` → High |\n93\t| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `combine(levels)`: any High or ≥2 Medium → High, exactly 1 Medium → Medium, otherwise none. Keep it in the same pure module as FR-25 for the NFR-9 unit tests |\n94\t| FR-27 | DM, JOB | New model + migration. Unique `(studentId, termId)`. Indexes on `(termId, level)`. Add `RiskLevel` enum (HIGH, MEDIUM, NONE). Hook into the dispatch route as an isolated pass, gated on `max(computedAt) < now − 1h` |\n95\t| FR-28 | DM | Conflicts with the \"one row\" rule. See §3 Q3 |\n96\t| FR-29 | UI, AUTH, SVC | Page `/insights/at-risk` (ADMIN, TEACHER). Server-side scope filter. Use the shared `DataTable`. Reason chips are formatted from `reasons` JSON. \"Message parents\" = link to the existing new-conversation flow (PRD-13) |\n97\t| FR-30 | SVC, API | The same service function serves the table and the CSV (`toCsv`), so their rows match. Filters: level, reason, grade level, section |\n98\t| FR-31 | CFG, UI, AUTH | Add `{ key: 'insights', roles: ['ADMIN','TEACHER'] }` to `studentTabs` + page `/students/[id]/insights` with `assertCanViewStudent` |\n99\t| FR-32 | JOB, XC | On upsert, if prev ∈ {none, MEDIUM} and new = HIGH, and there was no notification for this student in 14 days → `notify()` the homeroom teacher. A `lastHighNotifiedAt` column on the snapshot gives a DB-side 14-day claim, with no Notification table scan. If there is no homeroom teacher, skip and log |\n100\t\n101\t### Reports centre\n102\t\n103\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n104\t|---|---|---|\n105\t| FR-33 | UI, SVC, API | `/admin/reports` with year/term selectors (`x-date-pickers` for ranges) and one sub-route per report. Use a `REPORTS` registry in `src/server/reports/index.ts`: `key → { schema (Zod), run(filters), columns }`. The page, the API and the CSV all use that one registry, which also makes FR-44's 404 for unknown keys trivial |\n106\t| FR-34 | SVC | Enrollment: SectionMember/grade/gender groupings. Monthly new/archived from `createdAt`/`archivedAt` |\n107\t| FR-35 | SVC | Reuse `attendance-service.getReport`/aggregate. Group by grade/section/course + daily trend + bottom 20 |\n108\t| FR-36 | SVC | Batch `computeStudentTerm` grouped by course and subject + `letterFor`. Section comparison within the same grade × subject. Shares the batch loader with FR-19/FR-25 |\n109\t| FR-37 | SVC | On-time/late = submission `submittedAt` vs `dueAt`. Missing = shared predicate. Group by course and teacher |\n110\t| FR-38 | SVC | LessonProgress completion by course. Parent sign-ins = distinct `actorId` on `auth.login.success` in the last 7 and 30 days (and/or `lastLoginAt`). Announcement read rate is omitted (§3 Q1) |\n111\t| FR-39 | SVC | Per teacher: courses, distinct students, TimetableSlot count/week, grading backlog (reuse the FR-5 query) |\n112\t\n113\t### Navigation, API, seed\n114\t\n115\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n116\t|---|---|---|\n117\t| FR-40 | CFG | Add 'Reports' (ADMIN) and 'At-risk students' (ADMIN, TEACHER) after 'Dashboard' |\n118\t| FR-41 | API, AUTH | `GET /api/dashboard/{teacher,student,admin}` use the same service functions as the widgets, plus `requireRole`. Refresh uses POST, ADMIN only |\n119\t| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Zod query schema. **Intersect** the filtered ids with accessible ids so filters cannot widen scope. `?format=csv` → `text/csv` with a Content-Disposition header |\n120\t| FR-43 | API, AUTH | `assertCanViewStudent`, then the snapshot + current signal values |\n121\t| FR-44 | API | `reportKey` validated against the registry keys. Unknown key → 404 `NOT_FOUND` |\n122\t| FR-45 | XC | `prisma/seed-large.ts` + `\"seed:large\"` script. Use a seeded PRNG (a small mulberry32, no new dependency) |\n123\t| FR-46 | XC | The default seed builds ≥3 students per level. Tests should assert this by running `risk.ts` on the seed, not by hard-coding snapshot rows |\n124\t\n125\t### Non-functional\n126\t\n127\t| Req | Concern | Notes |\n128\t|---|---|---|\n129\t| NFR-1 | CACHE, SVC | Budget: 600 students × ~8 courses. Avoid per-student queries in risk, the grade distribution and reports. See §4 |\n130\t| NFR-2 | UI, XC | Every chart needs an `aria-label` summary built from the data + a visually hidden table. Use the MUI `visuallyHidden` util from `@mui/utils`, which comes in with material. Risk badges always show text (High/Medium), never colour alone |\n131\t| NFR-3 | AUTH | Enforce in the services (take `AccessUser`), not only in pages. Cached teacher data must be keyed per teacher id. **Never** share a teacher cache entry across users |\n132\t| NFR-4 | XC | MUI only: StatCard, DataTable, Gauge/LineChart/BarChart, Chip, Skeleton |\n133\t| NFR-5 | XC | The mui-mcp lookup is a dev/QA-phase process step and has no architectural impact. Flag it so dev-planning schedules it |\n134\t| NFR-6 | XC | Validators go in `src/lib/validators/dashboards.ts`, `insights.ts` and `reports.ts`. Use thin handlers and standard response shapes. Paginate the at-risk list |\n135\t| NFR-7 | XC | All windows (today, 7 days, 30 days, 30 school days) are computed from `schoolToday(now, tz)` |\n136\t| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse is listed per row above. **Do not** fork the attendance/gradebook calcs |\n137\t| NFR-9 | XC | Pure `risk-rules.ts` → boundary unit tests. Report integration tests on the seed. Playwright + axe per role |\n138\t| NFR-10 | XC | Use `logger`, not `console.log` |\n139\t| NFR-11 | XC | Rule-based only. No layout editor. No scheduled report emails |\n140\t\n141\t## 3. Open questions — proposed defaults for arch-design-system\n142\t\n143\t1. **Announcements (FR-8, FR-14, FR-38): proposed default is an empty state.** Render `EmptyState` with \"Announcements not available yet\", following the same stub pattern as `parent/overview-service.listUnreadAnnouncements` (ADR-11). Leave the announcement read rate out of the engagement report and add a note row. Hide 'New announcement' in FR-9 because the route does not exist. Record this as a dependency gap on PRD-12.\n144\t2. **Upcoming events (FR-21): read `CalendarEvent` directly.** Copy the `getUpcomingEvents` approach from the parent overview service: school-wide audience, `expandOccurrences`, next 5. Recurrence expansion already exists, so recurring events can be included.\n145\t3. **Snapshot history (FR-28): proposed option is (a), no new table.** Keep the unique `(studentId, termId)` row and add `previousLevel RiskLevel?` and `history Json` (an array capped at 10 entries of `{ level, reasons, computedAt }`, appended only when the level or the reasons change). That covers the trend arrow (level vs `previousLevel`) and the \"short history\" (FR-31) while keeping the \"one row per student per term\" rule in FR-27. Option (b), a `StudentRiskSnapshotHistory` table, is cleaner for analytics, but no requirement asks for it.\n146\t4. **Missing-work definition (FR-11/25/37):** published (`visibleWhere`), `dueAt` within the window and in the past, `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION`, no submission, no `GradeExemption`, student actively enrolled. Extract this into one shared function used by reminders, risk, the student widget and the completion report.\n147\t5. **No-data students: no signal.** If a student has no attendance records, the attendance signal is none. If a course has a null percent, it is ignored.\n148\t6. **\"Their students\":** `getAccessibleStudentIds` for the dashboard and list scope. The FR-32 notification goes **only** to the homeroom teacher (`Section.homeroomTeacherId` of the current-year section).\n149\t7. **New (not in intake):** the cache key for the FR-16 safeguarding KPI. Fetch that count outside the shared admin cache, per user, because it is cheap. A shared cached value would otherwise leak the count to admins who are not safeguarding leads.\n150\t8. **New:** with several cron processes, two could run the hourly recompute at the same time. Upserts are idempotent. The FR-32 notification needs an atomic claim (`updateMany where lastHighNotifiedAt < now−14d`), the same claim pattern that `reminders.ts` already uses.\n151\t\n152\t## 4. Performance hot spots (NFR-1)\n153\t\n154\t| Hot spot | Risk | Suggested approach |\n155\t|---|---|---|\n156\t| Grades for every student (FR-19, FR-25, FR-36) | `getStudentGrades` in a loop = 600 × several queries | One batch loader: load the grade items, grades, categories and overrides for the current term in ~5 queries, then run `computeStudentTerm` in memory. Share it across the three uses. FR-19 is cached for 15 min. Risk reads it only during recompute |\n157\t| Attendance aggregates (FR-16/17/25/35) | Row scans over a year of records | `groupBy` on `(studentId, status)` and on `(session.date, status)`. Check the indexes on `AttendanceRecord(studentId)` and `AttendanceSession(date)` |\n158\t| Missing work (FR-11/25/37) | Anti-join for each student × assignment | One query over the assignments in the window × active enrolments, minus submissions and exemptions, counted in memory |\n159\t| AuditLog feed (FR-22) | No `createdAt` index | Add `@@index([createdAt])` if the seed:large measurement shows a slow query |\n160\t| At-risk list (FR-29/42) | — | Read snapshot rows only. Paginate them and include the student/section joins |\n161\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187","uuid":"21bf2a98-d113-4ad4-8de9-5d4ae9e09c30","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:30:27.077Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/React Projects/schoolhub/artifacts/architect/requirements-analysis-notes.md","content":"# Requirements Analysis Notes: ticket SH-16\n\nWritten by `arch-research-reqs` for `arch-design-system`. This is a supporting document, not a primary phase output.\nSource: `artifacts/intake/requirements.json` (2026-11-10T12:00:00Z), PRD-16 Role Dashboards, Reports & Early-Warning Insights. It has 46 FRs and 12 NFRs (58 requirements) at 91% confidence.\n`handoff-to-architect.json` lists **no blockers** and 7 warnings. §3 proposes a default for each open question so that `arch-design-system` can decide.\nThe previous SH-15 version of this file was moved to `artifacts/architect/.prev-SH-15/`. The other files in `artifacts/architect/` are still SH-15 outputs until their owning sub-tasks overwrite them.\n\n## 1. Codebase facts verified (2026-11-10)\n\n| Fact | Where | Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| The dashboard page is a placeholder. It already redirects PARENT to `/my-children` | `src/app/(app)/dashboard/page.tsx` | FR-1: replace the body and keep the redirect line |\n| `getAccessibleStudentIds(user)` returns `'ALL'` for ADMIN and `string[]` for TEACHER (active course enrolments + homeroom section members). `assertCanViewStudent` also exists | `src/server/auth/student-access.ts` | NFR-3, FR-7/29/42/43: one scope source. Students outside a teacher's scope get **FORBIDDEN**, not NOT_FOUND |\n| `src/server/dashboards/` and `src/server/reports/` do not exist | — | NFR-6: create both as new feature folders |\n| There is no `unstable_cache` or `revalidateTag` anywhere. Next is **14.2.18** | `package.json` | FR-23/24: `unstable_cache` + `revalidateTag` work on 14.2. There is no `'use cache'` |\n| `SchoolSettings.timezone` and `attendanceAlertThreshold` (default 90) exist. `schoolToday(now, tz)` and `addDays` exist | `schema.prisma:222`, `attendance/attendance-rules.ts` | NFR-7, FR-17, FR-25: reuse these. Do not write new date helpers |\n| `getCurrentTerm(date)` exists. `Term` has start and end dates and belongs to an academic year | `src/server/services/academicYears.ts:96` | FR-3, FR-15, FR-25, FR-33: use it as the \"current term\" source |\n| Attendance service exports `getOverview(date)` (registers taken/missing + status counts), `getReport(filters)`, `getBelowThreshold()`, `attendanceRate()` and `countStatuses()` | `attendance/attendance-service.ts`, `attendance-rules.ts` | FR-16 (missing registers, today's rate), FR-17, FR-25 (attendance signal), FR-35: reuse these. Check `getReport` filters before you write new SQL |\n| `computeStudentTerm`, `letterFor` and `isUngradedPastDue` are pure. `getStudentGrades(user, studentId, termId)` is the Grades-tab source | `gradebook/grade-calc.ts`, `student-grades-service.ts` | FR-13 \"consistent with Grades tab\", FR-19, FR-25, FR-36: call the same calc. Calling `getStudentGrades` per student will not scale to 600 students (NFR-1), so use a batch path that runs `computeStudentTerm` |\n| \"Missing\" is derived. `SubmissionStatus` = SUBMITTED \\| RETURNED. `reminders.ts` uses `visibleWhere(now)` + `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION` + no submission + not exempt. Its lookback is 8 days | `assignments/reminders.ts` | FR-11, FR-25, FR-37: extract one shared `missingWhere(window)` predicate. Risk needs a 30-day window |\n| Parent overview service has `getToday` (timetable plus `isNoSchool` holiday check), `getRecentGrades`, `getAssignmentsSummary` and `getUpcomingEvents` (CalendarEvent + `expandOccurrences`). `listUnreadAnnouncements` is a stub that returns `[]` (ADR-11 precedent) | `src/server/parent/overview-service.ts` | FR-10/11/12: student widgets can call these with `studentId = user.id`. FR-14 follows the same stub precedent. FR-21 copies the events query with a school-wide audience and no meetings |\n| `CalendarEvent` (recurrence, `isNoSchool`) and `expandOccurrences(event, from, to, tz)` exist. There is still no calendar service or API | `schema.prisma:1281`, `calendar/recurrence.ts` | FR-21: read the model directly and expand recurrences. This removes the warning's \"non-recurring only\" limit |\n| There is no `Announcement` model, only `announcements/audience.ts` | `schema.prisma` | FR-8, FR-14, FR-38: show an empty state or omit the metric |\n| `messaging/conversations.unreadCount(userId)`. `isSafeguardingLead(user)`. `safeguarding.listReports` | `src/server/messaging/` | FR-8 unread count. FR-16 KPI only when `isSafeguardingLead`. For the count, add `count` on open reports. Do not page through the list |\n| `audit({ action: 'auth.login.success' })` is written on login. `User.lastLoginAt` exists. `AuditLog` is indexed on `action` and `[actorId, createdAt]`, but not on `createdAt` alone | `auth/credentials.ts:83`, `schema.prisma:202` | FR-22: filter by action prefix and order by createdAt desc. This may need `@@index([createdAt])` for NFR-1. FR-38 parent sign-ins |\n| `Gender` enum, `Section.homeroomTeacherId`, `TimetableSlot` and `LessonProgress` exist | `schema.prisma` | FR-18, FR-32 (homeroom recipient), FR-39, FR-13/38 |\n| Notification types are a static map `NOTIFICATION_TYPES`. `notify()` is in `notify.ts` | `notifications/types.ts`, `notify.ts` | FR-32: add the key `insights.student_high_risk` (ACADEMIC, TEACHER, email default true) |\n| The cron dispatch route runs isolated try/catch passes on every call. The daily purge uses an in-memory `lastPurgeAt` | `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | FR-27: add a risk pass. The \"at most once per hour\" rule must be stored in the DB (`max(computedAt)`), not in memory, because there are multiple processes |\n| `csv.ts` exports `escapeCsvCell` and `toCsv(columns, rows)` | `src/server/csv.ts` | FR-30, FR-33: reuse these. They already guard against formula injection |\n| `studentTabs` registry, and `navigation` with `roles` + `requires` flags | `src/config/student-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts` | FR-31, FR-40: append entries only |\n| `@mui/material`, `@mui/x-charts` and `@mui/x-data-grid` are 9.5.0. Prisma is 5.20, Zod 3.23 | `package.json` | NFR-4/5: no new dependencies are needed |\n| There is no `seed:large` script. The seed lives in `prisma/seed.ts` | `package.json` | FR-45/46 |\n\n## 2. Requirement → architectural concern\n\nConcern codes: **UI** = new UI surface, **SVC** = service/query, **API** = endpoint, **DM** = data-model change, **JOB** = background/cron, **AUTH** = auth/scope boundary, **CACHE**, **CFG** = config registry, **XC** = cross-cutting rule.\n\n### Dashboards shell\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | UI, AUTH | `/dashboard` page switches on `getCurrentUser().role`. Keep the PARENT redirect. Use three role components under `src/app/(app)/dashboard/_components/` (or similar) |\n| FR-2 | UI | One async server component per widget inside `<Suspense fallback={<LoadingSkeleton/>}>` + a client error boundary with a Retry button (`router.refresh()`). This needs one shared `WidgetCard` wrapper (title, updated-ago, boundary). It is used by ~20 widgets, so the abstraction pays for itself |\n| FR-3 | SVC, XC | Greeting by the hour in `SchoolSettings.timezone` (NFR-7) + `getCurrentTerm().name`. Pure function `greetingFor(now, tz)`, which is unit-testable |\n\n### Teacher widgets (all scoped by `getAccessibleStudentIds` / taught courses, NFR-3)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-4 | SVC, UI | Today's TimetableSlots for the teacher's courses + attendance session existence per (course, period, date). `getToday(user)` in attendance-service probably already covers this. Check it before writing a new query. Now/Next comes from period times in the tz |\n| FR-5 | SVC | Union of ungraded submissions (no grade on the linked GradeItem) and quiz attempts needing manual grading in the teacher's courses. Count + oldest 5 |\n| FR-6 | SVC | Assignments/quizzes due within 7 days. Submission rate = submissions / active enrolments. Use one grouped query, not N+1 |\n| FR-7 | SVC, AUTH | Read `StudentRiskSnapshot` filtered by accessible ids, order High > Medium, take 5. Do not compute live |\n| FR-8 | SVC | `messaging.unreadCount` + announcements empty state (§3 Q1) |\n| FR-9 | UI | Static links. No data. Check that the target routes exist (new announcement route is absent → omit or disable it, §3 Q1) |\n\n### Student widgets (scope = self)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-10 | SVC | Reuse the parent `getToday(user, user.id)`, which already handles `isNoSchool` holidays |\n| FR-11 | SVC | Due in the next 7 days + missing items first. Share the missing predicate with FR-25/37 |\n| FR-12 | SVC | Reuse the parent `getRecentGrades` |\n| FR-13 | SVC | `getStudentGrades` (same as the Grades tab) + LessonProgress ratio + first incomplete visible lesson (`isLessonVisible`) |\n| FR-14 | SVC | Empty state (§3 Q1) |\n| FR-15 | SVC, UI | Term attendance rate via `countStatuses`/`attendanceRate` over the term range. Display with x-charts `Gauge` |\n\n### Admin widgets (ADMIN, cached)\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-16 | SVC, CACHE, AUTH | Counts: active students/teachers, `getOverview(today)` rate + missing registers, the same weekday −7 days for the delta, pending absence notes (`absence-notes` service), safeguarding count **only if** `isSafeguardingLead`. The cache key must vary on lead status, or the safeguarding count must be fetched uncached separately |\n| FR-17 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Daily rate for the last 30 **school days**. A school day is a date with ≥1 attendance session. That is simpler and more accurate than combining calendar + weekday logic. One `groupBy` on session date × status. `LineChart` + reference line at the threshold |\n| FR-18 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Active students grouped by current-year section → grade level × gender. Stacked `BarChart` |\n| FR-19 | SVC, CACHE, UI | Batch `computeStudentTerm` for all students in the current term → histogram in 10 % buckets, plus average and median. This is the most expensive admin query. See §4 |\n| FR-20 | SVC | Group snapshots by level and reason. Reads the snapshot table only |\n| FR-21 | SVC | The next 5 school-wide `CalendarEvent` occurrences via `expandOccurrences` (§3 Q2) |\n| FR-22 | SVC | `AuditLog` where `action startsWith user./report_card./settings.`, latest 10, actor joined |\n\n### Caching\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-23 | CACHE | `unstable_cache` wrappers in `src/server/dashboards/insights.ts`. Key = role scope (ADMIN: `'all'`; TEACHER: userId). Tags: `dashboard:admin`, `dashboard:teacher:<id>`, `insights:risk`. `revalidate` 900 s; risk 3600 s. Cached values must be JSON-serialisable, so convert Decimal/Date to number/string |\n| FR-24 | CACHE, API, UI | Return `computedAt` from each cached function → \"Updated N min ago\". `POST /api/dashboard/refresh` → `revalidateTag(...)` + `recomputeRisk({ force: true })`. Audit this admin action |\n| NFR-12 | CACHE, JOB | Satisfied by FR-23 (60 min) + FR-27 (hourly recompute) |\n\n### Early-warning risk\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-25 | SVC | `risk.ts` has two parts. (a) Pure `scoreSignals({ attendancePct, coursePcts, missingCount }, threshold)` → per-signal level. (b) A batch loader that collects the three inputs for all ACTIVE students in the current term in a few grouped queries. Thresholds: attendance `< threshold` → Medium, `< 80` → High. Grades: any `< 60` → Medium, `≥2 < 60` or any `< 50` → High. Missing: 3–4 → Medium, `≥5` → High |\n| FR-26 | SVC | Pure `combine(levels)`: any High or ≥2 Medium → High, exactly 1 Medium → Medium, otherwise none. Keep it in the same pure module as FR-25 for the NFR-9 unit tests |\n| FR-27 | DM, JOB | New model + migration. Unique `(studentId, termId)`. Indexes on `(termId, level)`. Add `RiskLevel` enum (HIGH, MEDIUM, NONE). Hook into the dispatch route as an isolated pass, gated on `max(computedAt) < now − 1h` |\n| FR-28 | DM | Conflicts with the \"one row\" rule. See §3 Q3 |\n| FR-29 | UI, AUTH, SVC | Page `/insights/at-risk` (ADMIN, TEACHER). Server-side scope filter. Use the shared `DataTable`. Reason chips are formatted from `reasons` JSON. \"Message parents\" = link to the existing new-conversation flow (PRD-13) |\n| FR-30 | SVC, API | The same service function serves the table and the CSV (`toCsv`), so their rows match. Filters: level, reason, grade level, section |\n| FR-31 | CFG, UI, AUTH | Add `{ key: 'insights', roles: ['ADMIN','TEACHER'] }` to `studentTabs` + page `/students/[id]/insights` with `assertCanViewStudent` |\n| FR-32 | JOB, XC | On upsert, if prev ∈ {none, MEDIUM} and new = HIGH, and there was no notification for this student in 14 days → `notify()` the homeroom teacher. A `lastHighNotifiedAt` column on the snapshot gives a DB-side 14-day claim, with no Notification table scan. If there is no homeroom teacher, skip and log |\n\n### Reports centre\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-33 | UI, SVC, API | `/admin/reports` with year/term selectors (`x-date-pickers` for ranges) and one sub-route per report. Use a `REPORTS` registry in `src/server/reports/index.ts`: `key → { schema (Zod), run(filters), columns }`. The page, the API and the CSV all use that one registry, which also makes FR-44's 404 for unknown keys trivial |\n| FR-34 | SVC | Enrollment: SectionMember/grade/gender groupings. Monthly new/archived from `createdAt`/`archivedAt` |\n| FR-35 | SVC | Reuse `attendance-service.getReport`/aggregate. Group by grade/section/course + daily trend + bottom 20 |\n| FR-36 | SVC | Batch `computeStudentTerm` grouped by course and subject + `letterFor`. Section comparison within the same grade × subject. Shares the batch loader with FR-19/FR-25 |\n| FR-37 | SVC | On-time/late = submission `submittedAt` vs `dueAt`. Missing = shared predicate. Group by course and teacher |\n| FR-38 | SVC | LessonProgress completion by course. Parent sign-ins = distinct `actorId` on `auth.login.success` in the last 7 and 30 days (and/or `lastLoginAt`). Announcement read rate is omitted (§3 Q1) |\n| FR-39 | SVC | Per teacher: courses, distinct students, TimetableSlot count/week, grading backlog (reuse the FR-5 query) |\n\n### Navigation, API, seed\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-40 | CFG | Add 'Reports' (ADMIN) and 'At-risk students' (ADMIN, TEACHER) after 'Dashboard' |\n| FR-41 | API, AUTH | `GET /api/dashboard/{teacher,student,admin}` use the same service functions as the widgets, plus `requireRole`. Refresh uses POST, ADMIN only |\n| FR-42 | API, AUTH | Zod query schema. **Intersect** the filtered ids with accessible ids so filters cannot widen scope. `?format=csv` → `text/csv` with a Content-Disposition header |\n| FR-43 | API, AUTH | `assertCanViewStudent`, then the snapshot + current signal values |\n| FR-44 | API | `reportKey` validated against the registry keys. Unknown key → 404 `NOT_FOUND` |\n| FR-45 | XC | `prisma/seed-large.ts` + `\"seed:large\"` script. Use a seeded PRNG (a small mulberry32, no new dependency) |\n| FR-46 | XC | The default seed builds ≥3 students per level. Tests should assert this by running `risk.ts` on the seed, not by hard-coding snapshot rows |\n\n### Non-functional\n\n| Req | Concern | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| NFR-1 | CACHE, SVC | Budget: 600 students × ~8 courses. Avoid per-student queries in risk, the grade distribution and reports. See §4 |\n| NFR-2 | UI, XC | Every chart needs an `aria-label` summary built from the data + a visually hidden table. Use the MUI `visuallyHidden` util from `@mui/utils`, which comes in with material. Risk badges always show text (High/Medium), never colour alone |\n| NFR-3 | AUTH | Enforce in the services (take `AccessUser`), not only in pages. Cached teacher data must be keyed per teacher id. **Never** share a teacher cache entry across users |\n| NFR-4 | XC | MUI only: StatCard, DataTable, Gauge/LineChart/BarChart, Chip, Skeleton |\n| NFR-5 | XC | The mui-mcp lookup is a dev/QA-phase process step and has no architectural impact. Flag it so dev-planning schedules it |\n| NFR-6 | XC | Validators go in `src/lib/validators/dashboards.ts`, `insights.ts` and `reports.ts`. Use thin handlers and standard response shapes. Paginate the at-risk list |\n| NFR-7 | XC | All windows (today, 7 days, 30 days, 30 school days) are computed from `schoolToday(now, tz)` |\n| NFR-8 | XC | Reuse is listed per row above. **Do not** fork the attendance/gradebook calcs |\n| NFR-9 | XC | Pure `risk-rules.ts` → boundary unit tests. Report integration tests on the seed. Playwright + axe per role |\n| NFR-10 | XC | Use `logger`, not `console.log` |\n| NFR-11 | XC | Rule-based only. No layout editor. No scheduled report emails |\n\n## 3. Open questions — proposed defaults for arch-design-system\n\n1. **Announcements (FR-8, FR-14, FR-38): proposed default is an empty state.** Render `EmptyState` with \"Announcements not available yet\", following the same stub pattern as `parent/overview-service.listUnreadAnnouncements` (ADR-11). Leave the announcement read rate out of the engagement report and add a note row. Hide 'New announcement' in FR-9 because the route does not exist. Record this as a dependency gap on PRD-12.\n2. **Upcoming events (FR-21): read `CalendarEvent` directly.** Copy the `getUpcomingEvents` approach from the parent overview service: school-wide audience, `expandOccurrences`, next 5. Recurrence expansion already exists, so recurring events can be included.\n3. **Snapshot history (FR-28): proposed option is (a), no new table.** Keep the unique `(studentId, termId)` row and add `previousLevel RiskLevel?` and `history Json` (an array capped at 10 entries of `{ level, reasons, computedAt }`, appended only when the level or the reasons change). That covers the trend arrow (level vs `previousLevel`) and the \"short history\" (FR-31) while keeping the \"one row per student per term\" rule in FR-27. Option (b), a `StudentRiskSnapshotHistory` table, is cleaner for analytics, but no requirement asks for it.\n4. **Missing-work definition (FR-11/25/37):** published (`visibleWhere`), `dueAt` within the window and in the past, `submissionType != NO_SUBMISSION`, no submission, no `GradeExemption`, student actively enrolled. Extract this into one shared function used by reminders, risk, the student widget and the completion report.\n5. **No-data students: no signal.** If a student has no attendance records, the attendance signal is none. If a course has a null percent, it is ignored.\n6. **\"Their students\":** `getAccessibleStudentIds` for the dashboard and list scope. The FR-32 notification goes **only** to the homeroom teacher (`Section.homeroomTeacherId` of the current-year section).\n7. **New (not in intake):** the cache key for the FR-16 safeguarding KPI. Fetch that count outside the shared admin cache, per user, because it is cheap. A shared cached value would otherwise leak the count to admins who are not safeguarding leads.\n8. **New:** with several cron processes, two could run the hourly recompute at the same time. Upserts are idempotent. The FR-32 notification needs an atomic claim (`updateMany where lastHighNotifiedAt < now−14d`), the same claim pattern that `reminders.ts` already uses.\n\n## 4. Performance hot spots (NFR-1)\n\n| Hot spot | Risk | Suggested approach |\n|---|---|---|\n| Grades for every student (FR-19, FR-25, FR-36) | `getStudentGrades` in a loop = 600 × several queries | One batch loader: load the grade items, grades, categories and overrides for the current term in ~5 queries, then run `computeStudentTerm` in memory. Share it across the three uses. FR-19 is cached for 15 min. Risk reads it only during recompute |\n| Attendance aggregates (FR-16/17/25/35) | Row scans over a year of records | `groupBy` on `(studentId, status)` and on `(session.date, status)`. Check the indexes on `AttendanceRecord(studentId)` and `AttendanceSession(date)` |\n| Missing work (FR-11/25/37) | Anti-join for each student × assignment | One query over the assignments in the window × active enrolments, minus submissions and exemptions, counted in memory |\n| AuditLog feed (FR-22) | No `createdAt` index | Add `@@index([createdAt])` if the seed:large measurement shows a slow query |\n| At-risk list (FR-29/42) | — | Read snapshot rows only. Paginate them and include the student/section joins |\n","numLines":161,"startLine":1,"totalLines":161}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JjYG59fSwyqjpRKJVe8mxz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
