{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgtd23GgFdTRfEQ18wFUw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written `artifacts/architect/system-design.md` for ticket SH-16 (status: complete). It covers every requirement: all 46 functional and 12 non-functional ids are cited, and none are made up (checked against `requirements.json` with a script).\n\n**Main design choices:**\n- **One set of functions per feature:** the dashboard widgets, the `/api/*` routes and the CSV exports all call the same server functions. Those functions also enforce which students a user may see, so a teacher's filters can only narrow their own student list, never widen it.\n- **Dashboard widgets:** each widget loads on its own behind a loading skeleton. If one fails, it shows an error with a Retry button and the rest of the page still works. This adds one shared `Widget` wrapper and a small error-handling component.\n- **Risk scoring:** the threshold rules are plain functions with no database access, so every boundary can be unit-tested. A separate loader pulls the data for all 600 students in a fixed number of queries, never one student at a time. The intake conflict between \"one row per student per term\" and needing a trend arrow and history is resolved by keeping one row per student per term and adding `previousLevel` plus a short `history` list (last 10 level changes).\n- **No duplicate teacher alerts:** the high-risk notification records when it was last sent and claims that slot in one database step. Two copies of the hourly job running at once can't both send it.\n- **Hourly recompute:** it runs from the existing internal cron route. The \"at most once an hour\" check reads the newest snapshot time from the database, not a value held in memory.\n- **Shared code:** one grade loader serves the grade chart, the risk scoring and the performance report, and uses the same grade calculation as the Grades tab, so the numbers match. One shared definition of \"missing work\" replaces the copy in `reminders.ts`.\n- **Caching:** teacher cache entries always include the teacher's id, so no teacher sees another's cached data. The safeguarding count is never cached, so admins who aren't safeguarding leads can't see it.\n- **Reports:** a single list of the six report types drives the pages, the API and the CSV. CSV rows always match the table, and an unknown report name returns 404.\n\n**Gaps (no blockers from intake):**\n- **Announcements:** there is no Announcement model yet, so those widgets show an empty state and the engagement report leaves out the read rate. One constant switches them on once that feature ships.\n- **Upcoming events:** there is no calendar service, so this widget reads the existing `CalendarEvent` model directly, including recurring events.\n\nThe old SH-15 `system-design.md` is moved to `.prev-SH-15/`. `api-contracts.json` and `handoff-to-dev-planning.json` are still SH-15 leftovers until `arch-api-contracts` runs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378,"cache_read_input_tokens":76621,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":378,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2edbcc3a-ff1f-4530-a14b-b4daf8da1187","uuid":"7ece0c7e-91f7-4453-a247-70402643a31f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T04:32:40.650Z","request_id":"req_011Cgtd234XRkaoPHDZZZ8dm"}
